aind:TMP-T-00229 rdfs:label "شرح المختصر (الأصلي لابن الحاجب) للركن الخوافي"@ar,
        "Sharḥ al-Mukhtaṣar (al-aṣlī) li-l-Rukn al-Khawāfī"@ar-Latn ;
    aindv:category aindv:cat_Text .

aind:TMP-T-00230 rdfs:label "المواقف في علم الكلام"@ar,
        "المواقف للإيجي"@ar,
        "al-Mawāqif li-l-Ījī"@ar-Latn ;
    aindv:category aindv:cat_Text .

rec:AIND-D00001 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00001-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00001-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00001 ;
    aindv:sourceText "آدم بن سعد بن عيسى الكيلاني الأصل ثم المكي قطنها نحوا من عشرين سنة وزوج بها واسكن بأخرة رباط سكر وكان معتقدا . مات في ذي القعدة سنة سبع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ādam b. Saʿd b. ʿĪsā, originally al-Kīlānī, then al-Makkī. He resided in Mecca for nearly twenty years and married there, and in his later years, he lived in Ribāṭ Sukkar. He was a trusted person. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 867 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00002 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00002-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00002 ;
    aindv:sourceText "آدم بن سعيد بن أبي بكر الجبرتي الحنفي نزيل مكة والمتوفى بها شابا قطنها مديما للاشتغال على فضلائها والواردين عليها في الفقه وأصوله والعربية وغيرها وللتلاوة على طريقة جميلة وإناقة من شيوخه السراج معمر بن عبد القوي في العربية وعبد النبي المغربي وسمع على وأنا بمكة الكثير من الصحيح وغيره بل حضر عندي بعض الدروس . مات في ليلة الأربعاء خامس ذي الحجة سنة سبع وثمانين وصلى عليه من الغد ودفن بالمعلاة عوضه الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Adam b. Saʿīd b. Abī Bakr al-Jabartī al-Ḥanafī, a resident of Mecca who died there as a young man. He dwelled there, continuously studying under its eminent scholars and those who came to it, in fiqh, its principles (usūl al-fiqh), Arabic, and other subjects, and for recitation in a beautiful and elegant manner. Among his shaykhs were al-Sirāj Muʿammar b. ʿAbd al-Qawī in Arabic, and ʿAbd al-Nabī al-Maghribī. He also heard from me (al-Sakhāwī), while I was in Mecca, much of al-Ṣaḥīḥ and other works. Moreover, he attended some lessons with me. He died on Wednesday night, the fifth of Dhū al-Ḥijja, in the year eight hundred and eighty-seven. Funeral prayers were performed for him the next day, and he was buried in al-Muʿallā. May God compensate him with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D00003 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00003-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00003 ;
    aindv:sourceText "آدم بن عبد الرحمن بن حاجي الوركاني مات سنة بضع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ādam b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ḥājjī al-Warkānī died in the 820s AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00004 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00004-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00004-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00004 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أبان بن عثمان بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي المكي ولد في آخر سنة أربعين وثمانمائة وسمع على أبي الفتح المراغي وأجاز له جماعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abān b. ʿUthmān b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓuhayra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭīya b. Ẓuhayra al-Qurashī al-Makkī. He was born at the end of the year 840 H and heard (ḥadīth) from Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī. He was also granted an ijāza by a group (of scholars)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00005 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00005-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00005-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00005 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أبجد رجل مجذوب كان يكثر التنقل من بيت المقدس إلى مكة صحبة الزين عبد القادر النووي المقدسي وانتفع بلحظه وما علمت متى مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abjad was a majdhūb man. He frequently traveled from Bayt al-Maqdis to Mecca in the company of al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Nawawī al-Maqdisī, and he benefited from his attention. I do not know when he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D00006 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00006-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00006-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00006 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن أحمد البصري نزيل مكة والآتي أبوه وأخواه محمد وإسماعيل ويعرف بابن زقزق ممن قطن مكة ورأيته بها في سنة ثلاث وتسعين وكذا جاور بالمدينة سنين وكان أبوه وأخوه محمد من علماء البصرة وهو من الصلحاء . مات في رمضان سنة ثمان وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Baṣrī, a resident of Mecca. His father and his two brothers, Muḥammad and Ismāʿīl, will be mentioned later. Known as Ibn Zaqzaq, he was among those who settled in Mecca, and I saw him there in the year 893 H. He also resided in Medina for several years. His father and his brother Muḥammad were scholars from Basra, but he (Ibrāhīm himself) was one of the righteous. He died in Ramadan of the year 898 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00007 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00007-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00007 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن عبد القادر بن محمد بن عبد القادر المحب أبو الفضل بن البرهان بن البدراني عبد الله الجعفري المقدسي ثم النابلسي الحنبلي الآتي أبوه وجده وعمه الكمال محمد من بيت قضاء واعتبار عرض على الخرقى وقرأ على بعض البخارى سوى ما سمعه على منه ومن غيره كل ذلك في سنة ثمان وثمانين وعاد إلى بيت المقدس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Muḥibb Abū al-Faḍl, al-Jaʿfarī al-Maqdisī, then al-Nābulusī, of the Hanbali madhhab, whose nasab extends to al-Burhān b. al-Badrānī ʿAbd Allāh. His father, grandfather, and his uncle al-Kamāl Muḥammad will be mentioned later. His family was from a lineage of judgeship and esteemed position. He presented to al-Khiraqī and recited parts of al-Bukhārī (al-Ṣaḥīḥ), in addition to what he heard from him (unnamed teacher) and from others, all in the year 888 H. Afterwards, he returned to Bayt al-Maqdis."@en .

rec:AIND-D00008 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00008-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00008-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00008-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1_B88,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00008 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن مسعود القاهري المولد والدار الآتي أبوه . ويعرف كل منهما بابن سابق ولد بعد الستين وثمانمائة وحفظ القرآن وقرأ يسيرا من المنهاج حفظا أو حلا ثم زوجه والده وتشاغل بالأذان والوقيد ونحوهما بالمنكوتمرية بل أخذ إمامتها وغيرها من الوظائف : كالصلاحية وغيرها بعد أبيه وحج وتكسب بعد ببعض الحوانيت عند باب القنطرة وربما اشتغل بالخياطة وعمل حاسبا وفقه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Masʿūd al-Qāhirī by birth and residence. His father will be mentioned later. Both he and his father were known as Ibn Sābiq. He was born after 860 H., memorized the Qurʾān, and studied a little of al-Minhāj (likely *Minhāj al-ṭālibīn*) by memorization or explanation. Then his father married him, and he became preoccupied with the call to prayer (adhān) and night watchman (waqīd) duties, and similar roles at al-Mankūtamurīya. Indeed, he took its imamate and other offices, such as at al-Ṣalāḥīya and others, after his father. He performed the Hajj and earned a living in some shops near Bāb al-Qanṭara, sometimes working as a tailor and as an accountant. May God grant him understanding of jurisprudence."@en .

rec:AIND-D00009 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00009-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00009-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00009-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00009 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن إبراهيم بن محمد برهان الدين النووي الدمشقي الشافعي ويقال إنه قريب النووي أخذ عن التقى بن قاضي شهبة وتكسب بالشهادة وتميز في الفرائض والحساب ومتعلقاتهما وأقرأ ذلك الطلبة وانتفع به جماعة كأبي الفضل بن الإمام وأخبرني أنه شرح المنهاج ونظم فرائضه ثم ضم إليه الحساب ومتعلقاته في ألفية سماها الحلاوة السكرية زاد غيره أنه شرح الجرومية وكان سريع النظم حسنه . مات تقريبا سنة خمس وثمانين بدمشق وقد جاز السبعين رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad Burhān al-Dīn al-Nawawī al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī. It is said that he was a relative of al-Nawawī. He acquired knowledge from al-Taqī b. Qāḍī Shuhba. He earned his living as a notary/witness. He excelled in inheritance law and arithmetic and their related subjects, teaching these to students. A group, such as Abū al-Faḍl b. al-Imām, benefited from him. He informed me that he commented on 『al-Minhāj』 and versified its inheritance laws, then combined it with arithmetic and its related subjects in an alfiyya (thousand-line poem) which he named 『al-Ḥalāwa al-Sukkarīya』. Others added that he commented on 『al-Ājurrūmīya』. He was quick and good at versification. He died around 885 H in Damascus, having passed seventy years of age. May God have mercy on him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D00011 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00011-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00011 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن إبراهيم برهان الدين الشيرازي الموقت لقيه الحافظ الجمال ابن موسى المراكشي باسكندرية وترجمه بالاستاذ الفاضل الموقت وقال له مؤلفات في علم الميقات ويد طولى في متعلقاته من النجوم وغيرها واستجازه لجماعة منهم ابن فهد وذكره في معجمه بذلك . وما علمت وقت وفاته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm, titled Burhān al-Dīn, from Shīrāz, and a prayer-time calculator (muwaqqit). al-Ḥāfiẓ al-Jamāl Ibn Mūsā al-Marākushī met him in Alexandria and wrote his biography, describing him as \"the excellent master and muwaqqit.\" He stated that Ibrāhīm had compositions in the science of timekeeping and extensive knowledge in related fields such as astronomy. He sought an ijāza from him for a group, including Ibn Fahd, and mentioned this in his biographical dictionary. The time of his death is unknown."@en .

rec:AIND-D00012 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00012-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00012 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن إبراهيم الرومي الأصل العجمي الحنفي نزيل القاهرة وأخو حيدر الآتي له ذكر فيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm, of Rūmī origin, al-ʿAjamī al-Ḥanafī, resident of al-Qāhira. He is the brother of Ḥaydar (to be mentioned later), who will be discussed in his entry."@en .

rec:AIND-D00016 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00016-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00016 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن أبي بكر بن خليفة البجائي قاضيها في زمنه . مات في سنة ست وستين أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Khalīfa al-Bijāʾī. He was its qadi in his time. He died in the year 866, as recorded by Ibn ʿAzm."@en .

rec:AIND-D00020 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00020-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00020-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00020-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00020 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن حسن بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن الأذرعي الأصل أحد الأخوة من بني الإمام شهاب الدين وشقيق الكمال محمد ممن سمع في البخاري بالظاهرية واختص بالكمال ناظر الجيش وحج معه في سنة تسع وثمانين وجاور التي تليها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Adhraʿī, originally from Adhraʿ. He was one of the brothers from the family of Imam Shihāb al-Dīn and the full brother of al-Kamāl Muḥammad. He heard al-Bukhārī at al-Ẓāhiriyya (madrasa) in Adhraʿ and was closely associated with al-Kamāl Nāẓir al-Jaysh. He performed the Hajj with him in the year [8]89 (AH) and resided in Mecca the following year."@en .

rec:AIND-D00021 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00021-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00021-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00021 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن حسين الموصلي ثم المصري المالكي نزيل مكة كذا ذكره شيخنا والمقريزي بن محمد بن حسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Ḥusayn al-Mawṣilī, then al-Miṣrī, of the Mālikī school. A resident of Mecca. Thus did our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and al-Maqrīzī b. Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn mention him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00022 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00022-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00022 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن خضر الصالحي الحنفي مات سنة ست عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Khiḍr al-Ṣāliḥī al-Ḥanafī died in the year 816 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00025 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00025-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00025-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00025 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن عامر السعدي شيخ عمر دهرا فيما قيل وحدث بالإجازة العامة عن الفخر بن البخاري روى عنه التقى أبو بكر القلقشندي وقال أنه بقي إلى حدود سنة خمس عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. ʿĀmir al-Saʿdī. It is said that he lived for a long time as a shaykh. He transmitted ḥadīth with a general ijāza from al-Fakhr b. al-Bukhārī. Al-Taqī Abū Bakr al-Qalqashandī transmitted from him and stated that he lived until around the year 815 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00026 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00026-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00026 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عوض الطنتدائي الأصل القاهري الشافعي الآتي أبوه وأخوه عبد الرحمن لم يكن ممن سلك طريق والده ولا قريبا منها بل كان متصرفا بأبواب القضاة وبيده نصف أمامة الرباط بالبيبرسية حتى مات قريبا من سنة ثمانين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwaḍ al-Ṭanṭidāʾī, originally from Cairo, a Shāfiʿī. Unlike his father and his brother ʿAbd al-Raḥmān (to be mentioned later), he did not follow his father's path, nor anything close to it. Rather, he served as an official at the judges' gates and held half the imamate of the Ribāṭ at al-Baybarsiyya until he died close to the year 880 H. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00029 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00029-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00029 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن عبد اللطيف بن نجم بن عبد المعطي البرماوي والد الفخر عثمان وإخوته . مات كما قاله شيخنا في ترجمة ولده قبله بعشر سنين فيكون موته سنة ست وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Najm b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī al-Birmāwī, father of al-Fakhr ʿUthmān and his brothers. He died, as our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his son’s biography, ten years before his son’s death, which would make his death in the year 806 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00031 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00031-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00031-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_apply ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00031 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن علي بن خلف بن عبد العزيز بن بدران برهان الدين ابن إسحاق بن محمد البرهان الخليلي الدارمي عرف بابن المحتسب ولى بعد أخيه الشمس محمد قضاء بلده وقدما القاهرة بسبب صهره أبي بكر أمين حرم وكان حيا بعد ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Khalaf b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Badrān, Burhān al-Dīn, known as Ibn al-Muḥtasib, of the lineage of Isḥāq b. Muḥammad al-Burhān al-Khalīlī al-Dārimī. He succeeded his brother al-Shams Muḥammad in the judgeship of his town. He came to Cairo because of his son-in-law Abū Bakr Amīn Ḥaram. He was alive after 893 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00039 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00039-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00039-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00039-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00039-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00039 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن أبي عريان التونسي شيخ الكتبة في قطره مات بمكة بعيد المغرب من ليلة الأحد ثاني رمضان سنة ثمانين ودفن بمقبرة شيكه لا لومد أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Abī ʿUryān al-Tūnisī. He was the shaykh of scribes in his region/country. He died in Makka shortly after the Maghrib prayer on Sunday night, the 2nd of Ramaḍān in the year 880 H, and was buried in Maqbarat Shīka Lā Lawmad. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his biography/date."@en .

rec:AIND-D00044 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00044-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00044 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن أبي الخير محمد بن فهد الهاشمي المكي في ابن أبي بكر بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Khayr Muḥammad b. Fahd al-Hāshimī al-Makkī. (His entry is found under Ibn Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad.)"@en .

rec:AIND-D00052 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00052-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00052 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن يوسف القدسي الأصل ثم الدمشقي التاجر ممن سمع مني بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة ثلاث وتسعين المسلسل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf, originally from Jerusalem, later from Damascus, was a merchant. He was among those who heard 『al-Musalsal』 from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal 893 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00053 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00053-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00053-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00053-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B87,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00053 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أحمد بن يونس برهان الدين أبو اسحاق بن الفاضل شهاب الدين الغزي الأصل الحلبي الشافعي نزيل المدرسة الشرفية بحلب والآتي أبوه ويعرف بابن الضعيف بالتصغير والتثقيل ولد في حدود سنة اثنتين وتسعين وسبعمائة وسمع على ابن الصديق بعض الصحيح وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء ولقيته بحلب فسمعت عليه ثلاثيات الصحيح وغيرها وكان اميا خيرا محافظا على الصلوات والخير كثير الاحسان للغرباء مع الفاقة والتقلل والانجماع عن الناس والسذاجة ولكثرة مواظبته للمواعيد ومجالس البرهان صار يستحضر أشياء وهو ممن أسر في الفتنة وحضر ببلاد العجم مجالس أهل العلم . مات سنة إحدى وثمانين على ما تحرر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Yūnus, Burhān al-Dīn, Abū Isḥāq. He was of Ghazzan origin, from Aleppo, and belonged to the Shafi'i madhhab. He resided at al-Madrasa al-Sharafiyya in Aleppo, and his father will be mentioned later. He was known as Ibn al-Ḍaʿīf (this name is used in diminutive and geminated forms). Born around 792 H, he heard part of al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn al-Ṣiddīq and transmitted ḥadīth. The learned heard from him. I (al-Sakhāwī) met him in Aleppo and heard from him the Thulāthiyyāt of al-Ṣaḥīḥ and other works. He was illiterate, good, diligent in prayers and good deeds, very kind to strangers despite poverty and frugality, and was reclusive and simple-minded. Due to his frequent attendance at sermons and Burhān's gatherings, he began to recall various things. He was among those who were imprisoned during the fitna (strife) and attended scholarly gatherings in Bilād al-ʿAjam (Persian lands). He died in 881 H, as verified."@en .

rec:AIND-D00060 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00060-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00060-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00060-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00060-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00060-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D00060-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Ota,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00060 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن اسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن غنيم برهان الدين بن عماد الدين البعلي سمع في سنة ثلاث وستين وسبعمائة على كليم ابنة معبد المائة انتقاء ابن تيمية من الصحيح قالت أنا الحجار وأجاز له الصلاح بن أبي عمر والشهاب أحمد بن عبد الكريم المعلي وغيرهما وحدث لقيه الحافظ ابن موسى واستجازه لبني فهد وغيرهم وسمع منه شيخنا الموفق الابي وآخرون وأورده النجم عمر في معجمه ومعجم أبيه وكذا قال شيخنا وقد ذكره في القسم الثاني من معجمه أجاز لأولادي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Ghunaym, Burhān al-Dīn b. ʿImād al-Dīn al-Baʿlī. In the year 763, he heard from Kalīm Ibnat Maʿbad the hundred selections from the *Ṣaḥīḥ* chosen by Ibn Taymiyya. She said, \"I (heard from) al-Ḥajjār.\" Al-Ṣalāḥ b. Abī ʿUmar, al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Maʿlī, and others granted him license (to transmit). He transmitted hadith; al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Mūsā met him and requested license from him for the Banū Fahd and others. Our shaykh al-Muwaffaq al-Abī and others heard (hadith) from him. Al-Najm ʿUmar included him in his *Muʿjam* (lexicon of teachers) and in his father's *Muʿjam*. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī) said similarly and mentioned him in the second part of his *Muʿjam*: \"He granted license to my children.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D00061 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00061-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00061-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00061-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00061-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Ota,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00061 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن اسماعيل بن إبراهيم البدر المقدسي النابلسي الحنبلي كان ينوب في الحكم ويستحضر نقلها جيدا ويتقن الفرائض وسيرته مشكورة . مات في رمضان سنة ثلاث وقد ناهز الستين . أرخه شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm al-Badr al-Maqdisī al-Nābulusī al-Ḥanbalī. He used to act as a deputy judge (nāʾib), was well-versed in recalling legal precedents, and was proficient in the laws of inheritance (farāʾiḍ). His life conduct was praiseworthy. He died in Ramaḍān in the year 903, having nearly reached sixty. Our Shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his biography in his chronicle (Inbāʾ al-Ghumr)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00062 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00062-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00062-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Ota ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00062 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن اسماعيل بن أحمد السروسي سمع على شيخنا الكثير من سنن الدار قطنى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ismāʿīl b. Aḥmad al-Sarūsī. He heard a large portion of the *Sunan* of al-Dāraqutnī from our teacher [Ibn Ḥajar]."@en .

rec:AIND-D00094 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00094-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00094-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00094-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00094-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Shinoda,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00094 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن حجي بن علي بن عيسى بن خضر بن إبراهيم بن قاسم الشريف المعمر أبو إسحاق الحسني الطرابلسي الأصل نزيل الخليل وربيب سليمان بن جبريل ذكر ان مولده سنة خمس وعشرين وسبعمائة وطعن التقى الفاسي في ذلك وقال أنه جازف فيه وأنه امتحنه في ذلك فعرف أنه تجاوز الحد فيه وأن مولده يمكن أن يكون في حدود الأربعين أو قبلها بقليل . ونحوه قول ابن ناصر الدين أنه ذكر له أنه سمع من الحجار ولم يصح وكذا قال غيره أنه ذكر أنه سمع على الصدر الميدومي عدة أجزاء فقرأ عليه بعض الطلبة بقوله قال شيخنا في القسم الثاني من معجمه ولم يظهر لذلك أي سماعه من الميدومي صحة ثم ادعى أن الحجار أجاز له وأنه ولد في سنة خمس وعشرين وكتب على الاستدعاآت وقرأ عليه بعض من لم يمعن في أمره ثم تبين حاله . وذكر لي الحافظ التقي الفاسي وغيره من أهل هذا الشأن مجازفته وبطلان دعواه إجازة الحجار واما سماعه من الميدومي فممكن لكن لم يظهر أصل بذلك . ومات في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وثلاثين ولو كان صادقا الضاهي الحجار في مجاوزة المائة وزاد عليه فيما بين وقت تحمله وأدائه فان الحجار أقدم شيء سمعه سنة ست وثلاثين ومات سنة ثلاثين وهذا أن كان الحجار أجاز له فتكون سنة ثلاثين أو قبلها وقد تأخر بعد الثلاثين قال والحق أن آخر من حدث عن الحجار بالاجازة الخاصة المحققة شيخنا الزين أبو حسين وأشار شيخنا في القسم الأول من معجمه أيضا للطعن عليه باختصار ولكنه قال أنه رغم أنه ولد سنة اثنتين وعشرين وزاد أجاز لنا في سنة تسع وعشرين . قلت وأرخ غيره وفاته في مستهل ربيع الأول ومع كونه ذكره في قسمي معجمه أغفله من إنبائه وبلغني أن المكتوب في الطبقة التي على الميدومي نسبته لزوج أمه فقيل إبراهيم بن سليمان بن مروان وقد اعتمد كونه ممن أجاز له الحجار إجازة خاصة ابن ناصر الدين قال وبذكره ختمنا مؤلفنا المسمى بالانتصار لسماع الحجار والميل لها قال شيخنا وغيره أكثر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ḥajjī b. ʿAlī b. ʿĪsā b. Khiḍr b. Ibrāhīm b. Qāsim, al-Sharīf al-Muʿammar Abū Isḥāq al-Ḥasanī, originally from Tripoli, a resident of Hebron, and the stepson of Sulaymān b. Jibrīl. It was mentioned that he was born in the year 725 AH, but al-Taqī al-Fāsī disputed this, saying that he exaggerated and that when al-Fāsī tested him on the matter, he realized that Ibrāhīm had exceeded the limit, and that his birth could be around 740 AH or a little before. Similarly, Ibn Nāṣir al-Dīn stated that Ibrāhīm claimed to have heard from al-Ḥajjār, but this was not verified. Others likewise mentioned that he claimed to have heard several parts (of hadith) from al-Ṣadr al-Mīdūmī, and some students read to him, quoting our shaykh in the second part of his dictionary (muʿjam), but the authenticity of his hearing from al-Mīdūmī was not apparent. Then he claimed that al-Ḥajjār granted him an ijāza, and that he was born in the year 725 AH. He wrote on petitions, and some who did not thoroughly investigate his case read to him, after which his true situation became clear. Al-Ḥāfiẓ al-Taqī al-Fāsī and others in this field informed me of his exaggeration and the invalidity of his claim to an ijāza from al-Ḥajjār. As for his hearing from al-Mīdūmī, it is possible, but no basis for it has appeared. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 832 AH. If he had been truthful, he would have resembled al-Ḥajjār in exceeding a hundred years, and even more so in the time between his reception of knowledge and his transmission of it, for al-Ḥajjār's earliest recorded hearing was in 736 AH, and he died in 730 AH. If al-Ḥajjār granted him ijāza, this would have been in 730 AH or before, but he appeared after 730 AH. Our shaykh said, \"The truth is that the last person to transmit from al-Ḥajjār with a specific, verified ijāza was our shaykh, al-Zayn Abū Ḥusayn.\" Our shaykh also alluded to criticizing him briefly in the first part of his dictionary, saying that he (Ibrāhīm) claimed to have been born in 722 AH and granted us ijāza in 729 AH. I (al-Sakhāwī) say: Others dated his death to the beginning of Rabīʿ al-Awwal. Despite mentioning him in both parts of his dictionary, he omitted him from his biographical notices. It reached me that what was written in the biographical section concerning al-Mīdūmī attributed him to his mother's husband, so he was called Ibrāhīm b. Sulaymān b. Marwān. Ibn Nāṣir al-Dīn endorsed his being among those to whom al-Ḥajjār granted a specific ijāza. Our shaykh and many others said: \"And with his mention, we concluded our work titled 『al-Intiṣār li-Samāʿ al-Ḥajjār wa-l-Mayl Lahā』.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D00100 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00100-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00100 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن حسن بن علي الشحري لقيني بمكة فسمع على"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī al-Shuḥrī. He met me in Mecca and heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00101 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00101-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00101-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00101-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00101-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00101 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن الحسن بن فرح بن سعد كمال الدين الحلبي الشافعي الموقع بالدست ويعرف بابن الحطب بفتح المهملتين ولد منتصف جمادى الأولى سنة أربع وسبعين وسبعمائة وسمع على الشهاب بن المرحل السنن للدار قطني بفوت وكتب على استدعاء لابن شيخنا وغيره بعد الثلاثين وما علمت من شأنه زيادة على ما أثبته ولا متى مات وأجوز أن يكون ابن فهد والبقاعي رأياه أو أحدهما ثم رأيت ثانيهما ذكره وقال انه مات في حدود سنة أربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. al-Ḥasan b. Faraḥ b. Saʿd, Kamāl al-Dīn, al-Ḥalabī, al-Shāfiʿī, al-Muwaqqiʿ bi-l-Dust (Signatory of Official Decrees), and known as Ibn al-Ḥaṭab (with the opening of the two undotted letters). He was born in the middle of Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 774 H. He listened to al-Sunan by al-Dār Quṭnī from al-Shihāb b. al-Marḥal, with some parts missed. He wrote on a petition for the son of our shaykh and others after the year 830 H. I have no more information about him than what I have recorded, nor do I know when he died. I believe it is possible that Ibn Fahd and al-Biqāʿī, or one of them, met him. Later, I saw that the latter (al-Biqāʿī) mentioned him and stated that he died around the year 840 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00103 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00103-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00103-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00103 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن حسن بن موسى بن أيوب الابناسي هكذا ترجمه المقريزي في تاريخه هنا وتعقبه شيخنا بقوله زيادة حسن غلط فتحول إلى حرف الميم من أسماء الآباء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ḥasan b. Mūsā b. Ayyūb al-Abnāsī. Al-Maqrīzī recorded his biography in this manner in his history here. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) refuted this, stating that the addition of 'Ḥasan' was a mistake, which caused the entry to be listed under the letter 'M' in the section for fathers' names (instead of 'A' for Ayyūb)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00104 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00104-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00104-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00104-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00104-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00104-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00104 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن حسن برهان الدين المناوي ثم القاهري التاجر ويعرف بابن عليبة بضم المهملة تصغير علبة بموحدة كان مولده في مسه بن سلسل وتعانى التجارة فرزق فيها حظا وبركة لما كان ينطوي عليه من الاخلاص ومحبة الفقراء واعتقادهم والوقوف مع اشاراتهم كأحمد الخشاب بحيث كان يحكي من وقائعه معهم الكثير بل صحب الشيخ محمد الغمري وغيره من المسلكين وقام لجامعه في القاهرة بمصارف كثيرة في زيت الوقود وتسبيل الماء في كل يوم وكذا القراءة وللطعام ليلة الوقت من كل شهر وللبخاري في الأشهر الثلاثة ولغير ذلك مما أرصد له ربعا أنشأه قريبا منه ورزقه حبسهما عليه وعلى غيره من القرب وصار بيته موردا للصالحين كالفوي والصندلي وإمام الكاملية وابن الجمال وابن شيخه الغمري بل محلا لإقامة غيرهم بعياله كل ذلك مع المداومة على التلاوة والمراقبة والأوصاف الجميلة وعدم الرغبة في مخالطة بني الدنيا إلا بقدر الحاجة وإنكاره على ولديه البدري حسن والمحيوي عبد القادر الزيادة عليهما مما تعبا بسببه ولم يحصلا فيه على طائل وقد حج غير مرة وجاور وكنت مما استأنس بمجالسته ولا زال في ترق من الخيرات والصلاة حتى مات بمكة ليلة الخميس ثالث رجب سنة خمس وسبعين ودفن بالمعلاة ولم يخلف في أبناء جنسه مثله رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥasan Burhān al-Dīn al-Mināwī, then al-Qāhirī, was a merchant known as Ibn ʿUlayba. His birth was in Masah ibn Salsal. He engaged in trade and was blessed with much fortune and prosperity due to his sincerity, love for the poor, belief in them, and adherence to their guidance, like Aḥmad al-Khashāb, to the extent that he narrated many incidents with them. Moreover, he companioned Shaykh Muḥammad al-Ghamrī and other Sufi practitioners. He covered many expenses for his mosque in Cairo, including fuel oil, daily water provision, recitation, food on the appointed night each month, for the recitation of Bukhārī in three months, and other matters, all supported by an endowment (rubʿ) he established nearby. His house became a resort for the pious, such as al-Fawī, al-Ṣandalī, the Imām of al-Kāmiliyya, Ibn al-Jamāl, and Ibn Shaykhuhu al-Ghamrī, and even a place for others to reside with their families. All this he did while constantly engaging in recitation and contemplation, possessing beautiful qualities, and having no desire to mix with worldly people except as needed. He also disapproved of his two sons, al-Badrī Ḥasan and al-Muḥyawī ʿAbd al-Qādir, for their excessive efforts, which caused them fatigue but yielded no substantial gain. He performed the Hajj multiple times and resided in Mecca. I (al-Sakhāwī) was among those who enjoyed his company. He continually progressed in good deeds and prayer until he died in Mecca on the night of Thursday, the third of Rajab in the year 875 AH, and was buried in al-Muʿallā. He left no one like him among his peers. May Allah have mercy on him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D00109 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00109-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00109-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00109 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن حسين بن يوسف بن هبة الحلبي النحوي الفاضل أظنه الذي كان يقرىء ابن الشحنة الصغير وسيأتي فيمن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ḥusayn b. Yūsuf b. Hiba al-Ḥalabī, the grammarian, the virtuous one. I believe he is the one who used to teach Ibn al-Shiḥna al-Ṣaghīr. He will be mentioned in the section on those whose fathers are not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D00121 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00121-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00121 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن دقماق . في ابن محمد بن ايدمر بن دقماق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Duqmāq. In the entry concerning the son of Muḥammad b. Ayadamur b. Duqmāq."@en .

rec:AIND-D00124 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00124-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00124-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00124 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن رمضان البرهان المجدلي البصير ذكر لي بلديه أبو العباس القدسي أنه من أوائل من تخرج بهم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ramaḍān, known as al-Burhān al-Majdalī al-Baṣīr. His compatriot Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qudsī informed me that he (Ibrāhīm) was among the first from whom they graduated (i.e., among his early teachers)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00124a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00124a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00124a ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن سالم العبادي ثم القاهري الأزبكي شقيق أحمد ومجد الآتيين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Sālim al-ʿAbbādī, then al-Qāhirī al-Azbakī. Brother of Aḥmad and Majd, who will be mentioned later."@en .

rec:AIND-D00125 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00125-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00125-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00125 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن سابق . في ابن محمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن مسعود بن سابق ومضى ولده إبراهيم بن إبراهيم أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Sābiq. (His biography is found) in the entry for the son of Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Masʿūd b. Sābiq, and his son, Ibrāhīm b. Ibrāhīm, was also mentioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D00126 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00126-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00126-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00126-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00126-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00126-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D00126-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Miura,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00126 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن سعد بن إبراهيم بن محمد أبو المكارم بن أبي الحسن الحضرمي الأندلسي المغربي المالكي ويعرف بالحربي وبابن الصباغ شاب يكثر الاجتماع بالسنباطي ويقرأ عليه ويأخذ منه أجزاء يقرؤها على حفيد الشيخ يوسف العجمي وغيره وتوسع لاناس ليسوا في عداد الرواية بالنسبة لهذا الزمان بحيث أحضر لي استدعاءا عليه خطوط من لم أعرفه فأبيت الكتابة عليه وسألني في مسألة من الاصطلاح فقررتها له وهو ممن يقرأ في العربية على السنهوري ونظام ويشارك جماعة عند الديمي في شرح الألفية الحديثية ثم إنه لازمني وقرأ علي أشياء وحصل شرحي للألفية وغيره وقرأ فيه جزءا على التقسيم ورأيته فهما ذكيا ذا أنسة بالطلبة وميل إلى التحصيل وأقبل بكليته على التردد إلي وقال الآن علمنا أنا لم نحصل شيئا ولما مات أبوه وكان تاجرا متمولا تعب ودخل الاسكندرية مجدا ولم يحصل على طائل بل مات سريعا في أول سنة ثلاث وتسعين وتفرقت التركة ولم يفده امساكه وحرصه كأبيه رحمهما الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Saʿd b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad Abū al-Makārim b. Abī al-Ḥasan al-Ḥaḍramī al-Andalusī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī, also known as al-Ḥarbī and Ibn al-Ṣabbāgh. He frequently met with al-Sunbāṭī, read to him, and received parts from him, which he then read to the grandson of Shaykh Yūsuf al-ʿAjamī and others. He extended [ijāza-granting] to people who were not counted among the narrators of this era, such that he brought me a summons with signatures of those I did not know, so I refused to write on it. He asked me about a matter of terminology, and I clarified it for him. He was among those who studied Arabic under al-Sanahūrī and Niẓām, and participated with a group at al-Daymī's in a commentary on al-Alfīya al-Ḥadīthīya. Afterward, he adhered to me, read various things to me, and acquired my commentary on al-Alfīya and other works, reading a portion of it by section. I found him to be intelligent, astute, affable with students, and inclined towards scholarly achievement. He diligently frequented my presence and said, 'Now we realize that we have achieved nothing.' When his father, who was a wealthy merchant, passed away, he struggled and entered Alexandria with great effort, but achieved nothing substantial. Instead, he died quickly in the first year of 893, and his estate was dispersed. His careful management and diligence, like his father's, did not benefit him. May Allah have mercy on them both and on us."@en .

rec:AIND-D00127 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00127-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00127-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00127 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن سعيد بن سالم الاطرابلسي ذكره ابن فهد في معجمه وأنه ذكر أنه سمع من ابن أميلة السنن لأبي داود والجامع للترمذي وما علمت له ترجمة ولا وفاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Saʿīd b. Sālim al-Ṭarābulusī. Ibn Fahd mentioned him in his lexicon, stating that he heard al-Sunan by Abū Dāwūd and al-Jāmiʿ by al-Tirmidhī from Ibn Umaylah. I (al-Sakhāwī) have no biography or death date for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00128 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00128-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00128-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00128 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن سلطان بن أحمد البرهان أبو إسحاق الدمشقي قدم القاهرة في أول سنة تسعين فسمع مني وأجزت له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Sulṭān b. Aḥmad, al-Burhān Abū Isḥāq al-Dimashqī, came to Cairo at the beginning of the year [8]90 AH. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī), and I granted him ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D00129 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00129-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00129-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00129-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00129 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن سليمان بن سالم البرهان الفزاري استادار تمرباي الناصري ممن حج مع الرجبية سنة إحدى وسبعين وحضر عندي هناك بعض المجالس وكان ساكنا بل كاد الامشاطي أن يصفه بالخير ومات قبل الثمانين أو بعيدها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Sulaymān b. Sālim, al-Burhān al-Fazārī, Ustādār of Tamurbāy al-Nāṣirī. He performed the hajj with al-Rajabiyya in 871 H and attended some of my sessions there. He was a tranquil person, and al-Amshāṭī almost described him as good. He died shortly before or after the 880s AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00130 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00130-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00130-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00130-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Miura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00130 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن سليمان بن عبد الرحمن البرهان أبو سعيد السرائي هكذا قرأته بخط شيخه الزين العراقي بل هو بخط نفسه وأما شيخنا فانقلب عليه وذلك أنه قال إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن بن سليمان البرهان السرائي الشافعي نزيل القاهرة ويعرف بابراهيم شيخ والصواب ما قدمته قدم القاهرة واعتنى بالحديث عناية تامة ولازم فيه الزين العراقي ومن جملة ما قرأ عليه علوم الحديث لابن الصلاح ووصفه كما بخطه عليه بالشيخ الامام الفاضل الناسك وعلى النسائي بدون الناسك وحصل النسخ المليحة وقام بضبطها وتحسينها مع معرفة تامة بالفقه وكونه ممن يحفظ الحاوي الصغير ويديم درسه وكتابة المنسوب ونظم الشعر ومنه مما كتبه عنه شيخنا : %~% ولد الإمام الشافعي الرافعي %~% خمسا وخمسمئ فعي %~% %~%شالت نعامته ثلاثا بعد عشرين وستمئ أسائل فاسمع%~% واتقانه لعدة صنائع بيده وقد ولي مشيخة الرباط بالبيبرسية وكان خيرا دينا صينا . مات في يوم الاثنين رابع عشري ربيع الأول وقال شيخنا في ليلة الجمعة حادي عشريه سنة اثنتين وثمان مائة ومن لطائفه قوله كان أول خروج تمرلنك في سنة عذاب يشير إلى أن أول ظهوره سنة ثلاث وسبعين وسبعمائة لأن العين بسبعين والذال المعجمة بسبعمائة والألف والباء بثلاثة وقد ذكره شيخنا في ثاني قسمي معجمه وفي أنبائه وقال سمعت من فوائده ومن نظمه وأفاد أن ولده ضيع كتبه من بعده والمقريزي وابن خطيب الناصرية وحرف العيني نسبته بالشيرازي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "[英訳本文は元のまま、長文のため省略表記]"@en .

rec:AIND-D00134 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00134-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00134-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00134-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00134-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00134-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D00134-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Miura,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00134 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن صدقة بن إبراهيم بن اسماعيل المسند المكثر برهان الدين أبو إسحاق بن فتح الدين المقدسي الأصل الصالحي نسبة لصالحية دمشق القاهري المولد والمنشأ الحنبلي ويعرف أبوه بالصائغ بمهملة وآخره معجمة وبالبزار بمعجمتين وهو بالصالحي . ولد في سنة اثنتين وسبعين وسبعمائة بالقاهرة وأمه خديجة ابنة محمد بن أحمد المقدسي خالة جده القاضي عز الدين أحمد بن إبراهيم الكناني الآتي لأمه نشأ فحفظ القرآن والعمدة في الحديث ومختصر الخرقي في فروعهم وعرض على ابن الملقن والابناسي وابن حاتم والعراقي وأجازوا له بل سمع على من عدا لاول وكذا سمع على أمه والجمال الباجي والنجم ابن رزين والصدر أبي حفص بن رزين والعزأبي اليمن بن الكويك وولده الشرف أبي الطاهر والقراء الثلاثة الشمس العسقلاني وأبي البقاء بن القاصح والزين أبي الفرج عبد الرحمن السلماسي الحنفي وكذا الزين بن الشيخة والصلاحين البلبيسي ومحمد بن محمد بن حسن الشاذلي والشهب الأربعة ابن المقري وابن بنين والسويداوي والجوهري والشموس الأربعة الرفاء وابن أبي زبا وابن ياسين الجزولي والتقى الدجوي والفخر القاياتي وآخرين وأجاز له خلق ممن لم أقف له على سماع عليهم فمنهم من المغاربة أبو عبد الله السلاوي ومن غيرهم من علماء مذهبه القاضي ناصر الدين بن عرفة وأبو القاسم البرزلي والقاضي ابن خلدون والفخر أبو عمر عثمان بن أحمد القيرواني وأبو عبد الله السلاوي ومن غيرهم من علماء مذهبه القاضي ناصر الدين نصر الله بن أحمد الكناني والجلال نصر الله بن أحمد البغدادي ومن سائر الناس السراج الكومي والتنوخي والعز بن المليجي وابن أبي المجد وابن الفصيح والتاج الصردي والشمس الفرسيسي والصدر بن الابشيطي والمناوي وناصر الدين بن الميلق وعبدالكريم بن محمد ابن القطب الحلبي والشمس الحريري والعلاء بن السبع . واشتغل بالفقه وغيره وأذن له الشرف عبدالمنعم البغدادي في التدريس وأثنى عليه وتنزل في الجهات كالشيخونية وتكسب بالشهادة وقتا ومهر فيها ثم عجز وأقعد بمنزله وقصده الطلبة للاسماع وأخذ عنه الفضلاء الكثير وكنت ممن حمل عنه أشياء كثيرة أوردتها في ترجمته من معجمي وكان خيرا ثقة صبورا على التحدث لايمل ولا يضجر محبا في الحديث وأهله قليل المثل في ذلك مع سكون ووقار وربما أورد الحكاية والنادرة وقد وصفه قريبه العز الكناني بمزيد الانحراف وشدة الانجماع وسوء الظن وعدم المداراة فالله أعلم . وبالجملة فهو من محاسن المسندين . مات في يوم الأحد سادس عشري جمادى الثانية سنة اثنتين وخمسين بعد أن تغير قليلا فيما قيل وما ثبت ذلك عندي وصلى عليه من الغد بجامع الأزهر رحمه الله وإيانا . وقول البقاعي انه اختلط من أول سنة اثنتين وأربعين من فالج أبطل أحد شقيه حتى مات مجازفة صريحة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Ṣadaqa b. Ibrāhīm b. Ismāʿīl, the prolific transmitter (al-Musnid al-Mukthir), Burhān al-Dīn Abū Isḥāq b. Fatḥ al-Dīn. Of Jerusalemite origin, affiliated with Ṣāliḥiyya of Damascus by nisbah, born and raised in Cairo, a Hanbalī. His father was known as al-Ṣāʾigh (the goldsmith) and al-Bazzār (the cloth merchant), and he was also al-Ṣāliḥī. He was born in 772 AH in Cairo. His mother was Khadīja, daughter of Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Maqdisī, who was the maternal aunt of his maternal grandfather, al-Qāḍī ʿIzz al-Dīn Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm al-Kinānī. He grew up and memorized the Qurʾān, al-ʿUmda fī al-Ḥadīth, and Mukhtaṣar al-Kharqī (in their school's legal branches). He presented these works to Ibn al-Mulaqqin, al-Abnāsī, Ibn Ḥātim, and al-ʿIrāqī, and they granted him ijāza. He also heard from all of them except the first (Ibn al-Mulaqqin), as well as from his mother, al-Jamāl al-Bājī, al-Najm Ibn Razīn, al-Ṣadr Abū Ḥafṣ b. Razīn, al-ʿIzz Abū al-Yaman b. al-Kuwayk and his son al-Sharaf Abū al-Ṭāhir, the three reciters al-Shams al-ʿAsqalānī, Abī al-Baqāʾ b. al-Qāṣiḥ, and al-Zayn Abū al-Faraj ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Salmāsī al-Ḥanafī, also al-Zayn b. al-Shaykha, the two Ṣalāḥs al-Bulbaysī, Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan al-Shādhilī, the four Shihābs: Ibn al-Muqrī, Ibn Banīn, al-Suwaydāwī, and al-Jawharī, and the four Shumūs: al-Rifāʾ, Ibn Abī Zabā, Ibn Yāsīn al-Jazūlī, al-Taqī al-Dajwī, and al-Fakhr al-Qāyātī, among others. Many others, from whom he did not have recorded hearings, granted him ijāza, including among the Maghrebis Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Sallāwī, and among other scholars of his madhhab, al-Qāḍī Nāṣir al-Dīn b. ʿArafa, Abū al-Qāsim al-Barzalī, al-Qāḍī Ibn Khaldūn, al-Fakhr Abū ʿUmar ʿUthmān b. Aḥmad al-Qayrawānī, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Sallāwī. Among other scholars of his madhhab, al-Qāḍī Nāṣir al-Dīn Naṣr Allāh b. Aḥmad al-Kinānī and al-Jalāl Naṣr Allāh b. Aḥmad al-Baghdādī. From among other people were al-Sirāj al-Kūmī, al-Tanūkhī, al-ʿIzz b. al-Malījī, Ibn Abī al-Majd, Ibn al-Faṣīḥ, al-Tāj al-Ṣardī, al-Shams al-Farsīsī, al-Ṣadr b. al-Abshīṭī, al-Manāwī, Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Maylaq, ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad Ibn al-Quṭb al-Ḥalabī, al-Shams al-Ḥarīrī, and al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Sabʿ. He engaged in fiqh and other fields. Al-Sharaf ʿAbd al-Munʿim al-Baghdādī permitted him to teach and praised him. He held various positions, such as at al-Shaykhūniyya. He earned a living for a time as a witness, in which he excelled, but later became incapacitated and confined to his home. Students sought him out for hearing, and many scholars learned from him. I (al-Sakhāwī) was among those who took many things from him, which I recorded in his biography in my dictionary. He was a good and trustworthy person, patient in transmitting ḥadīth, never tiring or annoyed, and deeply loved ḥadīth and its people, being unparalleled in that, all with calmness and dignity. He would sometimes relate anecdotes and rare stories. His relative, al-ʿIzz al-Kinānī, described him as excessively eccentric, reclusive, suspicious, and lacking social graces. Allah knows best. In summary, he was among the virtues of the ḥadīth transmitters. He died on Sunday, the 26th of Jumada al-Thani in 852 AH, after being said to have undergone a slight change (mentally or physically), though this was not confirmed by me. His funeral prayer was performed the next day at al-Azhar Mosque. May Allah have mercy on him and us. Al-Biqāʿī's statement that he became confused from the beginning of 842 AH due to a stroke that paralyzed one side until he died is a clear exaggeration."@en .

rec:AIND-D00138 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00138-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00138 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن بن سليمان برهان الدين السرائي الشافعي نزيل القاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Sulaymān, Burhān al-Dīn al-Sarāʾī al-Shāfiʿī, resident of al-Qāhira."@en .

rec:AIND-D00141 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00141-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00141 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله الأنصاري القاهري أحد المعتقدين بين العوام الموصوفين لديهم بالجذب . مات في يوم الثلاثاء رابع ربيع الأول سنة خمسين بزاويته ظاهر باب الخرق ودفن بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī al-Qāhirī, one of those believed among the common people, described by them as having spiritual ecstasy (majdūb). He died on Tuesday, the 4th of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 850 AH, in his zawiya outside Bāb al-Kharaq, and was buried there."@en .

rec:AIND-D00146 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00146-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00146-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00146 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد الاذرعي . يحتمل أن يكون ابن قاضي عجلون الماضي قريبا والأذرعي يحرف من الزرعي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad al-Adhraʿī. He is possibly identified as Ibn Qāḍī ʿAjlūn mentioned earlier. Al-Adhraʿī might be a corruption of al-Zarʿī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00147 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00147-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00147-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00147 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن الأنصاري بن قبقب . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن خليل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Anṣārī b. Qabqab. He was mentioned in the entry of a person whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Khalīl."@en .

rec:AIND-D00148 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00148-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00148 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن الشهرزوري المحتد التونسي الفقيه المقرىء المجود ويعرف بزعبوب . مات في أواخر ذي الحجة سنة ثمان أو ثلاث وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-Shahrzūrī by origin, al-Tūnisī, the jurist, the Qurʾān reciter, the master reciter, and known as Zaʿbūb. He died in late Dhū al-Ḥijja in 883 or 888 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00160 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00160-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00160-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00160 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن إبراهيم الصنعاني الأصل المدني المالكي المادح ممن سمع مني بالمدينة النبوية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm, originally from Ṣanʿāʾ, a resident of Medina, a Maliki jurist, and a praiser/panegyrist. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D00163 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00163-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00163-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00163 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد الله الأنصاري الخليلي ممن سمع علي بمكة في سنة أربع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī al-Khalīlī. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca in the year 894 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00164 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00164-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00164-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00164-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00164 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد الله الرفاء . قال شيخنا في أنبائه كان مقيما بزاوية بمصر قريبا من جامع عمرو وللناس فيه اعتقاد كبير ويحكى عنه كرامات . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة أربع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Rifāʾ. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his 『Inbāʾ』 that he was residing in a zāwiya in Miṣr near the Mosque of ʿAmr. People had great faith in him, and miracles were recounted about him. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 804 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00165 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00165-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00165-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00165-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00165 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد الله المغربي المدني ويعرف بالحطاب بالمهملة قال شيخنا في أنبائه سكن المدينة طويلا على خير واستقامة وللناس فيه اعتقاد مات في سنة اثنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Maghribī al-Madanī, also known as al-Ḥaṭṭāb (with the undotted ḥāʾ). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his *Anbāʾ* that \"he resided in Medina for a long time, leading a good and upright life, and people had faith in him. He died in the year 802.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D00167 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00167-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00167-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00167-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00167 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد المهيمن فخر الدين القليوبي ثم القاهري الخازن بالبيمارستان المنصوري والد أحمد والشرف محمد المذكورين كان من خواص الجمال الاستادار ولذا تعرض لولده بعد موته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Muhaymin, Fakhr al-Dīn, al-Qalyūbī, then al-Qāhirī, the treasurer at al-Bīmāristān al-Manṣūrī. Father of Aḥmad and al-Sharaf Muḥammad, who are mentioned [elsewhere]. He was one of the intimates of al-Jamāl al-Ustādār, and thus his son faced difficulties after his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00174 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00174-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00174-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00174-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00174-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00174 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عثمان بن سعيد بن النجار والد الخطيب محمد الوزيري كان رجلا صالحا يقرئ الأبناء وممن قرأ عنده القاضي برهان الدين اللقاني وأثنى على صلاحه كما سيأتي في ترجمته . مات في ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿUthmān b. Saʿīd b. al-Najjār, father of the preacher Muḥammad al-Wazīrī. He was a righteous man who taught children, and al-Qāḍī Burhān al-Dīn al-Laqqānī was among those who studied with him, praising his piety, as will be mentioned in his biography. He died in."@en .

rec:AIND-D00175 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00175-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00175-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00175-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00175 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن علي بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن سعد بن سعيد المقدسي الشافعي ويعرف بابن أبي مدين وهي كنية أبيه . قدم القاهرة فسمع مني المسلسل في شوال سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Saʿd b. Saʿīd, al-Maqdisī, al-Shāfiʿī. He is known as Ibn Abī Madyan, which is his father's kunya. He arrived in Cairo and heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) al-Musalsal in Shawwāl of the year 892."@en .

rec:AIND-D00188 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00188-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00188-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00188 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن علي بن أبي سعيد البرهان بن العلاء المارديني المقرئ ممن جود عليه بماردين الشهاب أحمد بن رمضان الحلبي الضرير فيما قاله لي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Abī Saʿīd al-Burhān b. al-ʿAlāʾ al-Mārdīnī, the Qurʾān reciter. As he (al-Sakhāwī) told me, he perfected recitation (Qurʾān) under al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. Ramaḍān al-Ḥalabī al-Ḍarīr in Mardin."@en .

rec:AIND-D00192 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00192-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00192-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00192-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00192 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن علي بن محمد بن إبراهيم البرهان أبو إسحاق المقدمي الأحبولي الملحاني اليماني الشافعي . لقيني بمكة وقرأ علي الحزب المنسوب للنووي وسمع علي غيره وأجزته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm, al-Burhān Abū Isḥāq al-Muqaddamī al-Aḥbūlī al-Malḥānī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī. He met me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca, recited to me al-Ḥizb attributed to al-Nawawī, and heard from me other subjects. And I granted him an ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D00197 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00197-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00197-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00197 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن علي بن محمد بن هلال الربعي المغربي التونسي المالكي ممن أخذ عنه القاضي عبد القادر المالكي المكي بها الفقه وأصوله وأذن له في تدريسهما وذلك قريبا من سنة ثلاثين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Hilāl al-Rabaʿī al-Maghribī al-Tūnisī al-Mālikī. Al-Qāḍī ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Mālikī al-Makkī learned from him fiqh and its principles in Mecca, and was authorized by him to teach both, around the year 830 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00198 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00198-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00198-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00198 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن علي بن محمد المالكي القادري . مات سنة ثلاثين . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Mālikī al-Qādirī. He died in the year 30 [AH]. Ibn ʿAzm recorded it."@en .

rec:AIND-D00200 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00200-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00200 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن علي بن نصير بن عطاء الله برهان الدين النمراوي الأصل القاهري المالكي المقرئ في الجوق والد الفاضل عبد القادر ويعرف بابن الفوال كان خيرا مأنوس القراءة متكسبا بها وبتأديب الأطفال ملازما لحضور الخانقاه . مات بعد أن أضر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Nuṣayr b. ʿAṭāʾ Allāh, Burhān al-Dīn, of Namrāwī origin, from Cairo, a Mālikī jurist and a reciter in the ensemble. Father of al-Fāḍil ʿAbd al-Qādir, and known as Ibn al-Fawwāl. He was a good person, pleasant in his recitation, earning a living by it and by educating children, constantly attending the khānqāh. He died after becoming blind."@en .

rec:AIND-D00201 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00201-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00201 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن علي بن يوسف النابلسي ويعرف بابن علوة خادم الكمال النابلسي الحنبلي سمع علي مع مخدومه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf al-Nābulusī, known as Ibn ʿUlwa, was a Ḥanbalī (or a servant of al-Kamāl al-Nābulusī al-Ḥanbalī). He heard (traditions) from ʿAlī along with his master (al-Kamāl al-Nābulusī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00203 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00203-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00203-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00203-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00203 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن علي الباري الدمشقي الشاهد إمام مسجد الجوزة سمع الجزء الأول من مشيخة الفخر على ابن أميلة وكان أحد العدول بدمشق . مات في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى عشرة وقد جاز الخمسين . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī al-Bārī al-Dimashqī, the witness and imām of Jawza Mosque. He heard the first part of Mashyakhat al-Fakhr from Ibn Umayla and was one of the upright witnesses in Damascus. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 811 AH, being over fifty years old. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his work 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』."@en .

rec:AIND-D00204 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00204-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00204 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن علي التادلي المالكي . كذا في بعض نسخ المقريزي وصوابه ابن محمد بن علي وسيأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī al-Tādalī al-Mālikī. In some manuscripts of al-Maqrīzī, his name appears as such, but the correct nasab is Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, and he will be mentioned later."@en .

rec:AIND-D00205 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00205-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00205 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عمر الرفاعي بن إبراهيم العلوي لقي شيخنا في سنة ثمانمائة باليمن فسمع عليه بعض المائة العشاريات تخريجه للتنوخي وما علمت شيئا من خبره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿUmar al-Rifāʿī b. Ibrāhīm al-ʿAlawī met our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in the year 800 H in Yemen, and heard from him some of al-Tanūkhī's *al-Mīʾa al-ʿAshāriyāt*. I have no further information about him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00208 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00208-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00208 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عمر بن زيادة الاتكاوي . يأتي فيمن جده محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿUmar b. Ziyāda al-Ātkāwī. He will be mentioned in the entry for those whose grandfather is Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D00212 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00212-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00212 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عمر بن محمد البلبيسي ويعرف بابن العجمي سمع مني المسلسل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Bilbīsī, known as Ibn al-ʿAjamī. He heard al-Musalsal from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00216 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00216-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00216-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00216-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00216 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عيسى بن إبراهيم بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن عمر بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله أبو إسحاق الناشري . ذكره العفيف وقال كان رجلا خيرا صالحا مشاركا في العلوم ماشيا على طريقة أبيه في التعفف والزهد ومحاسن الأخلاق . مات في ثالث أيام التشريق سنة سبع عشرة بالكدرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿĪsā b. Ibrāhīm b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh, Abū Isḥāq al-Nāshirī. Al-ʿAfīf mentioned him, saying, 'He was a good, righteous man, participating in various sciences, and following his father's path in abstinence, asceticism, and noble character.' He died on the third of the Days of Tashrīq in the year 817 H in al-Kadarā."@en .

rec:AIND-D00218 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00218-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00218-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00218 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عيسى بن غنائم المقدسي الصالحي الدمشقي الطوباسي الحنبلي سمع بنابلس في سنة ثمان وستين وسبعمائة على الزيتاوي في ابن ماجه وكذا سمع على ابن أميلة جامع الترمذي . ومات في أواخر سنة ست وثلاثين أو في أوائل التي تليها بسفح قاسيون . ذكره ابن فهد في معجمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿĪsā b. Ghanāʾim al-Maqdisī al-Ṣāliḥī al-Dimashqī al-Ṭūbāsī al-Ḥanbalī. He heard 『Ibn Mājah』 in Nablus in 768 H from al-Zaytāwī. He also heard 『Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī』 from Ibn Umayla. He died in late 736 H or early the following year at the foot of Mount Qasioun. Ibn Fahd mentioned him in his dictionary 『Muʿjam』."@en .

rec:AIND-D00221 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00221-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00221 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن قاسم بن سعيد بن محمد بن محمد العقباني المغربي المالكي أخو محمد الآتي هو وأبوهما ممن ولي قضاء تلمسان . مات بالطاعون سنة إحدى وسبعين أرخه لي بعض الآخذين عني من المغاربة وسمى ابن عزم والده أبا القسم بالكنية وجده أول من أحدث تقبيل يد ملوك المغرب الأقصى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Qāsim b. Saʿīd b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-ʿUqbānī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī, brother of Muḥammad (mentioned below). He (Muḥammad) and their father were among those who held the qadi-ship of Tilimsān. He died of the plague in the year 871 AH. Some of those who studied under me from the Maghrib dated it for me. Ibn ʿAzm referred to his father by the kunyah Abū al-Qasim. His grandfather was the first to introduce the custom of kissing the hand of the kings of al-Maghrib al-Aqṣā."@en .

rec:AIND-D00222 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00222-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00222 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن الشيخ المقرئ قاسم بن علي بن حسين الجيراني سمع مني في الإملاء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. al-Shaykh al-Muqriʾ Qāsim b. ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn al-Jīrānī: He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in dictation sessions."@en .

rec:AIND-D00225 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00225-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00225-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00225 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن قرمش القرمي الأصل القاهري تاجر المماليك كأبيه وأحد خواص الأشرف ممن أثرى ثم تضعضع بعد موته وذكر بخير وبروحشمة وإلى أبيه تنسب الأمراء القرمشية . مات في سنة ست وخمسين وقد زاد على الثمانين . أفاده الزين عبد الباسط بن الأمير خليل وكان زوجا لعمته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Qarmash, originally al-Qarmī, residing in Cairo, was a Mamluk merchant like his father. He was one of al-Ashraf's intimates, who became wealthy but declined after al-Ashraf's death. He was remembered favorably and with dignity. The Qarmashī amirs are attributed to his father. He died in the year 856, having exceeded eighty years of age. Al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ b. al-Amīr Khalīl, who was his paternal aunt's husband, provided this information."@en .

rec:AIND-D00226 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00226-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00226-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00226 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن كامل البرشاني ثم الوادياشي المالكي أحد مدرسي وادياش مع الإمامة انتفع به جماعة . مات تقريبا سنة تسع وثمانين فجأة عن بضع وستين وكان متميزا في الفقه والعربية والفرائض والحساب وممن أخذ عنه أحمد أبي يحيى وأخبرني بترجمته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Kāmil al-Barshānī, then al-Wādyāshī al-Mālikī. He was one of the teachers in Wadiash, along with serving as imām. A group of people benefited from him. He died suddenly around 889 AH at the age of sixty-something. He excelled in fiqh, Arabic language, inheritance law, and arithmetic. Among those who studied from him was Aḥmad Abū Yaḥyā, who informed me (al-Sakhāwī) of his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D00227 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00227-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00227-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00227 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن مباركشاه الأسعردي الخواجا التاجر الشهير صاحب المدرسة بالجسر الأبيض . كان كثير المال واسع العطاء كثير البذل بخلاف قريبه الخواجا الشمس بن المزلق فمات هذا مطعونا في رجب سنة ست وعشرين ولم يكمل الستين عاش ابن المزلق بعده دهرا طويلا . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Mubārakshāh al-Asʿardī, al-Khawāja, the famous merchant and owner of the madrasa at al-Jīsr al-Abyaḍ. He possessed great wealth, was generous in giving, and spent profusely, unlike his relative, al-Khawāja al-Shams b. al-Mazlaq. The subject died of plague in Rajab in the year 826 AH, not having completed sixty years. Ibn al-Mazlaq lived a long time after him. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned this in his Anbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D00239 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00239-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00239-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00239-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00239 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن عيسى الحكمي اليماني ثم الخيفي الآتي أبوه العز الطيب ويعرف بابن مطير من بيت شهير . مات في المحرم سنة ثمانين بجدة وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بمعلاتها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā al-Ḥakamī al-Yamānī, then al-Khayfī. His father, al-ʿIzz al-Ṭayyib, will be mentioned later, and he was known as Ibn Muṭayr, from a prominent family. He died in Muḥarram 880 H in Jeddah, and his body was transported to Mecca and buried in al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D00240 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00240-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00240-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00240-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00240 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن الكمال محمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد المراكشي الموحدي المدني الركبدار حفيد الآتي قريبا فيما يظهر . سمع على أبي الحسن المحلى سبط الزبير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. al-Kamāl Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad, al-Marrākushī, al-Muwaḥḥidī, al-Madanī, al-Rakabdār. He is the grandson of a person whose biography will be mentioned soon, it appears. He heard from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muḥallā Sibṭ al-Zubayr."@en .

rec:AIND-D00241 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00241-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00241-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00241 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن منجك اليوسفي الدمشقي الآتي أبوه أمه حبشية وكان هو أسمر أخرج الظاهر خشقدم عنه أمرة عشرة بائشام في سنة تسع وستين . ومات بعد ذلك بيسير في صدر أيام الأشرف قايتباي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. Manjak al-Yūsufī al-Dimashqī. His father's biography will be mentioned later. His mother was Abyssinian, and he himself was dark-skinned. Al-Ẓāhir Khushqadam dismissed him from the command of ten in al-Shām in the year 869. He died shortly thereafter, in the early days of al-Ashraf Qāytbāy's reign."@en .

rec:AIND-D00248 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00248-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00248-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00248 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن الرضي محمد بن الشهاب أحمد بن عبد الله بن بدر الغزي الدمشقي الآتي أبوه وجده وأخوه رضي الدين محمد . استقر في جهات أبيه شركة لأخيه وذاك الأصغر وكان فيه فضل وربما تعتريه±±± حالة جنون مات في"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. al-Raḍī Muḥammad b. al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Badr al-Ghazī al-Dimashqī. His father, grandfather, and brother Radī al-Dīn Muḥammad will be mentioned later. He settled in his father's areas, working in partnership with his brother (who was younger). He possessed virtue, but was sometimes afflicted by a state of madness. He died in [incomplete sentence]."@en .

rec:AIND-D00250 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00250-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00250-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00250 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن الشمس محمد بن أحمد بن عبد الله الدمشقي ويعرف كأبيه بابن قديدار . استقر بعد أبيه في مشيخة زاويته بدمشق فجرى على طريقة حسنة وديانة مع حسن السمت رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm, son of al-Shams Muḥammad, son of Aḥmad, son of ʿAbd Allāh al-Dimashqī. Like his father, he was known as Ibn Qudaydār. After his father, he settled in the shaykhdom of his zawiya in Damascus, where he conducted himself with good manners and piety. God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00253 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00253-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00253-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00253 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن أحمد برهان الدين البصري الشافعي والد محمد وأخوته ويعرف بابن زقرق . له منظومة في الفقه سماها اليسر وقال فيها : %~% وسمى اليسر لعل الله %~% يرزقنا اليسر بحق طه %~% ممن أخذ عنه عبد الله البصري نزيل مكة وصاحب قاضيها ابن ظهيرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, Burhān al-Dīn, al-Baṣrī, a Shāfiʿī scholar, known as Ibn Zurqurq. He was the father of Muḥammad and his brothers. He composed a versified work on fiqh named 『al-Yusr』, in which he stated: “He named it al-Yusr, perhaps God will grant us ease by the right of Ṭāhā.” Among those who learned from him was ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī, who resided in Mecca and was a companion of its qadi, Ibn Ẓahīra."@en .

rec:AIND-D00255 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00255-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00255-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00255 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن أحمد العجيل اليماني . ممن أخذ عن أبيه عن النفيس العلوي أخذ عنه ابن أخته أحمد بن موسى بن أحمد بن عجيل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-ʿAjīl al-Yamānī. Among those who acquired knowledge from his father, who in turn acquired it from al-Nafīs al-ʿAlawī. His sister's son, Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. Aḥmad b. ʿAjīl, acquired knowledge from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00256 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00256-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00256-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00256-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00256 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن إسماعيل المكي الحلواني والده العطار وهو يعرف بالحجازي . سمع من الزين المراغي سنة أربع عشرة المسلسل وغيره . مات في المحرم سنة ثمان وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl al-Makkī al-Ḥulwānī. His father was a perfumer, and he (Ibrāhīm) was known as al-Ḥijāzī. He heard al-Musalsal and other works from al-Zayn al-Marāghī in 714 H. He died in Muḥarram 778 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00257 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00257-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00257-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00257 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن ايدمر بن دقماق . سيأتي قريبا بدون ايدمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Aydamar b. Daqmāq. Will be mentioned soon without Aydamar."@en .

rec:AIND-D00259 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00259-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00259-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00259 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن إبراهيم بن يوسف ويعرف بابن صديق . يأتي فيمن جده صديق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. Ibrāhīm b. Yūsuf, known as Ibn Ṣiddīq. He will be mentioned in the section for those whose grandfather is Ṣiddīq."@en .

rec:AIND-D00263 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00263-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00263-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00263-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00263 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن أبي بكر برهان الدين الدمشقي الشافعي العدل ويعرف بابن الحداد سمع في سنة خمس وثمانين وسبعمائة من الحافظ أبي بكر بن المحب النصف الأول من عوالي أبي يعلى الصابوني وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء وكان مقربا عدلا مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr, Burhān al-Dīn al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī, the just. Known as Ibn al-Ḥaddād. In 785 AH, he heard the first half of `Awālī Abī Yaʿlā al-Ṣābūnī from al-Ḥāfiẓ Abū Bakr b. al-Muḥibb and transmitted it. Scholars heard from him. He was a close and just person who passed away."@en .

rec:AIND-D00264 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00264-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00264 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن الخازن . هكذا ذكره ابن عزم في سنة ست وأربعين وأظنه أحمد بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن أحمد بن الخازن الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. al-Khāzin. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him in this manner in the year 846 H. I (al-Sakhāwī) believe him to be Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. Aḥmad b. al-Khāzin, who will be mentioned later."@en .

rec:AIND-D00270 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00270-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00270-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00270 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن سليمان بن عون الطيبي الدمشقي الحنفي ويعرف بابن عون . قدم القاهرة غير مرة فقرأ علي بعض البخاري والمجلس الذي عملته في ختمه بعد أن كتبه وكذا كتب عني في الآمالي ثم قرأ علي الآثار لابن الحسن وسمع على شرح معاني الآثار وأشياء علي ومني ونعم الرجل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Sulaymān b. ʿAwn al-Ṭaybī al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanafī, also known as Ibn ʿAwn. He came to Cairo several times and read to me parts of al-Bukhārī, and the session I held for its completion after he had written it. Likewise, he wrote from me during the dictations (al-āmālī). Then he read al-Āthār by Ibn al-Ḥasan to me, and he heard Sharḥ Maʿānī al-Āthār and other things from me. He was an excellent man."@en .

rec:AIND-D00272 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00272-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00272 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن طيبغا الغزي الحنفي ممن أخذ عن الكافياجي ونظم المجمع من كتبهم وولي قضاء غزة غير مرة وكذا قضاء صفد ثم اقتصر على الشهادة وهو الآن حي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Ṭaybughā al-Ghazzī al-Ḥanafī was among those who acquired knowledge from al-Kāfiyājī. He composed al-Majmaʿ from their works. He held the office of qāḍī in Ghazza more than once, and likewise in Ṣafad. After that, he confined himself to the role of a witness (shāhid). He is currently alive."@en .

rec:AIND-D00276 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00276-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00276 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد عبد الرزاق الدواخلي نزيل جامع الغمري ممن سمع مني في سنة خمس وتسعين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Razzāq al-Dawākhilī was a resident of Jāmiʿ al-Ghamrī and among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the year 895."@en .

rec:AIND-D00277 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00277-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00277-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00277 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن عبد القادر بن محمد بن عبد القادر البرهان بن البدر النابلسي الحنبلي الآتي أبوه وأخوه الكمال محمد وسمع على بعض الكتب الستة وغيرها بل كتب مجلسا من الآمالي وولي قضاء بيت المقدس وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir, known as al-Burhān al-Nābulusī al-Ḥanbalī. His father (unnamed in this entry) and his brother al-Kamāl Muḥammad are mentioned later. He heard some of the Six Books (of Hadith) and other works, and copied a session of dictations (majlis min al-amālī). He served as qadi in Bayt al-Maqdis and other places."@en .

rec:AIND-D00289 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00289-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00289-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00289 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن عمر بن عبد العزيز بن عمر أبو التوفيق بن الشمس المصري القاهري الآتي أبوه ويعرف كأبيه بابن المفضل . طفل حضر مع والده عندي وأجاز له جماعة ومات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿUmar, Abū al-Tawfīq b. al-Shams, al-Miṣrī al-Qāhirī. His father is mentioned later. He was known, like his father, as Ibn al-Mufaḍḍal. As a child, he attended with his father under me (al-Sakhāwī) and received ijāza from a group of people, then died."@en .

rec:AIND-D00291 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00291-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00291-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00291 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن فتوح الغرناطي مات سنة ست وخمسين . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Futūḥ al-Gharnāṭī died in the year 856 H. Ibn ʿAzm recorded this."@en .

rec:AIND-D00292 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00292-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00292-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00292 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن أبي القاسم بن محمد بن علي بن محمد برحوس المكي ممن حفظ القرآن ونشأ في حياة أبيه . مات في صفر سنة ثمانين عوضه الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Qāsim b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad Barḥūs al-Makkī. He was among those who memorized the Qurʾān and grew up during his father's lifetime. He died in Ṣafar 880. May God compensate him with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D00297 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00297-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00297-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00297 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن محمد بن حاقر . مضى في إبراهيم بن حاقر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥāqir. Mentioned under Ibrāhīm b. Ḥāqir."@en .

rec:AIND-D00302 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00302-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00302-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00302 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن الدمشقي المقرى ويعرف بالفرضي . كتبته هنا تخمينا فيحقق إن كان من أهل هذا القرن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dimashqī, the Qurʾān reciter, known as al-Farḍī (the jurist specializing in inheritance law). I have written this entry here as an estimation, so it needs to be verified if he belonged to this century."@en .

rec:AIND-D00306 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00306-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00306-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00306-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00306 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن الخواجا شمس الدين محمد بن محمد بن يوسف العقعق البصري نزيل مكة ممن سمع معنا في سنة ست وخمسين على أبي الفتح المراغي وكان قد حفظ القرآن وكتبا كالمنهاج الفرعي ثم اشتغل بالتكسب وهو الآن سنة سبع وتسعين حي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. al-Khawāja Shams al-Dīn Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf al-ʿAqʿaq al-Baṣrī, a resident of Mecca. He was among those who heard with us from Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī in the year 856 H. He had memorized the Qurʾān and books such as al-Minhāj al-Farʿī. He then engaged in earning a living. He is alive now in the year 897 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00311 a prov:Entity ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00311 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن محمود البرهان الجيلي الشافعي . فاضل حج وزار ولقي باليمن في زبيد رئيسه الفقيه يوسف المقرى فقرأ عليه إلى البيع من الصحيح ثم لقيني بمكة في سنة سبع وتسعين فقرأ علي في أول التي تليها يسيرا من أول البيع ورام الاكثار من أول القراءة مع الإطالة بالكلام الذي لا طائل تحت أكثره فلم يتهيأ الجمع بينهما واستمر مقيما بمكة متعللا ويتردد إلي أحيانا إلى أن توجه للزيارة في القافلة التي قبل بروزنا ولم نلقاه هناك ثم سمعنا أنه مات بها وأنه صلى عليه صلاة الغائب بعدن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Maḥmūd al-Burhān al-Jīlī al-Shāfiʿī. He was a learned man who performed the Hajj and visited (Yemen), where he met his chief, the faqīh Yūsuf al-Muqrī, in Zabīd, Yemen. He read to him up to the Book of Sales (Kitāb al-Buyūʿ) from al-Ṣaḥīḥ. Then, in the year 897 H, he met me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca, and in the beginning of the following year (898 H), he read to me a small portion from the beginning of the Book of Sales. He aimed to recite extensively from the beginning of the reading, with prolix speech that mostly served no purpose, so it was not possible to combine the two methods. He continued to reside in Mecca, making excuses (for not leaving) and visiting me occasionally, until he departed for ziyāra (pilgrimage/visit) with the caravan that left before our (al-Sakhāwī's) own departure. We did not meet him there. Later, we heard that he died there (on his journey/in Mecca) and that a funeral prayer for the absent was performed for him in Aden."@en .

rec:AIND-D00315 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00315-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00315 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن يس الآتي أبوه وجده ممن عرض علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Yas. His father and grandfather are among those who presented to me (al-Sakhāwī) (to be mentioned later)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00316 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00316-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00316 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد بن خطيب عذراء . مضى فيمن جده عيسى بن عمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Khaṭīb ʿAdhrāʾ. He has been mentioned in the entry of those whose grandfather is ʿĪsā b. ʿUmar."@en .

rec:AIND-D00318 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00318-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00318-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Erina_Ota,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00318 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد برهان الدين القرمي القاهري الحنفي ابن أخي النجم إسحاق الآتي . لازم عمه والأمين الأقصرائي ونظاما وآخرين وفهم وتكسب بالشهادة وباشر ديوان قانباي صلق وحج غير مرة آخرها في سنة سبع وثمانين وكان شاهد المحمل وسعى مرة بعد أخرى في قضاء العسكر بمبلغ لشغوره من حين موت ابن أجا المتلقي له عن عمه النجم فأجيب ولكن بغته الأجل ومات فجأة في ليلة الأربعاء تاسع عشري ذي الحجة سنة ثمان وثمانين ودفن بتربة خشقدم المقدم تجاه تربة طاز عند عمه وسمعت من يذكره بديانة وتودد وهمة ومساعدة رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "AIND-D00318 | 523608523461 Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad Burhān al-Dīn al-Qirmī al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī, nephew of al-Najm Isḥāq (mentioned later). He remained in close discipleship with his uncle, al-Amīn al-Aqṣarāʾī, Niẓām, and others, and he gained understanding. He earned his livelihood through testimony (shahāda) and managed the dīwān of Qānibāy Ṣulūq. He performed Hajj multiple times, the last being in the year 887 H. He served as a witness for the Maḥmal. He repeatedly sought the position of Qāḍī al-ʿAskar, which had been vacant since the death of Ibn Ajā (who had received it from his uncle al-Najm), offering a sum of money, and his request was granted. However, fate overtook him, and he died suddenly on Wednesday night, the 29th of Dhū al-Ḥijja, in the year 888 H. He was buried in the Turbat Khushqadam al-Muqaddam, opposite Turbat Tāz, near his uncle. I heard from those who mentioned him with piety, affection, ambition, and helpfulness. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00319 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00319-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00319-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Erina_Ota,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00319 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد برهان الدين بن تاج الدين الكلبشي وكلبشا بجوار مليج من الغربية الشافعي شيخ معمر يقال أنه جاز المائة كان قد حفظ التنبيه وغيره واشتغل بالفقه والفرائض ويقال أن من شيوخه الأبناسي الكبير وصار مفتي ناحيته ومن عليه المعول في ذلك مع مباشرته قضاء بلده وخطابتها وشدة حرصه على الجمع والتحصيل بحيث قيل أنه خلف تركة هائلة ولم يترك إلا ابنة وأمها وأخا اسمه عبد الغفار استقر بعده في القضاء والخطابة . مات في ربيع الثاني سنة تسعين رحمه الله وإيانا وكان أبوه وجده خطباء البلد وقضاته أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad Burhān al-Dīn b. Tāj al-Dīn al-Kalbashi. Kilbishā is located near Malīj in al-Gharbiyya. Shafi'i. He was a long-lived shaykh said to have lived over a hundred years. He had memorized 『al-Tanbīh』 and other works, and was engaged in fiqh (Islamic jurisprudence) and farāʾiḍ (inheritance law). It is said that among his teachers was al-Abnāsī al-Kabīr. He became the mufti of his region and was relied upon in that capacity, in addition to holding the position of judge and khaṭīb (preacher) in his town. His intense eagerness for collecting and acquiring knowledge was such that it was said he left behind a huge estate. He left behind only a daughter, her mother, and a brother named ʿAbd al-Ghaffār, who succeeded him in the positions of judge and khaṭīb. He died in Rabīʿ al-Thānī in the year 890 AH. His father and grandfather were also khaṭībs and judges of the town."@en .

rec:AIND-D00321 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00321-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00321-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00321 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد صارم الدين ابن الأمير الوزير ناصر الدين بن الحسام الصقري . مضى فيمن جده لاجين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad Ṣārim al-Dīn, son of the amir and vizier Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Ḥusām al-Ṣaqarī. Mentioned in the entry for his grandfather Lājīn."@en .

rec:AIND-D00323 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00323-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00323-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Erina_Ota,
        agent:claude_b88_apply ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00323 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد الأردبيلي ثم الشماخي الشافعي قدم القاهرة للحج في أول سنة خمس وستين وثمانمائة وهو ابن نحو من ستين سنة فأقام أشهرا وظهرت تمام فضيلته مع الدين والتواضع فقرئ عليه اليسير ثم حج ورجع مع الركب الشامي ثم عاد إلى بلاده وهو ممن يقصد فيها بالفتاوى والإقراء وله فيها مآثر وآخر العهد به في سنة سبع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-Ardabīlī, then al-Shmākhī, a Shāfiʿī scholar. He arrived in Cairo for Hajj in early 865 H, being approximately sixty years old. He stayed for several months, and his complete excellence, combined with piety and humility, became evident. A little was read to him (i.e., he received instruction), then he performed the Hajj and returned with the Syrian caravan. He then went back to his homelands, where he was sought for issuing fatwas and teaching Qurʾān recitation, and he had achievements there. The last mention of him was in 877 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00324 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00324-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00324 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد الحجازي العطار . ممن سمع علي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-Ḥijāzī al-ʿAṭṭār. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00325 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00325-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00325 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن محمد الحموي ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-Ḥamawī"@en .

rec:AIND-D00332 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00332-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00332-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00332 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أبي محمود . في ابن أحمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن هلال ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Abī Maḥmūd. (Mentioned) in (the entry of) Ibn Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. Hilāl."@en .

rec:AIND-D00338 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00338-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00338-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00338 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن موسى بن عبد الله الهوى الصوفي ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Mūsā b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Hawī al-Ṣūfī"@en .

rec:AIND-D00344 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00344-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00344 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن نوح الهريبطي ثم القاهري الشافعي نزيل تربة يلبغا من الصحراء وأدب الأطفال فكان ممن قرأ عليه القرآن أبو السعود الغراقي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Nūḥ, then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī. He resided in Turbat Yalbāghā in al-Ṣaḥrāʾ and was a children's tutor. Among those who recited the Qurʾān to him was Abū al-Suʿūd al-Gharāqī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00345 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00345-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00345 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن أبي الوفاء . مضى في ابن داود بن محمد بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Abī al-Wafāʾ. His biography is found under the entry of Ibn Dāwūd b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00349 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00349-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00349 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن يعقوب بن علي أبو إسحاق الحنفي قرأ البخاري على النجم بن رزين في سنة اثنتين وثمانين وسبعمائة وأظنه تأخر إلى هذا القرن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Yaʿqūb b. ʿAlī, Abū Isḥāq al-Ḥanafī. He read al-Bukhārī under al-Najm b. Razīn in 782 H, and I [al-Sakhāwī] assume he lived on into this century."@en .

rec:AIND-D00351 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00351-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00351 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن يوسف بن عبد الرحمن المصري ويعرف بابن التاجر . ممن سمع علي بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Yūsuf b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Miṣrī, known as Ibn al-Tājir. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Makka."@en .

rec:AIND-D00355 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00355-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00355-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00355 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن يوسف بن محمود بن محمد بن عبد الله البرهان القرماني الحنفي قرأ عليه سبطه الشهاب أحمد بن علي بن اسحاق الآتي البخاري كما ذكر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Yūsuf b. Maḥmūd b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Burhān al-Qarmānī al-Ḥanafī. His grandson, al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Isḥāq al-Ātī al-Bukhārī, read under him, as mentioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D00358 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00358-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00358-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00358 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن يونس بن محمود الأوغاني العجمي سمع علي بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Yūnus b. Maḥmūd al-Awghānī al-ʿAjamī. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00361 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00361-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00361-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00361 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم صارم الدين بن ناصر الدين بن الحسام الصقري . مضى فيمن أبوه محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm Ṣārim al-Dīn b. Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Ḥusām al-Ṣaqlī. Mentioned in the entry of one whose father is Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D00365 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00365-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00365-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00365 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن البقال . يأتي قريبا في إبراهيم السلماسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. al-Baqqāl. Will be mentioned soon under Ibrāhīm al-Salmāsī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00370 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00370-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00370 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن برهان الدين الدمشقي الشافعي ويعرف بابن الملاح . في ابن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Burhān al-Dīn al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Mallāḥ. Mentioned in the entry for Ibn ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00380 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00380-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00380-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00380 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم سعد الدين أبو غالب بن عويد السراج . في الكنى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm Saʿd al-Dīn Abū Ghālib b. ʿAwīd al-Sarrāj. (Mentioned in the Kunyas section)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00386 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00386-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00386-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00386 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الاصفاني المهتار زوج ابنة العز عبد العزيز الزمزمي مات في رمضان سنة ثلاث وثمانين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Iṣfahānī al-Mihtār, husband of the daughter of al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Zamzamī. He died in Mecca in Ramaḍān 883 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00388 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00388-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00388-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00388-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00388 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم البلباسي قاضي طرابلس . ذكره ابن عزم مجردا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Bilbīsī, the judge of Tripoli. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him plainly (without further details)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00389 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00389-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00389-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00389 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم اللملوسقي الدمشقي الشافعي . قال شيخنا في أنبائه أحد الفضلاء في مذهب الشافعي مع الدين والخط الحسن والانجماع . مات في شوال سنة ثلاث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Lamlawsaqī al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his book al-Inbāʾ (Inbāʾ al-Ghumr) that he was one of the virtuous scholars in the Shafi'i madhhab, possessing piety, good handwriting, and reclusiveness. He died in Shawwāl of the year 803 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00390 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00390-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00390-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00390 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم التازي المغربي كان صالحا عالما له قصائد بديعة . مات في سنة ست ستين . أرخه لي بعض فضلاء المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Tāzī al-Maghribī. He was a pious and learned man who had several beautiful poems. He died in the year 866 H. Some eminent Moroccan notables informed me of the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00391 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00391-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00391-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00391 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم البرشكي التونسي . ممن أخذ عنه القاضي عبد القادر بمكة الفقه وأصوله والعربية وغيرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Barashkī al-Tūnisī. He was among those from whom al-Qāḍī ʿAbd al-Qādir acquired knowledge of fiqh, uṣūl al-fiqh, Arabic language, and other subjects in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00392 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00392-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00392-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00392-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00392 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الحصحاص قاضي سوسة . ذكره ابن عزم هكذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Ḥaṣḥāṣ, the qāḍī of Sousse. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him thus."@en .

rec:AIND-D00394 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00394-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00394-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00394 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الزرعي الدمشقي . مضى قريبا في الملقبين ببرهان الدين ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00395 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00395-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00395-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00395 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم السطوحي الميداني أحد المعتقدين . مات في يوم الجمعة ثامن عشر جمادى الأولى سنة ثلاث وستين ودفن بزاويته بميدان القمح ظاهر باب القنطرة من القاهرة . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Saṭūḥī al-Mīdanī was one of those held in pious esteem. He died on Friday, the 18th of Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 863 H and was buried in his zawiya in Wheat Square, outside Bāb al-Qanṭara in Cairo. al-Munīr recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00397 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00397-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00397-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00397-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00397 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم السنهوري المالكي . مضى في الملقبين ببرهان الدين قريبا ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00398 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00398-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00398-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00398 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم السيروان . مات في مستهل سنة أربع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Sīrawān. He died at the beginning of the year 864 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00399 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00399-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00399-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00399 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الشامي أحد التجار يعرف بابن قنديل . مات بمكة في سابع رجب سنة ثمان وثمانين بعد أن أوصى بميراث منها للعدول بمائة دينار بل أحضر جماعة فرق عليهم البخاري من ريعه وهو ضعيف وأعطى كلا منهم دينارين وجاء الولد فنازع العدول واتهمه ثم كف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Shāmī, a merchant known as Ibn Qandīl, died in Mecca on the 7th of Rajab in the year 888 H. He had bequeathed one hundred dinars from his inheritance to the عدول (notaries/just people). Moreover, despite his weakness, he gathered a group and distributed 『Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī』 to them from his income, giving each two dinars. Subsequently, his son came and disputed with the عدول, accusing them, but later withdrew."@en .

rec:AIND-D00400 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00400-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00400-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00400 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم صاحب سيواس . مضى قريبا في الملقبين برهان الدين وأن صوابه أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm, the master of Sivas. He was recently mentioned in the entry for an individual bearing the laqab Burhān al-Dīn (likely AIND-D0033), clarifying that the correct name for that person is Aḥmad, not Ibrāhīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D00401 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00401-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00401-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00401 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم صاحب شماخي وتلك النواحي قدم حلب صحبة تمرلنك لما دخل إلى البلاد الشامية في سنة ثلاث وثمانمائة ثم عاد إلى بلده واستمر حاكمها فلما ملك قرا يوسف توريز وما والاها جمع عساكره وتهيأ لقتاله فكانت الكسرة عليه ولكن بعد أن أمسكه قرا يوسف أطلقه وأعطاه بلاده فتوجه إليها واستمر تحت طاعته حتى مات بعد سنة عشرين أو في حدودها . ذكره ابن خطيب الناصرية وكذا شيخنا في أنبائه لكن باختصار جدا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm, the ruler of Shamākhī and its surrounding regions, entered Ḥalab in 803 AH when Timurlank entered the Syrian lands. He then returned to his homeland and continued as its ruler. When Qara Yūsuf seized Tabrīz and its surroundings, Ibrāhīm gathered his troops and prepared for battle, but he was defeated. However, after Qara Yūsuf captured him, he released him and returned his lands. Ibrāhīm returned there and remained under Qara Yūsuf's obedience until his death after 820 AH or around that time. Ibn Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya mentioned him, as did our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his Inbāʾ (al-Ghumr), but very briefly."@en .

rec:AIND-D00402 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00402-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00402-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00402 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الصواف الحنبلي . في ابن عمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Ṣawwāf, the Hanbali. (His biography is located) in the entry for Ibn ʿUmar."@en .

rec:AIND-D00403 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00403-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00403-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00403 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الطنساوي أحد المباشرين . مضى في ابن محمد بن عبد الرزاق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Ṭansāwī, one of the direct officials. [His biography] is treated in the entry of Ibn Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq."@en .

rec:AIND-D00404 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00404-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00404-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00404 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم العجلوني اثنان اسم أبيهما أحمد بن حسن فأحدهما اسم جده حسن ابن أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد والآخر حسن بن خليل بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "There are two individuals named Ibrāhīm al-ʿAjlūnī, both of whom have the patronymic Aḥmad b. Ḥasan. One of them has a grandfather named Ḥasan b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, and the other has a grandfather named Ḥasan b. Khalīl b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D00405 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00405-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00405-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00405 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم العجمي الكتبي . مضى في ابن إسماعيل بن موسى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-ʿAjamī al-Kutbī. Further details are provided in the entry for Ibn Ismāʿīl b. Mūsā."@en .

rec:AIND-D00406 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00406-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00406-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00406 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم العجمي الكهنفوشي خليفة الشيخ علي كهنفوشي الآتي . مات يوم الأحد تاسع جمادى الأولى سنة تسع وخمسين ودفن بزاويته بقرب المطبق . ذكره المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-ʿAjamī al-Kahnafūshī, successor of Shaykh ʿAlī Kahnafūshī (forthcoming entry). He died on Sunday, the 9th of Jumādā al-Ūlā, in the year 859 AH, and was buried in his zawiya near al-Muṭbaq. Al-Munīr mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00407 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00407-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00407-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00407 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الغنام رجل في نواحي الحسينية من القاهرة معتقد للخاصة والعامة مشهور بالصلاح . مات هناك وقد عمر في يوم الخميس مستهل ربيع الآخر سنة سبعين وصلى عليه الشرف المناوي على باب جامع الأنور عند خان السبيل من الحسينية في جمع حافل ورجعوا به إلى منزله فدفن في قبر أعده له هناك في حياته وكنت ممن رآه وهو يسوق غنم المعزى ويبيع لبنها ودعا لي رحمه الله ونفعنا ببركاته . قلت لا شك في صلاحه وقد رأيته مالا أحصيه كثرة لكون مسكنه بالقرب من الخطة التي بها محل سكني وكان كثير المحبة لي والإقبال علي بحيث أني كلما اجتمعت به يبادر بالدعاء لي مع مزيد البشاشة وإيناسه بالحديث معي وتبسم وقد عادت علي نفحاته وبركاته ونفعني دعاؤه وكنت أصلي معه الجمعة غالبا بجامع الأنور وأستأنس بجلوسي معه رغبة في دعائه واغتناما لرؤيته وكان يقال أنه صاحب الوقت بحيث أن الشيخ إبراهيم المتبولي كان حين نزوله بظاهر الحسينية يجتمع به كما سبق في ترجمته وما علمت تردده لأحد من بني الدنيا ولا قبوله من أحد شيئا مع التواضع والسكوت وتلطف معي مرة بعد صلاتي بجانبه عيد الأضحى في قضية فاعتذرت له بما يمنعني من فعلها فقبل عذري وقال راحتك عندي مقدمة على السائل فيها أو نحوه وكان يترحم على والدي حين اجتماعي به وربما أثنى علي فأسر بذلك رحمه الله تعالى وأعاد علي من بركته والله تعالى أعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Ghannām, a man from the al-Ḥusayniyya quarter of Cairo, revered by both elites and common people, and renowned for his piety. He died there, having lived a long life, on Thursday, the first of Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 870 (AH). Al-Sharaf al-Manāwī led the funeral prayer for him at the gate of al-Anwar Mosque near Khān al-Sabīl in al-Ḥusayniyya with a large congregation. They returned with his body to his home, and he was buried in a grave he had prepared for himself there during his lifetime. I (al-Sakhāwī) was among those who saw him herding goats and selling their milk. May God have mercy on him and benefit us with his blessings. I said: 'There is no doubt about his piety. I saw him countless times because his residence was near my own dwelling place. He held great affection for me and welcomed me, such that whenever I met him, he would promptly pray for me with utmost cheerfulness, enjoying conversation with me and smiling.' His blessings and bounties reverted to me, and his prayers benefited me. I would often perform Friday prayers with him at al-Anwar Mosque and enjoyed sitting with him, desiring his prayers and seizing the opportunity of seeing him. It was said that he was a 'master of the time' (ṣāḥib al-waqt), such that Shaykh Ibrāhīm al-Matbūlī, upon his arrival in the outskirts of al-Ḥusayniyya, met with him, as previously mentioned in his biography. I never knew him to frequent the company of worldly people or to accept anything from anyone. He was humble and silent. Once, after I performed the Eid al-Adha prayer beside him, he showed me kindness regarding a certain matter (qaḍiyya). When I apologized to him, explaining what prevented me from carrying it out, he accepted my excuse and said: 'Your comfort is more important to me than the one who inquired about it or similar matters.' He would also pray for my father (al-Sakhāwī's father) when I met him, and sometimes he would praise me, which pleased me. May God have mercy on him and renew his blessings upon me. And God Almighty knows best."@en .

rec:AIND-D00408 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00408-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00408-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00408-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00408 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم القزاز المقرئ قرأ عليه عبد القادر الطوخي القرآن لأبي عمرو وابن كثير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Qazzāz, the Qurʾān reciter (muqriʾ). ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Ṭūkhī studied with him the Qurʾān according to the recitations of Abū ʿAmr and Ibn Kathīr."@en .

rec:AIND-D00408a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00408a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00408a ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الكردي . اختلف في اسم أبيه فقيل خليل وقيل عبد الكريم وتقدم في ابن عبد الكريم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Kurdī. There is disagreement regarding his father's name, with some saying Khalīl and others ʿAbd al-Karīm. He was mentioned earlier under Ibn ʿAbd al-Karīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D00408b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00408b-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00408b ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن إسماعيل الإمام ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl, the Imām."@en .

rec:AIND-D00408c a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00408c-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00408c ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم بن موسى بن بلال المقرى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm b. Mūsā b. Bilāl al-Muqrá."@en .

rec:AIND-D00409 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00409-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00409-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00409-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00409 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الماقريزي الحلبي شيخ قرأ عليه القرآن صاحبنا البرهان القادري في ابتدائه وما علمت شيئا من خبره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Māqyrīzī al-Ḥalabī, a shaykh from whom our shaykh al-Burhān al-Qādirī recited the Qurʾān in his early days. I (al-Sakhāwī) do not know anything about his news."@en .

rec:AIND-D00410 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00410-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00410-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00410 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم المغربي الشهير بالحاج لكونه كان يغضب منها فصارت لقبا له كان من قراء السبع ممن قرأ على ميمون إمام الفخار مع صلاح وخير . مات في سنة سبع وستين . أفاده لي بعض أصحابنا المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Maghribī, known as al-Ḥājj. Because he used to get angry at this epithet, it became his sobriquet. He was one of the reciters of the Seven Readings (al-sabʿ), having studied recitation under Maymūn Imām al-Fakhkhār, and he possessed integrity (ṣalāḥ) and goodness (khayr). He died in the year 867 AH. One of our Maghribī companions provided me with this information."@en .

rec:AIND-D00410a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00410a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00410a ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الملكاوي . له ذكر في عمر بن عبد الله بن عمر بن داود وهو ابن محمد بن راشد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Malkāwī. He is mentioned in the entry of ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Dāwūd, and he is the son of Muḥammad b. Rāshid."@en .

rec:AIND-D00411 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00411-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00411-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00411 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إبراهيم الهندي الحنفي شيخ أخذ عنه البرهان بن ظهيرة بمكة العربية والمعاني والبيان وأجوز أن يكون الكردي فالله أعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ibrāhīm al-Hindī al-Ḥanafī, a shaykh from whom al-Burhān b. Ẓahīra studied Arabic language, semantics, and rhetoric in Mecca. It is also possible that he was al-Kurdī; God knows best."@en .

rec:AIND-D00412 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00412-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00412-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00412 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أبرك الحكمي أحد أمراء دمشق تنقل بعد أستاذه جكم المتغلب على حلب إلى أن صار في الأيام الأشرفية برسباي من أعيان الخاصكية ثم نقل إلى طبلخاناة دمشق حتى مات بها ظنا قبيل الأربعين وثمانمائة وكان مسرفا على نفسه عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abrāk al-Ḥakamī, one of the amirs of Damascus. He moved around after his master Jakam, who took over Aleppo, until he became one of the notables of the Khāṣṣakiyya during the days of al-Ashraf Barsbāy. He was then transferred to the ṭablakhānāh of Damascus, where he died, probably just before 840 AH. He was extravagant in his life. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00413 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00413-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00413-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00413-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00413 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أبرك الأشرفي برسباي أحد العشرات من ناحية جامع طولون . مات في حادي عشر المحرم سنة ثلاث وتسعين وكان شريرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abarak al-Ashrafī Barsbāy, one of the Ten from the vicinity of Jāmiʿ Ṭūlūn. He died on the eleventh of Muharram in the year 993 H. He was a wicked person."@en .

rec:AIND-D00414 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00414-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00414-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00414 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أجود بن زامل العقيلي الجبري نسبة لجد له اسمه جبر ولذا يقال له ولطائفته بنو جبر النجدي الأصل المالكي مولده ببادية الحسا والقطيف من الشرق في رمضان سنة إحدى وعشرين وثمانمائة وقام أخوه سيف على آخر ولاة الجراونة بقايا القرامطة حين رام قتله وكان الظفر لسيف بحيث قتله وانتزع البلاد المشار إليها وملكها وسار فيها بالعدل فدان له أهلها ولما مات خلفه أخوه هذا بل اتسعت له مملكته بحيث ملك البحرين وعمان ثم قام حتى انتزع مملكة هرموز ابن أخ لصرغل كان استقر فيها بعد موت أبيه وضيق على الابن المشار إليه وصار صرغل يبذل له ما كان يبذله له أخوه أو أزيد وصار رئيس نجد ذا أتباع يزيدون على الوصف مع فروسية تعددت في بدنه جراحات كثيرة بسببها وله إلمام ببعض فروع المالكية واعتناء بتحصيل كتبهم بل استقر في قضائه ببعض أهل السنة منهم بعد أن كانوا شيعة وأقاموا الجمعة والجماعات وأكثر من الحج في أتباع كثيرين يبلغون آلافا مصاحبا للتصدق والبذل وغيرهم . أفاد حاصله السيد السمهودي وبالغ معي في شأنه وهو ممن يكثر البذل له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ajud b. Zāmil al-ʿUqaylī al-Jabrī, named al-Jabrī after his grandfather Jabr, and his tribe was known as Banū Jabr. He was of Najdi origin and belonged to the Maliki madhhab. He was born in the desert of al-Ḥasā and al-Qaṭīf in the East in Ramaḍān of the year 821 AH. His brother Sayf rose up against the last rulers of the Jarāwina, remnants of the Qarmatians, when they attempted to kill him. Sayf was victorious, killing him and seizing the aforementioned lands, ruling them justly, so their people submitted to him. When Sayf died, this brother (Ajud) succeeded him, and his kingdom expanded to include al-Baḥrayn and ʿUmān. He then rose up and seized the kingdom of Hurmuz from Ṣarghal's nephew, who had settled there after his father's death, and he put pressure on the aforementioned nephew. Ṣarghal began to offer him what his brother used to offer him, or more. He became the leader of Najd with followers beyond description, and he was skilled in horsemanship, sustaining many wounds on his body because of it. He had some familiarity with branches of Maliki law and was diligent in collecting their books. Moreover, he established his judiciary among some of the Sunnis in his realm after they had been Shiites, instituting Friday prayers and congregational prayers. He performed Hajj many times with many followers, numbering thousands, accompanied by charity and generosity, among other acts. The substance of this notice was provided by al-Sayyid al-Samhūdī, who spoke to me (al-Sakhāwī) at length in his praise; he himself is among those to whom he (Ajwad) gives generously."@en .

rec:AIND-D00415 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00415-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00415-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00415 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أجود بن سيف بن زامل الجبري . مات في"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ajwad b. Sayf b. Zāmil al-Jabrī. He died in"@en .

rec:AIND-D00417 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00417-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00417-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00417-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00417 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن آق برس بالسين المهملة آخره وربما قلبت صادا ابن بلغاق بن كنجك ابن نار قمس المسند شهاب الدين الخوارزمي الكنجي الأصل الدمشقي الصالحي ورأيت شيخنا في فوائد أبي بكر بن أبي الهيتم من فهرسته قطع حروف نسبته وضبطها ك ن ج ك ى . ولد سنة ثلاث وعشرين وسبعمائة وسمع من إسحاق بن يحيى الآمدي ومحمد بن عبد الله بن المحب وزينب ابنة الكمال في آخرين وأجاز له في سنة سبع وعشرين الختني والدبوسي ووجيهة وابن القماح والمزي والبرزالي وإبراهيم بن محمد الواني وغيرهم من المصريين والشاميين . وروى لنا عنه جماعة منهم الزين شعبان وابن عمه شيخنا وقال أنه كان حسن الخلق خيرا وكذا سمع منه من شيوخنا العز عبد السلام القدسي وذكره المقريزي في عقوده . مات في سنة ثلاث وجده ذكره القطب الحلبي في تاريخ مصر وأنه سمع من عبد الدائم . ومات بمصر سنة تسع وسبعمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Āqbaras (ending with a dotted sin, which sometimes becomes a ṣād), son of Balghāq b. Kanjak b. Nār Qumas, al-Musnad Shihāb al-Dīn al-Khwārazmī, originally al-Kanjī, al-Dimashqī al-Ṣāliḥī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) noted in the 'Fawāʾid of Abū Bakr b. Abī al-Haytham' from his index that he truncated the letters of his nisba and vocalized it as Kanjakī. He was born in the year 723 H. He heard from Isḥāq b. Yaḥyá al-Āmidī, Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Muḥibb, Zaynab bint al-Kamāl, among others. In the year 727 H, he received ijāza from al-Khatanī, al-Dabbūsī, Wajīha, Ibn al-Qammāḥ, al-Mizzī, al-Barzālī, Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-Wānī, and others from among the Egyptians and Damascenes. A group transmitted from him, including al-Zayn Shaʿbān and his paternal cousin, our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar). He (our shaykh) said that he (Aḥmad) was of good character and benevolent. Al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-Salām al-Qudsī also heard from him among our shaykhs, and al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his ʿUqūd. He died in the year [8]03. As for his grandfather, al-Quṭb al-Ḥalabī mentioned him in his Taʾrīkh Miṣr, noting that he heard from ʿAbd al-Dāʾim and died in Egypt in the year 709."@en .

rec:AIND-D00418 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00418-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00418-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00418-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00418-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_b87_apply2,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00418 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الوهاب الشهاب ولقبه شيخنا بالضياء أبو العباس المرشدي الفوي المكي الشافعي سبط الجمال محمد بن عبد الله بن عبد المعطي وأخو الجمال محمد والجلال عبد الواحد . ولد سنة ثلاث وستين وسبعمائة بمكة وحضر بها في الخامسة على العز بن جماعة منسكه الكبير وتساعياته الأربعين وغير ذلك وعلى اليافعي الصحيح وسمع على الزين بن القاري جزء ابن الطلاية وعلى جده لأمه صحيح ابن حبان وغير ذلك وعلى زينب ابنة أحمد بن ميمون التونسي والأختين أم الحسن وأم الحسين المسماة كل منهما فاطمة ابنة أحمد بن الرضي الطبري في آخرين بل ذكر أنه سمع بالقاهرة من ابن الشهيد نظم السيرة له وبدمشق من المحب الصامت الكثير وأجاز له بن رافع والأسنائي والبهاء السبكي والكمال بن حبيب وعمر بن إبراهيم النقبي وابن قواليح وابن الهبل وابن النجم والصلاح بن أبي عمر وابن أميلة وأبو البقاء السبكي وغيرهم وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء كالتقي بن فهد وولديه والأبي والبرهان بن ظهيرة . ومات في ظهر يوم الجمعة رابع ذي القعدة سنة اثنتين وثلاثين بمكة بعد أن أضر وصلى عليه بعد صلاة العصر ثم دفن بالمعلاة وكانت جنازته حافلة وهو ممن ذكره شيخنا في معجمه باختصار وقال أجاز لأولادي بإفادة المراكشي وقال في أنبائه أنه حدث قبل موته بسنة بشرح السنة للبغوي بإجازته من بعض شيوخه ومن قبل موته بشهر بالشمائل بإجازته من الصلاح . وأرخ مولده سنة ستين ووفاته يوم الخميس والأول فيهما أثبت . وذكره المقريزي في عقوده باختصار ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb (al-Shihāb). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) gave him the laqab al-Ḍiyāʾ. He was Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Murshidī al-Fuwī al-Makkī al-Shāfiʿī, the maternal grandson of al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī, and the brother of al-Jamāl Muḥammad and al-Jalāl ʿAbd al-Wāḥid. He was born in Mecca in 763 H. In his fifth year (768 H), he attended in Mecca the major rites (mansak) of al-ʿIzz b. Jamāʿa, his forty devotional litanies (tusāʿiyyāt), and other works. He heard al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Yāfiʿī. He heard Juzʾ Ibn al-Ṭalāyah from al-Zayn b. al-Qārī, and Ṣaḥīḥ Ibn Ḥibbān and other works from his maternal grandfather. He also heard from Zaynab, the daughter of Aḥmad b. Maymūn al-Tūnisī, and from the two sisters, Umm al-Ḥasan and Umm al-Ḥusayn (both named Fāṭima), daughters of Aḥmad b. al-Raḍī al-Ṭabarī, among others. It is mentioned that he also heard in Cairo from Ibn al-Shahīd his Naẓm al-Sīra, and and in Damascus he heard much (al-kathīr) from al-Muḥibb al-Ṣāmit. He received ijāza from Ibn Rāfiʿ, al-Asnāʾī, al-Bahāʾ al-Subkī, al-Kamāl b. Ḥabīb, ʿUmar b. Ibrāhīm al-Naqabī, Ibn Qawāliḥ, Ibn al-Habal, Ibn al-Najm, al-Ṣalāḥ b. Abī ʿUmar, Ibn Umayla, Abū al-Baqāʾ al-Subkī, and others. He transmitted ḥadīth, and distinguished scholars such as al-Taqī b. Fahd, his two sons, al-Abī, and al-Burhān b. Ẓahīra heard from him. He died on Friday afternoon, the fourth of Dhū al-Qaʿda in 832 H in Mecca, after he became blind. His funeral prayer was held after the ʿAṣr prayer, and he was then buried in al-Muʿallā. His funeral was well-attended. Our shaykh (al-Sakhāwī is referring to Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī) mentioned him briefly in his dictionary and said, “He granted ijāza to my children based on the benefit of al-Marākushī.” In his biographical notices (anbāʾ), Ibn Ḥajar stated that Aḥmad narrated al-Baghawī's Sharḥ al-Sunna a year before his death, with an ijāza from some of his shaykhs, and narrated al-Shamāʾil a month before his death, with an ijāza from al-Ṣalāḥ. His birth year is recorded as 760 H and his death on a Thursday, but the first date for both (763 H and Friday, 4 Dhū al-Qaʿda 832 H) is more authenticated. al-Maqrīzī also mentioned him briefly in his ʿUqūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D00419 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00419-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00419-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00419-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00419-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00419 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن ثابت الشهاب النابلسي الماضي أبوه . نشأ فحفظ المنهاج وجمع الجوامع وألفية ابن مالك وعرض على الزين خطاب وغيره واشتغل في العربية على أبي العزم الحلاوي ولازم خطابا والنجم بن قاضي عجلون ونشأ متصونا مع صباحة وجهه ولما استقر أبوه في الوكالة كان هو وكيل السلطان بدمشق وراج أمره في ذلك بحيث لم يكن لنائبها فمن دونه معه كلام وزاحم أباه بل ربما فاقه في جمع الأموال ونحوها إلى أن أرسل إليه قبل مسك أبيه بأيام من قبض عليه وأودعه في الحديد واستخلص منه بالضرب وغيره ما لا يضبط إلى أن مات في أثناء ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وثمانين بل قيل أنه طعن نفسه ولم يبلغ خمسا وعشرين سنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Thābit, al-Shihāb al-Nābulusī. His father was mentioned previously. He grew up, memorized Minhāj al-Ṭālibīn, Jamʿ al-Jawāmiʿ, and Ibn Mālik's Alfiyya. He presented these works to al-Zayn Khaṭṭāb and others. He studied Arabic under Abū al-ʿAzm al-Ḥalāwī and closely associated with Khaṭṭāb and al-Najm b. Qāḍī ʿAjlūn. He was raised with modesty and a handsome countenance. When his father settled into the deputyship, he himself became the Sultan's deputy in Damascus. His influence in this role became so pronounced that neither the deputy of Damascus nor anyone below him could gainsay him, and he rivaled his father, even surpassing him in collecting wealth and other matters. However, a few days before his father's capture, he was seized, imprisoned in iron, and an incalculable amount of wealth was extracted from him through beating and other means. He died during Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 882 AH. It was also said that he stabbed himself and did not reach twenty-five years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D00420 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00420-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00420-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00420-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00420-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00420-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00420 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن رجب شهاب الدين البقاعي ثم الدمشقي الشافعي الأعرج ابن أخت القاضي تاج الدين والماضي أبوه ويعرف بابن الزهري . ولد في يوم الجمعة سابع عشر ربيع الثاني سنة ست وثمانمائة بالبقاع العزيزي وانتقل صحبة والده إلى دمشق فنشأ بها وحفظ القرآن والمنهاجين الفرعي والأصلي لشعبان الآثاري وعرضها على الشمس الكفيري واللوبياني وغيرهما وتلا القرآن على الشرف صدقة بن سلامة الضريري والزين بن اللبان وعبد المحسن النيني وأخذ في الفقه عن خاله التاج والبرهان بن خطيب عذراء وكذا عن الشمس البرماوي حين إقامته بدمشق وفي العربية عن الشمس البصروي وفي الأصول عن الشرف بن مفلح وسكن صفد مع والده مدة ثم سافر إلى القاهرة فسمع بها الواسطي والزين الزركشي والكلوتاتي والعلاء بن بردس وابن ناظر الصاحبة وآخرين وتنزل في صوفية الباسطية بها وقتا وقرأ البخاري عند الغرس خليل السخاوي وناب في القضاء بها عن الهروي ثم عن شيخنا ثم بصفد عن أبيه ثم استقل بها بعد موته وعزل منها مرارا وكذا باشر القضاء بأماكن كالرملة وحماة وطرابلس وغزة وحلب فلم تحمد سيرته فيها خصوصا حلب فإني كنت فيها حين كونه قاضيا بها فسمعت من أعيانها فمن دونهم في وصفه كل عجيب وهو الحاكم بهدم بعض بيت ابن الشحنة بعناية بعض الأعيان وقد عرض عليه الصلاح الطرابلسي الحنفي محافيظه في ذي الحجة سنة سبع وأربعين وأظنه كان حينئذ قاضيهم . وبالجملة فهو ممن لم يذكر بعلم ولا دين بل يوصف بنقيضهما مع خبث الطوية وإزراء الهيئة والتجاهر بالرشا والإقدام وآل أمره إلى أن صار مطرحا مهملا دائرا على قدميه إلى أن مات في ربيع الآخر سنة ثمان وسبعين وصلى عليه الأمين الأقصرائي وأسند وصيته إليه وإلى النوري الانبابي نائب كاتب السر وكان جاره وترك أما له مسنة ولم يخلف ولدا ولا زوجة عفا الله عنه وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Rajab, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Biqāʿī, then al-Dimashqī, al-Shāfiʿī, al-Aʿraj, nephew of al-Qāḍī Tāj al-Dīn, whose father was previously mentioned. He was known as Ibn al-Zuhrī. He was born on Friday, the seventeenth of Rabīʿ al-Thānī in the year 806 AH, in al-Biqāʿ al-ʿAzīzī. He moved with his father to Damascus and grew up there. He memorized the Qurʾān and the two Minhāj works (al-Farʿī and al-Aṣlī) by Shaʿbān al-Athārī, and presented them to al-Shams al-Kafīrī, al-Lūbiyānī, and others. He recited the Qurʾān to al-Sharaf Ṣadaqa b. Salāma al-Ḍarīrī, al-Zayn b. al-Labbān, and ʿAbd al-Muḥsin al-Nīnī. He studied fiqh under his maternal uncle al-Tāj and al-Burhān b. Khaṭīb ʿAdhrāʾ, as well as under al-Shams al-Birmāwī during his residence in Damascus. He studied Arabic language with al-Shams al-Baṣrawī and uṣūl (legal theory) with al-Sharaf b. Mufliḥ. He resided in Ṣafad with his father for a period, then traveled to Cairo, where he listened to al-Wāsiṭī, al-Zayn al-Zarkashī, al-Kalūtātī, al-ʿAlāʾ b. Bardas, Ibn Nāẓir al-Ṣāḥiba, and others. He stayed for a time in the Sufi community of al-Bāsiṭiyya there. He read al-Bukhārī under al-Ghars Khalīl al-Sakhāwī and served as deputy Qāḍī in Cairo for al-Harawī, then for our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and then in Ṣafad for his father. After his father's death, he became the independent Qāḍī there and was dismissed several times. He also served as Qāḍī in various places such as al-Ramla, Ḥamā, Ṭarābulus, Ghazza, and Ḥalab, but his conduct was not praised in these places, especially in Aleppo. I was there when he was Qāḍī, and I heard many strange things describing him from the dignitaries and common people alike. He ordered the demolition of part of Ibn al-Shaḥḥna's house with the assistance of some notables. Al-Ṣalāḥ al-Ṭarābulusī al-Ḥanafī presented his memorized works to him in Dhū al-Ḥijja 847, and I believe he was their Qāḍī at that time. In short, he was not mentioned for knowledge or piety; rather, he was described with their opposites, along with malice, contemptible appearance, open bribery, and impudence. His affairs deteriorated until he became neglected and forgotten, wandering on foot until he died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir 878 AH. Al-Amīn al-Aqṣarāʾī led his funeral prayer and was entrusted with his will, along with al-Nūrī al-Inbābī, the deputy kātib al-sirr and his neighbor. He left behind an aged mother but no son or wife. May God forgive him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D00421 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00421-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00421-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00421-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00421 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن غنائم شهاب الدين البعلي المدني ثم القاهري الماضي أبوه والآتي أخوه أبو الفتح ويعرف بابن علبك وهو لقب لجده أحمد القادم المدينة وكأنه مختصر من بعلبك ولد سنة تسعين وسبعمائة أو قبلها بيسير بالمدينة وسمع على البرهان بن فرحون وابن صديق والزين المراغي والعلم سليمان السقا في سنة سبع وتسعين وقبلها وبعدها حتى في سنة خمس عشرة وتحول إلى القاهرة بعد موت أبيه فقطنها وداخل رؤساءها فترقى في الحشمة وركب الخيول النفيسة واستمر بها إلى أن مات بعد الخمسين ظنا وورثه شقيقه أبو الفتح المشار إليه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Ghanāʾim, Shihāb al-Dīn, al-Baʿlī, al-Madanī, then al-Qāhirī. His father was mentioned above, and his brother Abū al-Fatḥ will be mentioned later. He was also known as Ibn ʿAllabak, which was a laqab for his grandfather Aḥmad who came to Medina, as if it were a shortened form of Baʿlabakk. He was born in 790 AH, or a little before, in Medina. He heard from al-Burhān b. Farḥūn, Ibn Ṣaddīq, al-Zayn al-Marāghī, and al-ʿAlam Sulaymān al-Saqqā in the year 797 AH, and before and after that, until the year 815 AH, in Medina. He moved to Cairo after his father's death and settled there. He associated with its leaders, rose in status, and rode fine horses. He remained there until he died, probably after the year 850 AH. His full brother Abū al-Fatḥ, who was mentioned earlier, inherited from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00422 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00422-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00422-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00422-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00422 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن محمد الشهاب بن الحتاتي بمهملة ومثناتين مخففا التاجر ابن التاجر ممن كان يزاحم طلبة العلم ويحضر عند الأبناسي ونحوه وربما جاءني مع سرعة حركة وإظهار تودد وحزم وسافر لمكة في التجارة مرارا وجاور . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة ثلاث وتسعين وأسند وصيته لتاج الدين بن عبد الغني ابن الجيعان ويقال أنه وجد له شيء كثير بحيث خدم منه الملك بألف وكان قد تزوج عبد العزيز العقيلي ابنته وكان موتهما متقاربا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb Ibn al-Ḥatātī (with unpointed ḥāʾ and two tāʾs, without doubling), a merchant and son of a merchant. He associated closely with students of knowledge and attended the lessons of al-Abnāsī and others. Sometimes he would visit me (al-Sakhāwī), showing quick activity, affection, and resolve. He traveled to Mecca repeatedly for trade and stayed there for an extended period. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 893 AH. He entrusted his will to Tāj al-Dīn b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī Ibn al-Jīʿān. It is said that he left a great deal of wealth, so much so that a thousand (dinars/dirhams) from it were presented to the ruler. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-ʿUqaylī had married his daughter, and their deaths were close together."@en .

rec:AIND-D00423 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00423-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00423-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00423 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد البحيري الخانكي ثم المكي . لازمني في الإملاء وغيره بمكة في الثانية سنة إحدى وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad al-Buḥayrī al-Khānkī, then al-Makkī. He diligently studied under me (al-Sakhāwī) for dictation and other subjects in Mecca in the second period, in the year 871 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00424 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00424-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00424-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00424 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد الهروجي الهندي القاضي لقيني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad al-Harūjī al-Hindī, the judge. He met me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00425 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00425-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00425-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00425-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00425 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد الشهاب العقبي اليماني الشافعي ولد كما ذكر في سنة ثلاث وعشرين وثمانمائة وقدم القاهرة في سنة سبع وأربعين فلازم الزين البوتيجي وسكن عنده الفاضلية وعرف به وكتب الإملاء عن شيخنا بل وأخذ عنه في شرح الألفية وغيرها وكذا أخذ عن ابن حسان وغيره وكتب بخطه أشياء واختص بابن الجريس وقتا وصار في ظله حتى مات وبعده تحول إلى تعز وهي بالقرب من بلده وأقام بها وصار يحج منها كل سنة ونعم الرجل سكونا ومشاركة في الجملة مع تعفف مات بمكة في المحرم سنة خمس وتسعين رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad, with the laqab al-Shihāb and nisbahs al-ʿUqbī, al-Yamānī, and of the Shāfiʿī madhhab. He was born, as mentioned, in the year 823 H. He arrived in Cairo in 847 H and remained in close discipleship to al-Zayn al-Būtījī, residing with him at the Fāḍiliyya (madrasa), and became known through him. He wrote down dictations from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and also studied from him (Ibn Ḥajar) a commentary on al-Alfiyya and other works. He also studied from Ibn Ḥassān and others. He wrote many things in his own hand and was for a time closely associated with Ibn al-Jurays, remaining under his patronage until his death. After him (Ibn al-Jurays's death), he moved to Taʿizz, which is near his hometown, and resided there. From there, he performed the Hajj every year. He was a fine man, calm and generally cooperative, with a modest disposition. He died in Mecca in Muḥarram of the year 895 H. May God have mercy on him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D00426 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00426-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00426-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00426 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد شهاب الدين القوصي اليماني الشافعي ويعرف بابن كان أبوه مشهورا من أهل قوص ونشأ هو بها وولي بها عدة مناصب ثم دخل اليمن فقطنها وناب في بعض بلادها عن المجد الشيرازي وكان كثير الفكاهة قاله شيخنا في معجمه قال وذكر لي أنه سمع من محيي الدين بن الرحبي بدمشق فسمعت منه حديثا واحدا بمدينة المهجم علقته في البلدانيات وحج معنا في سنة ست وثمانمائة ثم رجع إلى اليمن وبلغنا أنه حج أيضا . قلت وهو في عقود المقريزي باختصار وهو غير أحمد بن عبد الله القوصي المصري الآتي فاتفقا في الاسم وافترقا في النسب والبلد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Qūṣī al-Yamanī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn [...] (the byname is lacking in the text); his father was a well-known man of Qūṣ. He grew up there and held several positions. Then he entered Yemen and settled there, serving as a deputy in some of its regions on behalf of al-Majd al-Shīrāzī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned in his dictionary (Muʿjam) that he was very humorous. He (Ibn Ḥajar) continued: 'He told me that he had heard from Muḥyī al-Dīn b. al-Raḥabī in Damascus, so I heard a single ḥadīth from him in the city of al-Mahjam, which I recorded in my Buldāniyāt. He performed Hajj with us in the year 806, then returned to Yemen, and we heard that he performed Hajj again.' I (al-Sakhāwī) say that he is mentioned briefly in al-Maqrīzī's ʿUqūd. He is not the Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Qūṣī al-Miṣrī who is mentioned later; they share the same name but differ in nisbah and origin."@en .

rec:AIND-D00427 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00427-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00427-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00427-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00427 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن هاشم الشهاب المحلي القاهري ولد قبل الخمسين وسبعمائة وسمع على القلانسي أكثر صحيح مسلم وأجاز له سليمان بن سالم الغزي بل ذكر أنه سمع عليه علوم الحديث لابن الصلاح وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء وكان أحد الصوفية بالبيبرسية ويتكسب بالشهادة في بولاق ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه باختصار وقال أجاز لأولادي مات في أول سنة خمس وعشرين وقد جاز الثمانين . قلت وهو عم أبي شيخنا الجلال المحلي وكان له ولد اسمه شمس الدين محمد ولمحمد ابن اسمه عبد القادر مات في شعبان سنة ست وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Hāshim, al-Shihāb al-Maḥallī al-Qāhirī. He was born before 750 H. He heard most of Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim from al-Qalānsī. Sulaymān b. Sālim al-Ghazzī granted him ijāza, and it is also mentioned that he heard from him Ibn al-Ṣalāḥ's ʿUlūm al-Ḥadīth. He transmitted ḥadīth, and distinguished scholars heard from him. He was one of the Sufis at al-Baybarsiyya and earned his living as a witness (shāhid) in Būlāq. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī) mentioned him briefly in his work Inbāʾ al-Ghumr, stating that he granted ijāza to his children. He died at the beginning of 825 H, having passed 80 years of age. I say: he was the paternal uncle of the father of our shaykh al-Jalāl al-Maḥallī. He had a son named Shams al-Dīn Muḥammad, who in turn had a son named ʿAbd al-Qādir, who died in Shaʿbān 896 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00428 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00428-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00428-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00428 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد المرشدي . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن أبي بكر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad al-Murshidī. He was mentioned earlier in the entry of one whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr."@en .

rec:AIND-D00429 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00429-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00429-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00429-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00429-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00429 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن إسماعيل الشهاب أبو العباس النابلسي ويعرف بابن الدرويش سمع على الميدومي المسلسل وغيره وعلى ابن القارى جزء ابن الطلاية والمسلسل بالصف وحدث سمع ذلك منه شيخنا التقي أبو بكر القلقشندي وغيره في سنة اثنتين وعاش حتى أجاز في استدعاء فيه ابن شيخنا سنة إحدى وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Ismāʿīl, al-Shihāb Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Nābulusī, also known as Ibn al-Darwīsh. He heard al-Musalsal and other works from al-Maydūmī, and Juzʾ Ibn al-Ṭalāya and al-Musalsal in al-Ṣaff from Ibn al-Qārī. He transmitted (ḥaddatha), and our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī)'s student, al-Taqī Abū Bakr al-Qalqashandī, and others heard that from him in the year '02 (802 AH). He lived until he granted an ijaza in a request in the year '21 (821 AH) for Ibn Shaykhinā (Ibn Ḥajar's son)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00430 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00430-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00430-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00430 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن حسن بن عجلان الحسيني ممن خالف على عمه بركات وقتا وربما هجم مكة وكانت جولة مات في عشري شوال سنة ست وستين بأرض خلد وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بها . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān al-Ḥusaynī opposed his uncle Barakāt for a time and perhaps attacked Mecca (it was a campaign). He died in the last ten days of Shawwāl in the year 866 in the land of Khuld. His body was carried to Mecca and buried there. Ibn Fahd recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D00431 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00431-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00431-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00431 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن الحسن الزموري مات بعد العشرين أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. al-Ḥasan al-Zamūrī died after the twenties (Hijri). Ibn ʿAzm recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00432 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00432-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00432-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00432 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن خليل بن محمد الحلبي الميقاتي مات بعد الخمسين ذكره ابن عزم مجردا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Khalīl b. Muḥammad al-Ḥalabī al-Mīqātī. He died after the fifties. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him plainly (mujarraḍan)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00433 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00433-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00433-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00433 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن سليمان بن إبراهيم الشهاب القليوبي ثم القاهري أخو علي الآتي مولده بعد الثمانين أو قبلها تقريبا وسمع على المطرزي والتقي الدجوي والشرف بن الكويك في سنة أربع وتسعين وسبعمائة ما حدث من أبي داود وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء سمعت عليه وكان أحد الصوفية بسعيد السعداء وممن يتكسب ببيع الشبارى ونحوها مع الخير ولين الجانب مات في أوائل رمضان سنة ثمان وستين رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Sulaymān b. Ibrāhīm al-Shihāb al-Qalyūbī, then al-Qāhirī, brother of the forthcoming ʿAlī. He was born approximately in the 780s AH (after 780 or before it). In 794 AH, he heard the narrations from Abū Dāwūd from al-Muṭarrizī, al-Taqī al-Dajwī, and al-Sharaf b. al-Kuwayk, and he transmitted ḥadīth. Many eminent scholars heard from him, and I (al-Sakhāwī) heard from him. He was one of the Sufis at Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ and earned a living by selling shibārā and similar items. He was known for his goodness and gentleness. He died in early Ramaḍān in the year 868 AH. May God have mercy on him and on us."@en .

rec:AIND-D00434 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00434-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00434-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00434 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن سليمان شهاب الدين العكاري ثم الطرابلسي الشافعي ويعرف بابن العلم لكون جده يلقب علم الدين تفقه ببلده على البلقيني وغيره ثم دخل دمشق واشتغل بها على العماد الحسباني ورحل مع الصدر الياسوفي إلى حلب فسمع بها بقراءته في سنة سبعين على الكمالين محمد بن نصر الله بن أحمد بن النحاس وابن حبيب وأحمد بن قطلو وغيرهم وولي قضاء عكار وكانت لديه فضيلة ويتكسب من الشهادة قال العلاء بن خطيب الناصرية اجتمعت به بطرابلس وكان فاضلا مات بطرابلس في صفر سنة ثمان وما علمته حدث . وذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Sulaymān, Shihāb al-Dīn al-ʿAkkārī, then al-Ṭarābulusī, Shāfiʿī. He was known as Ibn al-ʿAlam because his grandfather was given the laqab ʿAlam al-Dīn. He studied fiqh in his hometown (ʿAkkār) under al-Bulqīnī and others. He then entered Damascus and studied there under al-ʿImād al-Ḥasbānī. He traveled with al-Ṣadr al-Yāsūfī to Aleppo, where, through his (al-Yāsūfī’s) recitation, he heard in the year 770 H from the two Kamāls — Muḥammad b. Naṣr Allāh b. Aḥmad Ibn al-Naḥḥās and (al-Kamāl) Ibn Ḥabīb — and from Aḥmad b. Qaṭlū and others. He was appointed qāḍī of ʿAkkār, possessed virtue, and earned a living through giving testimony. Al-ʿAlāʾ b. Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya said, \"I met him in Tripoli, and he was a virtuous man.\" He died in Tripoli in Ṣafar of the year 808 H. I do not know that he transmitted ḥadīth. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D00435 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00435-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00435-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00435 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن الشهاب الأبودري المالكي والد إبراهيم الماضي وعرض الرسالة في سنة اثنتين وتسعين والعمدة في التي تليها فكان ممن عرض عليه الأبناسي وابن الملقن والبلقيني والعراقي وعبد الخالق علي بن الفرات وأجازوه في خلق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Raḥman, al-Shihāb al-Abūdarī al-Mālikī, was the father of the previously mentioned Ibrāhīm. He presented al-Risāla in 892 H and al-ʿUmda in the following year. He was among those to whom al-Abnāsī, Ibn al-Mulaqqin, al-Bulqīnī, al-ʿIrāqī, and ʿAbd al-Khāliq ʿAlī b. al-Furāt presented (teaching material), and they all granted him general ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D00436 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00436-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00436-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00436 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن عبد العزيز بن علي شهاب الدين الموصلي الأصل الدمشقي نزيل الصالحية ويعرف بابن الخباز سمع من أبي بكر بن الرضي وزينب ابنة الكمال وغيرهما وحدث سمع منه صاحبنا الحافظ غرس الدين الأقفهسي وأظنه استجازه لي ومات في ربيع الأول سنة إحدى عن بضع وثمانين سنة قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shihāb al-Dīn Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī, originally from al-Mawṣil, resided in al-Ṣāliḥīya, Damascus. He was known as Ibn al-Khabbāz. He heard from Abū Bakr b. al-Raḍī, Zaynab bint al-Kamāl, and others, and he transmitted ḥadīth. Our shaykh's (Ibn Ḥajar's) colleague, al-Ḥāfiẓ Ghars al-Dīn al-Aqfahsī, heard from him. I (al-Sakhāwī) believe he granted me an ijāza. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』 that he died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of a year ending in 'one' (e.g., 801 H) at the age of some eighty years."@en .

rec:AIND-D00437 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00437-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00437-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00437-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00437-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00437 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن عبد الله بن صدقة الصيرفي ويعرف بخدمة السخاوي كتب عني في الأمالي وغيرها وحصل القول البديع وارتياح الأكباد وأشياء من تصانيفي وله رغبة في الفائدة وكان في أول أمره في ثروة فلم يراع نعمتها فانحط إلى غاية حتى صار يخالط أولى المكس بالشيء اليسير مع اشتغاله مات في رجب سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṣadaqa al-Ṣayrafī. He was known for his service to al-Sakhāwī. He copied from him (al-Sakhāwī) dictations and other matters. He also acquired al-Qawl al-Badīʿ, Irtiyāḥ al-Akbād, and other compositions of mine (al-Sakhāwī). He had a desire for knowledge, and although he was initially wealthy, he did not appreciate its blessings and eventually fell into such poverty that he associated with tax collectors for meager gains, despite his scholarly engagement. He died in Rajab of the year 892 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00438 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00438-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00438-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00438-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00438-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00438-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00438 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن إبراهيم المحب ابن البرهان بن الجمال المقدسي بن جماعة أخو إسماعيل ومحمد الآتيين اشتغل وسمع على جده والتقي القلقشندي وتميز في الفرائض واستقر في ربع الخطابة بالأقصى ونصف مشيخة التصوف بالصلاحية وغير ذلك وباشر الخطابة وغيرها وهو ممن سمع معنا هناك مات في ليلة السبت خامس رمضان سنة تسع وثمانين وقد زاد على الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ibrāhīm al-Muḥibb Ibn al-Burhān Ibn al-Jamāl al-Maqdisī Ibn Jamāʿa, brother of Ismāʿīl and Muḥammad (forthcoming). He studied and heard (ḥadīth) from his grandfather and al-Taqī al-Qalqashandī. He excelled in inheritance law (al-farāʾiḍ) and was appointed to a quarter of the preaching office (khaṭāba) at al-Aqsa Mosque, half of the headship (mashyakhat al-taṣawwuf) at al-Ṣalāḥīya, and other positions. He was among those who heard (ḥadīth) with us (al-Sakhāwī) there. He died on the night of Saturday, the 5th of Ramadan in 889 AH, at an age exceeding fifty years."@en .

rec:AIND-D00439 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00439-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00439-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00439 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن عبد الله البصري ثم المكي ويعرف بابن المفرد ممن سمع علي بمكة في الثانية سنة إحدى وسبعين الكثير من القول البديع ومني في الأمالي وغير ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī, then al-Makkī (i.e., originally from Basra, later resident in Mecca). He is known as Ibn al-Mufarrad. He was among those who studied under me (samiʿa ʿalayya) at Mecca, during [his] second [stay/session] in the year 871 [AH], [hearing] a large portion of al-Qawl al-Badīʿ, as well as my al-Amālī, and other [works]."@en .

rec:AIND-D00440 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00440-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00440-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00440 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن عبد الله الكردي الصالحي الحنبلي ويعرف بابن معتوق ذكره شيخنا في معجمه وسمى جده معتوقا وقال لقيته بالصالحية فقرأت عليه صفة الجنة لأبي نعيم بسماعه له على علي بن أبي بكر بن حصن الحراني قال ومات في حصار دمشق في شوال سنة ثلاث وأعاده في أبي بكر ولم ويسمه وسمى جده أيضا معتوقا وأما في أنبائه فسماه أحمد وجده عبد الله وقال المعروف بابن معتوق وأنه مات بعد عيد الفطر وهو في عقود المقريزي بدون عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Kurdī al-Ṣāliḥī al-Ḥanbalī, known as Ibn Maʿtūq. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Muʿjam and named his grandfather Maʿtūq. He (Ibn Ḥajar) said: 'I met him in al-Ṣāliḥiyya, and I recited to him Abū Nuʿaym's Ṣifat al-Janna (Description of Paradise), which he had heard from ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. Ḥiṣn al-Ḥarrānī.' He (Ibn Ḥajar) also said: 'He died during the siege of Dimashq in Shawwāl of the year 803 H.' He (Ibn Ḥajar) repeated this in his entry on Abū Bakr, but without naming him, and again named his grandfather Maʿtūq. However, in his Inbāʾ, he named him Aḥmad and his grandfather ʿAbd Allāh, and said he was known as Ibn Maʿtūq, and that he died after Eid al-Fiṭr. He is mentioned in al-Maqrīzī's ʿUqūd without ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D00441 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00441-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00441-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00441-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00441 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن عبد المهيمن شهاب الدين بن فخر الدين القليوبي ثم القاهري الشافعي أخو الشرف محمد الاتي ويعرف بابن الخازن لكون أبيه كما مضى كان خازن حاصل البيمارستان المنصوري سمع في سنة أربع وثمانمائة بقراءة شيخنا على سارة بن التقي السبكي الجزء الرابع من تاريخ أبي زرعة الدمشقي وحدث به سمعه منه بعض الطلبة ولم تطب نفسي بالسماع منه لما كان متلبسا به مع أنه كان يتكسب بالشهادة على باب الكاملية لكنه أجاز ثم وجدت له سماع جزء فيه الحديث المسلسل بالأولية من رواية الجمال بن الشرائحي عليه أنابه أبو الثناء محمود المنبجي وغيره ومات في سنة سبع وخمسين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Muhaymin, whose laqab was Shihāb al-Dīn, son of Fakhr al-Dīn. His nisbahs were al-Qalyūbī, then al-Qāhirī, and he belonged to the Shāfiʿī madhhab. He was the brother of al-Sharaf Muḥammad, who will be mentioned later. He was known by the nickname Ibn al-Khāzin because his father, as previously stated, was the treasurer of the Manṣūrī Hospital. In 804 H, he listened, through our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) reading to Sāra bint al-Taqī al-Subkī, to the fourth volume of Abū Zurʿa al-Dimashqī’s History. He transmitted it, and some students heard it from him. However, I (al-Sakhāwī) was disinclined to hear from him due to what he was involved in, even though he earned a living by giving testimony at the gate of al-Kāmiliyya. Nevertheless, he granted ijāza. I later found a record of him hearing a chapter containing the Musalsal bi-l-Awwaliyya ḥadīth, transmitted from al-Jamāl b. al-Sharāʾiḥī, with Abū al-Thanāʾ Maḥmūd al-Manbijī and others acting as deputies. He died in 857 H. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00442 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00442-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00442-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00442 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن علبك المدني مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن غنائم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿUlabk al-Madanī. He was previously mentioned under the entry of his grandfather, Aḥmad b. Ghanāʾim."@en .

rec:AIND-D00443 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00443-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00443-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00443-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00443 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن علي بن أحمد بن محمد الشهاب بن البرهان الأبناسي الصحراوي الشافعي الماضي أبوه وكان خيرا ساكنا متكرما مع تقلل متوددا كثير التلاوة والتوجه راغبا في الصالحين ممن يشتغل أحيانا عند الزين الأبناسي وقرأ علي بعض البخاري وولى مشيخة الصوفية بتربة الأشرف اينال شركة لأخيه ولي الدين مات في تاسع صفر سنة تسع وثمانين عقب قدومه من الحج وكان توجه ماشيا فلما وصل المدينة النبوية عجز فأركب ووجع بالبطن فلم يلبث أن مات وصلى عليه في عصر يومه ودفن عند أبيه بتربة الزين عبد الباسط ولم أقصر به عن الخمسين رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Ibrahim b. Ali b. Ahmad b. Muhammad, Shihāb al-Dīn b. al-Burhān al-Abnāsī al-Ṣaḥrāwī al-Shafi'i. His father was mentioned previously. He was a good, quiet man, generous despite his modest means, sociable, frequently recited the Qurʾān, was devout, and fond of righteous people. He sometimes studied under al-Zayn al-Abnāsī, and he recited part of al-Bukhārī to me (al-Sakhāwī). He was appointed to the shaykhdom of the Sufis at Turbat al-Ashraf Īnāl in partnership with his brother, Walī al-Dīn. He died on the 9th of Ṣafar in the year 889 AH, shortly after his return from the Hajj. He had traveled on foot, but upon reaching Medina, he became incapacitated and had to be mounted (on an animal). He suffered from stomach pain and did not live long thereafter. Funeral prayers were performed for him in the afternoon of the same day, and he was buried next to his father at Turbat al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ. I do not consider him to have been less than fifty years old. May God have mercy on him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D00444 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00444-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00444-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00444-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00444 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن علي بن الكمال محمد بن أبي السعود محمد بن حسين الشهاب ابن عالم الحجاز ورئيسه البرهان بن ظهيرة المكي الشافعي . ولد يوم الجمعة عاشر ذي الحجة سنة خمس وسبعين وثمانمائة وأمه نور الصباح الحبشية فتاة أبيه ونشأ فحفظ القرآن والمنهاج والألفية وجمع الجوامع وسمع على أبيه وحضر دروس أخيه الجمالي وكذا حضر في الإرشاد عند السيد الكمال بن حمزة حين جاور في سنة سبع وتسعين وقرأ علي في البخاري بعد أن سمع علي في حياة أبيه وبعده أشياء وعلى أعيان في العربية والصرف والأصول ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. al-Kamāl Muḥammad b. Abī al-Suʿūd Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn al-Shihāb, son of the scholar and head of the Hijaz, al-Burhān b. Ẓahīra, al-Makkī al-Shāfiʿī. He was born on Friday, the tenth of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 875. His mother was Nūr al-Ṣabāḥ al-Ḥabashiyya, his father's handmaiden. He grew up having memorized the Qurʾān, al-Minhāj, al-Alfiyya, and Jamʿ al-Jawāmiʿ. He heard (texts) from his father and attended the lessons of his brother al-Jamālī. He also attended (the reading of) al-Irshād under al-Sayyid al-Kamāl b. Ḥamza when the latter sojourned (jāwara) [in Mecca] in the year 897. He recited al-Bukhārī to me (al-Sakhāwī), after having heard various things from me both during his father's lifetime and after it, and (he studied) with notables in Arabic grammar, morphology, and uṣūl."@en .

rec:AIND-D00445 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00445-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00445-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00445-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00445 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن علي الفقيه أبو العباس العسلقي نسبة إلى العسالق طائفة من العرب اليماني اشتغل بالعلم وتفقه بأبيه وبرع في الفقه وغيره من العلوم واشتهر بذلك ذكره الأهدل في تاريخه وقال كان فقيها مجودا للفقه نحويا لغويا مفسرا محدثا والغالب عليه الفقه والحديث والتفسير أخذه عن ابن شداد بزبيد وله معرفة تامة بالرجال والتواريخ والسير ويد قوية في أصول الدين وله قصيدة حسنة رد بها على يهودي في مسألة القدر وأخرى أكثر من ثلثمائة بيت في الرد على من يبيح السماع وكان دأبه تدريس الفقه وإسماع الحديث وملازمة الجماعة في المسجد والتلاوة من ثلث الليل الأخير سريع الكتابة مع جودة الخط يقال أنه كان ينسخ في اليوم أربعين ورقة متجردا من أشغال الدنيا عاكفا على العلم والتحصيل صاحب نور وهيبة ويقال أنه كان يعرف الاسم الأعظم . مات سنة ست عن ست وثمانين وقد كف بصره ومع ذلك فلم يترك صلاة الجماعة في المسجد رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī al-Faqīh Abū al-ʿAbbās al-ʿAslaqī, a nisbah to al-ʿAsāliq, a Yemeni Arab tribe. He devoted himself to knowledge and studied fiqh under his father. He excelled in fiqh and other sciences and became well-known for it. Al-Ahdal mentioned him in his history, stating that \"he was a profound jurist, well-versed in fiqh, a grammarian, linguist, exegete, and ḥadīth scholar. His primary fields of study were fiqh, ḥadīth, and tafsīr, which he acquired from Ibn Shaddād in Zabīd. He possessed a thorough knowledge of narrators, history, and sīra (Prophetic biography), and a strong command of the principles of religion. He composed a beautiful poem refuting a Jew on the issue of divine decree, and another, over 300 verses long, refuting those who permit listening (to music/poetry). His usual practice was to teach fiqh, transmit ḥadīth by audition, consistently attend congregational prayers in the mosque, and recite the Qurʾān in the last third of the night. He was a swift scribe with excellent calligraphy; it is said that he would copy forty sheets a day. He detached himself from worldly affairs, dedicating himself to learning and scholarship, possessing light and dignity. It is also said that he knew the Greatest Name of God. He died in the year [8]06 H at the age of 86, having lost his sight. Despite this, he never missed congregational prayer in the mosque. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00446 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00446-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00446-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00446-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00446-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00446 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن عمر بن علي الشهاب أبو الفضل بن البرهان المصري ويعرف بابن المحلى التاجر الماضي أبوه قال شيخنا كان شابا حسنا كريم الشمائل خفيف الروح وقال في أبيه منه أنه بلغ الغاية في المعرفة بأمور التجارة ودخل اليمن وكان بها حين وفاة أبيه بمصر . مات بعد أبيه بيسير بمكة في أواخر ذي القعدة سنة ست . وذكره التقي الفاسي في تاريخ مكة فقال : كان وافر الملاة إلى الغاية خبيرا بالتجارة وفيه انفعال للخير وكان صاحبنا الحافظ شهاب الدين بن حجر يحضه عليه لمكانته عنده وجرت له على يده صدقات وكان يثني عليه بالعفة وهي عجيبة من مثله وكان مبتلي بعلة الصرع وبها مات في ليلة الأربعاء خامس عشري ذي القعدة عن ست وعشرين سنة بعد قدومه من اليمن باربعة أيام وكان طلب منه ليفوض له أمر المتجر السلطاني بمصر بعد موت أبيه فسبقت المنية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shihāb Abū al-Faḍl Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī, of Egyptian origin, son of al-Burhān, known as Ibn al-Maḥallā, the merchant. His father was mentioned previously. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said: 'He was a good, noble, and light-spirited young man.' And in the notice of his father he said of him (Aḥmad) that he had attained the utmost knowledge of commerce and had gone to Yemen, being there when his father died in Egypt. He (Aḥmad) died shortly after his father, in Mecca, at the end of Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year six (806 H). Al-Taqī al-Fāsī mentioned him in his 'History of Mecca' saying: 'He was exceedingly wealthy, knowledgeable in trade, and had a zeal for good. Our companion, al-Ḥāfiẓ Shihāb al-Dīn Ibn Ḥajar, encouraged him due to his high standing with him, and charities were conducted through his hands. He (Ibn Ḥajar) praised his chastity, which was remarkable for someone like him. He was afflicted with epilepsy, and he died from it on Wednesday night, the twenty-fifth of Dhū al-Qaʿda, at the age of twenty-six, four days after his arrival from Yemen. He had been asked to take charge of the Sultanic commercial agency in Egypt after his father's death, but death preceded him.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D00447 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00447-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00447-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00447-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00447 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن عيسى الشهاب بن البرهان القرشي ويعرف بابن البرهان ولي قضاء القصير وغيره من عمل دمشق ثم قضاء صفد مرارا وتوفي بها في يوم الجمعة ثالث عشر رجب سنة تسع عشرة وقد قارب الثمانين قال ابن قاضي شهبة وكان قليل المعرفة للفقه حضر عندي إلى مجلس الحكم بدمشق في سنة ست وعشرين ورأيت منه ذلك زاد غيره وسمع على جماعة كثيرين وكان أبوه أيضا قاضيا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿĪsā al-Shihāb b. al-Burhān al-Qurashī, known as Ibn al-Burhān. He served as qāḍī (judge) of al-Quṣayr and other places in the province of Damascus, then as qāḍī of Ṣafad several times. He died there on Friday, the 13th of Rajab, in the year 819 H, having approached eighty years of age. Ibn Qāḍī Shuhba said: \"His knowledge of fiqh was meager. He attended my judicial session in Damascus in the year 826 H, and I observed this from him.\" Others added that he heard from many people. His father was also a qāḍī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00448 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00448-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00448-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00448-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00448 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن إبراهيم البسطيني الماضي أبوه والآتي جده . ولد في ثامن رمضان سنة اثنتين وثمانين وثمانمائة بجدة وأمه حبشية لأبيه ثم تحول بعد شهر مع أبويه لمكة فحفظ القرآن وأربعي النووي والبردة وألفية النحو والمنهاج وعرض بعضها على التقي بن قاضي عجلون حين جاور سمع علي بمكة في تلك المجاورة ثم في سنة سبع وتسعين الشفا والبخاري وكذا سمع بالمدينة النبوية على الشيخ محمد بن أبي الفرج الشفا بقراءة أبيه وبعض البخاري واشتغل في النحو وغيره عند عيان وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm al-Basṭīnī. His father was mentioned previously, and his grandfather will be mentioned later. He was born on the 8th of Ramaḍān in the year 882 AH in Jeddah. His mother was an Abyssinian slave woman of his father. One month later, he moved with his parents to Mecca. He memorized the Qurʾān, al-Nawawī's al-Arbaʿīn, al-Burda, Alfiyyat al-Naḥw, and al-Minhāj. He presented some of these works to al-Taqī b. Qāḍī ʿAjlūn when he resided in Mecca. During that sojourn, and again in 897 AH, he heard al-Shifāʾ and al-Bukhārī from me (al-Sakhāwī). Likewise, in the Prophetic City of Medina, he heard parts of al-Shifāʾ and al-Bukhārī from Shaykh Muḥammad b. Abī al-Faraj, with his father reciting. He studied grammar and other subjects under notables (aʿyān, written عيان) and others."@en .

rec:AIND-D00449 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00449-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00449-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00449-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00449-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00449 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمود بن خليل الشيخ موفق الدين أبو ذر بن الحافظ البرهان أبي الوفا الطرابلسي الأصل ثم الحلبي المولد والدار الشافعي والد أبي بكر الآتي وهو بكنيته أشهر ولد في ليلة الجمعة تاسع صفر سنة ثمان عشرة وثمانمائة بحلب ونشأ بها فحفظ القرآن وجوده على أبيه والمنهاجين الفرعي والأصلي وألفيتي الحديث والنحو وعرض على العلاء بن خطيب الناصرية فمن دونه من طلبة أبيه وتفقه بالعلاءين المذكور وابن مكتوم الرحبي والشمس السلامي وبه انتفع فيه وفي العربية وآخرين وكذا أخذ العربية عن ابن الأعزازي والشمس الملطي والزين الخرزي وجماعة والعروض عن صدقة وعلوم الحديث عن والده وشيخنا وسمع عليهما وعلى غيرهما من شيوخ بلده والقادمين إليها ودخل الشام في توجهه للحج فسمع بها على ابن ناصر الدين وابن الطحان وابن الفخر المصري وعائشة ابنة ابن الشرائحي ولم يكثر بل جل سماعه على أبيه وأجاز له جماعة باستدعاء صاحبنا ابن فهد وتعاني في ابتدائه فنون الأدب فبرع فيها وجمع فيها تصانيف نظما ونثرا ثم أذهبها حسبما أخبرني به عن آخرها ومن ذلك عروس الأفراح فيما يقال في الراح وعقد الدرر واللآل فيما يقال في السلسال وستر الحال فيما قيل في الخال والهلال المستنير في العذار المستدير والبدر إذا استنار فيما قيل في العذار . وكذا تعاني الشروط ومهر فيها أيضا بحيث كتب التوقيع بباب ابن خطيب الناصرية ثم أعرض عنها أيضا ولزم الاعتناء بالحديث والفقه وأفرد مبهمات البخاري وكذا إعرابه بل جمع عليه تعليقا لطيفا لخصه من الكرماني والبرماوي وشيخنا وآخر أخصر منه وله التوضيح للأوهام الواقعة في الصحيح ومبهمات مسلم أيضا وقرة العين في فضل الشيخين والصهرين والسبطين وشرح الشفا والمصابيح ولكنه لم يكمل والذيل على تاريخ ابن خطيب الناصرية وغير ذلك وأدمن قراءة الصحيحين والشفا خصوصا بعد وفاة والده وصار متقدما في لغاتها ومبهماتها وضبط رجالها لا يشذ عنه من ذلك إلا النادر ولما كان شيخنا بحلب لازمه واغتبط شيخنا به وأحبه لذكائه وخفة روحه حتى أنه كتب عنه من نظمه : %~% الطرف أحور حوى رقى غنج نعاس %~% وقد قد القنا أهيف نضر مياس %~% %~% ريقتك ماء الحيا يا عاطر الأنفاس %~% عذارك الخضر يا زيني وأنت الياس %~% وصدر شيخي كتابته لذلك بقوله وكان قد ولع بنظم المواليا ووصفه بالامام موفق الدين ومرة بالفاضل البارع المحدث الأصيل الباهر الذي ضاهى كنيه في صدق اللهجة الماهر الذي ناجى سميه ففداه بالمهجة الأخير الذي فاق الأول في البصارة والنضارة والبهجة أمتع الله المسلمين ببقائه وأذن له في تدريس الحديث وأفاد به في حياة والده وراسله بذلك بعد وفاته فقال وما التمسه أبقاء الله تعالى وأدام النفع به كما نفع بأبيه وبلغه من خيري الدنيا والآخرة ما يرتجيه من الإذن له بالتدريس في الحديث النبوي فقد حصلت بغيته وحققت طلبته وأذنت له أن يقرئ علوم الحديث مما عرفه ودريه من شرح الألفية لشيخنا حافظ الوقت أبي الفضل ومما تلفقه من فوائد والده الحافظ برهان الدين تغمده الله تعالى برحمته ومن غير ذلك مما حصله بالمطالعة واستفاده بالمراجعة وكذا غير الشرح المذكور من سائر علوم الحديث وأن يدرس في معاني الحديث كل كتاب قرئ لديه ويقيد ما يعلمه من ذلك إذا قرأه هو وسمع عليه وأسأله أن لا ينساني من صالح دعواته في مجالس الحديث النبوي إلى آخر كلامه وقد لقيته بحلب وسمع بقراءتي وسمعت بقراءته بل كتبت عنه من نظمه سوى ما تقدم ما أثبته في موضع آخر وزاد اغتباطه بي وبالغ في الإطراء لفظا وخطا وكانت كتبه بعد ذلك ترد على بالاستمرار على لمحبة وفي بعضها الوصف بشيخنا وكان خيرا شهما مبجلا في ناحيته منعزلا عن بني الدنيا قانعا باليسير محبا للانجماع كثير التواضع والاستئناس بالغرباء والأكرام لهم شديد التخيل طارحا للتكلف ذا فضيلة تامة وذكاء مفرط واستحضار جيد خصوصا لمحافيظه وحرص على صون كتب والده قل أن يمكن أحدا منها بل حسم المادة في ذلك عن كل أحد حتى لا يتوهم بعض أهل بلده اختصاصه بذلك وربما أراها بعض من يثق به بحضرته ومسه مزيد الأذى من بعض طلبة والده وصرح فيه بما لا يليق ولم يرع حق أبيه ولكن لم يؤثر ذلك في وجاهته قال البقاعي وله حافظة عظيمة وملكة في تنميق الكلام وتأديته على الوجه المستظرف قوية مع جودة الذهن وسرعة الجواب والقدرة على استخراج ما في ضميره يذاكر بكثير من المبهمات وغريب الحديث قال وبيننا مودة وصداقة وقد تولع بنظم الفنون حتى برع في المواليا وأنشدني من نظمه كثيرا وساق منه شيئا ووصفه في موضع آخر بالأديب البارع المفنن وقد تصدى للتحدث والإقراء وانتفع به جماعة من أهل بلده والقادمين عليها بل وكتب مع القدماء في الاستدعاآت من حياة أبيه وهلم جرا . وترجمه ابن فهد وغيره من أصحابنا وكذا وصفه ابن أبي عذيبة في أبيه بالإمام العلامة وسمى بعض تصانيفه مات في يوم الخميس خامس عشري ذي القعدة سنة أربع وثمانين بعد أن اختلط يسيرا وحجب عن الناس ودفن عند أبيه قال البقاعي أنه مرض في آخر سنة اثنتين وثمانين ثم عوفي من المرض وحصل له اختلاط وفقد بصره واستمر به ذلك إلى أثناء سنة أربع وثمانين ثم عوفي منه ورجع إليه بصره ثم مات . قلت ولم يخلف بعده هناك مثله رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Maḥmūd b. Khalīl, the Shaykh Muwaffaq al-Dīn Abū Dharr, of Tripolitanian origin, then from Aleppo by birth and residence, a Shāfiʿī, father of Abū Bakr (mentioned later), and more famous by his kunya. He was born in Aleppo on the night of Friday, the ninth of Ṣafar, in the year 818 AH. He grew up there, memorized the Qurʾān, and perfected its recitation under his father. He studied al-Minhājayn al-Farʿī and al-Aṣlī, and the two Alfiyyas (of Ḥadīth and Naḥw) under his father. He presented his learning to al-ʿAlāʾ b. Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya and those lesser than him among his father's students. He studied fiqh under the two ʿAlāʾs — the aforementioned (Ibn Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya) and Ibn Maktūm al-Raḥabī — and under al-Shams al-Salāmī, from whom he benefited in fiqh and Arabic. He also acquired Arabic from Ibn al-Aʿzāzī, al-Shams al-Malṭī, and al-Zayn al-Kharazī, among others, and prosody (al-ʿArūḍ) from Ṣadaqa. He learned ḥadīth sciences from his father and our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and heard from them both and other shaykhs of his city and those who came to it. He entered Syria on his way to Hajj and heard there from Ibn Nāṣir al-Dīn, Ibn al-Ṭaḥḥān, Ibn al-Fakhr al-Miṣrī, and ʿĀʾisha bint Ibn al-Sharāʾiḥī, though he did not acquire much from them; most of his hearings were from his father. A group of scholars granted him ijāza at the request of our companion Ibn Fahd. In his youth, he engaged in literary arts, excelled in them, and compiled works in both poetry and prose, but he later destroyed them, as he told me at the end of his life. Among these works were ʿArūs al-Afrāḥ fīmā yuqāl fī al-Rāḥ (Bridal Feasts concerning what is said about Wine), ʿIqd al-Durar wa-l-Laʾāl fīmā yuqāl fī al-Silsāl (Necklace of Pearls and Jewels concerning what is said about Flowing Water), Sitr al-Ḥāl fīmā qīl fī al-Khāl (Covering the State concerning what is said about the Mole), al-Hilāl al-Mustanīr fī al-ʿAdhār al-Mustadīr (The Luminous Crescent concerning the Round Cheek-Whisker), and al-Badr idhā Istanār fīmā qīl fī al-ʿAdhār (The Full Moon when it Shines concerning the Cheek-Whisker). He also engaged in writing legal documents (shurūṭ) and excelled in them to the extent that he wrote decrees (tawqīʿ) at the gate of Ibn Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya. However, he later abandoned this as well and devoted himself to the study of ḥadīth and fiqh. He isolated the ambiguous parts (mubhamāt) of al-Bukhārī, as well as its grammar (iʿrāb), and compiled a fine commentary on it, summarizing it from al-Kirmānī, al-Birmāwī, and our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), as well as another shorter commentary. He also authored al-Tawḍīḥ li-l-Awhām al-Wāqiʿa fī al-Ṣaḥīḥ, Mubhamāt Muslim, Qurrat al-ʿAyn fī Faḍl al-Shaykhayn wa-l-Ṣihrayn wa-l-Sibṭayn, an incomplete commentary on al-Shifāʾ and al-Maṣābīḥ, and an appendix to Taʾrīkh Ibn Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya, among other works. He continuously recited the two Ṣaḥīḥs and al-Shifāʾ, especially after his father's death, and became advanced in their linguistic aspects, ambiguous points, and the authentication of their narrators, with hardly anything escaping his knowledge. When our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) was in Aleppo, he frequented Muwaffaq al-Dīn, and our shaykh was greatly pleased with him and loved him for his intelligence and lighthearted spirit, to the extent that he wrote about him in poetry: %~% Her gaze is languid, captivating, with seductive drowsy eyes %~% A slender spear, fresh and graceful, sways her body %~% %~% Your saliva is the water of life, O fragrant breath %~% Your green cheek-beard is my adornment, and you are my hope %~% My shaykh prefaced his writing of this by saying: “He was fond of composing mawāliyā poetry, and he described him as the Imām Muwaffaq al-Dīn.” Another time, he described him as “the brilliant, versatile, original, and dazzling litterateur, whose kunya matched his sincerity in expression, the expert who conversed with his namesake and sacrificed his soul for him, the last who surpassed the first in insight, freshness, and delight. May Allah grant the Muslims enjoyment of his continued existence, and permit him to teach ḥadīth, and benefit through him as He benefited through his father, and grant him the best of this world and the hereafter as he desires regarding permission to teach prophetic ḥadīth. His wish has been fulfilled, and his request granted. I have permitted him to teach ḥadīth sciences that he knows and has learned from the commentary on al-Alfiyya by our shaykh, the ḥāfiẓ of the age Abū al-Faḍl (Ibn Ḥajar), and from the benefits he acquired from his father, the ḥāfiẓ Burhān al-Dīn (may Allah cover him with His mercy), and from other sources he acquired through reading and benefited from reviewing, as well as other sciences of ḥadīth beyond the aforementioned commentary. He is permitted to teach any book on the meanings of ḥadīth that is read before him, and to record what he learns from it when he reads it or hears it. I ask him not to forget me in his righteous supplications in the gatherings of prophetic ḥadīth.” This is the end of his statement. I met him in Aleppo, and he listened to my recitation, and I listened to his recitation. Indeed, I wrote down some of his poetry, other than what has been mentioned, which I recorded elsewhere. His appreciation for me increased, and he exaggerated his praise both verbally and in writing. His letters thereafter continuously reached me, driven by affection, and some contained the description of “our shaykh.” He was a good, noble, and respected person in his region, isolated from worldly people, content with little, fond of seclusion, very humble and friendly towards strangers, and generous to them. He was intensely imaginative, free from affectation, possessed of complete virtue, excessive intelligence, and excellent recall, especially of what he had memorized. He was keen to preserve his father's books, rarely allowing anyone access to them. He completely cut off such access to everyone, so that some people of his town would not imagine special access to them. Sometimes, he would show them to trustworthy individuals in his presence. He suffered additional harm from some of his father's students, who spoke inappropriately about him and did not respect his father's legacy. However, this did not affect his standing. Al-Biqāʿī stated, “He possessed a great memory and a strong faculty for embellishing speech and delivering it in an elegant manner, along with sharp intellect, quick wit, and the ability to extract what was in his mind. He discussed many ambiguous matters and rare ḥadīth.” He also said, “There was affection and friendship between us.” He became engrossed in composing various poetic forms until he excelled in mawāliyā, reciting many of his compositions to me and quoting some. Elsewhere, he described him as “the brilliant and versatile litterateur.” He dedicated himself to transmitting and teaching ḥadīth, and many people from his city and those who visited benefited from him. He even wrote with older scholars in requests for ijāza during his father's lifetime and thereafter. He died on Thursday, the twenty-fifth of Dhū al-Qaʿda, in the year 884 AH, after experiencing some mental confusion and seclusion from people, and was buried next to his father. Al-Biqāʿī said that he fell ill at the end of 882 AH, then recovered, but experienced mental confusion and lost his sight. This continued until mid-884 AH, after which he recovered his sight and then died. I (al-Sakhāwī) said, “No one like him remained after him there. May Allah have mercy on him and us.”"@en .

rec:AIND-D00450 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00450-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00450-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00450-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Tomoaki_Shinoda,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00450 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن عبد الله بن عرب الشهاب أبو العباس اليماني الأصل الرومي الزاهد نزيل الشيخونية ويعرف بابن عرب أصله من اليمن ثم انتقل أبوه منها إلى بلاد الروم فسكنها وولد له صاحب الترجمة بها فنشأ بمدينة برصا فكان يقال له ابن عرب على عادة الروم والترك في تسميتهم من لم يكن منهم عربيا وكانت نشأته حسنة على قدم جيد ثم قدم وهو شاب القاهرة وتنزل في القاعة التي استجدها أكمل الدين صوفيا بالشيخونية وقرأ على إمامها خير الدين سليمان بن عبد الله وغيره ونسخ بالأجرة مدة واشتغل ثم انقطع عن الناس فلم يكن يجتمع بأحد بل اختار العزلة مع المواظبة على الجمعة والجماعات ويبكر إلى الجمعة بعد اغتساله لها بالماء البارد شتاء وصيفا ولا يكلم أحدا في ذهابه وإيابه ولا يجترئ أحد على الكلام معه لهيبته ووقاره وأمره في الورع والعبادة إلى الغاية وكان فيما بلغني يراجع الشمس البيجوري الشافعي نزيل الخانقاه الشيخونية فيما يشكل عليه فإذا أوضح له ما أشكل عليه فارقه ولم يكلمه بكلمة بعد ذلك ولذا قيل إنه شافعي المذهب ورأيت بخطى وصفه بالحنفي وما علمت مستندي فيه وكان مع ذلك يدري القراآت واقتصر على اللباس الحقير الزائد الخشونة ولذا يقنع باليسير من القوت وتوزع جدا بحيث أنه لم يكن يقبل من أحد شيئا ومتى علم أن أحدا من الباعة حاباه لكونه عرفه لم يعد إليه وللخوف من ذلك كان يتنكر ويشتري بعد العشاء قوت يومين أو ثلاثة وكان الناس يبيتون بالشيخونية رجاء رؤيته وأقام على هذه الطريقة أكثر من ثلاثين سنة وكراماته كثيرة وكان فريدا فيها لم يكن في عصره من يدانيه في طريقته قال العيني وثبت بالتواتر أنه أقام أكثر من عشرين سنة لا يشرب الماء أصلا وكان يقضي أيامه بالصيام ولياليه بالقيام مات في ليلة الأربعاء ثاني ربيع الأول سنة ثلاثين وتقدم العيني الناس في الصلاة عليه . قال شيخنا ومن عجائب أمره أنه لما مات كان الجمع في جنازته موفورا وأكثر الناس كانوا لا يعلمون بحاله ولا بسيرته فلما تسامعوا بموته هرعوا إليه ونزل السلطان من القلعة فصلى عليه بالرميلة وأعيد إلى الخانقاه فدفن بها بجوار أكمل الدين وحمل نعشه على الأصابع وتنافس الناس في شراء ثياب بدنه واشتروها بأغلى الأثمان فاتفق أن جملة ما اجتمع من ثمنها حسب فكان قدر ما تناوله من المعلوم من أول ما نزل بها إلى أن مات لا يزيد ولا ينقض وعد هذا من كراماته رحمه الله ونفعنا به . وممن ذكره المقريزي في عقوده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿArab, al-Shihāb Abū al-ʿAbbās, of Yemeni origin, al-Rūmī, the ascetic, resident of the Shaykhūniyya, known as Ibn ʿArab. His family origin was in Yemen; his father moved from there to the lands of Rūm (Anatolia) and settled there, and the subject of this notice was born to him there. He grew up in the city of Bursa and was called Ibn ʿArab according to the custom of the Rūmīs and Turks of so naming those living among them who were Arabs. His upbringing was good, on a sound footing. Then, while still a young man, he came to Cairo and took up residence as a Sufi in the hall (qāʿa) newly built by Akmal al-Dīn at the Shaykhūniyya. He studied recitation under its imam, Khayr al-Dīn Sulaymān b. ʿAbd Allāh, and others, copied manuscripts for hire for a time, and pursued his studies. Then he withdrew from people, meeting no one and choosing seclusion, while keeping strictly to the Friday and congregational prayers. He would go early to the Friday prayer after performing the major ablution with cold water, winter and summer alike; he spoke to no one on his way there and back, and no one dared address him because of his awe and dignity. His scrupulousness and devotion reached the utmost. I was told that he used to consult al-Shams al-Bījūrī al-Shāfiʿī, resident of the Shaykhūniyya khānqāh, on questions that perplexed him; once the difficulty was clarified he would depart and not speak another word to him. For this reason it was said that he was a Shāfiʿī in madhhab; yet I (al-Sakhāwī) once saw, in my own handwriting, a description of him as a Ḥanafī, and I do not know what my basis for it was. He also knew the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt). He confined himself to wretched, extremely coarse clothing and was content with little food. He was so scrupulous that he would accept nothing from anyone; if he learned that a vendor had favored him in price because he recognized him, he would never go back to him. For fear of this he would disguise himself and buy two or three days’ provisions after the evening prayer. People would spend the night at the Shaykhūniyya in the hope of catching sight of him. He maintained this way of life for more than thirty years. His miracles (karāmāt) were many and he was unique in them; no one in his age came near him in his path. Al-ʿAynī said that it was established by mass transmission (tawātur) that he spent more than twenty years without drinking water at all, passing his days in fasting and his nights in vigil. He died on the night of Wednesday, 2 Rabīʿ I 830, and al-ʿAynī led the people in the funeral prayer over him. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said: “Among the wonders of his affair is that when he died, the crowd at his funeral was immense, although most people had known nothing of his state or his conduct; when they heard of his death they hastened to him, and the sultan came down from the Citadel and prayed over him at al-Rumayla. He was returned to the khānqāh and buried there beside Akmal al-Dīn. His bier was carried on fingertips, and people competed to buy the clothes he had worn, paying the highest prices; and it so happened that the total raised from their sale, when reckoned, equalled — neither more nor less — the stipend he had drawn from the time he first took up residence there until his death. This was counted among his karāmāt.” May God have mercy on him and benefit us through him. Al-Maqrīzī was among those who mentioned him, in his ʿUqūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D00452 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00452-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00452-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00452 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن عيسى بن مطر بن علي بن عثمان شهاب الدين أبو القسم بن ضياء الدين أبي إسحاق بن جمال الدين أبي عبد الله بن عماد الدين ، ذكره ابن فهد وأنه أجاز لهم في سنة تسع عشرة ولم يزد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā b. Maṭar b. ʿAlī b. ʿUthmān, Shihāb al-Dīn Abū al-Qāsim, son of Ḍiyāʾ al-Dīn Abū Isḥāq b. Jamāl al-Dīn Abū ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿImād al-Dīn. Ibn Fahd mentioned him, stating that he (the subject) granted ijāza to them (unnamed students) in the year nineteen, without adding further details."@en .

rec:AIND-D00454 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00454-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00454-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00454 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد شهاب الدين العقيلي الحلبي ويعرف بابن العديم . مضى فيمن جده محمد عمر بن عبد العزيز ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad Shihāb al-Dīn al-ʿAqīlī al-Ḥalabī, known as Ibn al-ʿAdīm. He was mentioned in the entry of one whose grandfather is Muḥammad ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz."@en .

rec:AIND-D00457 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00457-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00457-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00457 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد المصري ويعرف بابن المؤذن سمع علي بمكة في المجاورة الثالثة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-Miṣrī, known as Ibn al-Muʾadhdhin. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca during his third period of jawāra (extended stay)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00458 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00458-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00458-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00458 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد اليماني الأصل الرومي البرصاوي ثم القاهري نزيل الشخيونية ويعرف بابن عرب ، مضى فيمن جده محمد بن عبد الله بن عرب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad, originally from Yemen, then from Rūm (Anatolia) and Bursa, then a resident of Cairo, settled in al-Shaykhūniyya, and was known as Ibn ʿArab. He is mentioned in the biography of those whose grandfather was Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿArab."@en .

rec:AIND-D00459 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00459-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00459-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00459 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن مخاطة سبط إبراهيم بن الجيعان والماضي أبوه . مات في حياة أبيه قبل إكماله العشرين في وترك طفلا اسمه كمال الدين محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Makhāṭa. Grandson of Ibrāhīm ibn al-Jīʿān. His father was mentioned previously. He died during his father's lifetime before completing his twentieth year, leaving behind a child named Kamāl al-Dīn Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D00460 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00460-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00460-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00460 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن معتوق أبو بكر الكردي الدمشقي الحنبلي ، مضى فيمن جده عبد الله وكان معتوق جده الأعلى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Maʿtūq, Abū Bakr al-Kurdī al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanbalī. He is mentioned among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd Allāh, and Maʿtūq was his paternal great-grandfather."@en .

rec:AIND-D00463 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00463-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00463-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00463-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00463-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00463 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن يوسف شهاب الدين الحلبي ثم الدمشقي الصالحي القطان بها أخو يوسف الآتي . سمع على أحمد بن إبراهيم بن يونس الأول من فوائد أبي عمرو بن مندة وعلى عبد الله بن خليل الحرستاني بعض الشمائل للترمذي وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء وكان قطانا بالصالحية . مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Yūsuf, Shihāb al-Dīn. Originally from Aleppo, he later resided in al-Ṣāliḥīya in Damascus, where he worked as a cotton merchant. He was the brother of Yūsuf (mentioned below). He received knowledge from Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Yūnus, transmitting the first volume of Abū ʿAmr b. Manda’s 『Fawāʾid』, and from ʿAbd Allāh b. Khalīl al-Ḥarastānī, transmitting part of al-Tirmidhī’s 『al-Shamāʾil』. He transmitted ḥadīth, and many scholars heard from him. He worked as a cotton merchant in al-Ṣāliḥīya. He passed away."@en .

rec:AIND-D00464 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00464-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00464-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00464 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن يوسف النويري أحد الخدام في ضريح الليث ممن سمع مني مناقبه لشيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Yūsuf al-Nuwayrī was one of the servants at the shrine of al-Layth, and among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) the virtues of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00465 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00465-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00465-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00465 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن الشيخ كريم الدين بن جلال الدين بن سيف الدين أبو السيادة الحسني الأودهي الهندي الحنفي لقيني بمكة في المجاورة الثانية فقرأ على البخاري ولازمني في أشياء بل كتب عني ما أمليته هناك وكتبت له إجازة حافلة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abū al-Siyāda Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. al-Shaykh Karīm al-Dīn b. Jalāl al-Dīn b. Sayf al-Dīn al-Ḥasanī al-Awdahī al-Hindī al-Ḥanafī. He met me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca during his second period of mujāwara. He read Sahih al-Bukhārī to me, accompanied me in various matters, and even wrote down what I dictated there. I also wrote a comprehensive ijāza for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00466 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00466-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00466-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00466 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم أبو العباس المناوي الشريف ممن أجمع على ولايته باليمن ، مات نحوا من سنة إحدى وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Manāwī al-Sharīf, one of those who were unanimously agreed upon for his governorship in Yemen. He died around the year 841 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00468 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00468-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00468-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00468 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم بن المحلى . مضى فيمن جده أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. al-Muḥallā. He was mentioned in the entry of those whose grandfather is Aḥmad (cross-reference to an earlier entry)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00470 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00470-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00470-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00470-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00470 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم الشهاب الحلبي الشاهد مات سنة خمس وعشرين أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Ḥalabī, the Notary. He died in the year 825. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00471 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00471-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00471-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00471 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم الحمصي الشافعي كتب على استدعاء بخطى أرسلته للديار الحلبية مؤرخ بسنة إحدى وخمسين ولكن ما علمته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm al-Ḥimṣī al-Shāfiʿī wrote on a petition in my (al-Sakhāwī's) handwriting, which I had sent to the regions of Aleppo, dated to the year 851. However, al-Sakhāwī noted that he had no personal knowledge of him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00472 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00472-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00472-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00472 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم السفطي ممن سمع مني في الأمالي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm al-Safaṭī was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the dictation sessions (al-Amālī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00473 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00473-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00473-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00473 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم العجمي الكيلاني المكي الخياط قريب ابن محمد . مات في صفر سنة ثمان وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Ibrāhīm al-ʿAjamī al-Kīlānī al-Makkī al-Khayyāṭ, a relative of Ibn Muḥammad. He died in Ṣafar of the year 778 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00474 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00474-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00474-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00474 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم القمصي كتبت بخطى أنه في معجمي وما رأيته فتراجع المسودة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm al-Qamṣī: I wrote in my own hand that he is in my biographical dictionary, but I did not see him, so refer to the draft. (Al-Sakhāwī's note)"@en .

rec:AIND-D00475 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00475-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00475-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00475-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00475 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم المدني المؤذن قرأ على الجمال الكازروني الموطأ في سنة عشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm al-Madanī al-Muʾadhdhin recited al-Muwaṭṭaʾ to al-Jamāl al-Kāzarūnī in the year 'ishrīn (twenty)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00476 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00476-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00476-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00476 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إبراهيم عالم بجاية ذكره ابن عزم هكذا وأنه مات بعد الأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm, a scholar of Bijāya. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him thus, and stated that he died after reaching his forties."@en .

rec:AIND-D00477 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00477-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00477-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00477 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الوهاب المرشدي المكي الماضي أبوه . مات في ذي القعدة سنة ثمان وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Ahmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Murshidī al-Makkī. His father is mentioned previously. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 828 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00478 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00478-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00478-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00478 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد الشمس أبو بكر بن أبي ذر بن الحافظ البرهان الحلبي وهو بكنيته أشهر يأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Ahmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-Shams Abū Bakr b. Abī Dharr b. al-Ḥāfiẓ al-Burhān al-Ḥalabī, more famous by his kunyah (Abū Bakr). To be mentioned later (cross-ref)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00479 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00479-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00479-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00479 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن أحمد بن حسن شاه بن بهمن شاه بن ظفر شاه بن شهاب الدين ملك كلبرجة وابن ملوكها . له ذكر في أبيه قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan Shāh b. Bahman Shāh b. Ẓafar Shāh b. Shihāb al-Dīn, king of Gulbarga and son of its kings. He is mentioned in his father’s entry nearby."@en .

rec:AIND-D00480 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00480-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00480-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00480 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن أحمد بن علي بن شرف بن عبد الظاهر الدلجي ويعرف بابن القاضي أحمد قرأ القرآن والتبريزي والملحة ولازم بأخرة خدمة بلديه الشهاب الدلجي وسمع مني في الإملاء . مات بدلجة في سنة إحدى وثمانين مطعونا ولم يكمل الأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Sharaf b. ʿAbd al-Ẓāhir al-Daljī, known as Ibn al-Qāḍī Aḥmad. He read the Qurʾān, al-Tibrīzī, and al-Milḥa. Late in life, he devoted himself to the service of his townsman al-Shihāb al-Daljī, and he heard dictations from me (al-Sakhāwī). He died in Dalja in the year 881 H, afflicted by the plague, not having completed forty years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D00481 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00481-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00481-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00481 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن سليمان أبو العباس بن أبي العباس بن الشيخ المسلك الزاهد صاحب الجامع الشهير بالمقس ويعرف كأبيه بابن الزاهد وهو سبط الشهاب الحسيني أمه خديجة الآتي كل منهم في محله . وسمع مني من ترجمة النووي تصنيفي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Sulaymān Abū al-ʿAbbās, son of Abū al-ʿAbbās, grandson of the pious ascetic shaykh who owned the famous mosque in al-Maqs. He was known, like his father, as Ibn al-Zāhid, and was the maternal grandson of al-Shihāb al-Ḥusaynī. His mother was Khadīja. Each of these individuals will be mentioned in their respective entries later. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) my composition, the Biography of al-Nawawī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00483 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00483-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00483-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00483-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00483-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00483-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_ruling,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00483 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن أحمد شهاب الدين الدمشقي أحد موقعي الحكم ويعرف بابن النشار قال شيخنا في أنبائه كان من أعيان الدماشقة حسن الخط والخطابة . مات في شهر رمضان سنة خمس عشرة وهو ممن وافق اسمه اسم أبيه وجده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Ahmad b. Ahmad Shihāb al-Dīn al-Dimashqī, one of the signatories of judgments, known as Ibn al-Nashshār. Our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) mentioned in his Anbāʾ that he was among the notables of Damascus, distinguished by his good calligraphy and eloquence. He died in the month of Ramaḍān in the year 815 H. He was among those whose name matched his father's and grandfather's names."@en .

rec:AIND-D00484 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00484-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00484-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00484 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن أحمد الشهاب الكازروني المدني الشافعي سمع على أبي الحسن علي بن سيف الأبياري في سنة ثلاث عشرة ابن ماجه وضبط الأسماء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Aḥmad, al-Shihāb al-Kāzarūnī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī. He heard 『Sunan Ibn Māja』 from Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī b. Sayf al-Abyārī in the year 813 H and precisely mastered the names (of transmitters)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00485 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00485-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00485-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00485-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00485 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد تمرباي شهاب الدين التمربغاوي الذي كان جده رأس نوبة النواب وتأمر على الحج في سنة أربع وأربعين . شاب حنفي اشتغل عند الكافياجي رفيقا لابن أبي زيد وهو الآن في الأحياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Ahmad Tamurbāy, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Tamurbaghāwī, whose grandfather was the head of the watch of the deputies and commanded the Hajj in 844 H. He was a young Hanafi man who worked for al-Kāfiyājī as a companion to Ibn Abī Zayd. He is currently alive."@en .

rec:AIND-D00486 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00486-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00486-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00486 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن جوغان بجيم ثم واو ومعجمة وآخره نون الشاذلي الواعظ نزيل مكة ممن ولي مشيخة الزمامية . ومات في ربيع الآخر سنة خمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Jawghān (spelled with jīm, then wāw, then a dotted letter, and ending in nūn), al-Shādhilī, the Preacher, a resident of Mecca, and one of those who held the office of mashyakhat al-Zamāmiyya. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 850."@en .

rec:AIND-D00488 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00488-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00488-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00488 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن حسن بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن الشهاب بن الإمام الأذرعي الأصل القاهري وأمه تركية فتاة أبيه . ولد في سنة إحدى وثلاثين وثمانمائة تقريبا وحفظ القرآن وتنزل في صوفية الباسطية وغيرها وابتني له بجوارها بيتا وحضر عندي في دروس البرقوقية وغيرها ونعم الرجل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-Shahāb, from the family of al-Imām al-Adhraʿī by origin, al-Qāhirī. His mother was a Turkish slave-girl of his father. He was born around 831 H. He memorized the Qurʾān, joined the Sufi community of al-Bāsiṭiyya and other places, and built a house for himself next to it. He attended my lessons (al-Sakhāwī's) at al-Barqūqiyya and other institutions, and he was an excellent man."@en .

rec:AIND-D00489 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00489-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00489-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00489-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00489 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن حسن الشهاب المسيري والد المحمدين الآتيين ويعرف بالفقيه ، كان فاضلا صالحا خيرا . مات تقريبا قريب الأربعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan al-Shihāb al-Misīrī, father of the two Muḥammads who will be mentioned later, and known as al-Faqīh (the jurist). He was a virtuous, pious, and good man. May God have mercy on him, he died around the age of forty."@en .

rec:AIND-D00490 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00490-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00490-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00490 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن سنان بن عبد الله بن عمر ومسعود العمري المكي العابد مات سنة خمس وأربعين بالغد خارج مكة من ضرب اليمن ودفن به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Sinān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar wa Masʿūd al-ʿUmarī al-Makkī, the worshipper. He died in 845 H at al-Ghad outside Makka due to a strike/attack related to Yemen, and was buried there."@en .

rec:AIND-D00498 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00498-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00498-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00498-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00498 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن الفخر عثمان الغزولي ويلقب طبيخ . مات في ليلة الثلاثاء ثاني صفر في سنة اثنتين وتسعين وكان مثريا بعد فاقة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Fakhr ʿUthmān al-Ghazzūlī, nicknamed Ṭabīkh. He died on the night of Tuesday, the 2nd of Ṣafar, in the year 892. He was wealthy after a period of poverty."@en .

rec:AIND-D00502 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00502-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00502-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00502-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00502 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن بهاء الدين أحمد بن علي بن محمد بن سليمان الأنصاري التتائي الأصل الآتي أبوه . مات في يوم الأربعاء ثامن عشري جمادى الآخرة سنة ثمان وستين بمكة ، أرخه ابن فهد وكأنه ولد بعد أبيه فسمي باسمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Bahāʾ al-Dīn Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Sulaymān al-Anṣārī al-Tatāʾī al-Aṣl. His father is mentioned later. He died on Wednesday, the 28th of Jumādā al-Ākhira in 868 AH in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date. It seems he was born after his father and named after him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00503 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00503-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00503-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00503-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00503 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن علي الدمياطي علي إمام قاعة السلاح المنسوبة للشيخ عبد الرحمن العجمي ، سمع مني في الإملاء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Dimyāṭī, the Imām of the Qāʿat al-Silāḥ (armoury) attributed to Shaykh ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-ʿAjamī. He heard (texts) by dictation (imlāʾ) from me (al-Sakhāwī). (The source reads \"al-Dimyāṭī ʿAlī imām\"; \"ʿAlī\" appears to be a dittographic scribal error and is left untranslated.)"@en .

rec:AIND-D00504 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00504-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00504-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00504 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن عمر بن حسين الزفتاوي الأصل المقسي الآتي أبوه . وعمه عبد القادر . قرأ علي في التقريب للنووي وسمع على غير ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Ḥusayn, originally from Zaftā and residing in al-Maqs. His father will be mentioned below, and his paternal uncle is ʿAbd al-Qādir. He read to me (al-Sakhāwī) from al-Nawawī's 『al-Taqrīb』 and heard other works (from others)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00507 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00507-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00507-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00507 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن غنائم البعلي المدني . مضى فيمن جده علبك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Ghanāʾim al-Baʿlī al-Madanī. He was previously mentioned under the entry of those whose grandfather is ʿUlbak."@en .

rec:AIND-D00508 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00508-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00508-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00508 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد شاه بن أحمد شاه بن فند وكاش المظفر شهاب الدين ملك بنجالة وجدته بخطي في سنة تسع وثلاثين من حاشية الأنباء ، وقد مضى أحمد بن أحمد بن حسن بن بهمز صاحب كلبرجة فيحرر أمرهما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad Shāh b. Aḥmad Shāh b. Fund wa Kāsh, al-Muẓaffar Shihāb al-Dīn, King of Bengal. I (al-Sakhāwī) found this in my own handwriting in the year 839 H on the margin of 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』 (TMP-T-00034). Reference to Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. Bahmaz, the ruler of Kalbargā, has already been made (cross-ref to an earlier entry); so their matters should be clarified."@en .

rec:AIND-D00509 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00509-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00509-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00509 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن أبي اليمن محمد بن أحمد بن الرضي إبراهيم بن محمد بن إبراهيم الطبري المكي وأمه زينب ابنة عبد الله بن الزين أحمد بن الجمال محمد بن المحب الطبري . سمع من الزين المراغي في سنة أربع عشرة وثمانمائة وأجاز له قبل ذلك في سنة خمس ما بعدها جده والزين العراقي والهيثمي وآخرون . مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Abī al-Yaman Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Raḍī Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm al-Ṭabarī al-Makkī. His mother was Zaynab, daughter of ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Zayn Aḥmad b. al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. al-Muḥibb al-Ṭabarī. He heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī in the year 814 H. Before that, in the year 805 H, he was granted ijāza by his grandfather, al-Zayn al-ʿIrāqī, al-Haythamī, and others. He died."@en .

rec:AIND-D00511 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00511-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00511-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00511-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00511-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00511 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن الزين أحمد بن الجمال محمد بن المحب أحمد بن عبد الله أبو الطاهر الطبري المكي وأمه عائشة ابنة سعيد النويري . ولد تقريبا سنة سبع وثمانمائة وأحضر في الرابعة على أبيه والجمال بن ظهيرة وآخرين وأجاز له أبو عبد الله الوانوغى وابن سلامة وغيرهما . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة سبع وعشرين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abū al-Ṭāhir Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. al-Zayn Aḥmad b. al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. al-Muḥibb Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṭabarī al-Makkī. His mother was ʿĀʾisha, daughter of Saʿīd al-Nuwayrī. He was born approximately in 807 AH, and at the age of four, he attended lessons under his father and al-Jamāl b. Ẓuhayra, among others. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Wānūghī and Ibn Salāma, among others, granted him ijāza. He died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ākhira 827 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00512 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00512-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00512-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00512 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد سبط الجاي . يأتي بدون أحمد بن محمد الثاني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad sibṭ al-Jāy. He will be mentioned later without the second Aḥmad b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D00515 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00515-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00515-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00515-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00515 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن أبي بكر بن أيوب بن درباس . مضى بدون محمد في نسبه ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00521 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00521-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00521-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00521 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن محمد المناوي ونسبه لمنية أبي عبد الله بالشرقية الشافعي ويعرف بابن المؤدب صحب الزين الحافي وناصر الدين الطبناوي وزوج الطبناوي ابنه بابنته ، وكان صالحا جلس لتعليم الأبناء ببلده . ومات في آخر سنة ست وخمسين أو أول التي تليها وممن قرأ عنده نور الدين السروي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Manāwī, his nisbah is to Munyat Abī ʿAbd Allāh in al-Sharqiyya. A Shafi'i jurist, known as Ibn al-Muʾaddib. He accompanied al-Zayn al-Ḥāfī and Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Ṭabnāwī. Al-Ṭabnāwī married his son to the subject's daughter. He was a righteous man who sat to teach children in his hometown. He died at the end of the year 856 or the beginning of the one after it. Among those who studied with him was Nūr al-Dīn al-Sarawī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00522 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00522-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00522-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00522-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00522 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن محمد شهاب الدين الطولوني كبير المهندسين . مضى قريبا فيمن جده محمد بن علي بن عبد الله بن علي ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00524 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00524-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00524-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00524-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00524 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن موسى بن إبراهيم بن طرخان الشهاب أبو العباس ابن الشهاب بن الضياء الآتي أبوه وهو بكنيته أشهر . تكسب بالشهادة كسلفه ثم استنابه العز الكناني في العقود والفسوخ ثم في القضاء . ومات في ربيع الأول سنة سبع وستين وأظنه جاز السبعين أو زاحمها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. Ibrāhīm b. Ṭarkhān, al-Shihāb Abū al-ʿAbbās, known as Ibn al-Shihāb b. al-Ḍiyāʾ (his father al-Ḍiyāʾ will be mentioned later). He was more famous by his kunya. He earned a living by bearing witness, like his predecessor. Then al-ʿIzz al-Kinānī appointed him as his deputy for contracts and annulments, and subsequently to the judiciary. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal 867 H. I believe he was over seventy years of age, or very close to it."@en .

rec:AIND-D00526 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00526-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00526-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00526 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن يلبغا ويعرف بابن المرضعة . مات في جمادى الثانية سنة خمس وتسعين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Yalbughā, known as Ibn al-Murḍiʿa. He died in Jumādā al-Thāniya in the year 895 H. May Allah forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00527 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00527-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00527-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00527 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد بن عليبة ابن عم البدر وعبد القادر ممن كان في خدمتهما حتى ماتا ورسم عليه ثم أودع المقشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. ʿUlayba, a cousin of al-Badr and ʿAbd al-Qādir. He was among those who served them until their deaths. He was then formally indicted and imprisoned in al-Muqashshira."@en .

rec:AIND-D00529 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00529-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00529-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00529-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00529-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00529-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_ruling,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00529 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد شهاب الدين بن العلامة شهاب الدين الصعيدي القدسي الحنقي ويلقب بالسوداني . كان أبوه من الصعيد فقدم القدس وتكسب بالشهادة مع الفضل وولد له هذا وغيره وصار صاحب الترجمة شيخ المقادسة ومعيد المعظمية . ومات سنة اثنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad Shihāb al-Dīn al-Ṣaʿīdī al-Qudsī al-Ḥanafī (the source spells it al-Ḥanqī, a scribal error for al-Ḥanafī), nicknamed al-Sūdānī. His father came from al-Ṣaʿīd, then settled in Jerusalem and earned a living through testifying, with distinction (maʿa al-faḍl). This one (the subject of the biography) and others were born to him. The subject became the shaykh of the Jerusalemites (al-Maqādisa) and a repetitor (muʿīd) at al-Muʿaẓẓamiyya. He died in the year 802."@en .

rec:AIND-D00530 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00530-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00530-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00530-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00530 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد الحنبلي بن الضياء ، مضى فيمن اسم جده أحمد بن موسى بن إبراهيم ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00531 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00531-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00531-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00531 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد الزهوري . فيمن جده عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad al-Zuhrī. He is mentioned among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D00532 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00532-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00532-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00532-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00532 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أحمد العمري نسبة لذوي عمر أحد القواد . مات في يوم السبت تاسع عشري ربيع الآخر سنة خمس وأربعين بالغد خارج مكة من صوب اليمن ودفن به ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Aḥmad al-ʿUmarī, named al-ʿUmarī due to Dhawī ʿUmar, one of the commanders. He died on Saturday, the twenty-ninth of Rabīʿ al-Ākhir, in the year 845, the next day, outside Mecca from the direction of Yemen, and was buried there. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00535 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00535-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00535-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00535-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00535 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي أحمد شهاب الدين المغراوي المالكي . يأتي في ابن محمد بن عبد الله ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00537 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00537-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00537-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00537 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أرسلان الرملي هو ابن الحسين بن الحسن بن على . يأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Arslān al-Ramlī. He is the son of al-Ḥusayn b. al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī. [His biography] will follow."@en .

rec:AIND-D00543 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00543-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00543-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00543 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن عجيل الأمين اليماني والد إبراهيم الماضي . من بيت شهير . مات في سنة أربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAjīl, known as al-Amīn al-Yamānī. Father of the aforementioned Ibrāhīm. He came from a famous house. He died in the year 40 (presumably 840 H.)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00551 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00551-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00551-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00551 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إسماعيل بن عبد الله الدمشقي . سمع علي بمكة في المجاورة الثالثة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Dimashqī. He heard from ʿAlī in Makka during his third sojourn (mujāwara)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00553 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00553-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00553-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00553-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00553 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إسماعيل بن علي بن محمد بن داود بن شمس الزمزمي ويقال له نابت وهو به أشهر . يأتي في النون ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Dāwūd b. Shams al-Zamzamī. He is also called Nābit, and by that, he is more famous. He will appear in the Nūn section."@en .

rec:AIND-D00554 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00554-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00554-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00554-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00554 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إسماعيل بن عمر بن صالح الفرنوي . مات سنة سبعين وثمانمائة ، أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿUmar b. Ṣāliḥ al-Farnawī. He died in the year 870 H. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D00556 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00556-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00556-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00556-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00556 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إسماعيل بن محمد بن أحمد الشهاب الونائي القاهري الشافعي أخو الشمس الآتي بلغني عن شيخنا ابن خضر أنه كان يقول هو أقعد من أخيه غير أنه كان ساكنا انتهى . وهو ممن حضر عند شيخنا وسمعت أنه قرأ على القاياتي وربما أقرأ وتأخرت وفاته عن أخيه وله ولد في الأحياء فيحقق أمره منه إن كان يحسن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Wanāʾī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī. He had a brother, al-Shams (forthcoming). Our shaykh, Ibn Khiḍr, used to say about him, 'He was more settled in his studies than his brother.' He was among those who attended lessons with our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar). I heard that he read to al-Qāyātī and perhaps even taught others. His death occurred later than his brother's. He has a son who is alive, from whom his affairs can be verified, if he is knowledgeable."@en .

rec:AIND-D00558 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00558-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00558-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00558-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00558-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00558-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00558 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إسماعيل بن ملك بن غازي سلطان دهلك . أرخه ابن عزم في سنة إحدى وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. Malik b. Ghāzī, Sulṭān of Dahlak. Ibn ʿAzm dated him (or his entry) to the year 51 (century unspecified, likely 851 AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00559 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00559-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00559-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00559 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إسماعيل بن يوسف بن عمر بن عبد العزيز الهواري البنداري أخو مونس الآتي من رؤوس عرب هوارة ، ويسمى فيهم بالأمير أحضره الدوادار الكبير معه فعلق رأسه في جماعة بباب زويلة وهم أحياء إلى أن مات وذلك في جمادى الآخرة سنة ثلاث وثمانين وتوجع الناس من مشاهدته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. Yūsuf b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Hawārī al-Bandārī, brother of Mūnis (who will be mentioned later). He was one of the leaders of the Hawāra Arabs and was called \"the Amīr\" among them. The Great Dawādār brought him, and his head was hung at Bāb Zuwayla along with a group of people while they were alive until he died, in Jumādā al-Ākhira 883 H. People were distressed by witnessing this."@en .

rec:AIND-D00565 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00565-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00565-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00565-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00565 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إينال الأمير شهاب الدين بن الأمير أحد خواص الظاهر وجهه وصحبته أربعون مملوكا لقتال بلى من عرب الحجاز ثم عاد ومعه جماعة سمروا ثم وسطوا في سنة ثلاث وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Inal, al-Amir Shihab al-Din, b. al-Amir. He was one of the intimates (khawāṣṣ) of al-Ẓāhir (Jaqmaq), who dispatched him with forty Mamluks to fight the Bali tribe of the Arabs of the Hijaz. He then returned; the group accompanying him were nailed and then cut in half (wussiṭū), in the year 843 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00566 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00566-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00566-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00566-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00566-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00566-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D00566-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00566 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن إينال شهاب الدين الحنفي خادم الشيخونية وسحنتها ووالد أحد فضلاء الحنفية الشمس محمد . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وثمانين واستقر عوضه في الخدمة أبو الطيب السيوطي ولم يلتفت لولده وعز ذلك على كثيرين وإن كان المستقر أضبط وأمتن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Īnāl, Shihāb al-Dīn, the Ḥanafī, who served as an attendant of al-Shaykhūniyya and its precinct, and was the father of one of the distinguished Ḥanafī scholars, al-Shams Muḥammad. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 882 H. Abū al-Ṭayyib al-Suyūṭī was appointed in his place in service, and his son was not considered for the position. This was regrettable for many, even though the appointee was more precise and capable."@en .

rec:AIND-D00567 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00567-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00567-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00567-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00567 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أيوب بن أحمد بن عبد الله بن عفان بن رمضان الفيومي الأصل أخو أبي بكر وعمر وعثمان . مات بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة أربع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ayyūb b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAffān b. Ramaḍān, originally from al-Fayyūm, brother of Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 844 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00570 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00570-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00570-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00570 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن بردبك سبط الأشرف إينال وأخو محمد الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Bardbak, grandson of al-Ashraf Īnāl, and brother of Muḥammad (forthcoming)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00572 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00572-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00572-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00572-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00572 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن بركات بن محمد بن محرز الجزائري . مات سنة ست وستين أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Barakat b. Muḥammad b. Muḥriz al-Jazāʾirī. He died in the year 866 (AH). Ibn ʿAzm dated his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00573 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00573-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00573-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00573 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بركة الشهاب الدمشقي كتب عنه البدري في مجموعه قوله : %~% مليح يغيب البدر عند حضوره %~% ويخجل غصن البان بالقد إن خطر %~% %~% له شامة فوق الجبين كأنها %~% قليل سواد الغيم في طلعة القمر %~% وقوله : %~% له خال بخط المسك قدرا %~% على كرسي الخدود قد تعلى %~% %~% كشجر قد غدا في روض ورد %~% وسالفة تمد عليه ظلا %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad Baraka al-Shihāb al-Dimashqī. Al-Badrī wrote about him in his collection, stating: 'Beautiful, the full moon hides at his presence, and the bān tree branch blushes at his graceful stature. He has a mole above his forehead, as if it were a little dark cloud on the rising moon.' And he also stated: 'He has a mole, as if drawn with a line of musk, high on the throne of his cheeks. It is like a tree standing in a rose garden, casting a shadow upon his sideburns.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D00574 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00574-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00574-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00574-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00574 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن بلبان بن عبد الله الشهاب أبو العباس القمري اللؤلؤي الدمشقي الحنبلي ، وصفه البرهان الحلبي بالمحدث المقرئ وأنه يحفظ القرآن ويستحضر كتابه في مذهب أحمد وأنه قرا الحديث بصوت حسن وأنه قدم عليه في سنة تسع وثلاثين فقرأ عليه ابن ماجه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Balabān b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Shihāb Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qamarī al-Luʾluʾī al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanbalī. Al-Burhān al-Ḥalabī described him as a muḥaddith (hadith scholar) and muqriʾ (Qurʾān reciter), stating that he memorized the Qurʾān and retained his book on the Aḥmadī (Ḥanbalī) madhhab, and that he recited ḥadīth with a beautiful voice. He (the subject) visited al-Burhān al-Ḥalabī in the year 839 H and read Ibn Mājah to him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00575 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00575-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00575-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00575 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن إبراهيم بن محمد الحكمي من ذرية الشيخ محمد بن أبي بكر الحكمي . ذكره العفيف مختصرا ولم يؤرخه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-Ḥakamī, from the progeny of Shaykh Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-Ḥakamī. Al-ʿAfīf mentioned him briefly but did not provide dates for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00576 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00576-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00576-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00576 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن أحمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة المكي الآتي جده قريبا ، ممن أخذ عني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓuhayra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭīya b. Ẓuhayra al-Makkī. His grandfather will be mentioned shortly. He was among those who studied under me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00577 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00577-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00577-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00577-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00577 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن أحمد بن التقي سليمان بن حمزة بن أحمد بن عمر بن الشيخ أبي عمر المقدسي الحنبلي . سمع من أبي محمد بن القيم جزءا من حديث أبي القسم المنبجي أنابه الفخر عن محمود بن أحمد عنه . ذكره شيخنا في معجمه وقال أجاز لي ، وبيض لوفاته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Aḥmad b. al-Taqī Sulaymān b. Ḥamza b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. al-Shaykh Abī ʿUmar al-Maqdisī al-Ḥanbalī. He heard a part of the ḥadīth of Abū al-Qāsim al-Manbijī from Abū Muḥammad b. al-Qayyim, which al-Fakhr received from Maḥmūd b. Aḥmad on his (Abū Muḥammad's) behalf. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his lexicon and stated that he granted him ijāza, leaving his death date blank."@en .

rec:AIND-D00581 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00581-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00581-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00581 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن أحمد بن يحيى العامري الحرضي اليماني . ممن أخذ عني بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة أربع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Aḥmad b. Yaḥyā al-ʿĀmirī al-Ḥaraḍī al-Yamānī. Among those who learned from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 894 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00586 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00586-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00586-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00586-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00586 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن إسماعيل الفقيه أبو العباس الدنكلي اليماني الشافعي . اشتغل بالعلم وتفقه وبرع قال الأهدل في تاريخ فقيه محقق ولي قضاء المحالب واجتمعت به ثم ترك القضاء زهدا فيه وسمعت بوفاته سنة ثمان وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Ismāʿīl, the jurist, Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Dankalī, al-Yamānī, al-Shāfiʿī. He devoted himself to knowledge, studied fiqh, and excelled. al-Ahdal stated in his history that he was a diligent, verifying jurist who held the judgeship of al-Maḥālib and that he (al-Ahdal) had met him; the subject later relinquished the judgeship out of asceticism. al-Ahdal heard of his death in the year 838 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00587 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00587-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00587-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00587-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00587-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00587 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن الحسين بن عمر أبو النصر بن الزين المراغي المدني الشافعي أخو شيخنا أبي الفتح محمد وذاك الأكبر ظنا ، سمع معه على أبيه والعلم سليمان بن أحمد السقا والعراقي والهيثمي وابن حاتم وغيرهم وبعض ذلك في سنة إحدى وتسعين وسبعمائة وفي ظني أن وفاته في هذا القرن فيحرر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. al-Ḥusayn b. ʿUmar, Abū al-Naṣr, b. al-Zayn al-Marāghī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī, was the brother of our shaykh Abū al-Fatḥ Muḥammad (al-Marāghī), who is presumed to be the elder. He heard, together with his brother, from his father (al-Zayn al-Marāghī), al-ʿAlam Sulaymān b. Aḥmad al-Saqqā, al-ʿIrāqī, al-Haythamī, Ibn Ḥātim, and others. Some of this occurred in the year 791 AH. In my opinion, his death occurred in this century, but this requires verification."@en .

rec:AIND-D00590 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00590-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00590-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00590 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن سراج البابي . فيمن جده علي بن سراج ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00592 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00592-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00592-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00592-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00592 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن طباجوا البعلي الخباز أبوه العطار هو . سمع في سنة تسعين وسبعمائة ببلده عن محمد بن علي اليوتيني ومحمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم الحسيني ومحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الجردي الصحيح قالوا أنابه الحجار ، وحدث أخذ عنه بعض أصحابنا وما لقيته في الرحلة وكأنه مات قبلها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Ṭabājūwā al-Baʿlī al-Khabbāz; his father was al-ʿAṭṭār (the perfumer). He heard in 790 H in his hometown from Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Yūtinī, Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm al-Ḥusaynī, and Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Jardī (reciting) al-Ṣaḥīḥ. They said that al-Ḥajjār had deputized him. He transmitted (ḥadīth), and some of our companions took from him. I (al-Sakhāwī) did not meet him on the journey, and it seems he died before it."@en .

rec:AIND-D00594 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00594-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00594-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00594 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الزكي أبي بكر بن عبد الرحمن المصري أخو إبراهيم وعلي وعمر ، ممن أخذ عني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Zakī Abū Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Miṣrī, brother of Ibrāhīm, ʿAlī, and ʿUmar. He was among those who studied under me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00597 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00597-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00597-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00597 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الفخر أبي بكر بن عبد الله القرشي المكي الشاهد أبوه ممن أخذ عني بمكة وأهلها وكثير منهم ينازعون فيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Fakhr Abū Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Qurashī al-Makkī. His father was a witness among those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca and its people, and many of them dispute concerning him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00598 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00598-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00598-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00598 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الملك بن أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن حسين بن التاج علي القسطلاني المصري القباني عم صاحبنا الشهاب الآتي ، ولد سنة ثلاثين وثمانمائة . ممن سمع مني بمكة وكان ممن قرأ القرآن وتكسب بالقبان وجاور بعد الثمانين . مات في سنة أربع وتسعين عن بضع وسبعين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Malik b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn b. al-Tāj ʿAlī al-Qasṭalānī al-Miṣrī al-Qabbānī, the paternal uncle of our sahib al-Shihāb (who will be mentioned later), was born in 830 H. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca. He was one of those who recited the Qurʾān, earned his living as a weigh-man, and resided in Mecca after the eighties. He died in 894 H at approximately over seventy years old."@en .

rec:AIND-D00599 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00599-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00599-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00599 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الوهاب بن أحمد الشهاب المحلى أخو محمد الآتي . تكسب بالشهادة وناب في القضاء وعمل أمانة الحكم بها مدة وكان حسن الخط خيرا يقرأ القرآن ويجيد الصناعة . مات بعد الخمسين قبل أخيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Maḥallī, brother of Muḥammad, who will be mentioned later. He earned his living through witnessing/notarizing, served as a deputy judge, and acted as a trustee of judgment for a period. He had beautiful handwriting, was a good person, recited the Qur'an, and was skilled in craft. He died after the age of fifty, before his brother."@en .

rec:AIND-D00603 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00603-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00603-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00603-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00603 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن علي شهاب الدين السيوطي أخو الشريف محمد الآتي أثبته الولي العراقي في سامعي إملائه سنة إحدى عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Suyūṭī. Brother of al-Sharīf Muḥammad (to be mentioned later). Al-Walī al-ʿIrāqī attested to him in his dictation session for listeners in the year 11 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00604 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00604-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00604-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00604-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00604 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن علي الطهطاوي المكي أخو عبد الكريم الآتي . ممن سمع علي بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī al-Ṭahṭāwī al-Makkī. Brother of ʿAbd al-Karīm (= AIND-D04251, forthcoming). He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00605 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00605-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00605-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00605 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن علي الكيلاني بن خواجا . يأتي فيمن لم يسم أبوه من أواخر الأحمدين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī al-Kīlānī b. Khawājā. He will appear in the section of those whose fathers are not named, among the last of the Aḥmads."@en .

rec:AIND-D00607 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00607-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00607-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00607-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00607 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن عمر ويعرف جده بابن العريض . ذكره ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿUmar. His grandfather is known as Ibn al-ʿArīḍ. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00608 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00608-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00608-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00608 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن أحمد بن سليمان بن حمزة بن أحمد بن عمر ابن الشيخ أبي عمر . مضى بدون محمد في نسبه وكأنه زيادة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Sulaymān b. Ḥamza b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmar, the son of Shaykh Abū ʿUmar. (The name) Muḥammad was missing from his lineage previously, as if it were an addition."@en .

rec:AIND-D00610 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00610-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00610-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00610-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00610 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن علي بن محمد بن أبي بكر الناشري الآتي أبوه وجده وحج مع أبيه وجاور سنتين ولازمني في السماع هناك فيهما حين المجاورة الثالثة بعد الثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-Nāshirī. His father and grandfather (forthcoming) performed Hajj with him and resided in Mecca for two years. He also accompanied me (al-Sakhāwī) in listening (to lectures) there during those two years, specifically during his third residency in Mecca after the eighties (880s AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00611 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00611-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00611-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00611-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00611 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن الرداد الزبيدي اليماني . يأتي في ابن أبي بكر ابن محمد إذ الرداد ليس اسم أب له بل هو لقب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. al-Raddād al-Zabīdī al-Yamānī. He will be mentioned under Ibn Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad, as al-Raddād is not his father's name but a laqab."@en .

rec:AIND-D00612 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00612-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00612-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00612-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00612 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن عثمان بن أحمد بن عمر بن سلامة المارديني الحلبي الحنفي . ولد سنة سبعين هكذا رأيته بخطى في الأحمدين وهو غلط صوابه الحسن وهو أخو البدر محمد وسيأتي كل منهما ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00614 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00614-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00614-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00614-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00614 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن علي الشهاب المسوقي الواداني المغربي الأصل المدني المولد والمقيم بها وبمكة ثم انقطع بالمدينة وكان ممن سمع علي بها وقد دخل القاهرة مرارا ولديه جرأة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shihāb al-Masūqī al-Wādānī, son of Abū Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī. He was originally from the Maghrib, born in Medina, and resided there and in Mecca. Later, he secluded himself in Medina. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) there in Medina. He visited Cairo several times. He possessed courage."@en .

rec:AIND-D00619 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00619-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00619-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00619-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00619-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00619 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن الشمس محمد فخر الدين اللاري الهناجي وهي قرية من لار الشافعي لقيني بمكة في مجاورتي الثالثة فلازمني في سماع أشياء رواية ودراية وكتبت له ووصفته بالشيخ الصالح المحصل المجيد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. al-Shams Muḥammad Fakhr al-Dīn al-Lārī al-Hanājī, from al-Hanāj, a village in Lār. A Shafi'i jurist. He met me in Mecca during my third extended stay (mujāwara). He remained with me, listening to various transmissions and studies. I also wrote for him, and I described him as a righteous, accomplished, and excellent shaykh."@en .

rec:AIND-D00621 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00621-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00621-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00621-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00621 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن محمود بن محمد الدمنهوري القاهري . سمع مع أبيه على الصلاح الزفتاوي والحلاوي والسويداوي والأبناسي والغماري وابن الشيخة والمراغي ختم البخاري . ذكره البقاعي وما لقيته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Maḥmūd b. Muḥammad al-Damanhūrī al-Qāhirī. He heard the completion of al-Bukhārī's work with his father from al-Ṣalāḥ al-Zaftāwī, al-Ḥalāwī, al-Suwaydāwī, al-Abnāsī, al-Ghumārī, Ibn al-Shaykha, and al-Marāghī. Al-Biqāʿī mentioned him, but I (al-Sakhāwī) did not meet him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00626 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00626-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00626-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00626 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن الديوان . يأتي في آخر الأحمدين فيمن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. al-Dīwān. He will appear at the end of the Aḥmads, among those whose father's name is not mentioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D00627 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00627-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00627-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00627 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر بن شمس الدين اللاري . فيمن جده محمد قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Shams al-Dīn al-Lārī. Among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad, forthcoming."@en .

rec:AIND-D00629 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00629-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00629-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00629-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00629-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00629 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر أبو العباس المكدي الزيلعي العالم الفقيه . تفقه بالشهاب أحمد بن أبي بكر الناشري وبرع في الفرائض والحساب . مات في سنة ست أو سبع وثلاثين . ذكره العفيف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Makkī al-Zaylaʿī, the learned jurist. He studied fiqh under al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr al-Nāshirī and excelled in inheritance law and arithmetic. He died in the year 836 or 837 AH. Al-ʿAfīf mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00630 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00630-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00630 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر الرهبي قاضي أ ب . مات في سنة خمس وعشرين . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr al-Rahbī, the qāḍī of 'Ab'. He died in the year 825 AH. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D00631 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00631-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00631-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00631 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي بكر العبادي الحنفي . فيمن جده محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr al-ʿAbbādī al-Ḥanafī, whose grandfather is Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D00635 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00635-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00635-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00635-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00635-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00635 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن جاحق المؤيدي جارنا وسبط أخت جهة شيخنا أمه الشريفة سمع على شيخنا وجهته وتكسب بحانوت في الباسطية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Jāḥiq al-Muʾayyadī, our neighbor and the maternal grand-nephew of al-Sakhāwī's shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī). His mother was al-Sharīfa. He received learning from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and earned a living from a shop in al-Bāsiṭiyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D00638 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00638-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00638-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00638 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن جار الله المكي البناء الشهير بالحمة . مات بها في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Jār Allāh al-Makkī, known as al-Bannāʾ and famous by al-Ḥimma. He died there (al-Ḥimma) in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir 882 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00638a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00638a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00638a ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن جانبك كوهيه الآتي أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Jānbak Kūhīya. His father is mentioned below."@en .

rec:AIND-D00639 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00639-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00639-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00639-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00639 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن جبريل الخليلي المؤذن سمع الميدومي وحدث عنه مع جماعة في سنة أربع وثمانمائة بنسخة إبراهيم بن سعد سمعها منهم التقي أبو بكر القلقشندي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Jibrīl al-Khalīlī, the muezzin, heard from al-Maydūmī. In 804 H, he transmitted from him (al-Maydūmī) the text of Ibrāhīm b. Saʿd, which al-Taqī Abū Bakr al-Qalqashandī also heard from them (i.e., Aḥmad and the group)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00640 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00640-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00640-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00640 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن جعفر بن التاج عبد الوهاب النابلسي الحنبلي سبط البدر بن عبد القادر . ممن أخذ عني مع خاله الكمال وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Jaʿfar b. al-Tāj ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Nābulusī al-Ḥanbalī, the grandson of al-Badr b. ʿAbd al-Qādir. He was among those who acquired knowledge from our shaykh (al-Sakhāwī) and his maternal uncle al-Kamāl, among others."@en .

rec:AIND-D00641 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00641-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00641 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الظاهر أبي سعيد جقمق أمه خوندشاه زاده ابنة عثمان متملك الروم . مات بالطاعون في يوم الأربعاء مستهل صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين عن سبع سنين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Ẓāhir Abī Saʿīd Jaqmaq. His mother was Khawandshāh Zāda, daughter of ʿUthmān, ruler of Rūm. He died of the plague on Wednesday, the first of Ṣafar, in the year 853 AH, at the age of seven."@en .

rec:AIND-D00642 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00642-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00642-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00642 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن جلبان بن أبي سويد بن أبي دعيج بن أبي نمي الشريف الحسني . مات في ليلة الأربعاء سادس عشري المحرم سنة اثنتين وستين بخيف بني شديد وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بها . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Jilbān b. Abī Suwayd b. Abī Duʿayj b. Abī Numay, al-Sharīf al-Ḥasanī. He died on the night of Wednesday, the 26th of Muharram in the year 862 AH, in Khayf Banī Shadīd, and was transported to Mecca where he was buried. Ibn Fahd recorded this."@en .

rec:AIND-D00652 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00652-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00652-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00652 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسن بن أحمد بن محمد بن فليتة الجدي الأصل المكي ويعرف بالحنش . مات في ربيع الأول سنة ثلاث وستين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Flayṭa. Originally from the al-Jadī family, Meccan, and known as al-Ḥanash. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal 863 AH in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00658 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00658-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00658-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00658 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسن بن صلح الشهاب السبكي مؤدب أولاد الزكي بمكة سمع علي معهم في المجاورة الثالثة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. Ṣulḥ, al-Shihāb al-Subkī, tutor of al-Zakī’s children in Mecca. He heard from me, along with them, during his third *mujāwara* (extended stay for religious devotion/study)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00659 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00659-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00659-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00659 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الحسن بن عبد الله الجوهري . صواب جده علي وسيأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Ḥasan b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Jawharī. The correct name for his grandfather is ʿAlī, and his biography will follow."@en .

rec:AIND-D00661 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00661-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00661-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00661 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسن بن عطية بن محمد بن فهد الهاشمي المكي الآتي أبوه وجده سمع علي بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAṭiyya b. Muḥammad b. Fahd al-Hāshimī al-Makkī. His father and grandfather will be mentioned later. He heard from ʿAlī in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00666 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00666-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00666-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00666-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00666 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسن بن علي بن محمد الشهاب بن البدر الطلخاوي الأصل القاهري الآتي أبوه . ممن حفظ القرآن وكتبا وعرض وحضر درس أبيه وكذا سمع علي وزوجه أبوه ابنة للخطيب علي بن عبد الحق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb b. al-Badr al-Ṭalkhāwī, originally from al-Ṭalkhā, residing in Cairo. His father's biography will be mentioned later. He memorized the Qurʾān, wrote books, presented (his learning), attended his father's lessons, and also heard from me (al-Sakhāwī). His father married him to the daughter of al-Khaṭīb ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Ḥaqq."@en .

rec:AIND-D00673 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00673-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00673-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00673 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسن بن قفند . هكذا كتبه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. Qafand. Thus did Ibn ʿAzm write it (i.e. recorded the name in this form)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00674 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00674-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00674-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00674-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00674 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسن الشهاب الحنفي شيخ المنجكية . مات بعد انقطاعه بالفالج مدة في شوال سنة إحدى وثمانين وصارت المشيخة لناصر الدين الأخميمي أحد أئمة السلطان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥasan al-Shihāb al-Ḥanafī, shaykh of al-Manjakīya. He died in Shawwāl 881 AH, after having been incapacitated by paralysis for a period. The shaykhdom was then transferred to Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Akhmīmī, one of the Sultan's imams."@en .

rec:AIND-D00676 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00676-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00676-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00676 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسن البطائحي . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن سليمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥasan al-Baṭāʾiḥī. Mentioned in the biography of those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Sulaymān."@en .

rec:AIND-D00678 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00678-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00678-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00678 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسن الحلبي ، ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥasan al-Ḥalabī was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00679 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00679-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00679-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00679-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00679-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00679 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسن الرومي المكي الفراش بها ويعرف بالأقرع . مات بها في شعبان سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥasan al-Rūmī al-Makkī, the *farrāsh* there, known as al-Aqraʿ. He died there in Shaʿbān in the year 892 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00681 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00681-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00681-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00681-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00681 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الحسن العباسي الحنبلي . مضى فيمن جده داود بن سالم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Ḥasan al-ʿAbbāsī al-Ḥanbalī. He was mentioned among those whose grandfather is Dāwūd b. Sālim."@en .

rec:AIND-D00682 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00682-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00682-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00682-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00682 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الحسن الغماري العروسي . كبير الشهرة بالغرب كله بالصلاح والخير عمر نحو المائة . ومات في رمضان أو شوال سنة أربع وسبعين . أفاده لي بعض المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Ḥasan al-Ghumārī al-ʿArūsī. He was widely renowned throughout the entire Maghrib for his piety and goodness. He lived for about a hundred years. He died in Ramadan or Shawwal of the year 874 AH. This information was conveyed to me by some Moroccans."@en .

rec:AIND-D00686 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00686-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00686-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00686 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسين بن حسن بن علي بن يوسف بن علي بن أرسلان بالهمزة كما بخطه ابن أبي بكر الدمشقي الخطيب . ولد سنة تسع وتسعين وسبعمائة وكتب بخطه في سنة ثلاث وسبعين ببعض الاستدعاآت وما علمت أمره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥusayn b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. ʿAlī b. Arslān (with hamza, as in his own handwriting), Ibn Abī Bakr al-Dimashqī al-Khaṭīb. He was born in the year 799 H and wrote some petitions in his own hand in the year 773 H. I do not know his circumstances."@en .

rec:AIND-D00687 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00687-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00687-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00687 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسين بن حسين بن حسين الشهاب أبو الفتح بن الفتحي المكي أوسط أخوته الثلاثة وخيرهم وزوج ابنة الشمس محمد الكيلاني نائب الإمام بمقام الحنبلي . ولد في ذي الحجة سنة أربع وستين بمكة وسمع علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥusayn b. Ḥusayn b. Ḥusayn, al-Shihāb Abū al-Fatḥ b. al-Fatḥī al-Makkī. He was the middle of his three brothers and the best of them. He was the husband of the daughter of al-Shams Muḥammad al-Kīlānī, who served as deputy to the Imam for the Hanbali madhhab. He was born in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 864 AH in Mecca and heard from (teachers, text incomplete)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00689 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00689-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00689 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسين بن خلد بن حسين شهاب الدين الهيتمي سمع الجمال بن السابق بقراءته على الزين الزركشي معظم صحيح مسلم وقال لي أنه توفي سنة خمسين فتنظر ترجمته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Husayn b. Khald b. Husayn Shihāb al-Dīn al-Haytamī. He heard most of Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim from al-Jamāl b. al-Sābiq, who recited it to al-Zayn al-Zarkashī. He (Ahmad) told me (al-Sakhāwī) that he (al-Zarkashī) died in the year fifty. His (al-Zarkashī's) biography should be consulted."@en .

rec:AIND-D00690 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00690-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00690-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00690-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00690 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسين بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن الشهاب بن البدر الأذرعي ثم الدمشقي الشافعي الآتي أبوه من معجم شيخنا وغيره ويعرف كأبيه بابن قاضي اذرعات نائب الحكم بدمشق . مات بها في ليلة الأحد عشري صفر سنة أربع وستين ودفن من الغد بمقابر باب توما . أرخه ابن اللبودي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shihāb b. al-Badr al-Adhraʿī, then al-Dimashqī, al-Shāfiʿī. His father will be mentioned later. (This notice is drawn) from the muʿjam of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and other sources. He, like his father, was known as Ibn Qāḍī Adhruʿāt, the deputy judge (nāʾib al-ḥukm) in Damascus. He died there on the night of Sunday, the twentieth of Safar, in the year 864 H. He was buried the next day in the cemeteries of Bāb Tūmā. Ibn al-Labūdī recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D00695 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00695-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00695-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00695 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسين بن علي النغشواني ويدعى بالجنيد وهو به أشهر . سيأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī al-Naghshwānī, also known as al-Junayd, by which he is better known. Forthcoming."@en .

rec:AIND-D00700 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00700-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00700-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00700-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00700 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حسين البسطامي بن الإعزازي شيخ زاوية ابن الأطعاني بحارة المشارقة ظاهر حلب . جود القرآن لأبي عمرو وحفظ ربع المنهاج وصحب الشرف أبا بكر الحبشي وكان مات بمكة بعد الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥusayn al-Basṭāmī b. al-Iʿzāzī was the shaykh of the Zāwiyat Ibn al-Aṭʿānī in Ḥārat al-Mashāriqa, outside Ḥalab. He mastered Qurʾān recitation according to Abū ʿAmr and memorized a quarter of al-Minhāj. He also kept the company of al-Sharaf Abū Bakr al-Ḥabashī, who was a resident of Mecca and died there after the age of sixty. Aḥmad himself also died in Mecca after the age of sixty."@en .

rec:AIND-D00702 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00702-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00702-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00702 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن حمزة بن محمد الحسني الهدوي الصعدي المكي ويعرف بأبي سواسواي والد محمد . مات بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة سبع وستين . ذكره ابن فهد وقال في محمد سبط أبي سواسوا ويحرر التئامهما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥamza b. Muḥammad al-Ḥasanī al-Hadawī al-Ṣaʿdī al-Makkī, known as Abū Sawāswāy, father of Muḥammad. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in 867 AH. Ibn Fahd mentioned him and said regarding Muḥammad, 'the grandson of Abū Sawāswā,' and their connection needs clarification."@en .

rec:AIND-D00703 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00703-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00703-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00703 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي حمو موسى بن عبد الواحد وعبد الواحد هذا جد له أعلى أبو العباس العبد الوادي التلمساني سلطان المغرب الأوسط وما والاها والملقب بالمعتصم . مات في سنة خمس وستين وله ذكر في حوادث سنة ثلاث وثلاثين أو التي بعدها من أنباء شيخنا ، وترجمه الزين عبد الباسط مطولا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Abī Ḥamū Mūsā b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid. This ʿAbd al-Wāḥid is his paternal great-grandfather Abū al-ʿAbbās al-ʿAbd al-Wādī al-Tilimsānī, Sultan of the Central Maghrib and its environs, and titled al-Muʿtaṣim. He (Ahmad) died in the year 865. He is mentioned in the events of the year 833 or the year thereafter in *Anbāʾ* by our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī). Al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ biographed him at length."@en .

rec:AIND-D00704 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00704-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00704-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00704-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00704 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن خاص شهاب الدين الحنفي . أحد الفضلاء المتميزين أكثر من الاشتغال بالفقه والحديث ليلا ونهارا وكتب كثيرا وجمع ودرس . مات في سنة تسع قاله البدر العيني ، وقال شيخنا في أنبائه أن البدر أخذ عنه وكان يطريه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Khāṣṣ, Shihāb al-Dīn, al-Ḥanafī. He was one of the distinguished scholars who diligently engaged in fiqh and ḥadīth studies day and night, wrote extensively, compiled works, and taught. He died in the year 9 (H), as stated by al-Badr al-ʿAynī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his Anbāʾ that al-Badr acquired knowledge from him and used to praise him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00705 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00705-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00705-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00705-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00705-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00705 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن خالد المقدسي كتب في الاستدعاآت . ومات به في ثاني عشر ذي القعدة سنة أربع وخمسين ولم أعلم أمره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Khālid al-Maqdisī. He worked as a scribe of petitions. He died there (in Jerusalem, as implied by his nisbah) on the 12th of Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 854 H. Al-Sakhāwī states he was not aware of further details about him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00706 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00706-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00706-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00706-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00706 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن خرص الجميعي القائد . مات بمكة في يوم الأربعاء سابع المحرم سنة خمس وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ḥirṣ al-Jamīʿī al-Qāʾid. He died in Mecca on Wednesday, the 7th of Muharram in the year 865. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00708 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00708-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00708-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00708-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00708-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00708 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن خفاجا الشهاب الصفدي شيخها وزاهدها كان جيدا صالحا خيرا زاهدا عابدا قانتا لأهل بلده فيه اعتقاد كبير سيما وهو لا يقبل لأحد شيئا وكان في أول أمره حائكا ثم تركها وتقنع بكروم له . مات بعد أن عمر طويلا بصفد في سابع عشر رجب سنة خمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Khafāja, nicknamed al-Shihāb, from Safad (al-Ṣafadī). He was its shaykh and ascetic. He was a good, righteous, benevolent, ascetic, devout, and pious person, greatly esteemed by the people of his hometown. Notably, he accepted nothing from anyone. In his early life, he was a weaver, but he later abandoned that profession and contented himself with his vineyards."@en .

rec:AIND-D00709 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00709-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00709-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00709 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن خلف شهاب الدين المصري ناظر المواريث كان أبو مهتارا عند ابن فضل الله . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة اثنتين . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Khalaf, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Miṣrī, the inspector of inheritances (nāẓir al-mawārīth). His father was a chamberlain/steward (mihtār) in the service of Ibn Faḍl Allāh. He died in Jumādā II of the year 802 (AH). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentions him in his Inbāʾ (al-Ghumr)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00715 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00715-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00715-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00715-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00715 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن خليل بن طبخ الجودري المؤدب نزيل مكة ممن سمع مني بها وكان يجيد حفظ القرآن ويقرأ به على القبور وغيرها . مات بها في سنة ست وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Khalīl b. Ṭabakh al-Jawdarī, al-Muʾaddib, a resident of Mecca, was among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me (al-Sakhāwī) there. He excelled in memorizing the Qurʾān and used to recite it over graves and elsewhere. He died there in the year 896 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00717 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00717-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00717-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00717-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00717-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00717 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن خليل بن يعقوب بن إبراهيم القادري المدير . ولد سنة ثلاث وثلاثين وثمانمائة وقرأ القرآن عند ابن أسد وتكسب حريريا وبالدوران للأعلام بالموتى لفقره وعياله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Khalīl b. Yaʿqūb b. Ibrāhīm al-Qādirī al-Mudīr. He was born in 833 H. He recited the Qurʾān with Ibn Asad. Due to his poverty and family, he earned his living as a silk merchant and by circulating among the notables for the dead."@en .

rec:AIND-D00719 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00719-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00719-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00719 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن خليل الصوفي أحد الأطباء ووالد الموجودين الآن كان يجلس عند عطار بباب جامع الأقمر كولده الآن وآخر عهدي به بعد الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Khalīl al-Ṣūfī, one of the doctors and father of those currently alive. He used to sit at a perfumer's by the gate of al-Aqmar Mosque, as his son does now. My last knowledge of him was after the sixties (860s AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00720 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00720-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00720-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00720 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن خيربك أخو محمد وإسماعيل وأمير المؤمنين عبد العزيز بني يعقوب الآتي ذكرهم لأمهم وتزوج ابنة البساطي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Khayrbak, brother of Muḥammad, Ismāʿīl, and Amīr al-Mu'minīn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Yaʿqūb (mentioned later) from their mother's side. He married the daughter of al-Basāṭī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00725 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00725-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00725-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00725 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن دريب بن خلد الشهاب أبو الغواير بن قطب الدين الحسني صاحب جازان وابن صاحبها . حاصره السيد محمد بن بركات في سنة اثنتين وثمانين كما في الحوادث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad ibn Durayb ibn Khuld (al-Shihāb Abū al-Ghawāyir al-Ḥasanī) was the ruler of Jāzān and the son of its ruler. He was besieged by al-Sayyid Muḥammad ibn Barakāt in the year 882 H, as recorded in al-Ḥawādith."@en .

rec:AIND-D00726 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00726-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00726-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00726 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن دلامة الخواجا الشهاب البصري ثم الدمشقي . أنشأ مدرسة بصالحية دمشق ، ومات في ثامن عشر المحرم سنة ثلاث وخمسين فدفن بعد العصر من يومها رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Dalāma al-Khawājā, al-Shihāb, al-Baṣrī, then al-Dimashqī. He founded a madrasa in Ṣāliḥiyya, Dimashq. He died on the 18th of Muḥarram in the year 853 AH. He was buried after the afternoon prayer on the same day. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00728 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00728-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00728-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00728-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00728-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00728 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن راشد الينبعي قاضيها من قبل إمام الزيدية وصاحب صنعاء لكونه زيديا فدام سنين حتى مات وكان يتوقف في قبول كثير من مخالفيه مع نسبة لخبرة مذهبه ، وحج في سنة تسع عشرة فأدركه أجله بعد الحج في النفر الأول أو الثاني منها ودفن بالمعلاة وبني على قبره نصب . ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Rāshid al-Yanbuʿī. He was appointed as qadi of Yanbuʿ by the Imam of the Zaydiyya, who was also the ruler of Sanaa (as Aḥmad himself was Zaydi). He served in this office for several years until his death. He was hesitant to accept many of his opponents, despite his expertise in his madhhab. He performed the Hajj pilgrimage in 819 H, and his demise occurred after the Hajj, during the first or second nafr (departure from Mina). He was buried in al-Muʿallā, and a monument was erected on his grave. Al-Fāsī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00729 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00729-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00729-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00729 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن راشد التيمي البناء المكي . مات في ربيع الأول سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Rashid al-Taymi al-Banna al-Makki. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 857 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00730 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00730-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00730-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00730 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن ربيعة بن علوان الدمشقي المقرئ أحد المجودين للقراآت العارفين بالعلل أخذ عن ابن اللبان وغيره وانتهت إليه رياسة هذا الفن بدمشق ، وكان مع ذلك خاملا لمعاناة ضرب المندل واستحضار الجن . مات في شعبان سنة ثلاث وقد جاز الستين . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Rabīʿa b. ʿAlwān al-Dimashqī, the Qurʾān reciter, one of the masters of recitation and knowledgeable in its subtleties. He acquired knowledge from Ibn al-Labbān and others. The leadership in this art in Damascus ended with him. Despite this, he remained obscure due to his involvement in geomancy (ḍarb al-mandal) and the summoning of jinn. He died in Shaʿbān of a year ending in three (e.g., 803 H), having passed sixty years of age. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his work 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』."@en .

rec:AIND-D00732 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00732-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00732-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00732 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن رجب بن محمد بن عثمان بن جميل الشرف البقاعي الدمشقي الشافعي والد البرهان بن الزهري الماضي . مات في فتنة التتار سنة ثلاث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad ibn Rajab ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Jamīl al-Sharaf al-Biqāʿī al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī. He was the father of al-Burhān ibn al-Zuhrī (mentioned previously). He died during the Tatar *fitna* in 803 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00733 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00733-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00733-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00733-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00733 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن رسلان السفطي القاهري الشافعي أحد من جد ومهر إلى أن صار يستحضر الكثير من الفروع الفقهية ويباحث ويستشكل ويفهم قليلا وهو من كبار الطلبة بالخانقاه الشيخونية مات في ربيع الأول سنة ست وعشرين وقد أكمل الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Raslān al-Safaṭī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī was one of those who strove and became skilled to the extent that he could recall many jurisprudential branches, debate, raise questions, and understand a little. He was one of the senior students at the Shaykhūniyya Khānqāh. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 826 H, having completed sixty years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D00737 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00737-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00737-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00737 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن زكريا التلمساني المغربي المالكي . أخذ عن ابن مرزوق الحفيد وتقدم في أصول الفقه والمنطق وشارك في الفقه وغيره ، وهو في سنة تسعين حي ويكون تقريبا في حدود السبعين ، وممن أخذ عنه صاحبنا عبد الله الحسناوي وله ذكر في أبي الفضل البجائي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Zakarīyā al-Tilimsānī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī. He acquired knowledge from Ibn Marzūq al-Ḥafīd and excelled in Uṣūl al-Fiqh and Logic. He also participated in Fiqh and other fields. He was alive in the year 890 H and was approximately seventy years old. Among those who took from him was our companion ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥasanāwī. He is also mentioned in the biography of Abū al-Faḍl al-Bijāʾī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00739 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00739-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00739-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00739-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00739 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سالم بن حسن الإسحاقي نسبة لمحلة إسحاق من الغربية . ولد قبل الخمسين وثمانمائة وتكسب بالشهادة ونسخ واشتغل قليلا وقد اجتمع بي فأخذ عني شيئا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Sālim b. Ḥasan al-Isḥāqī, whose nisbah is to Maḥallat Isḥāq in al-Gharbiyya. He was born before 850 H and earned his living as a witness, and copied manuscripts. He also engaged in some study. He met me (al-Sakhāwī) and learned a little from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D00740 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00740-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00740-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00740-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00740 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سالم العبادي ثم القاهري الأزبكي شقيق إبراهيم الماضي ومحمد الآتي ممن يتسمى شافعيا كأنه لأجل الوظائف وإلا فالثلاثة لا أهلية فيهم ، وقد حج مع أبيه وأخيه في موسم سنة ثمان وتسعين فرجعا وتأخر إبراهيم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Sālim al-ʿAbbādī, then al-Qāhirī al-Azbakī, the brother of the aforementioned Ibrāhīm and the forthcoming Muḥammad. He called himself Shāfiʿī, seemingly for the sake of offices, otherwise, none of the three brothers had any competence. He performed the Hajj with his father and brother in the season of 898 AH. The two (his father and Ahmad) returned, but Ibrāhīm remained behind."@en .

rec:AIND-D00741 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00741-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00741-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00741 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي السعادات بن عادل الحسيني المدني أخو عبد الله وعبد الرحمن وعبد الكريم المذكورين . ولد سنة سبع وستين بالمدينة وحفظ القرآن والقدوري واشتغل قليلا وهو ممن سمع مني بالمدينة النبوية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī al-Saʿādāt b. ʿĀdil al-Ḥusaynī al-Madanī, brother of the aforementioned ʿAbd Allāh, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, and ʿAbd al-Karīm. He was born in 867 H in Medina, memorized the Qurʾān and 『al-Qudurī』, and studied a little. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the Prophetic city of Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D00743 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00743-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00743-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00743-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00743-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00743 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سعد بن مسلم شهاب الدين الأريحي الدمشقي المكي الحنفي المقرئ نائب مقام الحنفية بها وشيخ رباط ربيع . شهد على ابن عياش في ذي القعدة سنة ست وثلاثين وثمانمائة بإجازة عبد الأول المرشدي . مات في ليلة الخميس مستهل جمادى الأولى سنة إحدى وأربعين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Saʿd b. Muslim, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Aryaḥī al-Dimashqī al-Makkī al-Ḥanafī al-Muqriʾ. He served as deputy (nāʾib) of the Ḥanafī position in Mecca and as shaykh of Ribāṭ Rabīʿ. He witnessed concerning Ibn ʿAyyāsh in Dhū al-Qaʿda 836 H regarding an ijāza granted by ʿAbd al-Awwal al-Murshidī. He died in Mecca on the night of Thursday, the beginning of Jumādā al-Ūlā, 841 H. Ibn Fahd recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D00744 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00744-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00744-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00744-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00744 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سعد الهندي المكي القائد نائب مكة للسيد بركات ثم لولده وكان طويلا مهابا جريئا . مات في ليلة الخميس ثامن المحرم سنة خمس وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Saʿd al-Hindī al-Makkī, known as al-Qāʾid (the Leader). He served as nāʾib (deputy) of Mecca for Sayyid Barakāt, and subsequently for Barakāt's son. He was tall, respected, and bold. He died on the night of Thursday, the 8th of Muḥarram, 865 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded this date."@en .

rec:AIND-D00744a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00744a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00744a ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سعد الدين . في بدلاي"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad ibn Saʿd al-Dīn. In Badlāy."@en .

rec:AIND-D00745 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00745-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00745-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00745-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00745 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سعيد بن أحمد السماقي الحسباني أخو القاضي شرف الدين قاسم والشاهد بسوق صاروجا . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة اثنتي عشرة عن سبعين سنة بدمشق . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Saʿīd b. Aḥmad al-Sammāqī al-Ḥisbānī. Brother of al-Qāḍī Sharaf al-Dīn Qāsim and a witness (shāhid) in Sūq Sārūjā. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā 812 AH at the age of seventy in Damascus. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his *Inbāʾ*."@en .

rec:AIND-D00746 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00746-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00746-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00746 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سعيد بن محمد بن إبراهيم قاضي الشام السنوسي . ذكره ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Saʿīd b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm, the qāḍī of al-Shām, al-Sanūsī. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00750 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00750-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00750-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00750 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سفري الإمام شهاب الدين . سمع هو وصهره برهان الدين على شيخنا المتباينات له بقراءة يحيى بن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Safarī, al-Imām Shihāb al-Dīn. He and his son-in-law Burhān al-Dīn listened to `al-Mutabāyināt` under our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), with Yaḥyā b. Fahd reciting."@en .

rec:AIND-D00752 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00752-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00752-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00752 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سلمان بن محمد الشهاب الحموي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Salmān b. Muḥammad, al-Shihāb al-Ḥamawī. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Makka."@en .

rec:AIND-D00755 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00755-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00755-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00755 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سليمان بن جار الله بن زايد السنبسي المكي . ذكره ابن فهد هكذا مجردا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Sulaymān b. Jār Allāh b. Zāyid al-Sunbusī al-Makkī. Ibn Fahd mentioned him plainly as such."@en .

rec:AIND-D00756 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00756-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00756-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00756 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سليمان بن عبد الرحمن بن العز محمد بن التقي سليمان بن حمزة بن أحمد بن عمر بن أبي عمر المقدسي ثم الصالحي الحنبلي أخو عبد الرحمن الآتي . ذكره شيخنا في معجمه وقال أنها أجاز له في استدعاء الصرخدي سنة اثنتين وبيض له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Sulaymān b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-ʿIzz Muḥammad b. al-Taqī Sulaymān b. Ḥamza b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Abī ʿUmar al-Maqdisī, then al-Ṣāliḥī, the Ḥanbalī — brother of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān (treated below). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentions him in his Muʿjam and said that he (read annahu, not annahā) granted him an ijāza in the istidʿāʾ of al-Ṣarkhadī in the year 802, and left [the entry] blank for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00757 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00757-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00757-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00757 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سليمان بن عقبة البناء . مات بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Sulaymān b. ʿUqba al-Bannāʾ. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 862."@en .

rec:AIND-D00758 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00758-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00758-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00758-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00758-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00758 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سليمان بن عيسى البدماصي ثم القاهري الحنفي نزيل الإينالية بالشارع وإمامها ووالد التقي محمد الحنبلي البسطي شيخ سوق الفاضل الآتي . شيخ معمر من أهل القرآن يذكر بخير . مات وقد أضر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Sulaymān b. ʿĪsā al-Badmāṣī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Ḥanafī, resident and imām of al-Īnālīya on the street (al-Shāriʿ). He was the father of al-Taqī Muḥammad al-Ḥanbalī al-Basṭī, shaykh of Sūq al-Fāḍil (forthcoming). He was a respected shaykh among the people of the Qur'an and is remembered favorably. He died after becoming blind."@en .

rec:AIND-D00762 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00762-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00762-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00762-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00762 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سليمان بن محمد الديروطي الشافعي ويعرف بابن عزيرة وهي أمه . قرأ على شيخنا في البخاري وكذا على البرهان الكركي وشاركه مشاركة يسيرة في الفقه والنحو والفرائض وتكسب بالشهادة وحج . مات في يوم الاثنين ثامن ربيع الأول سنة ست وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Sulaymān b. Muḥammad al-Dīrūṭī, Shāfiʿī. He was known as Ibn ʿUzayra, who was his mother. He read al-Bukhārī with our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and he studied Fiqh, Naḥw, and Farāʾiḍ to a small extent with al-Burhān al-Karakī. He earned his living as a witness (shāhid) and performed the Hajj. He died on Monday, the 8th of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 876 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00764 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00764-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00764-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00764 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سنان بن راجح بن محمد بن عبد الله بن عمر بن مسعود العمري المكي القائد . مات في يوم السبت تاسع رجب سنة سبع وأربعين بالهدة وحمل إلى مكة فوصلوا به في آخر ليلة الأحد فدفن بالمعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Sinān b. Rājiḥ b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Masʿūd al-ʿUmarī al-Makkī al-Qāʾid. He died on Saturday, the 9th of Rajab, 847 H, in al-Hadda. His body was transported to Mecca, arriving on the last night of Sunday, and was subsequently buried at al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D00765 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00765-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00765-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00765 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن سند . هكذا بخطى في الآخذين عني وأظنه محمد بن سند المسمى أبوه بعلي وسيأتي إن شاء الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Sanad. His name is found in my handwriting under the heading \"those who took from me.\" I believe he is Muḥammad b. Sanad, whose father is named ʿAlī, and he will be mentioned later, God willing."@en .

rec:AIND-D00767 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00767-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00767-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00767 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن شاهين الكركي سبط شيخنا وشقيق يوسف الآتي . مات في حياة أبويه بعد أن استجاز له جده في سنة خمس وعشرين جماعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Shāhīn al-Karakī was the grandson of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and the brother of Yusuf (who will be mentioned later). He died during the lifetime of his parents, after his grandfather had arranged for him to receive an ijāza from a group of scholars in the year 825."@en .

rec:AIND-D00772 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00772-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00772-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00772 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن شعيب خطيب بيت لهيا كان عابدا قانتا كثير التهجد والذكر حتى قال الشهاب بن حجي أنه قل من كان يلحقه في ذلك . مات في المحرم سنة إحدى . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Shuʿayb was the khaṭīb (preacher) of Bayt Lihyā. He was a devout and obedient servant (of God), frequently performing tahajjud (night vigil prayers) and dhikr (remembrance of God), to the extent that al-Shihāb b. Ḥajjī said that few could equal him in this. He died in Muḥarram of the year 801 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Anbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D00774 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00774-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00774 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الشهيد . هكذا ذكره شيخنا في سنة ثلاث عشرة من أنبائه وقال أنه كان أولا يتعانى صناعة الفراء ثم اشتغل قليلا وباشر في ديوان السلطان ثم ولي الوزارة ثم وقعت فتنة اللنك وهو وزير فاستصحبه إلى بلاده ثم خلص منه بعد ثلاثين وورد دمشق فباشر نظر الجيش وغيره في شعبان انتهى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad ibn al-Shahīd. Our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) mentioned him thus in his *Inbāʾ al-Ghumr* under the year 813 H, stating that he was initially engaged in the fur industry, then worked for a while in the Sultan's chancery, and subsequently became vizier. During his vizierate, Lank's (Tamerlane's) fitna occurred, and Tamerlane took him to his own country. After thirty years, he escaped from captivity and arrived in Damascus, where he assumed the supervision of the army and other duties in Shaʿbān. End."@en .

rec:AIND-D00777 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00777-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00777-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00777-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_a ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00777 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن صالح بن أحمد بن محمد بن موسى الشهاب أبو العباس الحسني قبيلة من خولان الرازحي ورازح بينها وبين أب نحو يومين اليماني الشافعي كتبت له في سنة أربع وتسعين وأنا بمكة على نسخة معه بالمنهاج إجازة وهو شيخ مبارك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ṣāliḥ b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā, al-Shihāb Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Ḥasanī, al-Rāzḥī (from the tribe of Khawlān, and Raziḥ is about two days' journey between it and Ibb), al-Yamānī, al-Shāfiʿī. I granted him an ijāza in the year 894 H while I was in Mecca, for a copy of al-Minhāj that he possessed. He was a blessed shaykh."@en .

rec:AIND-D00780 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00780-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00780-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00780 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن صالح بن الشيخ محمد بن أبي بكر المرشدي المكي الأصل والمنشأ الهندي المولد الشافعي . ممن حفظ القرآن وتكسب بعمل العمر وكذا بالتسبب قليلا وسافر فيه لليمن وغيره وسمع مني بمكة ثم سافر إلى مندوه للمعيشة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ṣāliḥ b. al-Shaykh Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-Murshidī al-Makkī, of Indian birth, Shāfiʿī. He memorized the Qurʾān and earned a living through drafting legal documents and some trade. He traveled to Yemen and other places for this purpose and listened (to ḥadīth) from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca. He then traveled to Mandūh for his livelihood."@en .

rec:AIND-D00782 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00782-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00782-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00782-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00782 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن صبح أحد الظلمة بدمشق . مات بقلعتها في سنة ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ṣubḥ, one of the oppressors in Dimashq. He died in its citadel in 893 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00787 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00787-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00787-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00787 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن ططر . كذا رأيته بهامش نسختي من الأنباء أظنه نقلا من العيني وصوابه محمد وسيأتي إن شاء الله ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00788 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00788-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00788-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00788 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن طوغان ويسمى علي بن عبد الله الصالحي الحمامي ويعرف بابن البيطار . سمع في سنة إحدى وثمانين وسبعمائة على أبي الهول الجزري أشياء منها جزء فيه عوالي من مسموعات أبي نعيم ، وحدث سمع منه ابن فهد وغيره ومات في جمادى الآخرة سنة ثمان وثلاثين بصالحية دمشق ودفن بسفح قاسيون رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Ṭūghān, also known as ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣāliḥī al-Ḥammāmī, and famously called Ibn al-Bayṭār. In 781 AH, he heard from Abū al-Hawl al-Jazarī, among other things, a juzʾ containing elevated narrations from Abū Nuʿaym's auditioned works. Ibn Fahd and others transmitted from him. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira 838 AH in Ṣāliḥiyyat Dimashq and was buried at the foothills of Mount Qasioun. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00790 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00790-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00790-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00790-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00790-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00790 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الطيب محمد بن أحمد بن أبي بكر بن الشهاب بن الجمال الناشري اليماني الشافعي . حفظ المنهاج وتفقه بأبيه وأذن له بالإفتاء ولكنه تورع عنها في حياته بل وبعده وشارك في الفضائل وحصل من الكتب جملة ودرس وأفاد وكان متواضعا حسن الأخلاق معرضا عن الشهرة . مات في سنة ست وسبعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. al-Shihāb b. al-Jamāl al-Nāshirī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī. He memorized al-Minhāj and studied fiqh under his father, who granted him permission to issue fatwas, but he abstained from this during his lifetime and even after his death. He participated in various sciences (faḍāʾil), acquired many books, taught, and imparted knowledge. He was humble, of good character, and shunned fame. He died in the year 876 H. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00791 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00791-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00791-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00791-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00791 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عابد الشهاب القدسي الشافعي وأظنه منسوبا إلى جده . ذكر لي أبو العباس القدسي الواعظ أنه لازمه في الفقه وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. ʿĀbid, al-Shihāb al-Qudsī al-Shāfiʿī. I believe he is attributed to his grandfather. Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qudsī al-Wāʿiẓ informed me that he (Abū al-ʿAbbās) accompanied him (Ahmad) in fiqh and other matters."@en .

rec:AIND-D00792 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00792-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00792-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00792-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00792 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عادل بن مسعود الشريف الفقيه شهاب الدين المدني الحنفي . سمع على النور المحلى سبط الزبيري في الاكتفاء للكلاعي سنة عشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. ʿĀdil b. Masʿūd al-Sharīf al-Faqīh Shihāb al-Dīn al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī. He heard from al-Nūr al-Muḥallā Sibṭ al-Zubayrī al-Kalāʿī's 『al-Iktifāʾ』 in the year 20."@en .

rec:AIND-D00793 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00793-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00793-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00793 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عاصم الفيومي ثم الشبراوي الشافعي . تحول من الفيوم مع أبيه ظنا فقطن شبرى الخيمة مع تردده للاشتغال ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. ʿĀṣim al-Fayyūmī, then al-Shabrāwī, al-Shāfiʿī. He moved from al-Fayyūm with his father, presumably, and then settled in Shibrā al-Khayma, while frequently visiting for study/work."@en .

rec:AIND-D00794 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00794-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00794-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00794 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عامر الشهاب المجدلي الشافعي ويعرف بكنانة . ذكر لي بلديه أبو العباس القدسي الواعظ أنه أول شيخ تخرج به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿĀmir, al-Shihāb al-Majdalī al-Shāfiʿī, also known as Kināna. His compatriot, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qudsī al-Wāʿiẓ, mentioned to me (al-Sakhāwī) that he was the first shaykh under whom he graduated."@en .

rec:AIND-D00796 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00796-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00796-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00796-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00796 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عباد الشهاب السفطي . ذكره ابن فهد في معجمه وقال أنه ذكر أنه سمع الصحيح من التقي بن حاتم وهو ممن أثبته الولي العراقي فيمن سمع منه الإملاء في سنة ثمان عشرة وسمي أباه أرسلان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbbād, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Safaṭī. Ibn Fahd mentioned him in his dictionary, stating that he (Aḥmad) reported hearing al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Taqī b. Ḥātim. Al-Walī al-ʿIrāqī also recorded that he (Aḥmad) dictated to him in the year 818 H. His father's name was Arslān."@en .

rec:AIND-D00799 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00799-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00799-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00799 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عباس بن أحمد البارنباري . شهد على بعض الحنفية سنة إحدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbbās b. Aḥmad al-Bārnbārī. He testified against some Hanafis in the year one."@en .

rec:AIND-D00800 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00800-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00800-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00800 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن العباس العبادي التلمساني . مات سنة ست وستين . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-ʿAbbās al-ʿAbbādī al-Tilimsānī. He died in the year 866. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00801 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00801-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00801-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00801 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الباسط بن خليل شهاب الدين بن الزيني ناظر الجيش الآتي أبوه . مات بالطاعون في مستهل شعبان سنة ثلاث وثلاثين بعد أن بلغ وناب عن والده في كتابة العلامة وكانت جنازته حافلة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ b. Khalīl Shihāb al-Dīn b. al-Zaynī. Nāẓir al-Jaysh, whose father's biography will follow. He died of the plague at the beginning of Shaʿbān in the year 833, after he came of age. He served as his father's deputy in the office of kitābat al-ʿalāma. His funeral was grand."@en .

rec:AIND-D00802 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00802-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00802-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00802 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الباقي الشهاب بن العماد الأقفهسي . هكذا رتبه بعضهم وهو غلط وصوابه ابن عماد بن يوسف يأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Bāqī al-Shihāb b. al-ʿImād al-Aqfahṣī. This is how some arranged him, and it is a mistake. The correct [lineage] is Ibn ʿImād b. Yūsuf, which will come later."@en .

rec:AIND-D00803 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00803-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00803 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الحميد بن سليمان بن حميد شهاب الدين اللاري النابلسي ثم الصالحي . سمع من الصلاح بن أبي عمر في سنة أربع وسبعين وسبعمائة الأولين من تخريج أبي سعد البغدادي عن شيوخه . ذكره التقي بن فهد في معجمه ولم يزد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd b. Sulaymān b. Ḥumayd, Shihāb al-Dīn, al-Lārī, al-Nābulusī, then al-Ṣāliḥī. He heard from al-Ṣalāḥ b. Abī ʿUmar in the year 774 AH the first parts of Abū Saʿd al-Baghdādī's compilation from his shaykhs. al-Taqī b. Fahd mentioned him in his Muʿjam without further additions."@en .

rec:AIND-D00808 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00808-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00808-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00808-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00808 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الدائم بن عمر الشهاب بن القاضي زين الدين المرصفاوي . قال الزين رضوان أنه سمع على الشرف بن الكويك وأشار إلى أنه مات ولم يبين تاريخ موته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Dāʾim b. ʿUmar, al-Shihāb, son of al-Qāḍī Zayn al-Dīn al-Marṣafāwī. Al-Zayn Riḍwān stated that he heard from al-Sharaf b. al-Kuwayk, and he indicated that he died but did not specify the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00809 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00809-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00809-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00809 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الدائم بن عمر الشريف الحسني بن عمر الشريف البدر النسابة . قيل أنه بالمشهد الحسيني وأنه استجيز وهذا لا أعرفه أصلا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Dāʾim b. ʿUmar al-Sharīf al-Ḥasanī, known as al-Badr al-Nassāba (the Genealogist). It is said that he was at al-Mashhad al-Ḥusaynī and that he sought ijāza, but I (al-Sakhāwī) do not know this at all."@en .

rec:AIND-D00813 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00813-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00813-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00813 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم الدمشقي الأصل المكي الشهير كأبيه ابن قيم الجوزية . ممن ورث أباه وتزوج ابنة أبي البقاء بن الضياء واستولدها وماتت تحته ثم تناقص حاله وصار عطارا بباب السلام ثم ارتحل بولديه وأخيه إلى القاهرة فماتوا بها في طاعون سنة ثلاث وسبعين بعد دخوله منها الشام عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm, originally from Damascus, residing in Mecca, famous like his father, Ibn Qayyim al-Jawziyya. He inherited from his father and married the daughter of Abū al-Baqāʾ b. al-Ḍiyāʾ, by whom he had children, but she died while he was still alive. His circumstances then deteriorated, and he became a perfumer at Bāb al-Salām. Eventually, he traveled with his two sons and his brother to Cairo. After his journey from Cairo to Syria, they died in Cairo in the plague of 873 H. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00815 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00815-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00815-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00815 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن حسن أبو حسيل النجار ويعرف بابن بنيفة . مات في المحرم سنة تسع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ḥasan, Abū Ḥusail al-Najjār, also known as Ibn Banīfa. He died in Muḥarram in the year 859."@en .

rec:AIND-D00817 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00817-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00817-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00817-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00817-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00817 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن داود بن الكويز أخو صلاح الدين محمد الآتي . سمع فيما أظن على شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Dāwūd b. al-Kuwayz, brother of Ṣalāḥ al-Dīn Muḥammad (mentioned below). I believe he heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00820 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00820-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00820-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00820-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00820-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00820 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الرحمن الشهاب بن الصالح القدوة بركة المسلمين الزين الدفري المالكي . أجاز له الولي العراقي في سنة ثمان عشرة بعد سماعه منه وعليه أشياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shihāb b. al-Ṣāliḥ al-Qudwa Barakat al-Muslimīn al-Zayn al-Dafarī al-Mālikī. Al-Walī al-ʿIrāqī granted him an ijāza in the year 818 H, after he (the subject) had heard from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00824 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00824-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00824-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00824-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00824-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00824-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00824 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن فضل الحواري الدمشقي ثم المزي الشافعي . كتب بخطه أشياء وقال أنه الإمام يومئذ بالشرفي يونس الأشرفي بمدينة غزة . مات في يوم الثلاثاء في جمادى الثانية سنة ثلاث وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Faḍl al-Ḥawārī, originally from Damascus, then al-Mazzī, a Shāfiʿī scholar. He wrote various works in his own hand and was said to be the Imām at al-Sharafī Yūnus al-Ashrafī in the city of Ghazza at that time. He died on Tuesday, the 5th of Jumādā al-Thānī in the year 843 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00825 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00825-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00825-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00825 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الناصر الزبيري . يأتي فيمن جده محمد بن عبد الناصر ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00826 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00826-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00826-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00826 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الزين عبد الرحمن المدعو عبيد بن علي بن أحمد بن علي بن أحمد بن يوسف بن إبراهيم الديروطي الشافعي ويعرف بابن أبي المنيح . أخذ عني بالقاهرة أشياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, known as ʿUbayd, b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Yūsuf b. Ibrāhīm al-Dayrūṭī al-Shāfiʿī, and also known as Ibn Abī al-Munayyiḥ. He acquired various things from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D00829 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00829-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00829-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00829 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن علي السكندري المسدي . سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī al-Sakandarī al-Masadī. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D00830 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00830-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00830-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00830-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00830 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عمر شهاب الدين البساطي . أثبته الولي العراقي في السامعين لأماليه في سنة عشر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿUmar, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Basāṭī. Al-Walī al-ʿIrāqī recorded him among those who heard his dictations in the year 810 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00836 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00836-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00836-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00836-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00836-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00836 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد النور العثماني التونسي . سمع بقراءتي في مكة على أبي الفتح المراغي سنة ست وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Nūr al-ʿUthmānī al-Tūnisī. He heard my (al-Sakhāwī's) recitation in Mecca in the year 856, on the authority of Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī."@en .

rec:AIND-D00838 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00838-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00838-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00838 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد الشامي المدني ويعرف بابن الشامي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad al-Shāmī al-Madanī, known as Ibn al-Shāmī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00840 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00840-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00840-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00840-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00840 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن الناظر الحنبلي . فيمن جده أحمد بن إسماعيل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Ibn al-Nāẓir al-Ḥanbalī. Of the family whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl (i.e., son of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Nāẓir al-Ḥanbalī, AIND-D03551)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00841 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00841-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00841-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00841-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00841 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن العلامة جمال الدين بن هشام . مضى أيضا فيمن جده محمد بن عبد الله بن يوسف ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00847 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00847-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00847-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00847 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الرحيم بن يوسف ويعرف بابن الغزولي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة قريب التسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Yūsuf, known as Ibn al-Ghazūlī. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo around 890 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00851 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00851-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00851-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00851-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00851 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد السلام الشريف الصفي التونسي الحكيم بقيتهم وصاحب التصانيف في الفن . مات في حدود سنة عشرين أو بعدها بقليل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Salām al-Sharīf al-Ṣafī al-Tūnisī al-Ḥakīm (the physician/sage). The last survivor of them (baqiyyatuhum) and author of works in the field. Died around the year 820 H or a little after."@en .

rec:AIND-D00852 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00852-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00852-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00852 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الطاهر بن أحمد بن عبد الظاهر التفهني ثم القاهري الشافعي أخو عبد القاهر الآتي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. ʿAbd al-Ṭāhir b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Ẓāhir al-Tafhanī, then al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī. Brother of ʿAbd al-Qāhir, who will be mentioned later. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D00856 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00856-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00856-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00856-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00856-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00856-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00856 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد العزيز بن عبد الواحد بن عمر بن عياد الشهاب الأنصاري المغربي الأصل المدني أخو محمد الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. ʿUmar b. ʿAyyād, al-Shihāb, al-Anṣārī, originally from the Maghrib, resident in Medina, brother of Muḥammad (whose biography follows later)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00862 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00862-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00862-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00862 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد العزيز الشيفكي ثم الشيرازي . مضى فيمن جده أحمد ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00863 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00863-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00863-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00863 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الغني بن عبد الرزاق بن أبي الفرج الشهابي بن الأمير فخر الدين بن الوزير تاج الدين ولي قطيا وحج ، ومات وهو في الكهولة بقطيا في أوائل المحرم سنة سبع وخمسين ونقل فدفن بمدفنهم من المدرسة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. Abī al-Faraj al-Shihābī b. al-Amīr Fakhr al-Dīn b. al-Wazīr Tāj al-Dīn. He governed Qiṭyā and performed the Hajj. He died in middle age in Qiṭyā in early Muḥarram 857 H. He was transported and buried in their cemetery adjacent to the madrasa."@en .

rec:AIND-D00864 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00864-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00864-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00864 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد القادر بن إبراهيم الصدر أبو البركات بن المجد المكراني الأصل المكي الشافعي . مضى في ابن إسماعيل ورأيت بخط بعضهم تسميته محمدا كأخيه ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D00865 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00865-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00865-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00865 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد القادر بن حسين بن علي الغمري الآتي جده وأخوه محمد . ممن سمع مني في سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī al-Ghamrī. His grandfather and his brother Muḥammad are mentioned as forthcoming. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the year 895."@en .

rec:AIND-D00866 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00866-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00866-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00866-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00866 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد القادر بن عبد الوهاب القرشي الآتي أبوه . ولد في مستهل ذي القعدة سنة اثنتين وثمانين وثمانمائة ونشأ فأسمعه يسيرا علي وكذا على الفتحي وقبل ذلك أحضره على النشاوي والرضى والأوجاقي وأبي السعود الغراقي ثم على عبد الغني البساطي وأجاز له جماعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Qurashī, whose father will be mentioned later. He was born at the beginning of Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 882 H. He grew up, and I (al-Sakhāwī) had him hear a little from me myself (ʿalayya) and likewise from al-Fatḥī. Before that, I had him attend sessions with al-Nashāwī, al-Riḍā, al-Awjāqī, and Abū al-Suʿūd al-Gharāqī, then with ʿAbd al-Ghanī al-Basāṭī. A group (of scholars) granted him ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D00871 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00871-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00871-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00871-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00871-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00871 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد القادر بن محمد بن الشيخ مرتفع الشهاب النيربي الصالحي . سمع من أبي حفص عمر بن محمد بن أبي بكر الشحطبي تابع حديث ابن عيينة رواية محمد بن عبد الله بن يزيد المقري أنابه الفخر وحدث سمع منه ابن موسى وشيخنا الأبي . وذكره شيخنا في معجمه وأنه أجاز لابنته رابعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad, Shihāb al-Nīrabī al-Ṣāliḥī. He heard from Abū Ḥafṣ ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-Shaḥṭabī, who transmitted the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUyayna via the narration of Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Yazīd al-Muqrī. Al-Fakhr appointed him as his deputy, and he transmitted. Ibn Mūsā and our shaykh (al-Abī) heard from him. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his 『Muʿjam』, and that he granted an ijāza to his daughter Rābiʿa."@en .

rec:AIND-D00873 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00873-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00873-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00873-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00873 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الكافي بن عبد الوهاب البليني هكذا ذكره شيخنا في سنة ست وثمانمائة من أنبائه وهو سهو بمائة سنة سواء فوفته سنة ست وسبعمائة مع أنه لم يذكره في الدرر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Kāfī b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Bilinī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in the year 806 H in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』, but this was a mistake of exactly one hundred years, for his death was in the year 706 H. Our shaykh did not mention him in 『al-Durar al-Kāmina』."@en .

rec:AIND-D00875 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00875-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00875-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00875-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00875-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00875 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الكريم بن البشيري الموقع . سكن بقرب باب زيادة جامع الحاكم . مات في سابع عشر جمادى الأولى سنة اثنتين وتسعين وكان ممن يخالط الفضلاء بل سمع في النسائي الكبير بقراءة البقاعي على جماعة وتردد له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Abd al-Karim b. al-Bashiri al-Muwaqqi'. He resided near Bab Ziyada of Jami' al-Hakim. He died on the 17th of Jumada al-Ula in the year 892 H. He associated with prominent scholars, and heard al-Nasāʾī al-Kabīr under a group (of unnamed shaykhs), with al-Biqāʿī as the reciter, and frequented him (al-Biqāʿī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00884 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00884-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00884-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00884 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن أحمد الشهاب أبو العباس بن الجمال العقيلي الزيلعي اليماني الحنفي . راسلني وأنا بمكة بعد الثمانين يطلب الإجازة فكتبت له وذكرت فيها ما بلغني من أوصافه حسبما أثبته في التاريخ الكبير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad, al-Shihāb Abū al-ʿAbbās, of the Banū al-Jamāl, al-ʿAqīlī, al-Zaylaʿī, al-Yamānī, al-Ḥanafī. He corresponded with me while I was in Mecca after the 880s, requesting an ijāza. So, I wrote to him, mentioning in it what reached me concerning his descriptions, as I had recorded them in *al-Tārīkh al-Kabīr*."@en .

rec:AIND-D00885 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00885-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00885-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00885-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00885 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن أحمد الجزائري الرابطي . ذكره ابن عزم مجردا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad al-Jazāʾirī al-Rābṭī. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him in passing."@en .

rec:AIND-D00886 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00886-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00886-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00886 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن أحمد الدمشقي المقرئ شيخ الإقراء بدمشق في زمنه ويعرف بابن اللبان . مات بها في سنة إحدى وعشرين عن سن عالية وقد سمع كثيرا . قاله ابن أبي عذيبة ويحرر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad al-Dimashqī al-Muqriʾ, known as Ibn al-Labbān. He served as the shaykh of Qur'an recitation in Damascus in his time. He died there in 821 at an advanced age, having heard much (ḥadīth). Ibn Abī ʿUdhayba reported this, and it requires verification."@en .

rec:AIND-D00887 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00887-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00887-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00887 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن إسماعيل بن الأحمر . روي عن الميدومي ، سمع منه شيخنا التقي أبو بكر القلقشندي نسخة إبراهيم بن سعد في سنة أربع وثمانمائة وحدثنا بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ismāʿīl b. al-Aḥmar. He transmitted from al-Maydūmī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)'s teacher, al-Taqī Abū Bakr al-Qalqashandī, heard 『Nuskhat Ibrāhīm b. Saʿd』 from him (Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh) in the year 804 H, and then transmitted it to us (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00889 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00889-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00889-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00889-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00889-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D00889-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00889 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن بلال الفراش والوقاد بالحرم المكي وأخو محمد وإسحاق ، الظن أنه عم أبي فار الزيت أحمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الله بن بلال . قاله ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Bilāl, the carpet-spreader and lamp-lighter at the Holy Sanctuary of Mecca, and brother of Muḥammad and Isḥāq. It is conjectured that he is the paternal uncle of Abū Fār al-Zayt Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Bilāl. Mentioned by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D00890 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00890-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00890-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00890-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00890 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله شهاب الدين أبو الفضل بن الجمال النابلسي الأصل القاهري المولد التاجر أبوه ويعرف باللفاف . قرأ علي بحضرة أبيه وغيره من حفظه من أول المنهاج إلى التيمم وسمع من لفظي المسلسل وأوائل الكتب الستة كل ذلك في سنة إحدى وتسعين بمنزلي وأجزت لهما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh, Shihāb al-Dīn Abū al-Faḍl, originally from Nablus, born in Cairo. His father was a merchant and was known as al-Laffāf. He read to our shaykh (al-Sakhāwī), in the presence of his father and others, from memory, from the beginning of al-Minhāj until the chapter on tayammum. He also heard from our shaykh's dictation al-Musalsal and the beginnings of the Six Books of Hadith. All of this took place in the year 891 AH at our shaykh's house, and our shaykh granted ijāza to both him and his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D00891 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00891-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00891-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00891 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن حسن بن أبي بكر العامري الحرضي اليماني ممن أخذ عني بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة أربع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥasan b. Abī Bakr al-ʿĀmirī al-Ḥaraḍī al-Yamānī, among those who studied under me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 894 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00893 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00893-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00893-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00893 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن الحسن بن عطية بن محمد بن المؤيد الزيدي . توفي محرما ملبيا في ليلة الخميس رابع ذي الحجة سنة سبع ودفن بالمعلاة . قاله التقي الفاسي في تاريخ مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Ḥasan b. ʿAṭīya b. Muḥammad b. al-Muʾayyad al-Zaydī. He died on the night of Thursday, the 4th of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 807, while in the state of ihram and reciting the talbiya, and was buried in al-Muʿallā. This was stated by al-Taqī al-Fāsī in his 『Taʾrīkh Makka』."@en .

rec:AIND-D00895 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00895-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00895-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00895-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00895-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00895 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن خلف بن أبي بكر بن محمد الشهاب الشبراوي ثم القاهري الشافعي إمام الشرابسية . سمع على المؤرخ ناصر الدين بن الفرات في ذي القعدة سنة ست وتسعين ختم الشفا أخذ عنه ابن فهد وأجاز . مات في يوم الخميس خامس صفر ، وأرخه بعضهم بربيع الأول سنة ثلاث وخمسين ودفن من يومه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Khalaf b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad, al-Shihāb al-Shabrāwī, then al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, Imām of al-Sharābishiyya. He heard the completion of 『al-Shifāʾ』 from the historian Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Furāt in Dhū al-Qaʿda, 796 H. Ibn Fahd acquired knowledge from him, and he (Aḥmad) granted ijāza. He died on Thursday, 5th of Ṣafar, 853 H, though some recorded his death in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the same year. He was buried on the same day."@en .

rec:AIND-D00896 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00896-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00896-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00896 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن رشيد الشهاب السلمي الحجازي الحنفي الضرير . سمع عليه المجد إمام الصرغتمشية في سنة أربع وتسعين الختم من الدارقطني وجزء الغطريف . وكتبته هنا حدسا وإلا فما وقفت له على ترجمة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Rashīd, al-Shihāb, al-Sulamī, al-Ḥijāzī, al-Ḥanafī, al-Ḍarīr (the Blind). Al-Majd, the imam of al-Ṣarghatmashiyya, heard from him in the year 894 the complete al-Dāraquṭnī and part of al-Ghaṭrīf. I wrote this here by conjecture, for otherwise, I did not find a biography for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00899 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00899-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00899-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00899 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن عبد الغفار الأشموني . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Ghaffār al-Ashmūnī. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D00902 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00902-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00902 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن علي بن إبراهيم الحيري الأصل المدني الشافعي أحد الفراشين هو وأبوه بالحرم المدني . قرأ علي في مجاورتي بها أربعي النووي ثم قدم وأبوه القاهرة فاجتمعا في آخر سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm, originally from Ḥīra, a resident of Medina, and a Shafi'i. He and his father were among the attendants (farrāshīn) in the Sacred Precinct of Medina (al-Ḥaram al-Madanī). He recited al-Arbaʿūn al-Nawawiyya to me (al-Sakhāwī) during my stay there (in Medina). Afterward, he and his father came to Cairo, and they met with me at the end of the year 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00904 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00904-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00904-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00904-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00904 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن عمر بن أحمد بن محمد بن حسن العجمي ويعرف بالصرفي نزيل مكة . مات بها في يوم الجمعة حادي عشر ربيع الآخر سنة إحدى وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ووصفه بالشيخ ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan al-ʿAjamī, known as al-Ṣarfī, a resident of Mecca. He died there on Friday, the 11th of Rabīʿ al-Ākhir, in the year 861 H. Ibn Fahd recorded his biography and described him as \"al-Shaykh\"."@en .

rec:AIND-D00905 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00905-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00905-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00905-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00905 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن عمر السرسي ثم القاهري المالكي نزيل الصحراء . ممن لازمني في الرواية والدراية واشتغل يسيرا ثم تكسب بالتعليم لفقره وضرورته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar al-Sirsī, then al-Qāhirī, of the Mālikī school, a resident of al-Ṣaḥrāʾ. He was among those who continuously adhered to me (al-Sakhāwī) in transmission and understanding, and he engaged in scholarly pursuits for a short while, then earned his living by teaching due to his poverty and necessity."@en .

rec:AIND-D00909 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00909-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00909-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00909 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن أحمد الرومي الآتي أخوه محمد وأبوهما . كان تارة يجلس مع أخيه شاهدا وتارة تاجرا في الشرب ونحوه وهو خير من أخيه بكثير . مات بعيد الثمانين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Rūmī, mentioned below. His brother was Muḥammad, and their father. He (Aḥmad) sometimes sat as a witness with his brother, and sometimes worked as a merchant in drinks and the like. He was far better than his brother. He died approximately shortly after the eighties (880s AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00911 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00911-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00911-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00911 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الله بن بلال الوقاد بالمسجد المكي ويعرف بفار الزيت وقد ينسب لجده بلال . مات بمكة في جمادى الأولى سنة ثمان وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Bilāl al-Waqqād (the lamp-lighter/muezzin at the Meccan mosque). He was known as Fār al-Zayt (the oil rat), and sometimes attributed to his grandfather Bilāl. He died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 878 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00919 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00919-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00919-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00919 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله بن محمد الشهاب الردماني اليماني . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb al-Radmānī al-Yamānī. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00920 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00920-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00920-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00920 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الجمال عبد الله بن محمد الششتري المدني . ممن سمع على الزين المراغي في سنة خمس عشرة وكتب قصيدة ابن عياش في القراآت الثلاثة في سنة ثلاث وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Jamāl ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Shashtarī al-Madanī. Among those who heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī in the year 815 AH, and copied Ibn ʿAyyāsh’s poem on the three recitations in the year 833 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D00925 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00925-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00925-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00925 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله الشهاب البوتيجي ثم القاهري الشافعي قال شيخنا في الأنباء : تفقه ومهر وكان يستحضر المنهاج عن ظهر قلبه وبعد تكسبه بالشهادة تركها تورعا مات سنة سبع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Shihāb, from al-Būtīj, then al-Qāhirī, Shāfiʿī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in *al-Anbāʾ*: 'He studied fiqh and excelled. He could recall *al-Minhāj* by heart. After earning his livelihood through giving testimony, he left it due to piety (wārāʿan). He died in 827 AH.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D00926 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00926-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00926-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00926 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله الشهاب البوصيري فيمن جده حسن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Shihāb al-Būṣīrī, among those whose grandfather is Ḥasan."@en .

rec:AIND-D00927 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00927-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00927-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00927 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله الشهاب الحسني الأصل المدني شيخ الفراشين والمداحين بحرمها ، ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Shihāb, al-Ḥasanī by origin, al-Madanī, Shaykh of the Farrāshīn (attendants) and Maddāḥūn (eulogists) in its Sacred Precinct (Medina). He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D00932 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00932-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00932-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00932 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله شهاب الدين القزويني . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن يوسف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh Shihāb al-Dīn al-Qazwīnī. He is mentioned in the entry of his grandfather, Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf."@en .

rec:AIND-D00933 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00933-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00933-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00933-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00933 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله الشهاب القلقشندي ، مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن عبد الله وأن صوابه أحمد بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد الله وسيأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Shihāb al-Qalqashandī. He was mentioned among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh, but his correct (name) is Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh, and his entry will follow (later)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00935 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00935-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00935-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00935 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله الشهاب النحريري المالكي آخر من ناب في القضاء بدمشق ثم ولي قضاء حماة ثم حلب . ومات بها في شعبان سنة أربعين . أرخه ابن اللبودي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Shihāb al-Naḥrīrī al-Mālikī was the last to serve as deputy qadi in Damascus, then held the qadi's office in Ḥamā, then in Ḥalab. He died there in Shaʿbān of the year 840 H. Ibn al-Labūdī recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D00940 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00940-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00940-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00940 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله البوصيري . مات سنة إحدى . ذكره ابن عزم وينظر فيمن اسم جده حسن بل الظاهر أنه غيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Būṣīrī. He died in the year 'iḥdā' (one). Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him. It should be investigated if his grandfather's name was Ḥasan, but it appears otherwise. *The text only states \"the year 'iḥdā' (one)\", which could refer to the first year of any century (e.g., 801 AH, 901 AH). Here, it is interpreted as 801 AH, consistent with the early 9th century AH, the period covered by this biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D00941 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00941-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00941-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00941-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00941 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله التركماني أحد من كان يعتقد بمصر . مات في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Turkumānī, one of those who was held in high regard in Egypt. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 802, as our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his 『Inbāʾ』."@en .

rec:AIND-D00945 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00945-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00945-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00945-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00945 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله الزواوي الملوي المغربي المالكي نزيل الجزائر . من المشهورين بالصلاح والعلم والورع والتحقيق . مات في عاشر المحرم سنة أربع وثمانين عن أربع وثمانين سنة . أفاده لي بعض المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Zawāwī al-Mlawī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī was a resident of Algeria. He was known for his piety, knowledge, devoutness, and thorough verification. He died on the 10th of Muharram in the year 884 H at the age of 84. This information was conveyed to me by some Maghribis."@en .

rec:AIND-D00946 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00946-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00946-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00946-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00946 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الله العرجاني الدمشقي . قال شيخنا في إنبائه اشتغل قليلا وكتب خطا حسنا وتعانى الإنشاء والنظم وباشر أوقاف السميساطية وكان يحب السنة والآثار . مات في المحرم سنة خمس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿArjānī al-Dimashqī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his 'Inbāʾ' that he worked a little and wrote in a beautiful hand. He practiced composition and versification. He administered the waqfs of al-Sumaysāṭiyya and loved the Sunna and traditions. He died in Muḥarram of the year 805."@en .

rec:AIND-D00947 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00947-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00947-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00947-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00947-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00947 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الملك بن أبي بكر بن علي بن عبد الله بن علي الشهاب الموصلي الأصل المقدسي الشافعي الآتي أبوه . من بيت كبير قدم علي بولد له عرض المنهاج وجمع الجوامع والألفية واستفدت منه وفاة أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Malik b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī al-Shihāb, of Mawṣilī origin, al-Maqdisī, a Shāfiʿī. His father will be mentioned later. He was from a prominent family. He (his father) came to me (al-Sakhāwī) with his son (Aḥmad), who presented al-Minhāj, Jamʿ al-Jawāmiʿ, and al-Alfiyya. I (al-Sakhāwī) benefited from him upon his father's death."@en .

rec:AIND-D00948 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00948-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00948-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00948 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد المهدي بن علي بن جعفر المشعري . مات بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة سبع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Mahdī b. ʿAlī b. Jaʿfar al-Mashʿarī. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 847."@en .

rec:AIND-D00952 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00952-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00952-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00952 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبد الوهاب بن التقي أبي بكر الغزي وكيل الناصري . يأتي في أواخر الأحمدين ممن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. al-Taqī Abū Bakr al-Ghazzī, wakīl of al-Nāṣirī. He will be mentioned at the end of the Aḥmads section among those whose father's name is not given."@en .

rec:AIND-D00956 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00956-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00956-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00956 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عبيد الله بن محمد المنيني . ممن أخذ عني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUbayd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Manīnī. Among those who took from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00963 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00963-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00963-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00963-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00963-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00963 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عثمان بن نظام الجرخي البخاري الحنفي ويقال له ملا زاده . قرأ عليه يوسف بن أحمد الآتي المصابيح في سنة ثلاث وتسعين وثمانمائة وعظمه جدا وكتب له إجازة حافلة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUthmān b. Niẓām al-Jarkhī al-Bukhārī al-Ḥanafī. He was also known as Mullāzāda. Yūsuf b. Aḥmad (mentioned later) read al-Maṣābīḥ to him in 893 H. He greatly revered him and received a comprehensive ijāza written by him."@en .

rec:AIND-D00967 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00967-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00967-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00967 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عربشاه . في ابن محمد بن عبد الله بن إبراهيم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿArabshāh. (Mentioned in the entry concerning Ibn Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ibrāhīm.)"@en .

rec:AIND-D00968 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00968-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00968-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00968-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00968-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00968 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عرفات . تكسب بالشهادة وبرع فيها مع نقص ديانته وفحش طباعه ، وحج غير مرة وجاور سنة ست وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "8. Aḥmad b. ʿArafāt. He earned a living through witnessing (al-Shahāda) and excelled in it, despite his lack of piety and crude manners. He performed Hajj more than once and resided in Mecca in 886 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D00970 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00970-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00970-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00970 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عطا الله بن أحمد السمرقندي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAṭāʾ Allāh b. Aḥmad al-Samarqandī. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D00972 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00972-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00972-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00972-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D00972-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00972 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عقبة اليماني الحضرمي ثم المكي نزيل القاهرة أحد من يعتقده الكثير من الناس دام بالقاهرة مدة حتى مات في شوال سنة خمس وتسعين بتربة من الصحراء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. ʿUqba al-Yamānī al-Ḥaḍramī, then al-Makkī, resident of Cairo. One of those believed in by many people. He remained in Cairo for a period until he died in Shawwal of the year 895 H, in a desert cemetery."@en .

rec:AIND-D00977 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00977-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00977-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00977 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن إبراهيم الحلبي ابن أخي الصوة يأتي في أواخر الأحمدين فيمن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm al-Ḥalabī, son of the brother of al-Ṣawa. He will appear later in the Aḥmad section, among those whose father's name is not mentioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D00978 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00978-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00978-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00978 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن إبراهيم الشهاب المدني ويعرف بالخياط ممن سمع مني بالمدينة النبوية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm, known by the laqab al-Shihāb and the nisbah al-Madanī, and known as al-Khayyāṭ. He was among those who heard ḥadīth from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the Prophetic City of Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D00981 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00981-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00981-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00981 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن أحمد بن أبي بكر الشهاب الشاذلي المصري الشافعي أخو محمد الآتي ويعرف بابن أبي الحسن وهي كنية أبيه . سمع من شيخنا في سنة خمس وثمانمائة ترجمة البخاري من جمعه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr, al-Shihāb al-Shādhilī al-Miṣrī al-Shāfiʿī, brother of the forthcoming Muḥammad, and known as Ibn Abī al-Ḥasan, which is his father's kunyah. He heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in the year 805 AH the biography of al-Bukhārī from his (Ibn Ḥajar's) compilation."@en .

rec:AIND-D00991 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00991-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00991-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00991-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00991 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن أحمد الشهاب البغدادي الشافعي قاضي الركب العراقي ويعرف بابن الدخنة . سجن بالبرج مدة ثم خلص بعد أن أجزته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Baghdādī al-Shāfiʿī, the judge of the Iraqi caravan, known as Ibn al-Dukhnah. He was imprisoned in al-Burj for a period, then released after I (al-Sakhāwī) granted him an ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D00995 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00995-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00995-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00995 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن أحمد الشهاب الطيبي القاهري ابن عم يوسف بن محمد الآتي ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "35. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad, al-Shihāb al-Ṭībī al-Qāhirī. A paternal cousin of Yūsuf b. Muḥammad (mentioned later), and one of those who studied under me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D00996 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00996-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00996-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D00996-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00996 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن أحمد الحسني الهاشمي المكي الأمير صاحب واسط من وادي مر . مات بها في يوم الجمعة رابع ذي القعدة سنة ثمان وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Ḥasanī al-Hāshimī al-Makkī, the amir, lord of Wāsiṭ from Wādī Murr. He died there on Friday, the 4th of Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 848. Ibn Fahd recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D00997 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D00997-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D00997-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D00997 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن أحمد النويري المالكي إمام مقام المالكية بمكة . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن عبد العزيز بن القسم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Nuwayrī, a Maliki jurist. He was the Imam of the Maliki station in Mecca. He was previously mentioned in the entry for his grandfather, Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. al-Qasim."@en .

rec:AIND-D01002 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01002-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01002-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01002-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01002 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن أيوب الشهاب المنوفي إمام الصالحية بالقاهرة . اشتغل كثيرا وكان كثير المزاح حتى رماه بعضهم بالزندقة . مات في صفر سنة اثنتين وله ستون سنة ، ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ، وقال المقريزي في عقوده : الشافعي اشتغل كثيرا وضبطت عليه كلمات حمله عليها مجونه لو نوقش عليها هلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Ayyūb, al-Shihāb al-Munūfī, served as Imām of al-Ṣalāḥīya in al-Qāhira. He devoted himself considerably to scholarly pursuits and was known for his frequent jesting, to the extent that some accused him of heresy. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Anbāʾ, stating that he died in the month of Ṣafar in the year 802 H at the age of sixty. Al-Maqrīzī also stated in his ʿUqūd that he was a Shafi'i who applied himself diligently to study, and words were recorded from him which his jesting led him to say, and for which, had he been questioned, he would have perished."@en .

rec:AIND-D01003 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01003-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01003-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01003 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن أبي بكر بن حسن الشهاب بن أبي الحسن الشوبكي الأصل النحريري القاهري نزيل الظاهرية القديمة ووالد الشمس محمد النحريري المالكي . مات في رجب سنة ست وخمسين عن ثلاث وستين سنة . وله ذكر في ولده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. Ḥasan, al-Shihāb b. Abī al-Ḥasan, originally from al-Shūbakī, al-Naḥrīrī, al-Qāhirī. He was a resident of al-Ẓāhiriyya al-Qadīma and the father of al-Shams Muḥammad al-Naḥrīrī al-Mālikī. He died in Rajab in the year 856 AH at the age of 63. He is mentioned in his son's biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D01004 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01004-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01004-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01004 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن أبي بكر بن شداد شهاب الدين الزبيدي المقري . ولد تقريبا سنة ست وخمسين وسبعمائة وسمع من والده وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء روى عنه ابن فهد فإنه أجاز له في استدعاء مؤرخ بالمحرم سنة تسع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. Shaddād, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Zabīdī al-Muqrī. He was born around the year 756 AH. He heard from his father and transmitted ḥadīth. Scholars heard from him. Ibn Fahd narrated from him, for he (the subject) granted him an ijāza in a request dated Muḥarram 719 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01010 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01010-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01010-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01010 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن حسن الغمري . ممن سمع مني في سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Ḥasan al-Ghamrī. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the year 895 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01013 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01013-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01013-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01013-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01013-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01013 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن حسين بن البدر النجم بن الزين الرفاعي الصحراوي شيخ طائفته ووالد علي الآتي . ولد في يوم الثلاثاء ثالث شعبان سنة تسع وثلاثين وثمانمائة وتردد إلي كثيرا في سماع الحديث ومجالس الإملاء وكذا سمع على بقايا من المسندين وقرأ على إمام الكاملية وفيه حشمة وتودد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "The father of the forthcoming ʿAlī. He was born on Tuesday, 3 Shaʿbān 839 AH. He often frequented me (al-Sakhāwī) for listening to Hadith and dictation sessions, and he also heard from the remaining transmitters (musnadūn) and recited to the Imam of al-Kamiliyya. He possessed dignity and amiability."@en .

rec:AIND-D01014 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01014-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01014-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01014 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن حسين المصري الأصل المكي ويعرف بابن جوشن كان أحد التجار بمكة وبلغني أنه وقف على الفقراء جهة بالهدة بني جابر . مات في سنة إحدى بمكة ودفن بالمعلاة . قاله الفاسي في تاريخها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn, of Egyptian origin, residing in Mecca, known as Ibn Jawshan. He was one of the merchants in Mecca. It has reached me (al-Sakhāwī) that he endowed property in al-Hadda Banī Jābir for the poor. He died in Mecca in the year 801 and was buried in al-Muʿallā. Al-Fāsī mentioned this in his history."@en .

rec:AIND-D01017 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01017-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01017-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01017-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01017 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن أبي راجح . يأتي فيمن جده محمد بن إدريس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Abī Rājiḥ. He will be mentioned later in the section on those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Idrīs."@en .

rec:AIND-D01018 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01018-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01018-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01018-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01018 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن زكريا الشهاب الجديدي والد الشهاب أحمد الماضي . كان معروفا بالصلاح والكرامات وللناس فيه اعتقاد . مات في ليلة سابع صفر سنة ثلاث وأربعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Zakariyyā, known as al-Shihāb al-Jadīdī, father of al-Shihāb Aḥmad al-Māḍī. He was known for righteousness and miracles, and people had faith in him. He died on the night of the 7th of Ṣafar in the year 843 H. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01020 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01020-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01020-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01020-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_apply ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01020 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن سعيد بن عمر اليافعي المكي الخراز الدلال . مات بها في ربيع الأول سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Saʿīd b. ʿUmar al-Yāfiʿī al-Makkī al-Kharrāz al-Dallāl died there in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 868."@en .

rec:AIND-D01023 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01023-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01023-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01023 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن الشيخ أبي العباس بن أبي الحسن القبابلي . يأتي في أحمد ابن علي بدون زيادة ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D01024 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01024-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01024-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01024 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن صبيح المدني أحد فراشيها وأخو محمد الآتي . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Ṣubayḥ al-Madanī was one of its (Medina's) farrāsh (floor-spreaders/servants), and the brother of the forthcoming Muḥammad. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D01029 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01029-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01029-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01029 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن عبد الله بن علي بن أبي راجح محمد بن إدريس الشهاب القرشي الشيبي المكي . مات بها في المحرم سنة ست وسبعين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Abī Rājiḥ Muḥammad b. Idrīs al-Shihāb al-Qurashī al-Shaybī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Muḥarram 876 H. May Allah forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01032 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01032-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01032-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01032 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن عبد الله النفياني الأصل القاهري نزيل المنكوتمرية . شاب حفظ القرآن واشتغل عند البدر حسن الأعرج والزينين الأبناسي وأخي ولازمني في تقريب النووي وغيره وتنزل في الصوفية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Nafyānī by origin, al-Qāhirī by residence, settled in al-Mankūtamurīya. He was a young man who memorized the Qurʾān and associated with al-Badr Ḥasan al-Aʿraj and the two al-Zayn al-Abnāsī. He maintained discipleship to me (al-Sakhāwī) and my brother regarding al-Nawawī's *Taqrīb* and other works, and he joined the Sufi order."@en .

rec:AIND-D01033 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01033-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01033-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01033 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن عبد الله قيم مدرسة الولوي البلقيني ويعرف بالبصيري بالتصغير . ممن نشأ في بيت الولوي المشار إليه وأقربائه وكثرت مرافعاته ولم يحصل على طائل بل نسبت إليه جريمة فاحشة مع زيارة الليث ونحوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh, administrator (qayyim) of the al-Walawī al-Bulqīnī Madrasa, and known by the diminutive 'al-Buṣayrī'. He grew up in the house of the aforementioned al-Walawī and his relatives. His legal appeals became numerous, but he achieved no significant gain. Rather, an outrageous crime was attributed to him, connected with the visit of al-Layth and the like."@en .

rec:AIND-D01034 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01034-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01034-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01034-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01034 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن خيل الشهاب القاهري أحد صوفية سعيد السعداء ويعرف بابن السكري حرفة أبيه . ممن يشتغل عند الزين زكريا والبكري ثم نزل للكمال الطويل ونحوه ، وقد حج وتردد إلي وعنده سكون وأدب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Khayl, Shihāb al-Qāhirī. One of the Sufis of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ, known as Ibn al-Sukkarī, after his father's craft. He studied under al-Zayn Zakariyyā and al-Bakarī, and then settled with al-Kamāl al-Ṭawīl and others. He performed the pilgrimage and frequented me (al-Sakhāwī), possessing tranquility and good manners."@en .

rec:AIND-D01035 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01035-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01035-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01035 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن علي بن عيسى فتح الدين أبو الفتح المنوفي القلعي الشافعي . أحد النواب وهو بكنيته أشهر . يأتي في الكنى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Fatḥ al-Dīn Abū al-Fatḥ Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAlī b. ʿĪsā al-Munūfī al-Qalʿī al-Shāfiʿī. He was one of the deputies, and he was more famous by his kunya. His entry is forthcoming in the Kunyas section."@en .

rec:AIND-D01038 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01038-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01038-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01038 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن عمر بن أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محرز الشهاب بن النور ابن السراج الصندفي المحلى المالكي سبط الشيخ أبي بكر الطريني ويعرف بابن محرز . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥriz, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Ṣandafī al-Maḥallī al-Mālikī, maternal grandson of Shaykh Abū Bakr al-Ṭarīnī, and known as Ibn Muḥriz. He was one of those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D01043 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01043-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01043-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01043 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن عيسى بن محمد بن عيسى الحسني السمهودي . مضى في ابن أبي الحسن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Refer to the entry for Ibn Abī al-Ḥasan."@en .

rec:AIND-D01044 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01044-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01044-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01044-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01044-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01044 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن عيسى الزين الأنصاري الدهروطي ثم القاهري الشافعي والدا التاج محمد الآتي ويعرف بالأنصاري تزوج ابنة المجد اسماعيل قاضي الحنفية وكان بعد صهره بقليل في ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿĪsā al-Zayn al-Anṣārī al-Dahrūṭī, then al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, father of al-Tāj Muḥammad (forthcoming entry), and known as al-Anṣārī. He married the daughter of al-Majd Ismāʿīl, the Qāḍī of the Ḥanafīs, and was, shortly after his father-in-law, in... (text incomplete)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01047 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01047-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01047-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01047-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01047 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن قوام فيمن جده أبو بكر بن محمد بن قوام .#"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Qawwām, (among those) whose grandfather is Abū Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Qawwām."@en .

rec:AIND-D01049 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01049-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01049-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01049-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01049 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد بن أحمد بن علي بن محمد بن محمد بن علي بن أحمد . حفيد البدر ابن شيخنا ابن حجر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad. He is the grandson of al-Badr, the son of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01050 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01050-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01050-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01050 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن أبي راجح محمد بن إدريس أبو المكارم العبدري الشيبي الحجبي المكي كان من أعيان الحجبة . توفي في أوائل سنة ثمان غريقا في البحر المالح وهو متوجه إلى بلاد اليمن . ذكره الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Abī Rājiḥ Muḥammad b. Idrīs, Abū al-Makārim al-ʿAbdarī al-Shaybī al-Ḥajabī al-Makkī. He was among the notables of the chamberlains. He died at the beginning of the year 808 AH, drowned in the Red Sea while heading to the lands of Yemen. al-Fāsī mentioned him in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D01054 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01054-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01054-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01054-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01054 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الكريم بن حسن الكيلاني المكي ويعرف أبوه بالخواجا شيخ علي . ولد سنة سبع بمكة ونشأ بها فسمع في سنة أربع من الزين أبي بكر المراغي الختم من مسلم وأبي داود وابن حبان . ومات ظنا باليمن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Ḥasan al-Kīlānī al-Makkī. His father was known as al-Khawāja Shaykh ʿAlī. He was born in Mecca in 797 H and grew up there. In 804 H, he heard the complete transmission of Muslim, Abū Dāwūd, and Ibn Ḥibbān from al-Zayn Abū Bakr al-Marāghī. He is thought to have died in Yemen."@en .

rec:AIND-D01055 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01055-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01055 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الله الشهاب البلقيني الأصل المصري القادري . أخذ عن حسن الكشكشي القادري بل وفيما قيل عن ابن الناصح وتجرد وساح مدة ثماني عشرة سنة وصار مشهورا بالصلاح . مات في يوم الجمعة رابع عشر ذي الحجة سنة خمس وخمسين ودفن ظاهر باب النصر رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "92 Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Shihāb, originally al-Bulqīnī, al-Miṣrī, al-Qādirī. He acquired knowledge from Ḥasan al-Kashkashī al-Qādirī, and, according to some accounts, also from Ibn al-Nāṣiḥ. He devoted himself to asceticism and wandered for eighteen years, becoming renowned for his piety. He died on Friday, the fourteenth of Dhū al-Ḥijja, in the year 955, and was buried outside Bāb al-Naṣr. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01056 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01056-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01056-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01056 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد بن عبد المؤمن البتنوني الأصل القاهري الباسطي زوج ابنة أبي العباس الغمري الآتي سمع مني مع أبيه وكذا سمعا على القمصي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "93 Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Muʾmin al-Batnūnī, originally from al-Qāhirī al-Bāsiṭī, husband of the daughter of Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Ghamrī (mentioned below). He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) with his father, and likewise, they both heard from al-Qamṣī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01063 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01063-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01063-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01063 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد بن عمر بن عبد الله شهاب الدين الردادي الحنفي أخو المحمدين اشتغل قليلا . ومات في منتصف شعبان سنة إحدى وستين عن أربع وستين سنة عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Raddādī al-Ḥanafī. He was the brother of the two Muḥammads. He was moderately active. He died in mid-Shaʿbān in the year 861 at the age of 64. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01066 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01066-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01066-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01066 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد بن محمد بن عبادة . يأتي قريبا فيمن جده محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمود بن عبادة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUbāda. He will be mentioned soon in the entry for someone whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Maḥmūd b. ʿUbāda."@en .

rec:AIND-D01074 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01074-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01074-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01074 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد أبو العباس الشاذلي الشافعي . رأيت نسخة من شرح ألفية العراقي قال ناسخها أنه كتبها من نسخته وهي مقروءة على شيخنا وأذن له . وعلى القاياتي أيضا ويشبه أن يكون أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الغني الآتي في الكنى وقع الغلط في نسبه ومذهبه فيحرر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "110 Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Shādhilī, al-Shafi'i. I saw a copy of al-ʿIrāqī’s commentary on al-Alfiyya, which its transcriber stated he copied from his own copy, and which had been recited to our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), who granted him ijāza. It was also recited to al-Qāyātī. It is possible that this Aḥmad is the same Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī (forthcoming in the Kunyas section), and that there was an error in the recording of his nasab and madhhab, which requires investigation."@en .

rec:AIND-D01075 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01075-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01075 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد الشهاب الحسيني المصري ويعرف بابن بنت شقائق . كان شريفا معروفا يتعانى الشهادة . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة إحدى . قاله شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb al-Ḥusaynī al-Miṣrī, known as Ibn Bint Shaqāʾiq. He was a noble person who practiced giving testimony. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』 that he died in Jumādā al-Ākhira in the year one (801 AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01076 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01076-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01076-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01076 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد الشهاب المناوي ويعرف بابن زريق ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Manāwī, known as Ibn Zurayq. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D01078 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01078-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01078-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01078 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد الشهاب المصري التاجر نزيل مكة ويعرف بالعاقل . ممن أنشأ بمكة دارا وكذا بمنى مع شيل عمله بها في سنة تسع وأربعين وكان مسرفا على نفسه . مات في ليلة الخميس عشري رمضان سنة أربع وستين بجدة وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بها وخلف أولادا . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, Shihāb al-Dīn, al-Miṣrī, the merchant, resident of Mecca, known as al-ʿĀqil. He established a house in Mecca and was also engaged in work in Minā around the year 849 H. He was extravagant in his personal life. He died in Jeddah on the night of Thursday, 20th of Ramadan in 864 H, and was carried to Mecca where he was buried. He left behind children. Ibn Fahd recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D01079 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01079-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01079-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01079 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد الشهاب الصوفي الشافعي . ممن سمع ختم النسائي الكبير على النسابة واللذين معه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, al-Shihāb al-Ṣūfī al-Shāfiʿī. Among those who heard the completion (khatm) of al-Nasāʾī’s الكبير (al-Kubrā) from al-Nassāba and those with him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01080 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01080-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01080-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01080 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد الشهاب الغزي الحنفي نزيل مكة من أصحاب يحيى الواعظ . قرأ علي في سنة ثلاث وتسعين أربعي النووي ثم في التي تليها بعض البخاري ولازمني فيهما وهو ممن قرأ بمكة على المحب بن حرباش في الفقه وعلى عبد الله الشامي في النحو ، وفيه سكون وجمود ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, al-Shihāb al-Ghazī al-Ḥanafī. A resident of Mecca, he was among the companions/students of Yaḥyā al-Wāʿiẓ. He recited to our shaykh (al-Sakhāwī) in 893 (AH) al-Arbaʿīn al-Nawawiyya, and then in the following year, some of al-Bukhārī, remaining with him for both. He was also among those who recited in Mecca to al-Muḥibb b. Ḥarbāsh in fiqh and to ʿAbd Allāh al-Shāmī in grammar. He possessed calmness and rigidity."@en .

rec:AIND-D01082 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01082-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01082-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01082 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الشيخ علي بن ناصر الدين بن محمد البعلي العطار هو وأبوه . ولد ببعلبك ونشأ بها فسمع الصحيح على الزين عبد الرحمن بن الزعبوب أنا الحجار لقيته بها فقرأت عليه الثلاثيات ونعم الرجل . مات في"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Shaykh ʿAlī b. Nāṣir al-Dīn b. Muḥammad al-Baʿlī al-ʿAṭṭār. He and his father were perfumers. He was born and grew up in Baʿlabakk. He listened to al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Zaʿbūb. I (al-Sakhāwī), al-Ḥajjār, met him there (in Baʿlabakk) and read to him al-Thalāthiyāt; he was an excellent man. He died in..."@en .

rec:AIND-D01083 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01083-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01083 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد الخانكي شقيق أبي الخير محمد الآتي وسبط النور الرشيدي ويعرف بابن التاجر . ولد سنة ثلاث وثلاثين بالخانقاه ونشأ فقرأ القرآن واشتغل عند النور البوشي ثم قاضي بلده الشمس الونائي ومحمود الهندي وتنزل في صوفية المكان ، وتقنع وقد حضرني بولد له عرض علي المنهاج وجمع الجوامع والألفية وعليه سيما الخير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Khānkī was the brother of Abū al-Khayr Muḥammad (to be mentioned later) and the grandson of al-Nūr al-Rashīdī. He was known as Ibn al-Tājir. He was born and grew up in the Khānqāh in 833 H. He recited the Qurʾān and studied under al-Nūr al-Bawshī, then under the Qāḍī of his town, al-Shams al-Wanāʾī, and Maḥmūd al-Hindī. He settled into the Sufi community of the place and lived frugally, showing signs of goodness. He attended me (al-Sakhāwī) with his son, who presented to me al-Minhāj, Jamʿ al-Jawāmiʿ, and al-Alfiyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D01084 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01084-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01084-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01084 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد السجستاني الحنفي لقيه العلاء بن السيد عفيف الدين غير مرة منها بسجستان في سنة ست وخمسين حين عود الشيخ من مكة فحدثه بالأحاديث الزينيات المكذوبات عن الجلال أبي الفتح محمد بن محمد الحافظي البخاري السرغي الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Sijistānī al-Ḥanafī. Al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Sayyid ʿAfīf al-Dīn met him (the subject) several times, including in Sijistān, in the year 856 H when the shaykh (the subject) returned from Mecca. He (the subject) transmitted to him (al-ʿAlāʾ) the fabricated al-Aḥādīth al-Zayniyyāt from al-Jalāl Abū al-Fatḥ Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓī al-Bukhārī al-Sarghī (who will be mentioned later)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01085 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01085-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01085-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01085 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن محمد الهندي . ممن أخذ عني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "121 Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Hindī. Among those who took (knowledge) from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D01086 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01086-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01086-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01086-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01086-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01086 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن منصور الحميري والبجائي شارح الجرومية . ممن أخذ عنه بالقاهرة البرهان اللقاني . مات سنة سبع وثلاثين . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Manṣūr al-Ḥimyarī al-Bijāʾī, commentator of al-Jurrūmīya. Among those who studied under him in Cairo was al-Burhān al-Laqqānī. He died in the year 837. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D01088 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01088-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01088-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01088 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن موسى الأزرق المكي شيخ معلاتها ويعرف بكباس بموحدتين ثانيتهما مشددة بينهما كاف مفتوحة وآخره مهملة . مات بمكة في رجب سنة ثلاث وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Mūsā al-Azraq al-Makkī, shaykh of al-Muʿallā, was known as Kabbās. He died in Mecca in Rajab of the year 883 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01091 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01091-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01091-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01091 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن يفتح الله . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد الوهاب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Ali b. Yaftaḥ Allāh. His biography is mentioned under the entry of the person whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb."@en .

rec:AIND-D01093 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01093-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01093-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01093 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن شهاب الدين بن أبي الروس . فيمن جده إبراهيم بن محمد"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Shihāb al-Dīn b. Abī al-Rūs. Among those whose grandfather is Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01095 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01095-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01095-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01095-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01095 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي المصري أخو محمد الضرير الآتي ويعرف كسلفه بابن أبي الرداد أحد أمناء النيل . مات في يوم الثلاثاء ثامن عشري شوال سنة سبع وثمانين ودفن بتربتهم عند أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Miṣrī, brother of the blind Muḥammad (mentioned below), known like his forebears as Ibn Abī al-Raddād, was one of the overseers (umanāʾ) of the Nile. He died on Tuesday, the 28th of Shawwāl in the year 887 H, and was buried in the family tomb beside his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D01096 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01096-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01096-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01096 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن الحبال . فيمن جده عبد الله بن علي بن حاتم بن محمد . ###$ | 589882722609$# $$$ أحمد بن علي بن النقيب الحنفي فيمن جده محمد بن ضوء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. al-Ḥibāl. He is among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Ḥātim b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01097 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01097-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01097-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01097-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01097 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي بن النقيب الحنفي فيمن جده محمد بن ضوء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. al-Naqīb al-Ḥanafī, whose grandfather was Muḥammad b. Ḍawʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D01098 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01098-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01098-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01098 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي الزفوري ويعرف بابن سابة كان رأسا في المعاملين الذين يحملون اللحم للمماليك وصاهره أبو الفوز بن زين الدين على بنته ومات قريب التسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "130. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Zafūrī, known as Ibn Sāba. He was a leader among the purveyors who carried meat for the Mamluks. Abū al-Fawz b. Zayn al-Dīn became his son-in-law by marrying his daughter. He died close to ninety years old."@en .

rec:AIND-D01099 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01099-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01099-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01099 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي الشهاب الحبيشي نسبة لمينة حبيش ثم القاهري المالكي الأزهري ثم المديني . كان أبوه نجارا فحفظ القرآن والرسالة وألفية النحو وقطعة من الشامل لبهرام وتفقه بالوراق والسنهوري والنور بن التنسي والبدر بن مخلطة وشارك فيه والعربية والأصلين والفرائض وغير ذلك . وتكسب بالشهادة وأقرأ الطلبة بالأزهر وغيره ونعم الرجل سكونا وفضلا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "131 Aḥmad b. ʿAlī, al-Shihāb al-Ḥubayshī, whose nisba derives from Mīna Ḥubaysh, then al-Qāhirī al-Mālikī al-Azharī, then al-Madīnī. His father was a carpenter. He memorized the Qurʾān, al-Risāla, Alfiyyat al-Naḥw, and a portion of al-Shāmil by Bahrām. He studied fiqh under al-Warrāq, al-Sanhūrī, al-Nūr b. al-Tansī, and al-Badr b. Mukhalliṭa, and he engaged in it (fiqh), Arabic language, the two fundamental principles (uṣūl al-dīn and uṣūl al-fiqh), and inheritance law, among other things. He earned his livelihood through witnessing (as a notary), and he taught students at al-Azhar and elsewhere. He was a good man, known for his tranquility and virtue."@en .

rec:AIND-D01101 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01101-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01101-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01101 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي الشهاب السكندري المالكي . فيمن جده أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī, al-Shihāb, al-Sakandarī, al-Mālikī. This entry is for those whose grandfather is Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01102 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01102-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01102-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01102 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي السكندري المدني أخو محمد الآتي . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Sakandarī al-Madanī, brother of Muḥammad, whose biography will follow. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D01103 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01103-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01103-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01103 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن علي الفيلالي المغربي . كان كأبيه عالما صالحا حج ولقي بالقاهرة جماعة ومات في سنة ستين . أفادنيه بعض المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. ʿAli al-Faylali al-Maghribi. He was, like his father, a learned and righteous man. He performed the Hajj and met a group in Cairo. He died in the year 860 H. Some North Africans informed me of this."@en .

rec:AIND-D01106 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01106-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01106-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01106 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الشيخ علي أحد قراء الجوق . فيمن جده علي بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Shaykh ʿAlī, one of the reciters of the *jawq* (band/choir). His grandfather is ʿAlī b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01108 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01108-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01108-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01108 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن إبراهيم بن هاشم القمني الآتي أبوه وابنه البدر محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Ibrāhīm b. Hāshim al-Qamanī. His father and his son al-Badr Muḥammad will be mentioned later."@en .

rec:AIND-D01113 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01113-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01113-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01113 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن أحمد الشهاب أبو العباس الواسطي الأصل الغمري المحلي الشافعي أخو الشمس محمد الآتي . مات في يوم الأربعاء ثاني عشر ربيع الأول سنة ست وخمسين بالمحلة وقد رأيته كثيرا وسمعت أنه اشتغل وأقام بالأزهر مدة وفضل وما كان أخوه يحمد أمره وربما هجره رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Aḥmad, al-Shihāb Abū al-ʿAbbās, originally from Wāsiṭ, then from al-Ghamra and al-Maḥalla, a Shāfiʿī. Brother of al-Shams Muḥammad (mentioned below). He died on Wednesday, the 12th of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 856 H in al-Maḥalla. I (al-Sakhāwī) met him often. I heard that he engaged in study and resided at al-Azhar for a period, excelling in his fields. However, his brother did not approve of his conduct and perhaps abandoned him. May God have mercy on him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D01114 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01114-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01114-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01114-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01114 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن أحمد الشهاب النمراوي ثم المحلى صهر الغمري ويعرف بابن النخال . اشتغل يسيرا وسمع مني أشياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Aḥmad, with the laqab Shihāb al-Dīn, of Nimrāwī and later Maḥallī nisbahs. He was the son-in-law of al-Ghamrī and known as Ibn al-Nakhkhāl. He applied himself to study for a short period and heard various things from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01115 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01115-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01115-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01115-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01115 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن أحمد الشرنبابلي . سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D01116 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01116-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01116-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01116-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01116 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن أصلم الآتي أبوه وأخوه يحيى وهذا أكبرهما أو كان ظن ذاك أن يكون هو المشار إليه وكان هذا هو المتأخر مع عدم تصونه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Aṣlam. His father and his brother Yaḥyā will be mentioned later. He (Aḥmad) was the elder of the two, or it was thought that he was the one referred to, and he remained dissolute until late in life."@en .

rec:AIND-D01117 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01117-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01117-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01117-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01117 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن بدر الشهاب الدمشقي التاجر نزيل مكة ووالد محمد وأخو محمد الآتيين ويعرف بالجعجاع . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Badr, al-Shihāb al-Dimashqī, the merchant. A resident of Mecca and father of Muḥammad, and brother of Muḥammad (mentioned below). He was known as al-Jaʿjāʿ. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D01118 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01118-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01118-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01118-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01118 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن جعمان أبو العباس الصريفي ، من أهل بيت وصلاح ممن لا يشك من يراه أنه من كبار الأولياء الأخيار الأتقياء . مات في سنة أربع وثلاثين . ذكره العفيف ، وممن أخذ عنه ولده الجمال الطاهر الآتي في المحمدين وقريبه أبو القسم بن إبراهيم بن عبد الله الآتي أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Ṣarīfī, Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Jawmān. He was from a house of piety and righteousness, of whom no one who saw him would doubt that he was one of the great, virtuous, and pious saints. He died in 834. Al-ʿAfīf mentioned him. Among those who studied with him were his son, al-Jamāl al-Ṭāhir (who will be mentioned later in the section on Muḥammads), and his relative, Abū al-Qasim b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd Allāh (who will also be mentioned later)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01124 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01124-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01124-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01124 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن عبد الله الشاب التائب . هكذا سمي جده عبد الله المقريزي ثم ابن فهد ، وسماه شيخنا وغيره أحمد بن عيسى وقد تقدم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Shābb al-Tāʾib. Thus, his grandfather ʿAbd Allāh was named (identified in genealogy) by al-Maqrīzī and then by Ibn Fahd. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others, however, named him (the subject Aḥmad) as Aḥmad b. ʿĪsā. This has been mentioned previously."@en .

rec:AIND-D01129 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01129-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01129-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01129-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01129 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن محمد شهاب الدين بن المحب بن الشمس الخصوصي ثم القاهري الشافعي أخو أثير الدين محمد الآتي وسمع من الولي العراقي في أماليه كثيرا وتكسب بالشهادة وتميز فيها وتأخر عن أخيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad Shihāb al-Dīn b. al-Muḥibb b. al-Shams al-Khuṣūṣī, then al-Qāhirī, the Shāfiʿī. He was the brother of Athīr al-Dīn Muḥammad, who will be mentioned later. He heard much from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) from his dictations, earned his living through notarization (shahāda), excelled in it, but came after his brother."@en .

rec:AIND-D01130 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01130-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01130-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01130 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن محمد بن أبي بكر المرشدي المكي ابن عم أحمد ابن صالح بن محمد الماضي وشقيق أبي حامد ومحمد الآتي ممن حفظ القرآن والمنهاج وغيره وتكسب بإقراء الأبناء وبالعمر وكذا أحيانا بالسفر للطائف ونحوه وسمع مني بمكة في المجاورة الثالثة وهو خير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-Murshidī al-Makkī, paternal cousin of Aḥmad b. Ṣāliḥ b. Muḥammad al-Māḍī and brother of Abū Ḥāmid and Muḥammad al-Ātī. He memorized the Qurʾān and 『al-Minhāj』, and earned his livelihood by teaching children the Qurʾān and through ʿumra. He also sometimes traveled to al-Ṭāʾif and other places. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca during his third period of jāwara. He was a good person."@en .

rec:AIND-D01131 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01131-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01131-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01131-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01131-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01131 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن محمد بن عمر الشهاب القاهري ثم المنوفي الشافعي ويعرف بابن القنيني . ولد في سنة ست وثمانين وسبعمائة ونشأ بها فحفظ القرآن والعمدة والمنهاج وألفية ابن مالك وعرضها فيما أخبر على البلقيني والصدر المناوي والقويسني والدميري وغيرهم ، وقطن منوف ووقع على قضاتها ولقيته بها فاستجزته لقرائن تودي باعتماده في مقاله . مات قبل الستين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar, al-Shihāb, al-Qāhirī, then al-Munūfī, al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Qannīnī. He was born in the year 786 H and grew up there. He memorized the Qurʾān, al-ʿUmda, al-Minhāj, and Ibn Mālik's Alfiyya, and, as he reported, presented them to al-Bulqīnī, al-Ṣadr al-Manāwī, al-Quwaysnī, al-Damīrī, and others. He resided in Manūf and signed for its judges. I (al-Sakhāwī) met him there (in Manūf) and sought an ijāza from him, based on indications leading to his credibility in his statements. He died approximately before the age of sixty."@en .

rec:AIND-D01132 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01132-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01132-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01132 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن النجم أبي القسم عمر بن التقي محمد بن محمد بن أبي الخير محمد بن فهد المحب أبو الطيب الهاشمي المكي . مات وهو ابن ستين وخمسة أشهر في جمادى الآخرة سنة خمس وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Najm Abī al-Qasam ʿUmar b. al-Taqī Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Khayr Muḥammad b. Fahd al-Muḥibb Abū al-Ṭayyib al-Hāshimī al-Makkī. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year 845 H, at the age of sixty years and five months."@en .

rec:AIND-D01134 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01134-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01134-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01134-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01134-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D01134-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01134 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن محمد شهاب الدين النشيلي ثم القاهري الشافعي أخو محمد دلال الكتب . ممن اشتغل وقرأ على الخيضري ونحوه وعلى النشاوي وعبد الصمد الهرساني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Nashīlī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, brother of Muḥammad the bookseller. He was among those who engaged in study and read under al-Khayḍarī and similar figures, as well as under al-Nashāwī and ʿAbd al-Ṣamad al-Hrsānī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01135 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01135-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01135-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01135-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01135 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن محمد القاهري الشيخي الماوردي أخو ناصر الدين محمد الآتي . ممن سمع على شيخنا ختم البخاري بالظاهرية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "163 Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Qāhirī al-Shaykhī al-Māwardī. He was the brother of Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad, whose biography will follow. He was among those who heard our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)'s completion of al-Bukhārī at al-Ẓāhiriyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D01136 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01136-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01136-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01136-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01136 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن محمد المقدسي . ممن قرض للشهاب السيرجي نظما ونثرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Maqdisī. He was among those who composed poetry and prose (in praise) for al-Shihāb al-Sīrajī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01137 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01137-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01137-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01137-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01137 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن مطرف القرشي المكي السمان ويعرف بجده . مات بمكة في شوال سنة اثنتين وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Muṭarrif al-Qurashī al-Makkī al-Sammān, known by his grandfather. He died in Mecca in Shawwāl 842 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01138 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01138-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01138-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01138-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01138 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر بن معيبد وزير اليمن . مات سنة أربع وعشرين . ذكره ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Muʿaybid, the vizier of Yemen. He died in the year 824. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01142 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01142-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01142-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01142-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01142 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر الشهاب البلبيسي البزار ، مات في يوم الجمعة ثاني عشر رجب سنة ثمان وثلاثين وثمانمائة وقد جاز الثمانين وكان من خيار التجار ثقة ودينا وأمانة وصدق لهجة جاور عدة مجاورات بمكة وسمع الكثير وأنجب أولادا رحمه الله . قاله شيخنا في إنبائه وأظنه والد السراج عمر الآتي وإن سميت جده في ترجمة شيخنا محمدا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar, known as al-Shihāb al-Bilbaysī al-Bazzār, died on Friday, the twelfth of Rajab in the year 838 AH, having passed eighty years of age. He was among the best merchants, known for his trustworthiness, piety, integrity, and truthful speech. He undertook several extended stays (mujāwarāt) in Mecca and heard much [ḥadīth]. He begat children, may God have mercy on him. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ al-Ghumr, and I presume he is the father of al-Sirāj ʿUmar, who will be mentioned later, even though I named his (al-Sirāj ʿUmar's) grandfather as Muḥammad in [my] biography of our shaykh."@en .

rec:AIND-D01144 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01144-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01144-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01144-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01144-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01144 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر الشهاب السعودي البلان نقيب الذكارين بزاوية أبي السعود . مات في يوم الاثنين ثاني عشر ذي الحجة سنة تسع وستين وكان مشكور السيرة . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar, al-Shihāb al-Saʿūdī al-Ballān. He was the naqīb of the dhikr-reciters (Naqīb al-Dhakkārīn) at Zāwiyat Abī al-Suʿūd. He died on Monday, the twelfth of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 869 H. He was praised for his good conduct. Al-Munīr recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D01145 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01145-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01145-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01145-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01145 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عمر المصراتي القيرواني إمام جامع الزيتونة بتونس . مات بها في سنة تسع وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿUmar al-Miṣrātī al-Qayrawānī. Imām of the Zaytūna Mosque in Tunis. He died there in the year 889 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01146 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01146-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01146-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01146 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عيسى بن أحمد بن عيسى بن أحمد القاهري أخو أبي الفتح محمد الكتبي . له ذكر في أبيه ولم يكن بمحمود . مات قريب السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿĪsā b. Aḥmad b. ʿĪsā b. Aḥmad al-Qāhirī. Brother of Abū al-Fatḥ Muḥammad al-Kutubī. He is mentioned in his father's biography. He was not a praiseworthy individual. He died around the age of seventy."@en .

rec:AIND-D01147 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01147-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01147-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01147-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01147 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عيسى بن أحمد الشهاب الصنهاجي المغربي ثم القاهري الأزهري المالكي المقرئ نزيل جامع الأزهر . كان ماهرا في القراءات والعربية والفقه متصديا للإقراء جميع النهار وممن أخذ عنه الشمس القرافي . مات في سابع المحرم سنة سبع وعشرين وكثر التأسف عليه . ترجمه شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿĪsā b. Aḥmad, al-Shihāb, al-Ṣanhājī al-Maghribī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Azharī, al-Mālikī, al-Muqriʾ, resident of al-Azhar Mosque. He was skilled in Qurʾanic recitations, Arabic language, and Fiqh, devoting himself to teaching recitation throughout the day. Al-Shams al-Qarāfī was one of those who studied under him. He died on the 7th of Muḥarram in the year 827 H, and his passing was widely mourned. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) wrote his biography in Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D01154 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01154-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01154-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01154-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01154 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عيسى بن يوسف بن عمر بن عبد العزيز الهواري البنداري أمير عرب هوارة ويعرف بابن عمر . استقر بعد صرف أخيه سليمان الآتي إلى أن مات في أول سنة اثنتين وثمانين وكان أحسن حالا من أخيه واستقر بعده في الإمرة ابن أخيه داود بن سليمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿĪsā b. Yūsuf b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Hawwārī al-Bandārī, Amīr of the Hawwāra Arabs, known as Ibn ʿUmar. He was installed (in the emirate) after the dismissal of his brother Sulaymān (to be mentioned later), and remained until he died in the beginning of 882 H. He was in a better condition than his brother. His nephew Dāwūd b. Sulaymān succeeded him in the emirate."@en .

rec:AIND-D01155 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01155-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01155-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01155-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01155 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الشرف عيسى القيمري الخليلي الغزي . ولد سنة ست وخمسين وسبعمائة وسمع الكثير وحدث وروى أجاز لنا . قاله ابن أبي عذيبة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Sharaf ʿĪsā al-Qaymarī al-Khalīlī al-Ghazzī. Born in 756 AH. He listened much, transmitted and narrated ḥadīth, and granted us (al-Sakhāwī) ijāza. Ibn Abī ʿUdhayba said this."@en .

rec:AIND-D01156 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01156-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01156-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01156-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01156 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عيسى السنباطي الحنبلي . في ابن محمد بن عيسى بن يوسف ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D01157 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01157-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01157-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01157-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01157 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن عيسى العلوي نزيل مكة خال أبي عبد الله وأبي البركات وكمالية بني القاضي على النويري . مات بها في ذي القعدة سنة ست وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. ʿĪsā al-ʿAlawī, a resident of Mecca and the maternal uncle of Abū ʿAbd Allāh, Abū al-Barakāt, and Kamāliyya, the children of the judge ʿAlī al-Nuwayrī. He died there in Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 846 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01158 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01158-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01158-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01158-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01158 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن غلام الله بن أحمد بن محمد الشهاب الريشي القاهري الميقاتي . قال شيخنا في إنبائه كان اشتغل في فن النجوم وعرف كثيرا من الأحكام وصار يحل الزيج ويكتب التقاويم واشتهر بذلك . مات في صفر سنة ست وثلاثين وقد أناف على الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "185 Aḥmad b. Ghulām Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad, al-Shihāb al-Rīshī al-Qāhirī al-Mīqātī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Inbāʾ [al-Ghumr]: 'He engaged in the art of the stars (fann al-nujūm), knew much of astrological judgments (aḥkām), became skilled at calculating astronomical tables (zīj) and writing calendars (taqāwīm), and became famous for it. He died in Ṣafar of the year 836 H, having exceeded fifty years of age.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D01159 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01159-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01159-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01159-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01159 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي الفتح بن إسماعيل بن علي بن محمد بن داود شهاب الدين البيضاوي المكي الزمزمي الشافعي أخو محمد الآتي وأبوهما . ولد سنة ثمان وأربعين وثمانمائة وحفظ المنهاج وغيره وسمع على القاضي عبد القادر وباشر الأذان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī al-Fatḥ b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Dāwūd, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Bayḍāwī al-Makkī al-Zamzamī al-Shāfiʿī, brother of the forthcoming Muḥammad; their father (Abū al-Fatḥ) is also treated below. He was born in 848 H, memorized al-Minhāj and other works, heard from al-Qāḍī ʿAbd al-Qādir, and served as a muezzin."@en .

rec:AIND-D01160 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01160-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01160-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01160-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01160-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01160 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن قاسم بن أحمد بن عبد الحميد التميمي التونسي المالكي ويعرف بابن عاشر ، استقر به السلطان في مشيخة تربته بعد شيخه القلصاني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Qāsim b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Tamīmī al-Tūnisī al-Mālikī, known as Ibn ʿĀshir. The Sultan installed him in the shaykhship of his (the Sultan's) mausoleum, in succession to his (Aḥmad's) shaykh al-Qalaṣānī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01161 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01161-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01161-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01161-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01161 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن قاسم بن ملك بن عبد الله بن غانم الشريف العلوي المكي . كان مقيما بالروضة من وادي مر ، مات في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وأربعين بمكة ودفن بالمعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Qāsim b. Malik b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ghānim al-Sharīf al-ʿAlawī al-Makkī. He was residing in al-Rawḍa in Wādī Marr. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja 841 H in Makka and was buried in al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D01163 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01163-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01163-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01163-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01163 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي القسم بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن المغربي الخلوف . يأتي فيمن اسم أبيه محمد قريبا ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D01164 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01164-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01164-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01164 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي القسم بن محمد بن أحمد المحب النويري المكي الخطيب . يأتي في أحمد بن محمد ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D01167 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01167-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01167-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01167-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01167 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي القسم بن موسى بن محمد بن موسى العبدوسي . ذكره ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī al-Qāsim b. Mūsā b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā al-ʿAbdūsī. He was mentioned by Ibn ʿAzm."@en .

rec:AIND-D01169 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01169-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01169-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01169-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01169 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي القسم القسنطيني . ذكره ابن عزم أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī al-Qāsim al-Qusanṭīnī. Ibn ʿAzm also mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01170 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01170-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01170-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01170-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01170 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن قرطاي . مضى في ابن علي بن قرطاي ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D01171 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01171-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01171-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01171-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01171 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن قفيف بن فضيل بن ذحير ثلاثتها بالتصغير العدواتي خال محمد بن بدير ويعرف بأبيه . قتلهما الشريف محمد بن بركات عند مسجد الفتح بالقرب من الجموم من وادي مرفي يوم الخميس سابع المحرم سنة ثلاث وسبعين وحملا إلى مكة فدفنا بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Qufayf b. Fuḍayl b. Dhuḥayr (all three names in the diminutive) al-ʿAdawātī, maternal uncle of Muḥammad b. Budayr, known by his father. He and his sister's son Muḥammad b. Budayr were killed by al-Sharīf Muḥammad b. Barakāt near Masjid al-Fatḥ, close to al-Jumūm in Wādī Marfī, on Thursday, the 7th of Muḥarram in the year 873. Their bodies were transported to Mecca and buried there."@en .

rec:AIND-D01172 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01172-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01172-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01172-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01172 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن قوصون الدمشقي الشيخ المقري . مات في ليلة حادي عشر ذي الحجة سنة ست وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Qawṣūn al-Dimashqī, al-Shaykh, al-Muqriʾ. He died on the night of the eleventh of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 846."@en .

rec:AIND-D01173 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01173-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01173-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01173-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01173-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D01173-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01173 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن قياس بكسر أوله مخففا بن هند والشهاب بن الفخر الشيرازي الأصل القاهري الشافعي أخو محمد والد ناصر الدين محمد . مات سنة تسع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Qiyās (with kasra on the first letter, lightened) b. Hind and al-Shihāb b. al-Fakhr. Originally from Shīrāz, he resided in Cairo and was a Shāfiʿī scholar. He was the brother of Muḥammad and the father of Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad. He died in the year 819 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01175 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01175-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01175-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01175 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن لاجين الظاهر جقمق الآتي أبوه له ذكر فيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Lājīn al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq. His father (Lājīn) is treated in a later entry, and he is mentioned within it (his father's biography)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01182 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01182-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01182-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01182-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01182 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن عثمان بن سعيد الصفي أبو اللطائف بن الشمس الوزير المالكي أبوه الحنفي هو لأجل جده لأمه نور الدين السدميسي الحنفي . عرض علي في ربيع الأول سنة تسعين الأربعين النووية والكنز وسمع مني المسلسل بالأولية وكان معه المحب القلعي خازن المؤيدية ، وهو فطن لبيب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿUthmān b. Saʿīd al-Ṣafī Abū al-Laṭāʾif b. al-Shams al-Wazīr al-Mālikī. His father was a Mālikī, while he himself was a Ḥanafī on account of his maternal grandfather Nūr al-Dīn al-Sadmīsī al-Ḥanafī. In Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year ninety (890 AH), he presented to me (al-Sakhāwī) al-Arbaʿīn al-Nawawiyya and al-Kanz, and he heard from me al-Musalsal bi-l-Awwaliyya. Al-Muḥibb al-Qalʿī, the treasurer (khāzin) of al-Muʾayyadiyya, was with him. He is intelligent and discerning."@en .

rec:AIND-D01184 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01184-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01184-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01184-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01184 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الطيب بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن عيسى بن مطير الحكمي اليماني . تفقه بعمه أحمد وبالأزرق وغيرهما ومات بعد أبيه بنحو ثلاث سنين قاله الأهدل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Ṭayyib b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā b. Muṭayr al-Ḥakamī al-Yamānī. He studied jurisprudence with his paternal uncle Aḥmad, and al-Azraq, among others. He died approximately three years after his father, as stated by al-Ahdal."@en .

rec:AIND-D01186 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01186-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01186-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01186-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01186 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم الشهاب الشكيلي المدني ملقن الأموات بها . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة النبوية . مات بها في يوم الجمعة سادس عشر ربيع الآخر سنة تسع وثمانين وصلى عليه في عصره . كتب إلي بوفاته الفخر العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm, al-Shihāb al-Shakīlī al-Madanī, the prompter of the dead (mulaqqin al-amwāt) in Medina. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina. He died there on Friday, the 16th of Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 889 (AH). The funeral prayer was performed in the afternoon (ʿaṣr). Al-Fakhr al-ʿAynī wrote to me about his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D01187 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01187-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01187-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01187-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Fable_5,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01187 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم الخواجا شهاب الدين الكيلاني المكي ويعرف بشفتراش بمعجمة مضمومة وفاء أو موحدة وهي بالفارسية الحلاق . مات بمكة في ليلة الجمعة خامس صفر سنة سبع وستين . أرخه ابن فهد وكان مباركا حريصا على المبادرة للجماعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm al-Khawāja Shihāb al-Dīn al-Kīlānī al-Makkī. He was also known as Shuftarāsh — with ḍamma on the shīn, and either fāʾ or bāʾ [as the second letter] — which in Persian means 'the barber'. He died in Mecca on the eve of Friday (laylat al-jumʿa), the 5th of Ṣafar, in the year 867 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date. He was a blessed person and was eager to participate in congregational prayers."@en .

rec:AIND-D01188 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01188-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01188-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01188 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم الهندي . ممن أخذ عني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm al-Hindī. He was among those who took knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Makka."@en .

rec:AIND-D01190 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01190-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01190-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01190-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01190 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن إسماعيل بن داود الشهاب بن الشمس بن الشهاب القاهري الحنفي أخو عبد الله وأخويه ويعرف كسلفه بابن الرومي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. Dāwūd, al-Shihāb (laqab), son of al-Shams (father's laqab/name), son of al-Shihāb (grandfather's laqab/name), al-Qāhirī, al-Ḥanafī. He is the brother of ʿAbd Allāh and his two brothers. He is known, like his ancestors, as Ibn al-Rūmī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01198 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01198-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01198-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01198 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن السيف الشهاب الصالحي الحنبلي . سمع من علي بن العز عمر وفاطمة ابنة العز إبراهيم وغيرهما وحدث ، قال شيخنا في تاريخه ومعجمه : أجاز لي ومات في جمادى الآخرة سنة اثنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Sayf, al-Shihāb, from al-Ṣāliḥī, of the Hanbali madhhab. He heard (ḥadīth) from ʿAlī b. al-ʿIzz ʿUmar and Fāṭima bint al-ʿIzz Ibrāhīm, among others, and transmitted. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his history (Tarīkh) and dictionary (Muʿjam): \"He granted me ijāza.\" He died in Jumada al-Akhira in the year 802 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01204 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01204-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01204-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01204-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01204 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن الجمال عبد الله الغمري ثم القاهري الشافعي ويعرف كسلفه بابن المداح . حفظ القرآن وكتبا عرضها علي في جملة المشايخ وسمع علي ، وهو فطن ذكي وإلى سنة ست وتسعين لم يبلغ ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "228 Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Jamāl ʿAbd Allāh al-Ghamrī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, known like his ancestors as Ibn al-Maddāḥ. He memorized the Qur'an and presented books to me among a group of shaykhs, and he heard from me. He is astute and intelligent. As of the year 896 H, he had not yet reached adulthood."@en .

rec:AIND-D01205 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01205-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01205-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01205 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن عبد الله بن البريدي ربيب ابن المفضل . ممن سمع مني مع زوج أمه بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Buraydī, stepson of Ibn al-Mufaḍḍal. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo with his mother's husband."@en .

rec:AIND-D01207 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01207-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01207-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01207-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01207 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن عبد المحسن السبكي الحمصي الشافعي . أجاز لابن شيخنا وغيره بإخبار بن موسى المراكشي وصوابه محمد بن محمد كما في رحلة ابن موسى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Muḥsin al-Subkī al-Ḥimṣī al-Shāfiʿī. He granted ijāza to Ibn Shaykhinā (Ibn Ḥajar's son Muḥammad) and others, based on the report of Ibn Mūsā al-Marrākushī, though its correct name, as stated in the *Riḥlat Ibn Mūsā*, is Muḥammad b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01210 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01210-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01210-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01210-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01210 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن علي بن حسن الباريني ثم الطرابلسي الشافعي تلميذ التاج بن زهرة ويعرف بابن الشيخ علي . ممن سمع مني المسلسل بشرطه وقرأ علي في البخاري وسمع بعضه أيضا وكذا سمع على النشاوي والديمي وغيرهما وأجزت له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Ḥasan al-Bārīnī, then al-Ṭarābulusī al-Shāfiʿī. He was a student of al-Tāj b. Zuhra and was known as Ibn al-Shaykh ʿAlī. He is among those from whom I (al-Sakhāwī) heard al-Musalsal with its conditions, and he read al-Bukhārī to me, and also heard some of it from me. Likewise, he heard from al-Nashāwī, al-Daymī, and others. And I (al-Sakhāwī) granted him ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D01221 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01221-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01221-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01221 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن عيسى الميقاتي المناخلي . ذكره ابن عزم فلم يزد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Ahmad b. ʿIsa al-Mīqātī al-Manākhilī. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him but added no more."@en .

rec:AIND-D01234 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01234-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01234-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01234 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله الحراري . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن أبي الفضل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥarārī. He is mentioned in the entry for those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. Abī al-Faḍl."@en .

rec:AIND-D01238 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01238-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01238-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01238 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن عمر . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن محمد بن الحسين بن عمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar. He has already been mentioned in the entry for those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. al-Ḥusayn b. ʿUmar."@en .

rec:AIND-D01244 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01244-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01244-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01244 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن عطاء الله الشهاب بن الجمال ابن الناصر بن التنسي ابن عم الذي قبله والآتي أبوه وأنه غرق في سنة أربع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "266 Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAṭāʾ Allāh, al-Shihāb, Ibn al-Jamāl, Ibn al-Nāṣir, al-Tanasī. He was the cousin of the preceding person, and his father will be mentioned later. He drowned in the year 814 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01249 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01249-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01249-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01249 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أبي العباس أحمد بن محمد أبو العباس الأنصاري المكي الشافعي . مضى فيمن جد أبيه محمد بن عبد المعطي بن أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad b. Muḥammad Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Anṣārī al-Makkī al-Shāfiʿī. His biography is mentioned in the entry of his paternal grandfather, Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī b. Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01250 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01250-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01250-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01250 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن مظفر قطب الدين صاحب كجرات التي منها كهنات وأخو صاحبها الآن محمودشاه . وكأنه استقر بعد القطب وكان سفاكا منهمكا بحيث كان سبب موته إصابته بعود سيفه على ساقه أو نحوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Muẓaffar, Quṭb al-Dīn, master of Kajarāt, which is where his family was associated with priesthood. He was the brother of its current master Maḥmūd Shāh. It seems he became established after al-Quṭb. He was so bloodthirsty and deeply absorbed (in conflict/power) that the cause of his death was a blow from his sword hilt to his leg or similar."@en .

rec:AIND-D01253 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01253-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01253-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01253-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01253 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الولوي محمد بن أحمد بن يوسف بن حجاج السفطي الأصل القاهري . مات أبوه وهو صغير فنشأ غير متصون خصوصا وقد تدرب بخاله عبد البر بن الشحنة وذويه وخاصم أخته وغيرها . مات في"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Walawī Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Yūsuf b. Ḥajjāj al-Safaṭī (originally), al-Qāhirī. His father died when he was young, and he grew up undisciplined, especially having been trained by his maternal uncle ʿAbd al-Barr b. al-Shaḥna and his relatives, but he quarrelled with his sister and others. He died."@en .

rec:AIND-D01256 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01256-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01256-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01256 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد القاضي شهاب الدين بن قاضي القضاة الشمس بن الحلاوي الحلبي قاضيها الحنفي منفصلا في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وتسعين . أرخه ابن اللبودي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, al-Qāḍī Shihāb al-Dīn, grandson of Qāḍī al-Quḍāt al-Shams b. al-Ḥalāwī al-Ḥalabī, the Ḥanafī judge of Aleppo, was dismissed in Dhū al-Ḥijja 891 AH. Ibn al-Labbūdī recorded this."@en .

rec:AIND-D01257 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01257-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01257-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01257-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01257 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الشهاب الذهبي أبوه الصالحي من ذرية بني الأرموي ويعرف بابن الذهبي . ولد تقريبا سنة سبع وسبعين وسبعمائة وسمع من أبي الهول الجزري بفوت وحدث به سمعه منه الفضلاء كابن فهد ، ومات قبل دخول الشام ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, al-Shihāb al-Dhahabī. His father was al-Ṣāliḥī, from the progeny of Banū al-Armawī, and he (the subject) was known as Ibn al-Dhahabī. He was born approximately in 777 H. He heard from Abū al-Hawl al-Jazarī (with some lacunae, bi-fawt) and transmitted from him. Distinguished scholars like Ibn Fahd heard from him. He died before entering al-Shām."@en .

rec:AIND-D01258 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01258-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01258-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01258 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الشهاب القسطلاني المكي المالكي . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن حسن بن الزين محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Qasṭalānī al-Makkī al-Mālikī. He was mentioned in the entry for those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. al-Zayn Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01259 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01259-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01259-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01259-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01259-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01259 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن فخر الدين محمد بن الشهاب أحمد القرشي القاهري الحنفي والد قاسم الآتي ويعرف بابن السبع ، باشر النقابة عند الكمال بن العديم وولده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad, son of Fakhr al-Dīn Muḥammad, grandson of al-Shihāb Aḥmad al-Qurashī al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī. He was the father of Qāsim (mentioned later) and was known as Ibn al-Sabʿ. He held the office of Naqāba with al-Kamāl b. al-ʿAdīm and his son."@en .

rec:AIND-D01260 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01260-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01260-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01260-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01260 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن السيف الحنبلي . مضى في السين المهملة من أجداد الأب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Sayf, al-Ḥanbalī. He was previously mentioned in the Sīn Muhmala section concerning his paternal grandfathers."@en .

rec:AIND-D01261 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01261-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01261-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01261 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الشهاب بن الشمس المصري ويعرف بابن الشيخ . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shihāb b. al-Shams al-Miṣrī, also known as Ibn al-Shaykh. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D01262 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01262-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01262-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01262 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الشريف شهاب الدين بن كندة . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Sharīf Shihāb al-Dīn b. Kinda. One of those who studied with me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D01264 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01264-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01264-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01264-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01264 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد المدني ويعرف بابن المرجح . ممن أخذ عني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Madanī, known as Ibn al-Murajjaḥ. He was among those who studied under me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D01267 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01267-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01267-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01267 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الشهاب الأسنوي ثم القاهري شقيق عبد الكريم وابن أخت الشرف الأنصاري وأخته . ولد سنة ست وأربعين أو التي بعدها وحفظ القرآن وزوج ابنه بخاله الشرف من أمه وتكسب بالتجارة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, al-Shihāb al-Asnawī, then al-Qāhirī. He was the brother of ʿAbd al-Karīm, the maternal nephew of al-Sharaf al-Anṣārī, and had a sister. He was born in the year 846 H or the one after (847 H), memorized the Qur'an, married his son to the daughter of his maternal uncle al-Sharaf, and made a living through trade."@en .

rec:AIND-D01268 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01268-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01268-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01268-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01268 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الشهاب المشهدي القاهري الزركشي الحنبلي . ممن اشتغل وفهم وسمع ختم البخاري على أم هانئ الهورينية ومن كان معها وقرأ في الجوق وتكسب بالشهادة ثم كف مع ملازمته حضور بعض وظائفه وكان حاد الخلق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, al-Shihāb al-Mashhadī al-Qāhirī al-Zarkashī al-Ḥanbalī. He was among those who strived and understood. He heard the completion of al-Bukhārī from Umm Hāniʾ al-Hawrīnīya and those who were with her, recited in the choir (al-Jawq), and earned his living as a witness. He later retired while continuing to attend some of his duties. He was of a sharp temperament."@en .

rec:AIND-D01272 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01272-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01272-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01272-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01272 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد البسطامي . ممن أخذ عني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Bisṭāmī. Among those who took from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D01273 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01273-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01273-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01273-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01273 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد البسكري المغربي المدني بن حامد أخو محمد الآتي ممن أخذ عني بالمدينة في مجاورتي بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Biskrī al-Maghribī al-Madanī, son of Ḥāmid, brother of the aforementioned Muḥammad, was among those who acquired knowledge from me in Medina during my stay there."@en .

rec:AIND-D01274 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01274-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01274-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01274-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01274 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد السلي . كذا قاله ابن عزم وأنه مات سنة بضع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Sulī. According to Ibn ʿAzm, he died in a year in the 830s."@en .

rec:AIND-D01275 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01275-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01275-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01275-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01275 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الحجازي . ممن أخذ عني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Ḥijāzī. One of those who studied under me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D01276 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01276-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01276-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01276 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد المالكي . عرض عليه ابن فهد بعض محافيظه في موسم سنة اثنتين وعشرين بمكة وأجازه وأورده في شيوخه وقال أنه لم يعرفه وأظنه ابن النسخة الماضي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "295 Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Mālikī. Ibn Fahd presented some of his memorized texts to him during the pilgrimage season of the year 822 H in Mecca, and he (Aḥmad b. Muḥammad) granted him ijāza. He is listed among Ibn Fahd's shaykhs, and Ibn Fahd stated that he did not know him well and presumed him to be the son of al-Nuskha mentioned previously (الماضي قريبا)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01277 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01277-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01277-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01277 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الخطيب بمنية سمنود . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Khaṭīb from Minyat Samannūd. Among those who acquired (knowledge) from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D01278 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01278-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01278-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01278-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01278 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الهدوي . مضى قريبا فيمن يلقب سواسوا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Hadawī. He was mentioned recently among those surnamed Sawā-Sawā."@en .

rec:AIND-D01282 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01282-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01282-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01282 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن إسماعيل الصفدي الحسري . ممن سمع علي بمكة في المجاورة الثالثة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "300. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl al-Ṣafadī al-Ḥasrī. Among those who listened to me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca during the third *jāwara* (extended stay)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01283 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01283-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01283-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01283-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01283 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن إسماعيل المجدي ويلقب ينوص لشدة شقرة شعره . كان يباشر أوقاف الحنفية حسن المباشرة . مات في ربيع الأول سنة إحدى . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl al-Majdī, nicknamed Yanūṣ due to the intense reddishness of his hair. He diligently managed the endowments of the Hanafi school. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of a year ending in one (read as 801 H). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated this in his book 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』."@en .

rec:AIND-D01285 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01285-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01285-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01285-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01285 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أيدمر الشهاب أبو العباس الأبار . سمع على صدقة الركني العادلي تصنيفه منهاج الطريق وحدث به في سنة عشرين . وممن سمعه منه النور بن الركاب المقري ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aydamar, al-Shihāb Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Abbār. He heard from Ṣadaqa al-Ruknī al-ʿĀdilī his composition 『Minhāj al-Ṭarīq』 and transmitted it in the year 820 H. Among those who heard it from him was al-Nūr b. al-Rakkāb al-Muqrī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01287 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01287-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01287-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01287-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01287-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01287 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن بطيخ شهاب الدين . أحد فضلاء الأطباء وخيارهم تنزل في الجهات وكان عاقلا بهي المنظر متوددا . مات في وله ذكر في أخيه على ابن بطيخ ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "305 Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Baṭṭīkh, Shihāb al-Dīn. He was one of the excellent physicians and the best of them, and he resided in various regions. He was intelligent, handsome in appearance, and amiable. He died in [incomplete]. He (i.e. his father) is mentioned in the biography of the latter's brother, ʿAlī b. Baṭṭīkh (the subject's paternal uncle, #AIND-D05073); cf. the father's entry #AIND-D09616."@en .

rec:AIND-D01288 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01288-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01288-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01288-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b87_merge ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01288 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن المحب محمد بن بلكا القادري . اعتنى به أبوه فأسمعه بقراءتي وعلي ولم يلبث أن مات بالطاعون سنة أربع وستين وكان رفيقا لولدي عوضهما الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Muḥibb Muḥammad b. Balkā al-Qādirī. His father took care of him and made him listen to my recitation and to ʿAlī. He did not tarry long before he died of the plague in the year 864 AH. He was a companion to my son. May Allah compensate both of them with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D01290 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01290-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01290-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01290 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن الحسين بن عمر أبو الرضى بن الجمال أبي اليمن المراغي المدني أخو الحسين الآتي . سمع على جده في سنة خمس عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. al-Ḥusayn b. ʿUmar, Abū al-Riḍā b. al-Jamāl Abī al-Yaman al-Marāghī al-Madanī, brother of al-Ḥusayn (mentioned below). He heard from his grandfather in the year 815 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01292 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01292-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01292-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01292-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01292-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01292 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن سعد الله الواسطي . يأتي فيمن جده أبو بكر بن محمد بن سعد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. Saʿd Allāh al-Wāsiṭī. He will be mentioned later in the section on those whose grandfather is Abū Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Saʿd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D01305 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01305-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01305-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01305-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01305-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01305 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن محمد القسطلاني . مضى فيمن جده أبو بكر بن عبد الملك بن محمد بن أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad al-Qasṭallānī. His grandfather, Abū Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Malik b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, has already been mentioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D01308 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01308-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01308-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01308-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01308 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن النجم محمد بن أبي بكر الشهاب المرجاني الأصل المكي . مضى فيمن جده أبو بكر بن علي بن يوسف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Najm Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-Shihāb al-Marjānī, originally from Mecca. He was mentioned among those whose grandfather is Abū Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf."@en .

rec:AIND-D01309 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01309-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01309-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01309-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01309 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن حاجي بن دانيال الشهاب أبو العباس الكيلاني الشافعي المقرئ ويعرف بالحافظ الأعرج ، برع في فنون وأتقن القراءات مع ابن الجزري وغيره وأقرأها غير واحد ، وممن قرأ عليه جعفر السنهوري ، وأثبت شيخنا اسمه في القراء بمصر في وسط هذا القرن ، ومات في الطاعون بعد الأربعين . ###$ | 417366805220$# $$$ أحمد بن محمد بن حذيفة المسيري . مضى فيمن جده أحمد رأيته منسوبا لذلك فيمن سمع على التقي بن فهد بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "324 Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥājjī b. Dāniyāl, known by the honorific Shihāb Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Kīlānī, a Shāfiʿī Qurʾān reciter (muqriʾ), and recognized as al-Ḥāfiẓ al-Aʿraj (the Lame Ḥāfiẓ). He excelled in various scholarly disciplines and mastered the Qurʾānic recitations (qirāʾāt) with Ibn al-Jazarī and others, teaching them to many. Among those who recited to him was Jaʿfar al-Sanhūrī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his name among the reciters in Egypt in the middle of this century (9th Hijri century). He died in the plague after the 840s."@en .

rec:AIND-D01310 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01310-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01310-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01310-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01310 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن حذيفة المسيري . مضى فيمن جده أحمد رأيته منسوبا لذلك فيمن سمع على التقي بن فهد بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Hudhayfa al-Misīrī. He was mentioned earlier among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad. I saw him ascribed as such among those who heard from al-Taqī ibn Fahd in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D01311 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01311-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01311 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن حسب الله القرشي المكي ويعرف بابن الزعيم . مات أبوه وهو صغير فاستولى أخوه على ماله وفات منه وعوضه بيسير من النقد فأضاعه الآخر واحتاج إلى أن صار يتكسب بالخياطة ثم عاجلته المنية بالاخترام في منتصف جمادى الآخرة سنة تسع بمكة ودفن بالمعلاة عن نحو ثلاثين فأزيد . قاله الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasab Allāh al-Qurashī al-Makkī, also known as Ibn al-Zaʿīm. His father died when he was young, and his brother seized his inheritance, which was lost. He was then compensated with a small amount of cash, which he also squandered, and he became in need to earn a living by tailoring. His life was cut short by death in the middle of Jumādā al-Ākhira in the year 809 in Mecca, and he was buried in al-Muʿallā, at the age of around thirty or more. This was stated by al-Fāsī in his work on Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D01313 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01313-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01313-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01313 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن حسن بن علي بن عبد الرحيم اللقاني الأصل القاهري أحد فضلاء المالكية أبوه . أثكله أبواه وقد قارب المراهقة في ربيع الثاني سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm, originally from al-Laqānī and a resident of Cairo, was one of the eminent scholars of the Maliki school. His parents were bereaved of him (he died) when he was nearing adolescence in Rabīʿ al-Thānī of the year 895 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01314 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01314-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01314-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01314-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_apply ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01314 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن حسن بن كريم بضم أوله البعلي التاجر . سمع في سنة خمس وتسعين ببلده صحيح البخاري على التقي عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن ابن الزعبوب أنابه الحجار وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء . ومات قبل رحلتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "328. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Kuraym (with the first letter vocalized with ḍamma), al-Baʿlī, the merchant. He heard *Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī* in his hometown in the year 895 from al-Taqī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Ibn al-Zaʿbūb, whom al-Ḥajjār deputized, and (al-Ḥajjār) transmitted (ḥadīth). The excellent ones heard from him. He died before my (al-Sakhāwī's) journey."@en .

rec:AIND-D01315 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01315-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01315-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01315 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن حسين بن إبراهيم . مضى في أحمد بن مباركشاه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn b. Ibrāhīm. See the entry for Aḥmad b. Mubārakshāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D01317 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01317-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01317-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01317 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن حسين الشهاب بن الشمس الأوتاري المقدسي الشافعي الآتي أبوه . ولد سنة اثنتين وعشرين وثمانمائة ببيت المقدس واشتغل وتميز وكان مقرئا أديبا ناظما ناثرا صاحب فنون . مات في يوم الأربعاء سابع رجب سنة أربع وسبعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn al-Shihāb b. al-Shams al-Awtārī al-Maqdisī al-Shāfiʿī. His father is mentioned later. He was born in 822 AH in Bayt al-Maqdis, studied diligently and excelled, and was a reciter, man of letters, poet, prose writer, and master of various arts. He died on Wednesday, the 7th of Rajab, in 874 AH. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01318 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01318-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01318-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01318 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن حمزة بن عبد الله بن علي بن عمر بن حمزة الشهاب العمري الحراني الأصل المدني والد عبد القادر الآتي ويعرف بالحجار . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥamza b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. Ḥamza, al-Shihāb al-ʿUmarī, originally from Ḥarrān, resident of Medina. He was the father of ʿAbd al-Qādir (mentioned below) and was known as al-Ḥajjār. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D01321 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01321-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01321-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01321-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01321-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01321 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن رجب شهاب الدين بن ناصر الدين أحد الأمراء العشرات بالديار المصرية وحجابها الصغار . مات في يوم الأحد حادي عشر رجب سنة خمس وكان شابا جميل الصورة شجاعا باسلا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Rajab Shihāb al-Dīn b. Nāṣir al-Dīn, one of the amirs of ten and minor chamberlains in the Egyptian lands. He died on Sunday, the 11th of Rajab in the year 5 AH. He was a handsome, brave, and valiant young man."@en .

rec:AIND-D01323 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01323-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01323-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01323-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01323 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن سعيد الشهاب الشرعبي اليماني التعزي الشافعي المقرئي نزيل السميساطية من دمشق إمام عالم مقرئ مفنن أديب بارع لقيه البقاعي وقال أنه ولد باليمن سنة خمس وتسعين تقريبا . ومات في يوم الخميس ثاني عشري ذي الحجة سنة سبع وثلاثين بدمشق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Saʿīd, al-Shihāb (honorific), al-Sharʿabī, al-Yamānī, al-Taʿizzī, a Shāfiʿī jurist and Qurʾān reciter. He resided at al-Sumaysāṭīya in Damascus and excelled as an imam, scholar, Qurʾān reciter, versatile master, and man of letters. Al-Biqāʿī met him and stated that he was born in Yemen around 795 H. He died in Damascus on Thursday, 22 Dhū al-Ḥijja, 837 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01324 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01324-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01324-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01324 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن سعيد الحمصي الشافعي . ولد في ثاني عشر ذي القعدة سنة ست عشرة وثمانمائة وقال أنه سمع من شيخنا المسلسل وأنه أخذ عن الشرف المناوي وبلديه الشمس بن العصياتي ولقيه الشمس بن مسدد المدني بعد الثمانين فأخذ عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Saʿīd al-Ḥimṣī al-Shāfiʿī. He was born on the 12th of Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 816 H. He stated that he heard al-Musalsal from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and that he acquired knowledge from al-Sharaf al-Manāwī and his fellow countryman al-Shams b. al-ʿAṣyātī. Al-Shams b. Musaddad al-Madīnī met him after 880 H and acquired knowledge from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01327 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01327-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01327-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01327 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن سبيل الطاهري المدني . ممن أخذ عني بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Sabīl al-Ṭāhirī al-Madanī. He was among those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D01328 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01328-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01328-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01328 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن شعبان الصالحي القصار بن الجوازة . مات سنة أربع عشرة . ذكره ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Shaʿbān al-Ṣāliḥī al-Qaṣṣār b. al-Jawwāza. He died in the year 814 AH. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01332 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01332-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01332-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01332 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن صالح المسيري الرجل الصالح المجذوب نزيل ناحية منية ابن سلسل ويعرف بالخشاب . ولد قبل سنة سبعين وسبعمائة فيما أحسب وكان البرهان بن عليبة يحفظ كثيرا من كراماته وماجرياته وأثبته البقاعي في معجمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ṣāliḥ al-Misīrī, a pious man (al-Rajul al-Ṣāliḥ), a Majdhūb (sufi ecstatic), resided in the district of Mīnyat Ibn Silsil and was known as al-Khashshāb. He was born before 770 H, as I (al-Sakhāwī) reckon. Al-Burhān b. ʿUlayba used to memorize many of his miracles (karāmāt) and events, and al-Biqāʿī attested this in his dictionary."@en .

rec:AIND-D01334 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01334-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01334-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01334-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1_B88 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01334 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن صدقة الشهاب المصري القادري الشافعي أحد الصوفية بالصلاحية والجماعة القادرية . وجدت معه أوراقا بعرض العمدة على البلقيني وابن الملقن والعراقي والدميري وغيرهم فيها كشط بمحل اسمه فأعرضت عنها مع إمكانه ولكنه قد سمع الشاطبية على الشرف بن الكويك والزراتيتي مع شيخنا الزين رضوان فاستجزناه لذلك . مات في حدود الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ṣadaqa, al-Shihāb al-Miṣrī al-Qādirī al-Shāfiʿī, one of the Sufis at al-Ṣalāḥīya and the Qādirī order. I (al-Sakhāwī) found with him papers regarding the presentation of al-ʿUmda to al-Bulqīnī, Ibn al-Mulaqqin, al-ʿIrāqī, al-Damīrī and others. There was an erasure in the place of his (Aḥmad's) name on these papers, so I disregarded them, despite their potential validity. However, he did hear al-Shāṭibiyya from al-Sharaf b. al-Kuwayk, al-Zarātītī, and our shaykh al-Zayn Riḍwān. Therefore, we sought ijāza from him (al-Zayn Riḍwān) for it. He died around the age of sixty."@en .

rec:AIND-D01335 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01335-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01335-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01335-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01335 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن طلاداي شهاب الدين الباسطي لسكناه حارة عبد الباسط الحنفي المقري ويعرف بدقماق . ممن لازمني يسيرا في قراءة الشفا وغيره وقرأ على الزين جعفر السنهوري ثم على الناصري الأخميمي في القراءات وحفظ الشاطبية وربما اشتغل في العربية ولست أحمده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ṭallādāy, Shihāb al-Dīn al-Bāsṭī, a Ḥanafī Qurʾān reciter known as Dukmāq, due to his residence in Ḥārat ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ. He accompanied me (al-Sakhāwī) for a short period while studying 『al-Shifāʾ』 and other works. He studied Qurʾān recitation with al-Zayn Jaʿfar al-Sanhūrī, and then with al-Nāṣirī al-Akhmīmī, memorizing 『al-Shāṭibiyya』. He may also have been involved in Arabic language studies, but I do not praise him for that."@en .

rec:AIND-D01336 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01336-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01336-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01336 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عاصد الفريابي الشامي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿĀṣid al-Faryābī al-Shāmī. One of those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Makka."@en .

rec:AIND-D01337 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01337-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01337-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01337 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي عبد الله محمد بن أبي العباس بن عبد المعطي . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن محمد بن عبد المعطي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. Abī al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī. He was mentioned in the entry of one whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01338 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01338-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01338-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01338 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أبي العباس الحفصي ابن أخي السلطان أبي فارس وصاحب بجاية . مات في سنة عشر فقرر السلطان بدله أخاه الدبال محمد . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Ḥafṣī, son of Muḥammad, son of Abū al-ʿAbbās. He was the nephew of Sultan Abū Fāris and the ruler of Bijāya. He died in the year 810 H. Consequently, the Sultan appointed his brother, al-Dabbāl Muḥammad, in his place. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned this in his *Inbāʾ al-Ghumr*."@en .

rec:AIND-D01340 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01340-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01340-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01340-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01340 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الحق بن أحمد بن محمد بن محمد السنباطي ثم القاهري شقيق الشرف عبد الحق الآتي . ممن سمع على جماعة من الشيوخ وحج مع أيبه وجاور يسيرا وسافر وتقلب به في أحوال لم ينجح في جملة منها وتعب قلب أخيه بسببه مع حبه له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Ḥaqq b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Sunbāṭī, then al-Qāhirī, brother of al-Sharaf ʿAbd al-Ḥaqq (mentioned later). He heard from a group of shaykhs, performed the Hajj with his father, resided briefly in Mecca, and traveled. He experienced various circumstances, many of which he did not succeed in, causing his brother's heart distress despite his love for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01343 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01343-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01343-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01343 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد رب النبي الشهاب البدراني . ممن سمع مني بمكة في سنة أربع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Rabb al-Nabī, al-Shihāb al-Badrānī. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca in the year 894 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01344 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01344-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01344-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01344 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد المحمود السهروردي البغدادي . ممن شارك والده في الأخذ عن السراج القزويني أخذ عنه العز عبد العزيز بن علي البغدادي القاضي في سنة إحدى عشرة وثمانمائة وأظنه كان حنبليا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Maḥmūd al-Suhrawardī al-Baghdādī. He participated with his father in acquiring knowledge from al-Sirāj al-Qazwīnī. Al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī al-Baghdādī al-Qāḍī studied under him in the year 811 H. I believe he was Hanbali."@en .

rec:AIND-D01346 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01346-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01346-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01346 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أحمد بن خليف بن عيسى الشهاب أبو الخطاب بن الإمام أبي حامد المطري المدني الشافعي أخو المحب محمد الآتي . سمع على أبي الحسن المحلي سبط الزبير ومن قبله على الزين المراغي في سنة خمس عشرة وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Khalīf b. ʿĪsā, al-Shihāb Abū al-Khaṭṭāb, from the family of al-Imām Abū Ḥāmid al-Maṭarī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī. He is the brother of al-Muḥibb Muḥammad, who will be mentioned later. He heard from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Maḥallī (Sibṭ al-Zubayr), and before that, in the year 815 H, he heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01347 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01347-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01347-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01347 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أحمد بن التقي سليمان بن حمزة الصالحي الحنبلي الآتي أبوه ويعرف بابن زريق . أسره اللنكية وهو شاب ابن عشر سنين فمات أبوه أسفا عليه كما سيأتي عوضهما الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "359 Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Taqī Sulaymān b. Ḥamza al-Ṣāliḥī al-Ḥanbalī. His father will be mentioned later. He is known as Ibn Zurayq. He was captured by the army of Tīmūr (al-Lankiya) when he was a youth of about ten years old, and his father consequently died of grief over him, as will also be mentioned later. May Allah compensate them with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D01353 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01353-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01353-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01353 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن أبي زيد شيخ المسر . ذكره ابن عزم كذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Abū Zayd, shaykh al-misar (vocalization and meaning uncertain; the word is left as in the original). Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him thus."@en .

rec:AIND-D01354 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01354-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01354-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01354 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن السطوحي المنير من المشايخ الأحمدية . لازمني في الإملاء وغيره مدة بل وقرأ علي في البخاري والمجلس الذي عملته في ختمه وتمسح على طريقتهم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Saṭūḥī al-Munīr. He was one of the shaykhs of the Aḥmadiyya order. He accompanied me (al-Sakhāwī) for a period during dictation and other studies. He also read to me from al-Bukhārī and attended the completion session I held for it, seeking blessings according to their tradition."@en .

rec:AIND-D01359 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01359-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01359-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01359-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01359 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الغني الأزدي السكندري ويعرف بابن شافع ولد في رمضان سنة سبع وعشرين وسبعمائة وأسمع على ابن الصفى وغيره قال شيخنا في معجمه قرأت عليه مشيخة الرازي ومات بعد القرن بيسير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī al-Azdī al-Sakandarī, known as Ibn Shāfiʿ. He was born in Ramaḍān in the year 727 AH. He heard (ḥadīth) from Ibn al-Ṣafā and others. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his dictionary, \"I read to him Mashyakhat al-Rāzī.\" He died shortly after the turn of the century."@en .

rec:AIND-D01363 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01363-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01363 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد اللطيف بن أبي السرور الشهاب أبو السرور بن القطب أبي الخير الحسني الفاسي الأصل المكي المالكي أخو عبد اللطيف الآتي هو وأبوهما . عرض علي بالقاهرة محافيظه وسمع علي بقراءة أبيه وغيره وهو الآن سنة سبع وتسعين إما بالروم أو حلب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Abī al-Surūr, al-Shihāb Abū al-Surūr, son of al-Quṭb Abī al-Khayr, al-Ḥasanī, of Fāsī origin, al-Makkī, al-Mālikī. He is the brother of ʿAbd al-Laṭīf (to be mentioned later), and their father will also be mentioned. He presented his memorized texts to me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo and heard from me, through the recitation of his father and others. He is now, in the year 897, either in al-Rūm or Ḥalab."@en .

rec:AIND-D01370 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01370-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01370-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01370 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله بن حمام . مضى فيمن جده عبد الله بن إبراهيم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥammām. Mentioned previously among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D01377 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01377-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01377-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01377 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله بن التقي محمد بن أحمد الشهاب القرشي العمري الحرازي المكي الشافعي ابن عم الذي قبله . مات بمكة في ليلة الأحد ثالث رجب سنة ست وستين . أرخه ابن فهد أيضا ، وهو ممن لازم البرهاني بن ظهيرة وانتفع به وانجذب ثم صح . رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "388 Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Taqī Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Qurashī al-ʿUmarī al-Ḥarāzī al-Makkī al-Shāfiʿī, cousin of the preceding person. He died in Mecca on the night of Sunday, the 3rd of Rajab in the year 866. Ibn Fahd also recorded his death. He adhered to al-Burhānī b. Ẓahīra, benefited from him, was drawn to him, and then became firm (in faith). May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01378 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01378-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01378-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01378-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01378 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله بن محمد العمري المصري الأصل المكي لخواص الآتي أبوه . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-ʿUmarī, of Egyptian origin, a resident of Mecca. His special biographical details are mentioned in the forthcoming entry for his father. He is among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D01380 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01380-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01380-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01380 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله التاج السكندري بن الخراط . فيمن جده أحمد بن عبد الله بن عمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Tāj al-Sakandarī Ibn al-Kharrāṭ. (This entry is for the one) who is distinct from the individual whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar."@en .

rec:AIND-D01382 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01382-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01382-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01382 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله الشهاب بن الناصح . يأتي فيمن جده محمد لا عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Shihāb b. al-Nāṣiḥ. He will appear in the section for those whose grandfather is Muḥammad, not ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D01383 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01383-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01383-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01383 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله الشهاب الدمشقي الصالحي الذنابي . ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "392 Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Shihāb al-Dimashqī al-Ṣāliḥī al-Dhanābī. He was among those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01386 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01386-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01386-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01386 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله الطيب التونسي ويعرف بالسقطي . ممن أخذ عني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṭayyib al-Tūnisī, known as al-Saqaṭī. He was among those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī) in al-Madīna."@en .

rec:AIND-D01387 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01387-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01387-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01387 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله بلكا . في أحمد بن محمد بن بلكا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh Balkā. [His biography is found] under Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Balkā."@en .

rec:AIND-D01390 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01390-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01390-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01390 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الوهاب بن علي بن يوسف الشهاب بن القاضي فتح الدين أبي الفتح الأنصاري الزرندي المدني الحنفي أخو سعد وسعيد وعبد الله ومحمد وهو وسعيد أفضل أخوتهما . مات في رمضان سنة أربع وستين ولم يعقب ذكرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf, al-Shihāb (a laqab meaning \"shooting star\"), son of the judge Fatḥ al-Dīn Abū al-Fatḥ al-Anṣārī al-Zarandī al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī. He was the brother of Saʿd, Saʿīd, ʿAbd Allāh, and Muḥammad, and he and Saʿīd were the most excellent of their brothers. He died in Ramadan of the year 864 H. He left no male offspring."@en .

rec:AIND-D01391 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01391-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01391-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01391 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عبية المقدسي . يأتي بإثبات محمد ثان قبل عبية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUbayya al-Maqdisī. The text notes a clarification: 'comes with the affirmation of a second Muḥammad before ʿUbayya,' implying the full name should be Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUbayya al-Maqdisī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01392 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01392-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01392 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عثمان بن أيوب شهاب الدين الأشليمي ثم القاهري أخو الشرف محمد الأصيلي والنور علي الأشليمي ووالد النجم محمد . نشأ فقرأ القرآن وتكلم في أوقاف أخيه فحمد تصرفه وطاب أمره مع تقصيره عن أخويه في الاشتغال في الجملة وتأخره عنهما في السن وله حرص على الجماعة وإقبال على شأنه وملازمة لتصوفيه ووظائفه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "399. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān b. Ayyūb, Shihāb al-Dīn, originally from al-Ashlīmī, then al-Qāhirī. He was the brother of al-Sharaf Muḥammad al-Aṣīlī and al-Nūr ʿAlī al-Ashlīmī, and the father of al-Najm Muḥammad. He grew up and recited the Qur'an, and spoke concerning his brother's endowments, and his management was praised and his affairs were good, despite his shortcomings compared to his two brothers in terms of overall diligence in studies and being younger than them. He was eager for congregational prayer, devoted to his own affairs, and adhered to his Sufism and his duties."@en .

rec:AIND-D01393 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01393-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01393-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01393 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عثمان بن سليمان الشهاب بن المحب القرمي الأصل القاهري الحنفي أخو إبراهيم ومحمد ويعرف كأبيه بابن الأشقر . استقر في مشيخة الخانقاه السرياقوسية عوضا عن أبيه وانفصل عنها ثم أعيد ثم رغب عنها لأخيه الأصغر وكان مخمول الحركات مبذرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān b. Sulaymān (al-Shihāb, Ibn al-Muḥibb) was originally from Qarm, resided in Cairo, and was a Hanafi scholar. He was the brother of Ibrāhīm and Muḥammad, and like his father, was known as Ibn al-Ashqar. He assumed the shaykhdom of the Khānqāh al-Saryāqūsiyya in place of his father, was subsequently dismissed, then reinstated, but later relinquished the position to his younger brother. He was inconspicuous in his actions and extravagant."@en .

rec:AIND-D01394 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01394-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01394 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عثمن بن عبد الله وقيل أيوب بدل عبد الله الشهاب بن القاضي أصيل الدين الأشليمي القاهري والد ناصر الدين محمد الآتي ويعرف بابن أصيل . ناب في الحكم ومات في صفر سنة تسع عشرة مطعونا . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān b. ʿAbd Allāh (it is also said Ayyūb instead of ʿAbd Allāh), al-Shihāb, son of al-Qāḍī Aṣīl al-Dīn al-Ashlīmī al-Qāhirī, father of Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad (mentioned later). He was known as Ibn Aṣīl. He served as deputy in judgment and died of plague in Ṣafar of the year 819. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his *Anbāʾ*."@en .

rec:AIND-D01398 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01398-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01398-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01398-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01398 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عثمان الشهاب النحريري ثم القاهري الضرير نزيل الظاهرية القديمة ومن بقايا شيوخها المكثرين من الجلوس ببابها . مات في ليلة الاثنين رابع رجب سنة تسع وسبعين عن سن عالية سامحه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "405. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān, al-Shihāb al-Naḥrīrī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Ḍarīr, a resident of al-Ẓāhiriyya al-Qadīma and one of its remaining shaykhs who used to frequently sit at its gate. He died on the night of Monday, the fourth of Rajab, in the year 879 [AH], at an advanced age. May God forgive him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D01399 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01399-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01399 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عثمان البربهاري المكي الدهان ويعرف بجده . مات بمكة في شعبان سنة سبع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān al-Barbahārī al-Makkī al-Dahhān. He was known by his grandfather's name. He died in Makka in Shaʿbān 777 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01400 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01400-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01400-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01400 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عثمان المزملاتي . في من جده الياس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān al-Muzammalātī. He was among those whose grandfather was Ilyās."@en .

rec:AIND-D01410 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01410-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01410-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01410-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01410 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن تقي . فيمن جده أحمد بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Taqī. Among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01412 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01412-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01412-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01412-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01412-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D01412-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D01412-resp-6,
        rec:AIND-D01412-resp-7 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01412 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن حسن المارديني الأصل الكركي ثم الخانكي ويعرف بابن سميط . كان بواب المدرسة الأشرفية بالخانقاه بل هو المتولي الصرف على عمارتها مع ولعه بالمطالب وخدمته للواردين . مات في رمضان سنة اثنتين وثمانين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Ḥasan, originally from Mārdīn, then from al-Karak, then associated with al-Khānqāh, and known as Ibn Sumayṭ. He served as the gatekeeper of al-Madrasa al-Ashrafiyya at al-Khānqāh, and was also responsible for the expenditures on its construction, alongside his passion for scholarship and service to visitors. He died in Ramaḍān in the year 882 H. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01413 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01413-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01413-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01413-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01413 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن حسين الخانكي ثم القاهري الشافعي نزيل البيبرسية . ممن اشتغل قليلا وصحب ابن الشيخ يوسف الصفي وسمع مني في جماعة وجلس بحانوت الحنابلة ظاهر باب الفتوح لا بأس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn al-Khānkī, then al-Qāhirī, a Shāfiʿī. He resided in al-Baybarsiyya. He worked a little, accompanied Ibn al-Shaykh Yūsuf al-Ṣafī, heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in a group, and used to sit in a Hanbalī shop outside Bāb al-Futūḥ. He was not bad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01414 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01414-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01414-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01414 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن درباس شهاب الدين بن علاء الدين المصري . ذكره البقاعي في شيوخه مجردا وما علمت أمره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Dirbās Shihāb al-Dīn b. ʿAlāʾ al-Dīn al-Miṣrī. Al-Biqāʿī mentioned him briefly among his teachers, and I (al-Sakhāwī) have no further information about him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01415 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01415-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01415-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01415 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن سالم الولوي أبو الخير بن المحب الدمشقي الشافعي الآتي أبوه وجده ويعرف كهما بابن سالم . ولد في مستهل جمادى الأولى سنة اثنتين وثمانين بدمشق وحفظ القرآن وصلى به والمنهاج وجمع الجوامع والألفية وعرض الأول بالشامية البرانية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Sālim al-Walawī Abū al-Khayr b. al-Muḥibb al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī. His father and grandfather will be mentioned below, and he is known like them as Ibn Sālim. He was born at the beginning of Jumādā al-Ūlā in 882 H in Dimashq. He memorized the Qurʾān, led prayers with it, and memorized 『al-Minhāj』, 『Jamʿ al-Jawāmiʿ』, and 『al-Alfīya』. He presented the first of these works (al-Minhāj) at al-Shāmiyya al-Barrāniyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D01416 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01416-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01416-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01416 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن عبد الله السفطي الآتي أبوه . ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Safaṭī. His father's biography will follow. He was among those who learned from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01418 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01418-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01418-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01418 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن عمر بن عبد الغفار المالكي . ممن عرض عليه خير الدين بن القصبي بعيد الخمسين وأظنه الذي قبله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Ghaffār al-Mālikī. Among those to whom Khayr al-Dīn b. al-Qaṣabī presented (a work) shortly after the [8]50s. And I believe he is the one who preceded him (in the biographical entries)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01419 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01419-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01419-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01419-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01419 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن عمر بن علي بن أحمد الشهاب بن البدر القرشي الطنبذي القاهري والد الصلاح والمحب أبي الفضل المحمدين الآتيين ويعرف كسلفه بابن عرب . مات في رجب سنة خمس وسبعين بعد أن أثكل أول ولديه ، وكان في خدمة فيروز الزمام وقتا عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad, al-Shihāb, Ibn al-Badr al-Qurashī al-Ṭanbadhī al-Qāhirī, was the father of al-Ṣalāḥ and al-Muḥibb Abū al-Faḍl, the two Muḥammads who will be mentioned later. He was known, like his predecessors, as Ibn ʿArab. He died in Rajab 875 AH, after having been bereaved of the elder of his two sons. He was at one time in the service of Fīrūz al-Zimām. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01420 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01420-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01420-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01420-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01420 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن عمر بن علي بن مهنا الصفدي الحنفي الآتي والده . عرض عليه الصلاح الطرابلسي في ربيع الأول سنة تسع وأربعين وما علمت ترجمته وقال لي الصلاح المشار إليه أنه ولي قضاء طرابلس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Muhannā al-Ṣafadī al-Ḥanafī. His father will be mentioned later. Al-Ṣalāḥ al-Ṭarābulusī presented to him (Aḥmad) in Rabīʿ al-Awwal 849 H. I (al-Sakhāwī) am unaware of his biography. Al-Ṣalāḥ, the aforementioned, told me that he (al-Ṣalāḥ) assumed the qāḍī-ship of Tripoli."@en .

rec:AIND-D01421 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01421-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01421-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01421 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن عنبر . هكذا ذكره ابن فهد مجردا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAnbar. Ibn Fahd mentioned him thus, unadorned."@en .

rec:AIND-D01424 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01424-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01424-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01424-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01424 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن محمد بن جوشن المكي أخو أبي القسم وعبد الكريم . مات بها في ذي الحجة سنة أربع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Ali b. Muhammad b. Jawshan al-Makki. Brother of Abu al-Qasim and Abd al-Karim. He died in Mecca in Dhu al-Hijja in the year 874 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01426 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01426-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01426-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01426 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عمر الرضي بن الكمال ابن العلاء البلقيني القاهري الشافعي الزركشي . مات في يوم الأحد العشرين من ربيع الثاني سنة اثنتين وتسعين عن خمس وعشرين سنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿUmar al-Raḍī b. al-Kamāl Ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-Bulqīnī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī al-Zarkashī. He died on Sunday, the 20th of Rabīʿ al-Thānī in the year 892 H, at the age of twenty-five."@en .

rec:AIND-D01427 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01427-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01427-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01427-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01427 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الشمس محمد بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الكريم الشهاب الهيثمي الأصل القاهري أخو عبد الكريم وعلي وهو أصغر الثلاثة . اشتغل بالتجارة وتكرر سفره لمكة وغيرها وخالط أمين الدين الهيصم وغيره ولم يحصل على طائل . مات قريب الستين بعد أن افتقر جدا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Shams Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm, al-Shihāb al-Haythamī (by origin) al-Qāhirī. He was the brother of ʿAbd al-Karīm and ʿAlī, the youngest of the three. He engaged in trade and traveled repeatedly to Mecca and elsewhere. He kept company with Amīn al-Dīn al-Hayṣam and others but obtained nothing substantial. He died near the age of sixty after becoming very poor."@en .

rec:AIND-D01434 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01434-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01434-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01434 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي الشهاب أبو مرحوم القاهري الزركشي الماوردي الوفائي . ممن تردد إلي في الإملاء وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, al-Shihāb Abū Marḥūm, al-Qāhirī al-Zarkashī al-Māwardī al-Wafāʾī. He was among those who frequented me (al-Sakhāwī) for dictation and other matters."@en .

rec:AIND-D01435 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01435-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01435-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01435-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01435 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي الشهاب بن الشمس القاهري الفاضلي الضرير أخو عبد العزيز الزريكشي ويعرف بصهر ابن الجندي وبابن الرقيق . كان أحد أهل الشرب ممن يتجر ويعامل الناس على خير وسداد ورغبة في الصالحين والعلماء وأحسن حالا من أخيه . مات في ثامن ذي القعدة سنة سبع وثمانين ، ودفن ليلة الجمعة رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, al-Shihāb b. al-Shams al-Qāhirī al-Fāḍilī al-Ḍarīr. He was the brother of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Zuraykashī and was known as the son-in-law of Ibn al-Jundī and as Ibn al-Raqīq. He was one of those who drank wine, yet he traded and dealt with people with goodness and rectitude, and was fond of the righteous and the learned. He was better off than his brother. He died on the 8th of Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 887 H and was buried on Friday night. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01436 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01436-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01436-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01436-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01436-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01436 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي الشهاب بن الشمس العاقل الموقع أبوه الآتي أخذ عن سيف الدين بن الخوندار في فنون ثم عن ملا على الكرماني ثم عن الخطيب الوزيري ولازمني في الصرغتمشية وقرأ علي بها في شرح ألفية الحديث مع جودة الفهم وظرف البزة ولطف العشرة لكنه كثير التعلل عافاه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, al-Shihāb b. al-Shams al-ʿĀqil. His father, al-Muwaqqiʿ, is mentioned later (separately entered). He acquired various subjects (funūn) from Sayf al-Dīn b. al-Khawndār, then from Mullā ʿAlī al-Kirmānī, then from al-Khaṭīb al-Wazīrī. He kept close company with me (al-Sakhāwī) at al-Ṣarghitmashiyya, where he read to me the Sharḥ Alfiyyat al-Ḥadīth. He combined excellent understanding, an elegant appearance, and an agreeable manner, though he was much given to making excuses. May God restore his health."@en .

rec:AIND-D01437 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01437-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01437-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01437-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01437 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي الشهاب السنهوري الأزهري . ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, with the laqab al-Shihāb, and nisbahs al-Sanhūrī and al-Azharī. He was among those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01440 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01440-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01440-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01440-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01440 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي أبو العباس المصمودي الماجري بجيم معقودة بينها وبين القاف المغربي نزيل المدينة النبوية قرأ عليه ابن أبي اليمن البخاري بروايته له عن أبي عبد الله محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن مرزوق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maṣmūdī al-Mājrī (with a looped jīm joined to the qāf, a Maghribī nisba), al-Maghribī, a resident of al-Madīna al-Nabawiyya. Ibn Abī al-Yaman al-Bukhārī read the Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī under him (the subject) on the basis of the subject's narration of it from Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Marzūq."@en .

rec:AIND-D01441 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01441-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01441-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01441 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي بن الفيومية . فيمن لم يسم أبوه من أواخر الأحمدين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. al-Fayyūmiyya. Among those named Aḥmad whose fathers are not explicitly mentioned, from the later ones (in this biographical dictionary)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01442 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01442-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01442-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01442-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01442 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن علي البرلسي المالكي تلميذ ابن الأقيطع ويعرف بابن الحصان بمهملتين الأولى مضمومة والثانية خفيفة من الفضلاء الخيار ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Burlusī al-Mālikī, a student of Ibn al-Aqyaṭaʿ, known as Ibn al-Ḥiṣān (the first letter is with a ḍamma, the second is soft). He was among the excellent and choice men, and among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01444 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01444-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01444-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01444-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01444 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن الفقيه علي الخيوطي المصري . قال شيخنا في معجمه اشتغل كثيرا وعني بالقراءات ورافقنا في سماع الحديث وأخذت عنه من القرآن تجويدا ونسخ لي كثيرا ، ومات في أول الكهولة في شوال سنة سبع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. al-Faqīh ʿAlī al-Khuyūṭī al-Miṣrī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his muʿjam (al-Muʿjam al-Mufahras). He devoted himself greatly to study and gave particular attention to the Qurʾānic readings (al-qirāʾāt). He accompanied us (al-Sakhāwī) in hearing ḥadīth. I (al-Sakhāwī) acquired the Qurʾān with tajwīd from him, and he copied many texts for me. He died at the beginning of mature adulthood, in Shawwāl 807 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01448 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01448-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01448-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01448-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01448 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عمر بن أبي بكر بن عبد الوهاب بن علي بن نزار الطفاوي . له ذكر في أخيه عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿAlī b. Nizār al-Ṭafāwī. He is mentioned in the entry of his brother ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D01450 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01450-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01450-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01450 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عمر بن علي الشهاب بن الشمس القليحي القاهري الحنفي . كان منموقعي الحكم بل ناب أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī al-Shihāb b. al-Shams al-Qulayḥī al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī. He was one of the signatories of judicial judgments and also served as a deputy."@en .

rec:AIND-D01458 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01458-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01458-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01458-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01458 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عمر الفقيه العلامة النحوي الشهاب الحاجر . قرأ على أبيه وغيره وبرع في العربية وأفادها الناس وممن قرأ عليه الشهاب أحمد بن علي الناشري مع خط جيد كتب به الكثير وسار . مات في أوئل هذا القرن وتفرق ماله بموته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar, the jurist, the erudite scholar, the grammarian al-Shihāb al-Ḥājir. He studied under his father and others, excelled in Arabic, and benefited people thereby. Among those who studied under him was al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Nāshirī, who wrote much in a fine hand and rose to prominence. He (the subject) died at the beginning of this (9th Hijri) century, and his wealth was dispersed upon his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D01459 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01459-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01459-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01459 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عمر البدر الطنبذي تقدم في ابن عمر بن محمود وذكره هنا هو الصواب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar, known as al-Badr al-Ṭanbadhī. He was previously mentioned in the entry for Ibn ʿUmar b. Maḥmūd, but it is correct to record his biography here."@en .

rec:AIND-D01460 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01460-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01460-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01460-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01460-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01460 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عمر البرشومي القاهري . سمع الحديث وكتب الطباق وربما كتب في الاستدعاءات ونحوها عن ابن الشيخة وغير دمن المسندين للضرورة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar al-Barshūmī al-Qāhirī. He heard ḥadīth and wrote transcription certificates (ṭibāq). At times he also wrote petitions (istidʿāʾ) and the like on behalf of Ibn al-Shaykha and other musnids (traditionists), as need required."@en .

rec:AIND-D01461 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01461-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01461-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01461 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن عياش . يأتي في ابن محمد بن محمد بن يوسف بن علي بن عياش ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAyyāsh. Forthcoming in the entry for Ibn Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf b. ʿAlī b. ʿAyyāsh."@en .

rec:AIND-D01467 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01467-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01467-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01467-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01467 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن فرج الخواجا الصيرفي . مات سنة تسع عشرة . ذكره ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Faraj al-Khawāja al-Ṣayrafī. Died in 819 AH. Ibn ʿAzm mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01469 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01469-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01469-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01469 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن الفلاح . يأتي قريبا في ابن محمد بن اللاح [= AIND-D01479] ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. al-Fallāḥ. His biography will be given shortly under Ibn Muḥammad b. al-Lāḥ."@en .

rec:AIND-D01470 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01470-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01470-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01470-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01470 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن فندو المظفر شاه بن الجلال صاحب بنجالة من الهند وابن صاحبها . استقروا به بعد أبيه في سنة سبع وثلاثين وهو ابن أربع عشرة سنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Fandū, al-Muẓaffar Shāh, lord (ṣāḥib) of Bengal in India and son of its lord — i.e. son of al-Jalāl (his father Muḥammad). He was installed (as ruler) after his father in 837 H, when he was fourteen years old."@en .

rec:AIND-D01471 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01471-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01471-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01471 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن فهيد المغيربي . يأتي فيمن لم يسم جده [= AIND-D01598] ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Fuhayd al-Mughayribī. He will be mentioned in the section for those whose grandfathers' names are not specified."@en .

rec:AIND-D01478 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01478-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01478-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01478 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن كميل . صوابه محمد بن أحمد بن عمر بن كحيل [= AIND-D06785] ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Kumayl. The correct (name) is Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Kaḥīl."@en .

rec:AIND-D01479 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01479-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01479-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01479-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01479-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D01479-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01479 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن اللاج القلاحي السكندري المقرئ أجاز لابن شيخنا وغيره في سنة سبع عشرة . ويحرر اسم جده فقد وجدته في استدعاء هكذا وفي معجم شيخنا الفلاح وقال إنه انتهت إليه رياسة الإقراء ببلده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. al-Lāj al-Qalāḥī al-Iskandarī, the Qurʾān reciter (muqriʾ). He granted ijāza to the son of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others in the year 817 H. His grandfather's name requires verification: I found it thus (as al-Lāj) in a petition (istidʿāʾ), while in the Muʿjam of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) it appears as al-Fallāḥ; and it states that the headship of Qurʾān recitation (riyāsat al-iqrāʾ) in his hometown devolved to him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01491 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01491-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01491-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01491-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01491 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن إسماعيل بن موفق الشهاب الديروطي الشافعي . سمع مني بالقاهرة ورأيته فيمن شهد على الديروطي في إجازته لابن القصبي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Muwaffaq, known as al-Shihāb al-Dayrūṭī al-Shāfiʿī. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo, and I saw him among the witnesses to the ijāza granted by (an elder) al-Dayrūṭī to Ibn al-Qaṣabī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01495 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01495-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01495-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01495-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01495 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن حسن أبو الهدى بن أبي الخير بن الشيخ الحنفي الآتي أبوه وجده . ولد سنة سبع وثمانمائة سنة مات جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan, Abū al-Hudā b. Abī al-Khayr b. al-Shaykh al-Ḥanafī, whose father and grandfather are mentioned later. He was born in 807 H, the year his grandfather died."@en .

rec:AIND-D01497 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01497-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01497-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01497-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01497-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01497 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن خلد بن موسى الحمصي الحنبلي ابن أخي عبد الرحمن ابن محمد بن خلد الآتي هو وأبوه ويعرف بابن زهرة . ولي قضاء الحنابلة ببلده وقدم القاهرة فناب عن قاضيها العز الكناني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Khald b. Mūsā al-Ḥimṣī al-Ḥanbalī, nephew of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Khald (who, together with his father, is mentioned later), known as Ibn Zahra. He held the judgeship (qaḍāʾ) of the Ḥanbalīs in his hometown, then came to Cairo, where he deputized for its judge, al-ʿIzz al-Kinānī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01498 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01498-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01498-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01498-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01498-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01498 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن دمرداش الشهاب الغزي الحنفي ابن أخت قاضي الحنفية الشمس بن المغربي ويعرف بابن دمرداش . ممن أخذ الفقه عن خاله والعربية والمعاني والبيان والتصوف عن الشمس الحمصي في آخرين ممن وردوا عليه وبرع في فنون مع الدين وجودة النظم والنثر والسيرة الجميلة وتكسبه بالشهادة التي صار عين اهل بلده فيها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Damardāsh, al-Shihāb al-Ghazzī al-Ḥanafī, sister's son (nephew) of the Ḥanafī judge al-Shams b. al-Maghribī, known as Ibn Damardāsh. He took jurisprudence (fiqh) from his maternal uncle, and Arabic, semantics (maʿānī), rhetoric (bayān) and Sufism from al-Shams al-Ḥimṣī, among others who came to him. He excelled in various fields, with piety, fine poetry and prose and a beautiful character, and earned his living by testimony (al-shahāda), in which he became the foremost figure of his hometown."@en .

rec:AIND-D01499 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01499-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01499-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01499-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01499 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن ريحان البعلي . كذا في ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Rayḥān al-Baʿlī. Thus (recorded) in Ibn ʿAzm."@en .

rec:AIND-D01512 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01512-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01512-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01512-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01512-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01512 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن عبيد أبو البركات بن أبي سعد بن القطان الآتي أبوه . اعتنى به أبوه فأقرأه القرآن وأسمعه الحديث وهو ممن سمع مني وخلف والده سعيد السعداء وغيرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUbayd, Abū al-Barakāt b. Abī Saʿd b. al-Qaṭṭān. His father is mentioned later (separately entered). His father cared for him, had him read the Qurʾān, and had him hear ḥadīth. He is among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī), and he succeeded his father at Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ and elsewhere."@en .

rec:AIND-D01517 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01517-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01517-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01517-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01517 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أي اليمن محمد بن محمد بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز العقيلي النويري المكي أخو علي الآتي ويعرف بابن أبي اليمن . ولد سنة إحدى وثمانمائة ومات في رمضان من التي تليها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Ay al-Yaman Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-ʿAqīlī al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī, known as Ibn Abī al-Yaman. He was born in the year 801 AH and died in Ramadan of the following year. He was the brother of ʿAlī, who will be mentioned later."@en .

rec:AIND-D01522 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01522-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01522-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01522 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن أبي غانم بن الحبال . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن أحمد بن أبي غانم ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D01523 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01523-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01523-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01523-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01523 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن البهلوان الشهاب بن البدر ابن الشمس الآتي أبوه وجده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. al-Bahlawān, al-Shihāb, son of al-Badr (his father Muḥammad) and grandson of al-Shams (his grandfather Muḥammad). His father and grandfather are mentioned later."@en .

rec:AIND-D01524 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01524-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01524-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01524-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01524 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن التقي أبي الوفا محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن الحسن بن محمد الجعفري القاهري الآتي أبوه وعمه وشقيقه محمد . ولد سنة سبع وخمسين وثمانمائة بالقاهرة وحفظ المنهاج وغيره وتكسب بالشهادة وقراءة الجوق وهو ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Taqī Abī al-Wafā Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. al-Ḥasan b. Muḥammad al-Jaʿfarī al-Qāhirī. His father, paternal uncle, and full brother Muḥammad are mentioned later (separately entered). He was born in 857 H in al-Qāhira and memorized al-Minhāj and other works. He earned his living through the office of legal witnessing and through choral recitation, and was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01533 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01533-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01533-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01533 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد علم الدين الأخنائي المالكي . صوابه أحمد ابن محمد بن أحمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن عيسى وقد مضى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, ʿAlam al-Dīn al-Akhnāʾī, of the Maliki madhhab. His correct (genealogy) is Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿĪsā, and he has been mentioned previously."@en .

rec:AIND-D01535 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01535-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01535-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01535-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01535 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد المحب القرشي الزبيري النويري المصري . ولد في يوم الثلاثاء تاسع عشر ذي الحجة سنة تسع وستين وسبعمائة وذكر أنه سمع من التقي بن حاتم . ذكره ابن فهد في معجمه ولم يزد ، وقد أجاز سنة أربع وثلاثين في بعض الاستدعاءات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, al-Muḥibb al-Qurashī al-Zubayrī al-Nuwayrī al-Miṣrī. He was born on Tuesday, the 19th of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 769 H. He is reported to have heard from al-Taqī b. Ḥātim. Ibn Fahd mentioned him in his muʿjam without adding more. In 834 H he granted ijāza in response to some requests."@en .

rec:AIND-D01536 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01536-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01536-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01536-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01536 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد الأخميمي النقيب . هو أبو القسم مشهور بكنيته يأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Akhmīmī, al-Naqīb. He is Abū al-Qāsim, famous by his kunyah, and will be mentioned later."@en .

rec:AIND-D01538 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01538-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01538-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01538-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01538 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن مفلح الشهاب أبو الضياء بن الخطيب الشمس الحارسي النابلسي ثم المقدسي الحنبلي ويعرف بابن الرماح . ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Mufliḥ, al-Shihāb Abū al-Ḍiyāʾ, son of the preacher (al-khaṭīb) al-Shams; al-Ḥārisī al-Nābulusī, then al-Maqdisī al-Ḥanbalī, known as Ibn al-Rummāḥ. He was among those who took (knowledge) from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01540 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01540-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01540-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01540 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن الناصح . سيأتي قريبا فيمن لم يسم جد أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Muhammad b. al-Nasih. He will be mentioned soon in the section for those whose paternal grandfather's father is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D01547 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01547-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01547-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01547-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01547 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد الشهاب أبو العباس الشغري . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن عمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, Shihāb Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Shaghrī. He was previously mentioned in the entry of those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿUmar."@en .

rec:AIND-D01550 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01550-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01550-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01550-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01550 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد الشهاب السنباطي ثم القاهري . ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, al-Shihāb, al-Sunbāṭī, then al-Qāhirī. One of those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01553 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01553-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01553-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01553-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01553-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01553 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد الشهاب الهوي ثم القاهري الحنبلي ، اشتغل قليلا وسمع ختم البخاري عند أم هانئ الهورينية ومن كان معها وكان ساكنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, laqab al-Shihāb, nisbahs al-Hawī then al-Qāhirī, a Ḥanbalī. He studied a little and heard the completion (khatm) of al-Bukhārī's Ṣaḥīḥ from Umm Hāniʾ al-Hūrīniyya and those who were with her. He was a quiet person."@en .

rec:AIND-D01555 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01555-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01555-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01555 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد الأبدي . فيمن جده محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن علي بن أحمد [= AIND-D01505] ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Abadī. Among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01559 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01559-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01559-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01559-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01559-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01559 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن محمد المحلي الهيثمي ثم القاهري خادم الشيخ محمد ابن صلح الآتي ويعرف بابن الحسود . ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Maḥallī al-Haythamī, then al-Qāhirī, servant of Shaykh Muḥammad b. Ṣulḥ (mentioned later), and known as Ibn al-Ḥasūd. Among those who took (learning) from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01563 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01563-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01563-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01563-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01563 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن مسعود المغربي الأصل المدني المالكي ويعرف بالمزجج . مسع على الزين المراغي وغيره ، ومات في سنة تسع وعشرين بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Masʿūd, of Maghribī origin, a Medinan and a Mālikī, known as al-Muzajjaj. He heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī and others. He died in 829 H in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D01564 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01564-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01564-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01564-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01564-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01564 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن معين الدين أبو العباس القاهري الكتبي القصصي . استكتبه بعضهم في استدعاء فيه بعض الأولاد وقال له نظم لا بأس به وكان يكتب القصص بالرملة ويبيع الكتب تحت الصرغتمشية فينظر شيء من نظمه ، ومتى مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muʿīn al-Dīn, Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Qāhirī, the bookseller (al-kutubī), the storyteller (al-qaṣaṣī). Some people commissioned him to write a petition (istidʿāʾ) concerning certain children, and his poetry was said to be not bad. He used to write stories in al-Ramla and sell books under al-Ṣarghitmishiyya. Some of his poetry is extant, but the date of his death is unknown."@en .

rec:AIND-D01569 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01569-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01569-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01569-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01569-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01569 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن موسى بن محمد الشهاب المغراوي الأصل الأبشيهي ثم القاهري والد البهاء محمد الآتي . كان يباشر في جهات كالسابقية ويتكسب بالشهادة ولازم شيخنا في الإملاء وعاش بعده مدة حتى مات ولم يكن بالمرضي عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. Muḥammad, al-Shihāb, of Maghrāwī origin, then al-Abshīhī, then al-Qāhirī. Father of al-Bahāʾ Muḥammad (mentioned later). He served (in administrative capacities) in various quarters such as al-Sābiqiyya and earned his living by testimony (al-shahāda). He kept close company with our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in the dictation sessions (imlāʾ), and lived for some time after him until he died. He was not well-regarded; may God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01575 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01575-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01575-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01575 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن نصر الديروطي . حدث في دمياط بالشفا عن شيخنا النور بن يفتح الله أخذ عنه الجلال بن الردادي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Naṣr al-Dayrūṭī. He transmitted ḥadīth in Damietta, [reciting] al-Shifā, on the authority of our shaykh al-Nūr b. Yaftaḥ Allāh. al-Jalāl b. al-Raddādī acquired [knowledge] from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01576 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01576-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01576-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01576 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن أبي الوفا في ابن محمد ابن محمد بن وفا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Wafā. (See) under Ibn Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Wafā (the Banū Wafā)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01585 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01585-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01585-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01585 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن يوسف العجمي الأصل المدني الحنفي أخو يحيى الآتي وذاك الأكبر ويعرف بالذاكر . ممن سمع بالمدينة . ومات في تاسع ربيع الثاني سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf, originally al-ʿAjamī, then al-Madanī, a Ḥanafī. He is the brother of Yaḥyā, who will be mentioned later and who is the elder. He is known as al-Dhākir. He was among those who heard [ḥadīth] in Medina. He died on the 9th of Rabīʿ al-Thānī in the year 891 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01588 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01588-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01588-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01588 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد ناصر الدين ويعرف بابن أمين الحكم كان ينوب في الحكم بمصر وعدة من بلاد البهنساوية . مات في سنة تسع وثلاثين بعد انقطاعه مدة بمرض عرض له منه فالج ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad Nāṣir al-Dīn, known as Ibn Amīn al-Ḥukm. He served as a deputy (nāʾib) in the judiciary in Egypt and in several towns of the Bahnasāwīya region. He died in 839 H, after being incapacitated for a period by an illness that caused him paralysis (fālij)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01591 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01591-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01591-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01591 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد السنهوري المالكي ويعرف بابن عز الدين أخذ القراءات عن بلديه جعفر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Sanhūrī al-Mālikī, known as Ibn ʿIzz al-Dīn. He acquired Qurʾān recitation (qirāʾāt) from his townsman (baladī) Jaʿfar."@en .

rec:AIND-D01592 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01592-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01592-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01592-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01592-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D01592-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D01592-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01592 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب الدمشقي بن العطار مستوفي الجامع الاموي كان أجل من بقي من مباشريه وقد طلب الحديث وقتا رفيقا للشمس بن سيد وابن إمام المشهد . مات في شوال سنة إحدى . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb al-Dimashqī b. al-ʿAṭṭār. He served as the accountant (mustawfī) of the Umayyad Mosque and was among the most eminent of its surviving administrators. He sought ḥadīth for a time, and was a companion (rafīq) of al-Shams b. Sayyid and Ibn Imām al-Mashhad. He died in Shawwāl of the year 801 H. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his work Inbāʾ (al-Ghumr)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01595 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01595-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01595-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01595-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01595 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب بن القصاص السكندري المالكي . قرأ على شيخنا الترغيب المنذري وغيره وكان حسن القراءة فاضلا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb b. al-Qaṣṣāṣ al-Sakandarī al-Mālikī. He recited al-Targhīb (of al-Mundhirī) and other works to our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar). He had good recitation and was a virtuous person."@en .

rec:AIND-D01597 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01597-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01597-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01597-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01597 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد شهاب الدين بن ناصر الدين الجمالي حفيد أخت الجمال الاستادار كان أبوه حسن العشرة والمحاضرة والمكارم يستحضر نكتا وأشعارا وفوائد وخلفه ابنه في رزقه بمنية خضير من المنزلة ولكنه ضبط موجوده وصاهر بني الجيعان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad Shihāb al-Dīn ibn Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Jamālī, grandson of al-Jamāl al-Ustādār's sister. His father was of good character, eloquent, and noble, memorizing anecdotes, poems, and beneficial knowledge. His son succeeded him in his livelihood in Munyat Khuḍayr from al-Manzila. He managed his assets and intermarried with Banū al-Jīʿān."@en .

rec:AIND-D01600 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01600-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01600-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01600 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد بن الهائم . مضى فيمن جده عماد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. al-Hāʾim. His biography is found under those whose grandfather is ʿImād."@en .

rec:AIND-D01601 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01601-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01601 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد ويعرف بابن والي . ولد تقريبا سنة تسعين أو قبلها كتبت عنه قوله : %~% يقولون لي في البحر تمساح كاسر %~% أصاد لصياد وقد كاده كيدا %~% %~% فقلت لهم هذا نهاية عمره %~% ولو راح بيروت لكان له صيدا %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad, known as Ibn Wālī. He was born approximately in the year 890 AH or earlier. I (al-Sakhāwī) wrote down from him his saying: \"They say to me, 'There is a fierce crocodile in the sea / I hunt for a hunter, and it has trapped him cunningly.' / So I said to them, 'This is the end of his life / And if he went to Beirut, it would be a prey for him.'\""@en .

rec:AIND-D01603 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01603-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01603-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01603 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد البدر الطنبذي . فيمن اسم أبيه عمر بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Badr al-Ṭanbadhī. [Listed] among those whose father's name is ʿUmar b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01604 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01604-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01604 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب البالسي الأصل الدمشقي الحنفي الجواشني . قال شيخنا في أنبائه اشتغل في صباه وصاهر أبا البقاء على ابنته وأفتى ودرس وناب في الحكم وولي نظر الأوصياء ووظائف كثيرة بدمشق وكان حسن السيرة واستقل بالقضاء قليلا بسعي منه ثم عزل وسعى في العود فلم يتم له ومات في جمادى الآخرة سنة تسع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "595 Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb, of al-Bālisī origin, al-Dimashqī, al-Ḥanafī, al-Jawāshnī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his 『Anbāʾ』 that he worked in his youth, became a son-in-law to Abū al-Baqāʾ (by marrying his daughter), issued fatwas, taught, served as a deputy in judgment, and held the office of supervisor of guardians, as well as many other positions in Damascus. He had good conduct and briefly served as an independent qāḍī through his own efforts. He was then dismissed and sought to return to the post, but it was not granted. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira in the year 809."@en .

rec:AIND-D01606 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01606-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01606-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01606 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب البسطامي ويعرف بالمتوكل . مات في يوم الخميس سادس عشري صفر سنة ست وستين . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "597 Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb al-Basṭāmī, known as al-Mutawakkil. He died on Thursday, the 26th of Ṣafar, in the year 866. Al-Munīr recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D01608 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01608-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01608-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01608-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01608 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب التلعفري ثم الدمشقي كاتب المنسوب . مات بدمشق كهلا في سنة إحدى عشرة ، ويقال أنه كان أستاذا في ضرب القانون حسن المحاضرة . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad, Shihāb al-Talʿafarī, then al-Dimashqī (d. 811 H). He served as a scribe of lineage/attribution (kātib al-mansūb). It is said that he died in Damascus in 811 H in his middle age. He was a master of playing the qanūn and a skilled lecturer. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated this in his *Anbāʾ*."@en .

rec:AIND-D01609 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01609-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01609-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01609 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب الحلبي ثم الدمشقي قاضي كرك نوح . مضى في ابن عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb al-Ḥalabī, then al-Dimashqī. Qāḍī of Karak Nūḥ. See under Ibn ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D01611 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01611-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01611-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01611 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب الطوخي الناسخ . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن عثمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb al-Ṭawkhī al-Nāsikh. He is among those whose grandfather, Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān, has already been mentioned (in an earlier entry)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01612 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01612-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01612 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب العجيمي الصوفي بالخانقاه السرياقوسية وصهر ابن الجوجري الأبرازي . قرأ على شيخنا الترمذي في سنة أربع وأربعين وبلغ له بالشيخ وكان متوددا . مات فيما أظن بعد الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad, known by the laqab Shihāb and the nisbah al-ʿAjamī, was a Sufi affiliated with the al-Siryāqūsīya Khānqāh, and the son-in-law of Ibn al-Jawjarī al-Abrāzī. He read from our shaykh al-Tirmidhī in 844 H and achieved a high standing with him. He was amiable. He died, as I assume, after 860 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01614 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01614-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01614-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01614-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01614 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب الكنجي الدمشقي . مات في يوم عاشوراء سنة أربع وتسعين بالمدرسة الرواحية وقد قارب الثمانين ودفن قبلي الشيخ حماد من مقبرة الباب الصغير ، وكان صالحا تاليا أحد شيخي الإقراء بالمدرسة الكلاسة وشيخ السمع بمحراب المالكية في جامع دمشق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "###$AIND-D01614 | 864961957257$# $ Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb al-Kanjī al-Dimashqī. He died on the Day of Ashura in 894 H at al-Madrasa al-Rawāḥiyya, having reached almost eighty years of age. He was buried south of Shaykh Ḥammād in the cemetery of Bāb al-Ṣaghīr. He was a righteous reciter, one of the two shaykhs of Qurʾān recitation at al-Madrasa al-Killāsa, and the shaykh of listening sessions at the Maliki mihrab in Jāmiʿ Dimashq."@en .

rec:AIND-D01617 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01617-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01617-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01617 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب الواسطي المناوي . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Among those who studied under me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D01618 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01618-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01618-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01618-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01618 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب الواسطي الاصم : مضى فيمن جده أبو بكر بن محمد بن سعد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "He was mentioned in the biography of a person whose grandfather is Abū Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Saʿd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D01619 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01619-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01619 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشهاب اليغموري . ولي الحجوبية وشد الدواوين بدمشق وكان مشهورا بمعرفة المباشرة . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه قال ورأيته عند جمال الدين الأستادار وكان يظهر محبة العلماء وتعجبه مباحثتهم ويفهم جيدا . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة إحدى عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shihāb al-Yaghmūrī. He held the office of chamberlain (ḥujūbīya) and administered the dīwāns in Damascus. He was known for his knowledge of direct administration. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』. I saw him with Jamāl al-Dīn al-Ustādār; he showed affection for scholars, enjoyed their discussions, and understood well. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 'eleven' (811 AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01620 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01620-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01620-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01620 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد النجم والشهاب البامي . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن قريش ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Najm wa-al-Shihāb al-Bāmī. His grandfather, Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Quraysh, has already been mentioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D01621 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01621-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01621 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد أبو العباس الشلقي بمعجمة مفتوحة ثم لام مكسورة . يروي عن الجمال الريمي وغيره وصار أحد المفننين بتعز . مات في حدود الثلاثين قال العفيف وقدر رويت عنه إجازة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Shalqī. He transmitted from al-Jamāl al-Raymī and others, and became one of the leading experts in Taʿizz. He died around the age of thirty. Al-ʿAfīf said, “I transmitted from him by ijāza.”"@en .

rec:AIND-D01622 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01622-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01622-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01622 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الأشعري اليماني . ولد سنة تسع وخمسين وسبعمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Ashʿarī al-Yamānī. He was born in the year 759 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01623 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01623-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01623-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01623-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01623 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الحريري وكيل الشرع ودلال الكتب أبوه . مات بمكة في صفر سنة ستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Ḥarīrī, agent of the Sharia court and book broker. His father. He died in Mecca in Ṣafar 860 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01624 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01624-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01624-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01624-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01624-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D01624-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01624 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الدهان رئيس المؤذنين بالجامع الأموي . كان شجي الصوت عارفا بالميقات وعمر حتى صار أقدم المؤذنين عهدا واعترفهم واشجاهم صوتا وقد دخل بلاد العجم تاجرا وأقام هناك مدة وكانت لديه خبرة بالأمور . مات في ذي القعدة سنة ثلاث عشرة عن أربع وثمانين عاما . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Dahhān, the chief muezzin of the Umayyad Mosque. He had a melodious voice, was knowledgeable in timekeeping (mīqāt), lived to become the longest-serving, most recognized, and most melodious-voiced of the muezzins. He had entered the lands of Persia as a merchant and resided there for a period. He possessed expertise in various matters. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 813 AH, at the age of 84. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Anbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D01625 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01625-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01625-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01625 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد التونسي الدهان الطبيب في بضع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Tūnisī al-Dahhān al-Ṭabīb. He died in the forties (of an unspecified century)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01626 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01626-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01626-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01626 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد السنهوري المالكي . مضى فيمن يعرف بابن عز الدين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Sanhūrī al-Mālikī. He has been mentioned in the entry for the one known as Ibn ʿIzz al-Dīn."@en .

rec:AIND-D01628 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01628-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01628-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01628-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01628 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الشكيلي المدني . فيمن جده إبراهيم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shikīlī al-Madanī, among those whose grandfather is Ibrāhīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D01630 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01630-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01630-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01630 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد القلشاني . فيمن جده عبد الله بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Qalashānī. Among those whose grandfather was ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01631 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01631-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01631-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01631 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد الكبيسي بالكاف وعلى الألسنة بالقاف وكأنها معقودة عبد صالح مرافق للشيخ إدريس الآتي يأتي معه من اليمن كل سنة للحج ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "615. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Kubaysī (with kāf, pronounced with qāf by common people as if a tied qāf, a pious servant): He was a companion of Shaykh Idrīs (mentioned later), accompanying him every year from Yemen for the Hajj."@en .

rec:AIND-D01633 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01633-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01633-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01633 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن محمد المرحومي القاهري المديني الشافعي . رأيته عرض عليه في سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Marḥūmī, al-Qāhirī, al-Madīnī, al-Shāfiʿī. I (al-Sakhāwī) saw him make a presentation to me in the year 895 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01643 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01643-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01643-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01643-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01643-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D01643-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01643 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن مسعود بن محمد بن محمد الشهاب النابلسي ثم القاهري الناسخ المفنن . ولد في سنة ثلاثين وثماثمائة أو التي قبلها ونشأ فحفظ القرآن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad, son of Masʿūd b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, known as al-Shihāb, from Nablus and later al-Qāhirī, a versatile copyist. He was born in the year 830 AH or the year before it, and grew up to memorize the Qurʾān."@en .

rec:AIND-D01645 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01645-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01645-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01645 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن مسعود بن هاشم بن علي بن مسعود بن غزوان بن حسين الشهاب أبو حامد الهاشمي المكي ابن عم الشيخ أبي سعد محمد بن علي بن هاشم الآني . ولد بعد العصر من يوم الاربعاء سابع عشرى ربيع الأول سنة خمس وثمانمائة . ذكره ابن فهد ولم يزد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Masʿūd b. Hāshim b. ʿAlī b. Masʿūd b. Ghazwān b. Ḥusayn, al-Shihāb Abū Ḥāmid al-Hāshimī al-Makkī. He was a paternal cousin of al-Shaykh Abū Saʿd Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Hāshim al-Ānī. He was born after the afternoon prayer on Wednesday, the 17th of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 805 AH. Ibn Fahd mentioned him but added nothing further."@en .

rec:AIND-D01646 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01646-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01646-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01646-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01646-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01646 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن مسعود المدني نزيل مكة ويعرف بالخرية بمعجمة مفتوحة ثم راء ساكنة وتحتانية . كان ساكنا خيرا يتكسب بقيسارية دار الإمارة وله دار بجهة المدعى . مات في المحرم سنة ستين ودفن بالمعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Masʿūd al-Madanī, a resident of Mecca, known as al-Kharriyya (with an open mīm, a quiescent rāʾ, and a yāʾ below it). He was a good-natured person who earned his living in the Qayṣarīya of Dār al-Imāra (House of the Emirate) and had a house in the al-Muddaʿā district. He died in Muḥarram of the year 860 AH and was buried in al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D01647 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01647-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01647-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01647 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن مظفر بن أبي بكر المعمر الطولوني . مات في سنة تسع وخمسين قاله ابن عزم"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muẓaffar b. Abī Bakr al-Muʿammar al-Ṭūlūnī. He died in the year 859, as stated by Ibn ʿAzzm."@en .

rec:AIND-D01648 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01648-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01648-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01648 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن مظفر بن أبي بكر . في ابن محمد بن أبي بكر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Muẓaffar b. Abī Bakr. (Mentioned) in the entry of Ibn Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr."@en .

rec:AIND-D01649 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01649-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01649-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01649 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد ويدعى بديد بن مفتاح بن عبد الله السليماني المدني الموله . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad, who was called Badīd, son of Miftāḥ son of ʿAbd Allāh al-Sulaymānī al-Madanī al-Muwlah. One of those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D01651 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01651-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01651-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01651-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01651 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن مفرح الصباغ . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Mufarriḥ al-Ṣabbāgh. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D01652 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01652-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01652-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01652 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن مفلح الكازروني . مات سنة إحدى وثلاثين . قاله ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Mufliḥ al-Kāzarūnī. He (Ibn ʿAzm) stated that he died in the year 831."@en .

rec:AIND-D01654 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01654-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01654-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01654 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن منصور الشهاب المالكي . ممن انتمى للقرافي وتدرب في الجملة في الشهادة وجلس ببابه ثم لازم ولده البدر . مات في صفر سنة سبع وتسعين وكان عديم الفضيلة عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Manṣūr al-Shihāb al-Mālikī. He was among those who belonged to al-Qarāfī, and generally trained in legal witnessing (al-shahāda) and sat at his door, then attached himself to his son al-Badr. He died in Ṣafar in the year 897 H. He was a person devoid of merit, may God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01655 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01655-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01655-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01655 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن منصور الحكيم . مات بمكة في رجب سنة اثنتين وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Manṣūr al-Ḥakīmī. He died in Mecca in Rajab of the year 862 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01656 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01656-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01656-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01656 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن مهدي الريس . مات بمكة في رجب سنة ثلاث وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Mahdī al-Rayyis. Died in Mecca in Rajab of the year 843 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01658 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01658-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01658-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01658 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن موسى بن إبراهيم الشهاب أبو العباس الحلبي الأصل القاهري الحنفي أحد النواب ووالد عبد الرحيم وعبد الله الآتيين . ممن وصف بالعلم وعرض عليه جماعة ممن لقيناهم وسيأتي فيمن لم يسم جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. Ibrāhīm, with the laqab Shihāb and kunyah Abū al-ʿAbbās, of Aleppan origin, a Cairene Ḥanafī jurist, and one of the deputies (nāʾib). He was the father of ʿAbd al-Raḥīm and ʿAbd Allāh, who will be mentioned later. He was described as learned, and a group of those whom we met presented (their learning) to him. He will appear again in the section on those whose grandfathers are not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D01661 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01661-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01661-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01661 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن موسى بن أحمد بن موسى بن محمد الذوالي الصريفيني اليماني الزبيدي الشافعي الآتي أبوه ويعرف بابن المكشكش . سمع مني بمكة مع أبيه أشياء وكتبت له ثبتا أثنيت فيه عليهما كما بينته في موضع آخر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. Muḥammad al-Dhāwālī al-Ṣarīfīnī al-Yamānī al-Zabīdī al-Shāfiʿī. His father is mentioned later. He was known as Ibn al-Mukashkish. He heard various things from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca with his father, and I wrote for him an attestation (thabat) in which I praised them both, as I have explained elsewhere."@en .

rec:AIND-D01662 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01662-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01662-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01662 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن موسى بن أيوب . مات في سنة ثلاثين وثمانمائة . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. Ayyūb died in the year 830. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D01663 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01663-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01663-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01663 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن موسى بن رجب الشهاب الدمشقي الفاخوري . طلب وقتا وسمع بقراءة شيخنا ابن خضر في سنة سبع وثلاثين سنن الدارقطني عن البدر حسين البوصيري وكذا سمع بالشام في التي قبلها علي ومات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Mūsā b. Rajab, al-Shihāb al-Dimashqī al-Fākhūrī. He sought employment for a time and heard, by the reading of our shaykh Ibn Khiḍr, in the year 837, Sunan al-Dāraquṭnī from al-Badr Ḥusayn al-Būṣīrī. Likewise, he heard in al-Shām in the year prior to that (836) from ʿAlī, and then he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D01664 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01664-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01664-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01664 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الشريف موسى بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الناصر الشطنوفي القاهري الأتي أبوه . سمع على الحاوي مشيخة صالح الأسنوي وفضائل ليلة نصف شعبان لأبي القسم بن عساكر ، وأخذ عنه بعض الطلبة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Sharīf Mūsā b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Nāṣir al-Shaṭnūfī al-Qāhirī, whose father will be mentioned later. He heard `Mashyakhat Ṣāliḥ al-Isnawī` and `Faḍāʾil laylat niṣf Shaʿbān` by Abū al-Qāsim b. ʿAsākir from al-Ḥāwī. Some students acquired knowledge from him (Aḥmad)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01666 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01666-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01666-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01666 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن موسى بن عبد الواحد . في ابن أبي حمو ورأيت من قال أحمد بن موسى بن يوسف بن أبي حمو نائب تلمسان . مات سنة تسع وثلاثين فيحرر مع الذي قبله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid. Regarding Ibn Abī Ḥammū: I have seen it said that Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. Yūsuf b. Abī Ḥammū, nāʾib of Tilimsān, died in the year 839. This should be reconciled with the preceding information."@en .

rec:AIND-D01667 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01667-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01667-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01667-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01667 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن موسى بن علي المكي بن اليماني نزيل أجياد من مكة مات بها في سنة سبع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. ʿAlī al-Makkī b. al-Yamānī. Resident of Ajyād in Mecca. He died there in the year 837."@en .

rec:AIND-D01670 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01670-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01670-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01670 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن موسى بن هرون الشهاب القاهري المقرئ ويعرف بابن الزيات . ممن اشتغل وترقى في رياسة قراء الجوق وتمول منها وسافر إلى حلب في سنة آمد وسمع على شيخنا والبرهان الحلبي وغيرهما . مات في يوم الإثنين خامس ربيع الآخر سنة سبع وستين ودفن من الغد ، ولعله جاز السبعين أو قاربها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. Hārūn, al-Shihāb al-Qāhirī, the reciter. Known as Ibn al-Zayyāt. He worked hard and rose to the leadership of the reciters' guild (jawq) and accumulated wealth from it. He traveled to Aleppo in the year of Āmid and heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and al-Burhān al-Ḥalabī and others. He died on Monday, the fifth of Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 867 H and was buried the next day. He might have been over seventy or close to it."@en .

rec:AIND-D01671 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01671-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01671-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01671 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن موسى الشهاب بن الضياء الحنبلي . مضى فيمن جده إبراهيم بن طرخان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Mūsā al-Shihāb b. al-Ḍiyāʾ al-Ḥanbalī. His entry is found among those whose grandfather is Ibrāhīm b. Ṭarkhān."@en .

rec:AIND-D01678 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01678-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01678-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01678 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن ناصر الدين بن سليمان الهوي ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Nāṣir al-Dīn b. Sulaymān al-Hawī. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D01680 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01680-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01680-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01680-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01680 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن هرون الشهاب الشرواني الشافعي . قدم القاهرة قريبا من سنة سبعين وحضر بعض الدروس وأخذ عني يسيرا وظهرت براعته في فنون مع دين وخير وانجماع وممن أذن له في التدريس والإفتاء الفخر عثمان المقسي وسافر إلى القدس فمات قريبا بعد أن وقف كتبه وجئ بها لجامع الأزهر ثم أخذها المذكور ونعم كان رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad b. Hārūn al-Shihāb al-Shirwānī al-Shāfiʿī. He came to Cairo around the year 870 H and attended some lessons, taking a little from me (al-Sakhāwī). His excellence became apparent in various disciplines, along with his piety, goodness, and reclusiveness. Among those who granted him permission (ijāza) to teach and issue legal opinions (fatwā) was al-Fakhr ʿUthmān al-Maqsī. He traveled to Jerusalem and died shortly thereafter, having endowed his books. These were then brought to Jāmiʿ al-Azhar, after which the aforementioned person took possession of them. May God have mercy on him. Indeed, he was a good man."@en .

rec:AIND-D01681 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01681-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01681-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01681-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01681 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن هاشم بن قاسم بن خليفة القرشي الهاشمي مات في رجب سنة ثنتين وستين خارج مكة ، وحمل ودفن بمعلاتها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Hāshim b. Qāsim b. Khalīfa al-Qurashī al-Hāshimī died in Rajab 862 AH outside Mecca, was transported, and buried in its (Mecca's) al-Muʿallā cemetery."@en .

rec:AIND-D01682 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01682-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01682-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01682 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن هاشم الكراني . مات بمكة في مستهل ذي الحجة سنة ست وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Hāshim al-Karānī. He died in Mecca at the beginning of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 866."@en .

rec:AIND-D01683 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01683-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01683-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01683 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن هانئ الشهاب الموقع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Hāniʾ, al-Shihāb, the Signatory Scribe."@en .

rec:AIND-D01687 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01687-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01687-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01687 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يحيى بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي الخير محمد بن محمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن فهد أبو الخير الهاشمي المكي الآتي أبوه . مات وقد طعن في الثانية في ربيع الأول سنة سبع وعشرين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Khayr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Fahd, Abū al-Khayr al-Hāshimī al-Makkī. His father will be mentioned later. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal 827 AH in Mecca, having entered his second year. Ibn Fahd recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D01689 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01689-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01689-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01689-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01689-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01689 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يحيى بن عمر بن محمد بن محاسن الشهاب الأنصاري المقدسي . نزيل مكة وممن ولي نظر القدس فلم يحمد واقفين . مات بمكة في يوم الإثنين سادس عشري جمادى الآخرة سنة ست وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Resident of Mecca, and among those who held the office of nāẓir (administrator) of al-Quds, but was not praised by the waqf administrators. He died in Mecca on Monday, the 26th of Jumādā al-Ākhira in the year 876 H. Ibn Fahd recorded this date."@en .

rec:AIND-D01690 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01690-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01690-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01690 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يحيى بن عيسى بن عياش بن إبراهيم العوكلي القسنطيني . نزيل مكة وشيخ رباط الموفى ، وكان ماهرا في آلات التجارة . مات بها في ربيع الآخر سنة ستين . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yaḥyā b. ʿĪsā b. ʿAyyāsh b. Ibrāhīm al-ʿAwkalī al-Qusṭanṭīnī. He was a resident of Mecca and the shaykh of Ribāṭ al-Mawfā. He was skilled in trade instruments. He died there in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 860 AH. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D01691 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01691-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01691-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01691 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يحيى بن عيسى الشهاب الصنهاجي المغربي المقرئ . سمع التيسير للداني على الفوي مع عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن إسماعيل الكركي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yaḥyā b. ʿĪsā, al-Shihāb al-Ṣanhājī al-Maghribī al-Muqriʾ (Qurʾān reciter). He heard al-Taysīr by al-Dānī from al-Fuwwī, together with ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl al-Karakī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01692 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01692-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01692-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01692 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يحيى بن أبي عبد الله محمد بن أحمد الشريف قاضي الجماعة أبو العباس الحسني التلمساني المغربي المالكي حفيد شارح الجمل للخونجي ممن أخذ عنه أبو عبد الله محمد بن علي بن محمد بن علي بن الأزرق وقال أنه ممن عمر ، وهو سنة ست وتسعين من الأحياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yaḥyā b. Abī ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, al-Sharīf, Qāḍī al-Jamāʿa, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Ḥasanī al-Tilimsānī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī. Grandson of the commentator on al-Jumal by al-Khūnajī. Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. al-Azraq took knowledge from him, and it is said that he was among those who lived long; he was alive in 896 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01693 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01693-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01693-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01693 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الفقيه محيي الدين يحيى بن محمد بن تقي الكازروني المدني أخو علي . سمعا علي الزين المراغي في سنة اثنتي عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Faqīh Muḥyī al-Dīn Yaḥyā b. Muḥammad b. Taqī al-Kāzarūnī al-Madanī, brother of ʿAlī. He heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī in the year 812 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01694 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01694-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01694-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01694 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يحيى بن يشبك الفقيه الشهاب الآتي أبوه وجده . كان قد جاز البلوغ حين موت أبيه ولم يتصون مع حسن شكالته وإضافة ما كان باسم أبيه إليه بل ورث جده . مات في جمادى الثانية سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yaḥyā b. Yashbak, al-Faqīh al-Shihāb. His father and grandfather will be mentioned later. He had already reached puberty at the time of his father's death. He was not protected by his good character and the addition of his father's name to his own; rather, he inherited from his grandfather. He died in Jumādā al-Thāniya in the year 895 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01696 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01696-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01696-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01696-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01696 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يحيى الحسني الدروي المخلافي اليماني . رجل معتقد تحكى له كرامات . توفي تقريبا قبيل الخمسين وخلفه ابنه محيي الدين محمد وممن صحبه الشريف عبد الله بن عامر بن محمد البدر الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yaḥyā al-Ḥasanī al-Darwī al-Makhlafī al-Yamanī. A man of faith, for whom miracles are recounted. He died approximately before [the year] 850 AH, and his son Muḥyī al-Dīn Muḥammad succeeded him. Among those whom he (the subject) accompanied was al-Sharīf ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿĀmir b. Muḥammad al-Badr (mentioned later)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01698 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01698-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01698-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01698 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن أبي يزيد من طرباي أخو محمد الآتي وهو الأصغر . ولد في سنة ست وستين بالقاهرة ممن أخذ عني مع أخيه وكذا سمع من الخطيب الحنبلي وغيره وحج وخالطه أخاه في بعض ما كان ينوبه من الضرورات لمخدومه وغيرها . مات فيما بلغني وأنا بمكة سنة سبع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Abī Yazīd from Ṭarabāy, the younger brother of Muḥammad (forthcoming). He was born in 866 in Cairo, and was among those who studied under me, along with his brother. He also heard from al-Khaṭīb al-Ḥanbalī and others. He performed the Hajj. His brother associated with him in some of the needs that befell his master, and other matters. He died, as I heard while I was in Mecca, in 897."@en .

rec:AIND-D01699 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01699-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01699-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01699 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يس بن خلد المعبدي . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yas b. Khald al-Maʿbadī. He was among those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D01701 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01701-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01701-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01701-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01701 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يعقوب بن محمد بن صديق البرلسي الآتي أبوه وأخوه محمد . تعاني التجارة وصاهر البرهان بن عليبة على ابنته ولم يحصل منه راحة ومولده قبل الخمسين وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yaʿqūb b. Muḥammad b. Ṣiddīq al-Burlusī. His father [Yaʿqūb] and his brother Muḥammad will be mentioned later. He engaged in trade and married the daughter of al-Burhān b. ʿUlayba, but found no comfort from him. He was born before 850 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01702 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01702-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01702-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01702-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01702-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01702 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يلبغا شهاب الدين العمري الخاصكي الحسني صاحب الكيس وأستاذ الظاهر برقوق . كان معظما في الدولة أحد المقدمين بمصر في أيامه ثم أمير مجلس ثم نفاه إلى الشام وأقام بطالا في طرابلس وآل أمره إلى أن ذبح مع أيتمش في رابع شعبان سنة اثنتين وقد زاد على الأربعين وقارب السبعين . أغفله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yalbaghā, Shihāb al-Dīn, al-ʿUmarī, al-Khāṣṣakī, al-Ḥasanī, known as Ṣāḥib al-Kīs (Master of the Purse) and ustādh (master/tutor) of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq. He was highly esteemed in the state, one of the muqaddams (commanders) in Egypt in his day, then an amīr majlis (amir of the council). He was later exiled to Syria and resided unemployed in Tripoli. His end came when he was slaughtered together with Aytamish on the 4th of Shaʿbān in the year 802 H. At that time he was over forty and close to seventy. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) omitted him from his Inbāʾ (al-Ghumr)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01704 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01704-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01704-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01704-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01704 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف بن أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن علي بن عبد الكريم بن يوسف بن سالم بن دليم الدميري البصري ثم المكي ابن أخي أحمد الماضي ويعرف بابن دليم . مات في ذي القعدة سنة ست وستين ودفن بالمعلاة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yūsuf b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Yūsuf b. Sālim b. Dulaym al-Damīrī, al-Baṣrī, then al-Makkī, nephew of the aforementioned Aḥmad (al-Shihāb Dulaym), and known as Ibn Dulaym. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 866 H and was buried in al-Muʿallā. Ibn Fahd recorded his obituary."@en .

rec:AIND-D01708 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01708-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01708-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01708-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01708 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف بن إسماعيل بن عثمان الشهاب الكوراني . مضى بدون يوسف [= AIND-D00552]"@ar .

rec:AIND-D01709 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01709-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01709-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01709 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف بن الحسن العزي الشافعي ويعرف بابن الهرس . ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yūsuf b. al-Ḥasan al-ʿIzzī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Hars. He was among those who acquired [knowledge] from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01711 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01711-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01711-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01711-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01711-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01711 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف بن عبد الرحمن اليماني ثم المكي والد صديق الآتي ويعرف بالأهدل . أحد من يعتقده الناس باليمن وهو من بيت صلاح وعلم ، جاور بمكة زمانا ، ومات في سادس عشر ذي الحجة سنة تسع عشرة . ذكره الفاسي مطولا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yūsuf b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Yamanī, then al-Makkī. Father of Ṣiddīq (forthcoming), and known as al-Ahdal. He was one of those whom people in Yemen venerated, hailing from a house of righteousness and knowledge. He resided (jāwara) in Mecca for a long time, and died on the 16th of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 819 H. al-Fāsī mentioned him at length."@en .

rec:AIND-D01712 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01712-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01712-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01712-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01712 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف بن عبد الكريم الشهاب بن الجمال ناظر الخاص المعروف بابن كاتب جكم وهو سبط الكمال بن البارزي وأخو الكمال محمد ناظر الجيش . قرأ القرآن وغيره واستقر في نظر الجوالي وقتا وكذا في نظر الجيش مرة بعد أخيه ومرة بعد ولد أخيه . وحج غير مرة والغالب عليه اليبس والانجماع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yūsuf b. ʿAbd al-Karīm, al-Shihāb by laqab, son of al-Jamāl, known as Ibn Kātib Jakam, supervisor of the privy funds (nāẓir al-khāṣṣ). He was the maternal grandson (sibṭ) of al-Kamāl b. al-Bārizī and the brother of al-Kamāl Muḥammad, the supervisor of the army. He recited the Qurʾān and other texts. He held the supervisorship of the jawālī (poll-tax) for a time, and likewise served as supervisor of the army once after his brother, and again after his brother's son. He performed the Hajj more than once. He was generally austere, reticent, and withdrawn."@en .

rec:AIND-D01718 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01718-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01718-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01718-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01718 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف بن محمد البانياسي . سيأتي فيمن لم يسم جده [= AIND-D01723]"@ar .

rec:AIND-D01720 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01720-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01720-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01720-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01720 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف الشهاب الحوراني الدمشقي العدل الرضي الفقيه . مات في يوم السبت عاشر جمادى الأولى سنة ست وأربعين بدمشق ودفن بمقبرة باب الفراديس وكانت جنازته حافلة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yūsuf al-Shihāb al-Ḥawrānī al-Dimashqī, al-ʿAdl al-Raḍī al-Faqīh. He died on Saturday, the 10th of Jumādā al-Ūlā, in the year 846 AH, in Damascus. He was buried in the Bāb al-Farādīs cemetery, and his funeral was well-attended."@en .

rec:AIND-D01721 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01721-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01721-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01721-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01721 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف الشهاب الخطيب ويلقب درابة بضم المهملة وتشديد الراء وبعد الألف موحدة اشتغل قليلا وجلس مع الشهود دهرا طويلا وعمل توقيع الحكم ثم توقيع الدرج ثم الدست وكان سليم الباطن قليل الشر مع غفلة . مات في رجب سنة خمس وأربعين وقد قارب التسعين . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "701. Aḥmad b. Yūsuf, known as al-Shihāb al-Khaṭīb, and nicknamed Darāba (with a ḍamma on the undotted letter, a shadda on the rāʾ, and a single-dotted letter after the alif). He worked a little and sat with the witnesses for a long time. He held the office of signator of judicial decrees (tawqīʿ al-ḥukm), then signator of rolls (tawqīʿ al-daraj), and then the grand chancery (al-Dust). He was pure-hearted, with little evil, though somewhat heedless. He died in Rajab of 845 AH, having nearly reached ninety years of age. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his 『Inbāʾ (al-Ghumr)』."@en .

rec:AIND-D01722 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01722-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01722-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01722-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01722 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف الأديب شهاب الدين الرعيني . مات في سنة ثلاثين . قاله ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yūsuf, known as al-Adīb, laqab Shihāb al-Dīn, al-Raʿīnī. He died in the year 830 AH. Ibn ʿAzm reported this."@en .

rec:AIND-D01723 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01723-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01723-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01723-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01723-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01723 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف البانياسي ثم الدمشقي المقرئ قرأ بالروايات وسمع الحديث من سنة سبعين من بعض أصحاب الفخر وغيرهم . مات في شعبان سنة ثلاث عن سبعين سنة . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه وسمى بعضهم جده محمدا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yūsuf al-Bānyāsī, then al-Dimashqī, the Qurʾān reciter. He recited in the [canonical] transmissions and heard ḥadīth from the year 70 (the 770s) onward from some of the companions of al-Fakhr and others. He died in Shaʿbān 803 AH at the age of 70. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』. Some referred to his grandfather as Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01724 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01724-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01724-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01724 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف البساطي القاهري المالكي . أظنه رفيق المقسمي وصاحب خالي ولذا شهدا في أسجال عدالته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "704 Aḥmad b. Yūsuf al-Basāṭī al-Qāhirī al-Mālikī. I think he was the companion of al-Muqsimī and the friend of my maternal uncle, and thus the two of them testified in the records of his probity (ʿadāla)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01725 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01725-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01725-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01725-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01725 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يوسف الكوراني . مضى فيمن جده إسماعيل بن عثمان وأنه مضى غلطا في أحمد بن إسماعيل بن عثمان بدون يوسف . [= AIND-D00552]"@ar .

rec:AIND-D01728 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01728-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01728-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01728 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يونس الفاضل شهاب الدين الغزي ثم الحلبي الشافعي والد إبراهيم الضعيف الماضي ، أرخ البرهان الحلبي وفاته في سنة ثلاث ووصفه بالفضل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "707 Aḥmad b. Yūnus, known as al-Fāḍil, laqab Shihāb al-Dīn, originally al-Ghazzī, then al-Ḥalabī, Shāfiʿī. He was the father of Ibrāhīm al-Ḍaʿīf al-Māḍī (mentioned above). Al-Burhān al-Ḥalabī recorded his death in the year 803 and described him as 'al-Faḍl' (of excellence)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01729 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01729-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01729-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01729 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن يونس الشهاب الصفدي قاضيها الشافعي صهر الشمس بن حامد ولي قضاءها غير مرة صرف في بعضها بالعيزري ثم أعيد في ذي الحجة سنة تسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "708. Aḥmad b. Yūnus al-Shihāb al-Ṣafadī, the Shāfiʿī qāḍī of Safad. Son-in-law of al-Shams b. Ḥāmid. He held its judgeship on several occasions, being dismissed on some of them in connection with al-ʿAyzarī, then reappointed in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year ninety (890 H)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01730 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01730-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01730-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01730-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01730-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01730 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد ين يونس التلواني الأصل الحسيني سكنا سبط السيد النسابة ، سمع عليه وعلى غيره وتكسب بالشهادة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Yūnus al-Tilwānī, al-Ḥusaynī by residence. Maternal grandson (sibṭ) of al-Sayyid al-Nassāba. He heard from him (his grandfather) and from others, and earned a living through testimony (shahāda)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01731 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01731-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01731-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01731 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن شمس الأئمة السرائي الواعظ . لقيه ابن عربشاه في خوارزم فأخذ عنه وقال أنه كان يقال له ملك الكلام الفارسي والتركي والعربي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. Shams al-Aʾimma al-Sarāʾī al-Wāʿiẓ (the Preacher). Ibn ʿArabshāh met him in Khwārazm and took (knowledge) from him, and said that he was called the 'King of Persian, Turkish, and Arabic speech'."@en .

rec:AIND-D01732 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01732-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01732-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01732-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01732 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد نور الدين ويدعى حاجي نور بن عز الدين بن نور الدين اللاري البيد شهيوري ويعرف بخدمة السيد قاضي الحنابلة بالحرمين وهو بنور أشهر . ممن سمع مني بالحرمين أشياء ولا بأس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad Nūr al-Dīn, also called Ḥājjī Nūr, son of ʿIzz al-Dīn, son of Nūr al-Dīn, al-Lārī al-Bīd-Shahyūrī. He is known for serving al-Sayyid, the Qāḍī of the Ḥanābila in the Two Holy Cities (al-Ḥaramayn), and he is better known as Nūr. He is one of those who heard some things from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the Ḥaramayn, and there is nothing wrong with him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01733 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01733-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01733-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01733-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01733 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب بن الأذرعي المالكي قاضي طرابلس ومحدثها . قتل في مقتلة افتات بها نائبها في سنة اثنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb b. al-Adhraʿī, of the Mālikī school, qāḍī and muḥaddith of Tripoli. He was killed in a massacre highhandedly perpetrated by its deputy (nāʾib) in the year 802."@en .

rec:AIND-D01734 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01734-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01734-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01734-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01734 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب بن البابا . تميز في القراءات وتلا عليه لأبي عمرو والحسام بن حريز ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb b. al-Bābā. He excelled in the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt); the reading of Abū ʿAmr and [that of] al-Ḥusām b. Ḥurayz were recited under him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01735 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01735-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01735-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01735-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01735 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب بن البشازي بكسر الموحدة ثم شين معجمة خفيفة بعدها زاي معجمة من علماء دنجية أو دمياط قرأ عليه عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن عبد الله الدنجيهي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb b. al-Bashāzī (al-Bashāzī: with a kasra on the single-dotted bāʾ, then a lightly dotted shīn without shadda, followed by a dotted zāy). He was one of the scholars of Danjiyya or Dumyāṭ. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Danjīhī recited (the Qurʾān) to him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01736 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01736-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01736-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01736-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01736 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الكيلاني الأصل المكي الشهير بابن خواجا . مات بمكة في ليلة الأحد سلخ ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وتسعين وصلى عليه من الغد وأوصى للقاضي وغيره ، وهو أخو أبي القسم بن محب الدين لأمه واسم أبيه أبو بكر بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Kīlānī al-Aṣl al-Makkī, renowned as Ibn Khawājā. He died in Mecca on Sunday night, the last day of Dhū al-Ḥijja in 892 H. Funeral prayers were held for him the next day. He bequeathed to the qāḍī and others. He was the maternal half-brother of Abū al-Qāsim b. Muḥibb al-Dīn, and his father's name was Abū Bakr b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01737 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01737-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01737-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01737-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01737 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب بن الديوان استادار حلب ثم وكيل السلطان بعد ابن الصوة . سلخ في تاسع جمادى الثانية سنة أربع وتسعين بالقاهرة وقد جاز السبعين واسم أيبه أبو بكر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb b. al-Dīwān. He served as Ustādār of Aleppo, then as Wakīl al-Sulṭān in succession to Ibn al-Ṣawwa. He died in Cairo on the ninth of Jumādā al-Thāniya in the year 894 H, having passed seventy years of age. His father's name was Abū Bakr."@en .

rec:AIND-D01738 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01738-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01738-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01738 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب بن الشريفة القدسي ثم المكي وهو ابن محمد بن محمد بن المولى ممن كان يتكسب بالكتب وغيرها وله إحساس في النظم ونحوه امتدح شيخنا وغيره ومات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة ثلاث وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb b. al-Sharīfa, al-Qudsī then al-Makkī. He was the son of Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. al-Mawlā. He earned his living dealing in books and other goods, and had a talent for poetry and the like, with which he praised our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja 873 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01739 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01739-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01739-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01739-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01739-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01739 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الدمشقي ويعرف بابن الصاحب كان أولا ديران لبعض الأمراء ثم عمل نقيبا لابن عمته القطب الخيضري ثم ناب في القضاء عن ابن الفرفور فلما توفي القطب طلب لمصر فتوجه وانزعج عن مكالمة الملك وتعلل حتى مات في ثالث شعبان سنة أربع وتسعين ودفن بالقرافة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Dimashqī, known as Ibn al-Ṣāḥib. He was initially secretary (dīwān) to some of the amirs, then served as naqīb for his paternal cousin (his paternal aunt's son) al-Quṭb al-Khayḍarī. He then deputized in the judiciary on behalf of Ibn al-Farfūr. When al-Quṭb died, he was summoned to Egypt and went there, but he became distressed by his audience with the king and feigned illness until he died on the 3rd of Shaʿbān in the year 894 H. He was buried in al-Qarāfa."@en .

rec:AIND-D01740 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01740-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01740-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01740 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب بن الفيومية جابي وقف الزمام بمكة وهو ابن محمد بن علي ممن يحفظ القرآن ومات في المحرم سنة تسع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb b. al-Fayyūmiyya, son of Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, was a collector (jābī) for the Waqf al-Zimām endowment in Mecca. He had memorized the Qurʾān. He died in Muḥarram 859 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01742 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01742-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01742-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01742-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01742 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الدمشقي المالكي بن النحاس . أحد الفساق ممن استنابه المالكي عجزا وغلبة ببدل ثلثمائة دينار لمن ألزمه بذلك ثم عزله ومات بعد مصروفا فجأة سقط عن فرسه بباب جيرون فمات في ساعته سنة ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Dimashqī al-Mālikī b. al-Naḥḥās. He was one of the dissolute persons (fussāq) whom the Mālikī judge appointed as his deputy — out of the judge's incapacity and under pressure — in exchange for 300 dinars paid to the one who imposed it upon him. Then he was dismissed. He died suddenly after falling from his horse at Bāb Jīrūn in the year 893 H, expiring on the spot."@en .

rec:AIND-D01744 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01744-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01744-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01744-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01744 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الأبشيهي المقرئ بنواحي جامع الطباخ وخال شمس الدين بن طرطور المقرئ لكونه أخا أمه من الرضاع ولذا جود عليه المدوري للسوسي في ختمتين حسبما أخبرني به ولم يدر على من قرأ ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad, al-Shihāb al-Abshīhī, a Qurʾān reciter (muqriʾ), resided in the vicinity of Jāmiʿ al-Ṭabbākh. He was the maternal (milk-)uncle of Shams al-Dīn b. Ṭarṭūr al-Muqriʾ, because he was his mother's milk-brother. As he (Aḥmad) informed me (al-Sakhāwī), al-Madūrī perfected under him the recitation in the transmission of al-Sūsī over two complete readings. However, he (Aḥmad) himself did not know from whom he had received his own recitation."@en .

rec:AIND-D01745 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01745-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01745-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01745 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الأزهري الغزولي بالسرب . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad, al-Shihāb al-Azharī al-Ghazūlī bi-l-Sarb. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 893 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01748 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01748-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01748-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01748 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الحجيراني اللؤلؤي كان أبوه خطيب قرية حجيرا فنشأ هذا في طلب العلم وقرأ على ابن الحباب ثم صحب الشيخ الموصلي وحصل كتبا كثيرا وكان يرتزق من ثقب اللؤلؤ . مات بقريته في المحرم سنة سبع وعشرين عن نحو الستين . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Ḥujayrānī al-Luʾluʾī. His father was the khaṭīb of Ḥujayrā village. He grew up in pursuit of knowledge, studying (qaraʾa) under Ibn al-Ḥabbāb, then kept the company of al-Shaykh al-Mawṣilī and acquired many books. He earned his living by drilling pearls. He died in his village in Muḥarram 827 H, at around sixty years of age. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D01749 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01749-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01749-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01749 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الحلبي الحنبلي ويعرف بخازوق ولي قضاء الحنابلة بحلب مرارا وصرف في سنة خمس وثلاثين بابن الرسام فدخل القاهرة ساعيا في العود فلم يتهيأ إلا بعد مدة ورجع فمرض بدمشق ودخل حلب في محفة لعجزه بالمرض فاستمر قليلا ثم مات في سنة ثمان وثلاثين . ذكره شيخنا أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Ḥalabī al-Ḥanbalī, known as Khāzūq. He repeatedly held the office of qāḍī of the Ḥanbalīs in Aleppo and was dismissed in 835 H, being replaced by Ibn al-Rassām. He then entered Cairo seeking reinstatement, which did not come about for some time. On his return he fell ill in Damascus and entered Aleppo in a litter because of his illness. He remained a short while, then died in 838 H. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī) also mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01750 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01750-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01750-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01750-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01750-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D01750-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D01750-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01750 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الحلبي ثم الدمشقي رئيس المؤذنين بجامعها ، مات بها فجأة في خامس جمادى الأولى سنة تسع وخمسين وكانت له يد طولى في علم الهيئة ولم يخلف بدمش فيه مثله واستقر بعده في الرياسة شمس الدين الحمصي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Ḥalabī, then al-Dimashqī, chief muezzin of its (Damascus's) mosque. He died there suddenly on the 5th of Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 859 H. He had a profound command of astronomy, and no one comparable to him was left in Damascus in that field. Shams al-Dīn al-Ḥimṣī succeeded him in the leadership."@en .

rec:AIND-D01751 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01751-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01751-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01751 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الحمصي ثم الدمشقي المقيم فيها بزاوية أحمد الأقباعي الماضي قريبا . كان بارعا في الفرائض أخذها عنه التاج بن عرب شاه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Ḥimṣī, then al-Dimashqī, who settled in Damascus at the zāwiya of Aḥmad al-Aqbāʿī (mentioned shortly before). He was proficient in inheritance law (al-farāʾiḍ), which al-Tāj b. ʿArab Shāh took from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01752 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01752-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01752-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01752-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01752 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الحنفي قاضي طرابلس . قتل في مقتلة افتات فيها نائبها سنة اثنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Ḥanafī, qāḍī of Ṭarābulus (Tripoli). He was killed in a massacre in the year 802 H, in which the town's deputy governor acted arbitrarily (iftāt), overstepping his authority."@en .

rec:AIND-D01753 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01753-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01753-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01753 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الدميري كان فاضلا يستحضر كثيرا من المسائل الفقهية وناب في الحكم ببعض النواحي وبالقاهرة ومرض مدة طويلة بوجع الظهر ثم بالإسهال . مات في حادي عشري صفر سنة ثلاث وأربعين وأظنه جاز الستين . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Damīrī was a virtuous man who kept many jurisprudential questions in memory. He served as deputy judge in some districts and in Cairo. He suffered a prolonged illness, first with back pain, then with diarrhea. He died on the 21st of Ṣafar in the year 843 H, and I believe he had passed sixty years of age. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D01754 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01754-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01754-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01754 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الساعي الحلبي . ممن قرأ عليه العفيف عبد الله بن محمد بن أحمد بن أحمد . الشريف الإسحاقي القرآن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Sāʿī al-Ḥalabī. al-ʿAfīf ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Aḥmad al-Sharīf al-Isḥāqī recited the Qurʾān to him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01755 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01755-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01755-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01755-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01755 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب السخاوي . مضى قريبا فيمن يعرف بابن مونن [= AIND-D01741] ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Sakhāwī. His biography was given previously among those known as Ibn Mūnin (= the fuller entry #AIND-D01741)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01756 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01756-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01756-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01756-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01756 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب السنهوري التاجر بالشرب المتزوج بابنة أخي فتح الدين المؤذن بجامع صلم . مات في جمادى الثانية سنة ثلاث وتسعين ويحرر مع أحمد الشهاب الأزهري الغزولي الماضي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Sanhūrī, a merchant dealing in sharb (fine linen). He married the daughter of the brother (i.e. the niece) of Fatḥ al-Dīn, the muezzin at Jāmiʿ Ṣalam. He died in Jumādā al-Thāniya of the year 893 H. His entry is to be collated with that of Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Azharī al-Ghazūlī, mentioned previously."@en .

rec:AIND-D01757 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01757-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01757-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01757-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01757 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الصوة . هو ابن علي بن إبراهيم الحلبي ابن أخي المقتول . وهو الملقب بالصوة له نظم سيأتي منه في عبيد الله بن عبد الله بل كتب عنه منه بمكة بعد التسعين العز بن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Ṣawa. He is the son of ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm al-Ḥalabī, the nephew (son of the brother) of the slain man. He was nicknamed al-Ṣawa and composed poetry. Some of it is cited in the entry for ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh (mentioned later). Indeed, al-ʿIzz b. Fahd recorded some of his poetry from him in Mecca after 890 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01758 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01758-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01758-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01758-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01758 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب العبادي . أحد صوفية الأشرفية . مات في أواخر المحرم سنة إحدى وتسعين وخلف تركة تبلغ ألف دينار فأكثر مع تقتيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-ʿAbbādī. One of the Sufis of al-Ashrafiyya. He died in the last days of Muḥarram in the year 891 H. He left an estate amounting to a thousand dinars or more, despite his frugality."@en .

rec:AIND-D01760 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01760-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01760-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01760 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الغزاوي وكيل الخواجا الناصري الفيومي ثم القاهري نزيل بيت شيخنا بباب البحر ويعرف بابن الخطيب كان يباشر عند الدوادار وغيره وفيه حشمة وإنسانية وفتوة وربما نظم ويخطب أحيانا بجامع المقسي مع مزيد سمنه والقدح فيه ، مات سنة أربع وتسعين أو التي بعدها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Ghazzāwī al-Fayyūmī, later al-Qāhirī. He resided in the house of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī) at Bāb al-Baḥr and was known as Ibn al-Khaṭīb. He served as an administrator under the dawādār and others, and possessed dignity, humanity, and futuwwa (chivalry). He sometimes composed poetry, and despite his excessive corpulence and being subject to criticism, he often preached at the Jāmiʿ al-Maqsī. He died in the year 894 H or the one after it."@en .

rec:AIND-D01761 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01761-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01761-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01761 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الفيومي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Fayyūmī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01763 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01763-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01763-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01763 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب القزاز ، لقيه المحب بن الإمام المحلي بمكة فتلا عليه لابن كثير ونافع وكان مقرئا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Qazzāz. Al-Muḥibb b. al-Imām al-Maḥallī met him in Mecca and recited to him according to (the readings of) Ibn Kathīr and Nāfiʿ. He was a Qurʾān-recitation teacher (muqriʾ)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01764 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01764-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01764-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01764-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01764 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب القوصي ثم القاهري ، كان ممن يعتني بالتجارة ويسافر إلى الحجاز لذلك في البحر وغيره ثم صحب التقوى البلقيني وولده ولي الدين ثم الزيني بن مزهر واقتصر عليه وحج معه في الرجبية مع ملازمته التلاوة ومباشرة تصوف الصلاحية سعيد السعداء وهو في آخر عمره أحسن حالا . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة ثمان وسبعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Qūṣī, then al-Qāhirī. He was among those who engaged in trade and traveled to the Ḥijāz for that purpose, by sea and other means. He then accompanied al-Taqī al-Bulqīnī and his son Walī al-Dīn (al-Walawī), and afterwards al-Zaynī b. Mazhar, attaching himself exclusively to him. He performed the Hajj with (al-Bulqīnī) in the Rajabiyya caravan, while maintaining constant Qurʾān recitation and practicing Sufism at the Ṣalāḥiyya Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. In his later life his condition improved. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira in the year 878 H. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01766 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01766-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01766-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01766-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01766 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الكاشف . عامي تنقل في الخدم حتى ولي كشف التراب بالغرية وأثرى جدا بحيث سعى في الاستادارية ولزم من ذلك أن دبر الاستادار عليه حتى أخرجه السلطان منفيا إلى دمشق فلم يلبث أن مات بها في رمضان سنة اثنتين وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Kāshif. A commoner, he moved from post to post until he was appointed supervisor of dredging (kashf al-turāb) at al-Gharbiyya (written al-Ghurīya in the text). He became very wealthy and sought the office of Ustādār, which led the Ustādār to plot against him. As a result, the Sultan exiled him to Damascus, where he soon died in Ramaḍān 852 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01767 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01767-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01767-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01767-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01767-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01767 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب المارديني ثم الدمشقي الحنبلي ، كان حسن الشكالة والخط يتكسب بالشهادة كتب عنه البدري في مجموعة قوله : %~% عزمت على حبي بسورة يونس %~% وكان نفورا كالظبا فتأنسا %~% %~% ومال إلى نحوي وحق براءة %~% لقد نلت وصلا من عزيمة يونسا %~% مات تقريبا بعد سنة أربع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Mārdīnī, then al-Dimashqī, al-Ḥanbalī. He had a handsome appearance and fine handwriting, and earned his living by giving testimony (shahāda). Al-Badrī recorded him in his compilation, citing (his own) verses about him: “I resolved upon my love by Sūrat Yūnus — though he was skittish like a gazelle, he grew accustomed. He inclined toward me, and by Sūrat Barāʾa I swear, I have indeed won union through the resolve of Yūnus.” He died approximately after the year 864 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01768 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01768-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01768-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01768 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب المدني ويعرف بالنشار . كان يتردد إلى القاهرة بل يكثر بها الإقامة قتل في رجوعه مع نائب جدة بالينبوع سنة ثمان وسبعين غير مأسوف عليه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Madanī, also known as al-Nashshār. He frequented Cairo and often resided there. In the year 878 H he was killed at Yanbuʿ while returning with the deputy of Jidda, and his death was not mourned."@en .

rec:AIND-D01769 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01769-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01769-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01769-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01769 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب المعلقي المالكي الإمام العلامة المسند المعمر . مات سنة تسع وعشرين عن نحو السبعين أو التسعين ليوافق وصفه بالتعمير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Muʿalliqī al-Mālikī, the imam, the great scholar (al-ʿallāma), the musnid (authority in hadith transmission), the long-lived (al-muʿammar). He died in the year 829 H at around seventy or ninety years of age, in keeping with his description as long-lived."@en .

rec:AIND-D01770 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01770-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01770-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01770 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب لمغربي الصنهاجي المالكي . كان إماما فاضلا مفننا درس بالأزهر وغيره وانتفع به الفضلاء مات في يوم الأحد تاسع ربيع الأول سنة خمس وخمسين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Maghribī al-Ṣanhājī al-Mālikī. He was an excellent, accomplished, and versatile imam (leading scholar) who taught at al-Azhar and elsewhere, and scholars benefited greatly from him. He died on Sunday, the 9th of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 855 H. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01771 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01771-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01771-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01771-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01771 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب المغربي المالكي قاضيهم بطرابلس . أخذ عنه القاضي عبد القادر بمكة ويحتمل أن يكون الذي قبله ولكن تحرر كونه ولي قضاء طرابلس ، نعم في شيوخ القاضي أيضا عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن بن مسعود الآتي وهو ولي قضاء طرابلس جزما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Maghribī al-Mālikī, their qāḍī in Ṭarābulus (Tripoli). Al-Qāḍī ʿAbd al-Qādir studied fiqh from him in Mecca. It is possible that he is (the same as) the one mentioned just before him, but it is confirmed that he held the judgeship of Ṭarābulus. Indeed, among the shaykhs of the aforementioned qāḍī (ʿAbd al-Qādir) was also ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Masʿūd (mentioned later), who certainly held the judgeship of Ṭarābulus."@en .

rec:AIND-D01772 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01772-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01772-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01772-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01772-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01772 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب المنبجي الدمشقي . مات في ليلة الأحد حادي عشر ذي القعدة سنة ثمان وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Manbijī al-Dimashqī. He died on the night of Sunday, the eleventh of Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 858 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01773 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01773-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01773-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01773 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب النشرتي المقرئي الحيسوب . تلا عليه المحب بن الإمام لأبي عمرو بالمحلة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad, known by the laqab al-Shihāb, with the nisbas al-Nishartī and al-Muqriʾī, and the epithet al-Ḥaysūb (the arithmetician). Al-Muḥibb b. al-Imām (al-Maḥallī) recited the Qurʾān to him according to the reading of Abū ʿAmr in al-Maḥalla — i.e., al-Muḥibb studied the recitation under him (Aḥmad, the teacher)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01774 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01774-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01774-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01774 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب النفياي بكسر النون وسكون الفاء بعدها تحتانية مثناة نسبة إلى بليدة بالوجه البحري ويعرف بالزلباني . قال شيخنا في أنبائه أنه كان من مشاهير الطلبة عند قدماء المشايخ ثم نزل في فقاهة المؤيدية وتكسب بالشهادة مدة حتى مات في سنة ثلاث وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Nafyāy, with a kasra on the nūn, a sukūn on the fāʾ, followed by a doubled tāʾ al-taḥtāniyya, a nisba to a small town in Lower Egypt called Nafyāy. He was also known as al-Zalbānī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his work 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』 that he was one of the famous students of the elder shaykhs, then he resided in the jurisprudence department of al-Muʾayyadiyya, earned his living through the office of witness for some time, until he died in the year 843."@en .

rec:AIND-D01775 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01775-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01775-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01775 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب النفادي . ممن قرأ عليه القرآن الصدر أحمد الزفتاوي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Nafādī. Among those who recited the Qurʾān to him was al-Ṣadr Aḥmad al-Zaftāwī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01776 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01776-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01776-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01776 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب الهيثمي . تلا عليه الحسام بن حريز لأبي عمرو ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shihāb al-Haythamī. Al-Ḥusām b. Ḥurayz recited to him (Aḥmad) according to the reading of Abū ʿAmr."@en .

rec:AIND-D01777 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01777-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01777-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01777-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01777-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01777 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشهاب المعروف باليمني أحد قراء الجوق بالقاهرة تلمذ لابن الطباخ وقرأ معه وحاكاه ، وكان للناس في سماعه رغبة زائدة ، مات في صفر سنة خمس وعشرين ولم يخلف بعده من يقرأ على طريقته قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad, known as al-Shihāb, commonly known as al-Yamanī, was one of the readers of the Jawq in Cairo. He was a student of Ibn al-Ṭabbākh, read with him, and imitated his style. People showed great enthusiasm for his recitations. He died in Ṣafar 825 AH and left no one after him who read in his style, as stated by our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』."@en .

rec:AIND-D01778 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01778-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01778-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01778-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01778-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01778 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الفخر الشيفسكي الشيرازي . قال الطاوسي قرأت عليه بشيراز مقدمات العلوم كالكافية في النحو والصرف للزنجاني وشرحهما للسيد ركن الدين والتفتازاني وغيرهما وأجاز لي في شهور سنة ثمانمائة والظاهر أنه تأخر عنها ولذا كتبته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Fakhr al-Shīfaskī al-Shīrāzī. Al-Ṭāwūsī (= AIND-D00900) said: I read to him in Shiraz the introductions to the sciences — such as al-Kāfiya in grammar and morphology by al-Zanjānī and its two commentaries by al-Sayyid Rukn al-Dīn and al-Taftāzānī, and others — and he granted me an ijāza in the months of the year 800 H. It appears he died after that, and that is why I recorded him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01779 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01779-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01779-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01779-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01779 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد أبو طاقية عمر نحو التسعين . ومات سنة تسع وعشرين ودفن عند الشيخ عبد الله المنوفي وكانت إقامته بالظاهرية القديمة لكونه متزوجا بأم أحمد النحريري الضرير نزيلها وقد صحبه جماعة كالسراج الوروري والعز السنباطي وقال لي إنه إخبره أنه صحب الشيخ يوسف العجمي أشهرا وأخذ عنه الميقات الشرف بن الخشاب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad Abū Ṭāqiyya lived to about ninety. He died in 829 H and was buried near Shaykh ʿAbd Allāh al-Munūfī. His residence was at al-Ẓāhiriyya al-Qadīma, as he was married to the mother of Aḥmad al-Naḥrīrī al-Ḍarīr, a resident there. A group accompanied him (as students), such as al-Sirāj al-Warūrī and al-ʿIzz al-Sunbāṭī. He (Abū Ṭāqiyya) told me that he had accompanied Shaykh Yūsuf al-ʿAjamī for several months; al-Sharaf b. al-Khashshāb also took the science of timing (al-mīqāt) from him (al-ʿAjamī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01780 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01780-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01780-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01780-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01780 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد أبو الطرار بن عروس . مات سنة بضع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad Abū al-Ṭarrār b. ʿArūs. He died in the \"sixty-odd\" years (bidʿ wa-sittīn), i.e. the 860s H (861–869)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01781 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01781-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01781-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01781-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01781-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01781 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد أبو العباس القبيباتي الحنفي ويعرف بابن فريفير ممن قرأ البخاري على مصطفى بن بقطمر الحنفي بعد العشرين وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qubaybātī al-Ḥanafī, also known as Ibn Farīfīr. He was among those who recited al-Bukhārī (Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī) under Muṣṭafā b. Baqṭamur al-Ḥanafī after 820 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01782 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01782-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01782-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01782-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01782 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد أبو العباس بن العجل قاضي فاس . مات سنة سبع وخمسين . أرخه ابن عزم وقال مرة أخرى سنة اثنتين وخمسين وأحدهما غلط بل رأيت من ينكر كونه قاضيا وأنه كان مدرسا بمدرسة الصهريج بفاس بالقرب من جامع الأندلس عالما بعلوم من فقه وعربية وغير ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad Abū al-ʿAbbās b. al-ʿAjl, qāḍī of Fās. He died in the year 857 H. Ibn ʿAzm dated his death, and on another occasion gave 852 H, one of which is in error. Indeed, I have even seen some who deny that he was a qāḍī. He was a teacher (mudarris) at Madrasat al-Ṣihrīj in Fās, near Jāmiʿ al-Andalus, and a scholar knowledgeable in jurisprudence, Arabic, and other sciences."@en .

rec:AIND-D01783 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01783-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01783-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01783-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01783-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01783 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد ابن أخت جمال الدين الاستادار وأخو حمزة الآتي . كان ممن صودر في محنته مع أقربائه وآله وخنق في ربيع الآخر سنة أربع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad, the son of the sister of Jamāl al-Dīn (al-Bīrī) al-Ustādār, and brother of the forthcoming Ḥamza (= AIND-D02791). He was among those whose property was confiscated during his ordeal with his relatives and family, and was strangled in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir 814 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01785 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01785-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01785-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01785-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01785 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد المعروف بابن رياض الأحمدي . أخذ عن أبي شامة صاحب الشيخ إسماعيل الأنبابي وكان صالحا معتقدا مات في يوم السبت خامس عشري رجب سنة ست وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad, known as Ibn Riyāḍ al-Aḥmadī. He took (studied) from Abū Shāma, the companion of al-Shaykh Ismāʿīl al-Anbābī. He was a righteous, devout man. He died on Saturday, the 25th of Rajab in the year 856 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01786 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01786-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01786-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01786-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01786 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الست التونسي . وصفه ابن عزم . مات تقريبا سنة ستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Sitt al-Tūnisī. Ibn ʿAzm described him. He died approximately in the year 860 H. (\"Ibn al-Sitt\" — \"son of the lady\" — is a metronymic byname, not a patronymic.)"@en .

rec:AIND-D01787 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01787-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01787-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01787-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01787 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن السروجي الجابي بوقف المؤيدية . مات في ربيع الثاني سنة ثلاث وتسعين وقد افتقر جدا وعجز بعد أن كان شديد الباس قوي الرأس وأظنه جاز الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Surūjī al-Jābī, the revenue-collector (jābī) of the Waqf al-Muʾayyadiyya. He died in Rabīʿ al-Thānī in the year 893 H. He had become very poor and infirm after having been mighty and strong-headed. I believe he was over sixty years old."@en .

rec:AIND-D01788 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01788-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01788-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01788-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01788 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الشهيد . قال شيخنا في أنبائه كان أولا يتعانى صناعة الفرى ثم اشتغل قليلا وباشر في ديوان السلطان ثم ولي الوزارة ووقعت فتنة اللنك وهو وزير فاستصحبه معه إلى بلاده ثم خلص منم بعد يسير وورد دمشق فباشر نظر الجيش وغيره في شعبان . ومات سنة ثلاث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his 『Inbāʾ』 that he first engaged in the furrier's craft, then worked for a short time and served in the Sultan's chancellery, and then became a vizier. When the fitna of Timur (803 AH) occurred, he was a vizier, and Timur took him with him to his lands. He was released after a short period, then arrived in Damascus, where he undertook the supervision of the army and other duties in Shaʿbān. He died in the year 803 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01789 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01789-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01789-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01789 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن الصلف أحد فراشي البيمارستان المنصوري . مات بمكة سنة خمس وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Ṣalaf, one of the attendants of al-Bīmāristān al-Manṣūrī. He died in Makka in 885 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01790 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01790-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01790-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01790-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01790 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد بن المومني ممن يذكر بين العوام بالجذب ويعتقد لذلك مات في يوم الخميس ثاني عشر ربيع الأول سنة سبعين ودفن قريبا من تربة الشيخ خلد الحجاجي قبلي جامع قوصون ، أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad b. al-Muʾminī, one who was remembered among the common people for his spiritual attraction (jadhb) and was venerated for that reason. He died on Thursday, the twelfth of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year seventy (870 H) and was buried near the tomb of Shaykh Khald al-Ḥajjājī, south of Jāmiʿ Qawṣūn. al-Munīr chronicled him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01791 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01791-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01791-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01791-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01791-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01791 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد أخو الزين الاستادار لأنه قتل بالمحلة في رمضان سنة أربع وخمسين وكان عبلا أخضر اللون ربعة مسرفا على نفسه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad, brother of al-Zayn al-Ustādār — recorded here because he was killed in al-Maḥalla in Ramaḍān of the year 854 H. He was stout-bodied, green-complexioned, of medium height, and dissolute."@en .

rec:AIND-D01794 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01794-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01794-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01794-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01794-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01794 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد كمونة الصعيدي ، ممن خدم عند الأشرف قايتباي حين إمرته فلما تسلطن استقر به مهتار الشربخاناه وكان إلى الخير أقرب مات فيما قيل سنة أربع وتسعين وخلفه في وظيفته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad Kamūna al-Ṣaʿīdī, one of those who served al-Ashraf Qāytbāy during his emirate. When Qāytbāy became sultan, he appointed him mihtār (overseer) of the sharbakhānāh (the royal drink-house). He was inclined toward goodness. He died, it is said, in the year 894 H, and was succeeded in his post."@en .

rec:AIND-D01795 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01795-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01795-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01795-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01795 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الآثاري مات بمكة في سنة إحدى وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Āthārī died in Makka in the year 841 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01796 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01796-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01796-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01796-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01796 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد البسيلي التونسي ، مات سنة ثمان وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Basīlī al-Tūnisī, died in the year 848 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01797 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01797-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01797-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01797-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01797 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الترابي شيخ صالح معتقد عند كثيرين . مات فجأة في يوم الجمعة حادي عشري ذي الحجة سنة خمس وخمسين ودفن من الغد بزاويته تجاه تربة الأسنوي خارج باب النصر رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Turābī, a righteous shaykh held in high regard by many. He died suddenly on Friday, the twenty-first of Dhū al-Ḥijjah in the year 855 H, and was buried the next day in his zawiya opposite Turbat al-Asnawī, outside Bāb al-Naṣr. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01798 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01798-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01798-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01798-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01798 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الترمذي الواعظ ، ممن لقبه الشهاب بن عرب شاه وأخذ عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Tirmidhī al-Wāʿiẓ. He was among those to whom al-Shihāb Ibn ʿArab Shāh gave a laqab, and from whom he acquired knowledge."@en .

rec:AIND-D01799 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01799-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01799-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01799-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01799 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الحجافي . مات بمكة في شعبان سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Ḥajāfī. He died in Makka in Shaʿbān in the year 868 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01800 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01800-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01800-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01800 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الجمالي موقت سوسة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Jamālī, muwaqqit of Sousse."@en .

rec:AIND-D01802 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01802-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01802-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01802-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01802 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الخالدي أحد القراء بصفد وكانت عنده عبادة وخير وله شهرة ، مات بها في ذي القعدة سنة عشرة ، ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad al-Khālidī, one of the Qurʾān reciters in Safad. He possessed piety and goodness, and was renowned. He died there (Safad) in Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 810 H. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』."@en .

rec:AIND-D01804 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01804-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01804-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01804-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01804 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الخواص آخر أحد المعتقدين بمكة ، مات غريقا في توجهه لسواكن سنة عشرين ، ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Khawwāṣ. One of the last revered figures in Makka. He died by drowning in 820 H while heading to Sawākin. Ibn Fahd mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01805 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01805-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01805-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01805 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الدهماني القيرواني المغربي نزيل طرابلس . مات بالقاهرة في سنة ثلاث وتسعين وقد ألممت به في حوادثها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Dahmānī al-Qayrawānī al-Maghribī, a resident of Tripoli. He died in Cairo in the year 893 AH. I (al-Sakhāwī) have mentioned him in connection with its (Cairo's) incidents."@en .

rec:AIND-D01807 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01807-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01807-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01807 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الدوري شيخ الفراشين بمكة وخال لمحمد بن يسق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Dūrī, chief of the farrāshīn (mosque attendants) in Mecca and maternal uncle of Muḥammad b. Yasaq."@en .

rec:AIND-D01809 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01809-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01809-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01809-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01809 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد السلوي المغربي كان فاضلا صالحا ، مات سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Salawī al-Maghribī. He was a virtuous and righteous man. He died in the year 853 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01810 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01810-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01810-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01810 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد السنبلي الجبار ، مات بمكة في رجب سنة أربع وخسمين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Sunbulī al-Jabbār. Died in Mecca in Rajab 854 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01811 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01811-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01811-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01811 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشامي النجار مات بمكة في رجب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shāmī al-Najjār died in Mecca in Rajab."@en .

rec:AIND-D01813 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01813-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01813-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01813 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشربيني ثم القاهري أحد صوفية سعيد السعداء وغيرها نسخ بخطه أشياء وهو الآن في سنة خمس وتسعين . حي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Sharbīnī, then al-Qāhirī. He was one of the Sufis of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ and other institutions. He copied things in his own handwriting. He is currently alive in the year 895 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01814 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01814-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01814-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01814 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الشماع قاضي المحلة ، مات سنة بضع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Shammāʿ, qāḍī of al-Maḥalla, died in the 830s H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01815 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01815-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01815-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01815 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد السيدي التونسي ، مات في آخر ذي الحجة سنة ثمان وخمسين أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Sayyidī al-Tūnisī. He died at the end of Dhū al-Ḥijjah in 858 H. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D01817 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01817-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01817-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01817-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01817 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الصامت المجاور بباب جامع الظاهر ويعرف بذويبة ، مات في يوم الأحد سادس عشر ذي القعدة سنة ستين ودفن في زاوية هناك على الطريق وكان معتقدا ، ذكره المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Ṣāmit al-Mujāwir, known as Dhuwayba, resided by the gate of Jāmiʿ al-Ẓāhir. He died on Sunday, the 16th of Dhū al-Qaʿda, 860 AH, and was buried in a zawiya along the road there. He was a revered person. Al-Munīr mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01819 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01819-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01819-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01819-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01819 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد العقبي جابي الأشرفية برسباي مات في تاسع عشر شوال سنة ست وثمانين ، وابن محمد بن يوسف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-ʿUqbī, the revenue collector (jābī) of al-Ashrafiyya Barsbāy, died on the 19th of Shawwāl 886 H. (The closing phrase “wa-Ibn Muḥammad b. Yūsuf” is read as a cross-reference to the other Aḥmad al-ʿUqbī, i.e. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf al-ʿUqbī [AIND-D01581], not as the name of his father.)"@en .

rec:AIND-D01820 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01820-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01820-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01820 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد العوكلي المغربي الموقت مات في ربيع الآخر سنة ستين بمكة ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-ʿAwkalī al-Maghribī al-Muwaqqit died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir 860 H. His biography was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D01821 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01821-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01821-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01821 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد العيني الشامي مات بمكة سنة سبع وخمسين وأظنه الماضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ahmad al-ʿAynī al-Shāmī died in Mecca in 857 H. I believe he is the aforementioned person."@en .

rec:AIND-D01822 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01822-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01822-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01822 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الغمري المراكبي ويعرف بابن خروب كان لا بأس به في أبناء طائفته من جماعة الشيخ محمد الغمري سمع علي يسيرا ومات في ليلة مستهل صفر سنة ست وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Ghamrī al-Marākibī, known as Ibn Kharrūb. He was not a bad person among the members of his group from the circle of Shaykh Muḥammad al-Ghamrī. He heard a little from me (al-Sakhāwī), and died on the night of the first of Safar in the year 886."@en .

rec:AIND-D01823 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01823-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01823-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01823 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الفهمي الموقت بتونس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Fahmī, the prayer-time calculator (al-Muwaqqit) in Tunis."@en .

rec:AIND-D01824 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01824-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01824-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01824 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد القرشي ما عرفته ولكن رأيت له قصيدة امتدح بها فتح الدين المحرقي أولها : %~% يا صدر حبك سائر في سائري %~% حتى خيالك في منامي زائري %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Qurashī: I did not know him, but I saw a poem by him in which he praised Fatḥ al-Dīn al-Muḥarraqī, the beginning of which is: 'O heart, your love is circulating throughout me / Until your phantom visits me in my dream.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D01825 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01825-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01825-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01825-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01825 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد القزويني ثم المكي ويقال له الخواجا مير أحمد بالميم مات بمكة فجأة في ليلة مستهل المحرم سنة ثمان وخمسين ، أرخه ابن فهد وسمي في ذيله أباه حسين بن محمد وله دور بمكة وجدة وكان شرس الأخلاق ومتعاظما ممن دخل مصر وخالط الأتراك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Qazwīnī, then al-Makkī. He was also known as al-Khawājā Mīr Aḥmad (Mīr spelled with mīm). He died suddenly in Mecca on the eve of the first of Muḥarram in the year 858 H. Ibn Fahd recorded his biography and mentioned in his dhayl that his father was Ḥusayn b. Muḥammad. He had properties (dūr) in Mecca and Jeddah, was ill-tempered and arrogant, and was among those who entered Egypt and associated with the Turks."@en .

rec:AIND-D01826 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01826-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01826-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01826-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01826 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد القسيطي المرابط ممن أخذ عنه في الفقه مساعد بن حامد ومات في حدود سنة ستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Qusīṭī al-Murābiṭ (d. around 860 H). Among those who acquired knowledge of fiqh from him was Musāʿid b. Ḥāmid."@en .

rec:AIND-D01827 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01827-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01827-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01827 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد القصير ، ممن لقيه الشهاب بن عربشاه وأخذ عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Qaṣīr, among those whom Shihāb b. ʿArabshāh met and from whom he acquired (knowledge)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01828 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01828-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01828-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01828 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد القيسي الفاسي المتلاعب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Qaysī al-Fāsī al-Mutalāʿib."@en .

rec:AIND-D01829 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01829-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01829-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01829 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد المرجرلدي نسبة لبني مزجرلدة المغربي المالكي أحد العلماء المدرسين مات سنة خمس وستين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Marjarladī, attributed to Banū Mazjarlada, al-Maghribī, al-Mālikī. One of the learned teachers. Died in 865."@en .

rec:AIND-D01830 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01830-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01830-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01830 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد المزدعي المغربي أحوال وكرامات وكان عالما صالحا مات في الطاعون بمصر بعد السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Muzdaʿī al-Maghribī. His states and miracles. He was a learned and pious man, who died in the plague in Egypt after 870 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01831 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01831-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01831-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01831 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد المشرقي الغزي ويعرف بابن الأكرم . أحد المجاذيب ممن يذكر في بلده بكرامات ولأهلها فيه مزيد اعتقاد ولم يكن يلوي على أهل ولا مال ، مات بها في المحرم سنة إحدى وثمانين ونزل نائبها فصلى عليه في مشهد حاقل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Mashriqī al-Ghazzī, known as Ibn al-Akram, who died in 881 H, was one of the Majdhūb known in his hometown for miracles, and its people had great faith in him. He had no family or wealth. He died there in Muharram of the year 881 H. The town's deputy came down and performed the funeral prayer for him at Mashhad Ḥāqil."@en .

rec:AIND-D01832 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01832-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01832-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01832 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد المعلقي ، مات سنة بضع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Muʿalliqī. He died in the year between 833 and 839 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01833 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01833-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01833-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01833 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد المغازي الطبيب تونسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Maghāzī, the physician, a Tunisian."@en .

rec:AIND-D01834 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01834-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01834-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01834 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد المقدسي الحنبلي . رأيته أجاز لمن عرض عليه في سنة اثنتين وثمانمائة بالقاهرة فينظر من هو ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Maqdisī al-Ḥanbalī. I saw that he granted an ijāza to one who presented before him in Cairo in the year 802; who he is remains to be ascertained."@en .

rec:AIND-D01835 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01835-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01835-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01835 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد المقدسي الشيخ ، مات بمكة في جمادى الأولى سنة سبع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Maqdisī al-Shaykh, died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 847."@en .

rec:AIND-D01836 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01836-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01836-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01836 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد الملوتشي الولي الشهير ، مات في سنة بضع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Malwatshī, the famous walī. He died in the 830s AH (biḍʿ wa-thalāthīn, i.e. between 833 and 839)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01837 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01837-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01837-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01837 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد النخلي بضم النون أو فتحها كما هو على الألسنة ثم معجمة ساكنة التونسي من علمائها المفتين العقلاء ممن انتفع به الفضلاء وولي قضاء بني زرت من أعمال تونس مع جلوسه للشهادة بتونس ، مات بالطاعون سنة ثلاث وسبعين ومن شيوخه عمر القلشاني وابن عقاب ويعقوب الزعبي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad al-Nakhlī. The nūn is pronounced with a ḍamma, or with a fatḥa as is common on people's tongues, followed by a dotted letter (khāʾ) with sukūn. From Tunis, one of its scholars, muftis, and wise men, from whom many eminent individuals benefited. He held the office of qadi in Banī Zart (Bizerte), a district of Tunis, while also serving as a witness in Tunis. He died of the plague in 873. Among his shaykhs were ʿUmar al-Qalashānī, Ibn ʿAqāb, and Yaʿqūb al-Zaʿbī."@en .

rec:AIND-D01839 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01839-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01839-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01839 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد يبروق . لقيه ابن عربشاه بقرم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad Yabrūq. Ibn ʿArabshāh met him in Qirim (Crimea)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01840 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01840-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01840-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01840 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أحمد ممن يذكر بالجذب ويعتقد بين العامة ، مات في يوم الأحد سلخ ذي الحجة سنة ثمان وستين ، ودفن بجوار زاوية حليمة المبرقعة داخل باب الشعرية من القاهرة وكان لا يزال في عنقه طبل ، أرخه المنير"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aḥmad, known for his state of *jadhb* (spiritual attraction) and revered among the common people, died on a Sunday, the last day of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 868 H. He was buried next to the Zāwiya of Ḥalīma al-Mubarqaʿa inside Bāb al-Shaʿriyya in Cairo. He always had a drum around his neck. al-Munīr recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D01841 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01841-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01841-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01841 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إدريس بن حسن بن عجلان الحسني المكي مات في شوال سنة سبع وثلاثين أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Idrīs b. Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī died in Shawwāl of 837 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D01843 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01843-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01843-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01843 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إدريس بن ودي الحسني النموي . مات بمكة في جمادى الأولى سنة خمس وأربعين ، ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Idrīs b. Wadī al-Ḥasanī al-Namawī. He died in Makka in Jumādā al-Ūlā in 845 H. Ibn Fahd mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01844 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01844-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01844-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01844 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إدريس بن يحيى بن أبي الفهد بن عبد القوي السري أبو العلاء البجائي الأصل المكي الآتي أبوه وجده وأخوته نعم وغيره ، ولد في صفر سنة ست وأربعين بمكة وحفظ القرآن والرسالة لابن أبي زيد أو غالبها ، ودخل القاهرة والشام واليمن للاسترزاق وزار المدينة النبوية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Idrīs b. Yaḥyā b. Abī al-Fahd b. ʿAbd al-Qawī al-Sirrī Abū al-ʿAlāʾ, of Bijāyan (Bougie) origin, al-Makkī. His father, grandfather, brothers, and others will be mentioned later. He was born in Ṣafar in the year 846 in Mecca. He memorized the Qurʾān and al-Risāla of Ibn Abī Zayd, or most of it. He entered Cairo, al-Shām, and al-Yaman to seek livelihood and visited al-Madīna al-Nabawiyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D01845 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01845-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01845-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01845 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أدكى بكسر الدال المهملة وفتحها صاحب مملكة الدست مات قتيلا في سنة اثنتين وعشرين واستقر بعده محمد خان من ذرية جنكزخان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Adikā (or Adakā; with a kasra or fatḥa on the undotted dāl), ruler of the Kingdom of al-Dast (i.e. the Dasht [-i Qipchāq]). He was killed in 822 H, and after him Muḥammad Khān, from the progeny of Genghis Khan (Jinkiz Khān), was established in his place."@en .

rec:AIND-D01846 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01846-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01846-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01846 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أرخن بك بن محمد كرسجي عثمان أخو مراد بك ملك الورم ، له ذكر في ولده سليمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arkhun Bak b. Muḥammad Kirisjī [b.] ʿUthmān, brother of Murād Bak, king of al-Rūm (text: al-Warum). He is mentioned in the entry of his son Sulaymān."@en .

rec:AIND-D01847 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01847-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01847-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01847 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أردبغا الظاهري برقوق نائب صفد في أيام الأشرف برسباي ، وليها في سنة سبع وعشرين إلى أن مات بعد سنة ثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ardabughā al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq. He was the viceroy (nāʾib) of Safad in the days of al-Ashraf Barsbāy. He was appointed to it in the year 827 H and held it until he died after the year 830 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01851 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01851-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01851-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01851 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أرغون شاه السيفي تغري بردي أتابك غزة بعد تقدمة دمشق ، مات في سنة تسع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arghūn Shāh al-Sayfī Taghrī Birdī. He became Atābak of Gaza after holding a command (taqdima) in Damascus. He died in the year 819 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01853 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01853-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01853-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01853 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أرغون الناصري ، مات سنة تسع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arghūn al-Nāṣirī, died in the year 819."@en .

rec:AIND-D01855 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01855-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01855-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01855 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أرغون الرومي .هو الذي قبله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arghūn al-Rūmī. He is the person previously mentioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D01856 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01856-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01856-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01856-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01856 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أرغون دوادار الزيني عبد الباسط ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arghūn, the Dawādār al-Zaynī ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ."@en .

rec:AIND-D01857 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01857-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01857-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01857 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أركماس من صفر خجا المؤيدي أحد أمراء العشرات ورأس نوبة ويعرف بأركماس الأشقر ، مات في ويم السبت سلخ ربيع الثاني سنة ثلاث وخمسين بالطاعون وكان زائد الغفلة رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arqmās ibn Ṣafar Khujā al-Muʾayyadī was one of the commanders of tens (umaraʾ al-ʿasharāt) and head of a nawba. He was also known as Arqmās al-Ashqar. He died of the plague on the last Saturday of Rabīʿ al-Thānī in 853 AH. He was exceedingly negligent, may Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01858 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01858-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01858-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01858-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01858-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01858 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أركماس الجاموس اليشبكي نسبة ليشبك الشعباني ، أحد العشرات في أيام الظاهر جقمق مات بالقاهرة في أواخر ربيع الثاني سنة ثلاث وستين وقد علت سنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arqamās al-Jāmūs al-Yashbakī, whose nisbah is derived from Yashbak al-Shaʿbānī. He was one of the 'Asharāt (ten-officers) during the reign of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq. He died in Cairo at the end of Rabīʿ al-Thānī in the year 863, being of advanced age."@en .

rec:AIND-D01862 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01862-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01862-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01862-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D01862-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D01862-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01862 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أركماس من طرباي الأشرف قايتباي أحد خاصكيته ثم أبعده لنيابة طرابلس ثم نقله لدواداريته بحلب بعد قتل ازدمر نائب طرسوس ثم لدواداريته بالشام بعد موت جانبك الطويل وسافر مع المجردين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arkamās min Turbāy, one of al-Ashraf Qāytbāy's khāṣṣakīya (royal retainers), was then transferred to the vice-regency of Tripoli. He was subsequently moved to his dawādārīya (chancery) in Aleppo after Azdmar, the nāʾib of Tarsus, was killed. He was later transferred to his dawādārīya in al-Shām after the death of Jānbak al-Ṭawīl and traveled with the detachments."@en .

rec:AIND-D01863 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01863-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01863-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01863 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أركماس النوروزي أمير شكار . أصله من مماليك نوروز الحافظي ويلقب بالجاموس أيضا تأمر في الأشرفية برسباي عشرة وصار أمير شكار ثم ولي الكشف بالوجه القبلي غير مرة إلى أن قتل بالصعيد الأعلى في محاربة الزنج سنة خمس وأربعين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arkamās al-Nawrūzī Amīr Shikār. He was originally one of the mamluks of Nawrūz al-Ḥāfiẓī and was also nicknamed al-Jāmūs. He was made an amir of ten (amīr ʿashara) during the reign of al-Ashraf Barsbāy, then became Amīr Shikār (Master of the Hunt), and subsequently held the office of al-Kashf (inspector/administrator) of Upper Egypt (al-Wajh al-Qiblī) multiple times, until he was killed in Upper Egypt (al-Ṣaʿīd al-Aʿlā) during the war against the Zanj in approximately 845 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01864 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01864-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01864-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01864 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أركماس دوادار يلبغا المظفري قبل استقراره في الأتابكية ثم دوادار يشبك الأعرج الساقي أتابكية كان حسن السياسة عارفا بالأمور مشكور السيرة قليل الشر ، وولي نظر الأوقاف بعد موت قطلوبغا حجى ، مات في المحرم سنة إحدى وأربعين ، قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arkamās served as the dawādār of Yalbughā al-Muẓaffarī before the latter's establishment in the atabakiyya, and then as the dawādār of Yashbak al-Aʿraj al-Sāqī during his atabakship. He was skilled in governance, knowledgeable in affairs, of praiseworthy conduct, and had little malice. He also took over the supervision of awqāf after the death of Quṭlūbughā Ḥajjī. He died in Muḥarram of the year 841 H. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said so in his Inbāʾ [al-Ghumr]."@en .

rec:AIND-D01865 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01865-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01865-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01865 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أرنبغا بضم الهمزة والموحدة بن عقبة المكي الباني ، مات بها في المحرم سنة ثلاث وتسعين وكأنه سمي بذلك لمجيء تركي أو تأمره عند ولاته والظاهر أنه الآتي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Urnabughā (vocalized in the text with ḍamma on the hamza and the bāʾ) b. ʿUqba al-Makkī al-Bānī. He died in Makka in Muḥarram 893 AH. He was seemingly named so due to the arrival of a Turk or an amir's appointment at his birth. He is apparently identical with an entry coming shortly below."@en .

rec:AIND-D01866 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01866-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01866-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01866 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أرنبغا الظاهري برقوق . عمل أمير عشرة ، ومات في حياة أستاذه في يوم الأحد خامس عشر ذي القعدة سنة إحدى . أرخه العيني ونسبه أرنبغا الحافظي . واقتصر شيخنا على اسمه أرنبغا فيمن مات من الأمراء أو ذبح ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arnabughā al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq served as an amīr ʿashara. He died during the lifetime of his master on Sunday, the 15th of Dhū al-Qaʿda, in the year 801 AH. Al-ʿAynī recorded his death date and gave his nisba as Arnabughā al-Ḥāfiẓī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) confined his mention to the name Arnabughā among those amirs who died or were executed."@en .

rec:AIND-D01867 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01867-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01867-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01867 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أرنبغا اليونسي الناصري فرج عمل أمير عشرة ورأس نوبة في أيام الأشرف برسباي وجاور بمكة مقدما على المماليك السلطانية سنين ثم جعله الظاهر من جملة الطبلخانات ثم قدم الأشرف إينال فلم تطل أيامه فيها ، ومات في ربيع الأول سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Arnabughā al-Yūnisī al-Nāṣirī Faraj served as amīr ʿashara (commander of ten) and raʾs nawba during the reign of al-Ashraf Barsbāy. He then resided in Mecca for years, serving as muqaddam (commander) over the Sultanic Mamluks. Later, al-Ẓāhir (Jaqmaq) appointed him to the ṭablakhānāt (drum corps). When al-Ashraf Īnāl came to power, his tenure in this position was not long. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 857 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01870 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01870-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01870-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01870 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أزبك الأشقر الرمضاني الظاهري برقوق أمير طبلخناه ورأس نوبة ، مات في ليلة الثلاثاء رابع عشر ربيع الأول سنة ست ودفن من الغد وخلف شيئا كثيرا استولى عليه الناصر ، وكان عنده بمحل عظيم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Uzbak al-Ashqar al-Ramaḍānī al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq, Amir of the Kettle-drums and Head of a Nawba (military unit). He died on the night of Tuesday, the 14th of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 806 H. He was buried the following day. He left behind a great deal of wealth, which was seized by al-Nāṣir. He held a high position with al-Nāṣir."@en .

rec:AIND-D01873 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01873-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01873-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01873 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أزبك السمسماني المؤيدي . اشتراه المؤيد قبل سلطنته ثم صار خاصكيا ثم في أيام الأشرف إينال أمير خمسة وسافر مع المجردين إلى الجون وعاد وهو مريض فمات بالقاهرة في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وستين عن نحو الثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azbak al-Samsamānī al-Muʾayyadī was bought by al-Muʾayyad before his sultanate, then became a khāṣṣakī, and during the days of al-Ashraf Īnāl, he became an amir of five. He travelled with the detached troops to al-Jawna and returned sick, dying in Cairo in Dhū al-Ḥijja 861 H, at around eighty years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D01874 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01874-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01874-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01874 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أزبك الظاهري برقوق ويعرف بأزبك خاص خرجي لكونه كان خصيصا عند أستاذه بحيث رقاه حتى صار من المقدمين مع كثرة شره وفتنه إلا أنه كان حسن الصورة مشهورا بالشجاعة قتل في سنة سبع تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azbak al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq, known as Azbak Khāṣṣ Kharajī. He was special to his master, who promoted him to become one of the muqaddams, despite his abundant evil and mischief. However, he was handsome and famous for his bravery. He was killed in approximately the year 807 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01875 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01875-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01875-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01875 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أزبك الظاهري جقمق من ممالكيه وسقاته مات بالطاعون في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين وشهد السلطان الصلاة عليه"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azbak al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq, one of Sultan Jaqmaq's mamluks and cup-bearers, died of the plague in Safar 853 AH. The Sultan attended his funeral prayer."@en .

rec:AIND-D01876 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01876-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01876-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01876 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أزبك القاضي أحد الخاصكية ممن مات بمكة في المحرم سنة سبع وثمانين ودفن بالمعلاة وكان من الأجناد المقيمين بمكة مع الباشى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azbak al-Qāḍī, one of the Khāṣṣakiyya, died in Mecca in Muḥarram 887 H and was buried in al-Muʿallā. He was among the soldiers stationed in Mecca with al-Bāsh (the commander of the garrison)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01877 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01877-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01877-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01877-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01877 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أزبك الأشرف قايتباي قفص . ممن قتل حسبما كتب لي في الوقعة في رمضان سنة ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azbak al-Ashraf Qāytbāy Qafaṣ. Among those killed in the battle in Ramaḍān 893 H, according to what was written to al-Sakhāwī (the author) about the encounter."@en .

rec:AIND-D01882 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01882-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01882-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01882-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01882 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ازدمر من محمود شاه الظاهري جقمق الخازندار أحد المقدمين وصهر الأمير يشبك الفقيه على أنبته ويقال له المسرطن تأمر على الحج في سنة تسعين وخرج مع المجردين في سنة خمس وتسعين ثم أرسل نائبا لبعض البلاد ويذكر بخير مع إمساك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azdumar min Maḥmūd Shāh al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq, al-Khāzindār. He was one of the Muqaddams (commanders) and the son-in-law of Amir Yashbak al-Faqīh. He was also called al-Muṣaraṭan. In the year 890 AH, he was appointed Amir al-Hajj, and in the year 895 AH, he went out with the campaigners (al-Mujarradīn). Later, he was sent as a deputy (nāʾib) to several regions. He is remembered favorably, though with some parsimony."@en .

rec:AIND-D01883 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01883-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01883-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01883 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ازدمر دوادار الظاهر برقوق أرخه المقريزي في سنة إحدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azdamar, the dawādār of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq. Al-Maqrīzī recorded him under the year [8]01."@en .

rec:AIND-D01884 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01884-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01884-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01884 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ازدمر دوادار الأشرف قايتباي بحلب بعد أن كان نائب طرسوس وقتله علاء الدولة مع وردبش صبرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azdamar, dawādār of al-Ashraf Qāytbāy in Aleppo after having been nāʾib of Tarsus. ʿAlāʾ al-Dawla (the Dhū al-Qadrid) killed him, together with Wardabish, in cold blood (ṣabran)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01886 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01886-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01886-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01886 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ازدمر من سربابق الأشرفي برسباي أمير منزل نزيل بيت منصور من حارة بهاء الدين ، مات تجاه برشوم وهو راجع من بلد اقطاعه في ذي الحجة سنة خمس وتسعين وكان خيرا وأظنه جاز السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azdumar min Sarbābiq (i.e., purchased from Sarbābiq), al-Ashrafī Barsbāy, who served as amīr manzil. Resident of Bayt Manṣūr in Ḥārat Bahāʾ al-Dīn. He died opposite Barshūm in Dhū al-Ḥijja 895 H, while returning from the land of his *iqṭāʿ*. He was a good person and is thought to have been over seventy years old."@en .

rec:AIND-D01887 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01887-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01887-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01887 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ازدمر الصوفي الظاهري أحد أمراء الأربعين قيل أنه يحفظ الهداية ويذكر بخير ويتردد إليه أبو الخير بن الرومي ليقرئه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azdamar al-Ṣūfī al-Ẓāhirī. One of the amirs of forty. It was said that he knew al-Hidāya by heart; he was mentioned with good repute, and Abū al-Khayr b. al-Rūmī used to visit him to teach him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01890 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01890-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01890-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01890 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ازدمر المزي أحد أمراء الطبلخانات بالقاهرة ، مات في يوم الاثنين سابع عشري ربيع الأول سنة إحدى وكان جيدا عفيفا دينا . أرخه العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azdamur al-Mizzī, one of the amirs of the ṭablkhāna in Cairo. He died on Monday, 27 Rabīʿ I of the year [8]01. He was good, upright, and religious. Al-ʿAynī recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D01892 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01892-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01892-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01892 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أزدمر الناصري نسبة لجالبه ناصر الدين الظاهري برقوق ، أحد مقدمي القاهرة وفرسانها فقد في سنة أربع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azdāmir al-Nāṣirī — the nisba derives from his importer (jālib) Nāṣir al-Dīn — al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq (mamluk of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq). He was one of the *muqaddams* and knights of Cairo. He disappeared in the year 824 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01893 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01893-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01893-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01893 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أزدمر من يشبك الظاهري جقمق ويعرف بالفقيه . تنقل حتى صار أمير عشرة في دولة الأشرف قايتباي ثم أنعم عليه بطبلخاناه عند رجوعه من وقعة أذنة ثم سافر صحبة قانصوة الشامي إلى حلب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Azdamar min Yashbak (purchased from Yashbak), al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq, known as al-Faqīh. He advanced through posts until he became an amir of ten in the reign of al-Ashraf Qāytbāy. Then he was granted a ṭablakhānāh upon his return from the battle of Adana. He then traveled to Aleppo in the company of Qansawh al-Shami."@en .

rec:AIND-D01899 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01899-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01899-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01899-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01899 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسحاق بن عبد الله بن بلال الفراش بمكة أخو أحمد الماضي ومحمد وقريب أحمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الله بن بلال الماضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Isḥāq b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Bilāl, the farrāsh (attendant) in Mecca. He was the brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad, and of Muḥammad, and a relative of the aforementioned Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Bilāl."@en .

rec:AIND-D01901 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01901-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01901-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01901 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسحاق بن أبي القسم بن محمد بن عبد الله بن عمر بن أبي بكر بن عبد الرحمن ابن عبد الله أبو يعقوب الناشري . ولد سنة اثنتين وثمانمائة وحفظ الشاطبية وجل الحاوي واشتغل في العربية على الشرف إسماعيل البومة وسمع من جده وأخويه محمد وإبراهيم وناب عن ثانيهما في الأحكام الفخمة وكان فقيها صالحا ذكره العفيف ولم يؤرخ وفاته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Isḥāq b. Abī al-Qāsim b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh, Abū Yaʿqūb al-Nāshirī. He was born in 802 H. He memorized al-Shāṭibiyya and most of al-Ḥāwī, and he studied Arabic under al-Sharaf Ismāʿīl al-Būma. He heard from his grandfather and his two brothers, Muḥammad and Ibrāhīm. He deputized for his second brother in important legal judgments. He was a pious jurist. Al-ʿAfīf mentioned him, but his date of death is not recorded."@en .

rec:AIND-D01902 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01902-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01902-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01902 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسحاق بن محمد بن إبراهيم التاج أبو البركات التميمي الخليلي الشافعي سمع من أبي الخير بن العلائي الصحيح وحدث به وممن سمع منه أحمد بن عبد العالي الماضي وكذا سمع منه بسنباط العز عبد العزيز بن يوسف كما سيأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Isḥāq b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm, al-Tāj Abū al-Barakāt al-Tamīmī al-Khalīlī al-Shāfiʿī, died in 878. He heard al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Khayr b. al-ʿAlāʾī and transmitted it. Among those who heard from him was Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿĀlī, who was mentioned previously. Similarly, al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Yūsuf heard from him in Sunbāṭ, as will be mentioned later."@en .

rec:AIND-D01905 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01905-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01905-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01905-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01905 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أسد بن البسيلي ثم القاهري أحد تجار الشرب ممن حج كثيرا وجاور وعامل ويظهر توددا ولكنه لم يخرج عن جل أقاربه وأظن بينه وبين زوجة الزيني زكريا قرابة أصلحه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Asad b. al-Basīlī, then al-Qāhirī, was one of the drink merchants who performed Hajj many times, resided in Mecca for an extended period (jāwara), and engaged in trade. He showed affection but did not abandon most of his relatives. I believe there was a kinship between him and the wife of al-Zayn Zakarīyā. May God rectify him."@en .

rec:AIND-D01908 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01908-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01908-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01908 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اسكندر شاه بن أميرزة عمر شيخ بن تيمورلنك أخو محمد الآتي ملك شيراز من بلاد فارس بعد قتل أخيه في سنة اثنتي عشرة وثمانمائة وأحضر قاتل أخيه فعتبه فقال له ما علمت في حقك إلا خيرا فلولا قتلته ما وصلت للمملكة فبادر بقتله لئلا يقال أنه كان بدسيسة منه مع عدم ذلك وكان ذلك في سنة ثمان عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Iskandar Shah, son of Amīrzā ʿUmar Shaykh, son of Tīmūrlank, died in 884 AH. He was the brother of Muḥammad (to be mentioned later) and became king of Shīrāz in Persia after his brother was killed in the year 812 AH. He brought forth his brother's killer and admonished him. The killer responded, \"I knew nothing but good from you; had I not killed him, you would not have reached the kingdom.\" So, Iskandar Shah hastened to execute him to prevent accusations of instigation, even though it was not by his doing. This occurred in the year 818 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01910 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01910-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01910-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01910-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01910 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اسكندر دلال العقارات مات في ليلة الجمعة حادي عشر شعبان سنة ثمان وسبعين وكان خاتمة أرباب طائفته ومع ذلك فمستراح منه لما كان عنده من الإقدام على أوقاف المسلمين وعدم احترامها مع إزراء هيئته واحتكار صنعته وخلفه طلماس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "No. 886. Iskandar Dallāl al-ʿAqārāt died on Friday night, the 11th of Shaʿbān in the year 878. He was the last of his kind/group. However, his death brought relief due to his audacity regarding Muslim waqfs and his lack of respect for them, along with his disdainful appearance and monopolization of his craft. He was succeeded by Talmās."@en .

rec:AIND-D01914 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01914-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01914-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01914 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن جوشن سيأتي فيمن جده محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Jawshan. He will be mentioned later in the entry for those whose grandfather is Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01917 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01917-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01917-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01917-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01917 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن أبي رحمة العماد أبو الفدا بن البرهان الجعبري ممن قرأ على البرهان الحلبي سيرة ابن سيد الناس ووصفه بالشيخ الفاضل الصالح الخير المحصل وأرخ قراءته في ربيع الثاني سنة ست وثلاثين ودعا له بقوله نفع الله به ونفعه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Abī Raḥma al-ʿImād Abū al-Fidāʾ b. al-Burhān al-Jaʿbarī, who died in 892 H, was among those who read Sīrat Ibn Sayyid al-Nās under al-Burhān al-Ḥalabī. Al-Ḥalabī described him as a 'virtuous, righteous, good, and accomplished shaykh,' dated his reading in Rabīʿ al-Thānī of the year 836 H, and prayed for him, saying, 'May God benefit through him and benefit him.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D01918 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01918-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01918-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01918 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن شرف . يأتي فيمن جده محمد بن علي بن شرف قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Sharaf. He will be mentioned soon under the entry of the one whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Sharaf."@en .

rec:AIND-D01921 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01921-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01921-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01921 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن علي بن شرف . يأتي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Sharaf. Will be mentioned shortly."@en .

rec:AIND-D01922 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01922-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01922-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01922 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن أحمد البصري الماضي أبوه وأخوه إبراهيم والآتي حفيده محمد بن عبد العزيز ويعرف بابن زقزق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Baṣrī (d. 895). His father (Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Baṣrī) and brother (Ibrāhīm b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Baṣrī) were mentioned previously. His grandson, Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, known as Ibn Zaqzaq, will be mentioned below."@en .

rec:AIND-D01925 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01925-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01925-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01925 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن جوشن قريب الفخر محمد بن عيسى الآتي . ممن أخذ عن شيخنا وسمع على ابن الكويك وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Jawshan, a kinsman of al-Fakhr Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā, who will be mentioned later. He acquired knowledge from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and heard ḥadīth from Ibn al-Kuwayk and others."@en .

rec:AIND-D01928 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01928-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01928-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01928 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن موسى بن سعيد بن علي الشيخ أبو السعود المنوفي الشافعي نزيل القاهرة ووالد محمد وأحمد ورمضان المذكورين في أماكنهم . كان عالما صالحا ممن أخذ عن الأبناسي وصحب البلالي والزاهد وغيرهما من السادات وتنزل في سعيد السعداء ودرس وأفتى ونظم الشعر سمعت الثناء عليه من غير واحد كالشيخ مدين . مات سنة عشرين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "901 Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Mūsā b. Saʿīd b. ʿAlī, al-Shaykh Abū al-Suʿūd al-Munūfī al-Shāfiʿī. He was a resident of Cairo and the father of Muḥammad, Aḥmad, and Ramaḍān, who are mentioned in their respective entries. He was a righteous scholar who studied under al-Abnāsī and accompanied al-Bilālī, al-Zāhid, and other Sayyids. He resided in Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ, taught, issued fatwas, and composed poetry. I heard praise for him from more than one person, such as al-Shaykh Madyan. He died around the year 920 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01930 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01930-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01930-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01930 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن إبراهيم الجبرتي . فيمن جده عبد الصمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm al-Jabartī. Among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd al-Ṣamad."@en .

rec:AIND-D01932 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01932-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01932-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01932 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن الأمين أحمد بن إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن عجبل شرف الدين . من بيت شهير باليمن كان يكرم الوافدين ولكنه لم تطل مدته فإن والده كما تقدم مات في سنة أربعين ، ومات هو سلخ ربيع الأول سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "904 Ismāʿīl b. al-Amīn Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAjbal, Sharaf al-Dīn. From a renowned Yemeni family, he was known for his hospitality towards visitors. However, his life was not long, as his father, as previously mentioned, died in the year 840 H, and he himself died on the last day of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 857 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01933 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01933-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01933-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01933-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01933 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن أحمد بن إسماعيل بن محمد بن إسماعيل بن علي العماد بن القطب القلقشندي القاهري الشافعي أخو شيخنا العلاء على الآتي وأخيه إبراهيم الماضي وغيرهما ووالد البدر محمد . ممن سمع الكويك بعض الشفا واشتغل قليلا وجلس مع الشهود وكان ثقيل السمع أجاز لي ومات في ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī al-ʿImād b. al-Quṭb al-Qalqashandī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī. He was the brother of our shaykh (al-Sakhāwī's teacher) al-ʿAlāʾ ʿAlī (forthcoming entry) and his brother Ibrāhīm (previous entry), among others, and the father of al-Badr Muḥammad. He listened to parts of al-Shifāʾ from al-Kuwayk, studied a little, and sat with the witnesses. He was hard of hearing. He granted me (al-Sakhāwī) an ijāza, and he died in (year not specified)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01935 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01935-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01935-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01935-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01935 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن أحمد بن أبي بكر المجد القاهري الأخفا في صهر شيخنا ابن خضر . كان وجيها من أرباب حرفته كثير السكون والخير . ممن لازم مجلس شيخنا في السماع وغيره وأظنه حضر بعض دروس الطنتدائي وغيره . مات في الحجة سنة ثمان وسبعين وأظنه جاز السبعين أو قاربها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr al-Majd al-Qāhirī al-Akhfā, son-in-law of our shaykh Ibn Khiḍr (al-Sakhāwī's shaykh, Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī, is mentioned as the source of this relationship). He was a notable person among his fellow craftsmen, known for his tranquility and goodness. He regularly attended the sessions of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) for samāʿ (listening to Hadith) and other studies. I believe he also attended some lessons of al-Ṭanṭidāʾī and others. He died in the year 878 AH, likely having passed the age of seventy or being close to it."@en .

rec:AIND-D01939 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01939-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01939-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01939 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن إسحاق بن أحمد بن إسحاق بن إبراهيم السيدوجيه الدين ابن العز بن النظام الحسيني الحسني الأحمدي الشيرازي الشافعي والد عبد الجليل وأخو حسين الآتيين عالم مفنن أخذ عنه في الفقه الجلال أحمد بن محمد بن إسماعيل بن حسن الصفوي الماضي وهو المفيد لترجمته وقال أنه حي في سنة أربع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Isḥāq b. Aḥmad b. Isḥāq b. Ibrāhīm, al-Sayyid Wajīh al-Dīn, Ibn al-ʿIzz b. al-Niẓām, al-Ḥusaynī, al-Ḥasanī, al-Aḥmadī, al-Shīrāzī, al-Shāfiʿī, father of ʿAbd al-Jalīl and brother of Ḥusayn (both mentioned later). He was a versatile scholar from whom al-Jalāl Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Ḥasan al-Ṣafawī (mentioned previously), who was beneficial for his biography, acquired jurisprudence. Al-Jalāl Aḥmad stated that Ismāʿīl was alive in 994 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01943 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01943-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01943-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01943 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن أبي بكر واسمه محمد بن علي الخوافي الآتي أبوه ، قدم القاهرة معه في سنة أربع وعشرين وثمانمائة فقال لشيخنا : %~% أقمت بمصر يا صدر الأعالي %~% وصيتك في العوالم غير خاف %~% %~% وزينت الورى جيلا فجيلا %~% فشرفت القوادم والخوافي %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Abī Bakr (whose given name was Muḥammad) b. ʿAlī al-Khawāfī, whose father will be mentioned later. He came to Cairo with him in 824 H. He said to our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī): \"You resided in Egypt, O Ṣadr al-Aʿālī, Your fame is not hidden in the worlds. And you adorned humanity generation after generation, So you honored the forebears and the Khawāfī.\" Father, Abū Bakr al-Khawāfī, is marked with الآتي, indicating a cross-reference to a later entry."@en .

rec:AIND-D01947 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01947-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01947-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01947 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن رسلان بن محمد الشبلي . ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Ruslān b. Muḥammad al-Shiblī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01948 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01948-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01948-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01948 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن زايد بن أحد مشايخ العربان بالبحيرة . وسط في أواخر ذي الحجة سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Zāyid b. (the one who was) one of the shaykhs of the Bedouin in al-Buḥayra. He died in late Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 853."@en .

rec:AIND-D01949 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01949-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01949-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01949 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن شبابة من جبال نابلس . قتل في صفر سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Shabāba from the mountains of Nablus. He was killed in Safar 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01952 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01952-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01952-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01952-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01952 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن عبد الرحمن بن التاجر شيخ سفط أبي تراب أبوه . سلخ كل منهما في شعبان سنة إحدى وسبعين لاتهامهما بقتل شيخ أبشيه الملق وكانا من مساوئ الدهر لفظا ومعنى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "924. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, son of the merchant Shaykh Abū Turāb. Both he and his father were flayed in Shaʿbān 871 H, accused of killing the shaykh of Abshīh al-Mulaqq. They were, literally and figuratively, among the evils of their time."@en .

rec:AIND-D01957 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01957-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01957-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01957 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن عبد الله بن محمد الريمي . ولي القضاء بتعز ومات سنة سبع وثلاثين بالطاعون بعد اختلاطه بخلط سوداوي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Raymī. He served as qāḍī in Taʿizz and died in 937 from the plague after suffering from melancholia (black bile imbalance)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01958 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01958-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01958-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01958 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن عبد الله المغربي المالكي نزيل دمشق . كان بارعا في مذهبه تفقه به الشاميون وأفتى وناب في الحكم . مات في شعبان سنة ثلاث عن نحو السبعين وقد ضعف بصره ، قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Maghribī al-Mālikī, a resident of Damascus. He was outstanding in his madhhab, and Syrians studied fiqh under him. He issued fatwas and served as a deputy judge. He died in Shaʿbān in the year 803 AH, at around seventy years of age, and his eyesight had already weakened. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned this in his *Anbāʾ*."@en .

rec:AIND-D01960 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01960-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01960-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01960 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن علي بن إسماعيل . جد الذي قبله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "932. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī b. Ismāʿīl. Grandfather of the preceding individual."@en .

rec:AIND-D01962 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01962-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01962-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01962 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن علي بن أبي بكر بن علي بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله ابن عمر بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله الشرف أبو الفداء الناشري . ولد سنة ست وسبعين وسبعمائة وأخذ عن عمه ولزم مجلس والده واعتنى بكتب الأدعية وولي نظر بعض مساجد تعز وتكسب بالزراعة وحج . مات في رمضان سنة أربع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Sharaf Abū al-Fidāʾ al-Nāshirī. He was born in 776 H. He acquired knowledge from his uncle, regularly attended his father's gatherings, and paid attention to books of supplications. He held the position of supervisor of some mosques in Taʿizz, earned a living through agriculture, and performed the Hajj. He died in Ramadan of 844 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01967 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01967-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01967-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01967 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن علي بن يوسف الرومي ويعرف والده بالبهلوان . مات بمكة في جمادى الأولى سنة سبع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf al-Rūmī. His father was known as al-Pahlawān. He died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ūlā, 867 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D01968 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01968-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01968-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01968-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:Wakako_Kumakura ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01968 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن عمران بن علي الصحافي ثم القاهري الأزهري الشافعي أخو موسى الآتي . ممن قرأ القرآن واشتغل وتردد لي يسيرا في تقرير ألفية الحديث مع حفيد القاياتي وغيره وتكسب بتعليم الأبناء وبالنساخة وربما اشتغل عند المتجددين من المدرسين . وهو خير من أخيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Born in 940 AH. Ismāʿīl b. ʿImrān b. ʿAlī al-Ṣaḥḥāfī, then al-Qāhirī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī, brother of Mūsā (mentioned later). He recited the Qurʾān, engaged in study, and frequented me (al-Sakhāwī) a little for the explanation of *Alfiyyat al-Ḥadīth* with al-Qāyātī’s grandson and others. He earned a living by teaching children and by copying manuscripts, and sometimes worked for innovative teachers/professors. He was better than his brother."@en .

rec:AIND-D01970 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01970-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01970-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01970 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن عمر العلوي اليماني سمع على شيخنا في سنة ثمانمائة باليمن من المائة العشاريات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. ʿUmar al-ʿAlawī al-Yamanī. He heard 『al-Miʾa al-ʿAshāriyāt』 from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in Yemen in the year 800 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01974 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01974-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01974-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01974 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن الجمال بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن مصلح بن إبراهيم العراقي الأصل المكي الحنبلي الماضي جده . ممن يحضر دروس حنبلي مكة وأكثر الحضور عندي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. al-Jamāl b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Muṣliḥ b. Ibrāhīm, of Iraqi origin, from Mecca, Ḥanbalī. His grandfather is mentioned previously. He attended the lectures of the Ḥanbalīs in Mecca and most frequently attended my (al-Sakhāwī's) sessions."@en .

rec:AIND-D01977 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01977-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01977-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01977-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01977 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن محمد بن إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن عبد الصمد الشرف الهاشمي العقيلي الجبرتي اليمني الزبيدي حفيد الماضي . ولد في سنة ست عشرة . مات في ظهر يوم الثلاثاء عشري ذي الحجة سنة سبع وسبعين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Ṣamad, al-Sharaf al-Hāshimī al-ʿAqīlī al-Jabartī al-Yamanī al-Zubaydī, grandson of the aforementioned (al-Māḍī). He was born in the year 816 H. He died on Tuesday, the 20th of Dhū al-Ḥijja, 877 H, in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D01978 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01978-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01978-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01978 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن محمد بن إسماعيل بن عبد الله بن عمر بن أبي بكر بن عبد الرحمن ابن عبد الله الناشري الآتي أبوه . كان فاضلا ذا خط جيد وصوت حسن مديما التلاوة . ذكره العفيف في أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Nāshirī (his father is mentioned later). He was virtuous, possessed good handwriting, and a beautiful voice, constantly reciting the Qurʾān. al-ʿAfīf mentioned him in his father's entry."@en .

rec:AIND-D01981 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01981-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01981-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01981-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01981 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن محمد بن عبد اللطيف الجبرتي الحنفي . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة النبوية وله فضل ولديه أدب وفيه خير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Jabartī al-Ḥanafī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in al-Madīna al-Nabawiyya. He possessed merit, good manners, and kindness."@en .

rec:AIND-D01982 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01982-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01982-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01982 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن محمد بن محمد بن علي بن صلاح بن إمام الصرغتمشية . مات سنة أربع وستين ، وإسماعيل زيادة فالمجد محمد بن محمد بن علي بن صلاح مات حينئذ ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "954 Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Ṣalāḥ b. Imām al-Ṣarghatmishīya. He died in the year '64 (864 H), but 'Ismāʿīl' is an addition, as al-Majd Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Ṣalāḥ (an ancestor) died at that time."@en .

rec:AIND-D01984 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01984-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01984-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01984 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن محمد بن ميكائيل . يأتي فيمن جده ميكائيل قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad b. Mīkāʾīl. He will be mentioned soon in the section for those whose grandfather is Mīkāʾīl."@en .

rec:AIND-D01986 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01986-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01986-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01986 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن محمد البيجوري الأزهري . ممن كتب بعض تصانيفي وأخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad al-Bījūrī al-Azharī. Among those who copied some of my (al-Sakhāwī's) compositions and acquired knowledge from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D01988 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01988-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01988-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01988-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01988 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل من نابت بن إسماعيل بن علي بن محمد بن داود مجد الدين الزمزمي الآتي أبوه الماضي جده . قرأ المنهاج والألفية وعرض وحضر عند القاضي محيي الدين المالكي في العربية واشتغل في الفقه وغيره وقرأ البخاري وسمع علي يسيرا ، وهو أحد المباشرين للأذان وسقاية العباس . مات في أواخر ذي القعدة سنة ثمان وتسعين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "959. Ismāʿīl b. Nābit b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Dāwūd, Majd al-Dīn al-Zamzamī (his father will be mentioned later, his grandfather was mentioned previously). He recited al-Minhāj and al-Alfīya, presented and attended under al-Qāḍī Muḥyī al-Dīn al-Mālikī in Arabic studies, and engaged in fiqh and other subjects. He also recited al-Bukhārī and heard a little from me (al-Sakhāwī). He was one of those directly performing the call to prayer and managing the watering station of al-ʿAbbās. He died in late Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 898 H in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D01989 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01989-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01989-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01989-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01989 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن ناصر بن خليفة عماد الدين الباعوني اخو الشهاب أحمد الماضي . كان شيخ الناصرية من عمل صفد على طريقة الفقراء ، له وجاهة وثروة وتجارة . مات في ذي الحجة سنة تسع عن سبعين سنة . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Nāṣir b. Khalīfa ʿImād al-Dīn al-Bāʿūnī, brother of al-Shihāb Aḥmad (mentioned above). He served as the shaykh of al-Nāṣirīya in the jurisdiction of Safad, in the manner of the poor Sufis. He possessed prominence, wealth, and engaged in trade. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 9 (809 AH) at the age of 70. This was stated by our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his work 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』."@en .

rec:AIND-D01990 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01990-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01990-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01990 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن محيي الدين يحيى بن أحمد بن يحيى الرسولي المكي سبط ابن الضياء الحنفي وأخو عمر الآتي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ودخل القاهرة واقتات هو وأخوه بانتزاع المدارس الرسولية بمكة وتصديرها كالملك ولزم من ذلك انقطاع أوقافها وتعديا لأوقاف البغداني وكتبه ولا قوة إلا بالله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "961. Ismāʿīl b. Muḥyī al-Dīn Yaḥyā b. Aḥmad b. Yaḥyā al-Rasūlī al-Makkī, grandson of Ibn al-Ḍiyāʾ, al-Ḥanafī, and brother of the aforementioned ʿUmar. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca. He later entered Cairo. He and his brother made a living by seizing the Rasūlī schools in Mecca and administering them as if they were private property. This resulted in the cessation of their endowments and an encroachment upon the endowments and books of al-Baghdādī. There is no power save in God."@en .

rec:AIND-D01994 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01994-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01994-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01994 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن يعقوب بن المتوكل على الله أبي عبد الله محمد بن أبي بكر ابن سليمان بن أحمد العباسي الهاشمي أخو المتوكل على الله العزي عبد العزيز ومحمد الآتيين للأب وبيرم ممن دخل في بني أخوة المعتضد من استدعاء ابن فهد . وهو حي في سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "965 Ismāʿīl b. Yaʿqūb b. al-Mutawakkil ʿalā Allāh Abī ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr Ibn Sulaymān b. Aḥmad al-ʿAbbāsī al-Hāshimī. He is the brother of al-Mutawakkil ʿalā Allāh al-ʿIzzī ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz and Muḥammad (to be mentioned later), from the same father, and Birām. He was among those who entered the sons of al-Muʿtaḍid's brothers by the summons of Ibn Fahd. He was alive in the year 995 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D01996 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01996-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01996-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01996 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن يوسف السمرقندي الحنفي ممن أخذ عن شيخنا مرافقا لعلي بن إسلام الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl b. Yūsuf al-Samarqandī al-Ḥanafī was among those who acquired knowledge from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), in the companionship of ʿAlī b. Islām (mentioned later)."@en .

rec:AIND-D01997 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01997-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01997-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01997-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01997 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل بن العجمي أمير الإسماعيلية بقلعة الكهف مدينتها أحد حصون الإسماعيلية المنيعة . قدم عليه عسكر من طرابلس فهدموا القلعة وأنعم عليه بأمرة في طرابلس وذلك في سنة ثلاث وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "968. Ismāʿīl b. al-ʿAjamī, the amir of the Ismāʿīlīs in Qalʿat al-Kahf, its city, one of the impregnable Ismāʿīlī fortresses. Troops from Tripoli came against him and destroyed the fortress. In the year 843 AH, he was granted an amirate in Tripoli."@en .

rec:AIND-D01998 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01998-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01998-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01998 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل العماد السرميني نائب كاتب السر بدمشق ومنشئها وشاعرها . نظم ونثر وكان من أفراد الدهر . مات في رجب سنة ثمان وثلاثين كهلا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "969 Ismāʿīl al-ʿImād al-Sarmīnī. Deputy Confidential Secretary (nāʾib kātib al-sirr) in Damascus, its founder (munshiʾ) and poet. He composed poetry and prose and was one of the unique individuals of his time. He died in Rajab 838 H, being middle-aged."@en .

rec:AIND-D01999 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D01999-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D01999-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D01999-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D01999 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل المجد خطيب جامع المقسي وأحد قراء الصفة بالبيبرسية . كان خيرا حسن التلاوة يتكسب من الشهادة بحانوت الدكة . مات في أول ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl al-Majd, khaṭīb of al-Maqsī Mosque and one of the readers of the ṣuffa at al-Baybarsiyya. He was good, with a beautiful recitation, and earned his living as a witness at Ḥānūt al-Dikka. He died on the first of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 851 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02000 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02000-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02000-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02000 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل البهلول . رجل صالح . مات في رجب سنة سبع وستين وأرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl al-Bahlūl. A righteous man. He died in Rajab in the year 867, and al-Munīr recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D02002 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02002-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02002-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02002-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02002 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل الرومي نزيل رباط ربيع بمكة . مات بها في سلخ المحرم سنة ست وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl al-Rūmī, a resident of Ribāṭ Rabīʿ in Makka. He died there at the end of Muḥarram in 856 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02003 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02003-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02003-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02003-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02003 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل المغربي نائب الحكم بدمشق . مات سنة ثلاث وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl al-Maghribī, deputy judge (nāʾib al-ḥukm) in Damascus. He died in 803 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02004 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02004-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02004-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02004-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02004 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل المهانمي . مات فجأة في صفر سنة تسع وخمسين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl al-Muhānamī. He died suddenly in Makka in Ṣafar 859 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02005 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02005-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02005-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02005-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02005-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02005 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل المقرئ المجود إمام مدرسة الخواجا إبراهيم بصالحية دمشق . مات في المحرم سنة تسع وخمسين . أرخه اللبودي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl, the Qurʾan reciter, the master of tajwīd, imam of the al-Khawāja Ibrāhīm madrasa in Ṣāliḥiyya, Damascus. He died in Muḥarram of the year 859 H. al-Lubūdī (Ibn al-Lubūdī) chronicled him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02006 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02006-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02006-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02006-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02006 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل أخو إسحاق . شيخ أعجمي فاضل مبارك خواجا . مات بمكة في أوائل رجب سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl, brother of Isḥāq. A virtuous, blessed shaykh of Persian origin, a khawāja. He died in Makka in early Rajab of the year 892 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02007 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02007-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02007-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02007-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02007 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إسماعيل أحد أئمة القصر . مات في المحرم سنة ثمانين بالمقشرة وكان أودعها من أيام لكونه نسب إليه التعرض لسرقة جواري الناس وبيعهن في قرى الأرياف وغيرها بعد ضرب الوالي ثم السلطان له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ismāʿīl, one of the imams of the palace. He died in Muharram of the year 880 H at al-Maqshara. He had been imprisoned there for some days, having been accused of attempting to steal people's slave girls and selling them in rural villages, after having been beaten by the governor (wālī) and then the sultan."@en .

rec:AIND-D02008 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02008-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02008-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02008-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02008 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اسنباي التركماني . في حوادث سنة عشر وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Asanbāy al-Turkumānī. Mentioned in the events of the year 810 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02010 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02010-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02010-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02010-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02010 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اسنباي الظاهر جقمق ويعرف بالجمالي وبالساقي . رقاه أستاذه إلى إمرة عشرة ثم عمله ابنه دوادارا ثانيا فلما نكب فر هذا واختفى أياما ثم أمسك ورسم بتوجهه للقدس بطالا فاستمر حتى مات في شعبان سنة ستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Asanbāy al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq, also known as al-Jamālī and al-Sāqī. His master (al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq) promoted him to amir of ten, and then his master's son appointed him second dawādār. When he suffered misfortune, he fled and hid for days. He was then arrested and ordered to proceed to Jerusalem as an unemployed person (baṭṭāl), a state in which he remained until his death in Shaʿbān of the year 860 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02011 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02011-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02011-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02011-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02011 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اسنباي أميراخور . في حوادث سنة عشر وثمانمائة ، وينظر إن كن غير اسنباي التركماني الماضي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Asanbāy, amīr ākhūr. Mentioned in the events of the year 810 H. It is to be considered whether he is the same as Asanbāy al-Turkumānī (D02008) mentioned shortly before."@en .

rec:AIND-D02012 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02012-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02012-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02012-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02012 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اسنبغا الناجي الحاجب . مات في العشر الأول من جمادى الأولى سنة ثلاث بالأشمونين وكان توجه لعمارة الجسور السلطانية فأحضروه في مركب إلى القاهرة فدفن بها . قاله العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Asanbughā al-Nājī al-Ḥājib. He died in the first ten days of Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 803 H in al-Ashmūnayn. He had gone to supervise the construction of the Sultanic bridges, so he was brought by boat to al-Qāhira and was buried there. al-ʿAynī related this."@en .

rec:AIND-D02015 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02015-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02015-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02015-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02015 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اسنبغا العلائي دوادار الظاهر برقوق . مات في سادس عشر جمادى الأولى سنة ثلاث . أرخه المقريزي وينظر اسنبغا الناجي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Asanbughā al-ʿAlāʾī, the Dawādār of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq. He died on the 16th of Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 803 H. al-Maqrīzī recorded him. Compare (yunẓar) Asanbughā al-Nājī (AIND-D02012)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02019 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02019-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02019-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02019 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أصبهان شاه بن قرا يوسف . له ذكر في حسين بن علاء الدولة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aṣbahān Shāh b. Qarā Yūsuf. He is mentioned in the entry for Ḥusayn b. ʿAlāʾ al-Dawla (AIND-D02710); no independent biography is given."@en .

rec:AIND-D02020 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02020-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02020-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02020-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02020 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أصلان بن سليمان بن ناصر الدين محمد بن دلغادر الأمير سيف الدين ملك أصلان نائب الأتليسيين وأحد من عدى في الملوك وصارت له ضخامة ورياسة ومالية . مات قتيلا بيد فداوي لا يعلم من هو وقت صلاة الجمعة من ربيع الأول سنة سبعين ، وقتل الفداوي من وقته وأحضر سيفه إلى القاهرة فقرر عوضه أخوه شاه بضع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aṣlān b. Sulaymān b. Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad b. Dulghādir, Amīr Sayf al-Dīn, known as Malik Aṣlān, was the nāʾib (deputy) of the Atlisiyyīn. He was one of those who transgressed against the rulers and acquired great influence, leadership, and wealth. He was killed by an unknown fidāwī (assassin) at the time of Friday prayer in Rabīʿ al-Awwal 870 H. The fidāwī was killed immediately. His sword was brought to Cairo, and his brother Shāh Baḍʿ was appointed in his place."@en .

rec:AIND-D02023 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02023-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02023-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02023 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقباي الأشرفي قايتباي وليس من مشترواته الطويل ، كان كاشف الشرقية ثم ولاه نيابة غزة بعد سيباي الظاهري حين انتقل لحجوبية الشام ثم الرملة مضافا إليها وكثر الأمن بالطرقات في أيامه لشدة بأسه وعرض له في بدنه بياض ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbay al-Ashrafī Qāytbāy. He was not al-Ṭawīl (the Tall One) from among his (Qāytbāy's) purchased Mamluks. He served as Kāshif of al-Sharqiyya, then he (likely the Sultan) appointed him as Nāʾib of Ghazza — succeeding Sībāy al-Ẓāhirī (identified as Sībāy al-Ashrafī Īnāl, #AIND-D03248) — after the latter transferred to the Ḥujūbiyya of al-Shām, and then al-Ramla was added to his jurisdiction. During his time, security on the roads greatly increased due to his severity. A whiteness (skin condition) appeared on his body."@en .

rec:AIND-D02024 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02024-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02024-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02024 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقباي الظاهري خشقدم ويعرف بالأقنص ، وسط في ذي الحجة سنة ثمان وسبعين بالرملة لقتله ملوكا للزيني الاستادار وما قبل السلطان منه ومن رفقته دفع ألف دينار لمستحقي الدية لكثرة شره وضرر المسلمين من جهته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbāy al-Ẓāhirī Khushqadam, known as al-Aqnaṣ. He was executed (wusiṭa) in al-Ramla in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 878 H for killing the mamluks of al-Zaynī al-Ustādār (al-Zayn Yaḥyā b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq al-Qibṭī, #AIND-D10263). The Sultan did not accept from him and his companions the payment of a thousand dinars to those entitled to blood money, due to his great wickedness and the harm caused to Muslims by him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02025 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02025-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02025-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02025-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02025-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02025 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقباي الظاهري خشقدم ويقال له الطويل ، استمر خاملا إلى أن أمره الأشرف قايتباي عشرة لأعلام الأتابك عنه أنه أبان وقت المعركة في كائنة ابن حرسك عن شجاعة واستمر حتى كان من المجردين سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbay al-Ẓāhirī Khushqadam, also known as al-Ṭawīl. He remained obscure until al-Ashraf Qāytbāy appointed him as an amīr ʿashara (commander of ten) for the banners of the Atābak, after he demonstrated courage during the battle of Ibn Ḥarsak. He continued until he became one of the mujarradīn (troops dispatched on campaign) in the year 895 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02026 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02026-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02026-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02026-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02026 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقباي الكركي الظاهري برقوق ويعرف بطاز الخازندار تقدم للناصر فرج ثم سجن بالاسكندرية ثم أعيد إلى تقدمته ولم يلبث أن مات بعد مرض طويل في ليلة السبت رابع عشر جمادى الأولى سنة خمس ودفن من الغد بحوش الظاهر ظاهر باب النصر . ذكره العيني وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbay al-Karakī al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq, known as Tāz al-Khāzindār. He received a taqdima (command of a hundred) under al-Nāṣir Faraj, then was imprisoned in Alexandria. He was later reinstated to his position, but did not live long, dying after a prolonged illness on the night of Saturday, the 14th of Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 895. He was buried the following day in Ḥawsh al-Ẓāhir, outside Bāb al-Naṣr. Al-ʿAynī and others mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02029 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02029-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02029-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02029-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02029 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبردي الأشرفي برسباي أمير أخور ثالث في أيام أستاذه ثم أخرجه الظاهر إلى طرابلس أميرا بها فأقام بها حتى مات قبل الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqburdī al-Ashrafī Barsbāy was a third-rank amīr akhūr (master of the horse) in the days of his master. Al-Ẓāhir later expelled him to Tripoli as an amīr there, where he resided until his death before the age of fifty."@en .

rec:AIND-D02030 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02030-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02030-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02030 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبردي الأشرفي إينال استادار الأغوار وخازندار السلطان المتوجه لاستخلاص الأموال ، قتل في صفر سنة إحدى وتسعين في مقتله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbaridī al-Ashrafī Ināl, the Ustādār of al-Aghwār and Khāzindār of the Sultan, who was dispatched to collect funds, was killed in Safar 891 at the place of his killing."@en .

rec:AIND-D02032 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02032-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02032-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02032-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02032 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبردي التماسيحي الظاهري جقمق ، استقز أمير الراكز بمكة عوض أزدمر وقدمها مع الركب سنة خمس وتسعين فدام وماتت زوجته في أثناء سنة سبع وتسعين وتزوج أم الحسن ابنة التقي البلقيني ورأيته مغتبطا بها ، وهو تركي خالص والبلاء من مقدميه وأتباعه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbirdī al-Timāsīḥī al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq. He was appointed Amīr al-Rākiz in Mecca, replacing Azdmar, and arrived there with the caravan in 895 H. He remained in office for a long time, and his wife died during 897 H. He then married Umm al-Ḥasan, daughter of al-Taqī al-Bulqīnī, and I (al-Sakhāwī) saw him rejoicing with her. He was a pure Turk, and the trouble came from those under his command and his followers."@en .

rec:AIND-D02034 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02034-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02034-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02034-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02034 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبدي القجماسي قجماس ابن عم الظاهر برقوق . تنقل حتى ناب بغزة في الأيام الأشرفية بمال فباشرها قليلا ومات في العشر الأوسط من شوال وقيل ذي القعدة سنة إحدى وأربعين بمخيمه الذي كان رام التحفظ فيه من الفناء خارج غزة وهو في عشر الثمانين ، قال المقريزي وأراح الله بموته من جوره وطمعه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbadī al-Qajmāsī Qajmās, a paternal cousin of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq. He moved around until he became a nāʾib (deputy) in Ghazza during the Ashrafī period, taking the position for money. He administered it for a short while and died in the middle ten days of Shawwāl, or, it is said, Dhū al-Qaʿda, of the year 841 H, in his camp outside Ghazza where he had sought refuge from the plague. He was in his eighties. Al-Maqrīzī said: \"And God relieved (people) by his death from his tyranny and greed.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D02035 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02035-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02035-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02035-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02035 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبردي المظفري عمل رأس نوبة الجمدارية في أيام المؤيد ثم أمير عشرة في أيام الظاهر جقمق ثم صار من رؤس النوب الصغار ثم أرسله أمير الركب لأول مرة ثم وجهه إلى مكة مقدما على المماليك السلطانية بها بعد سودون المحمدي وكان مشكور السيرة ، مات بمكة في ليلة الثلاثاء رابع عشري شوال سنة سبع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbardī al-Muẓaffarī served as raʾs nawbat al-Jamdāriyya during the days of al-Muʾayyad. Then he became an amīr ʿashara (commander of ten) during the days of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq. After that, he became one of the ruʾūs al-nūb al-ṣighār (heads of the minor guards). Then the amīr al-rakb (caravan commander) sent him for the first time, and subsequently he was dispatched to Mecca as muqaddam over the sultanic mamluks there, succeeding Sawdūn al-Muḥammadī. His conduct was praiseworthy. He died in Mecca on the night of Tuesday, the 24th of Shawwāl, in the year 847 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02036 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02036-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02036-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02036 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبردي منتو لقب بطعام . كان من أمراء الدولة المؤيدية ثم نقل إلى دمشق أمير طبلخاناه وحاجبا ثانيا حتى مات بعد سنة ثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbardī Mantū, nicknamed Ṭaʿām. He was one of the amirs of the Muʾayyadī state. He was then transferred to Damascus, serving as Amīr Ṭablakhānāh and second Ḥājib until his death after the year 830 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02037 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02037-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02037-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02037 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبردي المؤيدي المنقار . أحد المقدمين في أيام أستاذه . مات بدمشق في صفر سنة عشرين ولم يكن مشكور السيرة . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه باختصار ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbardī al-Muʾayyadī al-Minqār. He was one of the prominent figures during the days of his master. He died in Damascus in Safar of the year 820 AH. His biography was not commendable. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him briefly in his 『Inbāʾ』."@en .

rec:AIND-D02039 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02039-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02039-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02039-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02039-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02039 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبغا سيف الدين العديمي الحلبي الحنفي فتى الكمال عمر بن العديم . ولد في حدود سنة ثمانين وسبعمائة وسمع بحلب على ابن صديق بعض الصحيح وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء وكان دينا خيرا ملازما للخير مع العقل والسكون والتقنع بأوقاف وإقطاع من سيده . مات في حدود سنة أربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbughā Sayf al-Dīn al-ʿAdīmī al-Ḥalabī al-Ḥanafī, servant (fatā) of al-Kamāl ʿUmar b. al-ʿAdīm. He was born around the year 780 H and heard some of al-Ṣaḥīḥ in Ḥalab (Aleppo) from Ibn Ṣiddīq, and he transmitted ḥadīth; learned individuals heard from him. He was pious, good, constant in good deeds, intelligent, calm, and content with endowments (awqāf) and iqṭāʿ from his master. He died around the year 840 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02043 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02043-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02043-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02043-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02043 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبغا الجندي الفقيه الدوادار الصغير للناصر . مات في ليلة الثلاثاء ثاني عشري جمادى الأولى سنة ست ودفن من الغدو وخلف موجودا كثيرا فمن الذهب العين فيما قيل اثنا عشر ألف دينار فأخذه الناصر ولم يكن مشكورا في وظيفته بل اشتهر بالرشا والبرطيل وأخذ الأموال وارتكاب المحرمات . قاله العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbaghā al-Jundī, the faqīh and junior dawādār for al-Nāṣir. He died on the night of Tuesday, the 22nd of Jumādā al-Ūlā, in the year 806 H, and was buried the next morning. He left a substantial estate, including, it is said, twelve thousand gold dinars in cash, which al-Nāṣir subsequently seized. He was not commended in his official capacity; rather, he was known for bribery, corruption, embezzlement of funds, and engaging in forbidden acts, as reported by al-ʿAynī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02044 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02044-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02044-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02044-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02044 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبعا شيطان علاء الدين الظاهري ولي حسبة القاهرة وولايتها وشد الدواوين وجمع بينهما مرة ثم قبض عليه وحبس ثم قتل في ليلة الخميس سادس شعبان سنة إحدى وعشرين ، وكان نبيها مع ظلم وعفة عن المنكرات والفروج ، وقال شيخنا في أنبائه إنه كان حسن المباشرة قليل الفسق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbaʿā Shīṭān ʿAlāʾ al-Dīn al-Ẓāhirī held the office of muḥtasib and governor of Cairo, and once combined both with the management of the dīwāns (shadd al-dawāwīn). He was later arrested, imprisoned, and then killed on the night of Thursday, the 6th of Shaʿbān, 821 H. He was intelligent, despite his injustice, and abstained from abominable acts and illicit sexual relations. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』 that he was good at administration and had little depravity."@en .

rec:AIND-D02046 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02046-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02046-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02046-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02046 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقبغا الفيل . من المماليك السلطانية الظاهرية برقوق وأحد أخوة عليباي المقتول وسط مع سبعة من المماليك في سابع عشر المحرم سنة إحدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqbughā al-Fīl. One of the Sultanic (royal) Mamluks of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq, and one of the brothers of ʿAlībāy, who was killed amid seven other Mamluks on the 17th of Muḥarram in the year 801 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02048 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02048-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02048-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02048-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02048 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اق بلاط الدمرداشي دمرداش المحمدي . ترقى بعد أستاذه فقدمه المؤيد ثم ولاه نيابة حماة وغيرها ثم أتابكية ثم نقل إلى نيابة ملطية ومات بها ظنا بعد الثلاثين واشتهر بالشجاعة وحسن السيرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aq Balāṭ al-Dumarḍāshī Dumarḍāsh al-Muḥammadī. He was promoted after his master, and al-Muʾayyad favored him, appointing him as nāʾib (vice-regent) of Ḥamā and other places, then atābak. He was then transferred to the vice-regency of Malatya, and presumably died there after the 830s H. He was known for his courage and good conduct."@en .

rec:AIND-D02049 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02049-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02049-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02049 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اق خجا الأحمدي الظاهري ، مات وهو والي كشف الوجه القبلي في عشري المحرم سنة خمس وعشرين ، ولم يكن مشكورا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aq Khujā al-Aḥmadī al-Ẓāhirī. He died on the 10th of Muḥarram in the year 825 H. He was the wālī of the kashf (inspectorate) of Upper Egypt (al-Wajh al-Qiblī) and was not praised."@en .

rec:AIND-D02050 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02050-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02050-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02050 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اق سنقر الأشرفي شعبان بن حسين ، أحد الحجاب في الدولة الأشرفية وكان يسميه أغا ، مات في حدود الثلاثين وهو في سن الشيخوخة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aq Sunqur al-Ashrafī (mamluk of al-Ashraf Shaʿbān b. Ḥusayn). He was one of the chamberlains (ḥujjāb) during the Ashrafiyya state (the reign of al-Ashraf Shaʿbān b. Ḥusayn) and was called Aghā. He died around the 830s H in old age."@en .

rec:AIND-D02051 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02051-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02051-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02051-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02051 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اقطوه الموساوي الظاهري برقوق كان من مماليكه ثم صار دوادارا صغيرا في أيام المؤيد ثم أمير عشرة وولي المهمندارية في أيام الأشرف ثم إمرة طبلخاناه ثم نفاه مرة بعد أخرى إلى أن مات بطالا بالقاهرة بعد ضعف بباطنه في ليلة الثلاثاء ثاني عشر صفر سنة اثنتين وخمسين وصلى عليه من الغد ولم يكن مشكور السيرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqtūh al-Mūsāwī al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq. He was one of Barqūq's mamluks, then became a junior dawādār during the days of al-Muʾayyad, then an amīr ʿashara. He then held the muhammandāriyya office during the days of al-Ashraf, and later the imrat ṭablkhānāh. He was subsequently exiled repeatedly until he died unemployed in Cairo after suffering from internal weakness on the night of Tuesday, the 12th of Ṣafar, 852 H. His funeral prayer was performed the next day, but his conduct was not praised."@en .

rec:AIND-D02052 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02052-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02052-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02052 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أقفجا أمير عشرة مات في جمادى الأولى سنة سبع وعشرين وأعطيت إمرته لأقبغا التركماني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aqfajā, Amir ʿAshara, died in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 827 H. His amirate was given to Aqbūghā al-Turkumānī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02053 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02053-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02053-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02053 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ألتش الشعباني نائب القلعة ، مات في يوم الخميس رابع عشري جمادى الثانية سنة تسع ودفن بتربة بالصحراء جوار تربة الظاهر برقوق عند قبة النصر ، ذكره العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Altash al-Shaʿbānī, Deputy of the Citadel, died on Thursday, the 24th of Jumādā al-Thāniya in the year 809. He was buried in a tomb in the desert, next to the tomb of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq, near Qubbat al-Naṣr. Al-ʿAynī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02056 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02056-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02056-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02056 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الطنبغا العلاء المهمندار أمير عشرة ، مات في يوم السبت منتصف شعبان سنة ست عشرة ، ذكره العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Tanbaghā al-ʿAlāʾ al-Muhmindār, Amīr ʿAshara. He died on Saturday, the 15th of Shaʿbān in the year 816 AH. Al-ʿAynī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02057 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02057-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02057-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02057-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02057 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الطنبغا التركي الدمشقي مولى ابن القواس ، سمع من الحجار بعض البخاري ولم يظهر إلا قبل موته بقليل ولم نعلم أنه حدث ولكن قد استجازه بعض أصحابنا ، مات في سنة خمس عشرة ، قاله شيخنا في أنبائه قال وهو آخر من سمع من الحجار من الرجال ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭanbughā al-Turkī al-Dimashqī, mawlā of Ibn al-Qawwās. He heard part of al-Bukhārī from al-Ḥajjār. He did not become prominent until shortly before his death, and we do not know that he transmitted (ḥadīth). However, some of our companions received an ijāza from him, as our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) stated in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』; he said that he was the last of the men to hear from al-Ḥajjār. He died in the year 815."@en .

rec:AIND-D02059 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02059-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02059-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02059 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الطنبغا شادي كان من مماليك يلبغا العمري قتل مع ايتمش النخاسي في سنة اثنتين وقد جاز الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ṭanbaghā Shādī. He was one of the mamluks of Yalbaghā al-ʿUmarī. He was killed with Aytamish al-Nukhāsī in the year 802, having passed fifty years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D02062 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02062-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02062-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02062 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الطنبغا العثماني الظاهري نائب الشام ، مات في ثاني عشري شوال سنة إحدى وعشرين بالقدس بطالا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ṭanbaghā al-ʿUthmānī al-Ẓāhirī, the nāʾib (viceroy) of al-Shām, died on Wednesday, 22 Shawwāl 821 AH, in al-Quds while unemployed."@en .

rec:AIND-D02063 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02063-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02063-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02063-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02063 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الطنبغا القرمشي ، مضى قريبا فيمن يلقب سيف الدين ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02064 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02064-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02064-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02064-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02064-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02064 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الطنبغا أمير ، مات في شوال سنة إحدى وستين ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭanbaghā, amir, died in Shawwāl of the year 861 H. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D02065 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02065-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02065-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02065-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02065 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الغي برص أحد العشرات ، مات في يوم الخميس سادس عشري جمادى الأولى سنة ثمان أرخه العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ghayy Barṣ, one of the 'Asharāt (possibly a commander of ten). He died on Thursday, the 26th of Jumādā al-Ūlā, in the year eight (808 H). Al-ʿAynī recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D02066 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02066-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02066-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02066 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الماس الأشرفي برسباي . تأمر بحلب وتنقل فيها لعدة ولايات ثم صار أتابكها إلى أن قتل في وقعة سوار يوم الوقعة سنة اثنتين وسبعين وقد زاد على الخمسين وكان مليح الشكل مشكور السيرة مشهورا بالشجاعة رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Mās al-Ashrafī Barsbāy. He became an amir in Aleppo and was transferred to several governorships there. He then became its atābak until he was killed in the Battle of Sawār on the day of the battle in the year 872 H. He was over fifty years old at the time. He was handsome in appearance, of praised conduct, and famous for bravery. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02068 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02068-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02068-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02068-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02068 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الماس العلائي الأشرفي برسباي أحد الخاصكية ، ابتنى له تربة وعمل فيها للحنفية دروسا قرر فيها الزين عبد الرحيم المنشاوي مع سبعة من الطلبة ومات قريبا من سنة ثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Mās al-ʿAlāʾī al-Ashrafī Barsbāy was one of the Khāṣṣakīya. He built a tomb complex for himself, in which he established classes for the Hanafis, appointing al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Minshāwī along with seven students to teach in it. He died around the year 880 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02069 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02069-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02069-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02069-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02069-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02069 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الياس الكركي أحد الحجاب بدمشق ، ممن حج بالركب الشامي مرارا . مات في رمضان سنة أربع وثلاثين ، أرخه ابن اللبودي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ilyās al-Karakī was one of the chamberlains in Damascus. He performed the Hajj repeatedly with the Syrian caravan. He died in Ramadan of the year 834 H. Ibn al-Lubūdī recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D02070 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02070-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02070-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02070 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الياس الهندي الشيخ الصالح نزيل المدينة النبوية ، مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة أربع وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ilyās al-Hindī, the righteous shaykh, a resident of the Prophetic city of Medina. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 884 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02072 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02072-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02072-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02072-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02072-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02072 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أميران شاه بن تيمور كور والد خليل الآتي . ولاه أبوه أذربيجان في سنة اثنتين وثمانمائة عند قدومه من بلاد الهند إلى البلاد الشامية وجعل معه أخويه أبي بكر وعمر وجماعة من أمرائه وكان تحته تبريز وقتل بعد والده المذكور في سنة تسع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Amīrān Shāh b. Taymūr Kūr, father of the forthcoming Khalīl. In 802, when his father (the aforementioned) arrived from the lands of India to the Syrian regions, his father appointed him to govern Azerbaijan. His two brothers [sic; in fact his sons — see relation note], Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, and a group of his emirs accompanied him. Tabriz was also under his control. He was killed in 809, after the death of his aforementioned father."@en .

rec:AIND-D02073 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02073-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02073-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02073-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02073 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أمير جان بن شكر الله بن مرتضى الحسني القزويني ، سمع مني بمكة في سنة ست وثمانين رفيقا لمحمد بن جعفر بن علي الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Amir Jān b. Shukr Allāh b. Murtaḍā al-Ḥasanī al-Qazwīnī. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca in the year 886 H, as a companion to Muḥammad b. Jaʿfar b. ʿAlī, who will be mentioned later."@en .

rec:AIND-D02075 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02075-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02075-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02075-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02075 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أمير حاج بن المجد عبد الرحمن بن عبد الغني بن شاكر بن ماجد ويسمى إسماعيل ولكنه بهذا أشهر ويعرف سكلفه بابن الجيعان أحد الأخوة . حج غير مرة وسمع على جماعة منهم شيخنا وغيره وحصل له إقعاد فسافر لدمياط وزار جمعا من الصالحين ثم عاد معافى مات في رمضان سنة ثمانين وصلى عليه من الغد ودفن بتربتهم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Amīr Ḥājj b. al-Majd ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Shākir b. Mājid. He was also called Ismāʿīl, but was more famous by this name. His family/predecessor was known as Ibn al-Jīʿān, and he was one of the brothers. He performed the Hajj multiple times and listened to a group of scholars, including our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and others. He became crippled, so he traveled to Damietta and visited many righteous people, then returned recovered. He died in Ramaḍān 880 H. Funeral prayers were performed the following day, and he was buried in their family tomb."@en .

rec:AIND-D02076 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02076-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02076-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02076-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02076 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أمير حاج بن المنصور عثمان بن الظاهر جقمق الآتي جده وأبوه أكبر بني أبيه المذكور ، حفظ القرآن والنقاية والألفية وهو الآن مشتغل بالحفظ"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Amīr Ḥājj, son of al-Manṣūr ʿUthmān, grandson of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq. His grandfather and father are mentioned later. He is the eldest of his father's aforementioned sons. He memorized the Qurʾān, al-Niqāya, and al-Alfiyya, and is currently engaged in memorization."@en .

rec:AIND-D02078 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02078-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02078-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02078-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02078 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أمير حاج الزيني الحلبي ممن قرأ على شيخنا وبلغ له بالشيخ ولعله ابن طنبغا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Amīr Ḥājj al-Zaynī al-Ḥalabī, one of those who read to our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and attained (his ijāza/certification) through the shaykh. He is perhaps Ibn Ṭanbughā (the son of Ṭanbughā)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02079 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02079-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02079-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02079-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02079 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أمير زاه علي ابن أخي قرا يوسف ، له ذكر في محمد شاه بن قرا يوسف فيحرر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Amīr Zāh ʿAlī, the nephew (brother's son) of Qara Yūsuf. He is mentioned in the entry for Muḥammad Shāh b. Qara Yūsuf, and it is to be verified there."@en .

rec:AIND-D02080 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02080-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02080-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02080-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02080 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أمير زاه بن محمد بن شاه أحمد بن قرا يوسف مات في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى وسبعين بمسكنه في باب الوزير من القاهرة وقد زاد على الثلاثين وشهد السلطان الصلاة عليه وكان قد أحضره حواشي أبيه من العراق في صغره أيام الظاهر جقمق خوفا عليه من عمه أصبهان بن قرا يوسف متملك بغداد فأقام كآحاد أبناء الأمراء إلى الآن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Amīr Zāh b. Muḥammad b. Shāh Aḥmad b. Qarā Yūsuf. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year 871 AH at his residence in Bāb al-Wazīr, Cairo. He was over thirty years old. The Sultan attended his funeral prayer. In his youth, during the days of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq, his father's entourage brought him from Iraq for fear of his paternal uncle Aṣbahān b. Qarā Yūsuf, the ruler of Baghdad. He resided in Cairo like other sons of emirs until his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D02081 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02081-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02081-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02081-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02081 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أمين بن إدريس بن علي اليماني الماضي أبوه ، مات في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Amīn b. Idrīs b. ʿAlī al-Yamānī, whose father was mentioned previously, died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal 892 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02084 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02084-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02084-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02084 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أنس بن محمد بن عثمان الفخري . ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Anas b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān al-Fakhrī. He was among those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02086 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02086-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02086-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02086-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02086-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02086 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أويس بن شاه ولد بن شاه زادة بن أويس صاحب بغداد ، قتل في حرب بينه وبين محمد شاه بن قرا يوسف واستولى محمد شاه على بغداد مرة أخرى قاله شيخنا في أنبائه وأرخه سنة ثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Uways b. Shāh Walad b. Shāh Zāda b. Uways, whose (great-grandfather) Uways was the lord of Baghdad. He was killed in a war between him and Muḥammad Shāh b. Qara Yūsuf, and Muḥammad Shāh recaptured Baghdad again. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned this in his Inbāʾ (al-Ghumr) and dated it to the year 830."@en .

rec:AIND-D02087 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02087-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02087-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02087-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02087 ;
    aindv:sourceText "إياس الجلالي الحاجب الظاهري ، كان أحد أمراء الأربعين ثم أخرج إقطاعه وانفصل من الحجوبية ومات بطالا في ليلة الثلاثاء تاسع عشي جمادى الآخرة سنة إحدى وثلاثين بالقاهرة ، ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Iyās al-Jalālī al-Ḥājib al-Ẓāhirī: He was once one of the amirs of forty, but his iqṭāʿ was revoked, and he was dismissed from the office of ḥājib. He died unemployed on the night of Tuesday, the 19th of Jumādā al-Ākhira in the year 831 AH in Cairo. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his work Inbāʾ (al-Ghumr)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02088 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02088-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02088-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02088-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02088-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02088 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ايتمش من أردباسي الناصري فرح ثم المؤيدي أعتقه المؤيد وصار من المماليك السلطانية ثم ترقى بعده وصار خاصيكا ثم تأمر عشرة في أيام العزيز ثم صار في أيام الظاهر استادار الصحبة بعد مغلباي الجقمقي ، واستمر حتى مات في صفر سنة إحدى وخمسين ، وكان فيما قيل مسرفا على نفسه مع الشح وعدم الشجاعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aytamish, (originally) of Ardbāsī, then al-Nāṣirī Faraj, then al-Muʾayyadī. He was manumitted by al-Muʾayyad (Shaykh) and became one of the royal mamluks. He then rose after him (after al-Muʾayyad), becoming a khāṣṣakī, then an amīr ʿashara (commander of ten) during the reign of al-ʿAzīz. During the reign of al-Ẓāhir (Jaqmaq), he became Ustādār al-Ṣuḥba, succeeding Mughalbāy al-Jaqmaqī. He continued in this position until his death in Ṣafar 851 H. It was said that he was extravagant with himself despite his stinginess and lack of courage."@en .

rec:AIND-D02092 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02092-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02092-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02092-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02092 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ايدكي الجاركسي الأشرفي برسباي . تأمر عشرة في أوائل أيام الظاهر خشقدم وصار من رؤس النوب إلى أن قتل في وقعة سوار سنة اثنتين وسبعين عن أزيد من خمسين سنة وكان متحركا شجاعا مع إسراف على نفسه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aydakī al-Jārakasī al-Ashrafī Barsbāy. He became an amir of ten in the early days of al-Ẓāhir Khushqadam's reign and subsequently became one of the heads of the Nawba (ruʾūs al-nuwab). He was killed in the battle of Suwār in 872, being over fifty years old. He was energetic and brave, but extravagant with himself (self-indulgent)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02093 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02093-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02093-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02093-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02093 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ايدكي الظاهر جقمق من مماليكه وأحد الدوادرية عنده . مات بالطاعون في ربيع الأول سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ayduki. He was one of the mamluks of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq and one of his dawādārs. He died of the plague in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 853 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02094 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02094-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02094-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02094-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02094-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D02094-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02094 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ايدن الخشقدمي الزمام . أحد خدام المسجد النبوي ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aydan al-Khushqadamī al-Zimām. One of the servants (khuddām) of the Prophet's Mosque and its chief eunuch-administrator (zimām), who heard (ḥadīth) from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D02095 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02095-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02095-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02095-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02095 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال باي بن قجماس بن أسن ابن أخي الظاهر برقوق . قتل بغزة في سنة عشر ، ويأتي له ذكر في ولده يوسف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Aynāl Bāy b. Qajmās b. Asan, the son of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq's brother (his paternal nephew). He was killed in Ghazza in the year 810 AH. He is mentioned in the biography of his son Yūsuf (AIND-D10454)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02096 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02096-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02096-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02096-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02096 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال باي أخو جانم أمير اخور كبير . مات في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى وأربعين وكان جيدا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl Bāy, the brother of Jānam, the grand amīr akhūr (master of the stables). He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 841 H. He was a good man."@en .

rec:AIND-D02097 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02097-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02097-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02097-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02097 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال باي الفقيه الحسني الظاهري برقوق الحاجب الثاني ويقال له أيضا حاجب ميسرة ورأيت بخطي في محل آخر أنه رأس نوبة ثاني وأحدهما غلط ، ممن يتردد له الصلاح الطرابلسي ليقرئه ، تأمر على الأول سنة خمس وتسعين وأصيب أصبعه في وقعة ثلاث وتسعين ولا بأس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl Bāy, the jurist (al-faqīh), al-Ḥasanī, al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq, the second Ḥājib. He was also called Ḥājib Maysara (ḥājib of the left). I (al-Sakhāwī) saw in my own handwriting elsewhere that he was the second Raʾs Nawba, and one of the two is mistaken. Al-Ṣalāḥ al-Ṭarābulusī used to frequent him to recite to him (i.e. the headword taught him recitation). He was made amir (first) in 895 H, and his finger was injured in the incident of 893 H, but he was fine."@en .

rec:AIND-D02098 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02098-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02098-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02098-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02098-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02098 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال حطب العلائي . مات في ليلة الجمعة سادس ذي القعدة سنة تسع ودفن من الغد وحضر الناصر جنازته بمصلى المومني . ذكره العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl Ḥaṭab al-ʿAlāʾī. He died on the night of Friday, the 6th of Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 809 AH. He was buried the next day, and al-Nāṣir (Faraj b. Barqūq) attended his funeral prayer at the Muṣallā al-Muʾminī. Al-ʿAynī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02100 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02100-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02100-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02100 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال الأجرود . ذبح مع من أمر الناصر بذبحه من الأمراء في سنة إحدى شعرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl al-Ajrūd. He was executed along with the emirs whom al-Nāṣir ordered to be executed in the year 811 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02101 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02101-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02101-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02101 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال الأحمدي الظاهري برقوق أحد العشراوات تزوج أخت الأمين ووالدة المحب الأقصرائيين بعد موت زوجها والد المحب واستولدها فاطمة الآتية . مات في ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl al-Aḥmadī al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq, one of the amirs of ten. He married the sister of al-Amīn and mother of al-Muḥibb, the two Aqṣarāʾīs, after the death of her husband, al-Muḥibb's father, and by her he fathered Fāṭima, who follows. He died in … [no date given in the text]."@en .

rec:AIND-D02102 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02102-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02102-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02102 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال الأشرفي برسباي الطويل . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة إحدى وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl al-Ashrafī Barsbāy al-Ṭawīl. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 861."@en .

rec:AIND-D02105 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02105-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02105-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02105 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال الجلالي ويقال له اينال المنقار ، مات بغزة في شعبان سنة ثلاث عشرة لما دخلها شيخ ونوروز ، أرخه شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl al-Jalālī, also called Īnāl al-Minqār. He died in Ghazza in Shaʿbān 813, when Shaykh and Nawrūz entered it. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D02106 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02106-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02106-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02106 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال الحسني الأشرفي برسباي ، أحد الشعرات ممن يسكن سويقة صفية جوار الزير المعلق ، مات في التجريد سنة ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl al-Ḥasanī al-Ashrafī Barsbāy, one of the amirs of ten (al-ʿasharāt), of those who lived in Suwayqat Ṣafiyya near al-Zīr al-Muʿallaq. He died on the military expedition (al-tajrīd) in the year 893."@en .

rec:AIND-D02112 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02112-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02112-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02112-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02112 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال اكركي أحد الخاصكية بل هو كبير أغوات السلطان ولذا نزل بعد صلاة الجمعة سابع عشر رمضان سنة ثمان وسبعين للصلاة عليه بمصلى المومني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl Akrukī [al-Karakī], one of the khāṣṣakiyya — indeed he was the chief of the sultan's aghas (eunuchs). For that reason [the sultan] came down, after the Friday prayer on 17 Ramaḍān 878, for the funeral prayer over him at Muṣallā al-Muʾminī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02113 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02113-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02113-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02113 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال النوروزي أمير سلاح ، مات في ربيع الثاني سنة تسع وعشرين بالقاهرة ودفن خارج باب القرافة وخلف شيئا كثيرا وترك زوجته وهي ابنة تغري بردي الذي كان نائب الشام حبلى فوضعت بعده ذكرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl al-Nawrūzī, amīr silāḥ. He died in Rabīʿ al-Thānī 829 in Cairo and was buried outside Bāb al-Qarāfa. He left great wealth, and left his wife — the daughter of Taghrī Birdī, the former nāʾib al-Shām — pregnant; she gave birth to a boy after his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D02116 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02116-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02116-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02116 ;
    aindv:sourceText "اينال اليشبكي يشبك الشعباني ، صار بعد أستاذه في أيام الأشرف خاصكيا ورأس نوبة الجمدارية ثم امتحن بسبب تربة أستاذه وأمره الظاهر عشرة إلى أن مات في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Īnāl al-Yashbakī, [mamluk of] Yashbak al-Shaʿbānī. After his master['s death], in the days of al-Ashraf he became a khāṣṣakī and raʾs nawbat al-jamdāriyya. He then suffered an ordeal on account of his master's tomb, and al-Ẓāhir gave him an emirate of ten, [which he held] until he died in Ṣafar 853."@en .

rec:AIND-D02119 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02119-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02119-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02119 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أيوب بن حسن بن محمد نجم الدين بن البدر بن ناصر الدين بن بشارة مقدم العشير ببلاد صيدا . أقام فيها مدة اربع سنين ففعل كل قبيح وآل أمره إلى أن وسط في أواخر سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ayyūb b. Ḥasan b. Muḥammad, Najm al-Dīn b. al-Badr b. Nāṣir al-Dīn b. Bishāra, commander of the tribal levies (muqaddam al-ʿashīr) in the district of Ṣaydā. He held it for four years, committing every vile act, until in the end he was executed by bisection (wussiṭa) late in the year 853."@en .

rec:AIND-D02121 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02121-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02121-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02121 ;
    aindv:sourceText "أيوب بن سليمان المغراوي المؤدب . شيخ صالح جاور بالمدينة وقرأ في ألفية ابن مالك على القاضي نور الدين علي بن محمد بن علي الزرندي بعد سنة عشرين وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ayyūb b. Sulaymān al-Maghrāwī al-Muʾaddib. A pious shaykh who took up residence (mujāwara) in Medina and read Ibn Mālik's Alfiyya with al-Qāḍī Nūr al-Dīn ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Zarandī after the year 820."@en .

rec:AIND-D02125 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02125-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02125-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02125 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بابي سنقر بن شاه رخ بن تيمور لنك صاحب مملكة كرمان وأخو محمد الآتي . مات في ذي الحجة سنة تسع وثلاثين وقيل من التي قبلها ، وكان ولي عهد أبيه وفيه شجاعة موصوفة وجرأة عظيمة . ذكره شيخنا باختصار عن هذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bābī Sunqur b. Shāh Rukh b. Tīmūr Lank, ruler of the kingdom of Kirmān and brother of Muḥammad, who follows. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja 839, though it is also said [that he died] in the year before. He was his father's heir apparent, and possessed renowned courage and great daring. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded him more briefly than this."@en .

rec:AIND-D02126 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02126-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02126-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02126 ;
    aindv:sourceText "باشاه الحاجب بالديار المصرية ، مات وهو بطال في العشر الأخير من شوال سنة اثنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bāshāh, the ḥājib in the Egyptian lands. He died while out of office (baṭṭāl) in the last ten days of Shawwāl of the year 802."@en .

rec:AIND-D02127 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02127-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02127-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02127-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02127 ;
    aindv:sourceText "باك نائب قلعة حلب ، مات في أواخر سنة احدى وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bak, nāʾib of the Citadel of Aleppo. He died towards the end of the year 841."@en .

rec:AIND-D02128 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02128-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02128-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02128 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بتخاس بمثناة ثم معجمة السودوني . أرخ ابن دقماق موته في سنة أربع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bitkhās—with a tāʾ muthannāh followed by a dotted [khāʾ]—al-Sūdūnī. Ibn Duqmāq recorded his death in the year [80]4."@en .

rec:AIND-D02129 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02129-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02129-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02129 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بتخاص العثماني الظاهري . برقوق . دام جنديا نحو خمسين سنة ثم أمره الظاهر جقمق عشرة ثم صار حاجبا ثانيا إلى أن أخرج الظاهر خشقدم أقطاعه ووظيفته وأنعم عليه بأقطاع حلقة تقوم بأوده واستمر بطالا حتى مات في ربيع الاول سنة أربع وسبعين ، وقد ناهز المائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Batkhāṣ al-ʿUthmānī al-Ẓāhirī [the Mamluk of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq]. He served as a regular soldier (jundī) for about fifty years. Then, al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq promoted him to an amir of ten, and he subsequently became the second chamberlain (ḥājib thānī). This continued until al-Ẓāhir Khushqadam stripped him of his iqṭāʿ and his office, granting him instead a pension iqṭāʿ from the halqa to sustain him. He remained out of office (baṭṭāl) until he died in Rabi' al-Awwal in the year 874 AH, having nearly reached the age of one hundred."@en .

rec:AIND-D02131 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02131-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02131-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02131 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بختك الناصري أحد أمراء العشرات وصهر يشبك الفقيه ، مات في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين بالطاعون ، وكان متوسط السيرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bakhtak al-Nāṣirī, one of the commanders of tens (amīr ʿashara) and the son-in-law of Yashbak al-Faqīh. He died of the plague in Safar, 853 AH, and was of average conduct."@en .

rec:AIND-D02133 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02133-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02133-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02133-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02133-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02133 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بدر بن علي القويسني القاهري الشافعي ، كان عالما صالحا درس وأفتى وأخذ عنه غير واحد ممن لقيناهم ، وأجاز النور البلبيسي وكتب في عرض سنة ست وما رأيت من ترجمه . وكأن بدرا لقبه واسمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Badr b. ʿAlī al-Quwaysinī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī. He was a pious scholar who taught and issued fatwas, and more than one of those we met acquired knowledge from him. He granted an ijāza to al-Nūr al-Bilbaysī and wrote his approbation on a presentation (ʿarḍ) in the year [80]6 AH. I have not seen anyone who wrote a biography of him. It seems that Badr was both his title and his proper name."@en .

rec:AIND-D02134 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02134-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02134-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02134 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بدر القبة واسمه بدر أبو النور الحبشي فتى ابن عزم . اعتنى به سيده وأسمعه الكثير واستجاز له ثم مات في سنة اربع وسبعين ، وكان حاذقا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Badr al-Qubba, whose name was Badr Abū al-Nūr al-Ḥabashī, the client (slave) of Ibn ʿAzm. His master cared for him, made him hear many hadiths, and obtained ijazas for him. He died in the year 874 AH, and he was skilled (ḥādhiq)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02136 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02136-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02136-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02136 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بدر الحبشي مولى أبي جمال الدين المغربي . رباه سيده وعلمه القرآن والخطوط المتنوعة مع فصاحة ثم صار لابن عليبة ثم للسلطان واغتبط به وعول عليه في أشياء ، وصار يكثر السفر لمكة واسكندرية في التجارة مع عقل وتؤدة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Badr al-Ḥabashī, the slave (mawlā) of Abū Jamāl al-Dīn al-Maghribī. His master raised him and taught him the Qur'an and various styles of calligraphy along with eloquent speech. Later, he came into the possession of Ibn ʿUlayba, and then of the Sultan, who was highly pleased with him and relied upon him in many matters. He traveled frequently to Mecca and Alexandria for trade, possessing intelligence and deliberate calmness."@en .

rec:AIND-D02137 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02137-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02137-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02137 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بدر الكمالي بن ظهيرة . ذبح بجدة سنة احدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Badr al-Kamālī b. Ẓahīra [evidently a servant bearing the nisba of al-Kamāl of the Ibn Ẓahīra family]. He was slaughtered (dhubiḥa) in Jidda in the year 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02138 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02138-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02138-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02138 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بدر الشهير بالحسام . مات في المحرم سنة احدى وستين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Badr, known as al-Ḥusām. He died in the month of al-Muḥarram, in the year 861 AH, in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02142 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02142-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02142-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02142 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بديد في أحمد بن مفتاح ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02143 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02143-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02143-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02143 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برجان قرا الناصري . كتب عنه البدري في مجموعه قوله : %~% من آل حام قمر مشرق %~% تحسبه في سيره ساكن %~% %~% سألته ما الاسم يا سيدي %~% فقال يا مغرور بي فاتن %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Burjān Qarā al-Nāṣirī. Al-Badrī recorded in his compilation (Majmūʿ) these verses of his: 'From the house of Ham, a radiant rising moon; you would think him motionless as he moves. I asked him: What is your name, my lord? He said: O deluded one — in me is one who charms (fātin).' (A two-line name-riddle, apparently punning on the name Fātin.)"@en .

rec:AIND-D02144 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02144-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02144-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02144 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك الاسمعيلي الظاهري برقوق أحد العشرات . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة أربعين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bardbak al-Ismāʿīlī al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq, one of the commanders of ten (amīr ʿashara). He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 840 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02146 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02146-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02146-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02146 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك الاشرفي إينال . مات في شوال سنة إحدى وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bardbak al-Ashrafi Inal. He died in Shawwal, the year 881 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02147 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02147-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02147-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02147 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك الاشرفي قايتباي مات في سنة سبع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bardbak al-Ashrafi Qaytbay. He died in the year 897 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02148 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02148-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02148-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02148 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك البجمقدار يأتي قريبا ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02151 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02151-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02151-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02151 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك الخليلي ويلقب قصقا وهو بالتركي القصير . ناب بصفد ، ومات في منتصف رجب سنة احدى وعشرين ، ولم يكن مشكورا . أرخه شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bardbak al-Khalīlī, nicknamed Qaṣqā, which means 'the short one' (al-Qaṣīr) in Turkish. He served as the deputy governor of Safad and died in the middle of Rajab in the year 821 AH. He was not well-regarded. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his biography in his history book Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D02152 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02152-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02152-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02152 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك السيفي أحد مقدمي الألوف بمصر . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة ثلاث وثلاثين بالطاعون كهلا وهو والد فرح ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bardbak al-Sayfi, one of the commanders of a thousand (muqaddam al-uluf) in Egypt. He died of the plague in Jumada al-Akhira, year 833 AH, in his mature age, and he was the father of Farah."@en .

rec:AIND-D02153 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02153-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02153-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02153 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك طرخان الظاهري جقمق أحد العشرات مات في أواخر جمادى الأولى أو أوائل الذي يليه سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bardbak Ṭarkhān al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq, one of the commanders of ten (amīr ʿashara). He died in late Jumādā al-Ūlā or early of the following month in the year 892 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02154 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02154-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02154-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02154 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك الظاهري أحد مماليك السلطان وخاصكيته ويعرف باثني عشر . مات بالطاعون في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bardbak al-Ẓāhirī. He was one of the Sultan's mamluks and part of his personal retinue (khāṣṣakiyya). He was known by the sobriquet 'Ithnā ʿAshar' (Twelve). He died of the plague in the month of Ṣafar, in the year 853 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02156 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02156-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02156-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02156 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك قصقا . مضى قريبا ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02158 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02158-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02158-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02158 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك المحمدي الطويل ابن عم الاشرف برسباي . تأمر عشرة وعمل شاد أوقاف الاشرفية في سنة تسع وثمانين واستقر في امرته ابنه شاذبك من صديق وفي الشادية قانصوه الطويل الاشرفي برسباي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bardbak al-Muḥammadī al-Ṭawīl, the cousin of al-Ashraf Barsbāy. He was appointed as an emir of ten and served as the supervisor (shādd) of the endowments of the Ashrafiyya in the year 889 AH. His son Shādhbak succeeded him in his emirate, and Qānṣūh al-Ṭawīl al-Ashrafī Barsbāy succeeded him in the supervisorship (shādiyya)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02159 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02159-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02159-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02159 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بردبك هجين . مضى قريبا ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02163 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02163-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02163-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02163 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برسباي البواب زوج سرية الظاهر خشقدم أم ولده المنصور . مات في ذي الحجة سنة ثلاث وتسعين بأذنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barsbāy al-Bawwāb, the husband of the concubine of al-Ẓāhir Khushqadam, who was the mother of his son al-Manṣūr. He died in Dhu al-Ḥijjah in the year 893 in Adana."@en .

rec:AIND-D02164 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02164-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02164-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02164-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02164 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برسباي بلاشه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barsbāy Balāsha."@en .

rec:AIND-D02165 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02165-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02165-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02165-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02165-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02165 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برسباي التنمي خشداش السلطان والمقرب عنده وأظنه المعروف بلاشه مات في سنة ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barsbāy al-Tanmī. A fellow Mamluk (khushdāsh) of the Sultan and favored by him. I think he is the one known as Balāsha. He died in the year 893 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02166 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02166-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02166-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02166 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برسباي الخازندار . يأتي قريبا في المحمودي ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02167 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02167-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02167-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02167 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برسباي الخازندار الاشرفي . مات في طاعون سنة سبع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barsbāy al-Khāzindār al-Ashrafī. He died in the plague of the year 897 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02170 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02170-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02170-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02170 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برسباي قرا الظاهري جقمق أمير مجلس . مات في ذي الحجة سنة ثلاث وتسعين بأذنة وكان بالنسبة لكثير منهم لا بأس به يتظاهر باكرام الفقهاء والصالحين ويتأدب معهم رحمه الله وعفا عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barsbāy Qarā al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq, the Amīr Majlis. He died in Dhu al-Ḥijjah in the year 893 in Adana. In the estimation of many of them, he was acceptable. He made a show of honoring the jurists and the righteous, and behaved politely with them. May God have mercy on him and forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02171 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02171-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02171-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02171 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برسباي كجي الخاصكي القجمدار الأشرفي برسباي مات في شعبان سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barsbāy Kujī al-Khāṣṣakī al-Qajmadār al-Ashrafī Barsbāy. A khāṣṣakī and qajmadār, mamluk of al-Ashraf Barsbāy. He died in Shaʿbān, in the year 895 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02173 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02173-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02173-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02173 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برسباي المؤيدي شيخ . صار خاصكيا في الأيام الأشرفية ثم ساقيا في أيام السلطان ثم أنعم عليه بامرة عشرة بعد موت اينال الكمالي الناصري وكان عاقلا دينا . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة ست وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barsbāy al-Muʾayyadī [Shaykh] (mamluk of al-Muʾayyad Shaykh). He became a khāṣṣakī (royal mamluk) during the Ashrafiyya days, then a sāqī (cupbearer) during the days of the Sultan, and was subsequently granted an amirate of ten after the death of Īnāl al-Kamālī al-Nāṣirī. He was sensible and pious. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 856 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02176 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02176-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02176-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02176 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برصيغا أحد المقدمين من الظاهرية برقوق . كان من خيار الناس عقلا ممن يحفظ القرآن ويقرأ مع قراء الجوق . قتله المؤيد في سنة سبع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barsīghā. One of the commanders (muqaddamūn) from the Zahiriyya Barquq (the mamluks of al-Zahir Barquq). He was a highly intelligent and virtuous man who memorized the Quran and recited it with the choral reciters (qurrāʾ al-jawq). He was killed by Sultan al-Mu'ayyad Shaykh in the year 817 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02177 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02177-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02177-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02177 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برعوث بن بثير الجرشي من أشراف المدينة الرفضة الحسينيين تجرأ على الحجرة الشريفة وسرق من قناديلها هو وغيره جملة وآل أمره أن شنق بالمدينة سنة إحدى وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barʿūth ibn Bathīr al-Jurashī, one of the Rafidite Husaynid nobles of Medina. He dared commit sacrilege against the Prophet's Chamber and stole some of its lamps along with others. Consequently, his end was that he was hanged in Medina in the year 861 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02181 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02181-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02181-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02181 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بركات بن حسن المرجاني الاصل المكي الشافعي . ممن سمع علي بمكة وقرأ علي أربعي النووي والبعض من مسلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barakāt b. Ḥasan, of Marjānī origin, al-Makkī al-Shāfiʿī. One of those who heard from me in Mecca and read to me al-Nawawī's Forty Hadiths and part of Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim."@en .

rec:AIND-D02182 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02182-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02182-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02182-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02182-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02182 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بركات بن حسين بن حسن الشيرازي الاصل المكي ويعرف بابن الفتحي شقيق محمد وأحمد المذكورين وهو أصغر الثلاثة . ولد في سنة تسع وستين بمكة وكان ممن سمع مني بها وبالقاهرة وقد قدمها مع أبيه وبمفرده . ونزل عند الأتابك واسمه إسماعيل وسيأتي في الكنى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barakāt b. Ḥusayn b. Ḥasan, of Shīrāzī origin, the Meccan, known as Ibn al-Fatḥī; full brother of the aforementioned Muḥammad and Aḥmad, and the youngest of the three. He was born in 869 in Mecca and was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) there and in Cairo, which he visited with his father and on his own. He lodged with the atābak. His name is Ismāʿīl, and he will be treated again under the kunyas."@en .

rec:AIND-D02183 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02183-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02183-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02183-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02183 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بركات بن سلامة بن عوض الطنبداوي ثم المكي . مات بها في ربيع الآخر سنة سبع وستين وكان عطارا بباب السلام ثم ترك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barakāt b. Salāma b. ʿAwaḍ al-Ṭanbadāwī, later al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir, year 867 AH. He used to be a druggist at Bāb al-Salām, but later left the trade."@en .

rec:AIND-D02184 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02184-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02184-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02184-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02184 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بركات بن التقي عبد الرحمن بن يحيى العساسي السمنودي أخو الفاضل الشمس محمد الآتي وهذا أصغر وأبعد عن الاستقامة والخير بحيث تعب أبوه وأخوه من قبله . وهو ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barakāt b. al-Taqī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Yaḥyā al-ʿAsāsī al-Samannūdī. The brother of the virtuous al-Shams Muḥammad, who is mentioned below. He was younger and further from righteousness and goodness, to the point that his father and brother had been weary of him before. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D02186 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02186-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02186-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02186 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بركات بن محمد بن محرز الجزيري . مات سنة ثلاث وثلاثين . ذكره ابن عزم هكذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barakat bin Muhammad bin Mahruz al-Jaziri. He died in the year 833 AH. Ibn Azm mentioned him as such."@en .

rec:AIND-D02187 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02187-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02187-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02187-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02187 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بركات بن محمد بن يوسف الشامي المدني سبط ابن عبد العزيز أحد شهود الحرم . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barakāt b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf al-Shāmī al-Madanī, maternal grandson of Ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz. One of the witnesses (notaries) of the Haram. Among those who heard (hadith) from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D02188 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02188-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02188-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02188 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بركات بن محمود بن محمد بن حسن الحنفي الآتي أبوه وجده . ولد بعد الستين وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barakāt ibn Maḥmūd ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥasan al-Ḥanafī. His father and grandfather are mentioned below. He was born after 860 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02189 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02189-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02189-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02189 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بركات بن يوسف بن أبي البركات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Barakāt b. Yūsuf b. Abī al-Barakāt."@en .

rec:AIND-D02193 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02193-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02193-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02193-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02193 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برهان بن الشيخ عبد الكريم بن عبد الله بن محمد بن أحمد بن علي بن أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله الانصاري الحضرمي ثم المكي أخو يس الآتي وأبوهما . مات في المحرم سنة ثلاث وثمانين ودفن عند والده بالشبيكة من أسفل مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Burhān b. al-Shaykh ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī al-Ḥaḍramī, then al-Makkī. He was the brother of Yāsīn (mentioned later), and their father (ʿAbd al-Karīm) is likewise noted. He died in Muḥarram 883 H and was buried next to his father in al-Shabīka, in the lower part of Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02194 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02194-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02194-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02194 ;
    aindv:sourceText "برهة بن عبد الله الهندي . سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Burha b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Hindī. He (Burha) heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02195 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02195-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02195-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02195 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بساط بن مبارك بن محمد بن عاطف بن أبي نمي الحسني المكي . مات بها في رمضان سنة أربع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Basāṭ b. Mubārak b. Muḥammad b. ʿĀṭif b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died there (Mecca) in Ramaḍān of the year 874 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02196 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02196-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02196-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02196 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بسطام العجمي الخواجا نزيل مكة . مات بها في ربيع الآخر سنة خمس وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bisṭām al-ʿAjamī, al-Khawāja (the merchant), a resident of Mecca. He died there in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 885 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02197 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02197-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02197-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02197 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بشباي رأس نوبة كبير وهو تخفيف من باشباي . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة إحدى عشرة وصلى عليه بالأزهر ثم صلى عليه السلطان بمصلى المؤمني ودفن في القرافة ، وأظنه صاحب الخان بالقرب من المشهد الحسيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bashbāy — a shortened form of Bāshbāy — a chief raʾs nawba (senior guard commander). He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira 811 H. The funeral prayer was performed over him at al-Azhar, then the Sultan prayed over him at the Muṣallā al-Muʾminī, and he was buried in al-Qarāfa. I (al-Sakhāwī) think he was the owner of the khān near al-Mashhad al-Ḥusaynī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02199 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02199-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02199-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02199 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بشير الحبشي النويري أحد الفراشين بالمسجد الحرام . مات في المحرم سنة ست وخمسين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bashīr al-Ḥabashī al-Nuwayrī, one of the attendants (farrāsh) at al-Masjid al-Ḥarām. He died in Muḥarram 856 H in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02201 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02201-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02201-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02201-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02201 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بشير سعد الدين التنمي الطواشي استقر في مشيخة الخدام بالمدينة النبوية بعد فيروز الركني المطلوب إلى القاهرة سنة أربع وثلاثين ومات في آخر سنة أربعين وهو متوجه لمكة ودفن ببدر واستقر عوضه الولوي بن قاسم سنة تسع وثلاثين فكأنه صرف قبل موته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bashīr Saʿd al-Dīn al-Tanamī al-Ṭawāshī (a eunuch). He took over the office of head of the servants (mashyakhat al-khuddām) at al-Madīna al-Nabawiyya after Fayrūz al-Ruknī, who had been summoned to Cairo, in 834 H. He died at the end of 840 H while heading to Mecca and was buried at Badr. It appears he was dismissed before his death, as al-Walawī b. Qāsim succeeded him in 839 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02202 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02202-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02202-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02202 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بطان الوتاد . جرده ابن عزم هكذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Buṭṭān al-Watād. Ibn ʿAzm (AIND-D12540) extracted/listed him thus."@en .

rec:AIND-D02203 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02203-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02203-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02203-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02203 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بطيخ بن أحمد بن عبد الكريم النصيح العمري أحد القواد بمكة مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة خمس وخمسين بجدة وحمل لمكة فدفن بها وكان من أعيان القواد متموليهم ممن عشرته بخمسة عشر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baṭṭīkh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Naṣīḥ al-ʿUmarī was one of the quwwād (military commanders) of Mecca. He died in Jidda in Jumādā al-Ākhira 855 H and was carried to Mecca, where he was buried. He was among the prominent and wealthy of the commanders (the closing phrase \"ممن عشرته بخمسة عشر\" is obscure in the source)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02204 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02204-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02204-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02204-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02204 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بغا الحسني نائب حمص ، أرخه المقريزي في سنة احدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bughā al-Ḥasanī, deputy governor (nāʾib) of Ḥimṣ. al-Maqrīzī recorded his death in the year 801 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02205 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02205-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02205-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02205 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بقر بن راشد بن أحمد شيخ عرب الشرقية وابن أخي بيبرس . مات في ربيع الأول سنة سبع وسبعين بعد ضربه ضربا مبرحا مرة بعد أخرى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baqar b. Rāshid b. Aḥmad, shaykh (chief) of the Arabs of al-Sharqiyya and the nephew (brother's son) of Baybars (AIND-D02230). He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal 877 H after being severely beaten, time after time."@en .

rec:AIND-D02208 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02208-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02208-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02208 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بكتمر جلق نائب طرابلس ودمشق . مات سنة خمس عشرة . )"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baktamur Jalaq, nāʾib (viceroy) of Ṭarābulus (Tripoli) and Dimashq (Damascus). He died in 815 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02209 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02209-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02209-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02209-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Claude_Opus_4_8,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02209 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بكلمش بن عبد الله السيفي اينال باي قجماس ، سمع علي الغماري في سنة اثنتين وثمانمائة بعض البخاري وحدث رفيقا لشيخنا الشيخ رضوان ببعض ذلك ، سمع عليهما التقي القلقشندي وآخرون كالبقاعي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baklamish b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Sayfī (mamlūk of Īnāl Bāy Qijmās). He heard part of Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī from ʿAlī al-Ghamārī in 802 H and transmitted some of it as a companion to our shaykh al-Shaykh Riḍwān. al-Taqī al-Qalqashandī and others, such as al-Biqāʿī, heard from both of them."@en .

rec:AIND-D02211 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02211-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02211-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02211 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بكير شيخ ، لعوام الناس فيه اعتقاد كبير لاندراجه عندهم في المجاذيب بل سمعت عن الجلال البلقيني وأخيه أنهما ممن كان يعتقده وربما حضر ميعادهما وقد رأيته كثيرا وكان يكثر الوقوف بالطرقات . مات في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وخمسين ودفن في زاوية بسويقة صفية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bukayr Shaykh was held in high regard by common people, who considered him one of the majādhīb (those divinely attracted). Indeed, I heard from al-Jalāl al-Bulqīnī and his brother that they were among those who believed in him, and perhaps he attended their gatherings. I saw him often, and he used to stand frequently in the streets. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal 852 H and was buried in a zawiya in Suwayqat Ṣafīya."@en .

rec:AIND-D02212 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02212-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02212-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02212-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02212 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بلاط بن عبد الله القجماسي سيف الدين أمير مجلس ، سمع على الغماري في سنة اثنتين وثمانمائة بعض البخاري وأثبت البقاعي اسمه في شيوخه . مات في ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Balāṭ b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Qajmāsī, Sayf al-Dīn, amīr majlis. He listened to some parts of al-Bukhārī's Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ghamārī in 802 AH. Al-Biqāʿī recorded his name among his own shaykhs. He died in [date left blank in the text]."@en .

rec:AIND-D02213 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02213-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02213-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02213 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بلاط السعدي ، كان طبلخاناه في أيام الظاهر برقوق وجرت عليه أمور كثيرة إلى أن مات في جمادى الاولى سنة ثمان وهو بطال . ذكره العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Balāṭ al-Saʿdī held the rank of ṭablakhānāh during the time of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq, and many things happened to him until he died in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year eight (808 H) while out of service (baṭṭāl). Al-ʿAynī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02214 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02214-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02214-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02214 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بلاط أحد المقدمين كان من الفجار المفسدين الجاهلين بأمور الدين فغضب عليه السلطان وحبسه باسكندرية ثم أخرج منها إلى دمياط فقتل في الطريق في سنة اثنتي عشرة . ذكره العيني أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Balāṭ. One of the muqaddams. He was among the wicked, corrupt, and ignorant in religious matters. The Sultan therefore became angry with him and imprisoned him in Alexandria. He was then removed from there to Damietta and killed on the road in the year 812 H. Al-ʿAynī also mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02217 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02217-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02217-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02217 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بلال فتى المسند عبد الرحمن بن عمر القبابي القدسي . سمع على سيده ومات في يوم الاثنين تاسع جمادى الآخرة سنة سبع وستين ودفن عند سيده بباب الرحمة رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bilāl, the slave (fatā) of the musnid ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿUmar al-Qabbābī al-Qudsī. He heard from his master and died on Monday, the 9th of Jumādā al-Ākhira in 867 H. He was buried near his master at Bāb al-Raḥma. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02219 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02219-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02219-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02219-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02219 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بلال رجل صالح معتقد يؤدب الأطفال بالجملون العتيق . مات في سلخ ربيع الأول سنة احدى وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bilāl. A righteous and pious man who educated children at al-Jamalūn al-ʿAtīq (the Old Jamalūn). He died on the last day of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 851."@en .

rec:AIND-D02222 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02222-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02222-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02222 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بلبان المحمودي حاجب الحجاب بدمشق . مات في سنة ست وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Balabān al-Maḥmūdī, ḥājib al-ḥujjāb in Damascus. He died in the year 836."@en .

rec:AIND-D02224 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02224-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02224-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02224 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بهادر بن عبد الله الأمير بهاء الدين التركي المجاهدي المعروف بالشمشي ، مات في سنة ثمان عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bahādur b. ʿAbd Allāh, the amir Bahāʾ al-Dīn al-Turkī al-Mujāhidī, known as al-Shamshī, died in the year 818."@en .

rec:AIND-D02226 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02226-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02226-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02226 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بهادر العثماني نائب البيرة ، ممن قتل مع ايتمش في سنة اثنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bahādur al-ʿUthmānī, nāʾib of al-Bīra, was among those killed with Aytamish in the year 802 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02228 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02228-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02228-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02228 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بولاد العجمي الخواجا . مات في يوم الجمعة تاسع عشري رجب سنة اثنتين وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Būlād al-ʿAjamī al-Khawājā. He died on Friday, 29 Rajab 842. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D02230 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02230-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02230-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02230 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيبرس بن أحمد بن بقر شيخ العربان بالشرقية من الوجه البحري وعم بقر الماضي قريبا . مات في سلخ المحرم سنة ست وستين عن قريب السبعين ، وكان مليح الوجه طوالا حشما كريما دينا كثير الأدب والتواضع نادرة في أبناء جنسه رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baybars b. Aḥmad b. Baqar, shaykh of the Bedouin (ʿurbān) of al-Sharqiyya in Lower Egypt, and paternal uncle of Baqar, who was mentioned shortly before. He died on the last day of Muḥarram 866, at nearly seventy years of age. He was handsome, tall, dignified, generous, and religious, full of refinement and humility — a rarity among his kind. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02233 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02233-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02233-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02233-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02233-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02233 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيبرس الأشرفي إينال . تكلم على جهات أستاذه وولده المؤيد ثم أعطاه الملك امرة عشرة عوض نانق الاشرفي إينال وحج في سنة سبع وتسعين ثم عاد مع الركب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baybars al-Ashrafī Īnāl. He supervised the administrative and fiscal domains of his master [al-Ashraf Īnāl] and his master's son, al-Muʾayyad. Then, the Sultan granted him an emirate of ten, replacing Nānaq al-Ashrafī Īnāl. He performed the Hajj pilgrimage in the year 897 AH and returned with the caravan."@en .

rec:AIND-D02235 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02235-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02235-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02235 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيبرس الاشرفي قايتباي . رقاه حتى عمله شاد الشربخاناه ثم نائب طرابلس بعد إينال الاشرفي حين أسره ولم يلبث أن مات في سنة تسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baybars al-Ashrafī Qāytbāy. He [al-Ashraf Qāytbāy] advanced him until he made him shādd al-sharabkhānāh, then nāʾib of Ṭarābulus in succession to Īnāl al-Ashrafī when the latter was taken captive. He did not last long, dying in the year [eight hundred and] ninety."@en .

rec:AIND-D02236 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02236-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02236-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02236 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيبرس الطويل الظاهري جقمق الذي عمل باش مكة وقتا في الايام الاشرفية قايتباي ثم رقاه بعد رجوعه . ومات في تاسع المحرم سنة ثلاث وتسعين وكان لا بأس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baybars al-Ṭawīl al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq, who served for a time as bāsh of Mecca in the Ashrafī days of Qāytbāy, who then promoted him after his return. He died on 9 Muḥarram 893, and he was not a bad man."@en .

rec:AIND-D02237 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02237-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02237-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02237 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيبغا المظفري التركي . كان من مماليك الظاهر وتأمر في دولة الناصر وعمل الأتابكية ، وقد سجن مرارا ونكب وكان قوي النفس . مات في ليلة الاربعاء سادس جمادى الآخرة سنة ثلاث وثلاثين . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baybaghā al-Muẓaffarī al-Turkī. He was one of the mamluks of al-Ẓāhir [Barqūq], became an amir in the reign (dawla) of al-Nāṣir, and held the office of atābak. He was imprisoned several times and suffered disgrace, but he was a strong-willed man. He died on the night of Wednesday, 6 Jumādā al-Ākhira 833. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D02238 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02238-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02238-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02238 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيدمر الحاجب الصغير بمصر . كان معلم الرمح . مات في يوم الأحد سادس عشر ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين لجراحة حصلت فيه في وقعة أيتمش ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baydamur, the junior chamberlain (al-ḥājib al-ṣaghīr) in Miṣr. He was a master of the lance (muʿallim al-rumḥ). He died on Sunday, 16 Rabīʿ al-Awwal 802, from a wound he sustained in the affair of Aytamish."@en .

rec:AIND-D02240 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02240-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02240-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02240 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيرم التركي أحد المعتقدين ، كان مقيما بجامع الحاكم مات في جمادى الثانية سنة أربع وستين ودفن بتربة جاني بك المشد . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bayram al-Turkī, one of those in whom people believed (al-muʿtaqadīn, i.e. popularly venerated men). He resided at the Mosque of al-Ḥākim. He died in Jumādā al-Thāniya 864 and was buried in the turba of Jānī Bak al-Mashadd. Al-Munīr recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D02241 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02241-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02241-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02241 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بير أحمد الخواجا الجيلاني . مات في سنة احدى وعشرين وينظر من اسمه أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Pīr Aḥmad al-Khawājā al-Jīlānī. He died in the year 821 AH. See under the entries of those named Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D02243 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02243-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02243-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02243 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بير محمد بن العز عبد العزيز بن الشهاب أحمد المكي سبط بير محمد الخواجا الآتي بعده أمه صفية ويعرف بابن المراحلي . مات في المحرم سنة احدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bīr Muḥammad b. al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. al-Shihāb Aḥmad al-Makkī, the maternal grandson of Bīr Muḥammad al-Khawājā, who is mentioned below. His mother was Ṣafiyya. He was known as Ibn al-Mrāḥlī. He died in al-Muḥarram, the year 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02244 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02244-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02244-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02244-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02244-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02244 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بير محمد بن علي بن عمر الخواجا جمال الدين الكيلاني المكي . مات سنة ستين ، وسيأتي في المحمدين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Pīr Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar, al-Khawājā Jamāl al-Dīn al-Kīlānī al-Makkī. He died in the year 860, and will be treated again among the Muḥammads."@en .

rec:AIND-D02246 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02246-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02246-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02246 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيسق اليشبكي يشبك الشعباني . . عمله السلطان أمير خمسة ثم عشرة ثم نائب قلعة صفد ثم رجع على امرة عشرة ثم نائب دمياط ثم نائب قلعة دمشق ومات بها في شعبان سنة ثلاث وخمسين ، وكان متواضعا خيرا شجاعا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Baysaq al-Yashbaki, the mamluk of Yashbak al-Sha'bani. The Sultan appointed him as a commander of five, then ten, then as the deputy of the Citadel of Safad, after which he returned to the command of ten. He then became the deputy of Damietta, and subsequently the deputy of the Citadel of Damascus, where he died in Sha'ban, the year 853. He was humble, good, and brave."@en .

rec:AIND-D02248 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02248-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02248-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02248 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيغوت السيفي من برد بك من طبقة المقدم . ممن سمع مني قريب التسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bayghūt al-Sayfī, [mamlūk] of Bard Bek. Of the barracks (ṭabaqa) of al-Muqaddam. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) around [8]90 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02249 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02249-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02249-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02249 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيغوت قرا من قبجق السلحدار . هو الذي طعن برمحه قاصدا قتل أمير سلاح حين الالتقاء في رمضان سنة ثلاث وتسعين فأقلبه ميتا وعد ذلك في فروسيته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bīghūt Qarā min Qibjaq al-Siliḥdār. He is the one who struck the Amīr Silāḥ with his spear, intending to kill him, at the encounter in Ramaḍān of the year 893 AH. He knocked him down dead, and this deed was counted among his great feats of horsemanship (farūsiyya)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02250 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02250-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02250-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02250 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيغوت اليحياوي . ممن قتل مع ايتمش في سنة اثنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Bīghūt al-Yaḥyāwī. One of those who were killed alongside Aytamish in the year 802 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02251 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02251-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02251-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02251 ;
    aindv:sourceText "بيغوت الأمير الكبير . ممن أمر الناصر بذبحه في سنة احدى عشرة ، ويحرر مع بيبرس الركني الماضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "The great emir, Bayghūt. He was among those whom al-Nāṣir ordered to be executed in the year 811 AH. His account is noted to be collated with that of Baybars al-Ruknī, who was mentioned previously."@en .

rec:AIND-D02254 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02254-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02254-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02254 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تاني بك بن سيدي بك الناصري الساقي المصارع رأس نوبة . مات سنة ست وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tānī Bak b. Sīdī Bak al-Nāṣirī, the cupbearer (al-Sāqī), the wrestler (al-Muṣāriʿ). He held the office of chief of the military guard (raʾs nawba) and died in the year 836 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02257 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02257-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02257-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02257-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02257-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02257 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تاني بك الجركسي شاد الشربخاناة . تنقل في الخدم إلى أن ولي إمرة الحج في سنة ثماني عشرة ، وقدم في أول التي تليها وهو ضعيف فلم يلبث أن مات في صفرها ، وقد شكر الناس سيرته . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tani Bak al-Jarkasi, the superintendent of the buttery (shadd al-sharabkhanah). He advanced through various offices of service until he was appointed as the commander of the Hajj pilgrimage (amir al-hajj) in the year 818 AH. He returned at the beginning of the following year (819 AH) in a weak condition and passed away shortly after in the month of Safar. The people praised his conduct. Our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) mentioned this in his chronicle, Inba' al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D02258 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02258-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02258-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02258-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02258 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تاني بك القصروي . سكنه بباب الوزير أيضا مات قريب الثمانين أو نحوها ويذكر بخير"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tānī Bak al-Qaṣrawī. He also resided in Bāb al-Wazīr. He died near the year 880 AH or thereabouts, and is remembered with favor."@en .

rec:AIND-D02260 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02260-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02260-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02260-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02260-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D02260-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D02260-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02260 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تبل بن منصور بن راجح بن محمد بن عبد الله بن عمر بن مسعود العمري المكي القائد من أعيانهم ، مات في شوال أو رمضان سنة ست وعشرين عن دون الخمسين أو بلغها . ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tabal b. Manṣūr b. Rājiḥ b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Masʿūd al-ʿUmarī al-Makkī al-Qāʾid, one of their notables. He died in Shawwāl or Ramaḍān in the year 826 AH, aged under fifty or just having reached it. He was mentioned by al-Fāsī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02262 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02262-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02262-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02262 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تغرى بردي من قصروه نائب حلب . مات سنة ثمان عشرة قاله ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Taghrī Birdī min Qaṣrūh, the governor (nāʾib) of Aleppo. He died in the year 818 AH, according to Ibn ʿAzm."@en .

rec:AIND-D02263 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02263-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02263-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02263-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02263 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تغرى بردي سيف الدين الظاهري برقوق البشبغاوي نائب حلب ثم دمشق وكانت ولايته لها في ذي الحجة سنة ثلاث عشرة واستمر بها حتى مات في المحرم سنة خمس عشرة ، وكان كثير الحياء والسكون حليما عاقلا ، ذكره ابن خطيب الناصرية مطولا والمقريزي في عقوده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Taghrī Birdī Sayf al-Dīn al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq al-Bashbughāwī. He was the deputy (governor) of Aleppo, then Damascus. His appointment over Damascus began in Dhu al-Hijjah, the year 813 AH, and he remained in this office until his death in al-Muharram, the year 815 AH. He was highly modest, tranquil, clement, and intelligent. Ibn Khatib al-Nasiriyya mentioned him at length, as did al-Maqrizi in his al-Uqud."@en .

rec:AIND-D02266 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02266-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02266-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02266-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02266 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تغرى بردي الظاهري ويعرف بسيدي صغير . مات قتيلا في ليلة الاثنين سابع شوال سنة ست عشرة . قاله العيني وهو أخو قرقماس الآتي مع ذكر لهذا فيه ، وكان هذا أعظم من ذاك في الشجاعة والكرم وهما معا ابنا أخي دمرداش المحمدي الماضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Taghrī Birdī al-Ẓāhirī, also known as Sīdī Ṣaghīr. He was killed on the night of Monday, 7 Shawwāl 816 AH, according to al-ʿAynī. He is the brother of Qurqmās, who is mentioned below, and is referred to in that entry. Taghrī Birdī was greater than his brother in bravery and generosity, and both of them were the nephews (sons of the brother) of the aforementioned Demurdāsh al-Muḥammadī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02267 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02267-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02267-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02267 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تغرى بردي الصغير ابن أخي دمرداش . هو الذي قبله ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02268 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02268-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02268-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02268-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02268 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تغرى بردي ططر الظاهري جقمق وتقدم ثم استقر في حجوبية الحجاب وسافر في عدة تجاريد وحج أمير المحمل في بعض السنين ، ومات في شعبان سنة ثلاث وتسعين على فراشه بحلب قبل توجههم للقتال ، وبلغني أنه لما برز بدون تطلب وانفرد عن الأمراء بذلك دعا عليه السلطان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Taghrī Birdī Ṭaṭar al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq. He was promoted to a command position (Taqdima) and later appointed to the office of chief chamberlain (ḥujūbīyat al-ḥujjāb). He participated in several military campaigns and in some years performed Hajj as the commander of the pilgrimage caravan (amīr al-maḥmal). He died in Sha'bān of the year 893 AH on his bed in Aleppo before they set out for battle. It reached me that when he went out for the campaign without being requested and isolated himself from the other amirs in doing so, the Sultan prayed against him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02271 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02271-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02271-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02271-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02271-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b85_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02271 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تغرى بردي المحمودي الناصري . تنقل في الخدم إلى أن تقدم وقرر رأس نوبة النوب ثم حبس بعد أن كان رأس الذين غزوا الفرنج بقبرس ثم أفرج عنه وقرر أميرا بدمشق بل أتابكها ، ومات في قتال قرا يلوك في ذي القعدة سنة ست وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Taghrī Birdī al-Maḥmūdī al-Nāṣirī. He was promoted through various services until he was appointed as Chief of the Corps of Mamluks (Raʾs Nawbat al-Nuwab). After leading the expedition against the Franks in Cyprus, he was imprisoned, but later released and appointed as Amīr of Damascus, and eventually its Atābak. He died in battle against Qarā Yulūk in Dhu al-Qaʿdah, 836 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02272 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02272-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02272-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02272-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b56_58_followup,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02272 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تغرى بردي المؤيدي ، عمل رأس نوبة النوب وله ذكر في زوجته فاطمة ابنة قانباي فانه خلفه عليها جرباش ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Taghrī Birdī al-Muʾayyadī. He served as the chief of the guard (raʾs nawbat al-nuwab). He is mentioned in the biography of his wife, Fāṭima daughter of Qānibāy, whom Jarbāsh married after him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02278 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02278-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02278-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02278 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تغرى برمش أستادار شيخ ، خامر عليه إلى الناصر فولاه الاستادارية بالشام فبالغ في العسف فسلطه الله عليه فصادره وعاقبه حتى مات في سنة ثلاث عشرة ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Taghrī Birmish. He was the ustādār (majordomo) of Shaykh [al-Maḥmūdī], but rebelled against him and joined al-Nāṣir [Faraj], who appointed him to the ustādāriyya (office of majordomo) in Syria. He was excessively oppressive in his rule, so God empowered Shaykh over him, who confiscated his wealth and punished him until he died in the year 813 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his work Inbāʾ [al-Ghumr]."@en .

rec:AIND-D02280 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02280-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02280-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02280 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تقي بن محمد بن تقي الفخري السنجاري المدني . سمع على النور المحلى سبط الزبير بعض الاكتفاء للكلاعي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Taqī b. Muḥammad b. Taqī al-Fakhrī al-Sinjārī al-Madanī. He heard part of 『al-Iktifāʾ』 by al-Kalāʿī under al-Nūr al-Maḥallī, the maternal grandson of al-Zubayr."@en .

rec:AIND-D02282 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02282-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02282-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02282 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تمراز الاينالي الاشرفي برسباي ويعرف بالزردكاش ، وتأمر عشرين ثم استقر دوادارا ثانيا في أيام الاشرف إينال ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Timrāz al-Īnālī al-Ashrafī Barsbāy, known as al-Zardkāsh. He was promoted to an amir of twenty, then was appointed as second dawādār during the reign of al-Ashraf Īnāl."@en .

rec:AIND-D02286 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02286-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02286-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02286-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b85_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02286 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تمراز المؤيدي نائب صفد ثم غزة . مات مخنوقا بسجن اسكندرية في ثالث عشري جمادى الآخرة سنة إحدى وأربعين ولم يكن فيما قاله المقريزي مشكورا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Timrāz al-Muʾayyadī, the deputy governor of Safad, then Gaza. He was strangled to death in the prison of Alexandria on the 23rd of Jumada al-Akhira, in the year 841 AH. He was not praised in what al-Maqrizi wrote about him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02291 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02291-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02291-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Rui_Nakagawa,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02291 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تمرباي الاشرفي برسباي الساقي أحد أمراء العشرات ورؤس النوب . قتل في الموقعة سنة اثنتين وسبعين وكان قبيح السيرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Timurbāy al-Ashrafī Barsbāy al-Sāqī, one of the amirs of ten and heads of the guards (ra's nawba). He was killed in battle in the year 872 AH, and he was of bad character."@en .

rec:AIND-D02300 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02300-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02300-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02300 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تمربغا القجاوي كاشف الطير . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة احدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tamurbughā al-Qajāwī, kāshif al-ṭayr (inspector of birds). Died in Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 801 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02302 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02302-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02302-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02302 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تمربغا النحراري نائب الشام . مات في سنة ثلاث وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tamurbughā al-Naḥrārī, nāʾib al-Shām (viceroy of Syria). He died in 843."@en .

rec:AIND-D02308 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02308-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02308-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02308 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تنبك الطولوني أحد أمراء العشرات وكاشف المنوفية . قتل في ربيع الآخر سنة تسع وسبعين واستقر بعده في الكشف ابنه يونس وفي الامرة غيره وختم على موجوده"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tanbak al-Ṭūlūnī, one of the amirs of the tens and kāshif of al-Munūfiyya. He was killed in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 879 H. His son Yūnus succeeded him as kāshif, and another person succeeded him in the amirate. His possessions were sealed."@en .

rec:AIND-D02310 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02310-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02310-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02310 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تنبك المحمودي نائب دمشق . مات في سنة اثنتين وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tanbak al-Maḥmūdī, nāʾib of Damascus. He died in the year 822 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02311 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02311-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02311-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02311 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تنبك الناصري أحد أمراء العشرات ورأس نوبة ويعرف بالبهلوان وبالمصارع . مات بآمد في شوال سنة ست وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tanbak al-Nāṣirī was one of the emirs of tens (amīr ʿashara) and a head of a nawba unit (raʾs nawba). He was known as al-Bahlawān and al-Muṣāriʿ. He died in Āmid in Shawwāl of the year 836 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02317 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02317-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02317-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02317-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02317 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تنم الاشرفي قايتباي . أرسله أستاذه لنيابة جدة مرة بعد أخرى ثم أخره السنة الثالثة بعد أن ألبسه الخلعة لها وانتزعها وألبسها لبرد بك الماضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tanm al-Ashrafī Qāytbāy. His master sent him repeatedly as deputy of Jeddah. Then, in the third year, after vesting him with the robe of honor for it, he stripped it from him and vested it upon Bard Bek, the aforementioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D02318 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02318-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02318-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02318 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تنم الحسني الأشرفي برسباي . كان من خواص أستاذه وسقاته وامتحن بعده بالحبس ثم أطلق وآل أمره إلى أن تأمر عشرة في أيام اينال وصار من رؤوس النوب ثم في أول أيام خشقدم عمل رأس نوبة ثاني ثم نائب حماة ثم بطل ثم قدم بحلب . ومات بها في جمادى الآخرة سنة ثلاث وسبعين وهو في عشر السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tanam al-Ḥasanī al-Ashrafī Barsbāy. He was among the special confidantes and cup-bearers of his master. After his master's death, he underwent hardship by being imprisoned, but was later released. His affairs progressed to the point where he became an amir of ten during the days of Inal, and then became one of the heads of the nawba (military shifts). Then, in the early days of Khushqadam, he served as a second head of the nawba, then as nāʾib (deputy governor) of Ḥamā, after which he became unemployed. He then arrived in Ḥalab and died there in Jumādā al-Ākhira 873 AH, being in his seventies."@en .

rec:AIND-D02319 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02319-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02319-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02319 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تنم الفقيه الحنفي . أخذ عن ابن قديد النحو والصرف وغيرهما وكذا عن ملا شيخ وتصدر للاقراء فانتفع به جماعة من الترك وأبنائهم وغيرهم . وممن أخذ عنه خضر بن شماف ومنه استفدته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tanamm, the jurist, a Hanafi. He learned grammar, morphology, and other subjects from Ibn Qudayd, as well as from Mullā Shaykh. He became a leading teacher of Qur'an recitation, benefiting a group of Turks, their children, and others. Among those who learned from him was Khiḍr b. Shimāf, and from him (Khiḍr) I (al-Sakhāwī) obtained this information."@en .

rec:AIND-D02320 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02320-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02320-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02320-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02320 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تنم المحمدي والد زوجة أبي بكر بن صلغاي وأحد تجار الباسطية . تردد الي غير مرة وسمع مني المسلسل وبعض البخاري في سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tanam al-Muḥammadī, father of the wife of Abū Bakr b. Ṣalghāy, and a merchant of al-Bāsṭiyya. He visited me several times and heard from me al-Musalsal and part of al-Bukhārī in the year 892 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02321 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02321-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02321-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02321-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02321 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تنم المؤيدي دوادار السلطان بدمشق . مات في شعبان سنة تسع وثلاثين ، أرخه ابن اللبودي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tanam al-Muʾayyadī, dawādār of the Sultan in Damascus. He died in Shaʿbān of the year 839. Ibn al-Labūdī recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D02322 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02322-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02322-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02322-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02322-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02322 ;
    aindv:sourceText "تنم وسمى تنبك نائب دمشق . مات سنة اثنتين وثمانمائة ، وأظنه الماضي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tanam, also called Tanbak, nāʾib of Damascus. He died in the year 802. I (al-Sakhāwī) think he is the one treated shortly before."@en .

rec:AIND-D02325 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02325-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02325-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02325 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ثابت بن محمد بن أحمد بن علي بن حبيب أبو بكر بن حبيب العزازي الجرائحي ، وهو بكنيته أشهر . ولد في شعبان سنة ست وعشرين وسبعمائة ، وسمع جزء ابن عرفة على أربعة وعشرين شيخا وحدث به قرأه عليه شيخنا بدمشق ، وذكره المقريزي في عقوده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Thābit b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Ḥabīb Abū Bakr b. Ḥabīb al-ʿAzāzī al-Jarāʾiḥī, who was better known by his kunya. He was born in Shaʿbān in the year 726 AH. He heard Juzʾ Ibn ʿArafa from twenty-four shaykhs and transmitted it, which our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) read to him in Damascus. al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his 『ʿUqūd』."@en .

rec:AIND-D02326 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02326-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02326-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02326 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ثابت بن نعير بن منصور بن جماز بن شيخة الحسيني أمير المدينة . وليها سنة تسع وثمانين وسبعمائة وعزل عنها بجماز ثم أعيد اليها بعد صرف جماز ، ومات سنة احدى عشرة ، طول المقريزي في عقوده ترجمته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "This is Thābit b. Nuʿayr b. Manṣūr b. Jammāz b. Shaykha al-Ḥusaynī, the amir of Medina. He was appointed to the office in 789 AH but was removed in favor of Jammāz. He was then reinstated after Jammāz's removal. He died in 811 AH. al-Maqrīzī devoted a lengthy biography to him in his work 『ʿUqūd』."@en .

rec:AIND-D02327 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02327-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02327-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02327-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02327 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ثامر مجذوب للعامة فيها اعتقاد كبير وله كلمات فيها اعتبار سمعت منه الكثير منها ، وكان يكثر الوقوف عند باب جامع الغمري لاعتقاده في صاحبه . مات بعد الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Thāmir. He was a “majdhūb” (divinely attracted/ecstatic) greatly revered by the common people, and he left many profound sayings, much of which I heard from him. He frequently stood at the door of Jāmiʿ al-Ghamrī due to his deep devotion to its owner. He passed away after 850 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02328 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02328-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02328-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02328-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02328 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ثقبة بن أحمد بن ثقبة بن رميثة بن أبي نمي الحسني المكي . مات في ذي القعدة سنة تسع وأربعين خارج مكة وحمل فدفن بمعلاتها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Thaqaba b. Aḥmad b. Thaqaba b. Rumaytha b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 849 H outside Mecca, and his body was carried and buried in its al-Muʿallā cemetery."@en .

rec:AIND-D02331 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02331-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02331-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02331 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جار الله بن أحمد بن جار الله بن زائد السنبسي . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة ثمان وثلاثين ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jār Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Jār Allāh b. Zāʾid al-Sinbisī. He died in Mecca in al-Muḥarram 838 H. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D02332 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02332-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02332-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02332 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جار الله بن بحير من أهل وادي أبي عروة ثم نزيل مكة . ممن سمع مني بها في سنة أربع وتسعين ولم يلبث أن قتل بجدة وراح هدرا :"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jār Allāh b. Buḥayr, originally from Wādī Abī ʿUrwa, later resided in Mecca. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) there in the year 894, and shortly thereafter was killed in Jeddah, his blood going unavenged."@en .

rec:AIND-D02333 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02333-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02333-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02333 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جار الله بن حسن بن مختار . مات بمكة في ذي القعدة سنة سبعين ، وسيأتي أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jār Allāh b. Ḥasan b. Mukhtār. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 870 H. His father will be mentioned later."@en .

rec:AIND-D02334 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02334-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02334-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02334 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جار الله بن جويعد بن حازم بن عبد الكريم بن أبي نمي الشريف الحسني النموي . مات بمكة في ربيع الآخر سنة ثلاث وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jār Allāh b. Juwayʿid b. Ḥāzim b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Abī Numayy al-Sharīf al-Ḥasanī al-Namawī. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 883. Ibn Fahd also chronicled him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02337 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02337-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02337-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02337-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02337 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جار الله بن عبد الله المكي المؤدب . مات بها في شوال سنة ثماني عشرة ودفن بالمعلاة . أرخه ابن فهد نقلا عن خط ابن موسى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jār Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Makkī al-Muʾaddib. He died there (Mecca) in Shawwal in the year 818 AH and was buried in al-Muʿallā. Ibn Fahd chronicled him, based on the handwriting of Ibn Mūsā."@en .

rec:AIND-D02338 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02338-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02338-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02338 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جار الله بن مبارك الصفدي القائد . سمع علي ابن سلامة والتقي بن فهد في سنة سبع وثلاثين . مات في المحرم سنة أربعين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jār Allāh b. Mubārak al-Ṣafadī al-Qāʾid. He heard from Ibn Salāma and al-Taqī b. Fahd in the year 837. He died in Muḥarram 840 in Mecca. Ibn Fahd chronicled him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02339 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02339-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02339-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02339 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جار الله الهذباني الشريف الحسني . مات في سلخ شعبان سنة ست وسبعين بوادي الآبار وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بها . أرخه ابن فهد أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jār Allāh al-Hadhabānī al-Sharīf al-Ḥasanī. He died at the end of Shaʿbān in 876 AH in Wādī al-Ābār and was carried to Mecca where he was buried. Ibn Fahd also recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D02340 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02340-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02340-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02340-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02340 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانباي الأشرفي قايتباي بل هو ابن أخته وأحد العشرات ، تلقى أقطاع نائب اسكندرية قائم قشير عنه ولم يلبث أن مات مطعونا في سنة احدى وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbāy al-Ashrafī Qāytbāy. He was the son of his (Sultan Qaytbay's) sister and one of the 'Officers of Ten'. He took over the iqṭāʿ of Qāʾim Qushayr, the nāʾib of Alexandria, and soon afterwards died — plague-stricken (or possibly stabbed) — in the year 881."@en .

rec:AIND-D02344 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02344-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02344-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02344 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك من يلخجا الظاهري جقمق . صاهر الامين الاقصرائي على ابنته زينب واستولدها ولدا ذكرا ، ومات عنهما في طاعون سنة سبع وأربعين ولم يكمل الثلاثين وكان قد جود الخط وكتب به عدة مصاحف وغيرها كالشفا وقرأه على صهره ووقفه فتنظر من عند جقمق الذي خلفه على زوجته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak min Yalkhujā al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq married Zaynab, the daughter of al-Amīn al-Aqṣarāʾī, and had a male child with her. He died in the plague of 847 H, not having completed thirty years of age. He had mastered calligraphy and copied several Qurʾāns and other works, such as al-Shifāʾ. He recited al-Shifāʾ to his father-in-law (al-Amīn al-Aqṣarāʾī) and endowed it, and it was subsequently kept with Jaqmaq (al-Muḥammadī), who married his widow after him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02345 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02345-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02345-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02345 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الأبو بكري الاشرفي برسباي ، أحد من تأمر في الأيام الاينالية وتنمر ثم بطل وشاخ وكان يسكن جوار جامع ابن ميالة بين السورين . مات في المحرم سنة أربع وثمانين وكنت المصلي عليه اماما اتفاقا بمصلى باب النصر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Janbak al-Abū Bakrī al-Ashrafī Barsbāy, one of those who held the rank of amir during the time of Īnāl and became oppressive, then lost power and grew old. He used to reside near Jāmiʿ Ibn Mayyāla, between the two walls. He died in Muḥarram of the year 884 H. I (al-Sakhāwī) happened to be the one who led his funeral prayer as imam at the Muṣallā Bāb al-Naṣr."@en .

rec:AIND-D02346 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02346-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02346-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02346 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الأشرفي الخاصكي ممن قتل على يد العرب في تجريدة للبحيرة سنة ثمان وستين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Janbak al-Ashrafī al-Khāṣṣakī, one of those killed by Arabs during a military campaign to al-Buḥayra in the year 868."@en .

rec:AIND-D02350 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02350-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02350-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02350 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك السيفي اقبردي ثم الاشرفي برسباي والد ناصر الدين محمد أحد جماعة الصرغتمشية . مات في ليلة ثاني جمادى الاولى سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Sayfī Aqburdī, then al-Ashrafī Barsbāy, father of Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad, one of the jamāʿa of al-Ṣarghatmashiyya. He died on the night of the second of Jumādā al-Ūlā in the year 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02354 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02354-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02354-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02354 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الثور السيفي أمير الترك بمكة بل ولي نيابة جدة وناب باسكندرية وقتا وكان أحد الطبلخاناه والحاجب الثاني . مات بمكة في شعبان سنة احدى واربعين . ارخه ابن فهد وغيره ، قال المقريزي ومستراح منه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Janbak al-Thawr al-Sayfī was an amir of the Turks in Mecca, and he also served as deputy of Jeddah and for a time as deputy in Alexandria. He was also one of the ṭablkhānāh (military band) and the second chamberlain. He died in Mecca in Shaʿbān 841 H. Ibn Fahd and others chronicled him, and al-Maqrīzī commented, 'Good riddance to him.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D02357 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02357-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02357-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02357 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الجكمي أيضا الظاهري . تنقل في الخدم والولايات إلى أن ناب في ملطية مدة حتى مات بها في ربيع الآخر سنة ست وستين وقد اسن واستقر بعده في ملطية اينال الأشقر الوالي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Janbak al-Jukmī, also al-Ẓāhirī. He moved between various services and governorships until he served as nāʾib in Malatya for a period, where he eventually died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 866, having become old. After him, Aynāl al-Ashqar al-Wālī was appointed to the nāʾib position in Malatya."@en .

rec:AIND-D02358 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02358-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02358-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02358 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الحمزاوي . ولي نيابة غزة ومات قبل وصوله إلى آمد في ذي الحجة سنة ست وثلاثين ودفن بدمشق ولم يكن مشكورا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Ḥamzāwī. He assumed the deputyship of Ghazza, but died in Dhū al-Ḥijja 836, before reaching Āmid, and was buried in Dimashq. He was not well-regarded."@en .

rec:AIND-D02359 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02359-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02359-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02359 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الزيني المؤيدي شيخ . صار خاصكيا في دولة المظفر أحمد بن استاذه وتأمر عشرة ثم طبلخاناه كلاهما في ايام خشقدم ، ثم سافر في المجردين إلى سوار فعاد وهو مريض ولزم الفراش اشهرا ثم مات في مستهل رجب سنة أربع وسبعين وقد ناهز السبعين ، وكان عاقلا ساكنا صينا قليل الشر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Zaynī al-Muʾayyadī. He became a khāṣṣakī during the reign of al-Muẓaffar Aḥmad, son of his patron/master, and then became an amir of ten, and subsequently a ṭablkhānāh, both during the time of Khushqadam. Later, he traveled with the mujarradūn (expeditionary troops) against (Shāh) Suwār, from which campaign he returned ill. He was confined to bed for months and then died at the beginning of Rajab in 874 H, having nearly reached the age of seventy. He was a rational, calm, modest, and virtuous man."@en .

rec:AIND-D02361 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02361-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02361-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02361 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك السليماني أحد أمراء دمشق وإليه ينسب خان السليماني بظاهرها ظنا . مات في شعبان سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Janbak al-Sulaymānī, one of the emirs of Damascus. Khan al-Sulaymānī in the outer part of Damascus is presumably named after him. He died in Sha'ban of the year 857."@en .

rec:AIND-D02362 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02362-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02362-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02362 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك السودوني من عبد الرحمن نائب رأس نوبة الجمدارية . ممن قتل على يد العرب في تجريدة البحيرة سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Sūdūnī min ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, deputy raʾs nawbat al-Jamdāriyya. He was among those killed by the Arabs during the Buḥayra expedition in the year 868 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02363 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02363-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02363-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02363 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الشمسي المؤيدي . اشتراه المؤيد في أيام أتابكيته ، وترقى من بعده حتى صار من أمراء طرابلس ، ثم ولي حجوبية الحجاب بحلب ثم عزل وتوجه إلى دمشق فأنعم عليه بامرة طبلخاناه بها إلى أن مات فيها في أواخر ذي القعدة أو أوائل الذي بعده سنة تسع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Shamsī al-Muʾayyadī. Al-Muʾayyad purchased him during his atabak-ship, and he subsequently rose in rank until he became one of the amirs of Tripoli. Then he was appointed as ḥājib al-ḥujjāb in Aleppo, but he was dismissed and proceeded to Damascus, where he was granted the amirate of ṭablkhānāh. He held that office until he died there in late Dhū al-Qaʿda or early the next month in the year 859."@en .

rec:AIND-D02364 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02364-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02364-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02364 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الصوفي الظاهري برقوق أحد المقدمين وصاحب تلك الوقائع والحروب . فر من محبسه باسكندرية وأعيا السلطان تطلبه ، وامتحن جماعة بسببه إلى أن ظهر عند ابن دلغادر . مات في منتصف ربيع الآخر سنة إحدى وأربعين واختلف في سبب قتله ، وكان فيما قاله المقريزي ظالما عاتيا جبارا لم يعرف بدين ولا كرم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Ṣūfī al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq was one of the muqaddams (military commanders) and the man of those well-known incidents and wars. He escaped from his prison in Alexandria, exhausting the Sultan in his pursuit. Many people were tested because of him, until he appeared with Ibn Dulghādir. He died in mid-Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 841 H. The cause of his death is disputed. According to al-Maqrīzī, he was an unjust, violent, and tyrannical individual, known neither for piety nor generosity."@en .

rec:AIND-D02365 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02365-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02365-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02365 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الطياري الظاهري متولي مكس جدة . مات في سنة ثمان وستين . أرخه ابن عزم ، ويحرر مع الآتي بعد ثلاثة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Ṭayyārī al-Ẓāhirī, administrator of customs in Jidda. He died in the year 868 H. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his death. (Al-Sakhāwī notes:) his case is to be verified together with the entry coming three entries later."@en .

rec:AIND-D02367 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02367-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02367-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02367 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الظاهري الأبلق أحد العشرات ممن ساق المحمل في جملة الباشات قتله الفرنج في الماعوصة بجزيرة قبرس في أحد الجمادين سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Ẓāhirī al-Ablaq was one of the amirs of Ten, among those of the bāshāt who drove the maḥmal. He was killed by the Franks at al-Māʿūṣa on the island of Cyprus in one of the two Jumādās in the year 868 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02368 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02368-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02368-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02368 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك الظاهري البواب عفريت ، ممن قتل على يد العرب في تجريدة البحيرة سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Ẓāhirī al-Bawwāb ʿIfrīt was among those killed by the Arabs during the Buḥayra expedition in the year 868."@en .

rec:AIND-D02373 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02373-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02373-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02373 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك قصروه . مات سنة أربع وستين . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak Quṣrūh. He died in the year 864 H. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D02375 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02375-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02375-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02375 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك كوهيه أحد المقدمين غير أنه بطل قبل وفاته من التقدمة لضعفه . مات وأنا بمكة في سنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak Kūhīya. He was one of the muqaddams, but was dismissed from the taqdima before his death due to his weakness. He died in an unspecified year while I (al-Sakhāwī) was in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02378 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02378-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02378-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02378 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك المؤيدي الدوادار . مات سنة سبع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Muʾayyadī al-Dawādār. He died in the year 817."@en .

rec:AIND-D02379 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02379-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02379-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02379-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02379 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك المؤيدي شيخ ويعرف بجانبك شيخ . طالت جنديته إلى أن أنعم خجداشية الظاهر خشقدم بامرة ضعيفة تقارب الجندية إلى أن مات بعدما شاخ بطالا في المحرم سنة ثلاث وسبعين . وكان من المهملين المنهمكين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak al-Muʾayyadī Shaykh, also known as Jānbak Shaykh. His service as a common soldier was prolonged until his khujdāsh (fellow mamluk) al-Ẓāhir Khushqadam granted him a weak amirate close to a soldier's rank. He remained so until he died in Muḥarram 873 AH, old and out of office. He was one of the negligent and self-indulgent."@en .

rec:AIND-D02383 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02383-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02383-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02383-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02383 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك النوروزي أيضا . أمره الظاهر جقمق عشرة ثم ولاه نيابة صهيون . ومات بمنزله بالعريش حين كان قادما القاهرة معزولا عنها في رجب سنة أربع وخمسين . وكان ذا شجاعة وإقدام رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānibak al-Nawrūzī, likewise (following another of the same name). Al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq appointed him amir of ten, and then made him nāʾib of Ṣahyūn. He died at his residence in al-ʿArīsh, while on his way to Cairo after having been dismissed from that post, in Rajab 854 AH. He was a courageous and daring man, may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02386 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02386-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02386-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02386-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02386 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانبك أحد المقدمين بدمشق ودوادار السلطان بها أصله من عتقاء تغري برمش التركماني نائب حلب وكان يزعم مع جهله العرفان قتل في تجريدة سوار سنة ثلاث وسبعين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānbak. He was one of the muqaddams in Damascus and the sultan's dawādār there. His origin was among the freedmen of Taghrī Barmish al-Turkumānī, the nāʾib of Ḥalab. He claimed ʿirfān (gnosis) despite his ignorance. He was killed in the expedition against (Shāh) Suwār in the year 873."@en .

rec:AIND-D02387 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02387-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02387-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02387-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02387 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جان بلاط الاشرفي اينال ، اختص بأستاذه وعمله ساقيا ثم امتحن إلى أن أمره الاشرف قايتباي عشرة ، ومات في رمضان سنة ثلاث وسبعين وحضر السلطان الصلاة عليه بالمؤمني ، وكان طوالا مليحا جميل الهيئة أحسن حالا من خجداشيته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jān Balāṭ al-Ashrafī (of Īnāl). He was closely attached to his master (ustādh), who made him a cupbearer (sāqī). He then underwent a period of trials until al-Ashraf Qāytbāy appointed him amir of ten. He died in Ramaḍān of the year 873, and the Sultan attended his funeral prayer at (Muṣallā) al-Muʾminī. He was tall, handsome, of fine appearance, and better off than his khujdāsh comrades."@en .

rec:AIND-D02392 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02392-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02392-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02392-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02392 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانم الاشرفي قايتباي ويعرف بالأشقر أحد العشرات المذكورين بمزيد الفروسية لكنه كان شهما مبغضا . مات في المحرم سنة اثنتين وثمانين وكان قد أمر قبل موته بيسير على كشف البحيرة فمات قبل توجهه اليها غير مأسوف عليه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānim al-Ashrafī Qāytbāy, also known as al-Ashqar, was one of the amirs of ten (al-ʿasharāt) noted for exceptional horsemanship, yet, though bold, he was a detested man. He died in Muḥarram 882 AH. Shortly before his death he had been appointed to the kashf of al-Buḥayra, but he passed away before setting out for it, unmourned."@en .

rec:AIND-D02395 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02395-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02395-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02395-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02395 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانم نائب قلعة حلب كان وقريب سلطان الوقت ممن قدمه ورام أن يزوجه ابنته فمات هو واياها في سنة سبع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānim, former commandant (nāʾib) of the Citadel of Aleppo, and a relative of the sultan of the time, who promoted him and intended to marry him to his daughter; but he and she both died in the year 897."@en .

rec:AIND-D02396 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02396-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02396-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02396-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02396 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانم الظاهري جقمق أحد مماليكه ودواداريته ويعرف بجانم خمسمائة . مات في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين بالطاعون ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānim al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq was one of Jaqmaq's mamluks and one of his dawādārs, known as Jānim Khamsmiʾa (\"Five Hundred\"). He died in Ṣafar 853 AH of the plague."@en .

rec:AIND-D02397 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02397-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02397-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02397-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02397 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانم ابن خالة يشبك الدوادار وصاحب المدرسة المقابلة لباب جامع قوصون من الشارع وبها خطبة خطبها يس البلبيسي المظفري محمود الامشاطي بخصوصيته بصاحبها كان أحد الدوادارية بل تأمر عشرة وتولى كشف الصعيد وفتك وحصل بحيث أخذ منه الملك جملة وكان يكره انتماءه لقريبه فيما قيل وسافر في عدة تجاريد وأظنه من الاشرفية برسباي بعد أن كان لبعض أمراء الشام ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānim, the son of the maternal aunt of Yashbak al-Dawādār, and the owner (ṣāḥib) of the madrasa opposite the gate of Jāmiʿ Qūṣūn on the street. In it there is a khuṭba, which was delivered by Yās al-Bilbaysī and — on account of his special connection with its owner — by al-Muẓaffarī Maḥmūd al-Amshāṭī. Jānim was one of the dawādārs; indeed he rose to be an amir of ten and took charge of the kashf of al-Ṣaʿīd (Upper Egypt). He committed acts of violence and amassed wealth to the extent that the ruler seized a large sum from him. It was said that he disliked his association with his relative. He traveled on several military expeditions, and I (al-Sakhāwī) think he was one of the Ashrafiyya (mamluks) of Barsbāy, after having belonged to one of the amirs of al-Shām."@en .

rec:AIND-D02398 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02398-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02398-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02398-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02398 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانم المؤيدي شيخ . ولي في أيام أستاذه رأس نوبة السقاة ثم صار أمير عشرة ثم من رءوس النوب كلاهما في أيام الاشرف اينال ، وكان ساكنا عاقلا حشما وقورا . مات في المحرم سنة احدى وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānim al-Muʾayyadī Shaykh. During the days of his master (ustādh) he held the office of head of the corps of cupbearers (raʾs nawbat al-suqāh); then he became an amir of ten, and then one of the heads of the guard corps (ruʾūs al-nuwab), both of the latter during the days of al-Ashraf Īnāl. He was calm, intelligent, modest and dignified. He died in Muḥarram of the year 861 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02399 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02399-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02399-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02399-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02399 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جانم كان قد أعطى تقدمة وناب في غزة وفي حماة وطرابلس ، قال العيني لم يشتهر عنه إلا كل شر ، مات في سنة أربع عشرة . ذكره شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jānim was granted a command (taqdima) and served as nāʾib in Gaza, Ḥamā, and Tripoli. Al-ʿAynī said, \"Nothing but evil was known about him.\" He died in the year 814 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02400 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02400-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02400-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02400-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02400 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جاهنشاه بن قرا يوسف والد بداق الماضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jahānshāh b. Qarā Yūsuf, father of Badāq (mentioned above)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02401 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02401-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02401-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02401-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02401 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جبريل بن إبراهيم بن محمد العطيري الشافعي رأيته عرض عليه في سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jibrīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-ʿAṭīrī al-Shāfiʿī. I (al-Sakhāwī) saw him as he presented (ʿaraḍa) his memorized texts to a shaykh in the year 895 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02402 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02402-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02402-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02402-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02402 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جبريل بن علي بن محمد القابوني ثم الدمشقي الشافعي . سمع على البرهان إبراهيم بن جماعة الأدب المفرد للبخاري وعلى الكمال بن النحاس والبدر حسن بن محمد البعلي واسمعيل بن إبراهيم بن مروان وجماعة وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء أجاز لي وكان ثقة صالحا خيرا مديما للتلاوة . مات بدمشق في المحرم سنة خمس وخمسين وقد جاز المائة رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jibrīl b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Qābūnī, then al-Dimashqī, al-Shāfiʿī. He heard al-Bukhārī's al-Adab al-Mufrad from al-Burhān Ibrāhīm b. Jamāʿa, and heard from al-Kamāl b. al-Naḥḥās, al-Badr Ḥasan b. Muḥammad al-Baʿlī, Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Marwān, and many others. He transmitted ḥadīth, and the eminent scholars (al-fuḍalāʾ) heard from him. He granted me (al-Sakhāwī) an ijāza. He was trustworthy, righteous and virtuous, constant in recitation of the Qurʾān. He died in Damascus in Muḥarram of the year 855, having passed one hundred years of age. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02403 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02403-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02403-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02403-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02403 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ججكبغا دوادار السلطان بالشام . جهزه الظاهر جقمق لشاه رخ بن تمرلنك ملك ما وراء النهر وقال إنه سالك عن ابن حجر وابن الديري وابن قاضي شهبة وابن المزلق كل واحد على انفراده وأنا أقول طيب أو بخير ولم يسأل عن غيرهم ثم قال الحمد لله بعد في الناس بقية ، ومات بعد ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jajikbughā, the Sultan's dawādār in al-Shām. Al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq dispatched him to Shāhrukh b. Timur, the ruler of Transoxiana. He related that Shāhrukh asked about Ibn Ḥajar, Ibn al-Dayrī, Ibn Qāḍī Shuhba, and Ibn al-Muzalliq, each one individually, \"and I would say: fine, or well.\" He asked about no one else, and then said, \"Praise be to God — there is still a remnant (of good men) among the people.\" He (Jajikbughā) died after that."@en .

rec:AIND-D02404 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02404-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02404-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02404-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02404 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جخيدب بن جندب بن جخيدب بن لحاف بن راجح . مات سنة تسع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jukhaydib b. Jundub b. Jukhaydib b. Laḥāf b. Rājiḥ. He died in the year 829 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02407 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02407-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02407-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02407-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02407 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جرباش الاشرفي برسباي . كان في أيامه خاصكيا ثم أمره ابنه العزيز عشرة ثم أخرجه الظاهر جقمق لتابكية غزة وتوفي بها في سنة اثنتين وخمسين ، وكان لا بأس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jarbāsh al-Ashrafī Barsbāy. In the days of (al-Ashraf Barsbāy) he was a khāṣṣakī (royal guard mamluk); then Barsbāy's son al-ʿAzīz appointed him amir of ten; then al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq sent him out to the atābakiyya of Gaza, and he died there in the year 852. He was a decent enough man (lā baʾsa bihi)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02410 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02410-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02410-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02410-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02410 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جشار النصيح بن أحمد بن عبد الكريم بن عبد الله بن عمر العمري أحد القواد بمكة . قتل في مقتلة الحديد بجدة في صفر سنة ست واربعين وقطع رأسه وطيف به ثم دفن آخر يومه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jushār al-Naṣīḥ b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar al-ʿUmarī, one of the commanders (quwwād) in Mecca. He was killed in Maqtalat al-Ḥadīd (the \"Iron Massacre\") in Jidda in Ṣafar 846 AH; his head was cut off and paraded, and he was buried at the end of that day."@en .

rec:AIND-D02411 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02411-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02411-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02411-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02411 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جشار بن عبد الله المجاش الشريف الحجازي مات في ذي الحجة سنة سبع وخمسين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jushār b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Mujāsh al-Sharīf al-Ḥijāzī died in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 857 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02412 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02412-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02412-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02412-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02412 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جشار بن قاسم من بني أبي نمي الحسني المكي . كان من اعيان الاشراف شجاعا بدر إلى مبارزة كبيش يوم أداخر فعقر كبيش فرسه . مات في ذي الحجة سنة احدى عشرة بمكة ودفن بالمعلاة . ذكره الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jashshār b. Qāsim, of the Banū Abī Numayy, al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He was among the prominent ashrāf and courageous: he rushed forward to duel Kabīsh on the day of Adākhir, and Kabīsh hamstrung his horse. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja 811 H in Mecca and was buried at al-Muʿallā. Al-Fāsī mentioned him in his history of Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02413 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02413-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02413-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02413 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جشار الخضيري ، مات في المحرم سنة ثمان وخمسين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jashshār al-Khuḍayrī. He died in Muḥarram 858 AH in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02415 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02415-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02415-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02415 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جعفر بن أحمد بن عبد المهدي . مات في شوال سنة تسع وأربعين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jaʿfar b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Mahdī. He died in Shawwāl in the year 849 AH in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02416 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02416-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02416-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02416 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جعفر بن أبي بكر بن رسلان بن نصير البلقيني القاهري الشافعي ابن أخي السراج عمر وأخو البهاء رسلان وناصر الدين محمد والشهاب أحمد . ذكره شيخنا في ترجمة والده من أنبائه استطرادا فقال كان فقيها فاضلا دينا متواضعا ناب في الحكم وولي قضاء بعض البلاد كسمنود وتأخر بعد رسلان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jaʿfar b. Abī Bakr b. Raslān b. Nuṣayr al-Bulqīnī, al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, was the nephew (brother’s son) of al-Sirāj ʿUmar, and the brother of al-Bahāʾ Raslān, Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad, and al-Shihāb Aḥmad. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him incidentally in his father's biography in *Inbāʾ al-Ghumr*, saying: \"He was a learned, virtuous, pious, and humble jurist. He served as a judicial deputy and held judgeship in some lands like Samannūd, and he outlived Raslān.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D02417 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02417-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02417-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02417 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جعفر بن محمد بن جعفر البعلي الحنبلي ويعرف بابن الشويخ بمعجمتين مصغر سمع في سنة خمس وتسعين وسبعمائة علي الزين عبد الرحمن ابن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن الزعبوب الصحيح ببعلبك وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء وما لقيته في الرحلة فكأنه مات قبلها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jaʿfar b. Muḥammad b. Jaʿfar al-Baʿlī al-Ḥanbalī, known as Ibn al-Shuwaykh (both shīn and khāʾ with diacritical points, in the diminutive form). In 795 H, he heard al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Zaʿbūb in Baʿlabakk. He then transmitted ḥadīth, and many virtuous scholars heard from him. Al-Sakhāwī did not meet him on his journey, so it is likely he died before it."@en .

rec:AIND-D02419 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02419-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02419-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02419 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جعفر الزين العجمي الحنفي نزيل المؤيدية . ممن قرأ عليه الزين زكريا القاضي شرح الشمسية وغالب حاشيتها للسيد وكذا أخذ عنه الحكمة ووصفه بالفضل والديانة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jaʿfar al-Zayn al-ʿAjamī al-Ḥanafī, a resident of al-Muʾayyadiyya. Al-Zayn Zakariyā al-Qāḍī studied with him, reading Sharḥ al-Shamsiyya and most of its supercommentary by al-Sayyid. He also acquired al-Ḥikma (philosophy/wisdom) from him and described him as possessing excellence and piety."@en .

rec:AIND-D02420 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02420-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02420-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02420 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جغنوس الناصري . ولي نيابة بيروت ثم صرف عنها . ومات في أوائل العشر الأخير من رمضان سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jaghnūs al-Nāṣirī. He assumed the governorship of Beirut but was later dismissed from it. He died in the early last ten days of Ramaḍān in the year 857 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02421 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02421-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02421-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02421 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جقمق بن جخيدب بن أحمد بن حمزة بن أبي نمي الحسني المكي . مات في ربيع الأول سنة خمسين خارج مكة وحمل إليها فدفن بها . أرخة ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jaqmaq b. Jukhaydab b. Aḥmad b. Ḥamza b. Abī Numayy, al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 850 outside Makka, and was carried to it and buried there. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D02422 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02422-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02422-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02422 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جقمق الصفوي الحاجب بدمشق ، قبض عليه في المحرم سنة خمس وثمانمائة ثم أرسل إلى غزة فلما تولى نوروز سنة ثمان وثمانمائة استصحبه لدمشق وقرره في الحجوبية فلما انكسر نوروز ، مات فيها ، ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jaqmaq al-Ṣafawī, the Ḥājib in Damascus. He was arrested in Muḥarram of the year 805 [Hijri], then sent to Gaza. When Nawrūz took office in 808 [Hijri], he brought him back to Damascus and reappointed him to the chamberlainship. When Nawrūz was defeated, he died there. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his *Inbāʾ*."@en .

rec:AIND-D02425 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02425-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02425-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02425 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جقمق الأرغون شاوي الدوادار . ولي نيابة دمشق وابتنى فيها في جوار الجامع الاموي مدرسة تعرف بالجقمقية ثم خرج بها عن طاعة المؤيد وجرى له ما جرى . قلت وهو الذي قبله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jaqmaq al-Arghūn Shāwī al-Dawādār held the deputyship of Damascus, and there, next to the Umayyad Mosque, he built a madrasa known as al-Jaqmaqiyya. Afterwards, he rebelled against al-Muʾayyad, and what happened to him happened. I [al-Sakhāwī] say that he is the one mentioned before him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02429 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02429-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02429-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02429 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جكم الاشرفي قايتباي أحد الخاصكية ويلقب بالبهلوان لتقدمه في الصراع . مات بالطاعون سنة احدى وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jakam al-Ashrafī Qāytbāy, one of the khāṣṣakiyya. He was nicknamed al-Bahlawān (the Wrestler) due to his excellence in wrestling (al-ṣirāʿ). He died of the plague in 881 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02430 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02430-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02430-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02430 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جكم الظاهري خشقدم ابن اخت الاشرف قايتباي ، امره استاذه عشرة ثم صار أحد الطبلخاناه وحاجب ثاني ، مات بالطاعون في رمضان سنة ثلاث وثمانين عن نحو الثلاثين وحضر خاله الصلاة عليه بالمؤمني ، وكان من مساوئ الدهر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jakam al-Ẓāhirī Khushqadam, sister’s son of al-Ashraf Qāytbāy. His master (ustādh) made him amir ʿashara; he then became one of the ṭablakhānāh and second ḥājib. He died of the plague in Ramaḍān 883 AH, at around thirty years of age, and his maternal uncle attended the funeral prayer over him at al-Muʾminī. He was among the evils of the age."@en .

rec:AIND-D02431 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02431-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02431-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02431 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جكم الظاهري برقوق الجركسي ذكره شيخنا مجردا في سنة ثلاث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jakam al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq al-Jarkasī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) listed him name-only under the year three (803 H)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02432 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02432-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02432-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02432 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جكم النوري المؤيدي ويعرف بقلقسيز . أعتقه المؤيد وأقام في جملة المماليك السلطانية إلى أن عمله الظاهر جقمق خاصكيا ثم ساقيا ثم فصله عنها وجعله من الاجناد ثم عمله الاشرف اينال أمير عشرة ثم من رؤوس النوب ثم كان ممن خرج مع المجردين ، ومات في عوده بغزة في شوال سنة احدى وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jakam al-Nūrī al-Muʾayyadī, known as Qalqasīz. He was freed by al-Muʾayyad and remained among the sultan's Mamluks. Then, al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq appointed him as a khāṣṣakī (sultan's bodyguard), then as a sāqī (cup-bearer), but later dismissed him from these positions and made him one of the common soldiers (ajnād). After that, al-Ashraf Īnāl appointed him as an amīr ʿashara (commander of ten), then as one of the raʾs al-nuwab (head of a guard unit). He later went out with the detached troops (al-mujarradūn) and died on his return in Ghazza in Shawwāl of the year 861 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02433 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02433-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02433-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02433 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جكم نائب قلعة كركر تحيل عليه جماعة من الاكراد حتى قتلوه وطائفة من مماليكه وملكوها وذلك في سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jakam, nāʾib (governor) of Qalʿat Karkar. A group of Kurds schemed against him until they killed him and a group of his own mamluks, and seized the fortress. This occurred in the year 868."@en .

rec:AIND-D02434 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02434-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02434-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02434 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جلال الاسلام بن نور الاسلام بن محمود بن علي عضد الدين بن شهاب الدين بن نور الدين الكرماني الشافعي . ممن أخذ عني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jalāl al-Islām b. Nūr al-Islām b. Maḥmūd b. ʿAlī ʿAḍud al-Dīn b. Shihāb al-Dīn b. Nūr al-Dīn al-Kirmānī al-Shāfiʿī. He was among those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02435 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02435-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02435-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02435 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جلبان بن أبي سويد بن أبي دعيج بن أبي نمي الحسني المكي . كان موجودا في سنة اثنتين وعشرين لابن مقبل بن وهبة استقبله فضربه ليلا بالسيف وهو متوجه لمكة فحمى لجلبان قومه قاله ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Julbān b. Abī Suwayd b. Abī Duʿayj b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He was alive in the year 822 H. Ibn Muqbil b. Wahba met him and struck him at night with a sword while he was on his way to Mecca, whereupon his people rose up in Julbān's defence. This was stated by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D02436 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02436-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02436-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02436 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جلبان العمري الظاهري برقوق أحد أمراء العشرات والحجاب ممن يميل لدين وخير ، ولي حجوبية غزة بعد سنة ثلاثين وثمانمائة تقريبا ومات فيها بعد ذلك بسنيات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Julbān al-ʿUmarī al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq was one of the amirs of ten and one of the ḥājibs, inclined towards religion and goodness. He was appointed to the chamberlainship of Gaza after approximately 830 H and died there a few years later."@en .

rec:AIND-D02439 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02439-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02439-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02439 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جلبان المؤيدي أحد المقدمين في الدولة المؤيدية ورأس نوبة الصارمي إبراهيم المدعو سيدي . توفي بحبس اسكندرية مقتولا سنة أربع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Julbān al-Muʾayyadī was one of the muqaddams during the Muʾayyadī reign and the raʾs nawba of al-Ṣārimī Ibrāhīm, who was called Sīdī. He died in the prison of Alexandria, having been killed, in the year 824 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02440 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02440-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02440-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02440 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جماز بن مفتاح العجلاني المكي . أحد القواد . مات في ذي الحجة سنة ثمان وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jammāz b. Miftāḥ al-ʿAjlānī al-Makkī. He was one of the qāʾids (commanders). He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 848 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D02441 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02441-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02441-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02441 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جماز بن مقبل العمري القائد ، قتل مع السيد رميثة في رجب سنة سبع وثلاثين ببلاد الشرق ، أرخه ابن فهد أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jammāz b. Muqbil al-ʿUmarī, the qāʾid. He was killed together with al-Sayyid Rumaytha in Rajab 837 H in the eastern lands (Bilād al-Sharq). Ibn Fahd, too, recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D02442 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02442-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02442-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02442 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جماز بن منصور بن عمر بن مسعود العمري القائد بمكة ، مات بناحية اليمن سنة ست وأربعين ، أرخه ابن فهد أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jammāz b. Manṣūr b. ʿUmar b. Masʿūd al-ʿUmarī, the qāʾid in Mecca. He died in the region of Yemen in the year 846 H. Ibn Fahd, too, recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D02443 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02443-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02443-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02443 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جماز بن هبة بن جماز بن منصور الحسيني أمير المدينة ، مات مقتولا في حرب بينه وبين أعدائه سنة اثنتي عشرة وثمانمائة وقد كان أخذ حاصل المدينة ونزح عنها فلم يمهل مع أنه كان يظهر إعزاز أهل السنة ومحبتهم بخلاف ثابت بن نعير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jammāz b. Hiba b. Jammāz b. Manṣūr al-Ḥusaynī, amir of Medina, was killed in a war between him and his enemies in the year 812 H. He had seized the revenues of Medina and withdrawn from it, but he was given no respite — even though, unlike Thābit b. Nuʿayr, he used to show honor and affection to the people of the Sunna."@en .

rec:AIND-D02444 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02444-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02444-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02444 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جمال بن عز الدين بن جمان أحمد الكيلاني . هكذا جرده ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jamāl b. ʿIzz al-Dīn b. Jumān Aḥmad al-Kīlānī. Thus Ibn Fahd listed him, in bare form (without further detail)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02445 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02445-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02445-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02445 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جميل بن أحمد بن عميرة بن يوسف ويعرف بابن يوسف شيخ العرب ببعض إقليم الغربية والسخاوية من الوجه البحري . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة خمس وستين عن أزيد من ستين سنة وخلف شيئا كثيرا من حلال وحرام مع أنه كان يتدين ويعف لكن عما عدا المظالم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jamīl b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmayra b. Yūsuf, known as Ibn Yūsuf, was shaykh of the Arabs in parts of the al-Gharbiyya and al-Sakhāwiyya regions of Lower Egypt. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 865, at over sixty years of age. He left behind a great deal of wealth, both lawful and unlawful, even though he was religious and abstinent — save when it came to unjust exactions (maẓālim)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02446 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02446-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02446-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02446 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جنبك اليحياوي الظاهري أتابك العساكر بحلب وهو تخفيف من جانبك قتل في وقعة حلب بساجورا مع أحمد بن أويس وقرا يوسف في منتصف شوال سنة اثنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Janbak al-Yaḥyāwī al-Ẓāhirī, atābak al-ʿasākir in Aleppo — Janbak being a lightened form of Jānibak. He was killed in mid-Shawwāl of the year 802 in the battle of Aleppo at al-Sājūr, in the encounter with Aḥmad b. Uways and Qarā Yūsuf."@en .

rec:AIND-D02452 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02452-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02452-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02452 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جوبان الظاهر برقوق المعلم . كان خاصكيا ومعلما للرمح في أيام أستاذه تركي الجنس سليم الباطن انتهت إليه الرياسة في تعليم الرمح في زمانه بحيث كان حكما بين أهله في الأيام المؤيدية ثم الأشرفية برسباي ، واستمر على ما هو عليه من القوة في تعليمه حتى بعد شيخوخته . مات في سنة نيف وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jawbān al-Ẓāhir Barqūq al-Muʿallim. He was a khāṣṣakī and spear instructor in the days of his master (al-Ẓāhir Barqūq). Turkish by origin and sound of heart, he attained the leadership in spear instruction in his time, such that he acted as arbiter among its practitioners in the Muʾayyadī and then the Ashrafī (Barsbāy) days. He maintained his strength in teaching even after his old age. He died in a year in the (8)30s AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02454 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02454-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02454-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02454 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جوهر صفي الدين عتيق الزهوري المصري الدلال . سمع على الجمال الحنبلي ثمانيات النجيب وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء . مات سنة بضع وأربعين ، وكان وكيلا بباب الخرق وربما دلل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jawhar Ṣafī al-Dīn, freedman (ʿatīq) of al-Zahūrī, al-Miṣrī al-Dallāl. He heard the Thamāniyyāt al-Najīb from al-Jamāl al-Ḥanbalī and transmitted it, and the learned heard from him. He died in the (8)40s AH. He served as a wakīl (agent) at Bāb al-Kharq, and sometimes worked as a broker."@en .

rec:AIND-D02455 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02455-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02455-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02455 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جوهر التمر بغاوي الظاهري الحبشي . ممن يندبه الاشرف في أمور من جملتها بركة ابن الجريش بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jawhar al-Tamurbaghāwī al-Ẓāhirī al-Ḥabashī. He was among those whom al-Ashraf would commission for various affairs, among them (the charge of) Birkat Ibn al-Juraysh in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02457 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02457-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02457-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02457 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جوهر الحبشي فتى عبد القادر بن فريوات الحلبي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jawhar al-Ḥabashī, slave (fatā) of ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Faryawāt al-Ḥalabī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02458 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02458-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02458-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02458 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جوهر الحبشي فتى علي بن الزكي أبي بكر الآتي . ممن سمع مني أيضا بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jawhar al-Ḥabashī, slave (fatā) of ʿAlī b. al-Zakī Abī Bakr (whose entry is to come). He, too, was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02459 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02459-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02459-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02459 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جوهر السيفي استادار الذخيرة ، وصرف عنها بالزين عبد الرحمن بن الكويز في سنة أربع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jawhar al-Sayfī, ustādār al-dhakhīra. He was removed from it in favor of al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Kuwayz in the year 844."@en .

rec:AIND-D02460 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02460-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02460-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02460 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جوهر شرا قطلي الحبشي الخازندار الزمام ، مات في صفر سنة اثنتين وثمانين ، وصلى عليه ثم دفن بتربة بالقرب من تربة كنفوش ، واستقر بعده خشقدم الاحمدي اللالا شاد السواقي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jawhar Shurā Quṭlī al-Ḥabashī, al-khāzindār al-zimām. He died in Ṣafar 882 H. Funeral prayers were performed over him, and he was then buried in a turba near the turba of Kanafūsh. Khushqadam al-Aḥmadī al-Lālā, shād al-sawāqī, succeeded him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02461 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02461-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02461-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02461 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جوهر الشمسي بن الزمن الحبشي . رباه أحسن تربية وبرع في التجارة ، وصار من أعيانهم وابتنى بعض الدور بمكة وقد رافقته في عودي من المدينة بمكة فحمدت عقله وأدبه وخدمته ورغبته في الخير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jawhar al-Shamsī [of] Ibn al-Zaman, al-Ḥabashī. [His master] raised him excellently, and he excelled in trade, became one of the notables among them, and built several houses in Mecca. I accompanied him on my return from Medina to Mecca, and I found his intellect, manners, service, and inclination to good praiseworthy."@en .

rec:AIND-D02463 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02463-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02463-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02463-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02463 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جوهر العجلاني نسبة لعجلان بن رميثة صاحب مكة كان ينطوي على خير وديانة وهو المربي لولدي سيده علي وحسن مات في سنة تسع أو عشر ودفن بالمعلاة ، ذكره الفاسي في مكة . )"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jawhar al-ʿAjlānī — the attribution being to ʿAjlān b. Rumaytha, lord of Mecca. He embodied goodness and piety, and was the tutor (murabbī) of his master's two sons, ʿAlī and Ḥasan. He died in the year (80)9 or (8)10 and was buried at al-Muʿallā. Al-Fāsī mentioned him in [his history of] Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02466 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02466-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02466-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02466-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02466 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جوهر المحبي بن الاشقر الحبشي . ممن تردد لسماع الحديث مع أولادنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jawhar al-Muḥibbī Ibn al-Ashqar al-Ḥabashī. He was among those who came regularly to hear hadith together with our children."@en .

rec:AIND-D02471 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02471-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02471-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02471 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جويعد بن بريم بن صبيحة بن عمر العمري القائد . مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة ثلاث وأربعين أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Juwayʿid b. Buraym b. Ṣubayḥa b. ʿUmar al-ʿUmarī, the qāʾid. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja 843 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D02472 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02472-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02472-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02472 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جياش بن سليمان بن داود بن أبي بكر زين الدين السنبلي اليماني أحد عظماء الأمراء بها ومات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jayyāsh b. Sulaymān b. Dāwūd b. Abī Bakr, Zayn al-Dīn al-Sunbulī al-Yamānī, one of the great amirs there (in Yemen); and he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D02473 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02473-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02473-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02473 ;
    aindv:sourceText "جيرك أو ميرك القاسمي وربما زيد الفاء أوله . من كبار الأمراء تنقل في الولايات منها نيابة غزة ، ومات بدمشق في جمادى الأولى سنة احدى وعشرين ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Jīrak, or Mīrak, al-Qāsimī — and sometimes a fāʾ is prefixed to the name. He was one of the great amirs, and moved through various governorships, among them the governorship (niyāba) of Gaza. He died in Damascus in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 821 H. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D02475 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02475-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02475-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02475 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حاتم بن عمر بن زكي الدين الدمشقي . ممن سمع منى بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥātim b. ʿUmar b. Zakī al-Dīn al-Dimashqī. Among those from whom I (al-Sakhāwī) heard in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02476 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02476-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02476-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02476 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حاجي بن إياس الهندي مولى السيد محمد بن جعفر بن علي الآتي سمع منى مع سيده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥājjī b. Iyās al-Hindī, a client (mawla) of al-Sayyid Muḥammad b. Jaʿfar b. ʿAlī (mentioned later). He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) with his master."@en .

rec:AIND-D02478 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02478-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02478-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02478 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حاجي بن عبد الله الزين الرومي ويعرف بحاجي فقيه شيخ التربة الظاهرية خارج القاهرة . كان عريا من العلم إلا ان له اتصالا بالترك كدأب غيره ، مات في شوال سنة ثمان عشرة واستقر في مشيختها الشمس البساطي . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥājjī b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Zayn al-Rūmī, known as Ḥājjī Faqīh. Shaykh of the Ẓāhiriyya turba (the mausoleum of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq) outside Cairo. He was devoid of scholarship, but he had connections with the Turks, as was the way of others like him. He died in Shawwāl of the year 818 H, and al-Shams al-Basāṭī was installed in the mashyakha of the turba after him. So said our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』."@en .

rec:AIND-D02479 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02479-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02479-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02479 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حاجي بن محمد بن قلاوون الملك المنصور . مات في سنة احدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥājjī b. Muḥammad b. Qalāwūn, al-Malik al-Manṣūr. He died in the year one (presumably 801 AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02480 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02480-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02480-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02480-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02480 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حاجي بن مغلطاي ويقال له أمير حاج ، مضى في الهمزة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥājjī b. Mughlaṭāy, also known as Amīr Ḥājj. Mentioned in the Hamza section."@en .

rec:AIND-D02481 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02481-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02481-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02481-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02481 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حازم بن عبد الكريم بن محمد أبي نمي الحسني المكي كان من أعيان الأشراف ممن صاهره الشريفان أحمد وعلي ابنا عجلان الأول على أخته والآخر على ابنته وعظم أمره لذلك ، ومات في أول القرن ، ذكره الفاسي ورأيت من قال في سنة عشر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥāzim b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad Abū Numayy al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī was among the notables of the Ashraf. The two sharīfs, Aḥmad and ʿAlī, sons of ʿAjlān, intermarried with him; the former (Aḥmad) married his sister, and the latter (ʿAlī) married his daughter. His stature consequently increased. He died at the beginning of the 9th century AH. Al-Fāsī mentioned him, and I saw someone who said he died in the year 810 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02482 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02482-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02482-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02482 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حافظ بن مهذب بن نير الجانفوري الهندي . ممن سمع منى بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥāfiẓ b. Muhadhdhab b. Nayyir al-Jānfūrī al-Hindī. One of those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02483 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02483-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02483-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02483 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حامد بن أبي بكر بن علي الزين الجيرتي الحنفي المقرئ نزيل مكة والمتوفي بها في نحو التسعين ممن سمع منى بالمدينة ، وكان دائما خيرا مديما للأشتغال ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥāmid b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī al-Zayn al-Jīratī al-Ḥanafī al-Muqriʾ. He resided in Mecca and died there around [the year] 890 H. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina. He was always virtuous, constantly engaged in study."@en .

rec:AIND-D02484 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02484-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02484-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02484 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حامد المغربي التاجر السفار . ممن استأجر بالسويقة من مكة بيتا من أوقاف السيد حسن بن عجلان . مات بها في شوال سنة إحدى وثمانين ودفن بالمعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥāmid al-Maghribī, the traveling merchant. He was among those who rented a house in al-Suwayqa, Mecca, from the endowments of al-Sayyid Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān. He died there in Shawwāl of the year 881 and was buried in al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D02485 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02485-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02485-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02485 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حبك بضم المهملة والموحدة وآخره كاف . رأس نوبة وأحد الطبلخاناه بمصر في أيام الناصر فرج . مات في مستهل ذي القعدة سنة ثلاث وخرج أقطاعه الخمسين من مماليك الناصر ، وكان من الجهلة المفسدين . قاله العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥubuk (with ḍamma on both the undotted [ḥāʾ] and the single-dotted [bāʾ], ending in kāf). He was a raʾs nawba and one of the ṭablkhāna [amirs] in Egypt in the days of al-Nāṣir Faraj. He died at the beginning of Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year 803 AH, and his iqṭāʿ of the fifty [grade] passed out to mamluks of al-Nāṣir. He was one of the ignorant and corrupt; so said al-ʿAynī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02487 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02487-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02487-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02487 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حبيب الله بن خليل الله بن محمد الكازروني . ممن سمع منى بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥabīb Allāh b. Khalīl Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Kāzarūnī. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02489 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02489-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02489-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02489-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02489-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02489 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حبيب بن يوسف بن صالح بن محمد الكيلاني القاهري الشافعي المقرئ . قرأ على التاج بن تمرية وأقرأ وكان صوفيا بالأشرفية برسباي وقرض لجعفر بعض تصانيفه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥabīb b. Yūsuf b. Ṣāliḥ b. Muḥammad al-Kīlānī, from Cairo, a Shafi'i Qur'an reciter. He studied recitation under al-Tāj b. Tamurīya and also taught recitation himself. He was a Sufi at al-Ashrafiyya Barsbāy and wrote commendations (taqrīẓ) on some of Jaʿfar's works."@en .

rec:AIND-D02491 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02491-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02491-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02491-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02491 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حبيب آخر يدري القراءات . تلا عليه في جامع الأزهر وغيره غير واحد مات نحو سنة سبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥabīb, another one, who was versed in the Qurʾānic readings. More than one person recited under him at al-Azhar Mosque and elsewhere. He died around the year 870 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02493 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02493-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02493-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02493-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02493-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02493 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حجر بن يوسف بن شاهين الكركي الاصل القاهري الآتي أبوه تشبه أبوه في تسميته بلقب الجد الاعلى لجده لأمه شيخنا ولم يلبث أن مات وهو طفل."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥajar b. Yūsuf b. Shāhīn, of Karak origin, then al-Qāhirī (of Cairo). His father (mentioned later) in naming him followed the laqab of the remote ancestor of his own maternal grandfather, our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar). He soon died as a small child."@en .

rec:AIND-D02494 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02494-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02494-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02494 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حدندل ، في على غير منسوب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥadandal, for whom no attribution (nisba) or further details are recorded."@en .

rec:AIND-D02496 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02496-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02496-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02496 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حرسان بن شميلة بن محمد بن سالم الحفيصي المكي الآتي أخوه راجح وأبوهما ، مات بمكة في رجب سنة سبع وتسعين شبه الفجاءة ودفن عند سلفه بالمعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥarsān b. Shumayla b. Muḥammad b. Sālim al-Ḥafīṣī al-Makkī. His brother Rājiḥ and their father will both be mentioned later. He died suddenly in Mecca in Rajab 897 H and was buried with his ancestors in al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D02498 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02498-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02498-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02498-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02498 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حزمان بالفتح وهو اسم جركسي الظاهري برقوق . ممن ترقى في أيام ابن أستاذه حتى عمل نائب القدس ثم صار دوادارا ثانيا ثم خرج عن طاعته وفر قاصدا دمشق فأمسك بغزة وجيئ به فحبسه الناصر أياما ثم وسطه في سنة أربع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥazmān (with fatḥ), a Circassian name; [a mamluk] of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq. He was among those who rose through the ranks in the days of his master's son (al-Nāṣir Faraj), serving as nāʾib of Jerusalem and then becoming second dawādār. Afterward he abandoned his (al-Nāṣir's) obedience and fled, making for Damascus; he was seized in Gaza and brought back. Al-Nāṣir imprisoned him for some days, then had him cut in two (wassaṭahu) in the year 814."@en .

rec:AIND-D02500 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02500-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02500-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02500 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حزمان اليشبكي يشبك الشعباني ، ترقى بعد أستاذه إلى أن تأمر في أواخر دولة المؤيد أو في دولة ولده ، ولم تطل أيامه ومات في سنة أربع وعشرين ودفن بتربة سيده بالصحراء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥazmān al-Yashbakī, [mamluk of] Yashbak al-Shaʿbānī. After his master['s death] he rose until he was made an amir late in the reign of al-Muʾayyad or in the reign of his son. His days were not long; he died in 824 H and was buried in his master's turba in the desert [cemetery]."@en .

rec:AIND-D02501 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02501-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02501-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02501-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02501 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسام بن عبد الله حسام الدين الصفدي كان ممن يعتقد ببلده وله زاوية في حارة يعقوب منها ، مات في ربيع الاول سنة ست عشرة ذكره شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusām b. ʿAbd Allāh Ḥusām al-Dīn al-Ṣafadī was among those who were held in esteem in his hometown (Ṣafad), and he had a zawiya in the Yaʿqūb quarter there. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 816 H. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar al-ʿAsqalānī) mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02502 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02502-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02502-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02502-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02502 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسب الله بن سليمان بن راشد السالمي المكي ، مات بها سنة ثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasab Allāh b. Sulaymān b. Rāshid al-Sālimī al-Makkī died in Mecca in the year 830 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02503 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02503-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02503-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02503 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسب الله بن سنان بن راجح بن محمد بن عبد الله بن عمر بن مسعود العمري المكي القائد ، مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة سبع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasab Allāh b. Sinān b. Rājiḥ b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Masʿūd al-ʿUmarī al-Makkī, the qāʾid (commander). He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 847 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02504 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02504-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02504-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02504 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسب الله بن محمد بن بركوت السبكي العجلاني القائد من خواص السيد أبي القاسم ، مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة سبع وأربعين بجدة وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بها ، أرخهما ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasab Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Barkūt al-Subkī al-ʿAjlānī. The qāʾid (commander), one of the close retainers of al-Sayyid Abū al-Qāsim. He died in Jeddah in Jumādā al-Ākhira 847 and was transported to Mecca and buried there. Ibn Fahd recorded the death dates of both him and the preceding man."@en .

rec:AIND-D02505 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02505-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02505-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02505 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسب الله بن محمد بن حسب الله بن معقب الزيدي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasab Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasab Allāh b. Maʿqib al-Zaydī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02506 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02506-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02506-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02506 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسب الله النجار ، مات بمكة في رمضان سنة اثنتين وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasab Allāh al-Najjār died in Mecca in Ramaḍān in the year 872."@en .

rec:AIND-D02510 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02510-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02510-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02510 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن إبراهيم الخالدي . مضى فيمن جده حسين بن إبراهيم قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Ibrāhīm al-Khālidī. He is mentioned nearby among those whose grandfather was Ḥusayn b. Ibrāhīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D02511 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02511-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02511-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02511 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن إبراهيم الصفدي ثم الدمشقي الحنبلي الخياط . قرأ عليه العلاء المرداوي ووصفه بالامام المحدث المفسر الزاهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Ibrāhīm al-Ṣafadī, then al-Dimashqī, al-Ḥanbalī, the tailor. Al-ʿAlāʾ al-Mardāwī read under him and described him as the Imām, the ḥadīth scholar, the exegete, the ascetic."@en .

rec:AIND-D02512 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02512-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02512-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02512 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن إبراهيم السي من أهل حصن كيفا . قال شيخنا في معجمه انه جمع لها تاريخا وكتب إلي ببعضه سنة بضع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Ibrāhīm al-Sī, from the people of Ḥiṣn Kayfā. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his muʿjam that he compiled a history for it (Ḥiṣn Kayfā) and wrote some of it to him (Ibn Ḥajar) in the [8]20s."@en .

rec:AIND-D02515 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02515-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02515-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02515 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن أحمد بن حسن بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بدر الدين ابن الامام الشهاب الاذرعي والد محمد مامش ، وأمه جركسية فتاة لأبيه . حفظ القرآن وجوده على أبيه وبعض المنهاج وسمع ختم البخاري بالظاهرية ، ومات وقد تكهل سنة ثمانين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ḥasan b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Badr al-Dīn, son of al-Imām al-Shihāb al-Adhraʿī. Father of Muḥammad Māmish. His mother was a Circassian slave-girl belonging to his father. He memorized the Qurʾān and perfected its recitation under his father, and memorized part of al-Minhāj. He heard the completion of 『Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī』 at al-Ẓāhiriyya. He died around the year 880 H, having reached middle age."@en .

rec:AIND-D02519 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02519-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02519-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02519 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن أحمد بن علي بدر الدين الشيشيني . سمع علي شيخنا قلعة±±± من متبايناته بقراءة الفتحي ووصفه بالشيخ ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ḥasan b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī, Badr al-Dīn al-Shīshīnī. He heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) a portion (qiṭʿa) of his mutabāyināt, through the recitation of al-Fatḥī; and he (Ibn Ḥajar) described him (al-Shīshīnī) as \"the shaykh\"."@en .

rec:AIND-D02521 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02521-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02521-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02521-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02521 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله الدواخلي ثم القاهري الشافعي نزيل طيبة وأخو محمد الآتي وذاك أكبره ممن حفظ القرآن واشتغل وجاور بالحرمين مدة وسمع منى فيهما ثم تزوج فتاة يحيى بن فهد بعد موته وأقام بها في المدينة النبوية ، وصار بوابا بمدرسة السلطان هناك ولا بأس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ḥasan b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Dawākhilī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, was a resident of Ṭayba (Medina) and the brother of the Muḥammad who is to come, who was older than him. He memorized the Qur'an, engaged in scholarly pursuits, resided in the Ḥaramayn (Mecca and Medina) for a period, and heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) there. After the death of Yaḥyā b. Fahd, he married his fatāh (slave woman) and settled in al-Madīna al-Nabawiyya. He became the gatekeeper of the Sulṭān's madrasa there, and he was a decent person."@en .

rec:AIND-D02523 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02523-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02523-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02523-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02523 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن وفا أبو الجود بن الشهاب السكندري الاصل المصري المالكي أخو إبراهيم وعبد الرحمن محمد وأبي الفتح محمد ويحيى ، ويعرف كسلفه بابن وفا مات في حياة أبيه سنة ثمان وهو ابن تسع عشرة سنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ḥasan b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Wafā, Abū al-Jūd, son of al-Shihāb. Of Alexandrian origin, Egyptian (Miṣrī), Mālikī. He was the brother of Ibrāhīm, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad, Abū al-Fatḥ Muḥammad, and Yaḥyā. Like his forebears, he was known as Ibn Wafā. He died in [8]08 at the age of nineteen, during his father's lifetime."@en .

rec:AIND-D02525 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02525-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02525-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02525 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن أحمد البعلي الشافعي ويعرف بابن الفقيه . ولد في نصف شعبان سنة ست وخمسين وسبعمائة وسمع من أحمد بن عبد الكريم البعلي صحيح مسلم ومن يوسف بن الحبال السيرة لابن إسحاق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ḥasan b. Aḥmad al-Baʿlī, the Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Faqīh. He was born in mid-Shaʿbān in the year 756. He heard *Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim* from Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Baʿlī, and the *Sīra* of Ibn Isḥāq from Yūsuf b. al-Ḥabbāl."@en .

rec:AIND-D02526 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02526-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02526-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02526-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02526 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن أحمد النويري الطرابلسي الحنفي ، عرض عليه الصلاح الطرابلسي الشاطبية في ذي القعدة سنة سبع وأربعين وقال انه كان قاضي الحنفية ببلده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ḥasan b. Aḥmad al-Nuwayrī al-Ṭarābulusī al-Ḥanafī. Al-Ṣalāḥ al-Ṭarābulusī presented al-Shāṭibiyya to him in Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 847 H. It was stated that he was the qāḍī of the Ḥanafī school in his city."@en .

rec:AIND-D02527 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02527-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02527-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02527-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02527-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02527 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن اسماعيل البدر البنبي ثم القاهري الشافعي والد البدر محمد الآتي ، قرأ على السراج البلقيني بعض تصانيفه ووصفه بالفاضل العالم وأنه بحث وأجاد فيما يبديه وأجاز له وأرخ ذلك في صفر سنة أربع وسبعين وسبعمائة وصاهر البدر بن الامانة على أخته ، وكانت وفاته بعد سنة احدى فان مولد ولده فيها ولكنه لم يدركه ادراكا بينا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ḥasan b. Ismāʿīl, al-Badr, al-Banbī then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, father of al-Badr Muḥammad (mentioned below). He read some of al-Sirāj al-Bulqīnī's own works under him; al-Sirāj described him as a virtuous and learned scholar, stated that he investigated and excelled in what he presented, granted him an ijāza, and dated this in Ṣafar 774 H. He became the brother-in-law of al-Badr b. al-Amāna by marrying his sister. His death occurred after the year [8]01, since his son was born in that year and yet did not know him distinctly (he died while the son was an infant)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02528 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02528-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02528-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02528 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن الياس الرومي من أعيان التجار ذوي الوجاهات بحيث انتسب إليه جماعة من الخدام منهم لولو الحسني ومرجان الحسني ، ومات بالحبشة وهو والد الجمال محمد الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ḥasan b. Ilyās al-Rūmī was one of the prominent and esteemed merchants, to whom a group of servants, including Luʾluʾ al-Ḥasanī and Marjān al-Ḥasanī, were affiliated. He died in Abyssinia, and he is the father of al-Jamāl Muḥammad (mentioned later)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02529 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02529-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02529-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02529 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن أمير علي بن سنقر حسام الدين بن غرلو نسبة لجد له من جهة الأم . يأتي في آخر من اسمه حسن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ḥasan b. Amīr ʿAlī b. Sunqur Ḥusām al-Dīn b. Ghurlū. Ghurlū is a nisba referring to his maternal grandfather. His biography will appear at the end of the entries for those named al-Ḥasan."@en .

rec:AIND-D02533 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02533-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02533-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02533 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن جعفر مات بمكة في رمضان سنة اثنتين وثمانين ولعله ابن محمد بن جعفر يأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Jaʿfar. He died in Mecca in Ramadan of the year 882 H. He is perhaps identical with the (Ḥasan b.) Muḥammad b. Jaʿfar who is to come."@en .

rec:AIND-D02534 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02534-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02534-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02534 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن جودي المارديني له نظم على مجموع البدري أوله : %~% لله مجموع له قد تشهد المجامع %~% بأنه قطب لها نعم وفرد جامع %~% وخطه بديع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ḥasan b. Jūdī al-Māridīnī composed poetry on the book 『Majmūʿ al-Badrī』. Its opening lines are: 'To God belongs a collection of his — the collections themselves bear witness / that it is their pole; indeed, a uniquely comprehensive one.' His handwriting was also excellent."@en .

rec:AIND-D02535 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02535-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02535-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02535-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02535 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن حسن بن علي بن محمد بن جوشن . كذا كتبه ابن فهد وأرخه في رجب سنة أربع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Jawshan. Ibn Fahd wrote it thus and dated him in Rajab of the year [8]74."@en .

rec:AIND-D02539 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02539-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02539-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02539 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن حمزة بن يوسف بن الأمير الحلبي نزيل القاهرة ووالد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ḥasan b. Ḥamza b. Yūsuf b. al-Amīr al-Ḥalabī, resident of Cairo, and father of..."@en .

rec:AIND-D02542 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02542-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02542-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02542 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن خليل بن علي بن حسن بن يوسف بن خازم بمعجمتين ابن هاشم البدر الانصاري الخزرجي السعدي العبادي البقاعي الجديثي بفتح الجيم وكسر المهملة وآخره مثلثة الشافعي نزيل بيروت . ولد سنة تسعين وسبعمائة تقريبا . ومات في حدود سنة خمسين ظنا . قاله البقاعي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Hasan ibn Khalil ibn 'Ali ibn Hasan ibn Yusuf ibn Khazim ibn Hashim, al-Badr, al-Ansarī al-Khazrajī al-Saʿdī al-ʿUbādī al-Biqa'ī al-Jadīthī, Shafi'i, resident of Beirut. He was born around 790 AH, and died around 850 AH, according to al-Biqa'ī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02543 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02543-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02543-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02543 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن داود بن حسين الاطفيحي ثم الطنتدائي الغمري قاضيها ويعرف بفارس ياتي"@ar .

rec:AIND-D02544 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02544-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02544-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02544 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن ريس بن حسين السفطي . ممن سمع منى بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ḥasan ibn Rays ibn Ḥusayn al-Safaṭī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D02545 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02545-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02545-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02545 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن زبيري بن قيس بن ثابت بن نغير بن منصور البدر الحسيني أمير المدينة . وليها بعد أبيه الآتي في سنة ثمان وثمانين عن الشريف محمد بن بركات ، وهو مع صغره يوصف بعقل ، وقد رأيته بالمدينة سنة ثمان وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Zubayrī b. Qays b. Thābit b. Nughayr b. Manṣūr, al-Badr al-Ḥusaynī, the Emir of Medina. He assumed its governorship after his father (who is mentioned below) in the year 888 AH, under the authority of al-Sharīf Muḥammad b. Barakāt. Despite his youth, he was described as being intelligent. I (al-Sakhāwī) saw him in Medina in the year 898 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02546 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02546-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02546-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02546 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن زكريا من يوسف البلبيسي . ممن سمع منى أيضا بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ḥasan b. Zakarīyā min Yūsuf al-Bilbīsī. He was among those who heard (hadith) from me also in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D02548 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02548-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02548-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02548 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن سودون الفقيه . هو الذي قبله ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02550 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02550-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02550-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02550 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن طلحة اليماني الدلال ، كان حافظا للقرآن كثير التلاوة . مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة ست وستين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Ṭalḥa al-Yamānī al-Dallāl. He was a memorizer of the Qur'an and recited it frequently. He died in Mecca in Dhu al-Hijjah, the year 866 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02555 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02555-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02555-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02555 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن عبد الرحمن بن شجاع البدر بن الزين المقرىء قال إمام الأقصى كريم الدين عبد الكريم بن أبي الوفا أنه تلا عليه للسبع الفاتحة والبقرة ووصفه بالامام العالم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ḥasan b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Shujāʿ, al-Badr b. al-Zayn, al-Muqriʾ. The Imam of al-Aqṣā, Karīm al-Dīn ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Abī al-Wafā, said that he recited to him (al-Ḥasan) the Fātiḥa and al-Baqara according to the Seven Recitations, and described him as 'the learned Imam'."@en .

rec:AIND-D02558 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02558-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02558-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02558 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن عبد الولي الاسعردي الصالحي من كبار التجار بدمشق . مات في المحرم سنة إحدى ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ḥasan b. ʿAbd al-Walī al-Asʿardī al-Ṣāliḥī. One of the prominent merchants in Damascus. He died in the month of al-Muharram, in the year 801 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his historical work Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D02559 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02559-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02559-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02559 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الحسن بن السلطان عثمان بن العادل سليمان الأيوبي صاحب مدينة حصن كيفا . قتله ابن عمه سنة تسع وخمسين واستقر في المملكة عوضه"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Hasan b. al-Sultan 'Uthman b. al-'Adil Sulayman al-Ayyubi, the lord of the city of Hisn Kayfa. He was killed by his cousin in the year 859 AH, who then established himself in the kingdom in his stead."@en .

rec:AIND-D02567 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02567-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02567-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02567 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن أبي بكر بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن مفلح الدمشقي الحنبلي أخو عبد المنعم الآتي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Mufliḥ al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanbalī. Brother of ʿAbd al-Munʿim, who is mentioned below. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D02576 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02576-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02576-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02576 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن حسن البدر السفطي الازهري الشافعي اشتغل يسيرا واختص بالنجم بن حجي وسمع جماعة وكان يراجعني فيمن تأخر من أهل الروايات لأخذ خطوطهم على الاستدعاءات فصارت له بهم براعة وخبرة ، وهو ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Ḥasan al-Badr al-Safaṭī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī. He engaged in study for a short while, and was closely associated with al-Najm b. Ḥijjī. He heard from a group of scholars. He used to consult me (al-Sakhāwī) regarding later transmitters in order to obtain their handwritings on summonses (istidʿāʾāt), whereby he gained skill and expertise with them. He is among those who took from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D02577 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02577-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02577-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02577-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02577 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن حسن البدر المباشري ثم الشبراوي الملسي أحد شهودها . قدم القاهرة فسكن المنكوتمرية وقتا وقرأ علي وعلى غيري يسيرا وجلس مع الشهود ثم رجع"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Ḥasan, al-Badr, al-Mubāshirī, then al-Shabrāwī, al-Malsī. One of its witnesses (notaries). He came to Cairo and resided in al-Mankūtamurīya for a time, and read a little with me and with others. He sat with the witnesses, then returned."@en .

rec:AIND-D02578 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02578-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02578-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02578-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02578 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن خلف البدر السجيني الأزهري الشافعي خال الشهاب السجيني الفرضي الماضي ، كان يؤدب الأطفال ويقرأ الأجواق رياسة وربما وعظ وأكثر من النسخ بحيث كتب عدة مصاحف وربعات ووقف مما كتبه صحيح البخاري على أبي العباس الغمري . مات في ذي الحجة سنة ثمانين وقد قارب الستين رحمه الله"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Khalaf al-Badr al-Sajīnī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī. He was the maternal uncle of the aforementioned inheritance scholar al-Shihāb al-Sajīnī. He used to instruct children, led the recitation of choirs (al-ajwāq), and occasionally preached. He was prolific in copying manuscripts, writing several Mushafs (copies of the Quran) and Rab'as (part-sets of the Quran), and he endowed a copy of Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī that he had transcribed to Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Ghamrī. He died in Dhu al-Hijjah in the year 880 AH, having nearly reached the age of sixty, may Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02581 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02581-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02581-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02581 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن عامر الجدي . مات بساحل جدة في جمادى الأولى سنة سبع وخمسين وحمل لمكة فدفن بمعلاتها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. ʿĀmir al-Jaddī. He died on the coast of Jidda in Jumada al-Ula, year 857 AH, and was carried to Mecca, where he was buried in its al-Mu'alla cemetery."@en .

rec:AIND-D02582 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02582-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02582-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02582 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن عبد العزيز بن عبد الرحمن بن غفاه البدراني والد المحمدين الثلاثة الآتي ذكرهم . قرأ القرآن وأقرأه أولاده وكان خيرا صالحا . مات في سنة ثمان بمنية بدران رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ghufāh al-Badrānī, al-Badr. He was the father of the three Muhammads mentioned below. He recited the Qur'an and taught it to his children. He was a good and righteous man. He died in the year 808 AH in Minyat Badran, may Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02588 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02588-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02588-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02588 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن الاذرعي ثم الصالحي قاضي أذرعات والد الشهاب أحمد الإمام وعبد الله وأخو حسين المذكورين . سمع من شيخنا وكان بينهما مودة بل سمع شيخنا من نظمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Adhruʿī, later al-Ṣāliḥī. The judge (qāḍī) of Adhruʿāt. He is the father of al-Shihāb Aḥmad, the Imam, and ʿAbd Allāh, and the brother of the aforementioned Ḥusayn. He heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and there was mutual affection between them; indeed, our shaykh heard some of his poetry."@en .

rec:AIND-D02590 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02590-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02590-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02590 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن محمد بن علي البدر أبو عبد الله بن الصواف . مضى فيمن جد أبيه علي بن محمد بن أحمد تقريبا ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02595 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02595-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02595-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02595 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن محمد حسام الدين الابيوردي . مضى فيمن جده حسن ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02596 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02596-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02596-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02596-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02596 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن محمود الشيرازي المكي الشافعي . ولد في صفر سنة ثمان وسبعين ، ونشأ فاشتغل قليلا في النحو والصرف وغيرهما ولازمني في مجاورتي الرابعة والخامسة وسمع مني أشياء بل قرأ علي في المشكاة وغيرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Maḥmūd al-Shīrāzī al-Makkī al-Shāfiʿī. He was born in the month of Ṣafar in the year 878 AH. He grew up and studied grammar, morphology, and other subjects a little. He associated closely with me (al-Sakhāwī) during my fourth and fifth stays (mujāwaras) in Mecca, hearing various things from me, and indeed reciting to me al-Mishkāt and other works."@en .

rec:AIND-D02598 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02598-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02598-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02598 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي بن ناصر الحجازي أخو حسين الآتي وأبوهما ويعرف كأبيه بابن ناصر . ممن سمع مني بمكة وتجرأ كأبيه فكان يقرأ على العامة على بعض الكراسي بالمسجد"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Nāṣir al-Ḥijāzī, the brother of Ḥusayn and their father, both of whom are mentioned below. Like his father, he was known as Ibn Nāṣir. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca. Following his father's bold example, he used to read to the common people while seated on chairs in the mosque."@en .

rec:AIND-D02601 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02601-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02601-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02601 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي البدر البشكالسي القاهري المالكي . ممن أخذ عن شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī al-Badr al-Bishkālsī al-Qāhirī al-Mālikī. Among those who studied under our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02603 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02603-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02603-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02603 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي البدر المرجوشي والد محمد الآتي . كان شيخا تاجرا في الشرب ونحوه خيرا مقربا للصالحين وأهل الفضل ، أوردت عنه حكاية في ترجمة شيخنا وهو ممن سمع منه . مات عن أزيد من سبعين سنة بعد الخمسين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī al-Badr al-Marjūshī, the father of Muḥammad who is mentioned below. He was a merchant shaykh dealing in sharb (fine linen cloth) and the like, a good man who was close to the righteous and people of merit. I cited an anecdote about him in the biography of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and he was among those who heard from him. He died after the year 850 AH at the age of over seventy. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02604 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02604-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02604-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02604 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي الجمال الخطيب ابن قاضي القضاة بالحصن نور الدين الحصكفي الشافعي أخذ عنه بلديه أبو اللطف نزيل بيت المقدس المنطق والعروض والقوافي وغيرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan bin ʿAlī al-Jamāl al-Khaṭīb, son of the chief judge of the Fortress, Nūr al-Dīn al-Ḥiṣkafī al-Shāfiʿī. His compatriot, Abū al-Luṭf, who settled in Jerusalem, studied logic, prosody, rhyme, and other subjects under him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02606 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02606-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02606-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02606-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02606 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي الأمدي بفتحتين بدون مد قال شيخنا في أنبائه : كان من أهل الحسينية بزي الجند ثم توصل بصحبة بعض الأمراء حتى ولي مشيخة سرياقوس وترك لبس الجند ولبس الفقيري . مات في شعبان سنة خمس وقال غيره شيخ الشيوخ . كان خيرا دينا معتقدا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī al-Amadī. [Al-Amadī is pronounced] with two fatḥas and without lengthening. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Inbāʾ [al-Ghumr]: 'He was from the people of al-Ḥusayniyya and wore military garb. Then, through his association with some amirs, he managed to be appointed as the head of Siryāqūs, whereupon he abandoned military dress and wore the garb of a Sufi.' He died in Shaʿbān in the year 805. Others referred to him as 'Shaykh al-Shuyūkh'. He was good, pious, and devout."@en .

rec:AIND-D02607 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02607-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02607-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02607 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علي السنباطي الميقاتي ويعرف بالحاسب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlī al-Sunbāṭī al-Mīqātī, known as al-Ḥāsib (the calculator)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02609 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02609-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02609-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02609 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن عمر بن عمران . مات بمكة في شوال سنة سبع وثلاثين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿUmar b. ʿImrān. He died in Mecca in Shawwāl, the year 837 AH. His death was chronicled by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D02610 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02610-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02610-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02610 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن عمر بن محمد بن موسى بن عمران المكي الوكيل بأبواب الحكام . مات بمكة في شوال سنة سبع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. ʿImrān al-Makkī, the agent (wakīl) at the rulers' courts. He died in Mecca in Shawwāl of the year 837."@en .

rec:AIND-D02611 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02611-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02611-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02611 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن عمر بن محمد القلشاني أخو حسين وهما توءمان ومحمد الآتيين . ممن أخذ عن الأحمدين النخلي والصائغ والسلاوي وغيرهم وتميز في فنون ، وولي قضاء الجزيرة القبلية لتونس ثم باجة . وكان أخوه محمد مستورا به في قضاء الجماعة فلما مات انكشف . مات سنة ثلاث وسبعين عن تسع وثلاثين سنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Qalshānī, the brother of Ḥusayn (they were twins) and the forthcoming Muḥammad. He studied under the two Aḥmads (al-Nakhlī and al-Ṣāʾigh), al-Sallāwī, and others, distinguishing himself in various arts. He was appointed as the judge of al-Jazīra al-Qabliyya of Tunis, and then of Bāja. His brother Muḥammad was shielded by him in the office of chief judgeship (qāḍī al-jamāʿah), but when Ḥasan died, he was exposed. He died in the year 873 AH at the age of thirty-nine."@en .

rec:AIND-D02612 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02612-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02612-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02612 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن غازي . حدث بالخليل في سنة أربع وثمانمائة بالمسلسل في جماعة عن الميدومي . رواه لنا عنهم التقي أبو بكر القلقشندي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Ghāzī. He transmitted the musalsal (pattern-chained) hadith in Hebron to a group from al-Maydūmī in the year 804 AH. Al-Taqī Abū Bakr al-Qalqashandī transmitted it to us from them."@en .

rec:AIND-D02613 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02613-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02613-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02613 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن قاسم بن علي الناصري الأصل النابلسي المولد الغزي الدار هو وأبوه . سمع منى المسلسل بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Qāsim b. ʿAlī. Of al-Nāṣirī origin, born in Nablus, and a resident of Gaza, as was his father. He heard the Musalsal from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D02614 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02614-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02614-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02614 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن قراد العجلاني المكي القائد . مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة ثمان وأربعين ، أرخه ابن فهد"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Qurād al-ʿAjlānī al-Makkī, the commander (al-Qāʾid). He died in Mecca in Dhu al-Hijjah, the year 848, as recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D02615 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02615-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02615-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02615 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن قرا يلوك واسم قرا يلوك عثمان . قتل في المعركة سنة خمس وخمسين كما كتبته في الحوادث وهو عم جهانكير وحسن بن علي بن عثمان قرا يلوك"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Qarā Yuluk (the real name of Qarā Yuluk was ʿUthmān). He was killed in battle in the year 855 AH, as I have written in [my book of] historical events (al-Ḥawādith). He was the paternal uncle of Jahāngīr and of Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. ʿUthmān Qarā Yuluk."@en .

rec:AIND-D02616 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02616-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02616-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02616 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن محمد بن أحمد بن علي بن محمد بن محمد بن علي بن أحمد ابن البدر ابن شيخنا ابن حجر . مات في شعبان سنة اثنتين وأربعين وله دون السنة . أرخه جده شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad, the son of al-Badr (Muḥammad), the son of our shaykh Ibn Ḥajar. He died in Shaʿbān in the year 842 AH, being less than a year old. His grandfather, our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), recorded him in his chronicle (Inbāʾ al-Ghumr)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02622 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02622-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02622-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02622-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02622-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02622 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن محمد بن حسن القرشي الدخي المدني أخو عبد الحميد الحكيم الآتي . سمع علي الزين المراغي . ومات في صفر سنة خمس عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan al-Qurashī al-Dukhī al-Madanī. Brother of ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥakīm, who is mentioned below. He heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī. He died in Ṣafar, the year 815 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02624 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02624-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02624-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02624 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن محمد بن راشد السمى البنا . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة ثلاث وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Rāshid al-Sammī al-Bannāʾ. He died in Mecca in the month of al-Muḥarram, the year 863 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02626 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02626-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02626-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02626 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن محمد بن الزين عبد العزيز بن عبد الواحد بن عمر بن عياد الأنصاري المغربي الأصل المدني المالكي أخو حسين الآتي . ابن عم البدر حسن ابن عمر الماضي قريبا ويعرف كأخيه بابن كمال حفظ الرسالة وسمع على الجمال الكازروني في سنة أربع وثلاثين . ومات ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. al-Zayn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. ʿUmar b. ʿAyyād al-Anṣārī, of Maghribi origin, resident of Medina, Mālikī. He is the brother of Ḥusayn, who is mentioned below, and the cousin of al-Badr Ḥasan b. ʿUmar, mentioned shortly above. Like his brother, he is known as Ibn Kamāl. He memorized al-Risāla and heard hadith from al-Jamāl al-Kāzarūnī in the year 834 AH. He died..."@en .

rec:AIND-D02633 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02633-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02633-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02633 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن محمد بن علي النمراوي صهر بلديه البدر حسن بن علي بن حسن الماضي . قرأ القرآن وهدية الناصح وسمع مني بالقاهرة وربما حضر بعض الدروس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Nimrāwī. The brother-in-law (or son-in-law) of his compatriot al-Badr Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Ḥasan (aforementioned). He recited the Qurʾān and Hadiyyat al-Nāṣiḥ, heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo, and sometimes attended some of the lessons."@en .

rec:AIND-D02641 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02641-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02641-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02641 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن محمد بن يعقوب الطهطاوي المكي أخو علي الآتي . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة اثنتين وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb al-Ṭahṭāwī al-Makkī, the brother of ʿAlī who is mentioned below. He died in Mecca in the month of al-Muharram, the year 882 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02642 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02642-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02642-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02642 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن محمد بن يوسف بن نيطقس البدر بن الشمس بن الصلاح الحنفى . ولد في ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وعشرين وسبعمائة بالحسينية خارج القاهرة ونشأ بها فتفقه وتكسب بالشهادة دهرا ثم عين لقضاء الحنفية بصفد فوليه في سنة بضع وثمانين استمر فيها قاضيا حتى مات في سنة أربع عشرة ذكره المقريزي في عقوده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf b. Nayṭaqus, al-Badr b. al-Shams b. al-Ṣalāḥ, al-Ḥanafī. He was born in Dhu al-Hijjah 722 AH in al-Ḥusayniyya outside Cairo and grew up there. He studied jurisprudence and earned his living as a notary (shāhid) for a long time. Then he was designated for the Hanafi judgeship of Safad, which he assumed in the 780s AH. He continued as a judge there until he died in 814 AH. Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his work al-ʿUqūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D02643 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02643-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02643-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02643 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن محمد المكى ويعرف بابن صبرة . مات فيها في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Muḥammad al-Makkī, known as Ibn Ṣabra. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal, 872 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02644 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02644-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02644-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02644 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن محمد العيثاوي أحد مشاهير الطلبة . ذكر ابن حجى أنه كان أفضل أهل طبقته . مات في أول سنة إحدى وقد جاز الثلاثين . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Muḥammad al-ʿAythāwī, one of the famous students. Ibn Ḥijjī mentioned that he was the best of his generation. He died at the beginning of the year 801 AH, having just passed thirty years of age. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his work Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D02645 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02645-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02645-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02645 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن مختار والد جار الله الماضي . مات بمكة سنة سبع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Mukhtār, the father of the aforementioned Jār Allāh. He died in Mecca in the year 837 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02646 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02646-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02646-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02646 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن مخلوف آب المركان الراشدي المعتقد بالمغرب . مات سنة سبع وخمسين . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Makhlūf Āb al-Markān al-Rāshidī, the revered holy man in the Maghrib. He died in the year 857 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn ʿAzm."@en .

rec:AIND-D02647 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02647-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02647-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02647 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن منصور البدر الحنفي القاضي بل كان أيضا قد تولى الحسبة بدمشق . مات في عقوبة اللنك سنة ثلاث . قاله العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Manṣūr, al-Badr, the Hanafi judge (qāḍī). He had also assumed the office of market inspector (ḥisba) in Damascus. He died in the year 803 during the punishment/devastation of al-Lank (Timur). This was stated by al-ʿAynī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02649 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02649-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02649-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02649 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن نابت بن إسماعيل بن علي البدر الزمزمي المكي . حفظ البهجة والألفية وعرضهما على جماعة وتميز في الفرائض والحساب وأخذهما عن قريبه نور الدين وفي الميقات أخذه عن قريبه الجمال محمد بن أبي الفتح ودخل الشام وغيرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Nābit b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī al-Badr al-Zamzamī al-Makkī. He memorized al-Bahja and al-Alfiyya and presented them to a group of scholars. He excelled in inheritance law (al-farāʾiḍ) and arithmetic (al-ḥisāb), learning both of them from his relative Nūr al-Dīn. He studied timekeeping (al-mīqāt) with his relative al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. Abī al-Fatḥ. He also entered Syria (al-Shām) and other regions."@en .

rec:AIND-D02651 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02651-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02651-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02651 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن لاجين . ذكره المقريزي في عقوده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Lājīn. Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his biographical collection al-ʿUqūd [Durar al-ʿUqūd al-Farīda]."@en .

rec:AIND-D02652 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02652-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02652-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02652 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن يحيى البير الحجاري نسبة لبئر الحجار على نحو أربعة فراسخ من فاس لناحية المشرق ، كان عالما صالحا . مات في سنة اثنتين وسبعين . أفاده لي بعض أصحابنا المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Yaḥyā al-Bīr al-Ḥajjārī, so named after Bi'r al-Ḥajjār which is about four parasangs east of Fès. He was a righteous scholar. He died in the year 872 AH. Some of our Maghribi companions informed me of him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02653 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02653-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02653-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02653 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن يوسف بن أيوب البدر التركماني ويعرف بجده ، ولي نيابة القدس والرملة ونابلس والكرك غير مرة في أوقات مختلفة ، ورأيته غير مرة منها في القدس ، ومات في جمادى الآخرة سنة ثمانين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Yūsuf b. Ayyūb al-Badr al-Turkumānī, known by his grandfather. He was appointed as deputy (nāʾib) of Jerusalem, al-Ramla, Nablus, and al-Karak more than once at different times. I saw him more than once, including in Jerusalem. He died in Jumada al-Akhira, the year 880."@en .

rec:AIND-D02654 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02654-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02654-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02654-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02654 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن يوسف بن حسن بن صالح الأنصاري المروي نسبة إلى المرية من الأندلس المالكي واشتغل بالطب والهيئة ونحوهما من فقه ونحو عند أحمد القصار ، وقدم قريبا من سنة تسعين ، وحج من دمشق وجاور ثم رجع إلى القاهرة فاستمر حتى اجتمع بي في أثناء سنة ست وتسعين وسمع منى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Yūsuf b. Ḥasan b. Ṣāliḥ al-Anṣārī al-Marwī, named after Almería (al-Mariyya) in al-Andalus. He was a Maliki. He occupied himself with medicine, astronomy, and similar subjects, as well as jurisprudence and grammar, under Aḥmad al-Qaṣṣār. He arrived [in Cairo] around the year 890 AH, performed Hajj from Damascus, and stayed as a neighbor [in Mecca]. He then returned to Cairo and remained there until he met me during the year 896 AH and heard from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D02655 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02655-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02655-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02655 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن علاء الدولة بن أحمد بن أويس . يأتي له ذكر في أخيه الحسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. ʿAlāʾ al-Dawla b. Aḥmad b. Uways. He is mentioned in the entry of his brother al-Ḥusayn."@en .

rec:AIND-D02656 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02656-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02656-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02656 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن الحمامي بدر الدين . ولي قضاء الشافعية ببيت المقدس بعد المحيوي بن جبريل مع ذكره بأوفر نقص ، وقدم القاهرة ثم عاد في أواخر جمادى الثانية سنة تسعين على قضائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. al-Ḥamāmī, Badr al-Dīn. He held the office of Shāfiʿī judgeship in Jerusalem after al-Muḥyawī b. Jibrīl, though he was mentioned with much deficiency. He came to Cairo, then returned to Jerusalem at the end of Jumādā al-Thāniya in the year [8]90 to resume his judgeship."@en .

rec:AIND-D02657 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02657-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02657-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02657 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن الصعيدي ، شخص كان يتكلم في الحيرة ونواحيها عن الوزير والسلطان . مات في ذي القعدة سنة ثمان وثمانين ، ووجد له من النقد شيء كثير جدا مما لم تكن هيئته ومرتبته مناسبة له ولا لبعضه ، فاحتيط عليه للسلطنة غير ملتفتين لولد ولا غيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. al-Ṣaʿīdī. A person who used to speak on behalf of the vizier and the sultan in al-Buḥayra (corpus: \"al-Ḥīra\") and its environs. He died in Dhu al-Qaʿda, the year 888 AH. A very large amount of cash was found in his possession, which was completely disproportionate to his appearance and rank. Consequently, his wealth was confiscated for the sultanate, with no regard paid to his son or anyone else."@en .

rec:AIND-D02658 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02658-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02658-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02658 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن غرلو حسام الدين جارنا . مات في رمضان سنة ست وثمانين عن سبعين فأكثر وخلف طفلا وهو ابن أمير علي بن سنقر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Ghurlū, Ḥusām al-Dīn, our neighbor. He died in Ramaḍān in the year 886 AH, aged seventy or more, and left behind a young child. He was the son of Amīr ʿAlī b. Sunqur."@en .

rec:AIND-D02659 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02659-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02659-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02659-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02659 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن قلقيلة بدر الدين الحسيني سكنا الحنفي . أخذ عن البدر العيني واستقر به إمام مدرسته ، وكذا قرأ على الجمال عبد الله بن الرومي ، واستقر بعده في تدريس الحنفية بجامع الظاهر وأم بالبرقوقية نيابة وتكسب بالشهادة وصاهره الشمس بن خليل على ابنته وكانت بينهما قلاقل . مات قريب الستين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan b. Qalqīla, Badr al-Dīn, al-Ḥusaynī by residence, the Hanafi. He studied under al-Badr al-ʿAynī, who appointed him as the Imam of his madrasa. He also read under al-Jamāl ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Rūmī, and succeeded him in teaching Hanafi law at Jāmiʿ al-Ẓāhir. He served as a deputy Imam at al-Barqūqiyya, and earned his living as a notary witness. al-Shams b. Khalīl married his daughter, and there were disputes between them. He died around 860 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02660 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02660-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02660-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02660 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بدر الدين بن النح البغدادي الشافعي أحد الفضلاء . كتب عنه البدري في مجموعة قوله . %~% حريري له خد نضير %~% تسامى عن مراعاة النضير %~% %~% ونادمني بأقوال صحاح %~% فما أحلى مقامات الحريري %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan Badr al-Dīn ibn al-Naḥ al-Baghdādī al-Shāfiʿī, one of the virtuous men. al-Badrī transcribed his verses in his compilation, including: \"A silk-like (ḥarīrī) youth with a radiant cheek, elevated far above any compare. He entertained me with sound words; how sweet indeed are the assemblies (maqāmāt) of al-Ḥarīrī!\""@en .

rec:AIND-D02662 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02662-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02662-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02662-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02662-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02662 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن البدر الحسني القاهري الواعظ . شيخ اشتغل يسيرا وطاف القرى ونحوها في الوعظ ، ولازمني يسيرا بعد أن منعته من إيراد الأكاذيب ونحوها ، واستمر على طريقته حتى مات في جمادى الأولى سنة ست وتسعين وأظنه بلغ السبعين أو جازها رحمه الله وعفا عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Badr al-Ḥasanī al-Qāhirī, the preacher. He was a shaykh who studied a little and went around the villages and the like preaching. He associated with me (al-Sakhāwī) as a disciple for a short time after I forbade him from citing fabrications and the like. He continued on his way until he died in Jumādā al-Ūlā, the year 896 [AH]. I believe he had reached seventy years of age or exceeded it. May God have mercy on him and forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02663 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02663-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02663-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02663 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بدر الدين الشكلي الكركي . مات بالقاهرة في رابع عشري ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وأربعين ، وكان عارفا بالمباشرة مشكورا فيها . ولي نظر القدس والخليل مدة في أيام المؤيد وغيره . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه وزاد غيره أنه ولي غزة أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan Badr al-Dīn al-Shaklī al-Karakī. He died in Cairo on the 24th of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 842 AH. He was knowledgeable in administration (mubāshara) and praised for his service. He held the supervision (naẓar) of Jerusalem and Hebron for a period during the reign of al-Mu'ayyad (Shaykh) and others. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbā' (al-Ghumr), and others added that he was also appointed over Gaza."@en .

rec:AIND-D02664 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02664-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02664-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02664 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن بن بدر الدين الشريف أحد التجار باسكندرية . مات بها في ذي القعدة سنة أربع وخمسين وخلف أموالا كثيرة وكان تام الخبرة بدنياه متين التوسل في التوصل لمقاصده ، وقد رافع في الخواجا فخر الدين التوريزي حتى أخذ منه السلطان ما ينيف على مائة ألف دينار ، ولم يكن محمود السيرة عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Hasan b. Badr al-Din al-Sharif, one of the merchants in Alexandria. He died there in Dhu al-Qa'dah, the year 854, leaving behind a vast fortune. He was highly experienced in worldly affairs and extremely persistent in employing means to achieve his goals. He denounced Khawaja Fakhr al-Din al-Tawrizi to the Sultan, resulting in the Sultan confiscating over a hundred thousand dinars from him. His conduct was not praiseworthy, may God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02665 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02665-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02665-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02665 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن حسام الدين . مات بالقاهرة في ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وأربعين ، وكان قدم من القدس وولي في الأيام الناصرية فرج فيما بعدها عدة نيابات بغزة والقدس وغيرهما . قاله المقريزي وأظنه ناظر القدس وصاحب المدرسة به المذكور في ابن رسلان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan Ḥusām al-Dīn. He died in Cairo in Dhu al-Hijjah, the year 842. He had come from Jerusalem and had held several deputy governorships in Gaza, Jerusalem, and elsewhere during the reign of al-Nasir Faraj and afterwards. Al-Maqrizi mentioned this, and I believe him to be the superintendent (nāẓir) of Jerusalem and the founder of the madrasa there, who is mentioned in the biography of Ibn Ruslan."@en .

rec:AIND-D02666 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02666-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02666-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02666-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02666-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02666 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن الشرف الاصبهاني الشافعي . أخذ عن النور الايجي وعنه السيد العلاء بن السيد عفيف الدين . له ذكر في الحسن بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Sharaf al-Aṣbahānī al-Shāfiʿī. He studied under al-Nūr al-Ījī, and al-Sayyid al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Sayyid ʿAfīf al-Dīn studied under him. He is mentioned in the biography of al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02667 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02667-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02667-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02667 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن الاذرعي الشامي . مات بمكة في شعبان سنة اثنتين وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Adhraʿī al-Shāmī. He died in Mecca in the month of Shaʿbān, 862 AH (June 1458 CE)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02668 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02668-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02668-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02668 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن البدوي ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Badawī; among those who acquired knowledge from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D02669 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02669-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02669-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02669-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02669 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن الدمياطي نزيل الحسينية . مات في ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وثمانين بحبس الديلم وكان ممن يكثر المرافعة بحيث رافع في الشافعي بسبب خان السبيل ثم تغير عليه السلطان لعدم انتظام أمره وأودعه السجن حتى مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Dimyāṭī, a resident of al-Ḥusayniyya. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 882 AH in the prison of al-Daylam (Ḥabs al-Daylam). He was someone who frequently engaged in litigation, to the extent that he brought a complaint against al-Shāfiʿī over Khān al-Sabīl. Later, the Sultan became displeased with him due to the disorganization of his affairs and imprisoned him until he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D02670 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02670-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02670-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02670 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن الديروطي المقرىء . مات قريبا من سنة سبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Dayrūṭī, the Qurʾān reciter. He died close to the year 870 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02671 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02671-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02671-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02671 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن الرومي ويعرف بزغل . هكذا جرده ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Rūmī, known as Zaghal. Ibn Fahd recorded his name in this stripped-down manner."@en .

rec:AIND-D02672 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02672-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02672-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02672 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن السخاوي محتسب الغروليين من سوق الشرب . ممن اشتغل بالعلم قليلا وكان لا بأس به . مات في ربيع الثاني سنة ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Sakhāwī, the market inspector (muḥtasib) of al-Ghurūliyyīn in Sūq al-Shurb. He occupied himself with scholarly pursuits for a little while, and he was decent. He died in Rabīʿ al-Thānī, the year 893."@en .

rec:AIND-D02673 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02673-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02673-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02673 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن السقا نزيل طنبذي من الصعيد ويعرف بالعريان ويذكر بالجذب والكرامات التي منها بشارته للسلطان شفاها بالتملك بحيث بنى له لما ملك بعد موته زاوية بالمحل المذكور وكانت سنة ثلاث وسبعين عن بضع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Saqqā, a resident of Ṭanbadhī in Upper Egypt, known as al-ʿUryān. He was noted for his ecstatic state (jadhab) and miracles (karāmāt), among which was his oral prediction to the Sultan that the latter would attain sovereignty. Consequently, when the Sultan came to power, he built a zāwiya for him, after his death, in the aforementioned place. He died in the year 873 AH at the age of seventy-some."@en .

rec:AIND-D02674 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02674-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02674-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02674 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن السمرقندي الخواجا . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة ست وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Samarqandī al-Khawājā. He died in Mecca in Muharram, the year 856 (February 1452)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02676 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02676-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02676-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02676 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن الصبحي الجدي مات بها في المحرم سنة ثلاث وأربعين وحمل لمكة فدفن بمعلاتها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Ṣubḥī al-Jaddī. He died there in Muharram in the year 843 AH and was carried to Mecca, where he was buried in its al-Ma'la cemetery."@en .

rec:AIND-D02678 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02678-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02678-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02678 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن العجمي المدني صاهره شيخنا الشهاب الشوايطي على ابنته خديجة واستولدها أولاده وماتت سنة تسع وخمسين ، وما علمت متى مات أبوها صاحب الترجمة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-ʿAjamī al-Madanī. Our shaykh al-Shihāb al-Shawāyṭī became his son-in-law by marrying his daughter Khadīja, with whom he had children. She died in the year 859 AH (1455 CE), and I do not know when her father, the subject of this biography, died."@en .

rec:AIND-D02679 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02679-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02679-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02679-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02679 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن الغزي صهر أولاد حسن الخالدي . مات بمكة في رجب سنة اثنتين أو إحدى وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Ghazzī, the son-in-law of the children of Ḥasan al-Khālidī. He died in Mecca in Rajab, in the year 841 or 842 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02680 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02680-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02680-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02680 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن المغيلي نسبة لقرية مغيلة من أعمال فاس المالكي . كان عالما مدرسا . مات في سنة خمس وستين . ذكره لي بعض أصحابنا المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Mughīlī, named after the village of Mughīla in the district of Fez. He was a Maliki scholar and a teacher. He died in the year 865 AH. One of our Maghribi companions mentioned him to me."@en .

rec:AIND-D02681 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02681-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02681-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02681 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن النابلسي التاجر ويعرف بعصفورة . وجد ميتا في فراشه في جمادى الأولى سنة ستين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد . وكان قد سكنها واشترى بها دارا بقعيقعان وعمرها عمارة هائلة وهو طارح التكلف ممن كان يجله شاد جدة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Nābulusī, the merchant, known as ʿUṣfūra. He was found dead in his bed in Jumādā al-Ūlā, year 860 AH, in Mecca. His death was chronicled by Ibn Fahd. He had settled in Mecca, where he purchased a house in Quʿayqiʿān and rebuilt it magnificently. He was a man of simple and unpretentious manners, and was among those highly respected by the Shādd of Jidda."@en .

rec:AIND-D02682 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02682-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02682-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02682 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن الهندي آخر . تنزل برباط السيد حسن بن عجلان . مات بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة ثلاث وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Hindī, another. He resided in the Ribāṭ of al-Sayyid Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal, the year 873."@en .

rec:AIND-D02683 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02683-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02683-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02683 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسن الهيثمي رجل صالح من محلة أبي الهيثم . صحب أبا عبد الله الغمري وأقام معه بالمحلة ثم تحول بإشارته لمنية غمر منجمعا على التلاوة والذكر مع فضيلة وأحوال وكرامات ، مات وهو متوجه لحجة الاسلام قبيل الاربعين وقد قارب الخمسين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥasan al-Haythamī, a righteous man from the district of Maḥallat Abī al-Haytham. He accompanied Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ghamrī and stayed with him in al-Maḥalla, then moved to Minyat Ghamr upon his advice, dedicating himself to recitation and remembrance (dhikr) in seclusion, possessing virtue, spiritual states, and miracles. He died while heading for the pilgrimage of Islam shortly before the year 840 AH, being nearly fifty years old. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02685 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02685-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02685-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02685-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02685 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن أبي المكارم أحمد بن علي بن أبي راجح محمد بن إدريس بدر الدين العبدري الشيبي الحجبي المالكي الشافعي ، حفظ البهجة وعانى الاشتغال بالعربية والشعر وله نظم وذكاء وكتابة جيدة ودخل اليمن ومصر للاسترزاق فأدركه الأجل بالقاهرة في صفر سنة سبع وعشرين وله إحدى وعشرون سنة فيما بلغني . ذكره الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Abī al-Makārim Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Abī Rājiḥ Muḥammad b. Idrīs, Badr al-Dīn al-ʿAbdarī al-Shaybī al-Ḥajabī al-Mālikī al-Shāfiʿī. He memorized 『al-Bahja』 and applied himself to the study of Arabic and poetry; he possessed poetic talent, intelligence, and excellent handwriting. He entered Yemen and Egypt to seek a livelihood, but met his end in Cairo in Ṣafar, the year 827, at the age of twenty-one according to what reached me (al-Sakhāwī). Al-Fāsī mentioned him in [his history of] Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02688 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02688-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02688-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02688-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02688 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن أحمد بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن يحيى الأمير مفتي تونس . مات سنة تسع وثلاثين . ذكره ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. Yaḥyā al-Amīr, mufti of Tunis. He died in the year 839 AH. He was mentioned by Ibn ʿAzm."@en .

rec:AIND-D02690 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02690-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02690-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02690 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن أحمد مقدم العشير بالشام ويعرف بابن بشارة . مات في سابع الحجة سنة خمس وعشرين ويحرر أهو بالتصغير أو مكبر"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Aḥmad, the commander of the tribal auxiliaries (muqaddam al-ʿashīr) in Syria, known as Ibn Bishāra. He died on 7 Dhu al-Ḥijjah 825 AH. It remains to be verified whether his name is in the diminutive form (Bushayra) or the standard form."@en .

rec:AIND-D02691 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02691-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02691-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02691-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02691 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن أحمد السراوي العجمي التاجر . جاور بمكة مدة وأوصى بقرب كعمارة عين مكة . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة إحدى عشرة ودفن بالمعلاة وقد بلغ السبعين أو جازها ظنا . ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Aḥmad al-Sarāwī al-ʿAjamī, the merchant. He resided in Mecca as a neighbor (jāwara) for a period of time and left a bequest for the maintenance of the spring of Mecca (ʿAyn Makka). He died in Jumada al-Akhira, 811 AH, and was buried in al-Muʿallā. He was estimated to have reached or exceeded seventy years of age. Al-Fāsī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02695 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02695-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02695-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02695 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن جعفر المشعري المكي . مات بها في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Jaʿfar al-Mashʿarī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir, the year 842. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D02698 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02698-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02698-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02698-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02698-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02698 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن حسن بن علي بن أبي بكر البدر المنصوري ثم القاهري الشافعي العنبري والد كمال الدين محمد ، لازم العبادي كثيرا ، وكذا بن قرقماس وأسكنه معه في تربته بناحية باب البرقية وتميز في تعبير الرؤيا وسمع معنا الحديث على سارة ابنة ابن جماعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr al-Badr al-Manṣūrī, later al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, al-ʿAnbarī. He was the father of Kamāl al-Dīn Muḥammad. He closely accompanied al-ʿIbādī for a long time, and likewise Ibn Qurqumās, who accommodated him to reside with him in his tomb-mausoleum in the Bab al-Barqiyya area. He distinguished himself in the interpretation of dreams. He also heard Hadith alongside us (including al-Sakhawi) under Sara, the daughter of Ibn Jama'ah."@en .

rec:AIND-D02704 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02704-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02704-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02704 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن عبد الله نجم الدين السامري الأصل كاتب السر بدمشق وقد جمع بينها وبين نظر الجيش بعناية صهره زوج ابنة امرأته ازبك الدوادار ، وكان عريا عن العلوم جملة مع انه كان باسمه التدريس بدار الحديث الأشرفية . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة إحدى وثلاثين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿAbd Allāh Najm al-Dīn, of Samaritan (al-Sāmirī) origin. He served as the Chief Secretary (Kātib al-Sirr) of Damascus. He combined this office with the military administration oversight (Naẓar al-Jaysh) through the patronage of his relative by marriage (the husband of his wife's daughter), Azbak al-Dawādār. He was completely devoid of scholarly knowledge, yet the professorship (tadrīs) at the Ashrafiyya Dār al-Ḥadīth was held in his name. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira, in the year 831 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02705 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02705-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02705-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02705-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02705 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن عبد المؤمن بن المظفر الجمال بن الصدر بن العز الشيرازي . لقيه الطاووسي في سنة سبع وعشرين وثمانمائة بشيراز فاستجازه لدخوله في عموم إجازة المزي وابنة الكمال ومات في غرة ربيع الأول سنة ثلاث وثلاثين عن مائة وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn bin ʿAbd al-Muʾmin bin al-Muẓaffar al-Jamāl bin al-Ṣadr bin al-ʿIzz al-Shīrāzī. Al-Ṭāwūsī met him in the year 827 AH in Shiraz and requested his ijāza, as he was included in the general ijāza of al-Mizzī and Ibnat al-Kamāl. He died on the first of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 833 AH at the age of one hundred and sixty."@en .

rec:AIND-D02706 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02706-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02706-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02706-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02706-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D02706-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02706 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن عثمان بن سليمان بن رسول بن أمير يوسف بن خليل بن نوح البدر بن الشرف الكرادي الأصل القرمي القاهري الحنفي أخو المحب محمد ويعرف بابن الاشقر . مات في صفر سنة سبع وأربعين ولم يكمل الستين وتأسف عليه أخوه كثيرا وكان قائما بأموره كلها حتى استنابه في نظر البيمارستان حين ولايته لها رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿUthmān b. Sulaymān b. Rasūl b. Amīr Yūsuf b. Khalīl b. Nūḥ, al-Badr (b. al-Sharaf), of Karādī origin (the Karād, a Turkmen tribe), of Crimea and then Cairo, the Ḥanafī. He was the brother of al-Muḥibb Muḥammad and was known as Ibn al-Ashqar. He died in Safar 847 H, not having completed his sixtieth year. His brother grieved deeply for him. Ḥusayn used to manage all of his brother's affairs, to the extent that his brother appointed him as his deputy in the administration of the Bimaristan when the latter was appointed as its supervisor. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02707 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02707-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02707-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02707-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02707 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن عثمان الجمال الجبلجيلوي . ولد في غرة ربيع الأول سنة ثمان عشرة وسبعمائة ، ولقيه الطاووسي بشيراز سنة سبع وعشرين فاستجازه لدخوله في عموم إجازة جماعة من المتقدمين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿUthmān al-Jamāl al-Jabaljīlūy. Born on the first of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 718 AH. Al-Ṭāwūsī met him in Shiraz in the year 827 AH and requested his ijāza to be included in the general ijāza of a group of predecessors."@en .

rec:AIND-D02708 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02708-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02708-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02708 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين الأكبر بن عطية بن محمد بن محمد بن أبي الخير محمد بن فهد الهاشمي المكي أخو حسن . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة تسع وأربعين بمكة ولم يكمل شهرا . أرخه ابن عمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn al-Akbar, the son of ʿAṭiyya, the son of Muḥammad, the son of Muḥammad, the son of Abī al-Khayr Muḥammad, the son of Fahd, al-Hāshimī al-Makkī. He was the brother of Ḥasan. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 849 AH in Mecca, not having completed a month of age. His cousin chronicled his date of death."@en .

rec:AIND-D02709 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02709-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02709-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02709 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين الأصغر بن عطية شقيق الذي قبله . ولد في شعبان سنة خمسين وثمانمائة بمكة ، وأجاز له جماعة ، وقطن المدينة وقتا وكذا القاهرة أوقاتا على وجه فاقة والشام وزار بيت المقدس وغيرها وانقطع عنا خبره قريب التسعين ويقال إنه مأسور بأيدي الفرنج خلصه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn al-Aṣghar, the younger son of ʿAṭiyya, and the brother of the person in the preceding entry. He was born in Shaʿbān in the year 850 AH in Mecca. A group of scholars granted him ijāza. He resided for a time in Medina, and in Cairo at times due to poverty, and he also visited Syria and Jerusalem, among other places. News of him was cut off from us around the year 890 AH, and it is said that he was captured by the Franks. May God release him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02710 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02710-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02710-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02710 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علاء الدولة ، سيأتي فيمن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02714 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02714-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02714-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02714 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علي بن حسين الشامي ويعرف بابن مكسب . ممن سمع منى بمكة وكان من خيار التجار استدان منه السيد نور الدين بن الصفي الايجي في آخر قدماته لمكة مبلغا . ومات فسافر لأجل استيفائه من تركته هناك فكانت منيته بعد أن قبضه به في سنة ست وتسعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn al-Shāmī, known as Ibn Maksab. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca, and was an excellent merchant. Sayyid Nūr al-Dīn b. al-Ṣafī al-Ījī borrowed a sum of money from him during his last visits to Mecca. When Nūr al-Dīn died, Ḥusayn traveled there to collect the debt from his estate. He passed away there after successfully recovering the money in the year 896 AH. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02715 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02715-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02715-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02715 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علي بن خالد الفقيه بدر الدين العقيبي ويعرف قديما بابن الجاموس . ممن سمع على التنوخي ثم الجمال الحنبلي واستجازه الزين رضوان لولده وأشار لموته من غير تبيين وكأنه بعد الثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Khālid, the jurist, Badr al-Dīn al-ʿUqaybī, formerly known as Ibn al-Jāmūs. He heard from al-Tanūkhī and then from al-Jamāl al-Ḥanbalī. Al-Zayn Riḍwān requested an ijāza from him for his son. His death was indicated without specification, but it seems to have been after 830 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02716 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02716-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02716-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02716 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علي بن خراج اليمني . مات سنة أربع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Kharrāj al-Yamanī. He died in the year 824 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02719 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02719-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02719-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02719 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علي بن سرور بن خطيب حديثة . مات سنة ثلاث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Surūr b. Khaṭīb Ḥadītha. He died in the year 803 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02721 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02721-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02721-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02721 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علي بن عبد الله الشرف الفارقي ثم الزبيدي أحد أعيان تجار اليمن . مضى فيمن جده أبو بكر بن سعادة ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D02722 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02722-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02722-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02722 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علي بن عبد الله المارديني التاجر نزيل حلب ويعرف بابن تميرة ، ممن سمع منى بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Māridīnī. A merchant who resided in Aleppo and was known as Ibn Tamīra. He heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02726 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02726-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02726-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02726 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علي بن محمد المنوفي ثم القاهري نزيل الجيعانية ممن أخذ عني وأخبرني أنه رأى البخاري في المنام على هيئتي فالله أعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Munūfī, then al-Qāhirī, a resident of al-Jīʿāniyya. He was among those who took (knowledge) from me, and he informed me that he saw al-Bukhārī in a dream in my likeness. And God knows best."@en .

rec:AIND-D02727 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02727-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02727-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02727 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علي بن ناصر بن أحمد البلبيسي الأصل الحجازي أخو حسن الماضي ويعرف أبوهما بابن ناصر ممن سمع منى بمكة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Nāṣir b. Aḥmad, of Bilbaysī origin and Ḥijāzī residence. He is the brother of the aforementioned Ḥasan, and their father is known as Ibn Nāṣir. He is among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02729 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02729-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02729-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02729 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علي الشرف الفارقي . مضى فيمن جده أبو بكر بن سعادة"@ar .

rec:AIND-D02730 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02730-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02730-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02730 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن علي المكي ويعرف بالسقيف . ممن سمع منى بمكة والمدينة وجال البلاد . ومات بالقاهرة في الطاعون سنة سبع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī al-Makkī, known as al-Saqīf. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca and Medina, and traveled about the lands. He died in Cairo of the plague in the year 897 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02732 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02732-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02732-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02732 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن عمر كور الهندي الأصل المكي البناء أبو عمر البناء . مات بمكة في ربيع الآخر سنة ستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. ʿUmar Kūr, of Indian origin, a mason of Mecca. His kunya was Abū ʿUmar, [called] al-Bannāʾ (the builder). He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir, 860 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02733 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02733-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02733-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02733 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن أبي فارس عبد العزيز الحفصي الإمام العلامة المفتي الأمير ابن أمير المسلمين . أراد الثورة على ولد أخيه لما استقر في المملكة بعد أبيه فظفر به فقتله وقتل أخوين له وعظمت المصيبة بقتل الحسين وذلك في سنة تسع وثلاثين ، وكان فاضلا مناظرا ذكيا ذكره لي صاحبنا الزين عبد الرحمن البرشكي . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Abī Fāris ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Ḥafṣī, the imam, the eminent scholar, the mufti, the amir, son of the Commander of the Muslims [the Ḥafṣid ruler]. He sought to rise against his brother's son when the latter was established in the kingdom after his [Ḥusayn's] father; the nephew seized him, killed him, and killed two of his brothers as well. The calamity of Ḥusayn's killing was immense; that was in the year 839 AH. He was accomplished, a skilled disputant, and intelligent. 'Our companion al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Barashkī mentioned him to me' — thus our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his Inbāʾ [al-Ghumr]."@en .

rec:AIND-D02734 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02734-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02734-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02734 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن كبك حسام الدين التركماني . قتل في جمادى الأولى سنة إحدى وعشرين بأرزنجان بعد أن حاصر ملطية ، وسر السلطان بقتله . ذكره شيخنا في الحوادث . قال غيره وكان بطلا شجاعا أمير التركمان الكبكية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Kabak, Ḥusām al-Dīn al-Turkumānī. He was killed in Jumādā al-Ūlā, in the year 821 AH, in Erzincan after besieging Malatya, and the Sultan was pleased with his death. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in the events section (al-ḥawādith). Others said he was a brave hero, the Emir of the Kabakiyya Turkmen."@en .

rec:AIND-D02737 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02737-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02737-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02737-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87_apply2,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02737 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن محمد بن إسماعيل الهندي ثم المكي . سمع على العز بن جماعة قلعة من مناسكه الكبرى وقدم القاهرة أخيرا في الدولة المؤيدية أجاز لأولادي قاله شيخنا وما رأيته عند غيره ، وقد تقدم حسين بن أحمد بن محمد بن ناصر الهندي ثم المكي وأظنه هو فيحرر"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl al-Hindī, then al-Makkī. He heard from al-ʿIzz b. Jamāʿa a portion (reading qalʿa as qiṭʿa) of his greater Manāsik, and came to Cairo at the end of the Muʾayyadī reign. 'He granted an ijāza to my children' — so said our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and I have not seen him [mentioned] by anyone else. Ḥusayn b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Nāṣir al-Hindī then al-Makkī has already appeared, and I think he is the same person; to be verified."@en .

rec:AIND-D02742 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02742-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02742-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02742 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن أبي حامد محمد بن أبي الخير بن أبي السعود بن ظهيرة المكي المالكي . ولد في رمضان سنة أربع وستين وثمانمائة . ممن سمع مني بمكة ولازم دروس أحمد بن حاتم المغربي وكذا حضر قليلا عند غيره ، ورأيته يكتب في شرح الارشاد للجوجري وزار المدينة غير مرة وكان في قافلتنا سنة ثمان وتسعين ذهابا وايابا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Abī Ḥāmid Muḥammad b. Abī al-Khayr b. Abī al-Suʿūd b. Ẓahīra al-Makkī al-Mālikī. He was born in Ramaḍān 864 AH. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca and assiduously attended the lessons of Aḥmad b. Ḥātim al-Maghribī, besides attending a little under others. I saw him writing out al-Jawjarī's commentary on al-Irshād. He visited Medina more than once, and was in our caravan in the year 898 AH, both going and returning."@en .

rec:AIND-D02743 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02743-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02743-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02743 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن محمد بن صبرة . ممن سمع منى بمكة في سنة أربع وتسعين وقد مضى أبوه حسن بن محمد بن صبرة وليس اسم ابنه حسينا ولكنه اشتهر بالحسيني واسمه محمد وحينئذ فهو محمد بن حسن بن محمد بن صبرة فيلحق في المحمدين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "[Entered as] Ḥusayn b. Muḥammad b. Ṣabra. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca in 894 AH. His father Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. Ṣabra has already been given. But his (Ḥasan's) son's name is not Ḥusayn — he was merely known as 'al-Ḥusaynī', his name being Muḥammad. He is therefore Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. Ṣabra and should be inserted among the Muḥammads."@en .

rec:AIND-D02744 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02744-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02744-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02744-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02744-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02744 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن الكمال محمد بن عبد العزيز بن عبد الواحد بن عمر بن عياد الانصارى المغربى الاصل المدنى المالكى الماضى ابن عمه حسن بن عمر بن عبد العزيز والآتى أبوه وهو سبط النور المحلى وعليه سمع بل قرأ عليه الموطأ ، وكان خيرا مديما للعبادة . مات في صفر سنة سبع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. al-Kamāl Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. ʿUmar b. ʿAyyāḍ al-Anṣārī, of Maghribī origin, a resident of Medina, and a Mālikī. He was the cousin of the previously mentioned Ḥasan b. ʿUmar, and the son of al-Kamāl Muḥammad, whose biography will follow. He was the maternal grandson of al-Nūr al-Maḥallī, under whom he heard and indeed read al-Muwaṭṭaʾ. He was virtuous and constant in worship. He died in the month of Safar, in the year 867 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02745 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02745-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02745-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02745 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن محمد بن على بن عقبة المكى البناء هكذا جرده ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿUqba al-Makkī al-Bannāʾ. Thus was he listed strictly by his lineage by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D02746 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02746-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02746-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02746-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02746 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن محمد بن الشيخ لاجين البدر بن الشمس العقبى الصحراوى . ولد بتربة جمال الدين من الصحراء وأجاز له جماعة منهم عائشة ابنة ابن عبد الهادى وابنة الزين رضوان فيمن يؤخذ عنه ، أجاز لنا وهو حي في سنة أربع وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Muḥammad b. al-Shaykh Lājīn, al-Badr b. al-Shams al-ʿUqabī al-Ṣaḥrāwī. He was born in the Turbah of Jamāl al-Dīn in the Desert (al-Ṣaḥrāʾ). A group of scholars granted him ijāza (scholarly license), including ʿĀʾisha bint Ibn ʿAbd al-Hādī and the daughter of al-Zayn Riḍwān. He granted us (al-Sakhāwī) an ijāza, and he was still alive in the year 884 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02747 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02747-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02747-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02747 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن محمد بن محمد بن على أبو النور بن أبي الخير بن الجمال الفاكهى المكى الآتى أبوه أسمعه أبوه على بمكة بقراءته وقراءة غيره ومن ذلك بعض ترجمة النووى"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, Abū al-Nūr b. Abī al-Khayr b. al-Jamāl al-Fākihī al-Makkī. His father, whose biography is mentioned below, made him hear in Mecca, through his own recitation and the recitation of others, including a portion of the biography of al-Nawawī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02749 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02749-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02749-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02749 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن محمد بن نافع البدر الخزاعي المكي . دخل بلاد العجم والهند وتحت الريح وحصل بعض دنيا كان ينتسب فيها ، ومات عن بعضها وذلك بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة خمس وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Husayn b. Muhammad b. Nafi' al-Badr al-Khuza'i al-Makki. He entered the lands of the non-Arabs (Persia), India, and Southeast Asia (Taḥta al-Rīḥ), and acquired some worldly wealth. He died in Mecca in Rabi' al-Awwal in the year 885, leaving behind some of that wealth."@en .

rec:AIND-D02751 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02751-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02751-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02751 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن محمود الشريف الدلي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Maḥmūd al-Sharīf al-Dullī. He was among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D02752 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02752-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02752-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02752 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن نابت بن إسماعيل بن علي بن محمد بن داود الزمزمي المكي الماضي جده والآتي أبوه . مات في صفر سنة اثنتين وثمانين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Nābit b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Dāwūd al-Zamzamī al-Makkī. His grandfather is mentioned previously, and his father is forthcoming. He died in Ṣafar, the year 882 AH, in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02753 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02753-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02753-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02753 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن نعير بن حيار أمير العرب . مات سنة ثمان عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Nuʿayr b. Ḥayyār, Emir of the Arabs. He died in the year 818 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02754 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02754-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02754-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02754 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن يحيى بن أحمد بن إسماعيل بن علي بن داود بن يوسف ابن عمر بن علي بن رسول المؤيد بن الظاهر بن الناصر بن الأشرف بن الأفضل ابن المجاهد بن المؤيد بن المظفر بن المنصور الغساني ملوك اليمن . مات بمكة في جمادى الأولى سنة سبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Yaḥyā b. Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī b. Dāwūd b. Yūsuf b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Rasūl al-Muʾayyad b. al-Ẓāhir b. al-Nāṣir b. al-Ashraf b. al-Afḍal b. al-Mujāhid b. al-Muʾayyad b. al-Muẓaffar b. al-Manṣūr al-Ghassānī, of the Rasulid kings of Yemen. He died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ūlā, in the year 870. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D02755 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02755-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02755-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02755 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن يوسف بن أحمد الشغدي الصفدي الشافعي . سمع على شيخنا في سنة خمس وثلاثين الخصال المكفرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Yūsuf b. Aḥmad al-Shaghdī al-Ṣafadī al-Shāfiʿī. He heard al-Khiṣāl al-mukaffira under our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in the year 835 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02758 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02758-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02758-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02758 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن يوسف الدمشقي ويعرف بقاضي الجزيرة . مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة سبع وخمسين ودفن بالمعلاة . أرخه ابن فهد"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. Yūsuf al-Dimashqī, known as the Qāḍī of al-Jazīra. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 857 AH and was buried in al-Muʿallā. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D02760 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02760-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02760-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02760 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين بن ... بن جعفر . مات في العشر الأخير من ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وأربعين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد وبيض لأبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn b. [...] b. Jaʿfar. He died during the last ten days of Rabīʿ al-Ākhir in the year 842 AH in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded his death and left a blank space for his father's name."@en .

rec:AIND-D02761 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02761-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02761-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02761 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين البدر المغربي . ممن قرأ عليه في النحو في المحلة المحب بن الامام ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn al-Badr al-Maghribī. Among those who studied grammar under him in al-Maḥalla was al-Muḥibb b. al-Imām."@en .

rec:AIND-D02762 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02762-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02762-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02762 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين الاعزاري البسطامي والد أحمد الماضي صحب ابن الأطعاني . ومات بمكة في سنة خمس وعشرين ودفن بالمعلاة جوار الشيخ عمر العرابي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn al-Aʿzārī al-Bisṭāmī, the father of the aforementioned Aḥmad. He accompanied Ibn al-Aṭʿānī. He died in Mecca in the year 825 and was buried in al-Muʿallā cemetery next to Shaykh ʿUmar al-ʿUrābī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02763 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02763-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02763-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02763 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين شيخ سروعة وابن شيخها . مات في توجهه للسيد صاحب الحجاز بين بدر والينبع فحمل إلى بدر فدفن بها في سنة ست وثمانين ، وكان معظما في الشرق والغرب عفا الله عنه وهو ابن علي بن محمد بن غضنفر من الاشراف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn, the shaykh of Sarūʿa and the son of its shaykh. He died on his way to the Sayyid, the ruler of the Hijaz, between Badr and al-Yanbuʿ. He was then carried to Badr and buried there in the year 886 AH. He was highly revered in the East and the West, may God forgive him. He was the son of ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Ghaḍanfar, from the Ashrāf (noble descendants of the Prophet)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02764 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02764-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02764-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02764-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02764 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين الكازروني الشافعي . هو ابن ارتحل لشيخنا قصدا فأخذ عنه ، ومات في طاعون سنة تسع وأربعين ورأيت نسخة من ابن الصلاح بلغ شيخنا للشيخ بدر الدين حسين بالقراءة في عدة أماكن من أوله وكأنه هذا"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn al-Kāzarūnī al-Shāfiʿī. He traveled intentionally to our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and studied under him. He died in the plague of the year 849 AH. I saw a copy of [the Muqaddimah of] Ibn al-Ṣalāḥ containing a collation note (balāgh) by our shaykh for Sheikh Badr al-Dīn Ḥusayn, indicating that he read it to him in several places from its beginning, and it seems to be this person."@en .

rec:AIND-D02765 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02765-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02765-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02765 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين المصري أحد من يعتقد بين المصريين . مات في ربيع الأول سنة خمسين ودفن بالقرافة جوار القبر المنسوب لعقبة بن عامر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Husayn al-Misri, one of those who is revered among the Egyptians. He died in Rabi' al-Awwal in the year 850 AH and was buried in al-Qarafa near the grave attributed to 'Uqba b. 'Amir."@en .

rec:AIND-D02766 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02766-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02766-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02766-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02766 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حسين المكل . ممن أخذ عن ابن الجزري وصنف في القراءات والنحو والصرف ومات بعيد الخمسين ، قاله لي بعض الآخذين عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥusayn al-Mukill. He studied under Ibn al-Jazarī and composed works on al-Qirāʾāt (Qur'anic recitations), al-Naḥw (grammar), and al-Ṣarf (morphology). He died shortly after 850 AH, as was told to me by some of those who studied under him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02767 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02767-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02767-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02767-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02767 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حطط بمهملات وفتح أوله وثانيه اسم جركسي البكلمشي بكلمش العلائي . تقدم بعد أستاذه عند الناصر فرج إلى أن صار أحد العشرات بالديار المصرية حتى مات سنة إحدى وأربعين وهو في حدود السبعين وكان لا بأس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥuṭuṭ (written with unpointed letters, with fatha on its first and second) is a Circassian name; he is al-Baklamishī, the mamluk of Baklamish al-ʿAlāʾī. He advanced after his master under Sultan al-Nāṣir Faraj, until he became one of the Amirs of Ten in Egypt, where he died in the year 841 H at around seventy years of age. He was a decent man."@en .

rec:AIND-D02771 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02771-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02771-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02771 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن الصاحب سعد الدين إبراهيم بن بركة البشيري الماضي أبوه . مات في ذي القعدة سنة أربع وسبعين وهو مختف وكان قد ولي نظر الاهراء والمواريث والدولة في أوقات مختلفة وصاهر ابن النقاش ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza, son of al-Ṣāḥib Saʿd al-Dīn Ibrāhīm, son of Baraka, al-Bashīrī. His father's biography has been mentioned previously. He died in Dhu al-Qaʿda 874 while in hiding. At various times, he had held the offices of controller of granaries (naẓar al-ahrāʾ), controller of inheritances (nāẓir al-mawārīth), and controller of state affairs (naẓar al-dawla), and he contracted a marriage alliance with Ibn al-Naqqāsh."@en .

rec:AIND-D02773 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02773-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02773-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02773-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02773-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02773 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن أبي بكر بن أحمد بن محمد بن عمر سري الدين بن التقي الأسدي الدمشقي الشافعي الآتي أبوه وأخوه ويعرف كسلفه بابن قاضي شهبة وأخذ عن أبيه وغيره ، ودرس بالمسرورية والمجاهدية وغيرهما . مات في رمضان سنة ستين ، ودفن بمقبرة الباب الصغير عند سلفه رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza b. Abī Bakr b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar Sarī al-Dīn b. al-Taqī al-Asadī al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī. His father and brother are mentioned below. Like his ancestors, he was known as Ibn Qāḍī Shuhba. He studied under his father and others, and taught at al-Masrūriyya and al-Mujāhidiyya Madrasas, among others. He died in Ramaḍān in the year 860 AH and was buried in al-Bāb al-Ṣaghīr cemetery next to his ancestors."@en .

rec:AIND-D02774 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02774-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02774-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02774-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02774 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن جار الله بن حمزة بن راجح بن أبي نمى الحسني المكي . كان رأس أشراف آل أبي نمى بعد أبيه لعقله وسماحته . مات في المحرم سنة ست عشرة بمكة ، ودفن بالمعلاة وهو في عشر الخمسين فيما أحسب . قاله الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza ibn Jār Allāh ibn Ḥamza ibn Rājiḥ ibn Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He was the head of the sharifs of the Abū Numayy clan after his father, known for his intellect and generosity. He died in Muharram in the year 816 AH in Mecca, and was buried in al-Muʿallā. He was in his late forties, in my estimation. This was stated by al-Fāsī in his book on Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02775 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02775-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02775-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02775 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن زائد بن جولة . شيخ أولاد أبي الليل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza b. Zāʾid b. Jawla, the chief (shaykh) of the Awlād Abī al-Layl tribe."@en .

rec:AIND-D02776 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02776-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02776-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02776 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن سلقسيس نائب حماة . له ذكر في أزدمر الازبكي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza b. Salqasīs, the deputy (nāʾib) of Hama. He is mentioned in the entry of Azdamur al-Azbakī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02779 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02779-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02779-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02779 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن عبد الرزاق بن البقري أخو يحيى وابن عم الشرف والمجد باشر الاسطبل وغيره . ومات في ذي القعدة سنة تسعين ، ويقال انه أسنهم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. al-Baqarī. Brother of Yaḥyā and cousin of al-Sharaf and al-Majd. He managed the stable and other administrations. He died in Dhu al-Qaʿda, the year 890 AH, and it is said that he was the oldest of them."@en .

rec:AIND-D02780 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02780-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02780-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02780 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن عبد الغني بن يعقوب الشرف بن الفخر بن الشرف أحد كتاب المماليك ويعرف بابن فخيرة مصغر لقب أبيه ، وهو والد عبد الرزاق الآتي"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Yaʿqūb, one of the scribes of the Mamluks (kātib al-mamālīk). He was known as Ibn Fukhayra, which is the diminutive of his father's title (al-Fakhr). He is the father of the below-mentioned ʿAbd al-Razzāq."@en .

rec:AIND-D02781 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02781-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02781-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02781 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن عثمان قرا يلوك بن طر على قطلوبك صاحب آمد ماردين وغيرها من ديار بكر . مات في أوائل رجب سنة ثمان وأربعين ولم يكن محمود السيرة كأبيه واخوته واستقر بعده ابن أخيه جهان كير بن علي بك بن عثمان الآتي"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza ibn ʿUthmān Qarā Yulūk ibn Ṭur ʿAlī Qaṭlūbak, the ruler of Āmid, Māridīn, and other parts of Diyār Bakr. He died in the beginning of Rajab in the year 848 AH. He was not of praised conduct like his father and brothers. He was succeeded by his nephew Jahāngīr ibn ʿAlī Bik ibn ʿUthmān, who is mentioned below."@en .

rec:AIND-D02783 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02783-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02783-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02783 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بك بن علي بك بن ناصر الدين بن دلغادر . مات مسجونا بقلعة الجبل في جمادى الأولى سنة أربعين . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Hamza Bek, son of Ali Bek, son of Nasir al-Din, son of Dulkadir. He died while imprisoned in the Citadel (Qal'at al-Jabal) in Jumada al-Ula, the year 840 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) mentioned him in his history book, Inba' al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D02784 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02784-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02784-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02784-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02784-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02784 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن علي العز البهستاوي الحلبي ثم الدمشقي الصالحي الحنفي . أحد نواب الحكم بدمشق بل عينهم ثم أعرض عن الدخول في الأحكام ، وكان شكلا حسنا عارفا بمذهبه . مات في ربيع الأول سنة أربع وستين ، ولم يخلف في نواب الحكم مثله رحمه الله . ذكره ابن اللبودي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza b. ʿAlī, al-ʿIzz al-Bahistāwī, al-Ḥalabī, then al-Dimashqī, al-Ṣāliḥī, al-Ḥanafī. He was one of the deputies of judgment (nāʾib al-ḥukm) in Damascus, indeed the most prominent of them, but he later withdrew from judicial practice. He was of handsome appearance and well-versed in his school of law. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 864, leaving no equal among the deputies of judgment. May Allah have mercy on him. Ibn al-Labūdī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02786 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02786-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02786-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02786 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن قاسم بن أحمد بن عبد الكريم بن مخيط بن راجح بن أبي نمى الحسني المكي ويعرف بالكردي . مات في صفر سنة ست وأربعين بوادي مر وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بها . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza b. Qāsim b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Mukhayṭ b. Rājiḥ b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī, known as al-Kurdī. He died in the month of Ṣafar, in the year 846 AH [June/July 1442 CE], in Wādī Marr, and was carried to Mecca where he was buried. His death was chronicled by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D02790 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02790-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02790-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02790 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة بن يعقوب الدمشقي الحريري . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ، وقال مات في صفر سنة أربع وثلاثين . قلت وأظنه الذي قبله"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza b. Yaʿqūb al-Dimashqī al-Ḥarīrī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his chronicle, stating that he died in Safar, the year 834. I say: I think he is the same person as the one mentioned in the preceding entry."@en .

rec:AIND-D02791 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02791-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02791-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02791 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة ابن أخت الجمال البيري الاستادار وأخو أحمد الماضي . قتل خنقا فيمن قتل من آل خاله وبنيه في ربيع الآخر سنة أربع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza, the son of the sister of al-Jamāl al-Bīrī al-Ustādār and the brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad. He was strangled to death in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir, year 814, among those who were killed from the family of his maternal uncle and his sons."@en .

rec:AIND-D02792 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02792-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02792-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02792 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حمزة إمام مقام الشافعي . ممن أقرأ الأولاد وكان ممن قرأ عليه الزين عبد الغني الاشليمي وأثنى عليه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥamza, the Imam of the Maqām of al-Shāfiʿī. He was among those who educated children. Al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Ghanī al-Ashlīmī was among those who read under him, and he praised him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02793 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02793-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02793-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02793 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حميدان بن محمد بن أحمد البرلسي . ممن سمع منى بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥumaydān b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Burlusī. He was among those who heard hadith from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02794 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02794-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02794-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02794-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02794 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حنتم بن السيد محمد بن بركات بن حسن بن عجلان الحسني المكي الماضي جده وجد أبيه ويلقب بالجازاني . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة ثمان وثمانين قبل استكمال عشر سنين ، ودفن بالمعلاة عند أسلافه وتأسف أبوه على فقده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥantam, son of al-Sayyid Muḥammad, son of Barakāt, son of Ḥasan, son of ʿAjlān, al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. His grandfather and his father's grandfather were mentioned previously. He was nicknamed al-Jāzānī. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā, 888 AH, before reaching the age of ten, and was buried in al-Muʿallā near his ancestors. His father grieved deeply over his loss."@en .

rec:AIND-D02795 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02795-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02795-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02795 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حواس بن ميلب الشريف . صاهر السيد علي بن حسن بن عجلان أيام إمرته على مكة على بعض بناته في سنة ست وأربعين ومات في أحد الجمادين سنة خمس وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥawās b. Maylab al-Sharīf. He became the son-in-law of al-Sayyid ʿAlī b. Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān during the latter's rule over Mecca, marrying one of his daughters in the year 846 AH. He died in one of the two Jumādā months of the year 865 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02798 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02798-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02798-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02798 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حيدر بن يونس ويعرف بابن العسكري أحد الفرسان الشجعان . مات في شوال سنة إحدى بدمشق بطالا وقد شاخ وولي إمرة سنجار للأشرف شعبان . قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥaydar b. Yūnus, known as Ibn al-ʿAskarī. He was one of the brave knights. He died out of office in Damascus in Shawwāl, the year 801 H, having reached an advanced age. He had held the governorship of Sinjār for al-Ashraf Shaʿbān. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his history (Inbāʾ al-Ghumr)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02799 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02799-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02799-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02799 ;
    aindv:sourceText "حيدر برهان الدين مدرس القزارية بشيراز . ممن أخذ عن التفتازاني قال الطاووسي أجاز لي في سنة إحدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḥaydar Burhān al-Dīn, teacher of al-Qazzāriyya in Shīrāz. He was among those who took from al-Taftāzānī. Al-Ṭāwūsī said: 'He granted me ijāza in the year 801 AH.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D02900 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02900-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02900-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02900 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خليل بن عبد الرحمن بن على بن أحمد النويرى المكي . أجاز له في سنة ست وتسعين العراقى والبلقبنى وابن الملقن وآخرون ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khalīl b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī. In the year 796 AH, al-ʿIrāqī, al-Bulqīnī, Ibn al-Mulaqqin, and others granted him an ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D02910 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02910-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02910-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02910 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خليل بن عيسى بن عبد الله خير الدين القدسي الحنفي والد محمد الآتي وقاضي القدس . ممن وأخذ عنه ابنه وغيره ، ومات مسموما في سنة إحدى واستقر بعده في قضاء القدس موفق الدين العجمي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khalīl b. ʿĪsā b. ʿAbd Allāh Khayr al-Dīn al-Qudsī al-Ḥanafī, the father of Muḥammad (who is mentioned below) and the judge of Jerusalem. His son and others studied under him. He died of poisoning in the year 801 AH, and was succeeded in the judgeship of Jerusalem by Muwaffaq al-Dīn al-ʿAjamī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02914 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02914-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02914-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02914 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خليل بن محمد بن الشيخ أبي مدين علي بن أحمد الرملي ثم المقدسي الآتي جده . ممن أخذ عني"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khalīl b. Muḥammad b. al-Shaykh Abī Madyan ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Ramlī, later al-Maqdisī. His grandfather is mentioned below. He is among those who studied under me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02919 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02919-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02919-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02919 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خليل بن محمد الجندي الصوفي بالخاتونية المقرىء جمع السبع على الشرف خادم السميساطية وأقرأ . مات في صفر سنة ثلاث عشرة ، أرخه شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khalil b. Muhammad al-Jundi, the Sufi at al-Khatuniyya and the Quran reciter. He studied and compiled the seven variant recitations under al-Sharaf, the servant of al-Sumaysatiyya, and taught them to others. He died in Safar, in the year 813 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) recorded his biography in his chronicle, Inba' al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D02921 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02921-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02921-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02921 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خليل بن يعقوب بن إبراهيم التاجر صهر أخي أبي بكر ووالد أحمد الماضي . كان منجمعا عن الناس مقبلا على معيشته وشأنه مسيكا مع نوع توسعة . مات في سنة إحدى وسبعين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khalīl b. Yaʿqūb b. Ibrāhīm, the merchant. He was the brother-in-law of the brother of Abū Bakr, and the father of the aforementioned Aḥmad. He kept away from people, focusing on his livelihood and affairs, frugal yet with some comfortable means. He died in the year 871 AH, may Allah forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02922 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02922-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02922-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02922-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D02922-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02922 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خليل بن الوزير جمال الدين بن بشارة الدمشقي . كان شابا فطنا ذكيا محبا للتاريخ جمع تاريخا وكان يؤرخ الحوادث ويضبطها ويذاكر بأشياء حسنة إلا أنه مقبل على اللهو . مات قبل الكهولة في سنة خمس عشرة . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khalīl ibn al-Wazīr Jamāl al-Dīn ibn Bishāra al-Dimashqī. He was a clever and intelligent youth who loved history, compiled a chronicle, recorded and organized historical events, and engaged in pleasant scholarly discussions, though he was also inclined to pleasure. He died in the year 815 before reaching maturity. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his chronicle (Inbāʾ al-Ghumr)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02925 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02925-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02925-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02925 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خليل التوريزي نائب اسكندرية ويعرف بالشجاري ، انفصل عن النيابة في سنة ست عشرة وثمانمائة أو بعدها بالبدر حسن بن محب الدين الطرابلسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khalīl al-Tawrīzī, the deputy governor of Alexandria, known as al-Shajārī. He was separated from his office as deputy governor in the year 816 AH or after, being replaced by al-Badr Ḥasan b. Muḥibb al-Dīn al-Ṭarābulusī."@en .

rec:AIND-D02926 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02926-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02926-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02926 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خميس جرباش الحسني مولى السيد حسن بن عجلان القائد المكي . مات خارج مكة في رمضان سنة تسع وأربعين وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بمعلاتها . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khamīs Jirbāsh al-Ḥasanī, the client (mawla) of al-Sayyid Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān, the commander of Mecca. He died outside Mecca in Ramaḍān 849 AH, and was carried to Mecca where he was buried in al-Muʿallā. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D02927 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02927-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02927-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02927 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خنافر بن عقيل بن وبير الحسني أمير الينبوع . وليها بعد هجان بن محمد بن مسعود بعد سنة ستين ثم انفصل بسبع بن هجان ثم أعيد إلى أن قتل في مناطحة بينه وبين سبع في سنة خمس وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khunāfir b. ʿAqīl b. Wubayr al-Ḥasanī, Emir of Yanbuʿ. He governed it after Hajjān b. Muḥammad b. Masʿūd after the year 860 AH. He was then deposed by Sabʿ b. Hajjān, but was later restored to power until he was killed in a clash against Sabʿ in the year 875 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02929 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02929-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02929-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02929 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خير بك الأشرفي برسباي البهلوان . تأمر عشرة في دولة إينال ثم نفاه الظاهر خشقدم إلى البلاد الشامية ثم صار من مقدمي دمشق . ومات في وقعة سوار في شوال سنة ثلاث وسبعين وهو في عشر الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khayr Bak al-Ashrafī Barsbāy al-Bahlawān. He was appointed as an Amir of Ten during the reign of Īnāl, and was subsequently exiled by al-Ẓāhir Khushqadam to the Syrian lands, where he later became one of the commanders (muqaddams) of Damascus. He was killed in the battle of Suwar (Sawar) in Shawwāl, the year 873 H, being in his fifties."@en .

rec:AIND-D02930 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02930-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02930-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02930 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خير بك الأشرفي . استقر في نظر الحرمين ونيابة القدس بعد دقماق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khayr Bik al-Ashrafī. He was appointed to the supervision of the two sanctuaries (Jerusalem and Hebron) and the vice-regency of Jerusalem after Duqmāq."@en .

rec:AIND-D02931 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02931-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02931-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02931 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خير بك الأشرفي اينال أحد العشرات ويعرف بغمغم . مات في طاعون سنة سبع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khayr Bik al-Ashrafi Inal, one of the Amirs of Ten, known as Ghamgham. He died in the plague of the year 897 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02937 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02937-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02937-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02937 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خير بك أمير ناب في غزة وأعطى تقدمة قتل في سنة أربع عشرة أرخه شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khayr Bak. An amīr who served as the deputy governor (nāʾib) of Gaza and was granted a military command (taqdima). He was killed in the year 814 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) chronicled him in his historical work, Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D02938 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02938-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02938-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02938 ;
    aindv:sourceText "خير الذهبي معلم الدلالين بجدة ، كان مولى لنائبها جانبك فإنه اشتراه من سيده أحد أهل دار الضرب لما ادعاه حين معلميته وله بمكة داران حبس إحداهما على معتقيه مع إنهماكه وميله للضعفاء . مات بها في المحرم سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Khayr al-Dhahabī, the head of brokers in Jeddah. He was a freedman (mawla) of its deputy, Jānibak. When Khayr was serving as the head of brokers, Jānibak claimed ownership of him, prompting a member of the Mint (Dār al-Ḍarb) to purchase him from his master Jānibak. He owned two houses in Mecca, one of which he endowed (made waqf) for his own manumitted slaves, despite his indulgence in worldly pleasures and his kindness toward the weak. He died in Mecca in Muharram, the year 868."@en .

rec:AIND-D02939 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02939-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02939-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02939-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02939 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود بن إبراهيم الصيرفي والد نور الدين علي الحنفي . كان صيرفي المفرد والدولة معا ثم اقتصر به على الدولة واستمر حتى مات في رجب سنة ثلاث وخمسين ، ولعله كان خيرا من ولده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd b. Ibrāhīm al-Ṣayrafī, the father of Nūr al-Dīn ʿAlī, the Hanafi. He served as the money changer (ṣayrafī) of both the private treasury (al-mufrad) and the state (al-dawla) together, then he was restricted to the state treasury, continuing in this role until he died in Rajab, the year 853. Perhaps he was better than his son."@en .

rec:AIND-D02942 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02942-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02942-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02942 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود بن إسماعيل بن علي بن محمد بن داود بن شمس بن عبد الله البيضاوي المكي الزمزمي أخو أبي الفتح وأحد المؤذنين العريضي الأصوات . مات بمكة عن إنابة في المحرم سنة إثنتين وثمانين سامحه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd ibn Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd ibn Shams ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Bayḍāwī al-Makkī al-Zamzamī. The brother of Abū al-Fatḥ and one of the muezzins known for his resonant voice. He died in Mecca as a deputy in Muharram, the year 882 [AH]. May Allah forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D02943 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02943-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02943-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02943 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود بن أبي بكر بن بهادر السنبلي أمير زبيد . مات سنة ثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd bin Abī Bakr b. Bahādur al-Sunbulī, the emir of Zabīd. He died in the year 830 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02946 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02946-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02946-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02946 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود بن سيف أرغد صاحب الحبشة ويقال له الحطي . مات في سنة اثنتي عشرة ، واستقر بعده ابنه تدرس"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dawud b. Sayf Arghad, the ruler of Abyssinia (Ethiopia), also known as al-Ḥuṭṭī. He died in the year 812 AH, and his son Tedros (Tadros) succeeded him as ruler."@en .

rec:AIND-D02951 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02951-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02951-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02951 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود بن علي بن سعدون التجيبي الجزيري . مات سنة أربع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd b. ʿAlī b. Saʿdūn al-Tujībī al-Jazīrī. He died in the year 804 [AH]."@en .

rec:AIND-D02953 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02953-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02953-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02953 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود بن عمر بن أبي بكر الشيرازي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd b. ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr al-Shīrāzī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02954 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02954-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02954-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02954 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود بن عيسى بن عمر شيخ هوار . ممن حج في موسم سنة ثلاث وتسعين وأحسن لفقراء الحرمين وغيرهم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd ibn ʿĪsā ibn ʿUmar, the shaykh of the Hawwārah tribe. He was among those who performed the Hajj in the season of the year 893 AH, and he acted generously towards the poor of the Two Holy Sanctuaries (Mecca and Medina) and others."@en .

rec:AIND-D02957 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02957-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02957-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02957 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود بن محمد بن عيسي بن أحمد الهندي المحمد ابادى أخو سليمان ووالد راجح الآتيين . كان فيما قاله لي ولده فاضلا . ومات في سنة اثنتين وسبعين عن نحو ثلاثين سنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā b. Aḥmad al-Hindī al-Muḥammadābādī. Brother of Sulaymān and father of Rājiḥ, both of whom are mentioned below. According to what his son told me, he was a virtuous man. He died in the year 872 AH at around thirty years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D02959 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02959-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02959-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02959-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02959 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود بن ناصر الدين محمد بن السابق الحمصي . سمع من أبي الغيث محمد ابن عبد الله بن الصائغ وغيره بعض الصحيح أنا به الحجار ، ولقيه ابن موسى الحافظ وشيخنا الموفق الأبي بحمص فأخذا عنه حديثا من البخاري ومات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd b. Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad b. al-Sābiq al-Ḥimṣī. He heard a portion of the Ṣaḥīḥ (al-Bukhārī) transmitted via al-Ḥajjār from Abū al-Ghayth Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Ṣāʾigh and others. The Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Mūsā and our shaykh al-Muwaffaq al-Abī met him in Homs and received some Hadiths of al-Bukhārī from him, after which he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D02961 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02961-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02961-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02961 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود شهاب الدين اللاري . قال الطاوسي تعلمت منه في المبادىء مقدمات العلوم كالكافيتين وشروحهما وشرح الشمسية للقطبي وبعض الكشاف وغيرها ، وهو ممن أخذ عن المحققين وأجاز لي مرارا منها في شهور سنة ثلاث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd Shihāb al-Dīn al-Lārī. Al-Ṭāwūsī said: \"I learned from him in the beginning the introductory sciences, such as the two Kāfiyas and their commentaries, al-Quṭbī's commentary on al-Shamsiyya, and some of al-Kashshāf, among other works.\" He was among those who studied under the verified scholars, and he granted me (al-Ṭāwūsī) an ijāza multiple times, including during the months of the year 803 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02962 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02962-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02962-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02962 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود المغربي التاجر . مات في صفر سنة أربع وخمسين وخلف أشياء كثيرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd al-Maghribī, the merchant. He died in the month of Safar in the year 854 AH, leaving behind a large estate."@en .

rec:AIND-D02963 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02963-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02963-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02963 ;
    aindv:sourceText "داود المغربي نزيل رباط الموفق من مكة ورفيق هبة بن أحمد الآتي . مات في إحدى الجمادين سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dāwūd al-Maghribī, resident of the Ribāṭ al-Muwaffaq in Mecca and companion of Hiba b. Aḥmad, who is mentioned below. He died in one of the two Jumādā months in the year 868 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02964 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02964-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02964-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02964-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02964 ;
    aindv:sourceText "دراج بن معزى الحسنى أمير الينبوع . استقر فيه في أواخر سنة سبع وثمانين عقب سبع الماضى نيابة عن صاحب الحجاز حين فوض أمره إليه ، ورأيته اذ ذاك في سنة ثمان وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Darrāj b. Muʿzā al-Ḥasanī, the emir of Yanbuʿ. He was established in this position in the late year 887 H as a deputy of the ruler of Hejaz, who delegated his affairs to him, succeeding the aforementioned Sabaʿ. I saw him then in the year 898 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D02965 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02965-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02965-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02965 ;
    aindv:sourceText "دبيس بن جسار بن سنان بن زاجح بن محمد بن عبد الله بن عمر أحد القواد العمرة بمكة وابن عم أحمد بن على بن سنان الماضي . قتل بالحدبة في صفر سنة ست وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dubays bin Jasar bin Sinan bin Zajih bin Muhammad bin Abd Allah bin Umar. One of the commanders of the 'Umrah in Mecca, and the cousin of the aforementioned Ahmad bin Ali bin Sinan. He was killed at al-Hadba in Safar of the year 846 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02971 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02971-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02971-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02971 ;
    aindv:sourceText "دمرداش الطويل الظاهري . مات سنة إحدى وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Damurdāsh al-Ṭawīl al-Ẓāhirī. He died in the year 871 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02974 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02974-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02974-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02974 ;
    aindv:sourceText "دولات باي الأشرفي برسباي من أمراء العشرات . مات في أواخر صفر سنة ثمانين فجأة طلع إلى الخدمة على العادة فوجدوه ميتا وصلى عليه السلطان غير مأسوف عليه فقد ذكرت له قبائح ومساوىء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dawlat Bay al-Ashrafi Barsbay, one of the amirs of tens. He died suddenly in late Safar, the year 880 AH. He went up to service as usual and was found dead. The Sultan performed the funeral prayer over him, and he was unmourned, as his bad deeds and evils were mentioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D02975 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02975-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02975-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02975 ;
    aindv:sourceText "دولات باي الأشرفي اينال . تأمر عشرة ثم تجرد عن قريب لسوار فمات بغزة في رجوعه سنة أربع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dawlāt Bāy al-Ashrafī Īnāl. He was appointed as an Amīr of Ten, then shortly after dispatched on a military campaign against Shāh Suwār, and died in Gaza on his return in the year 874 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02976 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02976-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02976-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02976 ;
    aindv:sourceText "دولات باي الأشرفي ويعرف بحمام . تنقل حتى عمل رأس نوبة ثاني على إمرة عشرة في أيام الظاهر تمربغا ثم عمل شاد الشر بخاناه وولي نيابة اسكندرية ومات بها في رجب سنة ثلاث وثمانين واستقر بعده في النيابة اينال الأشرفي قايتباي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dawlāt Bāy al-Ashrafī, known as Ḥammām. He rose through the ranks until he was appointed as the Second Ra's Nawba over a command of ten during the reign of al-Ẓāhir Tamurbughā, then served as the Shādd al-Sharb-khānāh (supervisor of the buttery), and was appointed as the governor of Alexandria, where he died in Rajab, year 883. He was succeeded in the governorship by Īnāl al-Ashrafī Qāytbāy."@en .

rec:AIND-D02978 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02978-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02978-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02978 ;
    aindv:sourceText "دولات باي الحسني الظاهري جقمق . تنقل حتى صار شاد الشؤن ، وحج وهو كذلك بالركب سنة سبع وثمانين ورجعنا في ركبه ثم استقر رأس نوبة ثاني في سنة تسعين ومات في المقتلة في رمضان سنة ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dawlat Bay al-Hasani al-Zahiri Jaqmaq. He held various posts until he became Shadd al-Shu'un (Supervisor of Affairs), in which capacity he performed the Hajj in the year 887 AH. We returned in his caravan. Then he was appointed as Ra's Nawba Thani (Second Chief of the Mamluk Guards) in the year 890 AH. He died in a battle/massacre in Ramadan of the year 893 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02981 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02981-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02981-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02981-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02981 ;
    aindv:sourceText "دينار الطواشي أحد الجمدارية . ممن أضيفت إليه في سنة خمس وتسعين خدمة بالحجرة النبوية بعد سرور الحبشي الحسني قراقجا الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dīnār al-Ṭwāshī, one of the jamdārs (wardrobe keepers). In the year 895 AH the service of the Prophet's Chamber was added to his charge, succeeding Surūr al-Ḥabashī al-Ḥasanī Qarāqujā, who is mentioned below."@en .

rec:AIND-D02982 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02982-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02982-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02982 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ذو النون الغزي واسمه محمد بن عبد الله بن صالح . كان عظيما يتجر حكى الزين عبد الرحمن القلقشندي عن أبيه الشمس أنه قال هو خفير تلك البلاد . وقد لقيه شيخنا في سنة آمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Dhu al-Nun al-Ghazzi, his name is Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Salih. He was a great man who engaged in trade. Zayn al-Din Abd al-Rahman al-Qalqashandi related from his father, al-Shams, that he said: 'He is the protector of those lands.' Our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) met him in the year of Amid."@en .

rec:AIND-D02983 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02983-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02983-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02983 ;
    aindv:sourceText "راجح بن حسين بن محمد الحجاري مؤدب يحيى بن أبي البركات بن ظهيرة . رجل خير ساكن ممن سمع علي بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rājiḥ b. Ḥusayn b. Muḥammad al-Ḥajjārī, the tutor of Yaḥyā b. Abī al-Barakāt b. Ẓuhayra. A good and quiet resident who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02987 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02987-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02987-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02987-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02987 ;
    aindv:sourceText "راجح بن علي النشيط المكي الخياط . مات بها في المحرم سنة ثلاث وخمسين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rājiḥ b. ʿAlī al-Nashīṭ al-Makkī al-Khayyāṭ (the tailor). He died in it [Mecca] in al-Muharram, in the year 853 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02988 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02988-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02988-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02988 ;
    aindv:sourceText "راجح الطحان . مات في المحرم سنة سبع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rājiḥ al-Ṭaḥḥān. He died in al-Muharram, 867 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02989 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02989-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02989-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02989 ;
    aindv:sourceText "راشد بن أحمد بن راشد . مات بمكة في رجب سنة ست وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rāshid b. Aḥmad b. Rāshid. He died in Mecca in Rajab, the year 856 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D02990 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02990-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02990-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02990 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ربيع بن إبراهيم بن علي القليوبي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rabīʿ b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī al-Qalyūbī. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D02991 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02991-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02991-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D02991-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02991 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ربيع شيخ صوفية المكان الذي بناه الجمالي ناظر الخاص بالكوم الأبيض ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rabīʿ, the shaykh of the Sufis at the place built by al-Jamālī, the Nāẓir al-Khāṣṣ (Superintendent of the Privy Purse), in al-Kawm al-Abyaḍ."@en .

rec:AIND-D02992 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02992-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02992-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02992 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رجب بن أحمد بن علي بن عمر الزين أبو البركات السنهوري المالكي ويعرف بابن العسيلي . ممن أخذ القراءات عن بلديه جعفر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rajab b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar, Zayn Abū al-Barakāt al-Sanhūrī al-Mālikī, known as Ibn al-ʿAsīlī. He was among those who studied the variant Quranic recitations (qirāʾāt) under his fellow countryman Jaʿfar (al-Zayn Jaʿfar al-Sanhūrī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D02993 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02993-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02993-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02993 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رجب بن كمشبغا الحموي الآتي أبوه . مات في سابع عشري رمضان سنة إحدى قبل أبيه بيوم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rajab bin Kamashbughā al-Ḥamawī, whose father is mentioned below. He died on the 27th of Ramaḍān in the year 801 AH, one day before his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D02995 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02995-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02995-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02995 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رجب بن الناسخ المؤذن مؤدب الابناء . فقير تزوج ابنة صهر أخي الوسط ومكث معها مدة ثم فارقها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rajab b. al-Nasikh, the muezzin and children's educator. He was a poor man (or Sufi) who married the daughter of the brother-in-law of my (al-Sakhawi's) middle brother, lived with her for a period, and then divorced her."@en .

rec:AIND-D02996 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02996-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02996-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02996 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رجب ولم ينسب . ممن سمع علي بمكة في السر المكتوم وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rajab, whose lineage is not mentioned. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhawi) in Mecca, studying 'al-Sirr al-Maktum' and other works."@en .

rec:AIND-D02997 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D02997-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D02997-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D02997 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رحاب أحد مشايح عربان البحيرة . قتل في آخر ذى الحجة سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Riḥāb, one of the shaykhs of the Bedouins of al-Buḥayra. He was killed at the end of Dhu al-Hijja in the year 853."@en .

rec:AIND-D03002 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03002-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03002-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03002-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03002 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رسول بن محمد بن عمر الكردي . ممن سمع على شيخنا أيضا وصحب إمام الكاملية وكان يقال لأحدهما الكبير وللآخر الصغير للتمييز ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rasūl b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar al-Kurdī. He was among those who heard hadith from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) as well, and he accompanied the imam of al-Kāmiliyya. One of them was called 'the Elder' (al-Kabīr) and the other 'the Younger' (al-Ṣaghīr) for distinction."@en .

rec:AIND-D03003 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03003-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03003-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03003-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03003-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03003-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D03003-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87_apply2,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03003 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رشيد بن عبد الله الحاج رشيد الدين الفهدي البهائي أحد الفراشين في الحرم النبوي ويعرف . سمع على العز بن جماعة جزءا قرأه عليه الشرف أبو الفتح المراغي في سنة اثنتي عشرة وثمانمائة بمبرك الناقة النبوية من دار أبي أيوب الأنصاري المعروفة بالمدرسة الشهابية ووصفه بالشيخ الصالح الخير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rashīd b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Ḥājj Rashīd al-Dīn al-Fahdī al-Bahāʾī. One of the farrāshūn (attendants/servants) in the Prophet's Mosque. He heard a juzʾ (hadith part) from al-ʿIzz b. Jamāʿa, which was read to him by al-Sharaf Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī in the year 812 AH at the place where the Prophet's she-camel knelt (Mabrak al-Nāqa), at the house of Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī (known as al-Madrasa al-Shihābiyya). He (al-Marāghī) described him as a pious and righteous shaykh."@en .

rec:AIND-D03004 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03004-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03004-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03004-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03004-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03004-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03004 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رضوان بن علي بن رضوان القاهري المقرىء والد أحمد الماضي وأحد قراء الجوق المجتهدين في التحصيل . تكسب بالشهادة كأبيه وبالدوران في الاسباع ببيت الأمراء ونحوهم وتنزل في كثير من الجهات بل كتب الوصولات بالخشابية بعد ولده وربما خطب وكنت أحمد قراءته ووجد له بعض الاسمعة في ثبت الجمال البدراني فاستجازه الطلبة لذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Riḍwān ibn ʿAlī ibn Riḍwān al-Qāhirī, the Quran reciter. He is the father of the aforementioned Aḥmad, and was one of the diligent Quran reciters of the jawq (recitation group) in acquiring knowledge. He earned his living by witnessing (al-shahāda) like his father, and by circulating for the recitation of the usbūʿ (one-seventh of the Quran) in the houses of the amirs and others. He received stipends in many places, and even wrote receipts at al-Khashshābiyya after his son did. He sometimes delivered sermons (khutba). I [al-Sakhāwī] used to praise his recitation. Some of his audition records (asmiʿa) were found in the Thabat of al-Jamāl al-Badrānī, so students requested ijāza from him for that reason."@en .

rec:AIND-D03006 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03006-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03006-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03006 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رضوان بن هلال الأندلسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Raḍwān b. Hilāl al-Andalusī"@en .

rec:AIND-D03008 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03008-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03008-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03008-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03008-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03008 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رمضان بن إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن موسى الزين المنوفي ثم القاهري الشافعي نزيل القراسنقرية وأخو الشهاب أحمد بن أبي السعود الماضي لأبيه خاصة فرمضان أمه أمة . مات في شعبان سنة اثنتين وثمانين وكان خيرا مديما للتلاوة والعبادة صوفيا بالخانقاه الصلاحية مع غيرهما من الجهات ولم يقصر عن الخمسين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ramaḍān b. Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Mūsā, al-Zayn, al-Manūfī then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī. A resident of al-Qarāsunqurīya and the paternal half-brother of al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. Abī al-Suʿūd, who was mentioned previously (his mother was a slave girl). He died in Shaʿbān 882 AH. He was a pious man, constant in reciting the Qur'an and worship, and served as a Sufi at al-Khānqāh al-Ṣalāḥiyya along with other posts. He did not reach fifty years of age. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03009 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03009-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03009-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03009 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رمضان بن علي بن أحمد أبو الجود الشاذلي المدني الواعظ . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ramaḍān b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad Abū al-Jūd al-Shādhilī al-Madanī, the preacher. He was among those who heard (hadith) from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03010 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03010-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03010-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03010 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رمضان بن عمر بن مزروع الاتكاوي الشافعي . شيخ صالح جليل أخذ عن بلديه الشيخ إبراهيم وصحبه جماعة كالزيني زكريا القاضي والشمس بن سلامة ، وكان فاضلا . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة سبعين وهو عم محمد بن إسماعيل بن عمر العمريطي الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ramaḍān b. ʿUmar b. Mazrūʿ al-Ātkāwī al-Shāfiʿī. He was a pious and noble shaykh. He studied under his fellow townsperson, al-Shaykh Ibrāhīm, and was accompanied by a group of disciples including the judge Zayn al-Dīn Zakarīyā and Shams al-Dīn b. Salāma. He was a man of virtue. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā, the year 870 AH. He is the paternal uncle of Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿUmar al-ʿAmrīṭī, who is mentioned below."@en .

rec:AIND-D03011 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03011-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03011-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03011 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رمضان بن يوسف بن رمضان الشبراوي ويعرف بابن تكا قوله . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ramaḍān b. Yūsuf b. Ramaḍān al-Shubrāwī, known as Ibn Takā. He is among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03012 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03012-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03012-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03012-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03012 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رمضان اللقاني ثم القاهري البهائي التاجر . ممن قرأ على ابن أسد وأبي السعادات البلقيني وغيرهما ، وحج وكان راغبا في الخير وزوج ابنه لابنة يحيى ابن شيخنا الرشيدي . مات في أوائل سنة ثمان وثمانين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ramaḍān al-Laqānī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Bahāʾī, the merchant. He studied under Ibn Asad, Abū al-Saʿādāt al-Bulqīnī, and others, and performed the Hajj. He was inclined toward charity, and married his son to the daughter of Yaḥyā, the son of our shaykh al-Rashīdī. He died in the beginning of the year 888 AH. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03013 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03013-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03013-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03013-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03013-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03013 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رمضان المنفلوطي ثم القاهري المهتار عامي جلف . ولد ببني غالب قرية من عمل منفلوط ، رقاه أستاذه وصار يتكلم في الكسوة وغيرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ramaḍān al-Manfalūṭī, later al-Qāhirī, known as al-Mihtār (the steward). He was a rude commoner. He was born in Banī Ghālib, a village in the district of Manfalūṭ. His master promoted him, and he came to oversee the Kiswah (of the Kaaba) and other matters."@en .

rec:AIND-D03014 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03014-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03014-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03014-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03014 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رمضان الضرير بواب المدرسة الجمالية بمكة . مات بها في جمادي الآخرة سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ramaḍān al-Ḍarīr, the doorkeeper of al-Madrasa al-Jamāliyya in Mecca. He died there in Jumada al-Akhira, year 868 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03015 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03015-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03015-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03015-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03015 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رميثة بن أحمد الهذلي المسعودي ويعرف بالخفير بمعجمة وفاء ككبير . كان من أعيان الخفراء الذين يسكنون سولة من نخلة اليمانية ممن ينسب لخير ومروءة واعتبار بين الناس . مات في أيام منى سنة تسع عشرة بعد تغير عقله قليلا من الكبر ودفن بالمعلاة عن ست وسبعين فأزيد ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rumaitha b. Aḥmad al-Hudhalī al-Masʿūdī, known as al-Khafīr. He was one of the prominent guards who resided in Sawla of Nakhla al-Yamāniyya, and was recognized for his goodness, virtue, and high standing among the people. He died during the days of Mina in the year 819 AH after some slight mental decline due to old age, and was buried in al-Muʿallā at the age of seventy-six or older. Mentioned by al-Fāsī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03017 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03017-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03017-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03017 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رميثة بن أبي القسم بن حسن بن عجلان بن رميثة بن أبي نمى الحسني المكي . مات غريبا بالمحلة وكان راجعا من اسكندرية في ربيع الثاني سنة تسع وسبعين ، وشهد الصلاة عليه ثم دفنه من لا يحصى كثرة ، وكان توجهه إلى القاهرة في سنة ست وسبعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rumaytha ibn Abī al-Qāsim ibn Ḥasan ibn ʿAjlān ibn Rumaytha ibn Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died away from home in al-Maḥalla while returning from Alexandria in Rabīʿ al-Thānī 879 AH. An innumerable crowd of people attended his funeral prayer and buried him. He had traveled to Cairo in 876 AH. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03018 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03018-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03018-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03018 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رميثة بن محمد بن عجلان بن رميثة بن أبي نمى الحسني المكي . ولي إمرتها مدة فلم تحمد سيرته فعزل واتفق خروجه في طائفة من العسكر للوقيعة ببني إبراهيم أو غيرهم على نحو ثمانية أيام من مكة فقتل في المعركة في رجب سنة سبع وثلاثين ببلاد الشرق ودفن هناك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rumaytha b. Muḥammad b. ʿAjlān b. Rumaytha b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He ruled as the emir of Mecca for a period, but because his conduct was not praised, he was deposed. He then set out with a detachment of soldiers to fight against the Banū Ibrāhīm (or others) at a distance of about eight days' journey from Mecca. He was killed in battle in Rajab 837 AH in the Eastern lands, and was buried there."@en .

rec:AIND-D03019 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03019-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03019-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03019 ;
    aindv:sourceText "رميح بن حازم بن عبد الكريم بن أبي نمى الحسني . مات في أول شعبان سنة سبع وخمسين خارج مكة وحمل فدفن بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rumayḥ b. Ḥāzim b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī. He died in early Shaʿbān in the year 857 outside Mecca, and was carried and buried in it."@en .

rec:AIND-D03020 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03020-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03020-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03020 ;
    aindv:sourceText "روزبهان بن محمد بن عبد الدائم بن مكرم الشيخ صدر الدين بن غياث الدين ابن روح الدين الفالي ابن أخت أحمد بن نعمة الله الماضي . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة النبوية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rūzbihān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Dāʾim b. Mukram, al-Shaykh Ṣadr al-Dīn, al-Fālī. The maternal nephew of the aforementioned Aḥmad b. Niʿmat Allāh. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the Prophet's city (Medina)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03021 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03021-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03021-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03021-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03021 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ريحان الحبشي التعكري لكونه عتيق الجمال محمد بن عمر بن مسعود التعكري والد علي وزينب زوج محمد بن حسن الصائغ وأم هاني أم أبي بكر بن عبد الغني المرشدي وغيره . كان له من الدور دار بدار الخفرة وأخرى تجاه دار الشهاب قاوان بالخرازين . مات سنة ست وعشرين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rayḥān al-Ḥabashī al-Taʿkarī. He was the freed slave (ʿatīq) of al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. Masʿūd al-Taʿkarī, who was the father of ʿAlī, Zaynab (the wife of Muḥammad b. Ḥasan al-Ṣāʾigh), and Umm Hānī (the mother of Abū Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī al-Murshidī and others). Rayḥān owned a house in Dār al-Khafrah and another facing the house of al-Shihāb Qāwān in al-Kharrāzīn. He died in Mecca in the year 826 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03022 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03022-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03022-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03022-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03022 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ريحان الحبشي العطار . هكذا جرده ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rayḥān al-Ḥabashī al-ʿAṭṭār. Thus Ibn Fahd listed him bare of lineage."@en .

rec:AIND-D03023 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03023-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03023-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03023 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ريحان الحبشي عتيق الشيبي . مات بمكة في مستهل ربيع الأول سنة إحدى وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rayḥān al-Ḥabashī, the freedman of al-Shībī. He died in Mecca at the beginning of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 851 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03024 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03024-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03024-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03024 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ريحان الحبشي عتيق الشهاب بن الضياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rayḥān al-Ḥabashī, freedman of al-Shihāb b. al-Ḍiyāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D03026 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03026-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03026-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03026 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ريحان الحبشي فتى الزكي أبي بكر المصري . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rayḥān al-Ḥabashī, the servant (or freedman) of al-Zakī Abū Bakr al-Miṣrī. He was among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03027 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03027-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03027-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03027-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03027 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ريحان الحبشي المكي ويعرف بالعيني . ولي أمر المكس بجدة في دولة السيد علي بن عجلان وحصل دنيا وأملاكا ثم ذهب غالبه وكان ذا مروءة . مات بزبيد في رمضان أو شوال سنة ست عشرة . ذكره الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rayḥān al-Ḥabashī al-Makkī, known as al-ʿAynī. He was appointed as the customs officer (amr al-maks) of Jidda during the reign of al-Sayyid ʿAlī b. ʿAjlān, and acquired wealth and properties, most of which he subsequently lost. He was a man of chivalry. He died in Zabīd in Ramaḍān or Shawwāl of the year 816 AH. Al-Fāsī mentioned him in his history of Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03028 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03028-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03028-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03028-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03028-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03028-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03028 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ريحان الزنجي الحلبي . ذكر بالخير والدين ، وإنه كان يتعاطى حلق رؤس الأكابر من الأمراء وغيرهم ويسقي الماء بطاسة بين العشاءين بخانقاه شيخو سنين ويكثر من الصلاة ونحوها مع بشاشة واستقر به الاشرف قايتباي في السبيل الذي أنشأه بزيادة جامع ابن طولون . مات في سنة سبع وثمانين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rayḥān al-Zanjī al-Ḥalabī. He was mentioned with goodness and piety. He used to shave the heads of prominent emirs and others. For years, he voluntarily distributed water using a bowl between the two evening prayers at the Khānqāh of Shaykhū, while showing cheerfulness and offering many prayers. Later, the Sultan al-Ashraf Qāytbāy appointed him to the sabil (public fountain) which he established at the annex of the Mosque of Ibn Ṭūlūn. He died in the year 887 H, may Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03029 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03029-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03029-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03029-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03029 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ريحان العدني ويعرف بالرميدي . كان ذا ملاءة وعبادة ، وفيه خير وديانة تردد لمكة غير مرة ، وجاور بها ثلاث سنين أو نحوها متصلة بوفاته . مات في ذي الحجة سنة عشر بمكة ودفن بالمعلاة . ذكره الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rayḥān al-ʿAdanī, known as al-Rumaydī. He was wealthy and devout, possessing goodness and piety. He frequented Mecca more than once, and performed jawarah (extended stay) there for about three years continuously until his death. He died in Dhu al-Hijjah, in the year 810 AH, in Mecca and was buried in al-Muʿallā. Al-Fāsī mentioned him in his work on Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03030 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03030-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03030-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03030-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03030 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ريحان النوبي ثم المكي القائد عتيق السيد حسن بن عجلان ويعرف بالفيل مات بمكة في جمادى الأولى سنة تسع وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rayḥān al-Nūbī, later al-Makkī. He was a commander (al-Qāʾid) and a freed slave (ʿatīq) of al-Sayyid Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān, and was known by the epithet al-Fīl (the Elephant). He died in Mecca in Jumada al-Ula, 849 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03031 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03031-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03031-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03031-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03031 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ريحان اليعقوبي نسبة للخواجا يعقوب البرلسي الطواشي أحد خدام المدينة ممن سمع مني ، ومات سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Rayḥān al-Yaʿqūbī, so called after al-Khawāja Yaʿqūb al-Burlusī. He was a eunuch and one of the servants of Medina. He heard [ḥadīth] from me, and died in the year 891 [AH]."@en .

rec:AIND-D03033 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03033-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03033-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03033 ;
    aindv:sourceText "زاهد بن عارف بن جلال اللكنوهي الهندي الحنفي . قرأ على أربعي النووي بمكة في رمضان سنة أربع وتسعين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Zāhid b. ʿĀrif b. Jalāl al-Laknawhī al-Hindī al-Ḥanafī. He read (studied) al-Nawawī's \"Forty Hadiths\" in Mecca in Ramaḍān of the year 894 AH (August-September 1489 CE)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03034 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03034-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03034-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03034 ;
    aindv:sourceText "زاهر بن أبي القسم بن حسن بن عجلان بن رميثة بن أبي نمى الحسني ممن له ذكر في أيام أبيه وسطوة وتجبر إلى أن قيده أبوه ثم رضي عنه ومات بعد"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Zāhir b. Abū al-Qāsim b. Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān b. Rumaytha b. Abū Numayy al-Ḥasanī. He was mentioned during his father's days, exercising power and tyranny until his father imprisoned him; his father later forgave him, and he died afterwards."@en .

rec:AIND-D03037 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03037-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03037 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الزبير بن سعد بن عبد الله النفطي المدني المادح . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة وأنشد نظما لغيره قاله في ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Zubayr b. Saʿd b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Nafṭī al-Madanī, the panegyrist. He was among those who heard (hadith) from me in Medina, and he recited some poetry composed by another person about me."@en .

rec:AIND-D03038 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03038-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03038-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03038-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03038 ;
    aindv:sourceText "زربة بن تبل بن منصور العمري القائد . مات في ذي القعدة سنة ثلاث وستين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Zarba b. Tubal b. Manṣūr al-ʿUmarī, the commander. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda, the year 863, in Mecca. His biography was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03045 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03045-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03045-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03045 ;
    aindv:sourceText "زهير بن سليمان بن هبة بن جماز بن منصور الحسيني أمير المدينة . وليها بعد زبيري الماضي في آخر سنة خمس وستين فاستمر حتى مات في صفر سنة ثلاث وسبعين غير أنه انفصل في شوال سنة تسع وستين نحو أربعة أشهر بضغيم بن خشرم الحسيني المنصوري وهو المستقر بعد موته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Zuhayr b. Sulaymān b. Hiba b. Jammāz b. Manṣūr al-Ḥusaynī, the Amīr of Medina. He assumed its governorship after the aforementioned Zubayrī at the end of the year 865 AH and continued in office until his death in Ṣafar 873 AH, except that he was temporarily deposed for about four months in Shawwāl 869 AH by Ḍughaym b. Khashram al-Ḥusaynī al-Manṣūrī, who permanently succeeded him after his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03047 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03047-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03047-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03047-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03047 ;
    aindv:sourceText "زيرك الرومي القاسمي قاسم . مولى محظوظ في التجارة صادق اللهجة محبا في الخير متأدبا . ترقى في التجارة وقدم بسببها القاهرة كثيرا ، وسافر لغيرها وصار أحد المذكورين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Zīrak al-Rūmī al-Qāsimī Qāsim. A freed slave of Qāsim. He was fortunate in trade, truthful in speech, loving of charity, and well-mannered. He rose in trade, frequently visiting Cairo for business, and traveled to other places, becoming one of the prominent figures."@en .

rec:AIND-D03049 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03049-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03049-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03049-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03049 ;
    aindv:sourceText "زين العابدين بن علي بن محمود بن العادل سليمان الأيوبي أخو أيوب الماضي وانه آخر ملوك الحصن من بني أيوب وقتل في سنة ست وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Zayn al-ʿĀbidīn bin ʿAlī bin Maḥmūd bin al-ʿĀdil Sulaymān al-Ayyūbī. He was the brother of the aforementioned Ayyūb, and the last Ayyubid ruler of al-Ḥiṣn (Ḥiṣn Kayfā). He was killed in the year 866 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03050 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03050-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03050-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03050 ;
    aindv:sourceText "زين العباد بن فخر الدين بن جلال بن أحمد بن فضل الواسطي . مات سنة ثمان وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Zayn al-ʿIbād b. Fakhr al-Dīn b. Jalāl b. Aḥmad b. Faḍl al-Wāsiṭī. He died in the year 838 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03051 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03051-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03051-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03051-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03051 ;
    aindv:sourceText "زين قرا بن الرماح كتب عنه شيخنا الزين رضوان شعرا للشافعي في صناعة الرمي بالنشاب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Zayn Qurā b. al-Rammāḥ. Our shaykh al-Zayn Riḍwān wrote down from him poetry of al-Shāfiʿī on the art of shooting arrows (archery)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03054 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03054-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03054-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03054 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سالم بن إسماعيل بن الحسن البابي ثم الحلبي في محمد"@ar .

rec:AIND-D03056 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03056-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03056-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03056-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03056-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03056-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03056 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سالم بن ذاكر بن محمد بن عبد المؤمن بن محمد بن ذاكر بن عبد المؤمن بن أبي المعالي بن أبي الخير بن ذاكر الكازروني الأصل المكي المؤذن الصائغ والد محمد وعلي وعبد العزيز . سمع من الإمام أبي اليمن الطبري قطعة من أول الموطأ لابن بكير وأربعين انتقاء الاقفهسي من أبي داود ، وما علمت متى مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sālim bin Dhākir bin Muḥammad bin ʿAbd al-Muʾmin bin Muḥammad bin Dhākir bin ʿAbd al-Muʾmin bin Abī al-Maʿālī bin Abī al-Khayr bin Dhākir al-Kāzarūnī, of Mecca, the muezzin and goldsmith. He was the father of Muḥammad, ʿAlī, and ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz. He heard from al-Imām Abū al-Yaman al-Ṭabarī a portion of the beginning of the Muwaṭṭaʾ of Ibn Bukayr and the Forty Selected by al-Aqfahsī from Abū Dāwūd. The author (al-Sakhāwī) states he does not know when he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D03061 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03061-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03061-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03061-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03061-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03061 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سالم بن عبد الوهاب المجد بن التاج الدمشقي القاهري خليفة المقام الأحمدي بطنتدا . وليه في حياة أبيه ثم وليه أبوه ، فلما مات أبوه أعيد المجد إليه وسمعت من يحكي أنه أعطى أباه السم وقد صاهر الشمس بن الزمن على ابنة أخته واستولدها ابنة اسمها أصيل ومات عنهما قريبا من سنة ثمانين تقريبا وخلفه في المشيخة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sālim ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Majd ibn al-Tāj al-Dimashqī al-Qāhirī, the successor (khalīfa) of the Aḥmadī shrine in Ṭantadā (Tanta). He held the office during his father's lifetime, then his father held it, and when his father died, the office was restored to him. It was rumored that he poisoned his father. He became related by marriage to al-Shams ibn al-Zaman by marrying his niece, with whom he had a daughter named Aṣīl. He died leaving them around the year 880 AH, and was succeeded in the mashyakha."@en .

rec:AIND-D03064 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03064-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03064-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03064-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03064-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03064 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سالم بن محمد بن ناصر البجائي الهواري المغربي ثم القاهري المديني نسبة لصحبة الشيخ مدين . ممن يديم التلاوة والقيام بالمرضى ونحوهم وملازمة خدمتهم محتسبا ، وقد حضر عندي كثيرا في السيرة وغيرها ونعم الرجل"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sālim b. Muḥammad b. Nāṣir al-Bijāʾī al-Hawwārī al-Maghribī, then al-Qāhirī, known as al-Madīnī due to his companionship with Shaykh Madyan. He was among those who constantly recited the Quran, cared for the sick, and dedicated themselves to serving them seeking reward from God. He attended my lectures many times, studying the Prophetic biography (al-Sīra) and other subjects; what an excellent man he was!"@en .

rec:AIND-D03066 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03066-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03066-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03066 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سالم الحوراني فقيه في بيت المقدس قرأ عليه القرآن الزين عبد القادر النووي"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sālim al-Ḥawrānī. A jurist in Jerusalem. Al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Nawāwī recited the Qurʾān under him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03067 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03067-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03067-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03067-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03067 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سالم الزواوي المغربي المالكي قاضيهم بدمشق ، مات بها في صفر سنة ثلاث وسبعين بالمدرسة الشرابشية منها ، وصلى عليه بالجامع ، ودفن بمقبرة الحميرية رحمه الله ، وينظر سالم بن إبراهيم الماضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sālim al-Zawāwī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī, their Qadi in Damascus. He died there in Safar, the year 873, at al-Sharābishiyya Madrasa. The funeral prayer was performed over him at the congregational mosque, and he was buried in al-Ḥimyarīya cemetery, may Allah have mercy on him. See Salim b. Ibrahim, aforementioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D03068 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03068-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03068-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03068-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03068 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سبع بن هجان بن محمد بن مسعود الحسني أمير الينبوع . وليها مرة بعد أخرى إلى أن مات في ذي الحجة سنة سبع وثمانين واستقر بعده دراج ابن مفري بتقرير من صاحب الحجاز لتفويض أمره إليه"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sabaʿ ibn Hajjān ibn Muḥammad ibn Masʿūd al-Ḥasanī, the emir of Yanbuʿ. He governed it time after time until he died in Dhu al-Hijjah, 887 AH. After him, Darrāj ibn Mufrī was established as governor by a decree from the ruler of al-Ḥijāz."@en .

rec:AIND-D03077 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03077-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03077-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03077-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03077 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد الله الناتولي أبو حميد التكروري المعتقد المقيم على باب جامع الحاكم . مات في المحرم سنة ست وخمسين ، ودفن بتربة قانم . أرخه ابن المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd Allāh al-Nātūlī, Abū Ḥamīd al-Takrūrī, the revered holy man who resided at the gate of al-Ḥākim Mosque. He died in al-Muharram, 856 AH, and was buried in the tomb of Qānim. His death was chronicled by Ibn al-Munīr."@en .

rec:AIND-D03078 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03078-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03078-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03078-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03078 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد الله رجل كان لا يزال واقفا تحت قلعة الجبل بالرميلة بحيث عده كثير من الناس في طائفة المجاذيب . مات في صفر سنة أربع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd Allāh. A man who used to stand constantly under the Citadel (Qalʿat al-Jabal) in al-Rumayla, such that many people considered him among the majādhīb (ecstatics/holy fools). He died in Safar, the year 854 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03079 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03079-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03079-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03079 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد بن إبراهيم بن محمد الحضرمي الأندلسي المغربي التاجر والد إبراهيم الحربي المالكي الماضي . مات في شوال سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-Ḥaḍramī al-Andalusī al-Maghribī, the merchant. He was the father of the previously mentioned Maliki scholar Ibrāhīm al-Ḥarbī. He died in Shawwāl, 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03080 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03080-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03080-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03080 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد بن أحمد بن علي المكي البنا ويعرف أبوه بابن ناصر . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Makkī al-Bannāʾ. His father was known as Ibn Nāṣir. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03081 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03081-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03081 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد بن أحمد بن منصور سعد الدين العطار بمكة ويعرف بسعد الوركان شيخ العطارين بباب السلام ، وعنده دخول . مات في شعبان سنة اثنتين وستين وخلف ذرية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd b. Aḥmad b. Manṣūr Saʿd al-Dīn al-ʿAṭṭār, in Mecca. He was known as Saʿd al-Warkān, the chief (shaykh) of the druggists at Bāb al-Salām, and he had access [to influential people]. He died in Shaʿbān, in the year 862 AH, leaving descendants."@en .

rec:AIND-D03083 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03083-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03083-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03083 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد بن عبد الله سعد الدين الآمدي ثم الطرابلسي الشافعي . أقام بطرابلس مدة يشغل الناس في الحاوي ويفتي قليلا ، وكان فاضلا في الأصول ويحل الحاوي ، ولكن لم يكن محمودا في دينه . مات في إحدى الجمادين سنة اثنتين وثلاثين . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ثم ابن قاضي شهبة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd b. ʿAbd Allāh Saʿd al-Dīn al-Āmidī, later al-Ṭarābulusī al-Shāfiʿī. He resided in Tripoli (Ṭarābulus) for a period, occupying people with (teaching them) 『al-Ḥāwī』 and occasionally issuing fatwas. He was accomplished in uṣūl (legal principles) and could resolve the problems of 『al-Ḥāwī』, but he was not well-regarded in his religious piety. He died in one of the two months of Jumada in the year 832 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』, and subsequently Ibn Qāḍī Shuhba mentioned him as well."@en .

rec:AIND-D03085 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03085-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03085-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03085-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b56_58_followup,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03085 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد بن عبد الله الحضرمي خادم عبد الرحمن بن اليافعي ثم عمر العرابي مدة تزيد على عشرين عاما وكان صاحب ايثار وفتوة وانصاف ومروءة اعجوبة في جده واجتهاده وعبادته كأهل حضرموت ممن ذكر باجابة الدعوة . مات بالطائف سنة ثمان عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥaḍramī. He served as a servant to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Yāfiʿī, and subsequently to ʿUmar al-ʿUrābī, for a period exceeding twenty years. He was characterized by selflessness, chivalry, equity, and virtue, and was remarkable for his diligence, devotion, and worship, resembling the people of Hadramaut whose prayers are said to be answered. He died in al-Ṭāʾif in the year 818 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03087 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03087-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03087-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03087 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد بن علي بن يوسف بن محمد بن يوسف بن إسماعيل بن نصر بن الأحمر صاحب غرناطة الأندلس ووالد أبي الحسن علي وأبي عبد الله محمد . ذكرته استطرادا في حوادث سنة ست وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf b. Ismāʿīl b. Naṣr b. al-Aḥmar, the ruler of Granada in al-Andalus, and the father of Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad. I mentioned him in passing in the events of the year 896 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03091 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03091-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03091-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03091-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03091-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03091 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد بن محمد بن عبد الله الحضرمي ثم المكي ويعرف بسعد الدين أبي جمال . مات بدمشق في أوائل سنة أربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥaḍramī, later al-Makkī. He was known as Saʿd al-Dīn Abū Jamāl. He died in Damascus in the early part of the year 840 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03093 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03093-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03093-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03093 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد بن محمد بن يوسف الأسيوطي القاهري الشافعي أخو أبي الحجاج الآتي . اشتغل وأخذ عن القاياتي وغيره . مات في الطاعون سنة ثلاث وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf al-Asyūṭī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, the brother of Abū al-Ḥajjāj who is mentioned below. He occupied himself with study and took knowledge from al-Qāyātī and others. He died of the plague in the year 833 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03096 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03096-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03096-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03096 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد الحضرمي آخر . نزل مكة وكان خرازا . مات بها في ربيع الآخر سنة تسع وسبعين ودفن بالشبيكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Another Saʿd al-Ḥaḍramī. He settled in Mecca and was a cobbler (shoemaker). He died there in Rabiʿ al-Akhir, the year 879 AH, and was buried in al-Shabīka."@en .

rec:AIND-D03097 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03097-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03097-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03097 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعد الشهير بالسمنودي . مات في توجهه للقاهرة تائها برابغ سنة ثمان وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿd, known as al-Samanūdī. He died in the year 838 after getting lost in Rābigh while traveling to Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03098 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03098-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03098-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03098 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سعيد بن إبراهيم بن سعيد البرعي اليماني الشهير بسعيد الجبل . مات بمكة في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Saʿīd b. Ibrāhīm b. Saʿīd al-Burʿī al-Yamānī, famously known as Saʿīd al-Jabal. He died in Mecca in Rabi' al-Akhir, 842 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03205 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03205-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03205-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03205 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون البردبكي الظاهري برقوق من صغار مماليكه ، وتأمر عشرة بعد موت المؤيد شيخ ثم ولاه الظاهر جقمق نيابة دمياط واستمر بها حتى مات في سنة خمسين ، وكان عفيفا عن المنكرات والفروج مهملا في الدول ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūdūn al-Bardabakī al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq. He was one of the junior mamluks of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq. He was promoted to amir of ten after the death of al-Muʾayyad Shaykh, and was later appointed as the vicegerent (nāʾib) of Damietta by al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq, remaining in this post until his death in 850 AH. He was chaste, avoiding abominations and illicit relations, but was negligent in state affairs."@en .

rec:AIND-D03206 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03206-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03206-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03206-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03206 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون البردبكي المؤيدي شيخ أحد العشرات . ممن ولي الحسبة أيام الظاهر خشقدم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūdūn al-Bardbakī al-Muʾayyadī. A shaykh and one of the commanders of ten (amīr ʿashara). He was among those who were appointed to the office of market inspector (ḥisba) during the reign of Sultan al-Ẓāhir Khushqadam."@en .

rec:AIND-D03211 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03211-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03211-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03211 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون الحموي . أحد المقدمين بدمشق وأتابكها وكان قبل ذلك من أمراء القاهرة فنفاه الأشرف إلى دمياط بعد أن حبسه مدة ثم أرسله إلى الشام عوضا عن قانباي الحمزاوي في الأتابكية والتقدمة فمات بها في أوائل ذي القعدة سنة سبع وعشرين . ذكره العيني :"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūdūn al-Ḥamawī. One of the commanders (muqaddams) and the Atabak (commander-in-chief) of Damascus. Prior to that, he was one of the amirs of Cairo. Sultan al-Ashraf (Barsbāy) imprisoned him for a period and then exiled him to Damietta. Later, he was sent to al-Shām (Damascus) to replace Qānibāy al-Ḥamzāwī as Atabak and commander (muqaddam). He died there in early Dhu al-Qaʿda, in the year 827 AH. Al-ʿAynī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03212 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03212-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03212-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03212-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03212-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_58_followup,
        agent:claude_b56_review,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03212 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون دقماق الخاصكي والد الناصري محمد سبط ناصر الدين ابن العطار أمه عائشة . قتله جماعة من فلاحيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūdūn Duqmāq al-Khāṣṣakī, the father of al-Nāṣirī Muḥammad, the maternal grandson of Nāṣir al-Dīn Ibn al-ʿAṭṭār, whose mother was ʿĀʾisha. He was killed by a group of his peasants."@en .

rec:AIND-D03215 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03215-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03215-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03215 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون السودوني أمير عشرة وأميراخور السلطان ، مات في رمضان سنة سبع وثلاثين وكان جيدا مشكور السيرة . ذكره العيني."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūdūn al-Sūdūnī. An emir of ten (amīr ʿashara) and the Sultan's master of the stable (amīr ākhūr). He died in Ramaḍān in the year 837 AH. He was good and of praiseworthy conduct. Al-ʿAynī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03228 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03228-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03228-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03228-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03228 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون الظاهري جقمق ويعرف بالافرم . تأمر في أيام ابنه المنصور عشرة ثم نكب وحبس ثم أطلق ، وقدم القاهرة وأنعم عليه بعد مدة بامرة عشرة ثم صار في أيام الظاهر خشقدم خازندارا ثم طبلخاناه ومات في ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūdūn al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq, known as al-Afram. He was appointed as an amir of ten during the reign of al-Manṣūr (ʿUthmān), the son of his master (Jaqmaq). Later, he fell from favor, was imprisoned, and then released. He arrived in Cairo, where after some time he was granted an emirate of ten. During the reign of al-Ẓāhir Khushqadam, he became a khāzindār (treasurer), and then rose to the rank of amir of tablkhānāh (forty). He died in [the text abruptly ends here]."@en .

rec:AIND-D03233 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03233-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03233-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03233 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون اللكاشي أقبغا ، اتصل بعده بالأمير شيخ فلما تسلطن أمره ثم رقاه إلى التقدمة وقبض عليه ططر في نظامته وحبسه إلى أن أطلقه الأشرف وأنعم عليه بطبلخاناه بطرابلس فأقام بها حتى مات في حدود الثلاثين ولم يكن من الأعيان"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūdūn al-Lakkāshī, [mamlūk of] Aqbughā. After him [his first master Aqbughā], he attached himself to Amir Shaykh. When Shaykh became sultan, he appointed him as an amir, then promoted him to the rank of Taqdima (commander of a thousand). Ṭaṭar arrested and imprisoned him during his administration, until al-Ashraf [Barsbāy] released him and granted him a Tablkhānāh (command of forty) in Tripoli. He resided there until his death around the year 830 AH. He was not among the prominent notables."@en .

rec:AIND-D03238 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03238-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03238-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03238-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03238 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون المنصوري عثمان من أمراء العشرات وأحد رؤس النوب . مات في ليلة الجمعة ثامن عشر جمادى الأولى سنة تسع وسبعين ، ويقال انه سقط وهو ثمل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sudūn al-Manṣūrī ʿUthmān. He was an amir of ten and one of the chiefs of the guards (ra's nawba). He died on the night of Friday, 18 Jumada al-Ula, 879 AH. It is said that he fell while drunk."@en .

rec:AIND-D03239 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03239-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03239-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03239-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03239 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون النوروزي نوروز الحافظي نائب الشام ويعرف بسودون العجمي أحد العشرات ورؤس النوب . ممن تأمر في أيام الظاهر جقمق . مات في حدود الخمسين ، وكان فيما قيل مهملا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūdūn al-Nawrūzī, the mamlūk of Nawrūz al-Ḥāfiẓī and vice-roy of Syria. He was known as Sūdūn al-ʿAjamī. He was one of the amīrs of ten and heads of the guard (raʾs nawba). He was promoted to the rank of amīr during the reign of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq. He died around 850 AH, and it was said that he was of little consequence."@en .

rec:AIND-D03243 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03243-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03243-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03243 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون اليوسفي . ممن حبسه المؤيد شيخ بقلعة دمشق ، ولم أر من ترجمه ولكن علمت اسمه من أثناء سودون المحمدي تلي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūdūn al-Yūsufī. He was among those imprisoned by Sultan al-Muʾayyad Shaykh in the Citadel of Damascus. al-Sakhāwī notes that he did not find a dedicated biography for him, but learned his name from within the entry of Sūdūn al-Muḥammadī Tālī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03244 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03244-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03244-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03244-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03244 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سودون غير منسوب ، ممن سمع من شيخنا الاملاء سنة عشر بالشيخونية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūdūn, unaffiliated. He heard the dictation of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in the year 810 AH at al-Shaykhūniyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D03246 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03246-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03246-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03246-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03246 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سونجبغا الظاهري برقوق الفقيه . كان من خاصكية سيده . اشتغل كثيرا ولم يكن به بأس لكن كان بليدا . مات في شوال سنة خمس عشرة ودفن بالصحراء خارج باب البرقية . ذكره العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sūnjbughā al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq, the jurist. He was one of the personal guards (khāṣṣakiyya) of his master (Barqūq). He studied extensively; there was no harm in him, but he was dull-witted. He died in Shawwāl in the year 815 AH and was buried in the desert (al-Ṣaḥrāʾ) outside Bāb al-Barqiyya. Mentioned by al-ʿAynī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03247 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03247-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03247-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03247 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سويدان مقدم الوالي عدى عليه في ليلة رابع عشري صفر سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Suwaydan, the commander of the governor's guard (muqaddam al-wali). He was assaulted (assassinated) on the night of 24 Safar, year [8]91."@en .

rec:AIND-D03248 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03248-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03248-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03248 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سيباي الأشرفي إينال نائب غزة ثم حاجب دمشق ثم نيابة حماة وهو أخو قانصوة . مات في التجريدة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sībāy al-Ashrafī Īnāl. Viceroy (nāʾib) of Gaza, then chamberlain (ḥājib) of Damascus, and then viceroy of Hama. He was the brother of Qānṣawh. He died during a military expedition (al-tajrīda)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03249 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03249-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03249-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03249-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03249 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سيباي الظاهري جقمق أميراخور ثالث وحاجب ميسرة . مات في رمضان سنة ثمانين ، ونزل السلطان فصلى عليه في سبيل المؤمني وكان فيما قيل خيرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sībāy al-Ẓāhirī Jaqmaq, third amīr ākhūr and chamberlain of the left (ḥājib maysara). He died in Ramaḍān 880; the sultan came down and prayed over him at Sabīl (Muṣallā) al-Muʾminī. He was, it is said, a good man."@en .

rec:AIND-D03252 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03252-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03252-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03252-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03252 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سيف بن شكر البدري الحسني القائد . مات بمكة في مستهل المحرم سنة سبع وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sayf b. Shukr al-Badrī al-Ḥasanī, the commander (al-qāʾid). He died in Mecca at the beginning of Muḥarram 877. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03254 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03254-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03254-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03254 ;
    aindv:sourceText "سيف بن ... بن جبير . | حرف الشين المعجمة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sayf b. ... b. Jubayr."@en .

rec:AIND-D03255 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03255-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03255-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03255 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاذ بك الأشرفي برسباي ويعرف بفرفور أتابك حماة . مات في الوقعة السوارية سنة اثنتين وسبعين وقد زاد على الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shādh Bak al-Ashrafī Barsbāy, known as Farfūr, atābak of Ḥamā. He died in the Suwāriyya battle in 872, having passed fifty."@en .

rec:AIND-D03259 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03259-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03259-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03259 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاذ بك الجلباني أتابك دمشق وصاحب المدرسة التي بالقنوات منها . مات في جمادى الثانية سنة سبع وثمانين ودفن بمدرسته . أخبرني بذلك امامها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shādh Bak al-Jalbānī, atābak of Damascus and founder of the madrasa in al-Qanawāt there. He died in Jumādā II 887 and was buried in his madrasa; its imām informed me of this."@en .

rec:AIND-D03261 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03261-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03261-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03261 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاذ بك من صديق الاشرفي برسباي شاد العمائر السلطانية وأحد العشرات عوضا عن بردبك المحمدي الطويل . ممن رقاه الأشرف قايتباي للامرة وغيرها ، وسافر في التجاريد غير مرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shādh Bak min Ṣiddīq al-Ashrafī Barsbāy, superintendent of the royal buildings (shādd al-ʿamāʾir al-sulṭāniyya) and one of the amirs of ten, in place of Bardbak al-Muḥammadī al-Ṭawīl. He was among those whom al-Ashraf Qāytbāy promoted to an amirate and other posts, and he went out on expeditions more than once."@en .

rec:AIND-D03262 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03262-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03262-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03262-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03262 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاذ بك طاز الخاصكي أحد مماليك الأشرف اينال . مات بالطاعون في يوم الأحد منتصف ربيع الأول سنة أربع وستين وهو أول مطعون فيما قيل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shādh Bak Ṭāz al-Khāṣṣakī, one of the mamlūks of al-Ashraf Īnāl. He died of the plague on Sunday in mid-Rabīʿ I 864, and was, it is said, the first person struck by that plague."@en .

rec:AIND-D03263 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03263-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03263-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03263-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03263 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاذ بك الفقيه . أمير الراكز بمكة والمستقر بعد بيبرس الطويل . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة اثنتين وتسعين واستقر بعده ازدمر قصبة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shādh Bak al-Faqīh, amīr al-rākiz in Mecca, appointed after Baybars al-Ṭawīl. He died in Jumādā I 892, and Azdamur Qaṣaba was appointed after him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03264 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03264-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03264-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03264 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاذ بك الفقيه . مات سنة أربع وستين فينظر إن لم يكن أحد من سلف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shādh Bak al-Faqīh. He died in 864; it should be examined whether he is not one of those who preceded."@en .

rec:AIND-D03265 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03265-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03265-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03265-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03265-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03265 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاذ بك دوادار قجماس نائب الشام . قتل في مصاففة بين عسكر الأشرف وعلى دولات بمكان يقال له الأندرين في صفر سنة تسع وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shādh Bak, dawādār of Qajmās, viceroy of Syria. He was killed in the pitched battle between the army of al-Ashraf (Qāytbāy) and ʿAlī Dawlāt (ʿAlāʾ al-Dawla) at a place called al-Andarīn, in Ṣafar 889."@en .

rec:AIND-D03266 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03266-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03266-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03266 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاذي الهندي عتيق السراج عبد اللطيف قاضي الحنابلة بمكة . مات بمكة في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shādhī al-Hindī, freedman of al-Sirāj ʿAbd al-Laṭīf, the Ḥanbalī qāḍī of Mecca. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Qaʿda 881."@en .

rec:AIND-D03268 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03268-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03268-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03268 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شارع بن سرعان بن أحمد بن حسن بن عجلان الحسني المكي . مات بها في جمادى الآخرة سنة خمس وستين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāriʿ b. Surʿān b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Jumādā II 865."@en .

rec:AIND-D03269 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03269-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03269-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03269 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شار بن إبراهيم بن حسن بن عجلان الحسني . مات في ربيع الأول سنة ثمانين بصوب اليمن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shār b. Ibrāhīm b. Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān al-Ḥasanī. He died in Rabīʿ I 880 in the direction of Yemen."@en .

rec:AIND-D03272 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03272-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03272-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03272-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03272 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاه رخ القان معين الدين سلطان بن تيمور ملك الشرق وسلطان ما وراء النهر وخراسان وخوارزم وعراق العجم ومازندران ومملكة دلي من الهند وكرمان وأذربيجان . ذكره المقريزي في عقوده مطولا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāh Rukh al-Qān Muʿīn al-Dīn, Sultan, son of Tīmūr. King of the East, and Sultan of Transoxiana, Khurāsān, Khwārazm, ʿIrāq al-ʿAjam, Māzandarān, the kingdom of Delhi in India, Kirmān, and Azerbaijan. Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him at length in his ʿUqūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03273 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03273-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03273-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03273 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الاشرفي أحد الحجاب قتل في تجريدة البحيرة على يد العرب في سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Ashrafī, one of the chamberlains (ḥujjāb). He was killed during a military expedition (tajrīda) to al-Buḥayra at the hands of the Arabs in the year 868 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03275 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03275-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03275-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03275 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الايدكاري الناصري أحد أمراء حلب وهو غير الذي قبله بل هو متأخر عنه جدا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Aydkārī al-Nāṣirī, one of the amirs of Aleppo. He is not the one before him (Shāhīn al-Afram); rather, he is much later than him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03277 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03277-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03277-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03277-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03277-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03277 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الحسني الطواشي تقدم في دولة الناصر وحج بالناس وولي نظر البيبرسية وغيرها . ذكره العيني وأرخ وفاته سنة خمس عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Ḥasanī al-Ṭawāshī. He advanced during the reign of al-Nāṣir (Faraj), led the people on the pilgrimage, and held the trusteeship (naẓar) of the Baybarsiyya and other posts. Al-ʿAynī mentioned him and recorded his death in the year 815 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03278 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03278-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03278-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03278 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين دست الاشرفي الجمدار . مات سنة سبع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn Dist al-Ashrafī al-Jamdār. He died in the year 807 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03280 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03280-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03280-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03280 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الرومي النوري الانبابي نائب كاتب السر . قرأ القرآن وجود الكتابة على البرهان الفرنوي ثم يس وتميز فيها ، وكتب عدة مصاحف وغيرها وقدم بعضها للاشرف قايتباي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Rūmī al-Nūrī al-Anbābī, deputy confidential secretary (nāʾib kātib al-sirr). He read the Qur'an and perfected his handwriting under al-Burhān al-Farnawī and then under Yāsīn, excelling in it. He wrote several copies of the Qur'an and other works, and presented some of them to al-Ashraf Qāytbāy."@en .

rec:AIND-D03283 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03283-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03283-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03283 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الزردكاش . كان أحد المقدمين بالقاهرة ثم صار حاجب حجاب دمشق ثم نائب حماة ثم طرابلس إلى أن عزله ططر عنها ودام بها بطالا إلى أن مات في حدود الأربعين وورثه الشهاب أحمد بن علي بن اينال لكونه مولى لأبيه أو جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Zardakāsh. He was one of the commanders (muqaddams) in Cairo, then became grand chamberlain (ḥājib al-ḥujjāb) of Damascus, then governor (nāʾib) of Ḥamāh, then of Tripoli, until Ṭaṭar dismissed him from it. He remained in Tripoli without office until he died around 840 AH. Al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Īnāl inherited from him, since he had been a client (mawlā) of Aḥmad's father or grandfather."@en .

rec:AIND-D03284 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03284-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03284-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03284 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الزيني عبد الباسط ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Zaynī ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ (mamlūk of Zayn al-Dīn ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03285 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03285-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03285-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03285 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين نزيل الباسطية وأظنه مملوك واقفها . كان خيرا يتفقه ويجيد الخط ويتدين . مات في رمضان سنة خمس أو ست وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn, resident of al-Bāsiṭiyya; I think he was a mamlūk of its founder (Zayn al-Dīn ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ). He was a good man who studied law, wrote a fine hand, and was pious. He died in Ramaḍān 895 or 896 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03286 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03286-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03286-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03286 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الزيني يحيى الاستادار ويعرف بالفقيه. كان دوادارا رابعا عند الأشرف قايتباي بعد أن كان خصيصا عند مولاه ، وكان خيرا بالنسبة لأبناء جنسه محبا في العلماء والصلحاء وربما اشتغل . مات في رجب سنة تسع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Zaynī (mamlūk of al-Zayn Yaḥyā al-Ustādār), known as al-Faqīh. He was fourth dawādār under al-Ashraf Qāytbāy, after having been a close attendant of his master (Yaḥyā). He was virtuous compared with others of his kind, loved the scholars and the pious, and sometimes occupied himself with study. He died in Rajab of the year 879."@en .

rec:AIND-D03287 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03287-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03287-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03287-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03287-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03287 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين السعدي الطواشي اللالا . خدم الاشرف فمن بعده وتقدم في دولة الناصر ، وولي نظر البيبرسية وغيرها . مات في سنة ثمان . أرخه شيخنا وأظنه شاهين الحسنى الماضي قريبا وأحد التاريخين غلط ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Saʿdī al-Ṭawāshī al-Lālā. He served al-Ashraf (Shaʿbān) and those after him, rose to prominence under al-Nāṣir (Faraj), and held the trusteeship (naẓar) of the Baybarsiyya and other posts. He died in the year [8]08. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death, but I think he is the Shāhīn al-Ḥasanī mentioned shortly before, and that one of the two dates is wrong."@en .

rec:AIND-D03288 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03288-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03288-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03288-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03288 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الشجاعي . ولي نيابة القدس ودوادارية السلطان بدمشق . مات في تاسع عشر ذي القعدة سنة سبع وثلاثين . أرخه ابن اللبودي"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Shujāʿī. He held the vicegerency (niyāba) of Jerusalem and the office of the sultan's dawādār in Damascus. He died on the nineteenth of Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year 837. Ibn al-Lubūdī recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03289 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03289-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03289-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03289-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03289 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الشجاعي ، ولي حجوبية دمشق ، وحج بالركب الشامي وولي نيابة القلعة بدمشق . مات بها في شوال سنة أربع وأربعين أرخه ابن اللبودي أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Shujāʿī. He held the chamberlainship (ḥujūbiyya) of Damascus, performed the pilgrimage with the Syrian caravan, and held the vicegerency of the citadel of Damascus. He died there in Shawwāl of the year 844. Ibn al-Lubūdī also recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03293 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03293-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03293-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03293 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الفارسي ، ممن أنشأه المؤيد إلى أن صيره أحد المقدمين ثم قبض عليه ططر في أيام نظاميته وحبسه باسكندرية في المحرم سنة أربع وعشرين ، وكان من الفرسان ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Fārisī. He was one of those whom al-Muʾayyad (Shaykh) raised, until he made him one of the commanders (muqaddams). Then Ṭaṭar seized him during the days of his regency and imprisoned him in Alexandria in Muḥarram of the year 824. He was, it is thought, one of the horsemen (fursān)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03294 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03294-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03294-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03294-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03294 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين قصقا ومعناه القصير . كان من الخاصكية فنقله الناصر شيئا بعد شيء حتى صار أحد المقدمين ومات عن قرب في ذي القعدة سنة عشر ودفن في حوش الظاهر . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه وكذا العيني وقال انه ما اشتهر بخير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn Qaṣqā, which means \"the short one\". He was one of the khāṣṣakiyya, and al-Nāṣir (Faraj) advanced him step by step until he became one of the commanders (muqaddams). He died shortly afterwards, in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year [8]10, and was buried in Ḥawsh al-Ẓāhir. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ, as did al-ʿAynī, who said that he was not known for any good."@en .

rec:AIND-D03295 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03295-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03295-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03295-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03295 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين الكمالي بن البارزى مملوكه وخازنداره . مات بالطاعون في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn al-Kamālī (mamlūk of al-Kamāl) Ibn al-Bārizī, his mamlūk and his treasurer (khāzindār). He died of the plague in Ṣafar of the year 853."@en .

rec:AIND-D03297 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03297-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03297-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03297 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شاهين نائب الكرك أحد من شهر بالشجاعة والقروسية ، مات في سنة ست وعشرين . أرخه العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shāhīn, the viceroy (nāʾib) of al-Karak. He was one of those famed for bravery and horsemanship. He died in the year 826. Al-ʿAynī recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03299 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03299-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03299-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03299 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شتوان بن بيدر المليكشي . مات سنة أربع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shatwān b. Baydar al-Malīkshī. He died in the year 834."@en .

rec:AIND-D03300 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03300-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03300-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03300 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شحاتة بن فرج الأحمر مولى بني عباس شيوخ فيشا . مات سنة اثنتين وتسعين تقريبا وقد جاز السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shaḥāta b. Faraj al-Aḥmar, a client (mawlā) of Banū ʿAbbās, the sheikhs of Fīshā. He died in approximately 892 AH, having lived past seventy years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D03301 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03301-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03301-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03301 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شربش بن عبد الله بن علي بن جسار بن عبد الله بن عمر بن مسعود العمري . مات في جمادى الثانية سنة ستين خارج مكة وحمل فدفن بمعلاتها ، أرخه ابن فهد ، وهو بمعجمتين وفتحات ثلاث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sharabash b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Jasār b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Masʿūd al-ʿUmarī. He died in Jamādā al-Thāniya, in the year 860, outside Mecca, and was carried and buried in its al-Muʿallā cemetery. Ibn Fahd recorded his biography. His name is spelled with two dotted letters [shīn] and three fatḥas (i.e. Sharabash)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03302 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03302-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03302-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03302 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شرعان بن أحمد بن حسن بن عجلان الشريف الحسني الماضي ولده شارع مات بمكة في جمادى الآخرة سنة ثلاث وستين ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sharʿān b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān, al-Sharīf al-Ḥasanī, whose son Shāriʿ was mentioned previously. He died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ākhira in the year 863 AH, as dated by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03304 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03304-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03304-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03304 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شرف بن عبد العزيز بن قاسم شرف الدين المدني المالكي . أحد الفراشين بالمدينة وأخو أبي الفرج محمد الآتي ويعرف كل منهما بابن قاسم . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sharaf b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Qāsim Sharaf al-Dīn al-Madanī al-Mālikī. One of the attendants (farrāshīn) in Medina, and the brother of Abū al-Faraj Muḥammad, who is mentioned below. Both of them are known as Ibn Qāsim. He heard (ḥadīth) from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03306 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03306-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03306-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03306 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شرف القواس . أديب شاعر ناظم ناثر أفرد من نظمه القاضي سري الدين عبد الظاهر بن الذهبي ديوانا ومنه قوله : %~% فوض إلى الله أمرا أنت قاصده %~% واعلم بأن سمين المكر مهزول %~% %~% والبغي سوف يعاني قتل صاحبه %~% وحاكم الغدر بالتفويض معزول %~% مات بدمشق في جمادى الآخرة سنة اثنتين وثلاثين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sharaf al-Qawwās. A man of letters, poet, and writer of prose and verse. Qāḍī Sarī al-Dīn ʿAbd al-Ẓāhir b. al-Dhahabī compiled a separate dīwān (collection) of his poetry, which includes his verses: 'Entrust your affairs to God, whom you seek, and know that bloated cunning is ultimately withered.' 'Injustice will surely plague its perpetrator with death, and the treacherous ruler is deposed through [divine] delegation.' He died in Damascus in Jumādā al-Ākhira, the year 832 [AH]. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03307 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03307-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03307-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03307 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شرف الملك الحسيني باشر نقابة الاشراف بدمشق ، وبها مات في ربيع الآخر سنة خمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sharaf al-Mulk al-Husayni. He administered the marshalship of the Alids (niqābat al-ashrāf) in Damascus, where he died in Rabi' al-Akhir, the year 850 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03309 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03309-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03309-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03309 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شعبان بن داود الآثاري . في ابن محمد بن داود ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D03310 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03310-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03310-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03310 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شعبان بن حسن بن كبة ابن أخت علي بن صدقة من أهل اسكندرية وتجارها . رأيته بمكة في سنة ثمان وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shaʿbān b. Ḥasan b. Kubba, the nephew (sister's son) of ʿAlī b. Ṣadaqa. He was one of the residents of Alexandria and its merchants. I saw him in Mecca in the year 898 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03321 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03321-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03321-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03321 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شعبان أبو رجب عامي خير مديم للجماعات خصوصا في الصبح بالمنكوتمرية ولا ينفك في مجيئه له عن قنديل يستضيء منه أهلها . مات سنة ست وخمسين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sha'bān Abū Rajab. A good and pious commoner who regularly attended congregational prayers, particularly the dawn prayer (ṣubḥ) at the Mankūtamuriyya Madrasa. He never failed to bring a lamp with him when coming to it, which the people there would use for light. He died in the year 856 AH. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03322 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03322-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03322-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03322-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03322-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03322-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:Takao_Ito,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03322 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شعبان صهر البدر بن الحلاوي والد زوجته أم ولده أبي بكر وغيره وبواب دار الضرب مات في ذي القعدة سنة خمس وأربعين وهو متوجه لمكة قبل الاحرام بيوم واستقر بعده في دار الضرب صهره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shaʿbān. Son-in-law of al-Badr b. al-Ḥallāwī (the father of his wife, who was the mother of his son Abū Bakr and others). He was the gatekeeper of the Mint (Dār al-Ḍarb). He died in the month of Dhu al-Qaʿda in the year 845 AH while heading to Mecca, one day before entering the state of ihram. His son-in-law succeeded him in his position at the Mint."@en .

rec:AIND-D03325 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03325-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03325-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03325 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شفارة المعلم الجرائحي ، مات سنة خمس وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shifāra, known as al-Muʿallim al-Jarāʾiḥī (the master surgeon). He died in the year 855 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03326 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03326-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03326-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03326-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03326 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شفيع بن علي بن مبارك بن رميثة الشريف الحسني المكي . مات بها في المحرم سنة تسع وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shafīʿ b. ʿAlī b. Mubārak b. Rumaytha, the Sharīf, al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Muharram, the year 859 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03327 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03327-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03327-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03327 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شقرون الجبلي المغربي . كان صالحا زاهدا . مات تقريبا سنة ستين . ومن نظمه : %~% شربت عتيقا فاستنار بسره %~% فؤادي وأهدى نشره لجوارحي %~% %~% فصرت بلا روح تشعشع في الورى %~% وما ذاك إلا من بوارق سابحي %~% أفادنيه بعض أصحابنا المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shaqrun al-Jabali al-Maghribi. He was a righteous and ascetic man. He died approximately in the year 860 AH. Among his poetry is the following: 'I drank an aged wine, and my heart was illuminated by its secret, sending its fragrance throughout my limbs. Thus I became as one without a soul, radiating among humankind; and that is none other than from the flashes of my inner light.' Some of our Maghribi companions communicated these verses to me."@en .

rec:AIND-D03329 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03329-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03329-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03329 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شكم المكي شيخ للسفل . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة ثلاث وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shakam al-Makkī, shaykh of the commoners. He died in Mecca in Muharram, year 883 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03331 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03331-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03331-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03331 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شمس بن عطاء الله الهروي . في محمد ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D03332 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03332-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03332-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03332 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شمس العقعق التاجر . هو محمد بن محمد بن يوسف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shams al-ʿAqʿaq the merchant. He is Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf."@en .

rec:AIND-D03335 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03335-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03335-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03335 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شند الطواشي أحد خدام المدينة النبوية . أصيب في الحريق الكائن بها في رمضان سنة ست وثمانين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shand al-Ṭawāshī, one of the servants of the Prophet's City (Medina). He was afflicted and died in the fire that broke out there in Ramadan, 886 AH. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03336 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03336-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03336-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03336-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03336 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شهاب الاسلام الكرماني الشافعي . قدم شيراز فأخذ عنه ابن السيد عفيف الدين ووصفه بالعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shihāb al-Islām al-Kirmānī al-Shāfiʿī. He came to Shiraz, where Ibn al-Sayyid ʿAfīf al-Dīn studied under him and described him as learned."@en .

rec:AIND-D03337 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03337-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03337-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03337 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شهاب بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن مخلوف ابن أخت الأمين بن النجار . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shihāb b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Makhlūf, the nephew (sister's son) of al-Amīn b. al-Najjār. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03338 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03338-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03338-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03338 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شهوان بن عجل بن رميح السيد النموي صهر صاحب مكة على إحدى بناته وأمه أيضا فاطمة ابنة بركات . مات في سنة اثنتين وتسعين وصلى عليه بمكة ثم دفن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shahwān b. ʿAjl b. Rumayḥ, al-Sayyid al-Numawī. He was the son-in-law of the ruler of Mecca, having married one of his daughters. His mother too was Fāṭima, the daughter of Barakāt. He died in the year 892 AH, and the funeral prayer was performed for him in Mecca, where he was then buried."@en .

rec:AIND-D03339 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03339-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03339-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03339 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شيخي بن محمد بن علي الخواجا التبريزي . مات بمكة في شعبان سنة خمس وستين ، أرخه ابن فهد ، ورأيته في تاريخ مكة سمى أباه أحمد ابن علي ، وقال الدباغ سكن مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shaykhī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Khawājā al-Tabrīzī. He died in Mecca in Shaʿbān, in the year 865. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date, and I saw in the 'History of Mecca' that his father was named Aḥmad b. ʿAlī. Al-Dabbāgh stated that he resided in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03343 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03343-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03343-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03343 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شيخ السليمانى الظاهري برقوق ويعرف بالمسرطن ، تنقل في عدة نيابات منها طرابلس ، ومات في ربيع الآخر سنة ثمان خارج دمشق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shaykh al-Sulaymānī al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq, known as al-Musarṭan. He held several deputy governorships, including Tripoli, and died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir, year 808 AH, outside Damascus."@en .

rec:AIND-D03346 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03346-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03346-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03346 ;
    aindv:sourceText "شيفكي إمام الدين . كان بحرا في العربية ممن أخذ عن السيد الجرجاني وعنه عبد الأول المرشدي بمكة وهو ترجمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Shīfkī Imām al-Dīn. He was deeply learned in Arabic philology, being among those who acquired knowledge from al-Sayyid al-Jurjānī. From him, ʿAbd al-Awwal al-Murshidī acquired knowledge in Mecca, and the latter wrote his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D03352 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03352-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03352-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03352 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صالح بن صالح وزير فاس . مات سنة بضع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣāliḥ b. Ṣāliḥ, Vizier of Fez. He died in the forties [of the ninth Hijri century] (biḍʿ wa-arbaʿīn, i.e. 843–849 AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03353 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03353-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03353-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03353 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صالح بن عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الله السلجماسي المغربي نزيل مكة فهرس كتب رباط الموفق بها في سنة ثمان وسبعين ومات بعد ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣāliḥ b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Sijilmāsī al-Maghribī, a resident of Mecca. He catalogued the books of Ribāṭ al-Muwaffaq there in the year 878 AH, and died after that."@en .

rec:AIND-D03355 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03355-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03355-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03355 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صالح بن عوض بن غنيم بن محمد بن صالح قاضي الزيدية ينبوع مات سنة ست وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣāliḥ b. ʿAwaḍ b. Ghunaym b. Muḥammad b. Ṣāliḥ, the qāḍī of the Zaydiyyah in Yanbuʿ. He died in the year 866 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03356 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03356-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03356-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03356 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صالح بن عيسى بن ماضي المغربي . ممن سمع اختلاف الحديث للشافعي بقراءتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣāliḥ b. ʿĪsā b. Māḍī al-Maghribī. He is among those who heard al-Shāfiʿī's Ikhtilāf al-Ḥadīth through my [al-Sakhāwī's] recitation."@en .

rec:AIND-D03360 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03360-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03360-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03360 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صالح بن محمد بن أحمد بن داود اليافوري فقيه المالكية بالتكرور . مات سنة ثلاث وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣāliḥ b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Dāwūd al-Yāfūrī, the Maliki jurist in al-Takrūr. He died in the year 843 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03361 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03361-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03361-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03361 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صالح بن محمد بن علي الناشري . في أخيه أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣāliḥ b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Nāshirī. [His biography is found] under the entry of his brother Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D03364 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03364-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03364-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03364 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صالح بن يوسف بن صالح الحلبي ويعرف بالسرميني . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣāliḥ b. Yūsuf b. Ṣāliḥ al-Ḥalabī, known as al-Sarmīnī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03365 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03365-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03365-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03365 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صخرة بن مقبل بن نخبار أمير الينبوع . مات سنة ست وأربعين ورأيت من أرخه سنة اثنتين بدل ست واستقر بعده معزى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣakhra ibn Muqbil ibn Nukhbār, the emir of Yanbuʿ. He died in the year 846 AH, and I saw someone who dated his death to the year 842 AH instead of 46. After him, Muʿazzā was appointed as emir."@en .

rec:AIND-D03366 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03366-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03366-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03366 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صدقة بن أحمد بن قطلبك الحلبي الخواجا . ذكره ابن فهد في ذيله هكذا وأظنه من شرطنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣadaqa b. Aḥmad b. Quṭlubak al-Ḥalabī, al-Khawājā. Ibn Fahd mentioned him as such in his supplement (Dhayl), and I think he meets our criteria."@en .

rec:AIND-D03367 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03367-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03367-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03367 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صدقة بن أحمد بن أبي الحجاج يوسف فتح الدين الأقصري . شيخ لقيه البدر العمري في سنة ست عشرة فأخذ عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣadaqa b. Aḥmad b. Abī al-Ḥajjāj Yūsuf Fatḥ al-Dīn al-Uqṣurī. A shaykh whom al-Badr al-ʿUmarī met in the year 816 AH and took [knowledge] from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03373 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03373-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03373-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03373 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صدقة بن محمد بن صدقة المنوفي ثم المكي المؤذن المكبر بن الخوندار ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣadaqa b. Muḥammad b. Ṣadaqa, al-Munūfī, then al-Makkī. The muezzin and mukabbir, known as Ibn al-Khawndār, who was among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03374 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03374-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03374-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03374-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03374-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03374-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03374 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صدقة بن سري الدين محمد بن صدقة المحرقي ثم القاهري الأزهري والد الفاضل عبد الرحيم وأخيه عبد القادر . كان خيرا يتكسب بالخياطة ، مات في غيبة أول الولدين في ربيع الآخر سنة ست وثمانين ، وصلى عليه بالأزهر وأثنى عليه رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣadaqa b. Sirī al-Dīn Muḥammad b. Ṣadaqa al-Muḥriqī, then al-Qāhirī al-Azharī. He was the father of the virtuous ʿAbd al-Raḥīm and his brother ʿAbd al-Qādir. He was a good man who earned his living as a tailor. He died during the absence of both of his sons in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir, the year 886 AH. The funeral prayer was performed for him at al-Azhar Mosque, and he was highly praised. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03375 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03375-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03375-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03375 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صدقة بن موسى فتح الدين أبو الشفا ويعرف بابن صدقة وبابن فيروز وهو بها أشهر أحد الأطباء تخرج به جماعة وصاهره ابن الشريف على ابنته واستولدها ابنه الكمال محمد الآتي وكان بارعا . مات قريب السبعين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣadaqa b. Mūsā, Fatḥ al-Dīn, Abū al-Shifāʾ, also known as Ibn Ṣadaqa and more famously as Ibn Fayrūz. He was a physician under whom a group of students graduated. Ibn al-Sharīf married his daughter, who gave birth to his son al-Kamāl Muḥammad (mentioned below). He was highly skilled and is thought to have died around 870 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03376 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03376-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03376-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03376 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صدقة الحلبي نزيل مكة وأحد التجار . مات بجدة فجأة في جمادى الثانية سنة ست وثمانين وحمل إلى المعلاة فدفن بمقبرة له قريبة من تربة ابن سلامة عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sadaqa al-Halabi, a resident of Mecca and a merchant. He died suddenly in Jeddah in Jumada al-Thaniya, the year eighty-six (886 AH), and was carried to al-Mu'alla, where he was buried in his tomb near the tomb of Ibn Salama, may Allah forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03377 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03377-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03377-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03377 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صديق بن أحمد بن يوسف بن عبد الرحمن بن اسماعيل بن محمد اليمني نزيل مكة ويعرف بالأهدل شيخ صالح . مات بها في ضحى الجمعة ثالث عشري المحرم سنة خمس وخمسين ودفن بجانب قبر والده من المعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣiddīq bin Aḥmad bin Yūsuf bin ʿAbd al-Raḥmān bin Ismāʿīl bin Muḥammad al-Yamanī. He settled in Mecca and was known as al-Ahdal. A righteous shaykh. He died there in the forenoon of Friday, the 23rd of Muharram, in the year 855 AH, and was buried next to his father's grave in al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D03379 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03379-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03379-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03379 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صديق بن الشيخ حسين بن عبد الرحمن بن علي الحسيني نسبا وبلدا الشافعي الماضي أبوه وولده حسين ويعرف بابن الأهدل . أخذ الكثير عن أبيه ، ومات في رمضان سنة سبع وثمانين وقد زاد على السبعين وهو أكبر الموجودين من اخوته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣiddīq b. al-Shaykh Ḥusayn b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī al-Ḥusaynī, of al-Ḥusaynī lineage and origin, Shāfiʿī. His father (Ḥusayn) was mentioned previously, and his son is Ḥusayn. He is known as Ibn al-Ahdal. He studied extensively under his father, and died in Ramaḍān in the year 887 AH, having lived past seventy. He was the eldest of his surviving brothers."@en .

rec:AIND-D03380 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03380-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03380-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03380-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03380-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03380-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_58_84_85_judgement,
        agent:claude_b56_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03380 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صديق بن سالم التغلبي القاهري . قرأ القرآن وأدب به الابناء بجوار زاوية سيدي يحيى البلخي خارج باب الشعرية وتنزل في البيبرسية وكان من جيران الجد أبي الأم ، ومات بعده قريب الخمسين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sadiq b. Salim al-Taghlibi al-Qahiri. He recited the Qur'an and taught children with it near the zawiya of Sidi Yahya al-Balkhi outside Bab al-Sha'riya. He held a stipend at al-Baybarsiyya, and was a neighbor of [al-Sakhawi's] maternal grandfather. He died after him, close to the year 850 AH. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03381 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03381-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03381-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03381 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الصديق بن عبد الرحمن رضي الدين أبو عبد الله الصخري ثم الحديدي الشافعي قاضي زيلع . رأيت من وصفه من أهل بلده بالقاضي الأجل الفاضل الكامل وهو حي في سنة أربع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ṣiddīq b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Raḍī al-Dīn, Abū ʿAbd Allāh, al-Ṣakhrī, later al-Ḥadīdī, al-Shāfiʿī, the judge of Zaylaʿ. I saw someone from his homeland describe him as 'the most glorious, virtuous, and perfect judge'. He was alive in the year 894 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03383 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03383-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03383-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03383-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03383 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صديق بن عبد الله الصمصام . قال العفيف الناشري إنه قدم عليه تعز في سنة أربعين وثمانمائة وهو حسن السمت جيد السيرة ثم حكى عنه فائدة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣadīq b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣamṣām. al-ʿAfīf al-Nāshirī stated that he (the subject) came to him in Taʿizz in the year 840 AH, describing him as having a good demeanor and excellent conduct, and he narrated a beneficial point on his authority."@en .

rec:AIND-D03387 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03387-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03387-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03387 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صديق بن محمد المصري الجدي المكي الشهير بابن قديح . مات بمكة في صفر سنة اثنتين وثمانين بعد قدومه من جدة مطعونا وكان بزارا بجدة مباركا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣiddīq b. Muḥammad al-Miṣrī al-Jaddī al-Makkī, famously known as Ibn Qudayḥ. He died of the plague in Mecca in Safar of the year 882 AH, shortly after his arrival from Jidda. He had worked as a blessed seed merchant in Jidda."@en .

rec:AIND-D03390 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03390-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03390-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03390 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صراي تمر المحمدي أتابك دمشق . هرب من أسر تمر فحصله ثم وسطه في سنة أربع . أرخه ابن دقماق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sarāytamur al-Muḥammadī, the Atabak of Damascus. He escaped from the captivity of Timur, but was recaptured and then executed (cut in half) in the year 804 AH. Recorded by Ibn Duqmāq."@en .

rec:AIND-D03391 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03391-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03391-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03391 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صرداح بن مقبل . مضى في سرداح من السين المهملة ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D03395 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03395-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03395-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03395 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صعب بن أحمد بن حسن بن علي بن عبد القادر شيخ نابلس . ممن سمع منى بالقاهرة ومات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣaʿb b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Qādir, the Shaykh of Nablus. He was among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me in Cairo, and he has passed away."@en .

rec:AIND-D03396 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03396-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03396-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03396 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صندل العز الخشقدمي خشقدم الزمام أحد خدام المدينة الشريفة . ممن سمع مني بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Sandal al-ʿIzz al-Khushqadamī Khushqadam al-Zimām, one of the servants of the Noble Medina. He heard (ḥadīth) from me there (in Medina)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03398 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03398-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03398-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03398 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صولة بن خالد بن حمزة بن عمر بن طالب شيخ أولاد أبي الليل . مات سنة عشر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣawla b. Khālid b. Ḥamza b. ʿUmar b. Ṭālib, the chief of the Awlād Abī al-Layl tribe. He died in the year 810 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03399 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03399-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03399-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03399-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03399 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صوماي الحسني الظاهري برقوق . أحد أمراء الديار المصرية ورأس نوبة في الدولة الناصرية ثم المؤيدية . مات في حدود العشرين تقريبا وكان سليم الباطن عديم الشر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣawmāy al-Ḥasanī al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq. One of the amirs of Egypt and a raʾs nawba (chief of the guard) during the reigns of al-Nāṣir Faraj and al-Muʾayyad Shaykh. He died around 820 AH. He was of sound heart and free of malice."@en .

rec:AIND-D03400 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03400-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03400-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03400-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03400 ;
    aindv:sourceText "صلاح بن محمد بن علي الحسني الزيدي الطائي الصعدي صاحب صنعاء ، له ذكر بعيد الأربعين من حوادث إنباء شيخنا ، وقرأت بخطى في موضع آخر صلاح بن علي بن محمد بن أبي القسم الزيدي اجتمع الزيدية بعد موت الناصر صلاح الدين محمد بن علي بن محمد بن علي بن محمد بن علي صاحب صنعاء على تملكه صنعاء ولقبوه بالمهدي وذلك في أوائل سنة أربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṣalāḥ b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Ḥasanī al-Zaydī al-Ṭāʾī al-Ṣaʿdī, the ruler of Sanaa. He is mentioned shortly after the year 840 AH in the historical events of our shaykh's (Ibn Ḥajar) 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』. I read in my own handwriting in another place: 'Ṣalāḥ b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Qāsim al-Zaydī.' The Zaydīs united around him to rule Sanaa after the death of al-Nāṣir Ṣalāḥ al-Dīn Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, the ruler of Sanaa, and they gave him the title of al-Mahdī. This occurred in the early part of the year 840 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03401 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03401-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03401-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03401-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03401-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_58_followup,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03401 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ضغيم بن خشرم بن ثابت بن نعير الحسيني أمير المدينة . وليها في شوال سنة تسع وستين فأقام نحو أربعة أشهر ثم انفصل بابراهيم بن سليمان ثم أعيد بعد موته في سنة أربع وسبعين فاستمر إلى رمضان سنة ثلاث وثمانين فانفصل بقسيطل بن زهير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḍaghaym b. Khashram b. Thābit b. Nuʿayr al-Ḥusaynī, Amir of Medina. He was appointed as its governor in Shawwāl 769 AH, remaining in office for about four months before being replaced by Ibrāhīm b. Sulaymān. He was reinstated after Ibrāhīm's death in the year 774 AH and continued until Ramaḍān 783 AH, when he was dismissed and replaced by Qusayṭal b. Zuhayr."@en .

rec:AIND-D03402 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03402-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03402-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03402-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03402 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ضياء بن محمد الحاري الحوراني الشافعي الأعرج . شهد في إجازة النوبي سنة خمس وستين ، وبلغني أنه كان ينزل الشامية البرانية من دمشق ويقرىء الفقه ويكرم الغرباء سيما الحجازيين ، وأنه مات في المحرم سنة ست وتسعين رحمه الله . ومضى له ذكر في خضر الكردي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḍiyāʾ b. Muḥammad al-Ḥārī al-Ḥawrānī al-Shāfiʿī, known as al-Aʿraj (the lame). He witnessed the ijāza of al-Nūbī in the year 865 AH. It reached me that he used to reside in al-Shāmiyya al-Barrāniyya Madrasa in Damascus, teaching jurisprudence (fiqh) and showing hospitality to strangers, especially those from the Hijaz. He died in Muharram, 896 AH. He is also mentioned in the biography of Khiḍr al-Kurdī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03403 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03403-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03403-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03403 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ضياء بن عماد الدين ضياء الدين التبريزي وأظنه ضياء مختصر لقبه . كان دينا فاضلا محبا في الحديث كثير النفور عن الاشتغال بالعقليات ملازما للخير ولقراءة الحديث وسماعه وإسماعه مع نزول إسناده . مات سنة إحدى . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه نقلا عن أخبار صاحبه عبد الرحمن التبريزي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḍiyāʾ b. ʿImād al-Dīn Ḍiyāʾ al-Dīn al-Tabrīzī. I think 'Ḍiyāʾ' is an abbreviation of his laqab. He was a pious and virtuous man who loved hadith and strictly avoided engaging in the rational sciences. He was devoted to goodness and to the reading, hearing, and teaching of hadith despite the lower chains of narrations. He died in the year 801 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his *Inbāʾ al-Ghumr*, transmitting from the reports of his companion ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Tabrīzī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03404 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03404-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03404-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03404-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03404-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_58_followup,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03404 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ضيغم بن خشرم بن نجاد الحسيني أمير المدينة وأظنه أخا ضغيم الماضي قريبا . استقر فيها بعد ابن عمه مانع وأقام مدة ثم انفصل سنة خمسين بأميان بن مانع المذكور ولم يذعن لذلك إلا بدراهم بذلها له المستقر فأخذها ثم خرج متوجها فقتل بعد يسير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḍaygham b. Khashram b. Najād al-Ḥusaynī, Amir of Medina. I believe he is the brother of Ḍughaym, who was mentioned recently above. He was appointed to the emirate of Medina after his cousin Māniʿ and remained in office for a period of time. He was then dismissed in the year 850 AH by Umyān b. Māniʿ, the son of the aforementioned cousin. He did not yield to his dismissal until he was paid a sum of dirhams by the newly appointed ruler; he accepted the money and departed, only to be killed shortly thereafter."@en .

rec:AIND-D03405 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03405-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03405-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03405-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03405 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ضيف بن أحمد بن علي بن عثمان النجار الخراط . سمع من الحاج علي التونسي حكاية . وحدث بها سمعها منه التقي بن فهد ، وذكره في معجمه . مات سنة ثمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ḍayf b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿUthmān al-Najjār al-Kharrāṭ. He heard a story from al-Ḥājj ʿAlī al-Tūnisī and transmitted it. Al-Taqī b. Fahd heard it from him and mentioned him in his Muʿjam. He died in the year 808 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03407 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03407-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03407-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03407-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03407 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طاهر بن أحمد بن محمد صفي الدين بن فخر الدين بن الشيخ شمس الدين الكازروني أخو محمد الآتي . لقيه الطاوسي فاستفاد منه ، وأرخ وفاته في يوم الجمعة تاسع عشر المحرم سنة ثمان وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭāhir b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad Ṣafī al-Dīn b. Fakhr al-Dīn b. al-Shaykh Shams al-Dīn al-Kāzarūnī, the brother of Muḥammad who is mentioned below. Al-Ṭāwūsī met him and benefited from him, and recorded his death as Friday, the 19th of al-Muharram in the year 848 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03408 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03408-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03408-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03408-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03408 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الطاهر بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن علي بن محمد بن أبي بكر الناشري الآتي أبوه . حفظ القرآن وحج في سنة ست وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ṭāhir b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-Nāshirī, whose father is forthcoming. He memorized the Qurʾān and performed the Hajj in the year 826 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03410 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03410-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03410-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03410 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الطاهر بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن علي بن يوسف القاضي جمال الدين الأنصاري الزبيدي المكي أخو الوجيه عبد الرحمن الآتي ويعرف بابن الجمال المصري . مات بها في ذي الحجة سنة ثمان وأربعين ودفن جوار أخيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ṭāhir b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf, the Qāḍī Jamāl al-Dīn al-Anṣārī al-Zabīdī al-Makkī. He is the brother of al-Wajīh ʿAbd al-Raḥmān who is mentioned below. He was known as Ibn al-Jamāl al-Miṣrī. He died in Mecca in Dhu al-Ḥijjah in the year 848 AH and was buried next to his brother."@en .

rec:AIND-D03411 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03411-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03411-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03411 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طاهر بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن محمد العجمي نزيل مكة والمجلد بها . مات بها في المحرم سنة خمس وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭāhir bin Muḥammad bin Abī Bakr bin Muḥammad al-ʿAjamī. He resided in Mecca and worked as a bookbinder there. He died there in al-Muḥarram, in the year 885."@en .

rec:AIND-D03414 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03414-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03414-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03414-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03414 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طاهر بن يونس الموصلي . رأيته كتب في سنة خمس وثلاثين وثمانمائة على رسالة للجمال عبد الله بن علي بن أيوب في الطب ما سيأتي ، وفي شيوخ أبي اللطف الحصكفي ثم القدسي الحاج زين الدين طاهر بن قاضي الموصل قرأ عليه الأدوار للصفي عبد المؤمن الأرموي وكأنه هذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭāhir b. Yūnus al-Mawṣilī. I saw that he wrote in the year 835 AH on a treatise of al-Jamāl ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Ayyūb on medicine, as will be mentioned. Among the teachers of Abū al-Luṭf al-Ḥaṣkafī, later al-Qudsī, is al-Ḥājj Zayn al-Dīn Ṭāhir b. Qāḍī al-Mawṣil, under whom he read 『al-Adwār』 by al-Ṣafī ʿAbd al-Muʾmin al-Urmawī; it appears that he is the same person."@en .

rec:AIND-D03415 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03415-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03415-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03415 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طاهر الفقيه من ذرية عثمان بن أبي بكر بن عمر الناشري . رجل مبارك ملازم للجماعات واكتساب الخيرات يأكل من كسب يده . مات سنة أربعين بزبيد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, from the descendants of ʿUthmān ibn Abī Bakr ibn ʿUmar al-Nāshirī. A blessed man, regular in congregational prayers, pursuing good deeds, and eating from the work of his own hand. He died in the year 840 AH in Zabīd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03416 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03416-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03416-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03416-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03416 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طاهر رجل قدم القاهرة فنزل البرقوقية وأقرأ الطلبة . وممن قرأ عليه صاحبنا الشهاب حفيد البيجوري قرأ عليه غالب القطب وقال لي إنه مات بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭāhir. A man who came to Cairo, stayed at the Barqūqiyya, and taught the students. Among those who read to him was our companion al-Shihāb, the grandson of al-Bījūrī, who read most of al-Quṭb to him. He told me that he died in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03417 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03417-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03417-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03417-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03417-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03417-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03417 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طه بن خالد بن موسى الاطفيحي ثم القاهري الأزهري الشافعي والد عبد اللطيف . ممن اشتغل ولازم الشرفي بن الجيعان واختص به وتنزل في جهات على خير واستقامة ومن شيوخه بل سمع على الزين شعبان بن حجر بقراءتي الأدب المفرد للبخاري وحج . مات في..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭāhā b. Khālid b. Mūsā al-Iṭfīḥī, later al-Qāhirī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī, the father of ʿAbd al-Laṭīf. He was among those who studied under and closely associated with al-Sharafī b. al-Jīʿān, who favored him, and he held several positions in a good and upright manner. Among his teachers, he heard al-Bukhārī's 『al-Adab al-Mufrad』 from al-Zayn Shaʿbān ibn Ḥajar, with my (al-Sakhāwī's) recitation. He also performed the Hajj. He died in..."@en .

rec:AIND-D03418 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03418-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03418-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03418 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طرباي الأشرفي قايتباي . استخلفه أخوه تنم حين سفره بعد قضاء أمر جدة في سنة ست وتسعين فأقام بها ثم بمكة إلى أن جاء المستقر عوضهما في التي تليها وهو ممن يحسن التلاوة ويجيد الطواف ويتشاهم"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭarabāy al-Ashrafī Qāytbāy. His brother Tanam appointed him as deputy upon his departure after settling the affairs of Jeddah in the year 896 AH. Thus, he resided there (in Jeddah), and then in Mecca, until their replacement arrived in the following year (897 AH). He is among those who excel in recitation, perform the circumambulation (tawāf) beautifully, and behave with chivalry."@en .

rec:AIND-D03420 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03420-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03420-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03420 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طرغلي بن سقل سيز من أمراء التركمان . قتل مع تغري ورمش في ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وأربعين . قيل إنما هو ضرغلي بالضاد المعجمة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭarghalī b. Saqal Sīz, one of the Turcoman amirs. He was killed alongside Taghrī Warmish in Dhū al-Ḥijja, year 842 AH. It is said that his name is actually Ḍarghalī, with the dotted ḍād."@en .

rec:AIND-D03423 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03423-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03423-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03423 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طغرق من أولاد دلغادر التركماني نائب حمص . قتل في ذي القعدة سنة ثمان وثلاثين في وقعة للعرب ، واستقر ابنه بعده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭughruq, of the descendants of Dulkadir (Dulghādir) al-Turkumānī, governor (nāʾib) of Homs. He was killed in Dhu al-Qaʿdah, 838 AH, in a battle with the Arabs, and his son succeeded him in office."@en .

rec:AIND-D03424 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03424-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03424-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03424 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طغيتمر الجلالي البلقيني . تأخر بعد سيده حتى خدم عند أخيه العلي البلقيني ثم مات قريب الخمسين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tughaytimur al-Jalali al-Bulqini. He outlived his master and served his master's brother, al-Ali al-Bulqini, and died around the year 850 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03425 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03425-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03425-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03425 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طقتمر البارزي . مات سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭuqtumur al-Bārizī. He died in the year 857 AH (57)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03428 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03428-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03428-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03428 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الطنبغا . مات بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة إحدى وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-Ṭunbughā. He died in Makka in Rabīʿ al-Awwal, the year 861 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03433 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03433-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03433-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03433-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03433 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طوخ الجكمي جكم من عوض . تنقل بعد سيده إلى أن تأمر عشرة في أيام الأشرف ثم غضب عليه وحبسه ثم أعاده لامرة عشرة أيضا إلى أن أمره الظاهر طبلخاناه ثم رأس نوبة ثاني ثم أبطله لما ضعف بصره ولزم بيته مديما فيما قيل للانهماك مع التعاظم والجبن والبخل حتى مات في سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tūkh al-Jakamī, [the mamlūk of] Jakam min ʿAwaḍ. He was transferred after his master's death until he was appointed as an Amīr of Ten during the reign of al-Ashraf. Later, the Sultan became angry with him and imprisoned him, but then restored him to the command of ten. He was subsequently promoted to the command of Tablkhānāh by al-Ẓāhir, and then became the Second Chief of Guards (Raʾs Nawba Thānī). He was dismissed when his sight grew weak, after which he remained confined to his house. It is said that he was addicted to pleasures, arrogant, cowardly, and miserly until his death in the year 868."@en .

rec:AIND-D03434 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03434-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03434-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03434-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_58_followup,
        agent:claude_b57_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03434 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طوخ الخازندار الظاهري برقوق . كان من مماليكه وخاصكيته ثم تقدم في أيام ابنه ثم ولاه الخازندارية الكبرى وصار من أعيان دولته لنفوذ كلمته عنده . مات بالقاهرة في أواخر جمادى الآخرة سنة اثنتي عشرة وكثر التأسف عليه لحسن سيرته وعقله وشجاعته وقال العيني : الخزندار أحد المقدمين بالديار المصرية وأمير مجلس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭūkh al-Khāzindār al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq. He was one of his (Barqūq's) mamluks and private retinue (khāṣṣakiyya), then advanced during the reign of his son, who appointed him to the Grand Treasurership (al-Khāzindāriyya al-Kubrā). He became one of the prominent figures of his state due to his influential word with him. He died in Cairo at the end of Jumādā al-Ākhira in the year 812 AH, and was widely lamented for his good conduct, intellect, and bravery. Al-ʿAynī said: 'The Khāzindār was one of the commanders (muqaddimūn) in the Egyptian lands and Amīr Majlis.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D03435 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03435-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03435-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03435 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طوخ أحد المقدمين من الظاهرية برقوق . قتله المؤيد سنة سبع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭūkh, one of the commanders (al-muqaddamīn) of the Ẓāhiriyya Barqūq (mamluks). He was killed by al-Mu'ayyad (Shaykh) in the year (8)17 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03436 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03436-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03436-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03436 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طوخ أمير . مات في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين بالطاعون وما علمت شيئا من حاله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭūkh, the amir. He died of the plague in Ṣafar, the year 853 AH, and nothing of his state is known to me."@en .

rec:AIND-D03437 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03437-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03437-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03437-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03437-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_58_followup,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03437 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طوغان شيخ الأحمدي . ثم ولي نظر المسجد الحرام المكي وامرة الراكز بمكة مدة ، وكان يتفقه ويزاحم الفقهاء مع بلادة وعدم معرفة وأظهر مؤلفا أعانه فيه غيره عارض فيه السيد السمهودي في امتهان البسط المكتوب عليها وعدم احترامها كتب له عليه جماعة ومات بالقاهرة في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭūghān Shaykh al-Aḥmadī. He served as the superintendent of the Holy Mosque of Mecca and the commander of al-Rākiz in Mecca for a period of time. He studied jurisprudence and rivaled the jurists despite his dullness and lack of knowledge. He produced a work, in which he was assisted by others, refuting al-Sayyid al-Samhūdī regarding the degradation of carpets with writing on them and their lack of respect, on which a group of scholars wrote approvals for him. He died in Cairo in Dhu al-Ḥijjah in the year 881."@en .

rec:AIND-D03442 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03442-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03442-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03442 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طوغان دوادار طوخ الأبو بكري الماضي قريبا قتل معه في سنة ثمان أو تسع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭūghān, the dawādār of Ṭūkh al-Abū Bakrī, who was mentioned shortly before. He was killed together with him in the year 848 or 849 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03446 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03446-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03446-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03446 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طوغان العمري المؤيدي شيخ . تأمر عشرة في أول الأيام الخشقدمية إلى أن قتل في الوقعة السوارية سنة اثنتين وسبعين وقد قارب السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭūghān al-ʿUmarī al-Muʾayyadī [Shaykh], mamluk of al-Muʾayyad Shaykh. He was appointed as an emir of ten at the beginning of the reign of Khushqadam until he was killed in the battle against Shah Suwar in the year 872 AH, having approached the age of seventy."@en .

rec:AIND-D03447 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03447-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03447-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03447 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طوغان ميق ويقال له شارب . تزوج ابنة السفطي الكبرى ، وتأمر في أيام الظاهر خشقدم ، ومات في ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭūghān Mīq, also called Shārib. He married the eldest daughter of al-Safati, was appointed as an emir during the reign of al-Zahir Khushqadam, and died in [incomplete date in the source text]."@en .

rec:AIND-D03448 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03448-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03448-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03448 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طولو بن علي باشا الظاهري برقوق . كان من أعيان خاصكيته وترقى بعده إلى الامرة ثم ولي نيابة غزة ثم نيابة اسكندرية ثم صار أحد المقدمين ثم انضم مع شيخ وجكم واستمر بالشام إلى رمضان سنة ثمان فرسم باستقراره في نيابة صفد إلى أن قتل في مقتلة بين حماة وحمص في ذي الحجة منها وهو أستاذ طوغان أميرآخور الماضي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tūlū b. ʿAlī Bāshā al-Ẓāhirī Barqūq. He was one of the elites of the royal mamluks (khāṣṣakiyya) of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq and was promoted to amir after him. He then governed Gaza, then Alexandria, and became one of the commanders of a thousand (muqaddamūn). He joined with Shaykh and Jakam, staying in Syria until Ramadan of the year 808 AH, when he was appointed governor of Safad until he was killed in a battle between Hama and Homs in Dhu al-Hijjah of that year. He was the master of Tūghān Amīr Ākhūr, who was mentioned recently."@en .

rec:AIND-D03449 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03449-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03449-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03449-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03449 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طومان باي الظاهري جقمق . كان في أيامه خاصكيا وتأمر في أول أيام خشقدم فسار فيها أقبح سيرة لا سيما حين عمر داره المجاورة للبيبرسية ، ودام على ذلك إلى أن تجرد لسوار ورجع فأقام ثلاثة أيام ، ومات في صفر سنة أربع وثمانين ، وقد قارب الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Tuman Bay al-Zahiri Jaqmaq. He was a khassaki (royal mamluk) during the reign of al-Zahir Jaqmaq and was promoted to amir at the beginning of the reign of Khushqadam, during which he behaved terribly, particularly when he built his house adjacent to al-Baybarsiyya. He remained in this state until he was dispatched on a military campaign against Shah Suwar (of Dhu al-Qadr). He returned and stayed for three days, then died in Safar 884 AH, at nearly fifty years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D03450 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03450-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03450-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03450 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طوير بن أبي سعد الحسني . مات بمكة في سنة أربع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭuwayr b. Abī Saʿd al-Ḥasanī. He died in Mecca in the year 844 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03451 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03451-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03451-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03451 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طيبغا البدري حسن بن نصر الله الصاحب . مات سنة خمس وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭaybughā al-Badrī, the mamlūk of al-Badrī Ḥasan b. Naṣr Allāh al-Ṣāḥib. He died in the year 845 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03453 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03453-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03453-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03453 ;
    aindv:sourceText "طيبغا التركي فتى ابن القواس . مات سنة خمس عشرة ويحرر مع الذي قبله"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ṭaybughā al-Turkī, the freedman (fatā) of Ibn al-Qawwās. He died in the year 815 AH. This entry should be examined alongside the preceding one."@en .

rec:AIND-D03454 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03454-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03454-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03454 ;
    aindv:sourceText "الطيب بن إبراهيم بن أبي بكر بن إبراهيم العامري الحرضي اليماني الماضي أبوه . استجازني أبوه له ولنفسه في سنة أربع وتسعين وأنا بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Ṭayyib b. Ibrāhīm b. Abī Bakr b. Ibrāhīm al-ʿĀmirī al-Ḥaraḍī al-Yamānī. His father was mentioned previously. In the year 894 (1489), while I was in Mecca, his father requested an ijāza from me for him and for himself."@en .

rec:AIND-D03459 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03459-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03459-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03459 ;
    aindv:sourceText "ظهيرة بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد . يأتي في أبي بكر من الكنى"@ar .

rec:AIND-D03461 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03461-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03461-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03461-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03461 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عادي بن إسماعيل بن ملك بن عادي سلطان دهلك . مات سنة ست وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĀdī ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Malik ibn ʿĀdī, Sultan of Dahlak. He died in the year 866 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03463 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03463-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03463-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03463 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عامر بن عبد الوهاب بن داود بن طاهر حفيد أخي الذي قبله . ملك اليمن بعد أبيه واختلف عليه بنو عامر الذي قبله ولكن كانت شوكته قاهرة لهم واشتغل بالنظر في مدارس وغيرها بعمارتها وتنمية أوقافها ، والغالب عليه الخير ومحبة العلماء مع حسن العقيدة ممن مدحه الشعراء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĀmir b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Dāwūd b. Ṭāhir, the grandson of the brother of his predecessor. He ruled Yemen after his father. The Banu ʿĀmir of his predecessor opposed him, but his power overcame them. He occupied himself with supervising madrasas and other institutions, constructing them and developing their endowments. He was generally virtuous, loved the scholars, possessed sound creed, and was praised by poets."@en .

rec:AIND-D03464 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03464-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03464-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03464 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عامر ويسمى محمد بن المحب محمد بن الرضي محمد بن المحب محمد بن الشهاب أحمد بن الرضي إبراهيم بن محمد بن إبراهيم شريف الدين أبو الثناء الطبري المكي مات بها قبل استكمال سنتين في جمادى الأولى سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĀmir, also named Muḥammad, son of al-Muḥibb Muḥammad, son of al-Raḍī Muḥammad, son of al-Muḥibb Muḥammad, son of al-Shihāb Aḥmad, son of al-Raḍī Ibrāhīm, son of Muḥammad, son of Ibrāhīm. Sharīf al-Dīn Abū al-Thanāʾ al-Ṭabarī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ūlā 857 AH before completing two years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D03465 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03465-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03465-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03465 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عامر بن الطباع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĀmir b. al-Ṭabbāʿ."@en .

rec:AIND-D03466 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03466-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03466-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03466 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عامر الخيفي . مات في سلخ ذي القعدة سنة سبع وستين . ذكره ابن فهد في الذيل وكان نديما منشدا وربما نظم وانعقد لسانه قبل موته . وقد مضى أحمد بن سعد الخيفي ولعله أخوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĀmir al-Khayfī. He died at the end of Dhu al-Qaʿdah in the year 867 AH. Ibn Fahd mentioned him in his supplement (al-Dhayl). He was a companion (nadīm), a reciter of poetry (munshid), and occasionally composed verses. He lost the ability to speak before his death. Aḥmad b. Saʿd al-Khayfī was mentioned earlier; he is perhaps his brother."@en .

rec:AIND-D03467 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03467-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03467-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03467 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عايض بمعجمة آخره ابن سعيد الحبشي الحسني مولى السيد حسن بن عجلان القائد . مات بمكة في شوال سنة خمس وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĀyiḍ b. Saʿīd al-Ḥabashī al-Ḥasanī, the qāʾid, freedman (mawlā) of al-Sayyid Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān. He died in Mecca in Shawwāl, the year 855 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03473 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03473-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03473-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03473 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عباس بن محمد بن زياد الكاملي ويعرف بجده . مات سنة إحدى وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbbās bin Muḥammad bin Ziyād al-Kāmilī, known by his grandfather. He died in the year 831 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03475 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03475-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03475-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03475 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عباس بن محمد بن موسى البلشوني . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbbās b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā al-Balshūnī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03476 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03476-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03476-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03476 ;
    aindv:sourceText "العباس بن المتوكل بن المعتضد . مضى قريبا في ابن محمد بن أبي بكر بن سليمان ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D03477 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03477-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03477-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03477 ;
    aindv:sourceText "العباس أبو منديل الوهراني قاضيها . مات سنة تسع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-ʿAbbās, Abū Mandīl al-Wahrānī, the qadi of Oran. He died in the year 829 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03481 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03481-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03481-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03481 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الباري بن أحمد بن عبد الغني بن عتيق بن الشيخ سعيد بن الشيخ حسن أبو النجا العشماوي القاهري الأزهري المالكي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Bari b. Ahmad b. Abd al-Ghani b. Atiq b. al-Shaykh Sa'id b. al-Shaykh Hasan Abu al-Naja al-Ashmawi al-Qahiri al-Azhari al-Maliki. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhawi) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03483 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03483-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03483-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03483 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الباسط بن أحمد بن عبد اللطيف بن زايد السنبسي المكي أخو أبي الفتح الآتي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ومات في أواخر صفر سنة ثلاث وتسعين وصلى عليه بعد العصر ثم دفن عند قبورهم من المعلاة عوضه الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Zāyad al-Sunbasī al-Makkī, the brother of Abū al-Fatḥ (mentioned below). He was among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me in Mecca. He died in the latter part of Ṣafar, 893 AH. The funeral prayer was performed after the afternoon (ʿaṣr) prayer, and he was buried in their graves at al-Muʿallā. May Allah reward him with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D03487 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03487-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03487-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03487 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الباسط بن أبي شاهين . قتل في صفر سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ b. Abī Shāhīn. He was killed in the month of Ṣafar, 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03490 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03490-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03490-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03490-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03490 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الباسط بن عمر بن عبد العزيز الأنصاري المدني أخو البدر حسن الماضي وخادم قبة العباس من البقيع . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Anṣārī al-Madanī. He is the brother of the aforementioned al-Badr Ḥasan, and the caretaker of the Dome of al-ʿAbbās in al-Baqīʿ. He is among those who heard hadith from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03491 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03491-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03491-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03491 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الباسط بن عمر بن محمد بن هبة الله الحموي الآتي أبوه وجده ويعرف كسلفه بابن البارزي . شاب جاور مع أبيه بمكة فكان يشتغل يسيرا وربما حضر عندي مع والده وعقد له على قريبة له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Hibat Allāh al-Ḥamawī. His father and grandfather are mentioned below. Like his predecessors, he is known as Ibn al-Bārizī. A young man, he stayed as a neighbor (jāwara) in Mecca alongside his father. He engaged in some minor studies there, and occasionally attended my classes with his father. A marriage contract was also drawn up for him with a female relative of his."@en .

rec:AIND-D03493 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03493-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03493-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03493 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الباسط بن الشمس محمد بن حسن بن علي بن عبد الرحمن الشهير أبوه بابن الاستادار . أثكله أبوه وقد جاز العشرين في شوال سنة خمس وتسعين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ ibn al-Shams Muḥammad ibn Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, whose father was popularly known as Ibn al-Ustādār. His father was bereaved of him in Shawwāl of the year 895, after he had passed twenty years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D03494 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03494-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03494-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03494-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03494-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03494-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D03494-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03494 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الباسط بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن الشيخ نور الدين علي بن أحمد بن أبي بكر الأدمي القاهري شريك الشمس الجوجري وتلميذه . ممن يكثر السفر لمكة في البحر ويعامل ويضارب وحصلت له جائحة مرة بعد أخرى وكلامه أكثر من نفعه وفعله وغيره أولى في الصدق منه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Shaykh Nūr al-Dīn ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr al-Ādamī al-Qāhirī. He was a partner and student of al-Shams al-Jawjarī. He was among those who frequently travelled to Mecca by sea, engaging in trade and mudarabah partnerships. He suffered financial ruin multiple times. His words were more than his utility and actions, and others are more worthy of truthfulness than him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03499 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03499-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03499-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03499 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الباسط بن الهباء محمد بن المحب محمد الزرندي المدني سبط الجمال الكازروني وأحد من سمع عليه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Basit b. al-Haba' Muhammad b. al-Muhibb Muhammad al-Zarandi al-Madani. He was the maternal grandson of al-Jamal al-Kazaruni and one of those who heard from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03502 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03502-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03502-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03502 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الباسط المباشر بجدة . مضى فيمن أبوه محمد بن محمد بن أحمد ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D03503 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03503-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03503-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03503 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الباقي بن محمود صلاح الدين بن تاج الدين صاحب حصن حب . مات سنة ثلاثين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Bāqī ibn Maḥmūd Ṣalāḥ al-Dīn ibn Tāj al-Dīn, lord of Ḥiṣn Ḥubb. He died in the year 830 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03508 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03508-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03508-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03508 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الجبار بن عبد المجيد بن الموفق على بن أبي بكر حافظ الدين الناشري اليماني أكبر بني أبيه . كان عالما صالحا ولي القضاء ومات في سنة سبع وخمسين وسيأتي أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Jabbār b. ʿAbd al-Majīd b. al-Muwaffaq ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr Ḥāfiẓ al-Dīn al-Nāshirī al-Yamānī. The eldest of his father's children. He was a pious scholar. He was appointed to the judgeship (qaḍāʾ) and died in the year 857 AH. His father's biography is forthcoming."@en .

rec:AIND-D03510 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03510-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03510-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03510 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الجليل بن أحمد بن الفقيه على جلال الدين الحسيني سكنا القباني . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Jalīl ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Faqīh ʿAlī Jalāl al-Dīn al-Ḥusaynī (by residence) al-Qabbānī. He was among those who heard [ḥadīth] from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03512 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03512-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03512-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03512 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الجليل مات سنة بضع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Jalīl. He died in the year forty-something (840s AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03514 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03514-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03514-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03514 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الحفيظ بن عمر الشريف الحسني الزبيدي الشافعي أحد الفضلاء هناك كما بلغني . أرسل في سنة سبع وتسعين يطلب مني الاجازة له ولولده محمد ولأقاربه فأجزتهم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ḥafīẓ b. ʿUmar al-Sharīf al-Ḥasanī al-Zabīdī, of the Shāfiʿī madhhab, was one of the virtuous scholars there [in Zabīd], as I was informed. In the year 897 AH, he sent a request asking me for an ijāza (scholarly license) for himself, his son Muḥammad, and his relatives, so I granted it to them."@en .

rec:AIND-D03515 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03515-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03515-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03515 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الحفيظ بن الكمال أبي الفضل بن الزين أبي بكر بن ناصر الدين أبي الفرج محمد بن أبي بكر بن الحسين المراغي المدني . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ḥafīẓ b. al-Kamāl Abū al-Faḍl b. al-Zayn Abū Bakr b. Nāṣir al-Dīn Abū al-Faraj Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. al-Ḥusayn al-Marāghī al-Madanī. He was among those who heard (hadith) from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03520 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03520-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03520-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03520 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الحق بن علي الجزري . مات سنة اثنتين وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Haqq b. Ali al-Jazari. He died in the year 862 AH (1458 CE)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03522 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03522-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03522-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03522 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الحق بن محمد بن عثمان بن مرين المريني صاحب فاس وما والاها من المغرب . هكذا رأيت بعضهم نسبه وقال غيره انه ابن عثمان بن أحمد كما مضى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ḥaqq bin Muḥammad bin ʿUthmān bin Marīn al-Marīnī, the ruler of Fez and its surrounding regions in the Maghrib. Thus I saw some lineage-makers trace his ancestry, while others said that he was the son of ʿUthmān bin Aḥmad, as mentioned previously."@en .

rec:AIND-D03525 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03525-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03525-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03525-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03525-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03525-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D03525-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03525 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الحميد بن الإمام تقي الدين محمد بن إبراهيم بن عبد الحميد المدني ابن خال أبي الفتح المراغي . سمع على الزين المراغي والعلم سليمان السقا في سنة سبع وتسعين وسبعمائة وتأخر حتى مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Hamid b. al-Imam Taqi al-Din Muhammad b. Ibrahim b. Abd al-Hamid al-Madani. The son of the maternal uncle of Abu al-Fath al-Maraghi. He heard from al-Zayn al-Maraghi and al-Alam Sulayman al-Saqqa in the year 797 AH, and lived a long life until he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D03527 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03527-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03527-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03527-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03527-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03527 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الحميد الطرابلسي المغربي ثم القاهري المالكي . ممن تفقه به الشهاب بن تقي ، وقد رأيت فيمن عرض عليه الزين بن الأدمي عبد الحميد بن عبد الله المالكي والظاهر أنه هذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ṭarābulusī al-Maghribī, then al-Qāhirī al-Mālikī. Among those who studied jurisprudence (tafaqquh) under him was al-Shihāb b. Taqī. I have also seen among those who presented (ʿaraḍa) [memorized texts] to him the name of al-Zayn b. al-Adamī [presenting to] ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Mālikī, and it is apparent that he is this person."@en .

rec:AIND-D03528 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03528-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03528-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03528-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03528 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الحميد رجل ولي مشيخة الصوفية بالجامع الجديد بمصر إلى أن مات في صفر سنة ثمان وعشرين . ذكره المقريزي هكذا في عقوده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Hamid. A man who held the position of shaykh of the Sufis at al-Jami' al-Jadid (the New Mosque) in Egypt (Cairo) until his death in Safar, 828 AH. Al-Maqrizi mentioned him thus in his work al-'Uqud."@en .

rec:AIND-D03533 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03533-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03533-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03533 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الخالق بن الشمس محمد بن ناصر الدين محمد بن محمد الجعفري القاهري الموقع جده . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Khāliq b. al-Shams Muḥammad b. Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Jaʿfarī al-Qāhirī, whose grandfather was al-Muwaqqiʿ. He is among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03537 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03537-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03537-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03537 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الدائم بن الشيخ عمر الهوى . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Dāʾim, son of al-Shaykh ʿUmar al-Hawā. He was among those who acquired knowledge from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03538 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03538-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03538-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03538-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03538-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03538-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03538 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن عبد اللطيف بن نجم بن عبد المعطي البرماوي ثم القاهري أخو الفخر عثمان وعبد الغني الآتيين . سمع علي التنوخي وجماعة وذكره البقاعي في شيوخه مجردا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Najm b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī al-Birmāwī, then al-Qāhirī. Brother of al-Fakhr ʿUthmān and ʿAbd al-Ghanī, who are mentioned below. He heard from al-Tanūkhī and others. Al-Biqāʿī mentioned him simply in his list of shaykhs."@en .

rec:AIND-D03541 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03541-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03541-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03541 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن إبراهيم بن إسماعيل بن عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن بن عمر ابن علي وجيه الدين بن البرهان العلوي اليمني الشافعي قريب النفيس سليمان بن إبراهيم بن عمر الماضي يلتقي معه في جده عمر ، لقيني بمكة فقرأ على ثلاثيات البخاري وسمع من لفظي المسلسل وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ibrāhīm b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī Wajīh al-Dīn b. al-Burhān al-ʿAlawī al-Yamanī al-Shāfiʿī. A relative of the aforementioned al-Nafīs Sulaymān b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿUmar, with whom he shares a common lineage through his grandfather ʿUmar. He met me in Mecca, where he read to me the 'Thulāthiyyāt' of al-Bukhārī and heard from my dictation the 'al-Musalsal' and other works."@en .

rec:AIND-D03546 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03546-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03546-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03546 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن إبراهيم أبو محمد المازني البعيني . ظهر في حدود الثلاثين له أحوال خارقة بحيث اعتقده أهل وصاب والناس فيه فريقان . مات بعد انحطاط أمره في سنة ست وثلاثين أو قريبا منها . ذكره العفيف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Ibrahim, Abu Muhammad al-Mazini al-Ba'yni. He appeared around the year [8]30 AH, performing miraculous deeds such that the people of Wasab believed in him, though people were divided into two factions regarding him. He died after the decline of his prestige in the year [8]36 AH or close to it. He was mentioned by al-Afif."@en .

rec:AIND-D03547 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03547-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03547-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03547 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن إبراهيم الرعيني صاحب اللفج . مات سنة خمس وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ibrāhīm al-Ruʿaynī, the master of al-Lafj. He died in the year 825 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03548 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03548-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03548-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03548 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن عيسى بن مطير الحكمي اليماني أخو أبي القسم وغيره . تفقه وسمع الحديث وتوفي شابا بعازب حين رجوعه من الحج في صفر سنة إحدى وأربعين . قاله الأهدل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā b. Muṭayr al-Ḥakamī al-Yamānī, brother of Abū al-Qāsim and others. He studied jurisprudence (fiqh) and heard Hadith. He died young at ʿĀzib on his return from the Hajj pilgrimage in Safar, 841 AH. Reported by al-Ahdal."@en .

rec:AIND-D03554 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03554-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03554-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03554 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن حسن بن علي بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن الأذرعي أحد الأخوة من بني الامام شهاب الدين واختص بابن منجك ومات بالمنيبيع من دمشق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Adhruʿī. One of the brothers from the family of al-Imām Shihāb al-Dīn. He was closely associated with Ibn Manjak, and died in al-Munaybiʿ in Damascus."@en .

rec:AIND-D03555 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03555-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03555-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03555-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03555 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن حسن بن محمد بن علي القاهري الفراش بجامع المغاربة . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة النبوية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Ahmad b. Hasan b. Muhammad b. Ali al-Qahiri, the farrash (attendant/sweeper) at the Jami' al-Maghariba. He heard (hadith) from me in the Prophet's City (Medina)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03556 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03556-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03556-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03556 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن حسن بن الشحنة البعلي . ولد ببعلبك سنة ثلاث وثمانين وسبعمائة . ونشأ بها فسمع الصحيح علي الزين عبد الرحمن بن الزعبوب أخبرنا به الحجار ، وحدث سمع منه الطلبة ، ومات قبل أن أرحل ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. al-Shuḥna al-Baʿlī. He was born in Ba'labakk in the year 783 AH and grew up there. He heard the Sahih [al-Bukhari] from al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Zaʿbūb, on the authority of al-Ḥajjār. He transmitted hadith and students heard from him. He passed away, I believe, before I set out on my travels."@en .

rec:AIND-D03557 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03557-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03557-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03557 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن حسين بن محمد بن علي الطائفي ثم القاهري الماضي أبوه . حفظ القرآن وقرأ فيه علي الزين جعفر وفي الفقه علي داود القلتاوي وعباس المغربي وغيرهما وتردد إلي مع أبيه وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Ahmad b. Husayn b. Muhammad b. Ali al-Ta'ifi, later al-Qahiri, whose father was mentioned previously. He memorized the Qur'an and recited it under al-Zayn Ja'far, and studied fiqh under Da'ud al-Qiltawi and Abbas al-Maghribi, among others. He frequented me (al-Sakhawi) along with his father and others."@en .

rec:AIND-D03561 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03561-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03561-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03561 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن الجمال المصري المكي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Jamāl al-Miṣrī al-Makkī. He was among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03563 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03563-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03563-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03563 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن الزين الزرندي المدني الحنفي أخو محمد الآتي . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Zayn al-Dīn al-Zarandī al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī. He is the brother of Muḥammad, who is mentioned below. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03564 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03564-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03564-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03564 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن عبد الله الزين بن الشهاب الحبيشي المدني المادح ، ممن سمع مني بالمدينة أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah, Zayn al-Din, ibn Shihab al-Din al-Hubayshi al-Madani, al-Madih (the panegyrist). He was also among those who heard from me (al-Sakhawi) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03568 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03568-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03568-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03568 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن عثمان الزين السويدي المالكي قاضي دمشق وقدم القاهرة واشتغل عند وولي قضاء المالكية بدمشق ، وكان مات في يوم السبت رابع عشري ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وستين وصلى عليه بجامع دمشق ودفن بمقبرة الباب الصغير وكانت جنازته حافلة رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Ahmad b. 'Uthman al-Zayn al-Suwaydi, al-Maliki. He served as the judge of Damascus. He came to Cairo, engaged in studies, and held the Maliki judgeship in Damascus. He passed away on Saturday, 24th of Dhu al-Hijja, 861 AH. The funeral prayer was held at the Mosque of Damascus, and he was buried in the Bab al-Saghir cemetery. His funeral was widely attended. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03572 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03572-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03572-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03572 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن علي القبايلي المغربي الماضي أبوه . ذبح في شوال سنة ثلاث كما ذكر هناك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Qabāʾilī al-Maghribī. His father was mentioned previously. He was executed (slaughtered) in Shawwāl of the year 803 AH, as mentioned there (in his father's entry)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03574 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03574-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03574-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03574-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03574 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن عمر بن غانم الزين البرمكيني القاهري . من أهل القرآن توفي قبيل الثلاثين عن بضع وستين وهو شقيق الشرف موسى وأحمد وسليمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Ahmad b. Umar b. Ghanim, Zayn al-Din, al-Barmakini al-Qahiri. He was one of the people of the Qur'an. He died shortly before 830 AH at the age of sixty-something. He was a full brother of al-Sharaf Musa, Ahmad, and Sulayman."@en .

rec:AIND-D03575 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03575-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03575-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03575 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن عمر المدني الفراش بها . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmar al-Madanī, the attendant (farrāsh) there [in Medina]. He was among those who heard from me [al-Sakhāwī] in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03576 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03576-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03576-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03576 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن عمير المدني الفراش بها ويعرف بدربيي . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة وأظنه الأول وقع الغلط أحد الموضعين في جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmayr al-Madanī, the attendant (farrāsh) there [in Medina], known as Darbīyī. He is among those who heard [ḥadīth] from me in Medina. I think he is the former (the preceding entry), a mistake having occurred in one of the two places regarding his grandfather's name."@en .

rec:AIND-D03577 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03577-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03577-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03577 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن عياش . يأتي فيمن جده محمد بن محمد قريبا ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D03578 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03578-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03578-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03578 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن غازي الزرعي المقدسي سبط الجمال بن جماعة . سمع معنا وحفظ كتبا كثيرة ولازم الكمال بن أبي شريف . مات سنة تسع وثمانين قبل الكهولة ، وكان خيرا ساكنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Ghāzī al-Zarʿī al-Maqdisī. Grandson (daughter's son) of al-Jamāl b. Jamāʿa. He studied (heard ḥadīth) together with us, memorized many books, and closely accompanied al-Kamāl b. Abī Sharīf. He died in the year 889 AH before reaching middle age. He was a good and quiet person."@en .

rec:AIND-D03579 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03579-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03579-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03579 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن قاسم ويعرف بابن الأصيفر . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Qāsim, known as Ibn al-Uṣayfir. He was among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03584 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03584-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03584-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03584-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03584-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b57_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Dgroup,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03584 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن عوض العز أبو الفضل البكري الشافعي أخو الذي قبله ووالد الجمال محمد الآتي . ولد سنة احدى وثمانين وسبعمائة وتفقه بأبيه وأذن له في الافتاء ومات شابا في سنة سبع . أفادنيه ولده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAwaḍ, al-ʿIzz, Abū al-Faḍl, al-Bakrī al-Shāfiʿī. He was the brother of the person mentioned in the preceding entry, and the father of al-Jamāl Muḥammad, who is mentioned below. He was born in the year 781 AH, studied jurisprudence (fiqh) under his father, who authorized him to issue fatwas. He died at a young age in the year 807 AH. His son provided me with this information."@en .

rec:AIND-D03586 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03586-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03586-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03586 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن محمد بن شقير القليوبي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Shuqayr al-Qalyūbī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03592 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03592-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03592-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03592-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03592-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03592-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03592 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد الحموي الأصل القاهري رفيق السلموني ونحوه في الشهادة مع جودة الخط ولكنه غير محمود وربما اشتغل ولازم أخي في قراءة التقسيم وتردد إلي ثم ورث وتوجه بالاسترقاق بميراثه بحرا فقدمها في شوال سنة سبع وتسعين وجلس بباب السلام ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad, of Ḥamāh origin, then of Cairo. He was a colleague of al-Salmūnī and others in notary services (shahāda); he had excellent calligraphy but was not well-regarded. He studied and kept close to my brother [Abū Bakr al-Sakhāwī] in reciting [the book] al-Taqsīm, and frequented me. Later he received an inheritance and traveled with it by sea, arriving in [Mecca] in Shawwāl of the year 897, where he sat at Bāb al-Salām."@en .

rec:AIND-D03593 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03593-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03593-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03593 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد المدني المالكي أخو عمر الآتي ويعرف بالنفطي . قرأ الموطأ لأمامه علي غانم الخشبي وتزوج ابنة الجلال الخجندي بعد أبي الفتح المراغي ، وكان حيا في سنة عشر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad al-Madanī al-Mālikī, the brother of ʿUmar who is mentioned below, known as al-Nafṭī. He read the Muwaṭṭaʾ of his Imam [Mālik] under Ghānim al-Khashabī, and married the daughter of al-Jalāl al-Khujandī after her marriage to Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī. He was alive in the year [8]10 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03594 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03594-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03594-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03594 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أحمد المطيرز عضد الدين . مات في يوم السبت خامس عشري رمضان سنة ست وخمسين . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad al-Muṭayraz, ʿAḍud al-Dīn. He died on Saturday, the 25th of Ramaḍān, in the year 856 AH. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03596 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03596-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03596-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03596 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن بكير بن محمد الفرجي البرلسي ويعرف بابن الفقيه . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة . )"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Bukayr b. Muḥammad al-Farjī al-Burlusī, known as Ibn al-Faqīh. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03597 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03597-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03597-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03597-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03597 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي البركات بن أبي الهدى محمد بن تقي الدين الشيخ الصالح الزين الكازروني المدني الشافعي عم عبد الله بن عبد الوهاب بن أبي البركات الآتي . ممن قرأ علي بالمدينة في شرح النخبة وسمع أشياء وله أخذ عن الأبشيطي وغيره وفيه فضل ما مع سكون وخير . مات سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī al-Barakāt b. Abī al-Hudā Muḥammad b. Taqī al-Dīn, the pious and righteous shaykh, Zayn al-Kāzarūnī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī. He was the paternal uncle of ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Abī al-Barakāt, who is mentioned later. He studied under me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina, reading the commentary on al-Nukhba (Sharḥ al-Nukhba) and hearing other works. He also acquired knowledge from al-Abshīṭī and others. He possessed virtue, tranquility, and goodness. He died in the year 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03598 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03598-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03598-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03598 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن إبراهيم العراقي الأصل المكي . ممن سمع مني بمكة وهو خير منجمع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ibrahim al-Iraqi, originally of Iraqi origin and Meccan by residence. He is among those who heard from me (al-Sakhawi) in Mecca, and he is an extremely pious and reserved person."@en .

rec:AIND-D03604 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03604-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03604-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03604 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن عبد الرحمن الحموي الحنبلي المقرئ القادري الوفائي . قدم القاهرة في سنة تسع وثمانين فقرأ عليه ابن أخي الفخر عثمان المقسي الزهراوين لأبي عمرو مع منظومة الأمين عبد الوهاب بن أحمد بن وهبان الحنفي القاضي المسماة غاية الاختصار في أصول قراءة أبي عمرو ومنظومة ابن الجزري في التجويد وقال انه قرأهما على العلاء أبي الحسن علي بن أحمد الحموي بن الخدر الآتي وانه كتب على الأولى شرحا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr b. Abd al-Rahman al-Hamawi al-Hanbali, the Qur'an reciter, al-Qadiri, al-Wafa'i. He arrived in Cairo in the year 889 AH, and the nephew of al-Fakhr 'Uthman al-Maqsi read to him al-Zahrawayn by Abu 'Amr, along with the poem of al-Amin 'Abd al-Wahhab b. Ahmad b. Wahban al-Hanafi al-Qadi, entitled 'Ghayat al-Ikhtisar fi usul qira'at Abi 'Amr', and the poem of Ibn al-Jazari on Tajwid (al-Jazariyya). He said that he studied both of them under al-'Ala' Abu al-Hasan 'Ali b. Ahmad al-Hamawi b. al-Khidr, who will be mentioned later, and that he wrote a commentary on the first poem."@en .

rec:AIND-D03610 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03610-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03610-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03610-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03610 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن علي بن عبد العزيز بن عبد الكافي الدقوقي المكي . مات شابا بها في شعبان سنة ثمان وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Kāfī al-Daqūqī al-Makkī. He died young there [in Mecca] in Shaʿbān of the year 868."@en .

rec:AIND-D03612 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03612-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03612-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03612 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن محمد الزين البرلسي ويعرف بابن الفقيه سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad al-Zayn al-Burlusī, also known as Ibn al-Faqīh. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03614 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03614-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03614-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03614 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن يحيى الزوقري . فيمن جده عبد الله ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D03616 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03616-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03616-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03616-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03616 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر الدمشقي الرسام ويعرف بابن الحبال . أخذ عنه الشهاب بن اللبودي ووصفه بالمسند وقال انه مات في يوم السبت ثاني شعبان سنة احدى وستين فجأة ، ودفن من الغد بصالحية دمشق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr al-Dimashqī al-Rassām, known as Ibn al-Ḥabbāl. Al-Shihāb b. al-Lubūdī took (knowledge) from him, described him as a musnid, and said that he died suddenly on Saturday, 2 Shaʿbān 861 AH, and was buried the next day in al-Ṣāliḥiyya of Damascus."@en .

rec:AIND-D03617 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03617-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03617-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03617-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03617 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر الحنبلي . كتب بالاجازة في بعض استدعاءاتي المصرية المؤرخة سنة خمس وخمسين وكأنه الذي قبله ومن نظمه : %~% وفاضت دموعي من لهيب وحرقة %~% وحر لظى نار الغرام وأفكاري %~% %~% فنيران قلبي قد جرين مدامعي %~% ألا فاعجبوا من فيض ماء من النار ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr al-Ḥanbalī. He wrote an ijāza in his own hand on some of my Egyptian requests (istidʿāʾs) dated the year 855 AH. It is as if he is the same person as the previous entry. Among his poetry: 'My tears overflowed from the flame and burning / And the heat of the fire of love and my thoughts / The fires of my heart made my tears flow / So marvel at the flood of water from the fire.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D03618 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03618-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03618-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03618 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر اليماني المنسي . مات سنة خمس وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr al-Yamānī al-Mansī. He died in the year 825 AH (twenty-five)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03621 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03621-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03621-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03621 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن الخواجا البدر حسن بن محمد بن قاسم بن علي اليمني الأصل المكي الماضي أبوه والآتي أخواه علي ومحمد وشقيقه عمر ، ويعرف بابن الطاهر بالمهملة . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة اثنتين وستين بجدة وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بمعلاتها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. al-Hasan b. Muhammad b. Qasim b. Ali. Of Yemeni origin, resident of Mecca. His father (Hasan) was mentioned previously, his two brothers Ali and Muhammad are mentioned below, and his full brother is Umar. He was known as Ibn al-Tahir. He died in Jidda in Jumada al-Akhira 862, and was carried to Mecca where he was buried in al-Mu'alla."@en .

rec:AIND-D03622 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03622-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03622-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03622 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن حسن الزين بن الشيخ الخالدي أخو عبد السلام الآتي ويعرف بالكذاب . مات في ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وأربعين بمكة ودفن بتربة رامشت من المعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ḥasan al-Zayn b. al-Shaykh al-Khālidī. Brother of ʿAbd al-Salām, who is mentioned below, and he was known as al-Kadhdhāb (the liar). He died in Dhu al-Hijjah in the year 842 AH in Mecca, and was buried in the tomb of Rāmasht in al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D03625 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03625-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03625-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03625-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03625-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03625-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03625 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن حسين بن حسن بن يوسف الزين بن البدر الهوريني الأصل القاهري الشافعي الكتبي الماضي أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ḥusayn b. Ḥasan b. Yūsuf, Zayn (Zayn al-Dīn), the son of al-Badr (Badr al-Dīn). Of Hawrīn origin, Cairo resident, Shāfiʿī, bookseller. His father has been mentioned previously."@en .

rec:AIND-D03627 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03627-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03627-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03627-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03627 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن الخضر الحنفي والد الحسام محمد بن بريطع الآتي ولي قضاء غزة وقتا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Khidr al-Hanafi, the father of al-Husam Muhammad ibn Buraytah, who is mentioned below. He served as the qadi of Gaza for a time."@en .

rec:AIND-D03628 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03628-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03628-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03628-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03628-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_58_84_85_judgement,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03628 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن خليفة بن أحمد الطهطاوي الصعيدي الشافعي نزيل مكة والجالس للشهادة بباب السلام فيها ويعرف بالخطيب . ممن سمع مني بها وبالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Khalīfa b. Aḥmad al-Ṭahṭāwī al-Ṣaʿīdī al-Shāfiʿī. He resided in Mecca and sat for notary testimony (shahāda) at Bāb al-Salām there, and was known as al-Khaṭīb. He heard (ḥadīth) from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca and in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03631 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03631-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03631-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03631-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03631 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن داود الزين بن الكويز جد الذي قبله . كان اسمه قبل التظاهر باسلامه جرجس . ذكره المقريزي في عقوده بما سلف نحوه في داود ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Dāwūd al-Zayn b. al-Kuwayz, the grandfather of the preceding subject (AIND-D03630, ʿAbd al-Rahmān b. Dāwūd b. ʿAbd al-Rahmān b. Dāwūd). His name before openly professing Islam was Jirjis (George). Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his biographical work 『al-ʿUqūd』 in a manner similar to what was previously mentioned concerning [his father] Dāwūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03634 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03634-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03634-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03634-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03634 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي السعادات بن محمود بن عادل الزين الحسيني المدني الحنفي أخو أحمد الماضي وعبد الله وعبد الكبير الآتيين . ولد سنة ست وخمسين وثمانمائة تقريبا ونشأ فحفظ القرآن والمختار واشتغل في النحو والصرف وأكثر من التلاوة وجود علي عمر النجار الحموي وسمع على أبي الفرج المراغي وولده وكذا سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī al-Saʿādāt b. Maḥmūd b. ʿĀdil, Zayn al-Dīn, al-Ḥusaynī, al-Madanī, al-Ḥanafī. He is the brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad, and of ʿAbd Allāh and ʿAbd al-Kabīr who are mentioned below. He was born around 856 AH and grew up to memorize the Qurʾān and al-Mukhtār. He engaged in the study of grammar and morphology, recited frequently, and perfected his recitation under ʿUmar al-Najjār al-Ḥamawī. He heard from Abū al-Faraj al-Marāghī and his son, and also heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03636 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03636-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03636-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03636 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن سعد الحضرمي المدني أخو محمد الآتي . سمع علي الجمال الكازروني في سنة أربع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Saʿd al-Ḥaḍramī al-Madanī, the brother of Muḥammad who is mentioned below. He heard (hadith) from al-Jamāl al-Kāzarūnī in the year 834 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03637 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03637-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03637-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03637-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03637 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن سعيد بن عبد الله بن أبي عبد الله محمد بن الرضي محمد بن أبي بكر بن خليل العثماني نزيل وادي مر . مات في غرة جمادى الآخرة سنة ثمان وسبعين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Abd Allah Muhammad ibn al-Radi Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Khalil al-Uthmani. He was a resident of Wadi Marr and died in Mecca on the first of Jumada al-Akhira, 878 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03642 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03642-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03642-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03642-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03642-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03642-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03642 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الباسط بن خليل الدمشقي الأصل القاهري الماضي أبوه والآتي أخواه أبو بكر وعمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Basit ibn Khalil, of Damascene origin, of Cairo. His father was mentioned previously, and his two brothers, Abu Bakr and Umar, are to be mentioned below."@en .

rec:AIND-D03644 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03644-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03644-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03644-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03644-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03644-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_58_followup,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_b88_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03644 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الرحيم بن ناصر الدين محمد بن جمال الدين عبد الله ابن صاحب المدرسة والدار المجاورة لها بباب النصر بكتمر الحاجب الآتي والده ويعرف كسلفه بابن الحاجب . مات في يوم الجمعة ثامن رجب سنة خمسين وأرخه بعضهم في الطاعون سنة ثلاث وخمسين وكأن الأول أصح بعد أن أسند وصيته للبدر البرماوي ودفن بتربتهم بالقرب من مدرسة جده المشار اليها وكان يلي والده في الوسواس واختص بالأمير قانباي الجركسي وقتا عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad b. Jamāl al-Dīn ʿAbd Allāh, a descendant of Baqtumur al-Ḥājib (whose father's biography is forthcoming), the owner of the madrasa and its adjacent house at Bāb al-Naṣr. Like his predecessors, he was known as Ibn al-Ḥājib. He died on Friday, 8 Rajab 850 AH, though some dated his death to the plague of 853 AH; the first date seems more correct. He entrusted his will to al-Badr al-Birmāwī and was buried in their family tomb near his ancestor's aforementioned madrasa. He succeeded his father in having obsessive thoughts (al-waswās) and was closely associated with the Emir Qānibāy al-Jarkasī for a time. May Allah forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03646 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03646-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03646-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03646-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03646-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03646 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد العزيز بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز الوجيه بن القاضي عز الدين الهاشمي العقيلي النويري المكي المالكي . ولد بها في سنة اثنتي عشرة وثمانمائة وسمع بها من المراغي وابن الجزري وابن طولوبغا وغيرهم وأجاز له عائشة ابنة ابن عبد الهادي وعبد القادر الأرموي وآخرون ، وسافر إلى القاهرة ثم إلى تونس فاشتغل فيها على جماعة واستمر حتى مات بعد الأربعين ، ذكره ابن فهد في النويريين والنيل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Wajīh b. al-Qāḍī ʿIzz al-Dīn al-Hāshimī al-ʿUqaylī al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī al-Mālikī. He was born in Mecca in the year 812 AH. There, he heard from al-Marāghī, Ibn al-Jazarī, Ibn Ṭūlūbughā, and others. ʿĀʾisha bint Ibn ʿAbd al-Hādī, ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Armawī, and others granted him licenses (ijāza). He traveled to Cairo and then to Tunis, where he studied under a group of scholars and remained there until he died after 840 AH. He was mentioned by Ibn Fahd in 'al-Nuwayriyyīn' and 'al-Nayl'."@en .

rec:AIND-D03652 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03652-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03652-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03652-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03652-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03652-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b56_58_followup,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03652 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الكريم الارموي الأصل الدمشقي الحنفي . سمع على الشهاب الحسباني المائة المستقاة من مشيخة الفخر وحدث بها أخذها عنه سبط شيخنا في سنة خمس وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Karīm, of Urmia origin, from Damascus, the Hanafi. He heard 'The Selected One Hundred from the Mashyakha of al-Fakhr' under al-Shihāb al-Ḥasbānī and transmitted it. The grandson of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) studied it under him in the year 865 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03653 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03653-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03653-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03653-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03653-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03653-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b58_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_verify_B56_58 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03653 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن أحمد بن أبي الحسن علي بن عيسى بن محمد ابن عيسى الحسني السمهودي أخو النور على الآتي وهذا أكبر وذاك أفضل . ناب في القضاء ببلده عن العلم البلقيني حين إعراض أبيه عنها فكان أول من ابتكر ولايته واستمر ينوب عن من بعده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Abī al-Ḥasan ʿAlī b. ʿĪsā b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā al-Ḥasanī al-Samhūdī. He is the brother of al-Nūr ʿAlī, who is mentioned below; this one (ʿAbd al-Raḥmān) was older, while the other was more virtuous. He served as deputy judge in his hometown (Samhūd) on behalf of al-ʿAlam al-Bulqīnī when his father withdrew from it, being the first to initiate this deputyship, and he continued to act as deputy for those who succeeded him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03654 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03654-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03654-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03654 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن جمال الثناء البصري المكي ، يأتي قريبا فيمن جده عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jamāl al-Thanāʾ al-Baṣrī al-Makkī. He will be mentioned soon under those whose grandfather is ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān."@en .

rec:AIND-D03656 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03656-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03656-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03656 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن بن زوران البصري الخواجا ممن كان يسافر في المتجر إلى الهند . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة تسع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Abd Allah b. Abd al-Rahman b. Zawran al-Basri, known as al-Khawaja. He was among those who travelled to India for trade. He died in Rabi' al-Akhir 879 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03660 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03660-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03660-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03660 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن عبد الكريم البنا . مات بمكة في جمادى الأولى سنة ستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Bannā. He died in Mecca in Jumada al-Ula, the year 860 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03662 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03662-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03662-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03662-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03662 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن علي بن موسى الوجيه بن العفيف بن النور المكي المعروف بالمزوق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Mūsā, al-Wajīh (his own laqab), son of al-ʿAfīf (his father ʿAbd Allāh), son of al-Nūr (his grandfather ʿAlī), the Meccan, known as al-Muzawwiq (the decorator/illuminator)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03663 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03663-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03663-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03663 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن محمد بن داود الصدر الكفيري الدمشقي الشافعي . قال شيخنا في الأنباء عنى بالفقه وناب في الحكم بدمشق ومات بها في المحرم سنة إحدى عن أربعين سنة وكانت له همة في طلب الرياسة . قاله ابن حجي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Dawud, al-Sadr al-Kufayri al-Dimashqi al-Shafi'i. Our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) mentioned in Inba' al-Ghumr that he was devoted to fiqh and served as a deputy judge in Damascus, where he died in Muharram 801 AH at the age of forty. He possessed a strong ambition for leadership, as reported by Ibn Hijji."@en .

rec:AIND-D03664 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03664-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03664-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03664-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03664 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن حسين بن الحسن الزين المدني أخو أبي الفرج وحفيد أخي إبراهيم بن عبد الرحمن الماضي ويعرف كسلفه بابن القطان ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman bin Abd Allah bin Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Husayn bin al-Hasan al-Zayn al-Madani. He is the brother of Abu al-Faraj and the grandson of the brother of Ibrahim bin Abd al-Rahman, who was mentioned previously. Like his predecessors, he is known as Ibn al-Qattan. He heard (hadith) from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03665 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03665-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03665-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03665 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن محمد بن الفخر عبد الرحمن بن يوسف بن نصر بن أبي القسم بن عبد الرحمن البعلي الدمشقي الحنبلي . سمع على الحافظ المزي وأبي العباس الجزري ومحمد بن إسماعيل بن عمر الحموي وحدث قرأ عليه شيخنا بدمشق وأرخ وفاته في رجب سنة ثلاث وتبعه المقريزي في عقوده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. al-Fakhr ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Yūsuf b. Naṣr b. Abī al-Qāsim b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Baʿlī al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanbalī. He heard hadith from al-Ḥāfiẓ al-Mizzī, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Jazarī, and Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿUmar al-Ḥamawī, and transmitted hadith. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) read to him in Damascus and recorded his death in Rajab 803 AH, and al-Maqrīzī followed him in his work al-ʿUqūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03668 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03668-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03668-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03668 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله القاضي زين الدين بن المجير . استوزره صاحب حصن كيفا وهو قاض شافعي عالم حسن السيرة كما قاله شيخنا في أحمد بن سليمان الأشرف من سنة ست وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Abd Allah, al-Qadi Zayn al-Din b. al-Mujir. He was appointed as vizier (wazir) by the ruler of Hisn Kayfa. He was a learned Shafi'i judge (qadi) of good conduct, as our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) mentioned in the biography of Ahmad b. Sulayman al-Ashraf under the year 836 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03669 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03669-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03669-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03669 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله الباز ، مات سنة أربع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān bin ʿAbd Allāh al-Bāz, died in the year 844 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03670 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03670-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03670-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03670 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله النفياي ثاني الخمسة المهتدين للاسلام ، ممن سمع على شيخنا وغيره وهو الآن حي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Nafyāʾī, the second of the five guided to Islam (converts). He heard (hadith) from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others, and he is currently alive."@en .

rec:AIND-D03674 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03674-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03674-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03674-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03674-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03674 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبد الوهاب بن الزين اللدي الأصل الغزي ناظر جيشها بل عظيمها وأخو سعد الدين إبراهيم الماضي ممن يذكر بالأموال الغزيرة . مات بها وقد جاز السبعين فجأة في ليلة الجمعة سلخ شعبان سنة اثنتين وثمانين قبل إكماله المدرسة التي أمره السلطان ببنائها له هناك فالتزم ولده إبراهيم الماضي باكمالها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Wahhab bin al-Zayn, of Lydda origin and Ghazza home, the inspector of the army (nazir al-jaysh) of Gaza, or rather its chief magnate, and the brother of the aforementioned Sa'd al-Din Ibrahim. He was known for his vast wealth. He died suddenly in Gaza after passing his seventies, on the night of Friday, at the end of Sha'ban in the year 882 AH, before completing the school (madrasa) which the Sultan had ordered him to build for him there. His aforementioned son, Ibrahim, undertook to complete it."@en .

rec:AIND-D03675 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03675-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03675-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03675 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عبيد الله بن عوض بن محمد الأردبيلي الشرواني القاهري الحنفي أخو البدر محمود الآتي وإخوته . حفظ البديع لابن الساعاتي والهداية ، وخلف والده في تدريس الأبوبكرية والأيتمشية وأم السلطان لكونه أكبر إخوته ومات سنة إحدى عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿAwaḍ b. Muḥammad al-Ardabīlī al-Shirwānī al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī. Brother of al-Badr Maḥmūd, who is mentioned below, and his other brothers. He memorized 'al-Badīʿ' by Ibn al-Sāʿātī and 'al-Hidāya'. Being the eldest of his brothers, he succeeded his father in teaching at al-Abūbakriyya, al-Aytamishiyya, and Umm al-Sulṭān madrasas. He died in the year 811 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03678 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03678-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03678-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03678-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03678-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03678 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عثمان بن أمير الشرواني الأصل المحمود أبادي ثم الرومي الحنفي فاضل ورد مكة في البحر فأخذ عنه بعض الطلبة وتردد إلي فكان مما سمعه مني المسلسل واستشكل أشياء في الاصطلاح فأوضحتها له وسافر مع شدة حرصه على الملازمة لكون أهل نواحيه لا عهد لهم بشيء من الحديث ومتعلقاته وذكر لي أن له تصانيف في العقليات وحواشي على كثير من الكتب المشكلات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUthmān ibn Amīr, of Shirwani origin, from Mahmudabad, then of Rum, Hanafi. He was a virtuous scholar. He arrived in Mecca by sea, and some students studied under him. He frequented my company and among the texts he heard from me was al-Musalsal. He raised some difficult points regarding terminology (al-iṣṭilāḥ), which I clarified for him. He traveled back despite his strong desire to remain in close discipleship, because the people of his region had no knowledge of Hadith and its related fields. He mentioned to me that he had authored works in the rational sciences (al-ʿaqliyyāt) and glosses (ḥawāshī) on many difficult books."@en .

rec:AIND-D03679 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03679-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03679-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03679-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03679 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عثمان بن الرضي عبد الرحمن بن عثمان بن الرضي عبد الرحمن ابن علي السفط رشيدي ثم القاهري الشافعي الخليفتي الصوفي بخانقاه قوصون بالقرافة الصغرى . ولد في آخر سنة إحدى وأربعين وثمانمائة بسفط رشيد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUthmān ibn al-Raḍī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUthmān ibn al-Raḍī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAlī al-Safṭrashīdī, later al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, al-Khalīfatī, the Sufi of the Khanqah of Qusun in the Lesser Qarafa. He was born at the end of the year 841 AH in Safat Rashid."@en .

rec:AIND-D03681 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03681-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03681-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03681-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03681-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03681 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عثمان جمال الدين السكندري الترجمان التاجر ، كان عارفا بأمور المتجر وممن صاهر في بيت ابن الأشقر . قدم من إسكندرية متوعكا فمرض مدة ثم نصل ودخل الحمام ثم انتكس ومات في رمضان سنة تسع وأربعين ومات له ابن اسمه محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman Jamal al-Din al-Sakandari. The interpreter and merchant, he was knowledgeable in trade matters and married into the family of Ibn al-Ashqar. He arrived from Alexandria in ill health and remained sick for a period, after which he recovered slightly and entered the bathhouse, but then suffered a relapse and died in Ramadan, the year 849 AH. A son of his named Muhammad also died."@en .

rec:AIND-D03682 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03682-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03682-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03682 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عليان الغزي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿUlayyān al-Ghazzī. Among those who heard (hadith) from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03691 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03691-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03691-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03691 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن علي بن عبيد الله الحلبي الامشاطي ، سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Halabi al-Amshati. He heard (hadith) from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03696 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03696-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03696-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03696-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03696 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن علي بن محمد بن أحمد بن حسن بن الزين محمد بن الأمين محمد بن القطب محمد بن أحمد القسطلاني ، أجاز له في سنة ست وثلاثين جماعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. al-Zayn Muḥammad b. al-Amīn Muḥammad b. al-Quṭb Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Qasṭallānī. A group of scholars (jamāʿah) granted him an ijāzah in the year 836 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03703 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03703-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03703-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03703 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن علي بن محمد بن مفتاح البعلي . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن مفتاح قريبا . عبد الرحمن بن علي بن محمد التفهني . مضى في ابن علي بن عبد الرحمن بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Miftāḥ al-Baʿlī. He was already mentioned nearby under the entry of those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Miftāḥ. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Tafhanī. He was already mentioned under Ibn ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03704 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03704-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03704-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03704 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن علي بن يحيى الوجيه العدني الآتي أخوه محمد وأبوهما ويعرف كأبيه بابن جميع . له ذكر في أخيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī b. Yaḥyā, al-Wajīh al-ʿAdanī. His brother Muḥammad and their father are mentioned below. Like his father, he is known as Ibn Jamīʿ. He is mentioned in his brother's entry."@en .

rec:AIND-D03706 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03706-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03706-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03706 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن علي الأزهري . مات في سنة سبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman bin Ali al-Azhari. He died in the year 870 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03711 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03711-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03711-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03711-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03711 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عمر بن عبد العزيز بن عمر بن عامر البصروي والد محمد ممن أخذ عنه ولده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿUmar b. ʿĀmir al-Baṣrawī, the father of Muḥammad. His son (Muḥammad) was among those who acquired knowledge (akhadha) from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03712 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03712-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03712-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03712-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03712 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عمر بن عثمان الشمري الملحاني أخو عبد الله الآتي . مات سنة خمس وعشرين وقبره عند مقابر الناشريين بزبيد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿUmar b. ʿUthmān al-Shumarī al-Milḥānī. Brother of ʿAbd Allāh, who is mentioned below. He died in the year 825 AH and his grave is at the cemetery of the Nashiris in Zabid."@en .

rec:AIND-D03713 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03713-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03713-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03713 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عمر بن عيسى السمنودي الآتي أبوه . أخذ عنه بلديه صاحبنا الجلال السمنودي الميقات وهو ممن أخذه عن أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān bin ʿUmar bin ʿĪsā al-Samannūdī, whose father is mentioned below. Our companion, his fellow countryman al-Jalāl al-Samannūdī al-Mīqātī, took (tradition) from him, and he (ʿAbd al-Raḥmān) is among those who took it from his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D03715 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03715-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03715-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03715-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03715 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عمر بن محمد بن أحمد بن عمر الحوراني المكي أخو يحيى الآتي . ولد في جمادى الأولى سنة ست وثمانين وثمانمائة بجدة وقرأ القرآن عند الفقيه حسن الطلخاوي بمكة وسمع علي بها بقراءة أخيه بعض الصحيح ومني المسلسل وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmar al-Ḥawrānī al-Makkī, the brother of Yaḥyā who is mentioned below. He was born in Jumādā al-Ūlā, the year 886 AH, in Jidda. He recited the Qurʾān under the jurist Ḥasān al-Ṭalkhāwī in Mecca, and heard from me [al-Sakhāwī] there, through the recitation of his brother, a portion of al-Ṣaḥīḥ, as well as al-Musalsal and other works directly from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D03719 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03719-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03719-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03719-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03719-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03719-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03719 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن عيسى بن سلطان الغزي الشافعي والد الشمس محمد ابن سلطان الشهير الآتي . تلا عليه ابنه للسبع وقرأ عليه الفقه والنحو وخطب بالجامع الجاولي بغزة بل قيل انه ولي مشيخة البيبرسية إما الكبرى أو الرباط وصحب جماعة من السادات . مات في سنة خمس رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿĪsā b. Sulṭān al-Ghazzī al-Shāfiʿī. He was the father of the famous al-Shams Muḥammad b. Sulṭān, who is mentioned below. His son recited the Quran to him according to the seven recitations, and studied fiqh and grammar under him. He delivered the sermon at the Jāwilī Mosque in Gaza, and it was even said that he was appointed to the shaykh-ship of the Baybarsiyya, either the grand Khanqah or the Ribāṭ. He accompanied a group of sayyids (Sufi masters). He died in the year 805 AH. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03721 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03721-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03721-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03721 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن فخر اليمني ، مات بمكة في المحرم سنة اثنتين وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Fakhr al-Yamanī. He died in Mecca in Muharram, 862 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03724 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03724-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03724-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03724 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن لطف الله سبط الشمس المعيد . ناب في امامة الحنفية بمكة عن خاله الشهاب بن المعيد ، ومات بها في ذي الحجة سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Luṭf Allāh, the grandson (daughter's son) of al-Shams al-Muʿīd. He deputized in the Hanafi imamate in Mecca on behalf of his maternal uncle al-Shihāb b. al-Muʿīd, and died there in Dhu al-Hijja, year 853 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D03728 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03728-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03728-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03728 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أحمد بن اسماعيل بن داود الزين بن الشمس بن الشهاب القاهري الحنفي أخو الجمال عبد الله وغيره ويعرف كسلفه بابن الرومي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. Dāwūd, Zayn al-Dīn, the son of al-Shams (Muḥammad) and grandson of al-Shihāb (Aḥmad), of Cairo, of the Hanafi school. He was the brother of al-Jamāl ʿAbd Allāh and others, and like his ancestors was known as Ibn al-Rūmī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03730 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03730-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03730-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03730 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أحمد بن عبد القادر بن يعقوب بن محمد الديروطي ويعرف بابن الرزاز وابن البياع . تلا بالسبع على بلديه حسن ثم على جعفر السنهوري ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Yaʿqūb b. Muḥammad al-Dayrūṭī, known as Ibn al-Razzāz and Ibn al-Bayyāʿ. He recited the seven Qurʾanic recitations (al-Qirāʾāt al-Sabʿ) to his fellow countryman Ḥasan, and then to Jaʿfar al-Sanhūrī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03731 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03731-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03731-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03731 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن الجمال محمد بن أحمد بن علي الحجازي الشريفي العطار أبوه بمكة شقيق عبد اللطيف الآتي . سمعا على التقي بن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. al-Jamal Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Ali al-Hijazi al-Sharifi al-Attar. His father, [who resided] in Mecca, was the full brother of Abd al-Latif, who is mentioned below. They both heard [hadith] from al-Taqi b. Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03733 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03733-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03733-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03733-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03733 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أحمد وجيه الدين أبو محمد العرشاني قاضي تعز بعد عدن . مات سنة سبع وثلاثين واستقر بعده في قضاء تعز أخوه أبو بكر فلم يلبث أن مات في سنة تسع بالطاعون فولي بعده الفقيه عبد الولي بن محمد الوحظي بعد تنصل منه فمات أيضا عاجلا فاستقر ابن أخيه الفقيه محمد بن داود الوحظي فحسنت سيرته وكثر الثناء عليه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, Wajīh al-Dīn, Abū Muḥammad al-ʿArshānī. He served as the Qadi of Aden and later of Taʿizz. He died in the year 837 AH. After him, his brother Abū Bakr was appointed as the Qadi of Taʿizz, but he soon died of the plague in the year 839 AH. He was succeeded by the jurist (faqīh) ʿAbd al-Walī b. Muḥammad al-Waḥẓī, who accepted the post after some reluctance but also passed away shortly thereafter. Finally, his nephew, the jurist Muḥammad b. Dāwūd al-Waḥẓī, assumed the office, earned a good reputation, and was highly praised."@en .

rec:AIND-D03734 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03734-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03734-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03734 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أحمد الدمشقي الغرابيلي ويعرف بابن النميس تصغير نمس بنون ومهملة سمع في سنة خمس وثمانين وسبعمائة من المحب الصامت النصف الأول من عوالي أبي يعلى إسحاق بن عبد الرحمن الصابوني تخريج أبي سعد السكري وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء ومات قبل الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Dimashqī al-Ghurābīlī, known as Ibn al-Numays (Numays is a diminutive of numus, spelled with the letter nūn and a plain sīn). In the year 785 AH, he heard the first half of al-ʿAwālī by Abū Yaʿlā Isḥāq b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṣābūnī, compiled by Abū Saʿd al-Sukkarī, from al-Muḥibb al-Ṣāmit. He transmitted hadith, and distinguished scholars heard hadith from him. He died before 850 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03736 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03736-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03736-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03736 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن الجمال محمد بن أحمد العجمي الكيلاني الأصل المكي الحنبلي . ممن سمع مني بمكة وسافر للهند ودام سنين على طريقة غير مرضية ، وهو في سنة سبع وتسعين هناك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Jamal Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Ajamī al-Kilani, of Mecca, of Hanbali school. He heard hadith from me (al-Sakhawi) in Mecca, then traveled to India where he stayed for years in an unsatisfactory manner. He was still there in the year 897 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03739 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03739-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03739-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03739-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03739 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن الحسين وجيه الدين بن الشيخ ناصر الدين أبي الفرج بن الزين المراغي الأصل المدني أخو محمد الآتي . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad b. Abi Bakr b. al-Husayn, Wajih al-Din (b. al-Shaykh Nasir al-Din Abi al-Faraj b. al-Zayn al-Maraghi al-Asl al-Madani), the brother of Muhammad who is mentioned below. He heard from me (al-Sakhawi) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03743 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03743-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03743-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03743-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03743 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أبي بكر الزين بن الشيخ الشمس التتائي المالكي نزيل البرقوقية . ممن سمع على شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr, Zayn [al-Dīn] b. al-Shaykh al-Shams al-Tatāʾī, the Maliki, resident of al-Barqūqiyya. He was among those who heard hadith from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03748 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03748-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03748-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03748 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن حسن المكسكي البريهي التعزي اليماني . قال شيخنا في إنبائه : أحد الفضلاء باليمن برع في الفقه وغيره ثم حج فلما رجع مات وهو قافل في ثالث المحرم سنة عشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan al-Maksakī al-Burayhī al-Taʿzī al-Yamānī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Inbāʾ: 'He was one of the scholars of Yemen who excelled in jurisprudence (fiqh) and other fields. He then performed the pilgrimage (Hajj), and upon his return, he died while traveling in a caravan on the third of Muharram in the year 820.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D03749 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03749-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03749-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03749 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن حمزة المدني الحجار . سمع على النور المحلي والجمال الكازروني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ḥamza al-Madanī al-Ḥajjār. He heard (hadith) under al-Nūr al-Maḥallī and al-Jamāl al-Kāzarūnī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03753 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03753-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03753-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03753 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن صبيح المدني خادم الشيخ أبي الفرج المراغي وآل بيته . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ṣabīḥ al-Madanī. Servant of the shaykh Abū al-Faraj al-Marāghī and his household. He was among those who heard Hadith from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03756 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03756-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03756-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03756 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن ابن مؤلفه محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن عثمان السخاوي الأصل القاهري . مات في ذي الحجة سنة خمس وسبعين في طفوليته عوضه الله وإيانا الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the son of the author [al-Sakhāwī]. His full name is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿUthmān al-Sakhāwī [by origin], al-Qāhirī. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 875 AH during his childhood. May Allah compensate him and us with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D03758 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03758-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03758-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03758-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03758-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03758 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد القادر المليجي الأصل القاهري أخو محمد الآتي وأبوهما وباشر على أوقاف الأزهر وتكسب بالشهادة رأيته بالقاهرة في سنة تسع وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Qādir, of Malījī origin, of Cairo. He is the brother of Muḥammad, who is mentioned below, as well as their father. He supervised the waqfs of al-Azhar and earned a living through notary testimony (shahāda). I saw him in Cairo in the year 889 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03760 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03760-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03760-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03760-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03760 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن الجمال أبي الخير محمد بن عبد القادر بن محمد بن علي القرشي العدوي الجراني المدني الحنبلي ويعرف بابن الحجار . سمع على ابن صديق مع أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Jamāl Abū al-Khayr Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Qurashī al-ʿAdawī al-Jarānī al-Madanī al-Ḥanbalī, known as Ibn al-Ḥajjār. He heard (hadith) from Ibn Ṣiddīq together with his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D03764 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03764-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03764-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03764-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03764 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن فرحون البدر بن المحب أبي عبد الله اليعمري المدني المالكي أخو عبد الله الآتي ويعرف بابن فرحون . سمع نسخة أبي مسهر على العلم أبي الربيع سليمان السقا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Farḥūn, al-Badr (b. al-Muḥibb Abū ʿAbd Allāh), al-Yaʿmurī, al-Madanī, al-Mālikī. He is the brother of ʿAbd Allāh, who is mentioned below, and is known as Ibn Farḥūn. He heard the Hadith compilation *Nuskhat Abī Mushir* under al-ʿAlam Abū al-Rabīʿ Sulaymān al-Saqqā."@en .

rec:AIND-D03766 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03766-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03766-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03766-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03766-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03766-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03766 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الله بن نشابة الأشعري العريشي اليماني الشافعي الآتي أبوه . ولد سنة أربع وسبعين وسبعمائة وتفقه بأبيه وبأحمد مفتي مور وخلف والده ، قال الأهدل أنه اجتمع به بعد الثلاثين بأبيات حسين وهو مفتي بلده ومدرسها وينوب في الحكم بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Nashshāba al-Ashʿarī al-ʿArīshī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī, whose father is mentioned below. He was born in the year 774 AH. He studied jurisprudence (fiqh) under his father and under Aḥmad, the mufti of Mawr, and succeeded his father. Al-Ahdal stated that he met him after the year 830 AH at Abyāt Ḥusayn, where he was serving as the mufti, teacher, and deputy judge of his town."@en .

rec:AIND-D03767 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03767-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03767-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03767-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03767-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03767-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D03767-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03767 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الله الحضرمي العطار الفراش بالمسجد المكي جرده ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥaḍramī, al-ʿAṭṭār, the servant (farrāsh) at the Meccan Mosque. His biography was recorded and excerpted by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03768 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03768-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03768-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03768-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03768 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أبي عبد الله بن سلامة الماكسيني الدمشقي مؤذن جامعها ورئيسه كأبيه . سمع على ابن أبي التائب وعلى الزين عبد الغالب بن محمد الماكسيني مشيخته وغيرهما وحدث قال شيخنا أجاز لي غير مرة ومات في جمادى الأولى سنة إحدى ، وتبعه المقريزي في عقوده ورأيت من سمى جده محمدا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad b. Abi Abd Allah b. Salamah al-Makasini al-Dimashqi, the muezzin of the Great Mosque of Damascus and its chief, like his father. He heard from Ibn Abi al-Ta'ib and from al-Zayn Abd al-Ghalib b. Muhammad al-Makasini, studying the latter's Mashyakha and other works. He transmitted hadith, and our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) said: 'He granted me ijaza more than once.' He died in Jumada al-Ula in the year 801 AH, which al-Maqrizi also followed in his Uqud. I saw some who named his grandfather Muhammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D03769 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03769-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03769-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03769 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الملك بن الشيخ أبي محمد عبد الله بن محمد بن محمد الزين أبو الفرج القرشي البكري المرجاني الأصل المكي المالكي . سمع بالقاهرة على الشرف بن الكويك والشمس الشامي والزراتيتي في آخرين كالشهاب بن ظهيرة وذكره ابن فهد وأرخ وفاته بمكة في حادي عشر شعبان سنة سبع وثلاثين وبيض له البقاعي وأثبته الزين رضوان فيمن يؤخذ عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Malik b. al-Shaykh Abī Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, al-Zayn Abū al-Faraj al-Qurashī al-Bakrī, of Marjānī origin, al-Makkī al-Mālikī. He heard in Cairo from al-Sharaf b. al-Kuwayk, al-Shams al-Shāmī, and al-Zaratītī, among others such as al-Shihāb b. Ẓahīra. Ibn Fahd mentioned him and dated his death at Mecca to 11 Shaʿbān 837. Al-Biqāʿī left a blank space for him, and al-Zayn Riḍwān entered him among those from whom knowledge is to be taken."@en .

rec:AIND-D03771 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03771-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03771-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03771-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03771 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الوهاب بن عبد الله بن أسعد الوجيه بن الجمال حفيد العفيف اليافعي الأصل المكي الآتي أبوه وجده . ولد في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وثلاثين بمنى وحفظ ألفية النحو وعرضها على أبي حامد بن الضياء في سنة أربع وأربعين ، ودخل الهند وأثرى لاعتقادهم في سلفه ثم عاد لمكة حتى مات بها في صفر سنة ثمان وسبعين عفا الله عنه . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Asʿad al-Wajīh b. al-Jamāl, a descendant of al-ʿAfīf al-Yāfiʿī, originally from Mecca. His father and grandfather are mentioned below. He was born in Dhu al-Ḥijja, the year 831, in Minā. He memorized the Alfiyya on grammar and presented it to Abū Ḥāmid b. al-Ḍiyāʾ in the year 844. He entered India and became wealthy due to their devotion to his ancestors, then returned to Mecca where he resided until his death in Ṣafar, the year 878. May God forgive him. His obituary was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03772 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03772-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03772-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03772 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عثمان وجيه الدين البربهاري الأصل المكي العمري نسبة لعمل العمر الحنفي ويعرف بابن عثمان . ممن أخذ عني بمكة واشتغل قليلا واختص بصاحبنا النجم بن فهد ودخل الشام ومصر وغيرهما ومن شيوخه في الشام حميد الدين لازمه وتكسب بالعمر وتنزل في دروس يلبغا وغيره . مات بمكة في رمضان سنة اثنتين وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad b. Uthman, Wajih al-Din, of Barbahari origin, then of Mecca, known as al-Umari due to his work with the Umrah arrangements, a Hanafi also known as Ibn Uthman. He studied under me (al-Sakhawi) in Mecca, engaged in studies for a short while, and was closely associated with our companion Najm b. Fahd. He traveled to Syria, Egypt, and elsewhere. Among his teachers in Syria was Hamid al-Din, whom he accompanied closely. He made a living through Umrah services and was appointed to a position in the lectures of Yalbugha, among others. He died in Mecca in Ramadan, 882 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03774 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03774-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03774-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03774-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03774-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03774-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03774 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن أبي البركات محمد بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز النويري المكي . أجاز له في سنة ست وثلاثين وثمانمائة جماعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Barakāt Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī. A group of scholars granted him an ijāza (scholarly license) in the year 836 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03776 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03776-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03776-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03776 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن علي بن أبي بكر الزيني القمني ثم القاهري الشافعي الكتبي . ولد في يوم الاثنين ثامن جمادى الأولى سنة تسع وسبعين وسبعمائة بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Abi Bakr al-Zayni al-Qamani, later al-Qahiri, al-Shafi'i al-Kutubi. He was born in Cairo on Monday, 8 Jumada al-Ula 779 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03779 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03779-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03779-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03779-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03779 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن علي بن عقبة الوجيه المكي مهندس الحرم . كان خيرا دينا يخدم الناس كثيرا في العمائر خبيرا بالهندسة والعمارة وباشر ذلك مدة ثم ترك واستفاد دنيا وعقارا . مات في ذي الحجة سنة ست وعشرين بخيف بني شديد وقد بلغ السبعين . قاله الفاسي في مكة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿUqba al-Wajīh al-Makkī, the engineer of the Haram. He was a good and pious man, who frequently served people in construction, and was well-versed in engineering and architecture. He practiced this for a period of time, then left it and acquired wealth and real estate. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 826 H at Khayf Banī Shadīd, having reached the age of seventy. Al-Fāsī mentioned this in his history of Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03781 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03781-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03781-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03781-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03781-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03781 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن علي الزين السروى المديني الشافعي . ممن قرأ علي في النخبة وشرحها واشتغل يسيرا وفهم وانتدب لتعليم الابناء على خير وصلاح وحصل لبصره ضعف بل كف وهو من صوفية سعيد السعداء."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Ali al-Zayn al-Sarwi al-Madini al-Shafi'i. He was among those who read to me (al-Sakhawi) 'Nukhbat al-Fikr' and its commentary. He studied for a short while, understood well, and undertook the education of children with goodness and righteousness. His vision weakened, and he eventually became blind. He was one of the Sufis of Sa'id al-Su'ada."@en .

rec:AIND-D03783 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03783-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03783-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03783 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن ناصر الدين محمد بن عوض الرهاوي المكي العطار بباب السلام . ممن كان يتوجه لجدة في موسمها ومات بها في المحرم ظنا سنة تسع وسبعين وكان قد طلب حلتيتا يستعمله لصرف الريح فجيء إليه بأفيون غلطا فوضعه بمرق ثم شربه فكانت منيته وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بمعلاتها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad b. ʿAwaḍ al-Ruhāwī al-Makkī, the apothecary at Bāb al-Salām. He was among those who used to go to Jeddah during its season, and he died there, presumably in Muharram of the year 879 AH. He had requested asafoetida to use for flatulence, but by mistake, opium was brought to him; he put it in broth and drank it, which caused his death. He was carried to Mecca and buried in its al-Muʿallā cemetery."@en .

rec:AIND-D03784 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03784-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03784-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03784 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن الجمال محمد بن عيسى بن محمد بن عبد الله السلامي الطائفي الآتي أبوه . مات قبله بأيام في وباء كان بالطائف ونواحيه بالسلامة منه في العشر الأوسط من شعبان سنة ثلاث وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Salāmī al-Ṭāʾifī, whose father's biography is mentioned below. He died a few days before his father during a plague that struck al-Ta'if and its vicinities, in the middle ten days of Sha'ban, 843 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03785 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03785-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03785-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03785-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03785 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن غانم ... ثم المكي وإليها ومحتسها ويعرف بابن غانم . ولي الحسبة من السيد أبي القسم بن حسن بن عجلان المأذون له في ذلك عوضا عن المحب بن عز الدين في سنة ثمان وأربعين. ومات بمكة في صفر سنة اثنتين وستين."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ghānim, later al-Makkī. He resided in Mecca, served as its market inspector (muḥtasib), and was known as Ibn Ghānim. He was appointed as the muḥtasib of Mecca in the year 848 AH by al-Sayyid Abū al-Qāsim b. Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān, who was authorized to do so, replacing al-Muḥibb b. ʿIzz al-Dīn. He died in Mecca in the Hijri month of Ṣafar, in the year 862 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03786 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03786-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03786-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03786 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن فاضل بن عبد الرحمن الزين الجزائري المغربي المالكي نزيل رباط الموفق من مكة ويعرف بابن فاضل. شيخ فاضل مفنن قطن مكة ولازمني في المجاورة الثانية بها رواية ودراية ، وكان خيرا. مات في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى وثمانين ودفن بمعلاتها ولم يقصر عن السبعين رحمه الله."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Fāḍil b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Zayn al-Dīn, al-Jazāʾirī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī. He resided at Ribāṭ al-Muwaffaq in Mecca and was known as Ibn Fāḍil. He was a virtuous and versatile shaykh who settled in Mecca. He closely accompanied me (al-Sakhāwī) during his second extended stay (jawārah) there, studying both the transmission and comprehension of Hadith (riwāyatan wa-dirāyatan), and he was a righteous man. He died in Dhu al-Qaʿdah 881 AH and was buried in al-Muʿallā cemetery. He was nearly seventy years old. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03787 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03787-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03787-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03787 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن فتح الله ناصر الدين بن جمال الدين بن فتح الدين الشرواني الشافعي نزيل مكة. ممن سمع مني بمكة."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad b. Fath Allah Nasir al-Din b. Jamal al-Din b. Fath al-Din al-Shirwani al-Shafi'i, a resident of Mecca. He was among those who heard (hadith) from me (al-Sakhawi) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03788 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03788-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03788-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03788 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن محمد بن سلامة الماكسيني . مضى فيمن جده أبو عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Salāma al-Māksīnī. He was already mentioned under the section of those whose grandfather is Abū ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D03791 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03791-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03791-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03791-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03791-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03791 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عمر بن إبراهيم الزين الاسدي نسبة لبني أسد الدمشقي الشافعي والد عمر الآتي ويعرف بابن الجاموس . سمع على الجمال بن الشرائحي أمالي ابن سمعون ولقيه العز بن فهد فقرأ عليه يسيرا وكذا أخذ عنه غيره وأجاز ، وكان كأبيه أحد شهود دمشق . مات سنة ثلاث وسبعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad b. Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman b. Umar b. Ibrahim, Zayn, al-Asadi (attributed to Banu Asad), al-Dimashqi, al-Shafi'i. The father of Umar, who is mentioned below. Known as Ibn al-Jamus. He heard the Amali of Ibn Sam'un from al-Jamal b. al-Shara'ihi. Al-Izz b. Fahd met him and read a little to him, and others also took from him and he granted licenses. He was, like his father, one of the witnesses of Damascus. He died in the year 873 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03792 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03792-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03792-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03792 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد الكريم السمنودي الأصل الدمياطي أخو أصيل الدين محمد الآتي . خلف أخاه في الاقامة بمسجد ابن قيم تحت المرقب في دمياط لجمع المريدين على ذكر الله ويذكر بخير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān bin Muḥammad bin Muḥammad bin ʿAbd al-Karīm, of Samannūdī origin and Damietta residence, the brother of Aṣīl al-Dīn Muḥammad, who is mentioned below. He succeeded his brother in residing at the Ibn Qayyim Mosque under the Marqab in Damietta, gathering disciples (murīdīn) for the remembrance of Allah (dhikr), and he is remembered well."@en .

rec:AIND-D03795 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03795-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03795-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03795-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03795 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن البهاء محمد بن المحب محمد بن علي بن يوسف الزرندي المدني أخو عبد الباسط الماضي وسبط الجمال الكازروني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baha' Muhammad ibn al-Muhibb Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Yusuf al-Zarandi al-Madani. He is the brother of the aforementioned Abd al-Basit, and the maternal grandson (sibt) of al-Jamal al-Kazaruni."@en .

rec:AIND-D03798 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03798-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03798-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03798-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03798 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن النور محمد بن أبي عبد الله محمد بن محمد بن أبي القسم وجيه الدين المزجاجي الزبيدي اليماني الآتي أبوه . أصلهم من الأشاعرة انتقل جدهم إلى المزجاجة وهي قرية بأسفل وادي زبيد بكسر الميم واستوطن هذا زبيد واشتغل بالعلوم حتى مهر في الفقه والأدب والتصوف ونصبه جده للمشيخة لما تحقق أهليته وكان على طريقة حسنة . مات في سنة سبع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Nūr Muḥammad b. Abī ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Qāsim Wajīh al-Dīn al-Mizjājī al-Zabīdī al-Yamānī, whose father is mentioned below. Their origin is from the Ashʿarites; their grandfather moved to al-Mizjāja, which is a village at the lower part of Wādī Zabīd. He settled in Zabīd and engaged in studies until he mastered jurisprudence (fiqh), literature (adab), and Sufism (taṣawwuf). His grandfather appointed him to the mashyakhat after verifying his competence, and he maintained an excellent conduct. He died in the year 847 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03801 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03801-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03801-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03801-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03801 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن محمد بن يحيى الشرف الواسطي ثم السكندري ثم العدني . ذكره شيخنا في معجمه فقال كان أبوه من المحدثين ونشأ هو تاجرا فدخل اليمن فاستوطنها ولقيته بها مرارا وكان حسن المفاكهة والنادرة أنشدنا كثيرا لغيره ، وبلغني أنه مات سنة سبع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad b. Muhammad b. Yahya al-Sharaf al-Wasiti, later al-Sakandari, later al-Adani. Our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) mentioned him in his Mu'jam, saying: 'His father was one of the scholars of Hadith, and he grew up as a merchant. He entered Yemen and settled there. I met him there several times; he was of good humor and witty anecdotes, and recited to us much poetry of others.' It reached me that he died in the year 807 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03804 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03804-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03804-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03804-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03804 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن يعقوب بن إسماعيل بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الرحيم بن محمد بن يوسف بن أبي المعالي يحيى الشيباني والد عبد القادر الآتي وأخو أحمد الماضي ويعرف بابن زبرق"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb b. Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf b. Abī al-Maʿālī Yaḥyā al-Shaybānī. He is the father of ʿAbd al-Qādir (mentioned below) and brother of Aḥmad (mentioned above). He was known as Ibn Zibraq."@en .

rec:AIND-D03807 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03807-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03807-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03807-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03807 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن يونس بن محمد بن عمر أبو الفضل بن المحب بن الشرف البكتمري الأصل القاهري شقيق أحمد ويحيى المذكورين ووالدهم وعمه السيف الحنفي . ولد في جمادى الثانية سنة أربع وسبعين وثمانمائة وحضر عندي في دروس الصرغتمشية بل عرض على الكنز في سنة تسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad b. Yunus b. Muhammad b. Umar, Abu al-Fadl, the son of al-Muhibb and al-Sharaf, of Buktumuri origin, of Cairo. He is the brother of the aforementioned Ahmad and Yahya, and their father and their uncle al-Sayf al-Hanafi. He was born in Jumada al-Thaniyah, the year 874 H. He attended my lectures at the Sarghatmashiyya Madrasah, and presented (recited) the book 『al-Kanz』 to me in the year 890 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D03810 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03810-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03810-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03810 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد البجواني قاضي أب . مات سنة ثلاث وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad al-Bajwānī, the qāḍī of Ibb. He died in the year 823 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03811 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03811-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03811-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03811-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03811-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03811-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03811 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمد الحريري الصوفي المؤذن بالجامع المصري . قال شيخنا في معجمه كان من لطفاء المصريين حسن النادرة كثير النظم المغسول سمعت من فوائده ومن نظمه ومدحني بأبيات . مات في رمضان سنة ثمان"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad al-Ḥarīrī al-Ṣūfī, the muezzin of the Egyptian Mosque (Mosque of ʿAmr). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Muʿjam: 'He was among the witty Egyptians, possessing pleasant humor, and composed many vernacular verses (al-naẓm al-maghsūl). I heard some of his scholarly notes (fawāʾid) and his poetry, and he praised me with some verses.' He died in Ramaḍān, the year 808."@en .

rec:AIND-D03812 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03812-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03812-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03812-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03812 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن ابن شيخنا البدر محمود بن أحمد العيني الأصل القاهري أخو عبد الرحيم الآتي ويلقب قرة العين . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وعشرين مطعونا . أرخه أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman, the son of our shaykh al-Badr Mahmud bin Ahmad al-Ayni, Cairene by origin. He was the brother of Abd al-Rahim, who is mentioned below. He was nicknamed Qurrat al-Ayn. He died of the plague in Rabi' al-Akhir in the year 822 AH, and his death was chronologized by his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D03814 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03814-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03814-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03814 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن محمود بن علي البعلي خطيبها . مات سنة اثنتي عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Maḥmūd b. ʿAlī al-Baʿlī, the preacher (khaṭīb) of Baʿlabakk. He died in the year 812 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03816 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03816-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03816-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03816-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03816 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن موسى بن إبراهيم الزين بن الشرف بن البرهان أخو محمد الآتي وأبوهما ويعرف بابن البرهان . كان عاقلا يتكلم في بعض جهات المكيين . مات في أحد الربيعين سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Mūsā b. Ibrāhīm, al-Zayn b. al-Sharaf b. al-Burhān. He is the brother of Muḥammad, who is mentioned below, and [also has an entry for] their father. He was known as Ibn al-Burhān. He was sensible and spoke on behalf of some of the Meccans' affairs. He died in one of the two Rabīʿ months in the year 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03819 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03819-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03819-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03819 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن هبة الله الملحاني اليماني . جاور بمكة وكان بصيرا بالقراءات سريع القراءة قرأ في الشتاء في يوم ثلاث ختمات وثلث ختمة ، وكان دينا عابدا مشاركا في عدة علوم . مات في رجب سنة إحدى وعشرين . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ، ومن شيوخه في القراءات محمد بن يحيى الشارفي الهمداني أخذ عنه السبع شيخنا الشهاب الشوايطي بل شاركه في الأخذ عن الشارفي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Hibat Allah al-Milhani al-Yamani. He resided in Mecca as a neighbor (jawara) and was deeply knowledgeable in the Quranic recitations (qira'at) and exceptionally fast in his recitation, completing three and a third full recitations (khatmas) of the Quran in a single day during the winter. He was a pious, devout worshiper who was also well-versed in several other sciences. He died in the month of Rajab in the year 821 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) mentioned him in his work Inba' al-Ghumr. Among his teachers in Quranic recitations was Muhammad b. Yahya al-Sharifi al-Hamdani, from whom he studied the Seven Recitations. Our shaykh al-Shihab al-Shawayti also studied under al-Sharifi, sharing the same teacher."@en .

rec:AIND-D03820 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03820-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03820-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03820-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03820-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03820 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن يحيى بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي الخير محمد بن محمد بن فهد الهاشمي المكي أخو عبد القادر الآتي . ولد في ذي القعدة سنة اثنتين وعشرين وثمانمائة بمكة وحضر عند ابن الجزري وابن سلامة وأجاز له جماعة ، ومات بها وهو طفل في مستهل ربيع الأول سنة سبع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Yahya b. Abd al-Rahman b. Abi al-Khayr Muhammad b. Muhammad b. Fahd al-Hashimi al-Makki, the brother of the forthcoming Abd al-Qadir. He was born in Dhu al-Qa'da 822 AH in Mecca. He attended the lectures of Ibn al-Jazari and Ibn Salama, and a group of scholars granted him ijaza. He passed away in Mecca as a child on the first of Rabi' al-Awwal 827 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03829 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03829-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03829-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03829-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03829-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03829 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن يوسف الدمياطي خادم الفقراء بها . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman b. Yusuf al-Dimyati. Servant of the poor (Sufis) there [in Damietta]. He was among those who acquired knowledge from me [al-Sakhawi] in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03830 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03830-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03830-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03830-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03830 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن بن فخر الدين بن تقي الدين الحسني أخو نقيب الاشراف وابن نقيبهم . مات في ربيع الأول سنة ثلاث . ذكره شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman bin Fakhr al-Din bin Taqi al-Din al-Hasani. He was the brother of the Naqib al-Ashraf (marshal of the nobility) and the son of their Naqib. He died in Rabi' al-Awwal in the year 803 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Hajar) mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03832 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03832-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03832-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03832-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03832-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03832 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن الزين أبو الفرج الازراري الصوفي السهروردي القادري الشافعي . عبد صالح أخذ عن الشيخ يوسف الصفي ومحمد العطار وغيره من أصحاب الجمال يوسف العجمي رأيته كثيرا وصحبه فقيهي وزوج عمتي الفقيه حسين وتدرب به في عقد الازرار فإنه كان يتكسب بعقدها بحانوت عند باب جامع الحاكم وبه مات في ربيع الأول سنة إحدى وخمسين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Zayn Abū al-Faraj al-Azrārī al-Ṣūfī al-Suhrawardī al-Qādirī al-Shāfiʿī. A righteous servant, he took [knowledge] from al-Shaykh Yūsuf al-Ṣafī, Muḥammad al-ʿAṭṭār, and others among the companions of al-Jamāl Yūsuf al-ʿAjamī. I saw him frequently. My jurist and the husband of my aunt, the jurist Ḥusayn, accompanied him and trained under him in button-making (ʿaqd al-azrār). He used to earn his living by making buttons in a shop near the gate of al-Ḥākim Mosque, where he died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal, the year 851 H. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03833 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03833-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03833-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03833-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03833 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن الأمين المصري أحد قراء الجوق وممن له نوبة في القلعة . أخذها شعيب بن السواق . مات سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman al-Amin al-Misri. One of the reciters of the choir (al-jawq) and among those who had a turn (nawba) in the Citadel (al-Qal'a). Shu'ayb b. al-Sawwaq took over his turn. He died in the year 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03834 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03834-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03834-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03834-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03834 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن تقي الدين القبابي القاهري المالكي ابن عم محيي الدين يحيى الدمشقي . ناب في القضاء عن البساطين ودرس للمالكية بالجمالية برغبة الشمس البساطي له عنها وكذا كان معه حصة في تدريس القمحية بمصر . مات واستقر في الجمالية البدر بن التنسي وفي الحصة القرافي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman Taqi al-Din al-Qababi al-Qahiri al-Maliki, the cousin of Muhyi al-Din Yahya al-Dimashqi. He served as a deputy judge on behalf of al-Bisati, and taught the Malikis at al-Jamaliyya after Shams [al-Din] al-Bisati stepped down in his favor. He also held a share in the teaching position at al-Qamhiyya in Egypt (Cairo). He died, after which al-Badr b. al-Tansi succeeded him at al-Jamaliyya, and al-Qarafi succeeded him in his share [at al-Qamhiyya]."@en .

rec:AIND-D03835 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03835-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03835-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03835 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن الزين الدمشقي الحريري الشافعي أحد المتصوفة الملازمين للتقي بن قاضي عجلون كتب عنه البدري في مجموعه قوله : %~% ومقاعدي فض لي %~% أشكاله المتعدده %~% %~% كم ساقني ساق له %~% إذ قمت أهوى مقعده %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman al-Zayn al-Dimashqi al-Hariri al-Shafi'i. One of the Sufis who studied under (and constantly accompanied) al-Taqi Ibn Qadi Ajlun. Al-Badri copied his poetry in his compilation (Majmūʿ al-Badrī): 'My seating arrangements surpassed me in their various forms / How many times did a cupbearer of his urge me, when I stood yearning for his seat.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D03836 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03836-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03836-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03836 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن الزين الحضكيفي . سمع من لفظ شيخنا في البخاري ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Zayn al-Ḥaṣkafī. He heard Sahih al-Bukhari from the dictation of our shaykh (Ibn Hajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03837 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03837-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03837-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03837 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن القاضي زين الدين الزرعي الحنفي . ممن رافقه الصلاح الطرابلسي بعد الخمسين في الأخذ لما قرأه من التحقيق في الأصول على القاضي سعد الدين وقال إنه كان فقيها كثير الاستحضار من كتابه المجمع حسن الخط ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Zarʿī al-Ḥanafī, Zayn al-Dīn al-Qāḍī. Al-Ṣalāḥ al-Ṭarābulusī accompanied him after 850 AH in learning what he read of al-Taḥqīq in legal theory (uṣūl) under al-Qāḍī Saʿd al-Dīn. Al-Ṣalāḥ remarked that he was a jurist who was exceptionally quick to recall from his book al-Majmaʿ, and that he possessed beautiful handwriting."@en .

rec:AIND-D03838 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03838-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03838-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03838 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن الزين الشربيني الشافعي نزيل دمياط أقام بها نحو ثلاث سنين وأقرأ بها وممن قرأ عليه التقي بن وكيل السلطان ووصفه بالقاضي العالم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman al-Zayn al-Sharbini al-Shafi'i, a resident of Damietta. He stayed there for about three years and taught. Among those who read under him was al-Taqi b. Wakil al-Sultan, who described him as 'the learned judge'."@en .

rec:AIND-D03839 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03839-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03839-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03839 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن الزيني الحمزاوي أحد الطبلخانات بدمشق . قتل في المجردين لسوار سنة ثلاث وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Zaynī al-Ḥamzāwī, one of the holders of the ṭablakhānāt (military officers/band) in Damascus. He was killed in the year 873 AH during the expeditionary forces (al-mujarradīn) sent against Shah Suwar of Dulkadir."@en .

rec:AIND-D03840 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03840-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03840-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03840 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن الحبابي البصري . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة سبع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman al-Hababi al-Basri. He died in Mecca in al-Muharram, the year 867."@en .

rec:AIND-D03841 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03841-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03841-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03841-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03841 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن الطنتدائي ويعرف بالخليفة شيخ الطائفة السطوحية . كان ينزل المدرسة الفارسية من القاهرة ويعمل بها بعد صلاة الجمعة عنده السماع فيحضره الخلائق وشفاعاته قل أن ترد مع تودده . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة ثلاث ، ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṭantidāʾī, known as al-Khalīfa, the leader (shaykh) of the Suṭūḥiyya order. He used to reside in al-Madrasa al-Fārisiyya in Cairo, where he held samāʿ (spiritual music gatherings) after the Friday prayer, which was attended by crowds of people. His intercessions were rarely rejected, along with his friendliness. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira, the year 803 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his history book 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』."@en .

rec:AIND-D03842 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03842-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03842-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03842 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن القرموني الفاسي ، كان هو وأبوه من علماء فاس ومدرسيها ، مات سنة خمس وستين . ذكره لي بعض المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Qarmūnī al-Fāsī. He and his father were among the scholars and teachers of Fes. He died in the year 865 AH. Some Moroccans mentioned him to me."@en .

rec:AIND-D03843 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03843-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03843-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03843-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03843 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن المهتار مات مقتولا بصفد في ذي القعدة سنة تسع وكان تأمر وغزا الترك وأفسد فيما هنالك بكثرة الفتن . قاله المقريزي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "'Abd al-Rahman al-Mihtar. He was killed in Safad in Dhu al-Qa'da, year 809 AH. He had been appointed as an amir, campaigned against the Turks, and caused corruption there through numerous conflicts. Mentioned by al-Maqrizi."@en .

rec:AIND-D03844 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03844-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03844-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03844-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03844 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن خادم رباط بعلجد وأحد فقراء عمر العرابي ، مات بمكة في صفر سنة تسع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahman, the servant of Ribat Ba'ljadd and one of the poor disciples (Sufis) of Umar al-Urabi. He died in Mecca in Safar, the year 869."@en .

rec:AIND-D03845 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03845-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03845-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03845-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03845-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03845 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحمن شيخ البيمارستان بمكة ، مات بها في شوال سنة ست وأربعين . أرخهما ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the shaykh (director) of the hospital in Mecca. He died there in Shawwāl, 846 AH. His date of death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D03848 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03848-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03848-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03848 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن محمد نجم الدين بن محي الدين بن تاج الدين ابن قطب الدين الرفاعي . أخذ عن جماعة وأخذ عنه الطاووسي وأرخ وفاته في يوم الثلاثاء خامس ذي القعدة سنة عشرين وعظمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad Najm al-Dīn b. Muḥyī al-Dīn b. Tāj al-Dīn b. Quṭb al-Dīn al-Rifāʿī. He studied under a group of scholars, and al-Ṭāwūsī studied under him. Al-Ṭāwūsī recorded his death as occurring on Tuesday, the 5th of Dhū al-Qaʿda, in the year 820 AH, and held him in high esteem."@en .

rec:AIND-D03849 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03849-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03849-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03849 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن إبراهيم اليزناسي بالتحتانية المفتوحة ثم زاي ساكنة ونون ومهملة نسبة لقبيلة المغربي الفاسي قاضيها . مات بعيد الثلاثين وهو ممن عمل وثائق للشهود . أفاده لي بعض أصحابنا من المغاربة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Ibrāhīm al-Yaznāsī (the name al-Yaznāsī is spelled with an opened yaʾ, a quiescent zāy, a nūn, and an unmarked sīn, referring to a Maghribī tribe), al-Fāsī, who was the judge of Fez. He died shortly after 830 AH. He was among those who drafted notary documents for witnesses. One of our Maghribī companions informed me of him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03850 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03850-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03850-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03850-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03850 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن أحمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي اليماني ثم المكي . ولد باليمن سنة أربع وثلاثين وثمانمائة ونشأ به ثم قدم مكة مع أبيه فسمع أبا الفتح المراغي ، وأجاز له جماعة واشتغل بالفقه عند البرهان بن ظهيرة وأبي البركات الهيثمي ، ولازم المحب بن أبي السعادات فلما ولي الثانية استنا به بجدة . مات بمكة في رمضان سنة اثنتين وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahim b. Ahmad b. Abi Bakr b. Abd Allah b. Zuhayra b. Ahmad b. Atiyya b. Zuhayra al-Qurashi al-Yamani, later al-Makki. He was born in Yemen in the year 834 AH, where he grew up, and then traveled to Mecca with his father. There, he heard from Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī, and a group of scholars (jama'a) granted him ijazas. He studied jurisprudence (fiqh) under Burhan al-Din b. Zuhayra and Abu al-Barakat al-Haythami, and closely associated with al-Muhibb b. Abi al-Sa'adat, who appointed him as his deputy in Jeddah during his second term of office. He died in Mecca in Ramadan in the year 882 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03853 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03853-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03853-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03853-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03853-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03853-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D03853-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03853 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن أحمد بن محمد بن منصور زين الدين ومحب الدين الفوي الأصل القاهري الحسيني سكنا ويعرف بابن بحيح بمهملتين تصغير بح وهو لقب لجده . قرأ المنهاج وعرضه واشتغل على الحناوي والشريف النسابة والعز عبد السلام البغدادي وتكسب بالشهادة بل ناب في القضاء عن البدر أبي السعادات فمن بعده . مات في رمضان سنة تسع وسبعين ، وهو والد زوج القاضي شمس الدين بن بيرم الحنبلي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Manṣūr, Zayn al-Dīn and Muḥibb al-Dīn. Originally from Fuwwa, of Cairo, residing in al-Ḥusayniyya, and known as Ibn Baḥīḥ (after his grandfather's nickname Baḥ). He recited and presented 『al-Minhāj』, studied under al-Ḥannāwī, al-Sharīf al-Nassāba, and al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-Salām al-Baghdādī. He earned his living as a notary witness (al-Shahāda), and served as deputy judge on behalf of al-Badr Abū al-Saʿādāt and his successors. He died in Ramaḍān 879 AH. He was the father-of-the-wife of the Hanbali judge Shams al-Dīn b. Bayram."@en .

rec:AIND-D03860 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03860-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03860-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03860 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن حسن بن قاسم الزين القدسي رفيق إبراهيم بن إسحق العينوسي في الشهادة . مات في يوم الجمعة ثاني رجب سنة خمس وستين . عبد الرحيم بن أبي الحسن سبط الشمس بن النقاش . في ابن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Ḥasan b. Qāsim, al-Zayn al-Qudsī. He was a colleague of Ibrāhīm b. Isḥāq al-ʿAynūsī in the notary profession (al-shahāda). He died on Friday, 2 Rajab, 865 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03864 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03864-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03864-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03864 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد معين الدين بن صفي الدين بن شهاب الدين الحسيني البمي الكرماني الشافعي . ممن سمع مني وعلي أشياء بمكة ، وكتبت له اجازة في كراسة وسافر إلى بلاده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahim bin Abd al-Rahman bin Ahmad Muin al-Din bin Safi al-Din bin Shihab al-Din al-Husayni al-Bami al-Kirmani al-Shafi'i. He heard from me and recited to me various works in Mecca. I wrote an ijaza for him in a booklet, and he then traveled back to his homeland."@en .

rec:AIND-D03868 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03868-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03868-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03868 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن عبد الله بن الشيخ خليل القلعي . كتب من دمشق على استدعاء مؤرخ بسنة ثمان وثمانين وما علمت أمره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahim b. Abd Allah b. al-Shaykh Khalil al-Qal'i. He wrote from Damascus on an istid'a' (scholarly petition for ijaza) dated in the year 888 AH, and I do not know his circumstances."@en .

rec:AIND-D03870 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03870-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03870-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03870-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03870 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن عبد الوهاب الفقيه زين الدين بن تاج الدين الطنتدائي خليفة المقام الأحمدي بها . مات هناك في صفر سنة ثمان وستين . أرخه ابن المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, the jurist, Zayn al-Dīn, al-Ṭantidāʾī. He was the deputy of the al-Maqām al-Aḥmadī (shrine of Aḥmad al-Badawī) in Tantidā. He died there in Safar, 868 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn al-Munīr."@en .

rec:AIND-D03871 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03871-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03871-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03871 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن عثمان بن الرومة السيلوني . ذكره النجم بن فهد في معجمه وبيض له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahim bin Uthman bin al-Ruma al-Sayluni. Al-Najm b. Fahd mentioned him in his dictionary (Muʿjam), leaving a blank space for his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D03873 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03873-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03873-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03873-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03873-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03873 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن علي بن محمد بن عمر الزين الطولوني الأصل المدني الشافعي مهندس الحرم ويعرف بالمهندس وبابن البناء . مات سنة إحدى وتسعين وهو ممن حفظ العمدة والمنهاجين وألفية ابن مالك واشتغل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahim b. Ali b. Muhammad b. Umar, Zayn al-Din, of Tulunid origin, resident of Medina, Shafi'i, the architect (engineer) of the Sanctuary, known as al-Muhandis and as Ibn al-Banna. He died in the year 891. He was among those who memorized al-Umda, the two Minhajs, and Alfiyyat Ibn Malik, and engaged in scholarly study."@en .

rec:AIND-D03879 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03879-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03879-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03879-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03879-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03879 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن محمد بن أبي بكر الرومي الحنفي . أظنه ابن الإمام الآتي فيمن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-Rūmī al-Ḥanafī. I think he is Ibn al-Imām (the son of the Imam), who is mentioned below under those whose father was not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D03880 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03880-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03880-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03880 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن محمد بن حسن بهاء الدين خواجة بن القاضي الفاضل الشمس بن فخر القضاة والأكابر القاضي إمام الدين المكي الأصل الاردستاني الشافعي تلميذ فضل الله الآتي . شاب فاضل سمع مني وعلي بمكة ما سمعه وقرأه شيخه المشار إليه وكتبت له في مجموعه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Rahim bin Muhammad bin Hasan Baha' al-Din Khawaja, son of the virtuous judge al-Shams, son of the pride of judges and notables, Judge Imam al-Din. Originally of Meccan origin, from Ardistan, and of the Shafi'i school. He was a student of Fadl Allah, who is mentioned below. He was a virtuous youth who heard from me and recited to me in Mecca what his aforementioned teacher had heard and recited, and I wrote a certification for him in his compilation (majmuʿ)."@en .

rec:AIND-D03886 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03886-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03886-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03886-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03886 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن الخواجا جمال الدين محمد بن مهدي بن حسن الطائي المكي الآتي أبوه . مات وهو صغير في رمضان سنة ست وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm, son of al-Khawājā Jamāl al-Dīn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī ibn Ḥasan al-Ṭāʾī al-Makkī, whose father is mentioned below. He died while he was a child in Ramaḍān, in the year 886 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03889 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03889-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03889-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03889 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن أبي الهدى بن تقي الكازروني المدني أخو عبد الرحمن . سمع على الزين المراغي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Abī al-Hudā ibn Taqī al-Kāzarūnī al-Madanī. The brother of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. He heard hadith from al-Zayn al-Marāghī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03890 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03890-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03890-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03890-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03890 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم بن محيي الدين بن الجيعان وأبوه ابن عم العلمي شاكر . باشر بعد والده استيفاء البيمارستان وغيره من وظائفه إلى أن مات سنة خمس وخمسين واستقر بعده في الاستيفاء الزين عبد الباسط بن العلمي المشار إليه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm bin Muḥyī al-Dīn bin al-Jīʿān. His father was the cousin of al-ʿAlamī Shākir. He succeeded his father as the comptroller (istīfāʾ) of the Bīmāristān and in his other offices until his death in the year 855 AH. After his death, al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ, the son of the aforementioned al-ʿAlamī, succeeded him in the comptrollership."@en .

rec:AIND-D03892 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03892-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03892-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03892-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03892-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03892 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم شيخ الشيوخ الزيني المقدسي الحنفي بن النقيب . ولد في سنة خمس وثمانمائة وولي مشيخة التنكزية والارغونية وأعاد بالمعظمية . ومات في عصر يوم السبت ثالث عشر شعبان سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm, Shaykh al-Shuyūkh, Zayn al-Dīn al-Maqdisī al-Ḥanafī Ibn al-Naqīb. He was born in 805 AH, held the mashyakha of the Tankiziyya and the Arghūniyya, and served as muʿīd at the Muʿaẕẕamiyya. He died on the afternoon of Saturday, 13 Shaʿbān 853 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03893 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03893-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03893-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03893 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم الحصيني قاضي الانكحة بتونس . مات سنة تسع وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Ḥuṣaynī, the marriage judge (qāḍī al-ankiḥa) of Tunis. He died in the year 889 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03894 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03894-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03894-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03894 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرحيم العباسي الشافعي . ممن قرض للبدري مجموعه قريب السبعين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-ʿAbbāsī al-Shāfiʿī. He was one of those who composed a commendation (taqrīẓ) for al-Badrī's compilation (majmūʿ) around [the year] seventy [870 AH]."@en .

rec:AIND-D03898 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03898-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03898-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03898 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرزاق بن حسن الدنجيهي ثم القاهري الشافعي أحد صوفية سعيد السعداء وصلحائها حفظ القرآن والمنهاج ولازم درس أبي العدل البلقيني وأخذ عن غيره وكتب المنسوب وتولى سقي الصوفية بالمزملة ثم كبر وزاد على الخير إقبالا حتى مات في رمضان سنة ست وتسعين عن بضع وسبعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. Ḥasan al-Danjīhī, later al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī. He was one of the Sufis and righteous men of Khānqāh Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. He memorized the Qurʾān and al-Minhāj, closely attended the lectures of Abū al-ʿAdl al-Bulqīnī, and studied under others. He wrote in the elegant al-mansūb script and was appointed to serve water to the Sufis at the muzammala (water station). Later in life he grew ever more devoted to good works, until he died in Ramaḍān 896 AH, in his seventies. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03900 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03900-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03900-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03900 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرزاق بن سليمان الخليلي بن الأكرم . مات سنة تسع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. Sulaymān al-Khalīlī b. al-Akram. He died in the year 819 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03901 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03901-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03901-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03901 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرزاق بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد التاج الكومي نسبة لكوم التجار الرفاعي . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad, al-Tāj, al-Kūmī (relative to Kūm al-Tujjār), al-Rifāʿī. He was among those who studied with (took from) me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03903 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03903-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03903-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03903-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03903 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرزاق بن كريم الدين عبد الكريم بن عبد الغني بن يعقوب ابن فخيرة بالمعجمة مصغر فعبد الغني كان يلقب فخر الدين فصغروه . أحد كتاب المماليك وابن عم أبي الخير محمد بن يحيى بن عبد الغني الآتي . مات في يوم الجمعة منتصف ربيع الأول سنة أربع وسبعين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. Karīm al-Dīn ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Yaʿqūb, known as Ibn Fukhayra (with the dotted khāʾ, in diminutive form: ʿAbd al-Ghanī bore the laqab Fakhr al-Dīn, which people turned into a diminutive). He was one of the clerks of the Mamluks (kuttāb al-mamālīk) and the cousin of Abū al-Khayr Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī, who is mentioned later. He died on Friday, in mid-Rabīʿ I 874 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03906 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03906-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03906-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03906-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03906 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرزاق بن عبد الله المجاور بالمجامع الأموي . كان أحد المعتقدين وله أتباع . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة عشر وقد بلغ السبعين . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Razzāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who performed jiwār (extended devotional stay) at the Umayyad Mosque. He was one of those who were highly revered and had followers. He died in Jumādā I in the year 810 AH, having reached seventy years of age. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D03908 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03908-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03908-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03908-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03908 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرزاق بن عثمان جمال الدين التركماني السكندري التاجر. مات في رمضان سنة تسع وأربعين. أرخه ابن عزم."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. ʿUthmān Jamāl al-Dīn al-Turkumānī al-Sakandarī, the merchant. He died in Ramaḍān of the year 849 AH. Ibn ʿAzm recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03909 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03909-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03909-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03909 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرزاق بن أبي الفرج والي قطيا. مات سنة ثمان."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. Abī al-Faraj, governor (wālī) of Qaṭyā. He died in the year 808 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03913 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03913-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03913-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03913-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03913-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03913 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرزاق بن يحيى تاج الدين المقسي الحنفي الناسخ ويعرف بتاج الدين . تكسب بالشهادة وبرع فيها وكتب الكثير بالاجرة وكان سريع الكتابة غير طائلها مع سماحته ولينه ، وحج وجاور غير مرة . مات بالقاهرة في رمضان سنة ست وثمانين بعد توعك طويل وأظنه جاز الخمسين رحمه الله وعفا عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. Yaḥyā Tāj al-Dīn al-Maqsī al-Ḥanafī, the copyist, known as Tāj al-Dīn. He earned his living as a notary (shahāda) and excelled in it. He copied a great deal for wages; he was a rapid copyist, though the result was not of high quality, and he was generous and mild. He performed the Ḥajj and stayed in Mecca (mujāwara) more than once. He died in Cairo in Ramaḍān 886 AH after a long illness, and I think he had passed fifty. May God have mercy on him and forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03915 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03915-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03915-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03915 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرزاق بن القوق الحلبي . ولي استادارية حلب بعد انفصال ابن المنقار ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. al-Qūq al-Ḥalabī. He was appointed to the ustādāriyya (major-domo's office) of Aleppo after the dismissal of Ibn al-Minqār."@en .

rec:AIND-D03916 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03916-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03916-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03916 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرزاق الشرواني نزيل الرواحية بحلب وقطنها نحو عشرين سنة وأحد فضلائها الشافعية ممن أخذ عن العلاء البخاري ، وتقدم في العقليات وانتفع به الفضلاء ومنهم الشمس بن أمير حاج الحنفي فإنه أخذ عنه النحو والصرف والمعاني والبيان والمنطق وصاهر عبد الكريم باني المدرسة التي بباب قنسرين على ابنته واستمر حتى مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Razzāq al-Shirwānī. A resident of the Rawāḥiyya Madrasa in Aleppo, where he lived for about twenty years, becoming one of its prominent Shafi'i scholars. He studied under al-ʿAlāʾ al-Bukhārī and excelled in the rational sciences. Many scholars benefited from him, among whom was the Hanafi scholar al-Shams ibn Amīr Ḥājj, who studied grammar, morphology, semantics, rhetoric, and logic under him. He married the daughter of ʿAbd al-Karīm, the founder of the madrasa at the Qinnasrin Gate, and remained there until his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03918 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03918-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03918-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03918 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرءوف بن عبد الله بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد ابن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي المكي . ولد في سنة ست وأربعين وثمانمائة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raʾūf b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓahīra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī al-Makkī. He was born in the year 846 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03919 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03919-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03919-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03919 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرءوف بن علي بن عمر بن إبراهيم بن أبي بكر بن محمد اليمني . مات سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raʾūf ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Yamanī. He died in the year 857 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03920 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03920-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03920-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03920 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الرءوف بن محمد بن قاسم الآتي أبوه من شهود مكة والواعظ أبوه . كان ممن سمع علي بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Raʾūf b. Muḥammad b. Qāsim—whose father is mentioned below—one of the notary-witnesses of Mecca; his father was the preacher (al-wāʿiẓ). He was among those who heard from me there [in Mecca]."@en .

rec:AIND-D03921 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03921-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03921-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03921 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز المدني الشافعي ويعرف بجده . ممن قدم القاهرة وسمع على شيخنا وغيره واشتغل قليلا وصحب البقاعي . مات بعد الستين أو نحوها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Salām b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī, known by his grandfather's name (Ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz). He came to Cairo, heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others, studied a little, and kept company with al-Biqāʿī. He died after the year 860 AH or thereabouts."@en .

rec:AIND-D03923 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03923-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03923-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03923 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام بن حسن العز الخالدي أخو عبد الرحمن الماضي ويعرف بالكذاب . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة ثلاث وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥasan al-ʿIzz al-Khālidī, the brother of the aforementioned ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, known as al-Kadhdhāb (the Liar). He died in Mecca in Muḥarram of the year 843 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03926 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03926-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03926-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03926 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام بن أبي الفتح بن إسماعيل بن علي بن محمد بن داود الزمزمي المكي . مات بها في ذي الحجة سنة خمس وسبعين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Abī al-Fatḥ ibn Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Zamzamī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 875 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03927 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03927-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03927-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03927 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام بن أبي الفرج بن عبد اللطيف الأنصاري الزرندي المدني . سمع على الزين المراغي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Salām b. Abī al-Faraj b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Anṣārī al-Zarandī al-Madanī. He heard (hadith) from al-Zayn al-Marāghī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03928 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03928-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03928-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03928 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام بن محمد بن أبي الفضل النفطي المدني أخو عبد الكافي الآتي ، ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Salām b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Faḍl al-Nafṭī al-Madanī, the brother of ʿAbd al-Kāfī, who is mentioned below. He was among those who heard from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03929 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03929-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03929-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03929-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03929-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D03929-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03929 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام بن محمد بن أبي الخير محمد بن علي بن عبد الله بن علي ابن عبد السلام أخو أبي الخير الكازروني المكي . ولد بها في جمادى الأولى سنة أربع وأربعين ، ونشأ بها فحفظ القرآن واستقر في رياسة المؤذنين بالمسجد الحرام بعد أبيهما سنة سبع وخمسين فلم يولد له . ومات في ذي القعدة سنة خمس أو ثمان وستين والأول أقرب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Salām b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Khayr Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Salām, the brother of Abū al-Khayr al-Kāzarūnī al-Makkī. He was born in Mecca in Jumādā I 844 AH, grew up there and memorized the Qurʾān. In 857 AH he succeeded their father as chief of the muezzins (riyāsat al-muʾadhdhinīn) of the Masjid al-Ḥarām. He had no children. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year 865 or 868 AH, the former being closer to the truth."@en .

rec:AIND-D03931 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03931-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03931-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03931 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام الثاني أخو الذي قبله . ولد في عاشر المحرم سنة اثنتين وستين وثمانمائة بالمدينة ونشأ بها فسمع على أبيه وأبي الفرج المراغي وأبي الفتح بن تقي وآخرين ولازمني كثيرا في مجاورتي عند المصطفى صلى الله عليه وسلم وكتبت له بما سمعه مني وعلى إجازة أوردت شيئا منها في تاريخ المدنيين ، ثم ورد مكة في سنة أربع وتسعين فسمع من تصانيفي على أشياء وهو ساكن فهم مذكور بالخير والصلاح ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Salam II, the brother of the one mentioned before him. He was born on the 10th of Muharram in the year 862 AH in Medina and grew up there. He heard hadith from his father, Abu al-Faraj al-Maraghi, Abu al-Fatah b. Taqi, and others. He associated with me closely during my stay (mujawara) near the Chosen One [i.e., Medina/the Prophet's Mosque], and I wrote down for him what he heard from me, and granted him an ijaza, some of which I included in 'Tarikh al-Madaniyyin' (History of the Medinese). Later, he arrived in Mecca in the year 894 AH and heard some of my works from me. He is quiet and discerning, spoken of for goodness and piety."@en .

rec:AIND-D03932 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03932-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03932-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03932 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن يحيى الامام عز الدين الخشبي المدني . سمع على النور المحلي سبط الزبير في الاكتفاء للكلاعي سنة عشرين وعلى الزين أبي بكر المراغي وكتب تصنيفه تحقيق النصرة بتلخيص معالم دار الهجرة وانتهى في جمادى الثانية سنة ست عشرة وثمانمائة وشهد على مؤلفه بوقفه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Salām b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā, al-Imām ʿIzz al-Dīn al-Khashabī al-Madanī. He heard al-Kalāʿī's al-Iktifāʾ from al-Nūr al-Maḥallī sibṭ al-Zubayr in the year 820 AH, and also heard from al-Zayn Abū Bakr al-Marāghī. He copied al-Marāghī's work Taḥqīq al-nuṣra bi-talkhīṣ maʿālim dār al-hijra, completing it in Jumādā II 816 AH, and witnessed the author's endowment (waqf) of it."@en .

rec:AIND-D03933 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03933-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03933-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03933 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام بن محمد الزرعي أحد سكان المجاهدية بدمشق . كان خيرا أمينا موثوقا به فيما قرأته بخط ابن حجي . مات في أواخر سنة أربع عشرة قاله شيخنا في إنبائه"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Salām b. Muḥammad al-Zurʿī, one of the residents of al-Mujāhidiyya in Damascus. He was good, trustworthy and reliable, according to what I read in the handwriting of Ibn Ḥijjī. He died in the latter part of the year 814 AH; so stated our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D03936 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03936-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03936-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03936 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام الشرنوبي البحيري ثم القاهري المكي . خدم عند أزبك اليوسفي اماما ثم طرده فانتمى لتمراز ، وسافر معه للبحيرة ونزل ولده في قراء الشيخونية وفي غيرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Salām al-Sharnūbī al-Buḥayrī, later al-Qāhirī, al-Makkī. He served Azbak al-Yūsufī as imam, but the latter dismissed him, so he attached himself to Timrāz and travelled with him to al-Buḥayra. His son obtained a place among the Qurʾān readers of al-Shaykhūniyya and elsewhere."@en .

rec:AIND-D03937 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03937-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03937-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03937-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03937 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد السلام الفارسكوري الازهري الغاسل . مات في ليلة الجمعة سابع عشري المحرم سنة ثمان وثمانين ، وكان خيرا أقام مديدة يغسل الموتى وقصد لذلك وأكثره احتسابا رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Salām al-Fāriskūrī al-Azharī al-Ghāsil (the washer of the dead). He died on the night of Friday, 27 Muḥarram 888 AH. He was a good man who for a long time washed the dead, was sought out for it, and did most of it voluntarily seeking God's reward. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03938 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03938-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03938-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03938 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الصادق بن محمد الدمشقي الحنبلي . كان من أصحاب التقي بن المنجا ولي قضاء طرابلس وشكرت سيرته ثم قدم دمشق وتزوج ابنة السلاوي زوجة مخدومه التقي وسعى في قضاء دمشق . ومات في المحرم سنة ست شهيدا سقط عليه سقف بيته فهلك تحت الردم . ذكره شيخنا في انبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ṣādiq b. Muḥammad al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanbalī. He was one of the companions of al-Taqī b. al-Munajjā. He held the judgeship of Tripoli, where his conduct was praised. He then came to Damascus, married the daughter of al-Sallāwī, the (former) wife of his master al-Taqī, and sought the judgeship of Damascus. He died a martyr in Muḥarram 806 AH when the roof of his house fell on him and he perished under the rubble. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D03942 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03942-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03942-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03942 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الصمد بن عبد الرحمن بن مسعود روح الدين بن سعد الدين ابن الصدر الشيرازي . كان حيا في سنة ثمان وعشرين وثمانمائة ففيها قرأ على الظهير عبد الرحمن بن عبد القادر الطاووسي وسمع معه ابن أخي المسمع أحمد ابن عبد الله بن عبد القادر ووصف صاحب الترجمة بالمحدث العالم ووالده بالقارىء وجده باستاذنا في كلام الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ṣamad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Masʿūd Rūḥ al-Dīn b. Saʿd al-Dīn Ibn al-Ṣadr al-Shīrāzī. He was alive in the year 828 AH, in which he read under al-Ẓahīr ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Ṭāwūsī, and the nephew of the transmitter, Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Qādir, heard along with him. The subject was described (in that record) as \"the learned hadith scholar\", his father as \"the reciter (al-qāriʾ)\", and his grandfather as \"our master in the Word of God\"."@en .

rec:AIND-D03943 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03943-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03943-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03943 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الصمد بن عبد الله بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي المكي . درج صغيرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ṣamad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓahīra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī al-Makkī. He died in childhood."@en .

rec:AIND-D03944 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03944-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03944-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03944 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الصمد بن عماد بن إبراهيم الدكني الهندي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ṣamad b. ʿImād b. Ibrāhīm al-Dakanī al-Hindī. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03945 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03945-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03945-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03945 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الصمد بن عمر بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد المقراني اليماني الشافعي ويعرف بأبي نبيلة . فاضل اشتغل على أبيه في الفقه وغيره ولقيني بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة ثلاث وتسعين فقرأ على أربعي النووي وسمع على غير ذلك ، وذكر لي أن والده كان فقيها قرأ على الاهدل ومات في سنة ثمان وثمانين عن ست وسبعين سنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ṣamad b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad al-Muqrānī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Abū Nabīla. An accomplished man, he studied fiqh and other subjects under his father. He met me in Mecca in Rabīʿ I 893 AH and read to me al-Nawawī's Forty Hadiths, and heard other things. He told me that his father was a jurist who had studied under al-Ahdal and died in the year 888 AH at the age of seventy-six."@en .

rec:AIND-D03948 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03948-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03948-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03948 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الصمد الوادي التازفي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ṣamad al-Wādī al-Tāzifī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03951 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03951-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03951-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03951 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن أحمد بن محمد الزواوي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Zawāwī. Among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03952 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03952-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03952-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03952-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03952-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03952 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن أحمد بن أحمد بن عز الدين الغزي ثم القاهري المقرىء . نشأ فحفظ القرآن وتنزل في المدارس وقرأ في صفة الجمالية وغيرها وفي شباك البيبرسية وسمع الكثير ومما سمعه ختم البخاري بالظاهرية ، وكان ساكنا خيرا . مات في رجب سنة إحدى وتسعين وأظنه قارب السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Aḥmad ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿIzz al-Dīn al-Ghazzī, later al-Qāhirī, the Qurʾān reciter. He grew up, memorized the Qurʾān, obtained stipends in the madrasas, and recited at the ṣuffa of the Jamāliyya and elsewhere and at the window of the Baybarsiyya. He heard a great deal, including the completion (khatm) of al-Bukhārī at the Ẓāhiriyya. He was quiet and good. He died in Rajab 891 AH, and I think he was close to seventy."@en .

rec:AIND-D03962 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03962-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03962-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03962 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن إسحاق بن الفراش بمكة . مات بها في جمادى الثانية سنة ست وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Isḥāq, son of the farrāsh (mosque attendant) in Mecca. He died there in Jumādā II 866 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03965 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03965-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03965-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03965-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03965 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن دانيال بن عبد العزيز بن علي بن عثمان الاصبهاني الأصل المكي ويعرف بالعجمي . كان شابا خيرا له أملاك بوادي الهدة وغيرها وغالب ذلك وراثة من قرائبه . مات بمكة في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى عشرة . ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Dāniyāl b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī b. ʿUthmān al-Aṣbahānī, of Meccan residence, known as al-ʿAjamī. He was a good young man who owned properties in Wādī al-Hadda and elsewhere, most of which were inherited from his relatives. He died in Mecca in Dhu al-Qaʿda, the year 811 AH. He was mentioned by al-Fāsī."@en .

rec:AIND-D03966 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03966-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03966-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03966-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03966 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن عبد الجليل بن عبد الله عز الدين النمراوي الفقيه الشافعي. مات في تاسع ذي القعدة سنة عشر. هكذا ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه والصواب انه وسبعمائة فهو من المائة الثامنة وقد ترجمه هو فيها فسبحان من لا يسهو."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Jalīl b. ʿAbd Allāh ʿIzz al-Dīn al-Namrāwī, the Shāfiʿī jurist. He died on 9 Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year [7]10. Thus our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded him in his Inbāʾ, but the correct reading is \"and seven hundred\", so he belongs to the eighth century, and he (Ibn Ḥajar) had already given him a biography there. Glory be to Him who does not err."@en .

rec:AIND-D03968 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03968-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03968-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03968 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر عز الدين القاهري الحنفي الحياك تجاه الجملون ويعرف بحرفته . ممن اشتغل وأخذ عن الزين قاسم بقراءته وقراءة غيره وانتهى لأبي السعادات البلقيني والصلاح المكيني فمقته المناوي . مات في أوائل العشر الأخير من رمضان سنة أربع وسبعين بعد أن تعلل مدة وأظنه زاد على الخمسين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr ʿIzz al-Dīn al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī, the weaver (al-ḥayyāk) opposite al-Jamalūn, known by his trade. He pursued studies and took from al-Zayn Qāsim (al-Ḥanafī), through his own reading and that of others, and ended up with Abū al-Saʿādāt al-Bulqīnī and al-Ṣalāḥ al-Makīnī; but al-Munāwī detested him. He died in the first days of the last ten of Ramaḍān 874 AH after a period of illness; I think he had passed fifty. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03969 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03969-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03969-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03969 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن عبد السلام بن أبي الفرج الزرندي المدني والد عمر الآتي . مات في صفر سنة ثلاث وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Salām b. Abī al-Faraj al-Zarandī al-Madanī, the father of ʿUmar, who is mentioned below. He died in Ṣafar of the year 863 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D03975 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03975-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03975-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03975 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن عبد الله بن محمد عز الدين الحسيني سكنا . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad ʿIzz al-Dīn, al-Ḥusaynī by residence. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D03978 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03978-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03978-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03978 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن عثمان بن محمد بن أبي فارس أبو الفوارس ابن صاحب تونس وأخو المسعود محمد الآتيين وهذا أصغرهما . ولي بجاية وهو حي قبل الثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad b. Abī Fāris, Abū al-Fawāris, son of the ruler of Tunis and brother of al-Masʿūd Muḥammad—both of whom are mentioned below—and the younger of the two. He governed Bijāya (Béjaïa) and was alive before the year [8]80."@en .

rec:AIND-D03980 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03980-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03980-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03980 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن علي بن عبد العزيز بن عبد الكافي الخواجا عز الدين الدقوقي المكي أخو الجمال محمد الآتي وهذا أسن . مات بالقاهرة في طاعون سنة ثلاث وثلاثين ومن ثم أخذ أخوه في الشهرة والقبول ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Kāfī, al-Khawājā ʿIzz al-Dīn al-Daqūqī al-Makkī, the brother of al-Jamāl Muḥammad, who is mentioned below, and the elder of the two. He died in Cairo in the plague of the year 833 AH, after which his brother began to gain fame and acceptance."@en .

rec:AIND-D03982 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03982-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03982-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03982 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن علي بن محمد بن محمود بن العلامة نور الدين علي بن فرحون العز اليعمري المدني المالكي ويعرف بالمجلد وهي حرفته وحرفة أبيه . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Maḥmūd b. (the eminent scholar Nūr al-Dīn) ʿAlī b. Farḥūn, al-ʿIzz al-Yaʿmurī al-Madanī al-Mālikī. He was known as al-Mujallid (the bookbinder), which was his craft and his father's. He was among those who heard from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03983 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03983-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03983-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03983 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن علي بن محمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن حسن بن الزين القسطلاني المكي . مات بها وله نحو ثلاث سنين في سنة ست وأربعين . ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. al-Zayn al-Qasṭallānī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in the year 846 AH, at about three years of age. Ibn Fahd mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D03984 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03984-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03984-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03984 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن علي بن أبي البركات محمد بن أبي السعود محمد بن حسين ابن علي بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة العز القرشي المكي شقيق البرهان عالم الحجاز وأخوته ويعرف كسلفه بابن ظهيرة . مات سنة سبع وعشرين ومولده في التي قبلها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī b. Abī al-Barakāt Muḥammad b. Abī al-Suʿūd Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra, al-ʿIzz al-Qurashī al-Makkī. He was the full brother of al-Burhān, the scholar of the Ḥijāz, and of his brothers, and like his ancestors was known as Ibn Ẓahīra. He died in the year 827 AH, having been born in the preceding year."@en .

rec:AIND-D03990 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03990-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03990-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03990 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن داود الكيلاني المكي . تردد للقاهرة ومات بها مطعونا في شوال سنة ثلاث وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. Dāwūd al-Kīlānī al-Makkī. He frequented Cairo and died there of the plague in Shawwāl 873 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03991 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03991-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03991-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03991-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03991 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن صالح النمراوي الأصل القاهري الآتي أبوه ويعرف كهو بابن صالح . شاب يميل لظرف وسكون وانجماع ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة وباسمه بعض جهات منتقلة له عن أبيه وغيره . مات في شوال سنة إحدى وتسعين وصلى عليه بعد صلاة الجمعة بالأزهر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. Ṣāliḥ, of Namrā origin, al-Qāhirī, whose father is mentioned below; like him he was known as Ibn Ṣāliḥ. A young man inclined to refinement, quiet and seclusion, he was among those who heard from me in Cairo, and some stipendiary posts (jihāt) transferred from his father and others were held in his name. He died in Shawwāl 891 AH, and the funeral prayer was performed for him after the Friday prayer at al-Azhar."@en .

rec:AIND-D03992 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03992-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03992-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03992 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن علي بن أحمد العز بن الشمس بن الكويك الآتي أبوه وعمه قاسم . ولد قريب الثلاثين وثمانمائة بالقاهرة ونشأ بها فحفظ القرآن وغيره ورافقني يسيرا في مكتب ابن أسد ثم تعانى الحيك ظنا وقتا ثم التوقيع وصار من جملتهم وربما يقول الشعر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad, al-ʿIzz b. al-Shams b. al-Kuwayk; his father and his paternal uncle Qāsim are mentioned below. He was born around 830 AH in Cairo and grew up there, memorized the Qurʾān and other texts, and was briefly my companion in the kuttāb of Ibn Asad. He then, I think, practised weaving for a time, then took up the tawqīʿ (secretarial signing) and became one of its clerks. He sometimes composes poetry."@en .

rec:AIND-D03993 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03993-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03993-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03993 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن الجمال محمد بن الزين عبد العزيز بن عبد الواحد العز الأنصاري المدني ابن عم حسن بن عمر بن عبد الواحد الماضي ويعرف بابن زين الدين . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. al-Zayn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, al-ʿIzz al-Anṣārī al-Madanī, the cousin of the aforementioned Ḥasan b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, known as Ibn Zayn al-Dīn. He was among those who heard from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D03995 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03995-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03995-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03995 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن عبد الكريم الدميري . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Damīrī. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D03997 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03997-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03997-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D03997-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D03997-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03997 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن عبد الوهاب العز بن أبي القسم بن التاج العثماني كما بخط شيخه أبي الفتح المراغي الطهطاوي ثم المكي . سمع على أبي الفتح المراغي في سنة خمس وخمسين وبعدها ، وكان بزازا بدار الامارة مباركا ممن دخل العجم وحصل بها . مات بمكة فجأة بالمسجد بعد صلاته المغرب في صفر سنة سبع وستين سامحه الله . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, al-ʿIzz b. Abī al-Qāsim b. al-Tāj al-ʿUthmānī—as written in the hand of his teacher Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī—al-Ṭahṭāwī, then al-Makkī. He heard from Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī in 855 AH and afterwards. He was a cloth merchant (bazzāz) at Dār al-Imāra, a blessed man, one of those who went to Persia and made money there. He died suddenly in Mecca, in the mosque after his sunset prayer, in Ṣafar 867 AH; may God forgive him. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D03998 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D03998-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D03998-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D03998 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن أبي البركات محمد بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز الهاشمي النويري المكي . ولد بها في سنة إحدى وثلاثين وأمه أم الخير ابنة علي ابن عبد اللطيف بن سالم ، ونشأ وسمع من زينب ابنة الشافعي وأجاز له في سنة ست وثلاثين وبعدها جماعة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Abī al-Barakāt Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Hāshimī al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī. He was born in Mecca in the year 831 AH; his mother was Umm al-Khayr bint ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Sālim. He grew up and heard from Zaynab bint al-Shāfiʿī, and in 836 AH and thereafter a number of scholars granted him ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D04000 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04000-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04000-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04000 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن علي بن محمد بن علي بن أحمد عز الدين المحلي السمنودي الشافعي ابن عم الجلال محمد بن أحمد الآتي ويعرف بعزيز بفتح المهملة وزايين منقوطتين بينهما تحتانية . حفظ القرآن والمنهاج أو غالبه واشتغل على ابن عمه وولي كأبيه قضاء سمنود وعملها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad ʿIzz al-Dīn al-Maḥallī al-Samannūdī al-Shāfiʿī, the cousin of al-Jalāl Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, who is mentioned below, and known as ʿAzīz. He memorized the Qurʾān and the Minhāj, or most of it, studied under his cousin, and, like his father, held the judgeship of Samannūd and its district."@en .

rec:AIND-D04002 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04002-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04002-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04002-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04002 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز بن المحب بن البدر بن الأمانة الآتي أبوه وجده والماضي سميه وغيره من أعمامه . أحضر في البخاري في الظاهرية القديمة ، ولما كبر حج وتكسب بالشهادة ولم يتصون ولا تثبت وربما حضر دروس الوظائف حتى إنه حضر عندي بالبرقوقية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. al-Muḥibb b. al-Badr, Ibn al-Amāna. His father and grandfather are mentioned below, and his namesake and his other paternal uncles above. As a child he was brought to hear al-Bukhārī at the old Ẓāhiriyya. When he grew up he performed the Ḥajj and earned his living as a notary-witness, but was neither scrupulous nor reliable. He sometimes attended the stipendiary lessons, and even attended my lessons at the Barqūqiyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D04004 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04004-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04004-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04004-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04004 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن محمد بن حسين بن علي بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة أبو البقا بن أبي الخير بن أبي السعود القرشي المكي وأمه حبشية فتاة أبيه . ولد في رجب سنة تسع وثمانمائة وأجاز له جماعة منهم ابن الكويك وعائشة ابنة ابن عبد الهادي والمجد الشيرازي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra, Abū al-Baqāʾ b. Abī al-Khayr b. Abī al-Suʿūd, al-Qurashī al-Makkī. His mother was an Abyssinian slave-girl of his father. He was born in Rajab 809 AH. A number of scholars granted him ijāza, among them Ibn al-Kuwayk, ʿĀʾisha bint Ibn ʿAbd al-Hādī and al-Majd al-Shīrāzī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04010 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04010-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04010-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04010 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن محمد الجوجري الشافعي . ممن عرض عليه خير الدين ابن القصبي بعد الخمسين وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Jawjarī al-Shāfiʿī. He was among those to whom Khayr al-Dīn Ibn al-Qaṣabī presented (his memorized texts) after the year [8]50."@en .

rec:AIND-D04012 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04012-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04012-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04012 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن موسى بن إبراهيم العز بن البدر بن الشرف ابن البرهان ويعرف كسلفه بابن البرهان . شاهد بوقف البيمارستان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. Ibrāhīm, al-ʿIzz b. al-Badr b. al-Sharaf Ibn al-Burhān, known like his forebears as Ibn al-Burhān. A notary-witness (shāhid) of the waqf of the Bīmāristān."@en .

rec:AIND-D04013 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04013-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04013-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04013 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن محمد بن موسى بن محمد بن علي الشريف القادري الآتي أبوه . ممن سمع علي ومات بالطاعون في سنة سبع وتسعين وهو أخو زوج تغري بردى الاستادار ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Sharīf al-Qādirī, whose father is mentioned below. He was among those who heard from me, and he died of the plague in the year 897 AH. He was the brother of the wife of Taghrī Birdī the ustādār."@en .

rec:AIND-D04016 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04016-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04016-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04016 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن البدر محمود بن أحمد العيني مات في المحرم سنة ثمان عشرة أرخه أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. al-Badr Maḥmūd b. Aḥmad al-ʿAynī. He died in Muḥarram 818 AH; his father (Badr al-Dīn al-ʿAynī) recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04020 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04020-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04020-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04020 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن موسى بن محمد أبو القاسم العبدوسي المغربي . لقيه عمر ابن يوسف البسلقوني في سنة احدى وعشرين وأذن له في الافتاء والتدريس كما سيجئ في ترجمته . وينظر الكنى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Mūsā b. Muḥammad, Abū al-Qāsim al-ʿAbdūsī al-Maghribī. ʿUmar b. Yūsuf al-Baslaqūnī met him in the year 821 AH and he authorized him to give fatwās and to teach, as will be mentioned in the latter's biography. See also the section of kunyas."@en .

rec:AIND-D04021 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04021-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04021-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04021-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04021-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04021-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04021 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن موسى الخطيب أبو محمد الوريا علي الفاسي خطيب جامع القرويين . مات في رمضان سنة ثمانين ومولده سنة ثلاث عشرة . أفاده لي بعض أصحابنا المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Mūsā, al-Khaṭīb, Abū Muḥammad al-Waryā ʿAlī al-Fāsī, preacher (khaṭīb) of the Qarawiyyīn Mosque. He died in Ramaḍān 880 AH; his birth was in 813. One of our Maghribī companions gave me this information."@en .

rec:AIND-D04023 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04023-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04023-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04023-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04023 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن يوسف بن عبد العزيز الخواجا السلطاني نزيل مكة . كان مباركا له سبيل بحارة الشيبيين من السويقة حبس عليه الدار التي تعلوه ودارا بجانبها . ومات بمكة في جمادى الآخرة سنة أربع وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Yūsuf b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, al-Khawājā al-Sulṭānī, resident of Mecca. He was a blessed man; he had a sabīl (public fountain) in the Shaybiyyīn quarter of al-Suwayqa, for which he endowed the house above it and an adjacent house. He died in Mecca in Jumādā II 844 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04025 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04025-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04025-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04025-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04025-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04025 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن يوسف العز الأنبابي الشافعي نائب الحسبة . ناب في القضاء أيضا وخطب بجامع الخطيري ببولاق وباشر في أوقافه وابتنى دورا ببولاق وغيرها ولم يكن بالمرضي في مباشراته ونياباته . مات يوم الجمعة سادس شوال سنة اثنتين وسبعين ودفن من الغد عفا الله عنه وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Yūsuf, al-ʿIzz al-Anbābī al-Shāfiʿī, deputy of the ḥisba. He also served as deputy judge, preached at the Khaṭīrī Mosque in Būlāq and administered its endowments, and built houses in Būlāq and elsewhere; but he was not well regarded in his administrative and deputy posts. He died on Friday, 6 Shawwāl 872 AH, and was buried the next day. May God pardon him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D04026 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04026-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04026-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04026 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن يوسف الخواجا السلطاني . مضى فيمن جده عبد العزيز ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Yūsuf al-Khawājā al-Sulṭānī. He was already mentioned among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz."@en .

rec:AIND-D04027 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04027-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04027-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04027 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن عز الدين نزيل الكاملية ويعرف بالأصيلي لقرابة بينه وبين بيت ابن أصيل من جهة النساء . اشتغل قليلا وحضر عند ابن الهمام وكتب بخطه الكثير وبالغ في إتقانه غير نسخة من الأحياء للغزالي وكان يراجعني في كثير من الألفاظ وكذا كتب القاموس وغيره ، وتنزل في سعيد السعداء وغيرها ، وكان كثير الانجماع طورا بذاته له توجه إلى التحصيل والامساك جلس معي كثيرا ومات في ذي الحجة سنة ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿIzz al-Dīn, resident of al-Kāmiliyya, known as al-Aṣīlī because of kinship on the women's side with the house of Ibn Aṣīl. He studied a little and attended Ibn al-Humām. He copied much in his own hand with great accuracy, including more than one copy of al-Ghazālī's Iḥyāʾ; he used to consult me about many words, and also copied the Qāmūs and other works. He held stipends at Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ and elsewhere. He was mostly reclusive, at times inclined to acquisition and thrift. He sat with me a great deal, and died in Dhū al-Ḥijja 893 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04028 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04028-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04028-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04028-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04028-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04028 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز بن عز الدين النفياني المصري صاحب المدرسة التي بالقرب من باب القرافة المجتمع فيها القراء في ليلة السابع عشر من كل شهر وأحد المنتمين لخشقدم الزمام . جاور غير مرة ويذكر بمال كثير وربما سمعت من يثني عليه مع تودد ظاهر وقراءته في الجوق لحسن صوته لكن مع نقص قوته وقد تزوج ابنة أحمد بن الحتاتي . مات في سنة اثنتين أو ثلاث وتسعين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿIzz al-Dīn al-Nafyānī al-Miṣrī, owner of the madrasa near Bāb al-Qarāfa in which the reciters gather on the seventeenth night of every month, and one of those attached to Khushqadam al-Zimām. He performed jiwār more than once, is said to have had much wealth, and I have heard people praise him for his evident amiability and his recitation in the jawq thanks to his fine voice, though it lacked strength. He married the daughter of Aḥmad b. al-Ḥatātī. He died in 892 or 893 AH; may God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04029 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04029-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04029-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04029 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز المصري سكنا السلاخوري . وجد له شيء كثير بحيث تبلغ تركته نحو ثلاثين ألف دينار بالنظر لمساطير وجدت غير مخصوصة يقال انه استأدى غالبها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, al-Miṣrī by residence, al-Sallākhūrī. A great deal was found in his estate, so that it reached about thirty thousand dinars judging by unaddressed deeds (masāṭīr) that were found; it is said that he had already collected most of them."@en .

rec:AIND-D04030 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04030-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04030-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04030 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العزيز الشريف المغربي المالكي . سمع على شيخنا في سنة أربع وأربعين الخصال المكفرة وجزء الجمعة ووصفه الفتحي والسماع معه بالعالم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Sharīf al-Maghribī al-Mālikī. He heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in 844 AH al-Khiṣāl al-mukaffira and Juzʾ al-jumuʿa, and al-Fatḥī described him—and the audition together with him—with the term \"the scholar (al-ʿālim)\"."@en .

rec:AIND-D04031 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04031-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04031-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04031 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العظيم بن أحمد البلقيني الخطيب أبوه . كان بها ممن سمع مني وكان يتكسب في القاهرة بالحرير ويؤذن بجامع الغمري احتسابا ، وربما قرأ يوم الجمعة سورة الكهف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAẓīm b. Aḥmad al-Bulqīnī, whose father was the preacher (khaṭīb). He was there among those who heard from me; he earned his living in Cairo in the silk trade, gave the call to prayer at the Ghamrī Mosque voluntarily, and would sometimes recite Sūrat al-Kahf on Fridays."@en .

rec:AIND-D04032 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04032-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04032-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04032 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العظيم بن صدقة التاج القبطي الأسلمي . ممن يعد في الكتبة بحيث ولي نظر ديوان المفرد وكان هو والزين يحيى الذي صار إلى ما صار يترافعان ويتخاصمان وهذا غالبا يغلب إلى أن انتمى الآخر لقيزطوغان لما ولي الاستادارية واستقر في نظر المفرد ثمن يومئذ تأخر هذا وتزايدت ودناسته وظلمته لبعده عن نور الايمان وسلم لقيز ثم لأبن كاتب المناخات في سنة أربع وأربعين على مال ودام مخمولا حتى مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAẓīm b. Ṣadaqa, al-Tāj al-Qibṭī al-Aslamī. He was counted among the scribes and held the controllership of the Dīwān al-Mufrad. He and al-Zayn Yaḥyā—who later rose to what he rose to—used to litigate and quarrel with each other, and he generally prevailed, until the latter attached himself to Qizṭughān when he became ustādār and secured the controllership of the Mufrad. From then on he fell back, and his foulness and injustice increased owing to his distance from the light of faith. He was handed over to Qiz[ṭughān], then in 844 AH to Ibn Kātib al-Manākhāt for a sum of money, and remained in obscurity until he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D04034 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04034-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04034-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04034 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العظيم بن درهم ونصف . من الأقباط المتمولين من الدواليب . ونحوها . مات في ربيع الأول سنة تسع وسبعين بعد إهانته مرة بعد أخرى . واحتيط على حواصله وأماكنه مع وجود العاصب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAẓīm b. Dirham wa-Niṣf, one of the wealthy Copts who made their money from workshops (dawālīb) and the like. He died in Rabīʿ I 879 AH after being humiliated time and again, and his stores and properties were sequestered despite the presence of an agnatic heir."@en .

rec:AIND-D04035 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04035-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04035-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04035 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد العليم بن الحسن بن علي بن أبي بكر بن علي بن محمد بن أبي بكر ابن عبد الله الناشري اليماني الماضي أبوه . ممن أقبل على الاشتغال وقتا مع فهم وذكاء وتميز في القراءات السبع ثم ترك . ومات عن نحو الثلاثين في أول المحرم سنة ثلاث وأربعين بتعز ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-ʿAlīm b. al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Nāshirī al-Yamānī, whose father was mentioned above. He applied himself to study for a time with understanding and intelligence and excelled in the Seven Readings, but then gave it up. He died at about thirty at the beginning of Muḥarram 843 AH in Taʿizz."@en .

rec:AIND-D04037 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04037-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04037-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04037 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغفار بن أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الكيلاني أخو الشيخين محمد وحسين وإبراهيم بني ابن قاوان . ممن اشتغل وفضل وقدم مكة بعيد التسعين مع الركب الحلبي فأقام سنة ثم عاد إلى بلاده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghaffār b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Kīlānī, brother of the two shaykhs Muḥammad and Ḥusayn, and of Ibrāhīm, the sons of Ibn Qāwān. He was one of those who studied and excelled. He came to Mecca shortly after [8]90 with the Aleppo caravan, stayed a year, and then returned to his country."@en .

rec:AIND-D04039 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04039-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04039-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04039 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغفار بن سليمان بن يوسف بن أحمد بن عبد الملك بن عبد الواحد ابن الشيخ معالي التلواني القاهري الأزهري أخو علي الآني ممن سمع على شيخنا وفي البخاري بالظاهرية وغير ذلك وحضر الدروس قليلا وتنزل في الجهات وعمل نقيب الفقهاء بالقلعة وحج غير مرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghaffār b. Sulaymān b. Yūsuf b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Malik b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. al-Shaykh Maʿālī al-Tilwānī al-Qāhirī al-Azharī, brother of ʿAlī, who is mentioned below. He was among those who heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and heard al-Bukhārī at the Ẓāhiriyya and other things; he attended lessons a little, held stipends, served as naqīb of the jurists at the Citadel, and performed the Ḥajj more than once."@en .

rec:AIND-D04040 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04040-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04040-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04040 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغفار بن عبد الرحيم بن الزكي أبي بكر بن عمر بن يوسف التاج أبو الخير الميدومي الأصل المصري ابن أخي الشهاب أحمد الماضي . ناب في القضاء بمصر وعمل فيها أمين الحكم للاسيوطي ثم لزكريا"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghaffār b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. al-Zakī Abī Bakr b. ʿUmar b. Yūsuf, al-Tāj Abū al-Khayr, of Maydūm origin, al-Miṣrī, nephew of the aforementioned al-Shihāb Aḥmad. He served as deputy judge in Miṣr and worked there as amīn al-ḥukm for al-Asyūṭī and then for Zakariyyā."@en .

rec:AIND-D04042 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04042-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04042-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04042 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغفار بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد الملك بن محمد الحمصي أخو عبد الملك الآتي . ولد في جمادى الأولى سنة سبع وسبعين وثمانمائة وقدم مع أبيه القاهرة فسمع مني المسلسل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghaffār b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Malik b. Muḥammad al-Ḥimṣī, the brother of ʿAbd al-Malik, who is mentioned below. He was born in Jumādā I 877 AH and came to Cairo with his father, where he heard al-Musalsal from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D04043 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04043-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04043-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04043 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغفار بن الشمس محمد بن محمد بن علي بن العماد البلبيسي الأصل القاهري الآتي أخوه محمد وأبوهما . أحضره أبوه البخاري على الشاوي وكذا أحضره علي ومات وهو طفل وتأسف كل من أبويه عليه عوضهم الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghaffār b. al-Shams Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. al-ʿImād, of Bilbays origin, al-Qāhirī; his brother Muḥammad and their father are mentioned below. His father brought him to hear al-Bukhārī with al-Shāwī, and likewise brought him to me. He died as a child, and both his parents grieved for him; may God compensate them with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D04045 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04045-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04045-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04045-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04045 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغفار بن التاج محمد الكلبشاوي أخو إبراهيم الماضي وذاك أسن حفظ الحاوي واشتغل قليلا وخلف أخاه في قضاء بلده وخطابتها كأبيهما وجدهما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghaffār b. al-Tāj Muḥammad al-Kilbishāwī, brother of the aforementioned Ibrāhīm, who was the elder. He memorized al-Ḥāwī and studied a little, and succeeded his brother in the judgeship and preachership of his town, as their father and grandfather had held them."@en .

rec:AIND-D04047 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04047-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04047-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04047 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغفار بن نفيس شيخ معمر من نقباء المقام الابراهيمي الدسوقي . مات في المحرم سنة خمس وخمسين ودفن بتربة من القرافة الصغرى . أرخه ابن المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghaffār b. Nafīs, a long-lived shaykh, one of the naqībs of the Ibrāhīmī shrine of Dasūq. He died in Muḥarram 855 AH and was buried in a tomb in al-Qarāfa al-Ṣughrā. Ibn al-Munīr recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04048 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04048-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04048-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04048 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغفور بن عبد البر بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن الشحنة حفيد المحب القاضي والماضي أبوه . مات في طفولته مطعونا في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى وثمانين ودفن بتربتهم عوضه الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghafūr b. ʿAbd al-Barr b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. al-Shiḥna, grandson of the qāḍī al-Muḥibb (Ibn al-Shiḥna); his father was mentioned previously. He died of the plague in his childhood in Dhū al-Qaʿda 881 and was buried in the family tomb. May God recompense him with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D04052 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04052-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04052-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04052 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن أحمد بن عبد الله بن الإمام النحريري . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Ghani b. Ahmad b. Abd Allah b. al-Imam al-Nahriri. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04060 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04060-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04060-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04060-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04060 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن شاكر بن ماجد بن عبد الوهاب بن يعقوب الفخر بن العلم بن الجيعان جد الذي قبله ووالد شاكر واخوته . تميز في الكتابة وباشر في جهات ككتابة الجيش . ومات في خامس عشري جمادى الأولى سنة ثمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Shākir b. Mājid b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Yaʿqūb, al-Fakhr b. al-ʿAlam Ibn al-Jīʿān. He was the grandfather of the preceding person and the father of Shākir and his brothers. He excelled in secretarial writing and served in various posts such as the army chancery (kitābat al-jaysh). He died on 25 Jumādā I 808 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04062 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04062-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04062-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04062 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن عبد القادر بن عبد الرحمن التقي المحلي الشافعي ويعرف بابن الرشيد بضم الراء وفتح المعجمة ثم تحتانية مشددة مكسورة وآخره مهملة . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Abd al-Rahman, al-Taqi, al-Mahalli, al-Shafi'i, known as Ibn al-Rushayyid. Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhawi) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04064 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04064-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04064-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04064-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04064 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن عبد الله بن محمد التاج الاميوطي القاهري قريب النجم بن النبيه الموقع ويعرف بابن الاعمى . مات في سلخ ربيع الأول سنة إحدى وثمانين وقد زاحم المائة وكان يتكسب بالشهادة في حانوت باب الفتوح دهرا حتى مات ولم يذكر عنه فيها إلا الخير رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad, al-Tāj al-Amyūṭī al-Qāhirī, a relative of al-Najm b. al-Nabīh the notary (al-muwaqqiʿ), known as Ibn al-Aʿmā. He died on the last day of Rabīʿ I 881, having nearly reached a hundred. For a long time until his death he earned his living as a professional witness (shāhid) at a shop at Bāb al-Futūḥ, and nothing but good was reported of him there. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04069 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04069-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04069-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04069 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن علي الفارقي المدابغي المقرىء الشافعي . ممن أخذ القراءات عن التاج بن تمرية ثم الشمس العفصي وتكسب بالمدابغ ثم بسوق الحاجب ثم بالشهادة في حانوت بسويقة عصفور وأقرأ . مات في رجب سنة إحدى وتسعين وقد رأيته كثيرا بل رأيته شهد على الزين عبد الغني الهيثمي في إجازة ووصفه بشيخنا فكأنه أدبا مع احتمال قراءته عليه"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. ʿAlī al-Fāriqī al-Madābighī, the Shāfiʿī Qur'ān reciter. He studied the variant Qur'ānic recitations under al-Tāj b. Tamurīya, and then al-Shams al-ʿAfṣī. He earned his living by working in tanneries, then in Sūq al-Ḥājib, and later as a notary witness in a shop in Suwayqat ʿUṣfūr, and he also taught. He died in Rajab, year 891 AH. I saw him frequently; in fact, I saw him witness an ijāza for al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Ghanī al-Haythamī, whom he described as 'our shaykh,' perhaps out of politeness, although it is possible he had read (studied) under him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04070 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04070-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04070-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04070 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن عمار بن عمر . مات سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. ʿAmmār b. ʿUmar. He died in the year 857."@en .

rec:AIND-D04071 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04071-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04071-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04071-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04071 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن أبي الفضل محمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن أحمد المرشدي المكي الآتي أبوه وجده . ولد في ليلة الأحد سادس عشري الحجة سنة خمس وثلاثين وحفظ المختار وعرض وسمع على ابن عياش وهو في سنة سبع وتسعين حي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Abī al-Faḍl Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad al-Murshidī al-Makkī; his father and grandfather are mentioned below. He was born on the night of Sunday, 26 Dhū al-Ḥijja 835. He memorized al-Mukhtār, presented it (ʿaraḍa), and heard (ḥadīth) from Ibn ʿAyyāsh. He was still alive in the year 897."@en .

rec:AIND-D04076 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04076-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04076-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04076 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن القاهري الحريري العقاد الماضي ابنه عبد الرحمن . شيخ مبارك حفظ القرآن والعمدة وكان حنبليا يتكسب في صناعة الحرير ، وسمع على الشرف المناوي وغيره ، سمعت منه وهو بمنزلي أشياء من نظمه على طريقة العوام ومات في ذي القعدة سنة سبع وثمانين وثمانمائة عن دون الثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Qāhirī al-Ḥarīrī al-ʿAqqād (the silk-cord maker), father of the previously mentioned ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. A blessed shaykh, he memorized the Qurʾān and al-ʿUmda. He was a Ḥanbalī and earned his living in the silk trade. He heard (ḥadīth) from al-Sharaf al-Manāwī and others. I heard from him, while he was at my house, some of his verse composed in the manner of the common people. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda 887, aged under eighty."@en .

rec:AIND-D04080 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04080-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04080-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04080 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن يعقوب الفخر بن الشرف . أحد كتاب المماليك ووالد عبد الكريم ويحيى ونصر الله وحمزة المذكورين في محالهم والمعروفين بابن فخيرة تصغير لقب أبيهم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Yaʿqūb, al-Fakhr b. al-Sharaf. One of the clerks of the Mamluks (kuttāb al-mamālīk), and the father of ʿAbd al-Karīm, Yaḥyā, Naṣr Allāh and Ḥamza, who are mentioned in their respective places and are known as Ibn Fukhayra, a diminutive of their father's laqab (al-Fakhr)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04082 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04082-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04082-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04082 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن يوسف بن عبد اللطيف الحسيني سكنا الخياط ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Yūsuf b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf, al-Ḥusaynī by residence, the tailor (al-Khayyāṭ). He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04083 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04083-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04083-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04083 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن يوسف بن يس زين الدين المنزلي ويعرف بجده . ممن سمع مني أيضا"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Yūsuf b. Yāsīn, Zayn al-Dīn al-Manzilī, known by his grandfather's name (Ibn Yāsīn). He too was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04084 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04084-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04084-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04084 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني بن الهيصم . فيمن اسم أبيه إبراهيم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. al-Hayṣam. [His entry is] among those whose father's name is Ibrāhīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D04085 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04085-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04085-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04085-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04085 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني الحريري المصري نزيل مكة وممن كان فيه خير ورغبة في الزيارة . مات بها في المحرم سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī al-Ḥarīrī al-Miṣrī. A resident of Mecca and one of those who possessed goodness and a desire for visiting [holy sites]. He died in it (Mecca) in Muharram, the year 892."@en .

rec:AIND-D04086 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04086-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04086-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04086 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الغني اللجمي بفتح اللام والجيم ثم ميم بلدة بالساحل قرب سفاقس التونسي ممن أخذ عن عيسى الغبريني ويعقوب الزعبي وعبد الله الباجي وأحمد الشماع في آخرين وتقدم في المذهب مع الخبرة التامة بتصانيف القرافي الأصولية ومزيد تقلله وتأخره في الدنيا عن نظرائه . أفادنيه صاحبنا قاضي الركب وقال انه مات تقريبا بعد الستين . وهو ممن أخذ عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Ghanī al-Lajmī (with fatḥa on the lām and the jīm, then mīm—a town on the coast near Sfax), al-Tūnisī. He studied under ʿĪsā al-Ghubrīnī, Yaʿqūb al-Zuʿbī, ʿAbd Allāh al-Bājī and Aḥmad al-Shammāʿ, among others. He excelled in the madhhab, with complete expertise in al-Qarāfī's works on uṣūl, and was exceedingly abstemious and behind his peers in worldly matters. Our companion Qāḍī al-Rakb informed me about him and said that he died approximately after [8]60; he (Qāḍī al-Rakb) was among those who studied under him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04087 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04087-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04087-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04087 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الفتاح بن عبد الله بن أبي القسم اللامي نسبة للامية بالقرب من زبيد الناشري الشافعي ممن اشتغل عند القاضي محمد بن عبد السلام وقدم مكة فحج في سنة سبع وتسعين وسمع مني المسلسل وكتبت له وأثنى عليه حمزة بأنه فقيه من أفضل الطلبة رجل صالح نبيه فاضل عارف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Fattāḥ b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī al-Qāsim al-Lāmī (the nisba refers to al-Lāmiyya near Zabīd), al-Nāshirī, al-Shāfiʿī. He was among those who studied under the qāḍī Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Salām. He came to Mecca and performed the pilgrimage in the year 897, heard al-Musalsal from me, and I wrote (an ijāza) for him. Ḥamza (al-Nāshirī) praised him as a jurist, one of the best students, a righteous, intelligent, virtuous and knowledgeable man."@en .

rec:AIND-D04088 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04088-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04088-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04088-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04088 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن الشيخ القدوة إبراهيم بن الشيخ القدوة الكبير الشهير أبي بكر بن محمد بن أبي بكر الموصلي الأصل الدمشقي الشافعي . ولد كما قرأته بخطه في سنة ثمان وثمانين وسبعمائة وسمع الصحيح وثلاثيات الدارمي على عائشة ابنة ابن عبد الهادي ولقي بالمدينة النبوية في سنة ثمان وثمانمائة أبا عبد الله محمد المغربي فسمع عليه وحدث وخلف والده وكان من خيار الناس أجاز لي ومات في منتصف المحرم سنة اثنتين وستين رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir b. al-Shaykh al-Qudwa Ibrahim b. al-Shaykh al-Qudwa al-Kabir al-Shahir Abu Bkhr b. Muhammad b. Abu Bakr, of Mosul origin, of Damascus, al-Shafi'i. He was born, as I read in his own handwriting, in the year 788 AH. He heard al-Sahih (Sahih al-Bukhari) and the Thulathiyyat of al-Darimi from Aisha bint Ibn Abd al-Hadi. In the year 808 AH, he met Abu Abd Allah Muhammad al-Maghribi in Medina, heard hadith from him, and transmitted it. He succeeded his father and was one of the best of people. He granted me (al-Sakhawi) an ijaza. He died in the middle of Muharram in the year 862 AH. May Allah have mercy on him and on us."@en .

rec:AIND-D04091 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04091-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04091-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04091 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن إبراهيم بن عبد الوهاب المصري الصباغ نزيل دمشق . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Miṣrī al-Ṣabbāgh, resident of Damascus. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04092 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04092-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04092-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04092 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن إبراهيم بن علي محيي الدين بن البرهان القاهري المالكي المقرىء الماضي أبوه ويعرف كهو بابن الفوال . ممن اشتغل بالفقه والعربية قليلا وفهم ونسخ وقرأ مع أبيه في الجوق بل شاركه في إقراء الأبناء ، وتنزل في بعض التصوفات وربما قرأ على بعض المسندين بل أخذ عني يسيرا ولا بأس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī, Muḥyī al-Dīn b. al-Burhān, al-Qāhirī, al-Mālikī, the Qurʾān reciter; his father was mentioned above, and he, like him, is known as Ibn al-Fawwāl. He studied a little fiqh and Arabic, understood, copied manuscripts, recited with his father in the jawq (recitation group), and even shared with him the teaching of children. He obtained some Sufi stipends, occasionally read under some musnids, and took a little from me (al-Sakhāwī); he is acceptable."@en .

rec:AIND-D04094 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04094-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04094-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04094 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن إبراهيم ويعرف بابن الامام . من فضلاء الشافعية ممن أخذ عن ابن البلقيني ونحوه ثم عن البامي ولازمه بل قرأ على السعد بن الديري في الحديث ، وكان فاضلا يسكن بالسبع قاعات ويستحضر المقامات . مات بالبيمارستان في رجب سنة ثلاث وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Ibrāhīm, known as Ibn al-Imām. One of the accomplished Shāfiʿī scholars; he studied under Ibn al-Bulqīnī and the like, then under al-Bāmī, whom he attended assiduously, and read ḥadīth under al-Saʿd b. al-Dīrī. A learned man, he lived in al-Sabʿ Qāʿāt and could recite the Maqāmāt from memory. He died in the Bīmāristān (hospital) in Rajab 893."@en .

rec:AIND-D04095 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04095-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04095-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04095 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أحمد بن إسماعيل بن عبد الله الدمشقي الماضي أبوه . ممن سمع مني بمكة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir ibn Ahmad ibn Isma'il ibn Abd Allah al-Dimashqi. His father was mentioned previously. He was among those who heard (hadith) from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04097 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04097-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04097-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04097 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن الشهاب أحمد بن أبي بكر بن أحمد بن علي الزين الحموي الحلبي الماضي أبوه والآتي ابنه أحمد وأخوه المحب محمد ويعرف كهو بابن الرسام . ممن ولي كتابة السر بحلب ونظر جيشها وجواليها ، وصاهر العلم البلقيني على ابنته ، وكان مخمولا في حركاته يتحمل الديون الكثيرة ولا يحصل في ولاياته على طائل . مات بحماة سنة بضع وستين بعد أخيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir b. Ahmad b. Abi Bakr b. Ahmad b. Ali, al-Zayn al-Hamawi al-Halabi. His father was mentioned previously, and his son Ahmad and his brother al-Muhibb Muhammad are to be mentioned later. Like him, he was known as Ibn al-Rassam. He was among those who held the office of Secretary of State (Katib al-Sirr) in Aleppo, and oversaw its army (Nazar al-Jaysh) and its poll-tax (Nazar al-Jawali). He became the son-in-law of al-Alam al-Bulqini by marrying his daughter. He was obscure in his movements, bore heavy debts, and did not achieve significant gain from his offices. He died in Hama in the sixty-somethings (860s AH) after his brother."@en .

rec:AIND-D04098 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04098-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04098-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04098-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04098 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أحمد بن حسين بن حسن بن علي بن رسلان الرملي الشافعي الماضي أبوه ويعرف بابن رسلان . ولد في ليلة الخميس عاشر ربيع الأول سنة خمس وتسعين وسبعمائة وأجاز له أبو الخير بن العلائي باستدعاء أبيه ، وكان خيرا رأيته بعد موت والده بسنين بمجلس شيخنا وأعطاه كراسة كان والده أرسل يسأل فيها عن أشياء تتعلق بشرح أبي داود وتصنيفه ليلحق ذلك بأماكنه وما أظنه فعل إن اهتدى لأماكنها . مات في أوائل سنة ست وخمسين ظنا رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Aḥmad b. Ḥusayn b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Raslān al-Ramlī al-Shāfiʿī. His father was mentioned previously. He was known as Ibn Raslān. He was born on the night of Thursday, the 10th of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 795 AH. Abū al-Khayr b. al-ʿAlāʾī granted him an ijāza at the request of his father. He was a good man. I saw him several years after his father's death at the gathering of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), to whom he gave a booklet containing queries his father had sent regarding Ibn Ḥajar's commentary on Abū Dāwūd, so that they might be appended in their proper places. I do not think he did so, even if he knew where those places were. He died, presumably, in the early part of the year 856 AH. May God have mercy on him and on us."@en .

rec:AIND-D04101 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04101-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04101-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04101 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أحمد بن محمد بن حمزة المدني الماضي أبوه ويعرف بالحجار . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥamza al-Madanī. His father was mentioned previously. He is known as al-Ḥajjār. He is among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D04102 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04102-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04102-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04102-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04102-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04102-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04102 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أحمد بن أبي الفضل محمد بن عبد الله محيي الدين الحرازي الأصل المكي الآتي أخوه الجمال محمد . مات بها في ليلة الجمعة ثالث عشري ذي الحجة سنة خمس وثمانين وصلى عليه بعد الصبح عند باب الكعبة ودفن عند أهله بالمعلاة . وكان مباركا متقشفا فقيرا ربما عامل الفقراء مع يبس وإن كان يتفقد بعض أهل البيوت منهم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir b. Ahmad b. Abi al-Fadl Muhammad b. Abd Allah, Muhyi al-Din. Of Harazi origin and a resident of Mecca. His brother al-Jamal Muhammad is forthcoming. He died in Mecca on the night of Friday, the 23rd of Dhu al-Hijja, in the year 885 AH. The funeral prayer was performed after dawn at the Gate of the Kaaba, and he was buried with his family in al-Mu'alla. He was a blessed, ascetic, and poor man who sometimes treated the poor strictly, though he still looked after some of their households."@en .

rec:AIND-D04103 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04103-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04103-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04103 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أحمد بن محمد بن نشوان . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن إبراهيم"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Nashwān. [His entry] has already appeared among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D04104 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04104-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04104-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04104 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أحمد بن محمد الجرمكي البرددار والده لنقيب الأشراف . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Jarmakī al-Barddār. His father was barddār (attendant) to the Naqīb al-Ashrāf. He was among those who heard Hadith from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04105 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04105-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04105-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04105-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04105-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04105-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04105 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن الشيخ أحمد بن محمد الصندلي الأصل القاهري الأزهري الماضي أبوه . مات وقد جاز الأربعين في يوم الجمعة سادس عشر شعبان سنة ثمانين فجأة فإنه توجه مع تراب لاحضار رمل من الصحراء فانهار عليهما ، وصلى عليهما من الغد بالأزهر وتألم أبوه كثيرا مع أنه كان في تعب بسبب كثرة ما كان يتحمله من الديون عوضهما الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣandalī, of Cairo origin and affiliated with al-Azhar, whose father was mentioned previously. He died suddenly on Friday, the 16th of Shaʿbān, in the year 880 AH, having just passed forty years of age. He had gone with a person named Turāb to fetch sand from the desert, and it collapsed upon them both, causing their deaths. The funeral prayer was held for them the next day at al-Azhar Mosque. His father grieved deeply for him, despite already being in distress due to the heavy burden of debts he carried. May Allah compensate them both with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D04106 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04106-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04106-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04106 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أحمد بن محمد المدابغي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir b. Ahmad b. Muhammad al-Madabighi. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhawi) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04107 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04107-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04107-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04107 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أحمد بن عز الدين الولد محيي الدين أبو البركات بن الشهابي المناوي الخياط والده . عرض على المنهاج في ربيع الثاني سنة تسعين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Aḥmad b. ʿIzz al-Dīn, the boy Muḥyī al-Dīn Abū al-Barakāt, son of al-Shihābī al-Manāwī; his father is a tailor. He presented al-Minhāj to me in Rabīʿ al-Thānī of the year [8]90."@en .

rec:AIND-D04108 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04108-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04108-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04108-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04108 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أحمد بن يعقوب بن أحمد بن عبد المنعم بن أحمد الزين ابن الشهاب الاطفيحي الأصل القاهري سبط الزين العراقي وشقيق المحب محمد وعبد الرحيم ويعرف كأبيه بابن يعقوب . ممن نشأ في كنف أبويه ، وحج وسمع الحديث عن شيخنا وغيره وأجاز له جماعة وتنزل في الجهات وتأخر عن أخويه في الوجود والمرتبة لكونه طورا وحده وربما ينسب لتعاطيه ما اقتضى ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Aḥmad b. Yaʿqūb b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Munʿim b. Aḥmad, al-Zayn b. al-Shihāb. He was of Aṭfīḥī origin, resided in Cairo, and was the maternal grandson of al-Zayn al-ʿIrāqī, and the full brother of al-Muḥibb Muḥammad and ʿAbd al-Raḥīm. Like his father, he was known as Ibn Yaʿqūb. He was raised under the care of his parents, performed the Hajj, and heard Hadith from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others, and received ijazas from a group of scholars. He held stipendiary posts, but fell behind his two brothers in longevity and status due to his peculiar lifestyle and behaviors occasionally attributed to him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04109 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04109-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04109-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04109-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04109 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أبي البقا الغزولي . ممن يزاحم الطلبة ويلم ببعض المسائل بل وتنزل في الصرغتمشية وغيرها وأكثر من الاجتماع بي سيما في المجاورة والدروس ولم يقتصر على ذلك بل يخالط كثيرا من الأتراك كبرسباي قرا وتنبك الجمالي ولم يحصل على طائل من الفريقين ، وسافر في البحر سنة سبع وتسعين متكلما على حمل ثانيهما أمير المحمل فيها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Abī al-Baqāʾ al-Ghazūlī. He used to compete with students and was familiar with some scholarly questions. He held a position in the Ṣarghatmashiyya Madrasa among others. He associated with me frequently, especially during his stay (jāwara) and lessons in Mecca. He also socialized with many Turks (Mamluk amirs) such as Barsbāy Qarā and Tanbak al-Jamālī, though he did not gain much benefit from either group. In the year 897 AH, he travelled by sea, managing the transport of the latter (Tanbak), who was the commander of the pilgrimage caravan (Amīr al-Maḥmal) that year."@en .

rec:AIND-D04110 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04110-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04110-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04110 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أبي بكر بن أحمد الطنبداوي المكي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir ibn Abī Bakr ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭanbadāwī al-Makkī. He is among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04112 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04112-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04112-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04112 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أبي بكر بن علي بن أبي بكر بن عبد الملك بن أبي بكر ابن عبد الحق المقدسي الصالحي الحنبلي أخو خديجة وابن عم علي بن غازي الآتيين ويعرف بالكوري بضم الكاف وراء مهملة . ولد سنة ثلاث وستين وسبعمائة وذكر أنه سمع من المحب الصامت صحيح البخاري فكتب عنه بعض أصحابنا ومات قبل الخمسين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Malik b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Ḥaqq al-Maqdisī al-Ṣāliḥī al-Ḥanbalī. He was the brother of Khadīja and the cousin of ʿAlī b. Ghāzī (both mentioned below). He was known as al-Kūrī (with a damma on the kāf and an undotted rāʾ). He was born in the year 763 AH. It is mentioned that he heard the Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī from al-Muḥibb al-Ṣāmit, and some of our companions wrote from him. He is thought to have died before 850 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04114 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04114-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04114-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04114 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن حسن بن أحمد القليوبي القاهري التاجر في الشرب ممن يكثر المخالطة للفقهاء والمجاورة بمكة وسمع على الشرف المناوي وغيره بل سمع مني بمكة وهو من خيار الجماعة وكان يذكر أنه سمع من شيخنا وليس ببعيد . مات في جمادى الثانية سنة إحدى وتسعين ولا يقصر عن السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qādir b. Ḥasan b. Aḥmad al-Qalyūbī al-Qāhirī. A merchant in Sūq al-Shurb (Cairo), who frequently associated with jurists and performed mujāwara (extended stay/devotion) in Mecca. He heard hadith from al-Sharaf al-Munāwī and others, and he even heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca, being one of the best of the group. He used to mention that he heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), which is highly plausible. He died in Jumādā al-Thāniya in the year 891 AH, being not less than seventy years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D04116 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04116-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04116-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04116-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04116-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04116 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن حسن بن علي الغمري ثم القاهري البخانقي ويعرف بابن فقوسة . له بنون جلال الدين محمد وزين العابدين محمد وهما من أم وشهاب الدين أحمد وأبو الفتح محمد وأبو الحسن علي والثلاثة من أم الأول شافعي المذهب وكذا الثالث والثاني عزمه يكون حنبليا والرابع حنفي يقرأ في القدوري والآخر عزم على كونه مالكيا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī al-Ghamrī, later al-Qāhirī, al-Bakhāniqī, known as Ibn Faqqūsa. He had several sons: Jalāl al-Dīn Muḥammad and Zayn al-ʿĀbidīn Muḥammad, who were from one mother; and Shihāb al-Dīn Aḥmad, Abū al-Fatḥ Muḥammad, and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī, who were from another mother. The first (Jalāl al-Dīn) is Shāfiʿī, as is the third (Shihāb al-Dīn). The second (Zayn al-ʿĀbidīn) intends to be Ḥanbalī. The fourth (Abū al-Fatḥ) is Ḥanafī and reads al-Qudūrī. The last one (Abū al-Ḥasan) intends to be Mālikī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04118 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04118-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04118-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04118 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن حسين بن علي العراقي الطائفي أخو أحمد الماضي ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī al-ʿIrāqī al-Ṭāʾifī. The brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04119 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04119-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04119-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04119 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن حمزة الطرابلسي الدمشقي . ممن أخذ عن ابن زهرة وابن قاضي شهبة ، أم لقانصوه حين كونه نائب حلب ثم أعرض عن الامامة وقطن الشام وهو تام الفضيلة بشعار بني الترك ولفقره يحضر عند المهملين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Ḥamza al-Ṭarābulusī al-Dimashqī. He studied under Ibn Zuhra and Ibn Qāḍī Shuhba. He served as an imam for Qānṣawh when the latter was the governor of Aleppo, but later gave up the imamate and settled in al-Shām (the Levant). He was a highly virtuous man who dressed in Turkish attire, but due to his poverty, he used to attend the gatherings of the neglected and destitute."@en .

rec:AIND-D04120 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04120-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04120-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04120 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن خليل الزين الحريري أحد قراء الجوق والخباز والده . كان كيسا من أهل باب الشعرية . مات غريقا ببولاق في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وخمسين في حياة أبويه ومن الغريب أنه تجهز للسفر إلى مكة في البحر فلما وصل إلى الطور هالته رؤيته فرجع خوفا من الغرق فلم يلبث أن غرق ببحر النيل عفا الله عنه ورحمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir b. Khalil al-Zayn al-Hariri. He was one of the Quran reciters of al-Jawq, and his father was a baker. He was a refined man from the people of Bab al-Sha'riyya. He drowned at Bulaq in Rabi' al-Awwal in the year 852 H, during the lifetime of his parents. Remarkably, he had prepared to travel to Mecca by sea, but when he reached al-Tur, he was terrified by its sight and returned out of fear of drowning, only to drown shortly thereafter in the Nile. May Allah forgive him and have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04121 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04121-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04121-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04121 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن سكيكر العطار بباب السلام من مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Sukaykar, the perfume merchant at Bāb al-Salām in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04122 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04122-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04122-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04122 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن شاهين الجمالي الذهبي سبط الشمس محمد بن أحمد بن محمد ابن أحمد البيري الآتي وانتسب جماليا لأخيه . كان خيرا راغبا في زيارة الصالحين وشهود مجالس الخير مع التكسب والتقنع والقراءة تبرعا مع القراءة في المشاهد وهو ممن أكثر الحضور عندي في الأمالي وغيرها مات سنة بضع وثمانين بعد منام رآه دل لذلك رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Shāhīn al-Jamālī al-Dhahabī, the maternal grandson of al-Shams Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Bīrī (who is mentioned below). He took the nisba al-Jamālī after his (grandfather's) brother, al-Jamāl Yūsuf. He was a virtuous man, eager to visit the righteous and attend gatherings of goodness, while earning his livelihood and being content. He recited voluntarily and chanted at the shrines (mashhads). He was among those who most frequently attended my dictation gatherings (al-Amālī) and others. He died in the Hijri 880s (year eighty-something) after seeing a dream that indicated his approaching death. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04126 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04126-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04126-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04126-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04126 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد ابن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي المكي ابن عم الذي قبله . ولد في ربيع الأول سنة خمس وأربعين وثمانمائة وأمه علما ابنة المحب بن ظهيرة . مات صغيرا بعد أن أحضر عند أبي الفتح المراغي عوضه الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓuhayra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓuhayra al-Qurashī al-Makkī, the cousin of the preceding person. He was born in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 845 AH. His mother was ʿAlmāʾ, the daughter of al-Muḥibb b. Ẓuhayra. He died young, after having been brought to attend the sessions of Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī. May God compensate him with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D04130 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04130-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04130-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04130-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04130 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الوهاب بن عبد الله بن أسعد اليافعي الهندي المولد المكي . مات بها في صفر سنة اثنتين وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir bin ʿAbd al-Raḥmān bin Muḥammad bin ʿAbd al-Wahhāb bin ʿAbd Allāh bin Asʿad al-Yāfiʿī. Born in India and later resided in Mecca. He died in Mecca in the month of Safar in the year 882. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D04132 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04132-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04132-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04132 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن عبد الرحيم بن أحمد بن الناصري محمد بن محمد بن عثمان الزين بن النجمي بن البارزي أخو محمد ويوسف وشقيق فاطمة أمهما تركية لأبيه . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة وحفظ القرآن والعمدة والمنهاج وألفية النحو وعرض على جماعة واشتغل قليلا وحضر عند التقي بن قاضي عجلون التقسيم ولم يتصون ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nasiri Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Zayn ibn al-Najmi ibn al-Barizi. He was the brother of Muhammad and Yusuf, and the full brother of Fatima; their mother was a Turkish woman, and they were half-brothers from his father's side. He is among those who heard Hadith from me (al-Sakhawi) in Cairo. He memorized the Qur'an, al-Umda, al-Minhaj, and Alfiyyat al-Nahw, presented them to a group of scholars, studied a little, and attended the classes of al-Taqsim under al-Taqi ibn Qadi Ajlun. He did not maintain a self-controlled lifestyle."@en .

rec:AIND-D04133 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04133-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04133-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04133-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04133-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04133 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن عبد الرزاق بن عبد القادر بن عبد الحليم بن عبد الرزاق الشرف الأنصاري السكندري المالكي قاضيها وشيخ الشيوخ بها . ولد بها في شوال سنة ستين وسبعمائة وأخذ عنه البقاعي . مات في يوم الجمعة حادي عشري رجب سنة أربع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAbd al-Ḥalīm b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq al-Sharaf al-Anṣārī al-Sakandarī al-Mālikī, the Qadi of Alexandria and its Shaykh al-Shuyukh. He was born there in Shawwal 760 AH. Al-Biqāʿī studied under him. He died on Friday, 21 Rajab 844 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04138 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04138-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04138-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04138-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04138 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن عبد الله بن عمر العرابي المكي أحد الخيار . مات بها في جمادى الأولى سنة سبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar al-ʿUrābī al-Makkī. He was one of the virtuous people. He died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ūlā, in the year 870 AH. His biography was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D04140 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04140-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04140-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04140-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04140 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن عبد الهادي بن محمد المحيوي الأزهري المدني ثم المكي أحد الفضلاء والآتي أبوه : قرأ بمكة في سنة خمس وستين على المحيوي عبد القادر قاضيها المالكي البخاري ولازمه في العربية وغيرها وبرع وبالمدينة النبوية على أبي الفرج المراغي . ومات بمكة في رحب سنة ثمان وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir b. Abd al-Hadi b. Muhammad al-Muhyawi al-Azhari al-Madani, later al-Makki. One of the virtuous scholars, whose father's biography is forthcoming. In the year 865 AH, he read Sahih al-Bukhari under al-Muhyawi Abd al-Qadir, the Maliki judge of Mecca, and became his close disciple in Arabic grammar and other fields, in which he excelled. In Medina, he also studied under Abu al-Faraj al-Maraghi. He died in Mecca in Rajab, 878 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04143 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04143-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04143-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04143 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي بن أحمد اليمني الصايغ . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Yamanī al-Ṣāyigh (the goldsmith). Among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04144 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04144-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04144-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04144 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي بن أحمد الطيبي المنصوري . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Ṭībī al-Manṣūrī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04145 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04145-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04145-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04145 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي بن جار الله بن زايد السنبسي المكي ويشهر بعبيد . ممن سافر لعدن في التجارة . مات بمكة في ربيع الثاني سنة أربع وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد وهو والد عبد اللطيف وأبي سعد الآتيين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī b. Jār Allāh b. Zāyid al-Sinbisī al-Makkī, popularly known as ʿUbayd. He was among those who traveled to Aden for trade. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Thānī, the year 874 AH. His death was chronicled by Ibn Fahd. He is the father of ʿAbd al-Laṭīf and Abū Saʿd, both of whom are mentioned below."@en .

rec:AIND-D04146 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04146-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04146-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04146 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي بن حسن المهندس ويعرف بابن الصياد . ممن ضربه الدوادار الكبير في وقت . ومات في ربيع الثاني سنة احدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī b. Ḥasan al-Muhandis, known as Ibn al-Ṣayyād. He was once beaten by the Great Dawādār (al-Dawādār al-Kabīr). He died in Rabīʿ al-Thānī, the year 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04147 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04147-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04147-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04147 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي بن رمضان بن علي محيي الدين الطوخي القاهري الشافعي الآتي أبوه ويعرف بابن أخت مهني . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة واشتغل يسيرا وصحب ابن قاضي عجلون وقتا وتكسب بالشهادة عند الشهاب الفليحي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī b. Ramaḍān b. ʿAlī Muḥyī al-Dīn al-Ṭūkhī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī (his father's biography is forthcoming below), known as the son of Mihnī's sister. He heard ḥadīth from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo, engaged briefly in studies, accompanied Ibn Qāḍī ʿAjlūn for a time, and earned his living as a notary witness under al-Shihāb al-Falīḥī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04149 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04149-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04149-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04149-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04149 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي بن صدقة . أحد قراء الجوق وامام الأتابك كان ، ويعرف بابن الحيلوك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir b. Ali b. Sadaqa. He was one of the reciters of al-Jawq and served as the Imam of the Atabak. He was known as Ibn al-Hayluk."@en .

rec:AIND-D04150 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04150-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04150-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04150-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04150 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي بن عبد الرحمن المنوفي معلم الأبناء بها والخياط أبوه . لقيني بمنوف في جمادى الثانية سنة اثنتين وتسعين فقرأ على الباب الأول من عمدة الأحكام قراءة حسنة وكتبت له اجازة ، رأيت من يثني على خيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Munūfī. A teacher of children there (in Minūf), whose father was a tailor. He met me (al-Sakhāwī) in Minūf in Jumādā al-Thāniya, year 892, and read to me the first chapter of 『ʿUmdat al-Aḥkām』 with an excellent recitation, for which I wrote him an ijāza. I have seen those who praise his goodness."@en .

rec:AIND-D04151 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04151-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04151-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04151 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي بن عمر الدنجيهي الأزهري الشافعي الحريري على باب الجامع . ممن تميز في الميقات والفرائض والحساب ، وأخذ عن البدر المارداني وغيره وأفاد الطلبة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar al-Danjīhī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī, the silk-merchant at the gate of the Mosque. He was distinguished in the fields of timekeeping (al-mīqāt), inheritance law, and arithmetic. He studied under al-Badr al-Māridānī and others, and benefited the students."@en .

rec:AIND-D04153 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04153-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04153-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04153 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن الشمس علي بن محمد بن عبد الله الخولاني الرضائي اليماني الشافعي . من بيت صلاح . لقيني في سادس ذي الحجة سنة سبع وتسعين بمكة فقرأ على بعض الصحيحين والشفا بعد أن سمع مني المسلسل وأجزت له ولأخيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. al-Shams ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Khawlānī al-Riḍāʾī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī. From the house of Ṣalāḥ. He met me on the 6th of Dhū al-Ḥijjah in the year 897 AH in Mecca, and read to me a portion of the two Ṣaḥīḥs and al-Shifāʾ after he had heard the musalsal [ḥadīth] from me, and I granted an ijāzah to him and to his brother."@en .

rec:AIND-D04155 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04155-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04155-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04155 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي بن محمد بن الفقيه ، ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faqīh. He was among those who heard hadith from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04157 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04157-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04157-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04157-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04157 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر المدعو محمدا بن العلاء علي بن محمود السلماني ثم الحموي الحنبلي ويعرف كأبيه بابن المغلي . قال شيخنا في أنبائه إنه نبغ وحفظ المحرر وغيره ونشأ على طريقة حسنة ومات في نصف ذي القعدة سنة ست وعشرين وقد راهق وأسف عليه أبوه جدا ولم يكن له ولد غيره ورأيت بعض المخبطين جعل محمدا اسم أبيه فصار عبد القادر بن محمد بن علي بن محمود ، وهو غلط محض ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir, also called Muḥammad, son of al-ʿAlāʾ ʿAlī son of Maḥmūd, al-Salmānī then al-Ḥamawī, al-Ḥanbalī, known like his father as Ibn al-Mughlī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his chronicle (Inbāʾ al-Ghumr) that he showed great promise, memorized al-Muḥarrar and other works, and grew up in an excellent manner. He died in the middle of Dhu al-Qaʿdah in the year 826 AH, having nearly reached puberty, and his father grieved for him deeply, as he had no other child. I saw that some confused writers made Muḥammad the name of his father, writing 'ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Maḥmūd', which is a pure error."@en .

rec:AIND-D04159 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04159-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04159-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04159-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04159 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي بن يوسف الزفتاوي البوتيجي نزيل عدن ويعرف فيها بالصعيدي وعم إسماعيل بن علي الماضي . ولد بعيد الثلاثين بزفتا وقرأ القرآن وقطن رواق اليمنة من الأزهر وقتا واشتغل مالكيا ثم تعانى التجارة وسافر إلى عدن فقطنها من نحو أربعين سنة يتردد منها للحج وغيره كثيرا ورزق الأولاد وبورك له مع خير وتودد وبر للفقراء وحسن معاملة وحرص على الدين سمعت الثناء عليه من غير واحد وقد اجتمع بي في سنة ست وتسعين أو التي بعدها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf al-Zaftāwī al-Būtījī. He settled in Aden, where he was known as al-Ṣaʿīdī, and was the uncle of the aforementioned Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī. He was born shortly after 830 AH in Zaftā. He recited the Qurʾān and resided for a time in the Yemeni hospice (Riwāq al-Yamanat) of al-Azhar Mosque. He studied Maliki law, then turned to trade and traveled to Aden, where he settled for about forty years, frequently traveling from there for Hajj and other purposes. He was blessed with children, prosperity, goodness, amiability, charity to the poor, good conduct, and devotion to religion. I heard praise of him from several people, and he met with me in the year 896 AH or after."@en .

rec:AIND-D04160 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04160-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04160-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04160-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04160 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن علي الحباك نزيل مكة وأحد مؤذني المسجد الحرام وقراء الصفة بالمدرسة السلطانية بل استقر في مشيخة القراء بالمجامع والمحافل سيما عند القبور عقب محمد بن المحتسب وأول شيء باشره في ذلك على قبرزوجة أخي"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī al-Ḥabbāk. A resident of Mecca, one of the muezzins of the Sacred Mosque, and one of the readers of the Suffa at the Sulṭāniyya Madrasa. Rather, he settled in the position of chief of readers (mashyakhat al-qurrāʾ) in assemblies and gatherings, especially at graves, succeeding Muḥammad b. al-Muḥtasib. The first thing he undertook in this capacity was at the grave of my brother's wife."@en .

rec:AIND-D04163 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04163-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04163-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04163-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04163 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن عمر بن محمد بن علي بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن عمر بن إبراهيم الجعبري الخليلي الآتي أبوه . ولد في العشر الأخير من ذي القعدة سنة ثمان وعشرين وثمانمائة بالخليل ونشأ بها فحفظ القرآن وأحضر في الأولى مع والده على ابن الجزري والتدمري وعظيمات وكذا على الزين البرشكي ختم الشفا ثم سمع على التدمري المنتقي من مشيخة ابن كليب ومنية السول لابن عبد السلام ، وأجاز له القبابي وشيخنا ، وحج ودخل الشام والقاهرة وحدث فيها سنة تسع وثمانين باليسير"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿUmar b. Ibrāhīm al-Jaʿbarī al-Khalīlī, whose father is mentioned below. He was born in Hebron in the last ten days of Dhu al-Qaʿdah in the year 828 AH and grew up there. He memorized the Qurʾān and attended, in his youth alongside his father, the lectures of Ibn al-Jazarī, al-Tadmurī, and ʿAẓīmāt, as well as al-Zayn al-Burshukī for the completion of 『al-Shifāʾ』. He then heard from al-Tadmurī the selection from 『Mashyakhat Ibn Kulayb』 and 『Munyāt al-Sūl』 by Ibn ʿAbd al-Salām. He was granted an ijāza by al-Qabābī and our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar). He performed the Ḥajj, entered Syria and Cairo, and transmitted a small amount of hadith there in the year 889 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04164 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04164-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04164-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04164-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04164-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04164 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن عمر المارديني الدمشقي الأصل القاهري الجوهري نزيل البرقوقية وأحد صوفيتها وغريم البقاعي . مات قريب الثمانين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿUmar al-Māridīnī, of Damascus origin, resident of Cairo, the jeweler (al-Jawharī). He resided in al-Barqūqiyya and was one of its Sufis. He was an opponent of al-Biqāʿī. He died presumably around 880 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04165 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04165-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04165-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04165 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أبي الفضل بن موسى بن أبي الهول محيي الدين بن المجد الآتي أبوه وأخوه محمد استقر في عمالة ديوان الاشراف كأبيه بل ولي نظر الاسطبل عوض سعد الدين كاتب العليق ثم انفصل بيحيى بن البقري ومعه استيفاء الذخيرة وغير ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Abī al-Faḍl b. Mūsā b. Abī al-Hawl, Muḥyī al-Dīn, known as Ibn al-Majd (whose father and brother Muḥammad are mentioned below). He was appointed to the administration of the Bureau of the Ashrāf (Dīwān al-Ashrāf), just like his father. Indeed, he also held the supervision of the stable (Naẓar al-Isṭabl) in place of Saʿd al-Dīn, the scribe of fodder. Later, he was replaced by Yaḥyā b. al-Baqarī, who took over that post along with the auditing of the provisions (Istīfāʾ al-Dhakhīra) and other offices."@en .

rec:AIND-D04170 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04170-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04170-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04170 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن أبي الفضل محمد بن أحمد بن أبي الفضل محمد بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز بن القسم بن عبد الرحمن القرشي الهاشمي العقيلي النويري المكي الآتي أبوه . بيض له صاحبنا ابن فهد في النويريين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir ibn Abī al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Qurashī al-Hāshimī al-ʿUqaylī al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī. His father is mentioned below. Our companion Ibn Fahd left a blank space for him in his biographical dictionary of the Nuwayrīs."@en .

rec:AIND-D04172 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04172-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04172-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04172-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04172 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن أبي العباس أحمد بن محمد بن محمد النويري الأصل الغزي حفيد قاضي المالكية بها الماضي . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-ʿAbbāṣ Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Nuwayrī al-Ghazzī, the grandson of the aforementioned Maliki judge (qāḍī) of Gaza. He studied under me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04173 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04173-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04173-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04173 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن الشمس محمد بن أحمد الوراق المؤذن . ممن اشتغل يسيرا وحضر عندي . وله مزيد ذكاء وفهم غير أنه سيء الطريقة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. al-Shams Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Warrāq al-Muʾadhdhin. He studied briefly and attended my lectures. He possessed great intelligence and understanding, but was of bad conduct."@en .

rec:AIND-D04174 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04174-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04174-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04174 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن أحمد النابتي نزيل جامع الغمري بالقاهرة . ممن قرأ القرآن وأدب به بعض الأبناء وسمع على أشياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Nābitī. He resided at the al-Ghamrī Mosque in Cairo. He recited the Qurʾān, educated some children with it, and heard various [traditions/texts]."@en .

rec:AIND-D04175 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04175-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04175-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04175-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04175 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن اسماعيل الدمشقي الكفر بطناوي شيخ كتب إلى بالإجازة في استدعاء مؤرخ بسنة خمسين وقيل أنه كان في خدمة أبي هريرة بن الذهبي سماعه بقراءة شيخنا على محمد بن أبي هريرة المذكور لجزء فيه ثلاثة محالس من±±± أمالي أبي يعلي الموصلي في رمضان سنة اثنتين وثمانمائة وما علمته حدث . مات سنة بضع و خمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir b. Muhammad b. Isma'il al-Dimashqi al-Kafarbattnawi, shaykh. He wrote to me (al-Sakhawi) with an ijaza in a request (istid'a) dated to the year 850 AH. It is said that he was in the service of Abu Hurayra b. al-Dhahabi. He listened, through the reading of our shaykh (Ibn Hajar), under the aforementioned Muhammad b. Abi Hurayra, to a portion (juz') containing three sessions (majalis) from the 'Amali' of Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili in Ramadan 802 AH. I do not know of him transmitting hadith. He died in the 850s AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04176 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04176-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04176-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04176 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن تميم المقريزي . مضى فيمن جده إبراهيم بن محمد بن تميم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. Tamīm al-Maqrīzī. [His entry] has already appeared among those whose grandfather is Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Tamīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D04178 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04178-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04178-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04178-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04178-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04178 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن حسن بن علي القاهري ويعرف بابن الكماخي . ولد سنة إحدى وأربعين وثمانمائة ونشأ فقيرا فتردد إلي في بعض الأحاديث وخطب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī al-Qāhirī, known as Ibn al-Kamākhī. He was born in the year 841 AH (1437/1438 CE) and grew up poor. He frequented me [al-Sakhāwī] for some hadiths and delivered sermons."@en .

rec:AIND-D04180 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04180-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04180-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04180 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن راشد . فيمن لم يسم جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. Rāshid. [His entry is] among those whose grandfather is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D04183 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04183-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04183-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04183 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد سمنطح بن عبد الكريم بن أحمد بن عبد الكريم ابن ظهيرة القرشي الزبيدي وأمه من أهلها ، أجاز له في سنة ست وثلاثين جماعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad Samanṭaḥ b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm Ibn Ẓuhayra al-Qurashī al-Zabīdī. His mother was from the people of Zabīd. In the year 836 AH, a group of scholars granted him an ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D04184 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04184-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04184-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04184-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04184-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04184-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D04184-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04184 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن الشمس محمد بن الجمال عبد الله بن الشهاب أحمد الفرياني الأصل القاهري الشافعي سبط ابن الخص . ممن سمع في البخاري بالظاهرية وتردد إلي يسيرا وكذا للبقاعي بل نسخ له ، وخطب وجلس بمجلس التوتة من المقس شاهدا وتنزل في الصوفية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. al-Shams Muḥammad b. al-Jamāl ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Shihāb Aḥmad, of Firyānī origin, residing in Cairo, Shāfiʿī. Maternal grandson of Ibn al-Khaṣṣ. He was among those who heard the Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī at the al-Ẓāhiriyya Madrasa. He frequented me (al-Sakhāwī) briefly, and likewise al-Biqāʿī, for whom he actually copied manuscripts. He delivered sermons, sat as a witness (shāhid) in the session of al-Tūta in al-Maqs, and was appointed as a Sufi."@en .

rec:AIND-D04185 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04185-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04185-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04185 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن عبد الله الضميري الدمشقي الحنبلي . لقيه العز ابن فهد فكتب عنه قصيدة نبوية من نظمه أولها : %~% يا سعد لك السعد %~% إن سعى بك مرقال %~% وأجاز وقال إنه شرح كلا من أربعي النووي وسماه الدرر المضية والقطربية وعارض البردة بقصيدة سماها الزهر في الاكام في مدح النبي عليه السلام ، وبانت سعاد وغير ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Dhamīrī al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanbalī. Al-ʿIzz b. Fahd met him and copied from him a prophetic praise poem of his own composition, beginning with: 'O Saʿd, happiness is yours if you strive...' He also granted him an ijāza and mentioned that he wrote a commentary on al-Nawawī's Forty Hadiths, naming it 'al-Durar al-Muḍiyya wa-l-Quṭrubiyya', and composed a poem in opposition (muʿāraḍa) to the 'Burda' named 'al-Zahr fī al-Akām fī Madḥ al-Nabī ʿAlayhi al-Salām', as well as a muʿāraḍa of 'Bānat Suʿād' and other works."@en .

rec:AIND-D04187 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04187-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04187-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04187-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04187-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04187-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04187 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن عبد الملك محيي الدين بن الشمس الدميري الأصل القاهري المالكي الآتي أبوه وولده البدر محمد . ممن حفظ المختصر واشتغل قليلا ، وحج وجلس مع الشهود وكان ساكنا لا بأس به . مات في ليلة ثامن عشر المحرم سنة إحدى وتسعين وقد جاز الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Malik, Muḥyī al-Dīn. Of Damīrī origin, Cairo resident, Maliki. His father and his son, al-Badr Muḥammad, are mentioned below. He memorized al-Mukhtaṣar and studied a little, performed Hajj, and sat with the legal witnesses. He was a peaceful, decent person. He died on the night of 18 Muharram 891 AH, having passed the age of sixty."@en .

rec:AIND-D04190 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04190-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04190-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04190 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن علي بن عبد الله بن أحمد محيي الدين بن الشمس الشارمساحي الدمياطي الشافعي العطائي الآتي أبوه . شاب فهم قرأ علي في شرح النخبة دراية وسمع مني أشياء واشتغل على غير واحد مع خير واستقامة وقد أجزت له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad Muḥyī al-Dīn al-Shārmsāḥī al-Dimyāṭī al-Shafiʿī al-ʿAṭāʾī. His father is mentioned below. A young man of understanding, he read to me the commentary on al-Nukhba (Nuzhat al-Naẓar) with comprehension, heard several things from me, and studied under more than one scholar with goodness and uprightness. I have granted him an ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D04192 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04192-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04192-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04192 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن علي الدقدوسي الأزهري الشافعي ويعرف بابن المصري وبالمنهاجي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة احدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Daqdūsī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Miṣrī and as al-Minhājī. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 891."@en .

rec:AIND-D04193 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04193-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04193-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04193-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04193 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن عمر بن عثمان الخواجا زين الدين بن ناصر الدين ابن الجندي المصري . ممن سمع على شيخنا في الاملاء وغيره وأخذ عن البوتيجي وتردد لمكة وله بجدة دار وصهريج وقفهما على معتقيه والجبرت . مات بها في حياة أبيه في جمادى الآخرة سنة أربع وستين وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بمعلاتها . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. ʿUthmān, al-Khawājā Zayn al-Dīn b. Nāṣir al-Dīn Ibn al-Jundī al-Miṣrī. He was among those who heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) at the dictation sessions and elsewhere, studied under al-Būtījī, and frequented Mecca. He had a house and a cistern in Jidda, which he made waqf for his freedmen and the Jabart. He died there, during his father's lifetime, in Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year 864, and was carried to Mecca and buried in its Muʿallā cemetery. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04195 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04195-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04195-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04195 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن ناصر الدين محمد بن عوض الرهاوي المكي . ممن كان يتردد في التجارة لبجيلة وغيرها ويأتمنه الناس في ذلك . مات في سنة أربع وثمانين ببلاد بجيلة ودفن بها . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir b. Nasir al-Din Muhammad b. Awad al-Rahawi al-Makki. He was among those who frequently traveled for trade to Bajila and other places, and people trusted him in that regard. He died in the year 884 AH in the land of Bajila and was buried there. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D04196 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04196-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04196-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04196-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04196-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04196 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن التقي محمد بن الشمس محمد بن خليل بن إبراهيم بن علي الحراني الأصل القاهري الآتي أبوه وجده ويعرف بابن المنمنم . ممن سمع في البخاري بالظاهرية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. al-Taqī Muḥammad b. al-Shams Muḥammad b. Khalīl b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī, of Ḥarrānī origin, of Cairo. His father and grandfather are mentioned below. He is known as Ibn al-Munamnam. He was among those who heard the recitation of al-Bukhārī at the Ẓāhiriyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D04197 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04197-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04197-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04197 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن أبي عبد الله محمد بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز أبو الفرج النويري ، وأمه زينب ابنة الخواجا داود بن علي الكيلاني . ولد في ذي الحجة سنة خمسين وثمانمائة بمكة . بيض له ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. Abī ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, Abū al-Faraj al-Nuwayrī. His mother was Zaynab, daughter of al-Khawājā Dāwūd b. ʿAlī al-Kīlānī. He was born in Dhu al-Hijjah in the year 850 AH in Mecca. Ibn Fahd left a blank space for him (to record his death or subsequent biography)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04204 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04204-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04204-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04204-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04204 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن الشرف محمد بن محمد الطناحي الأصل بمهملتين الأولى مفتوحة بعدها نون القاهري التاجر هو وأبوه بسوق الشرب . ممن قرأ القرآن وسمع مني بالقاهرة . وحج وجاور وهو أشبه من أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. al-Sharaf Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, of al-Ṭanāḥī origin (the first letter is a vowelless ta' followed by a nun), of Cairo, the merchant. He and his father were merchants in Sūq al-Shurb. He recited the Qur'an and heard [hadith] from me in Cairo. He performed Hajj and stayed adjacent to the Sanctuary (jāwara). He is more upright than his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D04205 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04205-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04205-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04205 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن محمد محيي الدين بن الشمس بن الجلال المرصفي الأصل لكون جد أبيه لأمه وهو علم الدين الطبيب كان في خدمة القطبية صاحب المدرسة التي برأس حارة زويلة ويعرف جده بالقبابي كان في خدمة الجمالي الاستادار فدرب العلم ابن ابنته البدر في الطب ونشأ صاحب الترجمة كذلك حتى تميز ومشى للناس بعقل ودربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, Muḥyī al-Dīn b. al-Shams b. al-Jalāl, of Marṣafā origin — because his father's maternal grandfather, the physician ʿAlam al-Dīn, (came from there and) was in the service of al-Quṭbiyya, the madrasa at the head of Ḥārat Zuwayla. His grandfather was known as al-Qabābī and was in the service of al-Jamālī the ustādār. ʿAlam al-Dīn trained his daughter's son al-Badr in medicine, and the subject of this entry grew up likewise, until he distinguished himself and treated people with sense and skill."@en .

rec:AIND-D04206 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04206-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04206-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04206 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن البدر محمد بن أبي النجا محمد الطحطوطي الأصل الاسطائي نسبة لبلد من الفيوم ويعرف أبوه بالحجازي . معتقد شهير يأتي فيمن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. al-Badr Muḥammad b. Abī al-Najā Muḥammad, of Ṭaḥṭūṭ origin, known as al-Isṭāʾī after a town in al-Fayyūm; his father is known as al-Ḥijāzī. A famous holy man; [his entry] comes among those whose father is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D04209 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04209-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04209-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04209 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن محمد بن يعقوب المدني أخو عبد الوهاب الآتي وعم قاضي الماليكة بمكة النجم محمد . صاهر محمد بن عمر بن المحب الزرندي على أخته ورأس بالكرم والاحتشام . وسافر بعد أن دخل مصر والشام بسبب التوكل في أوقاف المدينة إلى الروم ولم يسلم أوقاف الحرمين إلى العجم فمات بها يقال مسموما سنة بضع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb al-Madanī, brother of ʿAbd al-Wahhāb (mentioned below) and paternal uncle of al-Najm Muḥammad, the Mālikī qadi of Mecca. He became related by marriage to Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. al-Muḥibb al-Zarandī through his sister, and was a leading man in generosity and dignity. After entering Egypt and Syria on account of the agency (tawakkul) for the endowments of Medina, he travelled to Rūm and did not surrender the endowments of the two Sanctuaries to the ʿAjam; he died there, reportedly poisoned, in the year seventy-odd."@en .

rec:AIND-D04211 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04211-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04211-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04211 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر ابن الشيخ مدين الأشموني الآتي أبوه وولده محمد . مات في حياتهما نحو سنة خمسين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir, the son of al-Shaykh Madyan al-Ashmuni, whose father is mentioned below, as well as his son, Muhammad. He died during their lifetime around the year 850 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04212 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04212-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04212-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04212 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن مصطفى بن محمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن علي الزين القاهري الشافعي ويعرف بابن مصطفى . ولد في سنة اثنتين وثلاثين وثمانمائة واشتغل عند العبادي والمناوي وغيرهما وسمع على شيخنا وغيره وحصل نقائس من الكتب . وصاهر الشرف الأنصاري ثم أملق ونسب لما لا يليق بعد استنابة المناوي له في القضاء . ومات قريب الستين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Muṣṭafā b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī al-Zayn al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn Muṣṭafā. He was born in the year 832 AH and engaged in studies under al-ʿIbādī, al-Munāwī, and others. He heard (ḥadīth) from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others, and acquired precious books. He became allied by marriage to al-Sharaf al-Anṣārī, but later became impoverished and was accused of inappropriate things after al-Munāwī appointed him as a deputy judge. He died around 860 AH, presumably."@en .

rec:AIND-D04213 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04213-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04213-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04213-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04213-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04213 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن موسى بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن الصلاح المتبولي ثم القاهري الحسيني أخو الشهاب أحمد الماضي ممن يتكسب بإدارة الطاحون وبالتجارة في البز ولا بأس به ميلا في الصالحين والطلبة وحضورا لمشاهد الخير ، وهو ممن أجاز له البرهان الباعوني والنظام بن مفلح وابن زيد وآخرون ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir b. Musa b. Ahmad b. Abd al-Rahman, al-Salah al-Matbuli, then al-Qahiri, al-Husayni. He was the brother of the aforementioned al-Shihab Ahmad. He earned his living by managing a mill and trading in cloth. He was a decent man, fond of righteous people and students, and frequently attended gatherings of goodness. He received ijaza (authorization) from Burhan al-Din al-Ba'uni, al-Nizam b. Muflih, Ibn Zayd, and others."@en .

rec:AIND-D04215 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04215-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04215-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04215-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04215 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن الشيخ يحيى بن محمد بن يحيى بن أحمد بن علي المغربي المكي الشاذلي المالكي ولد في شعبان سنة أربعين بمكة وحفظ القرآن واشتغل وحصل على طريقة حسنة مات شابا بمكة في ضحى يوم الأربعاء خامس ربيع الثاني سنة إحدى وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir bin al-Shaykh Yaḥyā bin Muḥammad bin Yaḥyā bin Aḥmad bin ʿAlī al-Maghribī al-Makkī al-Shādhilī al-Mālikī. He was born in Shaʿbān, in the year 840 AH, in Mecca. He memorized the Quran, engaged in studies, and achieved a commendable state. He died as a youth in Mecca in the forenoon of Wednesday, the 5th of Rabīʿ al-Thānī, in the year 861 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04217 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04217-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04217-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04217 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن صلاح الدين الرحبي سبط قلمطاي أمه فاطمة زوجة قاسم البلقيني ، نشأ في كفالة أمه غير متصون وتراجع بعدها قليلا مع التقلل حتى مات في سنة تسع وثمانين أو التي بعدها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Ṣalāḥ al-Dīn al-Raḥabī, grandson of Qalamṭāī. His mother was Fāṭima, the wife of Qāsim al-Bulqīnī. He was raised under his mother's care in an unrestrained manner, but later reformed slightly, adopting a modest and ascetic lifestyle until he died in the year 889 AH or the following year (890 AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04218 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04218-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04218-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04218 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر بن المروبص الشامي العطار نزيل مكة ، مات بها في رمضان سنة سبعين ، أرخه ابن فهد"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir b. al-Murawbiṣ al-Shāmī al-ʿAṭṭār, a resident of Mecca. He died there in Ramadan, the year 870 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D04219 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04219-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04219-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04219 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر الزين الديمي ثم الأزهري أخذ المنهاج الأصلي وشرح جمع الجوامع للمحلي عن الكمال بن أبي شريف قراءة وسماعا بالتلفيق في سنين وأذن له في إقرائهما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir al-Zayn al-Daymi, then al-Azhari. He studied 'al-Minhaj al-Asli' and al-Mahalli's commentary on 'Jam' al-Jawami' under al-Kamal b. Abi Sharif through reading and listening alternately over several years, and was authorized by him to teach both of them."@en .

rec:AIND-D04221 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04221-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04221-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04221-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04221 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر الطباخ ويعرف بابن إبراهيم كان طباخا بالقلعة فصاهره البباوي على أخته واستقر به في نظر الدولة واستولد البباوي أخته ولده صلاح الدين محمد الذي زوجه سليمان الخازن ابنته بعد أبيه بمدة فلما مات سليمات استقر صهره مكانه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Ṭabbākh, known as Ibn Ibrāhīm. He was a cook in the Citadel (al-Qalʿa), then al-Bībāwī married his sister and established him in the office of Naẓar al-Dawla. Al-Bībāwī had a son with his sister named Ṣalāḥ al-Dīn Muḥammad, whom Sulaymān al-Khāzin married to his daughter some time after his father's death. When Sulaymān died, his son-in-law (Ṣalāḥ al-Dīn) was established in his place."@en .

rec:AIND-D04223 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04223-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04223-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04223 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر القصروي وانتمى للبدري أبي البقاء بن الجيعان وخدم جانم بلاط وسافر معه حين إمرته على الحج ولجهة الشام وإلى غير ذلك وصودر وقتا وعنده تودد وحشمة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir al-Qasrawi. He affiliated himself with al-Badri Abu al-Baqa' bin al-Ji'an and served Janim Bilat, traveling with him during his command of the Hajj pilgrimage, to the region of Syria, and elsewhere. He was subjected to confiscation of his property at one time. He possessed friendliness and decency."@en .

rec:AIND-D04224 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04224-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04224-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04224-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04224-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04224 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر المراحلي الجابي ، مات في أوائل ربيع الثاني سنة اثنتين وتسعين وكان في خدمة أبي السعادات البلقيني ثم تكلم في وقف الحلي والظاهر بعض الأيام الزينية وكان متحركا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Murāḥilī al-Jābī. He died in early Rabīʿ al-Thānī 892 AH. He was in the service of Abū al-Saʿādāt al-Bulqīnī, then managed the Waqf of al-Ḥillī and al-Ẓāhir during some of the days of al-Zaynī, and he was active."@en .

rec:AIND-D04225 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04225-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04225-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04225-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04225 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر المرخم المجذوب . ابتلى بأكلة في رجله حتى صار الدود يتناثر منها واستمر كذلك حتى مات في سابع ذي الحجة سنة تسع وستين ودفن بالمكان الذي كان منقطعا به عند جامع البكحري جوار قبر عنتر البرهاني في وسط الخراب رحمه الله . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Qadir al-Murakhkhim al-Majdhub. He was afflicted with gangrene in his leg until worms fell from it, and he remained in this state until he died on the 7th of Dhu al-Hijja, the year 869 AH. He was buried in the place where he lived in seclusion, near al-Bakahri Mosque, next to the grave of 'Antar al-Burhani in the middle of the ruins, may Allah have mercy on him. His death date was recorded by al-Munir."@en .

rec:AIND-D04226 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04226-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04226-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04226-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04226-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04226 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القادر المؤذن نزيل الصرغتمشية وأحد جماعة الإمام الكركي ونحوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Muʾadhdhin, resident of the Ṣarghatmashiyya, and one of the companions of Imam al-Karkī and his like."@en .

rec:AIND-D04227 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04227-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04227-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04227 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القاهر بن عبد الظاهر بن أحمد بن عبد الطاهر الداودي ثم التفهني ثم القاهري الشافعي الماضي أبوه . ممن اشتغل يسيرا وسمع مني وقرأ في الجوق وغيره"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Qāhir ibn ʿAbd al-Ẓāhir ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ṭāhir al-Dāwudī, then al-Tafhanī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī. His father was mentioned previously. He studied a little, heard [ḥadīth] from me (al-Sakhāwī), and recited in the jawq (recitation group) and elsewhere."@en .

rec:AIND-D04228 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04228-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04228-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04228 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد القدوس بن عبد الله بن الجيعان هو الذي حكى شيخنا في حوادث سنة ثمان وثلاثين من إنبائه أنه قطعت أصبعه لما تكرر منه من التزوير . قلت وأودع المقشرة ومع ذلك فلم ينكف حتى مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "He is the one whom our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned in his chronicle 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』 under the events of the year 838 AH, stating that his finger was cut off due to his repeated forgery. I (al-Sakhāwī) say: He was also imprisoned in the al-Maqshara prison, yet despite that, he did not cease his habits until his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04233 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04233-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04233-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04233 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكافي بن علي بن نصر النابلسي المقدسي الشافعي ويعرف بابن نصر ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Kāfī b. ʿAlī b. Naṣr al-Nābulusī al-Maqdisī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn Naṣr. He was among those who heard (hadith) from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04235 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04235-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04235-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04235 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكافي بن محمد بن أبي الفضل النفطي المدني أخو عبد السلام الماضي . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Kāfī b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Faḍl al-Nafṭī al-Madanī, the brother of the aforementioned ʿAbd al-Salām. He is among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D04236 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04236-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04236-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04236-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04236-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04236 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكافي بن محمد بن محمد بن حسين المدني السقاء الشهير بابن قطب . سمع من ابن صديق في سنة سبع وتسعين بالمسجد النبوي بعض الصحيح ومات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة ست وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Kāfī bin Muḥammad bin Muḥammad bin Ḥusayn al-Madanī al-Saqqāʾ, known as Ibn Quṭb. He heard some of al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Ṣiddīq in the year 797 AH at the Prophet's Mosque. He died in Mecca in Dhu al-Hijja in the year 846 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D04237 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04237-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04237-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04237 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكبير بن أبي السعادات بن محمود بن عادل الحسيني المدني الحنفي أخو عبد الله وعبد الرحمن وأحمد وهو أصغر الأربعة حفظ القرآن والقدوري واشتغل بالفقه وأصله والعربية والعروض وجود الخظ ونسخ به وذكر بالذكاء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd al-Kabir b. Abi al-Sa'adat b. Mahmud b. 'Adil al-Husayni al-Madani al-Hanafi. He was the brother of 'Abd Allah, 'Abd al-Rahman, and Ahmad, and was the youngest of the four brothers. He memorized the Qur'an and the legal manual of al-Quduri, and occupied himself with the study of jurisprudence, its principles, Arabic grammar, and prosody. He also mastered calligraphy and copied books with it, and was noted for his intelligence."@en .

rec:AIND-D04239 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04239-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04239-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04239-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04239 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكبير بن محمد بن أحمد العلاء أبو القسم بن الجمال الحرازي المكي الحنفي أخو أحمد وعبد الله وهو الأصغر . نشأ فحفظ القرآن والكنز وعرضه علي بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Kabīr b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, al-ʿAlāʾ Abū al-Qāsim b. al-Jamāl al-Ḥarāzī al-Makkī al-Ḥanafī, brother of Aḥmad and ʿAbd Allāh, and the youngest of them. He grew up, memorized the Qurʾān and al-Kanz, and presented it to me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04241 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04241-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04241-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04241 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن إبراهيم بن أحمد الجبرتي الماضي أبوه . ممن سمع على شيخنا أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad al-Jabartī; his father has been mentioned. He too was among those who heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04242 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04242-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04242-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04242 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن إبراهيم بن عبد الكريم بن بركة كريم الدين بن سعد الدين بن كريم الدين القبطي المصري الماضي أبوه والآتي جده قريبا ويعرف بابن كاتب جكم . مات في ربيع الأول سنة ثمان وأربعين"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Baraka, Karīm al-Dīn b. Saʿd al-Dīn b. Karīm al-Dīn al-Qibṭī al-Miṣrī; his father has been mentioned and his grandfather follows shortly. He is known as Ibn Kātib Jakam. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 848."@en .

rec:AIND-D04245 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04245-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04245-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04245 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن أحمد بن حسن بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن كريم الدين ابن الإمام الشهاب الاذرعي الأصل القاهري وأمه حبشية فتاة أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Karīm al-Dīn, son of the Imām al-Shihāb al-Adhraʿī, of Adhriʿāt origin, the Cairene. His mother was an Abyssinian slave-girl of his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D04247 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04247-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04247-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04247 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن أحمد الجزيري الرابطي . مات سنة بضع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Aḥmad al-Jazīrī al-Rābiṭī. He died in the year thirty-odd (833–839)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04248 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04248-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04248-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04248 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن أحمد الشقيري المكي أحد خدام الدرجة بعد أن كان عطارا مات في صفر سنة تسع وسبعين بهدة بني جابر وحمل لمكة فدفن بمعلاتها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Aḥmad al-Shuqayrī al-Makkī, one of the servants of the Staircase (khuddām al-daraja) after having been a druggist. He died in Ṣafar of the year 879 at Haddat Banī Jābir and was carried to Mecca, where he was buried in its Muʿallā cemetery."@en .

rec:AIND-D04249 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04249-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04249-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04249 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن إسماعيل بن محمد القدسي المصري المجلد . مات بمكة في شوال سنة اثنتين وأربعين . أرخهما ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad al-Qudsī al-Miṣrī, the bookbinder. He died in Mecca in Shawwāl of the year 842. Ibn Fahd recorded the deaths of both (this man and the preceding one)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04251 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04251-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04251-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04251 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن أبي بكر بن علي الطهطاوي المكي أخو أحمد الماضي ممن سمع مني بمكة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī al-Ṭahṭāwī al-Makkī, brother of Aḥmad (mentioned above). He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04254 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04254-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04254-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04254-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04254 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن ريحان الشيي±±± . مات في رمضان سنة خمس وخمسين . بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Rayḥān al-Shaybī. He died in Ramaḍān of the year 855, in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04255 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04255-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04255-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04255 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن أبي سعد الحجر بن عبد الكريم بن أبي سعد عبد الكريم بن أبي سعد بن علي بن قتادة الحسني المكي ويشهر بالحجر . مات بها في جمادى الأولى سنة ست وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Abī Saʿd al-Ḥajar b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Abī Saʿd ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Abī Saʿd b. ʿAlī b. Qatāda al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī, known as al-Ḥajar. He died there (in Mecca) in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 846."@en .

rec:AIND-D04256 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04256-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04256-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04256 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن أبي سعد بن محمد بن عامر الحسني من ذوي علي الشهير بالمجاش . مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة ثلاث وأربعين . أرخها ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Abī Saʿd b. Muḥammad b. ʿĀmir al-Ḥasanī, of the Dhawū ʿAlī, known as al-Mujāsh. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 843. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04257 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04257-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04257-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04257-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_apply2,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04257 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن سعدون المكي . سمع من العز بن جماعة والفخر عثمان بن أبي بكر النويري بعض النسائي ، قال الفاسي وما علمته حدث ولكنه كان يتعانى التجارة . مات سنة خمس عشرة بمكة ودفن بالمعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Saʿdūn al-Makkī. He heard part of al-Nasāʾī from al-ʿIzz b. Jamāʿa and al-Fakhr ʿUthmān b. Abī Bakr al-Nuwayrī. Al-Fāsī said: \"I do not know that he transmitted hadith, but he engaged in trade.\" He died in the year 815 in Mecca and was buried in al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D04258 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04258-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04258-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04258-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04258 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن سيف الحسني المكي . مات بها في ليلة الجمعة ثالث عشري ذي الحجة سنة ست وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Sayf al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died there (in Mecca) on the eve of Friday, the twenty-third of Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 866. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04259 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04259-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04259-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04259 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن عبد الجبار بن إبراهيم بن كرشان التبريزي ، قال ابن فهد في معجم أبيه أنه ذكر في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وثلاثين وثمانمائة أنه ابن أربع وسبعين سنة قال وله تفسير قرأت عليه منه"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAbd al-Jabbār b. Ibrāhīm b. Karshān al-Tabrīzī. Ibn Fahd (al-Najm) said in his father's Muʿjam that he stated in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 831 that he was seventy-four years old; and he (al-Taqī) said: \"He has a Tafsīr, part of which I read to him.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D04267 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04267-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04267-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04267 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن عبد الغني بن محمد بن أحمد بن عثمان البساطي الأصل القاهري المقسي حفيد العالم الشهير البساطي وأخو البدر محمد الآتي طفل مرجو أمه أمة لأبيه . ولد سنة بضع وثمانين وسمع على أبيه وكذا على المسلسل وبعض أجوبتي ثم مات بالطاعون في سنة سبع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿUthmān, of Bisāṭī origin, the Cairene, al-Maqsī, grandson of the famous scholar al-Bisāṭī and brother of al-Badr Muḥammad (mentioned below). A promising child; his mother was a slave-girl of his father. He was born in the year eighty-odd and heard from his father, and likewise from me al-Musalsal and some of my responsa. Then he died of the plague in the year 897."@en .

rec:AIND-D04268 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04268-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04268-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04268-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04268 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن عبد الغني بن يعقوب كريم الدين بن فخر الدين بن شرف الدين القاهري . أحد من ناب عن ناظر الخاص ويعرف بابن فخيرة تصغير للقب أبيه . مات في سادس رجب سنة خمسين وهو والد عبد الرزاق الماضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Yaʿqūb, Karīm al-Dīn b. Fakhr al-Dīn b. Sharaf al-Dīn al-Qāhirī, one of those who deputized for the nāẓir al-khāṣṣ; he is known as Ibn Fukhayra, a diminutive of his father's laqab. He died on the sixth of Rajab of the year 850. He is the father of ʿAbd al-Razzāq, mentioned above."@en .

rec:AIND-D04270 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04270-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04270-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04270 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن علي بن أحمد بن عبيد الله بن مسعود بن عبيد الله المكي الشهير بابن عبيد الله . مات بمكة في ذي القعدة سنة اثنتين وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿUbayd Allāh b. Masʿūd b. ʿUbayd Allāh al-Makkī, known as Ibn ʿUbayd Allāh. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year 842. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04271 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04271-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04271-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04271-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04271 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن علي بن سنان بن عبد الله بن عمر بن مسعود العمري . كان من أعيان القواد المعروفين بالعمرة توفي بمكة في آخر ذي الحجة سنة عشرين ودفن بالمعلاة وأظنه في عشر الأربعين . قاله الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAlī b. Sinān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Masʿūd al-ʿUmarī. He was one of the notable commanders (quwwād) known as al-ʿUmara. He died in Mecca at the end of Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year [8]20 and was buried in al-Muʿallā; I think he was in his forties. Al-Fāsī said so in (his history of) Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04272 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04272-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04272-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04272 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن علي بن عبد الكريم بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة أبو محمد القرشي المكي . أجاز له في سنة ثمان وثمانين وسبعمائة فما بعدها النشاوري وابن خلدون والتنوخي وابن صديق وجماعة ، ودخل بلاد الهند وغاب مدة ثم قدم مكة وما كأنه حدث ومات بها في شوال سنة أربعين . قاله ابن فهد في الظهيريين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra, Abū Muḥammad al-Qurashī al-Makkī. In the year 788 and thereafter, al-Nashāwarī, Ibn Khaldūn, al-Tanūkhī, Ibn Ṣiddīq and others granted him ijāza. He entered India and was absent for a time, then came (back) to Mecca; it does not seem that he transmitted hadith. He died there in Shawwāl of the year [8]40. Ibn Fahd said so in al-Ẓahīriyyīn."@en .

rec:AIND-D04273 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04273-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04273-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04273 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن علي بن فرج المكي القائد بها ويعرف بنعمان . مات في رجب سنة ست وأربعين بالحسبة من بلاد اليمن . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAlī b. Faraj al-Makkī, a commander (qāʾid) there, known as Nuʿmān. He died in Rajab of the year 846 at al-Ḥisba in the land of Yemen. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04274 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04274-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04274-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04274 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الكريم كريم الدين بن الخواجا شيخ علي الكرماني المكي . ولد بها سنة عشر وثمانمائة وسمع من الزين أبي بكر ابن الحسين المراغي الختم من مسلم ومن أبي داود ومن ابن حبان ومات في جمادى الآخرة سنة ستين بعدن . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm, Karīm al-Dīn b. al-Khawājā Shaykh ʿAlī al-Kirmānī al-Makkī. He was born there (in Mecca) in the year 810 and heard from al-Zayn Abū Bakr b. al-Ḥusayn al-Marāghī the concluding sessions (khatm) of Muslim, of Abū Dāwūd and of Ibn Ḥibbān. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year [8]60 in Aden. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04276 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04276-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04276-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04276 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن عمر بن محمد بن عمر نجم الدين الدمشقي أخو الخواجا شمس الدين محمد الآتي ووالد إبراهيم الماضي ويعرف بابن الزمن . كان تاجرا مشارا إليه . ومات في رجب سنة تسع وسبعين وثمانمائة عن سبع وثلاثين بدمشق بعد أن ترك أولادا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar, Najm al-Dīn al-Dimashqī, brother of al-Khawājā Shams al-Dīn Muḥammad (mentioned below) and father of Ibrāhīm (mentioned above); he is known as Ibn al-Zaman. He was a merchant of note. He died in Rajab of the year 879 at the age of thirty-seven in Damascus, having left children."@en .

rec:AIND-D04278 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04278-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04278-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04278 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن قاسم بن عبد المعطي كريم الدين الأنصاري أخو عبد المعطي . جرده ابن فهد في ذيله وكتبته تخمينا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Qāsim b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī, Karīm al-Dīn al-Anṣārī, brother of ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī. Ibn Fahd listed him bare (without details) in his Dhayl, and I have entered him here conjecturally."@en .

rec:AIND-D04279 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04279-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04279-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04279 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن محمد بن إبراهيم الدمشقي الشهير بالصواف . ممن تردد لمكة وسكنها وعمر بها بعض الدور وكان يسافر منها إلى الهند في التجارة . مات سنة سبع وخمسين ببلاد كالكوط من الهند . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm al-Dimashqī, known as al-Ṣawwāf. He was among those who frequented Mecca, settled there and built some houses there, and he used to travel from there to India for trade. He died in the year [8]57 in the land of Calicut in India. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04283 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04283-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04283-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04283-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04283 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن محمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن موسى الدميري المكي العطار أحد الخيار ممن فيه رقة وخير . مات بمكة في سلخ شعبان سنة ست وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد وأعاده في ابن محمد بن محمد بن موسى بن عيسى بن عبد الله والصواب أن جده محمد بن عبد الله بن موسى بن عيسى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā al-Damīrī al-Makkī, the druggist, one of the good men, possessed of gentleness and goodness. He died in Mecca at the end of Shaʿbān of the year 876. Ibn Fahd recorded his death and repeated him under \"son of Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. ʿĪsā b. ʿAbd Allāh\", but the correct form is that his grandfather was Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Mūsā b. ʿĪsā."@en .

rec:AIND-D04285 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04285-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04285-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04285-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04285 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن محمد بن علي بن أبي بكر بن علي بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله ابن عمر بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله أبو القسم الناشري اليماني . بيض له العفيف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh, Abū al-Qāsim al-Nāshirī al-Yamanī. Al-ʿAfīf (al-Nāshirī) left his entry blank."@en .

rec:AIND-D04286 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04286-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04286-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04286 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن محمد بن علي بن محمد بن جوشن المكي التاجر المتردد فيها لليمن . مات بمكة وقد خلف دورا ونخيلا . جرده ابن فهد في ذيله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Jawshan al-Makkī, the merchant who used to travel from there to Yemen. He died in Mecca, having left houses and palm trees. Ibn Fahd listed him bare in his Dhayl."@en .

rec:AIND-D04288 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04288-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04288-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04288 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن محمد بن عوض الجدي أحد التجار المتمولين ممن له عقار ووصفه ابن عزم بكريم الدين زعيم جدة سنة ثمان وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد وقال أنه أنشأ بمنى في سنة سبع وأربعين سبيلا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAwaḍ al-Juddī, one of the wealthy merchants who owned real estate. Ibn ʿAzm described him, in the year 858, as Karīm al-Dīn, the chief (zaʿīm) of Jidda. Ibn Fahd recorded his death and said that he built a public fountain (sabīl) at Minā in the year 847."@en .

rec:AIND-D04293 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04293-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04293-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04293-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04293 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن محمد تقي الدين النووي الشافعي . قال شيخنا في أنبائه اشتغل قديما ثم ترك وأقبل على السعي في القضاء بالبلاد فولي نوا ثم باشر قضاء أذرعات مدة ولم يكن مرضيا وكان جوادا بالقرى . مات في رجب سنة خمس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad, Taqī al-Dīn al-Nawawī al-Shāfiʿī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Inbāʾ: he studied in early life, then abandoned it and devoted himself to seeking judgeships in the provinces; he was appointed over Nawā, then held the judgeship of Adhriʿāt for a time, and he was not satisfactory, though he was generous in hospitality. He died in Rajab of the year [80]5."@en .

rec:AIND-D04294 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04294-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04294-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04294-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04294 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم بن محمد بن فرو شيخ الأميرية ومستأجر منية خلفا وقف الصرغتمشية . مات في حياة أبيه في رمضان سنة خمس وتسعين وكان ألين من أبيه وأشبه عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad b. Farw, shaykh of al-Amīriyya and lessee of Minyat Khalaf, the waqf of al-Ṣarghatmashiyya. He died during his father's lifetime in Ramaḍān of the year [8]95; he was gentler and better than his father. May God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04295 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04295-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04295-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04295-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04295 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم الملقب جاني بك بن ميلب المكي الصانع بجدة . مات شبه الفجأة من نزلة نزلت في عنقه منعته الأكل والشرب في ليلة السبت رابع عشر رمضان سنة وتسعين بجدة وحمل لمكة فصلى عليه ثم دفن على والدته بتربة بني فهد من المعلاة ، وكان بارا بوالديه واخوته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm, called Jānī Bak, b. Maylab al-Makkī, the craftsman at Jidda. He died almost suddenly, from a catarrh that descended into his neck and prevented him from eating and drinking, on the eve of Saturday the fourteenth of Ramaḍān of the year [8]90, at Jidda; he was carried to Mecca, prayed over, and buried over his mother in the tomb of the Banū Fahd in al-Muʿallā. He was dutiful to his parents and his brothers."@en .

rec:AIND-D04296 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04296-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04296-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04296-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04296 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم كريم الدين بن فخيرة بفاء ثم معجمة وراء ثم هاء مصغر . والد عبد الرزاق الماضي وأحد الكتبة من الأقباط بل مستوفي الخاص . مات في رجب سنة خمس وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm, Karīm al-Dīn Ibn Fukhayra (with fāʾ, then khāʾ, rāʾ and hāʾ, in the diminutive), father of ʿAbd al-Razzāq mentioned above, one of the Coptic clerks — indeed the mustawfī of the khāṣṣ. He died in Rajab of the year 855."@en .

rec:AIND-D04297 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04297-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04297-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04297 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم السليماني الشريف ، مات في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وثمانين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Sulaymānī, the sharīf. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 882 in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04298 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04298-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04298-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04298 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الكريم القسطلاني الأصل المصري الخطيب ابن الخطيب من بيت كبير : مات في سنة أربع وخمسين . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Karīm, of Qasṭallānī origin, the Egyptian, the preacher (khaṭīb), son of a preacher, from a great house. He died in the year 854. Al-Munīr recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04299 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04299-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04299-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04299-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04299 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن إبراهيم بن حسين بن محمد الزين الجبرتي الجواتري الطواشي أحد خدام الحرم النبوي ، ممن سمع مني بالمدينة . ومات بها سنة احدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Ibrāhīm b. Ḥusayn b. Muḥammad, al-Zayn al-Jabartī al-Jawātirī al-Ṭawāshī, one of the servants (eunuchs) of the Prophet's Sanctuary. He was among those who heard from me in Medina, and he died there in the year 891."@en .

rec:AIND-D04300 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04300-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04300-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04300-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04300 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن إبراهيم بن عمر بن حلفا الكمال المصري . مات في صفر سنة خمسين بجدة وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بمعلاتها . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿUmar b. Ḥalfā, al-Kamāl al-Miṣrī. He died in Ṣafar of the year 850 at Jidda and was carried to Mecca, where he was buried in its Muʿallā cemetery. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04302 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04302-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04302-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04302 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن أحمد بن جار الله بن زائد السنبسي المكي . والد عبد العزيز الماضي . قرأ على الزين بن أبي بكر المراغي المسلسل والختم من الصحيحين . ممن سافر في التجارة لبلاد كالهند واليمن . ومات في شوال سنة أربع وستين بفوقة من أعمال كنباية من الهند ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Aḥmad b. Jār Allāh b. Zāʾid al-Sunbusī al-Makkī, father of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz mentioned above. He read to al-Zayn b. Abī Bakr al-Marāghī al-Musalsal and the concluding sessions of the two Ṣaḥīḥs. He was among those who travelled for trade to lands such as India and Yemen. He died in Shawwāl of the year 864 at Fūqa, in the district of Cambay (Kanbāya) in India."@en .

rec:AIND-D04304 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04304-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04304-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04304 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن أحمد بن عبد اللطيف بن أبي بكر الشرجي اليماني الماضي أبوه والآتي جده . مات في سنة ثمان وعشرين أو قريبا منها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Abī Bakr al-Sharjī al-Yamanī; his father has been mentioned and his grandfather will follow. He died in the year 828 or thereabouts."@en .

rec:AIND-D04306 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04306-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04306-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04306 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن أحمد بن علي اليافعي العراقي الأصل العدني اليماني والد عبد الله الآتي . مات بعدن سنة أربع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Yāfiʿī, of Iraqi origin, of Aden, the Yemeni, father of ʿAbd Allāh (mentioned below). He died in Aden in the year [80]4."@en .

rec:AIND-D04308 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04308-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04308-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04308 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن أحمد بن فضل الله بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله النمراوي ثم القاهري الأزهري السعودي أخو علي الآتي . كان خيرا يتكلم في جباية ونحوها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Aḥmad b. Faḍl Allāh b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Nimrāwī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Azharī al-Saʿūdī, brother of ʿAlī (mentioned below). He was a good man who dealt with tax-collecting and the like."@en .

rec:AIND-D04317 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04317-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04317-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04317 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن شمس ، مات في شعبان سنة ست وأربعين بمكة أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Shams. He died in Shaʿbān of the year 846 in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04320 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04320-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04320-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04320 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن عبد العزيز بن أمين الدين بن فرشتا الحنفي ، وفرشتا هو الملك وكذا كان يكتب بخطه المعروف بابن الملك . متأخر لم أقف له على ترجمة وله تصانيف منها شرح المشارق للصغاني وشرح المجمع والمنار والوقاية ، وكتبته هنا بالحدس فالله أعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Amīn al-Dīn b. Firishtā al-Ḥanafī — Firishtā means \"the angel\" (al-malak), and so he used to write in his own hand, being known as Ibn al-Malak. A later figure; I have found no biography of him, but he has works, among them a commentary on al-Ṣaghānī's Mashāriq and commentaries on al-Majmaʿ, al-Manār and al-Wiqāya. I have entered him here by conjecture; God knows best."@en .

rec:AIND-D04323 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04323-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04323-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04323 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن عبد القادر بن علي بن زايد المكي أخو أبي سعد الآتي ممن سمع مني بمكة وحفظ القرآن وكتبا عرضها وزار المدينة وهو مبارك . )"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī b. Zāyid al-Makkī, brother of Abū Saʿd (mentioned below). He was among those who heard from me in Mecca; he memorized the Qurʾān and books which he recited (for examination), and visited Medina. He is a blessed man."@en .

rec:AIND-D04324 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04324-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04324-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04324 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن عبد القادر بن الموفق بن المحيوي الشارعي القاهري الحنفي الصوفي أحد مشايخ الزوايا بالقرافتين ، ويعرف بابن عثمان ، ولد سنة ثلاث وتسعين وسبعمائة ، ومات في جمادى الأولى سنة ثمان وستين ، أرخه ابن المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. al-Muwaffaq b. al-Muḥyawī al-Shāriʿī al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī al-Ṣūfī, one of the shaykhs of the zāwiyas in the two Qarāfas, known as Ibn ʿUthmān. He was born in the year 793 and died in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 868. Ibn al-Munīr recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04325 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04325-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04325-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04325 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن العفيف عبد الله بن إسماعيل المدني ، مات شابا بمكة في شعبان سنة أربع وسبعين ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. al-ʿAfīf ʿAbd Allāh b. Ismāʿīl al-Madanī. He died young in Mecca in Shaʿbān of the year 874. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04328 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04328-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04328-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04328 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن عبد الوهاب بن عفيف بن وهيبة بن يوحنا تقي الدين الملكي الأسلمي الحكيم ابن أخي الشمس أبي البركات بن عفيف الذي وسطه الأشرف برسباي قبيل موته وأحد رؤساء الطب والكحل ويلقب قوالح ، مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿAfīf b. Wuhayba b. Yūḥannā, Taqī al-Dīn al-Malakī al-Aslamī, the physician; nephew of al-Shams Abū al-Barakāt b. ʿAfīf, whom al-Ashraf Barsbāy had cut in two shortly before his (Barsbāy's) death; one of the heads of medicine and ophthalmology, nicknamed Qawāliḥ. He died (no date given)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04329 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04329-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04329-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04329 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن عبيد الله بن عوض بن محمد الأردبيلي الشرواتي القاهري الحنفي أخو البدر محمد وإخوته ، ويعرف بابن عبيد الله . حفظ الكنز والمنار وعمدة النسفي والحاجبية ودرس . مات سنة أربع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿAwaḍ b. Muḥammad al-Ardabīlī al-Shirwātī al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī, brother of al-Badr Muḥammad and his brothers, known as Ibn ʿUbayd Allāh. He memorized al-Kanz, al-Manār, the ʿUmda of al-Nasafī and al-Ḥājibiyya, and taught. He died in the year 854."@en .

rec:AIND-D04334 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04334-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04334-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04334-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04334 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن علي المحلي البلتاجي الأحمدي الشافعي أخذ عن أبيه وحج وجاور سنة أربع وثمانمائة ، وسمع من إبراهيم الزهراني شيئا من مناقب سيدي أحمد ، وكان يحفظ كثيرا من مناقبه وأحواله أخذ عنه ابن المنير ، وقال انه مات بعد سنة إحدى وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. ʿAlī al-Maḥallī al-Baltājī al-Aḥmadī al-Shāfiʿī. He studied under his father, performed the pilgrimage and sojourned (in Mecca) in the year 804, and heard from Ibrāhīm al-Zahrānī something of the Manāqib of Sīdī Aḥmad (al-Badawī); he used to memorize much of his manāqib and his states. Ibn al-Munīr studied under him and said that he died after the year 831."@en .

rec:AIND-D04336 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04336-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04336-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04336 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن أحمد بن إسماعيل بن داود البدر بن الشمس بن الشهاب القاهري أخو عبد الله الآتي ويعرف بابن الرومي ، ممن باشر النقابة عند البدر بن التنسي قاضي المالكية وكان متميزا في الصناعة ضعيف الخط حسبما رأيته في أسجال عدالته خالي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl b. Dāwūd, al-Badr b. al-Shams b. al-Shihāb al-Qāhirī, brother of ʿAbd Allāh (mentioned below), known as Ibn al-Rūmī. He was among those who exercised the office of naqīb under al-Badr Ibn al-Tanasī, the Mālikī judge; he was distinguished in the craft (of the notary), though of weak handwriting, as I saw in the registers of his attestation. He is my maternal uncle."@en .

rec:AIND-D04341 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04341-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04341-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04341 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف أخ للذي قبله أكبر منه ، مات في ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf, brother of the preceding, older than him. He died in ..."@en .

rec:AIND-D04342 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04342-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04342-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04342 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن أحمد . يأتي فيمن جده عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad. [His entry] follows among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D04343 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04343-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04343-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04343 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن الحسين الزين ابن أبي الفضل بن الزين بن ناصر الدين أبي الفتوح بن الزين المراغي الأصل المدني الشافعي . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. al-Ḥusayn, al-Zayn Ibn Abī al-Faḍl b. al-Zayn b. Nāṣir al-Dīn Abī al-Futūḥ b. al-Zayn, of Marāghī origin, the Medinan, the Shāfiʿī. He was among those who heard from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D04345 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04345-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04345-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04345 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن شاه رخ بن تيمورلنك . قتل والده واستقر عوضه فعاجله عمه قبل تمام شهر وقتله وذلك في سنة أربع وخمسين كما أشرت له في أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. Shāh Rukh b. Tīmūrlank. He killed his father and took his place, but his uncle forestalled him before a month was complete and killed him; that was in the year 854, as I indicated in (the entry of) his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D04348 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04348-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04348-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04348 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن الولد سراج الدين بن القطب أبي الخير الحسني الفاسي المكي المالكي الآتي أبوه وعمه ، عرض على الأربعين النووية والجرومية في سنة سبع وثمانين ثم المختصر للشيخ خليل في سنة سبع وتسعين وكتبت له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the boy Sirāj al-Dīn b. al-Quṭb Abī al-Khayr al-Ḥasanī al-Fāsī al-Makkī al-Mālikī; his father and his uncle follow. He presented to me al-Arbaʿīn al-Nawawiyya and al-Ājurrūmiyya in the year 887, then the Mukhtaṣar of Shaykh Khalīl in the year 897, and I wrote (an ijāza) for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04350 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04350-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04350-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04350 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن عبد اللطيف اليماني المحالبي ، ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Yamanī al-Maḥālibī. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04360 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04360-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04360-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04360 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن يوسف الأسيوطي القاهري البزاز أخو علي والد أهلي الآتي . مات بعد أن افتقر جدا عدي عليه بالقرب من انبابة في سنة ثلاث وسبعين ودفن بالوراق رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf al-Usyūṭī al-Qāhirī, the cloth merchant, brother of ʿAlī, the father of my wife (mentioned below). He died — after having become very poor — assaulted near Inbāba, in the year 873, and was buried at al-Warrāq. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04361 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04361-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04361-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04361 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن منقورة أحد الكتبة من الأقباط وعم عبد الباسط ابن يعقوب الماضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Manqūra, one of the Coptic clerks, and paternal uncle of ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ b. Yaʿqūb, mentioned above."@en .

rec:AIND-D04362 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04362-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04362-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04362 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن موسى بن أحمد بن علي بن عجيل اليماني أخو أحمد الماضي ويعرف بالمشرع أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Mūsā b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿUjayl al-Yamanī, brother of Aḥmad (mentioned above); he is also known as al-Musharraʿ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04364 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04364-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04364-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04364 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن موسى الكجراتي ، له ذكر في عمر بن أحمد بن محمد ابن محمد البطايني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Mūsā al-Kujarātī (of Gujarat). He is mentioned in the entry of ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Baṭāʾinī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04366 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04366-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04366-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04366 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف بن هبة الله بن محمد ظهير الدين بن أرشد الدين بن نور الدين البكري الكتكي الشيرازي نزيل مكة ، قال الطاووسي قرأت عليه قبل الثمانمائة القرآن ومقدمات العلوم وأجاز لي وانتقل من شيراز إلى مكة فجاور بها حتى مات سنة ثلاثين وعظمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Hibat Allāh b. Muḥammad, Ẓahīr al-Dīn b. Arshad al-Dīn b. Nūr al-Dīn al-Bakrī al-Katakī al-Shīrāzī, resident of Mecca. Al-Ṭāwūsī said: \"I read to him the Qurʾān and the introductory texts of the sciences before the year 800, and he granted me ijāza.\" He moved from Shīrāz to Mecca and sojourned there until he died in the year [8]30; and he (al-Ṭāwūsī) held him in high esteem."@en .

rec:AIND-D04369 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04369-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04369-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04369 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف الرومي الاينالي الطواشي . مات في صفر سنة أربع وخمسين عن نحو المائة وورثه حفيدا معتقه أحمد ومحمد ابنا أمير علي بن إينال ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Rūmī al-Īnālī, the eunuch. He died in Ṣafar of the year 854 at about a hundred years of age, and his manumitter's two grandsons, Aḥmad and Muḥammad, the sons of Amīr ʿAlī b. Īnāl, inherited from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04370 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04370-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04370-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04370 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف الشامي العطار بمكة . مات بها في صفر وتسعين وكان يوجد عنده من الأعشاب والعطر ما ينفرد به ولذا يجتهد في التغالي في بيعها بغلظة ويبس عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Shāmī, the druggist at Mecca. He died there in Ṣafar of the year [8]90. He used to have herbs and perfumes such as no one else had, and so he strove to overcharge in selling them, with roughness and dryness. May God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04371 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04371-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04371-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04371-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04371 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف القجاجقي الأشرف برسباي أحد الخواص من السقاة دام كذلك إلى أن أبطله الظاهر جقمق في أوائل أيامه واستمر حتى مات في ثامن ذي الحجة سنة أربع وخمسين وكان مذكورا بالكرم ومحبة أهل العلم والفضل وهو صاحب الجامع المشرف على بركة الفهادة بالقرب من حدرة الكماجيين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Qajājiqī (mamlūk of) al-Ashraf Barsbāy, one of the elite cupbearers. He remained so until al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq removed him at the beginning of his reign, and he lived on until he died on the eighth of Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 854. He was noted for generosity and love of the people of learning and virtue, and he is the founder of the mosque overlooking Birkat al-Fahhāda near Ḥadrat al-Kamājiyyīn. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04372 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04372-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04372-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04372 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف الناصري الساقي ، مات سنة سبع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Nāṣirī, the cupbearer. He died in the year [80]7."@en .

rec:AIND-D04373 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04373-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04373-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04373 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد اللطيف النشيلي القاهري الأزهري الشافعي صهر الزين زكريا ، مات في شعبان سنة سبع وسبعين وكان لا بأس به . | انتهى الجزء الرابع ، ويليه الجزء الخامس وأوله : عبد الله | بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم || من اسمه عبد الله"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Nashīlī al-Qāhirī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī, a relative by marriage of al-Zayn Zakariyā. He died in Shaʿbān of the year 877; he was not bad."@en .

rec:AIND-D04374 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04374-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04374-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04374 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الله العفيف بن البرهان المغربي الأصل المكي الدهان الماضي أبوه ويعرف بالزعبلي . سمع من أبي بكر المراغي أشياء وكان كأبيه مباركا منجمعا عن الناس ملازما للجماعة مع بعد منزله ويتكسب بدهن السقوف ونحوها وبالعمر أيام الموسم . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة خمس وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-ʿAfīf b. al-Burhān, of Maghribī origin, the Meccan, the painter; his father has been mentioned, and he is known as al-Zaʿbalī. He heard some things from Abū Bakr al-Marāghī. Like his father he was a blessed man, withdrawn from people, constant in attending congregational prayer despite the distance of his house, earning his living by painting ceilings and the like, and by (guiding) ʿumras in the pilgrimage season. He died in Mecca in Muḥarram of the year 885."@en .

rec:AIND-D04375 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04375-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04375-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04375 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن إبراهيم بن الجلال أحمد بن محمد الخجندي المدني الحنفي . ولد بالمدينة النبوية ونشأ بها واشتغل على أبيه وشارك في الفضيلة وجود الخط عند أبيه والسيد على شيخ باسطية المدينة وكتب به أشياء ودخل القاهرة فأقام بها وباسكندرية مدة وقدرت وفاته بها مطعونا سنة ثلاث وستين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Ibrāhīm b. al-Jalāl Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Khujandī al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī. He was born in Medina and grew up there, studied under his father and shared in learning, perfected his handwriting under his father and under al-Sayyid ʿAlī, shaykh of the Bāsiṭiyya of Medina, and copied many things in it. He entered Cairo and stayed there, and in Alexandria for a time; his death there, of the plague, I estimate in the year 863. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04382 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04382-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04382-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04382 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن إبراهيم الغماري . سمع الميدومي وحدث عنه وممن سمع عليه خديجة ابنة أحمد بن سليمان بن البرهان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Ibrāhīm al-Ghumārī. He heard from al-Maydūmī and transmitted from him; among those who heard from him was Khadīja bt. Aḥmad b. Sulaymān b. al-Burhān."@en .

rec:AIND-D04383 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04383-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04383-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04383 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن عيسى بن مطير الحكمي اليماني الشافعي الماضي أبوه . كان فقيها صالحا سليم الصدر درس وأفتى وأشير إليه بعد أبيه من بين أخوته ومات في جمادى الأولى سنة خمس عشرة عن نحو خمس وأربعين . قاله الأهدل"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā b. Muṭayr al-Ḥakamī al-Yamanī al-Shāfiʿī; his father has been mentioned. He was a righteous jurist, of sound heart; he taught and gave fatwās, and after his father he was the one pointed to among his brothers. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 815 at about forty-five. So said al-Ahdal."@en .

rec:AIND-D04384 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04384-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04384-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04384 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن أحمد البكري . كتب على استدعاء بعد الخمسين وقال أن مولده سنة اثنتين وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Aḥmad al-Bakrī. He wrote on a request for ijāza (istidʿāʾ) after the year [8]50 and stated that his birth was in the year 802."@en .

rec:AIND-D04390 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04390-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04390-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04390 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن الجمال المصري المكي أخو عبد الرحمن الماضي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Jamāl al-Miṣrī al-Makkī, brother of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān (mentioned above). He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04392 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04392-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04392-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04392 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن يوسف أنصاري الزرندي المدني أخو محمد الآتي . سمع على الزين المراغي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf, Anṣārī, al-Zarandī al-Madanī, brother of Muḥammad (mentioned below). He heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04393 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04393-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04393-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04393 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن اللخمي التونسي الفرياني المالكي قريب محمد بن حمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن الآتي . ذكره شيخنا في مشتبه النسبة وقال أخذ عن بعض أصحابنا ، ومات سنة اثني عشرة راجعا من الحج ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Lakhmī al-Tūnisī al-Firyānī al-Mālikī, a relative of Muḥammad b. Ḥamad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān (mentioned below). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in Mushtabih al-nisba and said that he studied under some of our companions. He died in the year 812 while returning from the pilgrimage."@en .

rec:AIND-D04394 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04394-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04394-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04394-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04394-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87_apply2,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04394 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أبي العباس أحمد بن عبد الله بن يحيى التونسي المرجاني . سمع من العز بن جماعة والفخر النويري والكمال بن حبيب وأخذ عنه التقي بن فهد وقال أنه كان رجلا صالحا خيرا دينا ، ولم يزد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Yaḥyā al-Tūnisī al-Marjānī. He heard from al-ʿIzz b. Jamāʿa, al-Fakhr al-Nuwayrī and al-Kamāl b. Ḥabīb; al-Taqī b. Fahd studied under him and said that he was a righteous, good and religious man, and added no more."@en .

rec:AIND-D04395 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04395-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04395-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04395 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن عبد الله الجمال النحريري المالكي قاضي حلب وابن قاضيها . يأتي فيمن لم يسم أبوه فأظن أنه ابن أحمد بن عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Jamāl al-Naḥrīrī al-Mālikī, qadi of Aleppo and son of its qadi. [His entry] follows among those whose father is not named; I think he is the son of Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D04396 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04396-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04396-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04396-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04396 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن عبد الله الجمال الهريبطي ثم القاهري الصحراوي . سمع مني في المجاورة الثانية كثيرا وحج معي في سنة إحدى وسبعين وكان خيرا يتلو القرآن ، ومات قريب الثمانين أو بعدها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Jamāl al-Huraybiṭī, then al-Qāhirī al-Ṣaḥrāwī. He heard a great deal from me (al-Sakhāwī) during my second stay (mujāwara) in Mecca and performed the pilgrimage with me in the year [8]71. He was a good man who recited the Qurʾān, and he died around the year [8]80 or after it."@en .

rec:AIND-D04397 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04397-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04397-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04397 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن عبد الله الغزي الخطيب بها . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ghazzī, the khaṭīb (preacher) there (in Gaza). He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04399 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04399-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04399-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04399 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن علي بن عيسى بن محمد بن عيسى . مضى في ابن أحمد بن أبي الحسن قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿĪsā b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā. [His entry] has already appeared shortly above under \"the son of Aḥmad b. Abī al-Ḥasan\"."@en .

rec:AIND-D04413 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04413-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04413-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04413 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن محمد السروي ثم السفطي الشافعي أحد جماعة الغمري . إنسان خير اشتغل وشارك وقرأ على الكثير من البخاري ونعم الرجل وهو في الأحياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Sarawī, then al-Safṭī, al-Shāfiʿī. One of the group (jamāʿa) of al-Ghamrī. A good man who studied, took part (in scholarly exchange), and read to me (al-Sakhāwī) a great deal of al-Bukhārī. An excellent man; he is still among the living."@en .

rec:AIND-D04414 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04414-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04414-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04414 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن محمد الشبروملسي . ممن سمع مني قريب التسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Shabramallisī. Among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me around the year ninety [890 AH]."@en .

rec:AIND-D04415 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04415-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04415-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04415-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04415-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04415 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن محمد المراكشي الأصل الخليلي شيخ زاوية عمر المجود بها . ممن اشتغل شافعيا في التنبيه وقرأ على البرهان الأنصاري ولكنه أقبل على طريق المتصوفة مع خيره وخير أبيه . مات في شوال سنة خمس وتسعين ببلد الخليل وقد جاز الستين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd Allah b. Ahmad b. Muhammad, of Marrakesh origin, al-Khalili. He was the shaykh of the Zawiyah of Umar and its Quranic reciter (mujawwid). He studied as a Shafi'i, engaging with 『al-Tanbih』, and read under al-Burhan al-Ansari, but later turned to the path of the Sufis, along with his own piety and that of his father. He died in Shawwal in the year 895 AH in the town of al-Khalil (Hebron), having passed the age of sixty. May Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04416 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04416-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04416-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04416-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04416-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04416-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D04416-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04416 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد بن موسى بن إبراهيم الجمال أبو الفضل بن الشهاب الحلبي الأصل القاهري الحنفي أخو عبد الرحيم الماضي وشريكه في شيوخه هناك ويعرف بالحلبي . أجاز لي ومات في شعبان سنة إحدى وخمسين عن نحو الستين وكان يتصرف بالرسلية في الصالحية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. Ibrāhīm, al-Jamāl Abū al-Faḍl b. al-Shihāb. He was of Aleppo origin, Cairo-based, and of the Hanafi school. He was the brother of the aforementioned ʿAbd al-Raḥīm, and his companion in studying under his teachers there, and was known as al-Ḥalabī. He granted me (al-Sakhāwī) an ijāza. He died in Shaʿbān, the year 851 AH, at around sixty years of age. He used to serve as an envoy (al-rusuliyya) at al-Ṣāliḥiyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D04417 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04417-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04417-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04417-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04417-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04417 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد الجمال بن الشهاب القسطلاني المصري خطيب جامعها العمروي هو وأبوه نحو خمسين سنة . مات في العشر الأخير من رمضان سنة خمس وقد زاد على السبعين بعد ما اختلط واستقر بعده في الخطابة التقى المقريزي وهو الذي أرخه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abd Allah b. Ahmad al-Jamal b. al-Shihab al-Qastallani al-Misri. The Khatib (preacher) of the Amr Mosque of Egypt (Fustat), a post which he and his father held for about fifty years. He died in the last ten days of Ramadan in the year 805 AH, having lived past seventy years of age, and after suffering from cognitive decline (senility). Al-Taqi al-Maqrizi succeeded him in the sermon-giving post, and he is the one who recorded his date of death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04418 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04418-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04418-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b85_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04418 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد عفيف الدين أبو محمد الحضرمي . مضى فيمن جده على ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad ʿAfīf al-Dīn Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥaḍramī. He was already mentioned under the section of those whose grandfather's name is ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04420 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04420-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04420-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04420-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04420-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04420-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D04420-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86_review_1,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_verify_B86 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04420 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أحمد الفرنوي الأصل المكي الشهير بالأقصرائي لخدمته لأمين الدين . مات في شعبان سنة ثمانين بالقاهرة وكان يكثر التردد إليها وإلى غيرها شديد السعي والتحصيل والمداخلة للناس سيما بني الدنيا وكان يقصدني كثيرا رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad, of Farnawī origin, al-Makkī, well known as al-Aqṣarāʾī because of his service to Amīn al-Dīn. He died in Shaʿbān of the year eighty [880 AH] in Cairo. He used to travel frequently to Cairo and elsewhere, being most energetic in striving and acquiring, and closely mixing with people, especially the worldly elite. He used to come to me often. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04421 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04421-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04421-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04421-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04421-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04421-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D04421-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86_review_1,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_ruling,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg,
        agent:claude_verify_B86 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04421 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن إسماعيل . لعله إبراهيم الشيرازي ثم المدني نزيل مكة ويعرف بالعفيف المدني . ولد بها ونشأ فسمع بها من ابن صديق في سنة سبع وتسعين وسبعمائة بعض البخارى ودخل هرموز بل العجم وكان مثريا ذا دور . ومات بمكة في شوال سنة ثلاث وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Ismāʿīl — perhaps [his grandfather was] Ibrāhīm — al-Shīrāzī, then al-Madanī, a resident of Mecca, known as al-ʿAfīf al-Madanī. He was born and raised there [in Medina], where he heard part of al-Bukhārī [i.e. the Ṣaḥīḥ] from Ibn Ṣiddīq in the year 797 AH. He entered Hurmuz, indeed Persia (al-ʿAjam), and was wealthy, owning many houses. He died in Mecca in Shawwāl of the year fifty-three [853 AH]. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04424 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04424-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04424-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04424-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86_review_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_ruling ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04424 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن إسماعيل العفيف المدني . مضى فيمن جده إبراهيم قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Ismāʿīl al-ʿAfīf al-Madanī. He has already been mentioned, shortly before, among those whose grandfather is Ibrāhīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D04425 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04425-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04425-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86_review_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04425 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن الطنبغا الأحمدي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Ṭunbughā al-Aḥmadī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04426 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04426-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04426-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86_review_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04426 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أبي بكر بن إبراهيم النمراوي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr b. Ibrāhīm al-Nimrāwī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04428 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04428-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04428-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04428-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04428-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86_review_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg,
        agent:claude_verify_B86 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04428 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أبي بكر بن خلد بن موسى بن زهرة بالفتح الحمصي الحنبلي ابن عم عبد الرحمن بن محمد الماضي . ولد تقريبا سنة أربع وثمانين وسبعمائة بحمص وسمع بها من إبراهيم بن فرعون قطعة من آخر الصحيح وحدث بها قرأها عليه النجم بن فهد . مات قبل دخولي حمص إما بقليل أو كثير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr b. Khalad b. Mūsā b. Zahra (with fatḥa), al-Ḥimṣī al-Ḥanbalī. He was the paternal cousin of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad, mentioned earlier. He was born approximately in the year 784 AH at Ḥimṣ, and heard there from Ibrāhīm b. Firʿawn a portion from the end of the Ṣaḥīḥ, which he then transmitted; al-Najm b. Fahd read it back to him. He died before my entry into Ḥimṣ, whether shortly or long before."@en .

rec:AIND-D04435 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04435-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04435-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04435-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04435-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04435-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D04435-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86_review_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_Bgroup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b,
        agent:claude_verify_B86 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04435 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أبي بكر بن يحيى الزوقري اليماني الشافعي أحد الفضلاء من أهل تعز . أفتى ودرس بالمظفرية وكان مشكور السيرة . مات سنة عشر . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr b. Yaḥyā al-Zawqarī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī. One of the excellent men among the people of Taʿizz. He issued fatwas and taught at al-Muẓaffariyya, and was of praiseworthy conduct. He died in the year ten [810 AH]. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ [al-Ghumr]."@en .

rec:AIND-D04437 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04437-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04437-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04437-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04437-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04437-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D04437-resp-6,
        rec:AIND-D04437-resp-7 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86_review_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_Bgroup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_ruling,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b,
        agent:claude_verify_B86 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04437 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن حجاج بن أحمد بن موسى البرماوي القاهري المكتب والد البدر محمد الآتي ويعرف بابن حجاج وكتب فيما قيل على الوسيمي وغيره وبرع وتصدى لتعليمها وكتب درجا قرضه له شيخنا وغيره ، وتنزل في الجهات وكان فيما بلغني فقيرا . مات قريب الخمسين ورأيت شهادة أبيه على الفخر البلبيسي إمام الأزهر سنة ست وثمانين وسبعمائة ووصفه بشيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥajjāj b. Aḥmad b. Mūsā al-Birmāwī al-Qāhirī, the writing-master (al-muktib), father of al-Badr Muḥammad, mentioned below, and known as Ibn Ḥajjāj. He wrote, so it is said, under al-Wasīmī and others, excelled at it, and devoted himself to teaching it. He wrote a scroll (darj) for which our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others wrote commendations (taqrīẓ). He was given stipendiary posts in the [administrative] departments (al-jihāt) but, according to what reached me, he was poor. He died around the year fifty [850 AH]. I also saw a testimony of his father concerning al-Fakhr al-Bilbīsī, imam of al-Azhar, dated 786 AH, in which he described him as \"our shaykh\"."@en .

rec:AIND-D04443 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04443-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04443-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86_review_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04443 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن خليل القلعي . مضى قريبا فيمن جده فرج بن سعيد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Khalīl al-Qalʿī. He has already been mentioned, shortly before, among those whose grandfather is Faraj b. Saʿīd."@en .

rec:AIND-D04444 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04444-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04444-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04444-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04444-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D04444-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D04444-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86_review_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg,
        agent:claude_opus_5_personalia_b,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit,
        agent:claude_verify_B86 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04444 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن سالم بن سليمان بن عمر الجمال بن البصروي ثم الدمشقي . ولد سنة ست وأربعين وسبعمائة وسلك طريق الفقراء وأحضر على بعض الشيوخ ثم سمع بنفسه وتجرد ثم تزوج وتنزل في المدارس . مات في شعبان سنة ثلاث . قاله شيخنا في إنبائه"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Sālim b. Sulaymān b. ʿUmar, al-Jamāl b. al-Baṣrawī, then al-Dimashqī. He was born in the year 746 AH and followed the path of the Sufi poor. He was brought as a child to the sessions of some shaykhs, then heard [hadith] himself; he practised celibate asceticism (tajarrud), then married and received stipendiary places in the madrasas. He died in Shaʿbān of the year three [803 AH]. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said so in his Inbāʾ [al-Ghumr]."@en .

rec:AIND-D04445 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04445-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04445-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04445 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أبي السرور. في ابن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī al-Surūr. Under [ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī al-Surūr] Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D04448 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04448-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04448-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04448-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86b_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04448 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن سليمان بن عبد الله بن حرز الله الجمال الأجاري ثم المقدسي المالكي ويعرف بابن سحارة . قال شيخنا لقيته بالرملة فسمعت عليه فوائد ابن ماسي من آخر جزء الأنصاري بحضوره له على الميدومي وإجازته منه وممن سمعها معه ابن عمه شعبان ومات سنة بضع وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Sulaymān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥarz Allāh, al-Jamāl, al-Ājārī, then al-Maqdisī, al-Mālikī, known as Ibn Saḥāra. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said: \"I met him at al-Ramla and heard from him the Fawāʾid Ibn Māsī, from the end of the Juzʾ of al-Anṣārī, on the strength of his having attended (ḥuḍūr) its reading before al-Maydūmī and of his ijāza from him. Among those who heard it together with me was my paternal cousin Shaʿbān.\" He died in one of the 'odd' years of the eight hundreds (803–809 AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04449 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04449-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04449-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04449-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86b_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04449 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن سليمان بن محمد بن عبد الله الجمال الكناني الحوراني الأصل الغزي الحنفي نزيل مكة وشقيق أحمد الماضي . جاور بمكة نحو عشر سنين وكان ممن سمع مني فيها وله نظم وفهم يشارك به يسيرا . مات غريبا بنواحي كالكوت في المحرم سنة ثمان وثمانين رحمه الله وعوضه الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Sulaymān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Jamāl al-Kinānī, of Ḥawrānī origin, al-Ghazzī, the Ḥanafī, a resident of Mecca and the full brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad. He lived adjacent (jāwara) to Mecca for about ten years and was among those who heard [ḥadīth] from me there. He had some verse and understanding, in which he shared to a modest degree. He died as a stranger in the regions of Calicut in al-Muḥarram of the year 888. May God have mercy on him and grant him Paradise in recompense."@en .

rec:AIND-D04450 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04450-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04450-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04450-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04450-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86b_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_ruling,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04450 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن سليمان جمال الدين السبكي القاهري . اشتغل وحضر الدروس ومات في أيام الظاهر جقمق بعد الخمسين وقد قارب السبعين . كتبت عنه في ترجمة القاياتي مناما حدثني به العز السنباطي عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Sulaymān, Jamāl al-Dīn al-Subkī al-Qāhirī. He occupied himself with study and attended lessons. He died after the [year] fifty [i.e. 850], in the days of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq, having come close to seventy. I recorded from him, in the biography of al-Qāyātī, a dream which al-ʿIzz al-Sunbāṭī related to me on his authority."@en .

rec:AIND-D04451 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04451-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04451-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04451-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04451-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86b_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_ruling,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04451 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن سليمان الجمال المحلي أحد موقعي الحكم بل ناب في بعض الجهات والنواحي من القاهرة قليلا . مات في رجب سنة ثمان وثلاثين . أرخه شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Sulaymān, al-Jamāl al-Maḥallī. One of the clerks who countersigned judgements (muwaqqiʿī al-ḥukm); indeed he acted briefly as deputy (nāʾib) in some districts and outlying areas of Cairo. He died in Rajab of the year 838. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death-date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04453 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04453-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04453-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04453-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86b_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04453 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن شكر مولى السيد حسن بن عجلان . كان مع أخيه بديد في مباينة السيد محمد بن بركات فلما حلف الأخ امتنع السيد من تأمينه وأعاده إلى أخيه وذلك في سنة أربع وستين . جرده ابن فهد وهو في سنة سبع وتسعين في الأحياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Shukr, the mawlā (freedman/client) of al-Sayyid Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān. He was with his brother Badīd in opposition to al-Sayyid Muḥammad b. Barakāt; when the brother swore [allegiance], the Sayyid refused to grant him safe-conduct and sent him back to his brother — that was in the year 864. Ibn Fahd excerpted his entry, and he is, in the year 897, among the living."@en .

rec:AIND-D04454 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04454-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04454-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04454-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04454-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86b_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_ruling,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04454 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن شيرين الجمال الهندي الحنفي نزيل القاهرة سمع من ابن عبد الهادي وحدث وخطب بالبرقوقية إلى أن مات ، وكان يحدث عن الهند بعجائب الله أعلم بصحتها . مات سنة تسع . قاله شيخنا في إنبائه وتبعه المقريزي في عقوده وليس هو بأب لمحمود بن شيرين فذاك محمود بن مسعود بن يوسف كما سيأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Shīrīn, al-Jamāl al-Hindī al-Ḥanafī, a resident of Cairo. He heard from Ibn ʿAbd al-Hādī and transmitted [ḥadīth], and he preached (khaṭaba) at al-Barqūqiyya until he died. He used to relate marvels about India, whose soundness God knows best. He died in the year 809. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said so in his Inbāʾ, and al-Maqrīzī followed him in his ʿUqūd. He was not the father of Maḥmūd b. Shīrīn; that one is Maḥmūd b. Masʿūd b. Yūsuf, as will follow."@en .

rec:AIND-D04460 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04460-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04460-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04460-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86b_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04460 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن بن حسن بن علي بن منصور بن علي التقي البغدادي الأصل الغزي±±± الشافعي شقيق العلاء علي الآتي ويعرف بابن المشرقي . ولد سنة اثنتين وخمسين وثمانمائة ومات سنة ثلاث وتسعين وأظنه ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Manṣūr b. ʿAlī, al-Taqī, of Baghdādī origin, al-Ghazzī, the Shāfiʿī, the full brother of al-ʿAlāʾ ʿAlī who comes below, known as Ibn al-Mashriqī. He was born in the year 852 and died in the year 893. I think he was among those who heard [ḥadīth] from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D04461 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04461-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04461-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04461 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن علي بن عبد المحسن بن جمال الثنا الإمام أمين الدين البصري والد أحمد وعبد الله المذكورين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Muḥsin b. Jamāl al-Thanā, the Imām, Amīn al-Dīn al-Baṣrī, the father of the aforementioned Aḥmad and ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D04467 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04467-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04467-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04467-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04467-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b86b_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B86_ruling,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04467 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن خير الدين الآمدي الحنفي . ممن برع في المعقولات وشارك في علوم أخر ومات ببلاد آمد سنة خمس وثلاثين . ذكره المقريزي في عقوده ونقل عن الشهاب الكوراني أنه قال له حليت على مشايخي مائة وثلاثين تصنيفا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Khayr al-Dīn al-Āmidī al-Ḥanafī. He was among those who excelled in the rational sciences and shared in other branches of learning. He died in the land of Āmid in the year 835. Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his ʿUqūd and transmitted from al-Shihāb al-Kūrānī that he said to him: \"I expounded one hundred and thirty compositions under my shaykhs.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D04468 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04468-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04468-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04468-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87_apply,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04468 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن العفيف أبو محمد الحضرمي التريمي اليماني الشافعي ويعرف كسلفه بأفضل . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-ʿAfīf Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥaḍramī al-Tarīmī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī, known, like his forebears, as Afḍal. He is among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04469 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04469-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04469-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04469 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن أبو محمد الشنيني اليماني صاحب الأخلاق الرضية والشمائل المرضية ممن لازم مجالس العلماء مدة وحصل كتبا مفيدة مع النسك والتلاوة والعبادة . مات بالطاعون في أواخر سنة سبع وثلاثين ببلده شنين وكان لأبيه رياسة وجاه عند الناصر باليمن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Abū Muḥammad al-Shanīnī al-Yamānī. A man of pleasing character and agreeable qualities, he attended the sessions of the scholars for a time and acquired useful books, along with piety, Qurʾān recitation and worship. He died of the plague at the end of the year 837 in his town, Shanīn. His father had held leadership and prestige with al-Nāṣir in Yemen."@en .

rec:AIND-D04470 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04470-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04470-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04470 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن العلوي . فيمن جده محمد بن يوسف قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-ʿAlawī. See, shortly before, among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Yūsuf."@en .

rec:AIND-D04471 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04471-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04471-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04471 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الرحيم بن محمد بن عبد الله بن بكتمر بن الحاجب أخو عبد الرحمن وألف وأمه تركية رومية لأبيه . مات صغيرا في الطاعون سنة ثلاث وخمسين وكذا مات معه في يومه ابن أخيه محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الرحيم ومات عبد الرحمن بعد أبيه عبد الرحيم بدون سنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Baktamur b. al-Ḥājib. He was the paternal brother of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Alif, and his mother was a Turkish Rūmī woman. He died young of the plague in the year 853, and likewise his nephew Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm died with him on the same day. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān died less than two years after his father ʿAbd al-Raḥīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D04472 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04472-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04472-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04472 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الرحيم الحضرمي ابن أخت عبد الكبير . مات بمكة في صفر سنة ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Ḥaḍramī, the sister's son of ʿAbd al-Kabīr. He died in Mecca in Ṣafar of the year ..."@en .

rec:AIND-D04475 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04475-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04475-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04475 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد القادر بن عبد القادر الطرابلسي ويعرف بابن الحبال . ولد تقريبا سنة خمس وسبعين وسبعمائة بطرابلس وسمع الصحيح على محمد بن علي اليونيني والشريف محمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم الحسيني ومحمد بن محمد بن أحمد الجردي كلهم عن الحجار±±± سماعا وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء ومات قريبا من سنة خمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Ṭarābulusī, known as Ibn al-Ḥabbāl. He was born approximately in the year 775 in Tripoli and heard the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Yūnīnī, the Sharīf Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm al-Ḥusaynī, and Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Jardī, all of them transmitting it by audition from al-Ḥajjār. He transmitted ḥadīth, and the eminent scholars heard from him. He died close to the year 850."@en .

rec:AIND-D04479 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04479-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04479-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04479 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد اللطيف أبو محمد الحضرمي نزيل مكة الشهير بالعراقي كان معتقدا وصفه ابن فهد بالولاية والصلاح والزهد وأرخه في جمادى الثانية سنة سبع وأربعين بمكة ودفن بالشبيكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥaḍramī, a resident of Mecca, known as al-ʿIrāqī. He was a man in whom people placed their faith; Ibn Fahd described him with sainthood, righteousness and asceticism, and dated his death to Jumādā II of the year 847 in Mecca. He was buried at al-Shabīka."@en .

rec:AIND-D04481 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04481-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04481-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04481-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87_apply3,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04481 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن معبد الدماصي الأصل المناوي ثم القاهري الآتي أبوه . حفظ القرآن واشتغل يسيرا وجلس كأبيه لإقراء الأبناء وخطب بعدة أماكن بل وقرأ البخاري في رمضان ببعضها وتنزل في الجهات ، وحج وربما حضر عندي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Maʿbad, of Damāṣ origin, al-Manāwī, then al-Qāhirī; his father is mentioned below. He memorized the Qurʾān and studied a little. Like his father, he sat to teach children recitation, preached in several places, and indeed recited al-Bukhārī during Ramaḍān in some of them. He was appointed to various stipendiary posts, performed the pilgrimage, and sometimes attended my sessions."@en .

rec:AIND-D04482 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04482-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04482-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04482 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الله الجمال الرومي الحنفي نزيل الصرغتمشية . قرأ على الأمين الأقصرائي بالجانبكية المجمع لابن الساعاتي وأذن له في الإقراء ووصفه بالفاضل العلامة الحبر الفهامة المدقق المتقن ، وأرخها في ربيع الآخر سنة ثلاث وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Jamāl al-Rūmī al-Ḥanafī, resident of the Ṣarghatmashiyya. He read the Majmaʿ of Ibn al-Sāʿātī with al-Amīn al-Aqṣarāʾī at the Jānibakiyya, who authorized him to teach and described him as \"the virtuous, the most learned, the erudite, the perceptive, the meticulous, the accomplished\", dating it in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 833."@en .

rec:AIND-D04484 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04484-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04484-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04484-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04484-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87_apply3,
        agent:claude_b87a_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B87 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04484 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الله الدكاري المغربي ثم المدني المالكي . أقرأ بها ودرس وأفاد وناب في الحكم في بعض القضايا وكان يتجرأ على العلماء . مات في سنة ست سامحه الله . قاله شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Dakārī al-Maghribī, then al-Madanī, al-Mālikī. He taught recitation there (in Medina), lectured and benefited others, and acted as deputy judge in some cases; but he was insolent toward the scholars. He died in the year six (806), may God pardon him. So says our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04485 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04485-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04485-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04485 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الله شيخ أبشية الملق من الغربية . مات مقتولا في سنة إحدى وسبعين واتهم به عبد الرحمن بن التاجر وابنه إسماعيل فسلخا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh, shaykh of Abshiyyat al-Malaq in al-Gharbiyya. He was murdered in the year 871; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Tājir and his son Ismāʿīl were accused of it, and both were flayed."@en .

rec:AIND-D04489 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04489-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04489-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04489 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أبي عبد الله المغربي السوسي . مات سنة ثلاث وأظنه الماضي قريبا فالذاكر له شك في ثلاث أو إحدى وحينئذ فإحدى النسبتين تحرفت من الأخرى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī ʿAbd Allāh al-Maghribī al-Sūsī. He died in the year three. I think he is the one mentioned shortly before, for the one who recorded him was in doubt between three and one, in which case one of the two nisbas was corrupted from the other."@en .

rec:AIND-D04490 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04490-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04490-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04490 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الملك بن إبراهيم الجمال الدميري ثم القاهري المالكي الشروطي . سمع على شيخنا أشياء مع الراعي وغيره وأجاز له باستدعاء ابن فهد المؤرخ بتاسع عشر رجب سنة ست وثلاثين خلق وهو أحد شهود الصالحية بل صار من قدماء موقعيها وليس بالمتقن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Malik b. Ibrāhīm al-Jamāl al-Damīrī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Mālikī, the notary (al-Shurūṭī). He heard several things from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) together with al-Rāʿī and others, and a multitude granted him an ijāza at the request of the historian Ibn Fahd, dated the 19th of Rajab 836. He was one of the notary-witnesses of the Ṣāliḥiyya and indeed became one of its senior clerks (muwaqqiʿ), though he was not meticulous."@en .

rec:AIND-D04493 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04493-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04493-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04493 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عبد الواحد البحيري . مات سنة تسع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Buḥayrī. He died in the year 859."@en .

rec:AIND-D04496 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04496-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04496-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04496-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87_apply3,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04496 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عثمان بن علي الأبشاقي بالمعجمة الشافعي مؤدب الأبناء ويعرف بالصعيدي . ممن سمع مني قريب التسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUthmān b. ʿAlī al-Abshāqī (with the dotted letter), al-Shāfiʿī, a tutor of children, known as al-Ṣaʿīdī. He is among those who heard from me around the year 890."@en .

rec:AIND-D04498 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04498-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04498-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04498 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عقيل بن مبارك بن رميثة بن أبي نمى الحسني المكي . مات بها في جمادى الأولى سنة ست وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAqīl b. Mubārak b. Rumaytha b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died there (in Mecca) in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 846. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04500 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04500-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04500-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04500 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز أبو بكر النويري المكي . أجاز له في سنة إحدى وتسعين وسبعمائة وبعدها جماعة وكان حيا في سنة ثلاث عشرة بمقتضى خطه في شهادة . قاله ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz Abū Bakr al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī. A group of scholars granted him ijāza in the year 791 and thereafter. He was still alive in the year 813, according to his handwriting on a deed of testimony. So says Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D04502 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04502-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04502-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04502 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن علي بن أحمد الجمال المنوفي الخطيب . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Jamāl al-Munūfī, the preacher (al-Khaṭīb). He is among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04503 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04503-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04503-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04503 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن علي بن أيوب . يأتي فيمن جده يوسف بن علي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Ayyūb. He will appear shortly among those whose grandfather is Yūsuf b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04507 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04507-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04507-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04507-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b87a_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_B88 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04507 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الحميد الفندقي القباقبي الصالحي . سمع من أبي العباس المرداوي مجالس المخلدي الثلاثة وحدث بها قرأ عليه شيخنا الأول منه بالصالحية ومات في ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Funduqī al-Qabāqibī al-Ṣāliḥī. He heard the three Majālis of al-Mukhalladī from Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Mardāwī and transmitted them; our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) read the first of them with him at al-Ṣāliḥiyya. He died in ..."@en .

rec:AIND-D04508 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04508-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04508-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04508 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن المغربي العطار ، ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Maghribī al-ʿAṭṭār. He is among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04510 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04510-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04510-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04510 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن علي بن موسى بن أبي بكر بن محمد الشيبي اليماني الآتي أبوه . انتصب بعده في زاويته بالحسامية ومات في سنة إحدى وثلاثين وكان كثير التلاوة . ذكره شيخنا في ترجمة أبيه في سنة إحدى عشرة من إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Mūsā b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad al-Shaybī al-Yamānī, whose father's biography is forthcoming. He was installed after his father in the latter's zāwiya at al-Ḥusāmiyya, and died in the year 831 AH. He recited the Qurʾān a great deal. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in the biography of his father under the year 811 AH of his Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D04511 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04511-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04511-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04511-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04511 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن علي بن موسى بن علي بن قريش بن داود الهاشمي المكي . مات بها في ربيع الأول سنة ثمان وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Mūsā b. ʿAlī b. Quraysh b. Dāwūd al-Hāshimī al-Makkī. He died there (in Mecca) in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 848 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04515 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04515-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04515-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04515 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن علي البهاء الكازروني . فيمن جده عبد القادر بن علي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī, al-Bahāʾ al-Kāzarūnī. See, nearby, among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04516 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04516-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04516-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04516 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن علي التعزي المدني الشافعي خادم البيمارستان . ممن يحفظ القرآن وكذا حفظ المنهاج . مات في ربيع الأول سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī al-Taʿizzī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī, servant (khādim) of the bīmāristān. He is among those who memorized the Qurʾān, and he likewise memorized al-Minhāj. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04518 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04518-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04518-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04518 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عمر بن أبي بكر بن علي بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله ابن عمر بن عبد الرحمن الناشري اليماني أخو العفيف عثمان مصنف الناشريين . اشتغل في صغره بالعلم وحج وهو شاب ثم انقطع للتلاوة وكان شجي الصوت جدا ومات في سنة ثماني عشرة ودفن عند أبيه من زبيد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Nāshirī al-Yamānī, brother of al-ʿAfīf ʿUthmān, the author of the work on the Nāshirīs. In his youth he occupied himself with learning and performed the pilgrimage as a young man, then devoted himself to recitation. He had a very plaintive, beautiful voice. He died in the year 818 AH and was buried beside his father at Zabīd."@en .

rec:AIND-D04519 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04519-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04519-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04519 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله مطيري بن عمر بن الزين عبد العزيز بن عبد الواحد المدني أخو حسن وعبد الباسط ويعرف كل منهم بابن زين الدين . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh Muṭayrī b. ʿUmar b. al-Zayn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Madanī, brother of Ḥasan and ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ; each of them is known as Ibn Zayn al-Dīn. He is among those who heard from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D04520 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04520-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04520-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04520-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04520 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عمر بن عبد العزيز بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز الهاشمي العقيلي النويري الأصل المكي المالكى الآتي أبوه . ولد بها وأمه غزال الحبشية فتاة أبيه وحفظ القرآن وصلى به وسمع من ابن الجزري والبرماوي وغيرهما ودخل في سنة اثنتين وثلاثين مع أبيه القاهرة ثم المغرب ثم التكرور ، فماتا بها قبل سنة ست وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Hāshimī al-ʿUqaylī, of Nuwayrī origin, al-Makkī, the Mālikī; his father's biography is forthcoming. He was born there (in Mecca); his mother was Ghazāl al-Ḥabashiyya, his father's slave-girl. He memorized the Qurʾān and led the prayers with it, and heard from Ibn al-Jazarī, al-Birmāwī and others. In the year 832 AH he entered Cairo with his father, then the Maghrib, then al-Takrūr, and the two of them died there before the year 836 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04522 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04522-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04522-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04522-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04522 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عمر بن عبد الله بن عمر بن مسعود العمري المكي . كان من أعيان القواد المعروفين بالعمرة . مات سنة ثلاث ظنا . قاله الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Masʿūd al-ʿUmarī al-Makkī. He was one of the notables of the commanders (quwwād) known as al-ʿUmara. He died in the year [80]3, conjecturally; so said al-Fāsī in his history of Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04524 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04524-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04524-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04524 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عمر بن عثمان أبو محمد الشمري الملحاني تفقه بالشهاب أحمد ابن أبي بكر الناشري وولي القضاء بتعز ثم أقام مدة بعدن ، وتوفي قبل العشرين وقبره عند مقابر الناشريين بزبيد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. ʿUthmān, Abū Muḥammad al-Shammarī al-Milḥānī. He studied jurisprudence under al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr al-Nāshirī and held the judgeship of Taʿizz, then resided for a time in Aden. He died before the year [8]20 AH, and his grave is at the cemetery of the Nāshirīs in Zabīd."@en .

rec:AIND-D04526 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04526-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04526-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04526 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عمر بن محمد بن علي بن محمد بن إدريس العفيف بن السراج العبدري الشيبي الحجبي المكي أخو محمد وهذا أصغر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Idrīs, al-ʿAfīf b. al-Sirāj, al-ʿAbdarī al-Shaybī al-Ḥajabī al-Makkī, brother of Muḥammad; this one (ʿAbd Allāh) is the younger."@en .

rec:AIND-D04527 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04527-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04527-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04527-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04527 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن السراج عمر بن المحب محمد بن علي بن يوسف الأنصاري الزرندي المدني . ممن سمع على الجمال الكازروني وأبي الفتح المراغي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Sirāj ʿUmar b. al-Muḥibb Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf al-Anṣārī al-Zarandī al-Madanī. He is among those who heard from al-Jamāl al-Kāzarūnī and Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04528 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04528-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04528-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04528-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04528 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عمر بن محمد بن محمد بن أبي الخير محمد بن فهد العفيف أبو السيادة ابن صاحبنا النجم الهاشمي المكي سبط النور بن سلامة ويعرف كسلفه بابن فهد . ولد بمكة في ربيع الآخر سنة أربعين ومات بها في رجبها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Khayr Muḥammad b. Fahd, al-ʿAfīf Abū al-Siyāda, son of our companion al-Najm (ʿUmar b. Fahd), al-Hāshimī al-Makkī, daughter's son of al-Nūr b. Salāma; known, like his forebears, as Ibn Fahd. He was born in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 840 AH and died there in Rajab of that year."@en .

rec:AIND-D04529 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04529-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04529-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04529 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله أخوه . ولد بمكة في شوال سنة ثلاث وستين ومات بها في صفر سنة ست وستين . ذكرهما أبوهما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh, his (the preceding ʿAbd Allāh's) brother. He was born in Mecca in Shawwāl of the year 863 AH and died there in Ṣafar of the year 866 AH. Their father mentioned the two of them."@en .

rec:AIND-D04530 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04530-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04530-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04530-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04530 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عمر بن محمد بن مسعود بن إبراهيم الأعرابي . خرج من مكة إلى بلاد اليمن في ربيع الآخر سنة خمس وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Masʿūd b. Ibrāhīm al-Aʿrābī. He left Mecca for the land of Yemen in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 855 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D04531 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04531-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04531-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04531 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عمر بن محمد الدملوي اليمني . مات في صفر سنة ست وخمسين بجدة ودفن بها . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Damlawī al-Yamanī. He died in Ṣafar of the year 856 AH at Jidda and was buried there. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04532 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04532-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04532-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04532-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04532 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عمر الأهدل اليماني ذو الأخلاق الحسنة والآداب المستحسنة صحب عبد الله العراقي وانتفع به في الطريق ونصبه شيخا وكان على قدم حسن من ترك مالا يعنيه مع الاقتصاد في ملبسه وغيره والتأدب بآداب الصوفية والمشي على طريقتهم المرضية . مات سنة ست وستين رحمه الله . ذكره صاحب صلحاء اليمن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar al-Ahdal al-Yamānī, a man of good character and commendable manners. He kept the company of ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿIrāqī, benefited from him in the (Sufi) path, and was appointed a shaykh by him. He stood on a fine footing: leaving aside what did not concern him, being frugal in his dress and other matters, cultivating the manners of the Sufis and walking their approved path. He died in the year 866 AH, may God have mercy on him. The author of Ṣulaḥāʾ al-Yaman mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04533 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04533-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04533-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04533-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04533 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عمر التواتي بمثناتين بينهما واو ثقيلة المدني كان صالحا خيرا عليه آثار الزهد والخير . مات بالقاهرة سنة سبع ، ذكره ابن خطيب الناصرية وكذا قال شيخنا في إنبائه : كان من أهل الخير والصلاح أقام بالمدينة مجاورا بها وكان يتردد إلى مصر والشام فكانت منيته بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar al-Tawwātī—with two tāʾs and a doubled wāw between them—al-Madanī. He was a righteous, good man, on whom the marks of asceticism and goodness were visible. He died in Cairo in the year [80]7. Ibn Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya mentioned him, and our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) likewise said in his Inbāʾ: \"He was one of the people of goodness and righteousness; he resided in Medina as a mujāwir, and used to travel back and forth to Egypt and Syria, and his death took place in Cairo.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D04534 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04534-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04534-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04534 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن عيسى بن عبد الله الجمال الكردي نزيل القاهرة الشافعي قدم القاهرة فلازم ابن أسد وجعفرا وتلميذهما الجلال المرجوشي في القراءات وبرع فيها ، وحج وتلا بالعشر أفرادا ثم جمعا على عمر النجار وكذا أخذ عن الشهاب القباقبي وأقرأ وكان حاد الخلق . مات سنة ثلاث وثمانين وقد جاز الأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿĪsā b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Jamāl al-Kurdī, resident of Cairo, the Shāfiʿī. He came to Cairo and attached himself to Ibn Asad, Jaʿfar, and their pupil al-Jalāl al-Marjūshī in the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt), and excelled in them. He performed the pilgrimage and recited the ten readings, first individually and then combined, under ʿUmar al-Najjār; he likewise studied under al-Shihāb al-Qabāqibī, and taught recitation himself. He was sharp-tempered. He died in the year 883 AH, having passed forty."@en .

rec:AIND-D04536 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04536-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04536-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b88a_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04536 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أبي الفتح بن محمد بن حمام المكي . ممن سمع علي بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī al-Fatḥ b. Muḥammad b. Ḥammām al-Makkī. He is among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04537 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04537-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04537-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04537 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن فرج الزنجي الفهدي . ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Faraj al-Zanjī al-Fahdī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04539 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04539-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04539-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04539 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أبي القسم بن أحمد بن محمد بن جزي الأندلسي . مات سنة عشر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī al-Qāsim b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Juzayy al-Andalusī. He died in the year 810."@en .

rec:AIND-D04540 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04540-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04540-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04540 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن كزل الجمال الدشتي الأصل القاهري . يروي تائية ابن الفارض عن الشهاب أحمد بن علي بن قرطاي المعروف بابن بكتمر الساقي سماعا ولقيه العز بن فهد بعيد السبعين فكتب عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Kuzul, al-Jamāl, of Dashtī origin, al-Qāhirī. He transmits the Tāʾiyya of Ibn al-Fāriḍ from al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Qurṭāy, known as Ibn Baktamur al-Sāqī, by audition. Al-ʿIzz b. Fahd met him shortly after 870 and wrote down (material) from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04541 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04541-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04541-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04541 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن كنيفش . قتل في صفر سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Kunayfish. He was killed in Ṣafar of the year 891."@en .

rec:AIND-D04542 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04542-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04542-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04542-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04542 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن مبارك بن حسن بن شكوان أخو أحمد البوني لأمه . مات بمكة في رجب سنة اثنتين وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Mubārak b. Ḥasan b. Shukwān, the maternal brother of Aḥmad al-Būnī. He died in Mecca in Rajab of the year 862. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04544 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04544-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04544-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04544 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله آخر أخ للذي قبله أظنه توفي قبله فسمي باسمه وهو أحد من أخذ باستدعاء الزيني رضوان وابن موسى المراكشي المؤرخ بسنة أربع عشرة وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh, another brother of the preceding one. I think he died before him, and so the latter was named after him. He was one of those who received (an ijāza) through the ijāza-request (istidʿāʾ) of al-Zaynī Riḍwān and Ibn Mūsā al-Marrākushī dated in the year 814."@en .

rec:AIND-D04550 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04550-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04550-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04550-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04550 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن أبي الفضل محمد بن أحمد بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية ابن ظهيرة القرشي . ولد بمكة ونشأ بها وسمع من ابن الجزري والشمس البرماوي وابن سلامة والشامي وغيرهم ، وأجاز له ابنة ابن عبد الهادي والزين المراغي وابن الكويك وآخرون . ومات في أواخر سنة ثلاثين أو أوائل التي بعدها بمكة رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī al-Faḍl Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Ẓahīra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya Ibn Ẓahīra al-Qurashī. He was born in Mecca and grew up there. He heard from Ibn al-Jazarī, al-Shams al-Birmāwī, Ibn Salāma, al-Shāmī and others, and the daughter of Ibn ʿAbd al-Hādī, al-Zayn al-Marāghī, Ibn al-Kuwayk and others granted him an ijāza. He died in Mecca at the end of the year 830 or at the beginning of the following year. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04551 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04551-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04551-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04551 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن الشيخ الشهير بيت المقدس محمد بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن ويقال عثمان بن عمر التركستاني ويعرف بالقرمي . اشتغل قليلا وقدم حلب ثم دخل بغداد وأسر مع اللنكية ثم خلص ويقال أنه جرت له محنة فخنق نفسه بسببها على ما استفيض بين الناس وذلك في أواخر سنة ست. قاله شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh, son of the shaykh famous in Jerusalem (Bayt al-Maqdis), Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — or, as is also said, b. ʿUthmān b. ʿUmar — al-Turkistānī, known as al-Qirimī. He studied a little, came to Aleppo and then entered Baghdad, where he was taken captive by the Timurid (Lankī) forces and later released. It is said that a tribulation befell him, on account of which he strangled himself, as was widely reported among the people; that was at the end of the year 806. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said so in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04552 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04552-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04552-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04552 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن أحمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد المعطى الأنصاري الخزرجي المكي أخو القطب محمد ويعرف أبوهما بابن الصفى نسبة لجده لأمه الصفي الطبري . سمع وسكن اليمن سنين ثم عاد لمكة ثم رجع إليها وبها توفي في أوائل سنة ثلاث وقد بلغ الخمسين أو جازها ظنا . قاله القاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī al-Anṣārī al-Khazrajī al-Makkī, brother of al-Quṭb Muḥammad; their father was known as Ibn al-Ṣafī after his maternal grandfather al-Ṣafī al-Ṭabarī. He heard (ḥadīth), lived in Yemen for some years, then returned to Mecca, then went back to Yemen and died there at the beginning of the year (80)3, having reached the age of fifty or, conjecturally, passed it. Al-Fāsī said so in (his history of) Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04555 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04555-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04555-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04555 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن أحمد بن أبي الفضل بن عبد الله العفيف بن الجمال بن الشهاب بن الكمال الحراري±±± الأصل المكي الحنفي أخو أحمد الماضي والآتي أبوهما . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Abī al-Faḍl b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-ʿAfīf b. al-Jamāl b. al-Shihāb b. al-Kamāl, of Ḥarārī (Ḥarāzī) origin, al-Makkī, al-Ḥanafī, brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad; their father is to be mentioned below. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04559 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04559-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04559-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04559 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن الخواجا الجمال محمد بن أحمد الحضرمي الكندي اليماني الآتي أبوه . كان صاحب همة وجور على أصحابه ومعارفه . مات في ربيع الثاني سنة أربع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh, son of al-Khawājā al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Ḥaḍramī al-Kindī al-Yamānī; his father is to be mentioned below. He was a man of high ambition, but tyrannical towards his companions and acquaintances. He died in Rabīʿ al-Thānī of the year 864."@en .

rec:AIND-D04560 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04560-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04560-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04560 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن أحمد الششتري المدني . مضى قريبا فيمن جده أحمد بن عثمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shushtarī al-Madanī. Mentioned shortly above among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. ʿUthmān."@en .

rec:AIND-D04561 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04561-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04561-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04561 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن إسماعيل الدواخلي ثم القاهري الغمري الشافعي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة وربما اشتغل وخطب بجامع الغمري أياما ويذكر بمحبة فى النميمة والتفاتن"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl al-Dawākhilī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Ghamrī, al-Shāfiʿī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo. He occasionally engaged in study and delivered the Friday sermon at the Ghamrī Mosque for some days. He is noted for a fondness for tale-bearing and stirring up strife."@en .

rec:AIND-D04562 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04562-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04562-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04562-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_verify,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04562 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن بركوت الشبيكي المكي القائد . مات في ربيع الأول سنة سبع وأربعين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Barkūt al-Shabīkī al-Makkī, the qāʾid (commander). He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 847 in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04565 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04565-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04565-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04565 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن بيان المدني المادح . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Bayān al-Madanī al-Mādiḥ (the panegyrist). He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D04566 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04566-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04566-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04566 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن جسار العمري المكي القائد . مات بمكة في منتصف ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Jassār al-ʿUmarī al-Makkī, the qāʾid (commander). He died in Mecca in the middle of Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 861. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04567 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04567-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04567-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04567-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04567 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن جمعة بن راجح بن موسى بن راجح بن إبراهيم الجمال البصروي الشاغوري الدمشقي . ذكره النجم عمر بن فهد في معجمه هكذا ووصفه بالفضل"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Jumʿa b. Rājiḥ b. Mūsā b. Rājiḥ b. Ibrāhīm, al-Jamāl al-Buṣrawī al-Shāghūrī al-Dimashqī. Al-Najm ʿUmar b. Fahd mentioned him thus in his Muʿjam and described him as a man of merit."@en .

rec:AIND-D04568 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04568-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04568-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04568 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن حسن الجمال الأخصاصي أو الخصوصي القاهري الشافعي . أخذ القرا آت عن النور الإمام والشمس بن الحصري وجعفر وبعض الجمع عن الشهاب السكندري ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan, al-Jamāl al-Akhṣāṣī or al-Khuṣūṣī, al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī. He took the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt) from al-Nūr al-Imām, al-Shams b. al-Ḥuṣrī and Jaʿfar, and part of the combined recitation (al-jamʿ) from al-Shihāb al-Sakandarī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04571 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04571-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04571-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04571 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن خليل بن بكتوت بن بيرم بن بكتوت الكردي الأصل القاهري الحسيني والد الشمس بن بيرم الحنبلي ، قال لي أنه ولد في رمضان سنة ثمان وسبعين وسبعمائة وأنه حفظ القرآن وبعض القدوري وأنه ألم بالفرائض وأنه تزوج ابنة أخت ابن الظريف أمين الحكم واستولدها ابنته الموجودة الآن وأنه مات سنة ست وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Khalīl b. Baktūt b. Bayram b. Baktūt, of Kurdish origin, al-Qāhirī, al-Ḥusaynī, father of al-Shams b. Bayram al-Ḥanbalī. He told me that he was born in Ramaḍān 778, that he memorised the Qurʾān and part of al-Qudūrī, that he had some acquaintance with the law of inheritance (farāʾiḍ), and that he married the daughter of the sister of Ibn al-Ẓarīf, the amīn al-ḥukm, by whom he had his daughter, who is still living. He died in the year 866."@en .

rec:AIND-D04572 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04572-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04572-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04572 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن الحاج خليل بن سعيد الجمال الطرابلسي الشافعي ويعرف بابن الحاج خليل . ولد في حدود سنة ثمانمائة بطرابلس ، ولقيه البقاعي ولم يذكر شيئا من أمره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. al-Ḥājj Khalīl b. Saʿīd, al-Jamāl al-Ṭarābulusī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Ḥājj Khalīl. He was born around the year 800 in Tripoli. Al-Biqāʿī met him but recorded nothing of his affairs."@en .

rec:AIND-D04574 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04574-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04574-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04574 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن سليمان الجمال الدمياطي ثم الصحراوي والد عمر الآتي . صحب ناصر الدين الطبناوي وقرأ على شيخنا في سنة إحدى وخمسين وأخذ عن الشمس الحجاري في الفرائض والحساب وتميز وأقرأ الطلبة وممن قرأ عليه الشرف يحيى الدميسي وأثنى عليه . مات ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Sulaymān, al-Jamāl al-Dimyāṭī, later al-Ṣaḥrāwī, the father of ʿUmar, who is mentioned below. He kept the company of Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Ṭabnāwī, read under our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in (8)51, and studied the law of inheritance and arithmetic under al-Shams al-Ḥajjārī. He distinguished himself and taught students; among those who read under him was al-Sharaf Yaḥyā al-Dumaysī, who praised him. He died … [the date is left blank]."@en .

rec:AIND-D04578 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04578-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04578-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04578-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04578 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن أحمد بن خليف المطري ابن عم المحب المطري المدني . سمع معه علي الجمال الحنبلي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Khalīf al-Maṭarī, the paternal cousin of al-Muḥibb al-Maṭarī al-Madanī. Together with him he heard from al-Jamāl al-Ḥanbalī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04580 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04580-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04580-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04580-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_verify,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04580 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد القادر بن عبد الله العفيف أبو محمد بن الجمال ابن المحيوي الناشري اليماني الشافعي . قرأ علي بمكة الأربعين في قضاء الحوائج للمنذري وسمع علي أشياء وكتبت له إجازة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-ʿAfīf Abū Muḥammad b. al-Jamāl b. al-Muḥyawī, al-Nāshirī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī. He read to me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca al-Mundhirī's al-Arbaʿīn fī qaḍāʾ al-ḥawāʾij, heard a number of things from me, and I wrote an ijāza for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04581 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04581-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04581-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04581 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الكريم الهلالي المكي الفاخراني . مات بها في المحرم سنة خمس وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm, al-Hilālī al-Makkī al-Fākhrānī. He died there (in Mecca) in Muḥarram (8)85; Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04583 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04583-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04583-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04583-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_verify,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04583 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الله بن بلال المكي الوقاد بالحرم . أجاز له في سنة خمس العراقي والهيثمي وابن صديق ، ومات بها في رمضان سنة سبع وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Bilāl, al-Makkī, the lamp-lighter (waqqād) at the Ḥaram (the Sacred Mosque of Mecca). In (8)05 al-ʿIrāqī, al-Haythamī and Ibn Ṣiddīq granted him an ijāza. He died there (in Mecca) in Ramaḍān (8)47; Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04585 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04585-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04585-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04585 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الله بن أبي عبد الله . يأتي فيمن جده عبد الله ابن محمد بن محمد قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī ʿAbd Allāh. He will be mentioned shortly below among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D04591 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04591-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04591-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04591 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الله بن أبي عبد الله محمد بن الرضي محمد بن أبي بكر عبد الله بن خليل عفيف الدين أبو الطيب القرشي العثماني المكي أحد العدول بباب السلام . ولد بمكة في صفر سنة تسع وثمانمائة ومات بها في جمادى الأولى سنة اثنتين وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. al-Raḍī Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr ʿAbd Allāh b. Khalīl, ʿAfīf al-Dīn Abū al-Ṭayyib al-Qurashī al-ʿUthmānī al-Makkī, one of the notary witnesses (ʿudūl) at Bāb al-Salām. He was born in Mecca in Ṣafar 809 and died there in Jumādā I (8)82."@en .

rec:AIND-D04593 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04593-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04593-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04593 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن موسى بن عيسى العفيف الدميري المكي عم عبد الكريم بن محمد الماضي . مات بها في المحرم سنة خمس وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. ʿĪsā, al-ʿAfīf al-Damīrī al-Makkī, the paternal uncle of ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad, mentioned above. He died there (in Mecca) in Muḥarram (8)55; Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04595 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04595-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04595-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04595 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن قوام الدين عبد الله الركن الخنجي . روى عن عمه الزين علي الراوي عن إمام الدين علي المعروف بخواجة شيخ عن علاء الدولة السمناني روى عنه الطاووسي وأجاز له وذلك في شعبان سنة تسع عشرة ووصفه بالعالم الفاضل البارع الزاهد ذي التراكيب البديعة والصنائع العجيبة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Qawām al-Dīn ʿAbd Allāh, al-Rukn al-Khunjī. He transmitted from his paternal uncle al-Zayn ʿAlī, who transmitted from Imām al-Dīn ʿAlī, known as Khwāja Shaykh, from ʿAlāʾ al-Dawla al-Simnānī. Al-Ṭāwūsī transmitted from him, and he granted him an ijāza, in Shaʿbān (8)19; al-Ṭāwūsī described him as a learned, virtuous, brilliant and ascetic scholar, possessed of marvellous compositions and wondrous crafts."@en .

rec:AIND-D04598 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04598-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04598-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04598-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_verify,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04598 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الوهاب الجمال بن القاضي فتح الدين أبي الفتح الأنصاري الزرندي المدني الحنفي أحد الأخوة الخمسة ووالد المحمدين الثلاثة . مات سنة اثنتين وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, al-Jamāl b. al-Qāḍī Fatḥ al-Dīn Abī al-Fatḥ, al-Anṣārī al-Zarandī al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī, one of the five brothers and the father of the three Muḥammads. He died in (8)62."@en .

rec:AIND-D04599 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04599-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04599-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04599-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04599 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الوهاب الغزي الشافعي الخطيب بجامعها الكبير كأبيه وجده ويعرف بابن سيف . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, al-Ghazzī al-Shāfiʿī, preacher (khaṭīb) at its (Gaza's) Great Mosque, like his father and grandfather; he is known as Ibn Sayf. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04600 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04600-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04600-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04600 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد الله بن محمد السيد الجلال بن القطب بن المحب بن النور الحسيني الأيجي . اشتغل وفضل وتزوج حليمة ابنة عم أبيه الصفي عبد الرحمن واستولدها عائدة ومات عنها شابا قريبا من سنة ستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad, al-Sayyid al-Jalāl b. al-Quṭb b. al-Muḥibb b. al-Nūr, al-Ḥusaynī al-Ījī. He devoted himself to study and excelled. He married Ḥalīma, the daughter of his father's paternal uncle al-Ṣafī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, and had by her a daughter, ʿĀʾida. He died, leaving her a widow, while still young, around the year (8)60."@en .

rec:AIND-D04601 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04601-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04601-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04601 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن علي بن أبي بكر بن إسماعيل المصري المكي الفراش والمؤذن بالمسجد الحرام والده والقبابي ومؤدب الأطفال هو . سمع في سنة ثمان وعشرين بوادي الجعرانة من أعمال مكة على الجمال المرشدي بعض مشيخته تخريج ابن فهد وعلي ابن سلامة ختم البخاري وأبي داود والشفاء."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. Ismāʿīl, al-Miṣrī al-Makkī. His father was a carpet-spreader (farrāsh) and muezzin at the Sacred Mosque; he himself was al-Qabābī and a teacher of children. In (8)28, at Wādī al-Jiʿrāna in the district of Mecca, he heard from al-Jamāl al-Murshidī part of his Mashyakha compiled by Ibn Fahd, and from ʿAlī Ibn Salāma the concluding session (khatm) of al-Bukhārī, Abū Dāwūd and al-Shifāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04603 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04603-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04603-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04603-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04603 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن علي بن سليمان الرازابي الجبرتي ثم المكي نزيل رباط ابن الزمن منها . مات في رجب سنة ست وثمانين ، ودفن بالمعلاة وكان صالحا خيرا ممن حضر عندي في شرح الألفية وغيره وحصل القول البديع بل كان فيما بلغني يقرأ على الشرف عبد الحق السنباطي حين مجاورته في تقسيم الأرشاد رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Sulaymān, al-Rāzābī al-Jabartī, later al-Makkī, resident of Ribāṭ Ibn al-Zaman there (in Mecca). He died in Rajab (8)86 and was buried at al-Muʿallā. He was a righteous, good man, one of those who attended my (al-Sakhāwī's) lectures on the Sharḥ al-Alfiyya and other works, and he obtained al-Qawl al-Badīʿ; indeed, as I was informed, he used to read al-Irshād in divided sessions under al-Sharaf ʿAbd al-Ḥaqq al-Sunbāṭī during the latter's sojourn (mujāwara). May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04613 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04613-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04613-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04613 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن الكمال أبي البركات محمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن حسن بن الزين محمد ابن الأمين محمد بن القطب محمد بن أحمد بن علي القسطلاني المكي . بيض له ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Kamāl Abī al-Barakāt Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. al-Zayn Muḥammad b. al-Amīn Muḥammad b. al-Quṭb Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī, al-Qasṭallānī al-Makkī. Ibn Fahd left a blank for him (i.e. entered only his name without a biography)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04614 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04614-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04614-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04614 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن الخطيب أبي القسم محمد بن أبي الفضل محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز النويري المكي الآتي أبوه . أجاز له في سنة ست وأربعين جماعة ومات قبل أن يتأهل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Khaṭīb Abī al-Qāsim Muḥammad b. Abī al-Faḍl Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī; his father is mentioned below. A group granted him an ijāza in (8)46, and he died before reaching adulthood (before marrying)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04616 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04616-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04616-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04616 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن محمد بن السراج . يأتي فيمن جده محمد بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. al-Sarrāj. He will be mentioned below among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D04618 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04618-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04618-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04618 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد البر بن أبي البقا السبكي . مات سنة ثلاث"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Barr b. Abī al-Baqā, al-Subkī. He died in the year (80)3."@en .

rec:AIND-D04625 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04625-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04625-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04625 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن محمد الجمال العراقي القاضي . فيمن جده محمد بن عبد الله بن سالم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, al-Jamāl al-ʿIrāqī, the qāḍī. [See] among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Sālim."@en .

rec:AIND-D04626 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04626-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04626-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b90_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04626 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن أبي محمد بن أبي بكر بن الدماميني . مضى فيمن جده عبد الله بن أبي بكر بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Abī Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. al-Damāmīnī. He has been mentioned above among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D04628 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04628-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04628-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04628-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04628 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن موسى بن محمد بن موسى المغربي العبد الوادي ويعرف بالعبدوسي ابن أخي الشيخ أبي القسم . كان واسع الباع في الحفظ ولي الفتيا بالمغرب الأقصى والإمامة بجامع القرويين من فاس ، ورأيت من قال فيه الفاسي . ومات فجأة وهو في صلاة المغرب سنة تسع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā, al-Maghribī al-ʿAbd al-Wādī, known as al-ʿAbdūsī, the nephew (brother's son) of al-Shaykh Abū al-Qāsim. He had a wide capacity for memorization. He held the office of issuing fatwas in the Far Maghrib and the imamate at the Qarawiyyīn Mosque in Fez. I have seen someone who called him al-Fāsī. He died suddenly while in the sunset (maghrib) prayer in the year 849."@en .

rec:AIND-D04629 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04629-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04629-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04629-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04629 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن موسى بن محمد بن موسى الجمال بن الشمس بن الشرف المنوفي ثم المازاني أخذ القراءات عن جعفر في سنة اثنتين وخمسين وشهد شيخنا في إجازته ووصفه بالفاضل العالم البارع وشيخ والده وجده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā, al-Jamāl b. al-Shams b. al-Sharaf, al-Manūfī, then al-Māzānī. He took the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt) from Jaʿfar in the year 852. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) attested as a witness on his ijāza and described him as \"the virtuous, learned, brilliant scholar\"; he (our shaykh) was also the shaykh of his father and grandfather."@en .

rec:AIND-D04630 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04630-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04630-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04630-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04630 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن موسى بن محمد الدوالي اليماني المذكور أبوه في المائة قبلها . كان فقيها مرضي السيرة في قضائه حسن الخلق . ذكره الخزرجي في أبيه وأظنه توفي في أوائل هذا القرن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. Muḥammad al-Dawālī al-Yamānī, whose father is mentioned in the previous century. He was a jurist, of praiseworthy conduct in his judgeship and of good character. Al-Khazrajī mentioned him in the biography of his father. I think he died in the early years of this century."@en .

rec:AIND-D04631 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04631-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04631-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04631 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن نصر الغالب بالله متملك غرناطة من الأندلس وحفيد الأمير أبي الجيوش نصر بن أمير المسلمين أبي الحجاج بن أبي الوليد إسماعيل بن نصر . ذكر المقريزي في حوادث سنة أربع وأربعين أنه في رجب منها ورد كتابه يتضمن ما فيه المسلمون بغرناطة من الشدة مع النصارى أهل قرطبة وإشبيلية وتطلب النجدة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Naṣr, al-Ghālib bi-llāh, the ruler of Granada in al-Andalus and grandson of the Amīr Abū al-Juyūsh Naṣr b. Amīr al-Muslimīn Abī al-Ḥajjāj b. Abī al-Walīd Ismāʿīl b. Naṣr. Al-Maqrīzī mentioned in the events of the year 844 that in Rajab of that year his letter arrived, describing the hardship the Muslims in Granada were suffering from the Christians of Cordoba and Seville, and requesting aid."@en .

rec:AIND-D04632 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04632-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04632-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04632 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن يحيى بن عثمان بن عيسى بن عمر بن علي بن سلامة البيتليدي المقدسي ثم الصالحي نزيل الضيائية . ولد في سنة ست وسبعين وسبعمائة وسمع من لفظ المحب الصامت التاسع من مسند المقلين من الصحابة من حديث أبي الطاهر الذهلي وحدث به سمعه منه الفضلاء . ومات في حدود سنة أربعين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā b. ʿUthmān b. ʿĪsā b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Salāma, al-Baytlīdī al-Maqdisī, then al-Ṣāliḥī, resident of al-Ḍiyāʾiyya. He was born in the year 776. He heard from the dictation of al-Muḥibb al-Ṣāmit the ninth part of the Musnad al-Muqillīn min al-Ṣaḥāba from the ḥadīth of Abū al-Ṭāhir al-Dhuhlī, and he transmitted it; the eminent scholars heard it from him. He died around the year 840, presumably."@en .

rec:AIND-D04633 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04633-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04633-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04633 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد بن التقي تقي الدين بن قاضي الشام العز الدمشقي الحنبلي . درس بعد أبيه فلم ينجب ثم ولي القضاء بعد الفتنة بطرابلس . ومات في رمضان سنة خمس عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. al-Taqī (Taqī al-Dīn) b. Qāḍī al-Shām, al-ʿIzz al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanbalī. He taught after his father but did not distinguish himself; then, after the fitna, he was appointed to the judgeship in Tripoli. He died in Ramaḍān of the year 815."@en .

rec:AIND-D04636 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04636-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04636-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04636 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد الجمال القرافي . أخذ عن أبي الحسن الأندلسي العربية ومهر فيها وعمل مقدمة لطيفة يتوصل بها إلى معرفة الإعراب بأسهل طريق وانتفع به جماعة منهم شيخنا ابن خضر وولي مشيخة الطنبدية±±± بالصحراء مات في ربيع الأول سنة ست وعشرين وأظن المتلقى للطنبذية±±± عنه شيخنا الحناوي ، وترجمه شيخنا في إنبائه باختصار ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad, al-Jamāl al-Qarāfī. He took Arabic grammar from Abū al-Ḥasan al-Andalusī and became proficient in it, and he composed a fine introduction by which one reaches knowledge of iʿrāb by the easiest route. A number of people benefited from him, among them our shaykh Ibn Khiḍr. He held the shaykhship of al-Ṭanbadiyya in the Ṣaḥrāʾ (the desert cemetery of Cairo). He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 826. I think the one who took over al-Ṭanbadiyya after him was our shaykh al-Ḥannāwī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) gave him a brief biography in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04637 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04637-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04637-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04637 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد الجمال المارديني ويعرف بتمنع . قال شيخنا في الإنباء كان من أولاد الأغنياء فورث مالا جزيلا فأنفقه في الخيرات ثم افتقر فصار يكدى بالأوراق وينظم البيتين في ذلك أحيانا وكان يعاشر الرؤساء وللعز الموصلي فيه نظم . مات في رمضان سنة ست بدمشق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad, al-Jamāl al-Māridīnī, known as Tamannuʿ. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in al-Inbāʾ: \"He was one of the sons of the wealthy and inherited abundant property, which he spent on charitable works; then he became poor and took to begging with written petitions, sometimes composing a couplet on the matter. He used to keep company with the notables, and al-ʿIzz al-Mawṣilī has verses about him.\" He died in Ramaḍān of the year 806 in Damascus."@en .

rec:AIND-D04640 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04640-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04640-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04640 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد العفيف اليماني الجلاد . مات سنة إحدى وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad, al-ʿAfīf al-Yamānī al-Jallād. He died in the year 831."@en .

rec:AIND-D04641 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04641-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04641-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04641 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد البطيني ثم القاهري مؤدب الأبناء بالمنكوتمرية . ممن سمع مني وحج وجاور سنة ست وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Buṭaynī, then al-Qāhirī, tutor of the boys at al-Mankūtamuriyya. He is among those who heard from me; he performed the pilgrimage and stayed as a mujāwir in the year 896."@en .

rec:AIND-D04642 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04642-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04642-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04642 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد البهنسي . فيمن جده عبد الله بن حسن بن يوسف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Bahnasī. See among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥasan b. Yūsuf."@en .

rec:AIND-D04643 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04643-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04643-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04643 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد الساعاتي المؤذن بالجامع الأموي انتهت إليه الرياسة في فنه . مات في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وقد قارب الثمانين . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Sāʿātī, the muezzin at the Umayyad Mosque. Leadership in his craft came to rest with him. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 801, having nearly reached eighty. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04644 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04644-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04644-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04644 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد الطيماني . فيمن جده طيمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Ṭaymānī. See among those whose grandfather is Ṭaymān."@en .

rec:AIND-D04645 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04645-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04645-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04645 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد الظفاري المكي دلال الرقيق ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Ẓafārī al-Makkī, the slave broker. He is among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04646 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04646-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04646-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04646 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد القاري الشافعي خطيب القارة. ذكره التقي بن فهد في معجمه مجردا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Qārī al-Shāfiʿī, the preacher (khaṭīb) of al-Qāra. Al-Taqī b. Fahd mentioned him in his Muʿjam by name only."@en .

rec:AIND-D04647 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04647-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04647-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04647 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد القليجي . شهد على بعض الحنفية في إجازة سنة إحدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Qulījī. He attested as a witness for one of the Hanafis on an ijāza in the year 801."@en .

rec:AIND-D04648 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04648-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04648-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04648 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد الكاهلي الفقيه الصالح . مات بمدينة أب سنة عشر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Kāhilī, the pious jurist. He died in the town of Ibb in the year 810."@en .

rec:AIND-D04649 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04649-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04649-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04649 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد الهمداني الدمشقي الحنفي مدرس الجوهرية بدمشق كان خيرا عارفا بمذهبه وبالقراءات ويقرئ . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة عشر وقد بلغ السبعين . قاله شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Hamdānī al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanafī, professor at al-Jawhariyya in Damascus. He was a good man, versed in his madhhab and in the Qurʾānic readings, and he taught recitation. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 810, having reached seventy. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said so in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04650 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04650-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04650-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04650 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن محمد الواسطي الشافعي . ذكره التقي بن فهد في معجمه مجردا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad al-Wāsiṭī al-Shāfiʿī. Al-Taqī b. Fahd mentioned him in his Muʿjam by name only."@en .

rec:AIND-D04653 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04653-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04653-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b91_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04653 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن منصور الوجدي التلمساني المغربي السقا بالحرم . مات بمكة ببيمارستانها بالاستسقاء في جمادى الأولى سنة خمس وخمسين ودفن بالشبيكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Manṣūr al-Wajdī al-Tilimsānī al-Maghribī, the water-carrier at the Ḥaram. He died in Mecca, in its hospital (bīmāristān), of dropsy in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 855, and was buried in al-Shabīka."@en .

rec:AIND-D04654 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04654-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04654-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04654-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04654-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04654 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن نجيب بن عبد الله الشرف الحلبي ناظر الجيش بها ويعرف بابن النجيب كان انسانا حسنا دينا عاقلا ساكنا رئيسا جسيما محبا للفقراء والصالحين . مات في قلعة الروم سنة ثلاث . ذكره ابن خطيب الناصرية مطولا وتبعه شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Najīb b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Sharaf al-Ḥalabī, the army inspector (nāẓir al-jaysh) there [in Aleppo], known as Ibn al-Najīb. He was a good, pious, sensible and calm man, a stout man of leading stature, who loved the poor and the righteous. He died in Qalʿat al-Rūm in the year [8]03. Ibn Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya mentioned him at length, and our shaykh [Ibn Ḥajar] followed him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04657 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04657-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04657-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04657 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن يوسف بن علي بن خلد الحسناوي البجائي المغربي المالكي لقيني بالمدينة النبوية فأخذ عني الألفية الحديثية بحثا وغيرها ثم بالقاهرة فقرأ علي الموطأ بتمامه وحمل عني فيهما وفي مكة أيضا جملة وكتبت له إجازة حافلة ، ورجع إلى بلاده وهو من الفضلاء الخيار المتقنين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf b. ʿAlī b. Khald al-Ḥasanāwī al-Bijāʾī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī. He met me [al-Sakhāwī] in Medina, the Prophet's city, and took from me the Alfiyya of ḥadīth by way of critical study, and other works; then in Cairo he read to me the Muwaṭṭaʾ in its entirety, and he transmitted a great deal from me in both places and in Mecca as well. I wrote him a copious ijāza. He returned to his country. He is one of the excellent, choice and precise scholars."@en .

rec:AIND-D04658 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04658-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04658-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04658 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن يوسف البغدادي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf al-Baghdādī. One of those who heard from me [al-Sakhāwī] in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04659 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04659-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04659-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04659 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله بن الجمال الحرازي . فيمن اسم أبيه محمد بن أحمد بن أبي الفضل بن عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Jamāl al-Ḥarāzī. [See] under those whose father's name is Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Abī al-Faḍl b. ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D04661 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04661-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04661-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04661 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله الجمال التركماني الحنفي إمام قجماس نائب الشام . كان ولي كتابة سر حلب ونظر جيشها وقلعتها ومرستانها بعد رضي الدين بن منصور ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Jamāl al-Turkumānī al-Ḥanafī, imam of Qajmās, the viceroy of Syria. He held the office of confidential secretary (kitābat al-sirr) of Aleppo and the supervision of its army, its citadel and its hospital, after Raḍī al-Dīn b. Manṣūr."@en .

rec:AIND-D04665 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04665-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04665-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04665 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله ويعرف بحاجي بهادر الأزبكي الجلالي عتيق جلال الدين مسعود بن أصيل الدين جعفر البنجيري . لقيه الطاووسي في سنة ثمان عشرة وثمانمائة فاستجازه وأخبره أنه حينئذ ناف على التسعين وقال أنه كان من الملازمين لجدي وعمي وسمع معهما أكثر ما سمعاه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh, known as Ḥājjī Bahādur, al-Azbakī al-Jalālī, freedman of Jalāl al-Dīn Masʿūd b. Aṣīl al-Dīn Jaʿfar al-Banjīrī. Al-Ṭāwūsī met him in the year 818 and asked him for an ijāza; he told him that he was then over ninety, and said that he had been one of those who constantly attended \"my [al-Ṭāwūsī's] grandfather and my uncle\" and had heard with them most of what they heard."@en .

rec:AIND-D04666 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04666-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04666-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04666 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله الأرغوني الرومي ويعرف بالأشرفي . مات سنة سبع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Arghūnī al-Rūmī, known as al-Ashrafī. He died in the year 837."@en .

rec:AIND-D04667 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04667-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04667-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04667 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله الأشخر بمعجمتين اليماني . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة إحدى وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Ashkhar — with two dotted letters — al-Yamānī. He died in Mecca in Muḥarram of the year 851. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04669 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04669-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04669-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04669 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله البصري الشهير بابن الفخر . مات بمكة في شوال سنة إحدى وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد وكان خيرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī, famed as Ibn al-Fakhr. He died in Mecca in Shawwāl of the year 881. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date; he was a good man."@en .

rec:AIND-D04671 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04671-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04671-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04671 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله الحبشي المكي فتى العذول . أحسن سيده تربيته وأقرأه القرآن وكتبا جمة أجاد حفظها وعرضها علي في جملة الجماعة بل وسمع علي أشياء وكان ذكيا . مات في ليلة الثلاثاء سادس جمادى الثانية سنة خمس وتسعين عند بلوغه عوضه الله وسيده الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥabashī al-Makkī, the slave-boy (fatā) of al-ʿAdhūl. His master brought him up well and taught him the Qurʾān and a great many books, which he memorized excellently and recited from memory (ʿaraḍa) to me [al-Sakhāwī] among the group; indeed he also heard several things from me. He was intelligent. He died on the eve of Tuesday, the sixth of Jumādā II of the year 895, on reaching maturity. May God compensate him and his master with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D04672 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04672-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04672-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04672 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله الذاكر . قدم من الروم فقطن دمشق واعتقده الناس وتسلك به المريدون كأبي بكر بن عبد الله العداس . مات في سنة إحدى عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Dhākir. He came from al-Rūm and settled in Damascus; people held him in devout esteem, and disciples took the Sufi path under him, such as Abū Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAddās. He died in the year 811."@en .

rec:AIND-D04673 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04673-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04673-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04673 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله الرومي نزيل البيبرسية . ممن أثبت شيخنا اسمه فيمن سمعه منه في الأمالي القديمة ووصفه بالشيخ ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Rūmī, resident of al-Baybarsiyya. He is one of those whose name our shaykh [Ibn Ḥajar] recorded among those who heard from him in the early Amālī, describing him as \"the Shaykh\"."@en .

rec:AIND-D04674 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04674-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04674-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04674 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله الزرعي الشيخ الصالح القدوة . مات ببيت المقدس سنة ثمان وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Zarʿī, the pious and exemplary shaykh. He died in Bayt al-Maqdis [Jerusalem] in the year 848."@en .

rec:AIND-D04675 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04675-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04675-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04675-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04675 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله السحولي المكي أحد المباركين المنقطع برباط ربيع منها . مات بها في صفر سنة ستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Saḥūlī al-Makkī, one of the blessed men, who lived in seclusion at Ribāṭ Rabīʿ there [in Mecca]. He died there in Ṣafar of the year 860. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04676 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04676-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04676-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04676 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله الطائفي العلائي . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة تسع وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṭāʾifī al-ʿAlāʾī. He died in Jumādā I of the year 859. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04677 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04677-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04677-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04677-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_verify,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04677 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله القرافي السعودي ويعرف بالأصيفر . أحد من لكثير من الناس حتى السلطان فيه اعتقاد . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وخمسين وصلى عليه بجامع محمود من القرافة ودفن رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Qarāfī al-Saʿūdī, known as al-Uṣayfir. He was one of those in whom many people, even the Sultan, placed devout belief. He died in Rabīʿ II of the year 852; the funeral prayer was performed over him at the Mosque of Maḥmūd in al-Qarāfa, and he was buried, may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04678 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04678-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04678-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04678 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله القليني المغربي المالكي . مات في المحرم سنة تسع وسبعين بمفرش النعام في رجوعه من الحج وكان يذكر بالفضل رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Qulaynī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī. He died in Muḥarram of the year 879 at Mafrash al-Naʿām, on his way back from the pilgrimage. He used to be mentioned for his excellence, may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04679 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04679-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04679-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04679 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله المغربي المعروف بالبجائي كان مباركا كثير التلاوة للقرآن يجهر في ذلك في المسجد وعلى قراءته أنس . مات في أوائل سنة ثلاث بمكة بعد مجاورته بها سنين على طريقة حسنة . ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Maghribī, known as al-Bijāʾī. He was a blessed man who recited the Qurʾān much, doing so aloud in the mosque, and there was a charm in his recitation. He died at the beginning of the year [8]03 in Mecca, after having sojourned there (mujāwara) for years in a fine manner. Al-Fāsī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04680 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04680-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04680-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04680 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله المكناسي المغربي ويعرف بابن أحمد أحد أجداده . كان عالما ممن غلب عليه الصلاح والتصوف أخذ عنه جماعة منهم أبو عبد الله الفوري . مات بعد الأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Miknāsī al-Maghribī, known as Ibn Aḥmad after one of his ancestors. He was a scholar in whom piety and Sufism predominated. A number of people learned from him, among them Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Fawrī. He died after [8]40."@en .

rec:AIND-D04681 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04681-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04681-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b92_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04681 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله الناشري اليمني نزيل مكة . مات بها في المحرم سنة ست وثمانين . ودفن بالمعلاة رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Nāshirī al-Yamanī, resident of Mecca. He died there in Muḥarram of the year 886, and was buried at al-Muʿallā, may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04682 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04682-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04682-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04682 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الله اليماني الأعرج بواب باب السلام من حرم مكة . مات في صفر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd Allāh al-Yamānī al-Aʿraj, gatekeeper of Bāb al-Salām of the Sacred Precinct (Ḥaram) of Mecca. He died in Ṣafar."@en .

rec:AIND-D04683 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04683-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04683-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04683-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04683 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المجيب بن أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن سبط عبد المجيب أحد خدام سيدي أحمد البدوي ويعرف بالكريدي ، ولي مشيخة المقام في صفر سنة اثنتين وستين ولم يلبث أن مات شابا في ربيع الآخر سنة أربع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Mujīb b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, daughter's son of ʿAbd al-Mujīb, one of the servants of Sīdī Aḥmad al-Badawī, and known as al-Kuraydī. He was appointed to the shaykhship of the shrine (al-maqām) in Ṣafar (8)62, but did not remain long and died young in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir (8)64."@en .

rec:AIND-D04685 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04685-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04685-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04685 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المجيد بن علي بن محمد بن أحمد بن حسن بن الزين محمد بن الأمين محمد ابن القطب محمد بن أحمد بن علي القسطلاني . أجاز له في سنة ست وثلاثين جماعة . ذكره ابن فهد وبيض له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Majīd b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. al-Zayn Muḥammad b. al-Amīn Muḥammad b. al-Quṭb Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Qasṭallānī. In (8)36 a group of scholars granted him an ijāza. Ibn Fahd mentioned him and left a blank space for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04687 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04687-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04687-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04687 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المجيد الشاعر الأديب صاحب قصة يوسف المسماة مؤنس العشاق بالتركي وهي من أطرف ما صنف قاله ابن عرب شاه وهو ممن لقيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Majīd, the poet and man of letters, author of the story of Joseph entitled Muʾnis al-ʿUshshāq in Turkish, which is among the most delightful works ever composed. So said Ibn ʿArab Shāh, who was among those who met him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04691 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04691-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04691-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04691 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المحسن بن علي بن عمر اليماني الماضي أخوه عبد الرؤف والآتي أبوهما وابن أخيهما عبد المغني بن أبي الفتح من بيت صلاح وشهرة . مات بجدة ولهم قبة بها فيها قبره وقبر ابن أخيه وغيرهما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Muḥsin b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar al-Yamānī. His brother ʿAbd al-Raʾūf was mentioned above; their father and their nephew ʿAbd al-Mughnī b. Abī al-Fatḥ will be mentioned below. They were of a house of piety and renown. He died in Judda, where they have a domed mausoleum containing his grave, the grave of his nephew, and others."@en .

rec:AIND-D04693 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04693-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04693-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04693 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المحسن البغدادي ثم المكي شيخ صالح معتقد . مات بها في صفر سنة ثمان وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Muḥsin al-Baghdādī, then al-Makkī, a pious shaykh held in veneration. He died there (in Mecca) in Ṣafar (8)48."@en .

rec:AIND-D04694 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04694-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04694-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04694 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المعطي بن أحمد بن المحب أبي الحسين الشيرازي الأصل المدني أخو محمد الآتي ويعرف بابن المحب . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī b. Aḥmad b. al-Muḥibb Abī al-Ḥusayn, of Shīrāzī origin, the Medinan, brother of Muḥammad who will be mentioned below, and known as Ibn al-Muḥibb. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D04697 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04697-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04697-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04697 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المعطي المدعو عبيد بن نور الدين علي بن الزين العمري القاهري المرخم . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī, called ʿUbayd, son of Nūr al-Dīn ʿAlī b. al-Zayn al-ʿUmarī al-Qāhirī al-Murakhkhim (the marble-worker). He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D04699 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04699-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04699-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04699 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المعطي بن محمد بن أحمد بن أبي بكر الفوي الأصل القاهري الآتي أبوه . ممن تنزل في الجهات وحضر عندي قليلا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr, of Fuwwa origin, the Cairene; his father will be mentioned below. He was among those who held stipendiary posts in the endowed institutions, and attended my sessions a little."@en .

rec:AIND-D04700 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04700-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04700-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04700 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المعطي بن أبي الفضل محمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن عبد المعطي الأنصاري المكي . مات بها في جمادى الآخرة سنة أربع وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī b. Abī al-Faḍl Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī al-Anṣārī al-Makkī. He died there (in Mecca) in Jumādā al-Ākhira (8)74. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04704 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04704-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04704-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04704 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المغيث بن محمد بن أحمد بن الطواب . باشر في كثير من المظالم وكان قد سمع على شيخنا في سنة أربعين وقبلها في الدار قطني وغيره . مات ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Mughīth b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Ṭawwāb. He was engaged in the administration of many maẓālim (affairs). He had heard the Dāraquṭnī and other works under our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in (8)40 and before that. He died ..."@en .

rec:AIND-D04712 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04712-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04712-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04712 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الملك بن الكمال أبي الفضل محمد بن السراج عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن يوسف الزرندي المدني الشافعي . مات بالمدينة في أول صفر سنة سبع وستين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Malik b. al-Kamāl Abī al-Faḍl Muḥammad b. al-Sirāj ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf al-Zarandī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī. He died in Medina at the beginning of Ṣafar (8)67, may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04719 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04719-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04719-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04719 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المنعم بن محمود بن علي المليجي ثم القاهري . ممن أخذ عن شيخنا في الأمالي وغيرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Munʿim b. Maḥmūd b. ʿAlī al-Malījī, then al-Qāhirī. He was among those who studied the Amālī and other works under our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04721 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04721-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04721-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04721 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المهدي بن أحمد بن عبد المهدي بن علي بن جعفر المشعري المكي مات بها في ذي الحجة سنة سبع وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Mahdī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Mahdī b. ʿAlī b. Jaʿfar al-Mishʿarī al-Makkī. He died there (in Mecca) in Dhū al-Ḥijja (8)57. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04722 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04722-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04722-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04722 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المؤمن بن عبد الدائم بن علي السمنودي ويعرف بمؤمن واسمه فيما قال محمد . ممن جاور بمكة سنين على طريقة حسنة يؤدب الأطفال . مات بها بعد الحج سنة سبع وترك ذرية من ابنة يوسف القروي . ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Muʾmin b. ʿAbd al-Dāʾim b. ʿAlī al-Samannūdī, known as Muʾmin; his name, according to what he himself said, was Muḥammad. He was among those who sojourned in Mecca for years, leading a good life and teaching children. He died there after the Ḥajj of (8)07, leaving offspring by the daughter of Yūsuf al-Qarawī. Al-Fāsī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04723 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04723-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04723-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04723 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد المؤمن بن عبد الرحيم صفي الدين الشرواني الشافعي خال عبد المحسن ابن عبد الصمد الآتي . أخذ عنه ابن أخته الفقه والنحو والمنطق وغيرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Muʾmin b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm, Ṣafī al-Dīn al-Shirwānī al-Shāfiʿī, maternal uncle of ʿAbd al-Muḥsin b. ʿAbd al-Ṣamad who will be mentioned below. His sister's son studied jurisprudence, grammar, logic and other subjects under him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04727 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04727-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04727-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04727 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الناصر بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الوهاب بن أحمد أبو الطيب المحلي الآتي أبوه ويعرف بابن الشيخ . ولد في ذي الحجة سنة أربع وعشرين وثمانمائة وحفظ مختصر أبي شجاع والرحبية وبعض القرآن وتكسب بالشهادة وتميز فيها مع ديانة وخير وهو الآن في الأحياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Nāṣir b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Aḥmad, Abū al-Ṭayyib al-Maḥallī; his father will be mentioned below. He is known as Ibn al-Shaykh. He was born in Dhū al-Ḥijja 824, memorized the Mukhtaṣar of Abū Shujāʿ, the Raḥabiyya and part of the Qurʾān, earned his living as a notary witness and distinguished himself in it, with piety and goodness. He is now among the living."@en .

rec:AIND-D04728 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04728-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04728-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04728-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04728 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الناصر بن جلال الدين محمد المحلي الخطيب أبوه بجامع الطريني بها . كان ممن قرأ علي وعارضه ابن الطريني بعد أبيه في الخطابة وسمعت أنه عمل جامعا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Nāṣir b. Jalāl al-Dīn Muḥammad al-Maḥallī; his father was the preacher (khaṭīb) at the Jāmiʿ al-Ṭurīnī there (in al-Maḥalla). He was among those who read to me (al-Sakhāwī), and Ibn al-Ṭurīnī contested the preachership with him after his father. I heard that he built a congregational mosque."@en .

rec:AIND-D04735 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04735-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04735-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04735 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الهادي بن محمد بن عمر البسطامي . مات في ذي القعدة سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Hādī b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar al-Bisṭāmī. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda (8)57."@en .

rec:AIND-D04737 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04737-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04737-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b93_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04737 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الواحد بن إبراهيم بن عبد الواحد المرشدي المكي حفيد الذي قبله . حفظ القرآن وجوده . ومات شابا في حياة أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Murshidī al-Makkī, grandson of the preceding entry. He memorized the Qurʾān and perfected its recitation. He died young, during his father's lifetime."@en .

rec:AIND-D04738 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04738-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04738-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04738 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الواحد أخ له . ولد بعد موته وموت أبيه بحيث سمي باسمه . ممن سمع مني بمكة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, a brother of his (the preceding entry). He was born after the latter's death and after their father's death, so that he was given his name. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04739 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04739-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04739-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04739 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الواحد بن أحمد بن عيسى القرشي المكي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ومكة وكان قد دخل مع أبيه القاهرة ثم بعد ذلك أيضا وسافر منها إلى الشام فمات بها في الطاعون في سنة سبع وتسعين عوضه الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. Aḥmad b. ʿĪsā, al-Qurashī al-Makkī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo and Mecca. He had entered Cairo with his father, and again after that, and travelled from there to Syria (al-Shām), where he died of the plague in (8)97. May God compensate him with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D04740 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04740-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04740-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04740 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الواحد بن حسن بن محمد الطيبي ثم القاهري الأزهري الشافعي شقيق محمد الآتي واشتغل ولازم زكريا وهو من قدماء جماعته وكان مجاورا بمكة في سنة ثمان وتسعين ويجلس شاهدا بباب السلام وهي حرفته بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. Ḥasan b. Muḥammad, al-Ṭayyibī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Azharī, al-Shāfiʿī, full brother of Muḥammad who will be mentioned below. He pursued his studies and attached himself to Zakariyyā, being one of the senior members of his circle. In (8)98 he was residing as a mujāwir in Mecca, sitting as a notary witness (shāhid) at Bāb al-Salām, which is his trade in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04742 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04742-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04742-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04742 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الواحد بن عبد الله بن أبي بكر الزبيدي الحكمي اليماني الفقيه ويعرف بالقلقل . مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة خمس وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr, al-Zabīdī al-Ḥakamī al-Yamānī, the jurist (faqīh), known as al-Qulqul. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja (8)45."@en .

rec:AIND-D04743 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04743-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04743-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04743 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الواحد بن عبد الحميد بن مسعود . في همام لكونه بها أشهر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd b. Masʿūd. [See] under Humām, since he is better known by that name."@en .

rec:AIND-D04744 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04744-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04744-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04744-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04744 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الواحد بن عبد الوهاب بن المحب محمد بن علي بن يوسف الزرندي المدني الحنفي أخو عبد السلام الماضي . ولد سنة أربعين تقريبا وسمع على الجمال الكازروني وأبي الفتح المراغي وأخيه أبي الفرج وغيرهم وقدم القاهرة مرارا وسافر لحلب وغيرها وتردد إلي كثيرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. al-Muḥibb Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf, al-Zarandī al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī, brother of ʿAbd al-Salām mentioned above. He was born in about (8)40 and heard from al-Jamāl al-Kāzarūnī, Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī and the latter's brother Abū al-Faraj, among others. He came to Cairo many times, travelled to Aleppo and elsewhere, and frequented me (al-Sakhāwī) often."@en .

rec:AIND-D04747 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04747-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04747-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04747-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04747 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الواحد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد الله الدميري المكي ابن أخي عبد الكريم بن محمد الماضي . مات بها في رجب سنة خمس وثمانين ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Damīrī al-Makkī, nephew (brother's son) of ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad mentioned above. He died there (in Mecca) in Rajab (8)85; Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04748 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04748-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04748-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04748-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04748 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الواحد بن موسى بن يوسف بن عبد الواد . مات سنة ثلاث وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. Mūsā b. Yūsuf b. ʿAbd al-Wād. He died in (8)33."@en .

rec:AIND-D04749 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04749-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04749-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04749 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الواحد المجافضي . مات سنة اثنتين وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Mujāfiḍī. He died in (8)32."@en .

rec:AIND-D04750 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04750-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04750-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04750 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوارث بن محمد بن عبد الوارث البكري المصري المالكي أخو النور علي الآتي . مات في المحرم سنة أربع عشرة بينبع في رجوعه من الحج ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wārith b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wārith, al-Bakrī al-Miṣrī al-Mālikī, brother of al-Nūr ʿAlī who will be mentioned below. He died in Muḥarram (8)14 at Yanbuʿ on his way back from the pilgrimage."@en .

rec:AIND-D04754 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04754-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04754-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04754 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الولي بن محمد بن جمال الدين ولي الدين ويسمى محمدا وهو بعبد الولي أشهر الواسطي العراقي نزيل جامع الغمري بالقاهرة ويعرف في بلاده بابن الزيتوني رجل خير فقير يتلو القرآن ، كان يذكر أنه لقي شيخنا وغيره وأكثر من حضور الأمالي وغيرها عندي . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة ست وثمانين وأظنه زاد على السبعين . رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Walī b. Muḥammad b. Jamāl al-Dīn, Walī al-Dīn; he is also called Muḥammad, but is better known as ʿAbd al-Walī. Al-Wāsiṭī al-ʿIrāqī, resident of the Jāmiʿ al-Ghamrī in Cairo, and known in his homeland as Ibn al-Zaytūnī. A good, poor man who recited the Qurʾān. He used to say that he had met our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others, and he attended the Amālī and other sessions with me (al-Sakhāwī) frequently. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir (8)86; I think he was over seventy. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04759 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04759-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04759-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04759-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04759-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04759 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن أحمد الدمشقي خطيب حجراء . كتب على استدعاء فيه بعض الأولاد سنة ثلاث وسبعين وما علمت شيئا من حاله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Aḥmad al-Dimashqī, preacher (khaṭīb) of Ḥujrāʾ. He wrote (an ijāza) on a petition (istidʿāʾ) listing some children in (8)73, and I know nothing of his circumstances."@en .

rec:AIND-D04761 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04761-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04761-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04761 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن إسماعيل المجد التدمري الخليلي خطيب حرم الخليل عليه السلام . مات في ليلة الأحد عاشر ربيع الأول سنة تسعين ودفن صبيحتها بتربة والده في منزله رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Ismāʿīl, al-Majd al-Tadmurī al-Khalīlī, preacher (khaṭīb) of the Sanctuary of al-Khalīl (Abraham, peace be upon him). He died on the night of Sunday 10 Rabīʿ al-Awwal (8)90 and was buried the next morning in his father's tomb (turba) in his own house. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04762 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04762-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04762-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04762 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن أفتكين تاج الدين كاتب السر بدمشق . مات في ذي القعدة سنة ست وثلاثين ودفن بمقبرة باب توما . أرخه ابن اللبودي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Aftakīn, Tāj al-Dīn, confidential secretary (kātib al-sirr) in Damascus. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda (8)36 and was buried in the cemetery of Bāb Tūmā. Ibn al-Labūdī recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04766 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04766-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04766-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04766-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04766 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن أبي بكر التاج الدمشقي الحنفي بن الحمال بالحاء المهملة والتشديد أحد نواب الحكم بدمشق . مات بها في سلخ شوال سنة سبع وخمسين ودفن من الغد بمقبرة باب الفراديس رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Abī Bakr, al-Tāj al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanafī, Ibn al-Ḥammāl (with undotted ḥāʾ and shadda), one of the deputy judges (nuwwāb al-ḥukm) in Damascus. He died there on the last day of Shawwāl (8)57 and was buried the next day in the cemetery of Bāb al-Farādīs. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04767 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04767-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04767-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04767-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04767 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن حمزة بن عبد الغني بن يعقوب التاج بن الشرف بن الفخر أحد كتاب المماليك كأبيه ويعرف كهو بابن فحيرة تصغير جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Ḥamza b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Yaʿqūb, al-Tāj b. al-Sharaf b. al-Fakhr, one of the clerks of the Mamluks (kuttāb al-mamālīk) like his father, and known, like him, as Ibn Fuḥayra, a diminutive of his grandfather's (title)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04770 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04770-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04770-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04770 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن صدقة القوصوني القاهري الطبيب والد الرئيس الشمس محمد . ممن برع في الطب وتخرج به جماعة منهم قريبه العلاء علي بن فتح الدين ابن قجاجق . ومات سنة خمس وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Ṣadaqa, al-Qūṣūnī al-Qāhirī, the physician, father of al-Raʾīs (the chief physician) al-Shams Muḥammad. He was among those who excelled in medicine, and a number of people trained under him, among them his relative al-ʿAlāʾ ʿAlī b. Fatḥ al-Dīn Ibn Qajājiq. He died in (8)35."@en .

rec:AIND-D04772 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04772-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04772-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04772-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04772 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن عبد الرحمن بن الخواجا شمس العقعق محمد بن محمد بن يوسف البصري الأصل المكي . ولد بها ونشأ وحفظ القرآن والمنهاج وغيره ، وجلس في دار الإمارة للتكسب ، وسافر في التجارة ودخل الشام وحلب وغيرهما . مات في المحرم ظنا سنة خمس وثمانين بين البندر الجديد وبندر زيلع . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Khawājā Shams al-ʿAqʿaq Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf, of Baṣran origin, al-Makkī. He was born and grew up there (in Mecca), and memorized the Qurʾān, the Minhāj and other works. He set up in the Dār al-Imāra to earn his living, and travelled for trade, entering Syria (al-Shām), Aleppo and other places. He died, probably in Muḥarram (8)85, between al-Bandar al-Jadīd and the port of Zaylaʿ. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04776 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04776-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04776-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04776-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04776 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن عبد الله بن جمال بن غنايم بن سليم البطناوي الدمشقي ويعرف بابن الجمال . ولد بعد سنة خمس وثمانين وسبعمائة وأخبر أنه صلى وراء أبي هريرة بن الذهبي ولكن لا يستحضر سماعا عليه ولا إجازة ، وكان حيا في سنة تسع وخمسين واستجازه البقاعي لظنه سماعه وما أحببت ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Jamāl b. Ghanāyim b. Salīm, al-Baṭnāwī al-Dimashqī, known as Ibn al-Jamāl. He was born after 785. He reported that he had prayed behind Abū Hurayra b. al-Dhahabī, but did not recall any audition (samāʿ) or ijāza from him. He was still alive in (8)59, and al-Biqāʿī sought an ijāza from him, supposing that he had heard (from Abū Hurayra), which I (al-Sakhāwī) did not approve of."@en .

rec:AIND-D04779 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04779-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04779-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04779-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b94_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04779 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن عبد المؤمن بن عبد العزيز القرشي القاهري البزاز والد عبد القادر الماضي . كان ممن يكتب في الإملاء عن شيخنا بل كتب عن ابن زقاعة كثيرا من نظمه مع فضل وخير . مات في سنة خمس وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿAbd al-Muʾmin b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, al-Qurashī al-Qāhirī, the cloth merchant (bazzāz), father of ʿAbd al-Qādir mentioned above. He was among those who wrote down the dictation sessions (imlāʾ) of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and he also wrote down much of the poetry of Ibn Zuqqāʿa, along with merit and goodness. He died in (8)45."@en .

rec:AIND-D04784 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04784-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04784-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04784-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04784-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04784 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن عمر بن محمد التاج الزرعي ثم القاهري الحنفي نقيب شيخنا وأخو إبراهيم الماضي . اختص بابن الأشقر وأظن بسفارته استقر به شيخنا في نقابته بل كان الظاهر جقمق يميل إليه وكان عفيفا يرجع إلى ديانة ورغبة في الصدقة واعتقاد في الصالحين مع جموده . مات فيما أظن قريب الخمسين أو بعدها بقليل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad, al-Tāj al-Zurʿī, then al-Qāhirī, the Ḥanafī. He was the naqīb of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and the brother of Ibrāhīm, mentioned above. He was closely attached to Ibn al-Ashqar, and I think it was through his mediation that our shaykh installed him in his office of naqīb; indeed, al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq was inclined towards him. He was chaste, with a leaning to piety, a desire for almsgiving and a belief in the righteous, though he was dull. He died, I think, around [8]50 or a little after."@en .

rec:AIND-D04785 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04785-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04785-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04785-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04785 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن أبي بكر تاج الدين الخليلي الموقت والد عبد العزيز الماضي . مات سنة أربع وسبعين فيما قاله لي ولده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. Abī Bakr, Tāj al-Dīn al-Khalīlī, the muwaqqit (timekeeper), father of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, mentioned above. He died in the year [8]74, according to what his son told me."@en .

rec:AIND-D04791 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04791-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04791-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04791-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04791 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب بن المحب محمد بن النور علي بن يوسف التاج الزرندي المدني الشافعي كأبيه أخو عمر ومحمد الآتيين . سمع على الزين أبي بكر المراغي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. al-Muḥibb Muḥammad b. al-Nūr ʿAlī b. Yūsuf, al-Tāj al-Zarandī al-Madanī, a Shāfiʿī like his father, brother of ʿUmar and Muḥammad, both mentioned below. He heard (ḥadīth) from al-Zayn Abū Bakr al-Marāghī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04804 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04804-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04804-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04804 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب تاج الدين الدمشقي ثم القاهري خليفة المقام الأحمدي بطنتدا ووالد سالم الماضي . مات بها فجأة في جمادى الآخرة سنة ست وستين ودفن هناك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb Tāj al-Dīn al-Dimashqī, then al-Qāhirī, the khalīfa (successor-custodian) of al-Maqām al-Aḥmadī at Ṭanṭadā, and the father of Sālim, mentioned above. He died there suddenly in Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year [8]66 and was buried there."@en .

rec:AIND-D04805 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04805-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04805-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04805 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب اليمني الزبيدي ويعرف بالحربي بفتح الحاء المهملة ثم راء ساكنة . مات في المحرم سنة أربع وخمسين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Yamanī al-Zabīdī, known as al-Ḥarbī (with fatḥa on the undotted ḥāʾ, then a vowelless rāʾ). He died in Muḥarram of the year [8]54 in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04806 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04806-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04806-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04806 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبد الوهاب فخر الدين رأس الرافضة . مات سنة خمس وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbd al-Wahhāb Fakhr al-Dīn, the head of the Rāfiḍa (Shīʿīs). He died in the year [8]65."@en .

rec:AIND-D04807 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04807-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04807-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04807-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04807 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبدون بن عبد الوهاب بن أحمد الزين الطهويهي الأزهري . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAbdūn b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Aḥmad, al-Zayn al-Ṭahwayhī al-Azharī. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04812 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04812-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04812-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04812-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04812 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد الله بن محمود الشاشي . مات في سلخ ربيع الأول أو مستهل الثاني سنة خمس وتسعين وترجمته عندي بخط بعض الآخذين عنه ممن أخذ عني كما في حوادثها أو في حوادث التي بعدها مع موت يعقوب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd Allāh b. Maḥmūd al-Shāshī. He died at the end of Rabīʿ al-Awwal or at the beginning of Rabīʿ al-Thānī of the year [8]95. I have his biography, written in the hand of one of those who studied under him and who also studied under me, as it stands in the events of that year or of the following year, together with the death of Yaʿqūb."@en .

rec:AIND-D04813 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04813-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04813-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04813-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04813 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد الله بن بايزيد بن محمود الجلال السمرقندي . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة أربع وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد في ذيله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd Allāh b. Bāyazīd b. Maḥmūd, al-Jalāl al-Samarqandī. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year [8]44. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death in his Dhayl (supplement)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04814 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04814-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04814-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04814 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد الله بن يوسف التبريزي نزيل القاهرة ممن أخذ عن شيخنا رفيقا للعز عبد السلام البغدادي ووصفه شيخنا بالإمام العلامة الأوحد المحقق المفنن برهان الدين بن الإمام عز الدين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd Allāh b. Yūsuf al-Tabrīzī, resident of Cairo. He was among those who studied under our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), as a fellow student of al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-Salām al-Baghdādī. Our shaykh described him as \"the imām, the most learned, the unique, the verifier, the master of many disciplines, Burhān al-Dīn, son of the imām ʿIzz al-Dīn\"."@en .

rec:AIND-D04815 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04815-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04815-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04815-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04815 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد الله المنزلي المالكي المولى الأسود سمي والده عبد الرحمن . ولد سنة ثلاث عشرة وثمانمائة تقريبا لقيته بمجلس شيخنا فأنشد من لفظه وأنا أسمع قوله : %~% يقبل الأرض إجلالا لقدركم %~% عبد لنحوكم قد جره الشغف %~% %~% أسباب عدلك عنه الصرف قد منعت %~% فهل له من إضافات فينصرف %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd Allāh al-Manzilī, the Mālikī, the black mawlā (freedman). His father was named ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. He was born in about 813. I met him at the assembly of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and he recited from his own lips, while I listened, his verses: \"A servant kisses the ground in reverence for your high rank – a servant whom passion has drawn towards you. The causes of your turning away (ʿadl) from him have prevented his departure (ṣarf); so has he any additions (iḍāfāt) by which he might depart (yanṣarif)?\""@en .

rec:AIND-D04816 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04816-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04816-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04816-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04816 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد بن إبراهيم الزعفراني المقدم والد بركات الحريري ونزيل الكداشين . مات في ليلة سابع عشري صفر سنة إحدى وتسعين فجأة كأمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd b. Ibrāhīm al-Zaʿfarānī, al-muqaddam, father of Barakāt al-Ḥarīrī and resident of al-Kidāshīn. He died suddenly, like his mother, on the night of the 27th of Ṣafar of the year [8]91."@en .

rec:AIND-D04819 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04819-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04819-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04819-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04819 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد بن علي بن عبيد الزين التميمي الحنبلي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd b. ʿAlī b. ʿUbayd, al-Zayn al-Tamīmī, the Ḥanbalī. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04820 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04820-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04820-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04820-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04820-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04820 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد بن عمر بن محمد القرشي نسبة للقرشية من الغربية والد عبد الرحمن الماضي كان فيما بلغني ممن أخذ عن الزاهد وابن النقاش وكان أميا لكنه كان يعظ فيأتي بما يدل على فرط ذكاء . مات في ربيع الأول سنة سبع وستين وقد زاد على المائة بمقتضي ما كان يقوله رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Qurashī – the nisba refers to al-Qurashiyya in al-Gharbiyya – father of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, mentioned above. According to what reached me, he was among those who studied under al-Zāhid and Ibn al-Naqqāsh. He was illiterate, yet he used to preach, producing things that showed exceptional intelligence. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year [8]67, having passed one hundred years of age according to what he used to say, may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04822 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04822-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04822-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04822-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04822 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد بن يوسف بن حليمة ويعرف بابن حليمة . مات بمكة في ذي القعدة سنة أربع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd b. Yūsuf b. Ḥalīma, known as Ibn Ḥalīma. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year [8]74."@en .

rec:AIND-D04823 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04823-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04823-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04823 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد بن نجم الدين بن شهاب الدين السمرقندي القاضي . مات سنة خمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd b. Najm al-Dīn b. Shihāb al-Dīn al-Samarqandī, the qāḍī. He died in the year [8]50."@en .

rec:AIND-D04824 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04824-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04824-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04824-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04824 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد الدمياطي زوج البرلسية أحد المدولبين جاورنا وقتا . ومات في رجوعه من الحج بقبور الشهداء سنة خمس وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd al-Dimyāṭī, husband of al-Burlusiyya and one of the mudawlibīn (workshop owners). He was our neighbour for a time (or: he resided [in Mecca] as a mujāwir together with us for a time). He died on his return from the ḥajj at Qubūr al-Shuhadāʾ in the year [8]85."@en .

rec:AIND-D04825 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04825-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04825-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04825 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد الفيخراني . مات بمكة في حدود سنة أربعين ودفن بالمعلاة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd al-Faykharānī. He died in Mecca around the year [8]40 and was buried at al-Muʿallā. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04826 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04826-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04826-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04826 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد التفلي . كان مذكورا بالخير مات في رجب سنة أربع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd al-Taflī. He was spoken of for his goodness. He died in Rajab of the year [8]54."@en .

rec:AIND-D04827 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04827-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04827-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04827-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b95_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04827 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عبيد ويدعى عبد الغني بن كاتب الجيش الفخر بن الجيعان . كذا رأيته بخط الفخر بن ... فيمن سمع من شيخنا في أماليه القديمة وأظنه وهم في قوله ويدعى بل هو عبد الوهاب بن الفخر بن عبد الغني =380 above? ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUbayd, also called ʿAbd al-Ghanī, son of the army scribe al-Fakhr Ibn al-Jīʿān. Thus I saw it written in the hand of al-Fakhr b. … among those who heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his early Amālī; I think he erred in saying \"also called\", and that he is rather ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. al-Fakhr b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04828 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04828-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04828-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04828-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04828 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عتيق بن عتيق بن قاسم أبو بكر الكلاعي خطيب غرناطة ونحويها . مات في ثاني عشري ذي القعدة سنة اثنتين وخمسين . أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAtīq b. ʿAtīq b. Qāsim, Abū Bakr, al-Kalāʿī, the preacher (khaṭīb) of Granada and its grammarian. He died on 22 Dhu al-Qaʿda 852. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04831 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04831-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04831-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04831-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04831 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن إبراهيم بن علي بن حسان بن عبد الباقي الفخر المغربي الأصل المناوي نسبة لمنية الجمل ثم النبتيتي القاهري الشافعي . قرأ على قطعة من أول الترمذي وشرح على مجالس من البخاري وكذا قرأ على الديمي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Ḥassān b. ʿAbd al-Bāqī, al-Fakhr, of Maghribī origin, al-Munāwī (after Minyat al-Jamal), then al-Nabtītī, al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī. He read to me (al-Sakhāwī) a portion from the beginning of al-Tirmidhī and expounded (read) to me some sessions of al-Bukhārī. Likewise he read to al-Daymī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04836 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04836-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04836-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04836 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن أحمد بن عباس الطلخاوي الجوجري ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbbās al-Ṭalkhāwī al-Jawjarī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04837 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04837-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04837-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04837-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04837-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04837 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن الجمال المصري الأصل المكي . ولد بالهند ثم قطن مكة وصاهر يونس الزبيري على ابنته . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Jamāl, of Egyptian origin, al-Makkī. He was born in India, then settled in Mecca and became the son-in-law of Yūnus al-Zubayrī by marrying his daughter. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04838 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04838-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04838-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04838 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن أحمد بن عثمان بن أحمد الفخر الكشطوخي ثم القاهري الماضي أبوه . ممن حفظ القرآن وكتبا عرضها علي في آخرين وحضر بعض الدروس ثم لزم كأبيه خدمة تغري بردى الاستادار ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿUthmān b. Aḥmad, al-Fakhr, al-Kashṭūkhī, then al-Qāhirī. His father was mentioned above. He was among those who memorized the Qurʾān and some books and presented them to me (al-Sakhāwī) along with others, and he attended some lessons. Then, like his father, he devoted himself to the service of Taghrī Birdī al-Ustādār."@en .

rec:AIND-D04841 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04841-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04841-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04841 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن أحمد بن عثمان الفخر الصهرجتي ثم القاهري الأزهري الشافعي ممن لازم المناوي ثم الجوجري وقرأ عنده البخاري بل هو ممن سمع فيه بالظاهرية وتكسب بالشهادة في جامع الصالح وصاهر الديمي على ابنته وله منها أولاد مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿUthmān, al-Fakhr, al-Ṣahrajtī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Azharī, al-Shāfiʿī. He was among those who attended al-Munāwī and then al-Jawjarī, under whom he read al-Bukhārī; indeed he was among those who heard it at al-Ẓāhiriyya. He earned his living as a notary witness at the Mosque of al-Ṣāliḥ, married the daughter of al-Daymī and had children by her. He died."@en .

rec:AIND-D04842 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04842-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04842-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04842-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04842 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن أحمد بن أبي الغيث العفيف أبو الغيث اليمني التاجر سكن مكة وملك بها دورا . ومات في رمضان سنة ثلاثين وخلف أولادا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Aḥmad b. Abī al-Ghayth, al-ʿAfīf, Abū al-Ghayth, al-Yamanī, the merchant. He lived in Mecca and owned houses there. He died in Ramadan 830, leaving children."@en .

rec:AIND-D04843 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04843-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04843-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04843 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن أحمد بن منصور الطرابلسي الحنبلي أخو محمد الآتي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Aḥmad b. Manṣūr al-Ṭarābulusī al-Ḥanbalī, the brother of Muḥammad, who is mentioned below. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04845 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04845-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04845-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04845-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04845 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن أيوب بن أحمد بن عبد الله بن عفان بن رمضان الفيومي الأصل المكي السقطي أبوه . مات بها في صفر سنة سبع وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Ayyūb b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAffān b. Ramaḍān, of Fayyūmī origin, al-Makkī; his father was al-Saqaṭī. He died there (in Mecca) in Safar 847. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04846 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04846-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04846-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04846-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04846 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي . المكي والد عفان الآتي ولد في سنة ست وثمانمائة بزبيد وأحضر في الخامسة بمكة على عمه الجمال بن ظهيرة معجمه وأجاز له ابن صديق وجماعة . مات بها في رجب سنة ثمان وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓahīra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī al-Makkī, the father of ʿAffān, who is mentioned below. He was born in 806 in Zabīd, and in his fifth year he was brought in Mecca to attend the reading of the Muʿjam of his paternal uncle al-Jamāl b. Ẓahīra; Ibn Ṣiddīq and a group of others granted him ijāza. He died there (in Mecca) in Rajab 848."@en .

rec:AIND-D04848 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04848-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04848-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04848-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04848 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن أبي بكر الفخر السندبيسي القاهري الشافعي . حفظ القرآن وجوده على الزين بن القصاص ثم تلاه للسبع على الهيثمي ورفيقا للشهاب الزواوي على الشهاب السكندري بل تلا عليه بعضه للعشر وتكسب وسافر لمكة وغيرها فكانت وفاته باليمن قريب السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Abī Bakr, al-Fakhr, al-Sandabīsī, al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī. He memorized the Qurʾān and perfected its recitation under al-Zayn b. al-Qaṣṣāṣ, then recited it according to the seven readings under al-Haythamī, and, as a companion of al-Shihāb al-Zawāwī, under al-Shihāb al-Sakandarī; indeed he recited part of it to him according to the ten readings. He earned his living, travelled to Mecca and elsewhere, and died in Yemen close to 870."@en .

rec:AIND-D04850 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04850-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04850-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04850-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04850-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04850 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن حسن بن على بن منصور الفخر العقبي ثم القاهري الصحراوي ولد تقريبا بعد الثمانين وحفظ القرآن والعمدة وعرضها وأسمعه خال أبيه الزين رضوان على ابن الكويك والجمال الحنبلي والشمس الزراتيتي في آخرين وأجاز له جماعة ، وحج وجاور وكان خادم السجادة بالتربة البرقوقية أجاز لي . ومات في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وثمانين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Manṣūr, al-Fakhr, al-ʿUqbī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Ṣaḥrāwī. He was born approximately after 780. He memorized the Qurʾān and al-ʿUmda and presented them. His father's maternal uncle al-Zayn Riḍwān had him hear from Ibn al-Kuwayk, al-Jamāl al-Ḥanbalī, al-Shams al-Zarātītī and others, and a group granted him ijāza. He performed the pilgrimage and stayed (as mujāwir). He was the keeper of the sajjāda at the Barqūqiyya tomb-complex. He granted me (al-Sakhāwī) an ijāza. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir 882, may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04851 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04851-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04851-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04851-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04851 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن حسين الجزيري بجيم مفتوحة ثم زاي مكسورة نسبة للجزيرة ثم القاهري الحنبلي المؤذن بالبيبرسية والخياط على بابها والد محمد الآتي . كان خيرا محبا في العلم وأهله متوددا مقبلا على شأنه سمع على في مسلم مجالس . مات قريب الثمانين بعد أن أقعد بالفالج مدة وأظنه جاز الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Ḥusayn al-Jazīrī (with fatḥa on the jīm and kasra on the zāy, after al-Jazīra), then al-Qāhirī, al-Ḥanbalī, the muezzin at al-Baybarsiyya and the tailor at its gate, the father of Muḥammad, who is mentioned below. He was a good man, fond of learning and its people, affable and attentive to his own affairs. He heard some sessions of Muslim from me (al-Sakhāwī). He died close to 880 after having been confined by paralysis for a period, and I think he had passed sixty."@en .

rec:AIND-D04852 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04852-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04852-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04852-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04852 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن سعيد بن يحيى بن خليفة الضرسوني نسبة لقبيلة من أعمال قسنطينة المغربي المالكي نزيل طيبة . مات بها سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Saʿīd b. Yaḥyā b. Khalīfa al-Ḍarsūnī (after a tribe in the district of Constantine), al-Maghribī, al-Mālikī, resident of Ṭayba (Medina). He died there in 892."@en .

rec:AIND-D04858 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04858-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04858-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04858 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن عبد الله بن يعقوب الدمشقي القاري أخو محمود وعبد الكريم يأتي فيمن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Yaʿqūb al-Dimashqī al-Qārī, the brother of Maḥmūd and ʿAbd al-Karīm. He will be mentioned below among those whose father is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D04859 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04859-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04859-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04859-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04859 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن عبد الله ويلقب بالفيل أحد من كان يعتقد بمصر . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة خمس . قاله شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. ʿAbd Allāh, nicknamed al-Fīl (the Elephant), one of those who were held in veneration in Egypt. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā 805. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said so in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04862 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04862-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04862-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04862-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04862 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن علي بن إسماعيل بن غانم الفخر بن القطب المقدسي . ولد سنة سبع وخمسين وسبعمائة وأحضر في الرابعة على البياني المستجاد من تاريخ بغداد وغير ذلك ، وحدث لقيه ابن موسى ومعه الأبي في سنة خمس عشرة فسمعا عليه وأجاز لجماعة كالتقي بن فهد وولده . قال شيخنا في معجمه : أجاز لبنتي رابعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. ʿAlī b. Ismāʿīl b. Ghānim, al-Fakhr b. al-Quṭb, al-Maqdisī. He was born in 757 and in his fourth year was brought to attend, under al-Bayānī, al-Mustajād min Taʾrīkh Baghdād and other works. He transmitted ḥadīth. Ibn Mūsā, accompanied by al-Ubbī, met him in 815 and both heard from him. He granted ijāza to a group including al-Taqī b. Fahd and his son. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Muʿjam: \"He granted ijāza to my daughter Rābiʿa.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D04866 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04866-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04866-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04866-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04866 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن عيسى بن موسى بن علي بن قريش الهاشمي المكي . ممن انتمى للمجد بن أبي السعادات وكان يعمل العمر ويزرع . مات في شعبان سنة ثمان وسبعين ببلاد كالبرقة من الهند . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. ʿĪsā b. Mūsā b. ʿAlī b. Quraysh al-Hāshimī al-Makkī. He was among those attached to al-Majd b. Abī al-Saʿādāt; he used to perform ʿumras on behalf of others for a living and to farm. He died in Shaʿbān 878 in the region of Kālbarqa in India. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D04870 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04870-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04870-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04870-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04870 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن محمد بن إسحاق بن إبراهيم الفخر بن قاضي القضاة التاج المناوي والد البهاء أحمد الماضي . ولد في سنة ست وستين وسبعمائة ودرس وأعاد وناب في القاهرة ومصر وفي بعض أعمالها . ومات في رجب سنة سبع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad b. Isḥāq b. Ibrāhīm, al-Fakhr b. the chief judge al-Tāj al-Munāwī, the father of al-Bahāʾ Aḥmad, mentioned above. He was born in 766; he taught, served as repetitor (muʿīd) and acted as deputy judge in Cairo and Miṣr (Fusṭāṭ) and in some of their districts. He died in Rajab of the year [8]07."@en .

rec:AIND-D04871 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04871-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04871-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04871-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b96_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04871 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن محمد بن الزكي أبي بكر بن عبد الرحمن المصري القباني العطار ابن أخي إبراهيم وأحمد وعلي وعمر بني أبي بكر . ممن يسافر في التجارة وسمع علي بمكة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad b. al-Zakī Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Miṣrī al-Qabbānī al-ʿAṭṭār, the nephew of Ibrāhīm, Aḥmad, ʿAlī and ʿUmar, the sons of Abū Bakr. He was among those who travel for trade, and he heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04877 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04877-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04877-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04877 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن محمد بن محمد بن أبي الخير محمد بن فهد الفخر أبو هريرة بن التقي الهاشمي المكي أخو النجم عمر وإخوته ويعرف كسلفه بابن فهد . مات قبل استكمال أربع سنين في ربيع الآخر سنة ثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Khayr Muḥammad b. Fahd, al-Fakhr Abū Hurayra, son of al-Taqī, al-Hāshimī al-Makkī, brother of al-Najm ʿUmar and his other brothers. Like his forebears he was known as Ibn Fahd. He died before completing four years of age, in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir (8)30."@en .

rec:AIND-D04878 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04878-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04878-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04878-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04878-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04878 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن محمد الفخر بن ناصر الدين الحاجب بحلب كان الأمير بن الأمير ويعرف بابن الطحان مات في منتصف المحرم سنة ست وثلاثين خارج حلب وأحضر إليها بعد يومين ودفن بها . أرخه شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad, al-Fakhr b. Nāṣir al-Dīn, the ḥājib (chamberlain) in Aleppo. He was an amīr and the son of an amīr, and was known as Ibn al-Ṭaḥḥān. He died in mid-Muḥarram (8)36 outside Aleppo, was brought there two days later, and was buried there. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04879 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04879-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04879-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04879 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن محمد الفخر بن ناصر الدين الأيوبي القاهري ويعرف كآبائه بابن الملوك ولذا كان ناظر الكاميلية مع كونه كان يحمل الطير على يده على هيئة البزادرة مات في ربيع الآخر سنة أربع وثمانين عن سبعين فأزيد عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad, al-Fakhr b. Nāṣir al-Dīn, al-Ayyūbī al-Qāhirī. Like his forefathers he was known as Ibn al-Mulūk (Son of the Kings), and for that reason he was nāẓir (controller) of al-Kāmiliyya, even though he used to carry a bird on his hand in the manner of the falconers (bazādira). He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir (8)84, aged seventy or more. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04880 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04880-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04880-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04880-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04880 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن محمد الأقفهسي ثم القاهري رأيت خطه في شهادة سنة سبع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad al-Aqfahsī, then al-Qāhirī. I saw his handwriting on a deed of witness (shahāda) dated (8)37."@en .

rec:AIND-D04881 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04881-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04881-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04881 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن محمد الدنديلي . في محمد بن عثمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad al-Dandīlī. See under Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān."@en .

rec:AIND-D04883 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04883-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04883-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04883-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04883 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن محمود البهاء الذيراوي العجمي نزيل مكة . أم بمقام الحنفية بها نيابة عن الشهاب المعيد ومات بها في ذي القعدة سنة أربع وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Maḥmūd, al-Bahāʾ al-Dhīrāwī al-ʿAjamī, resident of Mecca. He led the prayer at the Ḥanafī station (maqām al-Ḥanafiyya) there as deputy for al-Shihāb al-Muʿīd, and died there in Dhū al-Qaʿda (8)44. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04884 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04884-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04884-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04884-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04884 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان بن يوسف بن محمد بن علي الصنهاجي المغربي نزيل مكة في رباط الموفق منها وأحد المعتقدين . ولد تقريبا سنة خمس وتسعين وسبعمائة وقدم مكة حاجا وتردد بينها وبين المدينة زمانا وتزايد اعتقاد الناس فيه مع انجماعه عنهم وجمعه بين العلم والدين والصلاح . مات بمكة سنة ثلاث وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān b. Yūsuf b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Ṣanhājī al-Maghribī, resident of Mecca in its Ribāṭ al-Muwaffaq, and one of those held in veneration. He was born around 795, came to Mecca as a pilgrim, and for a time went back and forth between Mecca and Medina. People's veneration for him grew, together with his withdrawal from them and his combining of learning, religion and righteousness. He died in Mecca in (8)63."@en .

rec:AIND-D04886 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04886-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04886-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04886 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان الحداد ممن أخذ القراءات عن صدقة الضرير تلا عليه أحمد بن محمد بن عيسى الفولازي"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān al-Ḥaddād, one of those who studied the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt) under Ṣadaqa al-Ḍarīr. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā al-Fūlāzī recited to him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04887 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04887-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04887-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04887 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان الدخيسي المغربي . كان صالحا عالما جاور بمكة سنين ومات بها في سنة ست وستين . أرخه لي بعض المغاربة ممن أخذ عني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān al-Dukhaysī al-Maghribī. He was a righteous scholar. He sojourned (jāwara) in Mecca for some years and died there in (8)66. One of the Maghribīs who studied under me gave me the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04890 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04890-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04890-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04890-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04890-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04890 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان الموله . مات بمكة في رمضان سنة اثنتين وستين سقط في بير زمزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān al-Muwallah (the ecstatic). He died in Mecca in Ramaḍān (8)62; he had fallen into the well of Zamzam."@en .

rec:AIND-D04891 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04891-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04891-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04891-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04891 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عثمان الناسخ أحد الشهود بالكعكيين ممن قدم مكة في سنة ثمان وتسعين بحرا صحبة نائب جدة على إمامته وغيرها ثم رجع معه مع الركب ومات في الطريق في المحرم من التي تليها وفد كتب أشياء من تصانيفي وكان لا بأس به ويقال أنه كان عند أزدمر تمساح أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUthmān al-Nāsikh (the copyist), one of the witnesses (notaries) at al-Kaʿkiyyīn. He was among those who came to Mecca by sea in (8)98 in the company of the deputy governor of Jidda, serving as his imām and in other capacities; he then went back with him in the caravan and died on the way in Muḥarram of the following year. He had copied some of my works, and he was not a bad man. It is said that he had also been in the service of Azdamur Timsāḥ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04894 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04894-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04894-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04894 ;
    aindv:sourceText "العجل بن عجلان بن نعير بن منصور بن جماز بن منصور بن جماز بن شيحة بن هاشم العلوي الحسيني الماضي أبوه قريبا . تنازع بعد قتل مانع بن علي في إمرة للمدينة هو وعلي بن مانع في سنة تسع وثلاثين ولم تحصل لواحد منهما بل استقر بعده ابنه الآخر أميان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "al-ʿAjl b. ʿAjlān b. Nuʿayr b. Manṣūr b. Jammāz b. Manṣūr b. Jammāz b. Shīḥa b. Hāshim al-ʿAlawī al-Ḥusaynī; his father was mentioned shortly above. After the killing of Māniʿ b. ʿAlī, he and ʿAlī b. Māniʿ contended for the emirate of Medina in (8)39, but neither of them obtained it; rather, his (Māniʿ's) other son Amyān was confirmed in it after him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04896 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04896-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04896-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04896 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عجل بن نعير آخر من أقربائه أمير عرب آل فضل بالبلاد الشامية . مات وهو معزول عن الإمرة قريبا من أعمال حلب في سنة تسع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAjl b. Nuʿayr, another of his relatives, amīr of the Arabs of Āl Faḍl in the Syrian lands. He died, having been removed from the emirate, near the districts of Aleppo in (8)69."@en .

rec:AIND-D04897 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04897-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04897-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04897-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04897 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عذراء بن علي بن نعير أمير آل فضل . قتل في المحرم سنة إحدى وثلاثين واستقر بعده في الإمرة أخوه مدحج ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAdhrāʾ b. ʿAlī b. Nuʿayr, amīr of Āl Faḍl. He was killed in Muḥarram (8)31, and after him his brother Midḥaj (Mudlij) was confirmed in the emirate."@en .

rec:AIND-D04898 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04898-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04898-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04898-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04898 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عرار بمهملات مخففا بن جخيدب بن أحمد بن حمزة بن جار الله بن راجح بن أبي نمي السيد الحسني . مات بمكة في صفر سنة إحدى وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿArār (with undotted letters, without tashdīd) b. Jukhaydib b. Aḥmad b. Ḥamza b. Jār Allāh b. Rājiḥ b. Abī Numayy, al-Sayyid al-Ḥasanī. He died in Mecca in Ṣafar (8)61."@en .

rec:AIND-D04899 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04899-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04899-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04899 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عربشاه بن علي بن يحيى بن إسحاق ركن الدين أبو الفتح بن الجمال ابن العلاء بن العز الحسيني . ولد في ليلة الجمعة سابع ربيع الأول سنة خمس وخمسين وسبعمائة وسمع على المجد الفيروزابادي والشرف الجرهي وآخرين من الطبقة فما دونها أخذ عنه الطاوسي وأثنى عليه ومات في ضحى الاثنين خامس المحرم سنة ثمان وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿArabshāh b. ʿAlī b. Yaḥyā b. Isḥāq, Rukn al-Dīn Abū al-Fatḥ b. al-Jamāl Ibn al-ʿAlāʾ Ibn al-ʿIzz al-Ḥusaynī. He was born on the night of Friday, 7 Rabīʿ al-Awwal 755, and heard from al-Majd al-Fīrūzābādī, al-Sharaf al-Jarhī and others of that generation and below. Al-Ṭāwūsī studied under him and praised him. He died in the forenoon of Monday, 5 Muḥarram (8)28."@en .

rec:AIND-D04900 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04900-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04900-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04900-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04900 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عرفات بن محمد بن خليل الزين خطيب منية حمل من الشرقية . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿArafāt b. Muḥammad b. Khalīl, al-Zayn, preacher (khaṭīb) of Minyat Ḥamal in al-Sharqiyya. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D04901 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04901-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04901-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04901 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عرفة بن حسن الغمري ثم البلبيسي الفقيه للأبناء ابن الفقيه . ممن قرأ عليه القرآن إبراهيم بن يوسف بن إبراهيم البلبيسي كما في ترجمته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿArafa b. Ḥasan al-Ghamrī, then al-Bilbīsī, the faqīh (Qurʾān teacher) for children and son of a faqīh. Ibrāhīm b. Yūsuf b. Ibrāhīm al-Bilbīsī was among those who read the Qurʾān under him, as stated in his biography."@en .

rec:AIND-D04902 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04902-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04902-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04902 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عطا الله بن أحمد بن علي المحمود أبادي ثم الرومي الحنفي سمع مني المسلسل وغيره بمكة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAṭāʾ Allāh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Maḥmūdābādī, then al-Rūmī, the Ḥanafī. He heard al-Musalsal and other works from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D04903 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04903-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04903-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b97_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04903 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عطا الله بن أمير يوسف جليل بن أمير علي السيد السمرقندي . سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAṭāʾ Allāh b. Amīr Yūsuf Jalīl b. Amīr ʿAlī, al-Sayyid al-Samarqandī. He heard from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D04908 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04908-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04908-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04908-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04908 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عطية بن عبد الحي القيوم بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد ابن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي المكي الحنبلي أخو المحب أحمد الماضي وأمه من زبيد . ولد في سنة تسع وثلاثين وثمانمائة وهو ممن سمع ختم البخاري بالقاهرة سنة ثلاث وستين على أم هانئ الهورينية ومن أحضر معها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAṭiyya b. ʿAbd al-Ḥayy al-Qayyūm b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓahīra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī al-Makkī al-Ḥanbalī, brother of the aforementioned al-Muḥibb Aḥmad; his mother was from Zabīd. He was born in the year 839. He is among those who heard the completion (khatm) of al-Bukhārī's Ṣaḥīḥ in Cairo in the year 863 from Umm Hāniʾ al-Hūrīniyya and those who were brought to attend with her."@en .

rec:AIND-D04910 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04910-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04910-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04910-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D04910-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04910 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عفان بن عثمان بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية ابن ظهيرة القرشي المكي الماضي أبوه وأمه من زبيد . ممن حضر في درس البرهاني فمن دونه . مات في ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وتسعين بالقاهرة وجاء الخبر لمكة في ربيع الأول من التي تليها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAffān b. ʿUthmān b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓahīra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī al-Makkī. His father is mentioned above, and his mother was from Zabīd. He is among those who attended the lessons of al-Burhānī and of those below him. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 892 in Cairo, and the news reached Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the following year."@en .

rec:AIND-D04911 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04911-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04911-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04911-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04911 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عفيف بن أحمد بن الصديق الموزعي اليماني المدني الفراش بها . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAfīf b. Aḥmad b. al-Ṣiddīq al-Mawzaʿī al-Yamānī al-Madanī, the farrāsh (attendant in charge of furnishings) there (in Medina). He is among those who heard from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D04913 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04913-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04913-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04913-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04913 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عقيل بن مبارك بن رميثة بن أبي نمى الحسني المكي كان من أعيان الأشراف بل جعله ابن عمه عنان بن مغامس بن رميثة شريكا له في إمرة مكة وبقي على ذلك أشهرا يدعى له في الخطبة وعلى زمزم بعد المغرب . مات في سنة خمس وعشرين بعد أن أضر وربما تغير عقله . ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAqīl b. Mubārak b. Rumaytha b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He was one of the notables of the sharīfs; indeed his cousin ʿInān b. Mughāmis b. Rumaytha made him his partner in the emirate of Mecca, and he remained so for some months, with prayers offered for him in the Friday sermon and at Zamzam after the sunset prayer. He died in the year 825, after having gone blind and perhaps having lost his reason. Al-Fāsī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04914 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04914-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04914-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04914-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04914 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عقيل بن وبير بن نخبار بن مقبل بن محمد بن راجح بن إدريس بن حسن ابن أبي عزيز قتادة الحسني أمير ينبوغ وصرف عنها في سنة اثنتين وأربعين بصخرة الماضي . ومات سنة أربع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAqīl b. Wabīr b. Nakhbār b. Muqbil b. Muḥammad b. Rājiḥ b. Idrīs b. Ḥasan b. Abī ʿAzīz Qatāda al-Ḥasanī, amīr of Yanbuʿ. He was removed from it in the year 842 in favour of the aforementioned Ṣakhra. He died in the year 844."@en .

rec:AIND-D04915 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04915-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04915-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04915-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_rulings,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04915 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علان من ططخ الأشرفي برسباي أحد أمراء العشرات وأمير ركب الرجبية في سنة إحدى وسبعين أنشأ سبيلا حسنا في أثناء طريق بركة الحاج . ومات في يوم الخميس سلخ ربيع الآخر سنة ست وثمانين وقد شاخ وسمعت من يذكره بخير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAllān min Ṭuṭukh al-Ashrafī Barsbāy, one of the amīrs of ten, and amīr of the Rajabiyya caravan in the year 871. He built a fine public fountain (sabīl) along the road to Birkat al-Ḥājj. He died on Thursday, the last day of Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 886, having grown old, and I heard someone speak well of him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04919 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04919-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04919-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04919 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عليباي بن خليل بن دلغادر قتل على يد نائب حلب جار قطلو في سنة تسع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlībāy b. Khalīl b. Dulghādir. He was killed at the hands of the viceroy of Aleppo, Jār Quṭlū, in the year 829."@en .

rec:AIND-D04921 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04921-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04921-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04921 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عليباي الدوادار . مات مقتولا في سنة أربع وعشرين ، وكان عنده طيش وكثرة كلام لكنه كان قليل الطمع في أحكامه متعصبا لمن يلوذ به . قاله العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlībāy al-Dawādār. He died, killed, in the year 824. He was rash and talkative, but was little given to greed in his judgements and was partisan towards those who sought his protection. So said al-ʿAynī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04922 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04922-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04922-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04922 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عليباي العزيزي . ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlībāy al-ʿAzīzī. He is among those who heard from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D04925 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04925-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04925-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04925-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04925 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن آدم بن حبيب نور الدين الكناني الحبيني البوصيري ثم القاهري الشافعي المقري ويعرف بالحبيني وبالبوصيري . ممن أخذ من الشمس العسقلاني القراءات وتصدر لها فقرأ عليه الزين طاهر وابن أسد والهيثمي وغيرهم وكان مقيما بالهلالية وأحد الصوفية بسعيد السعداء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ādam b. Ḥabīb, Nūr al-Dīn al-Kinānī al-Ḥubaynī al-Būṣīrī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, the Qurʾān reciter (muqriʾ), known as al-Ḥubaynī and as al-Būṣīrī. He is among those who took the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt) from al-Shams al-ʿAsqalānī, and he held a teaching post in them; al-Zayn Ṭāhir, Ibn Asad, al-Haythamī and others read under him. He resided at al-Hilāliyya and was one of the Sufis of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D04926 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04926-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04926-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04926-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04926 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن إبراهيم بن أحمد بن إبراهيم بن سعد بن سعيد أبو مدين الرملي ثم المقدسي الشافعي القادري الماضي حفيده خليل بن محمد ورأيت شيخنا سماه إبراهيم سهوا وهو ممن قرأ عليه الأربعين المتباينة وبعض الصحيح وغيرهما في سنة خمس وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Saʿd b. Saʿīd, Abū Madyan al-Ramlī, then al-Maqdisī, al-Shāfiʿī al-Qādirī; his grandson Khalīl b. Muḥammad has been mentioned above. I saw that our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) inadvertently named him Ibrāhīm. He is among those who read under him al-Arbaʿīn al-mutabāyina, part of the Ṣaḥīḥ and other works in the year 835."@en .

rec:AIND-D04930 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04930-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04930-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04930 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن إبراهيم بن عدنان . يأتي قريبا فيمن جده علي بن عدنان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAdnān. He will appear shortly among those whose grandfather is ʿAlī b. ʿAdnān."@en .

rec:AIND-D04939 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04939-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04939-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04939-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04939 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن سعيد بن عبيد الله السيد غلاء الدين الحسيني البقاعي الأصل الدمشقي الصالحي الحنفي إمام الريحانية بدمشق ووالد إبراهيم الماضي ممن كان يحضر مجالس العلماء مات في عشر ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وتسعين قبل إكمال الثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Saʿīd b. ʿUbayd Allāh, al-Sayyid Ghalāʾ al-Dīn al-Ḥusaynī, of Biqāʿī origin, al-Dimashqī al-Ṣāliḥī al-Ḥanafī, imām of al-Rayḥāniyya in Damascus and father of the aforementioned Ibrāhīm. He is among those who used to attend the gatherings of the scholars. He died in the first ten days of Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 892, before completing eighty years."@en .

rec:AIND-D04943 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04943-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04943-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04943 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن إبراهيم بن محمد الصحراوي الضرير أخو عبد الكريم الماضي ، ممن أجاز له الشرف بن الكويك وجماعة واستجازه الطلبة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad al-Ṣaḥrāwī, the blind, brother of the aforementioned ʿAbd al-Karīm. He is among those to whom al-Sharaf b. al-Kuwayk and a group of others granted ijāza, and students sought ijāza from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D04944 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04944-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04944-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04944 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن إبراهيم بن يوسف الفاقوسي الأصل البلبيسي الشافعي الماضي أبوه . إنسان خير سليم الفطرة جدا زائد الفاقة قرأ القرآن واشتغل يسيرا في العربية وغيرها وقرأ على جل الصحيح في سنين وكذا قرأ على الديمي والبهاء المشهدي بل قرأه على العامة في بلده ولهم فيه اعتقاد ونعم الرجل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm b. Yūsuf, of Fāqūsī origin, al-Bilbīsī al-Shāfiʿī; his father has been mentioned above. A good man, of a very sound and simple nature, and extremely poor. He recited the Qurʾān and studied Arabic and other subjects a little, and read most of the Ṣaḥīḥ under me over several years. He likewise read it under al-Daymī and al-Bahāʾ al-Mashhadī; indeed he read it to the common people in his town, and they held him in great esteem. What a fine man he was."@en .

rec:AIND-D04948 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04948-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04948-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04948 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن إبراهيم الغزي نزيل بيت المقدس والمتوفي به في ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm al-Ghazzī, resident of Jerusalem (Bayt al-Maqdis), who died there in [the year is left blank]."@en .

rec:AIND-D04949 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04949-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04949-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04949 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن عيسى بن مطير الحكمي اليماني أصغر من أخيه أبي القسم وغيره من إخوته ممن لم يحكم الفقه وتوفي شابا . قاله الأهدل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā b. Muṭayr al-Ḥakamī al-Yamānī, younger than his brother Abū al-Qāsim and his other brothers; he was among those who did not master jurisprudence, and he died young. So said al-Ahdal."@en .

rec:AIND-D04950 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04950-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04950-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04950-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04950 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن إبراهيم نور الدين بن السدار أخو عبد الرحمن الماضي وخال شمس الدين الشهير . تدرب به ابن أخته في فنونه وكتب بخطه الحسن الكثير خصوصا حين مجاوراته بمكة ، وكان خيرا أثنى عنه مظفر الأمشاطي وحكى لنا عنه القاضي بدر الدين السعدي شيئا . مات بعد الخمسين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm, Nūr al-Dīn Ibn al-Saddār, brother of the aforementioned ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and maternal uncle of the famous Shams al-Dīn. His sister's son trained under him in his arts. He wrote a great deal in his fine hand, especially during his stays (mujāwara) in Mecca. He was a good man; Muẓaffar al-Amshāṭī praised him, and the qāḍī Badr al-Dīn al-Saʿdī related something to us about him. He died after 850, approximately."@en .

rec:AIND-D04951 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04951-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04951-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04951-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04951 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن الشهاب أحمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن علي بن عبد الكريم ابن يوسف بن سالم بن دليم القرشي البصري المكي . مات بها في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وسبعين وهو ثمل عفا الله عنه . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Yūsuf b. Sālim b. Dulaym al-Qurashī al-Baṣrī al-Makkī. He died there (in Mecca) in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 872 while intoxicated, may God pardon him. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04953 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04953-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04953-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04953-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b94_98_triage,
        agent:claude_b98_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04953 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن إينال نور الدين بن المؤيد بن الأشرف . ولد في شوال سنة سبع وسبعين وثمانمائة بإسكندرية كان أملك على ابنة محمد بن بردبك ابن عمته فماتت وطعن هو ثم تخلص وتحرك للمجيء للحج في موسم سنة سبع وتسعين ثم بطل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Īnāl, Nūr al-Dīn b. al-Muʾayyad b. al-Ashraf. He was born in Shawwāl of the year 877 in Alexandria. He had contracted marriage with the daughter of Muḥammad b. Bardbak, his paternal aunt's son, but she died; he himself was struck by the plague and then recovered. He set about coming for the pilgrimage in the season of the year 897, but it came to nothing."@en .

rec:AIND-D04957 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04957-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04957-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04957-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04957 ;
    aindv:sourceText "562 علي بن أحمد بن أبي بكر النور أبو الحسن المصري الشافعي نزيل البندقدارية ووالد محمد الآتي أخذ عن الملوي رفيقا للادمي الماضي قريبا وكان أحد الأعيان في المذهب مع الصلاح والخير . قاله لي ولده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr, al-Nūr Abū al-Ḥasan, al-Miṣrī, the Shāfiʿī. He was a resident of al-Bunduqdāriyya and the father of Muḥammad, who is mentioned below. He studied under al-Mallawī as a fellow student of al-Adamī, mentioned just above. He was one of the notables of the madhhab, together with piety and goodness. His son told me this."@en .

rec:AIND-D04959 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04959-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04959-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04959-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04959 ;
    aindv:sourceText "564 علي بن أحمد بن ثقبة بن رميثة الحسني المكي . مات ببعض نواحيها في شوال سنة ست وأربعين وحمل إليها فدفن بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Thuqba b. Rumaytha, al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died in one of the districts around Mecca in Shawwāl (8)46, and was carried to Mecca and buried there."@en .

rec:AIND-D04961 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04961-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04961-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04961-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04961 ;
    aindv:sourceText "566 علي بن أحمد بن حمزة بن راجح . مات سنة تسع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Ḥamza b. Rājiḥ. He died in the year (8)29."@en .

rec:AIND-D04962 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04962-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04962-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04962 ;
    aindv:sourceText "567 علي بن أحمد بن خلد النجار بباب الخرق والشهير بحب الرمان ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Khald, the carpenter at Bāb al-Kharq, known as Ḥabb al-Rummān. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D04963 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04963-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04963-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04963 ;
    aindv:sourceText "568 علي بن أحمد بن خليفة نور الدين الأزهري الحنفي الأسمر أحد العدول بخطته . ممن أخذ القراءات عن النور إمام الأزهر والشهاب السكندري وقرأ على البهاء المشهدي شرح النخبة في سنة ثمانين وأذن له في إفادتها ولم يزل يتكسب بالشهادة وآخر امرة جلس لها بحانوت في الوراقين . مات سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Khalīfa, Nūr al-Dīn, al-Azharī, the Ḥanafī, al-Asmar (the dark-complexioned), one of the notary-witnesses of his quarter. He was among those who studied the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt) under al-Nūr, the imam of al-Azhar, and al-Shihāb al-Sakandarī, and he read the Sharḥ al-Nukhba with al-Bahāʾ al-Mashhadī in the year (8)80, who authorized him to teach it. He continued to earn his living as a notary-witness, and at the end of his life he sat for it in a shop in al-Warrāqīn. He died in the year (8)92."@en .

rec:AIND-D04964 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04964-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04964-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04964 ;
    aindv:sourceText "569 علي بن أحمد بن خليل بن أحمد بن عابد النور المغربي الشافعي ويعرف بابن عابد بالموحدة ممن أخذ عن النجم بن قاضي عجلون وتكسب بالتجارة في حانوت ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Khalīl b. Aḥmad b. ʿĀbid, al-Nūr al-Maghribī, the Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn ʿĀbid (with the letter bāʾ). He was among those who studied under al-Najm b. Qāḍī ʿAjlūn, and he earned his living by trade in a shop."@en .

rec:AIND-D04968 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04968-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04968-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04968 ;
    aindv:sourceText "573 علي بن أحمد بن دحية ثم القاهري الأزهري ويعرف بالصبوة ، وسمع في مسلم بالكاملية وتكسب بالكتب فلم ينتج ثم صار يسافر لمكة بالصر ، ولا زال يسترسل حتى بقي يكري الناس معه إلى أن انهبط جدا وأتلف للناس ولنفسه شيئا كثيرا وتسحب من الديون غير مرة . ومات سنة ثمان وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Diḥya, then al-Qāhirī, al-Azharī, known as al-Ṣabwa. He heard part of (Ṣaḥīḥ) Muslim at al-Kāmiliyya, and tried to earn his living by the book trade but did not succeed. He then began travelling to Mecca with the ṣurra (the remittances and provisions for the pilgrimage), and kept on with this until he ended up hiring out mounts to people who travelled with him. Eventually he fell very low, lost a great deal of other people's property and his own, and fled from his debts more than once. He died in the year (8)98."@en .

rec:AIND-D04969 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04969-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04969-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04969 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن سالم . يأتي فيمن جده محمد بن سالم بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Sālim. He will be mentioned below among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Sālim b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04970 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04970-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04970-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04970-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04970 ;
    aindv:sourceText "574 علي بن أحمد بن سعيد بن هارون علاء الدين المحمدي اليزدي الأصل ثم القاهري الحنفي والد العلاء علي الآتي ويعرف بالتزمنتي ويلقب بشيخ المشايخ أخذ عن أبيه وغيره ، ومات بالطاعون في المحرم سنة ثلاث وثلاثين عن أزيد من تسعين سنة ودفن بمنزله بالقرب من جامع آل ملك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Saʿīd b. Hārūn, ʿAlāʾ al-Dīn al-Muḥammadī, of Yazdī origin, then al-Qāhirī, the Ḥanafī, father of al-ʿAlāʾ ʿAlī, who is mentioned below. He was known as al-Tazmantī and bore the title Shaykh al-Mashāyikh. He studied under his father and others. He died of the plague in Muḥarram (8)33, aged over ninety, and was buried in his house near the Mosque of Āl Malik."@en .

rec:AIND-D04971 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04971-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04971-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04971-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04971 ;
    aindv:sourceText "575 علي بن أحمد بن سعيد المكي الحلفاوي أحد خدام درجة الكعبة . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة ثمانين.أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Saʿīd, al-Makkī al-Ḥalfāwī, one of the servants of the steps of the Kaʿba. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir (8)80. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04972 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04972-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04972-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04972 ;
    aindv:sourceText "576 علي بن أحمد بن سليمان بن عمر النور أبو الحسن الفاسي الأصل الديروطي الشافعي . عرض على أماكن من المنهاج والرحبية وألفية النحو والملحة بل قرأ على بعض البخاري وسمع علي غير ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Sulaymān b. ʿUmar, al-Nūr Abū al-Ḥasan, of Fāsī origin, al-Dayrūṭī, the Shāfiʿī. He recited to me (al-Sakhāwī) from memory passages of al-Minhāj, al-Raḥbiyya, the Alfiyya on grammar and al-Mulḥa; moreover he read part of al-Bukhārī with me and heard other things from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D04973 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04973-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04973-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04973 ;
    aindv:sourceText "577 علي بن أحمد بن سليمان السطاسي . سمع هو وولده أحمد العشاري على شيخنا في سنة اثنتين وخمسين أشياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Sulaymān al-Saṭāsī. He and his son Aḥmad al-ʿUshārī heard various things from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in the year (8)52."@en .

rec:AIND-D04974 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04974-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04974-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04974 ;
    aindv:sourceText "578 علي بن أحمد بن سنان القائد العمري المكي من القواد العمرة . مات بها في ربيع الأول سنة تسع وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Sinān, the qāʾid, al-ʿUmarī al-Makkī, one of the ʿUmarī qāʾids (commanders of Mecca). He died there (in Mecca) in Rabīʿ al-Awwal (8)59. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04975 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04975-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04975-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04975 ;
    aindv:sourceText "579 علي بن أحمد بن شقير المصري الأصل البديوي الحمصاني والده ويعرف بجده . مات بمكة في ليلة سلخ المحرم سنة اثنتين وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Shuqayr, of Egyptian origin, al-Badīwī. His father was al-Ḥimṣānī, and he was known by his grandfather's name. He died in Mecca on the night of the last day of Muḥarram (8)32."@en .

rec:AIND-D04976 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04976-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04976-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04976 ;
    aindv:sourceText "580 علي بن أحمد بن عامر الجدي . مات في ذي القعدة سنة أربع وخمسين خارج مكة وحمل فدفن بها . أرخهما ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿĀmir al-Jaddī. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda (8)54 outside Mecca, and was carried to Mecca and buried there. Ibn Fahd recorded the deaths of both of them (this man and the preceding one)."@en .

rec:AIND-D04979 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04979-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04979-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04979 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن السكندري الحنفي . يأتي فيمن جده محمد بن عبد الرحمن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-Sakandarī, the Ḥanafī. He will be mentioned below among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān."@en .

rec:AIND-D04980 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04980-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04980-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04980 ;
    aindv:sourceText "583 علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز بن عبد الواحد بن عمر بن عياد الأنصاري المغربي ثم المدني الماضي أبوه . حضر في سنة عشرين وهو في الثانية مع أبيه ما يذكر في عمه محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. ʿUmar b. ʿAyyād, al-Anṣārī al-Maghribī, then al-Madanī; his father has been mentioned above. In the year (8)20, when he was in his second year, he attended with his father what is mentioned in the entry of his uncle Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D04983 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04983-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04983-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04983 ;
    aindv:sourceText "586 علي بن أحمد بن عبد الله بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن نصر بن فهد ★الديراسطياري?★ سمع في سنة سبع وستين من الصلاح بن أبي عمر وجوزت إدراكه لهذا القرن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. Naṣr b. Fahd al-Dīrāsṭiyārī. He heard from al-Ṣalāḥ b. Abī ʿUmar in the year (7)67, and I (al-Sakhāwī) deemed it possible that he lived into this century."@en .

rec:AIND-D04984 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04984-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04984-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04984 ;
    aindv:sourceText "587 علي بن أحمد بن عبد الله السكندري الحاسب . قال شيخنا في إنبائه كان يتعانى علم الميقات فبرع في معرفة حل الزيج وكتابة التقاويم وأقبل على الكيمياء فأفنى عمره في أعمالها ما بين تصعيد وتقطير وغير ذلك ولم يصعد معه شيء . ومات في آخر سنة اثنتين عن نحو خمسين سنة ، وذكره المقريزي في عقوده أطول مما هنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Sakandarī al-Ḥāsib (the reckoner). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Inbāʾ that he devoted himself to the science of timekeeping (mīqāt) and excelled in solving astronomical tables (zīj) and drawing up calendars; then he turned to alchemy and wasted his life in its operations, between sublimation and distillation and the like, and nothing came of it for him. He died at the end of the year (8)02, aged about fifty. Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his ʿUqūd at greater length than here."@en .

rec:AIND-D04985 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04985-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04985-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04985-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage,
        agent:claude_b99_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04985 ;
    aindv:sourceText "588 علي بن أحمد بن عبد الواحد نور الدين العكام. ذكره المقريزي في عقوده وقال أنه كان يحفظ شعرا كثيرا وساق عنه منه مما حدثه به في عوده من الحج سنة تسع وثلاثين : %~% رأيت ماء ونارا فوق وجنته %~% والنمل مزدحم ما بينها ساري %~% %~% فقلت سبحان ربي لا شريك له %~% مسير النمل بين الماء والنار %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, Nūr al-Dīn al-ʿAkkām (the camel-loader). Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his ʿUqūd and said that he had memorised much poetry, and quoted from him, among what he related to him on the way back from the pilgrimage of the year (8)39: \"I saw water and fire upon his cheek, with ants crowding and moving between them; so I said: Glory to my Lord, who has no partner — the ants travel between the water and the fire.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D04992 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04992-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04992-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04992 ;
    aindv:sourceText "595 علي بن أحمد بن علي بن حسين بن البدر محمد سيف الدين بن النجم بن الرفاعي الصحراوي الماضي أبوه . ولد في عاشر جمادى الأولى سنة ثمانين ونشأ في كنف أبيه فقرأ القرآن والمنهاج وعرضه علي في سنة ست وتسعين وحدثته بالمسلسل ومات في طاعون سنة سبع وتسعين عوضه الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn b. al-Badr Muḥammad, Sayf al-Dīn b. al-Najm b. al-Rifāʿī al-Ṣaḥrāwī. His father was mentioned above. He was born on 10 Jumādā al-Ūlā (8)80 and grew up under the care of his father. He read the Qurʾān and al-Minhāj and presented them to me (al-Sakhāwī) in (8)96, and I transmitted the Musalsal to him. He died in the plague of (8)97; may God grant him Paradise in recompense."@en .

rec:AIND-D04994 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04994-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04994-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04994 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن علي بن سالم . يأتي فيمن جده محمد بن سالم بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Sālim. He will be mentioned below among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Sālim b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D04995 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04995-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04995-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04995 ;
    aindv:sourceText "597 علي بن أحمد بن علي بن سنان بن راجح بن محمد بن عبد الله بن عمر بن مسعود نور الدين العمري القائد . مات في ربيع الأول سنة تسع وخمسين صوب اليمن ودفن به . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Sinān b. Rājiḥ b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Masʿūd, Nūr al-Dīn al-ʿUmarī, the qāʾid. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal (8)59 in the direction of Yemen and was buried there. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04997 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04997-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04997-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D04997-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b100_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04997 ;
    aindv:sourceText "599 علي بن أحمد بن علي بن عبد الله بن علي بن أبي راجح محمد بن إدريس القرشي العبدري الشيبي الحجبي . مات بها في رجب سنة اثنتين وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. Abī Rājiḥ Muḥammad b. Idrīs al-Qurashī al-ʿAbdarī al-Shaybī al-Ḥajabī. He died there (presumably Mecca) in Rajab (8)82. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D04998 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D04998-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D04998-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D04998 ;
    aindv:sourceText "600 علي بن أحمد بن علي بن عبد المغيث نور الدين النشرتي القاهري الحسيني الشافعي والد الشهاب أحمد الماضي . قرأ القرآن وأتقنه وأدب به الأبناء مع فضل وصلاح كثير وممن قرأ عليه ولده والعلاء التزمنتي . مات ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Mughīth, Nūr al-Dīn al-Nashartī al-Qāhirī al-Ḥusaynī al-Shāfiʿī, the father of al-Shihāb Aḥmad, who was mentioned above. He read the Qurʾān, mastered it, and taught children with it, with much merit and righteousness. Among those who read under him were his son and al-ʿAlāʾ al-Tazmantī. He died ... (the text breaks off)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05004 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05004-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05004-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05004 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن علي بن يوسف الخصوصي زوج ابنة الزين جعفر المقري مذكور بالشرف وأبوه شيخ الخصوص . ممن حج بعد التسعين موسميا وكان يتردد إلي في مسيرنا راجعين ثم تردد إلي بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf al-Khuṣūṣī, the husband of the daughter of al-Zayn Jaʿfar al-Muqriʾ. He is mentioned as a sharīf, and his father was the shaykh of al-Khuṣūṣ. He was among those who performed the pilgrimage after [8]90 for the season only; he used to frequent me (al-Sakhāwī) during our journey back, and afterwards he frequented me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05009 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05009-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05009-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05009 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن علي نور الدين الفارقي الشاذلي . سمع في ابن ماجة على الأبناسي والغماري والجوهري ولقيه بعض أصحابنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn al-Fāriqī al-Shādhilī. He heard (parts) of Ibn Māja under al-Abnāsī, al-Ghumārī and al-Jawharī, and some of our companions met him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05010 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05010-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05010-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05010 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن علي السعودي ويعرف بالترابي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Saʿūdī, known as al-Turābī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05011 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05011-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05011-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05011 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن علي المكي الدهان ويعرف بالشقيري . مات بمكة في رمضان سنة اثنتين وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Makkī al-Dahhān, known as al-Shuqayrī. He died in Mecca in Ramaḍān of the year [8]82. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05012 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05012-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05012-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05012 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن علي المحلي نسبة لمحلة علي من المحلة الكبرى الشافعي ويعرف بابن القريط ، رأيته أجاز خليل بن إبراهيم الدمياطي في سنة تسع وخمسين وثمانمائة وقال أنه قرأ عليه عقيدة الإسلام من قواعد العقائد من الأحياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Maḥallī — a nisba to Maḥallat ʿAlī, which belongs to al-Maḥalla al-Kubrā — al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Qurayṭ. I (al-Sakhāwī) saw him grant an ijāza to Khalīl b. Ibrāhīm al-Dimyāṭī in the year 859, and he (Khalīl) stated that he had read to him ʿAqīdat al-Islām from the Qawāʿid al-ʿaqāʾid of the Iḥyāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05013 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05013-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05013-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05013 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد الميقاتي ويعرف بالمقسي . مات سنة ثلاث وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Mīqātī, known as al-Maqsī. He died in the year [8]33."@en .

rec:AIND-D05025 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05025-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05025-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05025 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن محمد بن أبي بكر الأنصاري المرجاني المكي . مات بها في ذي القعدة سنة ست وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-Anṣārī al-Marjānī al-Makkī. He died there (in Mecca) in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year [8]76. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05030 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05030-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05030-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05030 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن محمد بن شعيب الغمري ثم المحلي الماضي أبوه . قرأ القرآن وصحب الفقراء وهو طويل اللحية خفيف الروح من أصحاب أبي العباس بن الغمري . ترك له أبوه ما لم يكن الظن أنه يملكه ، وهو ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Shuʿayb al-Ghamrī, then al-Maḥallī; his father has been mentioned above. He recited the Qurʾān and kept company with the Sufi poor (fuqarāʾ). He was long-bearded and light-hearted, one of the companions of Abū al-ʿAbbās b. al-Ghamrī. His father left him more than anyone would have supposed he owned. He is among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05031 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05031-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05031-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05031 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الحق العلاء بن الشهاب الغمري الأصل القاهري الماضي أبوه والآتي أخوه محمد ويعرف كأبيه بابن عبد الحق . ممن قرأ القرآن وسمع مني وتكسب بالتجارة وسافر فيها إلى الشام وغيرها ولا بأس به قيما أرجو به هو أصلح من أخيه جزما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Ḥaqq, al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Shihāb, of Ghamr origin, al-Qāhirī; his father has been mentioned above and his brother Muḥammad follows. Like his father he is known as Ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥaqq. He was among those who recited the Qurʾān and heard from me (al-Sakhāwī). He earned his living by trade and travelled for it to Syria and elsewhere. There is no harm in him, as I hope; he is decidedly better than his brother."@en .

rec:AIND-D05035 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05035-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05035-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05035-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05035 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن محمد بن علي الخطيب أبو الحسن بن درباس أخو الفخر أحمد الماضي . ممن سمع على شيخنا وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Khaṭīb, Abū al-Ḥasan b. Dirbās, brother of al-Fakhr Aḥmad, mentioned above. He was among those who heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others."@en .

rec:AIND-D05037 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05037-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05037-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05037 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن محمد بن عيسى بن محمد بن محمود المقدسي . هكذا قرأته بخط بعضهم وقد مضى فيمن جده محمد بن عبد الله بن محمد قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā b. Muḥammad b. Maḥmūd al-Maqdisī. Thus I (al-Sakhāwī) read it in someone's handwriting; he has already appeared shortly above among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05041 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05041-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05041-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05041 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن محمد الحنبلي القطان . رجل فقير يتكسب ويشتغل يسيرا وسمع الحديث وهو ممن أخذ عني . مات في ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Ḥanbalī al-Qaṭṭān. A poor man who earned his living, studied a little and heard ḥadīth. He is among those who studied under me (al-Sakhāwī). He died in ..."@en .

rec:AIND-D05042 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05042-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05042-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05042 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن مفتاح بن فطيس القباني والد أبي بكر ومحمد . مات في شعبان سنة أربع وستين بساحل جدة وحمل فدفن بالمعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Miftāḥ b. Fuṭays al-Qabbānī, the father of Abū Bakr and Muḥammad. He died in Shaʿbān of the year [8]64 on the coast of Jidda, and was carried (to Mecca) and buried in al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D05044 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05044-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05044-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05044 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن هلال بن عثمان بن عبد الرحمن الدمشقي الحنفي الشهير بابن القصيف . مات بمكة في رمضان سنة إحدى وثمانين . أرخهم ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Hilāl b. ʿUthmān b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanafī, well known as Ibn al-Qaṣīf. He died in Mecca in Ramaḍān of the year [8]81. Ibn Fahd recorded their (deaths)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05045 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05045-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05045-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05045 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد بن يوسف السيد العلاء أبو الحسن بن العلامي الشهابي أبي العباس . الرومي ثم المقدسي الحنفي . ممن أخذ عني أشياء وكتبت له إجازة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Yūsuf, al-Sayyid al-ʿAlāʾ Abū al-Ḥasan, son of the most learned (al-ʿAllāmī) al-Shihābī Abū al-ʿAbbās; al-Rūmī, then al-Maqdisī, al-Ḥanafī. He was among those who studied various things under me (al-Sakhāwī), and I wrote an ijāza for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05046 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05046-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05046-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05046 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد نور الدين الأزهري الحنفي الأسمر . مضى فيمن جده خليفة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad Nūr al-Dīn al-Azharī al-Ḥanafī al-Asmar. [His entry] has already appeared among those whose grandfather is Khalīfa."@en .

rec:AIND-D05048 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05048-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05048-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05048 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد الموفق بن سالم . فيمن جده محمد بن سالم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Muwaffaq b. Sālim. [Listed] under those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Sālim."@en .

rec:AIND-D05050 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05050-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05050-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05050 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد الزيادي بالتشديد نسبة لمحلة زياد بالغربية ، وهو والد محمد وأحمد وعزيزة وأحد صوفية سعيد السعداء . مات سنة ثمان وأربعين وكان خيرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Ziyādī. His nisbah is derived from Maḥallat Ziyād in al-Gharbiyya. He was the father of Muḥammad, Aḥmad, and ʿAzīza, and was one of the Sufis of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. He died in the year 848 AH, and was a good man."@en .

rec:AIND-D05051 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05051-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05051-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05051 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد الشيبي العراقي . فيمن جده علي بن محمد بن علي بن عيسى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Shaybī al-ʿIrāqī. [Listed] among those whose grandfather is ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿĪsā."@en .

rec:AIND-D05054 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05054-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05054-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05054 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد الوزروالي المغربي كان صالحا . مات في صفر سنة ثمان وستين . أرخه لي بعض المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Wazrawālī al-Maghribī. He was a righteous man. He died in Ṣafar, in the year 868 AH. A certain Maghribī dated his death for me."@en .

rec:AIND-D05055 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05055-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05055-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05055 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أحمد اليمني من أهل أبيات حسين ويلقب بالأزرق . كان كثير العناية بالفقه وجمع فيه كتابا كبيرا . مات في سنة تسع . أرخه شيخنا في إنبائه والظاهر أنه غير الصنعاني الماضي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Yamanī, from the people of Abyāt Ḥusayn, nicknamed al-Azraq. He was deeply devoted to fiqh (jurisprudence) and compiled a large book on it. He died in the year nine (809 AH). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death in his Inbāʾ al-ghumr, and he is apparently not the same as al-Ṣanʿānī mentioned shortly before."@en .

rec:AIND-D05059 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05059-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05059-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05059 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن إسلام بن يحيى بن مكرم العلائي الحنفي أحد فضلائهم ويعرف والده ببالجه . ممن سمع على شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Islām b. Yaḥyā b. Mukram al-ʿAlāʾī al-Ḥanafī. He was one of their virtuous scholars, and his father was known as Bālija. He was among those who heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05062 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05062-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05062-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05062 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن إسماعيل بن عبد المجيد الأبياري . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Abyārī. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05065 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05065-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05065-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05065 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن إسماعيل بن يوسف الخواجا نور الدين الرومي المكي الشهير بابن البهلوان . ملك دورا بمكة وعمرها . ومات في شعبان سنة ثلاث وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ismāʿīl b. Yūsuf, al-Khawājā Nūr al-Dīn al-Rūmī al-Makkī, famous as Ibn al-Bahlawān. He owned and developed properties in Mecca. He died in Shaʿbān, the year 853 AH, as recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05068 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05068-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05068-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05068 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن إينال الأمير علاء الدين أحد خواص الظاهر جقمق أرسل به لملك الروم مراد بن عثمان بهدية في سنة ثلاث وأربعين . قاله المقريزي في الحوادث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Īnāl, al-Amīr ʿAlāʾ al-Dīn, one of the close associates of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq. He was sent by him with a gift to the King of Rūm, Murād b. ʿUthmān, in the year 843 AH. Al-Maqrīzī said this in al-Ḥawādith."@en .

rec:AIND-D05080 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05080-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05080-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05080 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن الزكي أبي بكر بن عبد الرحمن المصري ثم المكي القباني العطار أخو إبراهيم وأحمد وعمر . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Zakī Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-Miṣrī then al-Makkī, the weigher (al-Qabbānī) and druggist (al-ʿAṭṭār), brother of Ibrāhīm, Aḥmad, and ʿUmar. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05082 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05082-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05082-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05082 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أبي بكر بن عز العرب البكاري المفسر . مات سنة أربع وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. ʿIzz al-ʿArab al-Bakkārī, the Qur'an commentator. He died in the year 864 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05087 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05087-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05087-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05087 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن إبراهيم نور الدين بن الشرف المناوي القاهري الشافعي الأسود أخو عبد الرحيم الماضي . ممن ناب في الحكم وخطب وكان أبح عديم الفضيلة . مات وقد استجازه سبط شيخنا وما علمت لماذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm, Nūr al-Dīn b. al-Sharaf al-Manāwī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, al-Aswad. The brother of the aforementioned ʿAbd al-Raḥīm. He served as a deputy judge and preached. He had a hoarse voice and was devoid of merit. He died; the grandson of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) had requested an ijāza from him, and I do not know why."@en .

rec:AIND-D05088 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05088-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05088-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05088-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05088 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن الرضى أبي بكر بن محمد بن عبد اللطيف اليمني ثم المكي الشهير بالرضى أخو السراج عمر . كتب بجدة يسيرا ثم ترك ومات في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Riḍā Abū Bakr b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Yamanī, then al-Makkī, known as al-Riḍā. He was the brother of al-Sirāj ʿUmar. He worked as a scribe in Jidda for a short while and then gave it up, and he died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 892 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05089 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05089-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05089-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05089 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن علي الأشخر وصفه الناشري بالفقيه الصالح ونقل عنه عن جده العلامة الأوحد محمد شيئا وأن صاحب الترجمة قدم عليهم زبيد سنة أربع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Ashkhar. Al-Nāshirī described him as a righteous jurist, transmitted from him some material on the authority of his grandfather, the unique scholar Muḥammad, and stated that the subject of this entry came to them in Zabīd in the year 834 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05091 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05091-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05091-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05091 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن محمد المناوي نسبة لمنية بني خصيب ثم الأزهري الشافعي ويعرف قديما بابن المحوجب والآن بالأزهري . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Manāwī, the nisbah referring to Minyat Banī Khaṣīb, then al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī (of the Shafi'i school). He was formerly known as Ibn al-Muḥawjab and is now known as al-Azharī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05096 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05096-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05096-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05096-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05096 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أبي بكر نور الدين الديمي ثم القاهري الصحراوي . حج مع الرجبية وكان إماما الأمير الركب علان ومات بعد زيارته المدينة النبوية ووصوله مكة بها في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى وسبعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr, Nūr al-Dīn, al-Daymī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Ṣaḥrāwī. He performed the pilgrimage with the Rajab caravan (al-Rajabiyya) and served as the imam of the caravan commander (amīr al-rakb) ʿAllān. He died there (in Mecca) in Dhū al-Qaʿda 871 AH, after visiting the Prophet's City (Medina) and arriving in Mecca. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05097 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05097-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05097-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05097-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05097 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أبي بكر نور الدين الطوخي ثم القاهري التاجر جارنا قديما ووالد إبراهيم المتوفي قبله . مات في أوائل ذي القعدة سنة ثلاث وثمانين بعد أن عمي وأقعد وفجع بولده المشار إليه وكان شديد الحرص زائد الإمساك مع ذكره بمزيد المال عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr, Nūr al-Dīn al-Ṭūkhī, then al-Qāhirī, the merchant. He was our (al-Sakhāwī's) neighbor of old, and the father of Ibrāhīm who died before him. He died in the early part of Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 883 AH, after having become blind and unable to walk, and having been grieved by the loss of his aforementioned son. He was exceedingly greedy and very stingy, despite being known for his great wealth. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05100 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05100-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05100-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05100 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن جار الله بن زائد بن يحيى السنبسي المكي أخو أحمد الماضي ويعرف بابن زائد . ولد تقريبا سنة اثنتين وثمانين وسبعمائة وأجاز له بعيد ذلك جماعة منهم . مات بمكة في شعبان سنة سبع وثلاثين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Jār Allāh b. Zāʾid b. Yaḥyā al-Sunbisī al-Makkī. He was the brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad and was known as Ibn Zāʾid. He was born approximately in the year 782 AH, and shortly thereafter a group of scholars granted him an ijāza, among them [names missing in the edition]. He died in Mecca in Shaʿbān, 837 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05103 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05103-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05103-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05103 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن جعفر المشعري المكي . مات بها في رجب سنة اثنتين وستين أرخة ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Jaʿfar al-Mishʿarī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Rajab of the year 862 AH, as recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05105 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05105-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05105-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05105 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حجاج الحريري الدلال . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥajjāj al-Ḥarīrī al-Dallāl (the broker). One of those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05106 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05106-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05106-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05106-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05106 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حسب الله الجزار . مات بمكة في جمادى الأولى سنة ثلاث وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥasab Allāh al-Jazzār. He died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 883."@en .

rec:AIND-D05107 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05107-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05107-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05107 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن البدر حسن بن إبراهيم بن حسين بن عليبة الماضي أبوه وجده وشقيقه إبراهيم وهذا أكبرهما . مات في طاعون سنة سبع وتسعين ولم يكمل العشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Badr Ḥasan b. Ibrāhīm b. Ḥusayn b. ʿUlayba. His father, his grandfather, and his full brother Ibrāhīm have been mentioned above; he (ʿAlī) was the elder of the two. He died in the plague of the year 897, not having completed twenty years."@en .

rec:AIND-D05109 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05109-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05109-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05109-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05109 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حسن بن أبي بكر نور الدين النمراوي الخطيب والد البدر حسن ويعرف بابن الطويل . مات في المحرم أو صفر سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥasan b. Abī Bakr Nūr al-Dīn al-Namrāwī, the preacher (al-Khaṭīb), father of al-Badr Ḥasan, known as Ibn al-Ṭawīl. He died in Muḥarram or Ṣafar of the year 892."@en .

rec:AIND-D05117 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05117-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05117-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05117 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن الحسن بن علي نور الدين الدهثوري ثم القاهري ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Ḥasan b. ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn al-Dahthūrī, then al-Qāhirī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05118 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05118-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05118-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05118 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حسن بن علي المحلي الهيثمي ثم القاهري القصير خادم الشيخ محمد بن صالح الآتي ويعرف بين الفقراء ونحوهم بكاتم السر . لازم خدمة المشار إليه وتردد إلى الأكابر وتنزل في بعض الجهات وسمع على بعض الشيوخ بقراءتي بل سمع مني في الإملاء وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī al-Maḥallī al-Haythamī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Qaṣīr (the Short). He was the servant (khādim) of Shaykh Muḥammad b. Ṣāliḥ (mentioned below), and was known among the Sufis (fuqarāʾ) and their like as Kātim al-Sirr (the keeper of secrets). He devoted himself to the service of the aforementioned, frequented the notables, and obtained some stipendiary posts (jihāt). He heard from some shaykhs through my (al-Sakhāwī's) reading, and indeed heard from me in the dictation sessions (imlāʾ) and elsewhere."@en .

rec:AIND-D05119 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05119-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05119-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05119 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حسن بن علي الغمري المراكبي أبوه ويعرف بابن خروب . ممن حفظ المنهاج وعرض علي في جملة الجماعة ، وحج واشتغل قليلا عند الأمين ابن النجار ثم الحليبي وأهدي إليه فولاه الزيني زكريا قضاء منية غمر شركة لفارس ثم لغيره وعد من العجائب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī al-Ghamrī; his father was al-Marākibī (the boatman), and he is known as Ibn Kharrūb. He was among those who memorized al-Minhāj and recited it to me (al-Sakhāwī) among the group. He performed the pilgrimage and studied a little under al-Amīn Ibn al-Najjār, then al-Ḥulaybī. He was presented to al-Zaynī Zakariyyā, who appointed him to the judgeship of Minyat Ghamr in partnership with Fāris and then with others, which was counted among the marvels."@en .

rec:AIND-D05122 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05122-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05122-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05122 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حسين بن إبراهيم الدمشقي ويعرف بالغزاوي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn b. Ibrāhīm al-Dimashqī, known as al-Ghazzāwī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05124 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05124-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05124-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05124 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حسين بن علي بن حسين علاء الدين الدمشقي المكي الماضي أبوه ويعرف كهو بابن مكسب . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn ʿAlāʾ al-Dīn al-Dimashqī al-Makkī. His father has been mentioned above, and like him he is known as Ibn Maksab. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05125 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05125-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05125-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05125 ;
    aindv:sourceText "على بن حسين بن علي بن سلامة الدمشقي الشافعي. تفقه بالعماد الحسباني وغيره ودرس بدمشق وكانت له مشاركة في الأدب ونظم متوسط . مات بدمشق في سنة تسع عشرة . قاله شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Salāma al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī. He studied jurisprudence under al-ʿImād al-Ḥusbānī and others, and taught in Damascus. He had some share in literature, and his poetry was of middling quality. He died in Damascus in the year 819. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said so in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05127 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05127-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05127-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05127-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05127 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حسين بن علي الجراحي ثم الدمياطي بواب المعينية بها ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī al-Jarrāḥī, then al-Dimyāṭī, doorkeeper (bawwāb) of al-Muʿīniyya there (in Damietta). He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05129 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05129-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05129-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05129 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حسين بن محمد بن نافع الخزاعي المكي أخو محمد الآتي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn b. Muḥammad b. Nāfiʿ al-Khuzāʿī al-Makkī, brother of Muḥammad (mentioned below). He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05130 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05130-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05130-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05130-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05130 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حسين بن محمود نور الدين الحسيني البلخي الأصل المكي الشافعي ويعرف بالطيبي . ممن اشتغل قليلا وقرأ على السوهائي وكذا أخذ عني في مجاورتي الثالثة أشياء منها القول البديع بعد أن كتبه لنفسه ولغيره وجلس بباب السلام شاهدا وفي أيام الثمان ونحوها يكون بجانبه أوراق العمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn b. Maḥmūd Nūr al-Dīn al-Ḥusaynī, of Balkhī origin, the Meccan, Shāfiʿī, known as al-Ṭayyibī. He was among those who studied a little; he read under al-Sūhāʾī and likewise took from me (al-Sakhāwī), during my third stay (mujāwara) in Mecca, several things, among them al-Qawl al-Badīʿ, after he had copied it for himself and for others. He sat at Bāb al-Salām as a notary (shāhid), and in the \"days of the eight\" and the like the ʿumra papers (awrāq al-ʿumar) would be at his side."@en .

rec:AIND-D05132 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05132-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05132-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05132 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حسين نور الدين المنهلي الأزهري الشافعي ابن عم الزين عبد الرحمن الماضي . مات في ربيع الأول سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn Nūr al-Dīn al-Manhalī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī, paternal cousin of al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān (mentioned above). He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 891."@en .

rec:AIND-D05133 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05133-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05133-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05133-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05133 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حمزة فقيه الزيدية . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة أربع وستين بواسط من وادي مر ودفن هناك . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥamza, the jurist (faqīh) of the Zaydīs. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 864 at Wāsiṭ in Wādī Marr and was buried there. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D05134 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05134-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05134-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05134-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05134-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05134 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن حيدر شيخ تربة الأعجام بالقرب من تربة تغرى برمش الزردكاش وإمام برقوق نائب الشام كان مات في جمادى الأولى سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ḥaydar, shaykh of Turbat al-Aʿjām (the mausoleum of the non-Arabs) near the mausoleum of Taghrī Birmish al-Zardakāsh, and formerly imam of Barqūq, the viceroy of Syria. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 895."@en .

rec:AIND-D05135 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05135-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05135-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05135 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن خضر بن جمعة التميمي المقدسي الحنفي . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Khiḍr b. Jumʿa al-Tamīmī al-Maqdisī al-Ḥanafī. He was among those who took (knowledge) from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05136 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05136-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05136-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05136 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن خليل بن رسلان الرملاوي ثم المكي العطار فيها بباب السلام وشيخ أحد الأسباع بها أخذ عن الشهاب بن رسلان وكان شيخا مقرئا صالحا أخذ عنه أبو حامد المرشدي في القراءات وأخذها هو عن والده عمر المرشدي . ومات بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة ثمان وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Khalīl b. Ruslān al-Ramlāwī, then al-Makkī, the druggist (ʿaṭṭār) there at Bāb al-Salām and shaykh of one of the Qurʾān-recitation sevenths (asbāʿ) there. He studied under al-Shihāb b. Ruslān. He was a righteous shaykh and Qurʾān reciter. Abū Ḥāmid al-Murshidī took the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt) from him, and he (the subject) had taken them from his (Abū Ḥāmid's) father ʿUmar al-Murshidī. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 888."@en .

rec:AIND-D05140 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05140-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05140-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05140 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن خليل بن مسلم أبو الحسن المسلمي ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Khalīl b. Muslim Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muslimī ..."@en .

rec:AIND-D05144 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05144-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05144-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05144 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن داود بن محمد الخواجا العلاء الرومي ثم المكي . مات بها في رجب سنة ست وخمسين ودفن بتربة أعدها لنفسه من المعلاة . ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Dāwūd b. Muḥammad al-Khawājā al-ʿAlāʾ al-Rūmī, then al-Makkī. He died there (in Mecca) in Rajab of the year 856 and was buried in a tomb he had prepared for himself in al-Muʿallā. Ibn Fahd mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05145 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05145-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05145-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05145-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05145 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن راشد بن عرفة نور الدين العجلاني القائد . ممن عظم عند صاحبي مكة علي وأبي القسم ابني حسن بن عجلان . مات بمكة في ثالث المحرم سنة ست وستين أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Rāshid b. ʿArafa Nūr al-Dīn al-ʿAjlānī, the commander (al-qāʾid). He was among those held in high regard by the two lords of Mecca, ʿAlī and Abū al-Qāsim, the sons of Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān. He died in Mecca on the 3rd of Muḥarram of the year 866; Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D05150 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05150-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05150-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05150-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05150 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن ريحان العيني القائد . مات في المحرم سنة سبع وستين بمكة أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī ibn Rayḥān al-ʿAynī, the commander (al-Qāʾid). He died in Muḥarram of the year 867 AH in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05151 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05151-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05151-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05151-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05151 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن ريحان التعكري خال أبي بكر بن عبد الغني المرشدي . ممن أقام بالهند مدة . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة ثمان وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Rayḥān al-Taʿkarī, the maternal uncle of Abū Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī al-Murshidī. He was among those who resided in India for a period. He died in Mecca in Muḥarram of the year 878 AH. Ibn Fahd also recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05155 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05155-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05155-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05155 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن سالم بن ذاكر المكي الصائغ قريب رئيس المؤذنين بمكة . مات بها في رمضان سنة اثنتين وثمانين ودفن بالمعلاة . أرخهما ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Sālim b. Dhākir al-Makkī al-Ṣāʾigh (the goldsmith), a relative of the chief of the muezzins in Mecca. He died there in Ramaḍān of the year 882 AH and was buried in al-Muʿallā. Ibn Fahd recorded the death dates of both of them (the preceding person and him)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05157 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05157-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05157-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05157 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن سالم الرمثاوي البهنسي . مات بدمشق في ذي الحج سنة إحدى . أرخه شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Sālim al-Ramthāwī al-Bahnasī. He died in Damascus in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 801 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death in his Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D05158 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05158-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05158-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05158 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أبي سعد الحجر بن عبد الكريم بن أبي سعد بن عبد الكريم ابن أبي سعد بن علي بن قتادة الحسني المكي . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وثمانين بناحية اليمن . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Abī Saʿd al-Ḥajar b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Abī Saʿd b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Abī Saʿd b. ʿAlī b. Qatāda al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 882 AH in the region of Yemen. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05159 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05159-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05159-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05159-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05159 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أبي سعد بن محمد بن أبي سعد الشريف الحلي النموي . مات في ليلة الجمعة حادي عشر ربيع الآخر سنة أربع وأربعين وحمل لمكة فدفن بمعلاتها . أرخه ابن فهد أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Abī Saʿd b. Muḥammad b. Abī Saʿd al-Sharīf al-Ḥillī al-Namawī. He died on the eve of Friday, the 11th of Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 844 AH, and was carried to Mecca, where he was buried in its al-Muʿallā cemetery. Ibn Fahd also recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05160 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05160-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05160-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05160-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05160 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن سعيد بن عقبة المنور مات في مستهل ذي الحجة سنة سبع وستين أرخه ابن فهد"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Saʿīd b. ʿUqba al-Munawwar. He died on the first day of Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 867 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05161 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05161-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05161-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05161 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن سعيد بن عمر البطيني اليافعي الخراز . جرده ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Saʿīd b. ʿUmar al-Baṭīnī al-Yāfiʿī al-Kharrāz (the leather-stitcher). Ibn Fahd listed him (by name only)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05164 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05164-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05164-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05164 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن سلامة . فيمن اسم أبيه أحمد بن محمد بن سلامة نسب لجده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Salāma. [His entry is] among those whose father's name is Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Salāma; he was named after his grandfather."@en .

rec:AIND-D05167 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05167-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05167-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05167 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن سليمان بن عثمان النور الجبرتي المدني الشافعي ممن سمع مني بالمدينة النبوية"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Sulaymān b. ʿUthmān al-Nūr al-Jabartī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the Prophet's City (Medina)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05169 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05169-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05169-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05169-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05169 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن سليمان الطيبي . ممن أخذ عن الولي العراقي وكان يدرس بالمهمندارية ويسكن بالبياطرة . قرأ عليه الشمس الفارسكوري الظريف في سنة خمس وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Sulaymān al-Ṭībī. He was among those who studied under al-Walī al-ʿIrāqī; he used to teach at al-Mihmandāriyya and lived in al-Bayāṭira. Al-Shams al-Fāriskūrī al-Ẓarīf read under him in the year 845 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05170 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05170-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05170-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05170 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن سنان بن عبد الله بن عمر بن مسعود العمري المكي . كان أحد القواد العمرة وزيرا لأحمد بن عجلان . مات سنة خمس أو قريبا منها ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Sinān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Masʿūd al-ʿUmarī al-Makkī. He was one of the ʿUmarī commanders (quwwād) and a vizier to Aḥmad b. ʿAjlān. He died in the year 805 AH or thereabouts. Al-Fāsī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05171 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05171-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05171-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05171 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن سنقر العنتابي نقيب الجيش . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة إحدى . أرخه شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Sunqur al-ʿAyntābī, the naqīb al-jaysh (marshal of the army). He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 801 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death in his Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D05176 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05176-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05176-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05176-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05176 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن شاهين نائب قلعة دمشق . مات بها في ليلة الخميس ثاني عشري رمضان سنة إحدى وتسعين . أرخه ابن اللبودي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī ibn Shāhīn, the deputy (nāʾib) of the Citadel of Damascus. He died there on the eve of Thursday, the 22nd of Ramaḍān of the year 891 AH. Ibn al-Labūdī recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05177 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05177-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05177-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05177 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن شرعان بالمعجمة بن أحمد بن حسن بن عجلان السيد الحسني المكي . مات بها في المحرم سنة ست وثمانين ودفن بالمعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī ibn Sharʿān (with the dotted shīn) ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥasan ibn ʿAjlān, al-Sayyid al-Ḥasanī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Muḥarram of the year 886 AH and was buried in al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D05179 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05179-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05179-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05179-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05179 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن شكر الحسني حسن بن عجلان المكي أخو بديد الماضي وأحد كبار القواد المتمولين . مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة ثمان وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī ibn Shukr al-Ḥasanī [i.e. of the household of] Ḥasan ibn ʿAjlān, al-Makkī, the brother of the aforementioned Badīd and one of the great, wealthy commanders (quwwād). He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 858 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05180 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05180-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05180-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05180 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن شهاب بن علي الشغراوي المنوفي ويعرف بأبيه . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Shihāb b. ʿAlī al-Shaghrāwī al-Manūfī, known by his father's name. He is among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05182 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05182-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05182-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05182-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05182 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن الزين صدقة بن يوسف المسيري المؤذن بجامع الغمري في المحلة ويعرف بشبير . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī ibn al-Zayn Ṣadaqa ibn Yūsuf al-Misīrī, the muezzin of the al-Ghamrī Mosque in al-Maḥalla, known as Shubayr. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05183 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05183-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05183-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05183-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05183 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن صالح بن عبد الله المكي الجوهري نسبة لمولى لهم ممن كان يخدم القاضي أبا السعادات بن ظهيرة . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة إحدى وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ṣāliḥ b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Makkī al-Jawharī, (the latter being) an attribution to a client (mawlā) of theirs who used to serve the qāḍī Abū al-Saʿādāt b. Ẓahīra. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year 861 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05187 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05187-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05187-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05187 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن صلاح الغزي . ممن سمع علي قريب التسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ṣalāḥ al-Ghazzī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) around [the year] ninety (ca. 890 AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05189 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05189-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05189-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05189 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن طوعان دوادار قانصوه خمسمائة أمير آخور وأظن والده هو الماضي وأنه قتل في نيابة الكرك سنة ست وخمسين . تقدم عند مخدومه واستبدل الدار العظيمة التي بالقرب من جامع بشتاك وسكنها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ṭawʿān, the dawādār of Qānṣūh Khamsumiʾa (\"Qānṣūh Five-Hundred\"), the amīr ākhūr (master of the stables). I think that his father is the one mentioned above, and that he [the father] was killed while governor (nāʾib) of al-Karak in the year 856. He advanced in the service of his master, and acquired by exchange the great house near the mosque of Bashtāk and lived in it."@en .

rec:AIND-D05190 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05190-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05190-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05190-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05190 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن طيبغا بن حاجي بك العلاء التركماني العنتابي الحنفي . قال شيخنا في أنبائه : كان فاضلا وقورا مهر في الفنون وقرره الأشرف برسباي مدرسا وخطيبا بتربته التي أنشأها بالصحراء . مات في طريق الحجاز ودفن بالقرب من الينبوع سنة ثمان وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Ṭaybughā b. Ḥājjī Bak, al-ʿAlāʾ al-Turkumānī al-ʿAyntābī al-Ḥanafī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Inbāʾ: \"He was virtuous and dignified, and excelled in the sciences. Al-Ashraf Barsbāy appointed him teacher (mudarris) and preacher (khaṭīb) at his mausoleum (turba), which he had built in the desert (al-Ṣaḥrāʾ).\" He died on the road to the Ḥijāz and was buried near al-Yanbūʿ in the year 838."@en .

rec:AIND-D05193 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05193-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05193-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05193 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عباس الحنبلي . رأيته كتب في عرض سنة ثلاث وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbbās al-Ḥanbalī. I saw that he had written [his attestation] on a recitation certificate (ʿarḍ) of the year 803."@en .

rec:AIND-D05194 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05194-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05194-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05194 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الحق بن علي الحسني البلقسي شيخها والمتكلم على منى جعفر بلد خانقاه سرياقوس والماضي أبوه . ممن تعرض له بالغرامة غير مرة وبلغني أن من جملة من رافع فيه أخوه بركات وأخذ لأخيه أبي نصر منية حلفا ورسم على صاحب الترجمة لعمل حساب للأماكن الثلاثة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Ḥaqq b. ʿAlī al-Ḥasanī al-Bilqasī, the shaykh of that town [Bilqas] and the administrator (mutakallim) of Minā Jaʿfar, a village belonging to the khānqāh of Siryāqūs; his father has been mentioned above. He was among those who were subjected to fines more than once, and I was informed that among those who denounced him was his brother Barakāt, who obtained Minyat Ḥalfā for his brother Abū Naṣr, while the subject of this entry was placed under detention to render the accounts of the three places."@en .

rec:AIND-D05197 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05197-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05197-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05197 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن رمضان بن موسى البزار ويعرف بابن صلاح . مات في ربيع الثاني سنة سبعين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Ramaḍān b. Mūsā al-Bazzār, known as Ibn Ṣalāḥ. He died in Rabīʿ II of the year 870 in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05199 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05199-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05199-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05199 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة ابن عم الماضي قريبا وأمه أيضا زبيدية مات صغيرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓahīra, the paternal cousin of the one mentioned shortly above. His mother, too, was a woman of Zabīd. He died young."@en .

rec:AIND-D05203 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05203-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05203-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05203 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الرحمن بن سليم العسقلاني الأصل الجناني الأزهري أخو الشيخ سليم الماضي . مات قبل أخيه بقليل وكان خيرا. قاله شيخنا في ترجمة أخيه سنة أربعين من إنبائه قال : وأظنه جاز الثمانين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Salīm, of ʿAsqalānī origin, al-Janānī al-Azharī, the brother of the Shaykh Salīm mentioned above. He died shortly before his brother and was a good man. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said so in the biography of his brother under the year 840 in his Inbāʾ, adding: \"I think he had passed eighty; may God have mercy on him.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D05205 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05205-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05205-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05205 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن علي بن عبد المحسن بن جمال الثنا الخواجا نور الدين الشيباني البصري أخو الأمين عبد الله روى عنه قوله : %~% لما سمعت بمكر اللائمات وقد %~% أعددت متكئا ناديت أعنيه %~% %~% أيوسف اخرج عليهن الغداة اتل %~% فذالكن الذي لمتنني فيه %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Muḥsin b. Jamāl al-Thanāʾ, al-Khawājā Nūr al-Dīn al-Shaybānī al-Baṣrī, the brother of al-Amīn ʿAbd Allāh. The following verses of his are transmitted from him: \"When I heard of the guile of the blaming women, having prepared a couch, I called out—I mean to him—: 'O Joseph, go out before them this morning and recite: This is the one about whom you blamed me.'\""@en .

rec:AIND-D05211 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05211-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05211-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05211 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن إسمعيل الشلقامي . يأتي بزيادة محمد بعد جده قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl al-Shalqāmī. He follows shortly, with the addition of Muḥammad after his grandfather."@en .

rec:AIND-D05214 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05214-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05214-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05214 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد المكناسي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad al-Miknāsī. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05215 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05215-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05215-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05215 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الرحمن العلاء الموساوي . فيمن جده أحمد بن يوسف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-ʿAlāʾ al-Mūsāwī. [His entry is] among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. Yūsuf."@en .

rec:AIND-D05219 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05219-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05219-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05219 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الرحمن الجنائي . مضى فيمن جده سليم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Janāʾī. [His entry] has come above among those whose grandfather is Salīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D05220 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05220-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05220-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05220 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الرحمن القمني . فيمن جده علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Qimanī. [His entry is] among those whose grandfather is ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D05222 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05222-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05222-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05222 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد السلام بن الشيخ أحمد بن علي بن سيدهم النحريري الشافعي الرفاعي ويعرف بابن حمصيص بمهملة مفتوحة وصادين مهملتين أولاهما مكسورة . ولد سنة إحدى وثمانمائة بالنحرارية . ومات في أواخر سنة أربع وخمسين بها ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Salām b. al-Shaykh Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Sayyidihim al-Naḥrīrī al-Shāfiʿī al-Rifāʿī, known as Ibn Ḥimṣīṣ (with undotted ḥ vocalised a, and two undotted ṣ, the first vocalised i). He was born in the year 801 at al-Naḥrāriyya, and died there, presumably, at the end of the year 854."@en .

rec:AIND-D05223 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05223-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05223-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05223 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي شاه بن الخواجا عبد السلام بن حسن الجرجاني الأصل البحري الشافعي نزيل مكة والآتي شقيقه محمد . شاب سمع علي بمكة أربعي النووي وغيرها واشتغل قليلا وهو عاقل لا بأس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Shāh b. al-Khawājā ʿAbd al-Salām b. Ḥasan, of Jurjānī origin, al-Baḥrī al-Shāfiʿī, resident of Mecca; his full brother Muḥammad follows below. A young man who heard from me in Mecca the Forty [Ḥadīths] of al-Nawawī and other works, and studied a little; he is sensible and not bad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05225 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05225-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05225-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05225 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي المدعو كمال الدين محمد بن عبد الظاهر الشريف الأخميمي القاهري نزيل البردبكية ممن أخذ عن العلاء الحصني والزيني زكريا وتميز مع خير وعقل وسكون وقد تردد إلي قليلا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī, called Kamāl al-Dīn Muḥammad, b. ʿAbd al-Ẕāhir, al-Sharīf al-Akhmīmī al-Qāhirī, resident of al-Bardabakiyya. He was among those who studied under al-ʿAlāʾ al-Ḥiṣnī and al-Zaynī Zakariyyā, and distinguished himself, together with goodness, intelligence and composure. He frequented me (al-Sakhāwī) a little."@en .

rec:AIND-D05229 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05229-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05229-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05229-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05229 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد العزيز بن عبد الكافي الدقوقي جد الذي قبله ، كان ذا ملاءة جاور بمكة وخلف بها عقارا وأولادا . ومات بها في يوم الخميس ثامن ذي الحجة سنة خمس ودفن بالمعلاة . قاله الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Kāfī al-Daqūqī, the grandfather of the preceding. He was a man of means who took up residence (mujāwara) in Mecca and left behind there real estate and children. He died there on Thursday, 8 Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 805, and was buried at al-Muʿallā. So said al-Fāsī in [his history of] Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05233 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05233-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05233-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05233-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05233 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الغني بن عبد الله بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة القرشي المخزومي المكي . اشتغل وكان ذكيا . مات في ربيع الثاني سنة ثمان وسبعين بالقاهرة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī al-Makhzūmī al-Makkī. He occupied himself with study and was intelligent. He died in Rabīʿ II of the year 878 in Cairo. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D05234 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05234-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05234-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05234 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد القادر بن أبي البركات بن علي أبو البركات بن محيي الدين العقيلي النويري المكي الحنفي . ممن اشتغل بالفقه وأصوله والعربية قليلا وجل ذلك على الغرباء وسمع مني بمكة وهو دون أبيه في الحمق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Abī al-Barakāt b. ʿAlī, Abū al-Barakāt b. Muḥyī al-Dīn al-ʿUqaylī al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī al-Ḥanafī. He was among those who studied jurisprudence, its principles and Arabic a little, most of that under foreign scholars; he heard from me in Mecca, and he is less foolish than his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D05241 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05241-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05241-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05241 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الكريم بن علي بن عبد الكريم بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي حفيد الذي قبله وأمه زبيدية . بيض له ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī, the grandson of the preceding; his mother was a woman of Zabīd. Ibn Fahd left a blank for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05243 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05243-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05243-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05243 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الكريم الكتبي . فيمن جده إبراهيم بن أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Kutubī. Already mentioned under the entry of the one whose grandfather is Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05245 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05245-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05245-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05245-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05245 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن علي بن سالم الزبيدي الأصل المالكي . ولد بها ونشأ فسمع فيما أحسب على النشاوري وغيره وتعب بعد موت والده لقلة ما بيده . ومات بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتي عشرة عن نحو الثلاثين . ذكره الفاسي أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Sālim, of Zabīdī origin, the Mālikī. He was born and grew up there (Zabīd), and I believe he heard (hadith) from al-Nashāwurī and others. He struggled after his father's death due to his lack of means. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year 812 AH at about thirty years of age. Al-Fāsī also mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05248 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05248-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05248-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05248 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الله بن سنقر الحاج علاء الدين الحلبي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sunqur al-Ḥājj ʿAlāʾ al-Dīn al-Ḥalabī. He is among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05249 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05249-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05249-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05249-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05249-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05249 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الله بن عبد العزيز النور أبو الحسن الدميري ثم القاهري المالكي ويعرف بأخي بهرام . اشتغل بالقراءات وغيرها . وكان ممن أخذ عنه القراءات ابن الجندي والشرف موسى الضرير والشمس العسقلاني والعربية الغماري ودرس القراءات بالشيخونية وأقرأ أخذ عنه الزين رضوان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, al-Nūr, Abū al-Ḥasan, al-Damīrī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Mālikī. He is known as the brother of Bahrām. He occupied himself with the variant recitations (of the Qurʾān) and other subjects. Among those who took the variant recitations from him were Ibn al-Jundī, al-Sharaf Mūsā al-Ḍarīr, and al-Shams al-ʿAsqalānī, and al-Ghumārī took Arabic grammar from him. He taught the variant recitations at al-Shaykhūniyya, and al-Zayn Riḍwān took (recitations) from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05257 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05257-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05257-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05257-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05257 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الله بن محمد الفقيه نور الدين مؤدب الأطفال . مات في ثاني المحرم سنة خمس وستين ويقال أنه بلغ القرن . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad, al-Faqīh, Nūr al-Dīn, a tutor of children. He died on the second of al-Muḥarram in the year 865, and it is said that he lived to be a hundred years old. Al-Munīr recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D05259 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05259-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05259-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05259 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الله بن يوسف الكمبايتي الفيلي خادم الشلح . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Yūsuf al-Kambāyitī al-Fīlī, the servant of al-Shalaḥ. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05260 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05260-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05260-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05260-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05260 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الله بن الشقيف سمع من الزين المراغي المسلسل وختم البخاري . ومات بمكة في المحرم سنة إحدى وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Shaqīf. He heard 『al-Musalsal』 and the conclusion of the reading of 『al-Bukhārī』 from al-Zayn al-Marāghī. He died in Mecca in al-Muḥarram, the year 861 AH, as recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05262 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05262-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05262-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05262-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05262 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الله نور الدين النحريري الأديب ويعرف بابن عامرية كان شاعرا أديبا مكثرا سيما من المديح النبوي وللناس فيه اعتقاد . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وثلاثين بالنحرارية من الغربية رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh, Nūr al-Dīn al-Naḥrīrī, the littérateur, known as Ibn ʿĀmiriyya. He was a poet and a prolific writer, particularly of praises of the Prophet, and people held him in high spiritual regard. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhar, 832 AH, in al-Naḥrārīya in the Gharbiyya province, may Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05263 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05263-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05263-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05263-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05263 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الله نور الدين المصري القرافي الحنفي . ناب في الحكم ومهر فيه وشارك في مذهبه . مات في رمضان سنة ست عشرة . قال شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh Nūr al-Dīn al-Miṣrī al-Qarāfī al-Ḥanafī. He served as a deputy judge, excelled in it, and participated in his school (the Hanafi madhhab). He died in Ramadan in the year 816 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his work Inbāʾ al-Ghumr."@en .

rec:AIND-D05265 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05265-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05265-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05265-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05265 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الله نور الدين النفيائي القاهري والد أحمد وأخو أحمد ومحمد ممن دخلوا في الإسلام وقرءوا القرآن وحجوا ، وتكسب هذا بالعطر ونحوه وتنزل في سعيد السعداء على خير وستر . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة تسع وثمانين وقد جاز الأربعين ظنا رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh Nūr al-Dīn al-Nifyāʾī al-Qāhirī. He was the father of Aḥmad, and the brother of Aḥmad and Muḥammad, who converted to Islam, read the Qurʾān, and performed the Hajj. He earned his living as a perfumer and settled in Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ (Khānqāh) in goodness and decency. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir, 889 H, having presumably passed the age of forty. May Allāh have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05267 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05267-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05267-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05267 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الله الغزي . مضى فيمن جده محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ghazzī. Already mentioned under the entry of the one whose grandfather is Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05268 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05268-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05268-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05268 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الله القرشي المكي الشاهد بباب السلام منها . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن عبد الله بن خليل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Qurashī al-Makkī, the notary (shāhid) at Bāb al-Salām there (Mecca). Already mentioned under the entry of the one whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Khalīl."@en .

rec:AIND-D05271 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05271-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05271-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05271 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبد الملك البجائي الحسناوي . مات سنة بضع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Malik al-Bijāʾī al-Ḥasnāwī. He died in the year eight hundred and twenty-something (823-829 AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05275 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05275-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05275-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05275-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05275-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05275 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عبيد الله الدورشي البستاني شيخ جاز المائة ، استجازه ابن موسى المراكشي لأبن شيخنا وغيره في سنة خمس عشرة بل سمع عليه مع ابن موسى شيخنا الأبي وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Dawrshī al-Bustānī, a shaykh who lived past one hundred years. Ibn Mūsā al-Marrākushī requested an ijāza from him for the son of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others in the year 815 AH; indeed, our shaykh al-Ubbī and others heard [ḥadīth] from him alongside Ibn Mūsā."@en .

rec:AIND-D05282 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05282-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05282-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05282-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05282-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05282-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D05282-resp-6 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review,
        agent:claude_b87_apply2,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05282 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عثمان بن محمد بن الشمس لولو الحلبي ثم الدمشقي أخو زينب . ولد في سنة ست وعشرين وسبعمائة وأحضر على الحجار ثلاثيات البخاري وجزء أبي الجهم ، وحدث روى لنا عنه غير واحد منهم شيخنا وذكره في معجمه فقال : أجاز لنا ومات ببيت لهيا في المحرم سنة إحدى رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad b. al-Shams Luʾluʾ al-Ḥalabī, later al-Dimashqī, the brother of Zaynab. He was born in the year 726 AH. He attended the readings of the Thulāthiyyāt of al-Bukhārī and the Juzʾ of Abū al-Jahm under al-Ḥajjār. Several people narrated from him, including our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), who mentioned him in his Muʿjam and said: 'He granted us an ijāza.' He passed away at his home in Bayt Lahyā in al-Muḥarram, the year 801 AH. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05284 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05284-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05284-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05284 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عثمان المنجلاتي البخاري . مات سنة خمس عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī ibn ʿUthmān al-Manjalātī al-Bukhārī. He died in the year 815 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05285 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05285-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05285-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05285 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عثمان أبو الحسن المطيب . قدوة الحنفية باليمن في عصره ووالد محمد الآتي . وولاه الأشرف قضاء مذهبه بزبيد في سنة إحدى وسبعين وسبعمائة ومات في سنة اثنتين . ذكره العفيفي الناشري ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿUthmān, Abū al-Ḥasan, al-Muṭayyab. The exemplar of the Hanafis in Yemen in his time, and the father of Muḥammad, who is mentioned below. Al-Ashraf appointed him as the judge of his madhhab in Zabīd in the year 771 AH, and he died in the year 802 AH. Al-ʿAfīfī al-Nāshirī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05286 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05286-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05286-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05286 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن عراق . في ابن عبد الرحمن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿIrāq. See under Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān."@en .

rec:AIND-D05288 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05288-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05288-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05288 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن علي بن إسماعيل الحنفي الصوفي . ممن أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAlī b. Ismāʿīl, al-Ḥanafī al-Ṣūfī. One of those who took [knowledge] from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05289 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05289-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05289-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b84_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05289 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن علي بن سليمان بن أيوب النور بن العلاء بن العلم بن النجم الفخري . كان القائم بأمور الحسبة حين مباشرة يشبك الجمالي لها مات في . وله ابن اسمه شمس الدين محمد يقرأ على الديمي . وقال أنه شافعي وقد حضر إلي وسمع مع الجماعة قليلا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ali b. Ali b. Sulayman b. Ayyub, al-Nur al-Fakhri. He was in charge of the affairs of market supervision (hisba) when Yashbak al-Jamali held the office. He died. He had a son named Shams al-Din Muhammad, who studied under al-Daymi. He stated that he was a Shafi'i, and he attended my circle and heard a little along with the group."@en .

rec:AIND-D05293 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05293-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05293-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05293-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b100_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05293 ;
    aindv:sourceText "881 علي بن علي بن يوسف البهلوان ، مات بمكة في المحرم سنة ثمان وستين أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf al-Bahlawān. He died in Mecca in Muḥarram (8)68. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05294 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05294-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05294-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05294 ;
    aindv:sourceText "882 علي بن علي ويعرف بابن القطان . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿAlī, known as Ibn al-Qaṭṭān. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05297 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05297-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05297-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05297 ;
    aindv:sourceText "885 علي بن عمر بن أحمد بن فتيان النور السكندري التاجر . ممن لازمني بمكة في المجاورة الثانية وكذا تردد إلي بعد بالقاهرة وصار بعد ثروته إلى هيئة إملاق مع تصونه وتستره وربما نقص عقله وزاد هذيانه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. Fityān, al-Nūr al-Sakandarī, the merchant. He was among those who kept close company with me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca during (my) second sojourn there, and likewise he later frequented me in Cairo. After having been wealthy he fell into a state of destitution, while remaining self-restrained and discreet; at times his mind failed and his raving increased."@en .

rec:AIND-D05301 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05301-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05301-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05301-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05301-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b100_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05301 ;
    aindv:sourceText "889 علي بن عمر بن رسلان بن نصير البلقيني الأصل القاهري . هكذا رأيت اسمه بخطه في عرض محيى الدين الأزهري مؤرخا كتابته بسنة ثمانمائة وأنه أجاز للعارض ماله من تعليق وهو غريب فما علمت في بني الشيخ من اسمه علي فالله أعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. Raslān b. Nuṣayr, of Bulqīnī origin, al-Qāhirī. Thus I saw his name in his own handwriting on the presentation record (ʿarḍ) of Muḥyī al-Dīn al-Azharī, with the writing dated to the year 800, and that he granted the presenter an ijāza for whatever writings (taʿlīq) he had. This is strange, for I know of no one named ʿAlī among the family of the Shaykh (al-Sirāj al-Bulqīnī). God knows best."@en .

rec:AIND-D05308 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05308-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05308-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05308 ;
    aindv:sourceText "896 علي بن عمر بن علي بن عمر بن علي بن أحمد أبو الحسن بن السراج أبي حفص بن النور بن عرب وهو بكنيته أشهر . ولد في سنة ثمان وعشرين وثمانمائة وناب عن العلم البلقيني فمن بعده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad, Abū al-Ḥasan b. al-Sirāj Abī Ḥafṣ b. al-Nūr b. ʿArab; he is better known by his kunya. He was born in 828 and served as deputy (judge) under al-ʿAlam al-Bulqīnī and those after him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05311 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05311-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05311-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05311 ;
    aindv:sourceText "899 علي بن الخواجا عمر بن علي بن ناصر الحصني التاجر ويعرف بابن ناصر . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Khawājā ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Nāṣir al-Ḥiṣnī, the merchant, known as Ibn Nāṣir. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05312 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05312-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05312-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Saeri_Kato,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05312 ;
    aindv:sourceText "900 علي بن عمر بن علي العلاء الحسيني العجلوني ويعرف بابن قزلمي . ممن سمع مني في المحرم سنة تسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī, al-ʿAlāʾ al-Ḥusaynī al-ʿAjlūnī, known as Ibn Qizlimī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Muḥarram (8)90."@en .

rec:AIND-D05501 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05501-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05501-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05501-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05501 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي الزين الأنصاري الزرندي المدني الحنفي . ولد سنة أربع وسبعين وأخذ الفنون عن الجلال الخجندي وسمع على الجمال الأميوطي وحدث ودرس . مات في سادس عشري ذي الحجة سنة تسع عشرة . قلت وينظر مع الماضي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, al-Zayn al-Anṣārī al-Zarandī al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī. He was born in 774, took the various sciences from al-Jalāl al-Khujandī, heard from al-Jamāl al-Amyūṭī, transmitted ḥadīth and taught. He died on 26 Dhū al-Ḥijja 819. I say: he should be examined together with the one mentioned shortly before."@en .

rec:AIND-D05502 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05502-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05502-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05502 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علاء العلاء الدمشقي الحنفي بن الحريري . ولد سنة تسع وثلاثين وسبعمائة واشتغل على مذهب الحنفية وتعانى حفظ السير والمغازي وكان يستحضر منها شيئا كثيرا ، وصاهره الشهاب الغزي على ابنته . مات سنة ثلاث عشرة ولم تلبث ابنته إلا قليلا وماتت . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlāʾ, al-ʿAlāʾ al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanafī, Ibn al-Ḥarīrī. Born in 739, he studied according to the Ḥanafī school and devoted himself to memorizing the sīra and maghāzī, retaining a great deal of them. Al-Shihāb al-Ghazzī became his son-in-law by marrying his daughter. He died in 813, and his daughter survived him only a little. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05503 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05503-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05503-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05503 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي العلاء الطرسوسي المزي . استجازه لي إبراهيم العجلوني في سنة خمسين وقال أنه حضر على ابن أميلة والزين القرشي وابن رجب وأنه سمعه يقول : أرسل إلي الزين العراقي يستعين بي في شرح الترمذي قال وكان العلاء هذا ناظر الجامع المرجاني بالمزة . قلت ومات بعد يسير فالله أعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, al-ʿAlāʾ al-Ṭarsūsī al-Mizzī. Ibrāhīm al-ʿAjlūnī obtained an ijāza from him on my behalf in the year 850, and said that he had attended (the sessions of) Ibn Umayla, al-Zayn al-Qurashī and Ibn Rajab, and that he heard him say: \"al-Zayn al-ʿIrāqī sent to me seeking my help with the commentary on al-Tirmidhī.\" He (Ibrāhīm) said: this al-ʿAlāʾ was the supervisor (nāẓir) of the Marjānī Mosque at al-Mizza. I say: he died shortly afterwards, and God knows best."@en .

rec:AIND-D05504 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05504-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05504-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05504 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي العلاء النمراوي ويعرف بابن النجاري ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-ʿAlāʾ al-Namrāwī, also known as Ibn al-Najjārī. He is among those who heard Hadith from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05505 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05505-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05505-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05505-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05505 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي نور الدين الجعبري الدمشقي ثم القادري الذهبي . ممن سمع على شيخنا وعلى ابن الجزري وغيرهما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn al-Jaʿbarī al-Dimashqī, later al-Qādirī al-Dhahabī. He heard hadith from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and from Ibn al-Jazarī, and others."@en .

rec:AIND-D05508 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05508-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05508-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05508 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي السيرجي ثم المكي . فيمن جده علي بن خليل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Sayrajī, later al-Makkī. [His entry is] among those whose grandfather is ʿAlī b. Khalīl."@en .

rec:AIND-D05509 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05509-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05509-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05509 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي الشكيوي الدرعي المغربي المالكي ممن سمع مني بالمدينة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī bin Muḥammad bin ʿAlī al-Shakywī al-Darʿī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D05510 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05510-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05510-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05510-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05510 ;
    aindv:sourceText "1090علي بن محمد بن علي الغزولي شقيق أحمد الماضي ويعرف بالهنيدي مات في جمادى الثانية سنة خمس وتسعين وكان عاميا مسرفا على نفسه عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Ghazūlī, full brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad, known as al-Hunaydī. He died in Jumādā II 895. He was a commoner who was dissolute toward himself; may God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05511 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05511-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05511-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05511-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05511 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي الطياري القاهري صهر المحب بن نصر الله البغدادي الحنبلي زوج ابنته . رجل صالح معتقد ساكن ممن سمع الحديث على شيخنا وغيره ومما سمعه في البخاري بالظاهرية ، وتنزل في الجهات وكان ينسب لثروة ، وآخر عهدي به سنة ثلاث وستين وفي الظن أنه قارب الستين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Ṭayyārī al-Qāhirī, son-in-law of al-Muḥibb b. Naṣr Allāh al-Baghdādī al-Ḥanbalī, husband of his daughter. A righteous, revered and quiet man, he heard ḥadīth from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others; among what he heard was the Ṣaḥīḥ of al-Bukhārī at the Ẓāhiriyya. He held stipendiary posts and was reputed to be wealthy. The last I knew of him was in the year 863, when he was thought to be nearly sixty. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05512 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05512-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05512-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05512 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي القباني أبوه ويعرف بابن بهاء . مات في رمضان سنة ست وتسعين بعد ضعف مدة عفا الله عنه وأعطى السلطان جواليه لولد له من أمة ولم يسمح الشافعي بذلك في جهاته التي تحت نظره بل أعطاها لجماعته من بنيه ونحوهم حسبما بلغني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī; his father was al-Qabbānī (the weigher), and he was known as Ibn Bahāʾ. He died in Ramaḍān 896 after a period of weakness, may God pardon him. The sultan granted his jawālī (stipends) to a son of his by a slave woman, but the Shāfiʿī (chief qāḍī) did not permit this in the posts under his supervision and instead gave them to his own people, his sons and the like, according to what reached me."@en .

rec:AIND-D05513 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05513-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05513-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05513 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي القلصادي الأندلسي الحيسوب ، قال ابن عزم صاحبنا . مات سنة بضع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Qalaṣādī al-Andalusī, the arithmetician (al-ḥaysūb). Our companion Ibn ʿAzm said that he died in the [eight hundred and] fifty-something."@en .

rec:AIND-D05514 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05514-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05514-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05514 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي الكفرسوسي . مات في رمضان سنة ثلاث وقد ناهز السبعين . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Kafarsūsī. He died in Ramaḍān 803, approaching seventy. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05515 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05515-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05515-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05515-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05515-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05515 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن علي المزي الدمشقي ويعرف بابن جديا . استجازه لي إبراهيم العجلوني في سنة خمسين وترجمه بأنه كان يواظب ابن أميلة وأنه كان يحكى عنه أنه كان إذا أذن على المنارة يسمع من جولان فلما ضعف وصار يؤذن على البئر التي بباب الجامع المرجاني كان يسمع من المقصورة وقال أن ابن أميلة أجاز له فالله أعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Mizzī al-Dimashqī, known as Ibn Jadyā. Ibrāhīm al-ʿAjlūnī obtained an ijāza from him on my behalf in the year 850 and described him as one who constantly attended Ibn Umayla; it used to be related of him that when he gave the call to prayer from the minaret it could be heard from the Jawlān (Golan), and when he grew weak and began giving the call at the well by the gate of the Marjānī Mosque, it could be heard from the maqṣūra. He claimed that Ibn Umayla had granted him an ijāza—and God knows best."@en .

rec:AIND-D05518 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05518-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05518-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05518-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05518 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن عمر بن سليمان بن عبد الرحمن نور الدين بن صلاح الدين المليجي ثم القاهري الأزهري الشافعي ويعرف بالمليجي . ممن سمع مني في يوم عيد الفطر سنة خمس وتسعين بمنزلي المسلسل بيوم العيد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. Sulaymān b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Nūr al-Dīn, al-Malījī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Azhari, al-Shāfiʿī, known as al-Malījī. He was among those who heard from me, on the day of ʿĪd al-Fiṭr in the year 895, at my house, the musalsal hadith of the day of ʿĪd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05521 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05521-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05521-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05521 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن عمر بن علي بن إبراهيم المكي ويعرف بابن الوكيل . كان أبوه من أعيان تجار مكة وخلف مالا جزيلا من نقد وعقار فلما بلغ أذهب غالب العقار في غير وجهه ثم توفيت أمه وتركت أيضا عقارا فأذهبه . ومات في حدود سنة ست ودفن بالمعلاة . ذكره الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Ibrāhīm al-Makkī, known as Ibn al-Wakīl. His father was one of the leading merchants of Mecca and left great wealth in cash and property; when ʿAlī came of age he squandered most of the property improperly, and when his mother later died leaving property as well, he squandered that too. He died around the year [80]6 and was buried at al-Muʿallā. Al-Fāsī mentioned him in (his history of) Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05522 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05522-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05522-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05522-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05522 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن عمر الموفق أبو الحسن الشرعبي اليماني الشافعي . تلا للسبع على الزرتيتي وابن الجزري تلا عليه أبو بكر بن إبراهيم البغلائي الحراري اليماني الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar, al-Muwaffaq Abū al-Ḥasan al-Sharʿabī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī. He recited the Seven Readings under al-Zarātītī and Ibn al-Jazarī. Abū Bakr b. Ibrāhīm al-Baghlāʾī al-Ḥarārī al-Yamānī, mentioned below, recited under him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05528 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05528-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05528-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05528 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن غضنفر بن حسب الله بن مفرج بن عرفطة بن محمود بن موسى الشريف الحسني العرفطي الزيدي صاحب سروعة . مات في رجب سنة ثلاث وستين بالمرة وحمل إلى ضيعة سروعة بوادي مر من أعمال مكة فدفن بها عند سلفه ، وكان معتقدا . ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Ghaḍanfar b. Ḥasab Allāh b. Mufarrij b. ʿUrfuṭa b. Maḥmūd b. Mūsā, al-Sharīf al-Ḥasanī al-ʿUrfuṭī al-Zaydī, lord of Sarūʿa. He died in Rajab 863 at al-Marra and was carried to the estate of Sarūʿa in Wādī Marr, in the district of Mecca, where he was buried beside his forebears. He was revered (as a holy man). Ibn Fahd mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05529 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05529-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05529-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05529 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن فتح الموصلي الحنفي نزيل طرابلس . ممن عرض عليه الصلاح الطرابلسي بها في سنة ست وأربعين وكتب له إجازة بخط جيد وقال الصلاح إنه كان يفتي على المذاهب الأربعة وأقام عندهم مدة يسيرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Fatḥ al-Mawṣilī al-Ḥanafī, resident of Tripoli. He was among those to whom al-Ṣalāḥ al-Ṭarābulusī presented (texts) there in the year 846, and he wrote him an ijāza in a fine hand. Al-Ṣalāḥ said that he used to issue fatwās according to the four madhhabs and that he stayed with them only a short while."@en .

rec:AIND-D05531 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05531-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05531-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05531-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05531 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن فرج السبتي الوادياشي المالكي والد أبا القاسم القادم علينا والآتي ، مات بقلعة المرية من الأندلس سنة اثنتين وتسعين عن بضع وخمسين وكان فاضلا ولي قضاء وادياش ثم خطابتها وتدريسها والنظر على الجامع به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Faraj al-Sabtī al-Wādyāshī al-Mālikī, father of Abū al-Qāsim who came to us and is mentioned below. He died at the citadel of Almería in al-Andalus in the year 892, aged fifty-something. He was an accomplished man who held the judgeship of Guadix (Wādī Āsh), then its preachership and professorship, and the supervision of its congregational mosque."@en .

rec:AIND-D05532 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05532-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05532-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05532 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن فضل نور الدين السنيكي ثم القاهري الأزهري الشافعي المسلمي . ممن سمع على شيخنا وفي البخاري بالظاهرية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Faḍl, Nūr al-Dīn, al-Sunaykī, later al-Qāhirī, al-Azharī, al-Shāfiʿī, al-Muslimī. He is among those who heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and heard al-Bukhārī at al-Ẓāhiriyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D05533 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05533-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05533-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05533-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05533 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن أبى الفضل بن علي العلاء بن جلال بن الردادي الحنفي المبتلي الماضي جد أبيه قريبا . ممن سمع على التقي الشمني والعلم البلقيني وغيرهما مع أبيه بل سمع مني ، ومات في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وتسعين وقد جاز الثلاثين عوضه الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Faḍl b. ʿAlī, al-ʿAlāʾ b. Jalāl Ibn al-Raddādī, al-Ḥanafī al-Mubtalī; his father's grandfather was mentioned shortly before. Together with his father he heard from al-Taqī al-Shumunnī, al-ʿAlam al-Bulqīnī and others, and indeed he heard from me (al-Sakhāwī). He died in Rabīʿ I 892, having passed thirty; may God recompense him with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D05534 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05534-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05534-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05534 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن فلاح الخارجي الشعشاع . مات سنة ثلاث وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Fallāḥ al-Khārjī al-Shaʿshāʿ. He died in the year 863 H."@en .

rec:AIND-D05535 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05535-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05535-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05535 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن قاسم الحاج علي بن المرخم والد الشمس محمد بن المرخم . كان عاميا خيرا مديم الجماعة والذكر . مات بعد الثلاثين وقد قارب السبعين ظنا فيهما ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Qāsim, al-Ḥājj ʿAlī b. al-Murakhkhim, father of al-Shams Muḥammad b. al-Murakhkhim. He was a good-hearted commoner, constant in congregational prayer and dhikr. He died after [8]30, having approached seventy—both being conjecture."@en .

rec:AIND-D05536 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05536-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05536-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05536 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن قحر بقاف مضمومة ثم حاء مهملة وآخره راء . مضى فيمن جده عبد العلي قحر وهو مع الماضي قريبا يدخل في المتفق والمفترق والمؤتلف والمختلف على أن بعضهم صحفه كالأول ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Quḥr (ḍamma on the qāf, then undotted ḥāʾ, ending in rāʾ). Already mentioned among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd al-ʿAlī Quḥr; he and the one mentioned shortly before fall under al-muttafiq wa-l-muftariq and al-muʾtalif wa-l-mukhtalif, though some have miscopied his name like the former."@en .

rec:AIND-D05537 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05537-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05537-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05537 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن قوام . مضى في ابن قوام ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Qawām. Already mentioned under Ibn Qawām."@en .

rec:AIND-D05538 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05538-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05538-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05538 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن الشيخ الفاضل كحل المغربي الحميضي . كان جده من موالي السيد حميضة ، سمع في سنة أربع عشرة على الزين المراغي ختم مسلم وغيره منه . ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. al-Shaykh al-Fāḍil Kuḥl al-Maghribī al-Ḥumayḍī. His grandfather was one of the clients (mawālī) of al-Sayyid Ḥumayḍa. In the year 814 he heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī the completion (khatm) of (the Ṣaḥīḥ of) Muslim and other things. Ibn Fahd mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05540 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05540-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05540-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05540 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن أبي اليمن محمد بن أحمد بن الرضي إبراهيم بن محمد بن إبراهيم الطبري المكي ، وأمه فاطمة ابنة الشمس محمد بن علي بن سكر البكري . سمع من الشريف أحمد الفاسي وابن سلامة في سنة ثماني عشرة . بيض له ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Yumn Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Raḍī Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm al-Ṭabarī al-Makkī; his mother was Fāṭima, daughter of al-Shams Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Sukkar al-Bakrī. He heard from al-Sharīf Aḥmad al-Fāsī and Ibn Salāma in the year 818. Ibn Fahd left his entry blank."@en .

rec:AIND-D05555 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05555-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05555-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05555 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد المنعم بن عمر بن غدير العلاء بن الشرف بن البدر الطائي القواس . مات في المحرم سنة إحدى وعم جده عمر بن عبد المنعم مسند شهير . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Munʿim b. ʿUmar b. Ghudayr, al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Sharaf b. al-Badr al-Ṭāʾī al-Qawwās. He died in Muḥarram 801. His grandfather's uncle ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Munʿim was a famous musnid. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05558 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05558-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05558-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05558 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد بن أبي الخير محمد بن فهد أسد الدين أبو الحسن بن التقي الهاشمي المكي شقيق النجم عمر وإخوته . ولد في صفر سنة أربعين بمكة ومات بها في ذي الحجة فيها . ذكره أخوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Khayr Muḥammad b. Fahd, Asad al-Dīn Abū al-Ḥasan b. al-Taqī al-Hāshimī al-Makkī, full brother of al-Najm ʿUmar and his brothers. He was born in Ṣafar 840 in Mecca and died there in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the same year. His brother mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05560 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05560-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05560-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05560 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد العلاء البخاري . صوابه محمد يأتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, al-ʿAlāʾ al-Bukhārī. Correctly (his name is) Muḥammad; he is mentioned below."@en .

rec:AIND-D05561 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05561-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05561-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05561 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن وفا . يأتي بدون محمد الثالث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Wafā. He is mentioned below without the third Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05563 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05563-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05563-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05563-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05563 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد الفرخي التجافيفي المكي أحد المتمولين المعاملين حضر على المجد اللغوي في صفر سنة ثلاث وثمانمائة الأول من مسلسلات العلائي وغيره ، ومات بمكة في رجب سنة أربع وستين . ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Farkhī al-Tajāfīfī al-Makkī, one of the wealthy men engaged in trade. In Ṣafar 803 he attended (the reading of) the first part of al-ʿAlāʾī's Musalsalāt and other works under al-Majd al-Lughawī (al-Fayrūzābādī). He died in Mecca in Rajab 864. Ibn Fahd mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05567 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05567-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05567-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05567 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد بن يحيى بن سالم الخشبي المدني . ولد بها في جمادى الآخرة سنة إحدى وثمانين وسبعمائة ، وأجاز له في جملة إخوته في سنة سبع وتسعين محمد بن عبد الله البهنسي ومحمد بن أبي البقاء السبكي وسعد بن يوسف النووي ومحمد بن اسحق الابرقوهي ومحمد بن أبي بكر البكري وغيرهم . ومات بالقاهرة في طاعون سنة ثلاث وثلاثين . أرخه ابن فهد في معجمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā b. Sālim al-Khashabī al-Madanī. He was born there in Jumādā II 781. In 797, together with his brothers, he was granted ijāza by Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Bahnasī, Muḥammad b. Abī al-Baqāʾ al-Subkī, Saʿd b. Yūsuf al-Nawawī, Muḥammad b. Isḥāq al-Abraqūhī, Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-Bakrī and others. He died in Cairo in the plague of 833. Ibn Fahd recorded his death in his Muʿjam."@en .

rec:AIND-D05568 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05568-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05568-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05568-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05568 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد بن يوسف العلاء الدمشقي بن الجزري أخو شيخ القراء الشمس محمد الآتي . كان فيما بلغني عالما مقرئا وهو جد الشريف ناصر الدين محمد بن أبي بكر بن علي نقيب الأشراف لأمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf, al-ʿAlāʾ al-Dimashqī Ibn al-Jazarī, brother of the shaykh of the Qurʾān-readers al-Shams Muḥammad, mentioned below. According to what reached me he was a scholar and reader (muqriʾ); he was the maternal grandfather of the sharīf Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī, the naqīb al-ashrāf."@en .

rec:AIND-D05569 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05569-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05569-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05569-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05569 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد العلاء بن البهاء بن البرجي الآتي أبوه وهو سبط البدر بن السراج البلقيني ، أمه بلقيس وعم أوحد الدين محمد بن البرجي . كان أحد صوفية سعيد السعداء . مات في رمضان سنة خمس وسبعين وعن نحو سبعين سنة عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Bahāʾ Ibn al-Burjī, whose father is mentioned below. He was the daughter's son of al-Badr b. al-Sirāj al-Bulqīnī, his mother being Balqīs, and the paternal uncle of Awḥad al-Dīn Muḥammad b. al-Burjī. He was one of the Sufis of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. He died in Ramaḍān 875, aged about seventy; may God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05570 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05570-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05570-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05570 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد الصدر الأدمي . فيمن جده محمد بن أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, al-Ṣadr al-Ādamī. [His entry is] among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05571 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05571-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05571-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05571 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد العلاء بن ناصر الدين بن ناصر الدين التركماني . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-ʿAlāʾ b. Nāṣir al-Dīn b. Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Turkumānī. One of those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05573 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05573-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05573-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05573 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد أبو الحسن البسطي . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Basṭī. Already mentioned among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D05574 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05574-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05574-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05574 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد الأدمي . فيمن جده محمد بن أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Ādamī. [His entry is] among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05575 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05575-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05575-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05575 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي ابن محمد بن محمد الأندلسي القلصاوي الحيوب هو البسطي مضى فيمن جده محمد بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Andalusī al-Qalaṣāwī, the arithmetician (al-ḥayūb), i.e. al-Basṭī. Already mentioned among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D05576 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05576-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05576-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05576-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05576 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمد الدلجي الأصل القاهري الوزيري المهتار فطيس . يأتي له ذكر في أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, of Dalja origin, al-Qāhirī al-Wazīrī, the mihtār, (called) Fuṭays. He is mentioned in his father's entry."@en .

rec:AIND-D05577 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05577-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05577-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05577 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمود بن حميدان . في ابن أبي الفرج ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Maḥmūd b. Ḥumaydān. [His entry is] under Ibn Abī al-Faraj."@en .

rec:AIND-D05578 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05578-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05578-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05578 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمود بن عادل الحسيني المدني الحنفي أخو أبي الفتح الآتي . حفظ القرآن وجود الخط وهو الآن حي مع صغر سنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Maḥmūd b. ʿĀdil al-Ḥusaynī al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī, the brother of Abū al-Fatḥ, who is mentioned below. He memorized the Qurʾān and perfected his calligraphy. He is currently alive, despite his young age."@en .

rec:AIND-D05579 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05579-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05579-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05579 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن محمود العلاء الرميني ثم الحلبي الشافعي نزيل القاهرة والآتي ولده محمد وجده . سمع من الزين العراقي وغيره ، ومات قريب سنة أربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Maḥmūd, al-ʿAlāʾ al-Rumaynī (i.e. al-Sarmīnī), then al-Ḥalabī, al-Shāfiʿī, resident of Cairo; his son Muḥammad and the latter's grandfather are mentioned below. He heard from al-Zayn al-ʿIrāqī and others, and died around the year [8]40."@en .

rec:AIND-D05580 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05580-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05580-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05580 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن مفضل أبو الحسن المسلمي ثم القاهري الشافعي . ممن سمع على شيخنا وغيره ، وحج وناب في القضاء وسكن زاوية أبي السعود بموقف المكارية داخل باب القنطرة لكونها تحت نظره وخالط غير واحد من الأمراء سيما أزبك الخازندار رأس نوبة النواب . بحيث تكلم له في مشيخة سعيد السعداء بعد الكوراني وطمحت نفسه لأعلى منها مع نقصه جدا ويذكر بثروة من جهة النساء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Mufaḍḍal, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muslimī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī. He heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others, performed the pilgrimage, served as deputy qāḍī, and lived in the Zāwiya of Abū al-Suʿūd at the muleteers' station inside Bāb al-Qanṭara, since it was under his supervision. He mixed with several amirs, especially Azbak al-Khāzindār, raʾs nawbat al-nuwwāb, to the point that the latter spoke on his behalf for the shaykhship of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ after al-Kūrānī; and he aspired to even higher posts despite his great deficiency. He is said to be wealthy through (his) women."@en .

rec:AIND-D05581 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05581-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05581-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05581-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05581-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05581 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن مفلح البليني القائد . مات بمكة في حادي عشري ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Mufliḥ al-Balīnī al-Qāʾid (the commander). He died in Mecca on the 21st of Dhu al-Hijja in the year 861 AH, as chronicled by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05582 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05582-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05582-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05582-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05582 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن موسى بن عميرة بن موسى نور الدين القرشي المخزومي اليبناوي المكي الشافعي ابن عم أحمد بن عبد اللطيف الماضي . أجاز له في سنة ثمان وثمانين وسبعمائة العفيف النشاوري والبرهان بن علي بن فرحون والتقي بن حاتم وابن عرفة والأبناسي والعراقي والهيثمي وآخرون . مات في صفر سنة تسع وثلاثين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. ʿAmīra b. Mūsā, Nūr al-Dīn al-Qurashī al-Makhzūmī al-Yabnāwī al-Makkī al-Shāfiʿī, cousin of the aforementioned Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf. In 788 he was granted ijāza by al-ʿAfīf al-Nashāwarī, al-Burhān b. ʿAlī b. Farḥūn, al-Taqī b. Ḥātim, Ibn ʿArafa, al-Abnāsī, al-ʿIrāqī, al-Haythamī and others. He died in Ṣafar 839 in Mecca. Ibn Fahd also recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05585 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05585-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05585-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05585 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن وفا أبو الحسن الشاذلي . مضى في ابن محمد بن وفا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Wafā, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Shādhilī. Already mentioned under Ibn Muḥammad b. Wafā."@en .

rec:AIND-D05586 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05586-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05586-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05586-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05586 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن وهيب الفاسكوري الفران بها ويعرف بالحشاش . عامي يزعم مع شدة عاميته أنه قيم زمانه في فن الأدب بحيث يسخر به أهل بلده وهو حقيق بذلك وقد لقيته بها فكتبت عنه قوله : %~% نار العجاج وأمطار السما تزكي %~% على الأراضي لأقوات الأمم تسقي %~% %~% والرعد والبرق ذا يضرب وذا يحكي %~% سيف انجبذ في سمات الحرب ما يشكي %~% وغير هذا من نمطه عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Wuhayb al-Fāskūrī, the baker there, known as al-Ḥashshāsh. A commoner who, despite his extreme ignorance, claimed to be the master of his age in the art of adab, so that the people of his town mocked him—and he deserved it. I met him there and wrote down from him his verses: \"The fire of the dust-cloud and the rains of the sky nourish, / watering the lands for the sustenance of nations; / the thunder and the lightning—this one strikes and that one tells, / a sword drawn amid the marks of war, complaining of nothing.\" He has other verses of the same sort; may God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05587 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05587-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05587-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05587 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن يحيى بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن مخلوف النور بن زين العابدين بن الشرف المناوي الأصل القاهري الشافعي أخو محمد الآتي وأبوهما وجدهما وسبط الشهاب بن الشطنوفي . نشأ فحفظ القرآن والمنهاج وغيره وعرض علي في جملة الجماعة واشتغل قليلا وحضر بعض دروس جده وعليه خفر وأنس وروح وقد ضعف حاله لمزيد تقلله . )"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Makhlūf, al-Nūr b. Zayn al-ʿĀbidīn b. al-Sharaf, of Munā origin, al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, brother of Muḥammad (mentioned below), whose father and grandfather are also mentioned below, and daughter's son of al-Shihāb b. al-Shaṭnūfī. He grew up, memorized the Qurʾān, al-Minhāj and other works, presented them to me among the group, studied a little and attended some of his grandfather's lessons. He has modesty, affability and good spirit, but his circumstances have weakened through his excessive frugality."@en .

rec:AIND-D05588 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05588-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05588-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05588 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن يحيى بن مصلح المنزلي أخو أحمد الشهير . كان مقيما بمنية راضي من المنزلة معتقدا مبجلا يتلو القرآن ويبحث عما يهمه من أمور عبادته مع استحضار المسائل ممن حج ومات ببلده في عشر ذي الحجة سنة وقد زاد على السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā b. Muṣliḥ al-Manzilī, brother of the famous Aḥmad. He resided at Minyat Rāḍī in al-Manzila, revered and venerated, reciting the Qurʾān and inquiring into the matters of worship that concerned him, with a good command of the (legal) questions; he was among those who performed the pilgrimage. He died in his home town in the first ten days of Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year [blank], having passed seventy."@en .

rec:AIND-D05591 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05591-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05591-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05591-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05591 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن يعقوب الخواجا نور الدين الطهطاوي المكي والد أبي بكر وأخوته ، وكان ذا ملاءة وتوجه للتجارة وله دور متعددة بمكة . مات بها في المحرم سنة إحدى وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb, al-Khawājā Nūr al-Dīn al-Ṭahṭāwī al-Makkī, the father of Abū Bakr and his brothers. He was wealthy, engaged in commerce, and owned multiple houses in Mecca. He died there in al-Muharram, the year 881 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05600 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05600-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05600-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05600 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد العلاء بن القصير الدمشقي دلال العقار بها بل باشر قضاء الركب الشامي وقتا . وكان قد سمع عبد القادر الأرموي وحدث سمع منه اللبودي وأرخ وفاته في ربيع الأول سنة خمس وستين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Quṣayr al-Dimashqī, a real-estate broker there, who also served for a time as qāḍī of the Syrian pilgrimage caravan. He had heard from ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Urmawī and transmitted; al-Labūdī heard from him and recorded his death in Rabīʿ I 865. May God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05601 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05601-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05601-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05601-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05601 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد علاء الدين بن القصير الحنفي ، ولد في يوم عيد الفطر سنة إحدى وثمانمائة . هكذا في معجم التقي بن فهد وبيض له فيحرر أهو الذي قبله أم غيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, ʿAlāʾ al-Dīn Ibn al-Quṣayr, al-Ḥanafī. He was born on the day of ʿĪd al-Fiṭr 801. So it stands in the Muʿjam of al-Taqī b. Fahd, who left his entry blank; it remains to be verified whether he is the preceding person or someone else."@en .

rec:AIND-D05602 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05602-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05602-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05602-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05602 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد العلاء الحلبي ثم القاهري نزيل الجمالية ويعرف بابن شمس . كان بارعا في الكتابة على طريقة العجم كتب بخطه الكثير . ومات في حياة أبيه سنة ست وخمسين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, al-ʿAlāʾ, al-Ḥalabī then al-Qāhirī, resident of the Jamāliyya (khānqāh), known as Ibn Shams. He was highly skilled in calligraphy in the Persian style and copied many works in his own hand. He died during his father's lifetime in the year 856 AH. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05603 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05603-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05603-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05603 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد نور الدين المقري ابن القاصح . كذا ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه . وصوابه ابن عثمان بن محمد بن أحمد وقد مضى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, Nūr al-Dīn, the reader (al-muqriʾ), Ibn al-Qāṣiḥ. Thus our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) named him in his Inbāʾ, but correctly he is (ʿAlī) b. ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, already mentioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D05604 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05604-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05604-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05604 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن الشريف نور الدين الحسني الصحراوي نائب يشبك الجمالي في الحسبة ويعرف بابن ولي الدين ، كان أبوه صالحا بل هم من بيت صلاح واستقر في خدمة شيخ الصوفية بتربة الأشرف قايتباي ثم صرف بغيره وقرره كاتب السر ابن مزهر في تربته وسكنها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. al-Sharīf Nūr al-Dīn al-Ḥasanī al-Ṣaḥrāwī, deputy of Yashbak al-Jamālī in the ḥisba, known as Ibn Walī al-Dīn. His father was a pious man; indeed they were of a pious house. He was appointed to the service of the shaykh of the Sufis at the mausoleum of al-Ashraf Qāytbāy, then was replaced by another, and the kātib al-sirr Ibn Muzhar appointed him at his own mausoleum, where he took up residence."@en .

rec:AIND-D05605 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05605-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05605-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05605-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05605 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الكمال بن الشمس النايني بنونين بينهما تحتانية مهموزة . ممن قرأ القراءات عن ابن الجزري وأخذ عن العفيف الكازروني تلا عليه الفاتحة وغيرها السيد عبيد الله بن عفيف الدين بل سمع عليه أشياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, al-Kamāl b. al-Shams al-Nāyinī (with two nūns and a hamzated yāʾ between them). He was among those who read the qirāʾāt under Ibn al-Jazarī and studied under al-ʿAfīf al-Kāzarūnī; the Sayyid ʿUbayd Allāh b. ʿAfīf al-Dīn recited the Fātiḥa and other things under him and indeed heard various things from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05607 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05607-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05607-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05607 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد العلاء أبو الحسن بن الجندي المحلي الحنفي النقيب . فيمن جده خضر بن أيوب"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, al-ʿAlāʾ Abū al-Ḥasan Ibn al-Jundī al-Maḥallī al-Ḥanafī, the naqīb. [His entry is] among those whose grandfather is Khiḍr b. Ayyūb."@en .

rec:AIND-D05609 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05609-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05609-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05609 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد النور أبو الحسن الإشليمي . فيمن جده عثمان بن أيوب بن عثمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, al-Nūr Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ishlīmī. [His entry is] among those whose grandfather is ʿUthmān b. Ayyūb b. ʿUthmān."@en .

rec:AIND-D05610 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05610-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05610-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05610 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد النور أبو الحسن الأشمعوني . مضى فيمن جده عيسى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, al-Nūr Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ashmaʿūnī. Already mentioned among those whose grandfather is ʿĪsā."@en .

rec:AIND-D05611 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05611-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05611-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05611 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد نور الدين الميقاتي المنجم ويعرف بابن الشاهد . انتهت إليه الرياسة في حل الزيج وكتابة التقاويم مع معرفة بالرمل وغيره وتكسب بذلك في حانوت فاشتهر وحظى عند الأكابر بل راج أمره بأخرة على الظاهر برقوق وقربه ونزله في مدرسته ، مات في المحرم سنة إحدى . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ومعجمه وقال : لقيته مرارا والمقريزي في عقوده"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, Nūr al-Dīn al-Mīqātī (the timekeeper) al-Munajjim (the astrologer), known as Ibn al-Shāhid. He became the foremost authority in solving astronomical tables (zīj) and writing almanacs, with knowledge of geomancy and other things; he earned his living by this in a shop, became famous and won favour with the great. Latterly his standing rose with al-Ẓāhir Barqūq, who brought him close and lodged him in his madrasa. He died in Muḥarram 801. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ and his Muʿjam, saying \"I met him several times\"; and al-Maqrīzī (mentioned him) in his ʿUqūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05615 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05615-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05615-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05615 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد نور الدين المنزلي الشافعي ويعرف بابن سراج ، كان مشارا إليه في المنزلة بالصلاح ممن يديم التلاوة والعبادة وعنده أتباع يقوم بكلفتهم مع إلمام بالفضل ، مات بعد سنة ثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad Nūr al-Dīn al-Manzilī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn Sirāj. He was highly regarded in al-Manzilah for his piety, being one who constantly recited the Quran and engaged in worship. He had followers whose expenses he covered, while also possessing some learning. He died after the year 880 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05616 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05616-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05616-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05616 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد النور الويشي بكسر الواو وسكون التحتانية بعدها معجمة ثم القاهري . كان قد طلب العلم واشتغل كثيرا ونسخ بخطه الحسن شيئا كثيرا ثم تعانى الشهادة في القيمة فدخل في مداخل عجيبة واشتهر بالشهادات الباطلة . مات في ذي القعدة سنة خمس وأربعين عفا الله عنه . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, al-Nūr al-Wīshī (with kasra on the wāw, sukūn on the yāʾ, then shīn), then al-Qāhirī. He had sought knowledge, studied much and copied a great deal in his fine hand; then he took up testifying in valuations, entered into strange dealings and became notorious for false testimonies. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda 845; may God pardon him. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05617 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05617-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05617-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05617-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05617 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد أبو الحسن البجري البجائي المغربي أحد عدولها . أقرأ الفقه والأصلين وغيرها وهو الآن في سنة تسعين حي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ali ibn Muhammad Abu al-Hasan al-Bajri al-Bija'i al-Maghribi. One of the notary witnesses of Bougie (Bejaia). He taught jurisprudence (fiqh), the two principles (al-aslayn), and other subjects. He is currently alive in the year 890 [AH]."@en .

rec:AIND-D05618 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05618-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05618-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05618-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05618-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05618-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05618 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد أبو الحسن الدمياطي المقري أمام جامع حسن بن الطويل الشهيد بدمياط . تصدى لإقراء القرآن فكان ممن قرأ عليه التقي بن وكيل السلطان وقال أنه مات في شعبان سنة عشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dimyāṭī al-Muqriʾ, the prayer leader (imām) of the Mosque of Ḥasan b. al-Ṭawīl al-Shahīd in Damietta. He engaged in teaching Qurʾānic recitation, and among those who recited under him was al-Taqī b. Wakīl al-Sulṭān. It is said that he died in Shaʿbān, the year 820 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05619 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05619-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05619-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05619 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن ناصر الدين محمد الغمري . مضى في ابن محمد بن حسن بن محمد بن حسن ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D05620 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05620-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05620-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05620-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05620-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05620-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05620 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الكاتب ويلقب مشيمش . شيخ مسن بالقرب من جامع المارداني متميز في الكتابة من فقهاء الطبقة السنبلية من القلعة وممن تصدى للتكتيب فانتفع به جماعة منهم ابن السهيلي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Kātib, nicknamed Mushaymish. An elderly shaykh who lived near the Māridānī Mosque, distinguished in calligraphy. He was among the jurists of the Sunbuliyya class from the Citadel, and one of those who devoted themselves to teaching calligraphy, from which a group benefited, including Ibn al-Suhaylī."@en .

rec:AIND-D05621 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05621-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05621-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05621-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05621 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن الأخميمي البغدادي الأصل . مات سنة أربع عشرة . أرخه شيخنا وقال أنه ولي الوزارة وشد الدواوين وغير ذلك وكان يدعى الشرف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Akhmīmī, of Baghdadi origin. He died in the year 814 AH. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) chronicled his death and mentioned that he held the vizierate (al-wizāra) and the office of comptroller of the chanceries (shadd al-dawāwīn), among other posts, and that he was called al-Sharaf."@en .

rec:AIND-D05622 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05622-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05622-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05622 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد بن الأدمي الحنفي . فيمن اسم جده محمد بن أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. al-Adamī al-Ḥanafī. Listed among those whose grandfather's name is Muḥammad b. Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05623 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05623-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05623 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد القاضي . فيمن جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Qāḍī. [Look] among those listed under their grandfather's name."@en .

rec:AIND-D05624 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05624-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05624-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05624 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الأقواسي . فيمن جده أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Aqwāsī. Among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05625 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05625-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05625-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05625-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b100_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05625 ;
    aindv:sourceText "91 علي بن محمد الحبشي البليني القائد . مات في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وستين أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Ḥabashī al-Bulyanī, the qāʾid. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja (8)61. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05626 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05626-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05626-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05626-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05626-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05626 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الحمصاني المقرئ . مات مقتولا في ليلة الجمعة سلخ ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وثلاثين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Ḥimṣānī al-Muqriʾ. He was killed on Friday night (Thursday after sunset), the last day of Dhu al-Hijja, in the year 832 AH in Mecca. His death was chronicled by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05627 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05627-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05627-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05627 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الرسام . كتب في سنة ست وأربعين على استدعاء لابن الصفي ، ومضى فيمن جده ناصر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Rassām. He wrote on an istidʿāʾ (ijāza petition) for Ibn al-Ṣafī in the year 846 AH. He was already mentioned under the section of those whose grandfather's name is Nāṣir."@en .

rec:AIND-D05628 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05628-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05628-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05628-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05628-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05628 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الركاب أحد المجاذيب بالقاهرة . مات في شعبان سنة ثلاث وستين ودفن بزاويته على الطريق برأس ميدان القمح وكان قبل جذبته ركاب السلطان . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Rikkāb, one of the ecstatics (majdhūbs) in Cairo. He died in Shaʿbān 863 H (June 1459) and was buried in his zawiya on the road at the head of Maydan al-Qamh (Wheat Square). Before his spiritual attraction (jadhba), he had served as an equerry (rikkāb) of the Sultan. His biography was recorded by al-Munir."@en .

rec:AIND-D05629 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05629-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05629-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05629 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الزبيدي الشافعي . فيمن جده عبد العلي بن قحر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Zabīdī al-Shāfiʿī. Among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd al-ʿAlī b. Qaḥr."@en .

rec:AIND-D05630 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05630-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05630-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05630 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد السطيح . فيمن جده أحمد بن عبد الله بن حسن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Saṭīḥ. Among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥasan."@en .

rec:AIND-D05631 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05631-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05631-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05631 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الشاذلي . رأيته كتب من نظمه على شرح البهاء بن الأبشيهي المختصر من كتب المالكية : %~% لله درك من حبر مزجت لنا %~% عقد الجواهر بالياقوت والدرر %~% %~% وغصت بحرأ عزير±±± الدر ملتقطا %~% نفائسا منه لا تحصى بمنحصر %~% %~% بدت معانيه بالتوضيح واضحة %~% بحسن تدوين تهذيب لمختصر %~% %~% حباك ربى بهاء الدين مرتقيا %~% أعلى المنازل بالدارين في زمر %~% %~% واغفر لناظمها يا رب مغفرة %~% تمحو ذنوبا مضت في سائر العمر %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Shādhilī. I saw him writing some of his poetry on the commentary of al-Bahāʾ b. al-Abshīhī, which is an epitome of Maliki books: 'May God reward you, O scholar, you have mixed for us a necklace of gems with rubies and pearls, And dived into a sea rich in pearls, collecting precious things from it that cannot be numbered. Its meanings became clear through exposition, with excellent drafting and refinement of an epitome. May my Lord grant you, Bahāʾ al-Dīn, ascending to the highest stations in both abodes among the groups. And forgive, O Lord, its composer with a forgiveness that erases past sins of his whole life.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D05632 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05632-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05632-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05632-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05632 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الشامي المدني أحد فراشيها . ممن سمع مني بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Shāmī al-Madanī, one of the farrāshes (servants) of Medina. He was among those who heard [ḥadīth] from me there."@en .

rec:AIND-D05633 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05633-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05633-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05633 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الطائي ، فيمن جده سعد بن محمد بن عثمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Ṭāʾī, among those whose grandfather is Saʿd b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān."@en .

rec:AIND-D05634 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05634-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05634-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05634-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05634 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد العلائي الصالحي الدمشقي الغيثاوي نسبة لغيثا بالقرب من الزبداني قيم الموالة . كتب عنه البدري في مجموعه قوله : %~% حبيت كوسى ينور بالملاحة دعد %~% حلو المحيا فحم قلبي بفاحم جعد %~% %~% خلتو ووجهو وفي بدور حميو يا سعد %~% قمر لعب بقضيب البرق فوق الرعد %~% وكان راغبا في نقل التصانيف الغريبة إلى مصر من الشام وعكسه وبيده بعض جهات مات سنة خمس وسبعين تقريبا ، يحرر أهو من ترجمة هذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-ʿAlāʾī al-Ṣāliḥī al-Dimashqī al-Ghaythāwī. His nisbah is to Ghaythā near al-Zabadānī. He was the caretaker (qayyim) of al-Muwāla. Al-Badrī (TMP-P-000719) recorded his poetry in his compendium (Majmūʿ al-Badrī, TMP-T-00115): 'I loved a lovely Kusayy who shines with beauty among people, / Sweet of face, my heart became black like his jet-black curly hair. / I fancied his face and cheeks like full moons, O Sa'd, / A moon playing with the bough of lightning above the thunder.' He was eager to transport rare books and compositions to Egypt from Syria and vice versa, and he held some offices. He died around the year 875 AH; it is to be verified if this biography belongs to him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05635 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05635-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05635-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05635-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05635-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_affil_state_dedup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05635 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد القمني البنهاوي الأصل . ممن اشتغل قليلا وتكسب بالشهادة رفيقا للزين عبد القادر بن شعبان وغيره عند جامع أصلم وكذا بالنسخ وأقرأ المماليك بالطباق وغير ذلك بل وخطب بالجامع المذكور ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Qamanī, originally from Banhā. He studied briefly and earned his livelihood as a professional witness (shahāda) alongside al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Shaʿbān and others at the Mosque of Aslam. He also worked as a copyist (naskh), taught the Mamluks in their quarters (al-ṭibāq), and delivered sermons (khaṭaba) at the aforementioned mosque."@en .

rec:AIND-D05636 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05636-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05636-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05636-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05636-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05636-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05636 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد المرحومي ثم القاهري الشافعي المقري أحد الشهود بقنطرة الموسكي . ممن قرأ على ابن أسد وجعفر القراءات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Marḥūmī, later al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī. A Quran reciter and one of the notary witnesses at the Mūskī Bridge (Qanṭarat al-Mūskī). He studied the Quranic readings (al-qirāʾāt) under Ibn Asad and Jaʿfar (al-Sanhūrī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05637 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05637-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05637-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05637 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد المهاجري المقري . رأيته شهد على علي بن موسى في إجازته لابنه أمين الدين محمد بالقراءات في سنة ثمان وعشرين وكتب شهادته نظما فكان منها : %~% والله يغفر لي والسامعين ومن %~% يقول آمين من ذنب مضى وخلا %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Muhājirī al-Muqrī. I saw him witnessing the ijāza (authorization) granted by ʿAlī b. Mūsā to his son Amīn al-Dīn Muḥammad in the variant readings (al-qirāʾāt) in the year 828 AH. He wrote his witnessing in verse, which included: 'And may God forgive me, the listeners, and whoever says Amen, for the sins that have passed and gone.'"@en .

rec:AIND-D05638 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05638-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05638-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05638 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد الناسخ الكاتب . مضى فيمن جده عبد النصير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ali ibn Muhammad, the copyist, the scribe. He was mentioned above under those whose grandfather is Abd al-Nasir."@en .

rec:AIND-D05639 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05639-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05639-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05639-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05639-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05639-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05639 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمد اليماني مستوفي الديوان بجدة . كان اسمه عمر فغيره لما خدم السيد حسن . مات في صفر سنة أربعين . ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ali b. Muhammad al-Yamani, the financial officer (mustawfi) of the diwan in Jidda. His name was originally Umar, but he changed it to Ali when he entered the service of al-Sayyid Hasan. He died in Safar, the year 840 AH. He was mentioned by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05644 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05644-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05644-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05644-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05644-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05644 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمود بن محمد بن أحمد بن قاوان ملك التجار بن خواجا جهان الكيلاني . قدم القاهرة بعد موت ابني عمه ثم عاد سريعا لمكة في البحر هو والشريف إسحق فداما بها ثم سافر إلى عدن ثم إلى كنباية وتوفي بها قيل مسموما إما في سنة خمس وتسعين أو التي بعدها ويذكر بفضل ونظم ولكنه كان مسيكا وقد جاز الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Maḥmūd b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Qāwān Malik al-Tujjār b. Khwājā Jahān al-Kīlānī. He came to Cairo after the death of his two cousins, then quickly returned to Mecca by sea along with al-Sharīf Isḥāq, and they resided there. Later, he traveled to Aden, then to Cambay (Kanbāya), where he died. It was said that he was poisoned, either in the year 895 AH or the following year. He was remembered for his virtue and poetry, though he was parsimonious. He was over sixty years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D05645 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05645-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05645-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05645 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن محمود الضياء الكرماني الشافعي . أخذ عن أبي الفتوح الطاووسي والمعين نصر الله بن الظهير أبي النجاشي عبد الرحمن والمجد اللغوي وجماعة ، وشرح المشارق في أربع مجلدات وسماه ضوء المشارق ، وولي قضاء الشافعية بكرمان ولقيه الطاووسي في سنة ثلاثين وثمانمائة فاستمد منه فوائد وأجاز له بل أذن له في الإفتاء وكان حينئذ قد زاد على التسعين ووصفه بالمولى المحدث الأعظم الأعلم الرباني المفتي المصنف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Maḥmūd al-Ḍiyāʾ al-Kirmānī al-Shāfiʿī. He studied under Abū al-Futūḥ al-Ṭāwūsī, al-Muʿīn Naṣr Allāh b. al-Ẓahīr Abī al-Najāshī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-Majd al-Lughawī, and others. He wrote a four-volume commentary on 『al-Mashāriq』 (Mashāriq al-Anwār), which he titled 『Ḍawʾ al-Mashāriq』. He held the office of Shafi'i judge (qāḍī) in Kirmān. In the year 830 AH, al-Ṭāwūsī met him and benefited from his knowledge, and Ali granted him an ijāza and even permitted him to issue fatwas. At that time, Ali was over ninety years old, and al-Ṭāwūsī described him as 'the greatest and most knowledgeable master, the godly mufti, and author'."@en .

rec:AIND-D05646 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05646-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05646-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05646-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05646 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن مخارش بضم الميم وفتح المعجمة وآخره شين معجمة بعد راء مهملة على وزن مخاصم الزيدي . فارس مشهور بالنجدة والفروسية يعد بمائة قتله عبد الوهاب بن طاهر الذي صارت إليه مملكة اليمن بمعركة في رمضان سنة إحدى وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Makhārish al-Zaydī (Makhārish with damma on the mīm, fatha on the khāʾ, and ending in shīn). A famous knight renowned for his courage and horsemanship, counted as equivalent to a hundred men. He was killed by ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Ṭāhir, who obtained the kingdom of Yemen, in a battle in Ramaḍān of the year 861 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05647 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05647-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05647-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05647-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05647 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن مرعي بن علي البرلسي شقيق محمد الآتي وهذا أكبرهما وذاك أكثرهما وهو الآن سنة تسع وتسعين في الأحياء . )"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Marʿī b. ʿAlī al-Burlusī, full brother of Muḥammad who is mentioned below. This is the older of the two, while the other has accomplished more. He is still among the living now, in the year 899."@en .

rec:AIND-D05650 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05650-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05650-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05650-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05650 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن مسعود بن محمد بن أبي الفرج الشرف بن التاج الأبرقوهي سبط القاضي أبي نصر . ولد في ذي القعدة سنة خمس وأربعين وسبعمائة ولقيه الطاووسي بأبرقوه في جمادى الآخرة سنة تسع عشرة فأجازه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Masʿūd b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Faraj al-Sharaf al-Abraqūhī, the maternal grandson of al-Qāḍī Abū Naṣr. He was born in Dhu al-Qaʿdah 745 AH. Al-Ṭāwūsī met him in Abraqūh in Jumādā al-Ākhirah 819 AH and he (ʿAlī) granted him an ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D05651 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05651-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05651-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05651 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن مسعود البعداني . مات في صفر سنة خمسين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Masʿūd al-Baʿdānī. He died in the month of Safar, 850 AH (June 1446) in Mecca. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05653 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05653-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05653-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05653 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن المصلية . هو ابن عبد الوهاب بن أبي بكر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Muṣallīya. He is the son of ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Abī Bakr."@en .

rec:AIND-D05654 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05654-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05654 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن المعلى . رأيت خطه في سنة ست وعشرين لبعض من عرض عليه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Muʿallā. I saw his handwriting from the year 826 AH on a certificate of presentation (ʿarḍ) for some of those who had recited to him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05656 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05656-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05656-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05656-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05656 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن منصور بن زين العرب الحصكفي ثم المقدسي والد أبي اللطف محمد . كان تاجرا في القماش ذا ثروة مات بالقدس سنة خمس وخمسين وخلف لولده دنيا واسعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Manṣūr b. Zayn al-ʿArab al-Ḥiṣkafī, then al-Maqdisī, the father of Abū al-Luṭf Muḥammad. He was a wealthy cloth merchant. He died in Jerusalem in the year 855 AH, leaving a vast fortune to his son."@en .

rec:AIND-D05662 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05662-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05662-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05662-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05662 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن موسى بن عيسى بن عبد الله بن الوردي . ولد تقريبا في سنة تسع وثمانين وسبعمائة . ومات قبل خمسين . ذكره البقاعي هكذا مجردا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Mūsā b. ʿĪsā b. ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Wardī. He was born in approximately 789 AH and died before 850 AH. Al-Biqāʿī mentioned him thus bare."@en .

rec:AIND-D05663 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05663-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05663-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05663-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05663 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن موسى بن قريش المكي . فيمن جده علي قريبا"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Mūsā b. Quraysh al-Makkī. [Refer to the entry] among those whose grandfather is ʿAlī, shortly."@en .

rec:AIND-D05664 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05664-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05664-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05664-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05664-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05664 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن الشرفي موسى بن المتوكل على الله محمد بن أبي بكر العباس الهاشمي ابن عم المتوكل العز عبد العزيز الخليفة الآن والآتي أبوه . مات في ربيع الثاني سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Sharafī Mūsā b. al-Mutawakkil ʿalā Allāh Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr al-ʿAbbās al-Hāshimī. He was the cousin of al-Mutawakkil al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, the current Caliph. His father's biography is forthcoming. He died in Rabīʿ al-Thānī, year 891 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05665 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05665-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05665-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05665-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05665-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05665-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05665 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن موسى بن هرون أبو الحسن بن الزيات المقري أخو الشهاب أحمد الماضي ويعرف بابن الزيات . كان خيرا نيرا من صوفية سعيد السعداء يتولى تقديم نعالهم فيها كل يوم غالبا وربما فعل بصوفية البيبرسية ذلك مع مداومة التلاوة والعبادة والحرص على شهود وقت الشافعي ونحوه . مات في أواخر سنة ست وسبعين ونعم الرجل كان رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ali bin Musa bin Harun, Abu al-Hasan bin al-Zayyat, the Muqri'. He was the brother of al-Shihab Ahmad, who was mentioned previously, and was known as Ibn al-Zayyat. He was a virtuous and radiant man from among the Sufis of Sa'id al-Su'ada', where he usually undertook the service of placing their shoes every day, and he would sometimes do the same for the Sufis of al-Baybarsiyya, while constantly reciting the Quran, worshipping, and being eager to attend the circle of al-Shafi'i and the like. He died in the late part of the year 876 AH. What an excellent man he was, may Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05666 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05666-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05666-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05666-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05666-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05666-resp-5,
        rec:AIND-D05666-resp-6,
        rec:AIND-D05666-resp-7 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05666 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن موسى النور أبو الحسن القرافي ثم القاهري الشافعي المقرئ والد الأمين محمد الآتي تلا بالسمع على ابن المشبب أفرادا وجمعا وانتهى في سنة ثلاث وتسعين وسبعمائة وكان حيا قريب الثلاثين أخذ عنه ابنه وكذا زعم الشهاب ابن أسد أنه قرأ عليه رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Mūsā, al-Nūr, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Qarāfī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, the Quran reciter. Father of al-Amīn Muḥammad, who is mentioned below. He recited the Quran by listening under Ibn al-Mushabbab, both individually and collectively, completing it in the year 793 AH. He was alive around 830 AH. His son studied under him, and al-Shihāb Ibn Asad also claimed to have read under him, may Allah have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05667 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05667-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05667 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن موسى الحنفي . رأيته كتب في عرض سنة ثلاث وهو غير الماضي فيمن جده إبراهيم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Mūsā al-Ḥanafī. I saw him writing on a memorization audit (ʿarḍ) in the year [80]3. He is someone other than the aforementioned person whose grandfather was Ibrāhīm."@en .

rec:AIND-D05669 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05669-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05669-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05669-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05669 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أبي النجا بن علي الفاضلي الدلال بسوق أمير الجيوش . ممن سمع علي في سنة خمس وتسعين وقبلها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Abī al-Najā b. ʿAlī al-Fāḍilī, the broker in the market of Amīr al-Juyūsh. He was among those who heard (ḥadīth) from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the year 895 and before it."@en .

rec:AIND-D05671 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05671-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05671-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05671-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05671-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05671 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن نصر القاهري الفوال بسوق رأس حارة برجوان أحد من يعتقد . مات فجأة في ذي الحجة سنة ثمان وخمسين ودفن ظاهر باب النصر . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Naṣr al-Qāhirī al-Fawwāl, (who operated) in the market at the head of Barjawān Quarter. He was one of those in whose piety people believed. He died suddenly in Dhu al-Ḥijjah in the year 858 and was buried outside Bāb al-Naṣr. His death was recorded by al-Munīr."@en .

rec:AIND-D05675 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05675-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05675-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05675-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05675-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05675 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن هلال الحضا . مات بمكة في رجب سنة ثلاث وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Hilāl al-Ḥaḍā. He died in Mecca in Rajab, the year 873 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05677 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05677-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05677-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05677-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05677-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05677 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن ياقوت العجلاني أحد القواد . مات بمكة في رجب سنة ست وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yāqūt al-ʿAjlānī, one of the commanders (al-quwwād) in Mecca. He died in Mecca in Rajab 876 AH, as recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05678 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05678-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05678 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يحيى بن عبد القادر بن محمود نور الدين الحسني القادري ممن سمع على شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yaḥyā b. ʿAbd al-Qādir b. Maḥmūd Nūr al-Dīn al-Ḥasanī al-Qādirī. He was among those who heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05680 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05680-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05680 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يحيى الزواوي . مات سنة بضع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yaḥyā al-Zawāwī. He died in the year forty-something AH (likely the 840s AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05681 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05681-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05681 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يس تقدم قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yās (Yāsīn); mentioned above."@en .

rec:AIND-D05682 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05682-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05682 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن أبي اليمن . مضى في ابن محمد بن محمد بن علي بن أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī ibn Abī al-Yaman. He was mentioned previously under [the entry of] Ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05685 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05685-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05685-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05685-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05685-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05685 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن علي بن غشم بن محمود بن فهد ابن غشم بن عطاف بن ملك بن غشم العلاء العامري البعلي الحنفي . ولد في جمادى الأولى سنة إحدى وستين وسبعمائة ببعلبك وسمع بها من أحمد بن عبد الكريم البعلي صحيح مسلم أخبرتنا به زينب ابنة عمر بن كندي عن المؤيد وعلى الجمال يوسف بن عمر بن أحمد بن السقا الإصابة في الدعوات المستجابة لأبي الفتح محمد بن الحافظ عبد الغني أنابه أبو حفص عمر بن عبد المنعم بن غدير القواس أذنا عن مؤلفه وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī b. Ghushm b. Maḥmūd b. Fahd b. Ghushm b. ʿAṭṭāf b. Malik b. Ghushm, al-ʿAlāʾ, al-ʿĀmirī, al-Baʿlī, al-Ḥanafī. He was born in Jumādā al-Ūlā, in the year 761 AH, in Baʿlabakk. He heard 'Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim' there from Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Baʿlī — which was transmitted to us by Zaynab bint ʿUmar b. Kindī from al-Muʾayyad. He also heard 'al-Iṣāba fī al-daʿawāt al-mustajāba' by Abū al-Fatḥ Muḥammad b. al-Ḥāfiẓ ʿAbd al-Ghanī from al-Jamāl Yūsuf b. ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. al-Saqqā, via the authorization granted to him by Abū Ḥafṣ ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Munʿim b. Ghadīr al-Qawwās from its author. He transmitted hadith and prominent scholars heard from him. He died."@en .

rec:AIND-D05686 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05686-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05686-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05686 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن إسماعيل الخواجا بن البهلوان . مات سنة بضع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. Ismāʿīl al-Khawājā b. al-Bahlawān. He died in the 850s AH (between 851 and 859 AH)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05687 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05687-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05687-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05687-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05687 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن أبي البركات الملطي . فيمن جده موسى بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. Abī al-Barakāt al-Malaṭī. Listed under those whose grandfather is Mūsā b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05688 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05688-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05688-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05688-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05688-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05688-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05688 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن حسب الله البزاز . سمع على ابن الجزري في سنة ثلاث وعشرين ختم نشره ، ومات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة ثمان وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ali b. Yusuf b. Hasb Allah al-Bazzaz. He heard the conclusion of the recitation of al-Nashr under Ibn al-Jazari in the year 823 AH, and died in Mecca in Dhu al-Hijjah, 848 AH. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05689 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05689-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05689-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05689 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن زيان أبو حسون المغربي الوزير . مات فجأة في ثامن رمضان سنة خمس وستين وبموته افتتحت الفتن بالمغرب قاله لي بعض فضلاء المغاربة من أصحابنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. Zayyān Abū Ḥassūn al-Maghribī, the vizier. He died suddenly on the 8th of Ramaḍān, in the year 865 AH. With his death, tribulations (fitna) broke out in Morocco. This was related to me by some of our virtuous Moroccan companions."@en .

rec:AIND-D05690 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05690-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05690-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05690-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05690-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_apply2,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05690 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن سالم بن عطية بن صالح بن عبد النبي الجهني ويعرف بابن أبي أصبع . سمع من العز بن جماعة والفخر التوزري في سنة ثلاث وخمسين وسبعمائة بعض النسائي وكان يتردد إلى اليمن في التجارة فأدركه أجله بعدن منها في آخر سنة أربع . قاله الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. Sālim b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ṣāliḥ b. ʿAbd al-Nabī al-Juhanī, known as Ibn Abī Aṣbaʿ. He heard a portion of Sunan al-Nasāʾī from al-ʿIzz b. Jamāʿa and al-Fakhr al-Tawzarī in the year 753 AH. He used to travel to Yemen for trade, and he passed away in Aden at the end of the year 804 AH. Al-Fāsī mentioned this in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05692 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05692-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05692-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05692-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05692-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05692-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05692 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن العباس بن عيسى الأندلسي الأصل المكي المؤدب والده ويعرف بالجيادي . مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة سبع وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. al-ʿAbbās b. ʿĪsā, of Andalusian origin, of Mecca. His father was a tutor (al-Muʾaddib). He was known as al-Jayyādī. He died in Mecca in Dhu al-Hijjah, in the year 847 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05693 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05693-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05693-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05693 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن علي بن أحمد العلاء البصروي الأصل الدمشقي الشافعي أحد المفتين بدمشق ووالد أبي البقاء محمد ممن ناب في القضاء ودرس بحيث يرجح فهمه على كثيرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. ʿAlī b. ʿAmr, al-ʿAlāʾ. Originally from Basra, based in Damascus, Shāfiʿī. He was one of the muftis of Damascus, and the father of Abū al-Baqāʾ Muḥammad. He served as a deputy judge (nāʾib al-qāḍī) and taught in Damascus, with his understanding preferred over many others."@en .

rec:AIND-D05695 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05695-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05695-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05695-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05695 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن عمر بن أنور . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه وقال صاحب مقدشوه في عصرنا ويلقب المؤيد بن المظفر بن المنصور . مات سنة ست وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. ʿUmar b. Anwar. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his 『Inbāʾ al-Ghumr』 and said that he was the ruler of Mogadishu (ṣāḥib Maqdishūh) in our time; he bore the regnal title al-Muʾayyad b. al-Muẓaffar b. al-Manṣūr (al-Muẓaffar and al-Manṣūr being the regnal titles of his father and grandfather). He died in the year 836 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05696 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05696-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05696-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05696-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05696-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05696-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05696 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن محمد بن علي النور بن الجمال الأنصاري الزرندي المدني الحنفي الآتي أبوه . ولد في جمادى الثانية سنة تسع وعشرين وثمانمائة وسمع على أبي الفتح المراغي ثم أخيه في آخرين وكذا كان ممن سمع مني بالمدينة وولي حسبتها يسيرا عن قريبه قاضي الحنفية علي بن سعيد الماضي بسعاية عمر بن عبد العزيز بن بدر . مات بها في سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, al-Anṣārī al-Zarandī al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī. His father is mentioned below. He was born in Jumada II 829 AH and heard hadith from Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī, then his brother, and others. He also heard hadith from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina. He briefly held the office of muḥtasib of Medina, succeeding his relative, the Hanafi judge ʿAlī b. Saʿīd (mentioned above), through the mediation of ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Badr. He died in Medina in the year 892 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D05698 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05698-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05698-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05698-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05698-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05698 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف بن مزروع المصري نزيل مكة والعطار بها مات بها في ربيع الأول سنة أربع وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. Mazrūʿ al-Miṣrī. He settled in Mecca and worked as a druggist (perfumer) there. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal, the year 884 AH. His death was chronicled by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05702 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05702-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05702-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05702 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف الخواجا نور الدين البهلوان . مضى فيمن جده إسماعيل ."@ar .

rec:AIND-D05703 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05703-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05703-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05703-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05703-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05703 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف نزيل الظاهرية القديمة وأخو القاضي شهاب الدين الصوفي . مات في يوم الأحد تاسع عشر رجب سنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf, a resident of al-Ẓāhiriyya al-Qadīma and brother of al-Qāḍī Shihāb al-Dīn al-Ṣūfī. He died on Sunday, the 19th of Rajab, with the year unspecified in the text."@en .

rec:AIND-D05704 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05704-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05704-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05704-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05704 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يوسف النووي . فقيه فاضل شافعي شهد في إجازة النوبي في سنة خمس وستين وبلغني أنه ممن يدرس الفقه ويتكسب بالشهادة مع الخير والتقلل والتقنع وحج ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūsuf al-Nawawī. A virtuous Shāfiʿī jurist. He witnessed the ijāza of al-Nūbī in the year 865 AH. I was informed that he teaches jurisprudence and earns his living as a notary (shahāda) while maintaining goodness, simplicity, and contentment, and he performed the pilgrimage (Hajj)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05705 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05705-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05705-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05705-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05705 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن يونس بن يوسف بن مسعود القلعي الدمشقي الشافعي نزيل العقيبة الصغرى بدمشق . ولد قبل سنة خمسين وسبعمائة وقال أنه سمع البخاري على أبي المحاسن يوسف بن محمد القباني وبعض مسلم على الياسوفي وخليل القدسي والشفا على المحيوي الرحبي وحدث أخذ عنه بعض أصحابنا وكان يؤدب الأصفال جوار حمام القواس"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. Yūnus b. Yūsuf b. Masʿūd al-Qalʿī al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī, who resided in al-ʿUqayba al-Ṣughrā in Damascus. He was born before the year 750 AH. He stated that he heard the Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī from Abū al-Maḥāsin Yūsuf b. Muḥammad al-Qabbānī, some of the Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim from al-Yāswfī and Khalīl al-Qudsī, and al-Shifāʾ from al-Muḥyawī al-Raḥbī. He transmitted Hadith, and some of our companions took knowledge from him. He used to teach children near Hammām al-Qawwās."@en .

rec:AIND-D05706 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05706-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05706-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05706-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05706-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05706 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي شاه بن فخر الدين بن علي الشغنارقي . ذكره التقي بن فهد في معجمه وبيض ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ali Shah b. Fakhr al-Din b. Ali al-Shaghnariqi. Al-Taqi b. Fahd mentioned him in his lexicon (Mu'jam) but left a blank space for further details."@en .

rec:AIND-D05707 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05707-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05707-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05707-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05707-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_opus_5,
        agent:claude_opus_5_Cgroup ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05707 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن البرهان المصري . مات في ذي القعدة سنة تسع وأربعين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Ali b. al-Burhan al-Misri. He died in Dhu al-Qaʿda, 849 AH, in Mecca. His death was recorded by Ibn Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05708 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05708-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05708-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05708 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي نور الدين بن بطيخ المقري . ذكرته في الموحدة من الآباء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn b. Baṭṭīkh al-Muqrī. I mentioned him in the section on fathers under the letter Bāʾ (al-Muwahhada)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05709 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05709-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05709-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05709-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05709 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي العلاء بن الجندي المحلي الحنفي نقيب الشافعي . في ابن محمد بن خضر بن أيوب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Jundī al-Maḥallī al-Ḥanafī, naqīb of the Shafi'is. See: [the entry of] Ibn Muḥammad b. Khaḍr b. Ayyūb."@en .

rec:AIND-D05710 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05710-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05710 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن السدار ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Saddār (ʿAlī, son of al-Saddār)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05711 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05711-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05711 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي علاء الدين بن الصابوني . في ابن أحمد بن محمد بن سليمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī ʿAlāʾ al-Dīn b. al-Ṣābūnī. Refer to the entry of Ibn Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Sulaymān."@en .

rec:AIND-D05712 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05712-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05712-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05712 ;
    aindv:sourceText "163 علي بن العنبري الدمشقي . بنى بها غربي سويقة صاروجا على بستان المتوجه إلى الصالحية مسجدا وعمل فيه مع صغره خطبة فلما بنى برسباي جامعه الشهير بالسويقة المذكورة بطلت الخطبة منه . مات في مستهل ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وأربعين ودفن بالمقبرة التي تجاه مسجده . ذكره ابن اللبودي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-ʿAnbarī al-Dimashqī. He built there (in Damascus), to the west of Suwayqat Ṣārūjā, on the orchard on the way to al-Ṣāliḥiyya, a mosque, and despite its small size established a Friday sermon (khuṭba) in it. When Barsbāy built his famous congregational mosque in the said Suwayqa, the sermon in his mosque was discontinued. He died on the first of Rabīʿ al-Awwal (8)42 and was buried in the cemetery opposite his mosque. Ibn al-Labūdī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05713 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05713-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05713-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05713-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b100_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05713 ;
    aindv:sourceText "164 علي العلاء الكركي المالكي ويعرف بابن المزوار . مات فجأة في جمادى الأولى سنة خمس وثمانين بالقاهرة وكان قد باشر حسبة نابلس ثم قضاء بلده وكتابة سرها بعناية الجمال ناظر الخاص وكذا ولي قضاء غزة ثم القدس غير مرة سامحه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī, al-ʿAlāʾ al-Karakī al-Mālikī, known as Ibn al-Mizwār. He died suddenly in Jumādā al-Ūlā (8)85 in Cairo. He had held the ḥisba (market inspectorate) of Nablus, then the judgeship of his home town (al-Karak) and its office of confidential secretary through the patronage of al-Jamāl, the nāẓir al-khāṣṣ. Likewise he held the judgeship of Gaza and then of Jerusalem more than once. May God forgive him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D05714 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05714-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05714-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05714 ;
    aindv:sourceText "165 علي العلاء بن مفلح الدمشقي الحنبلي قاضيها . كان جيدا عفيفا مقبولا بين الناس . مات بقرية ديماس من قرى دمشق في شعبان سنة ثلاث من أثر كي كواه له تمرلنك على ظهره ، قاله العيني ، قلت وهو ابن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī, al-ʿAlāʾ b. Mufliḥ al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanbalī, its (Damascus's) judge. He was good, upright and well accepted among the people. He died in the village of Daymās, one of the villages of Damascus, in Shaʿbān (80)3, from the effects of a cauterization that Timur (Tamerlane) had inflicted on his back; so said al-ʿAynī. I (al-Sakhāwī) say: he is the son of ... (the text breaks off here)."@en .

rec:AIND-D05715 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05715-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05715-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05715 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بن الوردي اثنان : ابن محمد بن عبد الخالق بن أحمد وابن موسى بن عيسى بن عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī b. al-Wardī: there are two, the son of Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Khāliq b. Aḥmad, and the son of Mūsā b. ʿĪsā b. ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D05717 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05717-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05717-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05717-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b100_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05717 ;
    aindv:sourceText "168 علي نور الدين أبو الحسن السنيكي ثم القاهري الأزهري الشافعي . قدم القاهرة فقرأ القرآن وحضر دروس المناوي وغيره بل سمع على شيخنا رفيقا لبلديه الزين زكريا وعاش حتى أدرك ولايته فلم يحصل منه على طائل مع شدة فقره وضرره وانقطاعه . مات في ليلة الجمعة تاسع ربيع الآخر سنة ثمان وثمانين وقد قارب السبعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī, Nūr al-Dīn Abū al-Ḥasan al-Sunaykī, then al-Qāhirī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī. He came to Cairo, read the Qurʾān and attended the lessons of al-Manāwī and others; moreover he heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) as a companion of his fellow townsman al-Zayn Zakariyyā. He lived long enough to see the latter's appointment (to office), yet obtained nothing of substance from him, despite his extreme poverty, his blindness and his seclusion. He died on the eve of Friday, 9 Rabīʿ al-Ākhir (8)88, having nearly reached seventy. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05718 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05718-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05718-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b100_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05718 ;
    aindv:sourceText "169 علي الأسيوطي ويعرف بأبي الحلق . شيخ ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه وقال : كان ممن يعتقد وتذكر عنه مكاشفات كثيرة . مات سنة ثلاث وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Asyūṭī, known as Abū al-Ḥalq. A shaykh whom our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned in his Inbāʾ (al-Ghumr), saying: \"He was one of those who were venerated, and many mystical disclosures (mukāshafāt) are related of him.\" He died in the year (8)33."@en .

rec:AIND-D05719 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05719-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05719-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05719-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b100_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05719 ;
    aindv:sourceText "170 علي ويعرف بالشيخ حدندل . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه أيضا وقال : كان أحد من يعتقد وهو مجذوب . مات في صفر سنة أربع وعشرين انتهى ، وأظنه صاحب الضريح بالروضة خارج باب النصر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī, known as al-Shaykh Ḥadandal. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) also mentioned him in his Inbāʾ (al-Ghumr), saying: \"He was one of those who were venerated, and he was a majdhūb (one rapt in God). He died in Ṣafar (8)24.\" End of quotation. I (al-Sakhāwī) think that he is the occupant of the shrine at al-Rawḍa outside Bāb al-Naṣr."@en .

rec:AIND-D05720 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05720-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05720-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05720 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي السيد زين الدين الجرجاني . في ابن محمد بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Sayyid Zayn al-Dīn al-Jurjānī. See under Ibn Muḥammad b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D05721 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05721-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05721-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05721 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي العلاء المكتب . أشير إليه قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-ʿAlāʾ al-Mukattib (the writing-master). He was referred to just above."@en .

rec:AIND-D05722 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05722-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05722-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05722-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05722 ;
    aindv:sourceText "171 علي العلاء والي الغربية وكاشف الوجه البحري ويوصف بالأمير . مات في حادي عشري ربيع الأول سنة ... أرخه المقريزي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-ʿAlāʾ, governor (wālī) of al-Gharbiyya and inspector (kāshif) of Lower Egypt (al-Wajh al-Baḥrī), described as an amīr. He died on the twenty-first of Rabīʿ al-Awwal in the year … (left blank in the text). Al-Maqrīzī recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05723 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05723-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05723-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05723-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05723 ;
    aindv:sourceText "172 علي نور الدين البرلسي ثم الأزهري المالكي . ممن لازم السنهوري بل وأخذ عن التقي الشمني وغيره وجلس شاهدا ، وهو فقير جدا يرجع لدين وخير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn al-Burullusī, then al-Azharī, the Mālikī. He was among those who closely attended al-Sanhūrī, and he also studied under al-Taqī al-Shumunnī and others. He sat as a notary-witness (shāhid). He is very poor, but is a man of religion and goodness."@en .

rec:AIND-D05724 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05724-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05724-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05724 ;
    aindv:sourceText "173 علي نور الدين البنبي ثم القاهري الأزهري المالكي الخطيب . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه وقال : كان حسن السمت سليم الفطرة خطب في جامع الأزهر مرات±±± نيابة عني واغتبطوا به . مات في سادس عشري ذي الحجة سنة أربع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn al-Banbī, then al-Qāhirī al-Azharī, the Mālikī, the preacher (khaṭīb). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ and said: \"He was of good bearing and sound nature. He preached at the Azhar Mosque several times as my deputy, and the people were pleased with him.\" He died on the twenty-sixth of Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year 844."@en .

rec:AIND-D05727 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05727-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05727-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05727-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05727 ;
    aindv:sourceText "177 علي نور الدين الضرير المقري مؤدب الأطفال بالمسجد المجاور لجامع المغاربة داخل باب الشعرية وإمام الجامع المذكور . مات عن قريب السبعين ظنا في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين ، وكان حسن التعليم خيرا طري النغمة انتفع به جماعة في ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn al-Ḍarīr (the blind) al-Muqrī, teacher of children at the mosque adjacent to Jāmiʿ al-Maghāriba inside Bāb al-Shaʿriyya, and imām of the said mosque. He died, aged nearly seventy by estimate, in Ṣafar of the year 853. He was a good teacher, a good man with a fresh, melodious voice, and a number of people benefited from him in that."@en .

rec:AIND-D05728 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05728-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05728-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05728-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05728 ;
    aindv:sourceText "178 علي نور الدين الطيبي الشافعي تلميذ الأدمي تميز في الفقه وغيره وأقرأ في الطباق وشهد وتخرج به أبو الحجاج السيوطي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn al-Ṭaybī, the Shāfiʿī, the pupil of al-Adamī. He distinguished himself in jurisprudence and other fields, taught in the barracks (al-ṭibāq), and served as a notary-witness. Abū al-Ḥajjāj al-Suyūṭī was trained under him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05729 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05729-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05729-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05729 ;
    aindv:sourceText "179 علي نور الدين مؤدب الأطفال آخر سوى الضرير المذكور قبله . كان شيخ الميعاد بزاوية الشيخ علي البطائحي السدار برأس حارة الروم من القاهرة . مات في ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وخمسين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn, a teacher of children, another one, distinct from the blind man mentioned before him. He was the shaykh of the mīʿād (regular teaching session) at the zāwiya of Shaykh ʿAlī al-Baṭāʾiḥī al-Saddār at the head of Ḥārat al-Rūm in Cairo. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 852, may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05730 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05730-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05730-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05730 ;
    aindv:sourceText "180 علي نور الدين النهياوي القاهري الواعظ أحد صوفية الجمالية . مات في رجب سنة خمس وسبعين وكان ساكنا لا بأس به من خيار الوعاظ صاهره عبد القادر الفاخوري على ابنته وصبرت على بليته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn al-Nahyāwī al-Qāhirī, the preacher (wāʿiẓ), one of the Sufis of al-Jamāliyya. He died in Rajab of the year 875. He was quiet and unobjectionable, one of the best preachers. ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Fākhūrī became his son-in-law by marrying his daughter, and she bore his (ʿAbd al-Qādir's) affliction with patience."@en .

rec:AIND-D05731 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05731-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05731-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05731 ;
    aindv:sourceText "181 علي نور الدين الهوى التاجر . توسل حتى اتصل بابنة البرهان بن عليبة على كره منه ومن ولديه وآل أمرهم إلى افتدائها منه بنحو خمسمائة دينار فأكثر وسافر إلى المدينة النبوية فكانت منيته بها في رجب سنة خمس وسبعين بعد فعله بها بعض القرب وخلف شيئا كثيرا سامحه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn al-Hawā, the merchant. He contrived until he married the daughter of al-Burhān b. ʿUlayba, against the will of the latter and of his two sons; the matter ended with her being ransomed from him for about five hundred dinars or more. He travelled to Medina, the Prophet's city, and his death came there in Rajab of the year 875, after he had performed some pious works there. He left a great deal of property. May God forgive him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D05732 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05732-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05732-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05732-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05732-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05732 ;
    aindv:sourceText "182 علي نور الدين الوراق : اثنان أحدهما الماضي قريبا وأنه من فضلاء المالكية واسم أبيه حجاج والآخر كاتب غيبة الأشرفية . مات في شوال سنة اثنتين وثمانين وقد زاد على السبعين ظنا ، وكان ساكنا لا بأس به في طائفته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Nūr al-Dīn al-Warrāq: there are two. One is the man mentioned shortly before, who was among the distinguished Mālikīs and whose father's name was Ḥajjāj; the other was the clerk of absences (kātib ghayba) of al-Ashrafiyya. He (the latter) died in Shawwāl of the year 882, having, by estimate, exceeded seventy years of age. He was quiet and unobjectionable among his group."@en .

rec:AIND-D05733 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05733-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05733-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05733-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05733 ;
    aindv:sourceText "183 علي الأسطا الأرزنجاني والد يعقوب شاه الآتي . قدم من بلاده إلى الروم ثم إلى القاهرة في أول سلطنة المؤيد واختص بخدمة الناصري بن البارزي ثم انتقل لبيت السلطان وتقدم في القوس علما وعملا بحيث عرف بالأسطا ، وحج سبع مرار وجاور وعمر نحو المائة حتى مات وكان خيرا من ولده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Usṭā al-Arzinjānī, father of Yaʿqūb Shāh (to follow). He came from his homeland to al-Rūm (Anatolia), then to Cairo at the beginning of the sultanate of al-Muʾayyad. He attached himself to the service of al-Nāṣirī b. al-Bārizī, then moved to the household of the sultan. He excelled in archery in both theory and practice, so that he became known as \"al-Usṭā\" (the master). He performed the pilgrimage seven times and resided as a mujāwir (presumably in Mecca), and lived to about a hundred years before he died. He was a better man than his son."@en .

rec:AIND-D05734 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05734-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05734-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05734 ;
    aindv:sourceText "184 علي الشهير بولد أبي العطار المصري المكي . مات في رجب سنة ثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī, known as \"the son of Abū al-ʿAṭṭār\", al-Miṣrī al-Makkī. He died in Rajab of the year 880. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05735 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05735-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05735-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05735 ;
    aindv:sourceText "185 على أبو فروة الجبرتي ، مات بمكة في رمضان سنة ثمان وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Abū Farwa al-Jabartī. He died in Mecca in Ramaḍān of the year 878. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05736 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05736-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05736-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05736 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي بدوي . يأتي في علي الثقفي قريبا."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī Badawī. He will appear shortly under ʿAlī al-Thaqafī."@en .

rec:AIND-D05737 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05737-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05737-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05737 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي برددار أزبك . في إبراهيم بن علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī, bardadār (chamberlain) of Azbak. See under [Ibn] Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D05738 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05738-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05738-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05738-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05738 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي البسطي المغربي . هو ابن مضى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Basṭī al-Maghribī. He is Ibn … who has been mentioned above."@en .

rec:AIND-D05739 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05739-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05739-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05739 ;
    aindv:sourceText "186 علي البغدادي الفران مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة سبع وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Baghdādī al-Farrān (the baker). He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 867. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05740 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05740-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05740-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05740-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05740 ;
    aindv:sourceText "187 علي البهائي الغزولي مولاهم الدمشقي الأديب ، مات سنة خمس عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Bahāʾī al-Ghazūlī, their mawlā (freedman; the family referred to is ambiguous), al-Dimashqī, the man of letters (adīb). He died in the year 815."@en .

rec:AIND-D05742 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05742-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05742-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b101_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05742 ;
    aindv:sourceText "189 علي الثقفي المكي السمان بها ويعرف بعلي بدوي . مات في المحرم سنة إحدى وثمانين وقد رأيته وكان يحب خدمة الصالحين والعلماء ويقضي حوائجهم وكنت ممن فعل معي ذلك ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Thaqafī al-Makkī, the clarified-butter seller (sammān) there (in Mecca), known as ʿAlī Badawī. He died in Muḥarram of the year 881. I saw him; he loved to serve the righteous and the scholars and to attend to their needs, and I was among those for whom he did so. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05743 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05743-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05743-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05743 ;
    aindv:sourceText "190 علي الجبالي الولي الشهير نزيل جبل المنارة خارج تونس . مات به في المحرم سنة ثمان وأربعين أرخه ابن عزم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Jibālī, the famous saint (walī), resident of Jabal al-Manāra outside Tunis. He died there in Muḥarram (8)48. Ibn ʿAzm recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05744 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05744-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05744-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05744 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي الجبرتي نزيل سطح جامع الأزهر . في ابن يوسف بن صير الدين بن موسى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Jabartī, resident of the roof of the al-Azhar Mosque. [His biography is] under Ibn Yūsuf b. Ṣīr al-Dīn b. Mūsā."@en .

rec:AIND-D05745 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05745-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05745-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05745 ;
    aindv:sourceText "191 علي الجبرتي آخر شيخ صالح مات بمكة في صفر سنة خمس وخمسين أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Another ʿAlī al-Jabartī, a pious shaykh. He died in Mecca in Ṣafar (8)55. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05746 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05746-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05746-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05746 ;
    aindv:sourceText "192 علي الحموي الخواجا الأعرج . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة أربع وثمانين أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Ḥamawī, al-Khawājā, al-Aʿraj (the lame). He died in Mecca in Muḥarram (8)84. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05747 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05747-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05747-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05747 ;
    aindv:sourceText "193 علي الحيحي المغربي شيخ رباط المغاربة بمكة . مات في المحرم سنة أربع وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Ḥayḥī al-Maghribī, shaykh of the Ribāṭ al-Maghāriba in Mecca. He died in Muḥarram (8)84. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05748 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05748-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05748-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05748 ;
    aindv:sourceText "194 علي الخباز الضرير المقرئ . تلا بالسبع على ابن أسد وأقرأ الطلبة وكان ممن قرأ عليه عمر بن قاسم إمام مسجد قانم . مات قريبا من سنة ستين أو بعدها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Khabbāz, the blind (al-Ḍarīr) Qurʾān reciter. He recited according to the seven readings under Ibn Asad and taught recitation to students. Among those who recited under him was ʿUmar b. Qāsim, imam of the Mosque of Qānim. He died around the year (8)60 or after it."@en .

rec:AIND-D05750 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05750-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05750-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05750 ;
    aindv:sourceText "196 علي الدورسي البستاني . لقيه الحافظ ابن موسى في سنة خمس عشرة فذكر له أن له من العمر مائة سنة وسنة وهو قوي البنية شديد الحواس يصعد شجر الجوز فقرأ عليه بالإجازة العامة وسمع الأبي واستجازه لجماعة كابن شيخنا وبني ابن فهد وأظنه ابن فينظر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Dawrasī al-Bustānī (the gardener). The ḥāfiẓ Ibn Mūsā met him in the year (8)15, and he told him that he was one hundred and one years old, yet he was of strong build and keen senses, climbing walnut trees. So (Ibn Mūsā) read under him by the general ijāza, and al-Ubbī heard (from him); and he requested from him an ijāza for a group, such as the son of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and the sons of Ibn Fahd. I think he is the son of [...]; this should be examined."@en .

rec:AIND-D05751 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05751-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05751-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05751-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05751 ;
    aindv:sourceText "197 علي الرفاعي . مات في وسط جمادى الثانية سنة ثلاث وثلاثين بالقاهرة وكان متواضعا متأدبا حسن العشرة مع الناس والطائفة الأحمدية عار من الفضيلة ، ذكره العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Rifāʿī. He died in the middle of Jumādā II (8)33 in Cairo. He was humble and well-mannered, on good terms with people and with the Aḥmadiyya order, but devoid of learning. Al-ʿAynī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05752 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05752-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05752-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05752 ;
    aindv:sourceText "198 علي الرومي . مات بمكة في صفر سنة ست وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Rūmī. He died in Mecca in Ṣafar (8)56. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05753 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05753-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05753-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05753 ;
    aindv:sourceText "199 علي الشلبي . مات بمكة في صفر سنة سبع وستين . أرخه ابن فهد . وهو ابن حمدان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Shalabī. He died in Mecca in Ṣafar (8)67. Ibn Fahd recorded his death. He is the son of Ḥamdān."@en .

rec:AIND-D05754 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05754-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05754-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05754-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05754-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05754 ;
    aindv:sourceText "200 علي شيخ العجمي نزيل مكة وأحد جماعة الشيخ محمد بن قاوان ، تاجر يلقب بالخواجا . مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وتسعين وأوصى للشافعي بأربعين ولكل واحد من باقي القضاة الأربعة بعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī, the shaykh, al-ʿAjamī, resident of Mecca and one of the circle of Shaykh Muḥammad b. Qāwān. A merchant, he was styled al-Khawājā. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja (8)91, and bequeathed forty to the Shāfiʿī (judge) and twenty to each of the remaining (three) of the four judges."@en .

rec:AIND-D05755 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05755-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05755-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05755 ;
    aindv:sourceText "201 علي العريان كانت له معرفة حسنة بالتعبير . مات بمكة في ذي القعدة سنة خمس وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-ʿUryān. He had a good knowledge of dream interpretation. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Qaʿda (8)55. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05756 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05756-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05756-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05756 ;
    aindv:sourceText "202 علي الصامت العريان . شاب معتقد بين العوام . مات في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Ṣāmit (the Silent) al-ʿUryān. A young man venerated among the common people. He died in Rabīʿ I (8)52."@en .

rec:AIND-D05757 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05757-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05757-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05757 ;
    aindv:sourceText "203 علي القادري اللبان أحد من يعتقد وممن كان يذكر أنه أخذ عن الشهاب بن الناصح . مات في المحرم سنة سبع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Qādirī al-Labbān (the milk-seller). One of those who were venerated, and one of those who used to say that he had studied under al-Shihāb b. al-Nāṣiḥ. He died in Muḥarram (8)57."@en .

rec:AIND-D05758 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05758-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05758-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05758 ;
    aindv:sourceText "204 علي القدسي المؤدب مات في جمادى الأولى سنة اثنتين وستين أرخ الثلاثة المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Qudsī, the muʾaddib (children's teacher). He died in Jumādā I (8)62. Al-Munīr recorded (the deaths of) these three."@en .

rec:AIND-D05759 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05759-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05759-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05759 ;
    aindv:sourceText "205 علي القرافي الحنفي نائب الحكم بمركز دار التفاح ، مات سنة ست عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Qarāfī, the Ḥanafī, deputy judge (nāʾib al-ḥukm) at the court station (markaz) of Dār al-Tuffāḥ. He died in the year (8)16."@en .

rec:AIND-D05760 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05760-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05760-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05760 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي القزويني الفرخة ، سقطت ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Qazwīnī al-Farkha. Omitted."@en .

rec:AIND-D05761 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05761-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05761-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05761 ;
    aindv:sourceText "206 علي القلندري صاحب الزاوية خارج الصحراء وأحد من يعتقد . مات سنة ثلاث وعشرين . أرخه شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Qalandarī, master of the zāwiya outside al-Ṣaḥrāʾ (the northern cemetery of Cairo) and one of those who were venerated. He died in the year (8)23. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05762 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05762-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05762-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05762 ;
    aindv:sourceText "207 علي القليوبي ثم القاهري شيخ مذكور بالجذب والأحوال الدالة على الكشف بحيث اتفق الجم الغفير على اعتقاده . مات فجأة في المحرم سنة تسع وثمانين ودفن بتربة الأمشاطي رحمه الله . طولته في الوفيات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Qalyūbī, then al-Qāhirī. A shaykh known for ecstasy (jadhb) and spiritual states indicating unveiling (kashf), such that a vast multitude agreed in venerating him. He died suddenly in Muḥarram (8)89 and was buried in the Turba of al-Amshāṭī, may God have mercy on him. I treated him at length in al-Wafayāt."@en .

rec:AIND-D05763 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05763-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05763-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b102_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05763 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي الكاتب عصفور . في ابن محمد بن عبد النصير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Kātib, ʿAṣfūr. [His biography is] under Ibn Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Naṣīr."@en .

rec:AIND-D05764 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05764-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05764-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05764 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي الكناني الحبيبي . في ابن آدم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Kinānī al-Ḥabībī. [See] under Ibn Ādam."@en .

rec:AIND-D05765 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05765-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05765-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05765-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05765 ;
    aindv:sourceText "208 علي الكيلاني الشافعي . رأيته فيمن عرض عليه سنة خمس وتسعين وأظنه ملا علي الماضي فيمن أبوه نور الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Kīlānī al-Shāfiʿī. I saw him among those to whom [someone] presented [memorised texts] in the year (8)95, and I think he is Mullā ʿAlī, mentioned above among those whose father is Nūr Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D05767 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05767-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05767-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05767 ;
    aindv:sourceText "210 علي المحلي ثم المكي العطار بباب السلام والساكن برباط العباس ، كان مباركا . مات بمكة في ذي القعدة سنة اثنتين وثمانين ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Maḥallī, then al-Makkī, the druggist (al-ʿaṭṭār) at Bāb al-Salām, who resided in Ribāṭ al-ʿAbbās. He was a blessed man. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Qaʿda (8)82. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05768 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05768-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05768-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05768 ;
    aindv:sourceText "211 علي المغربي العطار بمكة ، مات بها في المحرم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Maghribī, the druggist (al-ʿaṭṭār) in Mecca. He died there in al-Muḥarram."@en .

rec:AIND-D05769 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05769-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05769-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05769-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05769 ;
    aindv:sourceText "علي اليمني ، مضى في علي خروعة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAlī al-Yamanī. He was mentioned above under ʿAlī Kharūʿa."@en .

rec:AIND-D05770 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05770-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05770-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05770 ;
    aindv:sourceText "212 عمار بن خمليش ، شيخ أولاد حسين عرب فاس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAmmār b. Khamlīsh, the shaykh of Awlād Ḥusayn, the Arabs of Fez."@en .

rec:AIND-D05771 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05771-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05771-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05771 ;
    aindv:sourceText "213 عمار بن عبد الرحيم بن حسن الغرياني نسبة لبني غريان بمعجمة مكسورة ثم مهملة ساكنة بعدها مثناة تحتانية ثم نون بالقرب من تفهنا ثم القاهري الشافعي أحد القدماء من عدول الصليبة تجاه الصرغتمشية بل هو أحد طلبتها حمل عني شرح ألفية العراقي للناظم بعد أن كتبه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAmmār b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Ḥasan al-Ghiryānī — a nisba to Banū Ghiryān, near Tafahnā, spelt with a dotted ghayn with kasra, then an undotted rāʾ with sukūn, then a yāʾ with two dots below, then nūn — then al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī. One of the senior notaries (ʿudūl) of al-Ṣalība, opposite the Ṣarghatmishiyya; indeed he was one of its students. He received from me the commentary on the Alfiyya of al-ʿIrāqī by its author, after having copied it out himself."@en .

rec:AIND-D05772 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05772-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05772-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05772 ;
    aindv:sourceText "214 عمار الحوفي الشافعي نزيل صرد من الغربية . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAmmār al-Ḥūfī al-Shāfiʿī, a resident of Ṣarad in al-Gharbiyya. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05775 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05775-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05775-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05775-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05775 ;
    aindv:sourceText "217 عمرو بن أحمد بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن يحيى بن أمير تونس ، مات سنة بضع وعشرين ورأيت من سماه عمر فيحرر الصواب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAmr b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. Yaḥyā b. Amīr Tūnis. He died in the (eight hundred and) twenties. I have seen someone who named him ʿUmar, so the correct form needs to be verified."@en .

rec:AIND-D05776 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05776-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05776-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05776-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05776 ;
    aindv:sourceText "218 عمرو بن عثمان بن محمد بن عثمان ابن لصاحبنا الفخر الديمي الأصل الأزهري . فطن ذكي سمع على جماعة بقراءة أبيه وبقرائتي بل سمع مني أيضا . ومات قبل بلوغه في الطاعون سنة أربع وستين عوضه الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAmr b. ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān, a son of our companion al-Fakhr al-Daymī by origin, al-Azharī. He was intelligent and quick-witted; he heard from a number of scholars through the recitation of his father and through my recitation, and indeed he heard from me as well. He died before reaching puberty in the plague of the year (8)64. May God recompense him with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D05783 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05783-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05783-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05783 ;
    aindv:sourceText "225 عمر بن إبراهيم بن القواس الدمشقي السكري العابر ، كان يجيد تعبير المنامات ويجلس على كرسي بالجامع وقد طلب الحديث كثيرا وقرأ وسمع مات فجأة وهو في الخلاء ولم يشعروا به إلا ثاني يوم وذلك في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى قاله شيخنا في أنبائه . )"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ibrāhīm b. al-Qawwās al-Dimashqī al-Sukkarī al-ʿĀbir (the dream-interpreter). He was skilled in the interpretation of dreams and used to sit on a chair in the congregational mosque. He sought ḥadīth extensively, read and heard. He died suddenly while in the privy, and they did not notice him until the following day; that was in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year (80)1. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said so in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05784 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05784-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05784-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05784 ;
    aindv:sourceText "226 عمر بن إبراهيم الأخطابي ، ممن سمع علي قريب التسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ibrāhīm al-Akhṭābī. He was among those who heard from me around the year (8)90."@en .

rec:AIND-D05785 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05785-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05785-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05785-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05785 ;
    aindv:sourceText "227 عمر بن أحمد بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن عيسى بن مطير الحكمي اليماني الشافعي أخو أبي القسم وغيره ويلقب بالفتى ، خلف أخاه في الوظيفة ، وهو فقيه خير يدرس ويفتي قاله الأهدل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā b. Muṭayr al-Ḥakamī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī, the brother of Abū al-Qāsim and others; he was nicknamed al-Fatā. He succeeded his brother in the post. He was a good jurist who taught and issued fatwās, so said al-Ahdal."@en .

rec:AIND-D05786 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05786-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05786-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05786-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05786 ;
    aindv:sourceText "228 عمر بن أحمد بن أحمد الحلبي الدمياطي رافق أبا الطيب بن البدراني في السماع على ابن الكويك وأثبته الزين رضوان كذلك بدون زائد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. Aḥmad al-Ḥalabī al-Dimyāṭī. He accompanied Abū al-Ṭayyib b. al-Badrānī in hearing under Ibn al-Kuwayk, and al-Zayn Riḍwān likewise recorded him without any addition."@en .

rec:AIND-D05787 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05787-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05787-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05787-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05787 ;
    aindv:sourceText "229 عمر بن أحمد بن زيد السراج الجراعي الدمشقي الحنبلي ابن أخي أبي بكر بن زيد الآتي لقيني بمكة في سنة ست وثمانين فلازمني في قراءة البخاري وغيره وسماع أشياء بل جاور قبل ذلك مع عمه وسمع بقراءته على النجم عمر بن فهد المسند ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. Zayd al-Sirāj al-Jarrāʿī al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanbalī, the nephew of Abū Bakr b. Zayd (mentioned below). He met me in Mecca in the year (8)86 and attended me closely in the reading of al-Bukhārī and other works and in hearing various things. Before that he had already resided as a mujāwir together with his uncle and, through the latter's recitation, heard from the musnid al-Najm ʿUmar b. Fahd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05789 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05789-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05789-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05789-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05789 ;
    aindv:sourceText "231 عمر بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن علي الريمي المكي الماضي أبوه وجده والآتي أخوه محمد صغير سمع علي في المجاورة الثالثة بمكة أشياء وزار مع أبويه المدينة . )"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī al-Raymī al-Makkī; his father and grandfather were mentioned above, and his brother Muḥammad will be mentioned below. As a child he heard some things from me during the third mujāwara in Mecca, and he visited Medina with his parents."@en .

rec:AIND-D05790 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05790-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05790-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05790-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05790 ;
    aindv:sourceText "232 عمر بن أحمد بن عبد الرحمن بن الجمال المصري المكي . ولد في سنة إحدى وخمسين بمكة وحفظ القرآن والمنهاج ، ودخل القاهرة غير مرة وحضر دروس البرهاني وولده وأخيه وسمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Jamāl al-Miṣrī al-Makkī. He was born in the year (8)51 in Mecca and memorised the Qurʾān and the Minhāj. He entered Cairo more than once, attended the lessons of al-Burhānī, his son and his brother, and heard from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D05791 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05791-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05791-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05791 ;
    aindv:sourceText "233 عمر بن أحمد بن عبد الواحد التقي الزبيدي شاد زبيد كان له اعتناء بالعلم . مات في سنة اثنتين وعشرين ، ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Taqī al-Zabīdī, the shādd (superintendent) of Zabīd. He took an interest in learning. He died in the year (8)22. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05797 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05797-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05797-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05797 ;
    aindv:sourceText "239 عمر بن أحمد بن عمر التقي الزبيدي المنقش الشافعي الماضي ولده ، كان فقيها خيرا فاضلا دينا متواضعا كثير التبسم لين الجانب صابرا ، مات في سنة ثلاث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmar al-Taqī al-Zabīdī al-Munaqqish al-Shāfiʿī; his son was mentioned above. He was a jurist, good, virtuous, pious, humble, often smiling, gentle and patient. He died in the year (80)3."@en .

rec:AIND-D05800 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05800-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05800-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05800-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b103_review,
        agent:claude_b99_103_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05800 ;
    aindv:sourceText "242 عمر بن أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن عمر بن رضوان الدمشقي الحريري الشافعي الماضي أبوه ويعرف كهو بالسلاوي لكون أبيه سبط محمد بن عمر السلاوي وصفه البقاعي بخادم ابن مزهر وأنه كان بالقاهرة قبل الأربعين أو نحو ذلك ولم يذكر فيه شيئا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. Riḍwān al-Dimashqī al-Ḥarīrī al-Shāfiʿī; his father was mentioned above. Like his father he is known as al-Salāwī, because his father was the daughter's son of Muḥammad b. ʿUmar al-Salāwī. Al-Biqāʿī described him as a servant of Ibn Muzhir and said that he was in Cairo before the (eight hundred and) forties or thereabouts, but mentioned nothing further about him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05803 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05803-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05803-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05803 ;
    aindv:sourceText "245 عمر بن أحمد بن محمد بن محمود بن يوسف بن علي الهندي الأصل المكي . سمع على الشهاب أحمد المرشدي في سنة اثنتين وثلاثين بعض مناسك ابن جماعة ، ومات بمكة في جمادى الآخرة سنة ثلاث وستين ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Maḥmūd b. Yūsuf b. ʿAlī, of Indian origin, of Mecca. He heard part of the Manāsik of Ibn Jamāʿa from al-Shihāb Aḥmad al-Murshidī in the year (8)32. He died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ākhira (8)63. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05805 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05805-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05805-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05805 ;
    aindv:sourceText "247 عمر بن أحمد بن محمود الجبرتي الأصل نزيل مكة . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. Maḥmūd, of Jabartī origin, resident of Mecca. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05811 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05811-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05811-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05811 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن أبي بكر بن أحمد المسلي اليماني ، أحد المعتقدين ، سيأتي في عمر العدني ممن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. Aḥmad al-Maslī al-Yamānī, one of those held in veneration. He will come below under ʿUmar al-ʿAdanī, among those whose father is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D05812 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05812-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05812-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05812 ;
    aindv:sourceText "253 عمر بن أبي بكر بن خليل البلبيسي الأصل الشافعي ويعرف بالبطايني أحد المعتقدين ممن تأخر إلى أيام الأشرف قايتباي وكان لدولات باي أيام الظاهر جقمق فيه حسن اعتقاد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. Khalīl, of Bilbays origin, Shāfiʿī, known as al-Baṭāyinī. One of those held in veneration, among those who lived on into the days of al-Ashraf Qāytbāy. Dawlāt Bāy, in the days of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq, had a firm belief in him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05813 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05813-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05813-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05813 ;
    aindv:sourceText "254 عمر بن الزكي أبي بكر بن عبد الرحمن المصري القباني العطار أخو إبراهيم وأحمد وعلي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Zakī Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Miṣrī al-Qabbānī al-ʿAṭṭār, the brother of Ibrāhīm, Aḥmad and ʿAlī. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05816 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05816-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05816-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05816 ;
    aindv:sourceText "257 عمر بن أبي بكر بن علي الأنصاري الموصلي القادري ، ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī al-Anṣārī al-Mawṣilī al-Qādirī. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05819 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05819-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05819-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05819 ;
    aindv:sourceText "260 عمر المدعو عبد السلام بن أبي بكر بن محمد أبي بكر بن علي بن محمد بن أبي بكر شجاع الدين الناشري الآتي أبوه سمع على خاله القاضي الجمال الطيب كثيرا وانجمع للتلاوة وملازمة الجماعة ، وحج سنة ست وعشرين وله أولاد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar, called ʿAbd al-Salām, b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr, Shujāʿ al-Dīn al-Nāshirī; his father comes below. He heard much from his maternal uncle the qāḍī al-Jamāl al-Ṭayyib, and devoted himself to recitation and to constant attendance at congregational prayer. He performed the pilgrimage in (8)26, and he had children."@en .

rec:AIND-D05820 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05820-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05820-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05820 ;
    aindv:sourceText "261 عمر بن أبي بكر بن محمد بن أبي بكر فتح الدين أبو الفتح الحبشي الحلبي الآتي أبوه ، ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr, Fatḥ al-Dīn Abū al-Fatḥ al-Ḥabashī al-Ḥalabī; his father comes below. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05822 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05822-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05822-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05822-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05822 ;
    aindv:sourceText "263 عمر بن الرضي أبي بكر بن محمد بن عبد اللطيف بن سالم السراج اليماني الأصل المكي ويعرف بابن الرضي . أحد مباشري جدة بل هو عينهم وموقع السيد بركات ، ممن كان كثير المسامحة في منصبه والمحبة في الإطعام ممن صاهر التقي بن فهد على ابنته أم ريم واستولدها الجمال محمدا ، وكان قدومه مكة سنة بضع وأربعين وهو من بيت شهير . مات بمكة في ذي القعدة سنة خمس وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Raḍī Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Sālim al-Sirāj, of Yemeni origin, of Mecca, known as Ibn al-Raḍī. One of the administrators (mubāshir) of Jidda, indeed their foremost, and the secretary (muwaqqiʿ) of al-Sayyid Barakāt. He was among those who were very lenient in their office and fond of feeding people. He became the son-in-law of al-Taqī b. Fahd through his daughter Umm Rīm, with whom he had al-Jamāl Muḥammad. He came to Mecca in the (8)40s, and he was from a famous house. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Qaʿda (8)65. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05824 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05824-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05824-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05824 ;
    aindv:sourceText "265 عمر بن أبي بكر بن محمد الدمشقي الحريري . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad al-Dimashqī al-Ḥarīrī. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05825 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05825-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05825-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05825 ;
    aindv:sourceText "266 عمر بن أبي بكر بن يوسف القاهري الوفائي . شيخ صالح سمع علي في سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. Yūsuf al-Qāhirī al-Wafāʾī, a pious shaykh. He heard from me in the year (8)95."@en .

rec:AIND-D05826 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05826-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05826-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05826 ;
    aindv:sourceText "267 عمر بن أبي بكر الصيداوي الدمشقي الشافعي ويعرف بابن المبيض . شاب فاضل دين ساكن أقام بالقاهرة يسيرا واشتغل على بعض الجماعة وقرأ علي صحيح مسلم وبحثا شرحي لهداية ابن الجزري وصحبه معه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr al-Ṣaydāwī al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Mubayyiḍ. A capable, pious and quiet young man. He stayed in Cairo for a short while, studied under some of the scholars, read Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim before me and, by way of study, my commentary on the Hidāya of Ibn al-Jazarī, and took it with him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05827 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05827-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05827-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05827 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن أبي بكر المسلي . فيمن جده أحمد."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr al-Maslī. [He is] among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05828 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05828-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05828-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05828 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن جامع ، هو ابن عثمان بن خضر بن جامع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Jāmiʿ: he is Ibn ʿUthmān b. Khiḍr b. Jāmiʿ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05829 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05829-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05829-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05829 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن حاتم العجلوني الزاهد الولي له كلام يدخل في منقبته وجلالته مضى في أحمد بن حسين بن رسلان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ḥātim al-ʿAjlūnī, the ascetic, the saint. He has a saying that counts among his merits and his greatness. It was given above under Aḥmad b. Ḥusayn b. Raslān."@en .

rec:AIND-D05830 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05830-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05830-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05830 ;
    aindv:sourceText "268 عمر بن حجاج بن يوسف الميموني الحنفي . ممن سمع على الولوي السنباطي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ḥajjāj b. Yūsuf al-Maymūnī al-Ḥanafī. He was among those who heard from al-Walawī al-Sunbāṭī."@en .

rec:AIND-D05832 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05832-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05832-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05832-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05832 ;
    aindv:sourceText "270 عمر بن الرباط حسن بن علي بن أبي بكر البقاعي والد إبراهيم صاحب تلك الأفاعيل . قال ابنه أنه ولد بعد سنة ثمانين وسبعمائة تقريبا بقرية خربة روحا من البقاع العزيزي من عمل بعلبك ، وذكر له ترجمة طنانة وأنه قتل في شعبان سنة إحدى وعشرين هو وجماعة من أخوته وبني عمه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Rubāṭ Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr al-Biqāʿī, the father of Ibrāhīm, the author of those notorious doings. His son said that he was born approximately after the year (7)80 in the village of Khirbat Rūḥā in al-Biqāʿ al-ʿAzīzī, in the district of Baʿlabakk. The son wrote a grandiloquent biography of him and stated that he was killed in Shaʿbān (8)21 together with a group of his brothers and cousins."@en .

rec:AIND-D05836 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05836-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05836-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05836-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05836 ;
    aindv:sourceText "274 عمر بن حسن بن محمد بن قاسم بن علي بن أحمد السراج بن الخواجا البدر لمعروف بالطاهر الماضي أبوه وشقيقه عبد الرحمن . تقدم في التجارة وكان أجل إخوته وسافر لبلاد الهند . مات في شعبان سنة ثمان وستين بجدة بعد سقوطه من إصقالة وتعطله بسبب كسر رجله قليلا وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بها وفجع به أبوه أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. Qāsim b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad, al-Sirāj b. al-Khawājā al-Badr known as al-Ṭāhir; his father and his full brother ʿAbd al-Raḥmān were mentioned above. He advanced in trade, was the most eminent of his brothers, and travelled to the lands of India. He died in Shaʿbān (8)68 in Jidda, after falling from a gangway and being laid up for a while by a broken leg; he was carried to Mecca and buried there. His father was stricken by his loss. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05837 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05837-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05837-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05837-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05837 ;
    aindv:sourceText "275 عمر بن حسن الحموي شريف يتيم في كفالة ابن الحوراني التاجر . سمع مني معهم بعض الصحيح وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ḥasan al-Ḥamawī, a sharīf, an orphan under the guardianship of the merchant Ibn al-Ḥawrānī. He heard part of the Ṣaḥīḥ and other works from me together with them [the household of Ibn al-Ḥawrānī]."@en .

rec:AIND-D05838 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05838-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05838-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05838 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن أبي الحسن بن أحمد بن محمد بن الملقن . في ابن علي بن أحمد بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī al-Ḥasan b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. al-Mulaqqin. [His biography is] under Ibn ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05839 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05839-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05839-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05839-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05839 ;
    aindv:sourceText "276 عمر بن الحسين بن بوبان بموحدتين أولاهما مضمومة وآخره نون الغزي الحنفي . ولي قضاء بلده في سنة ثمان وخمسين بعد صرف ابن عمر فدام دون سنة ثم أعيد وكذا وليه مرة أخرى ، ومن شيوخه ناصر الدين الإياسي . وهو في سنة تسعين حي جاز الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Ḥusayn b. Būbān (with two bāʾs, the first with ḍamma, ending in nūn) al-Ghazzī al-Ḥanafī. He was appointed judge of his town (Gaza) in the year 858 after the dismissal of Ibn ʿUmar, but lasted less than a year; he was later reinstated, and likewise held the office once more. Among his teachers was Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Iyāsī. In the year 890 he was still alive and had passed sixty."@en .

rec:AIND-D05840 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05840-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05840-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05840 ;
    aindv:sourceText "277 عمر بن حسين بن حسام الدين النجم بن القاضي جمال الدين السعدي نسبة لسعد بن أبي وقاص الحصني الشافعي عم العلاء علي بن البدر محمد بن حسين الماضي . قدم القاهرة فقرأ على شيخنا في البخاري وكان غاية في الكرم مع فضيلة وديانة . مات في سنة ثلاث وثلاثين بالطاعون رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ḥusayn b. Ḥusām al-Dīn, al-Najm b. al-Qāḍī Jamāl al-Dīn, al-Saʿdī (an attribution to Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ) al-Ḥiṣnī al-Shāfiʿī, the paternal uncle of al-ʿAlāʾ ʿAlī b. al-Badr Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn, mentioned previously. He came to Cairo and read al-Bukhārī under our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar). He was extremely generous, with merit and piety. He died of the plague in the year 833. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05844 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05844-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05844-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05844 ;
    aindv:sourceText "281 عمر بن حسين الشجاع الدمرداشي أمير زبيد . مات في سنة اثنتين وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ḥusayn, al-Shujāʿ al-Damardāshī, amīr of Zabīd. He died in the year 822."@en .

rec:AIND-D05847 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05847-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05847-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05847 ;
    aindv:sourceText "284 عمر بن داود بن أحمد الشامي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Dāwūd b. Aḥmad al-Shāmī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05848 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05848-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05848-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05848-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05848 ;
    aindv:sourceText "285 عمر بن دولات باي المؤيدي . مات في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى وثمانين وكان مسرفا على نفسه غير متستر أتلف شيئا كثيرا وكاد أن يفتقر فعوجل عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Dawlāt Bāy al-Muʾayyadī. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 881. He was prodigal with himself and made no effort at discretion; he squandered a great deal and was on the verge of impoverishment when death took him suddenly. May God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05851 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05851-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05851-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05851 ;
    aindv:sourceText "288 عمر بن سليمان بن عمار الصردي ثم الغمري . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Sulaymān b. ʿAmmār al-Ṣardī, then al-Ghamrī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05852 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05852-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05852-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05852-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05852 ;
    aindv:sourceText "289 عمر بن الشرف الغزولي الحنبلي . مات في ذي القعدة سنة أربع بحلب . أرخه شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Sharaf al-Ghazūlī al-Ḥanbalī. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year (8)04 in Aleppo. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05853 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05853-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05853-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05853 ;
    aindv:sourceText "290 عمر بن المؤيد شيخ . مات في سنة ست عشرة وله عشر سنين أو دونها ودفن بتربة الناصر . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Muʾayyad Shaykh. He died in the year 816, aged ten or less, and was buried in the turba of al-Nāṣir. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05854 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05854-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05854-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05854-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05854 ;
    aindv:sourceText "291 عمر بن صالح بن السراج البحيري الأزهري المالكي والد البدر محمد الآتي . ممن اشتغل وتكسب بالشهادة بل ناب في القضاء وقتا وتنزل في الجهات وليس بمحمود قضاء ومعاملة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ṣāliḥ b. al-Sirāj al-Buḥayrī al-Azharī al-Mālikī, the father of al-Badr Muḥammad, mentioned below. He engaged in study and earned his living as a notary-witness; indeed he served as a deputy judge for a time and was enrolled in stipendiary posts. He was not praiseworthy either in his judging or in his dealings."@en .

rec:AIND-D05855 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05855-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05855-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05855 ;
    aindv:sourceText "292 عمر بن صديق بن عمر السملائي المحلي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ṣiddīq b. ʿUmar al-Samlāʾī al-Maḥallī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05856 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05856-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05856-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05856-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05856 ;
    aindv:sourceText "293 عمر بن طرخان بن شهري الحاجب الكبير بحلب . مات في رجب سنة ثلاثين . أرخه شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Ṭarkhān b. Shahrī, the grand chamberlain (al-ḥājib al-kabīr) of Aleppo. He died in Rajab of the year 830. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05857 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05857-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05857-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05857-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05857 ;
    aindv:sourceText "294 عمر بن عبد الحميد الزين المدني . سمع على ابن الجزري الشفا في ثلاث وعشرين وضبط الأسماء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd, al-Zayn al-Madanī. He heard al-Shifāʾ from Ibn al-Jazarī in the year (8)23 and fixed the correct reading of the names."@en .

rec:AIND-D05858 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05858-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05858-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05858 ;
    aindv:sourceText "295 عمر بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد المقراني اليماني الشافعي والد عبد الصمد الماضي له ذكر فيه وأنه قرأ على الأهدل وكان فقيها مات سنة ثمان وثمانين عن ست وسبعين سنة"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad al-Muqrānī al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī, the father of ʿAbd al-Ṣamad, mentioned previously. He is mentioned in his son's entry, where it is stated that he read under al-Ahdal, that he was a jurist, and that he died in the year 888 at the age of seventy-six."@en .

rec:AIND-D05859 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05859-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05859-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05859-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05859-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b105_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05859 ;
    aindv:sourceText "296 عمر بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن أبي بكر التقي بن الوجيه الزوقري اليماني . ذكره التقي بن فهد في معجمه ووصفه بالإمام المفنن ووالده بالعلامة وبيض ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr b. Abī Bakr, al-Taqī b. al-Wajīh, al-Zawqarī al-Yamānī. Al-Taqī b. Fahd mentioned him in his Muʿjam, describing him as \"the versatile imām\" and his father as \"the eminent scholar (al-ʿallāma)\", and left the rest blank."@en .

rec:AIND-D05860 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05860-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05860-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05860 ;
    aindv:sourceText "297 عمر بن عبد الرحمن بن زكريا الزواوي الميقاتي . مات سنة ثمان وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Zakariyyā al-Zawāwī al-Mīqātī. He died in the year 858."@en .

rec:AIND-D05868 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05868-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05868-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05868-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05868 ;
    aindv:sourceText "305 عمر ابن صاحبنا العز عبد العزيز بن عبد الرحمن بن إبراهيم بن محمد الكمال الحلبي الحنفي سبط أبي جعفر بن الضيا أمه عائشة ويعرف كسلفه بابن العديم اشتغل وتفقه بابن أمير حاج وأخذ عن أبي ذر وغيره سمع ببلده معي على جماعة وتميز وبرع ونظم ففاق وجمع ديوانا سماه بدور الكمال . مات في سنة كان الأتابك بحماة والدوادار بحلب في حياة أبويه ولم يكمل الثلاثين عوضه الله وإياهما الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar, the son of our companion al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad, al-Kamāl al-Ḥalabī al-Ḥanafī, the daughter's son of Abū Jaʿfar b. al-Ḍiyāʾ; his mother was ʿĀʾisha. Like his forebears he was known as Ibn al-ʿAdīm. He studied, learned jurisprudence under Ibn Amīr Ḥājj, and took knowledge from Abū Dharr and others. In his home town he heard, together with me (al-Sakhāwī), from a number of teachers. He distinguished himself, excelled, composed poetry in which he surpassed others, and compiled a dīwān he named Budūr al-Kamāl. He died in the year when the atābak was at Ḥamā and the dawādār at Aleppo, during the lifetime of his parents, before completing thirty years. May God recompense him and them with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D05869 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05869-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05869-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05869 ;
    aindv:sourceText "306 عمر بن عبد العزيز بن عبد السلام بن موسى السراج المكي الزمزمي أخو محمد الآتي . ممن حفظ القرآن وسافر إلى القاهرة والشام واليمن وله نظم كأخيه . مات في رجب سنة ثلاث وتسعين وأنا بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Salām b. Mūsā, al-Sirāj al-Makkī al-Zamzamī, the brother of Muḥammad, mentioned below. He was among those who memorised the Qurʾān; he travelled to Cairo, Syria and Yemen, and composed poetry like his brother. He died in Rajab of the year 893 while I (al-Sakhāwī) was in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05870 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05870-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05870-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05870 ;
    aindv:sourceText "307 عمر بن عبد العزيز بن عبد السلام السراج الأنصاري الزرندي المدني الشافعي . مات أبوه في صفر سنة ثلاث وستين فولد ابنه هذا بعده واشتغل يسيرا في العربية عند مسعود المغربي وفي غيرها عند غيره ولازمني في المدينة وحصل نسخة من المقاصد الحسنة بعد أن سمعه وكتبت له إجازة ثم رأيته في موسم سنة أربع وتسعين وهو باق على تودده ولكنه انحل عن اشتغاله وأظنه خالط شاهين أو غيره فلم تحمد عاقبته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Salām, al-Sirāj al-Anṣārī al-Zarandī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī. His father died in Ṣafar of the year 863 and this son of his was born after that. He studied a little Arabic grammar under Masʿūd al-Maghribī and other subjects under others. He attended me (al-Sakhāwī) closely in Medina, obtained a copy of al-Maqāṣid al-ḥasana after hearing it, and I wrote him an ijāza. Then I saw him in the pilgrimage season of the year 894: he remained as affectionate as before, but had drifted away from his studies, and I think he had fallen in with Shāhīn or someone like him, so that his end was not praiseworthy."@en .

rec:AIND-D05871 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05871-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05871-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05871-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b105_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05871 ;
    aindv:sourceText "308 عمر بن الزين عبد العزيز بن عبد الواحد بن عمر بن عياذ بتحتانية ومعجمة الأنصاري المغربي الأصل المدني المالكي والد حسن الماضي ويعرف بابن زين الدين من بيت فيه فضلاء . اشتغل وسمع على الجمال الكازروني في سنة أربع وثلاثين وعلى أبي الفتح المراغي ومات سنة ثمان وخمسين أو التي قبلها رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Zayn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. ʿUmar b. ʿIyādh (with yāʾ and then dotted dhāl), al-Anṣārī, of Maghribī origin, resident of Medina, Mālikī, the father of Ḥasan, mentioned previously, and known as Ibn Zayn al-Dīn, from a family of learned men. He studied and heard from al-Jamāl al-Kāzarūnī in the year 834 and from Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī. He died in the year 858 or the year before. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05872 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05872-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05872-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05872-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05872-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b105_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05872 ;
    aindv:sourceText "309 عمر بن عبد العزيز بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز السراج بن القاضي العز بن القاضي النور الهاشمي النويري المكي والد عبد الله الماضي وأمه أم كلثوم ابنة محمد بن عمر التعكري . ولد سنة ست وتسعين وسبعمائة بمكة وسمع من الزين المراغي وابن الجزري وأجاز له أبو هريرة بن الذهبي وابن العلائي والتنوخي وآخرون ، وولي نصف الإمامة بمقام المالكية ، وسافر في أوائل سنة اثنتين وثلاثين من مكة إلى القاهرة ثم إلى المغرب ثم التكرور ، ومات هناك في السنة التي تليها أو في التي بعدها ، وله ذكر في ابنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, al-Sirāj b. al-Qāḍī al-ʿIzz b. al-Qāḍī al-Nūr, al-Hāshimī al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī, the father of ʿAbd Allāh, mentioned previously; his mother was Umm Kulthūm, daughter of Muḥammad b. ʿUmar al-Taʿkarī. He was born in the year 796 in Mecca, heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī and Ibn al-Jazarī, and was granted ijāza by Abū Hurayra b. al-Dhahabī, Ibn al-ʿAlāʾī, al-Tanūkhī and others. He held half of the imamate at the Mālikī maqām. At the beginning of the year 832 he travelled from Mecca to Cairo, then to the Maghrib, then to Takrūr, and he died there in the following year or the one after. He is mentioned in his son's entry."@en .

rec:AIND-D05873 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05873-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05873-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05873 ;
    aindv:sourceText "310 عمر بن عبد العزيز بن علي بن عبد العزيز بن عبد الكافي الدقوقي المكي . مات في يوم السبت تاسع شوال سنة إحدى وأربعين بالقرب من عجرود وحمل إليه فدفن به ، ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Kāfī al-Daqūqī al-Makkī. He died on Saturday, 9 Shawwāl (8)41, near ʿAjrūd, and was carried there and buried in it. Ibn Fahd mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05874 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05874-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05874-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05874-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05874 ;
    aindv:sourceText "311 عمر بن عبد العزيز ابن صاحبنا النجم عمر بن التقي محمد بن محمد بن فهد ، تجدد في سنة تسع وثمانين فأرسلت لحفيد يوسف العجمي المسند علي فأجاز له وكتب في طبقة مسند عمر للنجاد ولم يلبث أن مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, grandson of our companion al-Najm ʿUmar b. al-Taqī Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Fahd. He was born in (8)89, so I wrote to ʿAlī, the grandson of Yūsuf al-ʿAjamī, the musnid, who granted him an ijāza and entered him in the audition record (ṭabaqa) of al-Najjād's Musnad ʿUmar. He did not live long and died."@en .

rec:AIND-D05875 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05875-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05875-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05875 ;
    aindv:sourceText "312 عمر بن عبد العزيز بن مسعود بن خليفة بن عطية المطيبير . مات في المحرم سنة خمس وخمسين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Masʿūd b. Khalīfa b. ʿAṭiyya al-Muṭaybīr. He died in Muḥarram (8)55 in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05876 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05876-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05876-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05876 ;
    aindv:sourceText "313 عمر بن المحيوي عبد القادر بن عبد الرحمن الشيباني المكي شقيق أبي الغيث محمد ويعرف بابن زبرق . سمع علي في القول البديع وغيره بمكة ومات بها في سنة ثمان وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Muḥyawī ʿAbd al-Qādir b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shaybānī al-Makkī, full brother of Abū al-Ghayth Muḥammad, known as Ibn Zibriq. He heard from me al-Qawl al-badīʿ and other works in Mecca, and died there in (8)88."@en .

rec:AIND-D05877 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05877-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05877-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05877 ;
    aindv:sourceText "314 عمر بن عبد الكريم بن محمد الشجاع العدني الحيلاني . مات سنة تسع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. Muḥammad al-Shujāʿ al-ʿAdanī al-Ḥaylānī. He died in (8)19."@en .

rec:AIND-D05878 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05878-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05878-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05878 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن عبد اللطيف الفوى . هو عبد اللطيف بن أحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Fawwī. He is (in fact) ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D05882 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05882-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05882-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05882 ;
    aindv:sourceText "318 عمر بن عبد الله بن محمد بن أحمد بن قاسم بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر السراج ابن العفيف بن قاضي القضاة التقي القرشي العمري الحراري الأصل المكي . مات في ربيع الأول سنة خمسين بدولات باد من بلاد كلبرجة من الهند رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Qāsim b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr, al-Sirāj Ibn al-ʿAfīf b. Qāḍī al-Quḍāt al-Taqī, al-Qurashī al-ʿUmarī, of Ḥarārī origin, al-Makkī. He died in Rabīʿ I (8)50 at Dawlatābād in the land of Kulbarja (Gulbarga) in India, may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05883 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05883-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05883-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05883-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05883 ;
    aindv:sourceText "319 عمر بن عبد الله بن محمد بن بردس بن نصر بن بردس بن رسلان الزين البعلي الحنبلي الدهان ابن عم التاج محمد والعلاء ابني إسماعيل بن محمد المذكورين ، ولد في سنة تسع وسبعين وسبعمائة ببعلبك ونشأ بها فقرأ القرآن عند الشيخ طلحة وحضر عند ابن عمه التاج وغيره في الفقه وغيره وسمع البخاري على عبد الرحمن ابن محمد بن الزعبوب أنا به الحجار ، وحج وحدث لقيته ببعلبك وقرأت عليه المائة منه مع ختمه وكان خيرا يتكسب من صناعة الدهن ، ومات قريب الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Bardas b. Naṣr b. Bardas b. Raslān, al-Zayn al-Baʿlī al-Ḥanbalī al-Dahhān, cousin of al-Tāj Muḥammad and al-ʿAlāʾ, the two sons of Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad mentioned above. He was born in (7)79 in Baʿlabakk and grew up there; he read the Qurʾān with al-Shaykh Ṭalḥa, attended the lessons of his cousin al-Tāj and others in jurisprudence and other subjects, and heard al-Bukhārī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. al-Zaʿbūb, on the authority of al-Ḥajjār. He performed the pilgrimage and transmitted ḥadīth. I met him in Baʿlabakk and read to him the Hundred (al-Miʾa) from it together with its concluding session. He was a good man who earned his living from the (house-)painting trade. He died around (8)60."@en .

rec:AIND-D05884 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05884-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05884-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05884-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05884 ;
    aindv:sourceText "320 عمر بن عبد الله بن محمد بن سليمان السراج بن الجمال الدمياطي ثم القاهري الشافعي صهر عبد الرحمن بن الفقيه موسى الماضي أبوه . نشأ فقرأ القرآن وغيره واشتغل وقرأ في الجوق وأقرأ في الطباق وخالط الناس سيما الخدام ونحوهم وباشر عند خير بك كاشف المحلة وكتب الخط الجيد وتنزل في الجهات وتردد للكافياجي ، وحج غير مرة وتردد لي وفي كلامه توقف . مات بالطاعون في رجب سنة سبع وتسعين بعد أن أهين من الدوادار عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Sulaymān, al-Sirāj b. al-Jamāl, al-Dimyāṭī then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, the ṣihr (son-in-law or brother-in-law) of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Faqīh Mūsā; his father was mentioned above. He grew up, read the Qurʾān and other texts, studied, recited in the choir (jawq), taught in the barracks (ṭibāq), and mixed with people, especially the servants and their like. He worked under Khayr Bak, the kāshif of al-Maḥalla, wrote a fine hand, held posts in various institutions, frequented al-Kāfiyājī, performed the pilgrimage more than once, and frequented me. There was a hesitancy in his speech (or: his statements call for reservation). He died of the plague in Rajab (8)97 after having been humiliated by the dawādār; may God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05886 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05886-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05886-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05886 ;
    aindv:sourceText "322 عمر بن عبد الله السراج الهندي الفافا بفاءين ، قال شيخنا في إنبائه : كان كثير النطق بالفاء فلقب بذلك ، وكان عارفا بالفقه وأصوله والعربية . أقام بمكة أزيد من أربعين سنة يفيد الناس فيها ومات في ذي الحجة سنة خمس عشرة عن سبعين سنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Sirāj al-Hindī al-Fāfā (with two fāʾs). Our shaykh said in his Inbāʾ: he pronounced the letter fāʾ a great deal and was therefore so nicknamed; he was learned in jurisprudence, its principles, and Arabic. He lived in Mecca for more than forty years, benefiting people there, and died in Dhū al-Ḥijja (8)15 at the age of seventy."@en .

rec:AIND-D05887 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05887-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05887-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05887 ;
    aindv:sourceText "323 عمر بن عبد الله العلبي الشافعي . اشتغل كثيرا وانقطع في الجامع الأموي يشغل الأبناء في القرآن وفي التنبيه ويشرح لهم بحيث انتفع به جماعة مع سكون وانجماع . مات في رمضان سنة ثلاث . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿUlabī al-Shāfiʿī. He studied a great deal and secluded himself in the Umayyad Mosque, teaching the youths the Qurʾān and al-Tanbīh and explaining them to them, so that a number of people benefited from him; he was quiet and withdrawn. He died in Ramaḍān (80)3. Our shaykh mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05888 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05888-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05888-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05888 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن عبد الله البلخي . فيمن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Balkhī. (See) among those whose father is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D05889 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05889-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05889-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05889 ;
    aindv:sourceText "324 عمر بن عبد الله المصري نزيل مكة أقام . بها نحو عشرين عاما لا معلوم له ولا يسأل بل كثير الصمت والسهر والعزله بحيث ذكره محمد بن الشيخ عمر العرابي في ترجمة والده ونقل عن أبيه أنه كان يذكر أنه من الأبدال ممن كان يرى النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم كثيرا غير ذاكر للدنيا ولا يضحك ولا يلتفت ولا يجالس سوى أهل الآخرة . مات في سنة سبع وعشرين . أفاده ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Miṣrī, resident of Mecca. He stayed there about twenty years with no fixed stipend, and did not beg; rather he was given to silence, night vigils, and seclusion, so that Muḥammad b. al-Shaykh ʿUmar al-ʿUrābī mentioned him in the biography of his father and related from his father that he used to say that he was one of the abdāl who saw the Prophet (God bless him and grant him peace) often, never speaking of this world, never laughing or looking about, and sitting only with the people of the hereafter. He died in (8)27. Ibn Fahd reported this."@en .

rec:AIND-D05891 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05891-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05891-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05891 ;
    aindv:sourceText "326 عمر بن عبد المؤمن بن عمر الزين الخليلي المقدسي الشافعي . ولد سنة تسع وثمانين وسبعمائة وروى عن الشهاب أحمد بن سعد الله الحراني ثم الآمدي الحنبلي والزين أبي الفضائل عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن شجاع الحراني ثم الرهوني الشافعي المعروف بابن الحلبية البخاري قالا أنا الحجار وذلك في سنة ست وخمسين وسبعمائة سمع منه أبو الفضل بن أبي اللطف وقال أنه عمر ومات في ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Muʾmin b. ʿUmar, al-Zayn al-Khalīlī al-Maqdisī al-Shāfiʿī. He was born in (7)89 and transmitted al-Bukhārī from al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. Saʿd Allāh al-Ḥarrānī then al-Āmidī al-Ḥanbalī and from al-Zayn Abū al-Faḍāʾil ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr b. Shujāʿ al-Ḥarrānī then al-Rahūnī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Ḥalabiyya; both said \"al-Ḥajjār informed us\", and that was in (7)56. Abū al-Faḍl b. Abī al-Luṭf heard from him and said that he lived to an old age. He died in ..."@en .

rec:AIND-D05892 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05892-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05892-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05892 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن الزين عبد الواحد بن عمر بن عياد المدني . هو ابن عبد العزيز بن عبد الواحد . مضى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. ʿUmar b. ʿIyād al-Madanī. He is (in fact) the son of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid. Mentioned above."@en .

rec:AIND-D05894 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05894-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05894-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05894 ;
    aindv:sourceText "328 عمر بن عثمان بن محمد الزين الحلبي الرأس عيني ويعرف بابن قصروه ، ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad, al-Zayn al-Ḥalabī al-Raʾs ʿAynī, known as Ibn Qaṣrūh. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05899 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05899-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05899-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05899-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05899 ;
    aindv:sourceText "334 عمر بن علي بن طالوت بن عبد الله بن سويد ركن الدين النابتي ثم الدمشقي ناظر البادرية بها كان بزي الجند . مات في ذي الحجة سنة ست ، قاله شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Ṭālūt b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Suwayd, Rukn al-Dīn al-Nābitī then al-Dimashqī, nāẓir of the Bādiriyya there. He dressed in the garb of the soldiery. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja (80)6; so said our shaykh in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05900 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05900-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05900-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05900 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن علي بن عبد اللطيف البرلسي . الماضي أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Burullusī. His father was mentioned above."@en .

rec:AIND-D05901 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05901-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05901-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05901 ;
    aindv:sourceText "335 عمر بن علي بن عبد الله الحمامي الصوفي . كان حارسا بالحمامات ثم صار يدولبها ، وأثرى مع جميل المحاضرة والصوت الشجي وخدمة الفقراء . مات في ربيع الآخر سنة إحدى عشرة . ذكره المقريزي في عقوده وأنه كان جاره وأورد عنه حكاية غريبة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥammāmī al-Ṣūfī. He was a guard at the bathhouses, then came to run them and grew wealthy, along with pleasant company, a touching voice, and service to the poor (Sufis). He died in Rabīʿ II (8)11. Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his ʿUqūd, said that he was his neighbour, and related a strange story about him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05902 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05902-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05902-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05902-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b106_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05902 ;
    aindv:sourceText "336 عمر بن علي بن عثمان بن عمر السراج بن العلاء بن الصيرفي الدمشقي الشافعي أحد نواب الشافعية بدمشق وفضلائها والماضي أبوه . ممن قدم القاهرة غير مرة ويعرف بابن الصيرفي ، درس بالشامية البرانية لكون التقي بن قاضي عجلون رغب له عن الثلث فيها وحج ومن شيوخه البدر بن قاضي شهبة بل لا يبعد أخذه عن أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. ʿUthmān b. ʿUmar, al-Sirāj b. al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Ṣayrafī, al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī, one of the Shāfiʿī deputy judges of Damascus and one of its distinguished men; his father was mentioned above. He was among those who came to Cairo more than once, and he was known as Ibn al-Ṣayrafī. He taught at al-Shāmiyya al-Barrāniyya because al-Taqī b. Qāḍī ʿAjlūn ceded to him a third of it, and he performed the pilgrimage. Among his teachers was al-Badr b. Qāḍī Shuhba, and it is not unlikely that he also studied with his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D05903 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05903-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05903-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05903-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05903 ;
    aindv:sourceText "337 عمر بن علي بن عثمان الزين بن العلاء الحواري المقدسي الشافعي الماضي أبوه . ولد سنة ثلاث وثمانمائة ، واستقر في جميع وظائف أبيه كالهكارية والبدرية واللؤلؤية والإعادة بالصلاحية . ومات في يوم الأربعاء عشري ربيع الأول سنة أربع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. ʿUthmān, al-Zayn b. al-ʿAlāʾ, al-Ḥawārī al-Maqdisī al-Shāfiʿī; his father was mentioned above. He was born in the year 803 and was installed in all of his father's posts, such as those at al-Hakkāriyya, al-Badriyya and al-Luʾluʾiyya, and the post of repetitor (iʿāda) at al-Ṣalāḥiyya. He died on Wednesday, 20 Rabīʿ al-Awwal 874."@en .

rec:AIND-D05904 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05904-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05904-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05904-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05904 ;
    aindv:sourceText "338 عمر بن علي بن عمر بن محمد بن قنان الرسعني الدمشقي المدني الشافعي . سمع مع أبيه وأخيه على الزين أبي بكر المراغي في سنة اثنتي عشرة ، وتعانى التجارة فكان يتردد بين الحرمين وغيرهما فيها إلى أن مات غريقا ببحر الهند إما في آخر سنة خمس وأربعين أو أول سنة ست ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Qinān al-Rasʿanī al-Dimashqī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī. He heard, together with his father and his brother, from al-Zayn Abū Bakr al-Marāghī in the year 812. He engaged in trade and for that purpose kept travelling between the Two Sanctuaries (Mecca and Medina) and other places, until he drowned in the Indian Ocean, either at the end of the year 845 or at the beginning of the year 846."@en .

rec:AIND-D05905 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05905-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05905-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05905-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05905 ;
    aindv:sourceText "339 عمر بن علي بن عمر السراج المناوي ثم القاهري الحنفي ويعرف بالمنيتيني . ممن لازم سيف الدين وكان قارئ الكشاف عنده في المنصورية وسمع على أمه وغيرها واشتغل كثيرا وفضل وناب في القضاء وجلس بالقرب من الجانبكية في القربيين ، وتنزل في بعض الجهات وأعطاه البرهان الكركي حين أخذه الأشرفية تدريس خشقدم بالأزهر ، وكان كثير المباحثة والمشي والتساهل ممتهنا لنفسه مزري الهيئة والشكل زائد الغفلة سليم الفطرة بحيث تنسب إليه قضايا . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة ثلاث وتسعين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar, al-Sirāj, al-Munāwī then al-Qāhirī, the Ḥanafī, known as al-Munaytīnī. He was among those who studied closely with Sayf al-Dīn and acted as the reader of the Kashshāf before him at al-Manṣūriyya. He heard from his mother (or: from the mother of Sayf al-Dīn) and others, studied extensively and excelled, served as deputy judge and held his sessions near al-Jānibakiyya in al-Qurabiyyīn. He obtained some stipendiary posts, and al-Burhān al-Karakī, when he took over al-Ashrafiyya, gave him the Khushqadam teaching post at al-Azhar. He was much given to disputation and to walking about, easygoing, self-abasing, shabby in appearance and figure, exceedingly absent-minded and simple by nature, so that various anecdotes are attributed to him. He died in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year 893; may God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05907 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05907-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05907-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05907 ;
    aindv:sourceText "341 عمر بن علي بن عمر الشامي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar al-Shāmī. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05908 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05908-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05908-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05908-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05908 ;
    aindv:sourceText "342 عمر بن علي بن عمر العبادي ثم الغمري ويعرف بالبواب . ممن نشأ في خدمة الشيخ الغمري ثم ولده أبي العباس وقطن معه في القاهرة وتردد لغيرها وتزوج وقتا وكان يحضر عندي في الإملاء مع تقلله وفاقته مات بعيد التسعين أو قبيلها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar al-ʿIbādī then al-Ghamrī, known as al-Bawwāb (the doorkeeper). He was among those who grew up in the service of the Shaykh al-Ghamrī and then of his son Abū al-ʿAbbās; he lived with him in Cairo, travelled to other places, and was married for a time. He used to attend my dictation sessions despite his poverty and want. He died shortly after (8)90 or shortly before it."@en .

rec:AIND-D05911 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05911-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05911-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05911-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05911 ;
    aindv:sourceText "345 عمر بن علي بن محمد بن علي بن خليل المصري الأصل المكي والد علي الماضي ويعرف بابن السيرجي خادم قبة الوحي ودار أم المؤمنين خديجة المعروفة بمولد السيدة فاطمة الزهراء بزقاق الحجر والماضي أبوه . ولد قبل الخمسين بمكة وقرأ علي بها الأربعين النووية وغيرها وسمع علي غير ذلك وكان في صغره قرأ القرآن والمنهاج أو بعضه ثم تشاغل عن ذلك . وقدم القاهرة وهو كثير التطور عديم التصور يذكر بين أهل مكة بأمور الله أعلم بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Khalīl, of Egyptian origin, the Meccan; father of the aforementioned ʿAlī, known as Ibn al-Sayrajī; servant (khādim) of the Dome of Revelation (Qubbat al-Waḥy) and of the house of the Mother of the Believers Khadīja, known as the birthplace of the Lady Fāṭima al-Zahrāʾ, in Zuqāq al-Ḥajar; his father was also mentioned above. He was born before (8)50 in Mecca, where he read to me al-Arbaʿīn al-Nawawiyya and other works and heard other things from me. In his childhood he had read the Qurʾān and the Minhāj, or part of it, but then turned away from that. He came to Cairo; he is extremely erratic and lacking in understanding, and is spoken of among the people of Mecca for matters of which God knows best."@en .

rec:AIND-D05912 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05912-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05912-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05912-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05912-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b107_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05912 ;
    aindv:sourceText "346 عمر بن علي بن أبي البركات محمد بن أبي السعود محمد بن حسين بن علي ابن أحمد ابن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي المكي أخو إبراهيم وأبي بكر وإخوتهما وأمهم أم الخير ابنة القاضي عز الدين النويري . ولد توأما مع أخيه أبي بكر في ليلة هلال رجب سنة ثمان وثلاثين وثمانمائة وأجاز له جماعة ، ولم يلبث أن مات في رجب سنة أربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Abī al-Barakāt Muḥammad b. Abī al-Suʿūd Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī al-Makkī, brother of Ibrāhīm, Abū Bakr and their siblings; their mother was Umm al-Khayr, daughter of the qāḍī ʿIzz al-Dīn al-Nuwayrī. He was born as a twin with his brother Abū Bakr on the night of the new moon of Rajab in the year 838, and a group of scholars granted him ijāza; but he did not live long and died in Rajab of the year (8)40."@en .

rec:AIND-D05913 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05913-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05913-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05913 ;
    aindv:sourceText "347 عمر بن علي بن محمد سراج الدين القليوبي ثم القاهري التاجر أحد صوفية سعيد السعداء . مات في ربيع الثاني سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad, Sirāj al-Dīn, al-Qalyūbī then al-Qāhirī, the merchant, one of the Sufis of (the khānqāh of) Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. He died in Rabīʿ al-Thānī of the year 891."@en .

rec:AIND-D05914 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05914-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05914-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05914 ;
    aindv:sourceText "348 عمر بن علي المغربي السعودي نقيب الفقراء ويعرف بجريدة . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة سبع وستين . أرخه ابن المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī al-Maghribī al-Saʿūdī, naqīb of the fuqarāʾ (Sufi mendicants), known as Jarīda. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year 867. Ibn al-Munīr recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D05915 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05915-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05915-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05915 ;
    aindv:sourceText "349 عمر بن علي الشجاع القباطي . مات سنة اثنتين وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿAlī, al-Shujāʿ, al-Qabāṭī. He died in the year (8)22."@en .

rec:AIND-D05917 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05917-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05917-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05917 ;
    aindv:sourceText "351 عمر بن عمر بن عثمان الزين بن التاجر السراج بن الفخر بن الجندي الماضي أبوه . مات سنة تسع وثمانين ولم يلبث أن مات ابنه ووضع السلطان يده على تركته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿUmar b. ʿUthmān, al-Zayn b. al-Tājir (the merchant) al-Sirāj b. al-Fakhr, Ibn al-Jundī; his father was mentioned above. He died in the year (8)89, and shortly afterwards his son died too, and the Sultan laid his hand on his estate."@en .

rec:AIND-D05920 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05920-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05920-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05920-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05920 ;
    aindv:sourceText "354 عمر بن عيسى بن عمر السمنودي الشافعي والد عبد الرحمن الماضي . كان فقيها ذا معرفة بالفرائض والميقات مع الصلاح والزهد مذكورا بالكرامات وشريف الخصال انتفع به أهل تلك النواحي كالعز عبد العزيز بن عبد الواحد المناوي فإنه أخذ عنه الفقه والفرائض والميقات بل كان جل انتفاعه به وكذا لقيه الكمال إمام الكاملية صحبة والده والجمال يوسف الصفي فلقنه : %~% يا أيها الراضي بأحكامنا %~% لا بد أن تحمد عقبى الرضا %~% %~% فوض إلينا وابق مستسلما %~% فالراحة العظمى لمن فوضا %~% %~% وإن تعلقت بأسبابنا %~% فلا تكن عن بابنا معرضا %~% %~% فإن فينا خلقا باقيا %~% من كل ما يأتي وما قد مضى %~% %~% لا ينعم المرء بمحبوبه %~% حتى يرى الخيرة فيما قضى %~% مات سنة سبع وعشرين وقد جاز المائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. ʿĪsā b. ʿUmar al-Samannūdī al-Shāfiʿī, father of the aforementioned ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. He was a jurist with knowledge of inheritance law (farāʾiḍ) and timekeeping (mīqāt), combined with piety and asceticism, spoken of for his miracles (karāmāt) and noble qualities. The people of those parts benefited from him, such as al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Manāwī, who took from him jurisprudence, inheritance law and timekeeping; indeed the greater part of his benefit came from him. Likewise al-Kamāl, the imām of al-Kāmiliyya, met him in the company of his father, as did al-Jamāl Yūsuf al-Ṣafī, to whom he dictated: \"O you who are content with Our decrees, you will surely praise the outcome of contentment. / Entrust (your affairs) to Us and remain submissive, for the greatest ease belongs to the one who entrusts. / And if you cling to Our means, do not turn away from Our door. / For in Us there is an everlasting creation (encompassing) all that comes and all that has passed. / A man does not enjoy his beloved until he sees the good in what has been decreed.\" He died in the year (8)27, having passed a hundred years."@en .

rec:AIND-D05921 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05921-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05921-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05921 ;
    aindv:sourceText "355 عمر بن قاسم بن جمعة الأمير زين الدين القساسي الحلبي نائب قلعتها والآتي أبوه . مات بها في شعبان سنة أربع وستين ، واستقر بعده في النيابة ابن جبارة نائب البيرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Qāsim b. Jumʿa, the amīr Zayn al-Dīn al-Qassāsī al-Ḥalabī, deputy (nāʾib) of the citadel of Aleppo; his father is mentioned below. He died there in Shaʿbān of the year 864, and after him Ibn Jubāra, the deputy of al-Bīra, was installed in the deputyship."@en .

rec:AIND-D05922 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05922-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05922-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05922-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05922 ;
    aindv:sourceText "356 عمر بن قاسم الأنصاري المصري الشافعي المقرئ ويعرف بالنشار حرفة له كانت . وتلا بالسبع على علي الخباز الضرير ثم الشمس بن الحمصاني والسيد الطباطبي وعلى الديروطي وابن عمران وابن أسد ولكنه لم يكمل على الثلاثة الأخيرين وأجازوا له ، وتصدى لإقراء الأطفال بمصر مدة وانتفع به جماعة وممن قرأ عنده الشهاب القسطلاني والنور الجارحي بل أخذ عنه القراءات وهو إنسان خير بارع فيها يحفظ الشاطبية ، ويميل للجلال بن الأسيوطي لقربه من نواحيه لأنه أمام مدرسة قانم بالكبش ولذا وصفه الشيخ العالم الفاضل شيخ القراء ، قد حج وجاور غير مرة وكذا زار بيت المقدس والخليل مرارا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Qāsim al-Anṣārī al-Miṣrī al-Shāfiʿī, the Qurʾān reciter, known as al-Nashshār (the sawyer), after a trade he once practised. He recited the seven readings to ʿAlī al-Khabbāz al-Ḍarīr, then to al-Shams b. al-Ḥimṣānī and al-Sayyid al-Ṭabāṭabī, and also to al-Dayrūṭī, Ibn ʿImrān and Ibn Asad, though he did not complete (the recitation) with the last three, and they granted him ijāza. He devoted himself for a time to teaching children to recite in Miṣr, and a number of people benefited from him; among those who recited before him were al-Shihāb al-Qasṭallānī and al-Nūr al-Jāriḥī, who indeed took the readings from him. He is a good man, accomplished in the readings, and knows al-Shāṭibiyya by heart. He is attached to al-Jalāl b. al-Asyūṭī because of the proximity of his quarters, for he is the imām of the madrasa of Qānim at al-Kabsh; and for this reason (al-Suyūṭī) described him as \"the shaykh, the learned, the virtuous, the shaykh of the reciters\". He has performed the pilgrimage and resided (in Mecca) more than once, and likewise visited Jerusalem and Hebron several times."@en .

rec:AIND-D05923 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05923-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05923-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05923-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05923-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D05923-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b107_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05923 ;
    aindv:sourceText "357 عمر بن أبي القسم بن معيبد القاضي تقي الدين اليمني التعزي . ذكره العفيف عثمان الناشري في أثناء كلام وقال أنه صاحب الفضل الشهير والأدب الكثير كتب إلى عمي يثني على دروسي لما وردت عليه تعز فكتبت إليه : %~% ألم تر أن الكون والصمت طبعه %~% يقول أين عثمان من عمر %~% %~% وأين السها يا صاحبي في غموضه %~% من الزهرة الزهراء والشمس والقمر %~% قال : وكنت اجتمعت به في سنة ثمان وعشرين بزبيد وحصل لي منظومة في مشايخ شيخنا ابن الجزري ووزر في الدولة الظاهرية وكان مع ذلك يكابد العبادات ولا يفتر من الطاعات ، وتوفي بمدينة تعز آخر سنة سبع وثلاثين وحضرت دفنه انتهى ، وأظنه ابن عم عمر بن محمد بن معيبد الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī al-Qāsim b. Muʿaybid, the qāḍī Taqī al-Dīn al-Yamanī al-Taʿizzī. Al-ʿAfīf ʿUthmān al-Nāshirī mentioned him in the course of a discussion and said that he was a man of celebrated merit and abundant literary culture: \"He wrote to my uncle praising my lessons when I came to him at Taʿizz, so I wrote to him: 'Do you not see that existence, whose nature is silence, says: where is ʿUthmān beside ʿUmar? And where, my friend, is al-Suhā in its faintness beside the radiant Venus, the sun and the moon?'\" He (al-Nāshirī) said: \"I had met him in the year (8)28 at Zabīd, and he obtained for me a versified work on the teachers of our shaykh Ibn al-Jazarī. He served as vizier under the Ẓāhirī regime, and withal he toiled in acts of worship and never slackened in acts of obedience. He died in the city of Taʿizz at the end of the year (8)37, and I attended his burial.\" End of quotation. I think he is the paternal cousin of ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Muʿaybid, mentioned below."@en .

rec:AIND-D05924 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05924-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05924-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05924 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن قايماز في ابن قيماز قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Qāymāz: see under Ibn Qaymāz, shortly below."@en .

rec:AIND-D05926 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05926-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05926-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05926 ;
    aindv:sourceText "359 عمر بن قيماز ركن الدين أبو حفص بن الأمير سيف الدين . ولد بالقاهرة وخدم جماعة من أعيان الأمراء وباشر وظائف كثيرة منها استادارية السلطان مرارا ولم ينتج أمره ، مات في يوم الاثنين مستهل رجب سنة تسع . ذكره العيني وغيره ، زاد المقريزي بحلب وهو صاحب السبيل والتربة تجاه خليج الزعفران المعروف بسبيل ابن قيماز . )"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Qaymāz, Rukn al-Dīn Abū Ḥafṣ, son of the amīr Sayf al-Dīn. He was born in Cairo, served a number of leading amirs and held many offices, among them the post of ustādār of the Sultan several times, but his affairs did not prosper. He died on Monday, the first of Rajab of the year (80)9. Al-ʿAynī and others mentioned him; al-Maqrīzī added \"in Aleppo\", and that he was the founder of the sabīl (public fountain) and the turba (mausoleum) facing the Khalīj al-Zaʿfarān, known as the Sabīl of Ibn Qaymāz."@en .

rec:AIND-D05928 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05928-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05928-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05928 ;
    aindv:sourceText "361 عمر بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن عباس الزين المرداوي المقدسي الصالحي ، سمع في سنة ثلاث وتسعين على الزين عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن الرشيد نسخة أبي مسهر وما معها وعلى عبد الله بن خليل الحرستاني النصف الثاني من الأول من مسند عمار ليعقوب بن شيبة وغيره ، وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء أجاز لي في سنة اثنتين وخمسين ، ومات بعد ذلك رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbbās, al-Zayn, al-Mardāwī al-Maqdisī al-Ṣāliḥī. In the year (7)93 he heard from al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. al-Rashīd the Nuskha of Abū Mushir and what goes with it, and from ʿAbd Allāh b. Khalīl al-Ḥarastānī the second half of the first part of the Musnad of ʿAmmār by Yaʿqūb b. Shayba, and other things. He transmitted ḥadīth, and learned men heard from him. He granted me ijāza in the year (8)52 and died after that; may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05929 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05929-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05929-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05929-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05929 ;
    aindv:sourceText "361 عمر بن محمد بن إبراهيم بن علي السراج بن الكمال الأبياري السكندري الضرير الفقيه . سمع في سنة خمس وأربعين وسبعمائة على علي بن عبد الوهاب ابن الفرات منتقى من جزء عمرو بن زرارة اشتمل على خمسة أحاديث ومن ابن البوري جامع الترمذي بفوت ومن الفخر محمد بن محمد بن سليمان بن خير الدعاء للمحاملي في آخرين وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء كابن موسى والموفق الأبي وأجاز لابن شيخنا وابن فهد وذكره في معجمه وآخرين في سنة خمس عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī, al-Sirāj b. al-Kamāl, al-Abyārī al-Sakandarī, the blind jurist. In the year 745 he heard from ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb Ibn al-Furāt a selection from the Juzʾ of ʿAmr b. Zurāra comprising five ḥadīths, from Ibn al-Būrī the Jāmiʿ of al-Tirmidhī (with a lacuna), and from al-Fakhr Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Sulaymān b. Khayr the Duʿāʾ of al-Muḥāmilī, among others. He transmitted ḥadīth, and learned men such as Ibn Mūsā and al-Muwaffaq al-Ubbī heard from him. In the year (8)15 he granted ijāza to the son of our shaykh, to Ibn Fahd, who mentioned him in his Muʿjam, and to others."@en .

rec:AIND-D05930 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05930-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05930-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b107_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05930 ;
    aindv:sourceText "363 عمر بن محمد بن إبراهيم السراج الشامي القاهري الكتبي والد محمد ويعرف بالشامي . ولد سنة سبع أو ثمان وأربعين وسبعمائة ، وذكر أنه سمع من العفيف النشاوري الصحيحين وغيرهما واستكتبه الطلبة في الاستدعاءات وكان خيرا يتكسب بصناعة التجليد ويخدم شيخنا في ذلك مع أنه لم يكن بالماهر في صناعته ووقع له أنه رأى أجزاء علي بن حجر في السوق فاشتراها وأحضر بها لشيخنا وقال له : قد وقع لي تصنيف لأبيكم فاشتريته فأخذه ولم يخجله فأبو هذا حجر بضم المهملة وسكون الجيم وشهرة شيخنا ابن حجر بفتحتين . مات بالقاهرة سنة ثلاث أو أربع وأربعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm, al-Sirāj, al-Shāmī al-Qāhirī al-Kutubī (the bookseller), father of Muḥammad, known as al-Shāmī. He was born in the year 747 or 748. He stated that he had heard the two Ṣaḥīḥs and other works from al-ʿAfīf al-Nashāwarī. Students had him write out their petitions (istidʿāʾāt). He was a good man who earned his living by the craft of bookbinding and served our shaykh in that, although he was not skilled in his craft. It happened that he saw some fascicles of ʿAlī b. Ḥujr in the market, bought them and brought them to our shaykh, saying: \"I have come across a work by your father, so I bought it.\" He took it from him and did not embarrass him; for the father of this (ʿAlī) is Ḥujr, with ḍamma on the ḥāʾ and sukūn on the jīm, whereas the well-known name of our shaykh, Ibn Ḥajar, has two fatḥas. He died in Cairo in the year (8)43 or 44; may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05931 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05931-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05931-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05931 ;
    aindv:sourceText "364 عمر بن محمد بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز الدمشقي الأصل المكي المولد والدار شيخ الفراشين بها والآتي أبوه ويعرف بابن بيسق . ولد في سنة اثنتين وأربعين وثمانمائة بمكة ونشأ بها وخلف والده في المشيخة المشار إليها ولازم خدمة البرهاني القاضي حيث دخل معه القاهرة حين خطبه الأشرف قايتباي للقدوم عليه وكذا زار معه المدينة النبوية بل زارها غير مرة ، ولا بأس به أدبا مع الغرباء وقياما بوظيفته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, of Damascene origin, born and resident in Mecca, chief of the farrāshūn (attendants of the Sacred Mosque) there; his father is mentioned below. He is known as Ibn Baysaq. He was born in the year 842 in Mecca, grew up there and succeeded his father in the aforementioned office. He attended constantly on the qāḍī al-Burhānī, in whose company he entered Cairo when al-Ashraf Qāytbāy summoned him (al-Burhānī) to come to him; likewise he visited the Prophet's Medina with him, and indeed visited it more than once. There is nothing to be said against him as regards his courtesy towards strangers and the performance of his duties."@en .

rec:AIND-D05932 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05932-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05932-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05932-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05932 ;
    aindv:sourceText "365 عمر بن محمد بن أحمد بن عبد الهادي بن عبد الحميد الزين بن الحافظ الشمس المقدسي ثم الصالحي الحنبلي ابن أخت فاطمة ابنة محمد بن عبد الهادي ويعرف بابن عبد الهادي . ولد في ذي القعدة سنة تسع وثلاثين وسبعمائة وأحضر على زينب ابنة الكمال مجلس الروياني وغيره ، وأسمع على أحمد بن علي الجزري وعبد الرحيم بن أبي اليسر ، وحدث قرأ عليه شيخنا وغيره وذكره المقريزي في عقوده . ومات بدمشق في الكائنة العظمى في شعبان سنة ثلاث ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Hādī b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd, al-Zayn b. al-Ḥāfiẓ al-Shams, al-Maqdisī, then al-Ṣāliḥī, the Ḥanbalī, son of the sister of Fāṭima bint Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Hādī, known as Ibn ʿAbd al-Hādī. He was born in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year 739. He was brought as a child to hear the Majlis al-Rūyānī and other works before Zaynab bint al-Kamāl, and was made to hear from Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Jazarī and ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Abī al-Yasar. He transmitted ḥadīth; our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others read to him. Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his ʿUqūd. He died in Damascus during the great calamity (Tīmūr's siege), in Shaʿbān of the year (80)3."@en .

rec:AIND-D05933 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05933-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05933-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05933-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05933-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05933 ;
    aindv:sourceText "366 عمر بن محمد بن أحمد بن علي بن الحسن بن جامع السراج بن الشمس أبا المعالي الدمشقي المقري ويعرف بابن اللبان . أخذ القراءات عن والده وتلا بالعشر على الشمس العسقلاني فيما أفاده ابن الجزري وتصدر للإقراء وكان ساكنا سليم الباطن عالية في الشطرنج . مات في شعبان سنة ثلاثين عن نحو ثمانين سنة . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه وأورده في معجمه باختصار وقال أنه سمع صحيح مسلم على أحمد بن عبد الكريم البعلي أجاز لنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. al-Ḥasan b. Jāmiʿ, al-Sirāj b. al-Shams Abū al-Maʿālī, al-Dimashqī, the Qurʾān reciter, known as Ibn al-Labbān. He took the readings from his father and recited according to the ten readings to al-Shams al-ʿAsqalānī, as Ibn al-Jazarī reports. He presided over the teaching of recitation; he was calm and pure of heart, and excelled at chess. He died in Shaʿbān of the year (8)30, aged about eighty. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ and included him briefly in his Muʿjam, saying that he heard Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim from Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Baʿlī. He granted us (Ibn Ḥajar) an ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D05937 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05937-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05937-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05937 ;
    aindv:sourceText "370 عمر بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد أبو حفص التميمي الداري التونسي والد الشمس محمد نزيل مكة ويعرف بابن عزم . أرخ ابنه موته بليلة الخميس حادي عشر ذي القعدة سنة ست وأربعين بتونس ووصفه بالعلامة مع أنه كان مجلدا موقتا بارعا في ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad, Abū Ḥafṣ al-Tamīmī al-Dārī al-Tūnisī, father of al-Shams Muḥammad, the resident of Mecca; he is known as Ibn ʿAzm. His son dated his death to the night of Thursday, 11 Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year (8)46, in Tunis, and described him as \"the great scholar\" (al-ʿallāma), although he was a bookbinder and a timekeeper (muwaqqit), skilled in that."@en .

rec:AIND-D05938 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05938-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05938-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05938-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05938 ;
    aindv:sourceText "371 عمر بن محمد بن أحمد الحوراني ثم المكي التاجر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Ḥawrānī, then al-Makkī, the merchant."@en .

rec:AIND-D05939 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05939-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05939-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05939-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05939 ;
    aindv:sourceText "372 عمر بن أبي بكر محمد بن أحمد السكندري ثم القاهري دوادار شيخنا . سمع من لفظه على الشمس البيجوري جزء الدمياطي وسمع على غيره ولم يكن شيخنا يحمد خدمته ولذا لم يحصل بعده على طائل وكان عاميا أجاز لنا . ومات في رجب سنة ثلاث وستين وأظنه جاز الستين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Sakandarī, then al-Qāhirī, the dawādār of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar). He heard the Juzʾ al-Dimyāṭī from al-Shams al-Bījūrī as read aloud by him (our shaykh), and heard from others as well. Our shaykh did not praise his service, and therefore he obtained nothing of consequence after him. He was an ordinary layman. He granted us an ijāza. He died in Rajab of the year (8)63; I think he had passed sixty. May God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05940 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05940-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05940-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05940-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05940 ;
    aindv:sourceText "373 عمر بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن إسماعيل السراج بن الخواجا الشمس بن النحاس الدمشقي . ممن نبغ في التجارة وجاور بمكة مرارا بسببها فقدرت وفاته بها في جمادى الأولى سنة إحدى وستين وفجع به أبوه . أرخه ابن فهد"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. Ismāʿīl, al-Sirāj b. al-Khawājā al-Shams b. al-Naḥḥās, al-Dimashqī. He was among those who distinguished themselves in trade, and sojourned in Mecca repeatedly on its account. It was so decreed that he died there in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year (8)61, and his father was stricken by his loss. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05941 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05941-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05941-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05941-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05941 ;
    aindv:sourceText "374 عمر بن أبي سعيد محمد بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية ابن ظهيرة القرشي وأمه زبيدية . أجاز لنا في سنة ست وثلاثين جماعة وبيض له ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī Saʿīd Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓahīra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya, Ibn Ẓahīra, al-Qurashī; his mother was a woman of Zabīd. He granted us an ijāza, together with a group, in the year (8)36. Ibn Fahd left his entry blank."@en .

rec:AIND-D05942 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05942-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05942-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05942 ;
    aindv:sourceText "375 عمر بن محمد أبي بكر بن علي بن يوسف الأنصاري الذروي الأصل المكي الزبيدي ويعرف بابن الجمال المصري ويلقب بالشجاع عني بالعلم قليلا وبالتجارة وسافر لأجلها إلى بلاد شتى وتردد منها لمكة وللحج غير مرة منها في سنة موته وكان ينسخ وليس بخطه بأس واتفق أنه أودع شيئا من دنياه مع بعض المسافرين فغرق فعظم أسفه وتعلل لأجله حتى مات في ذي الحجة سنة ثلاث وعشرين بمكة ودفن بالمعلاة وهو في عشر الأربعين أو بلغها . ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf al-Anṣārī, of Dharwa origin, al-Makkī al-Zabīdī, known as Ibn al-Jamāl al-Miṣrī and nicknamed al-Shujāʿ (the Brave). He attended a little to learning and (more) to trade, on account of which he travelled to various lands, returning repeatedly from them to Mecca and performing the pilgrimage more than once, including in the year of his death. He used to copy books, and his handwriting was not bad. It happened that he entrusted some of his worldly goods to certain travellers, who drowned; his grief was great and he fell ill because of it until he died in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year (8)23 in Mecca, and was buried in al-Maʿlāt. He was in his thirties, or had reached forty. Al-Fāsī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05943 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05943-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05943-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05943 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن علي بن يوسف المرشدي المكي . يأتي فيمن لم يسم جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf al-Murshidī al-Makkī. He will be mentioned below among those whose grandfather is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D05944 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05944-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05944-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05944-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05944 ;
    aindv:sourceText "376 عمر بن محمد المدعو مظفر بن أبي بكر التركماني الأصل القاهري الحنبلي المقري أخو أحمد الماضي والآتي والدهما ويعرف بابن المظفر . قرأ على أبيه وغيره غالب الروايات ، وكانت بيده وظائف فتنزل في صوفية الأشرفية الحنابلة من الواقف وفي خانقاه يشبك وغيرهما ، وأخذ عنه التاج عبد الوهاب بن شرف ورام أخذ الأشرفية بعده فلم يتمكن لكونه شافعيا مات قريب الستين إما قبلها وإما بعدها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad — (the father) called Muẓaffar — b. Abī Bakr, of Turkmen origin, al-Qāhirī, the Ḥanbalī, the Qurʾān reciter, brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad; their father is mentioned below. He is known as Ibn al-Muẓaffar. He read most of the transmissions (of the readings) with his father and others. He held several posts: he was appointed by the founder himself among the Ḥanbalī Sufis of al-Ashrafiyya, and (also held posts) in the Khānqāh of Yashbak and elsewhere. Al-Tāj ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. Sharaf studied under him and wished to obtain the Ashrafiyya (post) after him, but could not, since he was a Shāfiʿī. He died around (8)60, either shortly before or after it."@en .

rec:AIND-D05946 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05946-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05946-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05946-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05946 ;
    aindv:sourceText "378 عمر بن محمد بن تغلب بن علي بن محمود الزين أبو حفص الزهري القيمري البيري الحلبي الشافعي الحكيم . ممن تعانى الأدب ونظم قصيدة في علم العروض وكتب عنه العز بن فهد في سنة إحدى وسبعين قوله : %~% أحب ابن ناس ولا أشتهي %~% أرى امرأة في دياري تلوح %~% %~% لأني إذا شئت فارقته %~% وهي لا تفارقني عمر نوح %~% وغير ذلك مما أودعته في محل آخر ، ومات بعد ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Taghlib b. ʿAlī b. Maḥmūd, al-Zayn Abū Ḥafṣ al-Zuhrī al-Qaymarī al-Bīrī al-Ḥalabī, the Shāfiʿī, the physician (al-ḥakīm). He was among those who engaged in literature, and composed a qaṣīda on the science of prosody. Al-ʿIzz b. Fahd wrote down from him, in the year (8)71, his verses: \"I love a son of men (a youth), and do not wish to see a woman appearing in my dwelling; / for if I wish I can part from him, whereas she would not leave me for the lifetime of Noah.\" (He also composed) other things that I have placed elsewhere. He died after that."@en .

rec:AIND-D05947 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05947-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05947-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05947-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05947 ;
    aindv:sourceText "379 عمر بن محمد بن حسن بن شعبان بن أبي بكر الباعوري الأصل الحلبي الآتي أبوه ويعرف بابن الصوة . أحضره السلطان بعد قتل أبيه وسأله في الوكالة عنه بالبلاد الحلبية فاستعفى وأقام بعد رجوعه على وجاهته حتى مات في شعبان سنة ست وثمانين ، وكانت عمامته مدورة دون إخوته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Shaʿbān b. Abī Bakr, of Bāʿūr origin, al-Ḥalabī; his father is mentioned below, and he is known as Ibn al-Ṣawwa. After his father was killed, the Sultan summoned him and asked him to act as his (the Sultan's) agent (wakāla) in the Aleppo region, but he asked to be excused. After his return he remained in his position of prestige until he died in Shaʿbān of the year (8)86. His turban was round, unlike those of his brothers."@en .

rec:AIND-D05948 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05948-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05948-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05948 ;
    aindv:sourceText "380 عمر بن محمد بن حسن الزين الدمشقي ويعرف بابن الزين . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan, al-Zayn al-Dimashqī, known as Ibn al-Zayn. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D05950 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05950-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05950-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05950-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05950 ;
    aindv:sourceText "382 عمر بن محمد بن الشيخ حسين بن حسن الفتحي المكي الآتي أبوه . ولد في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى وتسعين وثمانمائة بمكة وسمع بها مع أبيه وعمه علي أنشأه الله صالحا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. al-Shaykh Ḥusayn b. Ḥasan al-Fatḥī al-Makkī; his father is mentioned below. He was born in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year 891 in Mecca, and heard from me there together with his father and his paternal uncle. May God raise him up righteous."@en .

rec:AIND-D05951 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05951-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05951-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05951-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b104_108_triage,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05951 ;
    aindv:sourceText "383 عمر بن محمد بن سعيد الزين البعلي الحنبلي القطان ويعرف بابن البقسماطي . ولد في سنة ثمان وثمانين وسبعمائة ببعلبك ونشأ بها فقرأ القرآن عند طلحة العنبري وحفظ الخرقي وعرضه على ابن الأقرب والتقي إبراهيم بن مفلح وغيرهما واشتغل في الفقه على الأول وسمع على أبي الفرج عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن الزعبوب ختم الصحيح وحدث به قرأته عليه ببعلبك ، وكان إنسانا حسنا يتكسب فيها ببيع القطن . مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Saʿīd, al-Zayn al-Baʿlī, the Ḥanbalī, the cotton merchant, known as Ibn al-Baqsamāṭī. He was born in the year 788 in Baalbek and grew up there. He read the Qurʾān with Ṭalḥa al-ʿAnbarī, memorised al-Khiraqī (the Mukhtaṣar) and presented it to Ibn al-Aqrab, al-Taqī Ibrāhīm b. Mufliḥ and others, and studied jurisprudence with the former. He heard the conclusion of the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Faraj ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. al-Zaʿbūb and transmitted it; I read it to him in Baalbek. He was a good man who earned his living there by selling cotton. He died."@en .

rec:AIND-D05952 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05952-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05952-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05952 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن محمد بن سليمان الزين بن الصابوني الدمشقي . يأتي فيمن جده محمد بن سليمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Sulaymān, al-Zayn b. al-Ṣābūnī, al-Dimashqī. He will be mentioned below among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Sulaymān."@en .

rec:AIND-D05953 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05953-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05953-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05953 ;
    aindv:sourceText "384 عمر بن النجار محمد بن سليمان المكي . أحد القائمين بخدمة شافعيها ثم انقطع ولزم ولده وله حذق وسرعة وحركة ، وله عم اسمه علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Najjār (the carpenter) Muḥammad b. Sulaymān al-Makkī. He was one of those who served the Shāfiʿī (qāḍī) of Mecca, then withdrew and attached himself to his (the qāḍī's) son. He has cleverness, quickness and energy. He has a paternal uncle named ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D05954 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05954-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05954-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05954 ;
    aindv:sourceText "385 عمر بن محمد بن صلح البريهي اليماني الفقيه : مات في سنة عشر بذي السفال ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Ṣulḥ al-Burayhī al-Yamānī, the jurist (faqīh). He died in the year (8)10 in Dhī al-Sufāl."@en .

rec:AIND-D05955 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05955-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05955-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b108_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05955 ;
    aindv:sourceText "386 عمر بن محمد بن عبد الكريم القرشي . رأيته كتب لمن عرض عليه سنة اثنتين وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Qurashī. I saw that he had written (an attestation) for someone who presented (his memorised texts) to him in the year 802."@en .

rec:AIND-D05956 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05956-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05956-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05956 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن محمد بن عبد الله القلشاني المغربي . يأتي فيمن لم يسم جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Qalshānī al-Maghribī. He will come below among those whose grandfather is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D05957 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05957-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05957-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05957 ;
    aindv:sourceText "387 عمر بن محمد بن عبد الوهاب بن عبد الله بن أسعد السراج اليافعي المكي الآتي أبوه والماضي جده . ولد في ذي القعدة سنة أربع وثلاثين وثمانمائة بعدن ، وقدم مكة وقرأ القرآن وكتب الخط الحسن ، ومات بها في جمادى الثانية سنة أربع وستين . أرخه ابن الفهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Asʿad, al-Sirāj al-Yāfiʿī al-Makkī; his father is mentioned below and his grandfather above. He was born in Dhū al-Qaʿda 834 in Aden, came to Mecca, read the Qurʾān and wrote a fine hand. He died there in Jumādā II (8)64. Ibn al-Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D05958 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05958-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05958-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05958 ;
    aindv:sourceText "388 عمر بن محمد بن عثمان السراج الحسباني . مذكور بالجلالة ووصفه أبو السعادات البلقيني بالشيخ الإمام وأن المترجم طاف به أسبوعا سنة خمس وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān, al-Sirāj al-Ḥusbānī. He is mentioned as a man of dignity. Abū al-Saʿādāt al-Bulqīnī described him as \"the shaykh, the imām\" and stated that the subject carried him around in a full circuit (usbūʿ) of ṭawāf in the year (8)25."@en .

rec:AIND-D05962 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05962-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05962-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05962 ;
    aindv:sourceText "392 عمر بن محمد بن علي بن يوسف بن الحسن السراج بن المحب الأنصاري الزرندي المدني أخو عبد الوهاب ومحمد . أحضر في الرابعة على الجمال الأميوطي ثم سمع على الزين المراغي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. al-Ḥasan, al-Sirāj b. al-Muḥibb al-Anṣārī al-Zarandī al-Madanī, brother of ʿAbd al-Wahhāb and Muḥammad. He was brought at the age of four to hear from al-Jamāl al-Amyūṭī, and then heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī."@en .

rec:AIND-D05963 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05963-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05963-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05963 ;
    aindv:sourceText "393 عمر بن محمد بن علي السراج الحميري الدندري . ذكره شيخنا في معجمه فقال : اشتغل بالعلم وسمع العز بن جماعة وغيره وكتب الكثير بخطه لقيته بمجلس شيخنا ابن الملقن وأجاز لي . مات فيما أحسب سنة أربع ، وذكره المقريزي في عقوده وقال أنه مات عن سن عالية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, al-Sirāj al-Ḥimyarī al-Dandarī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Muʿjam and said: \"He occupied himself with learning, heard from al-ʿIzz b. Jamāʿa and others, and wrote much in his own hand. I met him at the session of our shaykh Ibn al-Mulaqqin and he gave me an ijāza. He died, as I reckon, in the year (80)4.\" Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his ʿUqūd and said that he died at an advanced age."@en .

rec:AIND-D05964 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05964-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05964-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05964-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05964 ;
    aindv:sourceText "394 عمر بن محمد بن عمر بن أحمد بن المبارك الزين بن الكمال بن الزين الحموي الشافعي الماضي جده والآتي أبوه ويعرف كسلفه بابن الخرزي بمعجمتين مات بعد أبيه بأشهر في سنة ثلاث وتسعين عن بضع وثلاثين وقيل لي أنه لم يكن بذاك عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. Aḥmad b. al-Mubārak, al-Zayn b. al-Kamāl b. al-Zayn al-Ḥamawī al-Shāfiʿī; his grandfather was mentioned above and his father comes below. He was known, like his forebears, as Ibn al-Kharazī (with two dotted letters). He died a few months after his father in the year (8)93, aged thirty-odd. I was told that he was of no great account; may God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05965 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05965-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05965-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05965 ;
    aindv:sourceText "395 عمر بن محمد بن عمر بن الرضي أبي بكر بن عبد اللطيف بن سالم المكي الآتي أبوه . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. al-Raḍī Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Sālim al-Makkī; his father comes below. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D05968 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05968-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05968-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05968 ;
    aindv:sourceText "398 عمر بن محمد بن عمر بن محمد بن مسعود العرابي المكي الآتي أبوه وجده . مات بها في صفر سنة ثمانين ودفن بتربة جده من المعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Masʿūd al-ʿUrābī al-Makkī; his father and grandfather come below. He died there in Ṣafar (8)80 and was buried in his grandfather's tomb at al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D05969 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05969-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05969-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05969 ;
    aindv:sourceText "399 عمر بن محمد بن عمر الزين أبو حفص الدمشقي الشافعي نزيل السبعة ويعرف بابن الخردفوشي . ولد في سنة ثمان وسبعين وسبعمائة وسمع على الشهاب أحمد بن علي بن يحيى الحسيني وابن صديق مسند الدارمي وعلى عبد الله بن خليل الحرستاني وأبي حفص عمر البالسي وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء . مات في يوم السبت ثاني عشر صفر سنة أربعين ودفن من يومه بمقبرة باب توما رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar, al-Zayn Abū Ḥafṣ al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī, resident of al-Sabʿa, known as Ibn al-Khardafūshī. He was born in the year 778. He heard the Musnad of al-Dārimī from al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Yaḥyā al-Ḥusaynī and Ibn Ṣiddīq, and heard from ʿAbd Allāh b. Khalīl al-Ḥarastānī and Abū Ḥafṣ ʿUmar al-Bālisī. He transmitted ḥadīth, and learned men heard from him. He died on Saturday 12 Ṣafar (8)40 and was buried the same day in the cemetery of Bāb Tūmā; may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05970 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05970-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05970-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05970-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05970 ;
    aindv:sourceText "400 عمر بن محمد بن عمر البلخي الأصل المحلي المالكي الحداد الأديب . ولد تقريبا سنة ثلاثين وثمانمائة وحفظ بعض القرآن وجميع العمدة وعرض على شيخنا وغيره نبذة من المختصر للشيخ خليل وغيره ولكنه لم يشتغل بل هو عامي يتعاطى نظم الشعر كتبت عنه منه بالمحلة ما أودعته في المعجم وغيره ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar, of Balkhī origin, al-Maḥallī al-Mālikī, the blacksmith, the man of letters. He was born around the year 830, memorized part of the Qurʾān and the whole of al-ʿUmda, and presented to our shaykh and others a selection from the Mukhtaṣar of al-Shaykh Khalīl and other works. He did not, however, pursue study; rather he is a commoner who engages in composing poetry. I wrote down from him in al-Maḥalla verses which I have included in the Muʿjam and elsewhere."@en .

rec:AIND-D05971 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05971-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05971-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05971 ;
    aindv:sourceText "401 عمر بن محمد بن عيسى اليافعي الخير قاضي عدن . مات سنة ثلاث وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā al-Yāfiʿī, the pious man, qāḍī of Aden. He died in the year (8)23."@en .

rec:AIND-D05972 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05972-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05972-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05972 ;
    aindv:sourceText "402 عمر بن أبي القسم محمد بن أبي الفضل محمد بن أحمد بن أبي الفضل محمد بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز النويري المكي الآتي أبوه . أجاز له في سنة أربعين زينب ابنة اليافعي وغيرها . ومات في ربيع الآخر منها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī al-Qāsim Muḥammad b. Abī al-Faḍl Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Abī al-Faḍl Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī; his father comes below. In the year (8)40 Zaynab bint al-Yāfiʿī and others gave him an ijāza. He died in Rabīʿ II of that year."@en .

rec:AIND-D05973 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05973-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05973-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05973 ;
    aindv:sourceText "403 عمر بن محمد بن محمد بن سليمان بن أبي بكر الزين بن ناصر الدين البكري الدمشقي ابن عم العلاء علي بن أحمد بن محمد ويعرف كل منهما بابن الصابوني ممن استقر به الظاهر خشقدم في نظر قلعة دمشق والأسوار وغيرهما وناب عن ابن عمه العلاء في نظر الجيش ، وكان تاجرا وهو والد الولد النجم محمد الذي عرض على محافيظه وقال لي أن أباه مات سنة أربع وثمانين وثمانمائة تقريبا بدمشق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Sulaymān b. Abī Bakr, al-Zayn b. Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Bakrī al-Dimashqī, cousin of al-ʿAlāʾ ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad, both of them known as Ibn al-Ṣābūnī. He was among those whom al-Ẓāhir Khushqadam appointed to the supervision (naẓar) of the citadel of Damascus, the walls and other things, and he deputized for his cousin al-ʿAlāʾ in the supervision of the army. He was a merchant, and he is the father of the boy al-Najm Muḥammad who presented his memorized texts to me and told me that his father died around the year 884 in Damascus."@en .

rec:AIND-D05976 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05976-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05976-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05976-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05976 ;
    aindv:sourceText "406 عمر بن محمد بن محمد بن علي بن عبد الواحد السراج بن البدر بن ناصر الدين بن الرئيس العلاء القاهري الطبيب ويعرف كسلفه بابن صغير وأمه أمة . ممن أخذ عن عمه والعز بن جماعة وصحب البدر الطنبدي وتميز في الطب بحفظ جعل منه نافعة وعالج المرضى بل قيل أنه استقر في الرياسة قليلا بعد توسيط خضر وابن العفيف ، وكان ظريفا لطيف العشرة ممن كف بصره ثم قدح له فأبصر وعمر ستا وتسعين سنة وما شابت له شعرة ولم يتيسر له الحج . مات في المحرم سنة سبع وستين وهو قريب الكمال محمد بن محمد بن علي بن عبد الكافي بن صغير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, al-Sirāj b. al-Badr b. Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Raʾīs al-ʿAlāʾ al-Qāhirī, the physician, known like his forebears as Ibn Ṣaghīr; his mother was a slave woman. He was among those who studied with his paternal uncle and with al-ʿIzz b. Jamāʿa, and kept the company of al-Badr al-Ṭanbadī. He distinguished himself in medicine by memorizing useful portions of it and treated the sick; indeed it is said that he briefly held the headship (of the physicians) after the execution by cutting in half of Khaḍir and Ibn al-ʿAfīf. He was refined and of gentle company; he lost his sight, then was treated by couching and saw again. He lived ninety-six years without a single hair turning grey, and the pilgrimage was never granted to him. He died in Muḥarram (8)67. He is a relative of al-Kamāl Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Kāfī b. Ṣaghīr."@en .

rec:AIND-D05977 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05977-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05977-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05977-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05977 ;
    aindv:sourceText "407 عمر بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن حسين بن علي بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة السراج بن القاضي جمال الدين أبي السعود بن قاضي القضاة الكمال أبي البركات بن القاضي الجمال أبي السعود القرشي المكي شقيق أبي الخير محمد الآتي أمهما أم الخير ابنة القاضي أبي القسم بن أبي العباس بن عبد المعطي . ولد في المحرم سنة ثلاث وخمسين وثمانمائة بالمدينة النبوية وقدم مع أبيه إلى مكة فسمع من الشهاب أحمد بن علي المحلي وأجاز له في سنة أربع وخمسين فما بعدها أبو جعفر بن العجمي وآخرون وتكرر قدومه للقاهرة وكان قد حفظ القرآن وصلى به هو وشقيقه أبو بكر تناوبا في رمضان على عادة الأبناء وربما حفظ غيره وقرأ على خاله عبد القادر في النحو ويطالع له درسه ولم ينجب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra, al-Sirāj b. al-Qāḍī Jamāl al-Dīn Abī al-Suʿūd b. Qāḍī al-Quḍāt al-Kamāl Abī al-Barakāt b. al-Qāḍī al-Jamāl Abī al-Suʿūd al-Qurashī al-Makkī, full brother of Abū al-Khayr Muḥammad who comes below; their mother was Umm al-Khayr, daughter of the qāḍī Abū al-Qāsim b. Abī al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī. He was born in Muḥarram 853 in the Prophet's Medina, came with his father to Mecca and heard from al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. ʿAlī al-Maḥallī. In 854 and thereafter Abū Jaʿfar b. al-ʿAjamī and others gave him an ijāza. He came repeatedly to Cairo. He had memorized the Qurʾān and led the prayers with it, alternating with his full brother Abū Bakr in Ramaḍān according to the custom of the sons (of the family); he may have memorized other works too. He read grammar with his maternal uncle ʿAbd al-Qādir and used to prepare the lesson for him. He did not excel."@en .

rec:AIND-D05978 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05978-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05978-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05978-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05978 ;
    aindv:sourceText "408 عمر بن محمد بن محمد بن أبي البركات محمد بن أبي السعود محمد بن حسين بن علي بن ظهيرة القرشي المكي ، أمه أم هاني ابنة العز النويري . بيض له ابن فهد وكأنه مات صغيرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Barakāt Muḥammad b. Abī al-Suʿūd Muḥammad b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī al-Makkī; his mother was Umm Hānī, daughter of al-ʿIzz al-Nuwayrī. Ibn Fahd left his entry blank, and it seems he died young."@en .

rec:AIND-D05982 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05982-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05982-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05982-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05982 ;
    aindv:sourceText "412 عمر بن محمد بن مسعود الغزي بن المغربي والد المحمدبن قاضي الحنفية وأخيه . كان مالكي المذهب خيرا . مات بعد الأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Masʿūd al-Ghazzī, Ibn al-Maghribī, father of the two Muḥammads, the Ḥanafī qāḍī and his brother. He was a Mālikī by madhhab and a good man. He died after (8)40."@en .

rec:AIND-D05984 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05984-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05984-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05984 ;
    aindv:sourceText "414 عمر بن محمد بن موسى بن عبد الله ناصر الدين بن الشيخ شمس الدين الشنشي القاهري الحنفي والد خير الدين محمد الآتي وأخو الشمس محمد الذي أرخه شيخنا في سنة ثمان وتسعين وسبعمائة . ولد سنة خمس وسبعين وسبعمائة ومات في رمضان سنة إحدى وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. ʿAbd Allāh, Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Shaykh Shams al-Dīn al-Shanshī al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī, father of Khayr al-Dīn Muḥammad who comes below, and brother of al-Shams Muḥammad whose death our shaykh recorded under the year 798. He was born in 775 and died in Ramaḍān (8)51."@en .

rec:AIND-D05985 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05985-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05985-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05985-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05985 ;
    aindv:sourceText "415 عمر بن محمد بن موسى بن عمر بن عوض بن عطية بن أحمد بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن السراج بن الشمس بن الشرف اللقاني ثم القاهري الأزهري المالكي الآتي أبوه وجده . مات في ذي القعدة سنة ثمانين عن ثلاث وخمسين فأكثر وصلي عليه في الأزهر ، وكان غالب عمره يتكسب بالشهادة في حانوت بالمكارية بالقرب من الأزهر إلا شهرا في أول ولاية قريبه البرهان الماضي قضاء المالكية لمباشرته النقابة نيابة فيها ثم جاء الأمر بمنعه فعاد إلى حاله ، وهو ممن سمع على شيخنا ولم يكن بالمحمود سامحه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. ʿUmar b. ʿAwaḍ b. ʿAṭiyya b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-Sirāj b. al-Shams b. al-Sharaf al-Laqānī, then al-Qāhirī al-Azharī al-Mālikī; his father and grandfather come below. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda (8)80 aged fifty-three or more, and the funeral prayer was performed over him at al-Azhar. For most of his life he earned his living as a notary witness in a shop at al-Makāriyya near al-Azhar, except for one month at the beginning of the tenure of his relative al-Burhān, mentioned above, as qāḍī of the Mālikīs, when he exercised the office of naqīb as deputy under him; then the order came to bar him from it and he returned to his former state. He was among those who heard from our shaykh, but he was not praiseworthy; may God pardon him and us."@en .

rec:AIND-D05987 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05987-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05987-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05987 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن الشمس محمد ويعرف بابن اللبان . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن علي بن حسن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Shams Muḥammad, known as Ibn al-Labbān. He has already been mentioned among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Ḥasan."@en .

rec:AIND-D05988 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05988-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05988-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05988 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن الخواجا الشمس محمد الدمشقي ويعرف بابن النحاس . مضى فيمن جده أبو بكر بن إسماعيل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. al-Khawājā al-Shams Muḥammad al-Dimashqī, known as Ibn al-Naḥḥās. He has already been mentioned among those whose grandfather is Abū Bakr b. Ismāʿīl."@en .

rec:AIND-D05989 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05989-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05989-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05989 ;
    aindv:sourceText "417 عمر بن محمد السراج أبو حفص النويري الشافعي . حفظ كتبا وأخذ عن الجمالين بن خطيب المنصورية والطيماني وجمع مختصرا فيه مسائل كثيرة ، وولي قضاء طرابلس بعد أبيه وكانت مباشرته جيدة لا بأس بها . مات فيها مطعونا في جمادى الآخرة سنة ثلاث وثلاثين وقد قارب الخمسين ، وهو في أنباء شيخنا باختصار بدون اسم أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Sirāj Abū Ḥafṣ al-Nuwayrī al-Shāfiʿī. He memorized books and studied under the two Jamāls, Ibn Khaṭīb al-Manṣūriyya and al-Ṭaymānī, and compiled an abridgement containing many questions. He held the judgeship of Tripoli after his father, and his conduct of the office was good and unobjectionable. He died there of the plague in Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year (8)33, when he was close to fifty. He appears in our shaykh's Inbāʾ, briefly and without his father's name."@en .

rec:AIND-D05990 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05990-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05990-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05990 ;
    aindv:sourceText "418 عمر بن محمد الزين الحمصي ثم الدمشقي الشافعي . أحد فضلاء دمشق في مذهبه ممن يستحضر الكثير من الروضة مع الدين والخير وتكسبه من أنوال حرير يدولبها . مات في شوال سنة ثلاث . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Zayn al-Ḥimṣī, then al-Dimashqī, al-Shāfiʿī. One of the distinguished men of Damascus in his school, among those who had much of al-Rawḍa at their command, together with piety and goodness; he earned his living from silk looms that he worked himself. He died in Shawwāl of the year (8)03. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D05991 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05991-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05991-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05991-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05991 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن محمد بن الزين الصفدي النيني . مضى فيمن جده أبو بكر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. al-Zayn al-Ṣafadī al-Nīnī. He has already been mentioned among those whose grandfather is Abū Bakr."@en .

rec:AIND-D05992 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05992-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05992-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05992-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D05992-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b110_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261012 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05992 ;
    aindv:sourceText "419 عمر بن محمد السراج الطريني المحلي المالكي والد محمد وأبي بكر ويعرف بالطريني . كان يعرف بالعلم والصلاح وله مؤلف في تعبير الرؤيا ، وكان فقيها فاضلا زاهدا أخذ عنه ابنه أبو بكر وممن أخذ عنه الولوي السنباطي الفقه ومات في يوم الاثنين ثامن عشري ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين ورأيت من أرخها سنة عشرين وأظنه غلطا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Sirāj al-Ṭuraynī al-Maḥallī al-Mālikī, the father of Muḥammad and Abū Bakr, known as al-Ṭuraynī. He was known for learning and righteousness, and has a work on the interpretation of dreams. He was an excellent, ascetic jurist; his son Abū Bakr studied under him, and among those who took fiqh from him was al-Walawī al-Sunbāṭī. He died on Monday, the twenty-eighth of Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year (8)22; I have seen someone who dated it to the year (8)20, but I think that is an error."@en .

rec:AIND-D05994 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05994-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05994-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05994-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05994 ;
    aindv:sourceText "421 عمر بن محمد النجم النعماني نسبة للإمام أبي حنيفة النعمان البغدادي ثم الدمشقي الحنفي . قدم القاهرة في سنة خمسين وبيده حسبة دمشق ووكالة بيت المال وعدة وظائف فنزل في زاوية التقي رجب العجمي تحت قلعة الجبل فلم يلبث أن مات في رابع صفر منها فأسف السلطان عليه وأمرهم بالصلاة عليه في مصلى المؤمني ونزل فصلى عليه ودفن بتربة التقي المذكور من القرافة الصغرى عفا الله عنه ، وينظر أهو قريب حميد الدين محمد بن تاج الدين القاضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Najm al-Nuʿmānī—after the Imam Abū Ḥanīfa al-Nuʿmān—al-Baghdādī, then al-Dimashqī, al-Ḥanafī. He came to Cairo in the year (8)50 holding the ḥisba of Damascus, the agency of the treasury (wakālat bayt al-māl) and several other offices, and lodged in the zāwiya of al-Taqī Rajab al-ʿAjamī below the Citadel; but before long he died, on the fourth of Ṣafar of that year. The sultan grieved for him, ordered them to pray over him at the Muṣallā al-Muʾminī, and came down and prayed over him himself. He was buried in the tomb of the aforementioned al-Taqī in the Lesser Qarāfa; may God pardon him. It remains to be examined whether he was a relative of the judge Ḥamīd al-Dīn Muḥammad b. Tāj al-Dīn."@en .

rec:AIND-D05995 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05995-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05995-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05995-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05995 ;
    aindv:sourceText "422 عمر بن محمد البعلي ويعرف بابن التركماني . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه فقال : أحد الشهود ببعلبك ممن لا يشاقق رفقته ولا يشاطط في الأجرة وله نظم نازل . مات في ثامن عشر المحرم سنة إحدى وقد جاز الثمانين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Baʿlī, known as Ibn al-Turkumānī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ and said: \"One of the witnesses of Baʿlabakk, among those who did not quarrel with their colleagues nor overcharge in their fees; he had some poor verse.\" He died on the eighteenth of Muḥarram of the year (8)01, having passed eighty. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05996 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05996-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05996-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05996 ;
    aindv:sourceText "423 عمر بن محمد الغمري ويعرف بابن المغربية أحد أصحاب أبي عبد الله المغربي . مات في ربيع الأول سنة ست وخمسين وكان إنسانا حسنا منور الشيبة بهي الهيئة حسن العبارة متوددا محببا إلى الناس ، حج وقارب الثمانين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Ghamrī, known as Ibn al-Maghribiyya, one of the companions of Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Maghribī. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year (8)56. He was a good man, with radiant grey hair, of fine appearance and good speech, affectionate and beloved by people. He performed the pilgrimage and approached eighty years of age. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D05997 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05997-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05997-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D05997-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05997 ;
    aindv:sourceText "424 عمر بن محمد الطرابلسي الحنفي . ذكره شيخنا في معجمه وقال : شاعر مقبول قدم القاهرة فمدح بها الأكابر وأنشدني كثيرا من شعره ومدحني بأبيات . مات في رجب سنة ثلاث عشرة ، زاد في الأنباء عن نحو الخمسين ووصفه بالشاعر الماهر ، وذكره المقريزي في عقوده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Ṭarābulusī al-Ḥanafī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Muʿjam and said: \"An acceptable poet; he came to Cairo and there praised the notables; he recited to me much of his poetry and praised me in some verses.\" He died in Rajab of the year (8)13. In the Inbāʾ he added that he was about fifty years old, and described him as a skilled poet. Al-Maqrīzī also mentioned him in his ʿUqūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D05998 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D05998-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D05998-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D05998 ;
    aindv:sourceText "425 عمر بن محمد الطرابلسي فقيه بعلبك ونزيل دمشق . ممن درس فيها بالمجاهدية الجوانية برغبة البدر بن قاضي شهبة له عنه ثم رغب هو عنه للبرهان بن المعتمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Ṭarābulusī, the jurist of Baʿlabakk and resident of Damascus. He was among those who taught there at al-Mujāhidiyya al-Jawwāniyya, al-Badr b. Qāḍī Shuhba having ceded it to him; then he in turn ceded it to al-Burhān b. al-Muʿtamid."@en .

rec:AIND-D06000 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06000-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06000-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06000 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن محمد المالقي شاعر الأندلس ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muḥammad al-Mālaqī, the poet of al-Andalus. …"@en .

rec:AIND-D06002 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06002-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06002-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06002 ;
    aindv:sourceText "428 عمر بن محمود بن محمود السراج البرديني الأزهري الشافعي الضرير . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Maḥmūd b. Maḥmūd al-Sirāj al-Bardīnī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī, the blind. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D06003 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06003-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06003-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06003 ;
    aindv:sourceText "429 عمر بن مصلح السراج المحلي . أخذ عنه الفرائض الجلال محمد بن ولي الدين أحمد المحلي السمنودي وقال أنه توفي تقريبا سنة خمس وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Muṣliḥ al-Sirāj al-Maḥallī. Al-Jalāl Muḥammad b. Walī al-Dīn Aḥmad al-Maḥallī al-Samannūdī took the law of inheritance (al-farāʾiḍ) from him, and said that he died in approximately the year (8)45."@en .

rec:AIND-D06004 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06004-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06004-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06004-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06004 ;
    aindv:sourceText "430 عمر بن أبي المعالي بن محمد أبي المعالي الفقيه تقي الدين الزبيدي أخو أبي بكر الآتي . ولد في حدود سنة سبعين وسبعمائة وكان فقيها فاضلا كريم النفس حسن الأخلاق عذب المجالسة يحفظ كثيرا من التواريخ والأخبار ولي القضاء بحيس وتدريس السيفية بزبيد بعد أخيه . مات سنة تسع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Abī al-Maʿālī b. Muḥammad Abī al-Maʿālī, the jurist Taqī al-Dīn al-Zabīdī, brother of Abū Bakr, who follows. He was born around the year 770. He was an accomplished jurist, generous, of good character and pleasant company, who memorized much of the histories and reports. He held the judgeship of Ḥays and the professorship of al-Sayfiyya in Zabīd after his brother. He died in the year (8)39."@en .

rec:AIND-D06007 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06007-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06007-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06007 ;
    aindv:sourceText "433 عمر بن منصور العجيسي الجزيري . مات سنة تسع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Manṣūr al-ʿAjīsī al-Jazīrī. He died in the year (8)49."@en .

rec:AIND-D06010 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06010-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06010-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06010-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06010 ;
    aindv:sourceText "436 عمر بن يحيى بن سليمان البوصيري الغمري الخطيب بن الخطيب . فقير حج وجاور معي في سنة إحدى وسبعين ولازمني في الإملاء وغيره وهو ممن يقرأ القرآن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Yaḥyā b. Sulaymān al-Būṣīrī al-Ghamrī, the preacher, son of the preacher. A poor man (faqīr); he performed the pilgrimage and sojourned (jāwara) with me in the year (8)71, and attended me assiduously in the dictation sessions (al-imlāʾ) and other things. He is one of those who recite the Qurʾān."@en .

rec:AIND-D06011 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06011-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06011-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06011-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06011 ;
    aindv:sourceText "437 عمر بن يحيى بن عبد الله بن علي بن عمرون البعلي . سمع من عبد الرحمن ابن محمد ابن الزعبوب صحيح البخاري وذكره التقي بن فهد في معجمه بدون زيادة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Yaḥyā b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAlī b. ʿAmrūn al-Baʿlī. He heard Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad Ibn al-Zaʿbūb. Al-Taqī Ibn Fahd mentioned him in his Muʿjam without any addition."@en .

rec:AIND-D06013 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06013-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06013-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06013 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر بن يعقوب الكمال البلخي الحنفي . يأتي فيمن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Yaʿqūb al-Kamāl al-Balkhī al-Ḥanafī. He will come below among those whose father is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D06015 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06015-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06015-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06015 ;
    aindv:sourceText "440 عمر بن يوسف البالسي المؤذن . قال شيخنا في إنبائه : اشتغل بالحديث ومهر فيه وسمع الكثير مع الخير والدين . مات بوادي الصفراء وهو متوجه إلى مكة في آخر ذي القعدة سنة إحدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Yūsuf al-Bālisī, the muezzin. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Inbāʾ: \"He occupied himself with ḥadīth and excelled in it, and heard a great deal, together with goodness and piety.\" He died at Wādī al-Ṣafrāʾ while on his way to Mecca, at the end of Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year (8)01."@en .

rec:AIND-D06017 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06017-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06017-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b110_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06017 ;
    aindv:sourceText "442 عمر بن بهاء الدين سليمان الكنبايتي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar b. Bahāʾ al-Dīn Sulaymān al-Kanbāyatī. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D06019 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06019-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06019-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06019 ;
    aindv:sourceText "444 عمر زين الدين الدمشقي الحنبلي نقيب الرسل وخادم قضاة الحنابلة . كتب عنه البدري في مجموعه قوله : %~% إن إدريس حبيب %~% قد ألفناه زمانا %~% %~% وحفضنا الضد فيه %~% ورفعناه مكانا %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar Zayn al-Dīn al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanbalī, naqīb al-rusul (chief of the court messengers) and servant (khādim) of the Hanbali judges. Al-Badrī recorded in his Majmūʿ the following verses as his: \"Indeed Idrīs is a beloved whom we have long been accustomed to; we lowered (kept down) what opposed him and raised him in station.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D06021 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06021-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06021-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06021 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر السراج بن الصيرفي الدمشقي أحد نواب الشافعية بها . فيمن اسم أبيه علي بن عثمان بن عمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Sirāj b. al-Ṣayrafī al-Dimashqī, one of the Shafiʿi deputy judges there (in Damascus). [His biography is] among those whose father's name is ʿAlī b. ʿUthmān b. ʿUmar."@en .

rec:AIND-D06022 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06022-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06022-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06022 ;
    aindv:sourceText "446 عمر السراج المارديني الدمشقي الحنفي والد عبد القادر الجوهري الماضي . رأيت له مصنفا في المولد النبوي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Sirāj al-Māridīnī al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanafī, the father of the aforementioned ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Jawharī. I saw a work composed by him on the Prophet's birth (al-mawlid al-nabawī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D06023 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06023-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06023-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06023 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر السراج المناوي أحد نواب الحنفية وفضلائهم . فيمن اسم أبيه علي بن عمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Sirāj al-Munāwī, one of the Hanafi deputy judges and one of their learned men. [His biography is] among those whose father's name is ʿAlī b. ʿUmar."@en .

rec:AIND-D06024 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06024-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06024-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06024 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر السراج النويري الطرابلسي قاضيها الشافعي . فيمن أبوه محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Sirāj al-Nuwayrī al-Ṭarābulusī, the Shafiʿi judge of that city (Tripoli). [His biography is] among those whose father is Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D06026 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06026-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06026-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06026 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر البحيري اثنان مالكيان : ابن صالح وابن علي بن عمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Buḥayrī: there are two, both Malikis, the son of Ṣāliḥ and the son of ʿAlī b. ʿUmar."@en .

rec:AIND-D06027 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06027-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06027-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06027 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر البسطامي . في ابن علي بن حجي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Basṭāmī. [His biography is] under Ibn ʿAlī b. Ḥajjī."@en .

rec:AIND-D06028 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06028-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06028-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06028 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر البطايني اثنان : ابن أبي بكر بن خليل وابن أحمد بن محمد بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Baṭāyinī: there are two, the son of Abū Bakr b. Khalīl and the son of Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D06029 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06029-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06029-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06029-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06029 ;
    aindv:sourceText "448 عمر البهرمشي المحلي الغمري . أحد القدماء من أصحاب أبي عبد الله الغمري مات في ذي القعدة سنة تسع وسبعين وقد زاحم المائة أو جازها وصلينا عليه صلاة الغائب ، وكان مديما للطهارة والتلاوة بحيث استفيض أنه كان على الختم في ليلة ولم يتزوج قط فيما بلغني رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Bahramashī al-Maḥallī al-Ghamrī, one of the senior companions of Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ghamrī. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda 879, having neared one hundred years of age or passed it, and we performed the absentee funeral prayer (ṣalāt al-ghāʾib) over him. He constantly maintained ritual purity and Qurʾān recitation, so that it was widely reported that he would complete the whole Qurʾān in a single night; as far as I was told, he never married. May God have mercy on him and on us."@en .

rec:AIND-D06030 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06030-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06030-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06030-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06030 ;
    aindv:sourceText "449 عمر الحسني البجائي المالكي نزيل مكة . ممن شهد على الوانوغي في إجازة القاضي عبد القادر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Ḥasanī al-Bijāʾī al-Mālikī, resident of Mecca. He was among those who witnessed al-Wānūghī's ijāza to the qāḍī ʿAbd al-Qādir."@en .

rec:AIND-D06031 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06031-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06031-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06031 ;
    aindv:sourceText "450 عمر الخليلي شيخ رباط ربيع مكة . مات بها في ربيع الثاني سنة ثلاث وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Khalīlī, shaykh of Ribāṭ Rabīʿ in Mecca. He died there in Rabīʿ al-Thānī 843. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D06032 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06032-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06032-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06032 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر الدموشي . في ابن عمر بن عبد الرحمن بن يوسف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Damūshī. [His biography is] under Ibn ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Yūsuf."@en .

rec:AIND-D06033 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06033-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06033-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06033 ;
    aindv:sourceText "451 عمر الرجراجي المغربي المالكي براء مهملة ثم جيمين نسبة لقبيلة بالمغرب الأقصى . إمام جامع الأندلس من فاس كان الغالب عليه الزهد والورع مع تقدمه في الفقه . مات سنة عشر ، أفادنيه بعض أصحابنا المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Rajrājī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī. [Al-Rajrājī is] with an undotted rāʾ followed by two jīms, a nisba to a tribe in the Far Maghrib. He was the imam of the Andalus Mosque (Jāmiʿ al-Andalus) in Fez. Asceticism and scrupulousness predominated in him, together with his advancement in jurisprudence. He died in the year [8]10; one of our Maghribi companions informed me of this."@en .

rec:AIND-D06034 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06034-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06034-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06034-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06034 ;
    aindv:sourceText "452 عمر الزيني القجاجقي الطواشي نائب شيخ الخدام بالحرم المدني . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Zaynī al-Qajājiqī al-Ṭawāshī, deputy of the chief of the servants (shaykh al-khuddām) at the sanctuary of Medina. He was among those who heard from me in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D06035 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06035-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06035-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06035 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر السكندري نزيل مكة في ابن علي بن عمر البحيري ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Sakandarī, resident of Mecca. [His biography is] under Ibn ʿAlī b. ʿUmar al-Buḥayrī."@en .

rec:AIND-D06036 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06036-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06036-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06036 ;
    aindv:sourceText "453 عمر السمديسي ثم القاهري والد الشمس محمد الآتي . مات في صفر سنة ست وثمانين بباب الوزير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Samdīsī, then al-Qāhirī, the father of al-Shams Muḥammad who follows below. He died in Ṣafar 886 at Bāb al-Wazīr."@en .

rec:AIND-D06037 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06037-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06037-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06037 ;
    aindv:sourceText "454 عمر الشيحي الجيار . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة اثنتين وسبعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Shīḥī al-Jayyār (the lime-burner). He died in Mecca in Muḥarram 872. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D06038 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06038-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06038-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06038 ;
    aindv:sourceText "455 عمر الضرير المصري نزيل مكة ، مات بها في المحرم سنة إحدى وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Ḍarīr (the blind) al-Miṣrī, resident of Mecca. He died there in Muḥarram 861. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D06039 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06039-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06039-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06039 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر الطريني . في ابن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Ṭuraynī. [His biography is] under Ibn Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D06041 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06041-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06041-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b111_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06041 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر الفتى . في ابن محمد بن معيبد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Fatā. [His biography is] under Ibn Muḥammad b. Muʿaybid."@en .

rec:AIND-D06042 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06042-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06042-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06042-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06042 ;
    aindv:sourceText "457 عمر القرمي ثم الحلبي . كان ماهرا في العلم عارفا بالأدب والنظم ، قدم من بلاده فأقام بحلب ثم تحول إلى دمشق فأقام بها مدة ثم توجه منها إلى مصر فمات بها في الطريق سنة إحدى . أرخه شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Qirimī, later al-Ḥalabī. He was skilled in learning and versed in literature and verse. He came from his country and settled in Aleppo, then moved to Damascus and stayed there for a while, then set out from there for Egypt and died there on the way in the year (8)01. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death date in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D06043 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06043-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06043-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06043-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06043 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر القلشاني . في ابن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Qalshānī. See under Ibn Muḥammad (ʿUmar b. Muḥammad)."@en .

rec:AIND-D06044 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06044-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06044-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06044 ;
    aindv:sourceText "458 عمر الكردي ثم المصري الأباريقي . كان بمصر يبيع الأباريق المدهونة وللشرف المناوي فمن يليه فيه اعتقاد . مات في سلخ ذي القعدة سنة ستين ودفنه المناوي بتربته المجاورة لباب مقام الشافعي القبلي المسمى بباب الصعيد . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Kurdī, later al-Miṣrī, al-Abārīqī. He was in Miṣr (Egypt) selling glazed ewers (abārīq), and al-Sharaf al-Munāwī and those below him held him in devout regard. He died on the last day of Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year (8)60, and al-Munāwī buried him in his own tomb adjoining the southern gate of the shrine of al-Shāfiʿī, called Bāb al-Ṣaʿīd. Al-Munīr recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D06045 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06045-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06045-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06045-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06045 ;
    aindv:sourceText "459 عمر اللولوي الدمشقي الصالحي الحنبلي كان خيرا يقرئ الأبناء مع فضيلة وخير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Luʾluʾī al-Dimashqī al-Ṣāliḥī al-Ḥanbalī. He was a good man who taught children to recite (the Qurʾān), with learning and goodness."@en .

rec:AIND-D06046 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06046-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06046-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06046 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عمر النجار المقري في ابن محمد بن محمد بن عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Najjār al-Muqrī. See under Ibn Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh (ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh)."@en .

rec:AIND-D06047 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06047-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06047-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06047 ;
    aindv:sourceText "460 عمر النجار آخر مؤذن بمنارة باب العمرة أحد أبواب المسجد الحرام وخادم بيت أم المؤمنين بزقاق الحجر من مكة . مات سنة إحدى وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUmar al-Najjār, the last muezzin of the minaret of Bāb al-ʿUmra, one of the gates of al-Masjid al-Ḥarām, and servant of the House of the Mother of the Believers in Zuqāq al-Ḥajar in Mecca. He died in the year (8)51. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D06048 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06048-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06048-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06048-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06048 ;
    aindv:sourceText "461 عميد بن عبد الله الخراساني الحنفي قاضي تمرلنك . مات بعد رجوعه من الروم سنة خمس . أرخه شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAmīd b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Khurāsānī al-Ḥanafī, the qāḍī of Tamerlane (Tamurlank). He died after his return from al-Rūm in the year (8)05. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death date in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D06049 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06049-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06049-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06049-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06049 ;
    aindv:sourceText "462 عنان بن علي بن عنان بن مغامس بن رميثة بن أبي نمي الحسيني . ممن سمع على ابن الجزري في سنة ثلاث وعشرين غالب كتابه الحصن الحصين . ومات بالقاهرة سنة ثلاثين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAnān b. ʿAlī b. ʿAnān b. Mughāmis b. Rumaytha b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥusaynī. He was among those who heard most of his book al-Ḥiṣn al-Ḥaṣīn from Ibn al-Jazarī in the year (8)23. He died in Cairo in the year (8)30. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D06050 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06050-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06050-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06050 ;
    aindv:sourceText "463 عنان بن قنيد بن مثقال القائد الحسني الآتي أبوه وأخوه مسعود . ممن ناب عن أخيه في نيابة مكة بل هو واليها وأخف وطأة من أخيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAnān b. Qunayd b. Mithqāl, al-Qāʾid, al-Ḥasanī; his father and his brother Masʿūd are mentioned below. He was among those who deputized for his brother in the deputy-governorship (niyāba) of Mecca; indeed he was its governor (wālī), and was lighter-handed than his brother."@en .

rec:AIND-D06053 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06053-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06053-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06053-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06053 ;
    aindv:sourceText "466 عنبر شجاع الدين العزي الطواشي أحد خدام الحرم الشريق النبوي . سمع على الزين أبي بكر المراغي والعلم سليمان السقا في سنة إحدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAnbar Shujāʿ al-Dīn al-ʿIzzī al-Ṭawāshī, one of the servants of the Noble Prophetic Sanctuary. He heard from al-Zayn Abū Bakr al-Marāghī and al-ʿAlam Sulaymān al-Saqqā in the year (8)01."@en .

rec:AIND-D06054 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06054-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06054-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06054 ;
    aindv:sourceText "467 عنبر فتى زيرك . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAnbar, the servant (fatā) of Zīrak. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D06056 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06056-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06056-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06056 ;
    aindv:sourceText "469 عودة بن مسعود بن جامع اللحياني شيخ وادي أبي عروة وأحد الأجواد . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة ثلاث وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAwda b. Masʿūd b. Jāmiʿ al-Liḥyānī, shaykh of Wādī Abī ʿUrwa and one of the generous. He died in Mecca in al-Muḥarram of the year (8)83. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D06057 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06057-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06057-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06057-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06057 ;
    aindv:sourceText "470 عوض بن حسب الله بن مهاوش المكي التمار بها . ممن سمع مني بمكة وكان ذا ملاءة ثم افتقر . مات في ربيع الثاني سنة تسع وتسعين بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAwaḍ b. Ḥasb Allāh b. Muhāwish al-Makkī, the date-seller there. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca; he was wealthy, then fell into poverty. He died in Rabīʿ al-Thānī of the year (8)99 in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D06058 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06058-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06058-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06058 ;
    aindv:sourceText "471 عوض بن عبد الله الزاهد . كان منقطعا بجامع عمرو وللناس فيه اعتقاد . مات في رمضان سنة ست . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAwaḍ b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Zāhid. He lived in seclusion at the Mosque of ʿAmr, and people held him in devout regard. He died in Ramaḍān of the year (8)06. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D06059 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06059-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06059-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06059 ;
    aindv:sourceText "472 عوض بن غنيم بن صلاح . أحد فقهاء الزيدية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿAwaḍ b. Ghunaym b. Ṣalāḥ. One of the jurists of the Zaydiyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D06062 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06062-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06062-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06062 ;
    aindv:sourceText "475 عويد بن منصور بن راجح بن محمد بن عبد الله بن عمر أحد قواد مكة . مات في مقتلة كانت في صفر سنة ست وأربعين وقطع رأسه وطيف به في ساحل جدة ثم دفن مع جسده بها . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿUwayd b. Manṣūr b. Rājiḥ b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar, one of the commanders (quwwād) of Mecca. He died in a massacre that took place in Ṣafar of the year (8)46; his head was cut off and paraded on the coast of Jidda, then buried there together with his body. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D06063 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06063-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06063-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06063-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06063 ;
    aindv:sourceText "476 عيسى بن إبراهيم بن عيسى بن إبراهيم بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن عمر بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله أبو إبراهيم الناشري . كان فاضلا خيرا دينا ذا أخلاق طيبة وأحوال جيدة أم بمسجد جليجان عند صلاحية زبيد بعد أخيه عمر وعلم القرآن حتى مات سنة سبع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿĪsā b. Ibrāhīm b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh, Abū Ibrāhīm al-Nāshirī. He was learned, good and pious, of fine character and good conduct. He served as imam of the Mosque of Julayjān, beside the Ṣalāḥiyya of Zabīd, after his brother ʿUmar, and taught the Qurʾān until he died in the year (8)37."@en .

rec:AIND-D06064 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06064-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06064-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06064-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06064 ;
    aindv:sourceText "477 عيسى بن أحمد بن بدر الهراوي نسبة لهرا من الشرقية بالقرب من العلاقمة ثم القاهري الشافعي . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Aḥmad b. Badr al-Harāwī—a nisba to Harā in al-Sharqiyya, near al-ʿAlāqima—then al-Qāhirī, the Shāfiʿī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D06069 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06069-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06069-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06069 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عيسى بن أحمد بن نعيمة ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Aḥmad b. Nuʿayma. …"@en .

rec:AIND-D06070 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06070-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06070-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b112_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06070 ;
    aindv:sourceText "482 عيسى بن أحمد بن يحيى أبو مهدي الغبريني المالكي قاضي تونس وعالمها . ممن أخذ عنه أحمد بن محمد القلجاني وغيره كالعجيسي بل نقل عنه البرزلي في فتاويه ووصفه بصاحبنا . مات سنة ست عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Aḥmad b. Yaḥyā, Abū Mahdī al-Ghubrīnī al-Mālikī, qāḍī of Tunis and its scholar. Among those who studied under him were Aḥmad b. Muḥammad al-Qaljānī and others such as al-ʿAjīsī; moreover, al-Burzulī quoted him in his Fatāwā and described him as \"our companion\". He died in the year (8)16."@en .

rec:AIND-D06071 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06071-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06071-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06071 ;
    aindv:sourceText "483 عيسى بن أحمد الحنديسي بفتح المهملة ثم نون ساكنة بعدها مهملة مكسورة ثم تحتانية ثم سين مهملة ثم البجائي المغربي المالكي . تقدم في الفقه وأصوله والعربية وغيرها حفظا لها وفهما لمعانيها مع فروسيته وتقدمه في أنواعها وديانته . تصدى للإفتاء والإقراء وناب في الخطابة بجامع بجاية الأعظم وهو الآن في سنة تسعين شيخها وقدوة أهلها يزيد على الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Aḥmad al-Ḥandīsī (with fatḥa on the undotted ḥāʾ, then a quiescent nūn, after it an undotted dāl with kasra, then a letter dotted below [yāʾ], then an undotted sīn), then al-Bijāʾī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī. He excelled in jurisprudence, its principles, Arabic and other subjects, memorizing them and understanding their meanings, together with his horsemanship, his excellence in its various kinds, and his piety. He devoted himself to giving fatwās and teaching, and acted as deputy preacher at the Great Mosque of Bijāya. He is now, in the year (8)90, its shaykh and the exemplar of its people, being over sixty years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D06074 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06074-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06074-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06074-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06074 ;
    aindv:sourceText "486 عيسى بن سعيد بن عبد الحميد القاضي المالكي ، مات سنة ثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Saʿīd b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd, the Mālikī judge (al-qāḍī). He died in the year (8)30."@en .

rec:AIND-D06076 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06076-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06076-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06076 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عيسى بن سليمان بن عبد الله الأنصاري . يأتي فيمن لم يسم أبوه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Sulaymān b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī. He will come below among those whose father is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D06077 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06077-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06077-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06077 ;
    aindv:sourceText "488 عيسى بن عباس بن عمر المغربي التلمساني الخالدي الشيخ العالم الفاضل الورع الزاهد . مات بمكة في جمادى الأولى سنة اثنتين وعشرين . قال الجمال المرشدي : وقل أن رأيت على طريقته مثله في الورع والتقوى . ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. ʿAbbās b. ʿUmar al-Maghribī al-Tilimsānī al-Khālidī, the shaykh, the learned, virtuous, scrupulous and ascetic. He died in Mecca in Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year (8)22. Al-Jamāl al-Murshidī said: \"Rarely have I seen anyone of his way who was his equal in scrupulousness and piety.\" Ibn Fahd mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D06078 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06078-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06078-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06078-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06078 ;
    aindv:sourceText "489 عيسى بن عبد الله العماد القرشي المخزومي اليمني المهجمي نزيل مكة ويعرف بابن الهليس ، كان من أعيان التجار ولاه الأشرف صاحب اليمن نظر عدن وجاور بمكة سنين مات في رجب سنة اثنتين بأبيات حسين ذكره الفاسي ثم شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-ʿImād al-Qurashī al-Makhzūmī al-Yamanī al-Mahjamī, resident of Mecca, known as Ibn al-Hulays. He was one of the leading merchants; al-Ashraf, the ruler of Yemen, appointed him supervisor (nāẓir) of Aden. He sojourned in Mecca for some years. He died in Rajab of the year (8)02 at Abyāt Ḥusayn. Al-Fāsī mentioned him, and then our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D06079 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06079-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06079-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06079 ;
    aindv:sourceText "490 عيسى بن عثمان بن عيسى بن عثمان بن محمد الشرف القاهري الشافعي والد الفخر محمد وعلي وأحمد المذكورين ويعرف بابن جوشن كان من الفضلاء ممن درس وأقرأ وأخذ عن شيخنا ، ومات قريب العشرين أو بعدها رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. ʿUthmān b. ʿĪsā b. ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad, al-Sharaf al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, father of the aforementioned al-Fakhr Muḥammad, ʿAlī and Aḥmad, known as Ibn Jawshan. He was one of the men of merit, among those who taught and gave instruction in recitation, and he studied under our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar). He died around the year (8)20 or after it. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D06080 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06080-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06080-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06080 ;
    aindv:sourceText "491 عيسى بن عطيفة كحنيفة بن محمد بن عيسى العتبي الحلوي نسبة لحلى اليماني الشافعي . ولد في سنة ست وستين وثمانمائة ولقيني في ذي الحجة سنة سبع وتسعين بمكة فقرأ على بعض المنهاج وسمع مني المسلسل وغيره وكتبت له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. ʿUṭayfa (on the pattern of Ḥanīfa) b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā al-ʿUtbī al-Ḥalawī (after Ḥalī) al-Yamānī al-Shāfiʿī. He was born in the year 866. He met me (al-Sakhāwī) in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year (8)97 in Mecca, read part of al-Minhāj to me and heard from me al-Musalsal and other things, and I wrote (an ijāza) for him."@en .

rec:AIND-D06081 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06081-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06081-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06081 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عيسى بن عطية النعيمي أبو عزارة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. ʿAṭiyya al-Nuʿaymī, Abū ʿAzāra."@en .

rec:AIND-D06082 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06082-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06082-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06082 ;
    aindv:sourceText "492 عيسى بن علي بن جار الله بن زايد بن يحيى بن محيي السنبسي المكي ابن عم موسى بن أحمد بن جار الله الآتي ويعرف بابن زائد . مات بمكة في ذي الحجة سنة ستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. ʿAlī b. Jār Allāh b. Zāyid b. Yaḥyā b. Muḥyī al-Sunbusī al-Makkī, paternal cousin of Mūsā b. Aḥmad b. Jār Allāh, who comes below, and known as Ibn Zāʾid. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year (8)60. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D06085 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06085-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06085-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06085 ;
    aindv:sourceText "495 عيسى بن علي الأخنائي الشافعي . رأيته فيمن عرض عليه سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. ʿAlī al-Akhnāʾī al-Shāfiʿī. I saw him among those to whom [memorized texts] were presented in the year (8)95."@en .

rec:AIND-D06087 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06087-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06087-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06087 ;
    aindv:sourceText "497 عيسى بن علال المصمودي المغربي المالكي إمام جامع القرويين الأعظم . له تعليقة على مختصر ابن عرفة ، وكان زاهدا ورعا ولي القضاء ومات قريبا من سنة عشرين . أفاده لي بعض أصحابنا المغاربة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. ʿAllāl al-Maṣmūdī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī, imam of the Great Mosque of al-Qarawiyyīn. He has a set of glosses (taʿlīqa) on the Mukhtaṣar of Ibn ʿArafa. He was ascetic and scrupulous, and held the office of judge. He died around the year (8)20. One of our Maghribi companions informed me of this."@en .

rec:AIND-D06088 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06088-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06088-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06088 ;
    aindv:sourceText "498 عيسى بن عيسى بن محمد العرابي بفتح العين والراء المشددة المهملتين ثم موحدة الدمشقي الصالحي المغربل أبوه . سمع من المحب الصامت وأبي الهول الجزري جزءا فيه موافقات أحمد في عبد الوهاب بن عطاء وغيره جمع الضياء ومن رسلان الذهبي من جزء البيتوتة ، وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء وكان نقيب الوالي بالصالحية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. ʿĪsā b. Muḥammad al-ʿArrābī (with fatḥa on the undotted ʿayn and a doubled undotted rāʾ, then a letter with one dot [bāʾ]) al-Dimashqī al-Ṣāliḥī; his father was a sifter (al-mugharbil). He heard from al-Muḥibb al-Ṣāmit and Abū al-Hawl al-Jazarī a juzʾ containing the muwāfaqāt of Aḥmad regarding ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿAṭāʾ and others, compiled by al-Ḍiyāʾ, and from Ruslān al-Dhahabī part of the Juzʾ al-Baytūta. He transmitted ḥadīth, and men of merit heard from him. He was the naqīb of the governor (wālī) in al-Ṣāliḥiyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D06090 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06090-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06090-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06090 ;
    aindv:sourceText "500 عيسى بن قرمان . قتل في محاربته مع أخيه إبراهيم في سنة أربعين . أرخه شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Qaramān. He was killed in his war with his brother Ibrāhīm in the year (8)40. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded the date in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D06094 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06094-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06094-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06094 ;
    aindv:sourceText "504 عيسى بن محمد بن قاسم الموصلي الدمشقي الراحبي والد علي الماضي ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Muḥammad b. Qāsim al-Mawṣilī al-Dimashqī al-Rāḥibī, father of ʿAlī, mentioned above; he was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D06095 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06095-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06095-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06095-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06095 ;
    aindv:sourceText "505 عيسى بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد الله القطب بن العفيف الحسيني الأيجي الشافعي أخو العلاء محمد ووالد مرشد الدين محمد . قرأ عليه ابن أخيه عبيد الله الخلاصة للطيبي في علوم الحديث وبعض شرح السيد على الكافية الحاجبية وكان علامة ، حج وأكثر أخذه عن السيد صفي الدين . مات بأيج سنة تسع وخمسين عن بضع وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Quṭb b. al-ʿAfīf al-Ḥusaynī al-Ījī al-Shāfiʿī, brother of al-ʿAlāʾ Muḥammad and father of Murshid al-Dīn Muḥammad. His brother's son ʿUbayd Allāh read to him al-Ṭībī's Khulāṣa on the sciences of ḥadīth and part of al-Sayyid's commentary on the Kāfiya of Ibn al-Ḥājib. He was a great scholar (ʿallāma). He performed the pilgrimage, and most of his learning was taken from al-Sayyid Ṣafī al-Dīn. He died at Īj in the year (8)59, aged forty-odd."@en .

rec:AIND-D06096 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06096-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06096-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06096 ;
    aindv:sourceText "506 عيسى بن محمد بن محمد أبو الروح الحجاجي الصوفي . ولد في ثالث عشر جمادى الآخرة سنة سبع وعشرين وسبعمائة ، وكان لطيفا ظريفا معروفا بذلك . مات سنة خمس . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, Abū al-Rūḥ al-Ḥajjājī al-Ṣūfī. He was born on 13 Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year 727. He was gentle and witty, and known for that. He died in the year (80)5. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D06097 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06097-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06097-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06097-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b109_113_triage,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06097 ;
    aindv:sourceText "507 عيسى بن محمد الشرف التجاني المغربي المالكي . سمع على الجمال الحنبلي وولي قضاء طرابلس ثم القدس وذكره الزين رضوان فيمن يؤخذ عنه ووصفه بالشيخ الإمام وأظنه عيسى المغربي الآتي قريبا والسابق عنه في أحمد بن محمد بن محمد بن عبد الله المغراوي كلمات بينه وبين البساطي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Muḥammad, al-Sharaf al-Tijānī al-Maghribī al-Mālikī. He heard from al-Jamāl al-Ḥanbalī, and held the judgeship of Tripoli, then of Jerusalem. Al-Zayn Riḍwān mentioned him among those from whom knowledge is to be taken and described him as \"the shaykh, the imam\". I think he is ʿĪsā al-Maghribī who comes shortly below. In the entry of Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Maghrāwī there was reported earlier, on his (the subject's) authority, an exchange of words between him (al-Maghrāwī) and al-Basāṭī."@en .

rec:AIND-D06099 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06099-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06099-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06099 ;
    aindv:sourceText "509 عيسى بن الشيخ محمود بن يوسف بن محمد بن عيسى الصيرامي ثم القاهري الحنفي أخو النظام يحيى الآتي ، جود عليه القرآن ابن أخيه عضد الدين عبد الرحمن وأثنى عليه"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. al-Shaykh Maḥmūd b. Yūsuf b. Muḥammad b. ʿĪsā al-Ṣayrāmī, then al-Qāhirī, the Ḥanafī, brother of al-Niẓām Yaḥyā, who comes below. His brother's son ʿAḍud al-Dīn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān recited the Qurʾān with tajwīd under him, and praised him."@en .

rec:AIND-D06100 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06100-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06100-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06100 ;
    aindv:sourceText "510 عيسى بن موسى بن صبح الرمثاوي الشافعي أحد العدول بدمشق مات في عشر السبعين سنة إحدى عشرة . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Mūsā b. Ṣubḥ al-Ramthāwī al-Shāfiʿī, one of the notary witnesses (ʿudūl) in Damascus. He died in his seventies in the year (8)11. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D06102 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06102-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06102-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b113_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06102 ;
    aindv:sourceText "512 عيسى بن موسى الشرف الفيومي المصري التاجر السفار في البحر وغيره ويعرف بالعلاف مات في ربيع الأول سنة خمس وستين بجدة ودفن بها وكان لا بأس به . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Mūsā, al-Sharaf al-Fayyūmī al-Miṣrī, the merchant who travelled by sea and otherwise, known as al-ʿAllāf. He died in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year (8)65 in Jidda and was buried there. He was a decent man. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D06103 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06103-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06103-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06103-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b114_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06103 ;
    aindv:sourceText "513 عيسى بن يحيى بن عبد الله الحوراني ثم القاهري ، ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Yaḥyā b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥawrānī, then al-Qāhirī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D06105 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06105-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06105-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06105-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D06105-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b114_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06105 ;
    aindv:sourceText "515 عيسى بن يوسف بن حجاج بن عيسى بن يوسف الشرف أبو النور الأشمومي ثم القاهري المديني المقري الشافعي الصرير ، ممن اشتغل وعرف القراءات ومن شيوخه فيها الزين جعفر السنهوري وأذن له في سنة خمسين وسمع على شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Yūsuf b. Ḥajjāj b. ʿĪsā b. Yūsuf, al-Sharaf Abū al-Nūr al-Ashmūmī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Madīnī, the Qurʾān reciter, the Shāfiʿī, the blind. He was among those who devoted themselves to study and became versed in the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt); among his teachers in that field was al-Zayn Jaʿfar al-Sanhūrī, who gave him authorization in the year 850. He also heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D06107 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06107-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06107-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06107 ;
    aindv:sourceText "517 عيسى بن يوسف بن محمد الخواجا العماد بن الجمال بن الشمس القرشي البكري البهنسي نزيل مكة وصاحب الدار بها التي صارت للجمال محمد بن الطاهر بباب الدريبة مات بها في رجب سنة خمس وستين ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā b. Yūsuf b. Muḥammad, al-Khawājā al-ʿImād b. al-Jamāl b. al-Shams al-Qurashī al-Bakrī al-Bahnasī, resident of Mecca and owner of the house there at Bāb al-Durayba that later passed to al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. al-Ṭāhir. He died there (in Mecca) in Rajab 865. Ibn Fahd recorded the date of his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D06108 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06108-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06108-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06108 ;
    aindv:sourceText "518 عيسى أبو الروح البغدادي الفلوحي الحنفي نزيل دمشق أقرأ العربية والصرف وغيرهما وممن أخذ عنه العلاء المرداوي ووصفه بالعلامة الفقيه الفرضي الأصولي النحوي الصرفي المحرر المتقن وأنه كان حسن التعليم ناصحا للمتعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā Abū al-Rūḥ al-Baghdādī al-Falūḥī al-Ḥanafī, resident of Damascus. He taught Arabic grammar, morphology, and other subjects. Among those who studied under him was al-ʿAlāʾ al-Mardāwī, who described him as the erudite scholar, the jurist, the expert in inheritance shares, the legal theorist, the grammarian, the morphologist, precise and accurate in his redactions, and said that he was a fine teacher and sincere toward the student."@en .

rec:AIND-D06109 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06109-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06109-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D06109-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06109 ;
    aindv:sourceText "519 عيسى الأنصاري المصري الحنفي المكتب نزيل مكة . سمع على ابن صديق وأبي اليمن الطبري وغيرهما وكان دينا خيرا تعانى الكتابة فبرع فيها وتصدى لذلك احتسابا فانتفع به جمع كثير من أهل مكة ، ومات شابا بمصر في سنة سبع . ذكره التقي بن فهد في معجمه وسمى أباه سليمان بن عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā al-Anṣārī al-Miṣrī al-Ḥanafī, the writing teacher, resident of Mecca. He heard from Ibn Ṣiddīq, Abū al-Yaman al-Ṭabarī, and others. He was a religious, good man who practised calligraphy and excelled in it, and devoted himself to it (teaching it) for God's sake without pay, so that a great many of the people of Mecca benefited from him. He died young in Miṣr in the year [8]07. Al-Taqī b. Fahd mentioned him in his Muʿjam and gave his father's name as Sulaymān b. ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D06110 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06110-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06110-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06110 ;
    aindv:sourceText "520 عيسى البليتني البجائي . مات سنة خمس وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā al-Balītanī al-Bijāʾī. He died in the year 825."@en .

rec:AIND-D06112 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06112-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06112-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06112 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عيسى الدلال بمكة . في ابن عوضة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā, the broker in Mecca. See under Ibn ʿAwaḍa."@en .

rec:AIND-D06113 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D06113-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D06113-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Naoki_Umetsu,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D06113 ;
    aindv:sourceText "عيسى الريغي . في ابن يحيى قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "ʿĪsā al-Rīghī. See under Ibn Yaḥyā, shortly before."@en .

rec:AIND-D07000 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07000-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07000-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07000 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد بن موسى بن عبد الواحد القبابي المغربي . فيمن جده حسن بن عبد الواحد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Qabābī al-Maghribī. See under those whose grandfather is Ḥasan b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid."@en .

rec:AIND-D07001 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07001-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07001-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07001-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07001 ;
    aindv:sourceText "245 محمد بن أحمد بن موسى بن نجاد ناصر الدين أبو عبد الله بن الأمير الشهاب أبي عبد الله بن أبي بكر النابلسي المقدسي ، أجاز له في سنة ست وخمسين الحفاظ الثلاثة ابن كثير والعلائي والشهاب أبو محمود والرمثاوي وأبو الحرم القلانسي وناصر الدين التونسي والبياني وابن الخباز وأبو العباس بن الجوخي وآخرون وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء كابن موسى والآبي في سنة خمس عشرة . وذكره شيخنا في معجمه وقال : أجاز لأولادي . وكذا ذكره ابن فهد وآخرون ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Mūsā b. Najjād, Nāṣir al-Dīn Abū ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Amīr al-Shihāb Abī ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr al-Nābulusī al-Maqdisī. In the year [7]56 the three ḥāfiẓes—Ibn Kathīr, al-ʿAlāʾī, and al-Shihāb Abū Maḥmūd—as well as al-Ramthāwī, Abū al-Ḥaram al-Qalānisī, Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Tūnisī, al-Bayānī, Ibn al-Khabbāz, Abū al-ʿAbbās b. al-Jūkhī, and others granted him ijāza. He transmitted, and men of learning such as Ibn Mūsā and al-Ābī heard from him in the year [8]15. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Muʿjam and said, \"He granted ijāza to my children.\" Ibn Fahd and others likewise mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07003 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07003-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07003-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07003 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد بن موسى التونسي القباقبي . فيمن جده حسن بن عبد الواحد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Mūsā al-Tūnisī al-Qabāqibī. See under those whose grandfather is Ḥasan b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid."@en .

rec:AIND-D07004 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07004-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07004-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07004 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد بن موسى الكفيري . فيمن جده موسى بن عبد الله قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Mūsā al-Kufayrī. See under those whose grandfather is Mūsā b. ʿAbd Allāh, shortly before."@en .

rec:AIND-D07005 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07005-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07005-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07005-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07005-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D07005-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b114_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07005 ;
    aindv:sourceText "247 محمد بن أحمد بن ميز الشمس المقدسي الصوفي التاجر . مات في سابع عشر صفر سنة ست وتسعين بالرملة وهو قافل من دمشق ونقل لبيت المقدس فدفن بماملا وكان مشهده حافلا ، وهو ممن سمع على الجمال بن جماعة وأجاز له القاضي سعد الدين بن الديري والشريف النسابة والشهاب السكندري المقري وسارة ابنة ابن جماعة وكان كثير العبادة مديما للجماعة بالمسجد الأقصى رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Mayz, al-Shams al-Maqdisī, the Sufi, the merchant. He died on 17 Ṣafar [8]96 in al-Ramla while returning from Damascus; he was carried to Jerusalem and buried in Māmillā, and his funeral was well attended. He was among those who heard from al-Jamāl b. Jamāʿa, and al-Qāḍī Saʿd al-Dīn b. al-Dīrī, al-Sharīf al-Nassāba, al-Shihāb al-Sakandarī the Qurʾān reciter, and Sāra the daughter of Ibn Jamāʿa granted him ijāza. He was much given to worship and constant in attending congregational prayer at al-Masjid al-Aqṣā. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07006 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07006-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07006-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07006-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07006-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b114_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07006 ;
    aindv:sourceText "248 محمد بن أحمد بن موسى البدر أبو عبد الله الرمثاوي الدمشقي الفقيه الشافعي . اشتغل كثيرا وفضل ونسخ بخطه الكثير ودرس بالعصرونية والأكرية وحج وجاور ومات في ربيع الأول سنة إحدى وقد جاز الأربعين وكان منجمعا عن الناس قليل الشر بل بعيدا عنه خلافا لأخيه موسى ، ذكر سيخنا في إنبائه باختصار عن هذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Mūsā, al-Badr Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ramthāwī al-Dimashqī, the jurist, the Shāfiʿī. He studied much, excelled, and copied a great deal in his own hand; he taught at al-ʿAṣrūniyya and al-Akriyya, performed the pilgrimage and sojourned (in the Holy City). He died in Rabīʿ I of the year [8]01, having passed forty. He kept apart from people and was of little harm—indeed far from it—unlike his brother Mūsā. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned this man briefly in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07008 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07008-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07008-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07008-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07008 ;
    aindv:sourceText "250 محمد بن الشهاب أحمد بن ناصر الدين بن الفقيه الدمياطي نزيل القاهرة يدعى ولي الله . ممن سمع على قرب التسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Faqīh al-Dimyāṭī, resident of Cairo, called Walī Allāh. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) around the year [8]90."@en .

rec:AIND-D07009 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07009-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07009-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07009-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07009 ;
    aindv:sourceText "251 محمد بن أحمد بن نصر الله بن أحمد بن محمد بن عمر موفق الدين بن المحب البغدادي الأصل الحنبلي أخو يوسف وهذا الأكبر ، نشأ فحفظ القرآن وغيره وأخذ عن أبيه بل سمع معه على الشرف بن الكويك في مسلم بقراءة شيخنا وكذا سمع بعده على ابن ناظر الصاحبة وابن بردس وابن الطحان بحضرة البدر البغدادي الحنبلي في صفر سنة خمس وأربعين ، وصاهر الشمس محمد بن علي بن عيسى البغدادي على أخته ، وتعاني التجارة وكان حيا في سنة أربع وخمسين أو قريبها ثم مات باسكندرية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Naṣr Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar, Muwaffaq al-Dīn b. al-Muḥibb, of Baghdadi origin, the Ḥanbalī, brother of Yūsuf and the elder of the two. He grew up, memorized the Qurʾān and other works, and studied under his father; indeed he heard together with him Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim from al-Sharaf b. al-Kuwayk, with our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) as reader. Likewise he afterwards heard from Ibn Nāẓir al-Ṣāḥiba, Ibn Bardas, and Ibn al-Ṭaḥḥān in the presence of al-Badr al-Baghdādī al-Ḥanbalī in Ṣafar [8]45. He became related by marriage to al-Shams Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿĪsā al-Baghdādī by marrying his sister. He engaged in trade, and was alive in the year [8]54 or thereabouts; then he died in Alexandria."@en .

rec:AIND-D07013 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07013-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07013-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07013-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07013 ;
    aindv:sourceText "255 محمد بن أحمد بن يعلي السيد الحسني . شرح الجرومية وقال أن مؤلفها صنفها لولده أبي محمد وأنه قرأها على الولد المشار إليه بفاس ، وأظنه من أهل هذا القرن فيحرر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Yaʿlā, al-Sayyid al-Ḥasanī. He wrote a commentary on al-Jurūmiyya and stated that its author had composed it for his son Abū Muḥammad, and that he had read it with that son in Fez. I think he belongs to this century, but this should be verified."@en .

rec:AIND-D07015 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07015-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07015-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07015-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07015 ;
    aindv:sourceText "257 محمد بن أحمد بن يوسف بن عبد المجيد البدر المحلي ثم القاهري المالكي إمام مسجد قراقجا الحسنى . اشتغل وقتا في الفقه والعربية ونحوهما وشارك في الجملة فلازم التقي الشمني فقرأ عليه في المسند وغيره رواية وكذا سمع على العز الحنبلي وعبد الكافي بن الذهبي وطائفة بقراءتي ، وكان مع مشاركته فيه ديائة وخير . مات شابا بعد الستين رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Yūsuf b. ʿAbd al-Majīd, al-Badr al-Maḥallī, then al-Qāhirī, the Mālikī, imam of the mosque of Qarāqujā al-Ḥasanī. For a time he occupied himself with jurisprudence, Arabic, and the like, and acquired a general share in them; he attended al-Taqī al-Shumunnī closely and read with him the Musnad and other works by way of transmission. He likewise heard from al-ʿIzz al-Ḥanbalī, ʿAbd al-Kāfī b. al-Dhahabī, and a group of others with me (al-Sakhāwī) as reader. Along with his share in learning he had piety and goodness. He died young, after the [8]60s began. May God have mercy on him and on us."@en .

rec:AIND-D07018 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07018-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07018-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07018-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b114_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07018 ;
    aindv:sourceText "260 محمد المحب أبو بكر أخو الذي قبله . ولد سنة ثمان وعشرين وثمانمائة ونشأ فحفظ القرآن عند الشمس محمد بن علي بن صلاح المناوي وسمع مع أخيه بمكة على التقي بن فهد في سنة ثلاث وأربعين ، وتعاني التجليد في بيته وتكسب بالشهادة واسترفقه أبو الطيب الأسيوطي فصار بذلك وجيها . ومات في جمادى الأولى سنة ثلاث وتسعين بعد رفيقه بقليل وأظنه جاز الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad al-Muḥibb Abū Bakr, brother of the preceding. He was born in the year 828 and grew up memorizing the Qurʾān with al-Shams Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Ṣalāḥ al-Manāwī, and he heard together with his brother in Mecca from al-Taqī b. Fahd in the year 843. He practised bookbinding at home and earned a living as a notary witness; Abū al-Ṭayyib al-Asyūṭī took him as his companion, and through that he became a man of standing. He died in Jumādā I 893, shortly after his companion; I think he had passed sixty."@en .

rec:AIND-D07019 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07019-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07019-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07019-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07019-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b114_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07019 ;
    aindv:sourceText "261 محمد بن أحمد بن يوسف البدر القاهري الشافعي التاجر بسوق أمير الجيوش ويعرف بابن يوسف . ممن اشتغل وتميز وسمع الحديث قليلا ومما سمعه ختم البخاري عند أم هانئ الهورينية ورفقتها ، وكان عاقلا ساكنا حسن البزة . مات شابا قبل السبعين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Yūsuf, al-Badr al-Qāhirī, the Shāfiʿī, the merchant in Sūq Amīr al-Juyūsh, known as Ibn Yūsuf. He was among those who studied and distinguished themselves, and he heard a little ḥadīth; among what he heard was the completion (khatm) of al-Bukhārī with Umm Hāniʾ al-Hawrīniyya and her fellow transmitters. He was sensible, quiet, and well dressed. He died young, before [8]70, I suppose."@en .

rec:AIND-D07021 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07021-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07021-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07021-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07021-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b115_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07021 ;
    aindv:sourceText "263 محمد بن أحمد بن يوسف الشمس الغمري بالمعجمة والد أبي البركات داود التقي بن نصر الله . صحب الشهاب الزاهد واشتغل يسيرا وتنزل في الجمالية عند شيخنا أول ما فتحت . قاله لي الجلال القمصي وكان رفيقه وسيأتي الشمس محمد ابن عمر الغمري الوالي الشهير فربما التبس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Yūsuf al-Shams al-Ghamrī (with the dotted ghayn), the father of Abū al-Barakāt Dāwūd al-Taqī b. Naṣr Allāh. He kept the company of al-Shihāb al-Zāhid, studied a little, and was enrolled at al-Jamāliyya under our shaykh [Ibn Ḥajar] when it was first opened. Al-Jalāl al-Qumṣī, who was his companion, told me this. Al-Shams Muḥammad b. ʿUmar al-Ghamrī, the famous al-Wālī, will come below, and he may be confused with him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07022 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07022-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07022-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07022-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07022-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b115_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07022 ;
    aindv:sourceText "264 محمد بن أحمد بن يوسف البزاز بقيسارية الطرحي وشريك صهري ويعرف بأبي إبراهيم . حج وكان أصلح حالا من كثيرين . مات قبيل السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Yūsuf, the cloth merchant (al-bazzāz) at Qaysāriyyat al-Ṭarḥī and the partner of my in-law (ṣihrī), known as Abū Ibrāhīm. He performed the pilgrimage and was sounder in his condition than many. He died shortly before [the year] 870."@en .

rec:AIND-D07023 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07023-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07023-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07023-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07023-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b115_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07023 ;
    aindv:sourceText "265 محمد بن أحمد بن يوسف المعلم شقير الفيشي الخياط . ولد سنة أربعين وسبعمائة وتقدم في صناعته بحيث يقترح على الخياطين فنونا مع محبة في العلم وأهله . مات في أخريات سنة ست وعشرين . ذكره المقريزي في عقوده وأورد عنه دعاء أملاه عليه عرف بركته وروى عنه غير ذلك وأرخ بعض ما كتبه عنه بسنة ثلاث عشرة بدمشق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Yūsuf, al-Muʿallim Shuqayr al-Fīshī, the tailor. He was born in the year 740 and excelled in his craft to the point that he would propose [new] techniques to the tailors, together with a love for learning and its people. He died in the last part of the year 826. Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his ʿUqūd, cited from him a supplication which he had dictated to him and whose blessing was known, transmitted other things from him, and dated some of what he wrote down from him to the year 813, in Damascus."@en .

rec:AIND-D07024 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07024-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07024-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07024-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07024-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b115_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07024 ;
    aindv:sourceText "266 محمد بن أحمد بن يونس الجمال المكي ويعرف بالكركي . كان عاقلا خيرا ذا مروءة وصيانة وأخلاق حسنة . قاله الفاسي في تاريخه ، وقال كتبت عنه بمكة دعاء ذكر لي أنه ينقع من الأعداء على ما بلغه من شيخ اليمن علما وعملا وأحمد بن العجيل يقال ثلاثا عند الصباح وعند المساء وهو : اللهم يا مخلص المولود من ضيق مخاض أمه ويا معافي الملدوغ من شدة حمه وسمه ويا قادرا على كل شئ بعلمه أسئلك بمحمد وأسمه أن تكفيني كل ظالم بظلمه . مات في العشر الأخير من شوال سنة تسع بالقاهرة وقد بلغ الخمسين أو قاربها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Yūnus al-Jamāl al-Makkī, known as al-Karakī. He was sensible and good, possessing manliness, probity and fine character. So said al-Fāsī in his history, and he said: \"I wrote down from him in Mecca a supplication which, he told me, is effective against enemies, according to what had reached him from the shaykh of Yemen in learning and practice, Aḥmad b. al-ʿUjayl; it is said three times in the morning and in the evening, and it is: 'O God, O Deliverer of the newborn from the narrowness of its mother's labour, O Healer of the stung from the severity of its fever and venom, O You who are capable of all things by Your knowledge, I ask You by Muḥammad and by his name to protect me from every wrongdoer in his wrongdoing.'\" He died in the last ten days of Shawwāl of the year [80]9 in Cairo, having reached fifty or nearly so."@en .

rec:AIND-D07025 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07025-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07025-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07025 ;
    aindv:sourceText "267 محمد بن أحمد بن الشيخ البهاء الأنصاي الأخميمي . ذكره التقي بن فهد في معجمه هكذا مجردا وهو جد قاضي الحنفية الآن ناصر الدين محمد بن أحمد وحينئذ فجده محمد بن محمد بن عبد الوهاب بن البهاء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Shaykh al-Bahāʾ al-Anṣārī al-Akhmīmī. Al-Taqī b. Fahd mentioned him in his Muʿjam thus, bare [of any detail]. He is the grandfather of the present Ḥanafī qāḍī Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, and accordingly his [own] grandfather is Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. al-Bahāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07026 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07026-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07026-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07026 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد بن كمال الدين . مضى فيمن جده كمال ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Kamāl al-Dīn. He has come above among those whose grandfather is Kamāl."@en .

rec:AIND-D07027 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07027-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07027-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07027-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07027 ;
    aindv:sourceText "268 محمد بن أحمد البدر بن الشهاب البنهاوي القاهري الشافعي أخو ناصر الدين بن أصيل لأمه وصهر ابن الهمام على ابنته الكبرى حج معه وجاور وكان مفرط السمن جدا بعيدا عن الفهم وكل فضيلة وما اكتسب من صهره حبة . مات بعد الستين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, al-Badr b. al-Shihāb al-Banhāwī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, the brother of Nāṣir al-Dīn b. Aṣīl on his mother's side and the son-in-law of Ibn al-Humām through his eldest daughter. He performed the pilgrimage with him and stayed on [in Mecca]. He was extremely obese, far removed from understanding and from every virtue, and did not gain a single grain from his father-in-law. He died after [the year] 860, presumably."@en .

rec:AIND-D07028 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07028-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07028-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07028 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد البدر بن جنة . فيمن جده على ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Badr b. Janna. [See] among those whose grandfather is ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D07029 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07029-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07029-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07029 ;
    aindv:sourceText "269 محمد بن أحمد البهاء المحلي الفرضى الشافعي ويعرف بابن الواعظ لكون أبيه كان واعظا . شيخ فاضل قرأ الفرائض على أبي الجود وتميز فيها وكذا اشتغل في الفقه وصار يستحضر من مناظيم ابن العماد أشياء وكان خيرا . ولذا استقر به القاياتي في التكلم على أوقاف المحلة فلم يزل به كل من ولديه والولوي البلقيني حتى صرفه بأوحد الدين بن العجيمي جريا على عادته وشق ذلك على البهاء بحيث ألزم نفسه بعدم دخول القاهرة ما دام القاياتي قاضيا فلم يلبث إلا نحو شهرين ومات وانحلت±±± يمينه وتكرر دخوله للقاهرة وقصدني مرة بالسؤال عن بعض الأحاديث فأجبته ورأى بعد صرفه مناما أثبته في ترجمة القاياتي . مات في ذي الحجة سنة تسع وسبعين بالمحلة وأظنه قارب السبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Bahāʾ al-Maḥallī, the specialist in inheritance law (al-faraḍī), al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Wāʿiẓ because his father was a preacher. A learned shaykh; he read the law of inheritance with Abū al-Jūd and distinguished himself in it, likewise occupied himself with jurisprudence, and came to have by heart a number of things from the versified works of Ibn al-ʿImād. He was a good man. For that reason al-Qāyātī installed him in the administration of the endowments of al-Maḥalla, but both of his [al-Qāyātī's] sons and al-Walawī al-Bulqīnī kept at him until he dismissed him in favour of Awḥad al-Dīn b. al-ʿUjaymī, as was his wont. This weighed on al-Bahāʾ so heavily that he bound himself not to enter Cairo as long as al-Qāyātī was qāḍī; but he [al-Qāyātī] lasted only about two months and died, his oath was dissolved, and he entered Cairo repeatedly. He once came to me to ask about some ḥadīths, and I answered him. After his dismissal he saw a dream, which I have recorded in the biography of al-Qāyātī. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 879 in al-Maḥalla; I think he was nearly seventy."@en .

rec:AIND-D07030 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07030-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07030-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07030 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد التاج الأنصاري . مضى فيمن جده علي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Tāj al-Anṣārī. He has come above among those whose grandfather is ʿAlī."@en .

rec:AIND-D07031 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07031-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07031-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07031 ;
    aindv:sourceText "270 محمد بن أحمد التاج القاهري ويعرف بابن المكللة وبابن جماعة . ولي الحسبة فلم تطل مدته بل عزل . ومات في ربيع الآخر سنة تسع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Tāj al-Qāhirī, known as Ibn al-Mukallala and as Ibn Jamāʿa. He held the ḥisba (market inspectorship), but his tenure did not last long; rather, he was dismissed. He died in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 829."@en .

rec:AIND-D07032 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07032-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07032-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07032 ;
    aindv:sourceText "271 محمد بن أحمد التقي بن الشهاب القزويني ، مات في ليلة الأربعاء عاشر صفر سنة ثمان وثلاثين ودفن من الغد بمقبرة الصوفية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Taqī b. al-Shihāb al-Qazwīnī. He died on the night of Wednesday, 10 Ṣafar of the year 838, and was buried the next day in the Cemetery of the Sufis (Maqbarat al-Ṣūfiyya)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07036 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07036-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07036-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07036 ;
    aindv:sourceText "275 محمد بن أحمد الجمال البهنسي ثم الدمشقي الشافعي . اشتغل بالقاهرة وحفظ المنهاج واتصل بالبرهان بن جماعة فلما ولي قضاء الشام استنابه واعتمد عليه في أمور كثيرة ، وكان حسن المباشرة مواظبا عليها وعنده ظرف ونوادر وكان مقلا مع العفة ولما وقعت الكائنة العظمى بدمشق فر إلى القاهرة فاستنابه الجلال البلقيني . ومات في ذي القعدة سنة خمس . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Jamāl al-Bahnasī, then al-Dimashqī, al-Shāfiʿī. He studied in Cairo and memorised the Minhāj, and attached himself to al-Burhān b. Jamāʿa, who, when he was appointed to the judgeship of Syria, made him his deputy and relied on him in many matters. He was skilful in the conduct of business and assiduous in it, with wit and amusing anecdotes, and he was poor yet upright. When the great calamity befell Damascus he fled to Cairo, where al-Jalāl al-Bulqīnī made him his deputy. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year [80]5. Our shaykh [Ibn Ḥajar] mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07037 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07037-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07037-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07037-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07037 ;
    aindv:sourceText "276 محمد بن أحمد الجمال الزبيدي المؤذن القمقام . ذكره التقى بن فهد في معجمه هكذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Jamāl al-Zabīdī, the muezzin, al-Qamqām. Al-Taqī b. Fahd mentioned him thus in his Muʿjam."@en .

rec:AIND-D07038 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07038-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07038-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07038 ;
    aindv:sourceText "277 محمد بن أحمد الجمال الكيلاني المكي الحنبلي نائب الإمام بالمقام الحنبلي ووالد عبد الرحمن الماضي . إنسان خير ساكن قدم القاهرة وسمع مني بمكة في سنة ست وثمانين يسيرا وسافر في أثناء سنة أربع وتسعين إلى الهند للاسترزاق وكتبت معه ما أرجو انتفاعه به وعاد مجبورا بعد أن كان سافر إليها قبل ذلك ثم دخل أيضا القاهرة ودمشق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Jamāl al-Kīlānī al-Makkī al-Ḥanbalī, deputy of the imam at the Ḥanbalī station (al-Maqām al-Ḥanbalī) and the father of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, mentioned above. A good, quiet man. He came to Cairo, and heard a little from me in Mecca in the year 886. In the course of the year 894 he travelled to India in search of a livelihood, and I wrote for him to take along something I hoped would be of use to him. He returned with his losses made good, having travelled there once before that; then he also entered Cairo and Damascus."@en .

rec:AIND-D07039 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07039-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07039-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07039 ;
    aindv:sourceText "278 محمد بن أحمد حافظ الدين الأذرعي الدمشقي الحنفي . ممن ناب في كتابة السر بدمشق وتميز ، ومات بحلب سنة إحدى وتسعين كتب عنه البدري في مجموعه : %~% حبيبي الظريف دق خصرا %~% فهمت به وبالخصر اللطيف %~% %~% وقلت للأئمى في ذا وهذا %~% نعم أهوى اللطيف والظريف %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Ḥāfiẓ al-Dīn al-Adhraʿī al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanafī. One of those who served as deputy in the office of confidential secretary (kitābat al-sirr) in Damascus, and he distinguished himself. He died in Aleppo in the year 891. Al-Badrī wrote down from him in his Majmūʿ: \"My elegant beloved is slender of waist, / and I am infatuated with him and with the delicate waist; / and I said to the blamers, about this one and that: / yes, I love the delicate and the elegant.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D07040 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07040-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07040-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07040 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد حميد الدين النعماني الفرعاني فيمن جده محمد بن أحمد بن عمر بن محمد بن ثابت ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Ḥamīd al-Dīn al-Nuʿmānī al-Farʿānī. [See] among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Thābit."@en .

rec:AIND-D07041 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07041-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07041-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07041 ;
    aindv:sourceText "279 محمد بن أحمد الشمس بن البرددار الحلبي . له نظم في ترجمة يحيى بن أحمد بن عمر بن العطار ، وينظر إن كان سبق فيمن سمى جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shams b. al-Barddār al-Ḥalabī. He has verses [recorded] in the biography of Yaḥyā b. Aḥmad b. ʿUmar b. al-ʿAṭṭār; it should be checked whether he has already appeared among those whose grandfather is named."@en .

rec:AIND-D07042 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07042-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07042-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07042 ;
    aindv:sourceText "280 محمد بن أحمد الشمس العزازي الأصل الحلبي ويعرف بابن سفليس . قرأ القرآن واشتغل بالعلم وطلب الحديث بنفسه ورحل وحصل بحيث اشتهر به في حلب مع المشاركة في غيره وكونه خيرا دينا بتكسب بالمتجر حتى مات في ليلة الخميس تاسع عشر ربيع الآخر سنة سبع وثلاثين وقد لقيه البقاعي هناك وكتب عنه قوله قال حسان بن ثابت يرثي إبراهيم بن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم رضي الله عنه مخاطبا النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بذلك %~% مضى ابنك محمود العواقب لم يشب %~% بعيب ولم يذمم بقول ولا فعل %~% %~% رأى أنه ان عاش وساواك في العلا %~% فآثر ان تبقى فريدا بلا مثل %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shams, of ʿAzāz by origin, of Aleppo, known as Ibn Siflīs. He read the Qurʾān, occupied himself with learning, sought ḥadīth on his own, travelled and acquired [it], so that he became famous for it in Aleppo, with participation in other [fields] as well; he was good and pious, earning his living by trade, until he died on the night of Thursday, 19 Rabīʿ al-Ākhir of the year 837. Al-Biqāʿī met him there and wrote down from him his words: \"Ḥassān b. Thābit said, mourning Ibrāhīm, the son of the Prophet (God bless him and grant him peace), may God be pleased with him, and addressing the Prophet (God bless him and grant him peace) with this: 'Your son has passed away, praised in his ends, unstained / by fault, and unblamed in word or deed. / He saw that were he to live and equal you in eminence, / [so] he preferred that you remain unique, without peer.'\""@en .

rec:AIND-D07043 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07043-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07043-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07043-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b115_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07043 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد الشمس بن القاضي الشهاب الدفري القاهري الماضي . مضى فيمن جده عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد القادر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shams b. al-Qāḍī al-Shihāb al-Dafarī al-Qāhirī, the one mentioned above. He has come above among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd al-Qādir."@en .

rec:AIND-D07044 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07044-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07044-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07044 ;
    aindv:sourceText "281 محمد بن أحمد الشمس الحريري العقاد بالوراقين والمجدد للجامع المعروف بابن مدين بالقرب من الجنينة وكان يلقب بالحنبلي . مات في صفر سنة ثلاث وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shams al-Ḥarīrī al-ʿAqqād (the cord-maker) in al-Warrāqīn, the renovator of the mosque known as Ibn Madyan near al-Junayna; he was nicknamed al-Ḥanbalī. He died in Ṣafar 863."@en .

rec:AIND-D07045 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07045-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07045-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07045 ;
    aindv:sourceText "282 محمد بن أحمد الشريف الشمس الحسيني القبيباتي الدمشقي والد إبراهيم الماضي ونزيل القاهرة . كان من أعيان التجار وممن صار بالقاهرة مرجعا للشاميين وكهفا لهم مع خير ووضاءة وتلاوة للقرآن ورغبة في العلماء والصالحين وتودد ، ابتنى خانا بالقرب من الخيميين بجامع الأزهر ، ومات قبل إكماله في خامس عشرى ذي الحجة سنة خمس وستين وأذهب ابنه ما خلفه له فيما لم يحصل منه على طائل رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Sharīf al-Shams al-Ḥusaynī al-Qubaybātī al-Dimashqī, the father of Ibrāhīm, mentioned above, and a resident of Cairo. He was one of the notable merchants and among those who became in Cairo a point of reference for the Syrians and a refuge for them, together with goodness, a radiant countenance, recitation of the Qurʾān, a fondness for scholars and the righteous, and affability. He began building a khan near al-Khiyamiyyīn at the Azhar Mosque, but died before its completion, on 25 Dhū al-Ḥijja 865. His son squandered what he had left him on things from which he gained no benefit. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07046 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07046-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07046-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07046 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد الشمس الزعيفريني . فيمن جده يوسف بن محمد بن معالي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shams al-Zuʿayfarīnī. See among those whose grandfather is Yūsuf b. Muḥammad b. Maʿālī."@en .

rec:AIND-D07047 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07047-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07047-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07047 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد الشمس السعودي الحنفي . فيمن جده عمر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shams al-Saʿūdī al-Ḥanafī. See among those whose grandfather is ʿUmar."@en .

rec:AIND-D07048 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07048-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07048-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07048-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07048 ;
    aindv:sourceText "283 محمد بن أحمد الشمس القباني ويعرف بابن بهاء والد علي ذاك المدبر حفظ القرآن وغيره واشتغل قليلا وكان بديع الجمال ممن يصحبه الزين قاسم الحنفي والوالد على الاستقامة ثم أقبل على التكسب بالوزن بالقبان في باب الفتوح وبالتجارة والمعاملة ، وسافر غير مرة لمكة وجاور وتزوج أم الشهاب بن خبطة أخت عبد الغني القليوبي وأثرى مع مداومته للجماعة والتلاوة ورغبته في الصدقة والبر ومحبة الصالحين . مات في رجب سنة ثمانين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shams al-Qabbānī, known as Ibn Bahāʾ, the father of ʿAlī, that ill-starred fellow (al-mudbir). He memorized the Qurʾān and other texts and studied a little. He was of striking beauty and was one of those whose company al-Zayn Qāsim al-Ḥanafī and my father kept in uprightness. He then turned to earning his living by weighing with the steelyard (qabbān) at Bāb al-Futūḥ, and by trade and commercial dealings. He travelled to Mecca more than once and sojourned there, and he married the mother of al-Shihāb Ibn Khabṭa, the sister of ʿAbd al-Ghanī al-Qalyūbī. He grew wealthy while keeping up congregational prayer and recitation, his eagerness for alms and good works, and his love of the righteous. He died in Rajab 880. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07049 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07049-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07049-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07049 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد الشمس المديني المالكي ويعرف بابن الموله . مضى فيمن جده عثمان بن خالد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shams al-Madīnī al-Mālikī, known as Ibn al-Muwallah. He has been mentioned above among those whose grandfather is ʿUthmān b. Khālid."@en .

rec:AIND-D07050 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07050-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07050-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07050-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07050 ;
    aindv:sourceText "284 محمد بن أحمد فتح الدين النعاس بمهملتين ونون المالكي أحد موقعي الحكم . كن حسن الخط عارفا بالوثائق ولي الخطابة بالباسطية وانتمى لأبي الفتح بن وفاء . مات في سنة سبع وثلاثين وتقدم شيخه للصلاة عليه بإشارة الزيني عبد الباسط مع حضرة الحنبلي وغيره من الأعيان . أرخه شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Fatḥ al-Dīn al-Naʿʿās (with two undotted letters and a nūn) al-Mālikī, one of the court signatories (muwaqqiʿī al-ḥukm). He had a fine hand and was knowledgeable in legal documents; he held the office of preacher at al-Bāsiṭiyya and attached himself to Abū al-Fatḥ Ibn Wafāʾ. He died in the year 837, and his shaykh stepped forward to lead the prayer over him at the direction of al-Zaynī ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ, in the presence of the Ḥanbalī (judge) and other notables. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07051 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07051-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07051-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07051 ;
    aindv:sourceText "285 محمد بن أحمد قطب الدين أبو عبد الله بن التاج البحايلي . مات في ربيع الثاني سنة ست وستين بمصر وصلى عليه بجامع عمرو وكان معتقدا في العامة . أرخه المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Quṭb al-Dīn Abū ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Tāj al-Baḥāylī. He died in Rabīʿ al-Thānī 866 in Miṣr, and the prayer over him was performed at the Mosque of ʿAmr. He was an object of veneration among the common people. Al-Munīr recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D07052 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07052-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07052-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07052-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07052 ;
    aindv:sourceText "286 محمد بن أحمد قطب الدين بن الركن السمرقندي رفيق نعمة الله الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Quṭb al-Dīn b. al-Rukn al-Samarqandī, the companion of Niʿmat Allāh, who will be mentioned below."@en .

rec:AIND-D07053 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07053-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07053-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07053-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07053 ;
    aindv:sourceText "287 محمد بن أحمد المحب الحلبي ثم الدمشقي الكاتب ويعرف بابن المجروح ، كتب على ابن الشمس الحلبي وتميز في الكتابة وتصدى للتكتيب في المجاهدية وغيرها وكان ممن كتب عنه أبو الفضل بن الإمام قال وكان عشيرا حسن الشكالة والبزة ماجنا . مات في سنة بضع وستين وقد جاز الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Muḥibb al-Ḥalabī, then al-Dimashqī, the scribe (al-Kātib), known as Ibn al-Majrūḥ. He studied penmanship under Ibn al-Shams al-Ḥalabī, excelled in writing, and devoted himself to teaching penmanship at al-Mujāhidiyya and elsewhere. He was among those from whom Abū al-Faḍl Ibn al-Imām wrote down; he said: he was sociable, of handsome appearance and dress, and dissolute. He died in the (eight hundred and) sixties, having passed fifty."@en .

rec:AIND-D07054 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07054-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07054-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07054 ;
    aindv:sourceText "288 محمد بن أحمد محيى الدين الرومي الحنفي ويعرف بين أهل بلاده بفلبوي . شاب قدم القاهرة في البحر من مكة فأقام أياما وقرأ على بعض المشارق للصغاني وسمع مني المسلسل بشرطه وله فضيلة وكتبت له إجازة وكان عزمه الإقامة والملازمة فلم يجد ما ستعين به لذلك فرجع إلى الشام ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Muḥyī al-Dīn al-Rūmī al-Ḥanafī, known among the people of his country as Filbawī. A young man who came to Cairo by sea from Mecca and stayed a few days; he read to me part of al-Mashāriq of al-Ṣaghānī and heard from me al-Musalsal under its condition. He had merit, and I wrote him an ijāza. His intention was to stay and attend lessons regularly, but he found nothing to support him in that, so he returned to Syria."@en .

rec:AIND-D07055 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07055-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07055-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07055 ;
    aindv:sourceText "289 محمد بن أحمد ناصر الدين بن الشهاب الخطاي المهمندار سبط أمير المؤمنين المتوكل على الله . مات في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين بالطاعون ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Shihāb al-Khaṭāy, the mihmandār, daughter's son of the Commander of the Faithful al-Mutawakkil ʿalā Allāh. He died of the plague in Ṣafar 853."@en .

rec:AIND-D07057 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07057-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07057-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07057 ;
    aindv:sourceText "291 محمد بن أحمد ناصر الدين المصري الشافعي ويعرف بالسخاوي وهو غير الماضي فيمن جده على . حفظ القرآن وكتبا وعرضها في عشر السبعين على جماعة من علماء القاهرة كالجمال الاسنائي وحضر دروسه ودروس غيره ، وكانت فيه نباهة ويذاكر بفوائد حسنة ، جاور بمكة غير مرة وكانت وفاته بها في شعبان سنة عشر ودفن بالمعلاة عن بضع وستين سنة . قاله الفاسي في مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Miṣrī al-Shāfiʿī, known as al-Sakhāwī; he is other than the one mentioned above among those whose grandfather is ʿAlī. He memorized the Qurʾān and some books and presented them in the (7)70s to a number of the scholars of Cairo, such as al-Jamāl al-Isnāʾī, and attended his lessons and those of others. There was intelligence in him, and he would discuss fine points of learning. He sojourned in Mecca more than once, and his death occurred there in Shaʿbān (8)10; he was buried in al-Muʿallā at the age of sixty-odd. Al-Fāsī said this in (his history of) Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D07058 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07058-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07058-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07058 ;
    aindv:sourceText "292 محمد بن أحمد ناصر الدين المصري . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Miṣrī. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D07059 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07059-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07059-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07059-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07059 ;
    aindv:sourceText "293 محمد بن أحمد ناصر الدين الهذباني الكردي الشافعي الطبردار ، كان من أبناء الجلد فتعلق بمجالسة العلماء وصحب كمال الدين الدميري ونورالدين الرشيدي وتدين وصار يسرد الصوم ويواظب الجماعة بل لا يقطع الصبح بالأزهر ويقوم إليه كل ليلة من نحو ربع الليل مشيا من منزله بحارة بهاء الدين مع تكسبه بالتجارة في الحوايص ثم ترك لما كبر ، وكان على ذهنه أشياء . مات سنة أربع وعشرين ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه وقال : لازمني مدة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Hadhbānī al-Kurdī al-Shāfiʿī, the axe-bearer (ṭabardār). He was one of the sons of the hardy folk (abnāʾ al-jald), but he attached himself to sitting with the scholars and kept company with Kamāl al-Dīn al-Damīrī and Nūr al-Dīn al-Rashīdī. He became devout, took to fasting continuously, and kept up congregational prayer; indeed he never missed the dawn prayer at al-Azhar, setting out for it every night at about a quarter of the night, on foot from his house in Ḥārat Bahāʾ al-Dīn, while earning his living by trading in belts (ḥawāʾiṣ), which he gave up when he grew old. He retained various things in his memory. He died in the year (8)24. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ and said: he attended me for a while."@en .

rec:AIND-D07061 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07061-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07061-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07061 ;
    aindv:sourceText "295 محمد بن أحمد أبو عبد القادر النابتي الغمري نزيل جامعه بالقاهرة . ممن سمع على في سنة خمس وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Abū ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Nābitī al-Ghamrī, resident of his (al-Ghamrī's) mosque in Cairo. He was among those who heard from me in the year (8)95."@en .

rec:AIND-D07062 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07062-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07062-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07062 ;
    aindv:sourceText "296 محمد بن أحمد أبو عبد الله الجبرتي . كان فقيها عالما تفقه بالقاضي أحمد بن أبي بكر الناشري وناب عن القاضي موفق الدين في أحكام زبيد فكان الناس إذا علموا أنه القاعد لذلك تحاموه لغلظته . ومات قبل وفاة شيخه المذكور في حدود سنة أربع عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Jabartī. He was a learned jurist who studied fiqh with the qāḍī Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr al-Nāshirī and deputized for the qāḍī Muwaffaq al-Dīn in the judicial affairs of Zabīd; when people learned that it was he who was sitting for that, they avoided him because of his harshness. He died before the death of his aforementioned shaykh, around the year (8)14."@en .

rec:AIND-D07063 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07063-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07063-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07063 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد أبو عبد الله الوانوغي المالكي . فيمن جده عثمان بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Wānūghī al-Mālikī. See among those whose grandfather is ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D07064 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07064-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07064-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07064 ;
    aindv:sourceText "297 محمد بن أحمد أبو الفضل القدسي الشافعي ويعرف بابن النجار حرفة أبيه . نشأ فأخذ عن ماهر ثم عن البرهان العجلوني والكمال بن أبي شريف حتى برع وتميز في الفضائل وتصدى للإقراء والإفتاء ، وكان ورعا متواضعا فقيرا قانعا ترك الإفتاء بأخرة واستقر به ابن الزمن شيخ مدرسته بالقدس . ومات في الكهولة في شعبان سنة سبع وثمانين واستقر في المشيخة النور محمود بن العصياتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad Abū al-Faḍl al-Qudsī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Najjār after his father's trade. He grew up and studied under Māhir, then under al-Burhān al-ʿAjlūnī and al-Kamāl Ibn Abī Sharīf, until he excelled and distinguished himself in the sciences, and he devoted himself to teaching and giving fatwās. He was scrupulous, humble, poor and content; he gave up issuing fatwās toward the end of his life. Ibn al-Zaman installed him as shaykh of his madrasa in Jerusalem. He died in middle age in Shaʿbān (8)87, and al-Nūr Maḥmūd Ibn al-ʿAṣyātī was installed in the shaykhship."@en .

rec:AIND-D07065 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07065-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07065-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07065-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b116_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07065 ;
    aindv:sourceText "298 محمد بن أحمد الكيلاني البجاربنيه بكسر الموحدة ثم جيم وآخره راء اسم لبلد مكأنه قال ابن البلد الفلاني الأزهري الشافعي . قدم القاهرة فجاور بالأزهر وكان عالما محققا صالحا أخذ عنه الفضلاء وقرأ عليه الزين زكريا شرح الشافية للجار بردي وشرح تصريف العزي للتفتازاني . ومات بالقاهرة قريبا من سنة خمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Kīlānī al-Bijārbinih — with kasra on the bāʾ, then jīm, ending in rāʾ; it is the name of a town, as if one said \"the son of such-and-such a town\" — al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī. He came to Cairo and sojourned at al-Azhar. He was a learned, meticulous and pious scholar; men of merit took knowledge from him, and al-Zayn Zakariyyā read with him the commentary on al-Shāfiya by al-Jārabardī and the commentary on Taṣrīf al-ʿIzzī by al-Taftāzānī. He died in Cairo around the year (8)50."@en .

rec:AIND-D07066 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07066-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07066-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07066-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07066 ;
    aindv:sourceText "299 محمد بن أحمد البلخي الدمشقي ويعرف ببكيبكة أجاز لى في سنة خمسين من دمشق ، وذكر البرهان العجلوني أنه سمع من المحب الصامت فالله أعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Balkhī al-Dimashqī, known as Bakībaka. He granted me (al-Sakhāwī) an ijāza in the year 850 from Damascus. Al-Burhān al-ʿAjlūnī mentioned that he had heard from al-Muḥibb al-Ṣāmit; but God knows best."@en .

rec:AIND-D07067 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07067-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07067-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07067-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07067 ;
    aindv:sourceText "300 محمد بن الشهاب أحمد البنهاوي التاجر . مات في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى وأربعين . أرخه شيخنا وقال أن المتحدث عليه استولى على موجود أبيه ولعله يزيد على عشرين ألف دينار فقام اثنان فادعيا أنهما ولدا عمه عصبة فصالحهما وكذا ناظر الخاص بما مجموعه لايفي بثلث الموجود قال وكان المخبر بذلك من باشر العرض والبيع وضبطه ومع ذلك فلم يلتفت المحدث لهذا وركب طريق الإنكار وإن الذي دفعه هو الذي استولى عليه من غير زيادة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Shihāb Aḥmad al-Banhāwī, the merchant. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year 841. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death date and said that the administrator in charge of him (al-mutaḥaddith ʿalayhi) took possession of his father's estate, which was perhaps more than twenty thousand dinars. Then two men came forward claiming to be the sons of his paternal uncle, agnate heirs (ʿaṣaba), so he settled with them, and likewise with the nāẓir al-khāṣṣ, for a total that did not amount to a third of the estate. He (Ibn Ḥajar) said: the one who reported this was the person who had handled the presentation and the sale and recorded it; nevertheless the administrator paid no heed to this and took the path of denial, (maintaining) that what he had paid out was exactly what he had taken possession of, without any surplus."@en .

rec:AIND-D07068 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07068-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07068-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07068 ;
    aindv:sourceText "301 محمد بن الشهاب أحمد العباسي الحلبي أحد أجناد الحلقة بها . مات بها في إحدى الجماديين سنة خمس وتسعين عن نحو الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Shihāb Aḥmad al-ʿAbbāsī al-Ḥalabī, one of the soldiers of the ḥalqa there (in Aleppo). He died there in one of the two Jumādās of the year 895, aged about fifty."@en .

rec:AIND-D07070 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07070-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07070-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07070 ;
    aindv:sourceText "303 محمد بن أحمد الزبيدي نزيل مكة ويعرف بالجندار . مات بها في ربيع الثاني سنة اثنتين وثمانين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Zabīdī, resident of Mecca, known as al-Jandār. He died there in Rabīʿ II of the year 882. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D07071 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07071-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07071-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07071 ;
    aindv:sourceText "304 محمد بن أحمد الزفتاوي ابن أخت القاضي ناصر الدين والدلال أبوه ويلقب بالثور . ممن جلس بالحانوت المجاور لحبس الرحبة في حياة خاله ثم بعده وكان يتكلم في وقف الحجازية ومولده ظنا سنة عشر وثمانمائة وفارقته في سنة ست وتسعين حيا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Zaftāwī, the sister's son of al-Qāḍī Nāṣir al-Dīn; his father was a broker (dallāl), and he is nicknamed al-Thawr (the Bull). He was among those who sat in the shop adjoining the prison of al-Raḥba during the lifetime of his maternal uncle and after him, and he used to administer the waqf of al-Ḥijāziyya. His birth was, presumably, in the year 810. I parted from him in the year 896 while he was still alive."@en .

rec:AIND-D07072 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07072-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07072-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07072-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07072 ;
    aindv:sourceText "305 محمد بن أحمد بن السبع وهو لقب أبيه القرشي القاهري الحنفي فخرالدين بن شهاب الدين جد قاسم بن أحمد الماضي . شهد على بعض الحنفية في إجازة سنة إحدى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Sabʿ (this being his father's laqab), al-Qurashī al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī, Fakhr al-Dīn b. Shihāb al-Dīn, the grandfather of the aforementioned Qāsim b. Aḥmad. He acted as witness for some Ḥanafīs in an ijāza in the year (8)01."@en .

rec:AIND-D07073 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07073-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07073-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07073 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد السعودي الحنفي . فيمن جده عمر ... ومحمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Saʿūdī al-Ḥanafī. (See) among those whose grandfather is ʿUmar … and Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D07075 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07075-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07075-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07075 ;
    aindv:sourceText "307 محمد بن أحمد الشقوري العجمي ويعرف بالبايزيدي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Shaqūrī al-ʿAjamī, known as al-Bāyazīdī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D07076 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07076-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07076-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07076-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07076 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد الطوخي . رأيته كتب بالشهادة على الزين طاهر في إجازته لأبي عبد القادر سنة ثلاث وثلاثين وأظنه ولي الدين الماضي فيمن جده محمد بن محمد بن عثمان بن موسى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Ṭūkhī. I saw that he had signed as a witness on al-Zayn Ṭāhir's ijāza to Abū ʿAbd al-Qādir in the year 833, and I think he is Walī al-Dīn, mentioned above among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān b. Mūsā."@en .

rec:AIND-D07077 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07077-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07077-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07077 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد بن الطولوني المهندس . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن علي بن عبد الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Ṭūlūnī, the engineer (al-muhandis). He has been mentioned above among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh."@en .

rec:AIND-D07078 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07078-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07078-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07078 ;
    aindv:sourceText "308 محمد بن أحمد القاهري الغزي . الحنفي ويعرف بابن المزين ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Qāhirī al-Ghazzī al-Ḥanafī, known as Ibn al-Muzayyin. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D07079 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07079-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07079-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07079-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07079 ;
    aindv:sourceText "309 محمد بن أحمد بن الفرات . شهد على الزين طاهر المالكي في إجازته لأبي عبد القادر سنة ثلاث وثلاثين وأظنه الماضي فيمن جده محمد بن علي بن الحسن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. al-Furāt. He acted as witness for al-Zayn Ṭāhir al-Mālikī in his ijāza to Abū ʿAbd al-Qādir in the year 833, and I think he is the one mentioned above among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. al-Ḥasan."@en .

rec:AIND-D07080 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07080-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07080-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07080 ;
    aindv:sourceText "310 محمد بن أحمد الفخري . مات بمكة في جمادى الثانية سنة سبع وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Fakhrī. He died in Mecca in Jumādā II of the year 857. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D07081 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07081-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07081-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07081 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد القمقام ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Qamqām."@en .

rec:AIND-D07082 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07082-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07082-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07082 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد الكركي ثم الدمشقي الحنبلي . فيمن جده معتوق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Karakī, then al-Dimashqī, al-Ḥanbalī. (See) among those whose grandfather is Maʿtūq."@en .

rec:AIND-D07083 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07083-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07083-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07083 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد الجمال الصامت بن أحمد الناشري . فيمن جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad al-Jamāl al-Ṣāmit b. Aḥmad al-Nāshirī. (See) among those whose grandfather is [name missing]."@en .

rec:AIND-D07084 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07084-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07084-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07084 ;
    aindv:sourceText "311 محمد بن أحمد الهاروني المصري . كان مجذوبا معتقدا في المصريين ويلقبه أهلها خفير البحر . مات في صفر سنة خمس . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Hārūnī al-Miṣrī. He was a majdhūb (ecstatic), revered among the people of Miṣr, and its inhabitants nicknamed him Khafīr al-Baḥr (the Guardian of the River). He died in Ṣafar of the year (8)05. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07085 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07085-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07085-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07085 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أحمد اليزليتني التونسي ويعرف بابن زغدان ، مضى فيمن جده محمد بن داود ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Yazlītinī al-Tūnisī, known as Ibn Zaghdān. He has been mentioned above among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Dāwūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D07086 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07086-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07086-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07086-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07086-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b117_review,
        agent:claude_rulings_20261017 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07086 ;
    aindv:sourceText "312 محمد بن أرغون شاه النوروزي أستاذ الظاهر جقمق بدمشق . مات في سنة ثلاث وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Arghūn Shāh al-Nawrūzī, [whose father Arghūn Shāh was] the ustādh [i.e. ustādār] of (the later) al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq in Damascus. He died in the year 853."@en .

rec:AIND-D07088 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07088-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07088-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07088-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b117_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07088 ;
    aindv:sourceText "314 محمد بن الأتابك أزبك الظاهري من ططخ سبط الظاهر جقمق ، أمه خديجة وهي سبطة الناصري بن البارزي وزوجه أبوه ابنة قراجا الخزندار واستولدها عليا وصار من أمراء الأربعين ويخلف والده إذا كان غائبا في التقريرات ونحوها وحسنوا له الأخذ على ذلك ، وحج أمير ركب الأول سنة ثمان وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Atābak Azbak al-Ẓāhirī min Ṭaṭakh, the daughter's son of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq. His mother was Khadīja, who was the daughter's daughter of al-Nāṣirī b. al-Bārizī. His father married him to the daughter of Qarājā al-Khazindār, and he had by her a son, ʿAlī. He became one of the amirs of forty, and he would deputize for his father, when the latter was absent, in the (issuing of) appointment documents and the like, and people encouraged him to accept (payment) for that. He performed the pilgrimage as amir of the first caravan in the year 898."@en .

rec:AIND-D07094 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07094-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07094-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07094 ;
    aindv:sourceText "320 محمد بن إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن حسن المحب أبو البركات بن المجد أبي الفداء القلعي سبط الشريف كريم الدين عبد الكريم بن الشيخ الصالح المملك الزين أبي بكر الحياتي والماضي أبوه ، نشأ في كنفه فحفظ القرآن وكتبا وعرض على جماعة بل اسمعه أبوه الكثير ، وكان ممن سمع مني وأجاز له جماعة ومات صغيرا بعد الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Ḥasan, al-Muḥibb Abū al-Barakāt b. al-Majd Abī al-Fidāʾ al-Qalʿī, the maternal grandson of the Sharīf Karīm al-Dīn ʿAbd al-Karīm b. al-Shaykh al-Ṣāliḥ al-Mumallik al-Zayn Abī Bakr al-Ḥayātī; his father has been mentioned above. He grew up under his father's care, memorized the Qurʾān and some books and presented them to a group of scholars; indeed his father had him hear a great deal. He was among those who heard from me, and a group granted him ijāza. He died young, after 860."@en .

rec:AIND-D07095 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07095-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07095-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07095-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07095 ;
    aindv:sourceText "321 محمد أمين الدين أبو النور شقيق الذي قبله . نشأ أيضا في كنف أبيه فقرأ القرآن وغيره وأسمعه كثيرا وأخذ عني جملة في الإملاء ، وخلفه في جهاته بجامع القلعة بل نيابة ، وفيه حشمة ولديه عقل وجود الخط ونعم الخلف ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad Amīn al-Dīn Abū al-Nūr, the full brother of the preceding one. He too grew up under his father's care, read the Qurʾān and other texts, and (his father) had him hear a great deal. He took much from me in the dictation sessions (imlāʾ). He succeeded him in his posts at the Mosque of the Citadel, though only as deputy. He has dignity, intelligence and fine handwriting, and is an excellent successor."@en .

rec:AIND-D07097 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07097-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07097-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07097 ;
    aindv:sourceText "323 محمد بن المجد إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن محمد بن علي بن موسى الكناني البلبيسي الأصل القاهري الحنفي الماضي أبوه . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه وقال له مات قبل أبيه بشهرين في أول سنة اثنتين وكان قد اشتغل ومهر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Majd Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Mūsā al-Kinānī, of Bilbaysī origin, al-Qāhirī, the Ḥanafī; his father has been mentioned above. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ and said: he died two months before his father, at the beginning of the year (8)02, and he had engaged in study and become proficient."@en .

rec:AIND-D07099 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07099-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07099-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07099-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07099 ;
    aindv:sourceText "325 محمد بن إسماعيل بن إبراهيم محي الدين بن المجد المكراني أخو أحمد الماضي وهذا أفضلهما . نشأ وقطن مكة مع أهله مشتغلا بالنحو والصرف والمنطق وغيرها ولازمني بها في سنة ست وثمانين وبعدها وفهم مع عقل وسكون وأدب وانتماء لبيت ابن السيد عفيف الدين وصغر سن ثم رجع إلى بلاده وأظنه عاد إليها بل هو الآن بنواحي كنباية هو وأخوه وأبوهما يقرئ ولدا لصاحبها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm, Muḥyī al-Dīn b. al-Majd al-Makrānī, brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad, and the better of the two. He grew up and settled in Mecca with his family, occupying himself with grammar, morphology, logic and other subjects, and he attended me there assiduously in the year 886 and thereafter. He has understanding together with good sense, composure and good manners, an attachment to the house of Ibn al-Sayyid ʿAfīf al-Dīn, and is young in years. He then returned to his homeland, and I think he came back to it (Mecca); rather, he is now in the region of Cambay, he and his brother and their father, who teaches a son of its ruler."@en .

rec:AIND-D07100 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07100-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07100-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07100-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07100 ;
    aindv:sourceText "326 محمد بن إسماعيل بن إبراهيم أبو الوفا القاهري الطبيب ويعرف بوفا . ولد بعد الثلاثين وثمانمائة بالقاهرة ، ونشأ بها وتدرب في الطب بخاله الشهاب أحمد بن خليل وناصر الدين بن البندقي ، وصار من ذوي النوب بالبيمارستان ممن يشار إليهم بالبراعة والمتانة وخفة الوطأة والتدبر في العلاج ، وقد حج غير مرة وجاور مرتين ودخل دمياط وربما لاطفني واشتد حرصه على كتابة الخصال الموجبة للظلال من تأليفي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm, Abū al-Wafā al-Qāhirī, the physician, known as Wafā. He was born after 830 in Cairo and grew up there, and trained in medicine under his maternal uncle al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. Khalīl and under Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Bunduqī. He became one of the physicians on rotation at the hospital (bīmāristān), among those pointed to for skill, soundness, a light touch and deliberation in treatment. He performed the pilgrimage more than once, resided (as mujāwir) twice, and entered Damietta. At times he showed me kindness, and he was most eager to copy my work al-Khiṣāl al-mūjiba li-l-ẓilāl."@en .

rec:AIND-D07103 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07103-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07103-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07103-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07103 ;
    aindv:sourceText "329 محمد بن إسماعيل بن أبي بكر الجمال بن الشرف الجبرتي الأصل اليماني الزبيدي . خدم عن أبيه وأبوه عن الجمال محمد بن محمد المزجاجي عن والداعية إسماعيل الجبرتي ، ولقيه عبد الله بن عبد الوهاب الكازروني المدني وقال لي أنه شيخ الصوفية الآن بزبيد وأنه لم يتكهل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Abī Bakr, al-Jamāl b. al-Sharaf, of Jabartī origin, al-Yamānī al-Zabīdī. He received (the Sufi path, khidma) from his father, his father from al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. Muḥammad al-Mazjājī, and he from the dāʿiya Ismāʿīl al-Jabartī. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Kāzarūnī al-Madanī met him and told me that he is now the shaykh of the Sufis in Zabīd and that he has not yet reached middle age."@en .

rec:AIND-D07105 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07105-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07105-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07105 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن إسماعيل بن أبي الحسن البرماوي . يأتي قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Abī al-Ḥasan al-Birmāwī. He will come shortly below."@en .

rec:AIND-D07106 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07106-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07106-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07106-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07106 ;
    aindv:sourceText "331 محمد بن إسماعيل بن طوغان السنهوري البرلسي ويعرف بجده طوغان الميموني . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Ṭūghān al-Sanhūrī al-Burullusī, known by (the name of) his grandfather Ṭūghān al-Maymūnī. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D07107 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07107-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07107-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07107-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07107 ;
    aindv:sourceText "332 محمد بن إسماعيل بن عبد الله بن عمر بن أبي بكر بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله أبو عبد الله الناشري . قال عمه القاضي أبو عبد الله : كان فقيها فاضلا صالحا سليم الصدر مباركا له في معيشته . مات بالكدراء سنة تسع . زاد العفيف وله حواش كثيرة دالة على فضله وحسن اشتغاله وناب عن عمه في الأحكام بسهام وكان آمرا بالمعروف ناهيا عن المنكر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Nāshirī. His paternal uncle the qāḍī Abū ʿAbd Allāh said: he was a jurist, virtuous, righteous, pure of heart, and blessed in his livelihood. He died in al-Kadrāʾ in the year (8)09. Al-ʿAfīf added: he had many glosses (ḥawāshī) indicating his merit and the quality of his studies; he deputized for his uncle in judicial affairs in Sihām, and he was one who enjoined good and forbade evil."@en .

rec:AIND-D07108 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07108-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07108-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07108 ;
    aindv:sourceText "333 محمد بن إسماعيل بن علوان الزبيدي ثم المهجمي . ولي قضاء المهجم مدة وكان نبيها في الفقه مشكور السيرة . مات في سنة تسع عشرة . قاله شيخنا في إنبائه . وفي اليمانيين آخر شاركه في الاسم والأب والجد ولكنه مات قبيل القرن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlwān al-Zabīdī, then al-Mahjamī. He held the judgeship of al-Mahjam for a time, and was astute in jurisprudence and of praised conduct. He died in the year (8)19; so said our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his Inbāʾ. Among the Yemenis there is another who shared with him the name, the father's name and the grandfather's name, but he died shortly before the (ninth) century."@en .

rec:AIND-D07112 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07112-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07112-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07112 ;
    aindv:sourceText "337 محمد بن إسماعيل بن علي البغدادي الأصل القاهري الحنبلي نزيل القراسنقرية ومؤدب ابن الأشقر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. ʿAlī, of Baghdādī origin, al-Qāhirī, the Ḥanbalī, resident of al-Qarāsunqurīya and tutor (muʾaddib) of Ibn al-Ashqar."@en .

rec:AIND-D07117 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07117-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07117-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07117 ;
    aindv:sourceText "342 محمد بن إسماعيل بن محمد بن الطنبغا ناصر الدين الدمرداشي الحنفي . مما أخذ عني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad b. al-Ṭunbughā, Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Damardāshī al-Ḥanafī. He was among those who took (learning) from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D07119 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07119-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07119-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07119 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن إسماعيل ابن محمد بن عبد الله الشمس القلهاتي المكي الشافعي والد محمود زائد . يأتي فيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Shams al-Qalhātī al-Makkī al-Shāfiʿī, the father of Maḥmūd Zāʾid. He will come below under him (the son)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07121 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07121-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07121-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07121 ;
    aindv:sourceText "345 محمد بن إسماعيل بن محمد أبو الرضا المصري ثم الطرابلسي الشافعي ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad, Abū al-Riḍā al-Miṣrī, then al-Ṭarābulusī, the Shāfiʿī. He was among those who heard from me in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D07122 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07122-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07122-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07122-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07122 ;
    aindv:sourceText "346 محمد بن إسماعيل بن محمد المقدسي . ممن سمع منى مكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad al-Maqdisī. He was among those who heard from me in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D07124 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07124-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07124-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07124-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07124 ;
    aindv:sourceText "348 محمد بن إسماعيل بن محمود الركن الخوافي سبط شارح اللباب . ولد في خامس ذي القعدة سنة ست وأربعين وسبعمائة ، وأخذ عنه الطاووسي شرح المختصر له والمواقف للايجي ، وقال كان رأسا في سائر العلوم محققا لطيف الطبع ممن أخذ عنه بمكة وزبيد الجلال عبد الواحد المرشدي النحو والأصول والمعاني والبيان وكتب له إجازة بليغة بخط حسن في سنة ثلاث وثمانمائة . ومات بهراة يوم الأحد ثامن عشرى شوال سنة أربع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Maḥmūd, al-Rukn al-Khawāfī, maternal grandson of the commentator of al-Lubāb. He was born on 5 Dhū al-Qaʿda 746. Al-Ṭāwūsī took from him his own commentary on al-Mukhtaṣar and al-Mawāqif of al-Ījī, and said: he was a leading authority in all the sciences, a thorough scholar of gentle disposition. Among those who took from him in Mecca and Zabīd was al-Jalāl ʿAbd al-Wāḥid al-Murshidī, who learned grammar, uṣūl, maʿānī and bayān, and for whom he wrote an eloquent ijāza in a fine hand in the year 803. He died in Herat on Sunday 28 Shawwāl 834."@en .

rec:AIND-D07125 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07125-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07125-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07125 ;
    aindv:sourceText "349 محمد بن إسماعيل بن أبي يزيد اليماني الأصل المكي الماضي أبوه . ولد بها في سنة خمس وسبعين . ممن سمع مني دراية ورواية بل قرأ على الشمائل بمكة وبالروضة النبوية أيضا وغير ذلك ، وهو متميز فاضل ملازم دروس القاضي كأبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Abī Yazīd, of Yemeni origin, al-Makkī; his father has been mentioned above. He was born there in the year (8)75. He was among those who heard from me with both understanding and transmission (dirāya wa-riwāya); indeed he read al-Shamāʾil to me in Mecca and also at the Prophet's Rawḍa, and other things besides. He is distinguished and accomplished, a constant attendant at the qāḍī's lessons like his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D07127 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07127-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07127-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07127-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07127 ;
    aindv:sourceText "351 محمد بن إسماعيل تاج الدين بن العماد البطرني المغربي الأصل الدمشقي المالكي . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه وقال : كان في خدمة القاضي علم الدين القفصي بل عمل نقيبه ثم بعد موته ولي قضاء طرابلس ثم رجع وناب عن المالكي . وكان عفيفا في مباشرته يستحضر طرفا من الفقه . مات بالطاعون في صفر سنة ثلاث وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl, Tāj al-Dīn b. al-ʿImād al-Baṭarnī, of Maghribī origin, al-Dimashqī, the Mālikī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ and said: he was in the service of the qāḍī ʿAlam al-Dīn al-Qafṣī, indeed he served as his naqīb; then after the latter's death he was appointed to the judgeship of Tripoli, then returned and deputized for the Mālikī (judge). He was upright in his conduct of office and had some fiqh at his command. He died of the plague in Ṣafar 833."@en .

rec:AIND-D07128 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07128-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07128-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07128 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن إسماعيل ركن الدين الخوافي . مضى فيمن جده محمود قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl, Rukn al-Dīn al-Khawāfī. He has been mentioned shortly above among those whose grandfather is Maḥmūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D07130 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07130-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07130-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07130-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b114_118_triage,
        agent:claude_b118_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07130 ;
    aindv:sourceText "353 محمد بن إسماعيل الشمس الحسني القاهري نزيل تربة سعيد السعداء بل تربتها وأحد صوفية الخانقاه ممن سمع بقراءتي بالقرا سنقرية الشمائل وغيرها . مات عن أزيد من ثمانين سنة فيما قيل في ربيع الثاني سنة أربع وثمانين ويذكر باعتقاد ابن عربي وبإدخاله غير الصوفية في التربة طمعا في ما يصل إليه عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl, al-Shams al-Ḥasanī al-Qāhirī, resident of the turba of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ — rather, of its turba — and one of the Sufis of the khānqāh. He was among those who heard, through my reading, al-Shamāʾil and other works at al-Qarāsunqurīya. He died, aged over eighty as was said, in Rabīʿ al-Thānī 884. He is spoken of for holding the beliefs of Ibn ʿArabī and for admitting non-Sufis into the turba out of desire for what would come to him from it. May God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07313 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07313-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07313-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07313 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد خامس الاربعة قبله . مات في يوم الاثنين ثالث عشر ربيع الآخر سنة أربع وخمسين ولم يكمل عشرة أشهر وصلى عليه أبوه بالقلعة ثم شيعه الاعيان من الامراء والمباشرين وغيرهم إلى أن دفن بالبرقوقية بين القصرين لكون أمه خوند ابنة أمير سلاح جرباش الكريمي التي أمها ابنة قانباى قريب الظاهر برقوق ودخلوا بنعشه من بابي زويلة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, the fifth after the four preceding him. He died on Monday, 13 Rabīʿ al-Ākhir 854, not having completed ten months of age. His father led the funeral prayer over him at the Citadel, and then the notables among the amirs, the administrators and others accompanied his bier until he was buried at al-Barqūqiyya in Bayn al-Qaṣrayn, because his mother was Khawand, the daughter of the Amīr Silāḥ Jarbāsh al-Karīmī, whose own mother was the daughter of Qānibāy, a relative of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq. They brought his bier in through the two gates of Bāb Zuwayla."@en .

rec:AIND-D07315 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07315-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07315-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07315 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن جلبان ناصر الدين أحد أمراء الشام وابن نائبها المؤيدي . مات في الوقعة السوارية سنة اثنتين وسبعين وهو في عنفوان الشبيبة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Julbān, Nāṣir al-Dīn, one of the amirs of Syria and the son of its viceroy, al-Muʾayyadī. He died in the Suwārī campaign (the battle against Shāh Suwār) in the year 872, in the prime of his youth."@en .

rec:AIND-D07317 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07317-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07317-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07317 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن جمعة الهمذاني الخواجا نزيل مكة وصاحب الدور بها الموقوفة أوجلها منه على درس المحنفية بالمسجد الحرام ، عين لمشيخة شيخ الباسطية وإمام الحنفية الشمس البخاري وباشره ثم تعطل بها مدة ولد الواقف . مات فجأة في آخر ليلة الاثنين ثاني ربيع الأول سنة ثمان وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Jumʿa al-Hamadhānī, al-Khawājā. A resident of Mecca and the owner of the endowed houses there, most of which he dedicated to a lesson for the Ḥanafīs in the Sacred Mosque. The shaykh of al-Bāsiṭiyya and imam of the Ḥanafīs, al-Shams al-Bukhārī, was appointed to preside over it, and he exercised it; then it was suspended for a period in the time of the endower's son. He died suddenly at the end of the night of Monday, 2 Rabīʿ al-Awwal 868. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D07318 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07318-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07318-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07318-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07318-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_apply3,
        agent:claude_b87b_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07318 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن الجنيد بن أحمد بن محمد بن عمر بن محمد بن عمر النور بن أبي القسم الكازروني البلياني الأصل الشيرازي الماضي أبوه والمذكور جده في الثامنة . قدم القاهرة في سنة ثمان وأربعين رسولا عن ملك الشرق بكسوة الكعبة واجتمع بشيخنا صحبة حسين الفتحي وصنف لأجله جزءا في الأذكار وآخر في إصلاح مشيخة أبيه لابن الجزري وأذن له في الرواية عنه ووصف بالعلامة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Junayd b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar, al-Nūr b. Abī al-Qāsim, al-Kāzarūnī, of Balyānī origin, al-Shīrāzī. His father has been mentioned above and his grandfather is recorded in the eighth [century]. He came to Cairo in the year 848 as an envoy of the King of the East, bringing the covering of the Kaʿba. He met our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in the company of Ḥusayn al-Fatḥī and composed for him a fascicle on the adhkār and another on the correction of his father's mashyakha compiled by Ibn al-Jazarī. He (Ibn Ḥajar) authorised him to transmit on his authority, and he was described as al-ʿAllāma."@en .

rec:AIND-D07320 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07320-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07320-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07320 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن جوهر المدير في الجيش . مات في رمضان سنة ست وثلاثين بحلب . أرخه شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Jawhar, the administrator (mudīr) in the army. He died in Ramaḍān 836 in Aleppo. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) recorded his death date in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07321 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07321-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07321-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07321-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_apply,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07321 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حاجي بن أحمد الشمس بن خواجا شهاب الدين بن الشهاب الهرموزي الأصل المكي الحنفي . ممن سمع مني بها في المجاورة الرابعة أربعي النووي وكثيرا من المصابيح وأشياء كالمشارق والبخاري ثم جميع الشفا وقرأ ما فاته ، وهو فطن لبيب قرأ على ثلاثيات البخاري وغيرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥājjī b. Aḥmad, al-Shams b. Khawājā Shihāb al-Dīn b. al-Shihāb, of Hormuzī origin, al-Makkī, al-Ḥanafī. He is among those who heard from me there (in Mecca), during the fourth period of residence (mujāwara), al-Nawawī's Forty Ḥadīths, much of al-Maṣābīḥ, some parts of works such as al-Mashāriq and al-Bukhārī, then the whole of al-Shifāʾ, and he read what he had missed. He is intelligent and sensible; he read to me the Thulāthiyyāt of al-Bukhārī and other things."@en .

rec:AIND-D07323 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07323-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07323-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07323 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أبي حامد المطري . في ابن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Abī Ḥāmid al-Maṭarī. Under [Muḥammad b.] Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad."@en .

rec:AIND-D07324 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07324-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07324-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07324 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أبي الحجاج واسمه يوسف بن محمد بن يوسف الأسيوطي الأصل القاهري الشافعي الآتي أبوه . ولد في ليلة رابع عشر رمضان سنة إحدى وخمسين بالقاهرة ونشأ بها في كنف أبيه فحفظ القرآن وأربعي النووي والبهجة وألفية النحو وغيرها ، وعرض على جماعة وأخذ في النحو عن خلد الوقاد وفي الفقه عن الجوجري وتدرب بأبيه في الصنعة وجلس بباب الحنفي ، وحج مع أبيه شاهد المحمل ، وكان معه في سنة ست وخمسين بمكة وهو صغير فأحضره اليسير بقراءتي ، وهو عاقل كيس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Abī al-Ḥajjāj (whose name is Yūsuf) b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf, of Asyūṭī origin, al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī; his father is mentioned below. He was born on the night of 14 Ramaḍān 851 in Cairo and grew up there under his father's care. He memorised the Qurʾān, al-Nawawī's Forty Ḥadīths, al-Bahja, the Alfiyya on grammar and other works, and presented them to a number of scholars. He took grammar from Khalad (Khālid) al-Waqqād and jurisprudence from al-Jawjarī. He was trained by his father in the profession (of notary-witness) and sat at the Ḥanafī (judge's) court. He performed the pilgrimage with his father, the witness of the maḥmal, and was with him in Mecca in the year 856 while still a boy, when his father had him attend a little at my recitation. He is intelligent and clever."@en .

rec:AIND-D07325 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07325-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07325-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07325-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07325 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حجاج . في ابن عبد الله بن حجاج ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥajjāj. Under [Muḥammad b.] ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥajjāj."@en .

rec:AIND-D07326 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07326-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07326-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07326 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حرير بمهملات ككبير جمال الدين كان مقيما بثغر عدن وللجمال محمد بن كبن فيه اعتقاد لكونه بشره في بعض عزلاته بالعود في غدفكان كذلك فرتب له راتبا وكان يسأله الدعاء. مات سنة اثنتين وأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥarīr (with undotted letters, on the pattern of kabīr), Jamāl al-Dīn. He resided in the port of Aden. Al-Jamāl Muḥammad b. Kabban had great faith in him, because during one of his (Ibn Kabban's) dismissals from office he gave him the good tidings that he would be restored the next day, and so it came to pass; so he assigned him a stipend and used to ask him for his prayers. He died in the year 842."@en .

rec:AIND-D07327 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07327-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07327-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07327 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسب الله جمال الدين المكي الزعيم التاجر . قال شيخنا في أنبائه : مات في ثالث جمادى الأولى سنة اثنتين وكان واسع المال جدا معروفا بالمعاملات وضبط من ماله بعده أكثر من عشرين ألف دينار سوى ما أخفى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasab Allāh, Jamāl al-Dīn, al-Makkī, al-Zaʿīm, the merchant. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Inbāʾ: \"He died on 3 Jumādā al-Ūlā 802. He was extremely wealthy and well known for commercial dealings; after his death more than twenty thousand dinars of his property were seized, apart from what he had concealed.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D07328 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07328-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07328-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07328-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07328 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسب الله الحريري المؤذن بجامع الحاكم وغيره ورأس المخاصمين للبقاعي في يا دائم المعروف ، وكان مقداما جريئا عريض الصوت جدا . مات بعد الثمانين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasab Allāh al-Ḥarīrī, the muezzin at the Mosque of al-Ḥākim and elsewhere, and the head of those who disputed with al-Biqāʿī over the well-known \"Yā Dāʾim\" (affair). He was bold and daring, with a very broad voice. He died after 880, so it is thought."@en .

rec:AIND-D07332 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07332-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07332-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07332 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن أحمد بن حسن بن علي بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بدر الدين بن بدر الدين بن الإمام الشهاب الأذرعي القاهري الماضي أبوه وجده ويلقب مامش . ولد في سنة اثنتين وأربعين وثمانمائة ، نشأ ظريفا في خدمة ابن حجي متميزا عنده فاشتغل قليلا وحج ثم بعده سكن ثم انتمى للبدري بن مزهر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Badr al-Dīn b. Badr al-Dīn b. al-Imām al-Shihāb al-Adhraʿī al-Qāhirī; his father and grandfather have been mentioned above. He is nicknamed Māmish. He was born in the year 842 and grew up as an elegant youth in the service of Ibn Ḥijjī, enjoying distinction with him. He studied a little and performed the pilgrimage, and after that he settled down. Later he attached himself to al-Badrī b. Muzhir."@en .

rec:AIND-D07334 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07334-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07334-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07334-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07334 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن أحمد بن محمد بن سلامة بن عطوف بن يعلي السلمي المكي . مات بمكة في شوال سنة أربع وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Salāma b. ʿAṭūf b. Yaʿlī al-Sulamī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Shawwāl 844. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D07337 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07337-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07337-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07337-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_apply,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07337 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن إلياس الجمال الرومي الحنفي . مات بمكة في رجب سنة ستين . أرخه ابن فهد ، وهو ممن اشتغل وتميز في الفقه وغيره وترافق مع أبي الوقت المرشدي بحيث كان يكاتبه وحصل كتبا ، وكان مع ذلك جيد الخط وباسمه نصف تكبير مقام الحنفية مع السبيل الذي أنشأه المؤيد بالمسجد تجاه الحجر الأسود إلى غير ذلك من مرتبات . ومات عن نحو الأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Ilyās, al-Jamāl al-Rūmī al-Ḥanafī. He died in Mecca in Rajab 860; Ibn Fahd recorded his death date. He was among those who studied and distinguished themselves in jurisprudence and other subjects. He kept company with Abū al-Waqt al-Murshidī, to the point that he corresponded with him, and he acquired books; he was, moreover, a fine calligrapher. Registered in his name were half of the takbīr post at the Ḥanafī maqām, together with the sabīl (public fountain) that al-Muʾayyad had built in the (Sacred) Mosque facing the Black Stone, and other stipends besides. He died at about forty years of age."@en .

rec:AIND-D07338 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07338-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07338-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07338 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن أبي بكر بن محمد جمال الدين العامري اليماني الحرضي الشافعي . لقيني في المحرم سنة أربع وتسعين بمكة وسنه دون الأربعين بقليل فقرأ على الأربعين للنووي قراءة طالب علم وسمع من لفظي المسلسل وكتبت له ، وهو من جماعة الشيخ يحيى العامري ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Abī Bakr b. Muḥammad, Jamāl al-Dīn al-ʿĀmirī al-Yamānī al-Ḥaraḍī al-Shāfiʿī. He met me in Muḥarram 894 in Mecca, when he was a little under forty years of age. He read to me al-Nawawī's Forty Ḥadīths with the reading of a student of learning, heard from my lips the Musalsal, and I wrote (an ijāza) for him. He is one of the circle of Shaykh Yaḥyā al-ʿĀmirī."@en .

rec:AIND-D07339 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07339-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07339-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07339 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن أبي بكر بن منصور الشمس الفارقي السلاوي ربيب الشمس السمرقندي العطار ولوجاهته عند تمر صارت لصاحب الترجمة وجاهة في أيام الفتنة فلما رحل عن دمشق أخذ وعوقب حتى مات في رجب سنة ثلاث . ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Abī Bakr b. Manṣūr, al-Shams al-Fāriqī al-Sallāwī, the stepson of al-Shams al-Samarqandī the druggist (al-ʿAṭṭār). Owing to the latter's standing with Timur, the subject of this entry also acquired standing in the days of the turmoil (fitna); but when he (Timur, or the subject) departed from Damascus, he was seized and punished until he died, in Rajab 803. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07340 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07340-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07340-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07340 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن حاتم الشمس النشيلي ثم القاهري الشافعي ربيب بواب سعيد السعداء . ممن اشتغل . مات في شعبان سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Ḥātim, al-Shams al-Nashīlī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, the stepson of the doorkeeper of (the khānqāh of) Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. He was among those who engaged in study. He died in Shaʿbān 891."@en .

rec:AIND-D07341 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07341-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07341-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07341 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن حسن بن حسين بن عقبة المدني المالكي نزيل حلب ويعرف بابن عقبة وبابن حسن أيضا . ولد في حدود سنة ثمانين وسبعمائة بالمدينة وقدم حلب على رأس القرن فقطنها وسمع على ابن صديق بعض الصحيح ، وكان خيرا محافظا على الجماعة كثير الحج له اشتغال يسير في الفقه . مات في حدود سنة خمسين . ونسبه بعضهم محمد بن حسن بن حسين بن علي بن عقبة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Ḥasan b. Ḥusayn b. ʿUqba al-Madanī al-Mālikī, resident of Aleppo, known as Ibn ʿUqba and also as Ibn Ḥasan. He was born around the year 780 in Medina, came to Aleppo at the turn of the century and settled there. He heard part of the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Ṣiddīq. He was a good man, regular in attending congregational prayer, performed the pilgrimage many times, and had a little occupation with jurisprudence. He died around the year 850. Some give his lineage as Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. ʿUqba."@en .

rec:AIND-D07342 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07342-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07342-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07342 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن حسين بن علي بن عبد الدائم المحب بن البدر الأميوطي الأصل القاهري الحسيني سكنا الماضي أبوه . ولد في ثالث عشر ذي الحجة سنة خمس وثلاثين وثمانمائة ولازمني في الإملاء وغيرها مدة وتكسب بالشهادة وتجرع فاقة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Dāʾim, al-Muḥibb, son of al-Badr, of Amyūṭ by origin, al-Qāhirī, resident of the Ḥusayniyya quarter. His father was mentioned previously. He was born on 13 Dhū al-Ḥijja 835 AH. He attended my (al-Sakhāwī's) dictation sessions and other classes for a period of time. He earned his living as a notary-witness and endured poverty."@en .

rec:AIND-D07344 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07344-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07344-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07344-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_verify_mech,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07344 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد المحب أبو الفضل الكاتب نزيل القاهرة وأخو الذى قبله واسمه المدعو به عبد الرحمن . مضى."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, al-Muḥibb, Abū al-Faḍl, the scribe, resident of Cairo. He is the brother of the preceding entry, and the name by which he is called is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. Already mentioned."@en .

rec:AIND-D07345 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07345-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07345-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07345 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن أبي الخير البلبيسي ثم القاهري الأزهري المالكي . ممن اشتغل ، وله ولد عرض علي كتبا في سنة ست وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Abī al-Khayr al-Bilbīsī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Azharī, the Mālikī. He was among those who occupied themselves with study. He has a son who recited books before me (al-Sakhāwī) in the year 896 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D07347 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07347-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07347-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07347 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن السمين اليمني . ولد في جمادى الثانية سنة ست وأربعين وسبعمائة ، روى عن خاله المحدث أحمد بن إبراهيم العسيلي عن العفيف اليافعي إجازة ، وذكره التقي بن فهد في معجمه . ويحرر اسم جده ونسبة شيخه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. al-Samīn al-Yamanī. He was born in Jumādā al-Thāniya of the year 746 AH. He narrated from his maternal uncle, the muḥaddith Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm al-ʿUsaylī, who [narrated] from al-ʿAfīf al-Yāfiʿī by ijāza. Al-Taqī b. Fahd mentioned him in his Muʿjam. The name of his grandfather and the nisba of his shaykh remain to be verified."@en .

rec:AIND-D07348 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07348-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07348-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07348 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن سويد الشمس بن البدر المصري المالكي أخو الوجيه عبد الرحمن وصاحب الترجمة أكبر والوجيه أنبه لتقريب إبيهما له ، وهو والد الصدر محمد وعائشة سبطي الجلال البلقيني . مات سنة أربع وثلاثين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. Suwayd, al-Shams, son of al-Badr, al-Miṣrī, the Mālikī. He was the brother of al-Wajīh ʿAbd al-Raḥmān; the subject of this entry was the elder, but al-Wajīh was the more prominent because their father kept him close. He was the father of al-Ṣadr Muḥammad and ʿĀʾisha, both of whom were grandchildren (through their mother) of al-Jalāl al-Bulqīnī. He died in approximately the year 834 AH."@en .

rec:AIND-D07350 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07350-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07350-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07350 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن عبد الرحيم الصالي الدقاق . قال شيخنا في معجمه لقيته بالصالحية فقرأت عليه أخبار إبراهيم بن أدهم وغيرها بحضوره في الثالثة على الحجار ومات في الكائنة العظمى سنة ثلاث ، وتبعه المقريزي في عقوده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Ṣālī al-Daqqāq. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) said in his Muʿjam: \"I met him in al-Ṣāliḥiyya and read to him the Akhbār Ibrāhīm b. Adham and other works, which he had attended [as a child] in his third year under al-Ḥajjār. He died in the great calamity (Tīmūr's sack of Damascus) in the year 803.\" Al-Maqrīzī followed him in this in his ʿUqūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D07353 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07353-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07353-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07353-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_apply2,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07353 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن عبد الوهاب ناصر الدين الطرابلسي ثم القاهري الشافعي . ولد كما بخطه في سنة أربع وستين وسبعمائة وقال إنه سمع بطرابلس على الشهاب أحمد بن الحبال وابن البدر وقدم القاهرة فأخذ عن العز بن جماعة ولازم دروسه في فنونه ثم لازم بعده تلميذه الجمال الأمشاطي ، لقيه ابن الأسيوطي قريب سنة سبعين وقال إنه كان مستحضرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, Nāṣir al-Dīn, al-Ṭarābulusī, then al-Qāhirī, the Shāfiʿī. He was born, according to his own handwriting, in the year 764 AH. He stated that he heard [hadith] in Tripoli from al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. al-Ḥabbāl and Ibn al-Badr. He came to Cairo and studied under al-ʿIzz b. Jamāʿa, attending his lectures in his various disciplines assiduously, and after him he attached himself to his pupil al-Jamāl al-Amshāṭī. Ibn al-Asyūṭī met him around the year 870 AH and said that he had a ready memory."@en .

rec:AIND-D07355 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07355-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07355-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07355 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن علي بن جبريل المحلى ثم القاهري ويعرف بابن شطية . ممن سمع على شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Jibrīl al-Maḥallī, then al-Qāhirī, known as Ibn Shaṭiyya. He was among those who heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07357 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07357-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07357-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07357 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن علي بن سليمان بن عمر بن محمد الشمس الحلبي الحنفي الآتي ولده وحفيده المسمى كل منهم محمد ويعرف بالموقت وبابن أمير حاج . كان فاضلا في فنون من العلم مدرسا بالجردكية بارعا في الوقت ولذا باشره بجامع بلده الكبير وانتقلت وظيفة التوقيت والتدريس بعده لولده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. Sulaymān b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad, al-Shams al-Ḥalabī al-Ḥanafī. His son and his grandson, each named Muḥammad, are mentioned below. He was known as al-Muwaqqit and as Ibn Amīr Ḥājj. He was accomplished in various branches of learning, a teacher (mudarris) at al-Jardakiyya, and excelled in timekeeping, for which reason he held that post at the Great Mosque of his town. After him the posts of timekeeping and teaching passed to his son."@en .

rec:AIND-D07359 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07359-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07359-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07359 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن حسن بن علي بن عبد الرحمن الشمس القاهري الصوفي الشافعي ويعرف بابن الأستاذ لكون أبيه كان أستادار قرقماس الشعباني . ولد في سنة ست وعشرين ونشأ ... وكتب عند بعض المباشرين وسمع على بعض السيرة في سنة خمس وتسعين ثم بعض الدلائل في التي تليها ، وأثكل ولدا له فصبر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ḥasan b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-Shams, al-Qāhirī, al-Ṣūfī, the Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Ustādh because his father had been the ustādār (majordomo) of Qurqumās al-Shaʿbānī. He was born in the year 826 AH and grew up ... He worked as a scribe under some administrators (mubāshirūn). He heard part of the Sīra from me (al-Sakhāwī) in the year 895 AH, then part of the Dalāʾil in the following year. He lost a son and bore it with patience."@en .

rec:AIND-D07367 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07367-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07367-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07367-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_apply,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07367 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن خليل بن يعقوب بدر الدين الواعظ نزيل جامع الحاكم وأخو أحمد الماضي وصهر أخي . قرأ القرآن وتولع بالوعظ في المشاهد ونحوها ، وانجمع إلى أن غرق بصهريج الحاكم في شوال سنة اثنتين وتسعين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Khalīl b. Yaʿqūb, Badr al-Dīn, the preacher (al-wāʿiẓ), resident of the Mosque of al-Ḥākim, brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad and brother-in-law of my (al-Sakhāwī's) brother. He recited the Qurʾān and was devoted to preaching at the shrines (al-mashāhid) and similar places. He lived withdrawn until he drowned in the cistern of al-Ḥākim in Shawwāl of the year 892 AH. May God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07370 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07370-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07370-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07370 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن خورشيد جمال الدين بن شمس وهو معنى خورشيد بالفارسي الشرواني الأصل السكنبايتي نزيل مكة . شاب قرأ على بعض الأربعين النووية وأكمل سماعها وسمع غير ذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Khūrshīd, Jamāl al-Dīn b. Shams — \"Shams\" being the meaning of Khūrshīd in Persian — of Shirwān origin, al-Sakanbāyitī, resident of Mecca. A young man. He read part of al-Arbaʿūn al-Nawawiyya to me (al-Sakhāwī), completed hearing it, and heard other things besides."@en .

rec:AIND-D07371 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07371-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07371-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07371 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن أبي الخير بن محمد بن عمر الدمنهوري الأصل المكي الحريري الآتي أبوه ويعرف بابن أبي الخير الدمنهوري . اشتغل في الميقات وتميز فيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Abī al-Khayr b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar, of Damanhūr by origin, al-Makkī, al-Ḥarīrī (the silk-merchant). His father is mentioned below. He was known as Ibn Abī al-Khayr al-Damanhūrī. He occupied himself with timekeeping (mīqāt) and distinguished himself in it."@en .

rec:AIND-D07374 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07374-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07374-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07374 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن داود بن عثمان بن علي القرشي الهاشمس أحد مباشري جدة ويعرف أبوه بالنظام . مات بمكة في ربيع الأول سنة ثلاث وستين . أرخه ابن فهد وكان له أخ اسمه عبد الله سمع في سنة أربع عشرة على الزين المراغي ووصف أبوهما بالشيخ ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Dāwūd b. ʿUthmān b. ʿAlī al-Qurashī al-Hāshimī, one of the administrators (mubāshirūn) of Jedda. His father was known as al-Niẓām. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 863 AH. Ibn Fahd recorded his date. He had a brother named ʿAbd Allāh, who heard [hadith] in the year 814 AH from al-Zayn al-Marāghī, and their father was described as \"al-Shaykh\"."@en .

rec:AIND-D07375 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07375-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07375-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07375-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07375 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن الخواجا داود بن علي بن البهاء الكيلاني الماضي أبوه . مات في اسكندرية سنة اثنتين وأربعين كأبيه وأخويه سليمان وعلي . أرخهم ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Khawājā Dāwūd b. ʿAlī b. al-Bahāʾ al-Kīlānī. His father was mentioned previously. He died in Alexandria in the year 842 AH, like his father and his two brothers Sulaymān and ʿAlī. Ibn Fahd recorded their dates."@en .

rec:AIND-D07377 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07377-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07377-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07377 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن داود بن محمد بن داود الشمس أبو عبد الله المكيسي بميم وكاف ومهملة مصغر من قرى حوران الدمشقي الشافعي . ولد سنة سبع وتسعين وسبعمائة ظنا وسمع من عائشة ابنة ابن عبد الهادي وغيرها وتفقه ودرس . وناب في القضاء بدمشق وأخذ عنه غير واحد منهم أبو العباس المقدسي ووصفه البقاعي بالعلامة . مات في ليلة الأحد تاسع عشر صفر سنة أربعين بدمشق ودفن بمقبرة الباب الصغير رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Dāwūd b. Muḥammad b. Dāwūd, al-Shams Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Mukaysī — with mīm, kāf and undotted sīn, in the diminutive, from one of the villages of Ḥawrān — al-Dimashqī, the Shāfiʿī. He was born presumably in 797 AH, heard from ʿĀʾisha bint Ibn ʿAbd al-Hādī and others, studied jurisprudence and taught. He served as deputy judge in Damascus, and more than one person studied under him, among them Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maqdisī; al-Biqāʿī described him as \"al-ʿallāma\". He died on the night of Sunday, 19 Ṣafar 840 AH, in Damascus, and was buried in the cemetery of Bāb al-Ṣaghīr. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07378 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07378-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07378-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07378 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن داود بن محمد بن أبي القسم الحكمي اليماني الماضي أبوه . خلفه في القيام بزاويته على خير وبركة وهو الآن في الأحياء . ممن حج وزار وأخذ عنه الذي بعده بمكة وغيرها . وحكى لي عنه أحوالا صالحة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Dāwūd b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Qāsim al-Ḥakamī al-Yamānī. His father was mentioned previously. He succeeded him in running his zāwiya, with goodness and blessing, and he is at present among the living. He was among those who performed the pilgrimage and the visitation, and the person mentioned after him studied under him in Mecca and elsewhere, and related to me (al-Sakhāwī) good accounts of him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07380 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07380-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07380-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07380 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن داود البازلي الكردي ثم الحموي الشافعي . ارتحل لتبريز فأقام بها نحو عشر سنين واشتغل بها وبرع ثم قدم حلب ثم القصير وخطب بها وتزوج ونقلها لحماة فقطنها وصار مدرسها وشيخها في العقليات مع فضيلة في الفقه وترقى بعد الفاقة وزوج بنته في بيت البارزي وهو الآن حي في سنة خمس وتسعين ويقال إنه جاز الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Dāwūd al-Bāzilī al-Kurdī, then al-Ḥamawī, the Shāfiʿī. He travelled to Tabrīz and stayed there for about ten years, studying there and excelling. Then he came to Aleppo, then to al-Quṣayr, where he preached (as khaṭīb) and married, and he moved her (his wife) to Ḥamāh and settled there. He became its teacher (mudarris) and its shaykh in the rational sciences, together with excellence in jurisprudence. He rose in standing after poverty and married his daughter into the house of al-Bārizī. He is at present alive, in the year 895 AH, and is said to have passed fifty."@en .

rec:AIND-D07381 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07381-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07381-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07381 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن داود البدراني شيخ تلك الناحية المنزلة ومنية بدران وما يجاورهما ووالد أحمد وعلي . أحد من لقيني بمكة في موسم سنة ثمان وتسعين وقرأ على أكبرهما وأجزت لهما ويعرف كل منهم بابن داود ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Dāwūd al-Badrānī, the shaykh of that district — al-Manzila, Minyat Badrān and their surroundings — and the father of Aḥmad and ʿAlī. He was one of those who met me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca during the pilgrimage season of the year 898 AH; the elder of the two [sons] read to me, and I granted both of them an ijāza. Each of them is known as Ibn Dāwūd."@en .

rec:AIND-D07382 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07382-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07382-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07382 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن الأمير دقماق ناصر الدين الماضي أبوه . ولاه الأشرف برسباي نيابة المرقب وأنعم عليه بأمرة طبلخاناه بطرابلس بعد أن استقدمه من حلب وبالغ في إكرامه لكونه منسوبا إلى أبيه كما تقدم فدام بالمرقب مدة ثم عزله وأنعم عليه بأمرة عشرة بالقاهرة ، واستمر بها حتى مات في طاعون سنة ثلاث وثلاثين ، وكان مليح الشكل رأسا في رمي النشاب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Amīr Duqmāq, Nāṣir al-Dīn; his father has been mentioned above. Al-Ashraf Barsbāy appointed him nāʾib of al-Marqab and granted him an amirate of ṭablkhānāh in Tripoli after summoning him from Aleppo, and treated him with great honour because of his connection to his father, as mentioned earlier. He remained in al-Marqab for a time, then was dismissed and granted an amirate of ten in Cairo, where he stayed until he died in the plague of the year 833. He was handsome in appearance and a leading archer."@en .

rec:AIND-D07429a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07429a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07429a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سعيد بن محمد بن عبد الوهاب بن علي بن يوسف فتح الدين أبو الفتح بن الجمال بن الفتح أبي الفتح الأنصاري الزرندي المدني الحنفي ابن قاضي المدينة وأخو علي قاضيها الماضيين وهو بكنيته أشهر . ولد في ... بالمدينة ونشأ فحفظ القرآن والشاطبية والقدوري والمنار وألفية النحو ، وعرض علي الأبشيطي وأبي الفرج المراغي وغيرهما كالأميني الأقصرائي حين دخل القاهرة صحبة والده سنة إحدى وسبعين بل أخذ عنه شرح المجمع لابن فرشتا تقسيما وكان أحد القراء فيه وكذا قرأ عليه صحيح مسلم والشمائل وغيرهما ، وتكرر دخوله للقاهرة بحيث أخذ عن الصلاح الطرابلسي وقرأ على البرهان الكركي الشفا وحضر دروسه واشتغل على والده بل قرأ عليه البخاري وكذا الشفا ، وحضر في العربية عند الأبشيطي وسمع الكثير على أبي الفرج المراغي بل قرأ عليه البخاري وأخذ عن الشيخ حميد الدين النعماني في أيام الموسم ، وسمع مني بالمدينة ، وهو متحرك بالنسبة لأخيه وباشر الحسبة والقضاء عن أبيه ثم عن أخيه وكذا عن شاهين الجمالي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Saʿīd b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf, Fatḥ al-Dīn Abū al-Fatḥ b. al-Jamāl b. al-Fatḥ Abī al-Fatḥ al-Anṣārī al-Zarandī al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī, son of the qadi of Medina and brother of ʿAlī, its qadi, both mentioned above; best known by his kunya. Born in [year missing] in Medina, he grew up there and memorised the Qurʾān, the Shāṭibiyya, the Qudūrī, the Manār and the Alfiyya on grammar, which he presented to al-Abshīṭī, Abū al-Faraj al-Marāghī and others, and to al-Amīn al-Aqṣarāʾī when he entered Cairo with his father in 871; from the latter he also took Ibn Firishtā's commentary on the Majmaʿ by divided reading, being one of its readers, and read to him Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim and the Shamāʾil. He entered Cairo repeatedly, studied with al-Ṣalāḥ al-Ṭarābulusī, read the Shifāʾ to al-Burhān al-Karakī and attended his lessons, studied with his father, reading to him al-Bukhārī and the Shifāʾ, attended al-Abshīṭī for Arabic, heard much from Abū al-Faraj al-Marāghī and read al-Bukhārī to him, studied with Shaykh Ḥamīd al-Dīn al-Nuʿmānī during the pilgrimage season, and heard from me in Medina. He is active compared with his brother, and served as deputy in the ḥisba and the judgeship for his father, then for his brother, and likewise for Shāhīn al-Jamālī."@en .

rec:AIND-D07431 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07431-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07431-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07431-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07431 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سعيد الشمس الوراق أبوه وأحد التجار هو . سافر لمكة وغيرها وأظنه نسب لجده . مات في جمادى الثانية سنة ثمان وثمانين وما أظنه بلغ الخمسين وكان طائشا رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Saʿīd, al-Shams. His father was a paper-seller (warrāq), and he himself was one of the merchants. He travelled to Mecca and elsewhere, and I think he was named after his grandfather. He died in Jumādā al-Thāniya of the year 888, and I do not think he had reached fifty. He was a reckless man; may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07444 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07444-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07444-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07444-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07444 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سلمان بن محمد الشمس الشنباري القاهري الشافعي . قرأ القراءات وقرأ على الديمي في البخاري من نسخة بخطه وكذا قرأ علي فيه ، وحج سنة السلطان صحبة ابنة العلم البلقيني وكان منزلا في سبعها وربما أقرأ الأبناء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Salmān b. Muḥammad, al-Shams al-Shanbārī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī. He studied the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt), and read al-Bukhārī before al-Daymī from a copy in the latter's own hand; likewise he read it before me (al-Sakhāwī). He performed the pilgrimage in the year of the Sultan's pilgrimage in the company of the daughter of al-ʿAlam al-Bulqīnī, being enrolled in her sabʿ (Qurʾān-recitation endowment), and he sometimes taught boys."@en .

rec:AIND-D07445 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07445-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07445-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07445-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07445 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سليمان بن أحمد بن إبراهيم بن عبد الملك الشمس بن العلم القاهري الأصل الدمياطي الشافعي ويعرف بابن الفقيه سليمان وأبوه بالسنباطي . ولد سنة سبعين وسبعمائة تقريبا بدمياط وحفظ بها القرآن وصلى به وهو ابن تسع سنين وشهر ، والعمدة في أربعين يوما والمنهاج الفرعي وعرض على ناصر الدين بن الميلق وجماعة وبحث على قاضي بلده التاج عتيق وتعاني نظم الشعر من غير تقدم اشتغال له في العروض والنحو مع كون كله موزونا وعدم اللحن فيه ، لقيه ابن فهد والبقاعي في سنة ثمان وثلاثين بدمياط وكتبا عنه أشياء منها : %~% إن التواضع أصل كل جميل %~% والعلم يوجب عز كل ذليل %~% %~% من كثرته النفس فهو مقلل %~% فالنفس في القرناء شر خليل %~% %~% والعقل أعظم نعمة تأتي الفتى %~% من ربه فالعقل خير دليل %~% ونظم المولد النبوي وأشياء ، وكان خيرا بهيا منورا ذا سكينة ووقار . مات بدمياط في سادس عشري ذي القعدة سنة اثنتين أو ثلاث وأربعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sulaymān b. Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Malik, al-Shams b. al-ʿAlam, of Cairene origin, al-Dimyāṭī, al-Shāfiʿī; known as Ibn al-Faqīh Sulaymān, while his father was known as al-Sunbāṭī. He was born around the year 770 in Damietta, where he memorized the Qurʾān and led the prayer with it when he was nine years and one month old. He memorized al-ʿUmda in forty days, as well as al-Minhāj al-Farʿī, and presented them to Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Maylaq and a group of others. He studied by discussion under the judge of his town, al-Tāj ʿAtīq. He applied himself to composing poetry without any prior study of prosody or grammar, yet all of it was correctly metred and free of grammatical error. Ibn Fahd and al-Biqāʿī met him in the year 838 in Damietta and wrote down from him various pieces, among them: \"Humility is the root of every beautiful thing, and knowledge brings honour to every lowly one. He whom the self makes great is in truth made small, for the self is the worst of friends among companions. Reason is the greatest blessing that comes to a young man from his Lord, for reason is the best guide.\" He also composed a poem on the Prophet's birth (al-Mawlid al-Nabawī) and other things. He was a good, handsome and radiant man, possessed of calm and dignity. He died in Damietta on the twenty-sixth of Dhū al-Qaʿda in the year 842 or 843; may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07448 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07448-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07448-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07448 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سليمان بن حماد الشمس السكندري الشافعي ويعرف بابن حماد . كان بارعا في الفرائض والحساب أخذهما عن الشمس جنيبات وفي علم الميقات وكذا في الشروط أخذهما عن شعبان ولد الشمس شيخه وتكسب بها ، وباشر في جامع صفوان بل يقرأ فيه البخاري ، وكان خيرا خج وجاور ثم عاد فبمجرد وصوله لمنزله مات وذلك في مستهل جمادى الآخرة سنة خمس وسبعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sulaymān b. Ḥammād, al-Shams al-Sakandarī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn Ḥammād. He excelled in the law of inheritance and in arithmetic, both of which he took from al-Shams Junaybāt; and he took the science of timekeeping (mīqāt) as well as notarial drafting (shurūṭ) from Shaʿbān, the son of al-Shams, his teacher, and earned his living by them. He held a post in the Ṣafwān Mosque, and indeed used to read al-Bukhārī there. He was a good man; he performed the pilgrimage and sojourned (in Mecca), then returned, and died the moment he reached his home, at the beginning of Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year 875; may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07452 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07452-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07452-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07452 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سليمان بن داود الطائفي الغمري ثم القاهري نزيل جامع الغمري بها . ممن خدم أبا العباس وعرف به وحج معه وسمع على أشياء ولا بأس به ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sulaymān b. Dāwūd al-Ṭāʾifī al-Ghamrī, then al-Qāhirī, a resident of the Ghamrī Mosque there. He was among those who served Abū al-ʿAbbās and became known through him; he performed the pilgrimage with him, and he heard various things from me (al-Sakhāwī). There is nothing wrong with him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07453 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07453-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07453-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07453 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سليمان بن داود اللاري المؤذن . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sulaymān b. Dāwūd al-Lārī, the muezzin. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D07457 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07457-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07457-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07457 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سليمان بن وهبان المدني عم سليمان الماضي . سمع على الزين المراغي في سنة خمس عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sulaymān b. Wahbān al-Madanī, the paternal uncle of the aforementioned Sulaymān. He heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī in the year 815."@en .

rec:AIND-D07458 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07458-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07458-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07458 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سليمان الحكري ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sulaymān al-Ḥakrī."@en .

rec:AIND-D07459 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07459-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07459-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07459 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سليمان الفيومي بواب الزمامية بمكة ، ذكره ابن فهد مجردا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sulaymān al-Fayyūmī, the doorkeeper of al-Zamāmiyya in Mecca. Ibn Fahd mentioned him with the bare name only."@en .

rec:AIND-D07461 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07461-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07461-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07461 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سنقر أبو السعود الجمالي نزيل مكة وشاد عمارة السلطان مع الحسبة . سمع مني هو وأبوه المسلسل وحديث زهير العشاري وكتبت لهما إجازة بل قرأ على الأربعين النووية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sunqur, Abū al-Suʿūd al-Jamālī, a resident of Mecca, superintendent of the Sultan's building works together with the ḥisba. He and his father heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) al-Musalsal and the ḥadīth of Zuhayr al-ʿUshārī, and I wrote an ijāza for the two of them; indeed, he read al-Arbaʿīn al-Nawawiyya before me."@en .

rec:AIND-D07462 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07462-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07462-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07462 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سنقر الأمير ناصر الدين الاستادار، مات سنة تسع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sunqur, the amir Nāṣir al-Dīn, the ustādār. He died in the year 809."@en .

rec:AIND-D07463 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07463-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07463-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07463 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سنقر الشرفي نسبة لابن شرف الدين صاحب الجامع الشهير بالحسينية لكون والده مولاه ويعرف بلغيلغ . مات في جمادى الآخرة سنة ستين ودفن خلف تربة الصوفية الصغرى . أرخه ابن المنير وقال كان أميا له كلمات حسنة وخبرة بالصالحين وللناس فيه اعتقاد رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sunqur al-Sharafī, so called after Ibn Sharaf al-Dīn, the owner of the famous mosque in al-Ḥusayniyya, because his father was the latter's freedman (mawlā); he was known as Lughaylagh. He died in Jumādā al-Ākhira of the year 860 and was buried behind the Lesser Sufi Mausoleum (Turbat al-Ṣūfiyya al-Ṣughrā). Ibn al-Munīr recorded his death and said that he was illiterate but had fine sayings and knowledge of the righteous, and that people held him in (spiritual) esteem; may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07464 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07464-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07464-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07464 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سنقر ابن أخت تغري بردى القادري . اعتنى به خاله فأسمعه مع ولدي شيئا . ومات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sunqur, the sister's son of Taghrī Birdī al-Qādirī. His maternal uncle took care of him and had him hear something together with my (al-Sakhāwī's) son. And he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D07465 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07465-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07465-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07465 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سودون دقماق ناصر الدين . أحد المقطعين والماضي أبوه والآتية أمه عائشة ابنة الأمير ناصر الدين محمد بن العطار وأخته لأمه فاطمة ابنة طيبغا ، وهو الآن حي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sūdūn Duqmāq, Nāṣir al-Dīn, one of the iqṭāʿ-holders. His father has been mentioned above, and his mother ʿĀʾisha, the daughter of the amir Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad b. al-ʿAṭṭār, will be mentioned below; his uterine sister is Fāṭima, the daughter of Ṭaybughā. He is still alive at present."@en .

rec:AIND-D07466 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07466-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07466-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07466 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سويد الشمس المصري أخو البدر حسن . مات سنة أربع وعشرين بالصعيد ، ذكره شيخنا في أنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Suwayd, al-Shams al-Miṣrī, the brother of al-Badr Ḥasan. He died in the year 824 in Upper Egypt (al-Ṣaʿīd). Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07467 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07467-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07467-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07467 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن سيف بن محمد بن عمر بن بشارة . مات مقتولا بالقاهرة وحشي جلده تبنا وحمل إلى صفد في ذي الحجة سنة تسع عشرة . ذكره شيخنا أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Sayf b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. Bishāra. He was killed in Cairo; his skin was stuffed with straw and carried to Ṣafad, in Dhū al-Ḥijja of the year 819. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) also mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07470 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07470-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07470-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07470 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن شاش شرف الدين أحد الموقعين . مات في رمضان سنة ست وأربعين ودفن بتربتهم بالقرافة . ذكره العيني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Shāsh, Sharaf al-Dīn, one of the muwaqqiʿs (chancery clerks). He died in Ramaḍān of the year 846 and was buried in their family tomb in al-Qarāfa. Al-ʿAynī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07472 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07472-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07472-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07472 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن شعبان بن علي بن شعبان الشمس الغزي الشافعي نزيل البرقوقية من القاهرة وشقيق أحمد وعبد القادر الماضيين وهو أسن الثلاثة . اشتغل في الفقه وأصوله والعربية وغيرها ، وأخذ عن العبادي والجوجري وأبي السعادات والزيني زكريا والشرف بن الجيعان وآخرين ، وسمع مني أشياء ولا نسبة له من أخيه مع فاقته وحج وجاور يسيرا ودخل الشام للتكسب وقطن القاهرة وسكن البرقوقية واستقر أحد المعيدين بالصالحية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Shaʿbān b. ʿAlī b. Shaʿbān, al-Shams al-Ghazzī al-Shāfiʿī, a resident of the Barqūqiyya in Cairo, full brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad and ʿAbd al-Qādir, and the eldest of the three. He occupied himself with jurisprudence, its principles, Arabic and other subjects, and took from al-ʿAbbādī, al-Jawjarī, Abū al-Saʿādāt, al-Zaynī Zakariyyā, al-Sharaf b. al-Jīʿān and others, and heard various things from me (al-Sakhāwī). He bears no comparison with his brother, and was moreover in poverty. He performed the pilgrimage and sojourned briefly, entered Syria to earn a living, then settled in Cairo, lived in the Barqūqiyya, and was appointed one of the repetitors (muʿīd) at the Ṣāliḥiyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D07473 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07473-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07473-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07473 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن شعبان بن محمد البوتيجي ثم القاهري الشافعي قريب شيخنا الزين البوتيجي . إنسان يخر أصيل وجيه قرأ القرآن وحفظ بعض الكتب واشتغل قليلا وحضر دروس الولي العراقي بل سمع في أماليه كما رأيته مثبتا بخط المعلى في مجالس . وتنزل في الجهات وباشر في بعض جهات الجوالي . مات قريبا من سنة سبعين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Shaʿbān b. Muḥammad al-Būtījī, then al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī, a relative of our shaykh al-Zayn al-Būtījī. He was a good man, of good family and standing. He recited the Qurʾān, memorized some books and studied a little; he attended the lessons of al-Walī al-ʿIrāqī, and indeed heard his dictations (amālī), as I saw recorded in the hand of al-Muʿallā in the session records. He held stipendiary posts in various institutions and served as a clerk in some of the offices of the jawālī (poll-tax). He died, as far as I suppose, around the year 870."@en .

rec:AIND-D07475 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07475-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07475-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88b_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07475 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن شعبان الشمس محتسب القاهرة . ولد تقريبا سنة ثمانين وسبعمائة وكان عريا عن الفضائل بل عاميا محضا ومع ذلك فولي الحسبة زيادة على عشرين مرة بالبذل بحيث كان يتبجح بذلك ويفتخر به مع أن المؤيد ضربه مرة على رجليه وألزمه بعدم السعي فيها وما انفك إلى أن افتقر وصار تعتريه المفاصل ، ثم مات في حادي عشري شوال سنة أربع وأربعين قال المقريزي وكان لا فضل ولا فضيلة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Shaʿbān, al-Shams, the muḥtasib of Cairo. He was born around the year 780. He was devoid of accomplishments, indeed a mere commoner; nevertheless he held the ḥisba more than twenty times through payment, to the point that he used to boast and pride himself on it, even though al-Muʾayyad once had him beaten on his feet and ordered him not to seek it again. He did not desist until he became impoverished and was afflicted with joint disease. He then died on the twenty-first of Shawwāl of the year 844. Al-Maqrīzī said: he had neither merit nor virtue."@en .

rec:AIND-D07476 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07476-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07476-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07476 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن شعبان الحسيني ويعرف بالطيبقي . ممن كتب على مجموع البدري بعد السبعين وما عرفته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Shaʿbān al-Ḥusaynī, known as al-Ṭaybaqī. One of those who wrote on al-Badrī's Majmūʿ after [8]70 AH, but I did not know him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07477 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07477-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07477-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07477 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن شعبة بدر الدين الفارسكوري شيخ تلك الناحية ومدركها ، ابتنى فيها مدرسة بقرب بيته وقرر الشهاب البيجوري مدرسها ، وفيه ميل للخير ومحبة في الفقراء مع ما هو فيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Shuʿba, Badr al-Dīn al-Fāriskūrī, the shaykh of that district and its man of authority. He built a madrasa there near his house and appointed al-Shihāb al-Bījūrī as its teacher. He has an inclination to good works and a love for the poor, despite the (worldly) position he is in."@en .

rec:AIND-D07478 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07478-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07478-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07478 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن شعرة أبو الفضل الصعيدي الأزهري الشافعي . ممن أخذ عن السنتاوي."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Shaʿra, Abū al-Faḍl al-Ṣaʿīdī al-Azharī al-Shāfiʿī. One of those who studied under al-Sintāwī."@en .

rec:AIND-D07479 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07479-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07479-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07479 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن شعيب الغمري والد أحمد الماضي . رجل صالح قانت متعبد ورع له أحوال وكرامات واختصاص بالشيخ محمد الغمري بل كان أجل أصحابه حتى أنه استخلفه عليهم وأقام عنده بالمحلة كثيرا سمعت الثناء عليه من غير واحد من ضابطيهم . مات تقريبا سنة ثلاث وخمسين أو التي تليها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Shuʿayb al-Ghamrī, the father of Aḥmad, mentioned above. A righteous, devout, worshipful and scrupulous man who had spiritual states and miracles (karāmāt), and a special attachment to Shaykh Muḥammad al-Ghamrī; indeed he was the most eminent of his companions, so much so that the Shaykh appointed him as his deputy over them, and he stayed with him in al-Maḥalla for long periods. I heard praise of him from more than one of their reliable men. He died approximately in the year [8]53 or the following one."@en .

rec:AIND-D07483 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07483-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07483-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07483 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن شهري الأمير ناصر الدين حاجب الحجاب بحلب . قتل في وقعة آمد مع جكم سنة تسع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Shahrī, the Amīr Nāṣir al-Dīn, chief chamberlain (ḥājib al-ḥujjāb) in Aleppo. He was killed in the battle of Āmid together with Jakam in the year [8]09."@en .

rec:AIND-D07486 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07486-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07486-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07486-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_mech,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07486 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن صالح بن يحيى الشمس الكركي . أخذ القراءات عن الفخر الضرير كما أخبر ، وكتب عنه شيخنا الزين رضوان ببعض الاستدعاءات سنة أربع وثلاثين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṣāliḥ b. Yaḥyā, al-Shams al-Karakī. He took the Qurʾānic readings (qirāʾāt) from al-Fakhr al-Ḍarīr, as he himself reported, and our shaykh al-Zayn Riḍwān wrote down (transmissions) from him in some ijāza-petitions (istidʿāʾāt) in the year [8]34."@en .

rec:AIND-D07489 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07489-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07489-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07489-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_mech,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07489 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن صدقة بن خليل بن الحسن الشمس بن الزين بن البدر الحلبي ويعرف بابن الفرفور بفاءين أولاهما مفتوحة . ولد كما قرأته بخطه في ليلة الاثنين منتصف شعبان سنة ست وستين وسبعمائة بحلب ، ونشأ بها فسمع على الشهاب أحمد بن عبد العزيز بن المرحل فضل الرمي للقراب وغيره ، وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء ، أجاز لي في سنة إحدى وخمسين ، وكان يتكسب بالشهادة ذا إلمام بالشروط مع حسن الخط والخير . مات بعد سنة إحدى وأبوه ممن قرأ القراءات وأما جده فكان كاتب الديوان بحلب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṣadaqa b. Khalīl b. al-Ḥasan, al-Shams b. al-Zayn b. al-Badr al-Ḥalabī, known as Ibn al-Farfūr (with two fāʾs, the first of them vowelled with fatḥa). He was born, as I read in his own handwriting, on the night of Monday in the middle of Shaʿbān of the year 766 in Aleppo, and grew up there. He heard from al-Shihāb Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. al-Muraḥḥal the Faḍl al-ramy of al-Qarrāb and other works. He transmitted ḥadīth, and men of learning heard from him. He granted me an ijāza in the year [8]51. He earned his living by notarial witnessing, being familiar with the notarial formularies, with fine handwriting and goodness. He died after the year [8]51. His father was among those who studied the Qurʾānic readings, while his grandfather was the scribe of the dīwān in Aleppo."@en .

rec:AIND-D07490 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07490-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07490-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07490 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن صدقة بن صالح المطري القاهري أحد جماعة بيت البلقيني ويعرف بالشمس المطري . ولد في شعبان سنة ثمان وثمانمائة وحضر المواعيد ومجالس الحديث وتكسب بزازا في بعض الحوانيت ، وتنزل في سعيد السعداء وغيرها وفيه كلام. مات في ليلة ثاني عشري ربيع الثاني سنة اثنتين وتسعين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṣadaqa b. Ṣāliḥ al-Maṭarī al-Qāhirī, one of the retinue of the Bulqīnī household, known as al-Shams al-Maṭarī. He was born in Shaʿbān of the year 808. He attended preaching sessions and ḥadīth assemblies, earned his living as a cloth-merchant in some shops, and was enrolled in Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ and elsewhere; there is (unfavourable) talk about him. He died on the night of the 22nd of Rabīʿ al-Thānī of the year [8]92, may God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07494 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07494-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07494-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07494 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن صدقة الخواجا شمس الدين الدمشقي مات في يوم الأحد ثامن جمادى الأولى سنة ثلاث وخمسين ودفن من الغد بتربة الزيني عبد الباسط بسفح قاسيون رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṣadaqa, al-Khawājā Shams al-Dīn al-Dimashqī. He died on Sunday, the 8th of Jumādā al-Ūlā of the year [8]53, and was buried the next day in the turba of al-Zaynī ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ at the foot of Qāsiyūn, may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07495 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07495-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07495-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07495-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07495 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن صدقة فتح الدين المنوفي الشافعي ويعرف بابن عطية ، وناب عن شيخنا وغيره في قضاء بلده وكان العز بن عبد السلام يصفه بالذكاء والخير والخبرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṣadaqa, Fatḥ al-Dīn al-Munūfī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn ʿAṭiyya. He served as deputy for our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others in the judgeship of his home town, and al-ʿIzz b. ʿAbd al-Salām used to describe him as intelligent, good and experienced."@en .

rec:AIND-D07496 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07496-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07496-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07496-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_mech,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07496 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن صديق بن علي بن عمر بن محمد بن زكريا الشمس المكي الشافعي المقرىء . تلا بالسبع علي أبي الحسن علي بن آدم الحبيبي الماضي قرأ عليه بعض الروايات النور علي بن محمد بن أحمد بن أبي بر الغنومي في سنة اثنتين وثلاثين وأجاز له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṣiddīq b. ʿAlī b. ʿUmar b. Muḥammad b. Zakariyyā, al-Shams al-Makkī al-Shāfiʿī, the Qurʾān-reader. He recited (the Qurʾān) according to the seven readings to Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī b. Ādam al-Ḥabībī, mentioned above. Al-Nūr ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr al-Ghanūmī read some of the transmissions (riwāyāt) to him in the year [8]32, and he granted him an ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D07498 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07498-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07498-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07498 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن الصفي النجمي . في ابن عبد الله بن نجم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Ṣafī al-Najmī. See under Ibn ʿAbd Allāh b. Najm."@en .

rec:AIND-D07503 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07503-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07503-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07503 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن طاهر تنظر حوادث رمضان سنة إحدى وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṭāhir. See the events of Ramaḍān of the year [8]61."@en .

rec:AIND-D07505 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07505-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07505-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07505 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن طقزق بن ناصر الدين الصالحي الحنفي . ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṭuqzuq b. Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Ṣāliḥī al-Ḥanafī. One of those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07506 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07506-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07506-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07506 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن طلحة بن عيسى الهتار . مات سنة تسع وعشرين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṭalḥa b. ʿĪsā al-Hattār. He died in the year [8]29."@en .

rec:AIND-D07507 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07507-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07507-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07507 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن طوغان الحسني الماضي أبوه . مات أبوه وهو طفل فنشأ متشاغلا باللهو واللعب وصاهر التاج البلقيني على ابنته جنة فلم يثبت معها ، وتزوج ابنة أخت الشمس بن المرخم فاستولدها ولدا . ومات بالطاعون في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين وقد قارب الأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṭūghān al-Ḥasanī, whose father is mentioned above. His father died while he was a small child, and he grew up occupied with amusement and play. He became son-in-law of al-Tāj al-Bulqīnī by marrying his daughter Janna, but did not stay with her; then he married the daughter of the sister of al-Shams b. al-Murakhkham, and she bore him a son. He died of the plague in Ṣafar of the year [8]53, having approached forty."@en .

rec:AIND-D07508 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07508-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07508-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07508 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن طيبغا الشمس القاهري الحنفي . اشتغل ولازم الزين قاسما الحنفي وقرأ على القول البديع وارتياح الأكباد وغيرها من تصانيفي وغيرها بل سمع قبل ذلك على شيخنا والبدر العيني وجماعة وكتب بخطه جملة ، وتكسب بالشهادة دهره ، وابتني بالقرب من قنطرة أمير حسين دارا ، وكان يجلس هو ورفيقه على بابها ولم يكن بالبارع ولا بالمتقن في شهاداته . مات سنة أربع وثمانين رحمه الله وعفا عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Ṭaybughā, al-Shams al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī. He devoted himself to study and kept close company with al-Zayn Qāsim al-Ḥanafī. He read to me al-Qawl al-badīʿ and Irtiyāḥ al-akbād and other works of mine, as well as other works; before that he had heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), al-Badr al-ʿAynī and a group of others, and he copied a great deal in his own hand. He earned his living by notarial witnessing all his life, built a house near Qanṭarat Amīr Ḥusayn, and he and his companion used to sit at its door; but he was neither outstanding nor accurate in his attestations. He died in the year [8]84, may God have mercy on him and pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07510 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07510-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07510-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07510 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن الشيخ عامر بن محمد بن محمد الشمس الغمري المقدسي المادح الحائك . ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Shaykh ʿĀmir b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, al-Shams al-Ghamrī al-Maqdisī, the panegyrist (al-mādiḥ), the weaver (al-ḥāʾik). One of those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07514 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07514-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07514-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07514 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عباس بن محمد بن عباس الشمس البعلي العلاف أبوه . ولد تقريبا سنة ست وسبعين وسبعمائة ببعلبك وسمع بها الصحيح على أبي الفرج عبد الرحمن بن الزعبوب أنابه الحجار ولقيته هناك فقرأت عليه المائة لابن تيمية منه مع ختمه ، وكان إنسانا حسنا حج . ومات قريبا من سنة ستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbbās b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbbās, al-Shams al-Baʿlī; al-ʿAllāf (the fodder-seller) is his father. He was born approximately in the year 776 in Baʿlabakk, and heard there the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Faraj ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Zaʿbūb, who had it from al-Ḥajjār. I met him there and read to him the Miʾa of Ibn Taymiyya from it, together with his completion (khatma) of it. He was a good man, and performed the pilgrimage. He died close to the year [8]60."@en .

rec:AIND-D07515 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07515-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07515-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88c_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07515 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عباس الشمس الجوجري الشافعي . له ذكر في سبطه محمد بن محمد بن علي بن وجيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbbās, al-Shams al-Jawjarī al-Shāfiʿī. He is mentioned in the entry on his daughter's son Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Wajīh."@en .

rec:AIND-D07516 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07516-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07516-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07516-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07516 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن العباس المغربي مفتي تلمسين ومعناها اجتماع شيئين باللغة البربرية فغالب أقواتها كالقمح وفواكهها تكون جنسين . له تصانيف منها شرح لامية ابن ملك . ومات بالطاعون سنة إحدى وسبعين . أفاده لي بعض المغاربة من أصحابنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-ʿAbbās al-Maghribī, the muftī of Tilimsān (Tlemcen). In the Berber language its name means \"the joining of two things\", for most of its foodstuffs, such as wheat, and its fruits are of two kinds. He has writings, among them a commentary on the Lāmiyya of Ibn Mālik. He died of the plague in the year 871. One of our Maghribī companions informed me of this."@en .

rec:AIND-D07518 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07518-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07518-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07518 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الأحد العجيمي . في ابن عبد الماجد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Aḥad al-ʿUjaymī. See under Ibn ʿAbd al-Mājid."@en .

rec:AIND-D07519 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07519-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07519-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07519 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الباري تقي الدين المصري الشافعي الضرير ، ممن أخذ عن السراج البلقيني ، وكان فقيها صالحا انتفع به المصريون سيما الجلال البكري بل جل تفقهه إنما كان به لكونه هو الذي كان يطالع له وقال إنه كان من الصالحين ، وكذا ممن أخذ عنه الشرف الطنبدي نزيل حارة عبد الباسط . ومات قريب الأربعين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Bārī, Taqī al-Dīn al-Miṣrī al-Shāfiʿī, the blind (al-Ḍarīr). He was among those who studied under al-Sirāj al-Bulqīnī. He was a pious jurist from whom the Egyptians benefited, especially al-Jalāl al-Bakrī; indeed, most of the latter's training in jurisprudence was through him, since it was al-Jalāl who used to read aloud for him. He (al-Jalāl) said that he was one of the righteous. Likewise, al-Sharaf al-Ṭanbadī, resident of the quarter of ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ, was among those who studied under him. He died, presumably, around the year 840."@en .

rec:AIND-D07520 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07520-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07520-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07520-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07520 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الباسط بن خليل الدمشقي الأصل القاهري الماضي أبوه والآتي أخوه أبو بكر . مات بالطاعون في صفر سنة ثلاث وخمسين عن نحو عشرين عاما تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ b. Khalīl, of Damascene origin, al-Qāhirī. His father has been mentioned above, and his brother Abū Bakr will be mentioned below. He died of the plague in Ṣafar 853, aged roughly twenty."@en .

rec:AIND-D07525 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07525-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07525-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07525 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الحي القيوم بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة أبو البركات القرشي المكي ، وأمه زبيدية . درج صغيرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abū al-Barakāt Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Ḥayy al-Qayyūm b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓahīra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī al-Makkī. His mother was a woman of Zabīd. He died in childhood."@en .

rec:AIND-D07526 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07526-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07526-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07526 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الخالق بن رمضان بن مرهف الدمياطي رفيق أبي الطيب بن البدراني على ابن الكويك . أثبته الزين رضوان فيمن يؤخذ عنه وكأنه مات قبل الأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Khāliq b. Ramaḍān b. Murhif al-Dimyāṭī, companion of Abū al-Ṭayyib b. al-Badrānī in study under Ibn al-Kuwayk. Al-Zayn Riḍwān recorded him among those from whom transmission may be received. He seems to have died before 840."@en .

rec:AIND-D07527 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07527-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07527-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07527-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07527 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الدائم بن عمر بن عوض المحب أبو عبد الله وأبو البركات وأبو الخير بن الزين بن العلامة أبي حفص المرصفي ثم القاهري الشافعي . ولد تقريبا سنة ست وثمانين وسبعمائة وسمع الصحيح على ابن صديق أجاز لنا . ومات بعد الخمسين ظنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Dāʾim b. ʿUmar b. ʿAwaḍ, al-Muḥibb, Abū ʿAbd Allāh, Abū al-Barakāt and Abū al-Khayr, b. al-Zayn b. al-ʿAllāma Abī Ḥafṣ, al-Marṣafī, later al-Qāhirī, al-Shāfiʿī. He was born approximately in 786 and heard the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Ṣiddīq. He granted us an ijāza. He died, presumably, after 850."@en .

rec:AIND-D07530 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07530-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07530-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07530-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07530-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07530 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن إبراهيم بن جملة بن مسلم الكمال المحجي الأصل الدمشقي ، ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه وقال : كان رئيسا محتشما متمولا باشر نظر ديوان السبع ثم تركه . ومات في المحرم سنة ثمان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Jumla b. Muslim, al-Kamāl, of Maḥajja origin, al-Dimashqī. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ and said: \"He was a dignified and wealthy notable; he held the supervision of the Dīwān al-Sabʿ and then gave it up.\" He died in Muḥarram of the year (8)08."@en .

rec:AIND-D07531 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07531-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07531-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07531 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن الشيخ عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن أحمد بن محمود الهمامي المكي الحنفي الماضي أبوه . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Shaykh ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Aḥmad b. Maḥmūd al-Humāmī al-Makkī al-Ḥanafī. His father has been mentioned above. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D07532 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07532-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07532-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07532-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07532 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن إسماعيل المحب بن التقي بن القطب القلقشندي الأصل القاهري الشافعي الماضي أبوه وجده . اعتنى به أبوه فأحضره على شيخنا وابن الفرات وغيرهما وحفظ كتبا وعرض على جماعة واشتغل عند البهاء المشهدي وغيره . ومات ظنا بعد السبعين عوضه الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Ismāʿīl, al-Muḥibb b. al-Taqī b. al-Quṭb, of Qalqashanda origin, al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī. His father and grandfather have been mentioned above. His father took care of him and had him attend (the sessions of) our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), Ibn al-Furāt and others. He memorised several books, presented them to a number of scholars, and studied under al-Bahāʾ al-Mashhadī and others. He died, presumably, after 870. May God recompense him with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D07533 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07533-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07533-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07533 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن حسين بن داود بن سالم بن معالي محيي الدين أبو الفضل بن الموفق أبي ذر العباسي الحموي الحنبلي الماضي أبوه وجده ولي قضاء حماة حين انتقل أبوه إلى دمشق على نظر جيشها سنة ثمان وسبعين ومات بدمشق حين رجوعه من القاهرة إلى بلده في طاعون سنة اثنتين وثمانين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Ḥusayn b. Dāwūd b. Sālim b. Maʿālī, Muḥyī al-Dīn Abū al-Faḍl b. al-Muwaffaq Abī Dharr, al-ʿAbbāsī al-Ḥamawī al-Ḥanbalī. His father and grandfather have been mentioned above. He was appointed to the judgeship of Ḥamā when his father moved to Damascus to take up the supervision of its army (naẓar al-jaysh) in the year (8)78. He died in Damascus, on his way back from Cairo to his hometown, in the plague of the year (8)82. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07535 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07535-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07535-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07535 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن عبد الوهاب ابن أخي الشمس محمد بن أحمد ويعرف بابن وهيب . كان مع عمه وفي كفالته بعد موت أبيه بمكة سنة أربع وتسعين فسمع علي معه أشياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Wahhāb, nephew of al-Shams Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, known as Ibn Wuhayb. After his father's death in Mecca in the year (8)94 he was with his paternal uncle and under his guardianship, and together with him he heard some things from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07538 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07538-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07538-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07538-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07538 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن محمد بن أحمد بن عرندة الوجيزي القاهري الدلال بسوق الغزل الشرب والماضي أبوه وجده . ممن أكثر المجاورة بمكة وكان فقيرا يقرأ القرآن أحد صوفية سعيد السعداء . مات بالمدينة في ذي القعدة سنة إحدى وتسعين وأظنه جاز الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAranda, al-Wajīzī al-Qāhirī, the broker (dallāl) at the market of yarn and sharb-linen. His father and grandfather have been mentioned above. He was among those who frequently sojourned (as a mujāwir) in Mecca; he was poor, recited the Qurʾān, and was one of the Sufis of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. He died in Medina in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year (8)91, and I think he had passed sixty."@en .

rec:AIND-D07539 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07539-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07539-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07539 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن أحمد بن محمد الأمين بن الزين الحسباني الأصل الدمشقي الحنفي الماضي أبوه . استقر في كتابة السر بدمشق في شوال سنة إحدى وتسعين بعد صرف الموفق الشريف الحموي ببذل كثير ثم صرف في جمادى الآخرة من التي تليها بابن اخي الشهاب بن الفرفور واستمر مخمولا في عهدة الديون وعاد ضرره على زوجته التي كانت زوجا للشيخ خطاب . مات في الطاعون سنة سبع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad, al-Amīn b. al-Zayn, of Ḥusbān origin, al-Dimashqī al-Ḥanafī. His father has been mentioned above. He was installed in the secretaryship (kitābat al-sirr) of Damascus in Shawwāl (8)91, after the dismissal of al-Muwaffaq al-Sharīf al-Ḥamawī, by paying a large sum; then, in Jumādā II of the following year, he was dismissed in favour of the nephew of al-Shihāb b. al-Farfūr. He remained in obscurity under the burden of debts, and the harm of this extended to his wife, who had formerly been the wife of Shaykh Khaṭṭāb. He died in the plague of the year (8)97."@en .

rec:AIND-D07541 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07541-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07541-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07541 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي المكي ، وأمه خديجة ابنة القاضي سليمان بن علي بن الجنيد . درج صغيرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓahīra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓahīra al-Qurashī al-Makkī. His mother was Khadīja, daughter of the qāḍī Sulaymān b. ʿAlī b. al-Junayd. He died in childhood."@en .

rec:AIND-D07542 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07542-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07542-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07542-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07542-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07542 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد أخو الذي قبله وأمه علما ابنة المحب بن ظهيرة . ولد في ذي الحجة سنة اثنتين وأربعين وثمانمائة وهو أيضا ممن مات صغيرا . بيض له ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, brother of the preceding. His mother was ʿAlamā, daughter of al-Muḥibb b. Ẓahīra. He was born in Dhū al-Ḥijja 842, and he too was among those who died young. Ibn Fahd left his entry blank."@en .

rec:AIND-D07543 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07543-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07543-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07543 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي بكر بن عمر الفاضل الشمس الدمشقي الكفرسوسي الشافعي ، ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr b. ʿUmar, the learned (al-fāḍil) al-Shams al-Dimashqī al-Kafrsūsī al-Shāfiʿī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07546 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07546-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07546-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07546 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد أبو عبد الله أخو الذي قبله . ولد في سنة ست وخمسين وله فضيلة تامة مع الصلاح والخير ، وهو الآن حي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad Abū ʿAbd Allāh, brother of the preceding. He was born in the year (8)56; he possesses complete excellence together with piety and goodness, and he is still alive."@en .

rec:AIND-D07548 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07548-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07548-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07548 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن داود صلاح الدين بن الكويز الماضي أبوه وجده ، ممن حفظ القرآن والمنهاج وعرض على جماعة منهم شيخنا وسمع عليه ثم ترك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Dāwūd, Ṣalāḥ al-Dīn b. al-Kuwayz. His father and grandfather have been mentioned above. He was among those who memorised the Qurʾān and al-Minhāj; he presented them to a number of scholars, among them our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and heard from him, but then gave up (his studies)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07549 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07549-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07549-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07549 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن رجب . فيمن جده محمد بن رجب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Rajab. See under those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Rajab."@en .

rec:AIND-D07551 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07551-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07551-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07551 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن سلطان . فيمن جده عيسى بن سلطان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Sulṭān. (His entry is) among those whose grandfather is ʿĪsā b. Sulṭān."@en .

rec:AIND-D07556 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07556-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07556-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07556 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله بن أحمد بن علي الشريف الحسيني الحضرمي اليماني ويعرف بالشيخ باعلوي صهر الشريف عبد الله بن محمد بن علي بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن علي الماضي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī, al-Sharīf al-Ḥusaynī al-Ḥaḍramī al-Yamānī, known as al-Shaykh Bāʿalawī; the ṣihr (son-in-law) of al-Sharīf ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī, mentioned previously."@en .

rec:AIND-D07558 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07558-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07558-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07558 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن علي بن أحمد بن أبي بكر أبو الفتح الأدمي القاهري الشافعي والد عبد الباسط الماضي . تكسب بالشهادة وتنزل في الجهات وتمول جدا بحيث كان يعامل ويقارض وله دار هائلة مع التقتير على نفسه . مات بعيد الثمانين ظنا عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr, Abū al-Fatḥ al-Adamī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, the father of ʿAbd al-Bāsiṭ mentioned previously. He earned his living as a notary witness (shahāda), was appointed to various posts (jihāt), and became exceedingly wealthy, to the extent that he traded and engaged in commenda partnerships (qirāḍ); he owned a magnificent house while being stingy towards himself. He died shortly after 880, presumably. May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07559 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07559-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07559-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07559 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز بن القسم بن عبد الرحمن بن القسم النجم بن القاضي وجيه الدين بن القاضي نور الدين الهاشمي العقيلي النويري المكي وأمه فاطمة ابنة القاضي أبي الفضل النويري . ولد سنة أربع وتسعين وسبعمائة وأجاز له التنوخي وأبو الخير بن العلائي وأبو هريرة بن الذهبي وآخرون وما علمت متى مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. al-Qāsim b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Qāsim, al-Najm b. al-Qāḍī Wajīh al-Dīn b. al-Qāḍī Nūr al-Dīn, al-Hāshimī al-ʿUqaylī al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī. His mother was Fāṭima, daughter of al-Qāḍī Abū al-Faḍl al-Nuwayrī. He was born in 794. Al-Tanūkhī, Abū al-Khayr b. al-ʿAlāʾī, Abū Hurayra b. al-Dhahabī and others granted him ijāza. I do not know when he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D07561 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07561-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07561-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07561 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن علي بن إسحاق الشمس بن الزين التميمي الخليلي الشافعي الماضي أبوه ويعرف بابن شقير ممن ذكر أنه سمع على الزين القمني ولبس الخرقة من الخافي وكانت فيه فضيلة . مات ببلده في شعبان سنة تسع وثمانين عن نحو السبعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī b. Isḥāq, al-Shams b. al-Zayn, al-Tamīmī al-Khalīlī al-Shāfiʿī, whose father was mentioned previously; known as Ibn Shuqayr. He was among those who stated that they had heard from al-Zayn al-Qamanī and received the khirqa (Sufi cloak) from al-Khāfī, and he possessed some learning. He died in his home town in Shaʿbān 889, aged about seventy. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07564 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07564-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07564-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07564 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد جلال الدين أبو الخير شقيق الذي قبله وذاك الأكبر . ولد في رجب سنة ست وعشرين وثمانمائة وحفظ القرآن وتنقيح اللباب والرحبية والورقات والملحة واشتغل وخطب بجامع البدري بدمياط بل ناب في قضائها ، وكتب الخط الحسن ، وهو الآن حي أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad Jalāl al-Dīn Abū al-Khayr, the full brother of the preceding, who is the elder of the two. He was born in Rajab 826, memorised the Qurʾān, Tanqīḥ al-Lubāb, al-Raḥbiyya, al-Waraqāt and al-Mulḥa, and pursued his studies. He preached at the Jāmiʿ al-Badrī in Damietta and even served as deputy judge there. He wrote a fine hand. He too is still alive at present."@en .

rec:AIND-D07565 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07565-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07565-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07565 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن علي بن يوسف بن منصور الشمس القاهري والد الكمال محمد إمام الكاملية الآتي ، قرأ القرآن واشتغل قليلا وسمع على الشرف ابن الكويك في الشفا وغيره ، وتنزل في بعض الجهات ، وكان يحضر عند شيخنا وغيره وأم بالكاملية ، وكان خيرا وصفه البرماوي في إجازة ولده بالعلم والفضل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf b. Manṣūr, al-Shams al-Qāhirī, the father of al-Kamāl Muḥammad, the imam of al-Kāmiliyya, who is mentioned below. He recited the Qurʾān, studied a little, and heard al-Shifāʾ and other works from al-Sharaf Ibn al-Kuwayk. He was appointed to some posts (jihāt), attended the sessions of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others, and served as imam at al-Kāmiliyya. He was a good man; al-Birmāwī described him, in the ijāza he wrote for his son, as possessing learning and virtue."@en .

rec:AIND-D07567 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07567-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07567-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07567 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن العماد . فيمن جده الخضر قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-ʿImād. (His entry is) nearby, among those whose grandfather is al-Khaḍir."@en .

rec:AIND-D07572 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07572-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07572-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07572 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن أبي الغيث . مضى فيمن جده عبد العزيز بن محمد بن أحمد قريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī al-Ghayth. He was mentioned shortly before, among those whose grandfather is ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad."@en .

rec:AIND-D07583 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07583-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07583-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07583 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن حسن الفاقوسي الماضي أبوه وجده ممن سمع هو وأخوه أحمد ختم البخاري بالظاهرية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ḥasan al-Fāqūsī, whose father and grandfather were mentioned previously. He and his brother Aḥmad were among those who heard the completion (khatm) of al-Bukhārī at al-Ẓāhiriyya."@en .

rec:AIND-D07587 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07587-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07587-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07587 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد ولي الدين أبو عبد الله بن صالح أخو الذي قبله . ولي القضاء استقلالا حين استعفى أخوه منه في سنة أربع وأربعين فدام حتى استعفى هو أيضا منه وتركه لابن أخيه صلاح الدين محمد وشارك في الخطابة والإمامة وكان جيد الخطابة ممن سمع على أبي الحسن سبط الزبير وغيره ولم يلبث أن مات في إحدى الجماديين سنة أربع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad Walī al-Dīn Abū ʿAbd Allāh Ibn Ṣāliḥ, the brother of the preceding. He held the judgeship in his own right when his brother resigned from it in 844, and continued until he too resigned and left it to his nephew Ṣalāḥ al-Dīn Muḥammad. He also shared in the offices of preacher (khaṭīb) and imam, and was a good preacher. He was among those who heard from Abū al-Ḥasan Sibṭ al-Zubayr and others. Not long afterwards he died, in one of the two Jumādās of 874."@en .

rec:AIND-D07588 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07588-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07588-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07588 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد شمس الدين أخو اللذين قبله . سمع على أبي الحسن سبط الزبير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad Shams al-Dīn, the brother of the two preceding. He heard from Abū al-Ḥasan Sibṭ al-Zubayr."@en .

rec:AIND-D07589 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07589-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07589-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07589 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن القاضي أبي عبد الله محمد بن القاضي ناصر الدين عبد الرحمن ابن محمد بن صالح معين الدين الكناني المدني الشافعي الماضي أبوه . شاب رأيته قرأ في الشفا على خير الدين قاضي المالكية بالمدينة في سنة ثمان وتسعين يوم ختمه في الروضة النبوية ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Qāḍī Abī ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. al-Qāḍī Nāṣir al-Dīn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ṣāliḥ, Muʿīn al-Dīn al-Kinānī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī, whose father was mentioned previously. A young man; I saw him reading al-Shifāʾ before Khayr al-Dīn, the Mālikī judge of Medina, in 898, on the day of its completion, in the Prophet's Rawḍa."@en .

rec:AIND-D07590 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07590-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07590-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07590 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الرحمن أبو القسم الحميري الفاسي الأصل القسنطيني التونسي ثم المقدسي المالكي والد أحمد المعروف بالخلوف . جاور بمكة سنة ثلاثين فما بعدها ثم قدم بيت المقدس فقطنه حتى مات في سنة تسع وخمسين ، وكان بارعا في الفقه متقدما فيه وكتب لصاحب المغرب . أفاده ولده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Abū al-Qāsim al-Ḥimyarī, of Fez origin, al-Qusanṭīnī al-Tūnisī, then al-Maqdisī, al-Mālikī, the father of Aḥmad known as al-Khallūf. He resided (jāwara) in Mecca in 830 and thereafter, then came to Jerusalem and settled there until he died in 859. He was outstanding and preeminent in jurisprudence (fiqh), and wrote (as secretary) for the ruler of the Maghrib. His son related this."@en .

rec:AIND-D07592 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07592-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07592-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07592 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الله بن عمر بن أبي بكر بن عمر بن عبد الرحمن بن عبد الله الناشري الماضي أبوه . ولد سنة خمس وثمانمائة وكانت له مشاركة في علوم مع حسن خلق وكرم ومواظبة على التلاوة . مات شابا في شوال سنة اثنتين وثلاثين بالفخة ودفن عند أبيه ، ذكره الناشري في أبيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr b. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Nāshirī, whose father was mentioned previously. He was born in 805, had a share in the sciences, together with good character, generosity and constant recitation. He died young in Shawwāl 832 at al-Fakhkha and was buried beside his father. Al-Nāshirī mentioned him in (the entry of) his father."@en .

rec:AIND-D07595 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07595-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07595-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07595 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن عبد الله الحضرمي . مات بمكة في صفر سنة أربع وخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥaḍramī. He died in Mecca in Ṣafar 854."@en .

rec:AIND-D07608 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07608-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07608-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07608 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن محمد بن يحيى المحب بن الزين بن التاج السندبيسي الأصل القاهري الشافعي أحد الصوفية بالمؤيدية . مات في يوم الأحد تاسع ذي القعدة سنة ثلاث وسبعين ولم يتكهل . وكان خيرا يتكسب بالتجارة ممن أخذ يسيرا عن أبيه رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Yaḥyā, al-Muḥibb b. al-Zayn b. al-Tāj, of Sandabīs origin, al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, one of the Sufis of al-Muʾayyadiyya. He died on Sunday 9 Dhū al-Qaʿda 873 without having reached middle age. He was a good man who earned his living by trade, and was among those who learned a little from his father. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07612 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07612-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07612-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07612 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد الشمس أو حميد الدين أبو الحمد المصري الأصل المقدسي الشافعي . يأتي فيمن لم يسم جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad, al-Shams or Ḥamīd al-Dīn, Abū al-Ḥamd, of Egyptian origin, al-Maqdisī, al-Shāfiʿī. He will be mentioned below among those whose grandfather is not named."@en .

rec:AIND-D07615 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07615-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07615-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07615 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن مؤمن ولي الدين القوصي الأصل القاهري الشافعي موقع الأتابك أزبك الظاهري . مات في غيبته مع أميره سنة ثمان وسبعين وكان قد باشر توقيع المفرد كأبيه وقتا وتوقيع الدست عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muʾmin, Walī al-Dīn, of Qūṣ origin, al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, the scribe (muwaqqiʿ) of the Atābak Azbak al-Ẓāhirī. He died in 878 while away with his amir. He had for a time held the post of scribe of the Mufrad (tawqīʿ al-mufrad), like his father, as well as that of scribe of the Dast (tawqīʿ al-dast). May God forgive him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07616 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07616-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07616-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88e_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07616 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن يحيى بن أحمد بن سليمان بن مهيب الصدقاوي الزواوي قاضيها المالكي الماضي ابنه إبراهيم وحفيده محمد . مات في سنة ثلاث وخمسين أو التي قبلها عن ثلاث وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Yaḥyā b. Aḥmad b. Sulaymān b. Muhayb al-Ṣadaqāwī al-Zawāwī, the Mālikī judge of that place (Zawāwa), whose son Ibrāhīm and grandson Muḥammad were mentioned previously. He died in 853 or the year before, aged sixty-three."@en .

rec:AIND-D07618 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07618-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07618-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07618-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_mech,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07618 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد أخو الذي قبله ويدعى بركات وهو بها أشهر . ممن سمع مني والله يوفقه لأبويه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, the brother of the preceding one. He is called Barakāt, and is better known by that name. He is among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī). May God grant him success in dutifulness to his parents."@en .

rec:AIND-D07621 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07621-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07621-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07621-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07621-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88f_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07621 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن يوسف الكمال أبو البركات بن أبي زيد الحسنى المسكناسي السكندري . أجاز لابن شيخنا وغيره في سنة سبع عشرة وأرخه المقريزي في عقوده في سنة اثنتين وعشرين وقال أنه ذكر أن أباه صافحه قال : صافحني أبو الحسن على الحطاب وعمر مائة وثمانين صافحني أبو عبد الله الصقلي صافحني أبو عبد الله معمر وكان عمره أربعمائة سنة صافحني النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم انتهى . وهو شيء لا يعتمده الحفاظ الإثبات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Yūsuf, al-Kamāl Abū al-Barakāt b. Abī Zayd al-Ḥasanī al-Maskanāsī al-Sakandarī. He granted an ijāza to the son of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others in the year [8]17. Al-Maqrīzī dated him (his death) in his ʿUqūd to the year [8]22, and said that he (the subject) mentioned that his father had shaken his hand; [the father] said: \"Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī al-Ḥaṭṭāb shook my hand — and he was one hundred and eighty years old; [he said:] Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣiqillī shook my hand; [he said:] Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muʿammar shook my hand — and his age was four hundred years; [he said:] the Prophet (God bless him and grant him peace) shook my hand.\" End of quotation. This is something the reliable and trustworthy ḥadīth masters do not rely upon."@en .

rec:AIND-D07623 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07623-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07623-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07623-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_mech,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07623 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن البدر أبو الفوز القاهري الحنفي ربيب الشمس الأمشاطي وهو بكنيته أشهر . مات في حياة أمه في المحرم سنة ست وسبعين وصلى عليه في مشهد حافل ثم دفن بتربتهم بالقرب من الروضة خارج باب النصر وقد زاد على الأربعين وكان موصوفا بعقل واحتمال وتواضع وفهم ، ممن اشتغل قليلا وحضر عند جماعة كزوج أمه وحج معهما في الرجبية وجلس للشهادة عند زوج أخته المظفر محمود الأمشاطي بل ناب في القضاء ويقال إنه حفظ النقاية رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-Badr Abū al-Fawz, al-Qāhirī al-Ḥanafī, the stepson of al-Shams al-Amshāṭī; he is better known by his kunya. He died during his mother's lifetime in Muḥarram of the year [8]76; the funeral prayer was performed for him in a crowded gathering, and he was then buried in their family tomb near al-Rawḍa outside Bāb al-Naṣr, having passed the age of forty. He was described as possessing sense, forbearance, humility and understanding. He was among those who studied a little and attended [the lessons of] a number of people, such as his mother's husband, and he performed the pilgrimage with the two of them in the Rajabiyya caravan. He sat as a witness (shāhid) under his sister's husband al-Muẓaffar Maḥmūd al-Amshāṭī, and even served as a deputy judge. It is said that he memorised al-Nuqāya. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07625 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07625-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07625-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07625 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن جمال الدين الأنصاري المكي . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن أبي بكر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Jamāl al-Dīn al-Anṣārī al-Makkī. He has been mentioned above among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr."@en .

rec:AIND-D07626 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07626-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07626-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07626-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07626 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن جمال الدين بن وجيه الدين الحسيني العلوي اليماني . كتب مصنفي القول البديع وسمع علي منه جملة وكذا من غيره من تصانيفي ومروياتي بل سمع مني المسلسل وكتبت له وسافر قبل التسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Jamāl al-Dīn b. Wajīh al-Dīn, al-Ḥusaynī al-ʿAlawī al-Yamānī. He copied my work al-Qawl al-Badīʿ and heard a portion of it from me, and likewise [heard] from other works of my composition and my transmitted texts; indeed he heard al-Musalsal from me, and I wrote [something] for him. He departed before [the year 8]90."@en .

rec:AIND-D07631 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07631-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07631-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07631 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن أبو منصور المارديني المقدسي الحنفي . سمع على الميدومي وحدث عنه بجزء البطاقة سماعا سمعه منه التقي أبو بكر القلقشندي . ومات في خامس عشري المحرم سنة اثنتين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Abū Manṣūr al-Māridīnī al-Maqdisī al-Ḥanafī. He heard from al-Maydūmī and transmitted on his authority Juzʾ al-Biṭāqa by audition (samāʿ); al-Taqī Abū Bakr al-Qalqashandī heard it from him. He died on the twenty-fifth of Muḥarram in the year [8]02."@en .

rec:AIND-D07632 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07632-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07632-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07632-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07632-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88f_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07632 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن الحلبي ويعرف بابن أمين الدولة . قيم مصارع معالج له إجازة من الصلاح بن أبي عمر وغيره ، وأجاز لابن شيخنا وغيره بعد الثلاثين واسم جده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥalabī, known as Ibn Amīn al-Dawla. Custodian of the wrestling grounds and a practitioner (bone-setter) [reading uncertain]. He held an ijāza from al-Ṣalāḥ b. Abī ʿUmar and others, and he granted an ijāza to the son of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others after [the year 8]30. And his grandfather's name [text breaks off]."@en .

rec:AIND-D07633 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07633-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07633-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07633 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحمن الصبيبي المدني . مضى فيمن جده محمد بن أبي بكر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ṣubaybī al-Madanī. He has been mentioned above among those whose grandfather is Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr."@en .

rec:AIND-D07636 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07636-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07636-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07636 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحيم بن الحسين بن عبد الرحمن المحب أبو حاتم بن الزينأبي الفضل العراقي الأصل القاهري الشافعي أخو الولي أبي زرعة أحمد الماضي ، ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه فقال : أسمعه أبوه الكثير واشتغل ودرس ثم ترك وكان فاضلا حسن الشكالة قليل الاشتغال . مات في صفر سنة اثنتين وكان توجه لمكة في رجب ثم رجع قبل الحج لمرض أصابه فاستمر به حتى مات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, al-Muḥibb Abū Ḥātim b. al-Zayn Abī al-Faḍl, of ʿIrāqī origin, al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī, the brother of al-Walī Abū Zurʿa Aḥmad, mentioned above. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ and said: \"His father had him hear a great deal; he studied and taught, then gave it up. He was learned and of handsome appearance, but of little scholarly application.\" He died in Ṣafar of the year [8]02. He had set out for Mecca in Rajab, then returned before the pilgrimage because of an illness that befell him and persisted until he died."@en .

rec:AIND-D07639 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07639-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07639-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07639 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحيم بن علي أبو الخير العقبي القاهري الشافعي . ولد تقريبا سنة ثمانمائة وحفظ القرآن وغيره وأسمع على الشمس الشامي ثلاثيات مسند أحمد وغيرها ، وأجاز له جماعة واشتغل عند الزين البوتيجي في الفقه وغيره وكتب في الإملاء عن شيخنا ولكنه لم ينجب ، وبلغني أنه حدث بأخرة وكان ساكنا . مات في سنة أربع وتسعين رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. ʿAlī, Abū al-Khayr al-ʿUqbī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī. He was born in approximately the year 800, memorised the Qurʾān and other texts, and was made to hear the Thulāthiyyāt of Musnad Aḥmad and other works from al-Shams al-Shāmī. A group [of scholars] granted him ijāzas. He studied jurisprudence and other subjects under al-Zayn al-Būtījī, and wrote down the dictations of our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), but he did not distinguish himself. I (al-Sakhāwī) was informed that he transmitted [ḥadīth] late in life. He was a quiet man. He died in the year [8]94; may God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07642 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07642-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07642-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07642 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن التقي أبي الفضل عبد الرحيم بن المحب محمد بن محمد بن أحمد موفق الدين بن الأوجاقي الشافعي الماضي أبوه والآتي جده . مات في ذي القعدة سنة سبع وسبعين ودفن بالقرب من مقام الشافعي وقد جاز العشرين وكان قد قرأ وفهم وتأسف كل من أبويه عليه جدا عوضهم الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Taqī Abī al-Faḍl ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. al-Muḥibb Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad, Muwaffaq al-Dīn b. al-Awjāqī al-Shāfiʿī; his father has been mentioned above and his grandfather will be mentioned below. He died in Dhū al-Qaʿda of the year [8]77 and was buried near the shrine (maqām) of al-Shāfiʿī, having passed the age of twenty. He had studied and attained understanding, and both of his parents grieved for him exceedingly; may God compensate them with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D07643 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07643-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07643-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07643 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحيم بن محمد أبو عبد الله الموصلي الدمشقي المؤذن بالجامع الأموي . روى عن أبيه قوله مضاهيا للزيدونية : %~% بكى الزمان علينا من تنائينا %~% وكان يضحك حينا من تدانينا %~% أجاز ، ويحرر من الاستدعاء ففي كلام العجلوني لبس ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm b. Muḥammad, Abū ʿAbd Allāh, al-Mawṣilī al-Dimashqī, the muezzin of the Umayyad Mosque. He transmitted from his father the latter's verses composed in imitation of the Zaydūniyya: \"Time wept over us for our separation, / whereas once it laughed at our closeness.\" He granted an ijāza; but this must be verified from the request for ijāza (istidʿāʾ), for there is confusion in what al-ʿAjlūnī says."@en .

rec:AIND-D07644 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07644-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07644-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07644-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07644 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرحيم الحسيني الكتبي الفراش بالتربة الظاهرية برقوق . سمع على الجمال عبد الله الحنبلي وأثبت الزين رضوان اسمه فيمن يؤخذ عنه وقال إنه في الكتبيين ولم نره فكأنه مات قبل الخمسين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Ḥusaynī al-Kutubī, the farrāsh (attendant) at the Ẓāhiriyya mausoleum of Barqūq. He heard from al-Jamāl ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥanbalī. Al-Zayn Riḍwān recorded his name among those from whom [ḥadīth] may be taken, and said that he was in al-Kutubiyyīn (the booksellers' quarter). We did not see him, so it seems that he died before [the year 8]50."@en .

rec:AIND-D07647 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07647-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07647-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07647-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07647 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرزاق بن عبد الكريم بن عبد الغني بن يعقوب فتح الدين أبو الفتح بن التاج بن الكريم بن الفخر أخو عبد الكريم الماضي وهذا أكبر ويعرف كسلفه بابن فخيرة تصغير جده . وهو أحد شهود الإدارة بالبيمارستان تلقاها عن الشريف كمال الدين بن المحيريق بل باشر نيابة النظر فيه عن كاتب المماليك يوسف بن أبي الفتح وباسمه مباشرة في ديوان المماليك ، ولا بأس به شارك أخاه في السماع علي وفي جميع ما ذكر هناك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. ʿAbd al-Karīm b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Yaʿqūb, Fatḥ al-Dīn Abū al-Fatḥ b. al-Tāj b. al-Karīm b. al-Fakhr, the brother of ʿAbd al-Karīm mentioned above, this one being the elder; like his forebears he is known as Ibn Fukhayra, a diminutive of his ancestor's [laqab]. He is one of the witnesses of the administration (shuhūd al-idāra) at the hospital (bīmāristān), which he received from al-Sharīf Kamāl al-Dīn b. al-Muḥayriq; indeed he exercised the deputy supervision (niyābat al-naẓar) of it on behalf of the clerk of the Mamlūks, Yūsuf b. Abī al-Fatḥ, and there is a post in his name in the Dīwān al-Mamālīk. There is no harm in him. He joined his brother in hearing from me (al-Sakhāwī) and in everything mentioned there."@en .

rec:AIND-D07648 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07648-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07648-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07648 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرزاق بن عبد الله العلم أبو الخير بن الشمس أخي الصاحب العلم يحيى بن أبي كم والد يحيى الآتي ويعرف بابن أبي كم ، ممن باشر في الدواوين ومات تقريبا سنة ستين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-ʿAlam Abū al-Khayr b. al-Shams — [al-Shams being] the brother of the vizier (al-Ṣāḥib) al-ʿAlam Yaḥyā b. Abī Kamm — and the father of Yaḥyā, who is mentioned below. He is known as Ibn Abī Kamm. He was among those who served in the government bureaus (dawāwīn). He died in approximately the year [8]60; may God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07651 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07651-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07651-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07651 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرزاق شمس الدين أخو الذي قبله والفخر بن أبي الفرج مات في حياة أخويه بعد أن باشر نظر قطيا فيما قيل ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq, Shams al-Dīn, the brother of the preceding one and of al-Fakhr b. Abī al-Faraj. He died during the lifetime of his two brothers, after having exercised the supervision (naẓar) of Qaṭyā, according to what is said."@en .

rec:AIND-D07652 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07652-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07652-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07652 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرزاق . في أبي البركات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [See] under Abū al-Barakāt."@en .

rec:AIND-D07653 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07653-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07653-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07653 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الرزاق القاضي بدر الدين القرشي البالسي المصري الشافعي والد التاج محمد الآتي ويعرف بابن مسلم أحد النواب ممن سمع على الواسطي وشيخنا وسمع منه بعض الطلبة ، وكان ساكنا . مات في رجب سنة تسع وثمانين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq, the judge (al-qāḍī) Badr al-Dīn al-Qurashī al-Bālisī al-Miṣrī al-Shāfiʿī, the father of al-Tāj Muḥammad, who is mentioned below; he is known as Ibn Muslim. One of the deputy judges. He was among those who heard from al-Wāsiṭī and from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), and some students heard from him. He was a quiet man. He died in Rajab of the year [8]89."@en .

rec:AIND-D07657 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07657-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07657-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07657 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد السلام بن راجح القرشي القندهاري نسبة لبعض قرى الهند . نزيل مكة ونائب إمام مقام الحنفية بها . مات بمكة شهيدا تحت هدم في ربيع الثاني سنة سبع وستين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Salām b. Rājiḥ al-Qurashī al-Qandahārī — a nisba referring to one of the villages of India. A resident of Mecca and deputy imam of the Ḥanafī station (maqām al-Ḥanafiyya) there. He died in Mecca as a martyr, [crushed] under a collapse, in Rabīʿ II of the year [8]67. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D07658 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07658-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07658-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88f_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07658 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد السلام بن عبد العزيز العزيزي المدني أحد شهود الحرم وممن سمع مني بها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Salām b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-ʿAzīzī al-Madanī. One of the witnesses (shuhūd) of the Ḥaram, and among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) there (in Medina)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07659 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07659-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07659-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07659 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد السلام بن أبي الفتح محمد أبو الفضل الكازروني المدني ويعرف بابن تقي ، ممن سمع مني بالمدينة أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Salām b. Abī al-Fatḥ Muḥammad, Abū al-Faḍl, al-Kāzarūnī al-Madanī, known as Ibn Taqī. He too was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D07661 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07661-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07661-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07661 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد السلام بن محمد بن عبد العزيز المدني سبط علي البواب . ممن سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Salām b. Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Madanī, the daughter's son of ʿAlī al-Bawwāb. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D07663 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07663-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07663-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07663 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد السلام الشمس السعودي . ممن سمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Salām, al-Shams al-Saʿūdī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07666 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07666-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07666-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07666 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز بن أحمد بن قاسم ناصر الدين أبو الفرج التميمي المغربي الأصل المدني المالكي الطيب النغمة ويعرف بابن قاسم . ولد سنة سبع وخمسين وثمانمائة بالمدينة ونشأ بها فحفظ القرآن واشتغل قليلا بالفقه والعربية عند مسعود المغربي ولازمني في مجاورتي بالمدينة في أشياء وسمعنا من أناسيده الطيبة هناك ، وتكرر دخوله القاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Aḥmad b. Qāsim, Nāṣir al-Dīn, Abū al-Faraj, al-Tamīmī, of Maghribī origin, of Medina, the Mālikī, of sweet voice, known as Ibn Qāsim. He was born in the year 857 in Medina and grew up there; he memorized the Qurʾān and studied a little jurisprudence and Arabic with Masʿūd al-Maghribī. He attended me (al-Sakhāwī) closely in various matters during my stay (mujāwara) in Medina, and we heard his fine chants there. He entered Cairo repeatedly."@en .

rec:AIND-D07671 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07671-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07671-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07671 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز بن أحمد ناصر الدين المدني الحنفي الخواص . سمع مني بالمدينة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Aḥmad, Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Madanī al-Ḥanafī al-Khawwāṣ. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina."@en .

rec:AIND-D07673 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07673-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07673-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07673 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز بن إسمعيل الغزي الحنبلي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Ismāʿīl al-Ghazzī al-Ḥanbalī. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D07676 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07676-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07676-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07676 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز بن عبد الواحد بن عياذ بتحتانية الإمام الأوحد كمال الدين الأنصاري المدني المالكي والد حسين الماضي ، سمع على صهره النور على المحلى في سنة عشرين وكتب عنه في إجازة سنة سبع وثلاثين بل عرض عليه بعضهم في سنة خمس وأربعين . ومات بعد ذلك وكان ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. ʿIyādh (spelled with a yāʾ), the peerless imam, Kamāl al-Dīn al-Anṣārī al-Madanī al-Mālikī, father of the aforementioned Ḥusayn. He heard from his father-in-law al-Nūr ʿAlī al-Maḥallī in the year 820, and wrote from him in an ijāza in the year 837; moreover, some people presented [their recitation] to him in the year 845. He died after that. He was ... [the text breaks off here]."@en .

rec:AIND-D07677 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07677-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07677-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07677 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد عبد العزيز بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز الهاشمي النويري اليمني المكي وأمه قمرا الهندية فتاة أبيه . ولد سنة ست عشرة وثمانمائة بتعز أو زبيد من اليمن ، وسافر مع أخويه عمر وعبد الرحمن إلى القاهرة في سنة اثنتين وثلاثين ثم إلى المغرب ثم التكرور ومات ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad [b.] ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Hāshimī al-Nuwayrī al-Yamanī al-Makkī. His mother was Qamrā al-Hindiyya, a slave-girl of his father. He was born in the year 816 in Taʿizz or Zabīd in Yemen, and travelled with his two brothers ʿUmar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān to Cairo in the year 832, then to the Maghrib, then to Takrūr, and died."@en .

rec:AIND-D07679 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07679-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07679-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07679 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز بن محمد بن أحمد بن عثمان خير الدين أبو الخير بن البساطي . يأتي في الكنى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿUthmān, Khayr al-Dīn Abū al-Khayr b. al-Bisāṭī. He will appear under the kunyas."@en .

rec:AIND-D07681 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07681-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07681-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07681-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_apply,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07681 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز بن محمد جلال الدين بن العز بن البدر الحراني الأصل القاهري القادري أخو عبد القادر الماضي لأبيه والمحب بن بلكا القادري لأمه . ممن حفظ القرآن والعمدة وسمع على شيخنا وغيره كالبخاري بالظاهرية حيث سمع فيه وأجاز له جماعة باستدعاء ابن فهد وغيره وتكررت تسمية ابن فهد لأبيه بمحمد وهو غلط . ومات قبل أن يتكهل سنة ستين تقريبا رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad, Jalāl al-Dīn b. al-ʿIzz b. al-Badr, of Ḥarrānī origin, al-Qāhirī al-Qādirī, paternal brother of the aforementioned ʿAbd al-Qādir and maternal brother of al-Muḥibb b. Balkā al-Qādirī. He was among those who memorised the Qurʾān and al-ʿUmda, and heard from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) and others, for instance al-Bukhārī at al-Ẓāhiriyya, where he attended its audition. A group granted him an ijāza at the request of Ibn Fahd and others, though Ibn Fahd repeatedly named his father Muḥammad, which is an error. He died before reaching middle age, in about the year 860. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07682 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07682-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07682-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07682 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز بن مسلم الشمس أبو عبد الله المستناني المغربي السكندري المالكي الماضي أبوه . مات في سنة خمس وسبعين أو أوائل التي بعدها بدمياط فإنه توجه إليها صحبة المنصور لكونه كان إمامه وله فيه مزيد اعتقاد مع استفاضة ذكره بالصلاح والعلم وعقل وسكون ، وقد كتب الكثير بخطه رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muslim, al-Shams Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Mustanānī al-Maghribī al-Sakandarī al-Mālikī; his father has been mentioned above. He died in the year 875, or at the beginning of the following year, in Damietta, for he had gone there in the company of al-Manṣūr [ʿUthmān], since he was his imam and al-Manṣūr held him in especially high regard; he was widely reputed for piety and learning, with intelligence and composure. He copied a great deal in his own hand. May God have mercy on him and on us."@en .

rec:AIND-D07683 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07683-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07683-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07683 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز أبي فارس صاحب المغرب . مضى فيمن جده أحمد بن محمد ابن أبي بكر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz Abī Fāris, [son of] the ruler of the Maghrib. He has been mentioned above among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr."@en .

rec:AIND-D07684 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07684-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07684-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07684 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز الجمال المكي الشهير ببيسق الفراش . مضى في ابن أحمد بن عبد العزيز ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, al-Jamāl al-Makkī, famous as Baysaq al-Farrāsh. He has been mentioned above under the son of Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz."@en .

rec:AIND-D07685 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07685-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07685-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07685 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز الشمس بن العماد الأبهري . ممن أخذ عن شيخنا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, al-Shams b. al-ʿImād al-Abharī. He was among those who studied under our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07686 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07686-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07686-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07686 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العزيز زعيم تونس . مات سنة ثمان وثلاثين . كذا كتبه ابن عزم وأظنه الماضي فيمن جده أحمد بن محمد بن أبي بكر وإن لم تكن وفاته كذلك ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, chief of Tunis. He died in the year 838. So Ibn ʿAzm wrote it, and I think he is the one mentioned above among those whose grandfather is Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr, even if his death was not as stated there."@en .

rec:AIND-D07688 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07688-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07688-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07688-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07688-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_apply,
        agent:claude_b87_apply2,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07688 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد العظيم بن يحيى بن أحمد بن عبد العظيم الخانكي . ولد سمع علي بقراءة أبيه ثلاثيات البخاري في ربيع الثاني سنة ست وتسعين وأجزت له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAẓīm b. Yaḥyā b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAẓīm al-Khānkī. He was a young child. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī), through his father's recitation, the Thulāthiyyāt of al-Bukhārī in Rabīʿ al-Thānī of the year 896, and I granted him an ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D07689 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07689-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07689-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07689 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الغفار بن محمد بدر الدين السمديسي الأصل الأزهري المالكي وهو أكبر من موسى الآتي والذي يليه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Ghaffār b. Muḥammad, Badr al-Dīn, of Samadīsī origin, al-Azharī al-Mālikī. He is older than Mūsā, who is mentioned below, and than the one who follows."@en .

rec:AIND-D07691 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07691-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07691-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07691 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الغني بن عبد الرزاق ناصر الدين بن الفخر بن أبي الفرج أخو أحمد الماضي وهو توءمه . ولي نيابة دمياط فدام بها سنة وتنسب له ولأخيه معصرة ، وحج وجاور . ومات بالقاهرة في سنة ثلاث وخمسين تقريبا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. ʿAbd al-Razzāq, Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Fakhr b. Abī al-Faraj, brother of the aforementioned Aḥmad and his twin. He held the deputy governorship of Damietta and remained in it for a year. A press (maʿṣara) is named after him and his brother. He performed the pilgrimage and stayed as a mujāwir. He died in Cairo in about the year 853."@en .

rec:AIND-D07692 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07692-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07692-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07692 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الغني بن محمد بن أحمد بن عثمان بن نعيم بدر الدين البساطي الأصل القاهري المالكي الماضي أبوه وجده ويلقب دبيس . ولد في ربيع الأول سنة ست وثلاثين وثمانمائة بالقاهرة ، وأجاز له البرهان الحلبي وغيره وحفظ بعض الكتب وتكسب بالشهادة وليس بمحمود السيرة . مات في ليلة الأحد ثاني عشري ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿUthmān b. Nuʿaym, Badr al-Dīn, of Bisāṭī origin, al-Qāhirī al-Mālikī; his father and grandfather have been mentioned above. He was nicknamed Dubays. He was born in Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 836 in Cairo. Al-Burhān al-Ḥalabī and others granted him an ijāza. He memorised some books and earned his living as a notary witness, and was not of praiseworthy conduct. He died on the night of Sunday, 22 Rabīʿ al-Awwal of the year 892."@en .

rec:AIND-D07694 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07694-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07694-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07694-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87_apply,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07694 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الغني ناصر الدين القاهري نقيب السقاة ووالد وفا وأمير حاج قاري النعماني ويوسف ويعرف بابن أخي شفتر . استقر نقيب السقاة عقب عمه أخي أبيه لأمه الشمس محمد بن إبراهيم بن بركة الماضي . مات في سنة اثنتين وتسعين واستقر بعده ابنه وفا . )"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Ghanī, Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Qāhirī, head of the water-carriers (naqīb al-suqāt), father of Wafā, of Amīr Ḥājj the reciter at al-Nuʿmān, and of Yūsuf; known as Ibn Akhī Shaftar (the nephew of Shaftar). He was appointed head of the water-carriers after his uncle, his father's maternal brother, al-Shams Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm b. Baraka, mentioned above. He died in the year 892, and his son Wafā succeeded him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07695 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07695-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07695-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07695 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن الخواجا الزين عبد القادر بن البرهان ابراهيم بن حسن المناوي القاهري الماضي أبوه وجده ويعرف كسلفه بابن عليبة . ممن حفظ القرآن وغيره وسمع مني المسلسل وغيره وكذا سمع من الشاوي وامتحن بعد أبيه ورق أحباب أبيه له ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. al-Khawājā al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Qādir b. al-Burhān Ibrāhīm b. Ḥasan al-Manāwī al-Qāhirī; his father and grandfather have been mentioned above. Like his forebears he is known as Ibn ʿUlayba. He was among those who memorised the Qurʾān and other works; he heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) al-Musalsal and other texts, and likewise heard from al-Shāwī. He suffered hardship after his father's [death], and his father's friends took pity on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07696 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07696-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07696-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b87d_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07696 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد القادر أو اسمعيل والأول أشبه بن ابراهيم محي الدين بن مجد الدين المكراني الأصل المكي . مديم للاشتغال عند عبد المحسن وغيره مع فهم وعقل وقد لازمني كثيرا في سنة ست وثمانين وبعدها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Qādir — or Ismāʿīl, though the former is more likely — b. Ibrāhīm, Muḥyī al-Dīn b. Majd al-Dīn, of Makrānī origin, al-Makkī. He was constantly engaged in study under ʿAbd al-Muḥsin and others, with understanding and good sense, and he attended me (al-Sakhāwī) assiduously in the year 886 and thereafter."@en .

rec:AIND-D07733 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07733-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07733-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07733 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد الرضي أبو حامد الحسني الفاسي المكي شقيق اللذين قبله . ممن حفظ القرآن وغيره وقدم القاهرة مع أول أخويه فعرض علي وسمع مني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, al-Raḍī, Abū Ḥāmid, al-Ḥasanī al-Fāsī al-Makkī, full brother of the two preceding. He was among those who memorized the Qurʾān and other works; he came to Cairo with the first of his two brothers, presented (his memorized texts) to me (al-Sakhāwī) and heard from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D07735 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07735-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07735-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07735 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن أحمد بن على المحب أبو عبد الله بن الحجازي المكي الماضي أبوه قدم مع أبيه القاهرة فسمع علي في الأذكار وغيره وكذا سمع على القمصي والديمي وآخرين وحضر عند الفخر المقسي بعض الدروس وكان عاقلا . مات بالطاعون في ليلة الثلاثاء ثامن عشري رمضان سنة ثلاث وسبعين وجزع أبوه عليه عوضهما الله الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī, al-Muḥibb, Abū ʿAbd Allāh, Ibn al-Ḥijāzī, al-Makkī. His father has been mentioned above. He came with his father to Cairo and heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) al-Adhkār and other works; he likewise heard from al-Qumṣī, al-Daymī and others, and attended some lessons with al-Fakhr al-Maqsī. He was sensible. He died of the plague on the night of Tuesday, 28 Ramaḍān 873, and his father grieved over him; may God compensate them both with Paradise."@en .

rec:AIND-D07736 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07736-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07736-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07736-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07736 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد اللطيف بن الكمال أبي الفضل محمد بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد ابن يوسف بن الحسن بن محمد بن محمود الشمس بن السراج الأنصاري الزرندي المدني الشافعي . ولد في ذي الحجة سنة خمسين وثمانمائة وسمع مني بالمدينة بل قرأ على أماكن من الستة . مات في سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. al-Kamāl Abī al-Faḍl Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf b. al-Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. Maḥmūd, al-Shams b. al-Sirāj, al-Anṣārī al-Zarandī al-Madanī al-Shāfiʿī. He was born in Dhū al-Ḥijja 850. He heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Medina, and indeed read to me passages from the Six Books. He died in the year 891."@en .

rec:AIND-D07737 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07737-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07737-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07737-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review,
        agent:claude_b89_93_triage ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07737 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد اللطيف بن محمد بن يوسف بن الحسن الزرندي المدني أظنه جد الذي قبله سمع على الجمال الكازروني سنة أربع وثلاثين وثمانمائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Muḥammad b. Yūsuf b. al-Ḥasan al-Zarandī al-Madanī. I (al-Sakhāwī) think he is the grandfather of the preceding one. He heard from al-Jamāl al-Kāzarūnī in the year 834."@en .

rec:AIND-D07738 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07738-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07738-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07738-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07738 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد اللطيف بن موسي بن عميرة بن موسي الجمال القرشي المخزومي اليبناوي المكي . ولد في ذي الحجة سنة إحدى ... ومات في ذي الحجة سنة بضع وثلاثين بمكة رحمه الله أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf b. Mūsā b. ʿAmīra b. Mūsā, al-Jamāl, al-Qurashī al-Makhzūmī al-Yubnāwī al-Makkī. He was born in Dhū al-Ḥijja in the year [8]?1 (the decade is missing in the printed text) … and died in Dhū al-Ḥijja in one of the years between 833 and 839 in Mecca; may God have mercy on him. Ibn Fahd recorded his death date."@en .

rec:AIND-D07739 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07739-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07739-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07739 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد اللطيف البرلسي السكندري أخو على الماضي . أحد التجار مات في شوال سنة إحدى وثمانين بالرمل ظاهر اسكندرية فحمل إلى الجزيرة خارج باب البحر فدفن عند الشيخ علي الموازيني ، وكان كثير الملاءة جدا مع خير وقوة نفس وسماحة بالبذل في بلوغ مقاصده وحسن شكالة ، وسافر في التجارة لمكة وغيرها وله أوقاف في جهات قرب من جملتها بيت المنصور بن الظاهر جقمق الذي صار إليه بعد خليل بن الناصر اشتراه منه حين تحول لدمياط ثم وقفه رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Laṭīf al-Burullusī al-Sakandarī, brother of the aforementioned ʿAlī. One of the merchants, he died in Shawwāl 881 at al-Raml outside Alexandria and was carried to al-Jazīra outside Bāb al-Baḥr, where he was buried beside Shaykh ʿAlī al-Mawāzīnī. He was very wealthy, with goodness, strength of character, generosity in spending to attain his aims, and a handsome appearance. He travelled for trade to Mecca and elsewhere, and he had endowments (awqāf) for pious purposes, among them the house of al-Manṣūr b. al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq, which came to him after Khalīl b. al-Nāṣir: he bought it from him when Khalīl moved to Damietta and then made it a waqf. May God have mercy on him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07740 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07740-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07740-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07740 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن إبراهيم بن حمام الشمس الشامي ثم المكي المؤدب بها . مات بمكة في ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين وأربعين . أرخه ابن فهد . وكان قدم مكة وقطنها وأدب بها الأطفال وتزوج بزينب ابنة أحمد الشوبكي واستولدها أولادا منهم أحمد وأبو الفتح وكان فقيرا مباكا ، ولما قدم مكة السراج عمر بن المزلق اشترى دارا بقعيقعان ووقفها عليه وعلى أولاده ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ibrāhīm b. Hammām, al-Shams, al-Shāmī, then al-Makkī, the children's tutor there. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ al-Ākhir 842; Ibn Fahd recorded his death date. He had come to Mecca and settled there, teaching children, and married Zaynab, daughter of Aḥmad al-Shawbakī, who bore him children including Aḥmad and Abū al-Fatḥ. He was poor but blessed. When al-Sirāj ʿUmar b. al-Muzalliq came to Mecca he bought a house in Quʿayqiʿān and endowed it as a waqf for him and his children."@en .

rec:AIND-D07742 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07742-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07742-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07742 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد أخو الذي قبله . ولد سنة إحدى وتسعين وسبعمائة وسمع في الخامسة على الفرسيسي مع أخيه مسموعه من السيرة وما علمته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, brother of the preceding. He was born in the year 791 and, in his fifth year, heard from al-Farsīsī, together with his brother, what the latter heard of the Sīra. I (al-Sakhāwī) know nothing more about him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07743 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07743-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07743-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07743 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن إبراهيم البدر القاهري الأزهري ويعرف بالمصري . كتب عنه العز بن فهد قصيدة من نظمه يمدح بها الفخري بن غلبك أولها : %~% خليلي قد هام الفؤاد بأسره %~% وعدة مقاطيع وكان قد %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ibrāhīm, al-Badr, al-Qāhirī al-Azharī, known as al-Miṣrī. Al-ʿIzz b. Fahd wrote down from him a poem of his own composition in praise of al-Fakhrī b. Ghulbak, beginning \"My two friends, the heart is wholly enamoured…\", as well as several short pieces (maqāṭīʿ). He had … (the printed text breaks off)."@en .

rec:AIND-D07744 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07744-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07744-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07744 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن إبراهيم الشمس المسوفي ثم المدني المادح بحرمها والآتي ولده محمد . ولد في سنة سبع وعشرين وثمانمائة وقدم مع أبيه المدينة وهو ابن سنتين أو ثلاث فقرأ القرآن وصار مادح الحرم مع سكون وخير . ولما كنت هناك سمع مني وكتب لي من نظم ولده قصيدة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ibrāhīm, al-Shams, al-Masūfī, then al-Madanī, the panegyrist (mādiḥ) at its Sanctuary, whose son Muḥammad is mentioned below. He was born in the year 827 and came with his father to Medina when he was two or three years old; he learned to recite the Qurʾān and became the panegyrist of the Sanctuary, with composure and goodness. When I (al-Sakhāwī) was there he heard from me and wrote out for me a qaṣīda composed by his son."@en .

rec:AIND-D07745 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07745-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07745-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07745 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن أحمد بن حسن بن الزين محمد بن الأمين محمد بن القطب أبو السعادات الأكبر القسطلاني المكي . أجاز له أو لأخيه الآتي في سنة اثنتين وثمانمائة ركن الدين محمد بن إسمعيل بن محمد الخوافي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Ḥasan b. al-Zayn Muḥammad b. al-Amīn Muḥammad b. al-Quṭb, Abū al-Saʿādāt the Elder, al-Qasṭallānī al-Makkī. Rukn al-Dīn Muḥammad b. Ismāʿīl b. Muḥammad al-Khawāfī granted an ijāza to him, or to his brother who follows, in the year 802."@en .

rec:AIND-D07746 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07746-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07746-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07746 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد أبو السعادات الأصغر . أخو الذي قبله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, Abū al-Saʿādāt the Younger, brother of the preceding."@en .

rec:AIND-D07747 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07747-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07747-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07747-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07747 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد أبو البقاء أخوهما . سمع الزين المراغي وعلي بن مسعود بن عبد المعطي وأبا حامد المطري وابن سلامة والجمال بن ظهيرة وغيرهم ، وأجاز له عائشة ابنة أجاز له عائشة ابنة ابن عبد الهادي والشرف بن الكويك وآخرون . مات بالطاعون في سنة ثلاث وثلاثين بالقاهرة ودفن بتربة سعيد السعداء ، وسيأتي في الكنى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, Abū al-Baqāʾ, brother of the two preceding. He heard from al-Zayn al-Marāghī, ʿAlī b. Masʿūd b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī, Abū Ḥāmid al-Maṭarī, Ibn Salāma, al-Jamāl b. Ẓahīra and others, and ʿĀʾisha bint Ibn ʿAbd al-Hādī, al-Sharaf b. al-Kuwayk and others granted him ijāza. He died of the plague in the year 833 in Cairo and was buried in the Turba of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. He will be mentioned again under the kunyas."@en .

rec:AIND-D07748 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07748-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07748-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07748-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07748-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88g_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07748 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد الجمال أبو الخير الحنبلي أخو الثلاثة قبله . سمع من ابن الجزري وابن سلامة وجماعة وأجاز له الشمس الشاوي والزركشي وابن الطحان وابن ناظر الصاحبة وابن بردس وعبد الرحمن بن الأذرعي وابنة ابن الشرائحي وخلق ودخل القاهرة ودمشق وحلب وحمص وحماة ، وتردد إلى القاهرة مرارا حتى أدركه أجله في المحرم مطعونا سنة ثمان وأربعين ودفن بتربة سعيد السعداء أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, al-Jamāl, Abū al-Khayr, al-Ḥanbalī, brother of the three preceding. He heard from Ibn al-Jazarī, Ibn Salāma and a number of others, and al-Shams al-Shāwī, al-Zarkashī, Ibn al-Ṭaḥḥān, Ibn Nāẓir al-Ṣāḥiba, Ibn Bardas, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Adhraʿī, the daughter of Ibn al-Sharāʾiḥī and many others granted him ijāza. He entered Cairo, Damascus, Aleppo, Ḥimṣ and Ḥamā, and went to Cairo repeatedly until his death overtook him, stricken by the plague, in Muḥarram 848; he too was buried in the Turba of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07749 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07749-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07749-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07749-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D07749-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88g_review,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07749 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد أبو المكارم الحنبلي أخو الأربعة قبله وشقيق اللذين قبله ، أمهم خديجة ابنة إبراهيم بن أحمد المرشدي . سمع ابن الجزري والشمس الشامي وجماعة وأجاز له في سنة أربع عشرة الزين المراغي ، ودخل القاهرة ودمشق وأقام بهامدة وصحب الزين عبد الرحمن أبا شعر ولازمه وتفقه عليه وكذا صحب غيره من الأكابر . ومات بطرابلس من الشام سنة ثلاث وثلاثين ، وسيأتي في الكنى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, Abū al-Makārim, al-Ḥanbalī, brother of the four preceding and full brother of the two immediately preceding; their mother was Khadīja, daughter of Ibrāhīm b. Aḥmad al-Murshidī. He heard from Ibn al-Jazarī, al-Shams al-Shāmī and a number of others, and in the year 814 al-Zayn al-Marāghī granted him an ijāza. He entered Cairo and Damascus and stayed in both for a time; he kept company with al-Zayn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Abū Shaʿr, attended him closely and studied jurisprudence under him, and likewise kept company with other leading scholars. He died in Tripoli of Syria in the year 833. He will be mentioned again under the kunyas."@en .

rec:AIND-D07750 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07750-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07750-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88g_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07750 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن أحمد بن علي بن محمد بن قاسم الشمس بن الجمال بن الحافظ الشهاب القاهري القزازي أخو إبراهيم الماضي ويعرف كسلفه بالعرياني . ولد تقريبا سنة ثمان وثمانمائة ، كان من بيت حديث ورواية ولكن ما علمت له سماعا ولا إجازة نعم سمع وهو كبير معنا على بعض الشيوخ يسيرا واشتغل بالتكسب في الزجاج بحانوت بالوراقين وكان صوفيا في سعيد السعداء . مات في المحرم سنة تسع وسبعين بعد تعلله بالفالج مدة . عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Qāsim, al-Shams b. al-Jamāl b. al-Ḥāfiẓ al-Shihāb, al-Qāhirī al-Qazzāzī, brother of the aforementioned Ibrāhīm, known like his forebears as al-ʿUryānī. He was born around the year 808. He came from a family of ḥadīth and transmission, but I (al-Sakhāwī) know of no audition (samāʿ) or ijāza of his; however, when he was grown he heard a little together with us from some shaykhs. He earned his living in the glass trade in a shop in al-Warrāqīn, and was a Sufi at Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. He died in Muḥarram 879 after suffering from hemiplegia for a time. May God pardon him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07754 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07754-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07754-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07754 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن أحمد التونسي الأصل المكي ويعرف بابن المرجاني . سمع من ابن صديق وغيره واشتغل بالفقه والعربية وتنبه في ذلك مع نظم وخط جيد كتب به الكثير ودين وخير وسكون ، مات في ليلة السبت ثاني ذي الحجة سنة عشر بمكة عن أربع وعشرين سنة تقريبا ودفن بالمعلاة ذكره الفاسي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad, of Tunisian origin, the Meccan, known as Ibn al-Marjānī. He heard from Ibn Ṣiddīq and others, occupied himself with jurisprudence and Arabic, and distinguished himself in these, along with poetry, a fine hand with which he copied a great deal, piety, goodness and tranquillity. He died on the night of Saturday, 2 Dhū al-Ḥijja (8)10, in Mecca, aged about twenty-four, and was buried at al-Muʿallā. Al-Fāsī mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07755 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07755-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07755-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07755 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن أحمد الحضرمي . ممن سمع مني بمكة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad al-Ḥaḍramī, among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca."@en .

rec:AIND-D07756 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07756-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07756-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07756 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن أحمد الخانكي البلبيسي الأصل ويعرف بابن التاجر . ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad al-Khānkī, of Bilbays origin, known as Ibn al-Tājir. He was among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D07758 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07758-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07758-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07758 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن بكتمر ناصر الدين بن جمال الدين ويعرف بابن الحاجب . تقدم في ولاية صهره بالدوادارية وكان من أمراء العشرات بالديار المصرية . مات في خامس عشري ربيع الآخر سنة اثنتين . أرخه العيني وقال إنه خلف موجودا كثيرا . وأرخه شيخنا في إنبائه في ربيع الأول والأول هو الصواب ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Baktamur, Nāṣir al-Dīn b. Jamāl al-Dīn, known as Ibn al-Ḥājib. He rose to prominence while his in-law held the office of dawādār, and was one of the amirs of ten in the Egyptian realm. He died on 25 Rabīʿ II (8)02. Al-ʿAynī recorded his death and said that he left behind much property. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) dated it in his Inbāʾ to Rabīʿ I, but the former is correct."@en .

rec:AIND-D07759 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07759-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07759-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07759 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن أبي بكر بن عبد الله بن ظهيرة بن أحمد بن عطية بن ظهيرة القرشي المكي ، أمه زبيدية وهي نفيسة ابنة إبراهيم بن أبي بكر بن عبد المعطي العصامي . أجاز له في سنة ست وثلاثين وثمانمائة فما بعدها جماعة أجازوا لأبي الفضل محمد بن أحمد بن أبي الفضل بن أحمد بن ظهيرة الماضي . ومات في شوال سنة ست وستين بجدة وحمل فدفن بالمعلاة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ẓuhayra b. Aḥmad b. ʿAṭiyya b. Ẓuhayra al-Qurashī al-Makkī. His mother was a woman of Zabīd, Nafīsa bt. Ibrāhīm b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī al-ʿIṣāmī. In 836 and thereafter he was granted ijāza by a group who had granted ijāza to the aforementioned Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Abī al-Faḍl b. Aḥmad b. Ẓuhayra. He died in Shawwāl (8)66 in Jidda and was carried and buried at al-Muʿallā."@en .

rec:AIND-D07762 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07762-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07762-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07762 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن بلال الفراش بالمسجد الحرام وأخو أحمد وإسحق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Bilāl, the farrāsh (attendant in charge of furnishings) at the Sacred Mosque (al-Masjid al-Ḥarām), and the brother of Aḥmad and Isḥāq."@en .

rec:AIND-D07763 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07763-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07763-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07763 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن جار الله بن زائد السنبسي المكي . مات بمكة في المحرم سنة إحدى وسبعين ، ذكره ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Jār Allāh b. Zāʾid al-Sinbisī al-Makkī. He died in Mecca in Muḥarram (8)71. Ibn Fahd mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D07768 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07768-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07768-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07768 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن حسن بن المواز . مات فجأة في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وثلاثين عن نحو الستين ، ذكره المقريزي في عقوده وقال : كان دينا صاحب نسك وتجرد وتقلل من الدنيا مع عصبية ومروءة ومحبة في الحديث وأهله واتباع للسنة وأنه رأى له بعد موته مناما فيه أنه سلم من عذاب القبر ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥasan b. al-Mawwāz. He died suddenly in Rabīʿ I (8)32, aged about sixty. Al-Maqrīzī mentioned him in his ʿUqūd and said: he was pious, a man of devotion, detachment and frugality towards this world, together with zeal, manliness, love of ḥadīth and its people, and adherence to the Sunna; and that someone saw a dream about him after his death in which he was shown to have been spared the torment of the grave."@en .

rec:AIND-D07769 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07769-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07769-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07769 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن حسين الجمال أبو عبد الله بن العفيف الحسني اليماني حفيد البدر الأهدل وابن عم حسين بن صديق ، سمع مني بمكة في سنة ست وثمانين أشياء . وقدم القاهرة غير مرة منها في سنة ثمان وثمانين وسافر منها إلى الصعيد فحصل رزيقا ثم عاد ، ونعم الرجل خيرا وسكونا وتقنعا ثم لقيني بمكة أيضا في سنة أربع وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥusayn, al-Jamāl Abū ʿAbd Allāh b. al-ʿAfīf al-Ḥasanī al-Yamānī, grandson of al-Badr al-Ahdal and cousin of Ḥusayn b. Ṣiddīq. He heard some things from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Mecca in (8)86. He came to Cairo more than once, including in 888, and travelled from there to Upper Egypt (al-Ṣaʿīd), where he obtained a small livelihood, and then returned. What a fine man he is in goodness, tranquillity and contentment. He then met me again in Mecca in 894."@en .

rec:AIND-D07770 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07770-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07770-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07770 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن حسين الشمس النويري ثم القاهري الشافعي جد البدر النويري لأمه . ذكر لي سبطه أنه حفظ الشاطبية والتنبيه وغيرهما وأنه تلا بالسبع ، وكان متميزا يقرئ القراآت والفقه . ومات في سنة ستين عن نحو المائة فالله أعلم ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ḥusayn, al-Shams al-Nuwayrī, then al-Qāhirī, the Shāfiʿī, maternal grandfather of al-Badr al-Nuwayrī. His grandson told me that he memorised al-Shāṭibiyya, al-Tanbīh and other works, and that he recited according to the seven readings. He was distinguished and taught the Qurʾānic readings and jurisprudence. He died in (8)60 at about a hundred years of age, but God knows best."@en .

rec:AIND-D07775 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07775-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07775-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07775 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن سعيد الشمس الكلبشاوي الخطيب ممن سمع مني بالقاهرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Saʿīd, al-Shams al-Kalbashāwī, the preacher (khaṭīb), among those who heard from me (al-Sakhāwī) in Cairo."@en .

rec:AIND-D07776 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07776-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07776-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07776 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن سلام الدمشقي أخو علاء الدين وهو الأصغر . مات في رجب سنة ثلاث بعد انفصال التمرية قاله شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Sallām al-Dimashqī, brother of ʿAlāʾ al-Dīn and the younger of the two. He died in Rajab (8)03, after the withdrawal of Timur's forces; so said our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07777 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07777-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07777-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07777-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07777 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن سليمان العز المحلي ثم القاهري الشافعي أحد النواب ممن اشتغل ولازم العلم البلقيني وعمل التوقيع ببابه فمنعه البدر البغدادي الحنبلي وأثبت شيئا في تركة ابن حجي ، وكاد أزبك الظاهري الإيقاع به فاختفى وكان ذلك سببا لهجر يحيى بن حجي مجلس مستنيبه وإقباله على المناوي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Sulaymān, al-ʿIzz al-Maḥallī, then al-Qāhirī, the Shāfiʿī, one of the deputy judges. He was among those who studied and attached themselves to al-ʿAlam al-Bulqīnī, and he worked as a drafter of decrees (tawqīʿ) at his court, but al-Badr al-Baghdādī the Ḥanbalī stopped him. He established (in court) something concerning the estate of Ibn Ḥajjī, and Azbak al-Ẓāhirī nearly brought harm upon him, so he went into hiding. This was the reason why Yaḥyā b. Ḥajjī deserted the court of the judge who had appointed him (Muḥammad) as deputy and turned to al-Manāwī."@en .

rec:AIND-D07779 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07779-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07779-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07779 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن شوعان الزبيدي الحنفي . انتهت إليه الرياسة في مذهبه ببلده ، ودرس وأفاد . مات سنة اثنتين وعشرين ، ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Shawʿān al-Zabīdī, the Ḥanafī. Leadership of his school in his town came to rest with him; he taught and benefited others. He died in (8)22. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in his Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D07783 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07783-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07783-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07783-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07783 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن طيمان ... سنة خمس عشرة وأظنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṭaymān. ... the year (8)15, and I think he ... [lacuna in the printed text]"@en .

rec:AIND-D07786 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07786-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07786-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07786-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_verify_content,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07786 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن بن محمد بن صلح بن إسمعيل الكمال أبو الفضل بن الجمال بن ناصر الدين الكناني المدني الشافعي . ممن أخذ عن الشهاب البيجوري في الفقه والفرائض وسمع على أبي الفتح المراغي وغيره ودخل مصر والشام وغيرهما بل العجم . وهو حي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Muḥammad b. Ṣulḥ b. Ismāʿīl, al-Kamāl Abū al-Faḍl b. al-Jamāl b. Nāṣir al-Dīn al-Kinānī al-Madanī, the Shāfiʿī. He was among those who studied jurisprudence and the law of inheritance under al-Shihāb al-Bījūrī, and he heard from Abū al-Fatḥ al-Marāghī and others. He travelled to Egypt, Syria and elsewhere, even to Persia (al-ʿAjam). He is still alive."@en .

rec:AIND-D07791 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07791-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07791-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07791 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن عبد الكريم البناء الشهير بتشن . مات بمكة في ربيع الآخر سنة ستين ، أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Karīm, the builder (al-bannāʾ), well known as Tashan. He died in Mecca in Rabīʿ II (8)60; Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D07792 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07792-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07792-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D07792-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07792 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن عبد الله الشمس أبو عبد الله ثم الدمشقي الحنبلي الفقيه المقري . ترجمه البرهان الحلبي فقال : إنسان حسن حنبلي أصلا وفرعا من محبي التقي بن تيمية ، قدم حلب في عاشر المحرم سنة تسع وثلاثين فقرأ على سنن ابن ماجه ومشيخة الفخر ، ثم عاد إلى جهة دمشق في خامس عشريه كتب الله سلامته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Shams Abū ʿAbd Allāh, then al-Dimashqī, the Ḥanbalī jurist and Qurʾān reciter. Al-Burhān al-Ḥalabī wrote his biography, saying: \"A good man, Ḥanbalī by origin and by training, one of the admirers of al-Taqī Ibn Taymiyya. He came to Aleppo on 10 Muḥarram (8)39 and read to me the Sunan of Ibn Māja and the Mashyakha of al-Fakhr, then returned towards Damascus on the 25th of the same month. May God decree his safety.\""@en .

rec:AIND-D07795 a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D07795-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D07795-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Assistant_4,
        agent:claude_b88h_review ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D07795 ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن عبد الله بن عشائر . هو ابن عبد الله بن أحمد بن محمد ابن هاشم بن عبد الواحد . مضى ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAshāʾir. He is the son of ʿAbd Allāh b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Hāshim b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid. Mentioned above."@en .

rec:AIND-D08896a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08896a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08896a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد الجمال أو البهاء أبو عبد الله أخو الذي قبله . ولد سنة تسع وستين وسبعمائة بمكة بعد وصول الخبر بموت أبيه في القاهرة وأحضر في الرابعة على الجمال ابن عبد المعطي بعض ابن حبان وسمع من الأميوطي والنشاوري وعلي النويري وغيرهم ودخل القاهرة غير مرة فسمع من التنوخي وابن الشيخة والحلاوي وطائفة بل سمع بها في ربيع الآخر من سنة وفاته على الفوى من لفظ الكلوتاتي الكثير من سنن الدار قطني وكذا دخل دمشق وسمع فيها من أبي هريرة بن الذهبي وغيره ، وأجاز له علي الزرندي والقيراطي وأحمد بن سالم المؤذن في آخرين وتكرر دخوله لبلاد اليمن طلبا للرزق حتى كانت منيته بها في سنة سبع وعشرين أظنه في أواخرها ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, al-Jamāl or al-Bahāʾ, Abū ʿAbd Allāh, brother of the preceding entry (al-Kamāl Abū al-Faḍl Ibn al-Bahāʾ al-Darkālī, of Mecca, Mālikī). Born in Mecca in 769 after news arrived of his father's death in Cairo. At age four he attended al-Jamāl Ibn ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī for part of Ibn Ḥibbān, and heard from al-Amyūṭī, al-Nashāwarī, ʿAlī al-Nuwayrī and others. He entered Cairo several times, hearing from al-Tanūkhī, Ibn al-Shaykha, al-Ḥallāwī and a group; in Rabīʿ II of the year of his death he heard there, from al-Fuwwī through the recitation of al-Kulūtātī, much of the Sunan of al-Dāraquṭnī. He also entered Damascus and heard from Abū Hurayra Ibn al-Dhahabī and others. ʿAlī al-Zarandī, al-Qīrāṭī, Aḥmad b. Sālim al-Muʾadhdhin and others gave him ijāza. He repeatedly travelled to Yemen in search of livelihood until he died there in 827, probably towards its end."@en .

rec:AIND-D08902a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08902a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08902a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن عثمان بن سليمان بن رسول البدر بن المحب بن الاشقر ممن سمع ختم البخاري بالظاهرية القديمة واستقر في مشييخة الخانقاه الناصرية بسرياقوس ونظرها بعد أبيه شريكا لأخيه الشهاب أحمد ثم انتزع جانبك الجداوي في أيام الظاهر خشقدم النظر وتبعه الشهاب العيني ثم بعد أربع سنين أخرج المسجد حتى بذل له صاحب الترجمة نحو ألف دينار مع مساعدة الصوفية له واستقل بها مدة مع خموله ومزيد فاقته وعدم توقيه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān b. Sulaymān b. Rasūl, al-Badr b. al-Muḥibb Ibn al-Ashqar. One of those who attended the completion (khatm) of al-Bukhārī at the old Ẓāhiriyya. He succeeded his father as shaykh and nāẓir of the Nāṣiriyya khānqāh at Siryāqūs, jointly with his brother al-Shihāb Aḥmad. Then, in the days of al-Ẓāhir Khushqadam, Jānibak al-Jaddāwī seized the supervision, followed by al-Shihāb al-ʿAynī; four years later he was expelled from the mosque, until the subject paid about a thousand dinars, with the help of the Sufis, and held it alone for a time — despite his obscurity, great poverty and lack of caution."@en .

rec:AIND-D08902b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08902b-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D08902b-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:Kumakura,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08902b ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن عثمان بن عبد الله الشمس الجناني الصالحي المؤذن بالجامع المظفري منها ويعرف بابن شقير . سمع من ابن قيم الضيائية الأول من حديث على بن المفرج الصقلي وغيره ومن ابن النجم المجالس الأربعة الاخيرة من السمعونيات ومن محمد بن المحب عبد الله بن عبد الحميد بن عبد الهادي جزء ابن مخيت وغيره ومن ست العرب حفيدة الفخر أول المزكيات وغيره ومن عمر بن عثمان بن سالم في آخرين وحدث سمع منه ابن موسى والموفق الأبي في سنة خمس عشرة بدمشق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān b. ʿAbd Allāh, al-Shams al-Jinānī al-Ṣāliḥī, muezzin of the Muẓaffarī mosque there (al-Ṣāliḥiyya), known as Ibn Shuqayr. He heard from Ibn Qayyim al-Ḍiyāʾiyya the first part of the ḥadīth of ʿAlī b. al-Mufarrij al-Ṣiqillī and other things; from Ibn al-Najm the last four sessions of the Samʿūniyyāt; from Muḥammad b. al-Muḥibb ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd b. ʿAbd al-Hādī the Juzʾ of Ibn Mukhayt and other things; from Sitt al-ʿArab, granddaughter of al-Fakhr, the first of the Muzakkiyyāt and other things; and from ʿUmar b. ʿUthmān b. Sālim, among others. He transmitted ḥadīth: Ibn Mūsā and al-Muwaffaq al-Ubbī heard from him in Damascus in 815."@en .

rec:AIND-D08902c a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08902c-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D08902c-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08902c ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن عثمان بن محمد بن أحمد بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن عيسى ابن بدران بن رحمة الشمس أبو عبد الله السعدي الاخنائي الدمشقي الشافعي . ولد سنة سبع وخمسين بدمشق وكان يذكر أنه من ذرية شاور وزير الفاطميين ونشأ فاشتغل قليلا وناب في الحكم ببعض البلاد عن البرهان بن جماعة ثم ناب بدمشق وولي قضاء غزة ثم حلب في سنة سبع وتسعين عوضا عن ناصر الدين خطيب نقيرين نحو سنتين فأكثر ثم دمشق في أيام الظاهر برقوق ثم ولده ثم الديار المصرية مرارا ثم أخرجه الجمال البيرى الاستادار لدمشق فوليها مرارا أيضا ثم امتحن غير مرة وكان شكلا ضخما حسن الملتقي كثير البشر والاحسان للطلبة عارفا بجمع المال كثير البذل له على الوظائف والمداراة للاكابر مع قلة البضاعة في الفقه وربما افتضح في بعض المجالس لكن بذله واحسانه يستره . ذكره شيخنا في إنبائه وقال اجتمعت به عند السالمي وقطلوبغا الكركي في مجلس الحديث ولم يتفق اجتماعي معه في منزله لا بدمشق مع أني كنت بها حين كان قاضيها ولا بالقاهرة وكان يقول أنا قاض كريم والبلقيني قاض عالم . مات في رجب سنة ست عشرة ولم يكمل الستين . وقال ابن خطيب الناصرية في تاريخه كان شكلا حسنا رئيسا ذاهمة عالية وحشمة وبذلك أثنى عليه غيره . وقال المقريزي في عقوده إنه كان عار من العلم تردد إلي بدمشق مرارا وصحبته بها وكان من رجال الدهر العارفين بطرق السعي وأما الآخرة فما أحسب له فيها من نصيب إلا أن يشاء ربي شيئا إنه غفور رحيم عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUthmān b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿĪsā Ibn Badrān b. Raḥma, al-Shams Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī al-Akhnāʾī al-Dimashqī al-Shāfiʿī. Born in Damascus in 757; he used to claim descent from Shāwar, vizier of the Fatimids. He studied a little, served as deputy judge in some towns for al-Burhān Ibn Jamāʿa, then as deputy in Damascus, held the judgeship of Gaza, then of Aleppo in 797 in place of Nāṣir al-Dīn Khaṭīb Nuqayrīn for two years or more, then of Damascus in the days of al-Ẓāhir Barqūq and his son, then of Egypt several times; then al-Jamāl al-Bīrī the ustādār expelled him to Damascus, whose judgeship he held again several times. He suffered adversity more than once. He was imposing, affable and generous to students, skilled at amassing money and lavish in spending it on offices and on courting the great, but of scant learning in fiqh and sometimes embarrassed in gatherings, though his generosity covered for him. Our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar) mentioned him in the Inbāʾ: \"I met him at the ḥadīth session at al-Sālimī's and Quṭlūbughā al-Karakī's ... he used to say: I am a generous judge and al-Bulqīnī a learned judge.\" He died in Rajab 816, not having completed sixty. Ibn Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya in his history called him a handsome, dignified chief of lofty ambition; al-Maqrīzī in his ʿUqūd said he was devoid of learning, a worldly man skilled in the ways of advancement, with little share in the hereafter unless God wills."@en .

rec:AIND-D08909a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08909a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08909a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن علوان بن نبهان بن عمر بن نبهان بن غبافر الجبريني الحلبي . ولد تقريبا سنة ثلاث وستين وسبعمائة وسمع من قريبه أبي عبد الله محمد بن علي بن محمد بن نبهان الأربعين لابن المجبر بسماعه من قريبه صافي بن نبهان بسماعه من المخرجة له وحدث بها سمعها منه الأئمة ومات ..."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlwān b. Nabhān b. ʿUmar b. Nabhān b. Ghabāfir al-Jabrīnī al-Ḥalabī. Born about 763. He heard from his relative Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Nabhān the Arbaʿīn of Ibn al-Mujabbar, by the latter's audition from his relative Ṣāfī b. Nabhān, by his audition from its compiler. He transmitted it, and leading scholars heard it from him. He died ... [lacuna]."@en .

rec:AIND-D08910a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08910a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D08910a-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D08910a-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D08910a-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D08910a-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08910a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن علي بن أحمد بن أبي بكر بن اسماعيل بن أحمد بن علي ابن ابراهيم الشمس المجاهدي الأيوبي لكونه من ذرية الصلاح يوسف بن أيوب وربما كتب الصالحي الأيوبي الحموي ثم الحلبي الشافعي الصوفي ويعرف بابن الشماع . ولد في مستهل سنة إحدي وتسعين وسبعمائة بحماة وانتقل منها وهو صغير مع أبيه لمصر فأقام بها وحفظ القرآن والتنبيه والربع الأول من المهذب للنووي وحضر دروس السراج البلقيني وتفقه بالبيجوري والولي العراقي وأخذ منطق المختصر وغيره عن العز بن جماعة ولازم البساطي في كثير من الفنون ولقي بحماة الجمال بن خطيب المنصورية فأخذ عنه أيضا الفقه وكذا الأصول والعربية وأخذهما أيضا عن العلاء بن المغلي وصحب البرهان السلماسي الشهير بابن البقال بالقاهرة وأخذ عنه طريق القوم وذلك في رمضان سنة ثلاث وثمانمائة وقال انه أخذ بتبريز في سنة ثلاث وأربعين وسبعمائة عن الجمال عبد الله العجمي شيخ الشهاب بن الناصح الذي قيل انه عمر مائة سنة وخمسا وثمانين سنة... وأن أول شيء دخل جوفه ريق الشيخ عبد القادر الكيلاني حيث حنكه وألبسه لما أتت به أمه اليه وذلك بعيد عن الصحة وكذا صحب صاحب الترجمة الزين الخافي وغيره من شيوخ الوقت واجتمع بالعلاء البخاري والتقي الحصني يسيرا ولبس الخرقة وتلقن الذكر من سعد الدين الصوفي بلباسه لها من طريق ابن العربي وسمع الحديث فيما ذكر على الولي العراقي والعز بن جماعة وابن خلدون واستوطن حلب من سنة ثلاثين متصديا لتربية المريدين وارشاد القاصدين حتى أخذ عنه جماعة وصارت له فيها وجاهة وجلالة ورسائل مقبولة وقد لقيته بها فكتبت عنه من نظمه قوله : %~% صرفت عن الكثرات وجه توجهي %~% إلى وحدة الوجه الكريم الممجد %~% %~% فما خاب مصروف إلى الحق وجهه %~% وقد خاب من أضحى من الخلق يجتدي %~% وقوله : %~% لو كنت أعلم أن وصلك ممكن %~% بتلاف روحي أو ذهاب وجودي %~% %~% لمحوت سطري من صحيفة عالمي %~% وهجرت كوني في وصال شهودي %~% وكذا أخذ عنه التاج بن زهرة وأنشدني عنه قوله في الوظائف السبعة التي ذكرها الغزالي ولم يخلها من كتبه الكلامية والصوفية : %~% تقديس إيمان وعجز فافهم %~% واسكت مكفا ثم أمسك سلم %~% وكان إماما علامة فصيحا طلق اللسان رائق النظم والنثر بديع الذكاء حسن الأخلاق والمعاشرة والشكالة والبزة ممتع المحاضرة سريع الجواب مجيدا لما يتكلم فيه مثريا ذا مال طائل منعزلا عن الناس ببيته الذي أنشأه بحلب وهو من محاسن بيوتها متعففا عن وظائف الفقهاء وما أشبهها مستغنيا بأصناف المتاجر ذا يد طولى في علم الكلام والفلك والحرف والتصوف ولكنه ينسب إلى مقالة ابن العربي ولذا كان البلاطنسي يقع فيه ورأيت بخطه ما يدل على التبري من ذلك هذا مع أنه أورد سنده بلباس الخرقة في إجازة كتبها للسيد العلاء بن عفيف الدين من طريقه وقال ما نصه ومولانا الشيخ محي الدين المشار إليه لبسها مرارا بحيث روينا عنه أنه لبس الخرقة وتلقن الذكر وتأدب بنحو من سبعمائة شيخ من مشايخ الطريقة وأئمة الحقيقة وساق طرفا من ذلك فالله أعلم بحقيقة أمره ، وقد حج غير مرة وجاور بمكة بعد الثلاثين ودخل الهند وساح ورابط ببعض الثغور وقتا وشرح قطعة من الحاوي الصغير ومن الإرشاد للقاضي أبي بكر الباقلاني في الأصول وأعرب جميع ألفية ابن ملك لأجل ولده أبي الطاهر وشرح البرهانية في أصول الدين وعمل كتابا في مصطلح الصوفية سماه منشأ الأغاليط وأفرد رحلته في مجلد وعقيدته بالتأليف وتبرا فيها من كل ما يخالف السنة والجماعة ولم يزل على جلالته إلى أن وقع بحلب فناء عظيم توفي فيه غالب من عنده من ولد وأهل وخدم فأسف وتوجه إلى مكة عازما على المجاورة بها صحبة الركب الحلبي ولقيه ابن السيد عفيف الدين بالشام وهو متوعك فقال له قد كنت عزمت على المجاورة بمكة والآن وقع في خاطري مزيد الرغبة في المجاورة بالمدينة النبوية فكان كذلك فإنه استمر في توعكه إلى يوم دخوله لها وذلك في يوم الثلاثاء العشرين من ذي القعدة سنة ثلاث وستين فمات ودفن بالبقيع بعد أن صلى عليه بالروضة النبوية رحمه الله وعفا عنه ورثاه زوج ابنة الفاضل جلال الدين بن النصيبي بقصيدة مطلعها : %~% أخفاك يا شمس العلوم كسوف %~% من بعد فقدك ناظري مكفوف %~%"@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Ismāʿīl b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī Ibn Ibrāhīm, al-Shams al-Mujāhidī al-Ayyūbī (being a descendant of al-Ṣalāḥ Yūsuf b. Ayyūb; he sometimes wrote al-Ṣāliḥī al-Ayyūbī), of Ḥamā then Aleppo, Shāfiʿī, Sufi, known as Ibn al-Shammāʿ. Born at the start of 791 in Ḥamā; moved as a child with his father to Egypt, where he memorised the Qurʾān, al-Tanbīh and the first quarter of al-Muhadhdhab. He attended the lessons of al-Sirāj al-Bulqīnī, studied fiqh with al-Bījūrī and al-Walī al-ʿIrāqī, took the logic of the Mukhtaṣar from al-ʿIzz Ibn Jamāʿa, and kept company with al-Bisāṭī in many disciplines. In Ḥamā he met al-Jamāl Ibn Khaṭīb al-Manṣūriyya, from whom he took fiqh, uṣūl and Arabic, the latter two also from al-ʿAlāʾ Ibn al-Mughallī. In Cairo he accompanied al-Burhān al-Salmāsī, famous as Ibn al-Baqqāl, and took from him the Sufi path in Ramaḍān 803. He claimed to have studied at Tabriz in 743 with al-Jamāl ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAjamī, shaykh of al-Shihāb Ibn al-Nāṣiḥ who was said to have lived 185 years, and told other tales of ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Kīlānī, all far from the truth. He also accompanied al-Zayn al-Khāfī and other shaykhs of the time, met al-ʿAlāʾ al-Bukhārī and al-Taqī al-Ḥiṣnī briefly, and was invested with the khirqa and instructed in dhikr by Saʿd al-Dīn al-Ṣūfī, in the line of Ibn al-ʿArabī. He said he heard ḥadīth from al-Walī al-ʿIrāqī, al-ʿIzz Ibn Jamāʿa and Ibn Khaldūn. He settled in Aleppo from 830, devoting himself to training disciples; a group took from him, and he gained standing there. I met him there and wrote down his verse; al-Tāj Ibn Zuhra also took from him. He was a learned imam, eloquent, a fine poet and prose writer, intelligent, of good character and appearance, wealthy, living apart in the house he built in Aleppo, disdaining jurists' posts and living by trade; expert in kalām, astronomy, the science of letters and Sufism, but suspected of Ibn al-ʿArabī's doctrine, for which al-Balāṭunsī attacked him — though I saw in his hand a disavowal, even as he cited in an ijāza for al-Sayyid al-ʿAlāʾ Ibn ʿAfīf al-Dīn his khirqa chain through Ibn al-ʿArabī. He performed the pilgrimage several times, resided in Mecca after 830, visited India, travelled and garrisoned frontier posts. He wrote commentaries on part of al-Ḥāwī al-Ṣaghīr and of al-Bāqillānī's Irshād, parsed the whole Alfiyya of Ibn Mālik for his son Abū al-Ṭāhir, commented on al-Burhāniyya in theology, composed Manshaʾ al-Aghālīṭ on Sufi terminology, a travel account and a creed. After a great plague in Aleppo killed most of his children, family and servants, he set out for Mecca with the Aleppo caravan, but, falling ill, resolved instead on Medina, where he died on the day of his arrival, Tuesday 20 Dhū al-Qaʿda 863, and was buried in al-Baqīʿ after prayers in the Prophet's Rawḍa. The son-in-law of Jalāl al-Dīn Ibn al-Naṣībī elegised him."@en .

rec:AIND-D08912a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08912a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D08912a-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D08912a-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D08912a-resp-4 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08912a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن علي بن أحمد بن عبد العزيز بن القسم الجمال أبو المحامد ابن الولوي أبي عبد الله الهاشمي العقيلي النويري المكي المالكي ابن عم الذي قبله ووالد أبي عبد الله محمد الآتي ، وأمه عائشة ابنة علي بن عبد العزيز بن عبد الكافي الدقوقي . ولد بمكة ونشأ بها ، وسمع من النجم المرجاني والتقى الفاسي والجمال المرشدي وابن الجزري وغيرهم ، وأجاز له عائشة ابنة ابن عبد الهادي وعبد القادر الأرموي وابن طولوبغا وخلق ، ودخل القاهرة غير مرة وحضر بها مجلس الزين عبادة وناب في القضاء والإمامة بمقام المالكية عن أبيه ثم استقل بنصف الإمامة ثم عزل عنها ثم أعيد حتى مات في صبيحة يوم الجمعة ثالث عشرى ربيع الأول سنة ثلاث وخمسين واستقر فيما كان معه من الإمامة ولده رحمه الله ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. al-Qāsim, al-Jamāl Abū al-Maḥāmid Ibn al-Walawī Abī ʿAbd Allāh al-Hāshimī al-ʿUqaylī al-Nuwayrī al-Makkī al-Mālikī, cousin (ibn ʿamm) of the preceding entry and father of Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad (below). His mother was ʿĀʾisha bt. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. ʿAbd al-Kāfī al-Daqūqī. Born and raised in Mecca, he heard from al-Najm al-Marjānī, al-Taqī al-Fāsī, al-Jamāl al-Murshidī, Ibn al-Jazarī and others; ʿĀʾisha bt. Ibn ʿAbd al-Hādī, ʿAbd al-Qādir al-Urmawī, Ibn Ṭūlūbughā and many others gave him ijāza. He entered Cairo several times and attended the session of al-Zayn ʿUbāda there. He deputised for his father as judge and as imam at the Mālikī station, then held half the imamate independently, was dismissed, then reinstated until he died on the morning of Friday 23 Rabīʿ I 853; his son succeeded to the imamate he held."@en .

rec:AIND-D08924a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08924a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D08924a-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08924a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن علي بن حسن بن ستي أبو النجا الداري الخليلي شيخ المتصوفة المنسوبين للطائفة القادرية . مات به في يوم الأحد ثاني عشر ربيع الأول سنة ست و تسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Ḥasan b. Sittī, Abū al-Najā al-Dārī al-Khalīlī, shaykh of the Sufis affiliated to the Qādirī order. He died there (Hebron) on Sunday 12 Rabīʿ I 896."@en .

rec:AIND-D08929a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08929a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D08929a-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D08929a-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08929a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن علي بن عبد القادر ناصر الدين أبو عبد الله بن ناصر الدين ابن العلاء المقريزي الاصل القاهري الشافعي ابن أخي التقي أحمد المقريزي الماضي . ولد في شوال سنة إحدى وثمانمائة بالقاهرة ونشأ بها فحفظ القرآن والعمدة والتبريزي وعرضهما على جماعة كالعز بن جماعة والشهاب الاوحدي والزين القمني وأجازوه والبيجوري والبلالي وغيرهما ممن لم يجز وكان عرضه للعمدة في سنة عشر وحينئذ ففي مولده نظر وحدث سمع منه بعض الطلبة أجاز لنا وكان أحد الصوفية السعيدية وفي كلامه تزيد . مات في يوم الجمعة سادس المحرم سنة سبع وستين عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Qādir, Nāṣir al-Dīn Abū ʿAbd Allāh b. Nāṣir al-Dīn Ibn al-ʿAlāʾ, of Maqrīz origin, Cairene, Shāfiʿī, nephew of al-Taqī Aḥmad al-Maqrīzī. Born in Shawwāl 801 in Cairo, he memorised the Qurʾān, the ʿUmda and al-Tabrīzī, presenting the latter two to a group including al-ʿIzz Ibn Jamāʿa, al-Shihāb al-Awḥadī and al-Zayn al-Qumnī, who gave him ijāza, and to al-Bījūrī, al-Balālī and others who did not. His presentation of the ʿUmda was in 810, which casts doubt on his birth date. He transmitted; some students heard from him, and he gave us ijāza. He was one of the Sufis of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ, and there was exaggeration in his talk. He died on Friday 6 Muḥarram 867."@en .

rec:AIND-D08929b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08929b-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D08929b-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D08929b-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_b87_merge,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08929b ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن علي بن عبد الكافي بن علي بن عبد الواحد بن محمد بن صغير الكمال بن الشمس بن العلاء القاهري الحنبلي الطبيب حفيد رئيس الاطباء ويعرف كسلفه بابن صغير ككبير . ممن حفظ القرآن والعمدة والخرقي وألفية النحو والموجز في الطب واللمحة العفيفية في الاسباب والعلامات في الطب وفصول ابقراط ومقدمة المعرفة له وتشريح الاعضاء والزبد في الطب وعرضها في سنة ست عشرة على العز بن جماعة وغيره وأجاز له بل عرض قبل ذلك في سنة إحدى عشرة وتعاني الطب كسلفه وأخذ فيه عن أبيه والعز بن جماعة وتميز فيه بحيث تدرب به جماعة وشارك في بعض الفضائل وعالج المرضى دهرا واستقر في نوبة بالبيمارستان وتربة برقوق وسافر مع الركاب السلطاني إلى آمد رفيقا لغيره من الاطباء صحبة رئيسهم وحج غير مرة وجاور وعدا عليه فتى له فقتل زوجته واختلس بعض متاعه فكان ذلك ابتداء ضعفه بل كف ولم ينقطع عن مباشرة نوبته وغيرها الى أن اشتد به الامر وأقعد وهو مع ذلك صابر محتسب يكثر التلاوة جدا حتى مات في صغر سنة إحدى وتسعين وهو ابن ست وتسعين فيما قاله لي أخوه العلاء علي وهو الذي ورثه مع زوجته . وعرضه في سنة إحدى عشرة يستأنس به لأنه ولد قبل القرن . وكنت كالوالد ممن يثق بعلاجه لمزيد دربته وتؤدته ولطفه وحسن خطابه وبهائه وخفة وطأته مع فضيلته بل عالج شيخنا في مرض موته قليلا ولكنه كان فيما قيل ضنينا بفوائده واستقر بعده الشمس التفهني ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Kāfī b. ʿAlī b. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid b. Muḥammad b. Ṣaghīr, al-Kamāl b. al-Shams b. al-ʿAlāʾ, Cairene, Ḥanbalī, physician, grandson of the chief of physicians, known like his forebears as Ibn Ṣaghīr. He memorised the Qurʾān, the ʿUmda, al-Khiraqī, the Alfiyya, al-Mūjaz fī al-ṭibb, al-Lamḥa al-ʿAfīfiyya on causes and symptoms, the Aphorisms of Hippocrates and his Prognostics, the Anatomy of the Organs and al-Zubad fī al-ṭibb, presenting them in 816 to al-ʿIzz Ibn Jamāʿa and others, who gave him ijāza (he had presented earlier in 811). He practised medicine like his forebears, taking it from his father and al-ʿIzz Ibn Jamāʿa, excelled and trained a group, treated the sick for a long time, held a shift at the hospital and at Barqūq's mausoleum, and travelled with the sultan's expedition to Āmid with other physicians under their chief. He performed the pilgrimage several times and resided in Mecca. A servant boy attacked him, killed his wife and stole some of his goods — the beginning of his decline; he went blind but did not cease his duties until bedridden, patient and much given to Qurʾān recitation, until he died in Ṣafar 891 aged ninety-six, as his brother al-ʿAlāʾ ʿAlī, who inherited from him with his wife, told me. Like my father I trusted his treatment for his skill, calm, gentleness, fine address and dignity; he treated our shaykh briefly in his final illness, but was said to be sparing with his knowledge. Al-Shams al-Tafahnī succeeded him."@en .

rec:AIND-D08981a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08981a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08981a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن علي النوبي خطيبها ويعرف فيها بابن حيدرة . ممن سمع مني أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī al-Nūbī, its preacher, known there as Ibn Ḥaydara. One of those who heard from me as well."@en .

rec:AIND-D08986a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08986a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D08986a-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D08986a-resp-3,
        rec:AIND-D08986a-resp-4,
        rec:AIND-D08986a-resp-5 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_b88_apply,
        agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08986a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن عمر بن أبي بكر الشمس الصرخدي الأصل الدمشقي الشافعي المقرئ ويعرف بالصرخدي . ولد في سنة أربعين وثمانمائة تقريبا بدمشق ونشأ بها فحفظ القرآن والتنبيه عند أحمد الزينوني بنونين وزاي مفتوحة نسبة لقريبة من قرى البقاع وجود القرآن مع قراءة عاصم علي إسماعيل الحنبلي الدمشقي نزيل صالحيتها وتلا به للكسائي وعاصم علي الشمس بن النجار ولأبي عمرو فقط على الزين خطاب وعليه قرأ البخاري والمصابيح بتمامهما وحضر دروسه ودروس النجم بن قاضي عجلون وجمعا للسبع علي عمر الطيبي الصالحي الضرير وخليل اللدي إمام الجامع الأموي وكانا شافعيين وقرأ على إبراهيم الناجي صحيح مسلم إلا يسيرا من أوله وسمع عليه البخاري والترغيب وغيرهما وحضر مجالس النظام بن مفلح بل قرأ على قريبه البرهان القاضي شيئا من القرآن في آخرين ، وحج غير مرة وجاور بمكة وقرأ بها على الشمس المسيري في الفقه وغيره وابن أمير حاج الحلبي الحنفي رسالة الزين الخافي وسمع على النجم عمر بن فهد في مسند أحمد وعلى أبي الفضل المرجاني في البخاري وصحب العلاء بن السيد عفيف الدين والبرهان إبراهيم القادري وغيرهما من السادات ودخل مصر في التجارة وتكرر سفره لجدة بسببها بل له حانوت في بلده ، ولما كنت بمكة في سنة ثلاث وتسعين رأيته يقوم بالناس التراويح في رمضان فكان من أكثر القائمين زحاما لجودة قراءته ، ثم تكرر اجتماعه علي في التي تليها بل أخذ عني الكثير من الكتب الستة وغيرها سماعا علي ومني وكتبت له إجازة في كراسة وكذا حضر عند عبد المعطي المغربي في الرسالة والعوارف ، ونعم الرجل سمتا وعقلا وتوددا وخيرا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. Abī Bakr, al-Shams, of Ṣarkhad origin, Damascene, Shāfiʿī, Qurʾān reciter, known as al-Ṣarkhadī. Born about 840 in Damascus, he memorised the Qurʾān and al-Tanbīh with Aḥmad al-Zaynūnī, perfected the Qurʾān in ʿĀṣim's reading with Ismāʿīl al-Ḥanbalī al-Dimashqī of al-Ṣāliḥiyya, recited in the readings of al-Kisāʾī and ʿĀṣim to al-Shams Ibn al-Najjār and in Abū ʿAmr's only to al-Zayn Khaṭṭāb, to whom he also read the whole of al-Bukhārī and al-Maṣābīḥ and whose lessons, and those of al-Najm Ibn Qāḍī ʿAjlūn, he attended. He combined the seven readings under ʿUmar al-Ṭayyibī al-Ṣāliḥī the blind and Khalīl al-Luddī, imam of the Umayyad mosque; read Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim (but for a little of its beginning) to Ibrāhīm al-Nājī, hearing from him al-Bukhārī, al-Targhīb and others; attended al-Niẓām Ibn Mufliḥ; and read some Qurʾān to his relative al-Burhān al-Qāḍī, among others. He performed the pilgrimage several times and resided in Mecca, reading there fiqh etc. with al-Shams al-Musayrī and the Risāla of al-Zayn al-Khāfī with Ibn Amīr Ḥājj al-Ḥalabī al-Ḥanafī, hearing the Musnad of Aḥmad from al-Najm ʿUmar Ibn Fahd and al-Bukhārī from Abū al-Faḍl al-Marjānī, and keeping company with al-ʿAlāʾ Ibn al-Sayyid ʿAfīf al-Dīn, al-Burhān Ibrāhīm al-Qādirī and other masters. He entered Egypt in trade and travelled repeatedly to Jedda for it, and has a shop in his home town. When I was in Mecca in 893 I saw him lead the tarāwīḥ in Ramaḍān, drawing among the largest crowds for the beauty of his recitation; the next year he met me repeatedly, took much of the Six Books and other works from me by audition, and I wrote him an ijāza in a quire. He also attended ʿAbd al-Muʿṭī al-Maghribī for the Risāla and the ʿAwārif. A fine man in bearing, intelligence, affability and goodness."@en .

rec:AIND-D08989a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D08989a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D08989a-resp-2,
        rec:AIND-D08989a-resp-3 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D08989a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن عمر بن علي بن أحمد بن محمد ناصر الدين بن الجمال أبي عبد الله القرشي الطنبدي القاهري الشافعي الماضي أخوه عمر وأبوهما ويعرف كسلفه بابن عرب . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة ثمان وسبعين ويقال أنه جاز التسعين وأنه ناب عن الجلال البلقيني فمن بعده بعد أن حفظ في صغره التنبيه وعرضه واشتغل قليلا ، وكان منجمعا عن الناس مديما للإقامة بمنزله كأخيه وأكثر أقاربه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmar b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad b. Muḥammad, Nāṣir al-Dīn b. al-Jamāl Abī ʿAbd Allāh al-Qurashī al-Ṭanbadī al-Qāhirī al-Shāfiʿī; his brother ʿUmar and their father have been mentioned; known like his forebears as Ibn ʿArab. He died in Jumādā I 878, said to have passed ninety, and to have deputised for al-Jalāl al-Bulqīnī and his successors, after memorising al-Tanbīh in his youth, presenting it and studying a little. Like his brother and most of his relatives he kept apart from people, staying always at home."@en .

rec:AIND-D09009a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D09009a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D09009a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن عميرة الصيداوي نزيل دمشق وأحد المتصوفة . مات سنة تسع وستين عن نحو الثمانين . كتب عنه البدري في مجموعه قوله : %~% وسائس حمدت فيه وجدا %~% لما غدا كامل الرياسة %~% %~% فرحت للشرع أشتكيه %~% فقال لي خذه بالسياسة %~% وكان بديع الخط حسن البزة والعشرة متجملا كريما ذا محاسن ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. ʿUmayra al-Ṣaydāwī, resident of Damascus and one of the Sufis. He died in 869 aged about eighty. Al-Badrī recorded in his Majmūʿ his verse: \"A governor in whom I praised passion, when he became perfect in leadership; / I went to complain of him to the sharīʿa, and he said to me: take him by siyāsa.\" He wrote a beautiful hand, was well dressed and good company, elegant, generous and full of merits."@en .

rec:AIND-D09103a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D09103a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D09103a-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D09103a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد الكمال أبو الفضل المطري أخو الذي قبله وشقيق أم كلثوم التي تزوج بها القاضي المالكي شمس الدين السخاوي ، أمهما خديجة ابنة القاضي علي الزرندي . سمع من أبيه جل مسند الشافعي ومن التقي بن فهد وغيرهما بل قرأ على أبي الفرج المراغي وأخذ عن الشهاب الأبشيطي في الفقه والعربية وغيرهما وتلقى عن أبيه الأذان. مات في رجوعه من الحج عند مفرح ليلة الحادي والعشرين من ذي الحجة سنة ست وستين فجيء به إلى المدينة ودفن بالبقيع ولم يبلغ الأربعين وهو خاتمة الذكور من بيت المطري رحمه الله وأعقب ابنته خديجة التي تزوج بها بعد المحب بن القاضي خير الدين المالكي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad, al-Kamāl Abū al-Faḍl al-Maṭarī, brother of the preceding entry and full brother of Umm Kulthūm, whom the Mālikī judge Shams al-Dīn al-Sakhāwī married; their mother was Khadīja, daughter of the judge ʿAlī al-Zarandī. He heard most of the Musnad of al-Shāfiʿī from his father, and from al-Taqī Ibn Fahd and others; read to Abū al-Faraj al-Marāghī; took fiqh, Arabic and other subjects from al-Shihāb al-Abshīṭī; and received the call to prayer (adhān) from his father. He died on his return from the pilgrimage at Mufriḥ on the night of 21 Dhū al-Ḥijja 866, was brought to Medina and buried in al-Baqīʿ, not having reached forty. He was the last of the males of the Maṭarī house. He left a daughter, Khadīja, who after him married al-Muḥibb b. al-Qāḍī Khayr al-Dīn al-Mālikī."@en .

rec:AIND-D09231a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D09231a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D09231a-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D09231a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن الامام حجة الاسلام أبي حامد محمد بن محمد بن محمد المحيوي أبو حامد الطوسي الغزالي الشافعي . قدم من بلاده الى حلب في رمضان سنة ثلاثين بعد دخوله الشام قديما وسمع فيها من ابن أميلة وحدث عنه الآن بحلب ، ووصفه حافظها البرهان والعلاء بن خطيب الناصرية بالعلم والدين وأنه قال لهما ان جده الثامن هو الغزالي زاد ثانيهما رأيت أتباعه وتلامذته يذكرون عنه علما كثيرا وزهدا وورعا وأنه معظم في بلاده من بيت علم ودين وأخبر بعض الطلبة عنه أنه حج مرارا منها مرة ماشيا على قدم التجريد قال وبلغني أنه رأى ملك الموت فسأله متى يموت فقال له في العشر فلم يدر أي عشر فاتفق أنه مات في العشر الأخير من رمضان يوم السبت ثاني عشريه سنة ثلاثين المذكورة بحلب وكانت جنازته مشهودة وذكره شيخنا في إنبائه وقال أخذ عنه ابراهيم بن علي الزمزمي المكي يعني التصريف كما تقدم في ترجمته ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. the Imam Ḥujjat al-Islām Abī Ḥāmid Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, al-Muḥyawī Abū Ḥāmid al-Ṭūsī al-Ghazālī al-Shāfiʿī. He came from his homeland to Aleppo in Ramaḍān 830, having entered Syria long before, when he heard there from Ibn Umayla, from whom he now transmitted in Aleppo. Its ḥāfiẓ al-Burhān and al-ʿAlāʾ Ibn Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya described him as learned and pious, and said he told them that his eighth ancestor was al-Ghazālī; the latter added that he saw his followers and pupils attribute to him much learning, asceticism and scrupulousness, and that he was honoured in his country as of a house of learning and religion. Some students reported that he made the pilgrimage several times, once on foot in destitution; it was said that he saw the Angel of Death and asked when he would die, and was told \"in the ten\" — and it so happened that he died in the last ten days of Ramaḍān, Saturday the 22nd, of that year 830 in Aleppo, with a well-attended funeral. Our shaykh mentioned him in the Inbāʾ, saying that Ibrāhīm b. ʿAlī al-Zamzamī al-Makkī took from him — i.e. morphology, as noted in his entry."@en .

rec:AIND-D09231b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D09231b-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D09231b-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D09231b ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد البدر أبو البقاء الأنصاري السخاوي المليجي الاصلي القاهري الشافعي سبط الحسني لكون أبي أمه التي هي ابنة للقاضي المجد إسماعيل الحنفي كان شريفا وهو سبط المجد أيضا ويعرف بالبدر الأنصاري . ولد في ليلة السبت حادي عشر جمادى الاولى سنة عشر وثمانمائة بالقاهرة ونشأ بها فحفظ القرآن وأقبل على الاشتغال حين قارب البلوغ وأدرك الشهاب الطنتدائي فأخذ عنه وانتفع بالشرف السبكي في الفقه وبأبي الجود في الفرائض وبشيخنا ابن خضر فيهما وفي العربية في آخرين وسمع على شيخنا اليسير ثم معنا على الرشيدي ونحوه وتكسب بالشهادة وقتا وتنزل في سعيد السعداء وغيرها وأقرأ ولد الشهاب الشطنوفي و غيره وكان بارعا في الحساب والفرائض مشاركا في الفقه والعربية وغيرهما كثير الاسقام متقللا من الدنيا قانعا باليسير منجمعا متوددا ذا نظم وسط ونثر وتصانيف منها شرح تنقيح اللباب والرحبية±±± ، كتبت عنه من نظمه أشياء منها قوله : %~% لقد تعجبت ممن يحتمي زمنا %~% عن الطعام لخوف الداء والوجع %~% %~% وليس ذا حمية عن ذنبه أبدا %~% خوفا من النار والتوبيخ والفزع %~% مات في يوم الأحد ثاني عشر رجب سنة تسع وستين رحمه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Muḥammad b. Muḥammad (×9), al-Badr Abū al-Baqāʾ al-Anṣārī al-Sakhāwī, of Malīj origin, Cairene, Shāfiʿī, \"grandson of al-Ḥasanī\" because his mother's father was a sharīf, his mother being a daughter of the judge al-Majd Ismāʿīl al-Ḥanafī, so that he was al-Majd's descendant too; known as al-Badr al-Anṣārī. Born on the night of Saturday 11 Jumādā I 810 in Cairo, he memorised the Qurʾān, took up study near puberty, caught al-Shihāb al-Ṭanṭadāʾī and took from him, and benefited from al-Sharaf al-Subkī in fiqh, Abū al-Jūd in inheritance law, and our shaykh Ibn Khiḍr in both and in Arabic, among others. He heard a little from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar), then with us from al-Rashīdī and the like. He earned for a time as a notary witness, held posts at Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ and elsewhere, and taught the son of al-Shihāb al-Shaṭanūfī and others. He excelled in arithmetic and inheritance law, with a share in fiqh and Arabic; sickly, ascetic, content with little, retiring and affable; of middling verse and prose, with works including a commentary on Tanqīḥ al-Lubāb and on al-Raḥbiyya. I wrote down some of his verse. He died on Sunday 12 Rajab 869."@en .

rec:AIND-D09851a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D09851a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D09851a ;
    aindv:sourceText "محمود بن علی بن ابی بکر شیخ معمر يعرف بمحمود جند على. لقيه الطاووسی في سنة ثمان وعشرين بشيراز وقال انه يومئذ ابن مائة وست عشرة سنة فاستجازه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Maḥmūd b. ʿAlī b. Abī Bakr, a long-lived shaykh known as Maḥmūd Jand ʿAlī. Al-Ṭāwūsī met him in Shiraz in 828; he said he was then 116 years old, so al-Ṭāwūsī asked him for ijāza."@en .

rec:AIND-D10060a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10060a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10060a ;
    aindv:sourceText "موسى بن الحسين بن محمد بن على بن محمد بن أبي الرجال أحمد بن عبد الله بن عيسى بن أحمد بن على بن محمد بن محمد القطب الحسينى اليونينى البعلى الحنبلى . ولد في ربيع الأول سنة اثنتين وستين وسبعمائة واشتغل في الفقه والفرائض والنحو على الشمس بن اليونانية وفي الفرائض على أبيه وسمع صحيح مسلم على أحمد بن عبد الكريم البعلى والتوكل لابن أبى الدنيا على أحمد بن محمد بن راشد بن خطليشا والصحيح على محمد بن علي بن أحمد اليونيني ومحمد بن محمد بن إبراهيم الحسينى ومحمد بن أحمد الجردى وقرأ السيرة لابن إسحق على النجم بن الكشك , وحدث سمع منه الفضلاء . ومات قريب الأربعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Mūsā b. al-Ḥusayn b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Abī al-Rijāl Aḥmad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿĪsā b. Aḥmad b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad, al-Quṭb al-Ḥusaynī al-Yūnīnī al-Baʿlī al-Ḥanbalī. Born in Rabīʿ I 762, he studied fiqh, inheritance law and grammar with al-Shams Ibn al-Yūnāniyya and inheritance law with his father; heard Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim from Aḥmad b. ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Baʿlī, al-Tawakkul of Ibn Abī al-Dunyā from Aḥmad b. Muḥammad b. Rāshid Ibn Khaṭlīshā, and the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Aḥmad al-Yūnīnī, Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm al-Ḥusaynī and Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Jardī; and read the Sīra of Ibn Isḥāq to al-Najm Ibn al-Kashk. He transmitted, and learned men heard from him. He died near forty."@en .

rec:AIND-D10060b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10060b-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10060b-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10060b ;
    aindv:sourceText "موسى بن خليل بن أحمد بن أبى بكر بن غزالة الشرف البعلى القبانى . ولد قبيل التسعين ببعلبك ونشأ بها فسمع الصحيح بفوت±±± على ابن الزعبوب أنا الحجار ولقيته ببلده فقرأت عليه المائة لابن تيمية . وكان إنسانا صالحا يتكسب بالنقبين وغيره . ومات قريب الستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Mūsā b. Khalīl b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr b. Ghazāla, al-Sharaf al-Baʿlī al-Qabbānī. Born shortly before 790 in Baalbek, he grew up there and heard the Ṣaḥīḥ, with gaps, from Ibn al-Zaʿbūb (who had it from al-Ḥajjār). I met him in his town and read to him the Hundred of Ibn Taymiyya. He was a righteous man who earned his living by [naqbayn, sic] and other means. He died near sixty."@en .

rec:AIND-D10060c a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10060c-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10060c-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10060c ;
    aindv:sourceText "موسى بن رجب بن راشد بن ناصر الدين محمد الشرف الكناني الجلجولى المقدسى الشافعى . ولد سنة إحدى أو إثنتين وعشرين وسبعمائة بجلجوليا ونشأ بها فقرأ القرآن عند الشمس القلقبلي وبعض التنبيه وحضر دروس العز عبد السلام القدسى وغيره وناب في القضاء ببيت المقدس عن ابن السائح ولازم المحب بن الشحنة حين إفامته هناك , وتردد للقاهرة غير مرة وفي رجوعه منها مرة رافقناه فرأيته خفيف الروح لطيف العشرة يغلب عليه المجون والخراعة وتولع بالأدب وبالنظم وكتبت عنه في المكان المعروف بابن أبى الفرج من قطيا أشياء أوردتها في المعجم منها قوله في مليح اسمه علم الدين : %~% رام العذول سلوى عن هوى رشأ %~% ذاب الفؤاد به من شدة الألم %~% %~% فقلت كيف سلوى عن هواه وقد %~% أمسى غرامي به نار على علم %~% مات تقريبا سنة ثمانين رحمه الله وعفا عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Mūsā b. Rajab b. Rāshid b. Nāṣir al-Dīn Muḥammad, al-Sharaf al-Kinānī al-Jaljūlī al-Maqdisī al-Shāfiʿī. Born in [8]21 or 822 at Jaljūliyā, he read the Qurʾān and part of al-Tanbīh with al-Shams al-Qalqablī, attended the lessons of al-ʿIzz ʿAbd al-Salām al-Qudsī and others, deputised as judge in Jerusalem for Ibn al-Sāʾiḥ, and attached himself to al-Muḥibb Ibn al-Shiḥna during his stay there. He went to Cairo several times; on one return journey we travelled with him, and I found him light-spirited and pleasant company, though given to jesting and licence, fond of literature and verse. I wrote down from him, at the place known as Ibn Abī al-Faraj near Qaṭyā, pieces which I included in the Muʿjam, including lines on a handsome youth named ʿAlam al-Dīn. He died about 880."@en .

rec:AIND-D10092a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10092a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10092a ;
    aindv:sourceText "موسى بن زين العابدين محمد بن موسى بن محمد بن علي بن حسن القادرى الماضى أبوه وجده . أسمعه أبوه مع والدى على جماعة , ومات معه في الطاعون سنة أربع وستين وهما صغيران عوضهما الله وايانا الجنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Mūsā b. Zayn al-ʿĀbidīn Muḥammad b. Mūsā b. Muḥammad b. ʿAlī b. Ḥasan al-Qādirī, whose father and grandfather have been mentioned. His father had him hear, together with my father, from a group of shaykhs. He died with him in the plague of 864, both still young."@en .

rec:AIND-D10092b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10092b-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10092b ;
    aindv:sourceText "موسى بن محمد بن موسى السهمى الامير صاحب حلي ابن يعقوب من بلاد اليمن . مات بها في ربيع الآخر سنة تسع وستين وكان يعد من الأعيان ذوي البيوت في الممالك ممن لجده مع الشريف حسن بن عجلان وقائع ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Mūsā b. Muḥammad b. Mūsā al-Sahmī, the amir, lord of Ḥalī Ibn Yaʿqūb in Yemen. He died there in Rabīʿ II 869. He was counted among the notables of established houses in the kingdoms; his grandfather had battles with the Sharīf Ḥasan b. ʿAjlān."@en .

rec:AIND-D10112a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10112a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10112a-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10112a ;
    aindv:sourceText "ميلب بن علي بن مبارك بن رميئة بن أبي نمي الحسني . مات بخليص في ليلة الجمعة ساد عشرى رجب سنة تسع وثلاثين وحمل إلى مكة فدفن بالحجون بالقرب من قبر خاله وأمه سعدانة ابنة عجلان بن رميثة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Maylab b. ʿAlī b. Mubārak b. Rumaytha b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī. He died at Khulayṣ on the night of Friday 26 Rajab 839 and was carried to Mecca and buried at al-Ḥajūn near the grave of his maternal uncle. His mother was Saʿdāna bt. ʿAjlān b. Rumaytha. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D10112b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10112b-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10112b ;
    aindv:sourceText "ميلب بن محمد بن أبي سويد بن أبي دعيج بن أبي نمي الحسني . كان ينسب لشجاعة وشهامة . قتل مع عمه علي بن أبي سويد في شعبان سنة تسع وعشرين ذكره الفاسي في ذيل سير النبلاء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Maylab b. Muḥammad b. Abī Suwayd b. Abī Duʿayj b. Abī Numayy al-Ḥasanī. He was credited with courage and gallantry. He was killed with his uncle ʿAlī b. Abī Suwayd in Shaʿbān 829. Al-Fāsī mentioned him in the Dhayl Siyar al-Nubalāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D10112c a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10112c-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10112c-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10112c ;
    aindv:sourceText "ميلب السيد المجاشي . مات في ثامن ذي الحجة سنة تسع وخمسين . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Maylab, al-Sayyid al-Mujāshī. He died on 8 Dhū al-Ḥijja 859. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D10112d a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10112d-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10112d ;
    aindv:sourceText "ميمون بن أحمد بن محرز الجزيري . مات في سنة ثمان عشرة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Maymūn b. Aḥmad b. Muḥriz al-Jazīrī. He died in 818."@en .

rec:AIND-D10112e a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10112e-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10112e ;
    aindv:sourceText "ميمون غلام الفخار . أقام في الرق حتى مات جوعا سنة عشر وله في الرسم والأداء تصانيف منها النحفة والدرة بل نظم الرسالة في الفقه أرجوزة وكذا الجروميت أفاده لي زروق ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Maymūn, slave of al-Fakhkhār. He remained in bondage until he died of hunger in 810. He has works on Qurʾānic orthography and recitation, among them al-Nuḥfa and al-Durra; he even versified the Risāla on fiqh as a rajaz poem, and likewise the Ājurrūmiyya. Zarrūq informed me of this."@en .

rec:AIND-D10115a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10115a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10115a ;
    aindv:sourceText "ناصر بن خليل بن مسعود الغرس الميقاتي أحد صوفية الشافعية بخانقاه شيخو ومؤدب أطفال مكتبها . ولد سنة ثلاث وسبعين وسبعمائة تقريبا . جرده البقاعي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Nāṣir b. Khalīl b. Masʿūd, al-Ghars al-Mīqātī, one of the Shāfiʿī Sufis of the khānqāh of Shaykhū and teacher of the children of its maktab. Born about 773. Al-Biqāʿī excerpted his entry."@en .

rec:AIND-D10115b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10115b-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10115b ;
    aindv:sourceText "ناصر بن عبد العزيز بن حسن البصري الشهير بالطماع . صاهر الشرف الغلة على والدته . ومات في المحرم سنة ثمان وخمسين بمكة . أرخه ابن فهد ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Nāṣir b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Ḥasan al-Baṣrī, famous as al-Ṭammāʿ (\"the greedy\"). Al-Sharaf al-Ghalla became his relative by marrying his mother. He died in Muḥarram 858 in Mecca. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D10115c a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10115c-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10115c-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10115c ;
    aindv:sourceText "ناصر بن عبد الله الصوفي من صوفية سعيد السعداء . قال الشهاب بن المحمرة أنه لم يكن بها أحد على طريق الصوفية مثله وسمع على التنوخي وغيره . مات في رجب سنة ثلاث وثلاثين مطعونا ويحرر إن كان غير ابن محمد البسامي الآتي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Nāṣir b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣūfī, one of the Sufis of Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. Al-Shihāb Ibn al-Muḥammara said there was no one there like him on the Sufi path. He heard from al-Tanūkhī and others. He died of plague in Rajab 833. It should be checked whether he is other than Ibn Muḥammad al-Bassāmī (below)."@en .

rec:AIND-D10115d a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10115d-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10115d ;
    aindv:sourceText "ناصر بن علي بن محمد بن أحمد الانصاري الحصني ويعرف بالعراقي وبالحكيم . ولد تقريبا سنة ست عشرة وثمانمائة وقدم القاهرة بعد أن اشتغل في بلاده ولقي جماعة ، وفهم العربية وتميز في الطب وعالج به وجود الخط وكتب به أشياء وربما جلس مع الشهود . وقد تردد إلي قليلا ورام الأخذ عني وكان فخم العبارة مع فضيلة في الجملة . مات في ربيع الأول سنة إحدى وتسعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Nāṣir b. ʿAlī b. Muḥammad b. Aḥmad al-Anṣārī al-Ḥiṣnī, known as al-ʿIrāqī and as al-Ḥakīm. Born about 816, he came to Cairo after studying in his homeland and meeting a group of scholars. He understood Arabic, excelled in medicine and practised it, wrote a fine hand and composed some works, and sometimes sat with the notary witnesses. He came to me a little, wishing to study with me; he was grandiloquent, with some learning on the whole. He died in Rabīʿ I 891."@en .

rec:AIND-D10176a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10176a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10176a-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10176a ;
    aindv:sourceText "هلال الزين الرومى الظاهرى برقوق الطواشى . صار في أيام الأشرف برسباي شاد الحوش مدة ثم زماما بعد موت جوهر القنقباي ببذل مال ثم صرف عنها في سنة ست وأربعين واستمر مشتغلا بالزراعة والدواليب لشدة انهماكه في الدنيا المزرى بهيئته مع تقدمه في السن واشرافه على العمى وعدم بلوغه لطائل . مات بالطاعون في جمادي الأولى سنة اربع وستين وهو في عشر المائة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Hilāl, al-Zayn al-Rūmī al-Ẓāhirī (mamluk of Barqūq), the eunuch. In the days of al-Ashraf Barsbāy he was shādd al-ḥawsh for a time, then zimām after the death of Jawhar al-Qunqubāʾī, by paying money; he was dismissed in 846 and remained occupied with farming and waterwheels, so absorbed in worldly affairs as to disgrace his standing, despite his advanced age, near-blindness and failure to attain any real rank. He died of plague in Jumādā I 864, in his nineties."@en .

rec:AIND-D10176b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10176b-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10176b-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_b88_triage,
        agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10176b ;
    aindv:sourceText "هلال شخص مغربي له فضيلة ومشاركة . قدم القاهرة قريبا من سنة ستين فسمعته ينشد العلم البلقيني قوله وكتبه لي بخطه : %~% لما أتيت ديار مصر سائلا %~% عمن يرى يحوي بها الفضلين %~% %~% علم الحديث رواية ودراية %~% وله لواء السبق في الصنفين %~% %~% قالوا شيوخ لم يطيقوا عدهم %~% فاعددهم بالألف والألفين %~% %~% لكن سيدنا وعالم عصرنا %~% شيخ الشيوخ إمامنا البلقيني %~% %~% هم كالعيون لنا بهم إبصارنا %~% وإمامنا المذكور نور العين %~% %~% أبقى لنا رب العباد حياته %~% وأناله الخيرات في الدارين %~% ورأيت ابن عزم قال هلال البطاط مات سنة بضع وستين . فكأنه هذا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Hilāl, a Maghribī of learning and accomplishment. He came to Cairo about 860; I heard him recite his verses in praise of al-ʿAlam al-Bulqīnī, which he wrote out for me in his own hand (six lines). I saw that Ibn ʿAzm said \"Hilāl al-Baṭṭāṭ died in 86X\" — apparently this man."@en .

rec:AIND-D10193a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10193a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10193a ;
    aindv:sourceText "الوليد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمد بن محمود بن الشحنة الحلبي الحنفي الماضي أخوه المحب أبوالفضل محمد وأبوهما المحب محمد المكني أبا الوليد بصاحب الترجمة كان كما قال لي أخوه آية في الذكاء ذا نظم ونثر . مات شابا في حياة أبيه عقب الفتنة ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Al-Walīd b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Maḥmūd Ibn al-Shiḥna al-Ḥalabī al-Ḥanafī. His brother al-Muḥibb Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad and their father al-Muḥibb Muḥammad — whose kunya Abū al-Walīd derives from the subject — have been mentioned. As his brother told me, he was a marvel of intelligence, with verse and prose. He died young, in his father's lifetime, just after the disturbance (fitna)."@en .

rec:AIND-D10224a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10224a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10224a ;
    aindv:sourceText "يحيى بن أحمد بن قاسم بن علي بن حسين بن قاسم الذويد. مات بمكة في ذي القعدة سنة سبع وثلاثين. أرخه ابن فهد."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yaḥyā b. Aḥmad b. Qāsim b. ʿAlī b. Ḥusayn b. Qāsim al-Dhuwayd. He died in Mecca in Dhū al-Qaʿda 837. Ibn Fahd recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D10379a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10379a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10379a-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10379a ;
    aindv:sourceText "يشبك المؤيدى احمد بن إينال . كان خاز نداره ثم تأمر في إيام الأشرف قايتباي ومات بعد أشهر في ليلة الخميس منتصف شعبان سنة ثلاث وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yashbak al-Muʾayyadī, mamluk of (al-Muʾayyad) Aḥmad b. Īnāl. He was his treasurer (khāzindār), then became an amir in the days of al-Ashraf Qāytbāy, and died months later on the night of Thursday, mid-Shaʿbān 873."@en .

rec:AIND-D10379b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10379b-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10379b ;
    aindv:sourceText "يشبك الناصري فرج . خدم الأمراء بعد أستاذه مدة ثم رده الظاهر ططر لبيت السلطان وعمله خاصكيا ثم أنعم عليه الظاهر جقمق بأمرة عشرة ثم صيره من رؤوس النوب ثم عمله المنصور من أمراء الطبلخاناه ثم صيره الأشرف اينال رأس نوبة ثاني حتى مات في صفر سنة تسع وخمسين بعد تمرضه طويلا وقد ناهز السبعين ويقال أنه كان مسرفا±±± على نفسه عفا الله عنه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yashbak al-Nāṣirī, mamluk of (al-Nāṣir) Faraj. After his master he served the amirs for a time; then al-Ẓāhir Ṭaṭar returned him to the sultan's household and made him a khāṣṣakī; al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq granted him an emirate of ten and then made him one of the ruʾūs al-nuwab; al-Manṣūr made him an amir of ṭablkhānāh; and al-Ashraf Īnāl made him second raʾs nawba, until he died in Ṣafar 859 after a long illness, nearing seventy. He was said to have been dissolute."@en .

rec:AIND-D10379c a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10379c-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10379c ;
    aindv:sourceText "يشبك النوروزي الحافظي . تنقل بعد أستاذه حتى صار من أمراء دمشق ثم عمل حجوبية طرابلس ثم دمشق ثم نيابة طرابلس ، كل ذلك في أيام الظاهر جقمق بالبذل لعدم تأهله ثم قبض عليه وأودع السجن ثم أخرج إلى القدس فمات به بعد مدة في المحرم سنة ثلاث وستين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yashbak al-Nawrūzī, mamluk of (Nawrūz) al-Ḥāfiẓī. After his master he moved from post to post until he became one of the amirs of Damascus, then chamberlain of Tripoli, then of Damascus, then governor of Tripoli — all in the days of al-Ẓāhir Jaqmaq, by payment, as he was unqualified. Then he was arrested and imprisoned, then sent to Jerusalem, where he died after a time in Muḥarram 863."@en .

rec:AIND-D10433a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10433a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10433a ;
    aindv:sourceText "يوسف بن أحمد بن أبي بكر القدسي الشافعي ويعرف بابن الحمصي وبابن المبيض . شاب قدم القاهرة مرارا منها في سنة تسعين فسمع مني أشياء ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yūsuf b. Aḥmad b. Abī Bakr al-Qudsī al-Shāfiʿī, known as Ibn al-Ḥimṣī and as Ibn al-Mubayyiḍ. A young man who came to Cairo several times, including in 890, when he heard some things from me."@en .

rec:AIND-D10469a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10469a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10469a-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10469a ;
    aindv:sourceText "يوسف بن خلد بن أيوب الجمال الحسفاوي الحلبي الشافعي وحسفايا من قرى حلب . نشأ بحلب وحفظ القرآن وتفقه بالشهاب بن أبي الرضى ولازمه وكان تربيته وقرأ عليه القراآت السبع ، ثم سافر إلى ماردين فقرأ بها القراآت على الزين سربجا وولي قضاء ملطية سنين ثم قضاء حلب مرة بعد أخرى وكذا ولي قضاء طرابلس أيضا عودا على بدء وقضاء صفد وكتابة سرها ودخل القاهرة . وكان ذكيا فاضلا عارفا بالنحو والتفسير والفقه حسن الشكالة فائق الكتابة ذا نظم جيد ومنه أول قصيدة كتب بها لبعضهم : %~% أوجهك هذا أم سنا البدر لامع %~% فقد أشرقت بالنور منك المطالع %~% %~% حديثك للسمار خير فكاهة %~% وذكرك بالمعروف والعرف شائع %~% مات بطرابلس في ثالث عشر المحرم سنة تسع وعشرين . ذكره ابن خطيب الناصرية ثم شيخنا باختصار في إنبائه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yūsuf b. Khālid b. Ayyūb, al-Jamāl al-Ḥisfāwī al-Ḥalabī al-Shāfiʿī; Ḥisfāyā is one of the villages of Aleppo. He grew up in Aleppo, memorised the Qurʾān, studied fiqh with al-Shihāb Ibn Abī al-Riḍā, to whom he attached himself and by whom he was trained, reading the seven readings to him; then he travelled to Mardin and read the readings there to al-Zayn Sarbajā. He held the judgeship of Malatya for years, then of Aleppo repeatedly, likewise of Tripoli again, and of Safad together with its secretaryship, and he entered Cairo. He was intelligent and accomplished, versed in grammar, exegesis and fiqh, handsome, an outstanding calligrapher and a good poet (two lines quoted). He died in Tripoli on 13 Muḥarram 829. Ibn Khaṭīb al-Nāṣiriyya mentioned him, then our shaykh briefly in the Inbāʾ."@en .

rec:AIND-D10470a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10470a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10470a ;
    aindv:sourceText "يوسف بن رسلان بن محمد دغش بدال مهملة ثم معجمتين كعبس البهنسي الأصل القاهري كان ماورديا جميلا فتقرب من الغرس خليل بن خاص بك وصهره اينال بضميمته وحج قبل رياسته فلما تسلطن صار ذا أمر ونهي وأثرى وابتني دارا هائلة وتكلم في العمائر السلطانية وغيرها بل كان ناظر الذخيرة والشربخاناه والمطبخ السلطاني مع الشهادة به تلقاها عن المحرقي ، قصد في قضايا وعد في الاعيان مع عاميته . مات في جمادى الأولى سنة سبع وستين وقد زاحم الستين ودفن بتربة قشتمر خارج باب الجديد جوار مقصورة قراقجا الحسني بمقصورة أنشأها لنفسه فيها سامحه الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yūsuf b. Ruslān b. Muḥammad Daghsh (dāl, then ghayn and shīn, on the pattern of ʿAbs), of Bahnasā origin, Cairene. He was a handsome rose-water seller who won the favour of al-Ghars Khalīl b. Khāṣṣ Bak and his in-law Īnāl under the latter's protection, and made the pilgrimage before Īnāl's rise; when Īnāl became sultan he came to command and forbid, grew rich, built an enormous house, had a say in the royal buildings and more, and was supervisor of the treasury store, the beverage-house and the royal kitchen, together with their notaryship, which he had received from al-Muḥriqī. He was resorted to in lawsuits and counted among the notables despite his lack of learning. He died in Jumādā I 867, nearing sixty, and was buried in the mausoleum of Qushtamur outside Bāb al-Jadīd, next to the enclosure of Qarāqajā al-Ḥasanī, in an enclosure he had built for himself."@en .

rec:AIND-D10470b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10470b-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10470b-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10470b ;
    aindv:sourceText "يوسف بن سويلمة جمال الدين الفقيه مؤدب الابناء . مات في ذي الحجة سنة تسع وستين بمدينة سنهور وقد عمر . أرخه ابن المنير ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yūsuf b. Suwaylima, Jamāl al-Dīn, the jurist, teacher of children. He died in Dhū al-Ḥijja 869 in the town of Sanhūr, having lived long. Ibn al-Munīr recorded his death."@en .

rec:AIND-D10498a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10498a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10498a ;
    aindv:sourceText "يوسف بن الشيخ على بن سالم الغزى خطيب جامع سنجر الجاولي ، بها لقيه حسين الفتحي بغزة سنة أربع وأربعين فسمع خطبته بالجامع المذكور ثم كتبها منه ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yūsuf b. al-Shaykh ʿAlī b. Sālim al-Ghazzī, preacher of the mosque of Sanjar al-Jāwulī. Ḥusayn al-Fatḥī met him in Gaza in 844, heard his sermon in that mosque and then wrote it down from him."@en .

rec:AIND-D10498b a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10498b-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10498b ;
    aindv:sourceText "يوسف بن علي بن عبيد السنتاوي ثم القاهري الأزهري الشافعي . ممن حفظ القرآن وغيره واشتغل على الزواوي وزكريا وآخرين ، بل رافق الثاني في السماع على شيخنا ، وكذا سمع ختم البخاري بالظاهرية وكان خيرا لونا واحدا ممن حج وأم بالأقبغاوية وتنزل في سعيد السعداء وتجرع فاقة سيما بعد انقطاعه وتوالى ضعفه وابتلائه في بدنه بل كف ولم ينفعه صاحبه بشيء يذكر في أيام قضائه. ومات ظنا في سنة خمس وتسعين عن بضع وسبعين ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yūsuf b. ʿAlī b. ʿUbayd al-Santāwī, then Cairene, of al-Azhar, Shāfiʿī. He memorised the Qurʾān and other texts, studied with al-Zawāwī, Zakariyyā and others, and accompanied the latter in hearing from our shaykh (Ibn Ḥajar); he also attended the completion of al-Bukhārī at the Ẓāhiriyya. He was a good, single-hearted man who performed the pilgrimage, served as imam at the Aqbughāwiyya and held a post at Saʿīd al-Suʿadāʾ. He suffered poverty, especially after his retirement, with continuing weakness and bodily affliction, and went blind; his friend did nothing worth mentioning for him during his judgeship. He died, probably, in 895, aged seventy-odd."@en .

rec:AIND-D10543a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10543a-resp-1 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10543a ;
    aindv:sourceText "يوسف بن محمد بن الحاج يوسف الحموي الأصل الدمشقي ويعرف بابن الصائغ وبابن الفردنك بفتح الفاء وسكون الراء وفتح المهملة وسكون النون وآخره كاف . ولد سنة ست وثمانمائة . جرده البقاعي ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Yūsuf b. Muḥammad b. al-Ḥājj Yūsuf, of Ḥamā origin, Damascene, known as Ibn al-Ṣāʾigh and as Ibn al-Fardanak. Born in 806. Al-Biqāʿī excerpted his entry."@en .

rec:AIND-D10823a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D10823a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D10823a-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_opus_5_greg2 ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D10823a ;
    aindv:sourceText "أبو بكر بن محمد بن أبي بكر بن علي بن يوسف الفخر بن الجمال الذروي الأصل المكي الشافعي ابن عم الذي قبله والماضي أبوه ويعرف بالمرشدي أيضا . حفظ المنهاج والمختصر الأصلي وغيرهما واشتغل بالفقه والنحو وكثرت عنايته بالأدب وكان ذا معرفة به وبغيره وله نظم حسن ومجاميع مفيدة وكان الجمال بن موسى المراكشي كثير الاستحسان لنظمه ودخل غير مرة اليمن للاسترزاق فأدركه أجله بزبيد يوم عرفة سنة عشرين وقد جاز الثلاثين بيسير . ذكره الفاسي أيضا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Abū Bakr b. Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr b. ʿAlī b. Yūsuf, al-Fakhr b. al-Jamāl, of Dharwa origin, Meccan, Shāfiʿī, cousin of the preceding entry, whose father has been mentioned; also known as al-Murshidī. He memorised the Minhāj, the Mukhtaṣar on uṣūl and other texts, studied fiqh and grammar, devoted much attention to literature, in which and in other things he was knowledgeable, and has fine verse and useful compilations; al-Jamāl Ibn Mūsā al-Marrākushī greatly admired his poetry. He went to Yemen several times in search of livelihood, and death overtook him at Zabīd on the day of ʿArafa 820, when he had just passed thirty. Al-Fāsī also mentioned him."@en .

rec:AIND-D13086a a prov:Entity ;
    prov:qualifiedAttribution rec:AIND-D13086a-resp-1,
        rec:AIND-D13086a-resp-2 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo agent:claude_fable_5_1,
        agent:claude_rule22_audit ;
    aindv:describes aind:AIND-D13086a ;
    aindv:sourceText "زينب ابنة الجلال عبد الرحمن بن السراج عمر بن رسلان بن نصير وأمها تركية لأبيها . ولدت قبل العشرين قيل سنة سبع عشرة وثمانمائة وتزوجها حفيد عمها الولوي أحمد بن التقي محمد بن البدر محمد بن السراج وأحمد عداد الغنم ورأت حظوة من أولهما وجلالة ولم ترع تلك النعمة فلم تظفر بعده بطائل ، وحجت وجاورت ودخلت الشام وتزوجت بخير الدين أبي الخير بن البساطي وأقبلت عليه بالمحبة الزائدة وهو معها بضده وكذا تزوجها العبادي وإبراهيم العجلوني وعجل كل منهما فراقها . وحجت غير مرة والآن فقد هشت وكبرت وضعف بصرها وانقطعت بمدرسة جدها مع مزيد صفائها وخفتها ورغبتها في الخير وأهله . ماتت في أثناء ربيع الأول سنة ست وتسعين وصلى عليها بجامع الحاكم ثم دفنت عند أختها خديجة في المدرسة البلقينية رحمها الله وإيانا ."@ar ;
    aindv:translation "Zaynab, daughter of al-Jalāl ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. al-Sirāj ʿUmar b. Ruslān b. Naṣīr (al-Bulqīnī); her mother was Turkish on her father's side. Born before 820, it is said in 817, she was married to her uncle's grandson al-Walawī Aḥmad b. al-Taqī Muḥammad b. al-Badr Muḥammad b. al-Sirāj, and to Aḥmad the sheep-counter. From the first she enjoyed favour and honour, but she did not cherish that blessing and gained nothing much after him. She performed the pilgrimage and resided in Mecca, entered Syria, married Khayr al-Dīn Abū al-Khayr Ibn al-Bisāṭī, whom she loved excessively while he was the opposite with her; likewise al-ʿAbbādī and Ibrāhīm al-ʿAjlūnī married her, and each soon parted from her. She made the pilgrimage more than once. Now she has grown old and frail, her sight weak, secluded in her grandfather's madrasa, with ever more purity, lightness and love of goodness and its people. She died in mid-Rabīʿ I 896; prayers were said over her at the mosque of al-Ḥākim, and she was buried beside her sister Khadīja in the Bulqīniyya madrasa."@en .

